window.SECTOR_NARR={"xlb":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"body":"XLB bottomed October 3, 2011 as global markets troughed after the S&P 500 fell roughly 19% from its spring peak on eurozone sovereign-debt contagion (Dexia's breakup in Belgium, EFSF inadequacy, Greek default risk) and the US AAA credit-rating downgrade in August 2011. The subsequent 96.4% rally over 3.4 years was powered by Fed Operation Twist (September 2011), the October EU summit backstop pledge, ECB LTRO (December 2011 and February 2012), and QE3 (September 2012), collectively keeping yields suppressed (TLT +15.1% over the leg) and supporting industrial metals (copper-gold +14.1). XLB ranked #6 in a reflation/growth-up quad where cyclicals rose +105% vs defensives +99%, but a +18.9% DXY over the period became the structural headwind that kept Materials from leading the recovery.","body_zh":"XLB于2011年10月3日触底，当时全球股市在欧元区主权债务危机蔓延（比利时德克西亚银行拆分、欧洲金融稳定基金救助能力不足、希腊违约风险）及2011年8月美国AAA评级遭标普下调后探底，S&P 500自春季峰值下跌约19%。随后3.4年96.4%的涨幅由美联储2011年9月操作扭曲（Operation Twist）、10月欧盟峰会担保承诺、欧洲央行2011年12月及2012年2月LTRO、以及2012年9月QE3共同驱动，压制收益率（TLT全程+15.1%）并支撑工业金属（铜金比+14.1）。XLB排名第6，处于再通胀/增长向上象限，周期股涨幅+105%对比防御股+99%，但全程美元走强（DXY +18.9%）成为阻止材料板块领涨的结构性逆风。","drivers":["eurozone crisis trough","Fed Operation Twist and QE3","ECB LTRO","reflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["欧债危机触底","美联储操作扭曲与QE3","欧洲央行LTRO","再通胀象限"],"prev_key":"2011-10-03","prev_key_chain":["2011-10-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Eurozone trough; QE reflation lifts commodities","title_zh":"欧债危机触底；量化宽松再通胀提振大宗商品","turn_id":"xlb:trough:2011-10"},"2015-02-24":{"body":"XLB peaked February 24, 2015 and fell 24.2% (ranked #9, co-worst with Energy) as the commodity complex entered a full bear market. China's structural growth deceleration — steel consumption fell for the first time in over a decade, iron ore collapsed from its multi-year ~$120-130/tonne range toward $50/tonne, copper slumped toward $2.50/lb — was the primary driver, compounded by the strong-dollar regime that had begun in 2014. The August 11, 2015 yuan devaluation of roughly 1.9% by the PBoC added a global deflation-scare shock. Defensives fell only 6.9% vs cyclicals 13.8% as the quad shifted to slowdown/deflation-scare; VIX rose from 14 to 28 and copper-gold fell -11.4.","body_zh":"XLB于2015年2月24日见顶，随后下跌24.2%（排名第9，与能源并列末位），大宗商品全面进入熊市。中国经济结构性放缓——钢铁消费十多年来首次下降，铁矿石从多年约120-130美元/吨区间跌向50美元，铜价滑向2.50美元/磅——是主要驱动力，2014年以来形成的强美元体制进一步加剧压力。2015年8月11日中国人民银行宣布人民币贬值约1.9%，叠加了全球通缩恐慌冲击。防御股仅跌6.9%对比周期股跌13.8%，象限转为增长放缓/通缩恐慌；VIX由14升至28，铜金比跌-11.4。","drivers":["China growth deceleration","iron ore and copper bear market","strong dollar regime","yuan devaluation August 2015"],"drivers_zh":["中国经济增速结构性下滑","铁矿石与铜熊市","强美元体制","2015年8月人民币贬值"],"prev_key":"2015-02-24","prev_key_chain":["2015-02-24"],"status":"exact","title":"China slowdown and strong dollar crush commodities","title_zh":"中国放缓与强势美元重创大宗商品","turn_id":"xlb:peak:2015-02"},"2015-09-28":{"body":"XLB surged +18.2% in two months to lead all sectors (#1) as deeply oversold miners and chemical stocks bounced on short-covering and tentative China stabilization signals after the August 2015 yuan-devaluation panic. The Fed delayed its first rate hike at the September 17, 2015 FOMC meeting citing global headwinds, briefly easing dollar pressure, while the PBoC had cut rates on August 25 and continued easing through the autumn. The quad was goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation (cyclicals +13.9% vs defensives +6.8%), and Materials' #1 ranking was purely mean-reversion — copper-gold stayed negative (-2.4) and oil kept falling (-5.8%), confirming a relief rally rather than a genuine commodity-cycle inflection.","body_zh":"XLB两个月内飙涨+18.2%，领涨所有板块（第1），深度超卖的矿业股与化工股在2015年8月人民币贬值恐慌后随空头回补与中国经济企稳的初步信号强势反弹。美联储于2015年9月17日FOMC会议以全球逆风为由推迟加息，短暂缓解美元压力，中国人民银行则已于8月25日降息并在整个秋季延续宽松。象限为金发女孩/增长上行-通胀回落（周期股+13.9%对比防御股+6.8%），材料板块第1排名纯属均值回归——铜金比仍为负（-2.4），油价继续下跌（-5.8%），证实此为反弹而非真正的大宗商品周期转折。","drivers":["oversold short-covering bounce","Fed September rate hike delay","PBoC rate cuts","mean-reversion from August panic"],"drivers_zh":["超卖空头回补反弹","美联储推迟9月加息","中国人民银行降息","8月恐慌后的均值回归"],"prev_key":"2015-09-28","prev_key_chain":["2015-09-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Oversold bounce on China stabilization and Fed delay","title_zh":"超卖反弹：中国经济企稳预期与美联储推迟加息","turn_id":"xlb:trough:2015-09"},"2015-12-01":{"body":"XLB fell 18.4% (ranked #9) into January 25, 2016 as the Fed's first rate hike since 2006 on December 16, 2015 — lifting the funds rate from 0-0.25% to 0.25-0.5% — reinforced the strong-dollar regime, while oil crashed another 27.5% as OPEC maintained production into excess supply. The China circuit-breaker stock-market halt on January 4, 2016 (CSI 300 tripped the 7% breaker) reignited global deflation fears and sent the S&P 500 down sharply on its first trading day of the year. XLB and Energy (-21.8%) were co-worst cyclicals; defensives lost only 2.1% vs cyclicals 14.7% as VIX rose from 15 to 24.","body_zh":"XLB自2015年12月1日至2016年1月25日下跌18.4%（排名第9），美联储2015年12月16日自2006年以来首次加息（基准利率从0-0.25%升至0.25-0.5%）强化了强美元体制，同时欧佩克维持产量导致石油在过剩供应中再跌27.5%。2016年1月4日中国股市熔断机制触发（沪深300触及7%熔断阈值）重燃全球通缩恐慌，美股新年首个交易日S&P 500大幅下挫。XLB与能源（-21.8%）并列周期股末位；防御股仅跌2.1%对比周期股跌14.7%，VIX由15升至24。","drivers":["Fed first rate hike December 2015","oil crash -27.5%","China circuit-breaker crash January 2016","strong dollar continuation"],"drivers_zh":["2015年12月美联储首次加息","油价崩跌-27.5%","2016年1月中国股市熔断","强美元延续"],"prev_key":"2015-12-01","prev_key_chain":["2015-12-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed first hike and oil crash renew commodity selloff","title_zh":"美联储首次加息与油价崩跌重燃大宗商品抛售","turn_id":"xlb:peak:2015-12"},"2016-01-25":{"body":"XLB rallied +78.6% over two years (ranked #3) from the January 2016 commodity trough as three tailwinds aligned: the February 2016 Shanghai G20 meeting's tacit coordination toward a weaker dollar (DXY -10.4% over the leg) immediately relieved dollar-priced commodity pressure; crude oil recovered from ~$26/bbl to over $70 (oil +118%), and copper-gold surged +37.3; and Trump's November 2016 election unleashed the 'reflation trade' infrastructure bid, with the March 2018 Section 232 steel/aluminum tariff announcements marking the final peak. VIX was crushed from 24 to 11, cyclicals outperformed defensives +71.2% vs +30.9%, and Materials was a top-three beneficiary of the commodity-cycle revival.","body_zh":"XLB自2016年1月大宗商品触底后两年内大涨+78.6%（排名第3），三大顺风接连出现：2016年2月G20上海会议默契协调美元走弱（DXY全程-10.4%），立即缓解了以美元计价的大宗商品压力；原油从约26美元/桶复苏至70美元以上（油价+118%），铜金比涨幅达+37.3；2016年11月特朗普当选释放了以基础设施为核心的\"再通胀交易\"，2018年3月232条款钢铝关税宣布成为最终见顶催化剂。VIX从24压缩至11，周期股以+71.2%大幅跑赢防御股+30.9%，材料板块是大宗商品周期复苏中受益最多的板块之一。","drivers":["Shanghai Accord dollar weakness -10.4% DXY","oil recovery +118%","Trump reflation and infrastructure trade","broad cyclical risk-on"],"drivers_zh":["上海协议美元走弱（DXY -10.4%）","油价复苏+118%","特朗普再通胀与基础设施交易","大范围周期性风险偏好"],"prev_key":"2016-01-25","prev_key_chain":["2016-01-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Shanghai Accord, Trump reflation, oil recovery surge","title_zh":"上海协议、特朗普再通胀交易与油价复苏","turn_id":"xlb:trough:2016-01"},"2018-01-26":{"body":"XLB peaked January 26, 2018 alongside the S&P 500 and fell 24.7% (tied worst, #10 with Financials) as the cycle turned sharply negative. Trump's Section 232 tariffs on steel (25%) and aluminum (10%) announced March 8, 2018 directly hit the input-cost stack of key XLB names (LyondellBasell, Dow, Air Products), while retaliatory tariffs from China, Canada, and the EU pressured chemical and specialty-material exports. Simultaneously, the Fed hiked four times in 2018 (March, June, September, December), driving DXY up +8.4%, which dragged copper-gold down -9.9% and oil -35.7%. The slowdown/deflation-scare quad saw defensives fall only 6.8% vs cyclicals 21.9% as VIX exploded from 11 to 36.","body_zh":"XLB于2018年1月26日与S&P 500同步见顶，随后下跌24.7%（并列垫底，第10，与金融股齐平），周期转为急剧负面。2018年3月8日特朗普宣布的232条款钢铁（25%）铝（10%）关税直接打击了XLB重要成员的成本结构（利安德巴塞尔、陶氏、气体产品），中国、加拿大和欧盟的报复性关税施压化工及特种材料出口。与此同时，美联储2018年四次加息（3月、6月、9月、12月），推动DXY升+8.4%，铜金比跌-9.9%，油价跌-35.7%。增长放缓/通缩恐慌象限中防御股仅跌6.8%对比周期股跌21.9%，VIX由11激增至36。","drivers":["Section 232 steel/aluminum tariffs March 2018","US-China trade war escalation","Fed four rate hikes in 2018","dollar surge +8.4% DXY"],"drivers_zh":["2018年3月232条款钢铝关税","美中贸易战升级","美联储2018年四次加息","美元飙升+8.4% DXY"],"prev_key":"2018-01-26","prev_key_chain":["2018-01-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade war and tighter Fed choke the cyclical bid","title_zh":"贸易战与美联储收紧扼杀周期性买盘","turn_id":"xlb:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"XLB troughed Christmas Eve 2018 during the worst December for US equities in decades and rallied +32.5% over 2019 (ranked #8) as Fed Chair Powell's January 4, 2019 'patient' remarks pivoted to a pause, followed by three insurance rate cuts (July, September, October 2019) that crushed VIX from 36 to 14 and supported risk-on; oil recovered +43.6%. Notably copper-gold actually FELL over this leg (-15.2), so industrial metals were NOT the engine — this was a Fed-and-oil-driven recovery in a Tech/mega-cap-led tape (SMH +77.3%, growth vs value +12.4) where narrow breadth (equal-weight lagged cap-weight by 3.2%) meant Materials got far less lift than highflying software and semiconductor stocks, leaving XLB a deep laggard at #8.","body_zh":"XLB于2018年圣诞前夕触底（美股数十年来最差的12月），随后2019年全年反弹+32.5%（排名第8），美联储主席鲍威尔2019年1月4日\"耐心\"表态宣告暂停加息，随后三次预防性降息（7月、9月、10月）将VIX从36压缩至14并支撑了风险偏好；油价回升+43.6%。值得注意的是，铜金比在本轮反而下跌（-15.2），因此工业金属并非引擎——这是一轮由美联储与油价驱动、科技/巨头主导的复苏（SMH +77.3%，成长>价值+12.4），市场广度狭窄（等权重落后市值加权3.2%），材料板块获得的提振远不及飞涨的软件和半导体股票，最终XLB以第8深度落后。","drivers":["Fed insurance rate cuts 2019","Powell patient pivot January 2019","oil recovery +43.6%","tech-led narrow-breadth tape"],"drivers_zh":["2019年美联储预防性降息","2019年1月鲍威尔耐心转向","油价回升+43.6%","科技引领的窄幅市场"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot and trade truce fire the recovery","title_zh":"美联储政策转向与贸易休战点燃复苏","turn_id":"xlb:trough:2018-12"},"2019-12-31":{"body":"XLB fell 37.1% (ranked #8) as COVID-19 triggered a global demand collapse from late January through March 23, 2020. Copper fell to multi-year lows as industrial activity froze, oil cratered 61.7% after the Saudi-Russia price war erupted following the March 6 OPEC+ breakdown (Saudi cut its selling price and raised output), and the DXY surged +6.3% as investors fled to dollars. The slowdown/deflation-scare quad was extreme: VIX spiked from 14 to 62, copper-gold collapsed -27.3, defensives fell 26.2% but cyclicals crashed 38.6%, credit spreads blew out (HYG vs LQD -11.3%), and equal-weight lagged cap-weight by 7.1% as megacap Tech and Staples proved the relative shelter.","body_zh":"XLB下跌37.1%（排名第8），新冠肺炎从1月下旬至2020年3月23日引发全球需求崩溃。工业活动冻结导致铜价跌至多年低位，3月6日欧佩克+会议破裂后沙特与俄罗斯爆发价格战（沙特下调售价并提高产量），油价暴跌61.7%，投资者纷纷逃往美元导致DXY上涨+6.3%。增长放缓/通缩恐慌象限极端：VIX从14飙至62，铜金比崩跌-27.3，防御股跌26.2%但周期股崩跌38.6%，信用利差爆裂（HYG vs LQD -11.3%），等权重落后市值加权7.1%，巨头科技股与必需消费品成为相对避风港。","drivers":["COVID-19 global demand shock","oil price war -61.7% (Saudi vs Russia)","dollar surge +6.3% DXY","VIX spike 14 to 62"],"drivers_zh":["新冠肺炎全球需求冲击","石油价格战-61.7%（沙特vs俄罗斯）","美元飙升+6.3% DXY","VIX暴涨14至62"],"prev_key":"2019-12-31","prev_key_chain":["2019-12-31"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash; oil and copper collapse simultaneously","title_zh":"新冠崩盘：油价与铜价同步暴跌","turn_id":"xlb:peak:2019-12"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"XLB's 145.0% surge from March 23, 2020 to April 2022 was the second-best rally in the 15-year dataset, as Materials became a primary beneficiary of the commodity supercycle revival (#2, behind only Energy). The CARES Act ($2.2T, March 2020) and the subsequent $1.9T American Rescue Plan pumped fiscal demand; China's 2020 infrastructure-led stimulus drove copper to record highs through 2021; the Biden Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act (November 2021) extended the structural demand thesis; and oil recovered +339.9% off the April 2020 negative-price episode. DXY fell 2.0% (tailwind), copper-gold rose +94.8%, breadth was enormous (equal-weight beat cap-weight by +23.3%), and cyclicals rose +147.9% vs defensives +83.4%.","body_zh":"XLB从2020年3月23日至2022年4月大涨145.0%，是15年数据集中第二大涨幅，材料板块成为大宗商品超级周期复苏的首要受益者（第2，仅次于能源）。《CARES法案》（2.2万亿美元，2020年3月）及后续《美国救援计划》（1.9万亿美元）注入财政需求；中国2020年以基础设施为主的刺激计划推动铜价于2021年创历史新高；拜登《基础设施投资与就业法》（2021年11月）延续了结构性需求主题；油价从2020年4月负价格事件后上涨+339.9%。DXY下跌2.0%（顺风），铜金比上涨+94.8%，市场广度极大（等权重跑赢市值加权+23.3%），周期股上涨+147.9%对比防御股+83.4%。","drivers":["CARES Act and ARP fiscal stimulus","China infrastructure stimulus","copper and oil supercycle","Biden infrastructure law November 2021"],"drivers_zh":["《CARES法案》与《美国救援计划》财政刺激","中国基础设施刺激","铜与油超级周期","2021年11月拜登基础设施法"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID recovery; fiscal boom powers metals supercycle","title_zh":"新冠复苏：财政繁荣驱动金属超级周期","turn_id":"xlb:trough:2020-03"},"2021-12-31":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"xlb:peak:2021-12"},"2022-07-14":{"body":"Materials snapped back +14.9% as a softer June 2022 CPI print and Fed-pivot hopes pushed the dollar off its highs (-1.9% DXY), letting copper and beaten-down metals rebound with a tech/semis-led risk-on summer rally (SMH +16.3%). It was a reflation/growth-up quad — cyclicals (+16.7%) led defensives (+7.6%) and copper-over-gold turned up +9.2 — but XLB only ranked #5: deeply oversold miners and chemicals bounced on the easing-recession narrative and a weaker greenback that relieves dollar-priced commodities, lagging the higher-beta discretionary and industrials leaders.","body_zh":"材料板块反弹+14.9%，2022年6月温和CPI数据与美联储转向预期将美元拉离高位（-1.9% DXY），使铜和遭抛售的金属随科技/半导体引领的风险偏好夏季行情回升（SMH +16.3%）。这是再通胀/增长向上象限——周期股（+16.7%）领先防御股（+7.6%），铜金比转正+9.2——但XLB仅排名第5：深度超卖的矿业与化工股在衰退缓和叙事和走软美元（利好以美元计价的大宗商品）下反弹，落后于高贝塔的可选消费与工业领涨股。","drivers":["peak-inflation hope (June 2022 CPI)","dollar pullback -1.9% DXY","tech-led risk-on bounce","reflation/growth-up quad"],"drivers_zh":["通胀见顶预期（2022年6月CPI）","美元回落（-1.9% DXY）","科技引领风险偏好反弹","再通胀/增长向上象限"],"prev_key":"2022-07-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-07-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-inflation bounce, dollar relents","title_zh":"通胀见顶反弹，美元退潮","turn_id":"xlb:trough:2022-07"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"Powell's hawkish August 26, 2022 Jackson Hole speech sent the dollar surging toward a 20-year high (+7.1% DXY) and yields ripping (TLT -10.4%), a double rate-regime-and-FX wrecking-ball that pushed copper back down and dragged gold below $1,700, pressuring Freeport and Newmont. The -17.0% (#8) drop came in a slowdown/deflation-scare flight-to-safety — defensives (-9.1%) held up better than cyclicals (-15.1%), VIX 20 to 32 — so XLB fell as the dollar-sensitive cyclical caught in a higher-for-longer regime, not on a Materials-specific catalyst.","body_zh":"鲍威尔2022年8月26日在杰克逊霍尔的鹰派讲话将美元推向20年高位（+7.1% DXY），收益率飙升（TLT -10.4%），形成利率体制与汇率的双重打击，使铜价重新下行、黄金跌破1,700美元，施压自由港与纽蒙特。这-17.0%（第8）的下跌发生在增长放缓/通缩恐慌的避险中——防御股（-9.1%）比周期股（-15.1%）更抗跌，VIX由20升至32——因此XLB是作为陷入\"更高更久\"体制的美元敏感型周期股而下跌，并非材料板块独有的催化剂。","drivers":["Jackson Hole hawkish speech August 26 2022","dollar 20-year high +7.1% DXY","rate regime TLT -10.4%","flight-to-safety VIX 20 to 32"],"drivers_zh":["2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔鹰派讲话","美元20年高位（+7.1% DXY）","利率体制（TLT -10.4%）","避险（VIX 20至32）"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole reignites the dollar wrecking-ball","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔重启美元破坏力","turn_id":"xlb:peak:2022-08"},"2022-09-26":{"body":"XLB rallied +51.0% over two years as a soft-landing economy and a collapsing dollar (-9.3% DXY) powered copper toward record highs and gold to all-time highs; the Fed's jumbo 50bp cut in September 2024 plus China's roughly $560B aggregate stimulus package announced September 2024 supercharged industrial-metals demand. But this was a tech/semis-led melt-up (SMH +169.2%, growth vs value +33.4) with narrow breadth (equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -18.9%), so Materials (#5) trailed the mega-cap leaders — strong as a cyclical in a goldilocks quad, but not where the index leadership lived. Note copper-gold actually fell -36.0 over the leg as gold's safe-haven bid outran copper.","body_zh":"材料板块两年内上涨+51.0%，软着陆经济与崩跌的美元（-9.3% DXY）推动铜价逼近历史高位、黄金创历史新高；美联储2024年9月一次性降息50个基点叠加中国2024年9月宣布的约5,600亿美元综合刺激计划，提振工业金属需求。但这是科技/半导体引领的逼空行情（SMH +169.2%，成长>价值+33.4），市场广度狭窄（等权重落后市值加权-18.9%），因此材料（第5）落后于巨头领涨股——作为金发女孩象限中的周期股表现强劲，但并非指数领涨所在。值得注意的是，铜金比全程反而下跌-36.0，因黄金避险买盘跑赢了铜。","drivers":["Fed 50bp cut September 2024","weak dollar -9.3% DXY tailwind","China stimulus September 2024","narrow mega-cap breadth SMH +169.2%"],"drivers_zh":["2024年9月美联储降息50bp","弱美元（-9.3% DXY）顺风","2024年9月中国刺激","狭窄的巨头市场广度（SMH +169.2%）"],"prev_key":"2022-09-26","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Soft landing and weak dollar lift metals, but mega-caps lead","title_zh":"软着陆与弱美元提振金属，但巨头领涨","turn_id":"xlb:trough:2022-09"},"2024-10-18":{"body":"XLB cratered -23.2% (dead last, #11) as Trump's November 2024 election win, 25% steel and aluminum duties in March 2025, and the April 2025 reciprocal tariffs triggered a crash bottoming around April 8, 2025 — Materials sat squarely in the tariff bullseye. The macro was a slowdown/deflation-scare flight-to-safety (VIX 18 to 52) where defensives (-9.3%) sharply outperformed cyclicals (-15.5%), and XLB was the most-punished cyclical of all. The dollar barely moved (-0.5% DXY), so this was a tariff-and-de-risking story, not an FX squeeze — global-cyclical chemicals and miners absorbed the worst of the trade-war de-risk.","body_zh":"材料板块暴跌-23.2%（垫底，第11），特朗普2024年11月胜选、2025年3月落地的25%钢铝关税以及4月对等关税引发崩跌并在2025年4月8日前后见底——材料正处于关税靶心。宏观背景是增长放缓/通缩恐慌的避险（VIX由18升至52），防御股（-9.3%）大幅跑赢周期股（-15.5%），而XLB是所有周期股中受打击最重的。美元几乎未动（-0.5% DXY），因此这是关税与去风险的故事，而非汇率挤压——全球周期型化工与矿业股承受了贸易战去风险的最重一击。","drivers":["Trump tariff shock (25% steel/aluminum March 2025)","reciprocal tariffs April 2025","flight-to-safety VIX 18 to 52","slowdown/deflation-scare quad"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普关税冲击（2025年3月25%钢铝关税）","2025年4月对等关税","避险（VIX由18升至52）","放缓/通缩恐慌象限"],"prev_key":"2024-10-18","prev_key_chain":["2024-10-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff shock and flight-to-safety crush the cyclical","title_zh":"关税冲击与避险打压周期股","turn_id":"xlb:peak:2024-10"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"XLB rebounded +46.6% off the tariff-crash low as a weakening dollar (-6.0% DXY) and AI/datacenter structural copper demand ran the metal to record highs (LME copper above $13,000/tonne by late January 2026) and gold surged to an all-time high near $5,500/oz on January 28-29, 2026. It rode a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +131.2%, VIX 52 to 18) in a reflation/growth-up quad, but only ranked #4 with narrow breadth (equal-weight lagged -5.9%). By early 2026 it rolled over (leg peak February 11, 2026): the Iran/Hormuz oil shock firmed the dollar again and softening Chinese industrial demand sapped the industrial-metals bid even as structural copper tightness lingered.","body_zh":"材料板块自关税崩跌低点反弹+46.6%，走弱的美元（-6.0% DXY）与AI/数据中心结构性铜需求推动铜价创历史新高（2026年1月底LME铜突破13,000美元/吨），黄金于2026年1月28-29日飙升至约5,500美元/盎司的历史高位。它搭乘了科技/半导体引领的风险偏好逼空行情（SMH +131.2%，VIX由52降至18），处于再通胀/增长向上象限，但仅排名第4，市场广度狭窄（等权重落后-5.9%）。进入2026年初板块见顶回落（本轮峰值2026年2月11日）：伊朗/霍尔木兹油价冲击再度推升美元，中国工业需求走软削弱工业金属买盘，尽管结构性的铜供应紧张仍然存在。","drivers":["weak dollar -6.0% DXY tailwind","copper and gold record highs Jan 2026","tech-led risk-on SMH +131.2%","Hormuz oil shock strong-dollar rollover"],"drivers_zh":["弱美元（-6.0% DXY）顺风","铜与黄金创历史新高（2026年1月）","科技引领风险偏好（SMH +131.2%）","霍尔木兹油价冲击强美元回落"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Metals roar back on weak dollar, then roll over","title_zh":"金属借弱美元强势回归后回落","turn_id":"xlb:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"XLB is rolling over (RS rank #7 out of 11) after its 2025-2026 post-tariff-crash rally stalled. The sector is mid-pack year-to-date (+13.3%, #4) in a reflation/growth-up quad where cyclicals are beating defensives (11.2% vs 6.9%) and oil ripped +19.2%, but a +3.4% DXY (firmed by the Hormuz oil shock) is a direct headwind for dollar-priced metals and soft Chinese industrial demand is sapping the bid for copper and specialty chemicals. Copper-over-gold (+18.3) signals structural physical supply tightness rather than demand-driven momentum, and although breadth has broadened (equal-weight beat cap-weight by +2.9%), XLB's leadership role from the 2025 recovery has faded as Tech (+24.3%) and Energy (+21.5%) now absorb the bulk of cyclical flows. The current phase is a momentum plateau where the dollar ceiling and China demand drag prevent re-acceleration despite a supportive macro quad.","now_zh":"XLB正处于回落阶段（相对强度排名第7/11），2025-2026年关税崩跌后的反弹行情已告一段落。年初至今板块表现居中（+13.3%，排名第4），处于再通胀/增长向上象限——周期股整体跑赢防御股（11.2%对比6.9%），原油强势上涨（+19.2%）——但美元走强（DXY +3.4%，受霍尔木兹海峡油价冲击推动）对以美元计价的金属构成直接逆风，中国工业需求疲软也压制了铜及特种化工品的买盘。铜金比（+18.3）显示实物供应结构性紧张而非需求驱动的狂热，尽管市场广度已经扩散（等权重跑赢市值加权+2.9%），但2025年复苏期间XLB的领涨地位已褪色——科技（+24.3%）与能源（+21.5%）正吸走大部分周期性资金流入。当前阶段是动能高原期，美元天花板与中国需求拖累阻止了板块重新加速，尽管宏观象限仍具支撑。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"xlc":{"legs":{"2018-06-19":{"body":"XLC launched June 18, 2018, just before GICS restructured the old Telecom sector into Communication Services on September 28, 2018, pulling Facebook (~22% initial weight), Alphabet, Netflix, and Disney out of Tech and Discretionary into a new basket. Despite a broad tech-led melt-up (XLK +46.9%, SMH +46.3%), XLC ranked 9th of 11 sectors (+16.9%) because Facebook shed ~25% in calendar 2018 on Cambridge Analytica/FTC regulatory blowback plus a Q4 2018 macro selloff driven by Fed tightening and US-China trade fears. Over the full leg to February 2020, the sector lagged badly versus bond-proxy defensives (Utilities +46.8%, Real Estate +38.1%) as a slowdown/deflation-scare quad kept cyclicals and oil depressed (oil -18.1%) and yields fell (TLT +25.3%), while narrow mega-cap breadth (equal-weight lagged -8.2%) concentrated gains in the pure-play tech names XLC only partially owned.","body_zh":"XLC于2018年6月18日挂牌，随后GICS于同年9月28日将旧电信板块扩建为通讯服务板块，把Facebook（初始权重约22%）、Alphabet、奈飞及迪士尼从科技与非必需消费板块划入。尽管科技股大涨（XLK +46.9%、SMH +46.3%），XLC在11个板块中仅排第9（+16.9%），因Facebook受剑桥分析/FTC监管打击而在2018年全年下跌约25%，叠加美联储加息与中美贸易战引发的四季度宏观抛售。整个至2020年2月的腿期内，XLC大幅落后于债券替代型防御股（公用事业+46.8%、房地产+38.1%），慢增长/通缩恐慌象限压制了周期股与油价（-18.1%）、收益率走低（TLT +25.3%），窄幅大市值主导行情（等权重跑输-8.2%）令XLC结构性受损。","drivers":["GICS reclassification","Cambridge Analytica/FTC headwind","Q4 2018 macro selloff","mega-cap narrow breadth","defensives-led slowdown quad"],"drivers_zh":["GICS重组","剑桥分析/FTC监管","2018年四季度宏观抛售","大市值窄幅行情","防御股主导慢增长象限"],"prev_key":"2018-06-19","prev_key_chain":["2018-06-19"],"status":"exact","title":"GICS rebirth muted by mega-cap headwinds","title_zh":"GICS重组落地，大市值个股承压","turn_id":"xlc:trough:2018-06"},"2020-02-19":{"body":"From February 19 to March 20 2020, XLC fell -30.1% as COVID-19 panic detonated a system-wide deleveraging — VIX spiked from 14 to 66 and the S&P lost -32%. XLC ranked 3rd least-bad (only Staples -21.8% and Health -24.0% outperformed) because its streaming/digital-platform holdings were partially shielded versus cyclical carnage (Energy -52.9%, Industrials -38.9%), but the ad-market freeze and entertainment shutdowns gutted the basket's revenue outlook. Defensives held better (-25.9% avg) while cyclicals collapsed (-38.0%), confirming a flight-to-safety rotation rather than sector-specific resilience — XLC's relative outperformance was simply the absence of oil exposure and leverage.","body_zh":"2020年2月19日至3月20日，新冠疫情恐慌引爆系统性去杠杆，VIX从14飙至66、标普下跌-32%，XLC跌幅-30.1%，在11个板块中排名第3抗跌（仅必需消费-21.8%与医疗-24.0%表现更好）。流媒体/数字平台持仓对板块形成部分保护，使XLC免于遭受能源（-52.9%）与工业（-38.9%）的周期性崩塌，但广告市场骤冻和娱乐业停工重创了篮子营收前景。防御股相对抗跌（均值-25.9%）而周期股崩塌（-38.0%），印证了这是一次避险轮动而非XLC的板块优势——其相对韧性不过是缺乏能源与杠杆敞口而已。","drivers":["COVID pandemic shock","VIX 14-to-66 spike","ad-market freeze","flight-to-safety rotation","oil/cyclical collapse"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情冲击","VIX飙升至66","广告市场骤冻","避险轮动","油价/周期股崩塌"],"prev_key":"2020-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash hits media and ad revenue","title_zh":"新冠疫情冲击广告收入与媒体板块","turn_id":"xlc:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-20":{"body":"Off the March 20 2020 panic low, XLC surged +116.6% to rank 2nd of 11 sectors (trailing only XLK +126.2%) as the broadest fiscal and monetary stimulus in US history — the $2.2tn CARES Act, the Fed cutting to 0% and expanding QE to $120bn/month — unleashed a cyclical/growth recovery. XLC's holdings were turbo-charged: Netflix added 15.77mn subscribers in Q1 2020 alone (double projections), Disney+ reached ~50mn users by early April, and Alphabet/Facebook delivered record digital ad revenue as the economy reopened in H2 2020. The reflation/growth-up quad (VIX 66-to-16, dollar -10.1%, oil +205.8%, semis +169.4%) ran from March 2020 through September 2021, making XLC's mega-cap digital names a core beneficiary of the growth-over-value surge (+31.1%).","body_zh":"自2020年3月20日恐慌低点起，XLC大涨+116.6%，在11个板块中排名第2（仅次于XLK的+126.2%）。美国史上最大规模财政与货币刺激——2.2万亿美元CARES法案、美联储降息至零并将QE扩至每月1200亿美元——引爆周期性/成长修复。XLC持仓受结构性顺风加持：奈飞仅2020年一季度就新增1577万用户（是预期的两倍）、Disney+到4月初用户约达5000万、Alphabet/Facebook在经济重开后的2020年下半年创下数字广告收入纪录。整个2020年3月至2021年9月的再通胀/成长上行象限（VIX从66降至16、美元-10.1%、油价+205.8%、半导体+169.4%），令XLC大型数字平台股成为成长跑赢价值（+31.1%）行情的核心受益者。","drivers":["Fed zero rates + QE expansion","CARES Act fiscal stimulus","streaming subscriber surge","digital ad recovery","reflation growth-up quad"],"drivers_zh":["美联储零利率+QE扩张","CARES法案财政刺激","流媒体用户激增","数字广告复苏","再通胀/成长上行象限"],"prev_key":"2020-03-20","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Pandemic digital surge lifts streaming and ad giants","title_zh":"疫情数字化浪潮提振流媒体与广告巨头","turn_id":"xlc:trough:2020-03"},"2021-09-01":{"body":"XLC was 2022's worst-hit S&P sector (-46.7%, rank 11/11) as a digital ad recession gutted Meta and Alphabet and Netflix cratered ~35% in a day on its first subscriber loss in over a decade (Q1 2022, -200K subs). Apple's ATT/iOS 14.5 privacy framework (released April 26, 2021) vaporized ~$10bn of 2022 ad revenue across Meta, Snap, YouTube and Twitter, turning XLC's September 2021 peak into the start of a structural unwind. The pain was amplified by a brutal rate-regime move — the 10Y surged with TLT -34.1% and the dollar ripped +22.2% (DXY) — which crushed the long-duration, growth-heavy basket while Energy (+100.4%) ran on the commodity cycle.","body_zh":"XLC是2022年标普中受打击最严重的板块（-46.7%，11个中垫底），数字广告衰退掏空了Meta和Alphabet，奈飞因十余年来首次订户流失（2022年一季度，减少20万）单日暴跌约35%。苹果ATT/iOS 14.5隐私框架（2021年4月26日发布）从Meta、Snap、YouTube和Twitter抽走约100亿美元的2022年广告收入，将XLC 2021年9月的高点演变为结构性下行的起点。痛苦被剧烈的利率象限切换放大——10年期收益率飙升（TLT -34.1%）、美元暴涨+22.2%（DXY）——重创了长久期、偏成长的篮子，而能源（+100.4%）乘大宗商品周期大涨。","drivers":["ad recession","Meta/Netflix collapse","Apple ATT privacy shock","rate regime surge","strong dollar"],"drivers_zh":["广告衰退","Meta/奈飞崩跌","苹果ATT隐私冲击","利率象限激变","美元走强"],"prev_key":"2021-09-01","prev_key_chain":["2021-09-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Ad recession meets rate de-rating","title_zh":"广告衰退叠加利率杀估值","turn_id":"xlc:peak:2021-09"},"2022-11-03":{"body":"Off the 2022 low XLC ripped +137.2% to lead all sectors (rank 1/11) as the ad market healed and the genAI boom lifted its Meta/Alphabet-dominated basket. The Fed's pivot from ~525bp of hikes (last hike July 2023) to a cutting cycle (first cut September 2024) gave long-duration growth names a structural re-rate as real rates softened. This was a textbook tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +182.3%, growth>value +62.4, VIX 25 to 15, dollar -5.6%), and a hyper-narrow one — equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -31.3%, so the mega-cap concentration that crushed XLC in 2022 became its rocket fuel into the February 2025 high.","body_zh":"自2022年低点起，XLC暴涨+137.2%、领涨所有板块（11个中第1），广告市场回暖、生成式AI热潮提振了以Meta/Alphabet为主的篮子。美联储从累计加息约525个基点（最后一次加息为2023年7月）转向降息（2024年9月开启首次降息），令长久期成长股随实际利率回落而系统性重估。这是教科书式的科技/半导体主导的风险偏好暴涨（SMH +182.3%、成长跑赢价值+62.4、VIX从25降至15、美元-5.6%），且极度狭窄——等权重跑输市值加权-31.3%，于是2022年压垮XLC的大型科技股集中度，反而成了它冲向2025年2月高位的燃料。","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","AI/genAI boom","Fed pivot to cuts","narrow mega-cap breadth","Meta/Alphabet/Netflix"],"drivers_zh":["科技主导风险偏好","AI/生成式AI热潮","美联储转向降息","大市值窄幅行情","Meta/Alphabet/奈飞"],"prev_key":"2022-11-03","prev_key_chain":["2022-11-03"],"status":"exact","title":"AI mega-cap melt-up, narrow tape","title_zh":"AI大型科技股暴涨，窄幅行情","turn_id":"xlc:trough:2022-11"},"2025-02-14":{"body":"The late-January 2025 DeepSeek scare questioned AI-capex ROI across the hyperscaler stack (Nvidia shed ~$600bn on January 27) and April's reciprocal-tariff crash (Liberation Day, April 2, 2025) detonated a flight-to-safety — VIX spiked 15 to 52, defensives held (-6.5%) while cyclicals were hammered (-18.1%) and SMH fell -28.8%. XLC's Meta/Alphabet concentration left it on the wrong side of that rotation, down -18.0% (rank 9/11) into the April 8 low even as the selloff broadened (equal-weight +3.2% over cap-weight), confirming this was a macro repricing of growth multiples rather than stock-specific liquidation.","body_zh":"2025年1月底的DeepSeek恐慌质疑了超大规模云厂商AI资本开支的投资回报率（英伟达1月27日蒸发约6000亿美元），2025年4月2日对等关税冲击（解放日）随后引爆了避险情绪——VIX飙升15至52，防御板块抗跌（-6.5%），而周期股遭重创（-18.1%）、SMH下跌-28.8%。XLC对Meta/Alphabet的集中持仓使其站在了这次轮动的错误一侧，下跌-18.0%（11个中第9）至4月8日低点，尽管抛售在扩散（等权重跑赢市值加权+3.2%），印证这是成长估值倍数的宏观重定价，而非个股特定事件。","drivers":["flight-to-safety","DeepSeek AI scare","April tariff crash","mega-cap concentration","growth multiple compression"],"drivers_zh":["避险轮动","DeepSeek AI恐慌","4月关税崩跌","大型科技股集中度","成长溢价压缩"],"prev_key":"2025-02-14","prev_key_chain":["2025-02-14"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek and the tariff flight-to-safety","title_zh":"DeepSeek与关税引发的避险","turn_id":"xlc:peak:2025-02"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"From the April 8 2025 low XLC rebounded +40.7% (rank 3/11) as the tariff pause (April 9, 90-day moratorium on reciprocal duties) sparked a sharp relief rally and a tech/semis-led risk-on regime reasserted — SMH +124.9%, growth>value +12.2, VIX collapsed 52 to 17, dollar -5.8%. Alphabet re-rated on TPU/AI monetization beats and Meta on record ad revenue strength, but the advance ran on narrow, mega-cap-led breadth (equal-weight -9.5% under cap-weight) and faded into the late-January 2026 high as rising 2026 AI capex guidance (Meta up to $145bn, Alphabet to $190bn) reoriented flows away from XLC's ad-platform names and toward industrials, energy, and semis.","body_zh":"自2025年4月8日低点起，XLC反弹+40.7%（11个中第3），关税暂停（4月9日90天对等关税豁免）引发强劲缓和行情，科技/半导体主导的风险偏好象限重新占上风——SMH +124.9%、成长跑赢价值+12.2、VIX崩塌52至17、美元-5.8%。Alphabet因TPU/AI变现超预期重估、Meta因广告收入创纪录走高，但这轮上涨依赖狭窄的大市值主导广度（等权重跑输市值加权-9.5%），并在2026年1月底高位消退，因2026年AI资本开支指引飙升（Meta上调至1450亿美元、Alphabet升至1900亿美元）将资金重新引向工业、能源和半导体，而非XLC的广告平台持仓。","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","tariff-pause relief","narrow mega-cap breadth","AI monetization beats","hyperscaler capex concerns 2026"],"drivers_zh":["科技主导风险偏好","关税暂停缓和","大市值窄幅行情","AI变现超预期","超大规模云厂商2026年资本开支担忧"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-tariff AI rebound on a narrow tape","title_zh":"关税后AI反弹，窄幅行情","turn_id":"xlc:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"BOTTOMING (RS #10, deeply washed out) — XLC is the tape's worst sector at -9.6% (rank 11/11) since the January 2026 peak while Tech (+24.3%) and a +67.9% semis melt-up (SMH) lead a high-beta-over-low-vol risk-on regime (+20.7%). The contradiction is that this is a growth-up/reflation quad where cyclicals beat defensives by +4.3 points, yet growth is LAGGING value by -15.2% — confirming the bid is in semis, energy, and industrials (the AI infrastructure build), not in Meta/Alphabet (the AI spend recipients). The AI capex trap narrative — Meta guiding 2026 capex up to $125-145bn (raised from $115-135bn) and Alphabet $180-190bn against decelerating revenue-growth signals — has repriced the mega-cap ad/platform names that constitute ~55% of XLC. With VIX calm (14-18), breadth broadening (equal-weight +2.9% over cap-weight), and oil at +19.2% (a reflation signal), the washout looks like structural neglect rather than panic liquidation, positioning XLC to recover if Q2 2026 earnings show AI monetization accelerating faster than capex consumption.","now_zh":"XLC目前处于底部形成阶段（相对强度排名第10），自2026年1月高点以来大幅落后，表现为标普11个板块中垫底（-9.6%），而科技板块（+24.3%）与半导体（SMH +67.9%）引领高贝塔跑赢低波动达+20.7%的风险偏好行情。矛盾之处在于：当前处于成长上行/再通胀象限，周期股跑赢防御股+4.3个百分点，但成长风格却大幅跑输价值风格-15.2%——确认此轮资金流向半导体、能源和工业（AI基础设施建设方），而非Meta/Alphabet（AI支出受益方）。\"资本开支陷阱\"叙事——Meta将2026年资本开支指引上调至1250-1450亿美元（原为1150-1350亿美元）、Alphabet指引1800-1900亿美元，而营收增速放缓——已重新定价占XLC约55%权重的大型科技广告/平台股。VIX平静（14-18）、市场广度扩散（等权重跑赢市值加权+2.9%）、油价上涨19.2%（再通胀信号），此波下跌更像是结构性忽视而非恐慌性清仓，若2026年二季度财报显示AI变现加速快于资本开支消耗，XLC有望迎来修复。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"xle":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"body":"From the October 2011 panic low -- triggered by euro-zone debt contagion and a global growth scare that sent VIX to 45 -- Energy rallied +35.4% to rank #1/11 in a classic risk-on reflation rebound. WTI crude surged ~41% as the ECB's December 2011 LTRO operations stabilised European banking and the Fed extended Operation Twist, fuelling a dollar-weakening (-1.4% DXY) reflation trade. Cyclicals (+30.8%) trounced defensives (+13.6%), VIX collapsed from 45 to 17, and broad participation (equal-weight beat cap-weight +3.3%) confirmed a genuine beta recovery, not a defensive squeeze.","body_zh":"从2011年10月的恐慌低点（由欧元区主权债务传染与全球增长恐慌推动，VIX升至45）起，能源板块在经典风险偏好再通胀反弹中大涨+35.4%，跻身第1/11。WTI原油飙升约41%，欧央行2011年12月LTRO操作稳定了欧洲银行体系，美联储延长扭曲操作，合力引发美元走弱（-1.4% DXY）的再通胀交易。周期板块（+30.8%）大幅跑赢防御板块（+13.6%），VIX从45骤降至17，市场广度扩张（等权跑赢市值加权+3.3%）印证了这是真实的贝塔修复，而非防御性挤压。","drivers":["reflation quad","ECB LTRO / Fed Twist stimulus","oil +41% recovery","VIX collapse 45-17"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀象限","欧央行LTRO/美联储扭曲操作刺激","原油+41%修复","VIX从45跌至17"],"prev_key":"2011-10-03","prev_key_chain":["2011-10-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-crisis cyclical reflation lifts Energy","title_zh":"后危机周期再通胀推升能源","turn_id":"xle:trough:2011-10"},"2012-02-24":{"body":"From the February 2012 peak, Energy dropped -18.4% (#9 of 11) as the euro-zone crisis reignited -- Greek PSI restructuring talks stalled and Spanish borrowing costs surged, sending the dollar higher (+5.4% DXY) and oil tumbling -23.5%. This was a textbook slowdown/deflation-scare rotation: defensives led (+1.0%) while cyclicals cratered (-9.3%), VIX jumped 17 to 26, and TLT rallied +11.1% as capital fled to Treasuries. Energy was the worst cyclical, caught in the double-squeeze of a rising dollar and falling crude.","body_zh":"从2012年2月高点起，能源板块下跌-18.4%（排名第9/11），欧元区危机重燃——希腊债务重组谈判陷僵局、西班牙借贷成本飙升——推动美元走强（+5.4% DXY），油价暴跌-23.5%。这是教科书式的放缓/通缩恐慌轮动：防御板块领涨（+1.0%），周期板块崩跌（-9.3%），VIX从17跳至26，TLT大涨+11.1%，资本纷纷逃入美债。能源是最弱的周期板块，陷入强美元与油价下跌的双重挤压。","drivers":["slowdown/deflation-scare quad","euro-zone crisis reignited","dollar surge +5.4%","oil -23.5%"],"drivers_zh":["放缓/通缩恐慌象限","欧债危机重燃","美元飙升+5.4%","油价-23.5%"],"prev_key":"2012-02-24","prev_key_chain":["2012-02-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Europe reignites, dollar surges, oil/cyclicals crushed","title_zh":"欧债危机重燃，美元飙升，油价/周期板块被压垮","turn_id":"xle:peak:2012-02"},"2012-06-04":{"body":"Energy gained +70.5% over a 25-month bull run from mid-2012 to June 2014, ranking #4/11 in a broad reflation cycle. The Fed's September 2012 launch of QE3 ($40bn/month MBS, later expanded to $85bn) anchored long rates and weakened the dollar (-2.8% DXY over the leg), while rebounding global demand lifted WTI roughly +26% within a $90-105 band. Financials and Health led, but the energy sector benefited from rising oil and a broadening tape (equal-weight beat cap-weight +10.7%). OPEC maintained production discipline and US shale production was ramping but not yet tipping the balance.","body_zh":"从2012年6月至2014年6月的25个月牛市中，能源板块累涨+70.5%，排名第4/11，处于宽泛的再通胀周期。美联储2012年9月启动QE3（每月400亿美元MBS，后扩至850亿），压低长期利率并使美元走弱（整段下跌-2.8% DXY），全球需求回升推动WTI在90-105美元区间内累涨约26%。金融和医疗健康领涨，能源板块也受益于油价上行与市场广度扩张（等权跑赢市值加权+10.7%）。OPEC维持产量纪律，美国页岩油产量虽在爬升，但尚未打破供需平衡。","drivers":["reflation quad","Fed QE3 anchor","dollar weakness","oil up ~26%"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀象限","美联储QE3压锚","美元走弱","原油上涨约26%"],"prev_key":"2012-06-04","prev_key_chain":["2012-06-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed QE3, global reflation -- 2-year Energy boom","title_zh":"美联储QE3、全球再通胀——两年能源牛市","turn_id":"xle:trough:2012-06"},"2014-06-23":{"body":"Energy plummeted -27.2% (#9) from June 2014 as WTI collapsed -56% from $107 to below $50 by January 2015. The Saudi-led OPEC strategy shift -- announced November 27, 2014, at Vienna: no cut, defend market share to squeeze US shale -- combined with surging US tight-oil production (record output growth in 2014) and a USD surge (+15.1% DXY) created a historic supply glut. This was a pure flight-to-safety/deflation-scare: defensives led (+12.8%), cyclicals fell (-3.0%), TLT surged +23.1%, and VIX jumped 11 to 22 as Energy was last by a wide margin.","body_zh":"从2014年6月起，能源板块暴跌-27.2%（排名第9），WTI从107美元崩跌至2015年1月的50美元以下，跌幅-56%。沙特主导的OPEC战略转向——2014年11月27日维也纳会议宣布不减产、以市场份额挤压美国页岩油——叠加美国致密油产量激增（2014年创历史新高增速）以及美元大幅走强（+15.1% DXY），共同制造了历史性供应过剩。这是纯粹的避险/通缩恐慌：防御板块领涨（+12.8%），周期板块下跌（-3.0%），TLT飙升+23.1%，VIX从11跳至22，能源以巨大差距垫底。","drivers":["OPEC market-share strategy shift Nov 2014","US shale production record","dollar surge +15.1%","flight-to-safety / deflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["OPEC 2014年11月市场份额战略转向","美国页岩油产量创纪录","美元飙升+15.1%","避险/通缩恐慌象限"],"prev_key":"2014-06-23","prev_key_chain":["2014-06-23"],"status":"exact","title":"OPEC market-share war, shale glut -- 56% oil crash","title_zh":"OPEC市场份额战、页岩油过剩——油价暴跌56%","turn_id":"xle:peak:2014-06"},"2015-08-25":{"body":"Energy surged +21.5% (#1/11) from the August 25 crash low as oversold conditions, stabilising Chinese markets (PBOC rate cuts), and a brief oil squeeze drove a sharp rebound. WTI bounced ~22% off the ~$38 area as Chinese authorities injected liquidity and stabilised the CSI 300. Cyclicals (+15.1%) led defensives (+7.6%), VIX collapsed from 36 to 15, and oil's bounce (+21.9%) powered Energy to the top of the sector league table, though note the DXY firmed (+2.8%) which somewhat muted the rally's breadth (equal-weight lagged cap-weight -2.3%).","body_zh":"能源板块从8月25日崩盘低点大涨+21.5%（第1/11），超卖状态、中国市场企稳（中国人民银行降息）以及短期油价逼空共同驱动剧烈反弹。WTI从约38美元的底部反弹约22%，中国当局注入流动性并稳定了沪深300。周期板块（+15.1%）跑赢防御板块（+7.6%），VIX从36骤降至15，油价反弹（+21.9%）推动能源跃居板块榜首，但DXY走强（+2.8%）令广度略受抑制（等权跑输市值加权-2.3%）。","drivers":["reflation quad / crash-bounce","PBOC rate cuts / China stabilisation","oil bounce +21.9%","VIX collapse 36-15"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀象限/崩盘后反弹","中国人民银行降息/中国稳市","原油反弹+21.9%","VIX从36跌至15"],"prev_key":"2015-08-25","prev_key_chain":["2015-08-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Crash-low rebound -- Energy leads risk-on recovery","title_zh":"崩盘低点反弹——能源引领风险偏好复苏","turn_id":"xle:trough:2015-08"},"2015-11-03":{"body":"Energy plunged -26.8% (#10) from November 2015 to January 2016 as OPEC's December 4, 2015 meeting confirmed no production cut and Saudi Arabia doubled down on market-share strategy, while the July 2015 Iran nuclear deal JCPOA paved the way for Iranian supply to re-enter the market in January 2016. WTI crashed to $26.21 by February 2016, its lowest since 2003. This was a full-scale risk-off: VIX jumped 15 to 28, defensives (-3.6%) dramatically outperformed cyclicals (-15.6%), credit spreads widened, and TLT gained +5.2%.","body_zh":"从2015年11月至2016年1月，能源板块暴跌-26.8%（排名第10），OPEC 2015年12月4日会议确认不减产，沙特加倍押注市场份额战略；2015年7月达成的伊核协议（JCPOA）为伊朗于2016年1月重返供应市场铺路。WTI到2016年2月跌至26.21美元，为2003年以来最低。这是全面的风险规避：VIX从15跳至28，防御板块（-3.6%）大幅跑赢周期板块（-15.6%），信用息差走阔，TLT上涨+5.2%。","drivers":["OPEC Dec 2015 no-cut decision","Iran JCPOA / supply re-entry","oil crash to $26","deflation-scare / flight-to-safety"],"drivers_zh":["OPEC 2015年12月不减产决定","伊核协议/伊朗供应重返","油价崩至26美元","通缩恐慌/避险"],"prev_key":"2015-11-03","prev_key_chain":["2015-11-03"],"status":"exact","title":"OPEC no-cut, Iran sanctions lifted -- oil to $26","title_zh":"OPEC不减产、伊朗制裁解除——油价跌至26美元","turn_id":"xle:peak:2015-11"},"2016-01-20":{"body":"Energy surged +53.3% (#1/11) from the January 2016 low over an 11-month reflation leg. February 2016 preliminary talks between Saudi Arabia, Russia and non-OPEC producers led to the landmark November 30, 2016 Vienna Agreement -- OPEC cut 1.2mb/d (its first cut since 2008) -- that sent WTI from $26 to ~$55 by year-end (+99.5% oil). The November 2016 Trump election victory added a second leg: financials (+40.3%), materials (+38.4%) and energy joined the reflation/value trade, and VIX compressed 28 to 13. Value dominated growth (-12.9% growth-minus-value) in a broad, high-beta tape.","body_zh":"从2016年1月低点起，能源板块在长达11个月的再通胀行情中大涨+53.3%（第1/11）。2016年2月，沙特、俄罗斯与非OPEC产油国的初步谈判推动了2016年11月30日里程碑式的维也纳协议——OPEC削减120万桶/日（2008年以来首次减产）——推动WTI从26美元涨至年末约55美元（原油+99.5%）。2016年11月特朗普大选胜利带来第二段拉升：金融（+40.3%）、材料（+38.4%）和能源共同参与再通胀/价值交易，VIX从28压缩至13。价值大幅主导成长（成长减价值-12.9%），处于宽幅高贝塔盘面。","drivers":["reflation quad","OPEC Vienna Agreement Nov 2016","oil +99.5% ($26 to $55)","Trump reflation / value rotation"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀象限","OPEC 2016年11月维也纳协议","原油+99.5%（26至55美元）","特朗普再通胀/价值轮动"],"prev_key":"2016-01-20","prev_key_chain":["2016-01-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Vienna OPEC deal, Trump reflation -- Energy #1 for the year","title_zh":"维也纳OPEC协议、特朗普再通胀——能源年度第1","turn_id":"xle:trough:2016-01"},"2016-12-13":{"body":"Energy dropped -18.9% (#10) from December 2016 to August 2017 despite the Vienna Agreement being in force: US shale rebounded sharply on higher prices, with production rising from ~8.8mb/d back above 9mb/d by mid-2017, capping oil at $45-55 and eroding OPEC's cut impact. Meanwhile the broader tape was a tech/semis melt-up: defensives (+12.0%) led cyclicals (+4.0%) with yields falling (TLT +9.3%), and a weakening dollar (-7.8%) benefited other sectors more. Oil fell -10.6% even as copper held positive (+3.4%), confirming Energy's underperformance was oil-specific, not a broad commodity story.","body_zh":"从2016年12月至2017年8月，尽管维也纳协议已生效，能源板块仍下跌-18.9%（排名第10）：美国页岩油在价格上涨后强劲反弹，产量从约880万桶/日回升至2017年中的900万桶/日以上，将油价封顶在45-55美元区间，削弱了OPEC减产的效果。与此同时，更广泛的盘面是科技/半导体主导的逼空上涨：防御板块（+12.0%）跑赢周期板块（+4.0%），收益率回落（TLT +9.3%），美元走弱（-7.8%）更多惠及其他板块。油价下跌-10.6%，而铜价保持正值（+3.4%），印证能源跑输是油价本身的问题，而非大宗商品整体故事。","drivers":["US shale production rebound offsets OPEC","oil -10.6% / ceiling at $55","tech/semis-led tape flows away","dollar weakness favored others"],"drivers_zh":["美国页岩油反弹抵消OPEC减产","油价-10.6%/55美元压力位","科技/半导体主导资金流出","弱美元更多惠及其他板块"],"prev_key":"2016-12-13","prev_key_chain":["2016-12-13"],"status":"exact","title":"US shale offsets OPEC cuts -- Energy alone falls","title_zh":"美国页岩油抵消OPEC减产——能源独自下跌","turn_id":"xle:peak:2016-12"},"2017-08-21":{"body":"Energy surged +28.4% (#1/11) from the August 2017 low as OPEC compliance improved, drawing down global inventories: WTI rose from ~$47 to $66 by January 2018 as Saudi Arabia and Russia enforced cuts, and Saudi political risk rose via Crown Prince MBS's November 2017 consolidation of power. Trump's Iran-deal pressure also added a geopolitical premium. Cyclicals (+21.9%) trounced defensives (+4.9%), VIX compressed 13 to 11, and a weakening dollar (-2.9% DXY) was a tailwind. Financials (+22.4%) also led on tax-cut expectations -- the reflation trade was broad.","body_zh":"从2017年8月低点起，能源板块大涨+28.4%（第1/11），OPEC执行率改善，全球库存持续去化：沙特与俄罗斯强制执行减产，WTI从约47美元涨至2018年1月的66美元；沙特地缘政治风险上升，穆罕默德·本·萨勒曼于2017年11月集中权力。特朗普对伊核协议施压也带来了地缘政治溢价。周期板块（+21.9%）大幅跑赢防御板块（+4.9%），VIX从13压缩至11，美元走弱（-2.9% DXY）形成顺风。金融（+22.4%）也在减税预期下领涨——再通胀交易范围广泛。","drivers":["OPEC compliance improving / inventories drawing","oil $47 to $66","dollar weakness -2.9%","Trump-era reflation / tax cut expectations"],"drivers_zh":["OPEC执行率改善/库存去化","原油从47美元涨至66美元","美元走弱-2.9%","特朗普时代再通胀/减税预期"],"prev_key":"2017-08-21","prev_key_chain":["2017-08-21"],"status":"exact","title":"OPEC compliance tightens, oil to $66 -- Energy leads","title_zh":"OPEC执行率改善，油价升至66美元——能源领涨","turn_id":"xle:trough:2017-08"},"2018-01-22":{"body":"Energy fell -14.8% (#10) in a sharp two-month correction driven by the February 5, 2018 Volmageddon event: a stronger-than-expected January 2018 payrolls print (average hourly earnings +2.9% YoY, the highest since 2009) triggered an inflation scare that caused VIX to spike from ~13 to 37+, unwinding inverse-vol positions and dragging all risk assets lower. Oil barely moved (+1.4%) -- the Energy selloff was pure equity-risk repricing. Defensives (-5.9%) somewhat outperformed cyclicals (-9.0%), confirming a broad flight-to-safety, not an oil-specific bear market.","body_zh":"受2018年2月5日'波动率末日'事件冲击，能源板块在两个月的急跌中下跌-14.8%（排名第10）：2018年1月强于预期的非农数据（平均时薪同比+2.9%，为2009年以来最高）引发通胀恐慌，VIX从约13飙升至37以上，逆波动率头寸遭强制平仓，所有风险资产被拖累下行。油价几乎持平（+1.4%）——能源的下跌纯粹是股权风险重新定价。防御板块（-5.9%）略微跑赢周期板块（-9.0%），印证这是广泛的避险，而非油价特有的熊市。","drivers":["Volmageddon / VIX spike 11-23","inflation scare payrolls Jan 2018","equity risk repricing (oil flat)","flight-to-safety / deflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["波动率末日/VIX从11飙至23","2018年1月通胀恐慌非农数据","股权风险重新定价（油价平稳）","避险/通缩恐慌象限"],"prev_key":"2018-01-22","prev_key_chain":["2018-01-22"],"status":"exact","title":"Volmageddon inflation scare -- broad selloff, Energy worst","title_zh":"波动率末日事件+通胀恐慌——大盘普跌，能源垫底","turn_id":"xle:peak:2018-01"},"2018-03-28":{"body":"Energy surged +19.5% (#1/11) from late March to May 2018 as WTI climbed from $63 to $72 on tightening supply expectations. Trump's May 8, 2018 announcement to withdraw from the Iran JCPOA and re-impose oil sanctions on Iran -- threatening to remove ~1mb/d from global markets -- was the key catalyst, while strong US Q1 2018 earnings and synchronised global growth maintained a reflation-quad read. Cyclicals (+8.2%) led defensives (-1.3%) with VIX compressing 23 to 13; even a stronger dollar (+4.0% DXY) could not hold back the Iran-supply-squeeze premium.","body_zh":"从2018年3月底至5月，能源板块大涨+19.5%（第1/11），WTI从63美元攀升至72美元，供应收紧预期升温。特朗普2018年5月8日宣布退出伊核协议（JCPOA）并重新对伊朗实施石油制裁——威胁将全球供应削减约100万桶/日——是关键催化剂；强劲的美国2018年一季度财报和全球同步增长维持了再通胀象限。周期板块（+8.2%）跑赢防御板块（-1.3%），VIX从23压缩至13；即便美元走强（+4.0% DXY），也无法阻挡伊朗供应紧缺溢价推动的油价上涨。","drivers":["Trump Iran JCPOA withdrawal May 2018","oil $63 to $72 / supply-squeeze premium","reflation quad / earnings support","VIX compression 23-13"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普2018年5月退出伊核协议","原油从63美元涨至72美元/供应紧缺溢价","再通胀象限/财报支撑","VIX从23压缩至13"],"prev_key":"2018-03-28","prev_key_chain":["2018-03-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Iran deal withdrawal lifts oil -- Energy leads briefly","title_zh":"退出伊核协议推升油价——能源短暂领涨","turn_id":"xle:trough:2018-03"},"2018-05-21":{"body":"Energy crashed -30.2% (#11/11) from May to December 24, 2018 -- its worst 7-month stretch in years. WTI fell from $72 to ~$43 (-41.1%) as the Fed raised rates four times in 2018, strengthening the dollar (+3.1% DXY) and slowing global growth; US shale output hit record highs, surpassing Saudi Arabia and Russia as the world's largest producer; and Trump granted Iran sanction waivers to eight countries in November, removing the supply-risk premium. The Q4 2018 equity rout (VIX 13 to 36, TLT +5.4%) exacerbated the selloff as financial-market deleveraging compounded the oil bear.","body_zh":"从2018年5月至12月24日，能源板块崩跌-30.2%（第11/11）——多年来最惨烈的7个月。WTI从72美元跌至约43美元（-41.1%），美联储全年四次加息推高美元（+3.1% DXY）并拖慢全球增长；美国页岩油产量创历史新高，超越沙特和俄罗斯成为全球最大生产国；特朗普11月对八国给予伊朗制裁豁免，消除了供应风险溢价。2018年四季度股市暴跌（VIX从13飙至36，TLT +5.4%）加剧了下跌，金融市场去杠杆进一步深化油价熊市。","drivers":["Fed 4x hikes 2018 / dollar strength","US shale record output + Iran waivers","deflation-scare / flight-to-safety","oil -41.1% ($72 to $43)"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2018年四次加息/美元走强","美国页岩油创纪录+伊朗制裁豁免","通缩恐慌/避险","油价-41.1%（72至43美元）"],"prev_key":"2018-05-21","prev_key_chain":["2018-05-21"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed hikes + shale glut + Q4 panic -- Energy worst by far","title_zh":"美联储加息+页岩油过剩+四季度恐慌——能源大幅垫底","turn_id":"xle:peak:2018-05"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"Energy rebounded +28.4% (#4) from the December 24, 2018 capitulation low through April 2019. The January 4, 2019 Fed pivot -- Powell signalling a pause in rate hikes and patience -- alongside the December 7, 2018 OPEC+ agreement to cut 1.2mb/d (Saudi Arabia and Russia leading), Iran sanctions removing ~1mb/d of supply, and Venezuela sanctions (January 2019 PDVSA) converged to drive WTI from $43 to ~$65. Semis led (+45.3%) in a growth-led melt-up as VIX collapsed 36 to 12, supporting all cyclicals including Energy, though Tech (+35.8%) led the rank.","body_zh":"从2018年12月24日的投降式低点至2019年4月，能源板块反弹+28.4%（排名第4）。2019年1月4日美联储转向——鲍威尔表示暂停加息并保持'耐心'——叠加2018年12月7日OPEC+同意减产120万桶/日（沙特与俄罗斯领衔）、伊朗制裁削减约100万桶/日供应、委内瑞拉制裁（2019年1月PDVSA），多重因素推动WTI从43美元涨至约65美元。VIX从36骤降至12，半导体领涨（+45.3%），所有周期板块包括能源均受益于成长主导的逼空上涨，但科技（+35.8%）领跑排名。","drivers":["Fed Jan 2019 pivot / rate pause","OPEC+ 1.2mb/d cut Dec 2018","Iran + Venezuela sanctions","oil $43 to $65"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月转向/暂停加息","OPEC+ 2018年12月减产120万桶/日","伊朗+委内瑞拉制裁","原油从43美元涨至65美元"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot + OPEC+ cuts + Iran sanctions -- Energy rebounds","title_zh":"美联储转向+OPEC减产+伊朗制裁——能源反弹","turn_id":"xle:trough:2018-12"},"2019-04-22":{"body":"Energy fell -17.9% (#11) from late April to August 2019 as the US-China trade war re-escalated: Trump announced new 25% tariffs on $200bn Chinese goods in May 2019, and the yield curve inverted deeply (10yr-2yr), signalling recession fears. WTI fell from ~$65 to $55 (-16.4%) on global demand-growth downgrades; the IEA cut its 2019 demand estimate. TLT surged +21.7% as defensives (+6.8%) sharply outperformed cyclicals (-5.2%) and Energy in a classic flight-to-safety. Copper-gold cratered (-33.5%), confirming demand-destruction pricing across all commodities.","body_zh":"从2019年4月底至8月，能源板块下跌-17.9%（第11），中美贸易战重新升级：特朗普2019年5月宣布对2000亿美元中国商品加征25%关税，收益率曲线深度倒挂（10年-2年），发出衰退信号。WTI从约65美元跌至55美元（-16.4%），IEA下调了2019年需求预测；TLT飙升+21.7%，防御板块（+6.8%）大幅跑赢周期板块（-5.2%）和能源，呈现经典避险状态。铜金比暴跌（-33.5%），印证需求破坏预期已扩散至所有大宗商品。","drivers":["US-China trade war escalation May 2019","yield curve inversion / recession fears","oil $65 to $55 / demand downgrades","flight-to-safety / TLT +21.7%"],"drivers_zh":["中美贸易战2019年5月升级","收益率曲线倒挂/衰退恐慌","原油从65美元跌至55美元/需求预测下调","避险/TLT +21.7%"],"prev_key":"2019-04-22","prev_key_chain":["2019-04-22"],"status":"exact","title":"US-China trade war escalation -- Energy worst as bonds rally","title_zh":"中美贸易战升级——债券大涨，能源垫底","turn_id":"xle:peak:2019-04"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"XLE roared +99.8% (#1) from the March 2020 bottom through June 8 as unprecedented fiscal/monetary stimulus (CARES Act $2.2trn, Fed unlimited QE, OPEC+ April 12 historic 9.7mb/d cut) ignited a massive reflation rebound. WTI recovered from $22 to $40 by June (+87.5%) as travel curtailment loosened, inventories began drawing, and the dollar weakened (-4.5% DXY). Cyclicals (+53.3%) massively outperformed defensives (+16.5%), VIX compressed 76 to 26, and the broadest participation in years (equal-weight beat cap-weight +9.7%) confirmed a genuine reopening rotation.","body_zh":"从2020年3月低点至6月8日，XLE大涨+99.8%（第1），史无前例的财政/货币刺激（CARES法案2.2万亿美元、美联储无限量宽松、OPEC+ 4月12日历史性削减970万桶/日产量）点燃了大规模再通胀反弹。WTI从22美元回升至6月的40美元（+87.5%），出行管控松绑、库存开始去化、美元走弱（-4.5% DXY）。周期板块（+53.3%）大幅跑赢防御板块（+16.5%），VIX从76压缩至26，市场广度为多年最宽（等权跑赢市值加权+9.7%），印证了真实的复工复产轮动。","drivers":["CARES Act / Fed unlimited QE","OPEC+ 9.7mb/d historic cut April 2020","oil +87.5% / demand recovery","VIX 76-26 / reflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["CARES法案/美联储无限量宽松","OPEC+ 2020年4月历史性减产970万桶/日","原油+87.5%/需求修复","VIX从76降至26/再通胀象限"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Fiscal/monetary stimulus + OPEC+ record cut -- XLE nearly doubles","title_zh":"财政/货币刺激+OPEC+历史性减产——XLE近乎翻倍","turn_id":"xle:trough:2020-03"},"2020-06-08":{"body":"Energy crashed -39.1% (#11) from June 8 to October 28, 2020 as the COVID second wave (rising US case counts from June, mask-mandate debates) stalled reopening momentum and WTI plateaued near $40 (-2.1%), while the broader tape was entirely dominated by tech/mega-cap growth: Tech +10%, Discretionary +9.5%, growth-over-value spread +17.1 points, semis +14.1%. This was a stagflation-ish quad -- VIX rose 26 to 40, defensives (+1.6%) outperformed cyclicals (-4.5%), but the dollar was weak (-3.3%) and copper-gold held +8.5%. Capital abandoned energy for Big Tech WFH plays.","body_zh":"从2020年6月8日至10月28日，能源板块暴跌-39.1%（第11），新冠第二波（美国6月起病例数攀升、口罩令争议）令复工复产动能停滞，WTI在约40美元附近徘徊（-2.1%）；而更广泛盘面完全被科技/巨头成长主导：科技+10%、非必需消费+9.5%，成长减价值利差+17.1个百分点，半导体+14.1%。这是类滞胀象限——VIX从26升至40，防御板块（+1.6%）跑赢周期板块（-4.5%），但美元走弱（-3.3%），铜金比持稳+8.5%。资本从能源出逃，涌入大科技在家办公概念。","drivers":["COVID second wave / reopening stall","tech/growth melt-up drained flows","oil flat $40 / demand uncertainty","stagflation-ish quad"],"drivers_zh":["新冠第二波/复工复产停滞","科技/成长逼空抽走资金","油价平稳约40美元/需求不确定","类滞胀象限"],"prev_key":"2020-06-08","prev_key_chain":["2020-06-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tech melt-up + COVID second wave -- Energy starved out","title_zh":"科技逼空+新冠第二波——能源资金被抽离","turn_id":"xle:peak:2020-06"},"2020-10-28":{"body":"XLE roared off pandemic lows as the November 2020 vaccine news ignited the reopening/reflation trade in the most beaten-down sector -- Energy ranked #1/11 (+107.7%) in a reflation quad with cyclicals (+48.7%) trouncing defensives (+14.9%), oil +92.9% and copper-gold +43.1. A weaker dollar (-3.1% DXY) was a tailwind and broad participation (equal-weight beat cap-weight by +12.3%) confirmed the rotation. WTI climbed from the low-$30s past $70 by June 2021 on rebounding travel, OPEC+ supply discipline, and the February 2021 Texas freeze that shut in production.","body_zh":"随着2020年11月疫苗消息在跌幅最深的板块点燃复工/再通胀交易，XLE从疫情低点强劲反弹——能源在再通胀象限中排名第1/11（+107.7%），周期板块（+48.7%）大幅跑赢防御板块（+14.9%），原油+92.9%、铜金比+43.1。美元走弱（-3.1% DXY）形成顺风，市场广度宽阔（等权跑赢市值加权+12.3%）印证了这轮轮动。WTI在出行回升、OPEC+供应纪律以及2021年2月德州寒潮停产推动下，到2021年6月从30美元出头攀升至70美元上方。","drivers":["reflation quad","risk-on leadership","weak dollar tailwind","OPEC+ discipline"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀象限","风险偏好领涨","弱美元顺风","OPEC+供应纪律"],"prev_key":"2020-10-28","prev_key_chain":["2020-10-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Vaccine reflation, energy leads the reopening","title_zh":"疫苗再通胀，能源领涨复工","turn_id":"xle:trough:2020-10"},"2021-06-15":{"body":"Crude reversed as OPEC+ agreed in July 2021 to add back 400,000 b/d per month while the Delta variant sparked demand fears, dragging WTI from the mid-$70s toward the high-$60s and making Energy the worst sector (-17.7%, #11). This was a flight-to-safety wobble -- defensives (+5.7%) led cyclicals (-1.4%) with VIX 17 to 22 and yields falling (TLT +6.9%) -- plus a strong-dollar headwind (+3.3% DXY); a sentiment repricing, not a fundamental glut, with U.S. inventories still drawing.","body_zh":"OPEC+于2021年7月同意每月增产40万桶/日，叠加Delta变异株引发需求担忧，原油转跌，WTI从75美元中段跌向60美元后段，能源成为最弱板块（-17.7%，第11）。这是一次避险式震荡——防御板块（+5.7%）跑赢周期板块（-1.4%），VIX 17到22、收益率回落（TLT +6.9%）——叠加强美元逆风（+3.3% DXY）；属情绪重新定价，而非基本面过剩，美国库存仍在去化。","drivers":["flight-to-safety","rate regime (yields fell)","strong dollar","OPEC+ output increase"],"drivers_zh":["避险","利率环境（收益率回落）","强美元","OPEC+增产"],"prev_key":"2021-06-15","prev_key_chain":["2021-06-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Delta scare, OPEC+ hike -- Energy worst as defensives bid","title_zh":"Delta惊吓与OPEC+增产——防御被买入，能源垫底","turn_id":"xle:peak:2021-06"},"2021-08-19":{"body":"A global energy crunch and then Russia's February 2022 invasion of Ukraine sent Brent above $120 and WTI to ~$127, making Energy the sole leader (+108.6%, #1) while the broad tape was a rate-regime selloff (TLT -23.1% as yields surged) and a strong-dollar (+9.6% DXY) headwind crushed everything else -- Tech -8.4%, Comm -26.2%. Sanctions risk, record LNG exports and chronic shale discipline starved the market; XLE was the top sector of 2022 precisely because it inversely benefited from the inflation/rate shock punishing growth.","body_zh":"全球能源紧缺，继而2022年2月俄罗斯入侵乌克兰，使布伦特升破120美元、WTI升至约127美元，能源成为唯一领涨者（+108.6%，第1）；而大盘是一轮利率环境抛售（收益率飙升，TLT -23.1%），强美元（+9.6% DXY）逆风压垮其他一切——科技-8.4%、通信-26.2%。制裁风险、创纪录LNG出口和长期页岩气供应纪律使市场供应紧张；XLE恰因从惩罚成长的通胀/利率冲击中反向受益，而成为2022年最强板块。","drivers":["rate regime (yields surged)","Russia-Ukraine invasion","strong dollar","capex discipline + buybacks"],"drivers_zh":["利率环境（收益率飙升）","俄乌战争","强美元","资本开支纪律+回购"],"prev_key":"2021-08-19","prev_key_chain":["2021-08-19"],"status":"exact","title":"Energy crisis + Russia spike -- Energy alone vs a rate-regime selloff","title_zh":"能源危机+俄油飙升——能源独涨，对抗利率环境抛售","turn_id":"xle:trough:2021-08"},"2022-06-08":{"body":"From the June 8 peak crude rolled over hard as aggressive Fed hikes and the largest-ever SPR releases stoked recession and demand-destruction fears, knocking ~$30/bbl off WTI and making Energy the worst sector (-26.0%, #11). This was a slowdown/deflation-scare quad -- cyclicals (-13.0%) and Energy itself led the decline while defensives held up far better (-2.3%) in a flight-to-safety -- compounded by a strong-dollar (+5.9% DXY) headwind, even as physical fundamentals stayed tight.","body_zh":"从6月8日高点起，美联储激进加息与史上最大规模释放战略石油储备加剧衰退和需求破坏担忧，原油大幅回落，WTI下跌约30美元/桶，能源成为最弱板块（-26.0%，第11）。这是放缓/通缩恐慌象限——周期板块（-13.0%）与能源自身领跌，而防御板块在避险中表现稳健得多（-2.3%）——叠加强美元（+5.9% DXY）逆风，即便实物基本面仍紧张。","drivers":["deflation-scare quad","flight-to-safety","strong dollar","Fed hikes + SPR releases"],"drivers_zh":["通缩恐慌象限","避险","强美元","美联储加息+释放储备"],"prev_key":"2022-06-08","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Recession scare crushes the oil peak","title_zh":"衰退恐慌压垮油价顶部","turn_id":"xle:peak:2022-06"},"2022-07-14":{"body":"Energy bounced back to #1 (+24.6%) as the market refocused on tight supply: OPEC+ delivered only a token 100,000 b/d September hike and Russia throttled then shut Nord Stream gas. The rebound came in a clean reflation/growth-up quad -- cyclicals (+11.9%) led defensives (+3.6%), copper-gold +11.1 -- with the dollar flat and no flight-to-safety, so Energy led on its own merits rather than as a hedge. Resilient cash flows and buybacks supported XLE even as crude stayed choppy below its June highs.","body_zh":"市场重新聚焦供应紧张，能源反弹回到第1（+24.6%）：OPEC+仅象征性宣布9月增产10万桶/日，俄罗斯先限气后切断北溪天然气。这轮反弹处于干净的再通胀/增长上行象限——周期板块（+11.9%）跑赢防御板块（+3.6%），铜金比+11.1——美元持平、无避险情绪，因此能源是凭自身基本面领涨，而非作为对冲。稳健的现金流和回购支撑XLE，即便原油在6月高点下方震荡。","drivers":["reflation quad","sector-led (not hedge)","tight supply","Nord Stream cuts"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀象限","板块自身领涨（非对冲）","供应紧张","北溪减供"],"prev_key":"2022-07-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-07-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Tight supply sparks a reflation-quad rebound","title_zh":"供应紧张引发再通胀象限反弹","turn_id":"xle:trough:2022-07"},"2022-08-29":{"body":"Energy gave back gains as oil slid on a soaring dollar (+4.8% DXY), the most aggressive Fed tightening in decades (TLT -7.8% as yields surged), and recession fears that overwhelmed tight supply -- Energy was worst (-17.4%, #11). It was a slowdown/deflation-scare quad with a flight-to-safety tilt: defensives (-5.5%) held up far better than cyclicals (-11.4%) and Energy. Continued SPR releases and softening Chinese demand under COVID lockdowns added pressure, pulling WTI toward the mid-$70s.","body_zh":"在美元飙升（+4.8% DXY）、数十年来最激进的美联储紧缩（收益率飙升，TLT -7.8%）以及压倒供应紧张的衰退担忧下，油价下滑，能源回吐涨幅并垫底（-17.4%，第11）。这是放缓/通缩恐慌象限并带避险倾向：防御板块（-5.5%）远比周期板块（-11.4%）和能源稳健。持续释放战略石油储备以及中国新冠封控下需求走软增添了压力，将WTI拉向70美元中段。","drivers":["rate regime (yields surged)","strong dollar","flight-to-safety","Fed hikes + SPR releases"],"drivers_zh":["利率环境（收益率飙升）","强美元","避险","美联储加息+释放储备"],"prev_key":"2022-08-29","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Strong dollar + rate regime hit oil","title_zh":"强美元+利率环境打压油价","turn_id":"xle:peak:2022-08"},"2022-09-26":{"body":"Energy rallied back to #1 (+36.8%) after OPEC+ announced on October 5, 2022 its biggest cut since 2020 -- a headline 2 million b/d reduction -- to defend prices. The setup was textbook for the sector: a reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +16.6% over defensives +4.2%), a weakening dollar (-6.7% DXY) tailwind, and broadening participation (equal-weight beat cap-weight +4.0%). China-reopening hopes added fuel, lifting WTI and powering a sharp XLE recovery into mid-November.","body_zh":"OPEC+于2022年10月5日宣布2020年以来最大幅度减产——名义上削减200万桶/日以捍卫价格，能源反弹回到第1（+36.8%）。这一组合对该板块堪称教科书：再通胀/增长上行象限（周期+16.6%跑赢防御+4.2%）、美元走弱（-6.7% DXY）的顺风，以及市场广度扩张（等权跑赢市值加权+4.0%）。中国重启预期火上浇油，推升WTI，推动XLE在11月中旬前强劲复苏。","drivers":["reflation quad","weak dollar tailwind","broadening breadth","OPEC+ 2mb/d cut"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀象限","弱美元顺风","市场广度扩张","OPEC+减产200万桶"],"prev_key":"2022-09-26","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-26"],"status":"exact","title":"OPEC+ 2mb/d cut, weak dollar power a reflation bounce","title_zh":"OPEC+减产200万桶、弱美元推动再通胀反弹","turn_id":"xle:trough:2022-09"},"2022-11-15":{"body":"Energy faded into early 2023 as weak-demand worries capped crude, then crashed in mid-March when the SVB collapse and Credit Suisse turmoil routed risk assets -- WTI tumbled ~12% to near $66, its lowest since December 2021, leaving Energy worst (-17.3%, #11). The rate regime flipped: yields fell hard (TLT +8.7%) on a flight to Treasuries, which rotated money toward duration-sensitive growth (Tech +7.7%, Comm +9.1%) and away from value-cyclical Energy. A credit-instability shock, not a supply story, drove the move.","body_zh":"需求疲软担忧压制原油，能源进入2023年初回落，随后在3月中旬硅谷银行倒闭和瑞信动荡冲击风险资产时崩盘——WTI暴跌约12%至接近66美元，为2021年12月以来最低，能源垫底（-17.3%，第11）。利率环境反转：避险买入国债使收益率大幅回落（TLT +8.7%），资金随之轮动进入对久期敏感的成长板块（科技+7.7%、通信+9.1%），离开价值-周期的能源。驱动此轮的是信用不稳定冲击，而非供应因素。","drivers":["credit shock / risk-off","rate regime (yields fell)","growth over value rotation","SVB banking crisis"],"drivers_zh":["信用冲击/风险规避","利率环境（收益率回落）","成长跑赢价值轮动","硅谷银行危机"],"prev_key":"2022-11-15","prev_key_chain":["2022-11-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Demand worry, SVB shock, rate regime flips","title_zh":"需求担忧、硅谷银行冲击、利率环境反转","turn_id":"xle:peak:2022-11"},"2023-05-31":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"xle:trough:2023-05"},"2023-09-14":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"xle:peak:2023-09"},"2024-01-18":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"xle:trough:2024-01"},"2024-04-05":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"xle:peak:2024-04"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"Trump's April 2 'reciprocal tariff' shock triggered a global growth and demand scare that slammed crude, with WTI plunging toward $57-60 by April 8 and Energy worst (-18.8%, #11). It was a violent flight-to-safety: VIX spiked 22 to 52 and defensives (-7.4%) sharply outperformed cyclicals (-14.3%) and Energy as everything sold off. The rout was amplified when OPEC+ stunned the market by tripling its planned May output hike, piling supply onto collapsing demand expectations.","body_zh":"特朗普4月2日的对等关税冲击引发全球增长和需求恐慌，猛烈打压原油，到4月8日WTI暴跌至57-60美元，能源垫底（-18.8%，第11）。这是一次剧烈的避险：VIX飙升22到52，普跌之中防御板块（-7.4%）大幅跑赢周期板块（-14.3%）和能源。当OPEC+出人意料地将其计划中的5月增产幅度增至三倍、向崩塌的需求预期叠加供应时，这轮暴跌被进一步放大。","drivers":["flight-to-safety (VIX 22-52)","deflation-scare quad","tariff demand shock","OPEC+ accelerated unwind"],"drivers_zh":["避险（VIX 22-52）","通缩恐慌象限","关税需求冲击","OPEC+加速解除减产"],"prev_key":"2025-04-02","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Liberation Day tariff crash -- Energy worst in a panic","title_zh":"解放日关税崩盘——恐慌中能源垫底","turn_id":"xle:trough:2025-04"},"2026-03-27":{"body":"Energy rolled over to worst (-14.7%, #11) as the war-risk premium drained out of crude -- a mid-June 2026 ceasefire and Hormuz-reopening hopes sent oil tumbling (oil -23.1%) and WTI back below ~$70. The pain was doubled by where the money went: a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +76.3%, Tech +47.2%) in a narrow, mega-cap tape (equal-weight lagged by -6.8%) pulled flows into AI growth and out of value-cyclical Energy. With the oil tail priced out and Middle East supply returning, XLE gave back its war-driven gains (2026 = house view).","body_zh":"随着战争风险溢价从原油中抽干，能源见顶垫底（-14.7%，第11）——2026年6月中旬的停火以及霍尔木兹重新开放预期使油价大跌（原油-23.1%），WTI回落至约70美元下方。资金去向令痛苦加倍：科技/半导体主导的风险偏好逼空上涨（SMH +76.3%、科技+47.2%）发生在狭窄的巨头盘面中（等权跑输-6.8%），将资金拉入AI成长、抽离价值-周期的能源。在油价尾部风险被定价剔除、中东供应回归的情况下，XLE回吐了战争驱动的涨幅（本站观点）。","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","starved (out of favor)","narrow breadth","ceasefire / risk-premium drain"],"drivers_zh":["科技主导的风险偏好","被冷落（失宠）","市场广度狭窄","停火/风险溢价抽干"],"prev_key":"2026-03-27","prev_key_chain":["2026-03-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Ceasefire unwinds the oil premium as semis melt up","title_zh":"停火解除油价溢价，半导体逼空上涨","turn_id":"xle:peak:2026-03"}},"now":"Energy is rolling over as of mid-2026, printing RS rank #11 -- the weakest sector -- even though it still sits #2 over the trailing window (+21.5%). The current tape is a tech/semis melt-up (SMH +67.9%, high-beta over low-vol +20.7%), and capital is rotating hard into AI growth away from the post-ceasefire oil-premium unwind: a mid-June 2026 Iran-Israel ceasefire and Hormuz-reopening expectations have drained the war-risk bid out of crude (-23.1% oil from the March 2026 peak), pulling XLE back below levels it held during the conflict. The reflation-quad backdrop (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2% trailing) offers a re-bid scenario if the AI melt-up narrows, but a firming dollar (+3.4% DXY) and the narrow mega-cap tape suggest re-rotation is not imminent. XLE is a value/income play out of favor in a growth-led cycle phase.","now_zh":"截至2026年中，能源板块正在见顶回落，相对强弱排名第11——为最弱板块——尽管在拖尾窗口内仍以+21.5%位居第2。当前盘面是科技/半导体主导的逼空上涨（SMH +67.9%，高贝塔超低波动+20.7%），资金正大举从伊朗停火后的油价风险溢价抽离处轮动进入AI成长：2026年6月中旬停火及霍尔木兹重新开放预期已将战争风险溢价从原油中抽干（原油自3月高点下跌-23.1%），将XLE拉回战争期间所守位置以下。再通胀象限背景（周期+11.2%超防御+6.9%，石油+19.2%拖尾）为AI行情收窄时的重新竞价提供了可能，但美元走强（+3.4% DXY）与巨头主导的窄幅盘面表明再轮动并不迫切。XLE目前是在成长主导周期阶段不受待见的价值/收益型资产。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"oil.regime_shift.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"oil.regime_shift.v1","arch_state":"pass","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"xlf":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"body":"XLF surged +24.6% (rank #3/11) as European policymakers moved to contain the sovereign debt crisis: the ECB's Governing Council on October 6 decided to launch its CBPP2 covered-bond programme (details published November 3) and signaled support for bank liquidity, while the EU-IMF Troika worked toward a second Greek bailout of ~EUR 130bn. The tape was a textbook risk-on reflation blast -- cyclicals +22.1% vs defensives +8.6%, VIX collapsing 45 to 25, TLT -10.0% (yields surging), oil +20.2%, dollar -5.5% DXY -- that lifted all cyclicals violently off oversold levels. Banks ranked third, behind only Energy and Materials in a broad, high-beta reversal; credit spreads (HYG-LQD +8.8%) snapped sharply tighter, confirming the financial system stress was abating not worsening.","body_zh":"XLF大涨+24.6%（排名11档中第3），欧洲政策制定者采取行动遏制主权债务危机：欧洲央行管理委员会10月6日决定推出第二轮担保债券购买计划（CBPP2，细节于11月3日公布）并表态支持银行流动性，同时欧盟-国际货币基金组织三驾马车推进约1300亿欧元的第二轮希腊纾困。行情是教科书式的风险偏好/再通胀暴力反弹——周期股+22.1% vs 防御股+8.6%，VIX从45坍缩至25，TLT -10.0%（收益率急升），油价+20.2%，美元-5.5% DXY——将所有周期股从超卖水平猛力拉起。银行排名第三，仅落后能源和材料；信用利差（HYG-LQD +8.8%）急剧收窄，印证金融系统压力在缓解而非恶化。","drivers":["euro-crisis policy relief","ECB CBPP2 / liquidity support","risk-on cyclical surge","credit spread snap"],"drivers_zh":["欧债危机政策纾解","欧央行CBPP2/流动性支持","风险偏好周期股急涨","信用利差收窄"],"prev_key":"2011-10-03","prev_key_chain":["2011-10-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Euro-crisis relief bounce -- cyclicals surge","title_zh":"欧债危机纾解反弹——周期股急涨","turn_id":"xlf:trough:2011-10"},"2011-10-28":{"body":"XLF fell -16.4% (rank #9/11) as the eurozone crisis re-intensified in November 2011: Italian 10-year yields breached 7% on November 9 (closing ~7.25%, a psychological point-of-no-return), Greek PM Papandreou shocked markets on October 31 by calling a referendum on the bailout deal, and systemic risk of European banks spiked. Flight-to-safety was unambiguous -- defensives -5.3% vs cyclicals -11.0%, VIX 25 to 34, TLT +10.3%, DXY +5.2% -- with financials underperforming because US banks held European sovereign paper and funding costs spiked (dollar-euro cross-currency basis widened sharply). The selloff ranked XLF #9, with only Energy and Materials worse.","body_zh":"XLF下跌-16.4%（排名11档中第9），欧元区危机在2011年11月再度升温：意大利10年期收益率11月9日突破7%（收于约7.25%，心理上的不归点），希腊总理帕潘德里欧10月31日宣布对纾困协议举行公投令市场震惊，欧洲银行系统性风险骤升。避险倾向鲜明——防御股-5.3% vs 周期股-11.0%，VIX从25升至34，TLT +10.3%，DXY +5.2%——由于美国银行持有欧洲主权债券且融资成本飙升（美元-欧元货币基差急剧走宽），金融板块跌幅居后。XLF排名第9，仅能源和材料更差。","drivers":["Italy sovereign 7% breach","flight-to-safety rotation","European bank funding stress","strong dollar"],"drivers_zh":["意大利主权债7%关口","避险轮动","欧洲银行融资压力","强势美元"],"prev_key":"2011-10-28","prev_key_chain":["2011-10-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Italy/Greece contagion -- banks hardest hit","title_zh":"意大利/希腊蔓延——银行首当其冲","turn_id":"xlf:peak:2011-10"},"2011-11-23":{"body":"XLF exploded +37.3% (rank #1/11) as the ECB's December 21 three-year LTRO allotted EUR 489.2bn to 523 European banks, decisively taking the tail risk of a European bank funding crisis off the table; a second LTRO on February 29, 2012 added EUR 529.5bn to a record 800 banks. This was the single greatest catalyst: the liquidity bazooka collapsed funding stress, squeezed short positions in financials, and re-opened credit markets (HYG-LQD +7.5%). A risk-on reflation tape (cyclicals +24.3% vs defensives +13.1%, VIX 34 to 14, TLT -7.2%, oil +11.3%, copper-gold +19.2%) confirmed a systemic-risk unwinding rather than a mere bounce. US banks, far less exposed than European peers but caught in the cross-fire, rebounded hardest as global financial stress normalized.","body_zh":"XLF暴涨+37.3%（排名11档中第1），欧洲央行12月21日三年期LTRO向523家欧洲银行投放4892亿欧元，断然消除欧洲银行融资危机的尾部风险；2012年2月29日第二轮LTRO再向创纪录的800家银行投放5295亿欧元。这是单一最大催化剂：流动性大招压缩融资压力、逼空金融板块空头、重开信用市场（HYG-LQD +7.5%）。风险偏好/再通胀行情（周期股+24.3% vs 防御股+13.1%，VIX从34降至14，TLT -7.2%，油价+11.3%，铜金比+19.2%）印证这是系统性风险消散而非单纯反弹。比欧洲同行暴露度低得多但受到牵连的美国银行反弹最为强劲，随着全球金融压力正常化而领涨。","drivers":["ECB 3-year LTRO (EUR 489bn + 530bn)","systemic risk normalization","credit spread compression","reflation tape"],"drivers_zh":["欧央行三年期LTRO（4892亿+5295亿欧元）","系统性风险正常化","信用利差压缩","再通胀行情"],"prev_key":"2011-11-23","prev_key_chain":["2011-11-23"],"status":"exact","title":"ECB LTRO bazooka -- banks lead risk-on","title_zh":"欧央行LTRO大招——银行领涨风险偏好","turn_id":"xlf:trough:2011-11"},"2012-03-26":{"body":"XLF fell -16.4% (rank #9/11) in a slowdown/deflation-scare flight-to-safety rotation (defensives -1.3% vs cyclicals -12.0%, VIX 14 to 26, TLT +15.6%, DXY +4.6%, oil -21.5%). Two overlapping shocks hit financials specifically: starting in April-May 2012, JPMorgan disclosed losses from Bruno Iksil's London Whale CDS trades that eventually ballooned to more than USD 6bn; simultaneously, Spain's banking system required a EUR 100bn EU bailout (agreed June 9, 2012) as regional savings banks (cajas) faced solvency crises from collapsed real estate loans. Both events amplified investor anxiety over financial-sector hidden losses and regulatory backlash (Volcker Rule reinvigoration).","body_zh":"XLF下跌-16.4%（排名11档中第9），处于放缓/通缩恐慌的避险轮动中（防御股-1.3% vs 周期股-12.0%，VIX从14升至26，TLT +15.6%，DXY +4.6%，油价-21.5%）。两大叠加冲击专门打击金融板块：自2012年4-5月起，摩根大通披露布鲁诺·伊克西尔的伦敦巨鲸CDS交易亏损，最终膨胀至逾60亿美元；与此同时，西班牙银行体系因地方储蓄银行（cajas）地产贷款坏账面临偿付危机，需要欧盟1000亿欧元纾困（2012年6月9日达成）。两件事共同放大投资者对金融板块隐性损失和监管反弹（沃尔克规则强化）的焦虑。","drivers":["JPMorgan London Whale ($6bn loss)","Spanish banking bailout EUR 100bn","flight-to-safety","Volcker Rule fears"],"drivers_zh":["摩根大通伦敦巨鲸（60亿美元亏损）","西班牙银行1000亿欧元纾困","避险轮动","沃尔克规则担忧"],"prev_key":"2012-03-26","prev_key_chain":["2012-03-26"],"status":"exact","title":"JPMorgan Whale + Spanish bailout fears","title_zh":"摩根大通巨鲸事件与西班牙纾困担忧","turn_id":"xlf:peak:2012-03"},"2012-06-04":{"body":"XLF compounded +102.5% over three years (rank #2/11) in a structurally favorable multi-year recovery -- but note the tape was NOT cyclical-led: defensives (+76.1%) actually beat cyclicals (+68.9%) and Health (+128.4%) was the #1 sector, so banks compounded on stock-specific drivers, not a reflation rotation. The fuel: the Fed's QE3 (September 2012, open-ended USD 85bn/month MBS+Treasury purchases), rising EPS from cost cuts and reserve releases, and successive CCAR/stress-test clearances (2013-2015) that unlocked buybacks and dividend increases. The Dodd-Frank adjustment cycle let bank ROEs trough and recover. A sharply stronger dollar (+18.2% DXY from 2014 amid QE taper/Fed divergence from ECB/BoJ) and an oil crash (-41.4%) hammered the energy/materials/EM complex and diverted flows toward US financials.","body_zh":"XLF三年累计上涨+102.5%（排名11档中第2）——但需注意行情并非周期主导：防御股（+76.1%）实际跑赢周期股（+68.9%），医疗（+128.4%）才是第1板块，因此银行的累积上涨靠的是个股驱动而非再通胀轮动。燃料在于：美联储2012年9月推出QE3（每月850亿美元MBS+国债开放式购买）、成本削减和准备金释放推动EPS回升，以及历次CCAR/压力测试通过（2013-2015年）解锁回购和分红提升。多德-弗兰克调整周期使银行ROE触底回升。2014年QE缩减/美联储与欧央行/日央行政策分化带来的大幅美元走强（+18.2% DXY）和油价崩跌（-41.4%）重创能源/材料/新兴市场板块，将资金引向美国金融股。","drivers":["Fed QE3 + CCAR clearances","EPS recovery / buyback unlocks","credit spread tightening","EM/energy capital rotation"],"drivers_zh":["美联储QE3+CCAR通过","EPS复苏/回购解锁","信用利差收窄","新兴市场/能源资本轮动"],"prev_key":"2012-06-04","prev_key_chain":["2012-06-04"],"status":"exact","title":"QE-era bull run -- banks compound, but trail health","title_zh":"QE时代牛市——银行累积上涨，但落后医疗","turn_id":"xlf:trough:2012-06"},"2015-07-22":{"body":"XLF fell -22.3% (rank #9/11) as a global slowdown/deflation-scare unfolded: China's shock yuan devaluation on August 11, 2015 triggered a global risk-off cascade, collapsing oil prices (-46.7% by February 2016) raised energy-sector loan-loss fears for US banks, and the first Fed hike in nine years (December 2015, 25bp) paradoxically flattened the curve (TLT +13.5%) rather than lifting NIM. Flight-to-safety was clear -- defensives -2.8% vs cyclicals -15.2%, VIX 12 to 28, high-beta minus low-vol -26.3%. Investors feared energy-credit contagion through bank balance sheets, and credit spreads widened sharply (HYG-LQD -11.5%).","body_zh":"XLF下跌-22.3%（排名11档中第9），全球放缓/通缩恐慌展开：2015年8月11日中国突然宣布人民币贬值，引发全球避险连锁，油价崩跌（-46.7%至2016年2月）引发对美国银行能源贷款损失的担忧，九年来首次加息（2015年12月，25bp）反而使曲线扁平化（TLT +13.5%）而非提升净息差。避险倾向明确——防御股-2.8% vs 周期股-15.2%，VIX从12升至28，高贝塔-低波动-26.3%。投资者担忧能源信用通过银行资产负债表传染，信用利差大幅走阔（HYG-LQD -11.5%）。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation Aug 2015","oil crash -47% / energy loan fears","curve flattening post first Fed hike","flight-to-safety"],"drivers_zh":["2015年8月人民币贬值","油价崩跌-47%/能源贷款担忧","首次加息后曲线扁平化","避险轮动"],"prev_key":"2015-07-22","prev_key_chain":["2015-07-22"],"status":"exact","title":"China devaluation + oil crash -- credit fears","title_zh":"人民币贬值与油价崩跌——信用风险担忧","turn_id":"xlf:peak:2015-07"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"XLF delivered +95.7% (rank #1/11) in the strongest financial-sector cycle of the decade, driven by two phases: first, a Feb-2016 commodity/credit bottom relief rally as oil stabilized, then the definitive acceleration after Trump's November 2016 election. Bank ETFs surged 26%+ in the weeks after the election (vs SPY +7%) as markets priced in corporate tax cuts (toward a 21% rate), rollback of Dodd-Frank financial regulation, and fiscal stimulus-driven yield-curve steepening. A weak dollar (-6.8% DXY), oil +152.3%, copper-gold +50.5%, and VIX 28 to 11 confirmed the reflation/growth-up quad. Credit spreads tightened sharply (HYG-LQD +16.0%) and the tech/semis melt-up (SMH +141.8%) sustained the risk-on environment throughout.","body_zh":"XLF实现+95.7%（排名11档中第1），是十年中最强的金融板块周期，由两个阶段驱动：首先是2016年2月的大宗商品/信用底部纾解反弹（油价企稳），随后是特朗普2016年11月大选后的决定性加速。选举后数周内银行ETF上涨26%+（vs SPY +7%），市场为企业税率削减（迈向21%）、多德-弗兰克金融监管回滚和财政刺激驱动的收益率曲线变陡定价。弱势美元（-6.8% DXY）、油价+152.3%、铜金比+50.5%、VIX从28降至11确认再通胀/增长上行象限。信用利差大幅收窄（HYG-LQD +16.0%），科技/半导体熔涨（SMH +141.8%）在整个周期内维持风险偏好环境。","drivers":["Trump tax cuts + deregulation","curve steepening / NIM expansion","oil/commodity reflation","risk-on leader #1"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普减税+放松监管","曲线变陡/净息差扩张","油价/大宗商品再通胀","风险偏好领涨第1"],"prev_key":"2016-02-11","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump election trade -- deregulation + curve steep","title_zh":"特朗普选举交易——放松监管与曲线变陡","turn_id":"xlf:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-26":{"body":"XLF fell -24.7% (rank #9/11 tied with Materials, only Energy worse at -28.4%) as a multi-front growth scare played out: the Fed hiked four times in 2018 (March, June, September, December) to 2.25-2.50%, the yield curve flattened sharply (2s10s near zero by year-end), and US-China tariffs escalated through the year. Flight-to-safety was confirmed (defensives -6.8% vs cyclicals -21.9%, VIX 11 to 36, dollar +8.4% DXY, oil -35.7%), with a flat curve eliminating the NIM expansion that had driven the Trump-era bank trade. Loan growth decelerated and IB deal pipelines froze with equity volatility elevated, even if the HYG-LQD spread was only modestly wider (-0.7%).","body_zh":"XLF下跌-24.7%（排名11档中第9，与材料并列，仅能源-28.4%更差），多重增长恐慌同时爆发：美联储2018年四次加息（3月、6月、9月、12月）至2.25-2.50%，收益率曲线急剧扁平（年底2s10s接近零），中美关税全年升级。避险倾向明确（防御股-6.8% vs 周期股-21.9%，VIX从11升至36，美元+8.4% DXY，油价-35.7%），平坦的曲线消除了驱动特朗普时代银行交易的净息差扩张。贷款增速放缓，在股市波动性高企中投行交易管道冻结，即便HYG-LQD利差仅温和走阔（-0.7%）。","drivers":["Fed 4x hike / curve flattening","US-China trade war escalation","flight-to-safety","NIM expansion reversal"],"drivers_zh":["美联储四次加息/曲线扁平","中美贸易战升级","避险轮动","净息差扩张逆转"],"prev_key":"2018-01-26","prev_key_chain":["2018-01-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed over-tightening + trade war growth scare","title_zh":"美联储过度收紧与贸易战增长恐慌","turn_id":"xlf:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"XLF gained +42.6% (rank #6/11) off the Christmas Eve low as Jay Powell's January 4, 2019 signal that the Fed would be 'patient' and flexible on rates triggered a decisive risk-on reversal (VIX 36 to 14). However this was a tech/semis-led recovery (SMH +88.9%, growth>value +23.0, narrow breadth equal-weight lagging by -6.7%), meaning financials were mid-pack, not leaders. TLT +22.2% (yields fell as the Fed paused and eventually cut three times in H2 2019) actually compressed NIM; banks rallied on credit-quality stabilization, Phase-1 US-China trade-deal optimism (December 2019), and resilient consumer/labor fundamentals, but the rate environment was a structural headwind throughout.","body_zh":"XLF从平安夜低点反弹+42.6%（排名11档中第6），鲍威尔2019年1月4日暗示美联储将对利率保持\"耐心\"和灵活性，触发决定性的风险偏好逆转（VIX从36降至14）。但这是由科技/半导体主导的复苏（SMH +88.9%，成长>价值+23.0，等权重落后市值加权-6.7%的窄幅广度），金融板块居中而非领涨。TLT +22.2%（随着美联储暂停并在2019年下半年三次降息，收益率下跌）实际上压缩了净息差；银行凭借信用质量稳定、2019年12月中美第一阶段贸易协议乐观情绪和稳健的消费/劳动力市场基本面上涨，但整个周期利率环境都是结构性逆风。","drivers":["Powell Put / Fed pause","tech-semis led recovery","Phase-1 trade deal optimism","credit quality stabilization"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔看跌期权/美联储暂停","科技半导体领涨复苏","第一阶段贸易协议乐观情绪","信用质量稳定"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell Put + tech-led cyclical recovery","title_zh":"鲍威尔看跌期权与科技领衔的周期性复苏","turn_id":"xlf:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-14":{"body":"XLF collapsed -42.9% (rank #10/11) as the COVID-19 pandemic triggered the fastest bear market in S&P 500 history (33.6% SPY decline in 33 days). Banks were uniquely impaired: zero-rate emergency cuts (Fed to 0-0.25% on March 15) obliterated NIM, loan-loss provisions soared (JPMorgan Q1 2020 provision +USD 8.3bn), credit (HYG-LQD -9.8%) and funding markets seized, and the 'global dash for cash' created forced selling across all assets. The flight-to-safety was extreme (defensives -29.3% vs cyclicals -40.1%, VIX 14 to 62, TLT +15.0%, oil -55.1%), but financials suffered disproportionately relative to defensives given their direct exposure to a recession-driven credit cycle and the prospect of a prolonged ZIRP era.","body_zh":"XLF暴跌-42.9%（排名11档中第10），新冠疫情引发标普500史上最快熊市（SPY在33天内下跌33.6%）。银行遭受特殊打击：紧急零利率降息（美联储3月15日降至0-0.25%）摧毁净息差，贷款损失计提急升（摩根大通一季度计提+83亿美元），信用（HYG-LQD -9.8%）和融资市场冻结，\"全球现金争夺\"引发各类资产被迫抛售。避险极端化（防御股-29.3% vs 周期股-40.1%，VIX从14飙升至62，TLT +15.0%，油价-55.1%），但金融板块相对防御股损失尤为惨重，因其直接暴露于衰退驱动的信用周期和长期零利率时代的前景之中。","drivers":["COVID recession shock","Fed to ZIRP (NIM obliteration)","massive loan-loss provisions","credit market seizure"],"drivers_zh":["新冠衰退冲击","美联储降至零利率（净息差摧毁）","大规模贷款损失计提","信用市场冻结"],"prev_key":"2020-02-14","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-14"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash -- banks #2 worst sector","title_zh":"新冠崩盘——银行列全市场倒数第二","turn_id":"xlf:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"XLF rebounded +51.4% (rank #5/11) off the March 23 COVID low as the Fed's unlimited QE (March 23 FOMC emergency announcement), the CARES Act (USD 2.2 trillion, signed March 27), and stabilization of credit markets catalyzed a violent cyclical reversal. Energy +63.5%, Industrials +56.4%, and Materials +56.2% led, with financials mid-pack as the zero-rate backdrop (TLT -5.2%, but rates already at zero) provided no NIM boost. Breadth was exceptionally wide (equal-weight +12.8% over cap-weight, VIX 62 to 26, HYG-LQD +8.3%), and a dollar weaker by -5.7% DXY confirmed the reflation/growth-up quad. Bank balance sheets proved resilient: stress tests were modified, buyback restrictions helped preserve capital, and reserve builds were front-loaded in Q1.","body_zh":"XLF从3月23日新冠低点反弹+51.4%（排名11档中第5），美联储无限量QE（3月23日FOMC紧急声明）、《关爱法》（2.2万亿美元，3月27日签署）和信用市场企稳催化了剧烈的周期性逆转。能源+63.5%、工业+56.4%、材料+56.2%领涨，金融板块居中，因零利率背景（TLT -5.2%，但利率已在零位）未提供净息差提升。市场广度异常宽（等权重领先市值加权+12.8%，VIX从62降至26，HYG-LQD +8.3%），美元走弱-5.7% DXY确认再通胀/增长上行象限。银行资产负债表显示出韧性：压力测试被修改，回购限制帮助保存资本，准备金建立在一季度前置完成。","drivers":["Fed unlimited QE","CARES Act $2.2tn fiscal stimulus","credit market stabilization","violent cyclical reversal"],"drivers_zh":["美联储无限量QE","《关爱法》2.2万亿财政刺激","信用市场企稳","剧烈周期性逆转"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed bazooka + fiscal stimulus -- violent rebound","title_zh":"美联储大招与财政刺激——剧烈反弹","turn_id":"xlf:trough:2020-03"},"2020-06-08":{"body":"XLF fell -15.0% (rank #10/11) in a brief but sharp June selloff as US COVID-19 case counts surged to new records (daily cases exceeding 40,000+ in late June), reigniting fears that reopening would stall and loan losses would accelerate beyond Q1 provisions. Flight-to-safety (defensives -7.6% vs cyclicals -10.8%, VIX 26 to 35, TLT +5.4%) hit banks hardest alongside Energy (-21.1%), while Tech was effectively flat (-0.1%) as mega-cap growth held up on stay-at-home demand. A growth-minus-value rotation (+9.5%) and narrow breadth (equal-weight -5.8% vs cap-weight) confirmed capital rotated away from cyclical value/banks and into secular growth names as the recovery narrative wobbled.","body_zh":"XLF在6月短暂但剧烈的抛售中下跌-15.0%（排名11档中第10），美国新冠病例数在6月下旬升至每日40,000+的新纪录，重燃对复工停滞和贷款损失超出一季度计提的担忧。避险情绪（防御股-7.6% vs 周期股-10.8%，VIX从26升至35，TLT +5.4%）与能源（-21.1%）共同打击银行最重，而科技因居家需求基本持平（-0.1%）。成长-价值轮动（+9.5%）和窄幅广度（等权重落后市值加权-5.8%）印证在复苏叙事动摇之际，资本从周期价值/银行流向长期成长股。","drivers":["COVID second wave case surge","flight-to-safety rotation","growth beats value mega-cap","loan-loss acceleration fears"],"drivers_zh":["新冠第二波病例激增","避险轮动","成长战胜价值大型股","贷款损失加速担忧"],"prev_key":"2020-06-08","prev_key_chain":["2020-06-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Second COVID wave -- banks bear the brunt","title_zh":"第二波疫情——银行再度承压","turn_id":"xlf:peak:2020-06"},"2020-06-26":{"body":"Financials rode the post-COVID reopening to the #1 spot of all 11 sectors (+88.7%) in a textbook reflation/growth-up quad -- cyclicals +73.8% vs defensives +38.3%, oil +114.7%, copper-gold +67.7. A steepening curve and surging long yields (TLT -11.5%) widened net interest margins while reserve releases and buybacks lifted EPS; a weak dollar (-2.6% DXY) and broad participation (equal-weight +8.5% over cap-weight, VIX 35 to 18) confirmed banks were leading risk-on, not riding it.","body_zh":"金融板块乘着疫情后复工东风，在标准的再通胀/增长上行象限中登上全部11个板块的第1名（+88.7%）——周期股+73.8% vs 防御股+38.3%，油价+114.7%，铜金比+67.7。曲线变陡和长端收益率飙升（TLT -11.5%）扩大了净息差，准备金释放和回购提振每股收益；弱势美元（-2.6% DXY）和广泛参与（等权重领先市值加权+8.5%，VIX 35→18）印证了银行在领涨风险偏好，而非被动跟涨。","drivers":["reflation quad","risk-on leader #1","steepening curve / NIM","broad participation"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀象限","风险偏好领涨第1","曲线变陡/净息差","广泛参与"],"prev_key":"2020-06-26","prev_key_chain":["2020-06-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Reflation rally -- banks lead the cycle","title_zh":"再通胀上涨——银行领跑周期","turn_id":"xlf:trough:2020-06"},"2022-01-12":{"body":"As the Fed pivoted hawkish into 9% CPI, the tape flipped to flight-to-safety (defensives -8.9% vs cyclicals -16.1%, VIX 18 to 33) inside a stagflation-ish quad. Banks fell -25.3% but only ranked #8/11 -- geared to growth and credit, they held up far better than Tech (-26.7%) and Discretionary (-33.1%). A violent rate-regime move (TLT -21.3%) and a +9.1% DXY spike were the macro drivers; investors looked past higher NIM to peaking margins and a frozen IPO/IB-fee pipeline.","body_zh":"随着美联储在9% CPI下转向鹰派，行情切换为避险（防御股-8.9% vs 周期股-16.1%，VIX 18→33），处于偏滞胀象限。银行下跌-25.3%，但仅排名11档中第8——与增长和信用挂钩的它们远比科技（-26.7%）和可选消费（-33.1%）抗跌。剧烈的利率象限切换（TLT -21.3%）和美元跳升+9.1%是宏观驱动；投资者越过更高的净息差，看到息差见顶和冻结的IPO/投行手续费管道。","drivers":["flight-to-safety","rate regime (TLT -21%)","strong dollar","IB fee drought"],"drivers_zh":["避险","利率象限切换(TLT -21%)","强势美元","投行手续费枯竭"],"prev_key":"2022-01-12","prev_key_chain":["2022-01-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Hawkish pivot -- flight-to-safety hits banks","title_zh":"鹰派转向——避险情绪打击银行","turn_id":"xlf:peak:2022-01"},"2022-07-14":{"body":"Banks rebounded +16.7% with the broad market as a softer inflation print sparked a summer relief rally, but this was a tech/semis-led risk-on move (SMH +19.5%, growth>value +8.8, VIX 33 to 20) and XLF only ranked #6/11 -- a follower, not a leader. Long yields actually eased back over the leg (TLT +4.2%), so the move was a growth-led rebound, not a rate-driven NIM story; a +2.8% DXY and the goldilocks/disinflation flavor favored growth names over value banks. It was a bear-market bounce, not a credit all-clear.","body_zh":"随着偏软的通胀数据点燃夏季纾解上涨，银行随大盘反弹+16.7%，但这是由科技/半导体主导的风险偏好行情（SMH +19.5%，成长>价值+8.8，VIX 33→20），XLF仅排名11档中第6——是跟随者而非领涨者。这一段长端收益率实际回落（TLT +4.2%），因此这是成长主导的反弹，而非利率驱动的净息差行情；+2.8% DXY和金发姑娘/去通胀的味道更利好成长股而非价值类银行。这是熊市反弹，而非信用风险解除。","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","relief rally","yields eased (TLT +4%)","follower not leader"],"drivers_zh":["科技领涨风险偏好","纾解反弹","收益率回落(TLT +4%)","跟随非领涨"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"rekey_shift_days":28,"status":"shifted","title":"Tech-led bounce -- banks a follower","title_zh":"科技领涨反弹——银行跟随","turn_id":"xlf:trough:2022-07"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole message ended the summer bounce and reignited a rate-regime selloff: long yields surged again (TLT -13.0%) and the dollar ripped +6.4% inside a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (VIX 20 to 34). Banks fell -15.0% but ranked #4/11 -- recession and credit-cost fears returned as provisions climbed, yet financials held up better than rate-sensitive names like Real Estate (-24.7%) and Tech (-22.7%).","body_zh":"鲍威尔鹰派的杰克逊霍尔信息终结了夏季反弹，重新点燃利率象限抛售：长端收益率再度飙升（TLT -13.0%），美元在放缓/通缩恐慌象限中飙升+6.4%（VIX 20→34）。银行下跌-15.0%，但排名11档中第4——随着计提攀升，衰退和信用成本担忧卷土重来，但金融板块比房地产（-24.7%）、科技（-22.7%）等利率敏感板块更抗跌。","drivers":["rate regime (TLT -13%)","strong dollar","deflation-scare quad","rising provisions"],"drivers_zh":["利率象限(TLT -13%)","强势美元","通缩恐慌象限","计提上升"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole reset -- rate-regime selloff","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔重置——利率象限抛售","turn_id":"xlf:peak:2022-08"},"2022-10-12":{"body":"Banks rallied +22.9% off the October low to rank #3/11 as cooling CPI and peak-Fed hopes lifted risk assets in a reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +18.6% vs defensives +10.2%). A sharply weaker dollar (-8.7% DXY) and broad participation (equal-weight +3.3%, VIX 34 to 19) made this a value-friendly turn financials could lead, with resilient NIM and better-than-feared Q3/Q4 earnings adding fuel.","body_zh":"随着降温的CPI和美联储见顶预期在再通胀/增长上行象限中提振风险资产（周期股+18.6% vs 防御股+10.2%），银行从10月低点反弹+22.9%，排名11档中第3。大幅走弱的美元（-8.7% DXY）和广泛参与（等权重+3.3%，VIX 34→19）让这成为银行能够领涨的利好价值拐点，稳健的净息差和好于担忧的三/四季度业绩添柴加薪。","drivers":["reflation quad","weak dollar tailwind","broad participation","earnings beats"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀象限","弱势美元顺风","广泛参与","业绩超预期"],"prev_key":"2022-10-12","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-rate rally -- value-friendly reflation","title_zh":"利率见顶上涨——利好价值的再通胀","turn_id":"xlf:trough:2022-10"},"2023-02-07":{"body":"The collapse of Silicon Valley Bank and Signature triggered the worst bank panic since 2008. This was idiosyncratic, not a macro de-risk: XLF fell -16.3% and ranked dead last #11/11 while Tech was essentially flat (-0.1%) and the broad selloff was mild (SPY -5.7%). Defensives outperformed (-3.0% vs cyclicals -8.6%) and breadth narrowed (-4.3%) as deposit flight, unrealized bond losses and funding stress crushed regionals -- until the Fed's BTFP (launched March 12) and rescues stemmed the run.","body_zh":"硅谷银行和签名银行的倒闭引发2008年以来最严重的银行恐慌。这是特异性事件而非宏观去风险：XLF下跌-16.3%，垫底排名11档中第11，而科技基本持平（-0.1%），大盘抛售温和（SPY -5.7%）。防御股跑赢（-3.0% vs 周期股-8.6%），市场广度收窄（-4.3%），存款外流、未实现债券损失和融资压力压垮区域银行——直到美联储的BTFP工具（3月12日推出）和救助遏制挤兑。","drivers":["sector-specific shock","worst sector #11","deposit flight / unrealized losses","narrow breadth"],"drivers_zh":["板块特异冲击","最差板块第11","存款外流/未实现损失","市场广度收窄"],"prev_key":"2023-02-07","prev_key_chain":["2023-02-07"],"status":"exact","title":"SVB crisis -- XLF the lone casualty","title_zh":"硅谷银行危机——XLF独自受灾","turn_id":"xlf:peak:2023-02"},"2023-03-17":{"body":"Once contagion was contained, financials embarked on a +74.4% rally to rank #2/11 even inside a narrow, mega-cap melt-up (semis +107.8%, equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -24.1%). Banks rode a rate-regime tailwind -- long yields surged (TLT -11.2%), supporting NIM -- alongside a stronger dollar (+3.3% DXY) and the reflation quad. The 2024 soft landing, the Fed's September cut and the Trump-election deregulation/M&A 'bank trade' powered the move into early 2025.","body_zh":"在传染得到遏制后，金融板块开启+74.4%的上涨，即便在狭窄的大型股熔涨中（半导体+107.8%，等权重落后市值加权-24.1%）仍排名11档中第2。银行借力利率象限顺风——长端收益率飙升（TLT -11.2%）支撑净息差——以及更强的美元（+3.3% DXY）和再通胀象限。2024年的软着陆、美联储9月降息以及特朗普当选的放松监管/并购\"银行交易\"，推动行情直至2025年初。","drivers":["risk-on leader #2","rate regime (TLT -11%)","Trump deregulation / M&A","narrow breadth backdrop"],"drivers_zh":["风险偏好领涨第2","利率象限(TLT -11%)","特朗普放松监管/并购","狭窄广度背景"],"prev_key":"2023-03-17","prev_key_chain":["2023-03-17"],"status":"exact","title":"Crisis fades -- deregulation trade, banks #2","title_zh":"危机消退——放松监管交易，银行排名第2","turn_id":"xlf:trough:2023-03"},"2025-02-19":{"body":"Financials slid -15.5% into the April reciprocal-tariff crash, a sharp flight-to-safety event (defensives -7.7% vs cyclicals -18.7%, VIX spiking 15 to 52) inside a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Yet XLF ranked #5/11 -- geared to growth and credit, banks held up better than Tech (-25.7%) as breadth actually broadened (+2.8%) and the dollar weakened (-3.9% DXY), before the April-8/9 tariff-pause low.","body_zh":"金融板块下滑-15.5%，滑入4月的对等关税崩盘，这是放缓/通缩恐慌象限中的剧烈避险事件（防御股-7.7% vs 周期股-18.7%，VIX从15飙升至52）。但XLF排名11档中第5——与增长和信用挂钩的银行比科技（-25.7%）更抗跌，期间市场广度实际扩张（+2.8%），美元走弱（-3.9% DXY），直至4月8/9日关税暂缓低点。","drivers":["flight-to-safety","VIX 15 to 52","deflation-scare quad","relative resilience #5"],"drivers_zh":["避险","VIX 15→52","通缩恐慌象限","相对抗跌第5"],"prev_key":"2025-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2025-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-crash risk-off -- banks hold up","title_zh":"关税崩盘风险规避——银行抗跌","turn_id":"xlf:peak:2025-02"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"Off the tariff-pause low banks rallied +29.7% on deregulation, a capital-markets revival and a wave of megadeal M&A that revived IB fees -- yet XLF ranked only #6/11. This was a narrow, semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +116.1%, equal-weight lagged by -10.1%, growth>value +17.3) in a goldilocks/disinflation quad: value banks weren't broken, they were starved as flows chased Tech (+63.9%). A weaker dollar (-4.3% DXY) rounded out the backdrop.","body_zh":"从关税暂缓低点起，银行凭借放松监管、资本市场复兴以及重振投行手续费的一波巨型并购浪潮上涨+29.7%——但XLF仅排名11档中第6。这是金发姑娘/去通胀象限中由半导体主导的狭窄风险偏好熔涨（SMH +116.1%，等权重落后-10.1%，成长>价值+17.3）：价值类银行并未走坏，只是在资金追逐科技（+63.9%）时被冷落。走弱的美元（-4.3% DXY）补全了背景。","drivers":["starved by semis melt-up","narrow breadth","deregulation / M&A","goldilocks quad"],"drivers_zh":["被半导体熔涨冷落","市场广度狭窄","放松监管/并购","金发姑娘象限"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Recovery -- but starved by the semis melt-up","title_zh":"复苏——但被半导体熔涨冷落","turn_id":"xlf:trough:2025-04"},"2026-01-06":{"body":"The Iran/Hormuz oil shock pushed CPI to ~4.2% and flipped the Fed to a hiking bias, lifting the dollar (+1.6% DXY) into a stagflation-ish quad (oil +74.4%). XLF fell -14.8% and ranked dead last #11/11 -- even as breadth broadened (+4.2%) toward Energy (+38.0%) and defensives, growth-geared banks bore the brunt of renewed recession/credit-cost fears despite healthy NIM, with deregulation and deal flow only cushioning the pullback.","body_zh":"伊朗/霍尔木兹油价冲击将CPI推升至约4.2%，使美联储转向加息倾向，在偏滞胀象限中推升美元（+1.6% DXY，油价+74.4%）。XLF下跌-14.8%，垫底排名11档中第11——即便市场广度向能源（+38.0%）和防御股扩张（+4.2%），尽管净息差健康，与增长挂钩的银行仍首当其冲承受重燃的衰退/信用成本担忧，放松监管和交易流仅缓冲了回调。","drivers":["stagflation quad / oil shock","worst sector #11","Fed hiking bias","credit caution"],"drivers_zh":["滞胀象限/油价冲击","最差板块第11","美联储加息倾向","信用谨慎"],"prev_key":"2026-01-06","prev_key_chain":["2026-01-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil shock -- stagflation hits banks hardest","title_zh":"油价冲击——滞胀对银行打击最重","turn_id":"xlf:peak:2026-01"},"2026-03-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"xlf:trough:2026-03"}},"now":"XLF is in an Expansion/Trending phase, RS rank #5, sitting at the 51st percentile of its cycle range -- mid-cycle, not extended. The immediate picture is one of short-term underperformance: -2.7% (rank 9/11) in a tape dominated by a narrow semis-led melt-up (SMH +67.9%) where capital flows into Tech/Energy/Industrials and leaves cyclical-value banks behind. The underlying macro backdrop is constructive for financials structurally: a reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, copper-gold +18.3%, oil +19.2%), broadening participation (equal-weight outperforming cap-weight by +2.9%), and a negative growth-minus-value spread (-15.2%) all favor value/banks on a rotation basis. Deregulation momentum, the M&A/capital-markets revival, and stable-to-widening NIM are the bull case; the 2026 Fed hiking-bias re-pricing and a stronger dollar (+3.4% DXY) add headwinds. XLF is not broken -- it is out of favor in a mega-cap growth melt-up, and a rotation from growth to value/breadth is the single catalyst to watch for re-acceleration.","now_zh":"XLF处于扩张/趋势阶段，RS排名第5，周期位置约51百分位——处于中段，尚未过热。短期表现承压：-2.7%（排名9/11），行情被半导体领涨的窄幅熔涨（SMH +67.9%）主导，资金流向科技/能源/工业，价值类银行被边缘化。宏观底色仍对金融板块整体有利：再通胀/增长上行象限（周期股+11.2% vs 防御股+6.9%，铜金比+18.3%，油价+19.2%），市场广度扩张（等权重领先市值加权+2.9%），成长-价值利差-15.2%均从轮动角度支持价值/银行。放松监管动能、并购/资本市场复苏及稳定至扩张的净息差构成多头逻辑；2026年美联储加息预期重新定价和强势美元（+3.4% DXY）形成逆风。XLF并未走坏——只是在大型股成长行情中暂时失宠，市场风格从成长向价值/广度的切换，是最值得关注的加速催化剂。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"credit.spread_regime.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"credit.spread_regime.v1","arch_state":"fail","arch_fired_on":"2026-07-05","revision_note":null}},"xli":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"body":"XLI bottomed on October 3, 2011 near the S&P 500 trough of roughly a -19% to -20% correction driven by the European sovereign-debt crisis (Greece/Italy contagion fear) and the August 2011 U.S. credit-rating downgrade, which had sent VIX to the mid-40s. The ensuing 40-month, +119.2% recovery was powered by the Fed's Operation Twist (September 2011, ~$400bn long-for-short swap) and open-ended QE3 (September 2012, $85bn/month), which compressed credit spreads (HYG-LQD +15.7%) and reignited the reflation trade. A shale-driven U.S. industrial revival pushed manufacturing output to post-2008 highs by 2013, with Caterpillar and Boeing riding a global capex upswing; the reflation/growth-up quad kept cyclicals ahead of defensives (104.7% vs 97.5%) even as the DXY rose 18.6% — a tailwind for domestic-revenue industrials over commodity-exposed names (XLI ranked #4 of 11, behind Health/Discretionary/Financials).","body_zh":"XLI于2011年10月3日触底，接近标普500指数约-19%至-20%调整的低点——由欧洲主权债务危机（希腊/意大利传染恐慌）及2011年8月美国信用评级下调驱动，VIX一度升至40多。随后40个月+119.2%的复苏由美联储扭曲操作（2011年9月，约4000亿美元长短换购）和开放式QE3（2012年9月，每月850亿美元）提供动力，压缩信用利差（HYG-LQD +15.7%），重燃再通胀交易。2013年美国页岩驱动的工业复苏推动制造业产出升至2008年后高位，卡特彼勒与波音乘全球资本开支扩张顺风，再通胀/增长向上象限令周期股（104.7%）领先防御股（97.5%），即便美元指数+18.6%——仍有利于以国内营收为主的工业企业（XLI在11个板块中排名第4，落后于医疗/可选消费/金融）。","drivers":["Fed QE3/Operation Twist reflation","euro-debt crisis trough","shale-driven manufacturing revival","global capex upswing","credit spread compression"],"drivers_zh":["美联储QE3/扭曲操作再通胀","欧债危机触底","页岩气驱动制造业复苏","全球资本开支扩张","信用利差压缩"],"prev_key":"2011-10-03","prev_key_chain":["2011-10-03"],"status":"exact","title":"QE lifeline rescues cyclicals from euro-debt panic","title_zh":"量化宽松救援：欧债恐慌触底后周期股重生","turn_id":"xli:trough:2011-10"},"2015-02-20":{"body":"XLI peaked in February 2015 and fell -15.7% through January 2016 as a classic industrial mini-recession took hold: ISM Manufacturing slid toward and below 50 (hitting ~48 in late 2015), driven by a ferocious DXY rally (+5.1% in the leg, up 20%+ from mid-2014) that crushed multinational revenue and made U.S. exports uncompetitive. Oil collapsed -47.3% after the OPEC November 2014 no-cut decision triggered energy-capex evaporation, devastating industrial equipment orders. This was a flight-to-safety rotation: defensives (-2.7%) vastly outran cyclicals (-16.7%) as VIX ran 14 to 28 in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad, with China's August 2015 yuan devaluation amplifying the global demand-destruction narrative; XLI ranked #8 of 11.","body_zh":"XLI于2015年2月见顶，随后至2016年1月下跌-15.7%，经典工业小型衰退全面袭来：ISM制造业PMI滑向并跌破50（2015年末触及约48），驱动力来自凶猛的美元涨势（本段+5.1%，自2014年中以来累计+20%以上），大幅压制跨国公司营收、拖累美国出口竞争力。欧佩克2014年11月维持产量决定触发油价暴跌-47.3%，能源资本开支蒸发，工业设备订单随之重挫。这是一次明显的避险轮动：防御股(-2.7%)大幅跑赢周期股(-16.7%)，VIX从14升至28，市场处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限；2015年8月中国人民币贬值进一步强化全球需求毁灭叙事；XLI在11个板块中排名第8。","drivers":["ISM Manufacturing contraction below 50","dollar surge crushing multinational revenue","oil collapse and energy capex evaporation","flight-to-safety rotation","China slowdown and yuan devaluation fear"],"drivers_zh":["ISM制造业PMI收缩跌破50","美元飙升压制跨国营收","油价暴跌与能源资本开支蒸发","避险轮动","中国放缓与人民币贬值恐慌"],"prev_key":"2015-02-20","prev_key_chain":["2015-02-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Manufacturing recession: dollar surge kills global demand","title_zh":"制造业衰退：美元飙升扼杀全球需求","turn_id":"xli:peak:2015-02"},"2016-01-20":{"body":"XLI troughed around January 20, 2016 as oil bottomed near $27/barrel and China circuit-breaker panic peaked. The +75.9% recovery unfolded in waves: first the G20 Shanghai meeting (February 26-27, 2016) stabilized the yuan and oil, allowing an industrial bounce; then the Trump election victory (November 8, 2016) unleashed an infrastructure/defense-spending trade that surged machinery stocks; finally the 2017 synchronized global growth recovery (ISM Manufacturing sustained well above 55) and the December 2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (100% bonus depreciation) lifted capex. Cyclicals (75.0%) crushed defensives (34.8%) over the 32-month leg with oil surging +166.6% and DXY weakening -4.9%, placing Industrials at the #3 sector.","body_zh":"XLI约于2016年1月20日触底，彼时油价跌至约27美元/桶、中国熔断机制恐慌达到高峰。+75.9%的复苏分波展开：首先，G20上海会议（2016年2月26-27日）稳定了人民币与油价，推动工业股反弹；其次，特朗普当选（2016年11月8日）掀起基建/国防支出交易，机械股大涨；最后，2017年全球同步复苏（ISM制造业持续远高于55）及2017年12月《减税与就业法案》（100%加成折旧）提振资本开支。32个月的上涨段内周期股（75.0%）大幅跑赢防御股（34.8%），油价飙升+166.6%，美元走弱-4.9%，工业板块位列第3。","drivers":["Shanghai G20 and oil stabilization","Trump election infrastructure/defense trade","synchronized global growth recovery 2017","Tax Cuts and Jobs Act bonus depreciation capex","dollar weakening tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["上海G20稳定油价与人民币","特朗普当选基建/国防交易","2017年全球经济同步复苏","减税与就业法案加成折旧刺激资本开支","美元走弱顺风"],"prev_key":"2016-01-20","prev_key_chain":["2016-01-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Shanghai floor, Fed pause, Trump trade ignite reflation","title_zh":"上海会议托底、美联储暂停加息、特朗普交易点燃再通胀","turn_id":"xli:trough:2016-01"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"xli:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"XLI peaked September 21, 2018 and crashed -24.1% in roughly 94 days to the Christmas Eve low. The Fed delivered its fourth 25bp hike of 2018 on December 19 (funds rate 2.25-2.50%), and Powell's signal that the balance-sheet runoff would continue on a set path and that further gradual increases were likely spooked markets already stretched by a global PMI deceleration and U.S.-China tariff escalation (10% tariffs on $200bn of Chinese goods, effective September 2018). Caterpillar's October 23, 2018 results flagged tariff-driven cost increases and China demand risk, sinking the stock ~7.5%; VIX surged 12 to 36 in a flight-to-safety rotation where defensives (-8.9%) significantly outran cyclicals (-23.1%) and oil cratered -39.9% (XLI ranked #10 of 11).","body_zh":"XLI于2018年9月21日见顶，随后约94天内暴跌-24.1%至平安夜低点。美联储于12月19日第四次加息25个基点（联邦基金利率2.25%-2.50%），鲍威尔暗示缩表将按既定路径继续并将继续渐进加息，在全球PMI减速与中美关税升级（2018年9月对2000亿美元中国商品征收10%关税生效）的背景下令市场受惊。卡特彼勒2018年10月23日业绩警示关税推升成本并提示中国需求风险，股价当日跌约7.5%；VIX从12飙升至36，市场进入避险轮动，防御股（-8.9%）大幅跑赢周期股（-23.1%），油价暴跌-39.9%（XLI在11个板块中排名第10）。","drivers":["Fed overtightening and December 2018 hike shock","U.S.-China trade war tariff escalation","global PMI deceleration","flight-to-safety cyclical de-rate","Caterpillar tariff cost and demand warning"],"drivers_zh":["美联储过度收紧/2018年12月加息冲击","中美贸易战关税升级","全球PMI减速","避险轮动/周期股杀估值","卡特彼勒关税成本与需求预警"],"prev_key":"2018-09-21","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-21"],"rekey_shift_days":94,"status":"shifted","title":"Trade war tariffs and Fed overtightening crush cyclicals","title_zh":"贸易战关税+美联储过度收紧：周期股遭到重创","turn_id":"xli:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-12":{"body":"XLI peaked February 12, 2020 and crashed -42.3% to March 23 in about 40 days as COVID-19 travel bans decimated aviation and freight, with VIX exploding to 62 and the sector ranking #9 of 11. Airlines hemorrhaged cash as flights were cancelled en masse, GE Aviation cut jobs and furloughed MRO staff, and belly cargo capacity collapsed with grounded passenger flights. Oil collapsed -54.3% as demand destruction dwarfed the March 2020 OPEC+ supply war, the DXY surged +3.5%, and TLT rose +16.0% in a classic flight-to-safety panic. This was the fastest and deepest industrial-sector drawdown since 2008, driven purely by an exogenous demand shock — defensives (-28.8%) significantly outpaced cyclicals (-40.3%).","body_zh":"XLI于2020年2月12日见顶，随后约40天内暴跌-42.3%至3月23日，新冠疫情出行禁令摧毁航空与货运，VIX飙升至62，板块在11个中排名第9。航空公司大失血（航班大规模取消），GE航空裁员并让MRO员工休假，随客运航班停飞腹舱货运运力崩塌。油价暴跌-54.3%——需求毁灭完全压倒2020年3月OPEC+供给战；美元指数+3.5%，TLT+16.0%，市场陷入经典避险恐慌。这是自2008年以来工业板块最快、最深的回撤，纯粹由外生需求冲击驱动——防御股（-28.8%）明显优于周期股（-40.3%）。","drivers":["COVID demand shock and aviation collapse","freight and supply chain disruption","flight-to-safety VIX 14 to 62","oil collapse -54.3% and DXY surge","GE and Boeing aerospace immediate revenue loss"],"drivers_zh":["新冠需求冲击/航空崩塌","货运与供应链中断","避险轮动VIX由14飙升至62","油价暴跌-54.3%与美元急升","GE/波音航空航天营收即时崩塌"],"prev_key":"2020-02-12","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-12"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic collapses aviation, freight, and capex","title_zh":"新冠疫情冲击：航空、货运与资本开支全面崩塌","turn_id":"xli:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"XLI troughed March 23, 2020 and surged +125.2% over 22 months in a Fed-and-fiscal powered reflation blitz: the Fed went to zero rates and ~$120bn/month QE, while Congress passed the $2.2tn CARES Act, $900bn December 2020 relief, and $1.9tn American Rescue Plan (March 2021). The IIJA ($1.2tn, signed November 2021) added a multi-year capex pipeline for infrastructure machinery and the power grid. Reopening demand drove a freight and logistics boom (Caterpillar, Deere, UPS surged), and rising late-2021 geopolitical tension and defense-budget momentum added a tailwind for aerospace/defense names ahead of the February 2022 invasion of Ukraine. Semis led at +203.3% in a high-beta melt-up (VIX 62 to 17) with the dollar weakening -6.0% and oil surging +229.6% in a broadening reflation/growth-up quad (equal-weight beat cap-weight by +15.4%).","body_zh":"XLI于2020年3月23日触底，随后22个月内飙升+125.2%，由美联储与财政政策共同推动的再通胀猛药提供动力：美联储将利率降至零并启动约每月1200亿美元QE，国会相继通过2.2万亿美元CARES法案、2020年12月9000亿美元救济案及2021年3月1.9万亿美元美国救援计划。2021年11月签署的IIJA（1.2万亿美元）为基础设施机械与电网建设注入多年期资本开支管道。重开需求引爆货运/物流热潮（卡特彼勒、迪尔、UPS大涨），2021年末升温的地缘紧张与国防预算动能为航空航天/国防股提供顺风（领先于2022年2月俄乌入侵）。半导体领涨+203.3%，高贝塔融涨（VIX由62降至17），美元走弱-6.0%、油价飙升+229.6%，等权大幅跑赢市值加权+15.4%，呈现宽基再通胀/增长向上格局。","drivers":["zero-rate and massive QE reflation","CARES and ARP fiscal stimulus plus IIJA infrastructure pipeline","reopening freight and logistics boom","rising defense-budget momentum and geopolitical tension","dollar weakness and oil surge in reflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["零利率与大规模QE再通胀","CARES和ARP财政刺激加IIJA基建管道","重开需求货运/物流热潮","国防预算动能与地缘紧张升温","美元走弱与油价飙升再通胀象限"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Fiscal blitz and reopening power reflation mega-rally","title_zh":"财政猛药+经济重开：再通胀超级大反弹","turn_id":"xli:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-16":{"body":"Industrials de-rated hard (-19.8%) as the Fed pivoted to aggressive hiking — a rate-regime shock that crushed long-duration assets (TLT -21.4%) and a strong dollar (+8.7% DXY) that hit the multinational revenue base. This was a flight-to-safety rotation, not sector strength: defensives (-10.4%) outran cyclicals (-16.3%) as VIX ran 17 to 31. Caterpillar warned in late April that China COVID lockdowns would crimp demand, ISM rolled over, and the February 2022 Russia-Ukraine invasion spiked input/energy costs into a stagflation quad (oil +42.3%).","body_zh":"随着美联储转向激进加息，工业股大幅杀估值（-19.8%）——这是一次利率体制冲击，重创长久期资产（TLT -21.4%），强势美元（+8.7% DXY）则打击跨国企业的营收基础。这是一次避险轮动而非板块走强：防御股（-10.4%）跑赢周期股（-16.3%），VIX由17升至31。卡特彼勒在4月底警告中国新冠封控将抑制需求，ISM见顶回落，2022年2月俄乌入侵在滞胀象限中推高投入与能源成本（油价+42.3%）。","drivers":["rate regime shock and Fed liftoff","flight-to-safety rotation","strong dollar multinational headwind","China lockdown demand destruction","stagflation quad and ISM rollover"],"drivers_zh":["利率体制冲击/美联储启动加息","避险轮动","强势美元跨国营收逆风","中国封控需求毁灭","滞胀象限/ISM见顶回落"],"prev_key":"2022-01-04","prev_key_chain":["2022-01-04"],"rekey_shift_days":49,"status":"shifted","title":"Fed liftoff: rate-regime de-rate, money flees to safety","title_zh":"美联储启动加息：利率体制杀估值，资金避险","turn_id":"xli:peak:2021-11"},"2022-07-14":{"body":"Industrials rallied +18.0% off the June low on peak-inflation optimism and Fed-pivot hopes, but they were a passenger (rank #4), not the engine: this was a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +18.5%, growth over value +7.2, VIX 31 to 20) that pulled flows into high-beta, with discretionary and tech out front. July industrial production rose and ISM held in expansion, while aerospace/defense added support as Boeing deliveries recovered and the Ukraine war underpinned a multi-year defense tailwind — a goldilocks quad as oil rolled over (-21.0%).","body_zh":"工业股在6月低点反弹+18.0%，受益于通胀见顶乐观情绪与美联储转向预期，但它只是搭车者（排名第4）而非引擎：这是一次半导体领涨的风险偏好融涨（SMH +18.5%、成长跑赢价值+7.2、VIX由31降至20），资金涌入高贝塔，可选消费与科技领跑。7月工业生产回升、ISM维持扩张，航空航天/国防形成支撑——波音交付量回升，乌克兰战争奠定多年期国防顺风——油价回落（-21.0%）构成金发姑娘象限。","drivers":["tech-led risk-on and peak-inflation hope","Fed pivot speculation","resilient industrial production","defense tailwind and goldilocks quad","VIX decompression"],"drivers_zh":["科技领涨风险偏好/通胀见顶预期","美联储转向押注","工业生产韧性","国防顺风/金发姑娘象限","VIX压缩"],"prev_key":"2022-06-17","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-17"],"rekey_shift_days":27,"status":"shifted","title":"Peak-inflation bounce in a semis-led risk-on tape","title_zh":"半导体领涨风险偏好行情中的通胀见顶反弹","turn_id":"xli:trough:2022-07"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"The bounce reversed (-17.2%) as Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole speech (August 26, 2022) killed pivot hopes and a hot CPI drove another 75bp hike — a rate-regime selloff (TLT -11.4%) with a strong dollar (+5.3% DXY) headwind in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (oil -8.1%, VIX 20 to 32). The sector-specific gut-punch was FedEx pulling its full-year guidance and warning of a worldwide recession on September 15, 2022 — an approximately 21-22% one-day crash (its worst in over 40 years) that hammered transports and signaled collapsing global freight, sinking XLI even as the broad selloff was indiscriminate (defensives -12.4% barely beat cyclicals -15.3%).","body_zh":"反弹随后逆转（-17.2%）：鲍威尔在杰克逊霍尔的鹰派表态（2022年8月26日）浇灭转向预期，高企的CPI促使美联储再加息75个基点——这是一次利率体制抛售（TLT -11.4%），强势美元（+5.3% DXY）在放缓/通缩恐慌象限中构成逆风（油价-8.1%，VIX由20升至32）。板块层面的重击来自联邦快递于2022年9月15日撤回全年指引并警告全球衰退——单日暴跌约21-22%（逾40年最大单日跌幅），重创运输股、预示全球货运崩塌，拖累XLI；不过此次广泛抛售几乎无差别（防御股-12.4%仅略胜周期股-15.3%）。","drivers":["Powell Jackson Hole hawkish shock","hot CPI and 75bp rate hike","FedEx worldwide recession warning and freight demand collapse","strong dollar and slowdown quad","rate-regime re-pricing"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击","高CPI/加息75个基点","联邦快递全球衰退预警与货运需求崩塌","强势美元/放缓象限","利率体制重新定价"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkish shock and FedEx recession warning","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击与联邦快递衰退预警","turn_id":"xli:peak:2022-08"},"2022-09-30":{"body":"XLI rode a soft-landing macro and a capex super-cycle to +79.5%, the #3 sector, in a tech/semis-led risk-on regime (SMH +166.2%, growth over value +38.9, VIX 32 to 14) with a weaker dollar (-5.7% DXY) tailwind — though leadership narrowed sharply (equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -21.2%). Aerospace recovered hard (GE Aerospace, RTX) on record backlogs and rising defense budgets, while reshoring tailwinds from CHIPS (August 2022) and IIJA lifted machinery (Caterpillar, Deere) and electrical-equipment names tied to early AI/datacenter electrification. The Fed's first cuts (September 2024) plus the November 2024 election sparked a cyclical Trump trade into a goldilocks quad.","body_zh":"工业股乘着软着陆宏观与资本开支超级周期上行+79.5%，位列第3，处于半导体领涨的风险偏好体制（SMH +166.2%、成长跑赢价值+38.9、VIX由32降至14），并享美元走弱（-5.7% DXY）的顺风——但领涨明显收窄（等权落后市值加权-21.2%）。航空航天强劲复苏（GE航空航天、RTX）受订单积压创纪录与国防预算上升驱动，CHIPS法案（2022年8月）/IIJA的回流顺风提振机械（卡特彼勒、迪尔）及与早期AI/数据中心电气化挂钩的电气设备公司。美联储首次降息（2024年9月）叠加11月大选，在金发姑娘象限中点燃周期性特朗普交易。","drivers":["tech and semis-led risk-on soft landing","aerospace and defense record backlogs","reshoring plus CHIPS and IIJA capex","Fed cuts September 2024 and Trump trade rotation","AI and datacenter electrification early bid"],"drivers_zh":["科技/半导体领涨/软着陆","航空航天/国防订单积压创纪录","回流加CHIPS和IIJA资本开支","美联储2024年9月降息加特朗普交易轮动","AI/数据中心电气化早期买盘"],"prev_key":"2022-09-30","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Soft landing and AI capex: cyclicals lead, breadth narrows","title_zh":"软着陆+AI资本开支：周期股领涨，但广度收窄","turn_id":"xli:trough:2022-09"},"2024-11-29":{"body":"Trump's April 2025 reciprocal tariffs cratered industrials -18.5% into an April 8 low, with big China-exporting cyclicals leading the Dow down — Boeing fell roughly 9% and Caterpillar roughly 6% over two days. This was a flight-to-safety rotation as VIX spiked 14 to 52: defensives (-8.9%) sharply outran cyclicals (-19.2%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (oil -12.4%). Industrials' globalized supply chains and machinery/aerospace input costs made the sector a clear casualty even as a weaker dollar (-2.6% DXY) offered no offset.","body_zh":"特朗普2025年4月的对等关税将工业股打入4月8日低点（-18.5%），对华出口占比高的大型周期股领跌道指——波音两日内跌约9%、卡特彼勒跌约6%。这是一次避险轮动，VIX由14飙升至52：在放缓/通缩恐慌象限中，防御股（-8.9%）大幅跑赢周期股（-19.2%，油价-12.4%）。工业板块全球化的供应链以及机械/航空航天的投入成本使其成为明显的受害者，即便美元走弱（-2.6% DXY）也未能提供缓冲。","drivers":["April 2025 reciprocal tariffs shock","flight-to-safety VIX 14 to 52","Boeing and Caterpillar supply-chain hit","global growth recession fears","slowdown and deflation-scare quad"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月对等关税冲击","避险轮动VIX由14飙升至52","波音/卡特彼勒供应链受挫","全球增长衰退恐惧","放缓/通缩恐慌象限"],"prev_key":"2024-11-29","prev_key_chain":["2024-11-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Reciprocal tariffs gut supply chains, money flees to safety","title_zh":"对等关税冲击供应链，资金涌向避险","turn_id":"xli:peak:2024-11"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"Off the April 8 low industrials surged +60.3% as a genuine #2 leader, powered by aerospace/defense (GE Aerospace, RTX) and the AI-power/datacenter electrification capex boom — GE Vernova and Eaton riding a transformer/switchgear shortage — alongside bonus-depreciation reigniting machinery orders and reshoring. In a reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +51.4% vs defensives +20.4%, oil +20.7%) this was risk-on leadership, though the tape stayed narrow (equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -8.8%) under a roaring semis bid (SMH +255%). The leg held up through the 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock (strait blockade reimposed June 20, 2026) on durable defense and AI-infrastructure demand.","body_zh":"自4月8日低点起，工业股作为名副其实的第二领头飙升+60.3%，受航空航天/国防（GE航空航天、RTX）及AI电力/数据中心电气化资本开支热潮驱动——GE Vernova与伊顿乘着变压器/开关设备短缺上行，叠加加成折旧重新点燃机械订单与制造业回流。在再通胀/增长向上的象限中（周期股+51.4% vs 防御股+20.4%、油价+20.7%），这是风险偏好领涨；尽管在半导体强劲买盘下（SMH +255%）市场广度仍偏窄（等权落后市值加权-8.8%）。这一上涨段在2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹油价冲击中（6月20日海峡重新封锁）依靠稳健的国防与AI基础设施需求得以挺住。","drivers":["risk-on leadership in reflation quad","aerospace and defense plus AI-power electrification capex","reshoring and bonus depreciation machinery orders","tariff truce and trade deal optimism","semis-led high-beta surge pulling cyclicals"],"drivers_zh":["风险偏好领涨/再通胀象限","航空航天/国防加AI电力电气化资本开支","回流/加成折旧机械订单","关税休战与贸易协议乐观预期","半导体领涨高贝塔拉动周期股"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Industrials lead the rebound: genuine #2, not a passenger","title_zh":"工业股领涨反弹：真正的第二领头，而非搭车者","turn_id":"xli:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"XLI is the genuine RS #2 sector leader in 2026 (+15.8% leg return, relative-strength rank 2, #3 by raw return behind Tech and Energy), powered by the reflation/growth-up quad where cyclicals (+11.2%) are decisively outrunning defensives (+6.9%). The setup is distinctively broad-based: equal-weight is beating cap-weight by +2.9%, oil is up +19.2% and copper-gold +18.3, confirming a physical-economy demand pulse rather than a financial-engineering melt-up. Industrials leadership rests on three durable structural pillars: AI-power/datacenter electrification capex (GE Vernova record data-center orders, Eaton transformer/switchgear shortage), reshoring-linked machinery orders, and elevated defense budgets, all of which proved resilient through the 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil-shock episode (blockade reimposed June 20, 2026). With VIX low (14-18) and the sector at pos 46.8 within the current rally leg off the April 2025 low, this reads as mid-expansion rather than a top signal; the key watch is whether ISM Manufacturing sustains above 50 and whether the semis bid (+67.9%) keeps capex orders flowing into industrial end-markets.","now_zh":"工业股板块（XLI）目前是2026年名副其实的相对强度第二领头板块（本轮上涨+15.8%、相对强度排名第2、按原始回报为第3，仅次于科技与能源），在再通胀/增长向上象限中大幅跑赢——周期股（+11.2%）对防御股（+6.9%）构成明显优势。当前行情具有鲜明的宽基特征：等权指数跑赢市值加权+2.9%，油价+19.2%、铜金比+18.3，印证的是实体经济需求脉冲而非金融工程式融涨。工业股领涨的结构性支柱有三：AI电力/数据中心电气化资本开支（GE Vernova数据中心订单创纪录、伊顿变压器/开关设备短缺）、回流制造业带动的机械订单，以及高位国防预算——即便在2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹油价冲击中（6月20日重新封锁海峡）也展现了韧性。VIX处于低位（14-18），板块自2025年4月低点以来处于本轮上涨的46.8%分位，更像扩张中段而非顶部信号；关键风险监测点在于ISM制造业能否维持50以上，以及半导体强劲买盘（+67.9%）能否持续将资本开支订单传导至工业终端市场。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"business.cycle_trough.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"business.cycle_trough.v1","arch_state":"missing","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"xlk":{"legs":{"2011-08-19":{"body":"Starting from the August 2011 S&P downgrade trough, Tech embarked on a 7-year, 282% secular bull as ZIRP (Fed held rates at 0-0.25% through Dec 2015) inflated long-duration growth multiples while the mobile-cloud revolution drove earnings. Apple's iPhone/iPad super-cycle, the emergence of FANG hyper-growth platforms, Microsoft's pivot to Azure, and three rounds of QE (QE3 announced Sep 2012) channeled equity flows into mega-cap tech. The 10-year Treasury yield fell from ~3.0% to cycle lows (TLT +25%), the dollar strengthened 29.4%, and semis surged 329.4% -- a narrow, mega-cap-led melt-up (equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -12.5%) that left Energy and defensives far behind. The 2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act added final fuel: Apple, Microsoft, and Alphabet held $250B+ in offshore cash eligible for a one-time 15.5% repatriation tax, triggering massive buyback programs that compressed float and lifted EPS.","body_zh":"从2011年8月标普降级的低谷出发，科技板块开启了长达7年、涨幅282%的长期牛市，动力来自两方面：零利率政策（美联储将利率维持在0-0.25%直至2015年12月）拉升了长久期成长股的估值倍数；同时移动-云计算革命推动盈利持续增长。苹果iPhone/iPad超级周期、FANG超成长平台的崛起、微软向Azure的战略转型，以及三轮量化宽松（QE3于2012年9月宣布），将资金源源不断地引向大盘科技股。10年期美债收益率从约3.0%降至周期低点（TLT +25%），美元升值29.4%，半导体飙升329.4%——这是一场狭窄、大盘股主导的慢牛（等权落后市值加权-12.5%），能源和防御板块被远远甩在身后。2017年《减税与就业法案》更是火上浇油：苹果、微软、Alphabet持有逾2500亿美元海外现金，享受一次性15.5%的汇回税优惠，引发了规模浩大的股票回购潮，压缩流通股并拉升每股盈利。","drivers":["ZIRP/multi-round QE","mobile-cloud revolution","FANG earnings hyper-growth","tax reform buyback wave","mega-cap concentration"],"drivers_zh":["零利率/多轮量化宽松","移动互联网与云计算革命","FANG盈利爆发","税改回购潮","大盘龙头高度集中"],"prev_key":"2011-08-19","prev_key_chain":["2011-08-19"],"status":"exact","title":"ZIRP-era mega-cap tech secular bull","title_zh":"零利率时代大盘科技长期牛市","turn_id":"xlk:trough:2011-08"},"2018-10-03":{"body":"Tech peaked October 3, 2018 and fell 23.8% (rank 10/11) in a classic flight-to-safety rotation driven by two simultaneous shocks: the 10-year Treasury yield hit ~3.24% in early October -- its highest level since 2011 -- crushing long-duration growth multiples; and the US applied 10% tariffs on $200B of Chinese goods effective September 24, 2018, directly hitting supply-chain-dependent semis (SMH -22.9%). Powell raised rates for the 4th time in 2018 on December 19 and signaled ongoing balance-sheet runoff, with markets pricing a recession. VIX spiked from 12 to 36, oil collapsed -44.3%, and defensives (Utilities -1.0%) massively outperformed cyclicals (-22.5%) -- a textbook risk-off rotation out of growth.","body_zh":"科技板块于2018年10月3日见顶，随后下跌23.8%（排名10/11），演绎了一场由双重冲击引发的经典避险轮动：10年期美债收益率于10月初攀升至约3.24%（2011年以来最高），重创长久期成长股估值；美国自9月24日起对2000亿美元中国商品加征10%关税，直接打击供应链高度依赖中国的半导体板块（SMH -22.9%）。12月19日，鲍威尔第四次加息并暗示将继续缩表，市场开始为衰退定价。VIX从12飙升至36，油价暴跌-44.3%，防御板块（公用事业-1.0%）大幅跑赢周期板块（-22.5%）——教科书式的风险偏好撤退，资金出逃成长股。","drivers":["4th Fed rate hike 2018","10Y yield spikes to 3.24%","US-China tariff escalation","recession pricing","VIX surge 12 to 36"],"drivers_zh":["2018年第四次加息","10年期收益率升至3.24%","中美关税升级","市场为衰退定价","VIX暴涨至36"],"prev_key":"2018-10-03","prev_key_chain":["2018-10-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed + trade-war valuation reset","title_zh":"美联储加息叠加贸易战估值重置","turn_id":"xlk:peak:2018-10"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"Tech surged 80.7% (rank #1/11) from the Christmas Eve 2018 trough as Powell executed a U-turn: on January 4, 2019 he signaled patience, and the Fed cut rates three times in 2019 ('insurance cuts'), taking the funds rate from 2.5% back to 1.75%. Simultaneously, the US-China Phase One trade deal (announced late 2019, signed January 2020) removed the tariff escalation threat. FAANG earnings reaccelerated -- Microsoft and Apple each pushed toward $1T+ market cap in 2019 -- semis ripped +90.9%, and the tape was characteristically narrow (equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -6.9%). VIX normalized from 36 to 14 and 10-year yields fell (TLT +23.0%), extending the duration tailwind for growth stocks.","body_zh":"从2018年平安夜低谷出发，科技板块飙涨80.7%（排名第1/11），鲍威尔的政策急转弯是核心催化剂：2019年1月4日他释放鸽派信号，随后美联储三次降息（\"预防性降息\"），将联邦基金利率从2.5%降回1.75%。与此同时，中美第一阶段贸易协议（2019年底宣布、2020年1月签署）消除了关税升级威胁。FANG盈利重新加速——微软和苹果市值于2019年先后冲向1万亿美元——半导体飙涨+90.9%，盘面依然高度集中（等权落后-6.9%）。VIX从36正常化至14，10年期收益率下滑（TLT +23.0%），进一步延续了对成长股的久期顺风。","drivers":["Fed 'insurance' rate cuts","US-China Phase One deal","FANG earnings reacceleration","semis-led rally","long-duration tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["美联储预防性降息","中美第一阶段协议","FANG盈利重新加速","半导体领涨","长久期顺风"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot + trade truce recovery","title_zh":"美联储转向叠加贸易休战复苏","turn_id":"xlk:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-19":{"body":"Tech fell 31.2% in the 33-day COVID crash (February 19 to March 23), though it ranked 4th best out of 11 sectors -- defensives (Staples -24.2%, Health -27.9%) held up better while Financials (-42.8%) and Energy (-56.1%) cratered. VIX exploded from 14 to 62, oil collapsed -56.2%, credit spreads blew out (HYG-LQD -9.6%), and the dollar rose +2.9% as a global margin-call and dash-for-cash spared no asset class. Tech's relative resilience vs cyclicals (-40.2% avg) reflected its software/cloud exposure providing near-term earnings visibility (work-from-home thesis taking shape), but the initial margin liquidation overwhelmed any flight-to-quality argument in the acute phase.","body_zh":"科技板块在历时33天的新冠崩盘中（2月19日至3月23日）下跌31.2%，尽管在11个板块中排名第4——防御板块（消费必需品-24.2%，医疗-27.9%）表现相对抗跌，而金融（-42.8%）和能源（-56.1%）则大幅崩溃。VIX从14飙升至62，油价暴跌-56.2%，信用利差激增（HYG-LQD -9.6%），美元上涨+2.9%，全球性的追保和现金荒令所有资产类别无一幸免。相较于周期板块（平均-40.2%），科技板块的相对韧性源于其软件/云计算业务在近期盈利上的可见度（居家办公逻辑雏形初现），但急性阶段的初始强平浪潮压过了一切质量避险逻辑。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic outbreak","global margin call / dash-for-cash","VIX spike to 62","credit spread blowout","WFH thesis embryonic"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情爆发","全球流动性危机与现金荒","VIX暴涨至62","信用利差激增","居家办公概念萌芽"],"prev_key":"2020-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID-19 pandemic liquidation","title_zh":"新冠疫情全球清仓式抛售","turn_id":"xlk:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"Tech surged 154.7% (rank #2) as the Fed cut rates to zero, launched unlimited QE on March 23 2020, and Congress passed the $2.2T CARES Act -- the most aggressive macro backstop in history. Work-from-home digitization permanently pulled forward 5+ years of cloud/SaaS adoption: Microsoft Teams grew from 32M to 145M daily active users, Zoom FY2021 revenue more than tripled, and Nvidia's data-center segment accelerated sharply. Semis ripped +205.8%, growth demolished value (+33.4%), VIX fell from 62 to 18, dollar weakened (-6.2%), and equal-weight outpaced cap-weight by +12.8% -- broad participation in the 2020-21 recovery, unlike prior narrow legs. ZIRP again gave hyper-growth multiples a new ceiling, and the pandemic narrative made tech a defensive-growth hybrid in the public imagination.","body_zh":"科技板块飙涨154.7%（排名第2），动力来自三方面：美联储将利率降至零并于2020年3月23日启动无限量QE；国会通过2.2万亿美元《CARES法案》刺激——史上最激进的宏观托底组合。居家办公引发的数字化转型将5年以上的云/SaaS渗透率提前实现：微软Teams日活用户从3200万增至1.45亿，Zoom该财年营收增长逾两倍，英伟达数据中心业务急速加速。半导体飙涨+205.8%，成长股大幅跑赢价值（+33.4%），VIX从62回落至18，美元走弱（-6.2%），等权跑赢市值加权+12.8%——2020-21年复苏的参与广度远超以往狭窄行情。零利率再度抬高了超高成长股的估值天花板，疫情叙事使科技在公众眼中成为兼具防御与成长属性的板块。","drivers":["Fed zero rates + unlimited QE","CARES Act fiscal stimulus","WFH cloud/SaaS adoption surge","semis data-center acceleration","growth multiple re-rating"],"drivers_zh":["美联储零利率+无限量QE","万亿财政刺激","居家办公云/SaaS需求爆发","半导体数据中心业务加速","成长股估值多重扩张"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Pandemic digitization melt-up","title_zh":"疫情数字化浪潮驱动的飙升","turn_id":"xlk:trough:2020-03"},"2021-12-27":{"body":"As the Fed pivoted hawkish into a ~7-9% CPI regime, a rate-regime selloff (TLT -11.3%, yields surging) crushed long-duration tech, where rich multiples hung on far-future earnings. XLK finished near dead last (rank 10/11, -20.0%) as a strong dollar (+3.1% DXY) and the February Russia-Ukraine invasion added a stagflationary risk-off bid; only Energy (+32.9%) escaped the duration unwind.","body_zh":"美联储在7-9%的高通胀环境中转向鹰派，利率象限的抛售（TLT -11.3%、收益率飙升）重创长久期科技股——其高估值依赖于遥远的未来盈利。XLK接近垫底（排名10/11，-20.0%），强美元（+3.1% DXY）和2月俄乌战争叠加出滞胀式的避险买盘；只有能源（+32.9%）逃过了这场久期重定价。","drivers":["rate regime","duration de-rating","stretched valuations","strong dollar"],"drivers_zh":["利率象限","久期重定价","估值过高","强美元"],"prev_key":"2021-12-27","prev_key_chain":["2021-12-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-shock duration de-rating","title_zh":"利率冲击下的久期重定价","turn_id":"xlk:peak:2021-12"},"2022-03-14":{"body":"A sharp tech/semis-led risk-on rip (SMH +18.8%, growth>value +8.7, VIX 32 to 19) as the market digested the first Fed hike and an oversold growth complex snapped back. Tech ranked #2/11 in a narrow, mega-cap-led tape (equal-weight lagged by -2.4%) -- but nothing in the inflation or rates picture had actually turned.","body_zh":"一波由科技/半导体引领的风险偏好急涨（SMH +18.8%、成长跑赢价值+8.7、VIX 32降至19），市场消化了首次加息、超卖的成长板块强力反弹。在狭窄、大盘股主导的盘面中（等权落后-2.4%）科技排名第2/11——但通胀和利率的格局实际上并未转向。","drivers":["oversold bounce","tech-led risk-on","narrow breadth","short cover"],"drivers_zh":["超卖反弹","科技引领风险偏好","市场广度狭窄","空头回补"],"prev_key":"2022-03-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Oversold relief bounce","title_zh":"超卖后的反弹","turn_id":"xlk:trough:2022-03"},"2022-03-29":{"body":"The Fed accelerated to 50-75bp hikes and QT as inflation stayed near 9%, a rate-regime move (TLT -14.1%, +5.3% DXY) that re-crushed long-duration tech to dead last (rank 9, -24.5%). This was a genuine flight-to-safety -- defensives (-11.2%) far outperformed cyclicals (-18.2%) with VIX 19 to 33 -- as semis broke down (SMH -28.1%) into the June bear low.","body_zh":"通胀维持在9%附近，美联储加速至50-75个基点加息并缩表，这一利率象限的move（TLT -14.1%、+5.3% DXY）将长久期科技股再度打到垫底（排名9，-24.5%）。这是真正的避险——防御板块（-11.2%）远超周期板块（-18.2%），VIX 19升至33——半导体崩溃（SMH -28.1%），跌向6月熊市低点。","drivers":["aggressive hikes","rate regime","flight-to-safety","strong dollar"],"drivers_zh":["激进加息","利率象限","避险","强美元"],"prev_key":"2022-03-29","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Hiking-cycle bear leg","title_zh":"加息周期的熊市腿","turn_id":"xlk:peak:2022-03"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"Tech ripped ~23% on a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +20.8%, growth>value +9.2, VIX 33 to 20) as the market bet inflation had peaked and the Fed would soon pivot. Falling-yield hope lifted rate-sensitive growth and money edged out of safety -- Tech ranked #2/11 in a goldilocks tape -- before Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole speech (Aug 26) killed it.","body_zh":"科技急涨约23%，源于科技/半导体引领的风险偏好飙升（SMH +20.8%、成长跑赢价值+9.2、VIX 33降至20），市场押注通胀已见顶、美联储即将转向。收益率回落预期提振了对利率敏感的成长股，资金撤出防御——在金发姑娘式盘面中科技排名第2/11——直到鲍威尔8月26日在杰克逊霍尔的鹰派讲话终结了这轮反弹。","drivers":["peak-inflation hope","tech-led risk-on","pivot bet","goldilocks quad"],"drivers_zh":["通胀见顶预期","科技引领风险偏好","转向押注","金发姑娘象限"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-inflation hope rally","title_zh":"通胀见顶预期下的反弹","turn_id":"xlk:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-15":{"body":"Powell's August 26 Jackson Hole vow to hold rates 'higher for longer' was a rate-regime move (TLT -12.7%, +6.4% DXY pushing the dollar to new highs) that slammed long-duration tech to near the bottom (rank 10, -22.9%). A hot September CPI sealed the deflation-scare selloff and the SMH -28.8% breakdown into the October bear-market low.","body_zh":"鲍威尔8月26日在杰克逊霍尔誓言将利率维持\"更高更久\"，这是一记利率象限的move（TLT -12.7%、+6.4% DXY将美元推至新高），把长久期科技股打到接近垫底（排名10，-22.9%）。火热的9月CPI坐实了通缩恐慌式抛售，以及SMH -28.8%的崩溃，跌向10月熊市低点。","drivers":["Jackson Hole","rate regime","strong dollar","deflation-scare quad"],"drivers_zh":["杰克逊霍尔","利率象限","强美元","通缩恐慌象限"],"prev_key":"2022-08-15","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkish reset","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派重置","turn_id":"xlk:peak:2022-08"},"2022-10-12":{"body":"A softer October CPI marked the rate-peak inflection, and ChatGPT's late-November launch ignited a generative-AI super-cycle that made the semis the dominant theme (SMH +226.2%) in a goldilocks risk-on melt-up (growth>value +52.9, VIX 34 to 13, -7.3% DXY tailwind). XLK ranked #1/11 and more than doubled (+107%) -- but this was the narrowest of tapes, with equal-weight lagging cap-weight by a staggering -28.7%.","body_zh":"更温和的10月CPI标志着利率见顶拐点，ChatGPT于11月底发布点燃了生成式AI超级周期，使半导体成为主导主题（SMH +226.2%），处于金发姑娘式的风险偏好飙升中（成长跑赢价值+52.9、VIX 34降至13、-7.3% DXY顺风）。XLK排名第1/11并翻倍有余（+107%）——但这是极度狭窄的盘面，等权指数落后市值加权高达-28.7%。","drivers":["genAI super-cycle","tech-led risk-on","narrow breadth","goldilocks quad"],"drivers_zh":["生成式AI超级周期","科技引领风险偏好","市场广度狭窄","金发姑娘象限"],"prev_key":"2022-10-12","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-12"],"status":"exact","title":"The genAI bull run","title_zh":"生成式AI牛市","turn_id":"xlk:trough:2022-10"},"2024-07-10":{"body":"A BoJ rate hike and a weak US jobs report violently unwound the yen-carry trade, hitting the most crowded AI longs hardest -- Tech air-pocketed ~17% (dead last, rank 11) as semis cratered (SMH -24.8%). This was a flight-to-safety: defensives (+2.2%) led cyclicals (-5.5%) with VIX 13 to 28, a fast technical deleveraging, not a fundamental break.","body_zh":"日本央行加息与疲软的美国就业报告剧烈瓦解了日元套息交易，对最拥挤的AI多头打击最重——科技瞬间真空约17%（垫底，排名11），半导体暴跌（SMH -24.8%）。这是一次避险：防御板块（+2.2%）领先周期板块（-5.5%），VIX 13升至28，属于快速的技术性去杠杆，而非基本面破裂。","drivers":["yen-carry unwind","flight-to-safety","crowded momentum","growth-scare jobs print"],"drivers_zh":["日元套息瓦解","避险","拥挤动量","增长恐慌就业数据"],"prev_key":"2024-07-10","prev_key_chain":["2024-07-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Yen-carry air-pocket","title_zh":"日元套息交易的瞬间真空","turn_id":"xlk:peak:2024-07"},"2024-08-07":{"body":"Tech rebounded +23% as the carry-unwind panic faded into a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +22.2%, growth>value +12.1, VIX 28 to 15), with the Fed's September cut and post-election deregulation bets fueling Nvidia-led AI enthusiasm. Leadership stayed narrow and mega-cap (equal-weight lagged by -6.2%), even as a rate-regime backup (TLT -6.1%) and strong dollar (+3.8% DXY) built underneath.","body_zh":"随着套息瓦解的恐慌消退，科技反弹+23%，演变为科技/半导体引领的风险偏好飙升（SMH +22.2%、成长跑赢价值+12.1、VIX 28降至15），美联储9月降息与大选后放松监管的押注助燃了英伟达领涨的AI热情。领涨保持狭窄且集中于大盘股（等权落后-6.2%），尽管底层正酝酿利率象限回升（TLT -6.1%）与强美元（+3.8% DXY）。","drivers":["Fed cuts begin","tech-led risk-on","narrow breadth","rate regime"],"drivers_zh":["美联储开启降息","科技引领风险偏好","市场广度狭窄","利率象限"],"prev_key":"2024-08-07","prev_key_chain":["2024-08-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Soft-landing AI recovery","title_zh":"软着陆下的AI复苏","turn_id":"xlk:trough:2024-08"},"2025-02-19":{"body":"The late-January DeepSeek cheap-AI scare cracked the capex thesis (Nvidia's record ~$589B one-day value loss on Jan 27), and April's 'Liberation Day' reciprocal tariffs detonated a broad crash that sent Tech dead last (rank 11, -25.7%, SMH -30.1%). This was a violent flight-to-safety -- defensives (-7.7%) far outran cyclicals (-18.7%) as VIX exploded 15 to 52 -- bottoming around April 8.","body_zh":"1月底DeepSeek廉价AI恐慌击碎了资本开支逻辑（1月27日英伟达单日蒸发约5890亿美元，创历史纪录），4月\"解放日\"对等关税引爆了一场全面崩盘，将科技打到垫底（排名11，-25.7%，SMH -30.1%）。这是一次剧烈的避险——防御板块（-7.7%）远超周期板块（-18.7%），VIX暴涨15至52——在4月8日附近见底。","drivers":["DeepSeek scare","reciprocal tariffs","flight-to-safety","capex-thesis doubt"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek恐慌","对等关税","避险","资本开支逻辑动摇"],"prev_key":"2025-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2025-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek + tariff shock","title_zh":"DeepSeek叠加关税冲击","turn_id":"xlk:peak:2025-02"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"Trump's tariff pause and device exemptions detonated a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +104.8%, growth>value +29.9, VIX 52 to 17, -3.6% DXY tailwind) with hyperscaler spend estimates past $400B. XLK ranked #1/11 (+69.7%) on Nvidia/Broadcom records, but it was the textbook narrow tape -- equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -15.1% as money concentrated in a handful of AI names.","body_zh":"特朗普暂停关税并豁免设备，引爆了科技/半导体引领的风险偏好飙升（SMH +104.8%、成长跑赢价值+29.9、VIX 52降至17、-3.6% DXY顺风），云厂商资本开支预期突破4000亿美元。XLK排名第1/11（+69.7%），由英伟达/博通创纪录推动，但这是教科书式的狭窄盘面——资金集中于少数几只AI龙头，等权落后市值加权-15.1%。","drivers":["tariff de-escalation","tech-led risk-on","narrow breadth","AI-capex melt-up"],"drivers_zh":["关税降级","科技引领风险偏好","市场广度狭窄","AI资本开支飙升"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-pause AI melt-up","title_zh":"关税暂停下的AI飙升","turn_id":"xlk:trough:2025-04"},"2025-10-29":{"body":"A hawkish Fed turn repriced borrowing costs just as hyperscalers committed to the most expensive build-out in a generation, sparking an AI-complex valuation reset that sent Tech dead last (rank 11, -15.9%). Unusually, this wasn't a risk-off panic -- defensives and cyclicals fell roughly in line -- it was a stagflation-ish rotation OUT of crowded megacap growth (growth-value -19.5) into Energy (+42.9%, oil +70.1%), with equal-weight beating cap-weight by +8.2% as breadth finally broadened.","body_zh":"美联储转鹰重新定价了借贷成本，恰逢云厂商承诺一代人以来最昂贵的建设，引发AI板块的估值重置，将科技打到垫底（排名11，-15.9%）。不同寻常的是，这并非避险恐慌——防御与周期板块跌幅大体相当——而是一次滞胀式轮动，资金撤出拥挤的大盘成长（成长-价值-19.5），转入能源（+42.9%，油价+70.1%），等权跑赢市值加权+8.2%，市场广度终于扩散。","drivers":["hawkish Fed","AI valuation reset","rotation out of megacap","broadening breadth"],"drivers_zh":["美联储鹰派","AI估值重置","撤出大盘股","市场广度扩散"],"prev_key":"2025-10-29","prev_key_chain":["2025-10-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Hawkish valuation reset","title_zh":"鹰派下的估值重置","turn_id":"xlk:peak:2025-10"},"2026-03-30":{"body":"Tech ripped ~55% (rank #1) as the 2026 Iran-war oil tail faded toward the mid-June ceasefire (oil down ~20% from its 2026 highs) and the AI-capex trade roared back in a reflation/risk-on melt-up (SMH +74.4%, growth>value +10.9, VIX 31 to 16). It was again narrow and mega-cap-led (equal-weight lagged by -8.6%); the leg crested into early June as Broadcom's June 3 report -- holding rather than raising its full-year AI semiconductor target despite AI revenue up 143% -- detonated a $1T+ semis wipeout, the late-cycle top.","body_zh":"随着2026年伊朗战争的油价尾部风险消退、临近6月中停火（油价较2026年高点回落约20%），AI资本开支交易强势回归，科技在再通胀/风险偏好的飙升中急涨约55%（排名第1，SMH +74.4%、成长跑赢价值+10.9、VIX 31降至16）。盘面再度狭窄并由大盘股主导（等权落后-8.6%）；该上涨腿在6月初见顶，博通6月3日财报尽管AI营收同比大增143%，却仅维持而未上调全年AI芯片目标，引爆超过1万亿美元的半导体市值蒸发——这就是周期晚期的顶部。","drivers":["oil-tail unwind","tech-led risk-on","narrow breadth","AVGO outlook top"],"drivers_zh":["油价尾部风险消退","科技引领风险偏好","市场广度狭窄","博通展望见顶"],"prev_key":"2026-03-30","prev_key_chain":["2026-03-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil-fade AI rip","title_zh":"油价消退下的AI急涨","turn_id":"xlk:trough:2026-03"}},"now":"Tech is the undisputed #1 sector (RS rank 1, +24.3% vs SPY +6.3%) sitting at cycle position ~84/100 in a topping phase. The reflation/growth-up quad has been dominated by AI-capex spending by hyperscalers, with semis (SMH +67.9%) leading in a high-beta (+20.7% vs low-vol) tape. Critically, equal-weight is slightly outperforming cap-weight (+2.9%), suggesting early broadening beneath the leaders -- a late-cycle signature. The leg crested in early June 2026 when Broadcom (June 3 Q2 report) stuck to its existing full-year AI semiconductor target rather than raising it -- despite AI revenue up 143% -- detonating a $1T+ semis wipeout; XLK is now in distribution with the SELL signal active, growth underperforming value (-15.2% growth-value spread), and dollar strengthening (DXY +3.4%) providing a headwind to multinationals -- the classic setup preceding a major inflection.","now_zh":"科技板块以绝对优势蝉联第一（RS排名第1，+24.3% vs 标普+6.3%），周期位置约84/100，处于顶部阶段。再通胀/增长上行象限由超大规模云厂商的AI资本开支主导，半导体（SMH +67.9%）在高贝塔（+20.7% vs 低波动）的盘面中领涨。值得注意的是，等权微幅跑赢市值加权（+2.9%），显示领涨股之下出现初步扩散——这是周期晚期的典型特征。本轮上涨腿在2026年6月初见顶，博通（6月3日二季报）尽管AI营收同比大增143%，却仅维持而未上调全年AI芯片目标，引发超过1万亿美元的半导体市值蒸发；XLK目前处于派发阶段，卖出信号激活，成长股跑输价值（成长-价值价差-15.2%），强美元（DXY +3.4%）对跨国公司形成阻力——这是重大转折点前的经典布局。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"xlp":{"legs":{"2018-01-26":{"body":"The 10-year Treasury yield surged from ~2.4% at the January 26 SPY peak toward the 3% threshold by early May 2018 (it first crossed 3% on April 24), the fastest rate rise in years, driven by the December 2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act boosting deficit expectations and a February 2 payrolls print showing 2.9% wage growth (fastest since 2009). Consumer staples, a textbook bond-proxy sector whose dividend yields had compressed to near-Treasury levels, faced a mechanical re-rating: as risk-free rates rose, their relative yield advantage evaporated and capital rotated to tech and cyclicals. Company-specific blows compounded the macro headwind: Amazon-Whole Foods integration fears hammered grocery suppliers, General Mills cut its margin outlook in late March 2018 on input-cost inflation, and the February 5 Volmageddon VIX spike (the index jumped intraday from ~17 to ~37, its largest one-day point move on record) triggered risk-parity deleveraging across the tape. XLP ranked #10 of 11 sectors in this leg, falling -16.1% while SPY fell only -8.0%, confirming this was a bond-proxy de-rating rather than a fundamental earnings shock.","body_zh":"10年期美债收益率自1月26日SPY高点的约2.4%飙升，至5月初逼近3%关口（4月24日首次突破3%），为多年来最快升速，原因在于2017年12月《减税与就业法案》推高赤字预期，以及2月2日非农数据显示薪资增速达2.9%（2009年以来最快）。必需消费品是典型的债券替代品板块，其股息收益率已压缩至接近国债水平，利率上升机械性地消除了相对收益优势，资金转向科技与周期板块。个股利空叠加宏观逆风：亚马逊整合全食超市引发市场对食品供应商的冲击恐慌，通用磨坊于2018年3月末因投入成本通胀下调利润率展望，2月5日的Volmageddon VIX暴涨（盘中从约17升至约37，为有史以来最大单日点数跳升）触发风险平价策略去杠杆。XLP本轮排名第10/11，跌幅16.1%，远超SPY（-8.0%），确认这是债券替代品杀估值，而非基本面盈利冲击。","drivers":["rate-shock bond-proxy de-rating","Volmageddon deleveraging Feb 5","Amazon grocery disruption","strong dollar +3.7%"],"drivers_zh":["利率冲击杀债券替代估值","2月5日波动末日去杠杆","亚马逊冲击杂货供应商","美元走强+3.7%"],"prev_key":"2018-01-26","prev_key_chain":["2018-01-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Bond-proxy de-rating as 10Y yield surged toward 3%","title_zh":"10年期美债收益率逼近3%，债券替代品遭杀估值","turn_id":"xlp:peak:2018-01"},"2018-05-03":{"body":"Off the May 2018 trough, consumer staples entered a 21-month +39.2% rally as three distinct macro tailwinds converged. First, the Fed's late-2018 pause and then January 2019 pivot - Powell's dovish December 19, 2018 press conference signaled caution, and by January 4, 2019 he explicitly walked back rate-hike guidance - triggered a bond-proxy re-rating in reverse: the 10-year fell from ~3.2% back toward 2.0%, reviving staples' relative yield appeal. Second, the escalating US-China trade war (steel/aluminum tariffs March 2018, Section 301 China tariffs September 2018, May 2019 Huawei ban) drove persistent risk-off rotations into defensives whenever negotiations deteriorated. Third, the Fed cut rates three times in 2019 (July 31, September 18, October 30) as insurance against the trade shock, compressing yields further and lifting dividend-paying defensives. TLT gained +27.0% over the full leg; XLP ranked #4 of 11 at +39.2% as low-vol beat high-beta (-22.4 spread), matching the defensives-led slowdown/deflation-scare quad in which defensives (+39.5%) far outran cyclicals (+20.4%).","body_zh":"自2018年5月低点起，必需消费品开启长达21个月、涨幅39.2%的反弹，三重宏观顺风共振。其一，美联储2018年末暂停加息并于2019年1月转向——鲍威尔2018年12月19日发布会展现鸽派立场，2019年1月4日明确放弃加息路径——引发债券替代品逆向重评：10年期收益率自约3.2%回落至约2.0%，必需消费品相对息率吸引力复苏。其二，美中贸易战持续升级（2018年3月钢铝关税、2018年9月301条款对华关税、2019年5月华为禁令），每逢谈判恶化即触发持续性避险轮动至防御板块。其三，美联储2019年三度降息（7月31日、9月18日、10月30日）以对冲贸易冲击，进一步压低收益率并提振高息防御股。整个阶段TLT涨+27.0%；XLP的+39.2%排名第4/11，低波动跑赢高贝塔（利差-22.4），与防御主导的放缓/通缩担忧象限高度吻合，该象限下防御板块（+39.5%）大幅领先周期板块（+20.4%）。","drivers":["Fed pivot to cuts 2019","10Y yield fell from ~3.2% to 2.0%","US-China trade war risk-off","defensive dividend revival"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年转向降息","10年期收益率自约3.2%回落至2.0%","美中贸易战避险","防御型股息吸引力复苏"],"prev_key":"2018-05-03","prev_key_chain":["2018-05-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot plus trade war safety bid lifts defensives","title_zh":"美联储转向叠加贸易战避险买盘推升防御板块","turn_id":"xlp:trough:2018-05"},"2018-11-09":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"xlp:peak:2018-11"},"2018-12-24":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"xlp:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-14":{"body":"From the February 14 XLP peak (coinciding with the late-stage SPY peak on February 19), consumer staples fell -24.5% in just 37 days as the COVID-19 pandemic triggered the fastest bear market in S&P 500 history, with VIX exploding from 14 to 62. The panic was indiscriminate: on March 12 the S&P fell 9.5% in a single session (its worst day since 1987) the day after the WHO declared a global pandemic on March 11, with the Fed launching massive emergency repo operations. Consumer staples ranked #1 (least bad) of 11 sectors at -24.5% vs SPY -33.6% and cyclicals -40.1%, but even the defensive hedge could not escape the liquidity-driven forced selling: institutional portfolios sold whatever was liquid to meet redemptions and margin calls. Oil collapsed -55.1% (demand destruction plus the March 8 Saudi-Russia price war), TLT gained +15% as bonds were the only safe haven, and the DXY surged +3.4% as a dollar liquidity crunch hit global markets. In absolute terms, staples lost a quarter of their value in five weeks even while providing meaningful relative cushioning.","body_zh":"自XLP于2月14日见顶（SPY高点为2月19日），必需消费品在短短37天内跌幅达24.5%，新冠疫情引发标普500史上最快的熊市，VIX从14飙至62。恐慌情绪毫无判别：3月11日世卫组织宣布全球大流行，次日（3月12日）标普单日暴跌9.5%（1987年以来最惨一日），美联储同时启动大规模紧急回购操作。必需消费品以-24.5%成为11个板块中跌幅最小者（排名第1），显著优于SPY（-33.6%）和周期板块（-40.1%），但即便是防御对冲也无法逃脱流动性驱动的被动抛售——机构投资者出售一切流动性较好的资产以应对赎回和追缴保证金。油价崩塌-55.1%（需求毁灭叠加3月8日沙俄价格战），TLT涨+15%（债券成为唯一避险港湾），美元流动性紧缺推动DXY大涨+3.4%。尽管提供了有意义的相对缓冲，必需消费品在绝对收益上五周内也损失了四分之一的价值。","drivers":["COVID pandemic forced selling","VIX 14 to 62","Saudi-Russia oil price war -55%","relative defensive cushion #1 of 11"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情被动抛售","VIX从14飙至62","沙俄石油价格战-55%","防御相对缓冲跌幅最小第1/11"],"prev_key":"2020-02-14","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-14"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash: defensives cannot hide","title_zh":"新冠疫情冲击——防御板块亦无处遁形","turn_id":"xlp:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"Off the March 23, 2020 market trough - the day the Fed announced unlimited QE and days before Congress finalized the $2.2 trillion CARES Act (signed March 27) - consumer staples rallied +74.4% through April 20, 2022, but ranked #10 of 11 sectors. The reflation/growth-up quad created a brutal structural headwind: the CARES Act ($2.2T March 2020) and American Rescue Plan ($1.9T March 2021), zero interest rates, and vaccine-driven reopening drove Energy +277%, Materials +145%, and Financials +123% while low-vol defensives were systematically abandoned. High-beta outperformed low-vol by a record +113.3%, equal-weight beat cap-weight by +23.3%, and TLT fell -24.4% as yields surged - each was a mechanical negative for staples relative performance. Within the sector, the pandemic created a brief pantry-stocking tailwind for food companies in mid-2020, but from late 2020 onward the surge in oil (+340%) and commodity input costs began squeezing staples margins, with P&G, Colgate, and Kimberly-Clark unable to fully pass through cost inflation until well into 2021.","body_zh":"自2020年3月23日市场低点（美联储宣布无限QE的当日，国会数日后完成2.2万亿美元CARES法案立法、3月27日签署），必需消费品反弹+74.4%至2022年4月20日，但在11个板块中排名第10。再通胀/增长上行象限形成严峻的结构性逆风：CARES法案（2.2万亿，2020年3月）、美国救助计划（1.9万亿，2021年3月）、零利率与疫苗驱动的复工使能源+277%、原材料+145%、金融+123%，低波动防御板块遭系统性抛弃。高贝塔跑赢低波动高达+113.3%（历史之最），等权重跑赢市值加权+23.3%，TLT跌-24.4%（收益率飙升），每项指标均对必需消费品相对表现形成机械性拖累。板块内部，疫情在2020年中带来了短暂的囤货顺风，但自2020年底起，油价（+340%）与大宗商品投入成本飙升开始挤压利润率，宝洁、高露洁、金伯利等企业直至2021年底才得以充分转嫁成本通胀压力。","drivers":["reflation quad cyclical leadership","CARES plus ARP fiscal stimulus","10Y yield surge TLT -24%","high-beta dominance +113% spread"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀象限周期领涨","CARES+美国救助计划财政刺激","10年期收益率飙升TLT-24%","高贝塔主导+113%利差"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Pandemic recovery: cyclicals lead, staples lag reflation","title_zh":"疫情复苏：周期板块领涨，必需消费品落后于再通胀","turn_id":"xlp:trough:2020-03"},"2022-04-20":{"body":"This wasn't a clean flight-to-safety: with the 10Y surging (TLT -16.0%) and the dollar ripping +12.4% in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad, the rate-regime de-rating hit everything, and even staples fell ~16.3% as 9% CPI input-cost inflation compressed margins before pricing caught up. The Fed delivered its most aggressive tightening cycle since the 1980s - 75 bps hikes at the June, July, September, and November 2022 FOMC meetings - driving the DXY to a 20-year high near 114-115 (September 2022) and rapidly eroding consumer staples' bond-proxy premium. XLP only ranked #5/11 because the whole tape was red: defensives (-14.6%) barely edged cyclicals (-15.5%), so its outperformance was relative cushioning, not strength, into the October 2022 low.","body_zh":"这并非干净的避险行情：在10年期收益率飙升（TLT -16.0%）、美元在放缓/通缩担忧象限中暴涨+12.4%的背景下，利率体制的杀估值冲击了一切，连必需消费品也跌幅约16.3%——CPI高达9%的投入成本通胀在定价跟上之前先挤压了利润率。美联储实施1980年代以来最激进的紧缩周期——在2022年6、7、9、11月FOMC会议各加息75个基点——推动DXY于2022年9月贴近20年高点114至115，迅速蚕食必需消费品的债券替代溢价。XLP仅排名第5/11，只因整个市场一片惨红——防御板块（-14.6%）勉强好于周期板块（-15.5%）——跌幅相对较小是相对缓冲而非真正的强势，直至2022年10月低点。","drivers":["Fed 75bps hike cycle 2022","10Y yield surge TLT -16%","DXY 20-year high +12.4%","CPI 9% input-cost inflation"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2022年加息75基点周期","10年期收益率飙升TLT-16%","DXY创20年高点+12.4%","CPI高达9%的投入成本通胀"],"prev_key":"2022-04-20","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-driven de-rating: even defensives could not hide","title_zh":"利率驱动的杀估值，连防御板块也无处藏身","turn_id":"xlp:peak:2022-04"},"2022-10-07":{"body":"Off the October 2022 low staples did everything right - pricing power, steady demand and reliable dividends drew a flight-to-safety bid into early 2026 as tariff and oil-shock uncertainty flared, lifting XLP ~48% to its February 2026 peak. But it still ranked #9/11: nothing was wrong with the defensive, money simply rotated to tech in a narrow, mega-cap-led melt-up (SMH +341.8%, growth over value +42.4, equal-weight lagging cap-weight by -31.3%). The AI revolution, centered on Nvidia's generative-AI buildout from late 2022 onward and the ChatGPT launch in November 2022, created a one-way flow into semiconductors and hyperscalers that systematically drained capital from low-growth defensives. A weak dollar (-13.5% DXY) and goldilocks quad turbo-charged the risk-on leaders, leaving low-vol staples to win on an absolute basis while badly lagging on a relative one.","body_zh":"自2022年10月低点起必需消费品样样做对——定价权、稳定需求与可靠股息，在2026年初关税与油价冲击的不确定性升温时吸引了避险买盘，将XLP推升约48%至2026年2月峰值。但它仍排名第9/11：防御板块本身并无问题，资金只是在狭窄的、大市值主导的逼空行情中转向科技（半导体+341.8%，成长跑赢价值+42.4，等权重落后市值加权-31.3%）。以英伟达生成式AI建设为核心的AI革命（2022年11月ChatGPT发布为重要节点）形成单向资金流入半导体与超大规模云计算，系统性抽干低增长防御板块的资本。疲软的美元（-13.5% DXY）与金发女孩象限为风险偏好的领涨者火上浇油，令低波动的必需消费品在绝对收益上获胜，却在相对表现上严重落后。","drivers":["AI tech melt-up SMH +342%","narrow mega-cap breadth EW -31%","defensives starved of flows","weak dollar tailwind -13.5%"],"drivers_zh":["AI科技逼空行情半导体+342%","大市值主导市场广度收窄等权-31%","防御板块资金持续外流","美元弱势利多跨国巨头-13.5%"],"prev_key":"2022-10-07","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Starved by the AI melt-up: up 48%, but the laggard","title_zh":"被AI逼空行情冷落——上涨48%，却是落后者","turn_id":"xlp:trough:2022-10"},"2023-05-01":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"xlp:peak:2023-05"},"2023-10-12":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"xlp:trough:2023-10"}},"now":"ROLLING OVER (RS #8) - staples are being starved, not broken: XLP is up ~8.8% YTD (rank #6) inside a reflation/growth-up quad where tech (+24.3%), energy (+21.5%), and industrials (+15.8%) are leading and cyclicals are outpacing defensives by ~430 bps (11.2% vs 6.9%). The 2025 flight-to-safety bid that lifted XLP has faded now that VIX has compressed toward the low-to-mid teens (14-18 range), high-beta over low-vol is running +20.7%, and semis are up 67.9%, all pulling flows away from low-vol defensive names. The value-over-growth rotation (growth minus value at -15.2%) is the one tail-risk for this configuration: if mega-cap leadership cracks and equal-weight continues to beat cap-weight (+2.9%), XLP could reclaim relative strength, but for now the sector is in a late-cycle starved-not-broken phase with no near-term catalyst for a defensive rotation.","now_zh":"滚顶（相对强弱排名第8）——必需消费品被边缘化，而非基本面受损：XLP年初至今涨约8.8%（排名第6），但身处反通胀/增长上行象限，科技（+24.3%）、能源（+21.5%）、工业（+15.8%）领跑，周期板块跑赢防御板块约430个基点（11.2%对6.9%）。曾支撑XLP的2025年避险买盘正在消退——VIX已回落至10多点的低位区间（14至18），高贝塔跑赢低波动+20.7%，半导体大涨67.9%，资金持续流出低波动防御性品种。成长跑输价值（成长减价值为-15.2%）是当前格局唯一的尾部风险：若大市值领涨股崩塌、等权重持续跑赢市值加权（+2.9%），XLP或重获相对强势；但当前板块仍处于被冷落而非受损的周期后期，无明显近期催化剂触发防御轮动。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"xlre":{"legs":{"2015-10-08":{"body":"XLRE began trading in early October 2015, just after the Fed stood pat at the September FOMC, citing China's August 'Black Monday' crash (Shanghai -8.5% on Aug 24) and commodity deflation (oil at multi-year lows). Treasury yields fell as global deflation fears mounted (TLT +16.9% over the leg), mechanically lifting the REIT bond proxy into a classic slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Defensives dominated: Utilities +21.6% and Real Estate +18.5% ranked #1 and #2 while Energy fell -3.9% and credit spreads widened (HYG underperformed LQD by -4.7 pts); the December 2015 hike to 0.25-0.50% was well-telegraphed and shallow, insufficient to break the yield-fall tailwind sustaining REITs through mid-2016.","body_zh":"XLRE于2015年10月初开始交易，恰逢美联储9月议息会议按兵不动之后，理由是中国8月\"黑色星期一\"崩盘（8月24日上证大跌8.5%）及大宗商品通缩（油价创多年低点）。全球通缩恐慌加剧使美债收益率下行（TLT+16.9%），机械性地托举了REIT这一债券替代品，进入典型的放缓/通缩恐慌象限。防御板块主导：公用事业+21.6%、房地产+18.5%分列第1、第2，能源跌-3.9%，信用利差扩大（HYG跑输LQD达-4.7个百分点）；2015年12月加息至0.25-0.50%早有预期且幅度浅，不足以打破支撑REIT至2016年年中的收益率下行顺风。","drivers":["Fed hike delay","China deflation scare","yield decline","defensive rotation"],"drivers_zh":["美联储推迟加息","中国通缩恐慌","收益率下行","防御性轮动"],"prev_key":"2015-10-08","prev_key_chain":["2015-10-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed hike delay, deflation scare lifts bond proxy","title_zh":"美联储推迟加息、通缩恐慌推升债券替代品","turn_id":"xlre:trough:2015-10"},"2016-08-01":{"body":"The 10-year Treasury yield, which had troughed near 1.37% in early July 2016 on the Brexit shock, began reversing higher through August as global growth fears faded and commodity prices stabilised; Trump's election victory on November 8 then fired the 'reflation trade' in earnest — the 10Y surged from roughly 1.85% to about 2.35% in November alone (TLT -11.7% total leg), pricing in fiscal stimulus, deficit spending and higher inflation. REITs were the worst sector (-14.6%, rank #10) as fund outflows hit REIT ETFs post-election; Financials (+13.3%) and Energy (+9.2%) led the exact mirror rotation that punished the bond proxy. The dollar strengthened (+3.2% DXY) and the macro quad flipped to reflation/growth-up, confirming the full yield-driven regime change.","body_zh":"10年期美债收益率在2016年7月初受英国脱欧冲击触底约1.37%后开始回升，8月随全球增长担忧消退、大宗商品价格企稳而反弹；11月8日特朗普当选后\"再通胀交易\"全面引爆——仅11月10年期收益率便从约1.85%升至约2.35%（本段TLT累计-11.7%），市场押注财政刺激、赤字扩张和通胀走高。REIT成为最差板块（-14.6%，排名第10），大选后REIT基金遭遇净流出；金融股（+13.3%）和能源股（+9.2%）领涨，形成对债券替代品的完全镜像反转。美元走强（DXY+3.2%），宏观象限切换至再通胀/增长向上，确认了完整的收益率驱动政策环境转变。","drivers":["Trump reflation trade","yield surge","rate regime flip","dollar strength"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普再通胀交易","收益率飙升","利率象限翻转","美元走强"],"prev_key":"2016-08-01","prev_key_chain":["2016-08-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump reflation trade spikes yields, REITs crushed","title_zh":"特朗普再通胀交易推升收益率，REIT重挫","turn_id":"xlre:peak:2016-08"},"2016-11-10":{"body":"From the November 2016 reflation trough, XLRE staged a 59.8% three-year bull run to February 2020. The core driver was a secular decline in long-term yields (TLT +30.8% over the leg) as growth stayed moderate and the Fed's 2018 hiking cycle peaked at just 2.25-2.50%, then reversed with three cuts in 2019 on global slowdown fears — directly expanding REIT valuations via lower cap-rates. Subsector tailwinds amplified the gain: e-commerce drove industrial/logistics REIT demand (Prologis surging), multifamily benefited from housing-cost inflation, and data-centre REITs (Equinix, Digital Realty) rode cloud-build demand. Tech dominated at +123.7% in a mega-cap-led tape (equal-weight lagged by -15.3%); REIT's +59.8% lagged SPY's +63.7% in absolute terms but held up well on a risk-adjusted basis, with the slow-burn stagflation-ish quad enabling both duration and real-asset plays to compound.","body_zh":"从2016年11月再通胀低点出发，XLRE开启了历时三年的59.8%牛市至2020年2月。核心驱动是长端收益率的长期下行（TLT+30.8%），因增长温和且美联储2018年加息周期仅至2.25-2.50%便触顶，2019年因全球放缓恐慌三度降息——直接通过压低资本化率扩张了REIT估值。子板块结构性顺风放大了涨幅：电商驱动工业/物流REIT需求（普洛斯飙升）、多户型住宅受益于住房成本通胀、数据中心REIT（埃奎尼克斯、数字房地产信托）借助云基础设施建设需求腾飞。科技以+123.7%主导，行情结构狭窄（等权重落后-15.3%）；REIT的+59.8%绝对值落后于SPY的+63.7%，但风险调整后表现稳健，偏滞胀象限令久期与实物资产两类交易均得以持续复利。","drivers":["secular yield decline","Fed 2019 pivot","e-commerce/industrial demand","mega-cap melt-up"],"drivers_zh":["收益率长期下行","美联储2019年转向","电商/工业需求","大型股熔涨"],"prev_key":"2016-11-10","prev_key_chain":["2016-11-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-Trump low: 3-yr secular bull on falling yields","title_zh":"特朗普后低点：收益率下行驱动三年长牛","turn_id":"xlre:trough:2016-11"},"2020-02-21":{"body":"The February-March 2020 COVID-19 selloff hit REITs with compound blows: pandemic lockdowns directly impaired rent collection and physical use in office, retail (malls shuttered) and hotel REITs (lodging REITs among the hardest hit), while the broader panic (VIX 17 to 62) drained credit markets (HYG underperformed LQD by -9.2 pts). REITs fell -38.8% (rank #8 in a brutal tape), worse than the defensive average (-29.1%) but better than Financials (-42.1%) and Energy (-55.5%). The dual shock of sector-specific rent/use impairment and broad systemic panic made this leg unusually severe; only data-centre REITs held up relatively well, underscoring that the subsector composition of XLRE now matters as much as the rate regime.","body_zh":"2020年2-3月新冠疫情抛售对REIT造成复合打击：疫情封锁直接损害了写字楼、零售（购物中心关闭）和酒店REIT（住宿类REIT受创最重）的租金回收与实际使用，而更广泛的恐慌（VIX从17升至62）抽空了信用市场（HYG跑输LQD达-9.2个百分点）。REIT下跌-38.8%（排名第8），弱于防御股平均水平（-29.1%），但好于金融股（-42.1%）和能源股（-55.5%）。行业特有的租金/使用损伤与系统性恐慌的双重冲击使本段跌幅异常惨烈；仅数据中心REIT相对抗住，凸显XLRE的子板块构成已与利率象限同等重要。","drivers":["COVID-19 lockdowns","rent-collection collapse","VIX spike systemic panic","credit stress"],"drivers_zh":["新冠封锁","租金回收崩溃","VIX飙升系统性恐慌","信用压力"],"prev_key":"2020-02-21","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-21"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash: office/retail REIT implosion","title_zh":"新冠疫情崩盘：写字楼/零售REIT爆雷","turn_id":"xlre:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The March 23, 2020 Fed emergency cut to zero and unlimited-QE announcement triggered the recovery bottom. REITs rose +115.4% from the trough (rank #7), driven by the Fed holding rates near zero through 2021 (TLT -8.3% as yields normalised modestly but stayed historically low) and fiscal stimulus ($5T+ cumulative) that prevented a wave of commercial-mortgage defaults. The reflation/growth-up quad dominated: cyclicals gained +140% vs defensives +76%, with oil +222% and credit spreads tightening sharply (HYG beat LQD +16.7 pts). Within XLRE, the recovery was uneven — industrial, data-centre and residential REITs led the melt-up (benefiting from e-commerce acceleration and work-from-home demand for housing), while office and retail REITs lagged and never fully recovered their pre-COVID highs, permanently reshaping the index's subsector mix.","body_zh":"2020年3月23日美联储紧急降息至零并宣布无限量QE，触发复苏底部。REIT从低点反弹+115.4%（排名第7），驱动力是美联储将利率维持在接近零的水平至2021年（TLT-8.3%，收益率小幅正常化但仍处历史低位）及5万亿美元+累计财政刺激防止商业房贷违约潮。再通胀/增长向上象限主导：周期股涨+140% vs 防御股+76%，油价+222%，信用利差大幅收窄（HYG跑赢LQD达+16.7个百分点）。XLRE内部复苏分化——工业、数据中心和住宅REIT领涨（受益于电商加速和居家工作推动的住房需求），而写字楼和零售REIT落后，始终未能收复新冠前高点，永久改变了指数的子板块构成。","drivers":["Fed zero-rate QE","fiscal stimulus","industrial/residential outperformance","reflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["美联储零利率QE","财政刺激","工业/住宅领跑","再通胀象限"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed zero-rate QE reboot: REIT broad recovery","title_zh":"美联储零利率QE重启：REIT全面复苏","turn_id":"xlre:trough:2020-03"},"2021-12-31":{"body":"The Fed's hawkish turn against then-~7% CPI (the print was racing toward its mid-2022 9.1% peak) sent the 10Y surging (TLT -7.6%), and as the textbook rate-regime move it hammered the long-duration bond proxy first — REITs fell -15.1%, the worst defensive. This was a rate selloff, not a flight-to-safety: defensives actually lagged cyclicals (-7.4% vs -5.4%) with VIX 17 to 31, because rising discount rates compressed property valuations and made REIT yields uncompetitive versus Treasuries.","body_zh":"美联储在当时约7%（并加速冲向2022年年中9.1%峰值）的CPI下转向鹰派，使10年期收益率飙升（TLT-7.6%），作为典型的利率象限走势，它首当其冲地重创了长久期债券替代品——REIT下跌-15.1%，是表现最差的防御板块。这是一轮利率抛售，而非避险：防御股实际跑输周期股（-7.4% vs -5.4%），VIX由17升至31，因上升的贴现率压缩了房产估值，并使REIT收益率相对国债失去竞争力。","drivers":["rate regime","duration hit","valuation compression","reflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["利率象限","久期受挫","估值压缩","再通胀象限"],"prev_key":"2021-12-31","prev_key_chain":["2021-12-31"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-shock derating leads the tape down","title_zh":"利率冲击下修领跌大盘","turn_id":"xlre:peak:2021-12"},"2022-02-23":{"body":"With yields briefly stabilizing and inflation fears pausing, buyers rotated into beaten-down real assets — REITs bounced +15.7% (rank #3), behind only Energy and Utilities as defensives led cyclicals (+12.7% vs +7.9%) and semis stayed in the doghouse (SMH -4.2%). This was a value-over-growth, stagflation-quad relief move, but the bigger picture stayed bearish: the dollar firmed (+4.4% DXY) and the 10Y kept climbing (TLT -10.7%), capping the counter-trend rebound.","body_zh":"随着收益率短暂企稳、通胀担忧暂歇，买盘轮入被打压的实物资产——REIT反弹+15.7%（排名第3），仅次于能源和公用事业，防御股领先周期股（+12.7% vs +7.9%），半导体仍遭冷落（SMH-4.2%）。这是一轮价值跑赢成长的滞胀象限纾解走势，但大格局仍偏空：美元走强（DXY+4.4%）、10年期收益率续升（TLT-10.7%），封住了这轮逆势回升。","drivers":["defensive rotation","relief rally","rate pause","stagflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["板块轮动","纾解反弹","利率暂停","滞胀象限"],"prev_key":"2022-02-23","prev_key_chain":["2022-02-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Defensive rate-pause bounce, #3 sector","title_zh":"防御性利率暂停反弹，板块第3","turn_id":"xlre:trough:2022-02"},"2022-04-20":{"body":"As the Fed accelerated hikes and the 10Y surged (TLT -7.8%), the long-duration bond proxy sold off -23.2% into the June low — rank #10, worse even than other defensives (-14.5% avg). Higher cap rates compressed property values, a strong dollar (+3.2% DXY) added a stagflation-quad headwind, and recession fears deepened the de-rating as VIX climbed 20 to 33.","body_zh":"随着美联储加速加息、10年期收益率飙升（TLT-7.8%），长久期债券替代品抛售-23.2%至6月低点——排名第10，甚至弱于其他防御板块（平均-14.5%）。更高的资本化率压缩了房产价值，强势美元（DXY+3.2%）叠加滞胀象限逆风，衰退担忧随VIX由20升至33而加深了估值下修。","drivers":["rate regime","cap-rate rise","strong dollar","stagflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["利率象限","资本化率上升","强势美元","滞胀象限"],"prev_key":"2022-04-20","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Fastest hiking crushes the duration trade","title_zh":"最快加息压垮久期交易","turn_id":"xlre:peak:2022-04"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"REITs rallied +18.7% (rank #4) as rates pulled back from the June peak (TLT +3.7%) on softer-inflation hopes. But the leadership belonged to the risk-on melt-up — semis +20.8%, growth over value, VIX 33 to 20 — so the bond proxy rode a goldilocks-quad relief rather than leading; falling yields, not sector strength, lifted rate-sensitive real estate off its lows.","body_zh":"随着利率因偏软的通胀预期从6月高点回落（TLT+3.7%），REIT上涨+18.7%（排名第4）。但领涨权属于风险偏好熔涨——半导体+20.8%、成长跑赢价值、VIX由33降至20——因此债券替代品是搭上了金发女孩象限的纾解，而非领涨；是收益率回落而非板块自身强势，将利率敏感的房地产从低点托起。","drivers":["yield pullback","tech-led risk-on","duration relief","goldilocks quad"],"drivers_zh":["收益率回落","科技领涨风险偏好","久期缓解","金发女孩象限"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-Fed relief in a semis-led bounce","title_zh":"美联储见顶纾解，半导体领涨的反弹","turn_id":"xlre:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-15":{"body":"Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole speech (August 26, 2022) and a renewed climb in Treasury yields (TLT -14.2%) drove the bond proxy to fresh lows — REITs fell -25.5%, the single worst sector (#11). A surging dollar (+6.3% DXY) deepened the slowdown/deflation-scare quad, and the near one-for-one inverse link between REITs and the 10Y carried the drawdown into October even as VIX rose 20 to 32.","body_zh":"鲍威尔2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔鹰派讲话和美债收益率的新一轮攀升（TLT-14.2%），将债券替代品推向新低——REIT下跌-25.5%，是唯一最差板块（第11）。飙升的美元（DXY+6.3%）加深了放缓/通缩恐慌象限，REIT与10年期之间近乎一对一的反向关联将回撤延续至10月，其间VIX由20升至32。","drivers":["hawkish Powell","rate regime","strong dollar","rate sensitivity"],"drivers_zh":["鹰派鲍威尔","利率象限","强势美元","利率敏感性"],"prev_key":"2022-08-15","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole yield surge, worst sector","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔收益率飙升，最差板块","turn_id":"xlre:peak:2022-08"},"2022-10-14":{"body":"Cooling CPI sparked peak-rate hopes and yields fell hard (TLT +11.0%), so the duration-sensitive bond proxy roared back +25.3% (rank #2). A collapsing dollar (-10.2% DXY) and broadening tape (equal-weight +4.3%) drove a goldilocks-quad recovery, and discount-rate fears eased as VIX fell 32 to 19 into early 2023.","body_zh":"降温的CPI点燃利率见顶预期、收益率大幅回落（TLT+11.0%），久期敏感的债券替代品强势反弹+25.3%（排名第2）。崩塌的美元（DXY-10.2%）与扩张的市场广度（等权重+4.3%）驱动了金发女孩象限的复苏，贴现率担忧随VIX由32降至19而缓解，直至2023年初。","drivers":["disinflation hopes","rate regime","broadening breadth","goldilocks quad"],"drivers_zh":["去通胀预期","利率象限","市场广度扩张","金发女孩象限"],"prev_key":"2022-10-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Disinflation pivot snaps the duration trade higher","title_zh":"去通胀转向带动久期交易飙升","turn_id":"xlre:trough:2022-10"},"2023-02-02":{"body":"As the 10Y ground toward its October-2023 peak (TLT -21.3%), the bond proxy slid -21.1% — dead-last (#11) while SPY was flat and semis rose, a textbook rate-regime divergence. A narrow, mega-cap tape (equal-weight lagged by -12.7%) and a firmer dollar (+4.7% DXY) starved real estate of flows, and office-distress/work-from-home headlines weighed on sentiment even though office is a small index slice; the sector bottomed in late October.","body_zh":"随着10年期向2023年10月峰值缓步磨升（TLT-21.3%），债券替代品下滑-21.1%——垫底（第11），其间SPY持平、半导体上涨，是典型的利率象限背离。狭窄的大型股行情（等权重落后-12.7%）和走强的美元（DXY+4.7%）使房地产资金枯竭，办公楼困境与居家办公的头条拖累情绪——即便办公楼只是指数中的一小部分；该板块在10月底触底。","drivers":["rate regime","narrow breadth","office distress","duration drag"],"drivers_zh":["利率象限","市场广度狭窄","办公楼困境","久期拖累"],"prev_key":"2023-02-02","prev_key_chain":["2023-02-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Yields grind higher, the lone laggard","title_zh":"收益率磨升，唯一的落后者","turn_id":"xlre:peak:2023-02"},"2023-10-25":{"body":"Disinflation and the Fed's 2024 pivot lowered yields (TLT +16.3%), reviving the duration trade and lifting REITs +45.4% off the yield peak. The rally trailed the semis-led melt-up (SMH +72.8%) in a narrow, mega-cap tape (equal-weight -5.1%), but AI-datacenter demand and resilient industrial/healthcare names led the sector, with the September-2024 cut and election-year optimism extending a goldilocks-quad recovery as VIX fell 20 to 14.","body_zh":"去通胀和美联储2024年的政策转向压低收益率（TLT+16.3%），重振久期交易，使REIT从收益率峰值反弹+45.4%。在狭窄的大型股行情（等权重-5.1%）中，这轮上涨落后于半导体领涨的熔涨（SMH+72.8%），但AI数据中心需求和坚韧的工业/医疗标的领涨板块，2024年9月的降息和大选年乐观情绪延续了金发女孩象限的复苏，VIX由20降至14。","drivers":["rate-cut pivot","rate regime","AI datacenters","goldilocks quad"],"drivers_zh":["降息转向","利率象限","AI数据中心","金发女孩象限"],"prev_key":"2023-10-25","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-cut pivot revives the bond proxy","title_zh":"降息转向重振债券替代品","turn_id":"xlre:trough:2023-10"},"2024-09-16":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"xlre:peak:2024-09"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"REITs recovered +26.2% off the tariff-pause low on easing rates and durable AI-datacenter/industrial demand — but it was a middling rank #7, badly lagging the risk-on melt-up: semis ripped +240.9% and high-beta beat low-vol by +111 pts, draining flows from the low-vol bond proxy. By 2026 the Iran/Hormuz oil shock, ~4.2% CPI and a Fed hiking bias capped the rally in a narrow, mega-cap tape (equal-weight -8.7%), leaving the rate-sensitive sector topping.","body_zh":"REIT凭借利率缓解和持久的AI数据中心/工业需求，从关税暂缓低点复苏+26.2%——但仅排名第7，大幅落后于风险偏好熔涨：半导体狂飙+240.9%、高贝塔跑赢低波动+111个百分点，抽走了低波动债券替代品的资金。到2026年，伊朗/霍尔木兹油价冲击、约4.2%的CPI和美联储加息倾向在狭窄的大型股行情（等权重-8.7%）中封住了涨势，使这个利率敏感的板块筑顶。","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","defensives starved","oil-shock inflation","narrow breadth"],"drivers_zh":["科技领涨风险偏好","防御股被冷落","油价冲击通胀","市场广度狭窄"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Recovery starved by the semis melt-up","title_zh":"复苏被半导体熔涨冷落","turn_id":"xlre:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Real Estate is topping at RS rank #3 (pos ~81, SELL signal, above 200d), +12.1% YTD — an above-average absolute return that nonetheless trails the dominant risk-on melt-up where semis surged +67.9% and high-beta beat low-vol by +21 pts, starving the low-vol bond proxy of flows. The 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock has kept CPI elevated (~4.2%), imposing a Fed hiking bias that caps the duration trade (TLT only +1.1%); a stronger dollar (+3.4% DXY) adds a further headwind. Within-sector breadth is carried by AI-datacenter and industrial sub-REITs while office and retail lag; the reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2%) means XLRE is riding coat-tails rather than leading, and with the sector ~80% through its cycle the risk/reward is skewing toward the next rate-driven selloff leg.","now_zh":"房地产板块处于筑顶阶段，相对强势排名第3（位置约81%，卖出信号，站上200日均线），年初至今上涨+12.1%——绝对收益尚可，但远落后于主导风险偏好的熔涨行情，半导体飙升+67.9%、高贝塔跑赢低波动+21个百分点，抽干了低波动债券替代品的资金流。2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹油价冲击令CPI居高不下（约4.2%），美联储鹰派倾向封住了久期交易（TLT仅+1.1%）；美元走强（DXY+3.4%）进一步构成宏观逆风。板块内部由AI数据中心和工业子REIT支撑，写字楼和零售类落后。再通胀/增长向上象限（周期股+11.2% vs 防御股+6.9%，油价+19.2%）意味着XLRE更多是顺势借力而非领涨；板块已完成约80%周期路径，风险/回报正向下一轮利率驱动的回调倾斜。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"housing.bubble_peak.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"housing.bubble_peak.v1","arch_state":"missing","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"xlu":{"legs":{"2015-01-29":{"body":"XLU peaked in late January 2015 near multi-year highs after a bond-rally-fueled run, then fell 15.7% (worst of 11 sectors) as the 10-year Treasury yield surged roughly 75-100 bps off its late-January low near 1.65% toward 2.5% by early summer on strengthening US data and building Fed rate-hike expectations ahead of the December 2015 first hike. TLT fell 8.2% over the leg, confirming a pure rate-regime repricing as income investors rotated out of utility dividends into Treasuries. VIX climbed 19→28, but in a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation quad defensives actually fell MORE than cyclicals (-7.1% vs -5.4%), confirming this was rate-driven, not a flight-to-safety.","body_zh":"XLU于2015年1月底见顶（此前受债券牛市驱动），随后下跌15.7%（11个板块中最差）——10年期美债收益率从1月底低点约1.65%飙升约75-100个基点至2.5%，驱动力为美国经济数据走强及对美联储2015年12月首次加息的预期积累。TLT下跌8.2%印证了利率体制的纯粹重定价，收益型投资者将资金从公用事业股息转向国债。VIX从19升至28，但在金发女孩/增长向上-去通胀象限中，防御板块跌幅实际大于周期股（-7.1% vs -5.4%），确认此次下跌为利率驱动而非避险性抛售。","drivers":["rising Treasury yields","Fed rate-hike expectations","bond-proxy repricing","income rotation to Treasuries"],"drivers_zh":["美债收益率上行","美联储加息预期","债券替代品重定价","资金轮入国债"],"prev_key":"2015-01-29","prev_key_chain":["2015-01-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Bond-yield surge reprices the income proxy","title_zh":"债券收益率飙升重定价收益型板块","turn_id":"xlu:peak:2015-01"},"2015-09-04":{"body":"From the September 2015 trough, XLU rallied 49.9% over 26 months, finishing 2nd of 11 sectors, as a yield pullback (TLT +7.6%) and sustained low-rate Fed policy made utility dividends highly competitive against Treasuries. The August 2015 China-sparked equity correction (VIX had spiked to 28) delivered the initial risk-off bid; thereafter the Fed's delayed hiking pace, soft oil, and a weaker dollar (-2.5% DXY) sustained the bond-proxy bid. Even in a reflation/growth-up quad, XLU's stable cash flows and 3-4% dividends attracted income-seeking capital as yields stayed pinned near historic lows through 2016.","body_zh":"自2015年9月低点起，XLU在26个月内上涨49.9%，在11个板块中排名第二——收益率回落（TLT +7.6%）与美联储持续低利率政策使公用事业股息对国债极具竞争力。2015年8月中国引发的股市震荡（VIX曾飙升至28）带来初始避险买盘；此后，美联储加息节奏迟缓、油价低迷、美元走弱（-2.5% DXY）持续支撑债券替代品需求。即便在通胀复苏/增长向上象限中，XLU稳定的现金流与3-4%的股息也在收益率维持历史低位期间（延续至2016年）吸引了大批寻求收益的资本流入。","drivers":["yield pullback / low-rate Fed","dividend competitiveness vs Treasuries","flight-to-safety initial bid","weak dollar tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["收益率回落/低利率美联储","股息竞争力","初始避险买盘","弱美元顺风"],"prev_key":"2015-09-04","prev_key_chain":["2015-09-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Flight-to-safety and yield collapse lift bond proxy","title_zh":"避险买盘与收益率骤降提振债券替代品","turn_id":"xlu:trough:2015-09"},"2017-11-14":{"body":"XLU fell 15.6% (worst sector) from mid-November 2017 through early February 2018 as the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (signed December 22, 2017) accelerated Treasury yields upward — the 10-year rose toward 2.85% — while creating regulatory uncertainty for utilities whose allowed returns and rate-base calculations were disrupted by the cut in the corporate tax rate to 21%. Cyclicals led (Discretionary +8.3%, Financials +4.5%) while defensives were savaged (avg -5.5%), and the Volmageddon VIX spike (the leg's VIX ran 12→33) on February 5, 2018 delivered the final capitulation as correlation-driven risk-off ironically hit the overextended bond proxy.","body_zh":"XLU从2017年11月中旬至2018年2月初下跌15.6%（板块中最差）——《减税与就业法案》（2017年12月22日签署）加速美债收益率上行（10年期升至约2.85%），同时为公用事业带来监管不确定性，因为21%的企业税率削减扰乱了其允许回报率与费率基础计算。周期股领涨（可选消费+8.3%，金融+4.5%），防御板块遭受重创（均值-5.5%），2018年2月5日Volmageddon引发的VIX飙升（本段VIX由12升至33）则构成最后一跌——过度拉伸的债券替代品在相关性驱动的避险抛售中意外受伤。","drivers":["TCJA tax reform uncertainty","Treasury yield surge toward 2.85%","bond-proxy repricing","Volmageddon VIX spike Feb 2018"],"drivers_zh":["税改（TCJA）不确定性","美债收益率飙升至2.85%","债券替代品重定价","Volmageddon VIX冲击"],"prev_key":"2017-11-14","prev_key_chain":["2017-11-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Tax reform and yield surge hit bond proxy hard","title_zh":"税改与收益率飙升重创债券替代品","turn_id":"xlu:peak:2017-11"},"2018-02-08":{"body":"XLU rallied 59.2% from the February 2018 trough through February 2020, finishing #2 of 11 sectors in the longest leg of the series. The slowdown/deflation-scare quad (defensives +39.9% vs cyclicals +23.4%) tells the story: three Fed insurance rate cuts on July 31, September 18, and October 30, 2019 collapsed the 10-year yield (TLT +28.9%), while US-China trade-war uncertainty, global manufacturing contraction, and inverted yield curves drove persistent flight to defensive income. A strong dollar (+10.2% DXY) and falling oil (-14.9%) confirmed the growth-scare regime; with low-vol defensives outpacing high-beta cyclicals by ~25 percentage points, XLU's stable regulated earnings and rising dividend yield attracted capital fleeing volatile cyclicals.","body_zh":"XLU从2018年2月低点至2020年2月涨幅59.2%，11个板块中排名第二，是本系列最长的一段行情。放缓/通缩恐慌象限（防御板块+39.9% vs 周期股+23.4%）说明了一切：2019年7月31日、9月18日、10月30日三次预防式降息使10年期收益率骤降（TLT +28.9%），美中贸易战不确定性、全球制造业萎缩与收益率曲线倒挂驱动持续性的避险防御需求。强美元（+10.2% DXY）与油价下跌（-14.9%）印证了增长恐慌体制；低波动防御股跑赢高贝塔周期股约25个百分点，XLU稳定的受监管盈利与不断上升的股息率吸引了逃离波动性周期股的资金。","drivers":["Fed insurance rate cuts 2019 (Jul/Sep/Oct)","US-China trade war growth scare","10-year yield collapse (TLT +28.9%)","flight-to-defensive income"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年预防式降息（7月/9月/10月）","美中贸易战增长恐慌","10年期收益率骤降（TLT +28.9%）","资金涌入防御性收益资产"],"prev_key":"2018-02-08","prev_key_chain":["2018-02-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot and slowdown-scare fuel 2-year defensive rally","title_zh":"美联储转向与增长恐慌催生两年防御牛市","turn_id":"xlu:trough:2018-02"},"2020-02-18":{"body":"XLU fell 36.1% from February 18 to March 23, 2020 in the COVID pandemic crash. While defensives held up better than cyclicals (defensives avg -29.3% vs cyclicals -39.8%), XLU's loss was still severe because pandemic lockdowns cut US weekday electricity demand by roughly 9-16% across affected regions, directly threatening utility revenues, and many customers sought bill deferrals that complicated near-term cash flows. TLT rose 14.2% (yields fell) but this did not insulate utilities from the broad panic — VIX exploded 15→62, credit spreads blew out (HYG vs LQD -9.4%), and even the bond proxy's income appeal could not offset genuine demand-destruction fears.","body_zh":"XLU从2020年2月18日至3月23日下跌36.1%——即新冠疫情大崩盘。虽然防御板块表现优于周期股（防御均值-29.3% vs 周期-39.8%），XLU仍受重创，因为疫情封锁导致受影响地区工作日电力需求下降约9-16%，直接威胁公用事业收入；同时大量客户申请延迟缴费，使近期现金流更趋复杂。TLT上涨14.2%（收益率下行）但未能保护公用事业——VIX从15暴涨至62，信用利差扩大（HYG vs LQD -9.4%），即便债券替代品的收益吸引力也无法抵挡真实需求破坏的恐慌。","drivers":["COVID pandemic demand shock","electricity demand collapse (~10%)","VIX panic 15→62","broad risk-off liquidation"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情需求冲击","电力需求萎缩（约10%）","VIX恐慌15→62","全面避险抛售"],"prev_key":"2020-02-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-18"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash: demand shock overwhelms defensive shelter","title_zh":"新冠崩盘：需求冲击压倒防御庇护","turn_id":"xlu:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"XLU rallied 82.3% from the March 2020 trough to April 2022 but ranked 9th of 11 sectors — it was starved, not celebrated. A massive reflation/growth-up recovery (cyclicals +145.4% vs defensives +83.3%) driven by fiscal stimulus (CARES Act, American Rescue Plan), vaccine-led reopening, and surging commodities (Energy +272%, Materials +139%) meant capital chased high-beta cyclicals, not steady utility dividends. Rising yields (TLT -22.2%) were a headwind for the bond proxy; XLU's gain was carried by the rising tide of unlimited-QE-era liquidity (broad breadth, equal-weight +19.0% over cap-weight) and a weaker dollar (-2.6% DXY), with the sector's participation structurally capped by the reflation quad.","body_zh":"XLU从2020年3月低点至2022年4月累计上涨82.3%，但在11个板块中仅排名第9——属于被动参与而非领跑。财政刺激（CARES法案、美国救援计划）、疫苗驱动的经济重开与大宗商品价格飙升（能源+272%、材料+139%）催生了庞大的再通胀/增长复苏行情（周期股+145.4% vs 防御板块+83.3%），资金涌向高贝塔周期股而非稳定的公用事业股息。收益率上行（TLT -22.2%）对债券替代品构成阻力；XLU的涨幅依赖无限量宽松时代流动性的抬升效应（市场广度宽广，等权重跑赢市值加权+19.0%）与弱美元（-2.6% DXY），再通胀象限从结构上封顶了板块的表现空间。","drivers":["pandemic reflation / fiscal stimulus","cyclical rotation away from defensives","rising yields headwind (TLT -22.2%)","commodity/energy-led recovery"],"drivers_zh":["疫情再通胀/财政刺激","周期股轮动抽离防御股","收益率上行阻力（TLT -22.2%）","大宗商品/能源引领复苏"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Pandemic reflation starves low-vol defensives","title_zh":"疫情复苏再通胀使低波动防御股失色","turn_id":"xlu:trough:2020-03"},"2022-04-08":{"body":"Utilities are classic bond proxies, so the Fed's hiking campaign and surging Treasury yields (TLT -10.1%) repriced the rate-sensitive sector's multiples in the spring 2022 stagflation drawdown — a strong dollar (+4.9% DXY) compounded the macro pressure. XLU still cushioned the broad rout (-16% vs SPY -18%), but it slightly underperformed the defensive cohort (-15.7% vs defensives -14.8%) as VIX ran 21→31, since rising bond yields stripped the income proxy of its dividend edge into the mid-June low.","body_zh":"公用事业是经典的债券替代品，因此美联储加息与飙升的美债收益率（TLT -10.1%）在2022年春季滞胀回调中重新定价了这一利率敏感板块的估值倍数——强美元（+4.9% DXY）加剧了宏观压力。XLU仍缓冲了大盘抛售（-16% vs SPY -18%），但略逊于整体防御板块（-15.7% vs 防御板块 -14.8%），在VIX走高21→31之际，上行的债券收益率剥夺了这一收益替代品的股息优势，直至6月中旬低点。","drivers":["rate regime","bond-proxy repricing","strong dollar","stagflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["利率体制","债券替代品重定价","强美元","滞胀象限"],"prev_key":"2022-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-regime selloff hits the bond proxy","title_zh":"利率体制抛售冲击债券替代品","turn_id":"xlu:peak:2022-04"},"2022-06-17":{"body":"As recession fears mounted in summer 2022, defensives edged out cyclicals (+13.4% vs +13.1%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad, and utilities rallied ~21% (#2 of 11) on steady cash flows and dividends. With oil collapsing -19.9% and VIX easing 31→24, the flight-to-safety bid plus a brief lull in yields lifted the bond proxy into its mid-September peak — defensive demand, not a yield tailwind (TLT still -3.6%).","body_zh":"随着2022年夏季衰退担忧升温，在放缓/通缩恐慌象限中防御板块微幅跑赢周期股（+13.4% vs +13.1%），公用事业凭借稳定现金流与股息上涨约21%（11个板块中排名第2）。油价暴跌 -19.9%、VIX回落31→24，避险买盘叠加收益率短暂回落，将债券替代品推升至9月中旬峰值——靠的是防御需求，而非收益率顺风（TLT仍 -3.6%）。","drivers":["flight-to-safety","defensive safe-haven","growth scare quad","yield lull"],"drivers_zh":["避险","防御避险","增长恐慌象限","收益率回落"],"prev_key":"2022-06-17","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-17"],"status":"exact","title":"Defensive safe-haven rally as growth scare bites","title_zh":"增长恐慌中的防御避险反弹","turn_id":"xlu:trough:2022-06"},"2022-09-12":{"body":"A sharp rate-regime surge in Treasury yields past 4% into early October (TLT -6.4%) repriced the bond proxy violently — with safe bond yields topping utility dividend yields and a strong dollar (+4.6% DXY) tightening conditions, income investors rotated away. XLU fell ~21% in a month (#10 of 11), a deeper loss than even broad defensives (-12%), in a textbook rate-sensitive selloff as VIX spiked 24→34.","body_zh":"美债收益率在10月初前急升突破4%（TLT -6.4%）的利率体制冲击，对债券替代品进行了剧烈重新定价——当无风险债券收益率超过公用事业股息收益率、强美元（+4.6% DXY）收紧条件，收益型投资者纷纷转向。XLU一个月内下跌约21%（11个板块中排名第10），跌幅甚至超过整体防御板块（-12%），在VIX飙升24→34之际上演教科书式的利率敏感型抛售。","drivers":["rate regime","10Y yield >4%","bond-proxy repricing","strong dollar"],"drivers_zh":["利率体制","10年期收益率>4%","债券替代品重定价","强美元"],"prev_key":"2022-09-12","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Yield spike past 4% crushes the bond proxy","title_zh":"收益率破4%飙升重创债券替代品","turn_id":"xlu:peak:2022-09"},"2022-10-12":{"body":"When yields reversed lower off their October peak (TLT +7.8%) and the dollar rolled over (-8.2% DXY), the bond proxy bounced ~18% (#3 of 11) off the 2022 low. Defensives led cyclicals (+15.4% vs +13.4%) with broadening breadth (equal-weight +2.2% over cap-weight) and VIX collapsing 34→23 — the move tracked the inverse path of the 10-year yield, confirming the sector's rate-driven character.","body_zh":"当收益率从10月峰值反转下行（TLT +7.8%）、美元走软（-8.2% DXY）时，债券替代品自2022年低点反弹约18%（11个板块中排名第3）。防御板块领先周期股（+15.4% vs +13.4%），市场广度走宽（等权重跑赢市值加权 +2.2%），VIX骤降34→23——走势与10年期收益率呈反向路径，印证了该板块的利率驱动属性。","drivers":["rate regime","yield pullback","weaker dollar","broadening breadth"],"drivers_zh":["利率体制","收益率回落","美元走弱","市场广度走宽"],"prev_key":"2022-10-12","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-relief bounce on falling yields and weaker dollar","title_zh":"收益率回落、美元走弱下的利率缓和反弹","turn_id":"xlu:trough:2022-10"},"2022-12-13":{"body":"Utilities was not broken through 2023 — it was starved as a tech/semis-led melt-up (SMH +29.9%, growth over value +19.9, VIX 23→18) rotated money out of low-vol defensives, even as higher-for-longer rates (TLT -17.1%) and a stronger dollar piled on. With breadth narrow (equal-weight lagging cap-weight by -11.1%) and cash/bonds offering competitive yields, XLU drifted down ~20% (worst of 11) to a bottom in early October 2023 as the 10-year yield peaked near cycle highs around 5%.","body_zh":"整个2023年公用事业并未走坏——而是在科技/半导体引领的逼空行情（SMH +29.9%、成长跑赢价值 +19.9、VIX 23→18）将资金从低波动防御板块抽离时被冷落，叠加利率居高不下（TLT -17.1%）与走强的美元雪上加霜。市场广度狭窄（等权重落后市值加权 -11.1%），现金和债券提供有竞争力的收益率，XLU震荡下行约20%（11个板块中最差），在2023年10月初10年期收益率逼近周期高点约5%时见底。","drivers":["starved by tech-led risk-on","narrow breadth","higher-for-longer rates","bond competition"],"drivers_zh":["被科技引领风险偏好冷落","市场广度狭窄","更高更久利率","债券竞争"],"prev_key":"2022-12-13","prev_key_chain":["2022-12-13"],"status":"exact","title":"Starved by the 2023 AI risk-on, not broken","title_zh":"被2023年AI风险偏好冷落，而非走坏","turn_id":"xlu:peak:2022-12"},"2023-10-02":{"body":"From the October 2023 low, utilities staged a historic re-rating (#3 of 11, ~82%) as the AI-datacenter electricity-demand super-cycle reframed the sector from sleepy bond proxy to a structural growth story — power names (Vistra, Constellation, NextEra) led as hyperscaler load forecasts surged after years of flat demand. A goldilocks quad with falling yields (TLT +15.2%) and a weaker dollar (-8.7% DXY) gave the bond proxy a tailwind, letting defensives nearly keep pace with cyclicals (50.5% vs 57.1%) even as a narrow, semis-led tape (SMH +181.7%, equal-weight -13.4% behind cap-weight) dominated the index into the February 2026 peak.","body_zh":"自2023年10月低点起，公用事业上演历史性重估（11个板块中排名第3，约 +82%），AI数据中心电力需求超级周期将板块从沉闷的债券替代品重塑为结构性增长故事——电力公司（Vistra、Constellation、NextEra）领涨，超大规模厂商在多年需求平淡后负荷预测大幅上调。金发女孩象限下收益率回落（TLT +15.2%）、美元走弱（-8.7% DXY）为债券替代品提供顺风，使防御板块几乎追平周期股（50.5% vs 57.1%），尽管狭窄的、半导体引领的行情（SMH +181.7%、等权重落后市值加权 -13.4%）主导着指数，直至2026年2月峰值。","drivers":["AI-datacenter power demand","electricity super-cycle","rate tailwind / weaker dollar","Vistra/Constellation/NextEra"],"drivers_zh":["AI数据中心电力需求","电力超级周期","利率顺风/美元走弱","Vistra/Constellation/NextEra"],"prev_key":"2023-10-02","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-02"],"status":"exact","title":"AI-datacenter power super-cycle re-rating","title_zh":"AI数据中心电力超级周期重估","turn_id":"xlu:trough:2023-10"}},"now":"BOTTOMING (RS #9, pos 11.2%) — Utilities is being starved rather than broken: a tech/semis-led melt-up (SMH +67.9%, high-beta over low-vol +20.7%) is pulling capital out of low-vol defensives even as XLU still grinds +8.5% YTD. A strong dollar (+3.4% DXY) and a flat-to-firm rate backdrop (TLT only +1.1%) cap the bond proxy's re-rating room. The reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%; oil +19.2%) has not destroyed XLU — broadening breadth (equal-weight +2.9% over cap-weight) and the structural AI-datacenter electricity-demand thesis underpin a base. With VIX benign (14→18), any rotation off the narrow mega-cap tape or a yield rollover would trigger the next defensive re-rating leg.","now_zh":"触底中（RS排名第9，位置11.2%）——公用事业是被冷落而非走坏：科技/半导体引领的逼空行情（SMH +67.9%，高贝塔跑赢低波动 +20.7%）正将资金从低波动防御板块抽离，尽管XLU年初至今仍上涨+8.5%。强美元（+3.4% DXY）与企稳偏紧的利率环境（TLT仅+1.1%）压制着债券替代品的重估空间。通胀复苏/增长向上象限（周期股+11.2% vs 防御板块+6.9%；油价+19.2%）并未摧毁XLU——市场广度走宽（等权重跑赢市值加权+2.9%）与AI数据中心电力需求的结构性叙事构筑底部支撑。VIX仍温和（14→18），一旦狭窄的大盘股行情出现轮动或收益率回落，料将触发板块下一波防御性重估行情。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"xlv":{"legs":{"2011-08-10":{"body":"XLV surged 176% from the August 2011 debt-ceiling crash trough to July 2015 — the best sector return of the period, beating SPY by +71 percentage points. Three forces combined: the Affordable Care Act coverage expansion added roughly 20 million newly insured Americans, turbocharging managed care (UNH, Anthem) and hospital system (HCA, Tenet) earnings on higher patient volumes; a biotech super-cycle launched on next-generation sequencing cost collapse, record FDA approval rates, and oncology precision-medicine breakthroughs (the IBB biotech ETF roughly tripled in this window); and the macro backdrop was a falling-rate (TLT +21%), dollar-strengthening slowdown environment where defensives outpaced cyclicals (112.6% vs 92.7%), VIX compressed from 43 to 12, and quality compounded uninterrupted for nearly four years.","body_zh":"XLV自2011年8月债务上限危机低点至2015年7月累计上涨176%，为同期最佳板块，跑赢SPY约71个百分点。三股力量叠加：《平价医疗法案》（ACA）覆盖扩展新增约2000万参保人，大幅提升管理式医疗（UNH、安泰）和医院系统（HCA、Tenet）盈利；次世代基因测序成本暴跌、FDA审批创纪录、肿瘤精准医疗突破共同引爆生物科技超级周期（IBB生物科技ETF在此窗口约三倍涨幅）；宏观背景为利率下行（TLT +21%）、美元强势的放缓环境，防御股跑赢周期股（112.6% vs 92.7%），VIX从43压缩至12，优质资产近四年持续复利。","drivers":["ACA insured expansion","biotech super-cycle","falling rates","managed care earnings boom","precision medicine"],"drivers_zh":["ACA扩大参保","生物科技超级周期","利率下行","管理式医疗盈利爆发","精准医疗"],"prev_key":"2011-08-10","prev_key_chain":["2011-08-10"],"status":"exact","title":"ACA expansion and biotech super-cycle launch","title_zh":"ACA扩大参保与生物科技超级周期启动","turn_id":"xlv:trough:2011-08"},"2015-07-20":{"body":"XLV fell 16.4% in ten weeks — its worst near-term selloff of the cycle — driven by two distinct shocks. First, China's August 11 yuan devaluation triggered a global risk-off cascade (VIX 12 to 28, SPY -11%), hitting late-cycle high-valued healthcare names hard. Second, on September 21 Hillary Clinton tweeted about drug 'price gouging' after Turing Pharmaceuticals raised Daraprim by thousands of percent, sending the IBB biotech ETF down nearly 5% that session and XLV to a deeper loss than most peers (-16.4%, near the bottom of the table vs a defensives average of -7.7%). The combined macro selloff plus sector-specific pricing-policy fear ranked health care among the worst sectors of the leg.","body_zh":"XLV在十周内下跌16.4%，为该周期内最大短期回调，由两股冲击驱动。首先，中国8月11日人民币贬值引发全球风险厌恶级联反应（VIX从12升至28，SPY -11%），重创高估值的医疗保健后期标的。其次，9月21日希拉里·克林顿针对Turing制药将Daraprim大幅涨价数千个百分点而发推炮轰药品'价格掠夺'，当日IBB生物科技ETF暴跌近5%，令XLV跌幅深于多数同类板块（-16.4%，处于排名榜尾部，对比防御股均值-7.7%）。宏观抛售叠加板块特异性药价政策恐慌，使医疗保健成为该腿表现最差的板块之一。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation","risk-off cascade","Clinton drug-pricing tweet","biotech de-rating","VIX spike"],"drivers_zh":["人民币贬值冲击","风险厌恶级联","克林顿药价推文","生物科技杀估值","VIX骤升"],"prev_key":"2015-07-20","prev_key_chain":["2015-07-20"],"status":"exact","title":"China shock and Clinton drug-pricing tweet","title_zh":"中国冲击与克林顿药价推文","turn_id":"xlv:peak:2015-07"},"2016-02-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"xlv:trough:2016-02"},"2018-11-30":{"body":"In a compressed 24-day crash, XLV dropped 15.4% as the entire market repriced for a policy mistake. The Fed's December 19 rate hike — the fourth of 2018 — paired with Chair Powell's hawkish press conference signaling autopilot balance sheet runoff sent VIX from 18 to 36 and SPY down 14.5%. Health care held up modestly better than cyclicals (defensives avg -11.5% vs cyclicals -15.5%), ranking #8/11. The concurrent selloff in energy (-17.8%) and financials (-16.8%) confirmed a broad growth-scare panic, with TLT +5.7% and oil crashing -16.5% confirming the deflation-inflection fear.","body_zh":"在短短24天的暴跌中，XLV下跌15.4%，整个市场为政策失误重新定价。美联储12月19日第四次加息叠加鲍威尔鹰派新闻发布会（暗示自动驾驶式缩表），令VIX从18升至36，SPY下跌14.5%。医疗保健跌幅略好于周期股（防御股均值-11.5% vs 周期股-15.5%），排名第8/11。能源（-17.8%）与金融（-16.8%）同步暴跌确认了广泛的增长恐慌，TLT +5.7%、油价崩跌-16.5%印证了市场对通缩转折的担忧。","drivers":["Fed December rate hike","Powell hawkish presser","growth scare panic","VIX spike","oil crash"],"drivers_zh":["美联储12月加息","鲍威尔鹰派表态","增长恐慌","VIX骤升","油价暴跌"],"prev_key":"2018-11-30","prev_key_chain":["2018-11-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed rate hike panic and growth scare selloff","title_zh":"美联储加息恐慌与增长担忧式抛售","turn_id":"xlv:peak:2018-11"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"XLV gained 32.8% from Christmas Eve 2018 to January 2020 but finished dead last among sectors (#9/11) in a reflation tape where tech (+71%), communications (+47%), and financials (+41%) dominated. The Fed pivoted sharply — cutting rates three times in 2019 — supporting the broad market (SPY +44%) but creating a cross-current for healthcare: falling rates are a mild tailwind for defensive quality, but the rising prominence of Bernie Sanders' Medicare-for-All proposals hammered managed care stocks throughout 2019 (XLV was roughly flat YTD into April 2019 while SPY was up double digits, a divergence traders attributed squarely to Medicare-for-All fears). This idiosyncratic policy discount kept health care as the worst-performing defensive sector despite the supportive macro.","body_zh":"XLV自2018年圣诞夜至2020年1月上涨32.8%，但在科技（+71%）、通信（+47%）、金融（+41%）主导的再通胀行情中排名全板块垫底（第9/11）。美联储2019年大幅转向——全年三次降息——支撑了大盘（SPY +44%），但对医疗保健形成双向拉锯：利率下行对防御性优质资产有温和顺风，但桑德斯全民医保方案（Medicare for All）的曝光度不断提升贯穿2019年全年重压管理式医疗——至2019年4月XLV年内回报接近零而SPY已涨两位数，交易员将这一背离直接归因于全民医保恐慌。这一特异性政策折价令医疗保健成为宏观顺风期间表现最差的防御板块。","drivers":["Fed pivot rate cuts","Medicare for All fear","tech-led risk-on starved defensives","managed care policy discount","primary election uncertainty"],"drivers_zh":["美联储转向降息","全民医保恐慌","科技主导令防御资金匮乏","管理式医疗政策折价","大选初选不确定性"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot relief but Medicare-for-All drag","title_zh":"美联储转向带来喘息但全民医保拖累","turn_id":"xlv:trough:2018-12"},"2020-01-22":{"body":"XLV plunged 28.4% from its January 22 peak to the March 23 trough — one of the three least-bad sectors in a catastrophic broad selloff (defensives avg -28.3% vs cyclicals -39.3%; energy -58%, financials -42%). The driver was the COVID-19 pandemic: WHO declared a global health emergency January 30, U.S. markets began their plunge in late February as the Italian outbreak escalated, and VIX exploded from 13 to 62. Paradoxically, hospitals and healthcare providers faced catastrophic revenue collapses from the suspension of elective procedures (HCA admissions fell sharply in the final weeks of March), meaning XLV did not benefit from pandemic demand despite the medical crisis and held up only through the classic defensive flight-to-safety (TLT +19%, dollar +5%).","body_zh":"XLV自1月22日峰值至3月23日低点下跌28.4%，在整体惨烈的大跌中是三个跌幅最小的板块之一（防御股均值-28.3% vs 周期股-39.3%；能源-58%，金融-42%）。驱动因素为新冠疫情：WHO于1月30日宣布全球卫生紧急事件，意大利疫情升级后美国市场于2月下旬开始暴跌，VIX从13爆升至62。吊诡的是，医院和医疗服务提供商因暂停择期手术而遭遇营收灾难性坍塌（HCA在3月最后几周住院量大幅下降），意味着XLV并未从疫情需求中获益，仅凭典型的防御性避险轮动（TLT +19%，美元+5%）相对抵御了跌势。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic","WHO emergency declaration","VIX explosion","elective procedure shutdown","flight to safety"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情","WHO宣布全球卫生紧急状态","VIX爆升","择期手术暂停","避险资金流入"],"prev_key":"2020-01-22","prev_key_chain":["2020-01-22"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID-19 pandemic crash, elective procedure collapse","title_zh":"新冠疫情冲击与择期手术暂停","turn_id":"xlv:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"XLV gained 97% from the March 2020 trough to April 2022 but ranked a disappointing #8/11 in a roaring cyclical recovery. The massive fiscal stimulus (CARES Act $2.2T, ARP $1.9T), Fed QE, and vaccine rollout (Pfizer/Moderna authorized November-December 2020) unleashed a reflationary boom: energy (+272%), materials (+139%), financials (+123%), and industrials led. Health care was starved by a quad that favored high-beta cyclicals (high-beta minus low-vol +113, VIX 62 to 21) while TLT fell 22% and rising real rates hurt the bond-proxy defensive. Vaccine makers (Moderna revenue grew from ~$800M in 2020 to ~$18.5B in 2021) were stars within the sector but too small to lift XLV's massive managed-care and pharma weight.","body_zh":"XLV自2020年3月低点至2022年4月上涨97%，但在强劲的周期性复苏中仅排名令人失望的第8/11。大规模财政刺激（CARES法案2.2万亿、美国救援计划1.9万亿）、美联储QE及疫苗推出（辉瑞/莫德纳2020年11-12月获批）共同引爆再通胀繁荣：能源（+272%）、材料（+139%）、金融（+123%）与工业领跑。医疗保健被高贝塔周期股主导的象限所冷落（高贝塔减低波动+113，VIX从62降至21），而TLT下跌22%，实际利率上行打压防御性债券替代品。疫苗制造商（莫德纳营收从2020年约8亿增至2021年约185亿美元）虽是板块内明星，但体量不足以托起XLV庞大的管理式医疗和制药板块。","drivers":["fiscal stimulus boom","vaccine recovery trade","cyclical rotation","rising rates hurt bond proxy","high-beta over low-vol leadership"],"drivers_zh":["财政刺激爆发","疫苗复苏交易","周期性轮动","利率上行压制债券替代品","高贝塔主导"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Vaccine-led recovery, cyclical rotation starves healthcare","title_zh":"疫苗主导的复苏；周期性轮动令医疗保健资金匮乏","turn_id":"xlv:trough:2020-03"},"2022-04-08":{"body":"A rate-regime selloff: the Fed's aggressive 2022 hiking cycle and the June 9.1% CPI shock sent yields surging (TLT -10.1%) and the dollar +4.9% (DXY), crushing long-duration health care — biotech (XBI) sank to multi-year lows as rising real rates discounted distant cash flows. In a stagflation-ish quad, large-cap pharma and devices cushioned XLV (-16% vs cyclicals -16.3%, ranking #6/11), but quality could not fully offset the duration hit.","body_zh":"一轮利率体制驱动的抛售：美联储2022年激进的加息周期与6月9.1%的CPI冲击推动收益率飙升（TLT -10.1%）、美元+4.9%（DXY），重创长久期医疗保健——生物科技（XBI）跌至多年低位，因实际利率上升对远期现金流贴现折让。在偏滞胀的象限中，大型制药/器械相对缓冲了XLV（-16%，对比周期股 -16.3%，排名第6/11），但优质属性仍无法完全抵消久期冲击。","drivers":["rate regime","Fed rate hikes","9.1% CPI shock","biotech de-rating"],"drivers_zh":["利率体制","美联储加息","9.1% CPI冲击","生物科技杀估值"],"prev_key":"2022-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-regime de-rating hits biotech","title_zh":"利率体制杀估值冲击生物科技","turn_id":"xlv:peak:2022-04"},"2022-06-17":{"body":"Off the June 2022 low, health care first caught a defensive safe-haven bid (VIX 31 to 17) and re-rated on the GLP-1 obesity-drug super-cycle — Eli Lilly (whose tirzepatide won FDA obesity approval as Zepbound in November 2023) and Novo Nordisk drove leadership. But as the tech and semis melt-up took over (SMH +131%, growth minus value +36, narrow mega-cap breadth -18.7%), XLV was starved: nothing broke, money simply rotated to tech in a goldilocks quad, leaving it +36% but only #6/11.","body_zh":"自2022年6月低点起，医疗保健先获得防御避险买盘（VIX 31降至17），随后凭借GLP-1/减肥药超级周期重估——礼来（其替尔泊肽以Zepbound之名于2023年11月获FDA批准用于肥胖症）与诺和诺德引领涨势。但当科技/半导体的逼空式上涨接管行情后（SMH +131%、成长减价值 +36、狭窄大盘广度 -18.7%），XLV遭冷落：板块本身并未出问题，只是在金发女孩象限中资金转向科技，令其虽涨约36%却仅排名第6/11。","drivers":["defensives starved","tech-led risk-on","GLP-1 obesity drugs","narrow breadth"],"drivers_zh":["防御被冷落","科技主导风险偏好","GLP-1减肥药","市场广度狭窄"],"prev_key":"2022-06-17","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-17"],"status":"exact","title":"Defensive bid, then starved by the AI melt-up","title_zh":"防御买盘，随后被AI逼空式上涨冷落","turn_id":"xlv:trough:2022-06"},"2024-09-16":{"body":"This was not a market selloff — SPY rose +5.4% and cyclicals +6.1% — XLV alone got hit, ending the single worst sector (-17%, #11/11) as election and policy risk crystallized: RFK Jr. nominated to HHS, the looming Most-Favored-Nation drug-pricing threat (formalized by executive order on May 12, 2025), and threatened pharma tariffs pushed pharma valuations to historic lows. With yields surging (TLT -13.4%) and a narrow goldilocks tape rotating into Comm/Financials/Discretionary leaders, GLP-1 enthusiasm cooled on pricing and competition fears.","body_zh":"这并非大盘抛售——SPY上涨+5.4%、周期股+6.1%——唯独XLV遭重创，成为表现最差板块（-17%，第11/11），因选举/政策风险落地：小罗伯特·肯尼迪获提名执掌HHS、最惠国(MFN)药品定价威胁逼近（于2025年5月12日以行政令形式落地）以及医药关税威胁，将制药估值压至历史低位。在收益率飙升（TLT -13.4%）、狭窄的金发女孩行情转向通信/金融/可选消费龙头之际，GLP-1热情在定价/竞争担忧下降温。","drivers":["idiosyncratic selloff","MFN drug pricing","RFK Jr. / MAHA","rate regime"],"drivers_zh":["个股独立抛售","MFN药品定价","小罗伯特·肯尼迪/MAHA","利率体制"],"prev_key":"2024-09-16","prev_key_chain":["2024-09-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Policy hit while the tape rallied without it","title_zh":"政策独立打击，而大盘无此板块照样上涨","turn_id":"xlv:peak:2024-09"},"2025-05-14":{"body":"From the post-tariff washout, XLV rallied ~27% to #4/11 — but not on a flight-to-safety: this was a risk-on, cyclical-led reflation tape (cyclicals +25.6% vs defensives +18.7%, high-beta over low-vol +60, semis +147%). Health care's own tailwinds carried it: yields fell (TLT +7.5%), a boost for the bond-proxy quality defensive, while cheap post-selloff valuations and value beating growth (growth minus value -12.2) rewarded the rotation into cheap quality; clarity on drug-pricing arrived as 14 of the 17 largest manufacturers signed MFN agreements between September and December 2025 (announced en masse on December 19, 2025), stripping out tail risk; and a higher-than-proposed 2027 Medicare Advantage rate (~2.5%, finalized April 2026) combined with softening utilization drove June 2026 analyst upgrades across UNH, HUM, and CI.","body_zh":"自关税后的洗盘中，XLV反弹约27%至第4/11——但这并非避险买盘：当时是风险偏好、周期股领涨的再通胀行情（周期股 +25.6% 对比防御股 +18.7%、高贝塔减低波动 +60、半导体 +147%）。推动它的是医疗保健自身的顺风：收益率下行（TLT +7.5%），利好这一债券替代品类优质防御资产；关税抛售后的低估值、价值跑赢成长（成长减价值 -12.2）奖励了向低估值优质资产的轮动；药品定价明朗化随17家最大制造商中的14家于2025年9月至12月间签署MFN协议而落地（12月19日集中宣布），消除了尾部风险；加之高于提案的2027年Medicare Advantage费率（约2.5%，2026年4月最终确定）及医疗利用率下行趋势，推动2026年6月分析师相继上调UNH、HUM与CI评级。","drivers":["rate tailwind","cheap-quality rerating","value over growth","pricing-deal clarity"],"drivers_zh":["利率顺风","低估值优质资产重估","价值跑赢成长","定价协议明朗"],"prev_key":"2025-05-14","prev_key_chain":["2025-05-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate tailwind plus cheap-quality rerating","title_zh":"利率顺风加低估值优质资产重估","turn_id":"xlv:trough:2025-05"}},"now":"EXPANDING (RS #4 on the leg, #8/11 on the latest tape) — XLV is in the early-to-mid phase of a rally leg off the May 2025 tariff/policy washout low, up ~27% over the leg but currently lagging the freshest move (+3.3%, ranked #8/11) as a 2026 semis/AI melt-up dominates (SMH +68% on the recent window, high-beta over low-vol +21%). The macro quad is reflation/growth-up (cyclicals beating defensives), a regime that historically starves defensives. Yet XLV is holding above its 200-day and quietly improving relative traction: value is beating growth (growth minus value -15.2), broadening participation (equal-weight +2.9% over cap-weight) is leaking flows out of the narrow mega-cap tape, and managed care (UNH, HUM, CI) is catching a fresh bid on softening medical-cost trends (BofA upgraded UNH to Buy on June 4, 2026). Drug-pricing tail risk has largely cleared via the MFN manufacturer agreements struck from September through December 2025, stripping the binary policy overhang that crushed the sector in 2024-25. The setup is cheap-quality defensive rotation beginning to assert itself as the narrow tech tape shows early topping signals.","now_zh":"扩张阶段（当前反弹腿相对强度第4，最新行情中第8/11）——XLV正处于自2025年5月关税/政策洗盘低点以来当前反弹腿的早中期，整段涨幅约27%，但在最新一段行情中暂时落后（+3.3%，排名第8/11），因2026年半导体/AI逼空式上涨主导（近窗口SMH +68%、高贝塔减低波动+21%）。宏观象限为再通胀/经济向好（周期股跑赢防御股），该格局历史上往往令防御板块资金匮乏。但XLV正站稳200日均线上方并悄然改善相对强度：价值跑赢成长（成长减价值-15.2），市场广度扩散（等权重较市值加权+2.9%）令资金从窄幅大盘行情中外溢，管理式医疗（UNH、HUM、CI）受医疗成本趋势放缓提振获新买盘（美银于2026年6月4日将UNH上调至买入）。2025年9月至12月间陆续达成的MFN制造商协议已基本消除药品定价尾部风险，剥离了2024-25年打压板块的二元政策悬顶。整体格局是：随着窄幅科技行情出现早期见顶迹象，低估值优质防御资产的轮动开始显现。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"xly":{"legs":{"2011-07-07":{"body":"The US hit its statutory debt ceiling in May 2011, and congressional brinkmanship culminated in S&P's August 5 downgrade of US sovereign debt to AA+, triggering a global risk-off shock amplified by European sovereign debt contagion (Italian and Spanish bond spreads surging to crisis levels). VIX exploded 16 to 45 and Treasuries surged (TLT +32.8%) in a classic flight-to-safety rotation: defensives fell only -7.9% while cyclicals cratered -23.4%, confirming this was macro-driven panic, not sector fundamentals. XLY's credit-sensitive, big-ticket names — autos, homebuilders, home improvement, restaurants — fell a middling -18.4% (#5 of 11), with a stronger dollar (+6.0% DXY) and collapsing oil (-21.3%) and copper/gold (-37.4%) signaling a sharp global growth scare.","body_zh":"美国于2011年5月触及法定债务上限，国会的边缘政策最终以标普8月5日将美国主权信用评级下调至AA+告终，引发全球性风险规避冲击，欧洲主权债务危机蔓延（意大利/西班牙债券利差飙升至危机水平）进一步放大了恐慌情绪。VIX从16飙升至45，美债大涨（TLT +32.8%），呈现经典的避险轮动：防御板块仅下跌-7.9%，而周期板块暴跌-23.4%，证实这是宏观驱动的恐慌而非板块基本面问题。XLY中信用敏感的大额消费品类——汽车、房屋建筑商、家装、餐厅——下跌-18.4%，居中游（11个板块中第5位），美元走强（DXY +6.0%）、油价暴跌（-21.3%）及铜金比暴跌（-37.4%）共同发出全球增长急剧放缓的信号。","drivers":["flight-to-safety","US debt-ceiling / S&P downgrade","European sovereign debt crisis","VIX shock 16-to-45"],"drivers_zh":["避险","美国债务上限/标普下调评级","欧洲主权债务危机","VIX冲击16至45"],"prev_key":"2011-07-07","prev_key_chain":["2011-07-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Debt-ceiling crisis and S&P downgrade rout cyclicals","title_zh":"债务上限危机与标普下调评级重创周期板块","turn_id":"xly:peak:2011-07"},"2011-10-03":{"body":"The October 2011 trough marked the start of a secular 4+ year bull run that made XLY the top-performing sector (+156.4%, ranked #1 of 11), driven by the Fed's Operation Twist and then QE3 (September 2012) holding rates low, a recovering US housing market, and the explosive structural growth of Amazon, Netflix and online retail reshaping the sector's earnings power. The goldilocks quad (oil -44.5%, dollar +25.6% DXY, disinflation) kept real consumer purchasing power robust, while falling mortgage rates ignited a housing recovery that boosted homebuilders and home improvement retailers (Home Depot, Lowe's). VIX compressed from 45 to 15 as the European crisis faded, credit outperformed (HY beat IG +10.2%), and broad market breadth (RSP +4.3% vs SPY) confirmed wide participation in the expansion.","body_zh":"2011年10月触底标志着一轮超过4年的长期牛市启动，使XLY成为表现最佳的板块（+156.4%，11个板块中排名第1），驱动力来自美联储扭转操作及随后的QE3（2012年9月）将利率维持在低位、美国房地产市场复苏，以及亚马逊、奈飞和在线零售的爆炸式结构性增长重塑了板块盈利能力。金发女孩象限（油价-44.5%，美元+25.6%，去通胀）保持了强劲的消费者实际购买力，而抵押贷款利率下降点燃了房市复苏，推动房屋建筑商和家装零售商（家得宝、劳氏）上涨。随着欧洲危机消退，VIX从45压缩至15，信用债跑赢（高收益债跑赢投资级+10.2%），市场广度扩大（RSP跑赢SPY +4.3%）印证了扩张期的广泛参与。","drivers":["Fed Operation Twist/QE3 / low rates","Amazon/e-commerce secular growth","US housing recovery","goldilocks disinflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["美联储扭转操作/QE3/低利率","亚马逊/电商结构性增长","美国房地产复苏","金发女孩去通胀象限"],"prev_key":"2011-10-03","prev_key_chain":["2011-10-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Four-year goldilocks bull: e-commerce dominance drives XLY","title_zh":"四年金发女孩牛市：电商主导推动XLY登顶","turn_id":"xly:trough:2011-10"},"2015-11-25":{"body":"Three forces converged to end the four-year bull run: China's stock market crash and currency devaluation (August 2015 CNY fix shock) signaled a global growth scare; Brent crude plunged -39.1% from already-depressed levels on OPEC's refusal to cut and US shale supply glut; and the Fed delivered its first rate hike in nine years on December 16, 2015, raising credit costs for auto and housing. VIX rose 15 to 28 and defensives outperformed sharply (-1.1% vs cyclicals -15.3%), confirming a risk-off flight-to-safety: XLY fell -15.8% (#8 of 11), the least-bad of the three worst cyclical performers, as high-ticket auto, homebuilder and retail names repriced lower.","body_zh":"三股力量汇聚终结了四年牛市：中国股市暴跌和人民币贬值（2015年8月汇改冲击）发出全球增长警示；布伦特原油在OPEC拒绝减产和美国页岩油供应过剩背景下从已经低迷的水平再跌-39.1%；美联储于2015年12月16日实施九年来首次加息，抬高了汽车和住房的信贷成本。VIX从15升至28，防御板块大幅跑赢（-1.1%，对比周期板块-15.3%），确认了风险规避的避险轮动：XLY下跌-15.8%（11个板块中第8位），是表现最差的三只周期板块中相对抗跌的一只，高价汽车、房屋建筑商和零售股估值下修。","drivers":["China slowdown / CNY devaluation","oil crash / OPEC oversupply","first Fed rate hike Dec 2015","flight-to-safety"],"drivers_zh":["中国放缓/人民币贬值","油价崩盘/OPEC供应过剩","美联储2015年12月首次加息","避险"],"prev_key":"2015-11-25","prev_key_chain":["2015-11-25"],"status":"exact","title":"China slowdown, oil crash, and first Fed hike end the bull","title_zh":"中国放缓、油价崩盘与首次加息终结牛市","turn_id":"xly:peak:2015-11"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"The February 2016 trough coincided with the 'Shanghai Accord' (G20 coordinated dollar-weakening and Chinese stimulus) which arrested the oil crash and commodity selloff, igniting a global reflation trade that sent oil up +170.1% and copper/gold up +39.1% over the next two-plus years. XLY ranked #3 of 11 (+78.2%) in the risk-on expansion, with tech/semis leading (+141.2% semis), financials surging on steepening yield curves, and Amazon's dominance compounding structurally. Trump's November 2016 election added a pro-consumer fiscal stimulus narrative (tax cuts, deregulation), boosting autos, homebuilders and discretionary spending; VIX compressed 28 to 12 and credit outperformed (+21.1%) as the reflation/growth quad locked in.","body_zh":"2016年2月触底与'上海协议'（G20协调压低美元并推动中国刺激）时间吻合，终止了油价暴跌和大宗商品抛售，点燃了全球再通胀交易，推动油价上涨+170.1%、铜金比+39.1%。XLY在risk-on扩张中排名第3位（+78.2%），科技/半导体领涨（半导体+141.2%），金融股在收益率曲线陡峭化中飙升，亚马逊主导地位在结构上持续强化。特朗普2016年11月的大选胜利加入了对消费者友好的财政刺激叙事（减税、去监管），提振了汽车、房屋建筑商和可选消费支出；VIX从28压缩至12，再通胀/增长象限确立之际信用债跑赢（+21.1%）。","drivers":["Shanghai Accord / commodity reflation","oil recovery +170%","Trump fiscal stimulus / tax-cut narrative","tech/semis-led risk-on"],"drivers_zh":["上海协议/大宗商品再通胀","油价回升+170%","特朗普财政刺激/减税叙事","科技/半导体引领risk-on"],"prev_key":"2016-02-11","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Shanghai Accord reflation and Trump wave drive a cyclical surge","title_zh":"上海协议再通胀与特朗普波浪推动周期板块飙升","turn_id":"xly:trough:2016-02"},"2018-09-20":{"body":"The Fed raised rates four times in 2018 (to a 2.25-2.50% target) while the Trump administration escalated US-China trade tariffs to 10% on $200bn of goods by September 2018, injecting cost pressure into retail supply chains and dampening capex and consumer confidence. Apple's November 1, 2018 weak holiday guidance (and decision to stop reporting unit sales) exposed softening end-demand, VIX spiked 12 to 36, and a classic flight-to-safety rotation unfolded: defensives fell only -8.7% while cyclicals cratered -23.1%. XLY dropped -21.4% (#6 of 11), with homebuilders, autos, apparel, and Amazon all pricing in the combined demand and cost hit.","body_zh":"美联储2018年四次加息（目标利率升至2.25-2.50%），同时特朗普政府将对华贸易关税在9月升级至对2000亿美元商品征收10%，给零售供应链注入成本压力并压制资本支出和消费者信心。苹果2018年11月1日疲弱的假日季业绩展望（及停止披露单位销量的决定）暴露了终端需求走软，VIX从12飙升至36，经典避险轮动展开：防御板块仅下跌-8.7%，而周期板块暴跌-23.1%。XLY下跌-21.4%（11个板块中第6位），房屋建筑商、汽车、服装和亚马逊均在为需求与成本的双重冲击重新定价。","drivers":["Fed overtightening (2.5% terminal)","US-China trade tariffs","Apple guidance cut","flight-to-safety"],"drivers_zh":["美联储过度紧缩（2.5%终端利率）","中美贸易关税","苹果业绩展望下调","避险"],"prev_key":"2018-09-20","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed overtightening and trade-war tariffs end the cycle","title_zh":"美联储过度紧缩与贸易战关税终结周期","turn_id":"xly:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"Jerome Powell's January 4, 2019 speech signaling a pause in rate hikes ('patient' language) reversed the Q4 2018 selloff and sent money flooding back into high-beta growth. The Fed subsequently cut rates three times in 2019 (July, September, October), and a US-China Phase 1 trade deal signed January 15, 2020 removed the tariff escalation tail risk. XLY ranked #3 of 11 (+45.8%) in a tech-led melt-up (semis +87.9%, growth beating value +23.3%), with Amazon powering higher on AWS/advertising acceleration and a resilient consumer defying recession fears; VIX compressed 36 to 16 before COVID ended the expansion at the February 2020 peak.","body_zh":"鲍威尔2019年1月4日发表讲话释放暂停加息信号（'耐心'措辞），扭转了四季度的抛售态势，推动资金大举回流高贝塔成长股。美联储随后于2019年三次降息（7月、9月、10月），2020年1月15日签署的中美第一阶段贸易协议消除了关税升级的尾部风险。XLY在科技引领的逼空上涨中排名第3位（+45.8%，半导体+87.9%，成长跑赢价值+23.3%），亚马逊凭借AWS/广告业务加速持续走高，坚韧的消费者令衰退担忧落空；VIX从36压缩至16，直至新冠疫情终结了这轮扩张于2020年2月见顶。","drivers":["Fed pivot / 3 cuts in 2019","US-China Phase 1 trade deal","Amazon AWS acceleration","tech-led risk-on"],"drivers_zh":["美联储转向/2019年三次降息","中美第一阶段贸易协议","亚马逊AWS加速","科技引领risk-on"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pause, Phase 1 trade deal fuel a goldilocks recovery","title_zh":"美联储暂停加息与第一阶段贸易协议推动金发女孩复苏","turn_id":"xly:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-20":{"body":"SARS-CoV-2 spread out of China in late January 2020 and was declared a global pandemic by the WHO on March 11, triggering the fastest 30%-plus drawdown from a peak in S&P 500 history. VIX exploded 16 to 76 and oil collapsed -62.1% (Saudi-Russia price war compounding the demand shock), while US Treasuries barely caught a bid (TLT -1.4%) because forced liquidation was indiscriminate. XLY fell -33.9% (#8 of 11), relatively mid-field: defensives held -18.0% vs cyclicals -37.1%, but XLY's large e-commerce names (Amazon) cushioned the selloff versus energy (-56.2%) and financials (-38.2%) which bore the full brunt of the lockdown and credit fears.","body_zh":"SARS-CoV-2于2020年1月下旬从中国蔓延，世卫组织于3月11日宣布全球大流行，引发标普500史上最快的超30%跌幅。VIX从16暴涨至76，油价暴跌-62.1%（沙特-俄罗斯价格战叠加需求冲击），而美债几乎未获避险买盘（TLT -1.4%），因为强制清盘无差别蔓延。XLY下跌-33.9%（11个板块中第8位），相对居中：防御板块守住-18.0%，而周期板块暴跌-37.1%，但XLY中较大的电商类名称（亚马逊）对下跌起到了一定缓冲，优于能源（-56.2%）和金融（-38.2%）——后者承受了封锁和信贷担忧的全部冲击。","drivers":["COVID pandemic shock","VIX 16-to-76 / fastest bear market","oil -62% / Saudi-Russia price war","indiscriminate forced liquidation"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情冲击","VIX 16至76/史上最快熊市","油价-62%/沙特-俄罗斯价格战","无差别强制清盘"],"prev_key":"2020-02-20","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-20"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic panic: the fastest bear market ever","title_zh":"新冠疫情恐慌：史上最快的熊市","turn_id":"xly:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"The Fed's unlimited QE announcement on March 23, 2020, the $2.2 trillion CARES Act (March 27), and subsequent $900bn and $1.9 trillion stimulus packages created an unprecedented liquidity and fiscal surge that propelled XLY to #2 of 11 (+145.6%) over the next 20 months. The lockdown economy structurally accelerated Amazon's e-commerce and cloud dominance, and Tesla's EV parabola (aided by massive equity raises and inclusion in the S&P 500 in December 2020) made XLY a proxy for the growth/tech mega-cap trade. Oil rebounded +273.6% from its lows, semis surged +211.0%, high-beta led low-vol by +169.0%, and a weakening dollar (-5.0% DXY) added fuel; VIX compressed 76 to 18 as vaccine news in November 2020 and reopening euphoria carried the sector to its November 2021 peak.","body_zh":"美联储于2020年3月23日宣布无限量QE、2.2万亿美元CARES法案（3月27日）以及随后的9000亿和1.9万亿美元刺激方案，创造了前所未有的流动性和财政冲击，推动XLY在随后20个月中以+145.6%排名第2位（共11个板块）。封控经济在结构上加速了亚马逊电商和云计算的主导地位，特斯拉的电动车抛物线式上涨（得益于大规模股权融资和2020年12月纳入标普500）使XLY成为成长/科技大型股交易的代名词。油价从低点反弹+273.6%，半导体飙升+211.0%，高贝塔领先低波动+169.0%，美元走弱（DXY -5.0%）推波助澜；VIX从76压缩至18，2020年11月的疫苗消息和重新开放的欣快情绪将板块推向2021年11月的顶峰。","drivers":["CARES Act / $5T fiscal stimulus","Fed QE infinity / zero rates","Amazon e-commerce structural acceleration","Tesla S&P inclusion / EV parabola"],"drivers_zh":["CARES法案/5万亿美元财政刺激","美联储无限量QE/零利率","亚马逊电商结构性加速","特斯拉纳入标普500/电动车抛物线"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"CARES Act, QE infinity, and e-commerce boom drive a monster recovery","title_zh":"CARES法案、无限量QE与电商繁荣推动史诗级复苏","turn_id":"xly:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-19":{"body":"With CPI heading toward 9% and the Fed pivoting to aggressive hikes, the long-duration growth names that dominate XLY de-rated hard, led by Amazon and Tesla, and discretionary finished dead-last (#11 of 11, -22.7%). This was a flight-to-safety rotation, not just sector weakness: defensives held +3.3% against cyclicals -3.4% as VIX ripped 18 to 36, while the end of stimulus and rising mortgage rates squeezed real wages, big-ticket demand and homebuilders.","body_zh":"随着CPI迈向9%、美联储转向激进加息，主导XLY的长久期成长股大幅估值下修，以亚马逊和特斯拉为首，可选消费垫底（11个板块中第11位，-22.7%）。这是一轮避险轮动，而不只是板块走弱：在VIX从18飙升至36之际，防御板块守住+3.3%、周期板块为-3.4%，与此同时刺激政策退出和抵押贷款利率上升挤压了实际工资、大额需求和房屋建筑商。","drivers":["flight-to-safety","Fed hikes / inflation squeeze","Amazon/Tesla de-rate","stagflation quad (oil +57%)"],"drivers_zh":["避险","美联储加息/通胀挤压","亚马逊/特斯拉估值下修","滞胀象限（油价+57%）"],"prev_key":"2021-11-19","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-19"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed-hike shock de-rates Amazon, Tesla as money flees to safety","title_zh":"加息冲击重估亚马逊特斯拉，资金避险出逃","turn_id":"xly:peak:2021-11"},"2022-03-07":{"body":"After the Nasdaq's mid-March low, beaten-down discretionary mega-caps like Amazon and Tesla snapped back to lead the tape (#1 of 11, +17.5%) as the Fed's first March 16 hike removed near-term uncertainty and money rotated back into high-beta growth — semis +16.9%, growth beating value +7.2, VIX collapsing 36 to 19. The relief was narrow (equal-weight lagged cap-weight -2.0%) and rate-sensitive rather than a fundamental improvement in the consumer.","body_zh":"在纳指3月中旬见底后，亚马逊、特斯拉等被打压的可选消费大型股强劲反弹并领涨大盘（11个板块中第1位，+17.5%），因美联储3月16日首次加息消除了近期不确定性，资金重新轮动回高贝塔成长股——半导体+16.9%，成长跑赢价值+7.2，VIX从36回落至19。这轮纾解狭窄（等权落后市值权重-2.0%）且对利率敏感，而非消费者基本面的真正改善。","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","Fed clarity / short covering","Amazon/Tesla bounce","narrow breadth"],"drivers_zh":["科技引领risk-on","美联储明朗化/空头回补","亚马逊/特斯拉反弹","市场广度狭窄"],"prev_key":"2022-03-07","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Bear-market bounce: discretionary leads a risk-on snap","title_zh":"熊市反弹：可选消费引领risk-on弹升","turn_id":"xly:trough:2022-03"},"2022-03-29":{"body":"Walmart and Target delivered rare earnings misses in mid-May as freight, payroll and inventory costs crushed margins and shoppers pulled back on big-ticket goods, dropping discretionary to dead-last (#11, -28.0%). The selloff was a defensive rotation — defensives -2.8% vs cyclicals -11.9% with VIX 19 to 29 — compounded by a rate-regime move (TLT -8.8%) and a stronger dollar (+3.5% DXY) that hammered Amazon and the homebuilders.","body_zh":"沃尔玛和塔吉特在5月中旬罕见地业绩不及预期，因运费、薪资和库存成本压垮了利润率，消费者在大额商品上收紧开支，使可选消费跌至垫底（第11位，-28.0%）。这轮抛售是防御性轮动——防御板块-2.8%对周期板块-11.9%，VIX从19升至29——并叠加利率体制走高（TLT -8.8%）和走强的美元（DXY +3.5%），重创了亚马逊和房屋建筑商。","drivers":["flight-to-safety","Walmart/Target miss","rate regime (TLT -8.8%)","strong dollar"],"drivers_zh":["避险","沃尔玛/塔吉特不及预期","利率体制（TLT -8.8%）","美元走强"],"prev_key":"2022-03-29","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Retail margin shock and a flight-to-safety leg down","title_zh":"零售利润率冲击，叠加避险下挫","turn_id":"xly:peak:2022-03"},"2022-05-24":{"body":"After a historic losing streak, deeply oversold discretionary names bounced to #1 of 11 (+14.4%) as retailers' results were reframed as execution problems rather than a broken consumer. This was a risk-on snap led by cyclicals (+7.0% vs defensives +0.9%, reflation quad) with Amazon and beaten-down retail rebounding — a technical relief, not a fundamental turn.","body_zh":"在历史性的连跌之后，深度超卖的可选消费股反弹至11个板块中第1位（+14.4%），因零售商的业绩被重新解读为执行问题而非消费者崩塌。这是一轮由周期股引领的risk-on弹升（周期+7.0%对防御+0.9%，再通胀象限），亚马逊和被打压的零售股回升——属于技术性纾解，而非基本面扭转。","drivers":["risk-on leadership","oversold bounce","execution-not-consumer narrative","reflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["risk-on领涨","超卖反弹","执行问题而非消费者叙事","再通胀象限"],"prev_key":"2022-05-24","prev_key_chain":["2022-05-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Oversold relief: discretionary tops the leaderboard","title_zh":"超卖纾解：可选消费登顶榜首","turn_id":"xly:trough:2022-05"},"2022-06-02":{"body":"A scorching 8.6% CPI print (released June 10) and the Fed's first 75bp hike since 1994 (June 15) sent rate-sensitive discretionary names to dead-last (#11, -14.6%) into the mid-June bottom. This was an everything-down flush — defensives also bled (-9.5%) as VIX climbed 25 to 33 — with Amazon, Tesla and the homebuilders leading the slide as recession odds and mortgage rates spiked.","body_zh":"炙热的8.6% CPI数据（6月10日公布）和美联储自1994年以来首次75个基点加息（6月15日），使利率敏感的可选消费股跌至垫底（第11位，-14.6%），直至6月中旬触底。这是一轮无差别下跌——VIX从25升至33之际防御板块也失血（-9.5%）——随着衰退概率和抵押贷款利率飙升，亚马逊、特斯拉和房屋建筑商领跌。","drivers":["broad risk-off","hot CPI / 75bp hike","recession fear","deflation-scare quad"],"drivers_zh":["全面risk-off","高CPI/加息75个基点","衰退担忧","通缩恐慌象限"],"prev_key":"2022-06-02","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Hot CPI, 75bp hike trigger a broad risk-off flush","title_zh":"高CPI与75个基点加息触发全面risk-off抛售","turn_id":"xly:peak:2022-06"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"From the June low, hopes that inflation had peaked and the Fed might soon pivot made discretionary the strongest sector (#1 of 11, +28.8%) as money rotated into high-beta growth — semis +19.5%, growth beating value +8.8, VIX 33 to 20. Amazon and Tesla led rate-sensitive cyclicals higher on Amazon's Q2 report and cooling July CPI, before Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole speech ended the rally.","body_zh":"从6月低点起，对通胀已见顶、美联储可能很快转向的预期，使可选消费成为表现最强的板块（11个板块中第1位，+28.8%），资金轮动进入高贝塔成长股——半导体+19.5%，成长跑赢价值+8.8，VIX从33回落至20。亚马逊和特斯拉凭借亚马逊二季度业绩和7月CPI降温引领利率敏感的周期股走高，直至鲍威尔鹰派的杰克逊霍尔讲话终结了行情。","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","peak-inflation / Fed-pivot bets","Amazon rebound","goldilocks quad"],"drivers_zh":["科技引领risk-on","通胀见顶/押注美联储转向","亚马逊回升","金发女孩象限"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-inflation summer rally, discretionary leads","title_zh":"通胀见顶夏季上涨，可选消费领涨","turn_id":"xly:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole speech killed the pivot trade and a rate-regime move (TLT -13.1%) kept yields climbing, but the bigger drag was Tesla's record collapse into year-end as Musk dumped billions in shares for Twitter, demand softened and Tesla cut prices. The rotation was defensive (defensives -2.7% vs cyclicals -7.0%) as Amazon's slowing retail and a strained consumer carried XLY to dead-last (#11, -26.7%) at its December low.","body_zh":"鲍威尔鹰派的杰克逊霍尔讲话终结了政策转向交易，利率体制走高（TLT -13.1%）使收益率持续攀升，但更大的拖累是特斯拉在年底前的历史性崩盘——马斯克为收购推特抛售了数十亿美元股票，需求走软，特斯拉降价。轮动偏向防御（防御板块-2.7%对周期板块-7.0%），亚马逊放缓的零售和承压的消费者将XLY拖至垫底（第11位，-26.7%）的12月低点。","drivers":["flight-to-safety","Jackson Hole hawkish","Tesla collapse / Musk share sales","rate regime (TLT -13.1%)"],"drivers_zh":["避险","杰克逊霍尔鹰派","特斯拉崩盘/马斯克抛售","利率体制（TLT -13.1%）"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole and Tesla collapse drive a flight-to-safety","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔与特斯拉崩盘引发避险","turn_id":"xly:peak:2022-08"},"2022-12-28":{"body":"Disinflation, a resilient consumer and the AI-driven mega-cap rebound powered a ~41% rally led by Amazon and Tesla, the two names that drive the ETF (#3 of 11). This was a classic narrow, tech-led melt-up — semis +60.8%, growth beating value +27.7, equal-weight lagging cap-weight by -10.2%, VIX 22 to 14 — that pulled flows back into high-beta discretionary into the July 2023 peak.","body_zh":"去通胀、坚韧的消费者和AI驱动的大型股反弹，推动了一轮约41%的上涨，由驱动该ETF的两只股票——亚马逊和特斯拉领涨（11个板块中第3位）。这是一轮典型的狭窄、科技主导的逼空上涨——半导体+60.8%，成长跑赢价值+27.7，等权落后市值权重-10.2%，VIX从22降至14——将资金重新拉回高贝塔可选消费，直至2023年7月见顶。","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","Amazon/Tesla recovery","disinflation / resilient consumer","narrow breadth"],"drivers_zh":["科技引领risk-on","亚马逊/特斯拉复苏","去通胀/坚韧消费者","市场广度狭窄"],"prev_key":"2022-12-28","prev_key_chain":["2022-12-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Amazon, Tesla lead a narrow, tech-led recovery","title_zh":"亚马逊、特斯拉引领狭窄、科技主导的复苏","turn_id":"xly:trough:2022-12"},"2023-07-19":{"body":"The 10-year Treasury surging toward 5%, its highest since 2007, on stronger data and deficit worries was a pure rate-regime move (TLT -17.0%) that crushed XLY's long-duration valuations to dead-last (#11, -16.2%). A stronger dollar (+6.3% DXY) and higher borrowing costs hit Amazon, Tesla and rate-sensitive homebuilders, threatening auto and big-ticket spending.","body_zh":"受强劲数据和赤字担忧推动，10年期美债收益率飙升至接近5%——为2007年以来最高，这是一次纯粹的利率体制走高（TLT -17.0%），将XLY的长久期估值压至垫底（第11位，-16.2%）。走强的美元（DXY +6.3%）和上升的借贷成本打击了亚马逊、特斯拉和利率敏感的房屋建筑商，威胁汽车和大额消费。","drivers":["rate regime (TLT -17.0%)","10-year toward 5% / higher-for-longer","strong dollar","Amazon/Tesla pressure"],"drivers_zh":["利率体制（TLT -17.0%）","10年期接近5%/更高更久","美元走强","亚马逊/特斯拉承压"],"prev_key":"2023-07-19","prev_key_chain":["2023-07-19"],"status":"exact","title":"Yield spike to 5% de-rates duration-heavy discretionary","title_zh":"收益率升至5%重估久期偏重的可选消费","turn_id":"xly:peak:2023-07"},"2023-10-26":{"body":"Falling yields (TLT +12.0%), the Fed's September 2024 cut and a remarkably resilient consumer drove a ~63% melt-up that put discretionary back at #1 of 11 on record holiday spending. It was a narrow, tech-led tape — semis +82.9%, growth beating value +30.7, equal-weight lagging cap-weight by -13.1% — with Tesla exploding higher after Trump's November win and Amazon's strength carrying XLY to its December 17, 2024 record peak.","body_zh":"回落的收益率（TLT +12.0%）、美联储2024年9月降息和异常坚韧的消费者，推动了约63%的飙升，凭借创纪录的假日消费使可选消费重回11个板块中第1位。这是一轮狭窄、科技主导的行情——半导体+82.9%，成长跑赢价值+30.7，等权落后市值权重-13.1%——特斯拉在特朗普11月获胜后暴涨，亚马逊的强势将XLY推向2024年12月17日的纪录高点。","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","rate cuts (TLT +12%)","Tesla post-election surge","narrow breadth"],"drivers_zh":["科技引领risk-on","降息（TLT +12%）","特斯拉大选后飙升","市场广度狭窄"],"prev_key":"2023-10-26","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate cuts and a narrow, tech-led melt-up; Tesla rockets","title_zh":"降息与狭窄、科技主导的逼空上涨；特斯拉飙升","turn_id":"xly:trough:2023-10"},"2024-12-17":{"body":"The peak unwound as January's DeepSeek shock hit AI/mega-cap sentiment and Amazon, then April's reciprocal-tariff announcement crushed import-heavy retail and slapped 25% levies on autos and parts, sending discretionary to dead-last (#11, -26.0%). It was a flight-to-safety rout — defensives -4.0% vs cyclicals -16.6% as VIX exploded 16 to 52 — with Tesla collapsing from its post-election high into the April 8 low.","body_zh":"随着1月的DeepSeek冲击打击AI/大型股情绪和亚马逊，继而4月的对等关税公告重创进口依赖型零售并对汽车及零部件征收25%关税，顶部随之瓦解，可选消费跌至垫底（第11位，-26.0%）。这是一轮避险溃败——VIX从16暴涨至52之际，防御板块-4.0%对周期板块-16.6%——特斯拉从大选后高点崩跌至4月8日低点。","drivers":["flight-to-safety","DeepSeek shock","reciprocal / auto tariffs","Tesla/Amazon decline"],"drivers_zh":["避险","DeepSeek冲击","对等/汽车关税","特斯拉/亚马逊下跌"],"prev_key":"2024-12-17","prev_key_chain":["2024-12-17"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek then tariff crash trigger a flight-to-safety","title_zh":"DeepSeek继而关税崩盘触发避险","turn_id":"xly:peak:2024-12"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"Trump's 90-day tariff pause (April 9, 2025) sparked a furious rebound, and a still-resilient consumer plus AI euphoria drove discretionary to #2 of 11 (+42.1%) through 2025 into early 2026. It was a narrow, tech-led, weak-dollar melt-up — semis +117.8%, growth beating value +17.1, equal-weight lagging cap-weight -10.3%, VIX 52 to 15 — as Amazon and Tesla recovered and big-ticket demand held despite lingering tariff costs.","body_zh":"特朗普90天的关税暂缓（2025年4月9日）引发了一轮迅猛反弹，仍然坚韧的消费者叠加AI热潮，推动可选消费升至11个板块中第2位（+42.1%），贯穿2025年直至2026年初。这是一轮狭窄、科技主导、弱美元的逼空上涨——半导体+117.8%，成长跑赢价值+17.1，等权落后市值权重-10.3%，VIX从52降至15——亚马逊和特斯拉复苏，大额需求在残留的关税成本下保持稳健。","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","tariff pause / resilient consumer","Amazon/Tesla rebound","narrow breadth"],"drivers_zh":["科技引领risk-on","关税暂缓/坚韧消费者","亚马逊/特斯拉反弹","市场广度狭窄"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-pause recovery rides the narrow, tech-led tape","title_zh":"关税暂缓复苏，搭乘狭窄、科技主导的行情","turn_id":"xly:trough:2025-04"},"2026-01-12":{"body":"The Iran/Strait-of-Hormuz oil shock — the US-Israel strikes on Iran began February 28, 2026 and Iran's retaliation hit Hormuz tanker traffic — sent gas prices and CPI toward 4.2% (oil +72.9%, a stagflation quad), squeezing real wages and discretionary spending just as a hawkish Fed leaned toward hikes, dropping XLY to dead-last (#11, -15.0%). Notably it was not a clean flight-to-safety — breadth actually broadened (RSP beat SPY +4.3%) — but energy-led inflation and higher rates hit the big-ticket, rate-sensitive parts of XLY and pressured Amazon and Tesla.","body_zh":"伊朗/霍尔木兹海峡油价冲击——美以于2026年2月28日开始对伊朗发动打击，伊朗的反击冲击了霍尔木兹的油轮运输——使汽油价格和CPI升向4.2%（油价+72.9%，滞胀象限），在鹰派美联储倾向加息之际挤压实际工资和可选消费支出，使XLY跌至垫底（第11位，-15.0%）。值得注意的是这并非干净的避险——市场广度反而扩大（RSP跑赢SPY +4.3%）——但能源驱动的通胀和更高的利率打击了XLY中利率敏感的大额消费部分，并施压亚马逊和特斯拉。","drivers":["stagflation quad (oil +73%)","oil shock / gas squeeze","hawkish Fed","broadening breadth"],"drivers_zh":["滞胀象限（油价+73%）","油价冲击/汽油挤压","鹰派美联储","市场广度扩大"],"prev_key":"2026-01-12","prev_key_chain":["2026-01-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil shock and hawkish Fed leave discretionary stranded","title_zh":"油价冲击与鹰派美联储令可选消费搁浅","turn_id":"xly:peak:2026-01"},"2026-03-30":{"body":"The April 8, 2026 US-Iran ceasefire — a 60-day MOU that reopened the Strait of Hormuz to commercial traffic and lifted sanctions on Iranian crude — pulled Brent ~20% off its wartime high, easing the pump-price squeeze and sparking a relief bounce in Amazon and Tesla. But XLY (+15.3%) trailed a narrow, tech-led melt-up (Tech +46.4%, semis +65.5%, equal-weight lagging cap-weight -8.8%, VIX 31 to 16) — discretionary is rejoining risk-on, not leading it, with a hawkish Fed and below-trend positioning keeping the recovery tentative.","body_zh":"2026年4月8日的美伊停火——一份为期60天的谅解备忘录，重新开放霍尔木兹海峡的商业通行并取消对伊朗原油的制裁——使布伦特原油从战时高点回落约20%，缓解了汽油价格挤压，并在亚马逊和特斯拉中引发了纾解反弹。但XLY（+15.3%）落后于一轮狭窄、科技主导的逼空上涨（Tech +46.4%，半导体+65.5%，等权落后市值权重-8.8%，VIX从31降至16）——可选消费是在重新加入risk-on而非领涨，仍然鹰派的美联储和低于趋势的持仓使复苏保持谨慎。","drivers":["tech-led risk-on","April Iran ceasefire / oil relief","Amazon/Tesla bounce","narrow breadth"],"drivers_zh":["科技引领risk-on","四月伊朗停火/油价纾解","亚马逊/特斯拉反弹","市场广度狭窄"],"prev_key":"2026-03-30","prev_key_chain":["2026-03-30"],"status":"exact","title":"April ceasefire and oil relief spark a lagging bounce","title_zh":"四月停火与油价纾解引发滞后反弹","turn_id":"xly:trough:2026-03"}},"now":"XLY is in a confirmed trough/bottoming phase (cycle position 31, RS rank #6 of 11, below its 200-day MA) after the oil-shock and stagflation selloff that ran from January to late March 2026. The current cross-asset tape is reflation/growth-up, with cyclicals recovering (+11.2% vs defensives +6.9%), the dollar firming (+3.4% DXY), oil firming (+19.2%) and semis exploding +67.9%, but XLY sits #10 of 11 at -5.2% because a hawkish Fed and elevated pump prices are still squeezing real consumer purchasing power. With Amazon and Tesla comprising roughly a third of the ETF, the setup is a leveraged catch-up trade that requires two unlocks: oil/gasoline softening enough to ease real-wage pressure and the Fed signaling a pause or cut. Neither has fully arrived — the Iran ceasefire keeps re-fracturing around the Strait of Hormuz — keeping the bounce tentative and below the 200-day even as breadth broadens (RSP beat SPY +2.9%).","now_zh":"XLY正处于确认的底部/筑底阶段（周期位置31，相对强度排名第6位，位于200日均线下方），此前经历了从2026年1月延续至3月底的油价冲击和滞胀抛售。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-ai_agents":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"From January 2014, a 59% rally in early AI-adjacent software and analytics names was powered by the post-taper-tantrum calm: the Fed held zero rates, TLT rallied +24.4% as yields fell, and the dollar surged +21.7% as US growth outpaced the rest of the world. Health and Tech led the tape (+33%/+31%) while Energy collapsed -22.4% on the oil glut, a slowdown/deflation-scare quad that paradoxically benefited high-multiple growth as capital fled commodity cyclicals. The rally was narrow and mega-cap-led (RSP lagged SPY -3.9%), driven by multiple expansion in cloud SaaS (Salesforce, Workday, ServiceNow) and early big-data analytics names (Splunk, Tableau) whose recurring-revenue models re-rated sharply in a falling-yield, falling-commodity world. Google's DeepMind acquisition in January 2014 and Microsoft's Azure ML launch in 2014 signaled that enterprise AI budgets were real, pulling forward AI application valuations.","body_zh":"自2014年1月起，早期AI相邻软件与分析个股录得59%的涨幅，受益于缩表恐慌后的平静：美联储维持零利率、TLT上涨+24.4%（收益率下行）、美元大涨+21.7%（美国增长领先全球）。医疗和科技领涨（分别+33%/+31%），能源在油价供应过剩中暴跌-22.4%，放缓/通缩恐慌象限反而利好高估值成长股，因资金出逃大宗商品周期性行业。涨势窄幅且大盘股主导（RSP跑输SPY -3.9%），由云SaaS（Salesforce、Workday、ServiceNow）与早期大数据分析个股（Splunk、Tableau）的估值倍数扩张驱动，其经常性收入模式在收益率下行、大宗商品下跌的环境中获得大幅重估。谷歌2014年1月收购DeepMind及微软Azure ML平台上线，标志着企业AI预算的真实性，推动AI应用估值提前兑现。","drivers":["ZIRP multiple expansion","falling yields TLT +24.4%","cloud SaaS re-rating","oil collapse -57.5% deflation-scare quad","narrow mega-cap growth leadership"],"drivers_zh":["零利率估值扩张","收益率下行TLT +24.4%","云SaaS重估","油价暴跌-57.5%通缩恐慌象限","大盘股窄幅成长领涨"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Cloud and big-data re-rating, ZIRP tailwind","title_zh":"云计算/大数据重估，零利率顺风","turn_id":"ai_agents:trough:2014-01"},"2015-12-04":{"body":"A sharp 41% selloff from the December 2015 peak into February 2016 was driven by the global growth scare triggered by China's yuan devaluation (August 2015) and collapsing oil (WTI hit $26 in February 2016, down -25.7% in this window). The flight-to-safety was crisp: defensives outperformed cyclicals (-0.6% vs -13.2%), VIX spiked from 15 to 26, and TLT added +9.5% as yields fell. Semis dropped -15.8%, financials -17.1%, and the highest-beta growth software corner amplified the selloff; this was a macro-driven risk-off, not a fundamental re-rating of the AI software thesis.","body_zh":"自2015年12月峰值至2016年2月，市场暴跌41%，由中国人民币贬值（2015年8月）引发的全球增长恐慌与油价崩盘（WTI于2016年2月触及$26，本阶段跌-25.7%）驱动。避险情绪明确：防御股跑赢周期股（-0.6% vs -13.2%），VIX从15飙升至26，TLT上涨+9.5%（收益率下行）。芯片股下跌-15.8%，金融-17.1%，贝塔最高的成长软件领域放大跌幅；这是宏观驱动的风险规避，而非对AI软件逻辑的基本面重估。","drivers":["China growth scare","oil collapse WTI to $26 -25.7%","VIX spike 15 to 26","flight-to-safety into defensives","high-beta amplification"],"drivers_zh":["中国增长恐慌","油价崩盘WTI至$26 -25.7%","VIX飙升15至26","避险资金流入防御股","高贝塔放大效应"],"prev_key":"2015-12-04","prev_key_chain":["2015-12-04"],"status":"exact","title":"China growth scare and oil crash selloff","title_zh":"中国增长恐慌与油价崩盘引发抛售","turn_id":"ai_agents:peak:2015-12"},"2016-02-08":{"body":"The longest leg in the series: a 438% surge from the February 2016 oil/China bottom to the February 2020 COVID peak. Oil bottomed (~$26) in mid-February 2016, China fears faded, and the reflation/growth-up regime took hold; Trump's December 2017 tax cuts (corporate rate 35% to 21%) supercharged buybacks and enterprise capex budgets, directly expanding the AI software total addressable market. Tech led at +181% and semis at +244%; VIX collapsed from 26 to 14 and high-beta dominated over low-vol by +28.8%. The breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY by -14.3%), confirming a mega-cap-led FAAMG tape, but AI application names at this stage (Salesforce, Adobe, Veeva, Twilio, UiPath IPO) rode the secular cloud and early machine-learning re-rating, outperforming SPY's 97% by more than 4x.","body_zh":"本系列最长的一段涨势：自2016年2月油价/中国见底至2020年2月新冠峰值，暴涨438%。油价于2016年2月中旬触底（约$26），中国恐慌消退，再通胀/增长向上格局确立；特朗普2017年12月减税（企业税率从35%降至21%）大幅推动回购与企业IT资本开支，直接扩大了AI软件的潜在市场。科技领涨+181%，芯片+244%；VIX从26崩至14，高贝塔跑赢低波动+28.8%。广度窄幅（RSP跑输SPY -14.3%），印证大盘FAAMG主导，但此阶段AI应用个股（Salesforce、Adobe、Veeva、Twilio、UiPath上市）乘云计算与早期机器学习重估浪潮，4倍跑赢SPY的97%。","drivers":["oil/China bottom Feb 2016","Trump tax cuts Dec 2017","cloud enterprise secular buildout","semis +244% AI capex cycle","FAAMG mega-cap leadership"],"drivers_zh":["油价/中国2016年2月见底","特朗普2017年12月减税","云计算企业长期建设周期","芯片+244% AI资本开支周期","FAAMG大盘股领涨"],"prev_key":"2016-02-08","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Four-year bull: cloud, tax cuts, AI buildout","title_zh":"四年牛市：云计算、减税与AI建设浪潮","turn_id":"ai_agents:trough:2016-02"},"2020-02-19":{"body":"A 31% collapse from the February 19, 2020 peak to the March 16 trough as COVID-19 forced global economic shutdowns: the VIX spiked from 14 to 83 on March 16 (its highest level ever), SPY fell -29.1%, and TLT added +12.8% in a flight-to-safety where every asset class sold off indiscriminately. Oil plunged -46.1% as demand destruction collided with the Saudi-Russia price war. The pattern was maximum defensive outperformance (staples -18% vs industrials -34%, financials -36%, energy -49%); even defensive sectors collapsed, but the basket's high-beta profile amplified losses. The selloff was a pure liquidity/panic event, not an AI fundamentals shock.","body_zh":"自2020年2月19日峰值至3月16日低谷，新冠疫情迫使全球经济停摆，市场崩跌31%：VIX于3月16日飙升至83（历史最高），SPY下跌-29.1%，TLT上涨+12.8%（全资产类别无差别抛售中的避险流入）。油价暴跌-46.1%（需求毁灭叠加沙特-俄罗斯价格战）。防御股相对抗跌（必需消费-18% vs 工业-34%、金融-36%、能源-49%），但篮子高贝塔属性放大了损失。这是纯粹的流动性/恐慌事件，并非AI基本面冲击。","drivers":["COVID global shutdown","VIX 14 to 83 panic","oil -46.1% demand destruction + Saudi-Russia price war","indiscriminate high-beta liquidation","flight-to-safety TLT +12.8%"],"drivers_zh":["新冠全球停摆","VIX 14飙至83恐慌","油价-46.1%需求毁灭+沙特俄罗斯价格战","高贝塔无差别斩仓","避险TLT +12.8%"],"prev_key":"2020-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash, VIX to 83","title_zh":"新冠疫情崩盘，VIX飙至83","turn_id":"ai_agents:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-16":{"body":"A 239% surge from the March 16, 2020 trough to February 9, 2021 driven by the most aggressive monetary-fiscal stimulus in US history: the Fed cut rates to 0-0.25% on March 15 and launched unlimited QE, buying $700B+ in assets and ballooning its balance sheet above $7 trillion by May 2020. The $2.2 trillion CARES Act followed. Zero rates slashed the discount rate on speculative, cash-burning AI applications to near zero, while pandemic-driven digital acceleration (remote work, cloud migration, automation demand) pulled years of enterprise software demand forward. Discretionary +95%, Tech +91%, Materials +82% led in a reflation/growth-up quad; VIX collapsed from 83 to 22, DXY fell -7.8% (a tailwind for global-revenue tech), and high-beta dominated by +103%. The basket was among the biggest beneficiaries of the ZIRP regime.","body_zh":"自2020年3月16日低谷至2021年2月9日，涨幅达239%，受美国历史上最积极货币财政刺激驱动：美联储于3月15日将利率降至0-0.25%并启动无限量化宽松，资产购买超过7000亿美元，资产负债表于2020年5月飙升至7万亿美元以上。随后推出2.2万亿美元CARES法案。零利率将投机性、烧钱AI应用的贴现率压至接近零，叠加疫情驱动的数字化加速（远程办公、云迁移、自动化需求激增），拉动企业软件多年需求前置。可选消费+95%、科技+91%、材料+82%领涨，处于再通胀/增长向上象限；VIX从83崩至22，DXY下跌-7.8%（对全球营收科技股利好），高贝塔主导+103%。篮子是零利率制度最大受益者之一。","drivers":["ZIRP to 0.25% Fed March 2020","unlimited QE balance sheet $7T","CARES Act fiscal stimulus","pandemic digital acceleration","DXY -7.8% tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["2020年3月美联储降至零利率","无限量化宽松资产负债表达7万亿","CARES法案财政刺激","疫情驱动数字化加速","DXY -7.8%顺风"],"prev_key":"2020-03-16","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-16"],"status":"exact","title":"ZIRP, fiscal bazooka, pandemic digitalization","title_zh":"零利率、财政火箭筒与疫情数字化加速","turn_id":"ai_agents:trough:2020-03"},"2021-02-09":{"body":"Speculative application software topped in early February 2021 as the bond market's inflation re-pricing began: TLT fell -8.4%, and the growth-value spread collapsed by -13.2 percentage points as the reflation trade (Financials +19.7%, Energy +19.5%, Materials +18.5%) rotated capital out of long-duration cash-burning software. In a broadening reflation/growth-up tape (RSP beat SPY +5.4%), the most unprofitable, highest-beta corner led the decline even as SPY rose +5.5%, marking a classic high-beta top-ahead-of-index pattern. The 10-year yield moved sharply from ~1.1% to ~1.7% through March 2021, delivering the first real rate shock to a basket priced for zero discount rates.","body_zh":"投机性应用软件于2021年2月初见顶，因债市开始重新定价通胀：TLT下跌-8.4%，随着再通胀交易（金融+19.7%、能源+19.5%、材料+18.5%）将资金从长久期烧钱软件中轮出，成长-价值价差骤缩-13.2个百分点。在转宽的再通胀/增长向上行情中（RSP跑赢SPY +5.4%），盈利最差、贝塔最高的领域领跌，尽管SPY上涨+5.5%——这是高贝塔先于指数见顶的经典形态。10年期国债收益率从约1.1%跃升至约1.7%，为按零贴现率定价的篮子带来首次真实利率冲击。","drivers":["10yr yield surge 1.1% to 1.7%","growth-value rotation -13.2%","TLT -8.4%","reflation broadening RSP +5.4%","high-beta top before index"],"drivers_zh":["10年期收益率从1.1%飙至1.7%","成长-价值轮动-13.2%","TLT -8.4%","再通胀转宽RSP +5.4%","高贝塔先于指数见顶"],"prev_key":"2021-02-09","prev_key_chain":["2021-02-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Yield-surge rotation out of speculative growth","title_zh":"利率飙升引发投机性成长股轮出","turn_id":"ai_agents:peak:2021-02"},"2021-05-13":{"body":"A 45% melt-up from May to November 2021 as the Fed kept rates at zero and signaled a very slow taper path, the 10-year yield fell back (TLT +9.2%), and the tech-led narrow risk-on tape reasserted itself (SMH +30.1%, growth beat value +18.3, VIX fell 23 to 15). This was a narrow mega-cap rally (RSP lagged SPY -5.7%) in a reflation/growth-up quad with the dollar firming +4.0%, where AI application software benefited from continued enterprise SaaS spending and rising cloud hyperscaler capex commitments from AWS, Azure, and GCP. It was the final melt-up before the Fed's November 2021 taper announcement ended the zero-rate era.","body_zh":"2021年5月至11月45%的熔涨，因美联储维持零利率并释放极缓慢缩减路径信号，10年期收益率回落（TLT +9.2%），科技引领的窄幅风险偏好行情重新主导（SMH +30.1%、成长跑赢价值+18.3、VIX从23降至15）。这是窄幅大盘股反弹（RSP跑输SPY -5.7%），处于再通胀/增长向上象限，美元小幅走强+4.0%；AI应用软件受益于持续的企业SaaS支出以及AWS、Azure、GCP持续走高的云资本开支承诺。这是美联储2021年11月宣布缩减购债、零利率时代终结前的最后狂欢。","drivers":["Fed zero rates / slow taper signal","TLT +9.2% yields fall","semis +30.1% risk-on melt-up","narrow mega-cap breadth RSP -5.7%","enterprise SaaS spending acceleration"],"drivers_zh":["美联储零利率/极缓慢缩减信号","TLT +9.2%收益率回落","芯片+30.1%风险偏好熔涨","窄幅大盘股广度RSP -5.7%","企业SaaS支出加速"],"prev_key":"2021-05-13","prev_key_chain":["2021-05-13"],"status":"exact","title":"Liquidity-fueled final melt-up to peak","title_zh":"流动性驱动的最后熔涨至峰值","turn_id":"ai_agents:trough:2021-05"},"2021-11-04":{"body":"The November 2021 Fed taper announcement and subsequent pivot to rate hikes crushed the highest-multiple, lowest-profit software hardest: the basket collapsed -49% into March 2022 as yields surged (TLT -10.0%) and the dollar firmed +5.0% in a stagflation-ish quad (Energy +31.3% led; Tech -14.8%, Comm -21.3%). VIX spiked from 15 to 32 in a flight-to-safety (defensives +1.0% vs cyclicals -4.1%), and speculative cash-burners were re-rated from growth-at-any-price to show-me-the-earnings. The Fed's first rate hike came March 16, 2022, coinciding almost exactly with the basket's trough, confirming the market had fully priced the tightening cycle.","body_zh":"2021年11月美联储宣布缩减购债并随后转向加息，对估值最高、盈利最差的软件打击最重：篮子在2022年3月前崩跌-49%，收益率飙升（TLT -10.0%）、美元在类滞胀象限走强+5.0%（能源+31.3%领涨；科技-14.8%、通讯-21.3%）。VIX从15飙升至32，避险情绪浓厚（防御股+1.0% vs 周期股-4.1%），投机性烧钱股从\"成长不问价\"重估为\"请拿出盈利\"。美联储首次加息恰在2022年3月16日，几乎精准吻合篮子低点，印证市场已充分消化紧缩周期。","drivers":["Fed taper Nov 2021 / first hike Mar 2022","TLT -10.0% yield surge","stagflation quad Energy +31.3%","VIX 15 to 32 flight-to-safety","zero-profit re-rating"],"drivers_zh":["2021年11月美联储缩减/2022年3月首次加息","TLT -10.0%收益率飙升","滞胀象限能源+31.3%","VIX 15至32避险","零盈利重估"],"prev_key":"2021-11-04","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed hawkish pivot crushes long-duration growth","title_zh":"美联储鹰派转向重创长久期成长股","turn_id":"ai_agents:peak:2021-11"},"2022-03-14":{"body":"A violent 28% two-week bounce from the March 14 trough as the market absorbed the first Fed hike (March 16, 2022) and repositioned: VIX collapsed from 32 to 19, semis rallied +18.8%, and growth beat value +8.7 in a reflation/growth-up quad. The bounce was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -2.4%), positioning-driven, and lasted only about two weeks before the rate selloff resumed. Russia-Ukraine ceasefire talks in late March briefly lifted risk sentiment, but with Fed funds on a steep upward path the AI software relief was transient.","body_zh":"自3月14日低谷发生的两周28%剧烈反弹，因市场消化首次加息（2022年3月16日）并重新布仓：VIX从32崩至19，芯片反弹+18.8%，成长跑赢价值+8.7，处于再通胀/增长向上象限。反弹窄幅（RSP跑输SPY -2.4%）、由仓位驱动，仅持续约两周便再度遭遇利率抛售。3月下旬俄乌停火谈判短暂提振风险情绪，但美联储基金利率仍在陡峭上升路径上，AI软件的喘息极为短暂。","drivers":["post-hike positioning relief","VIX 32 to 19 collapse","semis +18.8% oversold bounce","narrow breadth RSP -2.4%","Russia-Ukraine ceasefire hopes"],"drivers_zh":["加息后仓位缓解","VIX 32至19崩落","芯片+18.8%超卖反弹","窄幅广度RSP -2.4%","俄乌停火希望"],"prev_key":"2022-03-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Oversold snapback on risk-on relief","title_zh":"风险偏好缓和中的超卖反弹","turn_id":"ai_agents:trough:2022-03"},"2022-03-29":{"body":"Surging real yields (10-year peaked near 3.0% by May 2022, TLT -9.5%) and a stronger dollar (+5.5%) drove the basket down another -39% into the May 11 trough in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. The flight-to-safety was sharp (defensives -4.2% vs cyclicals -13.1%, VIX 19 to 33) as the Fed accelerated to 50bp hike increments (May 4, 2022 first 50bp) and the prospect of sustained QT wiped out the remaining premium on zero-earnings AI applications. Tech -18.7%, Comm -19.2%, and Discretionary -24.0% led losses while Energy and Staples provided relative shelter.","body_zh":"实际收益率飙升（10年期于2022年5月触及约3.0%，TLT -9.5%）与美元走强（+5.5%）推动篮子在5月11日低谷前再跌-39%，处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限。避险情绪急剧（防御股-4.2% vs 周期股-13.1%，VIX 19至33），因美联储于2022年5月4日首次加息50bp并加速紧缩，QT前景彻底摧毁了零盈利AI应用的剩余溢价。科技-18.7%、通讯-19.2%、可选消费-24.0%领跌，能源和必需消费提供相对避风港。","drivers":["10yr yield 3.0% / TLT -9.5%","Fed 50bp hikes May 2022","DXY +5.5% stronger dollar","VIX 19 to 33 slowdown quad","zero-earnings premium destroyed"],"drivers_zh":["10年期收益率3.0% / TLT -9.5%","美联储2022年5月加息50bp","DXY +5.5%走强","VIX 19至33放缓象限","零盈利溢价彻底摧毁"],"prev_key":"2022-03-29","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Resumed rate selloff into May growth wipeout","title_zh":"利率抛售重启至5月成长股全面腰斩","turn_id":"ai_agents:peak:2022-03"},"2022-05-11":{"body":"A 33% bear-market rally from May 11 to June 2 fired on early peak-inflation narrative: April 2022 CPI (released May 11) printed 8.3% (slightly below the March 8.5% peak), and VIX eased from 33 to 25. Energy led the tape +13.6% with cyclicals broadly outperforming defensives (+8.0% vs +2.4%) in a reflation/growth-up quad; the high-beta AI basket amplified the relief (SMH +13.4% vs SPY +6.3%). There was no fundamental improvement in earnings or cash flow for AI application names; the rally was short-covering in the most beaten-down growth names, and it reversed quickly once it became clear inflation had not peaked.","body_zh":"自5月11日至6月2日的33%熊市反弹源于早期通胀见顶叙事：2022年4月CPI（5月11日公布）录得8.3%（略低于3月的8.5%峰值），VIX从33缓和至25。能源领涨+13.6%，周期股广泛跑赢防御股（+8.0% vs +2.4%），处于再通胀/增长向上象限；高贝塔AI篮子放大了缓和行情（SMH +13.4% vs SPY +6.3%）。AI应用个股盈利或现金流并无基本面改善；反弹是跌幅最深成长股的空头回补，一旦明确通胀尚未见顶便迅速逆转。","drivers":["April 2022 CPI 8.3% peak-inflation hope","VIX 33 to 25 short-covering","cyclicals outperform RSP vs SPY","high-beta amplification SMH +13.4%","no fundamental support"],"drivers_zh":["2022年4月CPI 8.3%通胀见顶预期","VIX 33至25空头回补","周期股跑赢RSP vs SPY","高贝塔放大SMH +13.4%","缺乏基本面支撑"],"prev_key":"2022-05-11","prev_key_chain":["2022-05-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Bear-market relief on peak-inflation hopes","title_zh":"通胀见顶预期下的熊市修复反弹","turn_id":"ai_agents:trough:2022-05"},"2022-06-02":{"body":"A 48% capitulation from June 2 to December 28, 2022, the ultimate cycle low, as the Fed delivered 75bp hikes at the June, July, September, and November 2022 meetings, taking the fed funds rate from ~1% to 4.25-4.5% in six months. TLT fell another -13.0% as yields surged, oil collapsed -32.4% on recession fears, and the macro quad was slowdown/deflation-scare with defensives outperforming cyclicals (+1.0% vs -7.2%). The AI application space was entirely abandoned: Comm -22.9%, growth trailed value -8.0%, and semis fell -19.9%. ChatGPT launched November 30, 2022, just as the basket hit its multi-year low, setting up the most explosive generative-AI re-rating in the next leg.","body_zh":"自2022年6月2日至12月28日（周期终极低点），篮子投降式下跌48%，因美联储在2022年6、7、9、11月连续加息75bp，半年内将联邦基金利率从约1%提至4.25-4.5%。TLT再跌-13.0%（收益率飙升），油价因衰退担忧崩跌-32.4%，宏观处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限，防御股跑赢周期股（+1.0% vs -7.2%）。AI应用领域被彻底抛弃：通讯-22.9%、成长跑输价值-8.0%、芯片下跌-19.9%。ChatGPT于2022年11月30日上线，恰在篮子触及多年低点之际，为下一段生成式AI最猛烈的重估埋下伏笔。","drivers":["Fed 75bp hikes June-November 2022 to 4.25%","TLT -13.0% yield surge","oil -32.4% recession scare","slowdown quad defensives outperform","ChatGPT launch at the low Nov 2022"],"drivers_zh":["2022年6-11月美联储75bp连续加息至4.25%","TLT -13.0%收益率飙升","油价-32.4%衰退恐慌","放缓象限防御股跑赢","ChatGPT于低点附近2022年11月上线"],"prev_key":"2022-06-02","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed hike cycle capitulation to the cycle low","title_zh":"美联储加息周期下的投降式下跌至周期低点","turn_id":"ai_agents:peak:2022-06"},"2022-12-28":{"body":"From the December 28, 2022 low, a 934% surge into February 2025 driven by the generative-AI re-rating triggered by ChatGPT's November 2022 launch. Microsoft's ~$10 billion OpenAI investment (January 2023) validated enterprise AI spending, and the hyperscalers (Microsoft, Google, Amazon, Meta) raised AI capex to hundreds of billions by 2024-2025. The Fed began cutting rates in September 2024 (first cut since 2020), removing the key headwind for zero-earnings AI applications. The macro was goldilocks (disinflation + growth, VIX 22 to 15, SMH +158%, growth beat value +65.0) but extremely narrow (RSP lagged SPY by -32.0%), confirming mega-cap concentration. Comm (+129%) and Tech (+100%) led the sector tape. As the highest-beta AI application basket, it amplified the whole AI buildout cycle, producing a 934% total return versus SPY's 66%.","body_zh":"自2022年12月28日低点，2025年2月前暴涨934%，由ChatGPT于2022年11月上线引发的生成式AI重估驱动。微软约100亿美元OpenAI投资（2023年1月）验证了企业AI支出，超大规模云厂商（微软、谷歌、亚马逊、Meta）到2024-2025年将AI资本开支提升至数千亿美元。美联储于2024年9月开启降息（2020年以来首次），消除了零盈利AI应用的核心阻力。宏观处于金发女孩格局（通缩+增长，VIX 22至15，SMH +158%，成长跑赢价值+65.0），但极度窄幅（RSP跑输SPY -32.0%），印证大盘股集中。板块层面通讯（+129%）与科技（+100%）领涨。作为贝塔最高的AI应用篮子，它放大了整个AI建设周期，产生934%总回报，远超SPY的66%。","drivers":["ChatGPT November 2022 / OpenAI ~$10B investment","Fed rate cuts September 2024","hyperscaler AI capex $100B+","goldilocks disinflation quad SMH +158%","extreme narrow breadth RSP -32% vs SPY"],"drivers_zh":["2022年11月ChatGPT/OpenAI约百亿美元投资","2024年9月美联储降息","超大规模云厂商AI资本开支超千亿","金发女孩通缩象限SMH +158%","极度窄幅广度RSP跑输SPY -32%"],"prev_key":"2022-12-28","prev_key_chain":["2022-12-28"],"status":"exact","title":"ChatGPT supercycle: highest-beta AI winner","title_zh":"ChatGPT超级周期：贝塔最高的AI赢家","turn_id":"ai_agents:trough:2022-12"},"2025-02-13":{"body":"A 38% selloff from February 13 to April 8, 2025 as two shocks converged: DeepSeek's January 2025 cheap-model reveal (official training cost claimed at ~$5.6M) ignited fears that commoditized foundation models would gut application-layer economics, and the April 2 'Liberation Day' tariff announcement sent VIX from 15 to 52 in a pure flight-to-safety panic. Tech fell -24.7% versus SPY -18.3%; defensives held relatively (staples -5.7%, utilities -7.3% vs cyclicals -18.0%), and high-beta was crushed (SPHB-SPLV -20.9). As the highest-beta AI application corner, the basket amplified both the model-commoditization fear and the macro risk-off into the April 8 trough.","body_zh":"自2025年2月13日至4月8日下跌38%，两大冲击共振：DeepSeek于2025年1月揭示廉价模型（官方训练成本声称约560万美元），引发对基础模型商品化将侵蚀应用层经济效益的担忧；4月2日\"解放日\"对等关税宣布，VIX从15暴涨至52，触发纯粹的避险恐慌。科技下跌-24.7%（vs SPY -18.3%）；防御股相对抗跌（必需消费-5.7%、公用事业-7.3% vs 周期股-18.0%），高贝塔遭重创（SPHB-SPLV -20.9）。作为贝塔最高的AI应用领域，篮子将模型商品化担忧与宏观风险规避双双放大至4月8日低谷。","drivers":["DeepSeek cheap-model scare January 2025","Liberation Day tariffs April 2 2025","VIX 15 to 52 flight-to-safety panic","high-beta crushed SPHB-SPLV -20.9","model commoditization fear"],"drivers_zh":["2025年1月DeepSeek廉价模型冲击","2025年4月2日解放日对等关税","VIX 15至52避险恐慌","高贝塔重创SPHB-SPLV -20.9","模型商品化担忧"],"prev_key":"2025-02-13","prev_key_chain":["2025-02-13"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek scare plus Liberation Day tariff crash","title_zh":"DeepSeek冲击叠加\"解放日\"关税崩盘","turn_id":"ai_agents:peak:2025-02"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"A 93% surge from April 8 to October 9, 2025 driven by the 90-day US-China tariff pause (April 9) and explosive enterprise adoption of agentic AI platforms: Salesforce Agentforce surpassed 8,000 customer deals (about half paid) with Data Cloud and AI ARR crossing the $900M-$1B milestone over FY25 into Q1 FY26; ServiceNow, Microsoft Copilot 365, and Azure AI gained mass enterprise adoption. The macro was goldilocks (VIX 52 to 16, SMH +91.8%, Tech +61.9%, DXY -3.3%) and high-beta dominated by +61.1%. The basket amplified the index (SPY +36%) by 2.6x in a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP lagged SPY -11.1%), leading to the October 2025 peak before the Hormuz oil shock reversed the cycle.","body_zh":"自2025年4月8日至10月9日，涨幅达93%，受美中关税90天暂停（4月9日）以及企业级智能体AI平台爆炸式采用驱动：Salesforce Agentforce在FY25至Q1 FY26期间突破8000家客户成交（约半数付费），数据云与AI的ARR跨越9亿至10亿美元里程碑；ServiceNow、微软Copilot 365与Azure AI获得大规模企业采用。宏观处于金发女孩格局（VIX从52崩至16、SMH +91.8%、科技+61.9%、DXY -3.3%），高贝塔主导+61.1%。篮子以2.6倍放大SPY的+36%涨幅，在窄幅大盘股行情中（RSP跑输SPY -11.1%）引领上涨，于2025年10月峰值前见顶，随后霍尔木兹石油冲击逆转周期。","drivers":["US-China tariff pause April 9 2025","Agentforce/Copilot enterprise wave","VIX 52 to 16 violent reset","semis +91.8% goldilocks quad","high-beta dominated +61.1%"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月9日美中关税暂停","Agentforce/Copilot企业浪潮","VIX 52至16猛烈重置","芯片+91.8%金发女孩象限","高贝塔主导+61.1%"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff pause ignites agentic-AI enterprise surge","title_zh":"关税暂停点燃智能体AI企业浪潮","turn_id":"ai_agents:trough:2025-04"},"2025-10-09":{"body":"A 49.5% collapse from October 9, 2025 to April 10, 2026, the deepest in the AI complex, driven by the 2026 Hormuz crisis: after US-Israel attacks on Iran beginning February 2026, Iran disrupted Strait of Hormuz tanker traffic, causing the largest oil-market disruption in history (WTI above $90, oil +57.0% in this window). The Fed maintained a hiking bias as energy-driven inflation re-accelerated; growth lagged value by -15.6 percentage points, Energy (+31.7%) and Materials (+18.3%) led as the quad turned reflation/growth-up but with duration pain crushing the AI application layer. Breadth broadened (RSP +2.9% vs SPY) as the narrow mega-cap AI trade unwound, and the basket lost half its value while SPY gained +1.8%.","body_zh":"自2025年10月9日至2026年4月10日崩跌49.5%，整个AI板块最深回撤，由2026年霍尔木兹危机驱动：美国-以色列于2026年2月对伊朗发动攻击后，伊朗扰乱霍尔木兹海峡油轮通行，造成史上最大石油市场中断（WTI突破$90，油价在本阶段涨+57.0%）。美联储维持加息倾向，因能源驱动的通胀重新加速；成长跑输价值-15.6个百分点，能源（+31.7%）与材料（+18.3%）领涨，象限为再通胀/增长向上，但贴现率上升对AI应用层造成久期重压。广度转宽（RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%），窄幅大盘股AI交易瓦解，篮子腰斩而SPY仅涨+1.8%。","drivers":["2026 Hormuz crisis oil +57.0%","Fed hiking bias inflation re-acceleration","growth lags value -15.6%","duration pain on unprofitable AI names","Energy +31.7% Materials +18.3% rotation"],"drivers_zh":["2026年霍尔木兹危机油价+57.0%","美联储加息倾向通胀重新加速","成长跑输价值-15.6%","无盈利AI个股久期重压","能源+31.7%、材料+18.3%轮动"],"prev_key":"2025-10-09","prev_key_chain":["2025-10-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Hormuz oil shock and Fed bias, deepest AI drawdown","title_zh":"霍尔木兹石油冲击与美联储加息倾向，AI最深回撤","turn_id":"ai_agents:peak:2025-10"},"2026-04-10":{"body":"The April 2026 US-Iran ceasefire and Iran's offer to reopen the Strait of Hormuz triggered a 40% high-beta snapback from April 10 to June 1: VIX fell from 19 to 16, oil dropped -4.6%, semis surged +39.1%, Tech led at +37.1%, and growth beat value +8.6 in a reflation/growth-up quad. As the highest-beta AI corner, the basket amplified the index (SPY +11.4%) by 3.5x in a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP lagged SPY -5.4%). Whether this snapback extends into a new leg depends on agent platform revenue conversion from pilots to recurring ARR and rate stabilization, with the basket currently in Recovery phase as of late June 2026.","body_zh":"2026年4月美伊停火及伊朗提议重开霍尔木兹海峡，触发自4月10日至6月1日40%的高贝塔急速反弹：VIX从19降至16，油价下跌-4.6%，芯片飙升+39.1%，科技领涨+37.1%，成长跑赢价值+8.6，处于再通胀/增长向上象限。作为贝塔最高的AI领域，篮子以3.5倍放大SPY的+11.4%涨幅，在窄幅大盘股行情中（RSP跑输SPY -5.4%）领涨。这一反弹能否延伸为新一轮上涨，取决于智能体平台能否将试点转化为经常性ARR以及利率走稳，截至2026年6月底篮子仍处于复苏阶段。","drivers":["US-Iran ceasefire April 2026","oil -4.6% Hormuz re-opening","semis +39.1% Tech +37.1% risk-on","VIX 19 to 16 high-beta reset","narrow breadth RSP -5.4%"],"drivers_zh":["2026年4月美伊停火","油价-4.6%霍尔木兹重开","芯片+39.1%、科技+37.1%风险偏好","VIX 19至16高贝塔重置","窄幅广度RSP -5.4%"],"prev_key":"2026-04-10","prev_key_chain":["2026-04-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Hormuz ceasefire high-beta snapback","title_zh":"停火后高贝塔急速反弹","turn_id":"ai_agents:trough:2026-04"}},"now":"The AI Agents and Applications basket is in a post-crash Recovery phase, sitting at just 18.1% of its prior cycle range after shedding 49.5% peak-to-trough between October 2025 and April 2026, the deepest drawdown in the AI complex, reflecting the basket's speculative, zero-profit, long-duration profile. The tape has turned reflation/growth-up (Tech +24.3%, Energy +21.5%, cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, DXY +3.4%), with VIX subdued in a 14-18 range, semis surging +67.9%, and high-beta crushing low-vol (+20.7%), all classic signals that the highest-beta AI corner finds its footing early in a recovery. However, a stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%) is a mild headwind for global-revenue names, and growth still trails value (-15.2%) on a trailing basis, meaning the basket's longest-duration, least-profitable components remain under pressure. The signal is BUY at a prime entry, but rs_rank of 37 versus the broader universe reflects the basket has not yet reclaimed leadership versus SPY; the setup hinges on whether the June 2026 Hormuz ceasefire sustains, enterprise agent adoption converts pilots to recurring revenue, and rates stabilize to permit multiple re-expansion.","now_zh":"AI智能体与应用篮子处于崩跌后的复苏期，历经2025年10月至2026年4月49.5%的峰谷跌幅（整个AI板块中最深），当前仅处于前周期区间的18.1%位置。行情已转为再通胀/增长向上格局（科技+24.3%、能源+21.5%、周期股+11.2% vs 防御股+6.9%、DXY +3.4%），VIX低位运行于14-18区间，芯片股飙升+67.9%，高贝塔大幅跑赢低波动（+20.7%）——这是贝塔最高的AI领域在复苏初期企稳的经典信号。然而美元走强（DXY +3.4%）对全球营收个股构成温和阻力，成长在滚动基础上仍跑输价值（-15.2%），意味着久期最长、盈利最差的成分股仍承压。信号为\"买入\"，处于黄金入场点，但相对全市场的rs_rank为37，表明篮子尚未夺回对SPY的领涨地位；后续走势取决于2026年6月霍尔木兹停火能否持续、企业智能体将试点转化为经常性收入，以及利率是否趋稳以支撑估值重扩张。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-ai_infra":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"From January 2014 through early March 2015, early AI-infrastructure precursors — data-center servers, networking gear, cloud-switch names — rose 41% as AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud began their first large-scale capacity ramp, driving enterprise workloads to the public cloud. The macro backdrop was a deflation-scare slowdown: oil -47%, copper-gold -18%, TLT +28%, DXY +18%, but semis surged +41% and growth outperformed value +5.4 in a ZIRP environment that supercharged long-duration tech multiples. The 41% gain doubled SPY (+18%), confirming the basket's high-beta character: defensives averaged +26% while cyclicals lagged at +13%, yet semis and cloud names outperformed both, driven by secular build rather than cyclical exposure.","body_zh":"2014年1月至2015年3月初，早期AI基础设施前驱——数据中心服务器、网络设备、云交换名称——上涨41%，得益于AWS、Azure和谷歌云开始大规模扩容，推动企业工作负载迁移至公有云。宏观背景为通缩恐慌放缓象限：油价-47%、铜金比-18%、TLT +28%、DXY +18%，但零利率政策环境下半导体+41%、成长跑赢价值+5.4，超长久期科技估值被放大。41%的涨幅是SPY（+18%）的两倍，印证了篮子的高贝塔特性：防御股均涨+26%而周期股仅+13%，但半导体与云名称均跑赢，由长期建设逻辑而非周期性敞口驱动。","drivers":["cloud capacity ramp (AWS/Azure/GCP)","ZIRP-driven duration re-rating","deflation-scare quad (TLT +28%)","oil shock tailwind (lower cost inputs)"],"drivers_zh":["云容量扩张（AWS/Azure/GCP）","零利率驱动的久期重估","通缩恐慌象限（TLT +28%）","油价下跌降低成本"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Cloud buildout melt-up, deflation-scare quad","title_zh":"通缩恐慌象限中的云基础设施熔涨","turn_id":"ai_infra:trough:2014-01"},"2015-03-02":{"body":"From March through late September 2015, AI-infrastructure names fell 23% as China's surprise yuan devaluation on August 11 detonated a global risk-off event: SSE dropped 43% in weeks, VIX spiked from 13 to 28, and the market entered a flight-to-safety rotation where defensives (-5.8%) led while cyclicals plummeted (-13.7%) and semis sold off -18%. The basket's 23% drop — more than double SPY's -10% — reflected its high-beta leveraged nature in a growth-scare environment where falling copper-gold (-10.5%) and oil (-10.4%) confirmed the deflation/slowdown quad.","body_zh":"2015年3月至9月底，AI基础设施名称下跌23%，因中国于8月11日突然贬值人民币引爆全球避险情绪：上证指数在数周内下跌43%，VIX从13飙升至28，市场进入避险轮动，防御股（-5.8%）领先、周期股暴跌（-13.7%）、半导体下跌-18%。篮子23%的跌幅超过SPY（-10%）两倍以上，反映出在成长恐慌环境中的高贝塔杠杆特性——铜金比（-10.5%）和油价（-10.4%）下跌印证了通缩/放缓象限。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation (Aug 11, 2015)","global growth scare","flight-to-safety (VIX 13 to 28)","semis -18% beta amplification"],"drivers_zh":["中国人民币贬值（2015年8月11日）","全球增长恐慌","避险（VIX 13至28）","半导体-18%贝塔放大"],"prev_key":"2015-03-02","prev_key_chain":["2015-03-02"],"status":"exact","title":"China devaluation risk-off selloff, -23%","title_zh":"人民币贬值引发的避险抛售，-23%","turn_id":"ai_infra:peak:2015-03"},"2015-09-28":{"body":"From late September 2015 through September 4, 2018 — a 36-month, 238% run — the basket rode the first hyperscaler capex supercycle as AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud ramped server, networking, and storage spending at 30%-plus annual rates. The macro was a reflation/growth-up quad: semis +139%, growth beat value +28.2, high-beta beat low-vol +20.5, VIX fell 28 to 13, and oil recovered +57%. The tape was narrow mega-cap-led (RSP -7.8% vs SPY), with cyclicals (+66%) far outpacing defensives (+37%), and tech +103% crowning the leadership. The early cloud-AI buildout (GPUs entering training workloads by 2016-2017) and Trump fiscal stimulus from early 2017 powered the final leg of the run.","body_zh":"2015年9月底至2018年9月4日——历时36个月、上涨238%——篮子乘上首个超大规模云厂商资本开支超级周期，AWS、Azure和谷歌云服务器、网络及存储支出以年均30%以上的速度扩张。宏观处于再通胀/增长向上象限：半导体+139%、成长跑赢价值+28.2、高贝塔跑赢低波动+20.5、VIX从28降至13、油价回升+57%。行情为窄幅大盘股主导（RSP跑输SPY -7.8%），周期股（+66%）大幅领先防御股（+37%），科技+103%居领导之冠。2016-2017年GPU进入训练工作负载的早期云AI建设，叠加2017年特朗普财政刺激，推动最后一段行情。","drivers":["hyperscaler capex ramp (AWS/Azure/GCP 30%+ annual growth)","ZIRP / reflation quad (VIX 28 to 13)","semis +139% (SMH)","Trump fiscal stimulus + tax cuts 2017"],"drivers_zh":["超大规模云厂商资本开支扩张（AWS/Azure/GCP年均增速30%+）","零利率/再通胀象限（VIX 28至13）","半导体+139%（SMH）","特朗普财政刺激与2017年减税"],"prev_key":"2015-09-28","prev_key_chain":["2015-09-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Hyperscaler capex supercycle, ZIRP-fueled +238%","title_zh":"超大规模云厂商资本开支超级周期，零利率驱动+238%","turn_id":"ai_infra:trough:2015-09"},"2018-09-04":{"body":"From September 4 to December 24, 2018, the basket shed 26.3% as the Fed hiked rates four times that year (funds rate to 2.5%), Powell signaled further hikes in December, and trade-war tariffs on $200B of Chinese goods spooked earnings outlooks for semiconductor and server supply chains. It was a full risk-off flush: VIX exploded 13 to 36, defensives (-7.2%) dramatically outperformed cyclicals (-21.7%), and semis fell -24.8% vs SPY -18.3%. As a high-multiple, long-duration group the basket amplified the rate-shock de-rating; FAANG names entered bear market territory by November 2018.","body_zh":"2018年9月4日至12月24日，篮子下跌26.3%，因美联储全年四次加息（联邦基金利率至2.5%）、鲍威尔12月发出进一步加息信号，以及对华2000亿美元商品关税令半导体和服务器供应链盈利展望承压。这是一次全面的风险厌恶冲洗：VIX从13飙至36、防御股（-7.2%）大幅跑赢周期股（-21.7%）、半导体下跌-24.8% vs SPY -18.3%。作为高估值、长久期群体，篮子放大了利率冲击下的估值重置；FAANG名称至2018年11月均进入熊市区间。","drivers":["Fed rate hikes to 2.5% (Dec 2018)","Powell hawkish December guidance","US-China trade war tariffs ($200B)","VIX 13 to 36 risk-off flush"],"drivers_zh":["美联储加息至2.5%（2018年12月）","鲍威尔鹰派12月指引","美中贸易战关税（2000亿美元）","VIX 13至36风险厌恶冲洗"],"prev_key":"2018-09-04","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed rate shock and trade-war peak, -26%","title_zh":"美联储利率冲击与贸易战见顶，-26%","turn_id":"ai_infra:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"From Christmas Eve 2018 through February 13, 2020 — a 14-month, 87% run — the basket recovered sharply as Powell pivoted on January 4, 2019, signaling 'patience' on rate hikes and ultimately cutting rates three times in H2 2019. Cloud-revenue reacceleration from AWS (+37% YoY by Q1 2019) and Azure confirmed the hyperscaler buildout cycle was intact. The macro was a reflation/growth-up quad: semis +90%, growth beat value +22.4, VIX fell 36 to 14, with narrow mega-cap leadership (RSP -6.5% vs SPY). TLT +21.6% showed ongoing rate-fall support for long-duration tech even as oil recovered +21%.","body_zh":"2018年圣诞节至2020年2月13日——历时14个月、上涨87%——篮子大幅回升，因鲍威尔于2019年1月4日转向，发出加息'耐心'信号并在2019年下半年三次降息。AWS（2019年一季度同比增速+37%）和Azure的云收入再加速印证了超大规模云厂商建设周期完整无缺。宏观处于再通胀/增长向上象限：半导体+90%、成长跑赢价值+22.4、VIX从36降至14，行情为窄幅大盘股主导（RSP跑输SPY -6.5%）。TLT +21.6%显示即便油价回升+21%，利率下行仍支撑长久期科技估值。","drivers":["Powell pivot (Jan 4, 2019)","Fed rate cuts x3 (H2 2019)","cloud revenue reacceleration (AWS +37%)","semis +90% risk-on melt-up"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔转向（2019年1月4日）","美联储三次降息（2019年下半年）","云收入再加速（AWS +37%）","半导体+90%风险偏好熔涨"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell pivot + cloud earnings reaccelerate, +87%","title_zh":"鲍威尔转向叠加云收入再加速，+87%","turn_id":"ai_infra:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-13":{"body":"From February 13 to March 18, 2020 — just 24 trading days — the basket collapsed 34.6% as COVID-19 spread globally and triggered a historic liquidity panic: VIX rocketed from 14 to 76, the broadest and fastest risk-off in a generation. Defensives (-18%) dramatically outperformed cyclicals (-37%), oil crashed -60% and semis fell -33% as every asset except US Treasuries was liquidated indiscriminately. Unlike later tech selloffs, AI-infra names had no pandemic-demand shelter at this stage — the selloff was pure systemic deleveraging, with SPY losing -29% and the basket amplifying at -35%.","body_zh":"2020年2月13日至3月18日——仅24个交易日——篮子崩跌34.6%，因新冠疫情全球蔓延引发历史性流动性恐慌：VIX从14飙至76，这是一代人中最广泛、最迅速的风险厌恶。防御股（-18%）大幅跑赢周期股（-37%），油价崩跌-60%，半导体下跌-33%，除美国国债外几乎所有资产均遭无差别抛售。与后来的科技抛售不同，此阶段AI基础设施名称尚无疫情需求庇护所——这是纯粹的系统性去杠杆，SPY损失-29%，篮子放大至-35%。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic shock (March 2020)","systemic deleveraging (VIX 14 to 76)","oil -60% demand collapse","indiscriminate liquidity selloff"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情冲击（2020年3月）","系统性去杠杆（VIX 14至76）","油价-60%需求崩塌","无差别流动性抛售"],"prev_key":"2020-02-13","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-13"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic panic selloff, -35%","title_zh":"新冠疫情恐慌性抛售，-35%","turn_id":"ai_infra:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"From March 18, 2020 through December 27, 2021 — 21 months, 259% — the basket exploded as the Fed cut to zero and launched unlimited QE on March 23, and the $2.2T CARES Act passed March 27. Work-from-home mandates triggered a structural pull-forward in cloud compute demand: Zoom hit 300M daily users by April 2020, AWS and Azure cloud revenues accelerated 30%+ YoY, and GPU-based inference loads began scaling. Semis surged +217%, high-beta crushed low-vol +160, breadth broadened (RSP +8.6% vs SPY), oil recovered +271%, and VIX normalized 76 to 18 — the most powerful reflation melt-up in the basket's history.","body_zh":"2020年3月18日至2021年12月27日——历时21个月、上涨259%——篮子爆涨，因美联储于3月23日降至零利率并启动无限量宽，2.2万亿美元CARES法案于3月27日通过。居家办公强制令引发云计算需求的结构性提前拉动：Zoom至2020年4月日活用户达3亿，AWS和Azure云收入年增速加速至30%以上，基于GPU的推理负载开始规模化。半导体+217%，高贝塔大幅跑赢低波动+160，市场广度转宽（RSP跑赢SPY +8.6%），油价回升+271%，VIX从76正常化至18——这是篮子历史上最强劲的再通胀熔涨。","drivers":["Fed zero rates + unlimited QE (March 23, 2020)","CARES Act $2.2T stimulus","WFH cloud demand pull-forward (AWS/Azure 30%+ growth)","semis +217% reflation melt-up"],"drivers_zh":["美联储零利率+无限量宽（2020年3月23日）","CARES法案2.2万亿美元刺激","居家办公云需求提前拉动（AWS/Azure增速30%+）","半导体+217%再通胀熔涨"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed QE + WFH cloud demand boom, +259%","title_zh":"美联储量化宽松叠加居家办公云需求爆发，+259%","turn_id":"ai_infra:trough:2020-03"},"2021-12-27":{"body":"From late December 2021 through July 1, 2022, the basket fell 36.9% as the Fed's pivot to aggressive tightening detonated a rate-shock de-rating of long-duration tech: TLT fell -21.4%, the dollar surged +9.4% in a stagflation-ish quad (Energy +32.1%, defensives -1.9% vs cyclicals -12.8%), and semis crashed -38.1% vs SPY -19.5%. Russia's invasion of Ukraine on February 24, 2022 added a second macro shock, pushing oil +43.5% and amplifying the risk-off impulse. This was a rate-regime and macro-event flush, not an AI-specific selloff — the group had no fundamental catalyst to offset brutal multiple compression as the growth-to-value spread inverted -16.8.","body_zh":"2021年12月底至2022年7月1日，篮子下跌36.9%，因美联储转向激进收紧引爆长久期科技的利率冲击估值重置：TLT下跌-21.4%，美元在类滞胀象限暴涨+9.4%（能源+32.1%，防御股-1.9% vs 周期股-12.8%），半导体崩跌-38.1% vs SPY -19.5%。2022年2月24日俄罗斯入侵乌克兰带来第二重宏观冲击，推动油价+43.5%并放大风险厌恶冲动。这是一次利率体制与宏观事件的冲洗，而非AI专项抛售——该板块没有任何基本面催化剂可以抵消随成长-价值利差逆转（-16.8）而来的残酷估值压缩。","drivers":["Fed rate-hike pivot (TLT -21.4%)","Russia-Ukraine invasion (Feb 24, 2022)","stagflation quad (oil +43.5%, DXY +9.4%)","growth-to-value spread -16.8, semis -38%"],"drivers_zh":["美联储加息转向（TLT -21.4%）","俄乌战争（2022年2月24日）","类滞胀象限（油价+43.5%，DXY +9.4%）","成长-价值利差-16.8，半导体-38%"],"prev_key":"2021-12-27","prev_key_chain":["2021-12-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-shock de-rating, flight-to-safety, -37%","title_zh":"利率冲击估值重置与避险抛售，-37%","turn_id":"ai_infra:peak:2021-12"},"2022-07-01":{"body":"In just six weeks from July 1 to August 15, 2022, the basket surged 29.4% on a sharp positioning-driven risk-on bounce as US CPI came in below expectations in July 2022, raising hopes that inflation had peaked and the Fed would pivot. The tape went into goldilocks mode: semis +25.8%, growth beat value +7.1, VIX cooled 27 to 20, and oil fell -17.5%. As one of the highest-beta growth baskets in the market, the group outperformed SPY (+12.5%) by more than double, but the rally had no AI-fundamental underpinning and defensives lagged (5.1% vs cyclicals 13.6%), confirming this was pure risk-on rotation.","body_zh":"仅六周内（2022年7月1日至8月15日），篮子在仓位驱动的风险偏好反弹中暴涨29.4%，因2022年7月美国CPI低于预期，引发通胀见顶、美联储转向的希望。行情进入金发女孩模式：半导体+25.8%、成长跑赢价值+7.1、VIX从27降至20、油价下跌-17.5%。作为市场中贝塔最高的成长篮子之一，该板块以SPY（+12.5%）两倍以上的幅度跑赢，但反弹没有任何AI基本面支撑，防御股落后（5.1% vs 周期股13.6%），印证了这是纯粹的风险偏好轮动。","drivers":["July 2022 CPI surprise (below expectations)","Fed pivot expectation","risk-on melt-up (semis +25.8%, VIX 27 to 20)","oversold high-beta positioning bounce"],"drivers_zh":["2022年7月CPI惊喜（低于预期）","押注美联储转向","风险偏好熔涨（半导体+25.8%，VIX 27至20）","超卖高贝塔仓位反弹"],"prev_key":"2022-07-01","prev_key_chain":["2022-07-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-inflation pivot hope, risk-on bounce, +29%","title_zh":"通胀见顶/转向预期推动风险偏好反弹，+29%","turn_id":"ai_infra:trough:2022-07"},"2022-08-15":{"body":"From August 15 to October 14, 2022, the basket shed 29.7% as Powell's August 26 Jackson Hole speech — the shortest and most hawkish in years — killed the pivot trade. He warned of 'some pain' ahead and committed to higher-for-longer rates, sending the Dow down 1,000 points that day. TLT fell -14.2% and the dollar ripped +6.3% in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad; VIX spiked 20 to 32. The move was broad-and-rate-driven (cyclicals -13.4%, defensives -12.5%), but as the most rate-sensitive corner of tech, the long-duration buildout led the laggards with semis -29.8% vs SPY -16.3%.","body_zh":"2022年8月15日至10月14日，篮子下跌29.7%，因鲍威尔于8月26日杰克逊霍尔会议发表数年来最短、最鹰派的演讲，终结了转向交易。他警告前方'有些痛苦'并承诺利率'更高更久'，当日道琼斯指数下跌1000点。TLT在放缓/通缩恐慌象限下跌-14.2%，美元暴涨+6.3%，VIX从20飙至32。这是一次广泛且由利率驱动的下跌（周期股-13.4%，防御股-12.5%），但作为科技板块对利率最敏感的领域，长久期建设股领跌——半导体-29.8% vs SPY -16.3%。","drivers":["Powell Jackson Hole speech Aug 26, 2022","rate-regime move (TLT -14.2%)","stronger dollar (+6.3% DXY)","VIX 20 to 32 risk-off"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔杰克逊霍尔演讲（2022年8月26日）","利率体制移动（TLT -14.2%）","美元走强（DXY +6.3%）","VIX 20至32风险厌恶"],"prev_key":"2022-08-15","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Hawkish Jackson Hole resets rates, -30%","title_zh":"鹰派杰克逊霍尔会议重置利率，-30%","turn_id":"ai_infra:peak:2022-08"},"2022-10-14":{"body":"From the October 2022 low through July 10, 2024 — 21 months, 261% — ChatGPT's November 30, 2022 launch detonated the generative-AI capex supercycle, with Nvidia H100 GPU demand sold out through Q1 2024 and hyperscalers pledging hundreds of billions in data-center buildout. The macro was a goldilocks disinflation quad: semis surged +231% (SMH), growth beat value +55.3, VIX fell 32 to 13, DXY weakened -7.3%, but breadth was the narrowest on record (RSP -28.4% vs SPY) as mega-cap AI names dominated. The Fed's first rate cut in September 2024 provided a final boost, but the fundamental driver was the unprecedented GPU-order cycle and hyperscaler capex commitments.","body_zh":"2022年10月低点至2024年7月10日——历时21个月、上涨261%——ChatGPT于2022年11月30日发布引爆生成式AI资本开支超级周期，英伟达H100 GPU需求排单至2024年一季度，超大规模云厂商承诺数千亿美元数据中心建设。宏观处于金发女孩去通胀象限：半导体暴涨+231%（SMH）、成长跑赢价值+55.3、VIX从32降至13、DXY走弱-7.3%，但市场广度创历史最窄（RSP跑输SPY -28.4%），由大盘AI名称主导。2024年9月美联储首次降息提供最后助力，但基本面驱动力是前所未有的GPU订单周期与超大规模云厂商资本开支承诺。","drivers":["ChatGPT launch (Nov 30, 2022)","Nvidia H100 GPU demand supercycle","hyperscaler capex pledges (Meta/Microsoft/Amazon/Google)","Fed first cut Sep 2024 (final boost)"],"drivers_zh":["ChatGPT发布（2022年11月30日）","英伟达H100 GPU需求超级周期","超大规模云厂商资本开支承诺（Meta/微软/亚马逊/谷歌）","美联储2024年9月首次降息（最后助力）"],"prev_key":"2022-10-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-14"],"status":"exact","title":"ChatGPT ignites genAI capex supercycle, +261%","title_zh":"ChatGPT引爆生成式AI资本开支超级周期，+261%","turn_id":"ai_infra:trough:2022-10"},"2024-07-10":{"body":"From July 10 to August 7, 2024 — just four weeks — the basket crashed 26.3% as the Bank of Japan hiked rates on July 31 and announced QE tapering, triggering the unwinding of an estimated $4 trillion in yen-carry positions. Crowded AI-compute longs were the hardest-hit: VIX exploded 13 to 28, defensives led (+2.2%) while cyclicals fell -5.5%, and breadth broadened (RSP +6.6% vs SPY) in a classic deleveraging signature. Semis fell -24.8% (SMH) vs SPY -7.6%; the AI-infrastructure buildout narrative was unchanged, but the basket functioned as a high-beta leveraged long subject to forced liquidation.","body_zh":"2024年7月10日至8月7日——仅四周——篮子崩跌26.3%，因日本银行于7月31日加息并宣布缩减量宽，触发约4万亿美元日元套息仓位的解除。拥挤的AI算力多头受冲击最重：VIX从13爆涨至28、防御股领先（+2.2%）而周期股下跌-5.5%、市场广度转宽（RSP跑赢SPY +6.6%），呈现经典的去杠杆特征。半导体下跌-24.8%（SMH）vs SPY -7.6%；AI基础设施建设叙事未变，但篮子作为高贝塔杠杆多头遭强制平仓。","drivers":["BOJ rate hike (July 31, 2024) + QE taper","yen-carry unwind (estimated $4T)","flight-to-safety (VIX 13 to 28)","forced liquidation of crowded AI longs"],"drivers_zh":["日本银行加息（2024年7月31日）+缩减量宽","日元套息交易平仓（约4万亿美元）","避险（VIX 13至28）","拥挤AI多头强制平仓"],"prev_key":"2024-07-10","prev_key_chain":["2024-07-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Yen-carry unwind air-pocket, -26%","title_zh":"日元套息交易平仓的空气陷阱，-26%","turn_id":"ai_infra:peak:2024-07"},"2024-08-07":{"body":"From August 7, 2024 through January 22, 2025 — about 5 months, +50% — the basket recovered as the yen-carry shock cleared and hyperscaler capex guidance from Q2 and Q3 2024 earnings reaccelerated: Microsoft guided Azure growth to 34-35% for FY2025, AWS and Google Cloud posted accelerating cloud quarters. The macro was a goldilocks tape: semis +27%, growth beat value +13.9, VIX cooled 28 to 15 in a narrow mega-cap-led tape (RSP -5.7% vs SPY). TLT fell -7.2% and DXY firmed +4.8% but the buildout reclaimed leadership, with Trump's election in November 2024 adding a deregulatory tailwind.","body_zh":"2024年8月7日至2025年1月22日——约5个月、+50%——篮子回升，因日元套息冲击消退，2024年二三季度财报中超大规模云厂商资本开支指引再加速：微软指引Azure增速2025财年达34-35%，AWS和谷歌云均录得加速的云季度增长。宏观处于金发女孩行情：半导体+27%、成长跑赢价值+13.9，VIX从28降至15，行情为窄幅大盘股主导（RSP跑输SPY -5.7%）。TLT下跌-7.2%，DXY走强+4.8%，但建设股夺回领导地位，特朗普2024年11月当选还带来放松监管的顺风。","drivers":["hyperscaler Q2-Q3 2024 capex guidance reacceleration","Trump election Nov 2024 (deregulatory tailwind)","narrow risk-on (semis +27%, VIX 28 to 15)","carry shock cleared, AI narrative intact"],"drivers_zh":["超大规模云厂商2024年二三季度资本开支指引再加速","特朗普2024年11月当选（放松监管顺风）","窄幅风险偏好（半导体+27%，VIX 28至15）","套息冲击消退，AI叙事完整"],"prev_key":"2024-08-07","prev_key_chain":["2024-08-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Hyperscaler capex resumes, narrow risk-on, +50%","title_zh":"超大规模云厂商资本开支重启，窄幅风险偏好，+50%","turn_id":"ai_infra:trough:2024-08"},"2025-01-22":{"body":"From January 22 to April 4, 2025, the basket collapsed 37.6% in two sequential shocks: DeepSeek's January 27 claim of training a frontier model for under $6M triggered Nvidia's largest-ever single-day market-cap loss ($589B) as investors questioned whether the GPU-intensive buildout thesis was intact; then Trump's April 2 Liberation Day tariffs — the largest import-duty hike in modern US history — crashed markets broadly. VIX rocketed 15 to 45, high-beta crushed low-vol by -27.1 (SPHB vs SPLV), defensives held (-2.2%) while cyclicals collapsed -16.3%, and semis fell -32.3% vs SPY -16.4%.","body_zh":"2025年1月22日至4月4日，篮子在两次连续冲击中崩跌37.6%：DeepSeek于1月27日宣称以不足600万美元训练出前沿模型，引发英伟达史上最大单日市值损失（5890亿美元），投资者质疑GPU密集型建设逻辑是否依然成立；随后特朗普4月2日的'解放日'关税——美国现代史上最大的进口关税加征——广泛冲击市场。VIX从15飙至45，高贝塔相对低波动暴跌-27.1（SPHB vs SPLV），防御股守住（-2.2%）而周期股崩跌-16.3%，半导体下跌-32.3% vs SPY -16.4%。","drivers":["DeepSeek Jan 27, 2025 (Nvidia -17%, $589B loss)","compute-efficiency threat to capex thesis","Liberation Day tariffs Apr 2, 2025","VIX 15 to 45, high-beta -27.1"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek 2025年1月27日（英伟达-17%，损失5890亿美元）","算力效率威胁资本开支逻辑","解放日关税2025年4月2日","VIX 15至45，高贝塔-27.1"],"prev_key":"2025-01-22","prev_key_chain":["2025-01-22"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek scare + Liberation Day tariffs, -38%","title_zh":"DeepSeek恐慌叠加解放日关税，-38%","turn_id":"ai_infra:peak:2025-01"},"2025-04-04":{"body":"From April 4, 2025 through June 22, 2026 — the basket surged 465%, the largest single leg in its history, as the tariff pause on April 9 halted the Liberation Day selloff and the US-China 90-day tariff truce on May 12 unlocked $837B of mega-cap market-cap in a single session. Hyperscaler Q1 2025 earnings then confirmed collective 2026 capex guidance of $725B (+77% YoY), with Nvidia's Blackwell GPU ramp providing the hardware spine. VIX collapsed 45 to 17, semis surged +271% (SMH), high-beta crushed low-vol +124.5, and Tech led sector returns +112%, all in a reflation/growth-up quad. The breadth was mega-cap narrow (RSP -13.4% vs SPY), confirming the basket as the concentrated leveraged long of the AI-compute trade.","body_zh":"2025年4月4日至2026年6月22日——篮子飙升465%，为历史上最大单腿涨幅，因4月9日关税暂停终止了解放日抛售、5月12日美中90天关税休战在单日释放8370亿美元大盘股市值。超大规模云厂商2025年一季度财报随后确认2026年合计资本开支指引7250亿美元（同比+77%），英伟达Blackwell GPU产能爬坡提供硬件骨干。VIX从45崩至17，半导体+271%（SMH），高贝塔大幅跑赢低波动+124.5，科技领涨+112%，均处于再通胀/增长向上象限。市场广度为大盘股主导（RSP跑输SPY -13.4%），印证了篮子作为AI算力交易的集中杠杆多头地位。","drivers":["Liberation Day tariff pause (Apr 9) + US-China truce (May 12, 2025)","hyperscaler 2026 capex $725B confirmed (+77%)","Nvidia Blackwell GPU ramp","VIX 45 to 17, semis +271%"],"drivers_zh":["解放日关税暂停（4月9日）+美中关税休战（2025年5月12日）","超大规模云厂商2026年资本开支7250亿美元确认（+77%）","英伟达Blackwell GPU产能爬坡","VIX 45至17，半导体+271%"],"prev_key":"2025-04-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff pause + hyperscaler capex rebound, +465%","title_zh":"关税暂停叠加超大规模云厂商资本开支反弹，+465%","turn_id":"ai_infra:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"AI Infrastructure is topping after a near-vertical 465% run off the April 2025 tariff low, a textbook macro risk-on melt-up (SMH +271%, VIX collapsed 45 to 17) driven by resurgent hyperscaler capex commitments ($725B guided for 2026). The basket sits at the 84.7th percentile of its range (phase: topping), RS rank 5 vs peers, above the 200-day with a SELL signal. The current quad is reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%), led by Tech +24.3% and Energy, while Comm (-9.6%) and Discretionary (-5.2%) lag. The June 2026 Broadcom guidance miss (Q3 AI chip revenue guided at $16B vs $17.2B expected, full-year target unchanged) cracked leadership just as the Fed dot-plot turned hawkish and the DXY firmed +3.4% — classic topping fingerprint: the AI-capex narrative is intact but marginal numbers are disappointing into a tighter-money, stronger-dollar tape, and high-beta positions amplify any wobble in hyperscaler capex confidence.","now_zh":"AI基础设施在2025年4月关税低点飙升465%后进入顶部区域，这是一次教科书式的宏观风险偏好熔涨（SMH +271%，VIX从45崩至17），由超大规模云厂商资本开支承诺（2026年预计7250亿美元）驱动。篮子处于历史分位84.7%（阶段：筑顶），相对强度排名第5，位于200日均线上方并出现卖出信号。当前象限为再通胀/增长向上（周期股+11.2% vs 防御股+6.9%，油价+19.2%，铜金比+18.3%），由科技+24.3%和能源领涨，通信（-9.6%）和非必需消费品（-5.2%）落后。2026年6月Broadcom业绩指引失望（第三季度AI芯片营收展望160亿美元，低于市场预期172亿美元且未上调全年目标），令领导地位动摇，恰逢美联储点阵图转鹰、DXY走强+3.4%——经典的顶部特征：AI资本开支叙事完整，但边际数据令人失望，面临更紧缩的货币环境，高贝塔头寸现在放大任何超大规模云厂商资本开支信心的波动。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"semis.top_2026.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"semis.top_2026.v1","arch_state":"pass","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-ai_neoclouds":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"Small-cap cloud and HPC-adjacent hosting names surged 103% in H1 2014 as ultra-easy Fed policy (taper only beginning at $10B/month in January 2014) kept real borrowing costs depressed and drove speculative capital into high-beta growth. The quad was stagflation-ish: yields fell (TLT +12.4%) despite oil rising +7.4%, defensives led (Utilities +15.5%, Energy +15.3%), and semis outperformed (SMH +21.1% vs SPY +9.0%). These pre-AI hosting names rode the cloud-infrastructure speculation wave of 2013-14, where enterprise cloud-adoption narratives justified premium small-cap-tech valuations even as the broader tape rotated defensively.","body_zh":"2014年上半年，小市值云计算和HPC相邻托管个股飙升103%，彼时美联储极度宽松（2014年1月才以每月仅缩减100亿美元的节奏开始Taper）压低了实际借贷成本，驱动投机性资本涌入高贝塔成长股。宏观象限呈类滞胀：收益率下行（TLT +12.4%），尽管油价上涨+7.4%，防御股领涨（公用事业+15.5%、能源+15.3%），半导体跑赢SPY（SMH +21.1% vs SPY +9.0%）。这批AI前时代托管个股乘的是2013-14年企业云采用叙事浪潮，小市值科技公司享受溢价估值，尽管大盘整体防御性旋转。","drivers":["QE taper slow-pace tailwind","speculative cloud infrastructure demand","yield collapse (TLT +12.4%)","high-beta amplification"],"drivers_zh":["QE缩减慢速顺风","投机性云基础设施需求","收益率下行(TLT +12.4%)","高贝塔放大效应"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Speculative cloud melt-up on QE tailwind","title_zh":"QE顺风中投机性云计算熔涨","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:trough:2014-01"},"2014-07-14":{"body":"The basket collapsed 65.7% over 16 months as the macro regime shifted into a slowdown/deflation-scare quad: the DXY surged +23.4% (strongest dollar rally in years), oil crashed -59.6% after OPEC abandoned its production-floor defense in November 2014, and the dollar surge fueled a global growth scare. Credit deteriorated (HYG-LQD -7.0%) and high-beta was crushed (SPHB-SPLV -17.6%) while VIX rose 12 to 20. These capital-intensive, leveraged, no-earnings hosting names were particularly punished in the risk-off flight that saw defensives lead (+9.4%) and cyclicals fall (-0.7%).","body_zh":"该篮子在16个月内下跌65.7%，因宏观切换至放缓/通缩恐慌象限：DXY飙升+23.4%（年内最强美元涨势）、油价在欧佩克2014年11月放弃产量下限防御后暴跌-59.6%，全球增长恐慌随美元走强而蔓延。信用市场恶化（HYG-LQD -7.0%），高贝塔遭重创（SPHB-SPLV -17.6%），VIX从12升至20。这批重资本、高杠杆、无盈利的托管个股在避险抛售中首当其冲，防御股领涨（+9.4%），周期股下跌（-0.7%）。","drivers":["oil crash -59.6% (OPEC Nov 2014)","DXY surge +23.4%","global growth scare / risk-off","credit deterioration (HYG-LQD -7.0%)"],"drivers_zh":["油价暴跌-59.6%(欧佩克2014年11月)","DXY飙升+23.4%","全球增长恐慌/风险规避","信用恶化(HYG-LQD -7.0%)"],"prev_key":"2014-07-14","prev_key_chain":["2014-07-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil crash and dollar surge wipe out high-beta","title_zh":"油价崩盘与美元飙升抹平高贝塔涨幅","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:peak:2014-07"},"2015-11-13":{"body":"From the November 2015 trough the basket surged 397.5% over 25 months in an epic reflation/growth-up regime. The initial catalyst was the global growth scare bottoming (China-devaluation impact fading, oil finding a floor in early 2016), followed by Trump's November 2016 election igniting a pro-cyclical reflationary melt-up (Tech +58.8%, Financials +49.9%, Industrials +47.1%, semis +97.4%). The dollar fell -5.6%, oil rallied +41.0%, copper-gold rose +27.5%, and VIX compressed from 20 to 10. The Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (December 2017) provided the final fuel, boosting capex outlooks for data-center-adjacent infrastructure names.","body_zh":"自2015年11月底部起，篮子在25个月内狂涨397.5%，进入史诗级再通胀/增长向上机制。初始催化剂是全球增长恐慌触底（中国贬值冲击消退、油价2016年初寻底），随后特朗普2016年11月大选点燃顺周期再通胀熔涨（科技+58.8%、金融+49.9%、工业+47.1%、半导体+97.4%）。美元下跌-5.6%、油价反弹+41.0%、铜金比上升+27.5%、VIX从20压缩至10。2017年12月《减税与就业法案》提供最后一把火，提振了数据中心周边基础设施个股的资本支出预期。","drivers":["global growth scare bottom","Trump election pro-cyclical melt-up","Tax Cuts and Jobs Act Dec 2017","semis melt-up (SMH +97.4%)"],"drivers_zh":["全球增长恐慌触底","特朗普大选顺周期熔涨","2017年12月减税与就业法案","半导体熔涨(SMH +97.4%)"],"prev_key":"2015-11-13","prev_key_chain":["2015-11-13"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump-era reflation and tech melt-up ignite","title_zh":"特朗普再通胀与科技熔涨点燃","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:trough:2015-11"},"2017-12-19":{"body":"The basket sold off 53.8% between December 2017 and April 2018 as 'Volmageddon' struck on February 5, 2018: the VIX more than doubled (+116%, its largest one-day move ever, closing ~37) after strong January 2018 average-hourly-earnings data (+2.9% YoY, fastest since 2009) sparked rate-shock fears, blowing up the XIV short-volatility ETP. The S&P fell 4.1% that day (SPY -2.0% over the leg), staples most damaged (-8.1%) in a reflation-up quad (DXY -3.5%, oil +10.5%); the basket's extreme high-beta amplified the vol-shock. The February drop was compounded by Trump's first steel/aluminum tariffs (March 2018) keeping risk appetite suppressed.","body_zh":"篮子在2017年12月至2018年4月间下跌53.8%，因2018年2月5日\"波动率末日\"来袭：强劲的2018年1月平均时薪数据（同比+2.9%，为2009年以来最快）引发利率冲击恐惧，VIX单日翻倍有余（+116%，史上最大单日涨幅，收盘约37），做空波动率ETP XIV崩溃。当日标普下跌4.1%（本段SPY -2.0%），必需消费品损失最重（-8.1%），处于再通胀象限（DXY -3.5%、油价+10.5%）；篮子极高贝塔放大了波动率冲击。2月跌势随特朗普首批钢铝关税（2018年3月）叠加，持续压制风险偏好。","drivers":["Volmageddon Feb 5 2018 (VIX +116%)","wage inflation shock (Jan 2018 AHE +2.9%)","XIV ETP collapse","first Trump tariffs (steel/aluminum Mar 2018)"],"drivers_zh":["2018年2月5日波动率末日(VIX +116%)","工资通胀冲击(2018年1月时薪+2.9%)","XIV ETP崩溃","特朗普首批钢铝关税(2018年3月)"],"prev_key":"2017-12-19","prev_key_chain":["2017-12-19"],"status":"exact","title":"Volmageddon and rate shock pause rally","title_zh":"波动率灾难与利率冲击暂停涨势","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:peak:2017-12"},"2018-04-03":{"body":"The basket rallied 105.7% from April 2018 through April 2019 as the tape shifted into a growth-scare/slowdown quad where Tech (+24.1%) and Discretionary (+22.2%) led while Financials and Materials lagged. The Fed's December 2018 hike (the fourth of 2018, to 2.25-2.5%) was followed by Chair Powell's January 2019 pivot ('patient' language), igniting a relief rally. VIX fell from 21 to 12, the dollar firmed +8.2%, and semis rallied +18.1%, but breadth was narrow (RSP -2.9% vs SPY) confirming a mega-cap-led tape that still benefited the high-beta cloud/hosting cohort disproportionately.","body_zh":"篮子自2018年4月至2019年4月涨幅105.7%，行情切换至增长恐慌/放缓象限，科技（+24.1%）和可选消费（+22.2%）领涨，金融与材料落后。美联储2018年12月第四次加息（升至2.25%-2.5%）后，鲍威尔2019年1月发出\"耐心\"转向信号，引发解脱式反弹。VIX从21降至12，美元走强+8.2%，半导体反弹+18.1%，但广度窄幅（RSP跑输SPY -2.9%），确认为巨型股主导行情，但仍使高贝塔云/托管板块不成比例受益。","drivers":["Fed Dec 2018 hike + Jan 2019 pivot signal","VIX compression (21 to 12)","tech-led narrow tape","semis recovery (SMH +18.1%)"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2018年12月加息+2019年1月转向信号","VIX收缩(21降至12)","科技主导窄幅行情","半导体复苏(SMH +18.1%)"],"prev_key":"2018-04-03","prev_key_chain":["2018-04-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot hope sparks tech-led recovery","title_zh":"美联储转向预期引燃科技主导复苏","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:trough:2018-04"},"2019-04-23":{"body":"The basket collapsed 79.6% as global risk-off reached its most extreme reading since the GFC: VIX exploded from 12 to 76 (March 2020 COVID peak), defensives essentially flat (-1.1%) while cyclicals cratered -30.1%, credit spreads blew out (HYG-LQD -7.8%), oil collapsed -69.3% (Saudi-Russia price war compounding COVID demand destruction), and TLT surged +20.1% in a flight-to-quality. The basket — capital-intensive, leveraged, and lacking the cloud-revenue moat of hyperscalers — bore the full force of the March 2020 deleveraging, with breadth crushing mega-caps (RSP -9.2% vs SPY).","body_zh":"篮子暴跌79.6%，全球风险规避达到金融危机以来最极端水平：VIX从12暴涨至76（2020年3月新冠峰值），防御股基本持平（-1.1%），周期股崩溃-30.1%，信用利差飙升（HYG-LQD -7.8%），油价暴跌-69.3%（沙特-俄罗斯价格战叠加新冠需求破坏），TLT飙升+20.1%引发质量避险。这批重资本、高杠杆、缺乏超大规模云收入护城河的托管个股首当其冲，承受了2020年3月去杠杆的全部冲击，广度压制巨型股（RSP -9.2% vs SPY）。","drivers":["COVID March 2020 panic (VIX 12 to 76)","oil collapse -69.3% (Saudi-Russia war)","flight-to-quality (TLT +20.1%)","leveraged balance-sheet impairment"],"drivers_zh":["新冠2020年3月恐慌(VIX 12升至76)","油价崩溃-69.3%(沙俄价格战)","质量避险(TLT +20.1%)","杠杆资产负债表受损"],"prev_key":"2019-04-23","prev_key_chain":["2019-04-23"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash obliterates leveraged high-beta","title_zh":"新冠崩盘摧毁杠杆化高贝塔","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:peak:2019-04"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"From the March 18, 2020 trough the basket exploded 5,407% over 20 months — one of the largest small-cap-cohort rallies on record — riding the most powerful risk-on reflation since 2009. The Fed cut to zero (March 15, 2020), Congress passed the $2.2 trillion CARES Act (March 27, 2020) and subsequent multi-trillion rounds, the dollar fell -6.0%, VIX collapsed from 76 to 16, and semis surged +200% (SMH). The COVID-accelerated cloud-adoption boom plus the emergence of GPU-compute demand (early ML training workloads) transformed these data-center-adjacent names into infrastructure plays, while Bitcoin's 2020-21 bull market catalyzed former mining-company hosts.","body_zh":"自2020年3月18日底部，篮子在20个月内暴涨5407%——小市值板块有史以来最大涨幅之一——乘的是2009年以来最强风险偏好再通胀。美联储3月15日降息至零，国会3月27日通过2.2万亿美元CARES法案及后续数轮万亿级刺激，美元下跌-6.0%，VIX从76崩至16，半导体飙升+200%（SMH）。新冠加速的云采用热潮叠加GPU算力需求萌芽（早期ML训练工作负载）将这批数据中心周边个股转型为基础设施标的，而比特币2020-21年牛市催化了前矿企托管商。","drivers":["zero-rate CARES Act stimulus","cloud adoption acceleration","Bitcoin 2020-21 bull market","semis surge (SMH +200%)"],"drivers_zh":["零利率+CARES法案刺激","云采用加速","比特币2020-21年牛市","半导体飙升(SMH +200%)"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Stimulus surge lifts all high-beta boats","title_zh":"刺激洪流托举所有高贝塔","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-12":{"body":"These capital-intensive, high-beta names (many former bitcoin miners) collapsed 84% as the Fed's November 2021 taper announcement turned the rate cycle: yields surged (TLT -21.2%), the dollar exploded +10.0%, and VIX rose 16 to 29 in a stagflation-ish quad. It was a simultaneous flight-to-safety (defensives +1.8% vs cyclicals -13.7%) and crypto/leverage unwind: Bitcoin peaked near $69,000 in November 2021 and began a prolonged bear, stripping the mining-transition narrative. As the highest-beta corner with no established AI-compute revenue, the group massively amplified the index selloff (SMH -32.0% vs SPY -18.4%).","body_zh":"这些重资本、高贝塔个股（许多是前比特币矿企）暴跌84%，因美联储2021年11月Taper公告切换利率周期：收益率飙升（TLT -21.2%）、美元在类滞胀象限暴涨+10.0%、VIX从16升至29。这是避险抛售（防御股+1.8% vs 周期股-13.7%）与加密/杠杆平仓的叠加：比特币2021年11月触顶约69000美元后开始漫长熊市，剥去了矿企转型叙事。作为没有AI算力收入的最高贝塔领域，该板块巨幅放大了指数跌幅（SMH -32.0% vs SPY -18.4%）。","drivers":["Fed taper Nov 2021 / rate cycle turn","yields surge (TLT -21.2%) / DXY +10.0%","crypto collapse (BTC peaked Nov 2021)","flight-to-safety (VIX 16 to 29)"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2021年11月Taper/利率周期转向","收益率飙升(TLT -21.2%)/DXY +10.0%","加密崩溃(BTC 2021年11月见顶)","避险(VIX 16升至29)"],"prev_key":"2021-11-12","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Pre-pivot leverage wipeout in a dollar surge","title_zh":"美元飙升中转向前的杠杆崩塌","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:peak:2021-11"},"2022-06-30":{"body":"A 103% rip off washed-out lows reflected the basket's extreme high-beta character, firing on peak-inflation hopes as the tape went risk-on (SMH +21.0%, growth>value +7.0, VIX 29 to 20) in a goldilocks quad with oil falling -15.5%. July 2022 CPI (released August 10, 2022) at 8.5% vs 9.1% prior was the key catalyst, sparking soft-landing hopes. The bounce was pure positioning — the highest-beta group ripped hardest off an oversold extreme — and reversed sharply within weeks as Powell's Jackson Hole speech (August 26, 2022) reasserted hawkish intent.","body_zh":"从超卖低点暴涨103%，反映该篮子极高的贝塔属性，由通胀见顶预期点燃——2022年8月10日公布的7月CPI（8.5%，低于前值9.1%）是关键催化剂，市场行情转向风险偏好（SMH +21.0%、成长跑赢价值+7.0、VIX 29降至20），处于金发女孩象限、油价下跌-15.5%。这波反弹纯属仓位驱动——最高贝塔群体在超卖极值处反弹最猛——数周后随鲍威尔2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔讲话重申鹰派立场而急剧逆转。","drivers":["peak-inflation hope (Aug 2022 CPI miss)","oversold positioning squeeze","risk-on melt-up (SMH +21.0%, VIX 29 to 20)","oil fall -15.5%"],"drivers_zh":["通胀见顶预期(2022年8月CPI低于预期)","超卖仓位挤压","风险偏好熔涨(SMH +21.0%, VIX 29降至20)","油价下跌-15.5%"],"prev_key":"2022-06-30","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Violent oversold bounce on peak-inflation hope","title_zh":"通胀见顶预期中的剧烈超卖反弹","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-15":{"body":"Powell's August 26, 2022 Jackson Hole speech — a terse hawkish reset — and the November 2022 FTX collapse drove the basket to new cycle lows, down 64.4% into late December. Yields surged (TLT -12.8%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad; defensives held (-2.3%) vs cyclicals -6.7% in a broadening tape (RSP +3.9% vs SPY). Crypto-winter contagion (FTX collapsed November 8-11, 2022, Bitcoin fell below $16,000) directly impaired the mining-origin names in this basket, while the pre-AI cohort had neither the revenue nor the narrative to defend valuations (SMH -19.0% vs SPY -11.4%).","body_zh":"鲍威尔2022年8月26日在杰克逊霍尔发表的简短鹰派讲话及2022年11月FTX崩溃，将篮子推至周期新低，12月底跌幅64.4%。收益率飙升（TLT -12.8%），处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限；防御股守住（-2.3%）vs 周期股-6.7%，处于广度转宽行情（RSP跑赢SPY +3.9%）。加密寒冬传染（FTX 2022年11月8-11日崩溃，比特币跌破16000美元）直接损害了本篮子中矿企起源的个股，而AI前时代的这批个股既无收入也无叙事来支撑估值（SMH -19.0% vs SPY -11.4%）。","drivers":["Jackson Hole hawkishness Aug 26 2022","yields surge (TLT -12.8%)","FTX collapse Nov 2022 / crypto winter","no AI narrative defense"],"drivers_zh":["2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔鹰派表态","收益率飙升(TLT -12.8%)","FTX崩溃2022年11月/加密寒冬","缺乏AI叙事防守"],"prev_key":"2022-08-15","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkishness and crypto-winter new lows","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派表态与加密寒冬再创新低","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:peak:2022-08"},"2022-12-28":{"body":"From the December 28, 2022 low, ChatGPT's launch (November 30, 2022) created the GPU-cloud leasing thesis, and these high-beta hosts exploded 560% as compute scarcity made leased GPU capacity precious. The macro was a tech-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +60.4%, growth>value +25.8, VIX 22 to 14, DXY -4.5%) in a goldilocks quad, narrow at the top (RSP -9.5% vs SPY). The ChatGPT catalyst transformed distressed former miners (Applied Digital, TeraWulf, Hut 8) into AI-infrastructure plays; NVIDIA's May 24, 2023 earnings blowout (Q2 revenue guided to $11.0B vs ~$7.2B prior) confirmed the GPU-scarcity story and drove the final leg into the July 2023 peak.","body_zh":"自2022年12月28日低点，ChatGPT的发布（2022年11月30日）催生了GPU云租赁逻辑，这些高贝塔托管商暴涨560%，因算力稀缺使租赁GPU产能变得珍贵。宏观是科技引领的风险偏好熔涨（SMH +60.4%、成长跑赢价值+25.8、VIX 22降至14、DXY -4.5%），处于金发女孩象限、顶部窄幅（RSP跑输SPY -9.5%）。ChatGPT催化剂将困顿的前矿企（Applied Digital、TeraWulf、Hut 8）转变为AI基础设施标的；英伟达2023年5月24日业绩超预期（二季度营收指引110亿美元 vs 此前约72亿）确认了GPU稀缺故事，推动最后一段涨势直至2023年7月顶部。","drivers":["ChatGPT launch Nov 30 2022","GPU-cloud thesis birth","NVIDIA May 2023 earnings blowout","risk-on melt-up (SMH +60.4%, VIX 22 to 14)"],"drivers_zh":["ChatGPT发布2022年11月30日","GPU云逻辑诞生","英伟达2023年5月业绩超预期","风险偏好熔涨(SMH +60.4%, VIX 22降至14)"],"prev_key":"2022-12-28","prev_key_chain":["2022-12-28"],"status":"exact","title":"ChatGPT birth ignites GPU-cloud thesis","title_zh":"ChatGPT诞生点燃GPU云逻辑","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:trough:2022-12"},"2023-07-13":{"body":"A 57.1% pullback hit as the long end surged through autumn 2023 (TLT -17.6%): the 10-year yield climbed from ~3.75% in July to a 16-year high near 5.0% in October, driven by persistent above-target inflation prints and the Fed's higher-for-longer messaging. DXY firmed +6.4%, compounding the headwind. VIX rose 14 to 22, breadth narrowed (RSP -4.1% vs SPY), and the basket's capital-intensive, high-beta profile amplified the rate-driven drawdown (SMH -10.2% vs SPY -6.0%). Energy was the only sector to gain (+8.7%), while all growth-adjacent names sold off.","body_zh":"随着长端收益率在2023年秋季大幅攀升（TLT -17.6%）——10年期收益率从7月约3.75%攀升至10月16年高位约5.0%，由持续高于目标的通胀数据与美联储\"更高更久\"表态驱动——篮子回调57.1%。DXY走强+6.4%加剧阻力。VIX从14升至22，广度收窄（RSP跑输SPY -4.1%），篮子重资本、高贝塔属性放大了利率驱动的回撤（SMH -10.2% vs SPY -6.0%）。能源是唯一上涨板块（+8.7%），所有成长相关个股均告回调。","drivers":["10-yr yield surge to ~5.0% Oct 2023","DXY +6.4%","Fed higher-for-longer messaging","high-beta rate sensitivity (SMH -10.2%)"],"drivers_zh":["10年期收益率2023年10月飙至约5.0%","DXY +6.4%","美联储更高更久表态","高贝塔利率敏感性(SMH -10.2%)"],"prev_key":"2023-07-13","prev_key_chain":["2023-07-13"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate surge crushes high-beta in summer pullback","title_zh":"利率飙升在夏季回调中重创高贝塔","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:peak:2023-07"},"2023-10-20":{"body":"As the 10-year yield peaked near 5.0% in mid/late October 2023 and reversed hard (TLT +21.9% into year-end), these GPU hosts ripped 179.7% in just 68 days on insatiable AI-compute demand. Falling rates plus scarcity supercharged the high-beta move as risk-on turned violently (SMH +24.5%, VIX 22 to 12, DXY -4.9%). Powell's December 13, 2023 FOMC pivot (dot-plot showing ~75bps of 2024 cuts) was the final catalyst; real estate led (+24.2%) alongside tech (+17.9%) and breadth broadened (RSP +2.2% vs SPY), confirming a regime change from rate shock to easing anticipation.","body_zh":"10年期收益率于2023年10月中下旬触顶约5.0%并急剧反转（TLT年末涨+21.9%），这些GPU托管商在短短68天内暴涨179.7%，受益于难以满足的AI算力需求。利率下行叠加稀缺性极大强化了高贝塔走势，风险偏好猛烈转向（SMH +24.5%、VIX 22降至12、DXY -4.9%）。美联储鲍威尔2023年12月13日FOMC转向（点阵图显示2024年降息约75个基点）是最后催化剂；房地产领涨（+24.2%）叠加科技（+17.9%），广度转宽（RSP跑赢SPY +2.2%），确认机制从利率冲击切换至宽松预期。","drivers":["10-yr yield peak Oct 2023","Fed pivot Dec 2023 (~75bps cuts signaled)","risk-on surge (TLT +21.9%, VIX 22 to 12)","GPU compute scarcity premium"],"drivers_zh":["10年期收益率2023年10月见顶","美联储2023年12月转向(预告降息约75基点)","风险偏好激增(TLT +21.9%, VIX 22降至12)","GPU算力稀缺溢价"],"prev_key":"2023-10-20","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Yield peak triggers GPU rip into year-end","title_zh":"收益率见顶触发年末GPU暴涨","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:trough:2023-10"},"2023-12-27":{"body":"A 51.1% flush in January 2024 unwound an overbought, over-owned position in the highest-beta AI corner as hot December 2023 jobs data and revised CPI expectations pushed yields back up (TLT -7.1%) and cooled 2024 cut expectations from ~6-7 to ~3-4. The broader market actually gained (SPY +1.9%) as Tech (+5.4%) and Comm (+4.5%) held up — the selloff was idiosyncratic to the most-speculative AI-hosting names, with narrow breadth (RSP -3.2% vs SPY) confirming a positioning reset, not a demand change. The cohort-specific high-beta flush (SPHB-SPLV -2.7) underscored its nature.","body_zh":"2024年1月的51.1%回吐平掉了AI最高贝塔领域超买、过度持仓头寸，因强劲的2023年12月就业数据与修正后的CPI预期将收益率重新推高（TLT -7.1%），将2024年降息预期从约6-7次压缩至约3-4次。大盘实际上涨（SPY +1.9%），科技（+5.4%）与通信（+4.5%）守住——抛售是最投机性AI托管个股的特有现象，窄幅广度（RSP跑输SPY -3.2%）确认这是仓位重置而非需求变化。板块特异性高贝塔回吐（SPHB-SPLV -2.7）凸显了这一点。","drivers":["hot Jan 2024 jobs / CPI re-pricing","rate tick-up (TLT -7.1%)","cut expectations reset (~6-7 to ~3-4)","overbought high-beta flush"],"drivers_zh":["强劲就业/CPI重定价(2024年1月)","利率小幅上行(TLT -7.1%)","降息预期重置(约6-7次缩至约3-4次)","超买高贝塔仓位回吐"],"prev_key":"2023-12-27","prev_key_chain":["2023-12-27"],"status":"exact","title":"January overbought flush resets positioning","title_zh":"一月超买回吐重置仓位","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:peak:2023-12"},"2024-01-24":{"body":"A 272% run from January 24 to December 6, 2024 was powered by massive GPU-cloud capacity deals and accelerating AI-compute demand as the CoreWeave/Applied Digital/TeraWulf cohort signed multi-year contracts; Microsoft alone made up ~62% of CoreWeave's ~$1.92B 2024 sales, and CoreWeave's June 2024 12-year deals with Core Scientific added ~$3.5B+ of contracted HPC capacity. Three Fed cuts (September 18, November 7, December 11, 2024) added fuel. The tape was a tech-led goldilocks melt-up (SMH +29.2%, growth>value +10.4, ultra-calm VIX 13 to 13), deliberately narrow at the top (RSP -6.2% vs SPY) even as the dollar firmed +2.6%, institutionalizing the neocloud investment thesis ahead of CoreWeave's confidential IPO preparations.","body_zh":"2024年1月24日至12月6日涨幅272%，由大规模GPU云产能交易与加速的AI算力需求驱动，CoreWeave/Applied Digital/TeraWulf阵营签署多年合同；仅微软就占CoreWeave 2024年约19.2亿美元销售额的约62%，CoreWeave 2024年6月与Core Scientific的12年合同新增约35亿美元以上的HPC产能。美联储三次降息（9月18日、11月7日、12月11日）进一步添油。行情是科技引领的金发女孩熔涨（SMH +29.2%、成长跑赢价值+10.4、VIX超平稳13至13），顶部刻意窄幅（RSP跑输SPY -6.2%），尽管美元走强+2.6%，在CoreWeave秘密筹备IPO前夕使新云投资逻辑机构化。","drivers":["GPU-cloud capacity deals (CoreWeave/Core Scientific)","Microsoft anchor customer (~62% of CW 2024 sales)","Fed three cuts Sept-Dec 2024","narrow goldilocks melt-up (SMH +29.2%)"],"drivers_zh":["GPU云产能交易(CoreWeave/Core Scientific)","微软锚定客户(占CW 2024销售约62%)","美联储2024年9-12月三次降息","窄幅金发女孩熔涨(SMH +29.2%)"],"prev_key":"2024-01-24","prev_key_chain":["2024-01-24"],"status":"exact","title":"CoreWeave-era buildout in a goldilocks tape","title_zh":"金发女孩行情中CoreWeave时代的产能建设","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:trough:2024-01"},"2024-12-06":{"body":"DeepSeek's R1 model release (late January 2025, ~Jan 20-23) triggered a record single-day wipeout in NVIDIA (stock -16.9% on January 27, ~$600B of market cap), spiking fears that efficient AI models would slash GPU demand and impair neocloud leasing economics. The basket was already fragile (post-peak positioning) and deepened into Liberation Day: Trump's April 2, 2025 tariff announcement sparked a deep US market crash (VIX 13 to 52). Defensives held (-6.7%) vs cyclicals -18.5%, high-beta crushed (SPHB-SPLV -22.7%), and the basket led the wreck (SMH -27.3% vs SPY -17.8%), falling 57.3% to the April 8, 2025 trough.","body_zh":"DeepSeek R1模型发布（2025年1月下旬，约1月20-23日）引发英伟达创纪录的单日暴跌（1月27日股价-16.9%，约6000亿美元市值蒸发），引爆高效AI模型将大幅削减GPU需求、损害新云租赁经济逻辑的恐慌。篮子此前已因过度持仓而脆弱，随\"解放日\"进一步深跌：特朗普2025年4月2日关税公告引发美股大幅崩盘（VIX 13升至52）。防御股守住（-6.7%）vs 周期股-18.5%，高贝塔遭重创（SPHB-SPLV -22.7%），篮子领跌（SMH -27.3% vs SPY -17.8%），下跌57.3%至2025年4月8日底部。","drivers":["DeepSeek R1 Jan 2025 (NVDA -16.9%, ~$600B)","GPU demand efficiency scare","Liberation Day tariffs Apr 2 2025 (VIX 13 to 52)","flight-to-safety (SPHB-SPLV -22.7%)"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek R1 2025年1月(英伟达-16.9%, 约6000亿)","GPU需求效率恐慌","解放日关税2025年4月2日(VIX 13升至52)","避险(SPHB-SPLV -22.7%)"],"prev_key":"2024-12-06","prev_key_chain":["2024-12-06"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek and tariff panic crush high-beta","title_zh":"DeepSeek与关税恐慌重创高贝塔","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:peak:2024-12"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"Trump's April 9, 2025 90-day tariff pause (S&P 500 +9.5% on the day, largest since 2008) plus proof that AI-compute demand only accelerated post-DeepSeek drove a 570.2% melt-up — the strongest in the entire AI complex. GPU-leasing backlogs swelled as CoreWeave's March 2025 IPO institutionalized the sector. The move rode the most violent risk-on reset of the cycle (VIX 52 to 16, SPHB-SPLV +122.0) in a reflation/growth-up quad with Tech +114.0% leading, narrow at the top (RSP -13.1% vs SPY). SMH surged +267.8%; CoreWeave's OpenAI contract built to ~$22.4B and it signed Meta for ~$14.2B (Sept 2025). The first macro test came June 3, 2026 with Broadcom: a record AI-chip quarter ($10.8B, +143%) and a raised ~$56B full-year AI guide, yet the stock fell ~10-13% as investors had priced an even bigger raise.","body_zh":"特朗普2025年4月9日宣布90天关税暂停（标普500当日涨9.5%，为2008年以来最大单日涨幅）叠加DeepSeek后AI算力需求只增不减的验证，推动篮子熔涨570.2%，为AI板块最强。CoreWeave 2025年3月IPO使这一赛道机构化，GPU租赁积压膨胀。这轮上涨乘的是本周期最猛烈的风险偏好重置（VIX 52降至16、SPHB-SPLV +122.0），处于再通胀/增长向上象限、科技+114.0%领涨、顶部窄幅（RSP跑输SPY -13.1%）。SMH飙升+267.8%；CoreWeave与OpenAI合同累积至约224亿美元，并与Meta签约约142亿美元（2025年9月）。首个宏观考验出现在2026年6月3日博通：AI芯片单季创纪录（108亿美元，+143%）并上调全年AI指引至约560亿美元，但股价仍下跌约10-13%，因投资者已price-in更大幅度的上调。","drivers":["tariff pause Apr 9 2025 (S&P +9.5%)","GPU-leasing backlog acceleration","violent risk-on reset (VIX 52 to 16, SPHB-SPLV +122.0)","CoreWeave IPO + mega-contracts (~$22B OpenAI, ~$14B Meta)"],"drivers_zh":["关税暂停2025年4月9日(标普+9.5%)","GPU租赁积压加速","猛烈风险偏好重置(VIX 52降至16, SPHB-SPLV +122.0)","CoreWeave IPO+超级合同(OpenAI约220亿, Meta约140亿)"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff pause and AI compute surge drive 570% melt-up","title_zh":"关税暂停与AI算力激增驱动570%熔涨","turn_id":"ai_neoclouds:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"AI Neoclouds and HPC Hosting sits in an Expansion/Trending phase ranked #2 in relative strength at the 50.2 percentile of its historical range, having surged 570% off the April 8, 2025 Liberation Day trough. The current reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, copper-gold +18.3%, oil +19.2%) provided the macro backdrop for this highest-beta AI-infrastructure cohort to lead; Tech ranks first sector (+24.3%) and SMH has risen sharply off the April low. Notably, breadth is actually BROADENING here (equal-weight RSP beating cap-weight SPY by +2.9%), arguing against a classic narrow late-stage top, even as high-beta excess remains stretched (SPHB-SPLV +20.7%) and DXY has firmed +3.4% (a headwind for capital-intensive borrowers). The first real macro test is Broadcom's June 3, 2026 print: despite a record AI-chip quarter ($10.8B, +143%) and a raised full-year AI guide (~$56B), the stock fell ~10-13% because investors had priced an even bigger raise — a sign the buildout's bar is now extreme rather than evidence GPU-leasing economics are breaking.","now_zh":"AI新云与高性能算力托管处于扩张/趋势阶段，相对强度排名第2，处于历史区间50.2百分位，自2025年4月8日\"解放日\"底部已飙升570%。当前再通胀/增长向上象限（周期股+11.2% vs 防御股+6.9%、铜金比+18.3%、油价+19.2%）为这一最高贝塔AI基础设施板块领涨提供了宏观背景；科技位列第一强势板块（+24.3%），SMH自4月低点大幅上涨。值得注意的是，当前广度实际在转宽（等权RSP跑赢市值加权SPY +2.9%），与典型的窄幅周期后期顶部相悖，尽管高贝塔溢价仍偏高（SPHB-SPLV +20.7%）、美元指数走强+3.4%（对重资本借贷方构成阻力）。首个真正的宏观考验是博通2026年6月3日财报：尽管AI芯片单季创纪录（108亿美元，+143%）并上调全年AI指引（约560亿美元），股价仍下跌约10-13%，因投资者已price-in更大幅度的上调——这表明产能建设的预期门槛已极高，而非GPU租赁经济效益破裂的证据。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-ai_semiconductors":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"Semiconductor stocks rallied 53% as global chip sales hit a record $335.8 billion in 2014 (up 9.9% YoY, DRAM up 34.7%), driven by the 4G LTE smartphone upgrade cycle, TSMC's 20nm ramp for Apple A8, and early enterprise cloud data-center build-outs. Crucially, the macro regime was a deflation-scare quad where defensives led (Health +33.8%, Utilities +23.2%) and TLT surged +28.4% as the dollar soared +18.2% — the semis basket's +53% outpaced SPY's +18.2% entirely on the strength of its growth/tech angle, not a risk-on regime, with oil collapsing -47.2% and credit spreads widening. The VIX fell from 14 to 13, suggesting a calm but narrow, sector-specific melt-up rather than broad cyclical expansion.","body_zh":"全球芯片销售额2014年创纪录达3358亿美元（同比+9.9%，DRAM同比+34.7%），4G LTE智能手机换机潮、台积电20nm为苹果A8处理器量产及早期企业云数据中心建设推动半导体股涨53%。宏观上处于通缩恐慌象限，防御板块领涨（医疗+33.8%、公用事业+23.2%），TLT大涨+28.4%，美元飙升+18.2%，油价崩跌-47.2%——该篮子+53%的涨幅完全依托成长/科技属性，而非宽泛的周期性风险偏好；VIX从14降至13，反映为窄幅板块性飙升而非广谱周期扩张。","drivers":["4G LTE upgrade cycle","TSMC 20nm ramp","cloud data-center","dollar strength","deflation scare"],"drivers_zh":["4G LTE换机潮","台积电20nm量产","云数据中心","美元走强","通缩恐慌"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Mobile/cloud semiconductor melt-up","title_zh":"移动互联网/云端半导体飙升","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:trough:2014-01"},"2015-03-02":{"body":"The basket fell 23.5% in a textbook risk-off rotation as China's Shanghai Composite crashed 43% from its June 2015 peak and the People's Bank of China devalued the RMB by nearly 4% across August 11-14, 2015, triggering a global 'Black Monday' on August 24. VIX spiked from 13 to 36, defensives led (Utilities -3.6% vs cyclicals -14.4%), oil fell -20.7% and copper/gold fell -8.6% in a slowdown/deflation quad — a pure risk-off deleveraging, not a semiconductor-specific story. The SMH fell -21.9% vs SPY -10.8%, amplifying the global growth scare as the high-beta chips bore the brunt of crowded-long unwinding.","body_zh":"中国上证指数从2015年6月高点崩跌43%，人民银行于8月11-14日累计贬值人民币近4%，引发全球\"黑色星期一\"（8月24日），篮子下跌23.5%，是典型的避险轮动行情。VIX从13飙升至36，防御板块领先（公用事业-3.6% vs 周期股-14.4%），油价-20.7%，铜金比-8.6%，处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限——这是纯粹的避险去杠杆，而非半导体基本面问题。SMH下跌-21.9% vs SPY -10.8%，高贝塔芯片在拥挤多头平仓中首当其冲。","drivers":["China RMB devaluation","Shanghai equity crash","global growth scare","VIX spike","risk-off deleveraging"],"drivers_zh":["人民币贬值","上证暴跌","全球成长恐慌","VIX飙升","避险去杠杆"],"prev_key":"2015-03-02","prev_key_chain":["2015-03-02"],"status":"exact","title":"China devaluation risk-off growth scare","title_zh":"人民币贬值避险，全球成长恐慌","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:peak:2015-03"},"2015-08-25":{"body":"A monster +303% run over three years off the China-shock low, ignited by Nvidia's Pascal (2016) and Volta (2017) GPU architectures that proved transformative for deep learning. Nvidia's data center business nearly tripled in fiscal 2017 and grew a further 2.5x in fiscal 2018 as every major cloud (Amazon, Google, Microsoft, Alibaba) adopted Volta for AI training. The macro regime was a clean reflation/growth-up quad (VIX 36 to 12, cyclicals +68.1% vs defensives +39%, oil +75.5%) with broad risk-on: tech led at +108.9%, semis at +144.1% vs SPY +64.9%. Breadth narrowed (RSP lagged SPY -8.9%) as mega-cap tech dominated, and the Fed hiked gradually without disrupting the expansion.","body_zh":"从中国冲击低点出发，历经三年涨幅高达+303%，由英伟达Pascal（2016年）和Volta（2017年）GPU架构引爆，这两款产品在深度学习领域证明了颠覆性实力。英伟达数据中心业务FY2017近三倍增长，FY2018再增2.5倍，亚马逊、谷歌、微软、阿里巴巴等云巨头全面采用Volta进行AI训练。宏观处于干净的再通胀/成长向上象限（VIX 36降至12，周期股+68.1% vs 防御股+39%，油价+75.5%），科技板块领涨+108.9%，SMH +144.1% vs SPY +64.9%。市场广度收窄（RSP跑输SPY -8.9%），大盘科技主导，美联储渐进加息未打断扩张节奏。","drivers":["Nvidia Pascal/Volta GPUs","deep learning adoption","cloud hyperscaler spend","reflation regime","risk-on melt-up"],"drivers_zh":["英伟达Pascal/Volta GPU","深度学习采用","云厂商支出","再通胀象限","风险偏好飙升"],"prev_key":"2015-08-25","prev_key_chain":["2015-08-25"],"status":"exact","title":"AI/deep learning supercycle ignition","title_zh":"AI/深度学习超级周期点燃","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:trough:2015-08"},"2018-09-14":{"body":"The basket fell 28.6% in Q4 2018 as two simultaneous shocks hit: the Fed's hawkish October 3 \"long way from neutral\" comment by Powell and its December 19 hike (fourth of the year to 2.25-2.5%), combined with the US-China trade war escalation and a smartphone demand collapse. Nvidia's stock fell over 50% in Q4 alone. The VIX spiked 12 to 36, defensives led (Utilities -3.4% vs cyclicals -22%), oil crashed -38.4% and the regime turned slowdown/deflation-scare — this was a full risk-off flush where this high-beta basket amplified SPY's -18.6% decline (SMH -22.7%).","body_zh":"2018年Q4该篮子下跌28.6%，遭遇双重冲击：美联储鲍威尔10月3日\"距中性利率尚远\"的鹰派表态以及12月19日第四次加息（联邦基金利率升至2.25-2.5%），叠加中美贸易战升级和智能手机需求暴跌。英伟达股价Q4单季跌逾50%。VIX从12飙升至36，防御板块领先（公用事业-3.4% vs 周期股-22%），油价崩跌-38.4%，象限转向放缓/通缩恐慌——这是全面避险抛售，高贝塔篮子放大了SPY -18.6%的跌幅（SMH -22.7%）。","drivers":["Fed hawkish shock","US-China trade war","smartphone demand collapse","oil crash","VIX spike"],"drivers_zh":["美联储鹰派冲击","中美贸易战","智能手机需求崩塌","油价暴跌","VIX飙升"],"prev_key":"2018-09-14","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade war and Fed rate shock crash","title_zh":"贸易战叠加美联储利率冲击崩盘","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"A +97.8% rally from the Christmas Eve 2018 low to the pre-COVID peak, powered by Fed Chair Powell's January 4 2019 dovish pivot (\"patient\" language removed the hiking bias), the US-China Phase 1 trade truce signed January 2020, and the 5G infrastructure build-out cycle that boosted Qualcomm, Qorvo and RF semis. Nvidia and AMD recovered strongly through 2019. The macro regime was reflation/growth-up (VIX 36 to 14, cyclicals +41.7% vs defensives +36.1%, tech +80.7%), with TLT gaining +23% as the Fed cut rates three times in 2019, and breadth narrowing (RSP lagged SPY -6.9%) as mega-cap tech led.","body_zh":"从2018年平安夜低点涨+97.8%至疫情前高点，由美联储主席鲍威尔2019年1月4日鸽派转向（\"耐心\"措辞移除加息倾向）、2020年1月签署中美第一阶段贸易协议，以及推动高通、Qorvo等射频芯片的5G基础设施建设周期驱动。英伟达和AMD在2019年强势复苏。宏观处于再通胀/成长向上象限（VIX 36降至14，周期股+41.7% vs 防御股+36.1%，科技+80.7%），美联储2019年三次降息（TLT +23%），市场广度收窄（RSP跑输SPY -6.9%），大盘科技主导。","drivers":["Fed dovish pivot Jan 2019","US-China Phase 1 truce","5G buildout","three Fed cuts 2019","tech melt-up"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月鸽派转向","中美第一阶段协议","5G建设周期","2019年三次降息","科技飙升"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot + 5G/cloud recovery rally","title_zh":"美联储转向+5G/云端复苏反弹","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-19":{"body":"The basket fell 33.3% in just four weeks as COVID-19 spread globally, triggering the fastest bear market in history. VIX exploded from 14 to 76 — the highest since 2008 — and a total risk-off panic ensued: defensives fell only -18.1% while cyclicals cratered -37.3%, oil collapsed -61.8% and breadth narrowed sharply (RSP lagged SPY -4.7%). This was pure systemic deleveraging, not semiconductor-specific: forced selling hit every liquid high-beta asset, with SMH -33.6% matching SPY's -29.1% decline with its characteristic beta amplification.","body_zh":"新冠疫情全球蔓延，触发史上最快熊市，四周内篮子下跌33.3%。VIX从14爆炸式升至76（2008年以来最高），引发全面避险恐慌：防御股仅跌-18.1%，周期股暴跌-37.3%，油价崩跌-61.8%，市场广度急剧收窄（RSP跑输SPY -4.7%）。这是纯粹的系统性去杠杆，与半导体基本面无关——强制平仓横扫所有流动性高贝塔资产，SMH -33.6%与SPY -29.1%的跌幅通过典型的贝塔放大效应高度匹配。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic","systemic deleveraging","VIX 76 peak","oil collapse","global recession fear"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情","系统性去杠杆","VIX暴至76","油价崩跌","全球衰退恐慌"],"prev_key":"2020-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic liquidity crisis selloff","title_zh":"新冠疫情流动性危机抛售","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"A +323% run from the March 2020 panic low to the December 2021 peak, driven by the largest fiscal and monetary stimulus in history (the CARES Act, zero rates, QE) igniting a tech-led recovery. Nvidia's data center revenue surged 80% YoY in Q1 FY2021 and 167% YoY in Q2 FY2021 as pandemic lockdowns exploded demand for gaming GPUs, cloud computing and AI training. The macro regime was textbook reflation/growth-up (VIX 76 to 18, cyclicals +130.4% vs defensives +50.8%, oil +271%, high-beta led by +160.1%), dollar fell -5% and breadth broadened (RSP beat SPY +8.6%). The semis melt-up (SMH +217.1%) was amplified by a genuine semiconductor supply shortage by late 2020-2021.","body_zh":"从2020年3月恐慌低点涨+323%至2021年12月高点，由史上最大规模财政货币刺激（CARES法案、零利率、QE）点燃，触发科技领涨的复苏行情。英伟达数据中心营收FY2021 Q1同比暴增80%、Q2同比+167%，疫情封锁激增游戏GPU、云计算及AI训练需求。宏观处于教科书式再通胀/成长向上象限（VIX 76降至18，周期股+130.4% vs 防御股+50.8%，油价+271%，高贝塔领涨+160.1%），美元走弱-5%，市场广度扩散（RSP跑赢SPY +8.6%）。半导体飙升（SMH +217.1%）到2020-2021年底进一步被真实的半导体供应短缺所放大。","drivers":["pandemic stimulus CARES Act","zero rates + QE","Nvidia data center surge","gaming/cloud demand","semis supply shortage"],"drivers_zh":["疫情刺激CARES法案","零利率+QE","英伟达数据中心爆增","游戏/云端需求","半导体供应短缺"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Pandemic stimulus + cloud/gaming supercycle","title_zh":"疫情刺激+云端/游戏超级周期","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:trough:2020-03"},"2021-12-27":{"body":"AI-chip names fell 35% as the Fed pivoted to aggressive hikes — yields surged (TLT -21.4%) and the dollar ripped +9.4%, a textbook rate shock for long-duration tech. The regime was a risk-off flight-to-safety (VIX 18 to 27, high-beta lagged low-vol by -19.5%) into a stagflation-ish quad, and this high-beta basket amplified it: SMH -38.1% versus SPY -19.5%. Real-yield compression plus digestion of the pandemic semis over-order cycle hit the richest GPU/accelerator multiples hardest, with semiconductor inventory normalization dragging the sector beyond pure rate sensitivity.","body_zh":"AI芯片股下跌35%，美联储转向激进加息——收益率飙升（TLT -21.4%）、美元大涨+9.4%，是典型的长久期科技股利率冲击。当时处于类滞胀象限的避险行情（VIX 18升至27，高贝塔跑输低波-19.5%），这只高贝塔篮子放大了跌幅：SMH -38.1% vs SPY -19.5%。实际收益率压缩叠加疫情期间半导体超额订单消化，对估值最高的GPU/加速器名字打击最重，库存周期下行拖累幅度超出纯粹的利率敏感性。","drivers":["Fed pivot to aggressive hikes","TLT -21.4% yield surge","dollar +9.4%","semis inventory cycle","multiple compression"],"drivers_zh":["美联储转向激进加息","收益率飙升TLT -21.4%","美元+9.4%","半导体库存周期","估值压缩"],"prev_key":"2021-12-27","prev_key_chain":["2021-12-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed-hiking bear crushes high-beta chips","title_zh":"美联储加息熊市重创高贝塔芯片","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:peak:2021-12"},"2022-07-01":{"body":"A sharp +37.9% bear-market rally as peak-inflation hopes eased VIX from 27 to 20 after the July 13 2022 CPI print came in softer than feared, triggering a broad risk-on squeeze with bonds roughly flat (TLT -0.6%). Tech/semis led (semis +23.4% vs SPY +12.2%, growth beat value +6.7%) in a goldilocks-flavored quad, and this high-beta basket led the squeeze higher. The move was positioning-driven, not a fundamental turn: semis still faced deep demand cuts from PC, smartphone and gaming channel destocking.","body_zh":"通胀见顶预期令VIX从27回落至20（2022年7月13日CPI数据低于预期是触发点），引发广泛的空头回补，债券基本持平（TLT -0.6%），带来+37.9%的急剧熊市反弹。科技/半导体领涨（半导体+23.4% vs SPY +12.2%，成长跑赢价值+6.7），处于金发姑娘象限，该高贝塔篮子主导了这波挤压。此乃仓位驱动而非基本面转向：半导体仍面临PC、智能手机和游戏渠道去库存引发的深度需求下修。","drivers":["peak-inflation trade","CPI miss July 2022","bear market short squeeze","goldilocks quad","high-beta lead"],"drivers_zh":["通胀见顶交易","2022年7月CPI低于预期","熊市空头回补","金发姑娘象限","高贝塔领涨"],"prev_key":"2022-07-01","prev_key_chain":["2022-07-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Semis-led bear bounce on peak-inflation hope","title_zh":"半导体领涨的熊市反弹，押注通胀见顶","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:trough:2022-07"},"2022-08-18":{"body":"Chips fell another 32% into the October low as Powell's August 26 2022 Jackson Hole speech killed the pivot trade with \"restrictive policy for some time\" language, sending stocks down 3.4% that Friday. Yields surged again (TLT -13.8%) and the dollar pushed +5.4% in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (VIX 20 to 32). The macro de-rating compounded a theme-specific blow: on August 26 Nvidia filed an 8-K disclosing the US government had immediately blocked exports of A100 and H100 chips to China (formalized in the October 7 BIS rule), amplifying the high-beta drawdown (SMH -28.4% vs SPY -16.1%).","body_zh":"鲍威尔2022年8月26日在杰克逊霍尔发表\"限制性政策将维持一段时间\"的鹰派讲话，当日股市下跌3.4%，击碎转向交易，芯片再跌32%至10月低点。收益率再度飙升（TLT -13.8%），美元推升+5.4%，处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限（VIX 20升至32）。宏观估值下杀叠加主题利空：英伟达同日（8月26日）提交8-K文件，披露美国政府已立即封锁A100和H100芯片对华出口（10月7日BIS正式成文），进一步放大了高贝塔回撤（SMH -28.4% vs SPY -16.1%）。","drivers":["Jackson Hole hawkish surprise","yields surged TLT -13.8%","A100/H100 China export ban","dollar +5.4%","slowdown quad"],"drivers_zh":["杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击","收益率飙升TLT -13.8%","A100/H100对华出口禁令","美元+5.4%","放缓象限"],"prev_key":"2022-08-18","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkish leg down","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派下跌","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:peak:2022-08"},"2022-10-14":{"body":"A monster +380.6% run off the October 2022 low, ignited by ChatGPT's launch in November 2022 and supercharged by Nvidia's blowout May 24 2023 Q1 FY2024 earnings report — data center revenue of $4.28 billion and Q2 guidance of $11 billion — which CEO Jensen Huang called the start of a transition to accelerated computing and generative AI. The macro regime was goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation (VIX 32 to 13, growth crushed value +55.3, dollar fell -7.3%) and breadth narrowed dramatically (RSP lagged SPY -28.4%), a mega-cap-led tape this high-beta basket led from the front (SMH +230.6% vs SPY +61.1%). AI accelerator demand became the single dominant market narrative through 2024.","body_zh":"从2022年10月低点涨+380.6%，由2022年11月ChatGPT上线点燃，再被英伟达2023年5月24日爆表的Q1 FY2024财报（数据中心营收42.8亿美元，Q2指引110亿美元，CEO黄仁勋称之为加速计算和生成式AI转型的起点）助燃。宏观处于金发姑娘/成长向上-去通胀象限（VIX 32降至13，成长大幅跑赢价值+55.3，美元下跌-7.3%），市场广度急剧收窄（RSP跑输SPY -28.4%），这只高贝塔篮子在大盘股主导的行情中一马当先（SMH +230.6% vs SPY +61.1%）。AI加速器需求成为贯穿2024年的单一主导叙事。","drivers":["ChatGPT launch Nov 2022","Nvidia May 2023 earnings blowout","AI capex supercycle","goldilocks disinflation regime","mega-cap narrow breadth"],"drivers_zh":["ChatGPT 2022年11月上线","英伟达2023年5月财报爆表","AI资本开支超级周期","金发姑娘去通胀象限","大盘股窄幅广度"],"prev_key":"2022-10-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-14"],"status":"exact","title":"GenAI supercycle melt-up","title_zh":"生成式AI超级周期飙升","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:trough:2022-10"},"2024-07-10":{"body":"A swift -27.4% drop as the August 2024 yen-carry unwind forced rapid deleveraging across crowded AI longs following the Bank of Japan's July 31 rate hike to 0.25% (its highest since 2008). VIX spiked from 13 to 28 in a flight-to-safety rotation where defensives gained (+2.2%) while cyclicals fell (-5.5%) and breadth broadened sharply (RSP beat SPY +6.6%). The slowdown-scare risk-off hit this leveraged high-beta basket disproportionately (SMH -24.8% vs SPY -7.6%), unwinding months of one-way positioning; semis quickly stabilized as the carry unwind exhausted itself.","body_zh":"日本央行2024年7月31日将利率上调至0.25%（2008年以来最高），8月日元套息平仓被迫快速去杠杆，拥挤的AI多头遭到冲击，篮子迅速下跌27.4%。VIX从13飙升至28，避险轮动中防御股上涨（+2.2%）、周期股下跌（-5.5%），市场广度急剧扩散（RSP跑赢SPY +6.6%）。放缓恐慌的避险对这只带杠杆的高贝塔篮子打击格外严重（SMH -24.8% vs SPY -7.6%），解除了数月单向多头仓位；随着套息平仓耗尽，半导体迅速企稳。","drivers":["yen-carry unwind","Bank of Japan rate hike Jul 31","crowded AI long deleveraging","risk-off rotation","high-beta amplification"],"drivers_zh":["日元套息平仓","日本央行7月31日加息","拥挤AI多头去杠杆","避险轮动","高贝塔放大"],"prev_key":"2024-07-10","prev_key_chain":["2024-07-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Yen-carry unwind shakeout","title_zh":"日元套息平仓震荡","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:peak:2024-07"},"2024-08-07":{"body":"A +65.9% recovery into January 2025 as the Fed's September 18 2024 50bp cut and election-driven risk appetite revived AI-capex enthusiasm — a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (VIX 28 to 15, growth beat value +13.9, semis +26.9%) even as yields rose (TLT -7.2%) and the dollar firmed +4.8% in a goldilocks quad. Breadth stayed narrow (RSP lagged SPY -5.7%), and Blackwell GPU ramp anticipation plus hyperscaler AI capex guidance carried this high-beta basket to new highs. The Trump election win on November 5 added a deregulation/AI-investment narrative boost.","body_zh":"美联储2024年9月18日降息50bp及大选后风险偏好重燃AI资本开支热情，篮子从低点回升+65.9%至2025年1月——这是一轮科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好飙升（VIX 28降至15，成长跑赢价值+13.9，半导体+26.9%），尽管收益率上行（TLT -7.2%）、美元走强+4.8%，处于金发姑娘象限。市场广度保持狭窄（RSP跑输SPY -5.7%），对Blackwell GPU量产的预期叠加云厂商AI资本开支指引推动该高贝塔篮子创新高。11月5日特朗普当选更增添去监管/AI投资的叙事加成。","drivers":["Fed 50bp cut Sep 2024","Blackwell GPU ramp anticipation","election-driven risk appetite","hyperscaler AI capex","narrow breadth melt-up"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2024年9月降息50bp","Blackwell GPU量产预期","大选后风险偏好","云厂商AI资本开支","窄幅广度飙升"],"prev_key":"2024-08-07","prev_key_chain":["2024-08-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed-cut-cycle relief rally, mega-cap-led","title_zh":"降息周期反弹，大盘股主导","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:trough:2024-08"},"2025-01-22":{"body":"Chips fell 41.6% as two sequential shocks hit: first, DeepSeek's January 27 2025 release of its R1 model — reportedly trained for under $6 million — erased nearly $600 billion from Nvidia's market cap in a single day (-17%), raising fundamental questions about AI training chip demand; second, the Trump administration's April 2 2025 'Liberation Day' reciprocal tariff announcement (32% on Taiwan, where most chips are made) deepened the rout. VIX exploded from 15 to 45, defensives (-2.2%) massively outperformed cyclicals (-16.3%) in a slowdown-scare quad, and this leveraged basket amplified the move (SMH -32.3% vs SPY -16.4%); yields fell (TLT +7.2%) and dollar weakened, confirming this was a growth scare, not a rate, selloff.","body_zh":"两波冲击接连打击芯片股，下跌41.6%：首先是DeepSeek 2025年1月27日发布R1模型——据称训练成本不足600万美元——单日蒸发英伟达近6000亿美元市值（-17%），引发对AI训练芯片需求的根本性质疑；其次，特朗普政府2025年4月2日\"解放日\"对等关税公告（对芯片主产地台湾征收32%关税）加深跌势。VIX从15暴涨至45，防御股（-2.2%）大幅跑赢周期股（-16.3%），处于放缓恐慌象限，该杠杆篮子放大了跌幅（SMH -32.3% vs SPY -16.4%）；收益率下行（TLT +7.2%）、美元走弱，确认这是成长恐慌而非利率主导的抛售。","drivers":["DeepSeek R1 launch Jan 27 2025","AI capex efficiency fear","Liberation Day tariffs Apr 2 2025","VIX 45 spike","growth scare not rate shock"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek R1 2025年1月27日发布","AI资本效率担忧","解放日关税2025年4月2日","VIX飙至45","成长恐慌而非利率冲击"],"prev_key":"2025-01-22","prev_key_chain":["2025-01-22"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek scare into the tariff crash","title_zh":"DeepSeek恐慌叠加关税崩盘","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:peak:2025-01"},"2025-04-04":{"body":"A +153% surge off the April 4 2025 low — the fastest recovery in the basket's history — as Trump's April 9 90-day tariff pause for all countries except China (and semiconductor exemptions confirmed April 12-14) restored confidence, and TSMC's Q1 2025 earnings reaffirmed the AI capex cycle was intact. The macro regime swung to goldilocks (VIX 45 to 17, cyclicals +28.9% vs defensives +9.1%, high-beta led by +67.5, growth beat value +28.3), dollar fell -3.1% and breadth stayed narrow (RSP lagged SPY -15.2%). Nvidia, Broadcom's custom-ASIC wins and TSMC pricing power drove the leaders to records by October 2025.","body_zh":"从2025年4月4日低点涨+153%，为该篮子历史上最快复苏——特朗普4月9日对除中国外所有国家暂停90天关税（4月12-14日确认半导体豁免）重建信心，台积电Q1 2025财报重申AI资本开支周期完好无损。宏观象限急速切换至金发姑娘（VIX 45降至17，周期股+28.9% vs 防御股+9.1%，高贝塔领涨+67.5，成长跑赢价值+28.3），美元走弱-3.1%，市场广度维持狭窄（RSP跑输SPY -15.2%）。英伟达、博通的定制ASIC订单和台积电定价权推动龙头股至2025年10月创历史新高。","drivers":["90-day tariff pause Apr 9 2025","semiconductor tariff exemptions","TSMC AI capex reaffirmation","custom ASIC Broadcom wins","goldilocks regime snap-back"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月9日90天关税暂停","半导体关税豁免","台积电AI资本开支重申","博通定制ASIC订单","金发姑娘象限急速回归"],"prev_key":"2025-04-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-tariff AI melt-up, V-shaped","title_zh":"关税后AI飙升，V型反转","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:trough:2025-04"},"2025-10-31":{"body":"A -26.6% pullback as hawkish Fed recalibration (new Chair Kevin Warsh signaling rates would stay higher longer and investors pricing additional 2026 hikes) and emerging AI vendor-financing concerns pressured extreme multiples. Tellingly, this was a leadership rotation rather than a crash: SPY fell only -6.8% and breadth broadened sharply (RSP beat SPY +7.7%) in a stagflation-ish quad with oil surging +68.7%, so capital rotated out of over-owned AI chips (SMH flat at +0.2%) into Energy, Materials and Staples. Growth underperformed value by -18.5% as AI-related debt-funded capex came under scrutiny.","body_zh":"鹰派的美联储重置（新任主席沃什暗示利率将长期保持高位，市场开始定价2026年再次加息）以及AI供应商融资担忧压制极端估值，回调26.6%。值得注意的是，这是领导力轮动而非崩盘：SPY仅下跌-6.8%，市场广度急剧扩散（RSP跑赢SPY +7.7%），处于类滞胀象限（油价飙升+68.7%），资金从被过度持有的AI芯片（SMH持平+0.2%）流向能源、材料和必需消费品。成长风格跑输价值-18.5%，以债务融资的AI资本开支遭到审视。","drivers":["hawkish Fed Warsh reset","AI financing loop concerns","growth-to-value rotation","oil +68.7% stagflation","valuation de-rating"],"drivers_zh":["美联储沃什鹰派重置","AI融资闭环担忧","成长至价值轮动","油价+68.7%类滞胀","估值下杀"],"prev_key":"2025-10-31","prev_key_chain":["2025-10-31"],"status":"exact","title":"Late-2025 hawkish reset, leadership rotates out","title_zh":"2025年末鹰派重置，领导力轮出","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:peak:2025-10"},"2026-03-30":{"body":"A +118.7% rebound from the March 2026 trough — AI semis recovering from the late-2025 hawkish correction — that rode a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (VIX 31 to 16, growth beat value +10.9, semis +74.4%) through the Iran/Hormuz oil crisis and CPI spike into the June 14 ceasefire. The advance stayed narrow (RSP lagged SPY -8.6%), a mega-cap-led tape in a reflation/growth-up quad (copper-gold +22.2%, cyclicals +13.5% vs defensives -1.5%). By June 5 Broadcom's earnings flagged a guidance miss on AI networking revenue, marking the cycle peak and initiating the current rolling-over phase.","body_zh":"从2026年3月低点反弹+118.7%——AI芯片从2025年末鹰派调整中复苏——搭乘科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好飙升（VIX 31降至16，成长跑赢价值+10.9，半导体+74.4%），穿越伊朗/霍尔木兹石油危机和CPI跳升，在6月14日停火后见顶。这波上涨广度狭窄（RSP跑输SPY -8.6%），处于再通胀/成长向上象限的大盘股主导行情（铜金比+22.2%，周期股+13.5% vs 防御股-1.5%）。6月5日博通财报暴露AI网络营收指引缺口，标志着本轮周期高点，触发当前的回落阶段。","drivers":["post-correction AI capex reacceleration","Hormuz ceasefire June 14 2026","narrow mega-cap breadth","Broadcom earnings peak signal","reflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["后调整期AI资本开支再加速","2026年6月14日霍尔木兹停火","窄幅大盘股广度","博通财报见顶信号","再通胀象限"],"prev_key":"2026-03-30","prev_key_chain":["2026-03-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Hormuz-shock rebound, then June top","title_zh":"霍尔木兹冲击后反弹再见顶","turn_id":"ai_semiconductors:trough:2026-03"}},"now":"The basket is in a Downturn/Rolling-over phase at the 87th percentile of its historical range after a +119% melt-up from the March-2026 trough to the June-2026 peak. The direct trigger for the rollover was Broadcom's June 5 2026 Q2 FY2026 earnings report: AI networking revenue of $4.1 billion missed the $17.2 billion Q3 guidance consensus and the full-year AI forecast was left unchanged, erasing over $1.3 trillion in chip-sector market cap in one session. The macro backdrop has shifted to a late-cycle reflation quad (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2%) with a strengthening dollar (+3.4% DXY) capping long-duration multiples, and new Fed Chair Kevin Warsh is pricing in additional rate hikes. SMH remains up 67.9% from the 2026 trough but the high-beta premium is fading: breadth is broadening (RSP beat SPY by +2.9%), growth is underperforming value by -15.2%, and the basket holds a SELL signal having definitively rolled over from an extreme concentration high, the same structural pattern that preceded the July 2024 and January 2025 selloffs.","now_zh":"本篮子当前处于\"下行/见顶回落\"阶段，处于历史区间第87百分位，此前经历了从2026年3月低点至2026年6月高点+119%的急涨行情。近期回落的直接导火索是博通2026年6月5日发布的FY2026 Q2财报——AI网络营收41亿美元，低于市场对Q3指引的172亿美元预期，且未上调全年AI预测，单日蒸发全球芯片板块逾1.3万亿美元市值。宏观背景已转向周期末段再通胀象限（周期股+11.2% vs 防御股+6.9%，油价+19.2%），美元走强（DXY +3.4%）压制长久期估值，新任美联储主席凯文·沃什的政策预期偏鹰。SMH相对2026年低点仍涨67.9%，但高贝塔溢价正在消退：市场广度扩散（RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%），成长风格跑输价值-15.2%，该篮子已触发\"卖出\"信号，从极端集中高位明确回落，与2024年7月和2025年1月AI叙事前高后的形态高度吻合。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"semis.top_2026.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"semis.top_2026.v1","arch_state":"pass","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-ai_software":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"The 2014-2015 leg was driven by the mainstreaming of enterprise cloud software as Salesforce, ServiceNow, Workday, and nascent Azure all delivered 30-70% revenue growth, prompting the market to re-rate the SaaS category on subscription-model durability. The macro was a slow-burn deflation/slowdown quad: TLT surged +24.4%, oil crashed -57.5%, and DXY rallied +21.7%, compressing commodity and cyclical sectors while tech (semis +37.3%, growth>value +11.1) melt-up on narrow mega-cap breadth (RSP -3.9% vs SPY). Low yields turbocharged DCF valuations on high-growth software, and defensives also outperformed (+26.2%) as the rate-fall lifted duration assets across the board.","body_zh":"2014-2015年的上涨由企业云软件主流化驱动——Salesforce、ServiceNow、Workday及初期的Azure均实现30-70%营收增长，市场凭借订阅模式的持久性对SaaS品类整体重新定价。宏观处于缓慢通缩/放缓象限：TLT飙升+24.4%、油价崩跌-57.5%、美元指数升值+21.7%，压制大宗商品与周期类资产，同时科技(半导体+37.3%、成长跑赢价值+11.1%)在窄幅大盘股格局下熔涨(RSP跑输SPY -3.9%)。低利率强化了高成长软件的DCF估值，防御板块亦因利率下行而同步跑赢(+26.2%)。","drivers":["SaaS subscription re-rating","oil/commodity crash (oil -57.5%)","falling yields (TLT +24.4%)","strong dollar (+21.7%)","mega-cap growth melt-up"],"drivers_zh":["SaaS订阅模式重定价","油价/大宗商品崩跌(油价-57.5%)","收益率下行(TLT +24.4%)","美元走强(+21.7%)","大盘成长股熔涨"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Cloud SaaS category re-rating rally","title_zh":"云SaaS品类重新定价上涨","turn_id":"ai_software:trough:2014-01"},"2015-12-04":{"body":"A triple shock compressed software into early February 2016: China's Shanghai Composite had crashed 40%+ from its June 2015 peak and was still roiling EM sentiment; Brent crude fell below $30/bbl by January 2016 on OPEC oversupply; and the Fed's December 16, 2015 rate hike (its first since 2008) raised discount-rate fears. The rotation was textbook flight-to-safety: defensives held (-0.6%) versus cyclicals -13.2%, VIX spiked 15 to 26, and TLT gained +9.5% as bonds caught a bid. High-growth software, the longest-duration corner of tech, was repriced sharply downward as the slowdown/deflation quad punished anything with a stretched multiple.","body_zh":"三重冲击将软件股压至2016年2月初：中国上证综指自2015年6月峰值崩跌逾40%，持续冲击新兴市场情绪；布伦特原油于2016年1月跌破30美元/桶(欧佩克供过于求)；2015年12月16日美联储时隔七年首次加息引发贴现率担忧。轮动呈教科书式避险特征：防御股守住(-0.6%) vs 周期股-13.2%，VIX从15飙至26，TLT获买盘上涨+9.5%。高成长软件作为科技中久期最长的品类，在放缓/通缩恐慌象限中因估值偏高而遭到最重的重定价。","drivers":["Fed December 2015 rate hike (first since 2008)","China stock market crash / EM contagion","oil below $30/bbl (OPEC surplus)","flight-to-safety (VIX 15->26)"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2015年12月加息(2008年后首次)","中国股市崩盘/新兴市场传染","原油跌破30美元(欧佩克供给过剩)","避险(VIX 15->26)"],"prev_key":"2015-12-04","prev_key_chain":["2015-12-04"],"status":"exact","title":"China slowdown, oil crash, Fed liftoff flush","title_zh":"中国经济放缓、油价暴跌与美联储首次加息冲洗","turn_id":"ai_software:peak:2015-12"},"2016-02-08":{"body":"The February 2016 trough was set around the implicit G20 Shanghai understanding (February 26-27, 2016, attended by Yellen, Lew, Draghi and Lagarde) where major policymakers signaled a coordinated easing tilt, the dollar reversed, and oil bottomed near $26/bbl before surging +153% over the leg. The resulting reflation/growth-up quad unleashed a 32-month, 140% melt-up in AI-adjacent software as the macro backdrop shifted decisively: semis surged +133%, growth beat value by +31 points, high-beta dominated (+53.5 vs low-vol), and VIX compressed from 26 to 12. Trump's election (November 2016) added fiscal stimulus expectations and corporate tax cut tailwinds (TCJA passed December 2017 cut rate to 21%), while cloud enterprise adoption accelerated through Salesforce, Workday, ServiceNow, and emerging Microsoft Azure commercial momentum.","body_zh":"2016年2月的低点在G20上海会议(2016年2月26-27日，耶伦、卢、德拉吉、拉加德出席)隐性共识附近触底——主要政策制定者发出协调宽松倾向、美元逆转、油价在约26美元/桶见底后飙升+153%。由此带来的再通胀/增长向上象限触发了持续32个月、涨幅达140%的熔涨行情：半导体+133%、成长跑赢价值+31个点、高贝塔大幅领先(+53.5 vs 低波)、VIX从26压缩至12。特朗普当选(2016年11月)带来财政刺激预期和企业减税顺风(2017年12月《减税与就业法案》将税率降至21%)，同时Salesforce、Workday、ServiceNow及微软Azure商业动能加速，企业云采用进入快车道。","drivers":["Shanghai understanding dollar/oil reversal","reflation macro inflection (oil +153%)","Trump election / TCJA 21% corporate tax","cloud enterprise adoption acceleration","semis melt-up (+133%)"],"drivers_zh":["上海会议美元/油价逆转","再通胀宏观拐点(油价+153%)","特朗普当选/TCJA企业税率降至21%","企业云采用加速","半导体熔涨(+133%)"],"prev_key":"2016-02-08","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Shanghai Accord reflation ignites 30-month bull","title_zh":"上海会议再通胀引燃30个月牛市","turn_id":"ai_software:trough:2016-02"},"2018-10-01":{"body":"Fed Chair Powell's October 3, 2018 statement that the Fed was 'a long way from neutral' on rates triggered a sharp repricing, and the December 19, 2018 fourth rate hike of the year — combined with Powell saying the balance sheet runoff was on 'autopilot' — pushed VIX from 12 to 36 and drove the S&P 500 to its worst December since 1931. It was a broad risk-off flush: defensives held (-8.3%) vs cyclicals -22.4%, Tech -23.5% and semis -22.7% led the selloff, and oil crashed -43.5% as China trade-war growth fears compounded the rate shock. Software/AI platforms, having run 140% from the trough, were among the hardest-hit as growth de-rated.","body_zh":"美联储主席鲍威尔于2018年10月3日表示利率'距中性水平尚远'，触发急剧重定价；2018年12月19日第四次加息叠加鲍威尔称缩表将'自动运行'，将VIX从12推升至36，驱动标普500录得1931年以来最差12月。这是一次全面避险冲洗：防御股守住(-8.3%) vs 周期股-22.4%，科技-23.5%、半导体-22.7%领跌，油价崩跌-43.5%，中美贸易战引发的增长担忧与利率冲击叠加。累涨140%的软件/AI平台在成长去杠杆中首当其冲。","drivers":["Powell 'long way from neutral' (Oct 3)","fourth Fed rate hike 2018 (Dec 19)","balance sheet autopilot shock","US-China trade war growth fears","oil crash -43.5%"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔'距中性尚远'(10月3日)","2018年第四次加息(12月19日)","缩表'自动运行'冲击","中美贸易战增长担忧","油价崩跌-43.5%"],"prev_key":"2018-10-01","prev_key_chain":["2018-10-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell 'long way from neutral' rate-shock flush","title_zh":"鲍威尔'距中性尚远'利率冲击平仓","turn_id":"ai_software:peak:2018-10"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"The December 24 Christmas Eve low was reversed almost immediately as Fed Chair Powell pivoted on January 4, 2019, signaling 'patience' on further hikes, then delivered three 'insurance' rate cuts in July, September, and October 2019 against a US-China trade-war growth scare. The result was a 14-month, 68.8% rally as the macro flipped to reflation: semis surged +90.9%, growth beat value by +24.3 points, VIX compressed 36 to 14, and TLT rose +23% in a falling-rate environment that turbo-charged software multiples. Microsoft Azure crossed $10B annualized run-rate in early 2019, Salesforce and ServiceNow accelerated bookings, and the narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -6.9% vs SPY) concentrated flows into the highest-quality cloud platforms.","body_zh":"平安夜低点几乎立即被逆转，鲍威尔于2019年1月4日发出'耐心'信号，此后在中美贸易战引发增长担忧的背景下于7月、9月、10月三次'预防性'降息。由此催生14个月、68.8%的涨幅：半导体+90.9%、成长跑赢价值+24.3个点、VIX从36压缩至14，TLT上涨+23%的降息环境为软件估值倍数提供双重加成。微软Azure于2019年初突破年化100亿美元，Salesforce与ServiceNow订单加速，窄幅大盘股行情(RSP跑输SPY -6.9%)将资金集中于最高质量云平台。","drivers":["Powell January 2019 pivot / patience signal","Fed three 'insurance' cuts (Jul/Sep/Oct 2019)","falling yields (TLT +23%)","Microsoft Azure $10B ARR milestone","semis melt-up (+90.9%)"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔2019年1月转向/'耐心'信号","美联储三次'预防性'降息(7/9/10月)","收益率下行(TLT +23%)","微软Azure年化100亿美元里程碑","半导体熔涨(+90.9%)"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot unlocks 14-month AI platform bull","title_zh":"美联储转向解锁14个月AI平台牛市","turn_id":"ai_software:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-19":{"body":"On February 20, 2020 — the day after the bundle peak — global equity markets began their pandemic crash as COVID-19 spread beyond China. The S&P 500 lost 34% by March 23 in its fastest-ever bear market, with the Dow losing 6,400 points in four trading days. VIX spiked from 14 to 83, the most extreme reading in history, as oil crashed -46.1% (Saudi-Russia price war compounded on March 8). Despite software being a relative 'winner' during work-from-home, the initial panic was indiscriminate: AI platforms fell -32% with the basket as the flight-to-safety was total (defensives -22.3% vs cyclicals -35.4%, credit spread blow-out). The trough came March 16 (Monday), one day after the Fed's emergency 100bp cut to zero and $700B QE announced Sunday, March 15.","body_zh":"2020年2月20日(束峰值次日)，随着新冠肺炎扩散出中国，全球股市开始崩盘。标普500于3月23日前下跌34%，创有史以来最快熊市，道指四个交易日蒸发6400点。VIX从14飙至83，为史上最极端读数；油价因3月8日沙特-俄罗斯价格战叠加崩跌-46.1%。尽管软件在居家办公中相对占优，初期恐慌仍无差别冲击：AI平台随大盘下跌-32%，避险情绪全面主导(防御股-22.3% vs 周期股-35.4%，信用利差飙升)。低点于3月16日(周一)形成，恰在美联储3月15日(周日)紧急降息100bp至零并宣布7000亿美元QE的次日。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic shock (VIX 14->83)","fastest-ever bear market (-34% S&P in 33 days)","Saudi-Russia oil price war (oil -46.1%)","credit spread blow-out"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情冲击(VIX 14->83)","史上最快熊市(标普33天跌34%)","沙特-俄罗斯油价战(油价-46.1%)","信用利差飙升"],"prev_key":"2020-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID-19 pandemic panic, VIX to 83","title_zh":"新冠疫情恐慌，VIX冲至83","turn_id":"ai_software:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-16":{"body":"The Fed's March 2020 emergency ZIRP and $700B+ QE (later unlimited) combined with $2.2T CARES Act fiscal stimulus to create the most powerful liquidity injection in history. Work-from-home mandates structurally accelerated enterprise software adoption: Microsoft Teams went from 32M to 115M daily users by November 2020, Salesforce and Zoom cloud ARR grew 20-30%, and the digital-transformation narrative pulled 5 years of cloud migration forward. By November 2021, semis had surged +200.8%, growth beat value by +40 points, VIX compressed from 83 to 16, and software platforms had risen +271.5% — the largest basket rally in the study period. The move was broad (RSP +9.2% vs SPY) as the cyclical reopening also contributed, and software maintained its premium as the secular AI infrastructure buildout began with massive cloud capex.","body_zh":"美联储2020年3月紧急实施零利率并推出7000亿美元+(后续无限量)量化宽松，叠加2.2万亿美元《CARES法案》财政刺激，共同制造了历史上最强劲的流动性注入。居家办公强制令在结构上加速企业软件采用：微软Teams日活用户从2020年3月的3200万增至11月的1.15亿，Salesforce与Zoom云ARR增长20-30%，数字转型叙事使云迁移进程提前五年。至2021年11月，半导体累涨+200.8%、成长跑赢价值+40个点、VIX从83压缩至16，软件平台累涨+271.5%——为本研究期内最大涨幅。行情较为宽泛(RSP跑赢SPY +9.2%)，周期复苏亦有贡献；随着大规模云资本开支推动AI基础设施建设启动，软件维持了其相对溢价。","drivers":["Fed ZIRP + unlimited QE","CARES Act $2.2T fiscal stimulus","work-from-home structural demand surge","cloud migration 5-year pull-forward","semis melt-up (+200.8%)"],"drivers_zh":["美联储零利率+无限量化宽松","《CARES法案》2.2万亿美元财政刺激","居家办公结构性需求激增","云迁移五年需求提前释放","半导体熔涨(+200.8%)"],"prev_key":"2020-03-16","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-16"],"status":"exact","title":"ZIRP+QE pandemic boom, generative-AI precursor","title_zh":"零利率+量化宽松疫情繁荣，生成式AI先驱","turn_id":"ai_software:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-16":{"body":"High-multiple application and platform software led the 2021-22 growth wreck as yields surged (TLT -8.7%) and the dollar firmed +3.3% in a stagflation-ish quad driven by CPI hitting 6.8% in November 2021, its highest since 1982. The rotation was risk-off but broadening — defensives held (+0.8%) vs cyclicals -5.1% with VIX rising 16 to 32, while equal-weight beat cap-weight (RSP +3.0% vs SPY) — driven by the Fed's November 2021 taper announcement and the early-2022 Russia-Ukraine war shock (invasion February 24, 2022). As the longest-duration corner of tech, AI software amplified the move (Tech -16.1%, SMH -21.2% vs SPY -10.8%). With generative AI monetization years away, the group had no near-term earnings story to defend its multiples against rising real yields.","body_zh":"高估值的应用与平台软件引领2021-22年的成长股崩塌——2021年11月CPI达6.8%(1982年以来最高)、美联储于11月宣布Taper、俄罗斯于2022年2月24日入侵乌克兰，收益率飙升(TLT -8.7%)、美元在类滞胀象限走强+3.3%。轮动偏避险但广度转宽——防御股守住(+0.8%) vs 周期股-5.1%，VIX从16升至32，同时等权跑赢市值加权(RSP跑赢SPY +3.0%)。作为科技中久期最长的板块，AI软件放大了跌幅(科技-16.1%、SMH -21.2% vs SPY -10.8%)。当时生成式AI变现尚需数年，板块缺乏近期盈利故事来对抗实际收益率上行压力。","drivers":["CPI 6.8% (Nov 2021, 40-year high)","Fed taper announcement Nov 2021","Ukraine invasion Feb 24, 2022","rates surge (TLT -8.7%)","SaaS multiple de-rating (VIX 16->32)"],"drivers_zh":["CPI 6.8%(2021年11月，40年最高)","美联储2021年11月宣布Taper","俄罗斯2022年2月入侵乌克兰","收益率飙升(TLT -8.7%)","SaaS估值下修(VIX 16->32)"],"prev_key":"2021-11-16","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-16"],"status":"exact","title":"SaaS de-rating leads the 2022 growth wreck","title_zh":"SaaS估值下修领跌2022年成长股崩塌","turn_id":"ai_software:peak:2021-11"},"2022-03-14":{"body":"A sharp but brief bounce off oversold conditions lifted software as VIX collapsed 32 to 19 and growth beat value by +9.5 points in a reflation/growth-up quad; the tape turned risk-on with semis +13.0% and high-beta outperforming. The bounce was mechanical positioning relief — the most-shorted names surged — rather than a macro inflection, and breadth remained narrow (RSP -3.0% vs SPY). Rates were essentially flat (TLT -0.1%) and oil barely moved (+0.3%) during the window, confirming this was pure sentiment and short-covering rather than a regime change. The rally faded in less than three weeks as the hiking path steepened.","body_zh":"超卖条件下爆发短暂剧烈反弹，VIX从32崩至19、成长跑赢价值+9.5个点，处于再通胀/增长向上象限；半导体+13.0%、高贝塔跑赢，行情转向风险偏好。这是机械性仓位修复——空头最多的个股涨幅最大——而非宏观拐点，广度依然收窄(RSP跑输SPY -3.0%)。窗口期内利率基本持平(TLT -0.1%)、油价几乎未动(+0.3%)，印证这是纯情绪与空头回补而非格局切换。随着加息路径加速收紧，反弹在三周内消退。","drivers":["oversold short-covering bounce","risk-on snapback (VIX 32->19)","growth>value (+9.5)","narrow breadth (RSP -3.0%)","flat rates/oil (no regime change)"],"drivers_zh":["超卖空头回补反弹","风险偏好回升(VIX 32->19)","成长跑赢价值(+9.5)","窄幅广度(RSP -3.0%)","利率/油价持平(无格局切换)"],"prev_key":"2022-03-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Oversold relief, narrow risk-on snapback","title_zh":"超卖修复、窄幅风险偏好回升","turn_id":"ai_software:trough:2022-03"},"2022-04-04":{"body":"Software resumed its decline as the Fed signaled an accelerated, 50bp-per-meeting hiking cadence (May 4, 2022 first 50bp hike since 2000) and real yields surged, with TLT falling -14.7% — the largest rate move of any single leg in this cycle. The macro was stagflation-ish: CPI hit 8.5% in March 2022, oil rose +13.9% as the Ukraine war drove energy shortages, and the dollar added +4.7%. Defensives led (-11.5%) vs cyclicals -17.1% with VIX rising 19 to 33, and tech/software — with no near-term earnings to offset the duration penalty — was among the hardest hit (Tech -23.5% vs SPY -19.7%). Zero-revenue SaaS names lost 70-80% peak-to-trough.","body_zh":"随着美联储释放每次会议加息50bp的加速信号(2022年5月4日首次加息50bp，为2000年以来最大)、实际收益率飙升，TLT下跌-14.7%——为本周期单一腿中最大利率波动，软件恢复下跌。宏观呈类滞胀：2022年3月CPI达8.5%，乌克兰战争驱动能源短缺使油价上涨+13.9%，美元走强+4.7%。防御股领先(-11.5%) vs 周期股-17.1%，VIX从19升至33；没有近期盈利来抵消久期惩罚的软件跌势最重(科技-23.5% vs SPY -19.7%)，零收入SaaS个股从峰值跌幅达70-80%。","drivers":["Fed 50bp hike May 4 (first since 2000)","CPI 8.5% (March 2022, 40-year high)","real yields surge (TLT -14.7%)","Ukraine war energy shock (oil +13.9%)","stagflation flush (VIX 19->33)"],"drivers_zh":["美联储5月4日加息50bp(2000年以来首次)","CPI 8.5%(2022年3月，40年最高)","实际收益率飙升(TLT -14.7%)","乌克兰战争能源冲击(油价+13.9%)","类滞胀冲洗(VIX 19->33)"],"prev_key":"2022-04-04","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Real-yield repricing in the stagflation flush","title_zh":"类滞胀冲洗中的实际收益率重定价","turn_id":"ai_software:peak:2022-04"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"A summer relief rally on hopes the worst of monetary tightening was priced lifted software off its June 2022 low, as inflation prints began decelerating (CPI peaked at 9.1% in June, then eased) and the tape turned risk-on: SMH +20.8%, growth>value (+9.2), VIX cooled 33 to 20, and oil crashed -24% as recession fears dampened demand. The goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation quad narrative drove a broad relief rally, but it lacked earnings underpinning — software companies were still burning cash and guiding down — and breadth was slightly narrow (RSP -0.7% vs SPY). The move unwound completely through the autumn as Jackson Hole (August 26, Powell's 'pain' speech) confirmed the hiking path was not over.","body_zh":"在通胀数据开始降温(CPI于2022年6月见顶9.1%后回落)、市场预期最紧货币政策已被消化的情绪下，夏季解脱性反弹将软件股托离6月低点：半导体+20.8%、成长跑赢价值(+9.2)、VIX从33降至20，衰退担忧压制需求使油价崩跌-24%。金发女孩/增长向上-去通胀象限叙事推动广泛解脱，但缺乏盈利基础——软件公司仍在烧钱并下调指引——广度略显窄幅(RSP跑输SPY -0.7%)。随着8月26日杰克逊霍尔会议(鲍威尔'阵痛'演讲)确认加息路径未终结，行情在秋季完全回吐。","drivers":["CPI deceleration hope (peaked 9.1% June)","risk-on melt-up (SMH +20.8%, VIX 33->20)","oil crash -24% (recession demand destruction)","disinflation quad narrative","no earnings floor"],"drivers_zh":["通胀降温预期(CPI 2022年6月见顶9.1%)","风险偏好熔涨(SMH +20.8%, VIX 33->20)","油价崩跌-24%(衰退需求破坏)","去通胀象限叙事","无盈利托底"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-rate-fear summer bounce, no earnings floor","title_zh":"利率恐慌见顶的夏季反弹，缺乏盈利托底","turn_id":"ai_software:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-15":{"body":"Powell's August 26, 2022 Jackson Hole speech — 'we must keep at it until the job is done' — dashed hopes of a Fed pivot and drove a final tightening leg into the January 2023 low. Yields surged (TLT -9.5%), value led growth by -14.2 points, and tech fell -19.6% vs SPY -10.8%. Critically, the breadth structure was unusual: RSP beat SPY by +4.9% as the selloff was rotation-led and rate-driven, not a panic — value, energy, and industrials held while long-duration software bore the brunt of a higher discount rate. The trough in early January 2023 was set just weeks after ChatGPT's launch (November 30, 2022; 100M users by February 2023) had begun to reframe the AI investment case.","body_zh":"鲍威尔2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔演讲——'必须坚持到底直到完成任务'——打碎了美联储转向的希望，推动最后一轮紧缩延伸至2023年1月低点。收益率飙升(TLT -9.5%)、价值领先成长-14.2个点，科技跌-19.6% vs SPY -10.8%。关键在于广度结构异常：RSP跑赢SPY +4.9%——这次下跌是轮动驱动与利率驱动，而非恐慌式抛售，价值股、能源与工业守住，长久期软件首当其冲。2023年1月初的低点在ChatGPT发布(2022年11月30日，2023年2月破亿用户)开始重塑AI投资逻辑数周后形成。","drivers":["Jackson Hole 'pain' speech (Aug 26, 2022)","rate surge (TLT -9.5%)","growth-lags-value by -14.2 points","value/energy rotation broadening (RSP +4.9%)","ChatGPT launch Nov 30 beginning narrative shift"],"drivers_zh":["杰克逊霍尔'阵痛'演讲(2022年8月26日)","收益率飙升(TLT -9.5%)","成长跑输价值-14.2个点","价值/能源轮动转宽(RSP +4.9%)","ChatGPT 11月30日发布推动叙事切换"],"prev_key":"2022-08-15","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole pain speech drives cycle trough","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔'阵痛'演讲驱动周期低点","turn_id":"ai_software:peak:2022-08"},"2023-01-05":{"body":"ChatGPT launched November 30, 2022, reaching 100M users by February 2023; Microsoft announced its ~$10B OpenAI investment on January 23, 2023; and the basket's January 5, 2023 trough marked the start of the generative AI supercycle. Over 25 months, software platforms rose +268.3% as Microsoft (Copilot), Palantir (AIP), and ServiceNow built the application layer for AI monetization. The macro was a textbook tech-led risk-on melt-up in a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation quad: semis +155.3%, growth>value by +67.1, VIX compressed 22 to 15, and breadth was extremely narrow (RSP -32.7% vs SPY) — the most mega-cap-concentrated tape in the study period. The Fed began cutting in September 2024 (50bp first cut), adding a multiple-expansion tailwind even as the overall rate level remained elevated (TLT -7.8% over the full leg).","body_zh":"ChatGPT于2022年11月30日发布，2023年2月用户突破1亿；微软于2023年1月23日宣布约100亿美元OpenAI投资；篮子的2023年1月5日低点标志着生成式AI超级周期的启动。历经25个月，软件平台上涨+268.3%，微软(Copilot)、Palantir(AIP)、ServiceNow构建了AI变现的应用层。宏观是教科书式科技引领的风险偏好熔涨，处于金发女孩/增长向上-去通胀象限：半导体+155.3%、成长跑赢价值+67.1个点、VIX从22压缩至15，广度极度收窄(RSP跑输SPY -32.7%)——为研究期内大盘股集中度最高的行情。2024年9月美联储首次降息50bp，在整体利率仍偏高(TLT全段-7.8%)的背景下带来额外的估值倍数扩张顺风。","drivers":["ChatGPT / Microsoft ~$10B OpenAI (Jan 23, 2023)","generative AI monetization narrative (Copilot, AIP)","semis melt-up (+155.3%)","Fed cuts Sep 2024 (50bp)","ultra-narrow mega-cap breadth (RSP -32.7% vs SPY)"],"drivers_zh":["ChatGPT/微软约100亿美元OpenAI投资(2023年1月23日)","生成式AI变现叙事(Copilot, AIP)","半导体熔涨(+155.3%)","美联储2024年9月首次降息50bp","极窄大盘股广度(RSP跑输SPY -32.7%)"],"prev_key":"2023-01-05","prev_key_chain":["2023-01-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Generative AI platform supercycle, goldilocks melt-up","title_zh":"生成式AI平台超级周期，金发女孩熔涨","turn_id":"ai_software:trough:2023-01"},"2025-02-18":{"body":"DeepSeek's R1 model release (January 20, 2025) — its base model trained on an alleged ~$6M budget versus US labs' billions — triggered fears that cheaper AI models would commoditize the application layer, eroding software moats. The selloff began February 18 and deepened dramatically through April 4 as President Trump's April 2 Liberation Day tariff announcement (reciprocal tariffs on dozens of countries, some steep) caused the single largest tariff-driven market crash since 2020 with the S&P 500 losing 12.4% in days. VIX rocketed 15 to 45, defensives held (-4.8%) vs cyclicals -16.7%, high-beta collapsed (SPHB-SPLV -25.0), and semis fell -29.4%. AI software, as a long-duration high-beta group with monetization still being proven, led the laggards (Tech -24.6% vs SPY -17.1%).","body_zh":"DeepSeek R1模型(2025年1月20日发布，其基础模型据称仅耗资约600万美元，远低于美国实验室数十亿美元)引发市场担忧，认为更廉价的AI模型将使应用层商品化、侵蚀软件护城河。回撤自2月18日开始，并因特朗普于4月2日宣布'解放日'对等关税(对数十个国家征收对等关税，部分税率高企)而急剧加深，触发2020年以来最大的关税驱动市场崩盘，标普500在数日内暴跌12.4%。VIX从15飙至45，防御股守住(-4.8%) vs 周期股-16.7%，高贝塔崩溃(SPHB-SPLV -25.0)，半导体跌-29.4%。作为变现仍待验证的长久期高贝塔群体，AI软件领跌(科技-24.6% vs SPY -17.1%)。","drivers":["DeepSeek R1 launch (Jan 20, 2025) commoditization fear","Liberation Day tariffs (Apr 2, 2025)","risk-off crash (VIX 15->45, high-beta -25.0)","semis -29.4%","monetization doubt"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek R1发布(2025年1月20日)商品化恐慌","'解放日'对等关税(2025年4月2日)","避险崩盘(VIX 15->45, 高贝塔-25.0)","半导体-29.4%","AI变现存疑"],"prev_key":"2025-02-18","prev_key_chain":["2025-02-18"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek commoditization fear + Liberation Day crash","title_zh":"DeepSeek商品化恐慌与解放日关税崩盘","turn_id":"ai_software:peak:2025-02"},"2025-04-04":{"body":"The April 4, 2025 trough coincided with Trump's April 9 announcement of a 90-day tariff pause for most countries (China excluded), which triggered the single largest single-day S&P 500 gain since 2008. Simultaneously, Microsoft's May 2025 earnings confirmed an AI annual revenue run rate of ~$37B (+123% YoY), Copilot seat count climbed toward 16-20M, and Palantir's AIP government and commercial bookings accelerated — proving the monetization thesis. The risk-on reset was violent: VIX collapsed 45 to 16, semis surged +99.1%, high-beta dominated (SPHB-SPLV +65.5), DXY fell -4.1%, and software rose +66.9% over six months. The stall came October 2025 as the Iran/Hormuz oil shock (oil +57.5%) reignited inflation fears.","body_zh":"2025年4月4日低点与特朗普4月9日宣布对大多数国家90天关税暂停(中国除外)同步形成，触发2008年以来标普500最大单日涨幅。同期微软2025年5月业绩确认AI年化收入约370亿美元(+123% YoY)，Copilot付费席位攀升至1600-2000万，Palantir AIP政府及商业订单加速——证明变现逻辑成立。风险偏好重置极为猛烈：VIX从45崩至16，半导体飙升+99.1%，高贝塔主导(SPHB-SPLV +65.5)，DXY下跌-4.1%，软件六个月上涨+66.9%。2025年10月因伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击(油价+57.5%)重燃通胀担忧而停滞。","drivers":["Trump 90-day tariff pause (Apr 9)","Microsoft AI ARR ~$37B +123% YoY","Copilot 16-20M paid seats","violent risk-on reset (VIX 45->16, semis +99.1%)","DXY weaker (-4.1%)"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普90天关税暂停(4月9日)","微软AI年化收入约370亿美元+123% YoY","Copilot 1600-2000万付费席位","猛烈风险偏好重置(VIX 45->16, 半导体+99.1%)","美元走弱(-4.1%)"],"prev_key":"2025-04-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff pause + AI bookings prove monetization real","title_zh":"关税暂停与AI订单证明变现可行","turn_id":"ai_software:trough:2025-04"},"2025-10-27":{"body":"A late-2025 hawkish repricing of software multiples (the 'Autumn Chill' — Microsoft stalling, Meta drawing down) collided with the 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock: strikes on Iran's infrastructure triggered Strait of Hormuz disruption, sending Brent toward ~$150/bbl and oil +57.5% over the leg. CPI was pushed toward 4.2% and the Fed adopted a hiking bias. The rotation was decisive: Energy +30.9%, Materials +17.9% led while growth lagged value by -15.7 points and breadth broadened (RSP +3.5% vs SPY). Long-duration software bore the brunt (Tech -4.3%) in a reflation/growth-up quad that punished anything running on DCF multiples — though semis actually held up (+21.8%) on supply-chain resiliency narratives, so this was a software/long-duration de-rating rather than a semis-led wipeout.","body_zh":"2025年末软件估值鹰派重定价('秋寒'——微软股价停滞、Meta回撤)与2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击叠加：对伊朗基础设施的打击触发霍尔木兹海峡封锁，布伦特原油冲向约150美元/桶，全段油价+57.5%。CPI被推升至约4.2%，美联储采取加息倾向。轮动果断：能源+30.9%、材料+17.9%领涨，成长跑输价值-15.7个点，广度转宽(RSP跑赢SPY +3.5%)。在惩罚DCF估值的再通胀/增长向上象限中，长久期软件首当其冲(科技-4.3%)——但半导体实际守住(+21.8%，受供应链韧性叙事支撑)，因此这是软件/长久期去估值，而非半导体引领的暴跌。","drivers":["Iran war / Hormuz closure (oil +57.5%)","CPI ~4.2% / Fed hiking bias","AI 'autumn chill' monetization gap","growth lags value -15.7 pts","energy/materials rotation (Energy +30.9%)"],"drivers_zh":["伊朗战争/霍尔木兹封锁(油价+57.5%)","CPI约4.2%/美联储加息倾向","AI'秋寒'变现缺口","成长跑输价值-15.7个点","能源/材料轮动(能源+30.9%)"],"prev_key":"2025-10-27","prev_key_chain":["2025-10-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Hormuz oil shock + AI 'autumn chill' valuation reset","title_zh":"霍尔木兹石油冲击与AI'秋寒'估值重置","turn_id":"ai_software:peak:2025-10"},"2026-04-10":{"body":"The April 2026 Iran-US ceasefire ended the Hormuz oil disruption overhang and triggered a sharp risk-on snapback: oil fell -4.6%, the inflation/rate pressure eased, and software reversed from deeply oversold levels. The move was high-beta amplified in a reflation/growth-up quad: semis surged +39.1%, growth>value (+8.6), VIX cooled 19 to 16, and Tech +37.1% led all sectors — AI software gained +52.7% in under two months. Breadth was narrow (RSP -5.4% vs SPY), confirming the move was concentrated in mega-cap AI platform names (Microsoft, Palantir, ServiceNow) rather than a broad sector recovery. The rally peaked June 1 as Broadcom's refusal to raise AI guidance stalled momentum.","body_zh":"2026年4月伊朗-美国停火终结了霍尔木兹石油中断压制，触发剧烈风险偏好反弹：油价下跌-4.6%，通胀/利率压力缓解，软件股从深度超卖水平逆转。行情在再通胀/增长向上象限中被高贝塔放大：半导体飙升+39.1%、成长跑赢价值(+8.6)、VIX从19降至16，科技+37.1%领涨所有板块——AI软件在不足两个月内上涨+52.7%。广度收窄(RSP跑输SPY -5.4%)，确认行情集中于大盘AI平台龙头(微软、Palantir、ServiceNow)而非板块整体复苏。2026年6月博通拒绝上调AI指引后，反弹于6月1日见顶。","drivers":["Hormuz ceasefire 2026 (oil -4.6%)","risk-on reset (semis +39.1%, VIX 19->16)","growth > value (+8.6)","mega-cap AI platform concentration (RSP -5.4%)","Broadcom guidance miss ends rally Jun 2026"],"drivers_zh":["霍尔木兹停火2026年4月(油价-4.6%)","风险偏好重置(半导体+39.1%, VIX 19->16)","成长跑赢价值(+8.6)","大盘AI平台集中(RSP -5.4%)","博通指引不及预期终结反弹2026年6月"],"prev_key":"2026-04-10","prev_key_chain":["2026-04-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Hormuz ceasefire triggers AI software snapback","title_zh":"霍尔木兹停火触发AI软件急速反弹","turn_id":"ai_software:trough:2026-04"},"2026-06-01":{"body":"Broadcom's early-June 2026 Q2 earnings held its full-year AI semiconductor sales forecast unchanged at a figure below analyst expectations, and management declined to raise the annual target despite rapid custom-chip adoption. The market read this as a capex ceiling signal for the entire AI stack and the selloff spread up the stack into software as the tape turned defensive: defensives led (+5.3%) vs cyclicals -0.1%, VIX rose 16 to 19, oil crashed -22.0% on demand-destruction fears, and growth lagged value by -11.5 points. Breadth broadened (RSP +4.6% vs SPY), confirming a rotation out of AI-growth names into defensives rather than a broad market panic — and notably semis themselves still rose +4.8%, so the damage concentrated in the long-duration software application layer.","body_zh":"博通2026年6月初第二季度财报维持全年AI芯片销售预测不变(低于分析师预期)，管理层尽管见到定制芯片快速放量仍拒绝上调年度目标。市场将此解读为整个AI产业链的资本支出天花板信号，抛售沿产业链向上蔓延至软件，行情转向防御：防御股领先(+5.3%) vs 周期股-0.1%，VIX从16升至19，油价因需求破坏担忧崩跌-22.0%，成长跑输价值-11.5个点。广度转宽(RSP跑赢SPY +4.6%)，确认这是从AI成长名称轮动至防御板块，而非全面市场恐慌——值得注意的是半导体本身仍上涨+4.8%，损伤集中于长久期软件应用层。","drivers":["Broadcom Q2 2026 AI guidance miss","AI capex ceiling signal","flight-to-safety (defensives +5.3% vs cyclicals -0.1%)","growth lags value -11.5 pts","oil crash -22% on demand fears"],"drivers_zh":["博通2026年Q2 AI指引不及预期","AI资本支出天花板信号","避险(防御股+5.3% vs 周期股-0.1%)","成长跑输价值-11.5个点","油价崩跌-22%需求担忧"],"prev_key":"2026-06-01","prev_key_chain":["2026-06-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Broadcom miss sparks AI-spend doubt selloff","title_zh":"博通业绩不及预期引发AI支出存疑抛售","turn_id":"ai_software:peak:2026-06"}},"now":"AI Software & Platforms is in an Expansion/Trending phase (pos 44.2, rs_rank 20) after the 22.5% June 2026 selloff triggered by Broadcom's guidance miss; it has since stabilized but remains below its 200-day moving average, signaling the bounce is still a recovery, not a resumption of trend. The backdrop is reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%; oil +19.2%; copper-gold +18.3%), with Tech leading at +24.3% and a broadening tape (RSP +2.9% vs SPY), suggesting the application layer is benefiting from the post-Broadcom relief rally but faces a genuine headwind: DXY +3.4% and growth lagging value by -15.2% compress the long-duration multiples that define this basket. The BUY signal reflects a high-beta bounce in a tech-led reflation quad, but the 200-day remains overhead and the growth-minus-value spread staying deeply negative argues caution until enterprise AI monetization (Copilot seat ramp now at 20M paid seats, Palantir AIP bookings) accelerates enough to justify re-rating.","now_zh":"AI软件与平台处于扩张/趋势阶段(仓位44.2，相对强度排名20)，在2026年6月因博通业绩指引不及预期引发22.5%回撤后趋于稳定，但仍处于200日均线下方，反映当前反弹仍属修复性质而非趋势恢复。宏观背景为再通胀/增长向上象限(周期股+11.2% vs 防御股+6.9%；油价+19.2%；铜金比+18.3%)，科技以+24.3%领涨、市场广度转宽(RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%)，显示应用层受益于博通事件后的风险偏好回归，但面临真实阻力：DXY +3.4%与成长大幅跑输价值(-15.2%)持续压制长久期估值倍数。买入信号反映科技引领再通胀象限下的高贝塔反弹，但200日均线悬于头顶、成长-价值价差维持深度负值，在企业AI变现(Copilot付费席位已达2000万、Palantir AIP订单)加速验证前需保持谨慎——当前为周期中段反弹，而非新一轮超级周期启动。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-big_pharma":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"Big pharma surged +52.4% from January 2014 to July 2015, nearly tripling the S&P 500's +19.6%, in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad where defensives (+29.1%) overwhelmed cyclicals (+11.5%) as oil crashed -46.6% and the dollar surged +21.3% (TLT +20.6%). The ACA's expansion of insured Americans to 20 million new beneficiaries structurally lifted prescription drug volumes for large branded-drug companies, while bond proxy flows flooded into pharma's high-yield, defensive cash flows as rates fell sharply. Health led all GICS sectors at +42.7%, narrow breadth (RSP lagged SPY by -2.3%) confirmed mega-cap safety buying, and growth beat value by 9.2 points — a classic melt-up in quality/defensives as commodity-heavy cyclicals collapsed.","body_zh":"大型药企自2014年1月至2015年7月上涨+52.4%，几乎是标普500（+19.6%）的三倍，彼时处于经济放缓/通缩恐慌象限，防御股（+29.1%）大幅领先周期股（+11.5%），油价暴跌-46.6%，美元飙升+21.3%（TLT +20.6%）。《平价医疗法案》将2000万新增参保人纳入覆盖，从结构上提升了大型品牌药企的处方量；利率大幅下行推动债券替代品资金涌入药企高股息、抗衰退的现金流。医疗健康以+42.7%领涨所有GICS板块，窄幅行情（RSP跑输SPY -2.3%）确认了大盘股防御性买盘，成长跑赢价值9.2个百分点——是大宗商品周期股崩溃背景下质量/防御板块的典型融化上涨。","drivers":["ACA coverage expansion boosted branded-drug volumes","Deflation quad: oil -46.6%, dollar +21.3%, defensives +29.1%","TLT +20.6% rate fall made pharma a bond-proxy bid","Health led all sectors at +42.7%; narrow mega-cap breadth"],"drivers_zh":["ACA扩展保险覆盖，提升品牌药处方量","通缩象限：油价-46.6%、美元+21.3%、防御股+29.1%","TLT +20.6%利率下行使药企成为债券替代品","医疗健康以+42.7%领涨全板块；行情窄幅集中于大盘股"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"ACA volume boom lifts defensives in deflation quad","title_zh":"ACA扩容助推防御股；通缩象限中独领风骚","turn_id":"big_pharma:trough:2014-01"},"2015-07-20":{"body":"The China yuan devaluation on August 11, 2015 and subsequent global equity selloff drove VIX from 12 to 28 and slammed risk assets broadly, but pharma took an extra hit: on September 21, 2015, Hillary Clinton tweeted about Turing Pharmaceuticals' 5,500% Daraprim price hike, pledging a crackdown on drug price gouging, sending the iShares Biotech ETF down nearly 5% in a single session and sparking sustained selling across big pharma. Health fell -16.4% in the period, the second-worst GICS sector behind Materials (-17.1%), even as defensives fared relatively better (-7.7%) than cyclicals (-12.3%) — the China-led risk-off hit everything, but pharma's politically specific policy overhang amplified the sector's drawdown by roughly double versus the defensive universe.","body_zh":"2015年8月11日人民币贬值及随后的全球股市抛售将VIX从12推至28，重创风险资产，但药企遭受双重打击：2015年9月21日，希拉里·克林顿就图灵制药将Daraprim价格提涨5500%发推文，誓言打击药品「价格掠夺」，当日iShares生物科技ETF单日大跌近5%，大型药企遭持续抛售。该期间医疗健康以-16.4%跌至GICS板块倒数第二，仅好于材料（-17.1%），即便防御股（-7.7%）相对抗跌于周期股（-12.3%）——中国主导的风险厌恶席卷一切，但药企特有的政策压制使其跌幅约为防御类整体的两倍。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation Aug-11 triggered global risk-off; VIX 12→28","Clinton Sep-21 drug-pricing tweet sent biotech -5% in one session","Health -16.4% underperformed defensives -7.7%, double the sector drag","Credit stress: HYG-LQD -6.6%; oil -11.4% compounded commodity selloff"],"drivers_zh":["人民币贬值（8月11日）触发全球风险厌恶；VIX 12→28","克林顿9月21日药价推文致生物科技单日跌近5%","医疗健康-16.4%，跑输防御股-7.7%，拖累约为板块整体两倍","信用承压：HYG-LQD -6.6%；油价-11.4%叠加大宗商品抛售"],"prev_key":"2015-07-20","prev_key_chain":["2015-07-20"],"status":"exact","title":"China shock plus Clinton drug-pricing tweet crushed pharma","title_zh":"中国市场冲击叠加克林顿药价推文引爆抛售","turn_id":"big_pharma:peak:2015-07"},"2015-09-28":{"body":"From the September 28, 2015 selloff trough, markets mounted a sharp five-week relief rally as VIX collapsed from 28 to 15 and cyclicals (+14.2%) led defensives (+7.7%), with Energy (+19.2%) and Materials (+17.4%) rebounding on stabilizing China data and a brief oil bounce (+7.8%). Big pharma rode this broad risk-on recovery, gaining +17.7%, though it lagged the cyclical leaders — the rotation was a broad VIX compression move rather than pharma-specific. The Fed's October 2015 FOMC meeting declined to raise rates for the third consecutive time, removing an overhang and allowing rate-sensitive and beaten-down growth names to recover alongside the general market rebound.","body_zh":"自2015年9月28日抛售低点起，市场掀起五周大幅技术性反弹，VIX从28骤降至15，周期股（+14.2%）领先防御股（+7.7%），能源（+19.2%）和材料（+17.4%）随中国数据企稳、油价短暂反弹（+7.8%）而回升。大型药企借助这一宽基风险偏好复苏上涨+17.7%，但仍落后于周期领头羊——该轮回升是宏观VIX压缩驱动的整体修复，而非药企特有的利好。美联储2015年10月FOMC会议再度暂停加息，消除了一项压制因素，使利率敏感和超跌的成长板块随大市反弹一并修复。","drivers":["VIX 28→15 compression drove broad risk-on relief rally","Cyclicals +14.2% led; Energy +19.2%, Materials +17.4% on China stabilization","Oil +7.8% bounce provided commodity relief bid","Fed Oct-2015 FOMC skipped rate hike; rate overhang removed"],"drivers_zh":["VIX 28→15压缩驱动宽基风险偏好反弹","周期股+14.2%领跑；能源+19.2%、材料+17.4%随中国数据企稳","油价反弹+7.8%提供大宗商品喘息空间","美联储2015年10月FOMC再度暂停加息，消除利率压制"],"prev_key":"2015-09-28","prev_key_chain":["2015-09-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Dead-cat VIX relief; cyclical rebound lifts all sectors","title_zh":"VIX恐慌释放后技术性反弹；周期股带动全面修复","turn_id":"big_pharma:trough:2015-09"},"2015-11-03":{"body":"From November 2015 to February 2016, a second wave of oil collapse (WTI fell -45.3% over the leg, copper-gold -25.9%) and renewed China slowdown fears drove a deep risk-off episode: VIX surged from 15 to 28, the 10-year Treasury yield fell sharply (TLT +11.2%), credit spread widened (HYG-LQD -9.9%), and defensives (-2.5%) vastly outperformed cyclicals (-16.0%). Big pharma fell -18.1% in sympathy with the broader health sector decline, but the macro forces — not pharma fundamentals — were the primary driver. Energy and Financials led the carnage (-23.9% and -19.1%), while pharma's defensive characteristics offered only partial buffer relative to cyclical sectors; the Clinton drug-pricing narrative continued to suppress any sector-specific bid.","body_zh":"2015年11月至2016年2月，油价第二轮崩溃（该区间WTI下跌-45.3%，铜金比-25.9%）和中国增长恐慌再起，引发深度风险厌恶：VIX从15飙升至28，10年期美国国债收益率大幅下行（TLT +11.2%），信用利差走阔（HYG-LQD -9.9%），防御股（-2.5%）大幅跑赢周期股（-16.0%）。大型药企随医疗健康板块整体下跌-18.1%，但宏观力量而非药企基本面是主要驱动因素。能源和金融领跌（分别-23.9%和-19.1%），药企的防御属性仅对周期板块提供了部分缓冲；克林顿药价叙事持续压制任何板块特异性买盘。","drivers":["Oil -45.3% second leg collapse; copper-gold -25.9% China slowdown","VIX 15→28; TLT +11.2%; HYG-LQD credit stress -9.9%","Defensives -2.5% vs cyclicals -16.0%; pharma -18.1%","Clinton drug-pricing narrative sustained political overhang"],"drivers_zh":["油价-45.3%第二轮崩溃；铜金比-25.9%反映中国放缓","VIX 15→28；TLT +11.2%；HYG-LQD信用承压-9.9%","防御股-2.5%对周期股-16.0%；药企-18.1%","克林顿药价叙事持续施加政治压制"],"prev_key":"2015-11-03","prev_key_chain":["2015-11-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil crash redux and China growth scare; pharma falls with market","title_zh":"油价再度崩溃叠加中国增长恐慌；药企随市下行","turn_id":"big_pharma:peak:2015-11"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"The February 2016 global equity trough coincided with a coordinated G20/central bank signal (the so-called Shanghai Accord) that drove a powerful reflation trade: oil surged +50.7%, cyclicals (+21.3%) led defensives (+15.6%), high-beta beat low-vol by +14.4%, and breadth broadened sharply (RSP beat SPY by +3.0%). Big pharma gained +23.3%, keeping pace with the broad market rally (+19.1%), carried less by pharma-specific drivers and more by the general risk-on recovery as the probability of a Clinton presidency (and her drug-pricing crackdown) began to look less certain amid Trump's primary surge, providing partial political relief. The VIX compression from 28 to 13 and credit spread tightening (HYG-LQD +6.0%) confirmed a full macro regime shift out of the January-February 2016 panic.","body_zh":"2016年2月全球股市低点恰逢G20/央行协调信号（即「上海协议」），引发强劲的反通胀交易：油价飙升+50.7%，周期股（+21.3%）领先防御股（+15.6%），高贝塔跑赢低波动率+14.4%，行情明显走阔（RSP跑赢SPY +3.0%）。大型药企上涨+23.3%，与大市涨幅（+19.1%）基本持平，驱动力更多来自宏观风险偏好的整体复苏——随着特朗普初选异军突起，克林顿当选概率（及其药价打压）的不确定性上升，提供了部分政策层面的喘息空间。VIX从28压缩至13、信用利差收窄（HYG-LQD +6.0%）确认宏观环境彻底跳出1-2月的恐慌。","drivers":["Shanghai Accord reflation trade: oil +50.7%, VIX 28→13","Cyclicals +21.3% led; RSP beat SPY +3.0%; HYG-LQD +6.0% credit rally","Trump primary surge lowered Clinton drug-pricing probability","Broad risk-on recovery pulled pharma up alongside the market"],"drivers_zh":["上海协议反通胀交易：油价+50.7%，VIX 28→13","周期股+21.3%领涨；RSP跑赢SPY +3.0%；HYG-LQD信用利差收窄+6.0%","特朗普初选崛起降低克林顿药价打压概率","宏观风险偏好全面复苏带动药企随市上行"],"prev_key":"2016-02-11","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Shanghai Accord commodity bottom; broad reflation lifts pharma","title_zh":"上海协议商品触底；反通胀浪潮带动药企回升","turn_id":"big_pharma:trough:2016-02"},"2016-08-02":{"body":"From August 2016 to the November 3 election trough, big pharma fell -14.4% in a rare idiosyncratic selloff: SPY was only -2.7% and cyclicals (+0.2%) were flat while Health fell -12.1%. Clinton's August 24, 2016 tweet on drug pricing triggered fresh sector selling, amplifying the standing election-risk discount as polls showed her leading. Defensives underperformed (-7.5%) in a reflation-ish quad (Energy +4.3%, Financials +3.4%), meaning pharma's pain was political, not macro. The California Proposition 61 drug-pricing ballot initiative and rising Senate scrutiny of Mylan's EpiPen price hike in August 2016 deepened the policy cloud, creating a sustained overhang into the November vote.","body_zh":"2016年8月至11月3日大选前低点，大型药企下跌-14.4%，呈现罕见的个体化抛售：标普500仅-2.7%，周期股（+0.2%）几乎持平，而医疗健康跌-12.1%。克林顿2016年8月24日发出药价推文，触发新一轮板块抛售，在民调显示其领先的背景下进一步放大了大选风险折价。防御股（-7.5%）在偏反通胀的象限中跑输（能源+4.3%、金融+3.4%），说明药企的痛苦来自政治面而非宏观面。加州第61号提案（药品定价）及参议院8月对迈兰EpiPen涨价的审查加深了政策阴云，持续压制板块直至11月投票。","drivers":["Clinton Aug-24 drug-pricing tweet: targeted pharma political selloff","Health -12.1% vs SPY -2.7%; idiosyncratic, not macro drawdown","CA Prop 61 drug-pricing ballot initiative deepened overhang","Mylan EpiPen Senate scrutiny August 2016 stoked pricing fears"],"drivers_zh":["克林顿8月24日药价推文：政治性定向抛售药企","医疗健康-12.1%对比标普-2.7%；个体化而非宏观回撤","加州第61号药价提案加深政策压制","参议院8月审查迈兰EpiPen涨价，助燃定价恐惧"],"prev_key":"2016-08-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-08-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Election risk returns; Clinton drug-pricing tweets hit pharma","title_zh":"大选风险重燃；克林顿药价推文压制药企","turn_id":"big_pharma:peak:2016-08"},"2016-11-03":{"body":"Trump's November 8, 2016 election victory triggered an immediate +2 to 6% single-day rally for pharma across US and European names, as the Clinton drug-pricing crackdown risk evaporated and the California Prop 61 drug-pricing ballot initiative was defeated. Big pharma then rallied +47.9% to January 2018 — a major leg that kept pace with a dominant reflation/growth-up tape (Financials +57.6%, Tech +52.5%, SPY +40.8%), driven by: the December 2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (21% corporate rate) worth over $6 billion in combined savings for top-5 pharma companies and enabling $10 billion buyback programs at Pfizer, Merck, and AbbVie; reduced regulatory threat; and buoyant M&A momentum. Trump's January 2017 press conference comment that pharma companies were getting away with murder briefly hit the sector, but the market quickly priced the lack of follow-through on that threat.","body_zh":"2016年11月8日特朗普胜选，美国及欧洲药企股票当日即大涨2-6%，克林顿药价打压风险消散，加州第61号药价提案也告落败。大型药企随后上涨+47.9%至2018年1月——这是一段重大涨势，基本跟上了反通胀/增长向上主线（金融+57.6%、科技+52.5%、标普500 +40.8%），驱动力包括：2017年12月《减税与就业法案》（企业税率降至21%），为前五大药企节税逾60亿美元，并触发辉瑞、默沙东、艾伯维各百亿美元回购计划；监管威胁降低；并购动能旺盛（百时美施贵宝/新基、艾伯维/艾尔建）。特朗普2017年1月新闻发布会上称药企「在谋杀中逃脱」，短暂冲击板块，但市场迅速定价其缺乏后续行动。","drivers":["Trump Nov-8 election win: Clinton drug-pricing overhang removed instantly","Dec-2017 TCJA: 21% corporate rate, $45B+ pharma buybacks","Reflation tape: Financials +57.6%, Tech +52.5%; dollar -8.3% tailwind","M&A boom: BMS/Celgene, AbbVie/Allergan pipelines being built"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普11月8日胜选：克林顿药价风险即时消散","2017年12月TCJA：企业税率21%，药企逾450亿美元回购","反通胀行情：金融+57.6%、科技+52.5%；美元-8.3%顺风","并购潮：百时美/新基、艾伯维/艾尔建管线布局"],"prev_key":"2016-11-03","prev_key_chain":["2016-11-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump win removed Clinton overhang; tax reform and M&A era","title_zh":"特朗普胜选消除克林顿风险；税改与并购时代开启","turn_id":"big_pharma:trough:2016-11"},"2018-01-26":{"body":"The January 26, 2018 broad market peak — driven by the late-January wage inflation scare and a surge in 10-year yields — triggered a sharp correction that paradoxically hurt defensives (-9.7%) more than cyclicals (-5.9%). Big pharma fell -15.4% from its peak, the second-worst GICS sector behind only Staples (-15.8%), as rising rates compressed the yield-spread appeal of pharmaceutical dividend stocks. The dollar strengthened +4.5%, further pressuring multinationals, and the goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation quad (Tech -1.1% led) showed investors rotating into quality growth not defensives. The correction bottomed in February 2018 ahead of Trump's May 2018 American Patients First drug-pricing speech, which paradoxically sent pharma stocks up 2-3% on the day by confining reforms to PBMs rather than manufacturers.","body_zh":"2018年1月26日大市见顶——1月下旬工资通胀恐慌及10年期美债收益率飙升驱动——随后引发急跌，防御股（-9.7%）的跌幅反而大于周期股（-5.9%）。大型药企自高点下跌-15.4%，仅次于必需消费品（-15.8%），成为GICS跌幅第二大板块，因利率上升压缩了药企高股息相对债券的利差吸引力。美元走强+4.5%，进一步压制跨国药企，而黄金时代/增长向上/低通胀象限（科技-1.1%领跌最少）显示投资者向优质成长轮动，而非防御。该次调整于2018年2月触底，此后特朗普5月宣布「美国患者优先」药价蓝图，当日药企股价反涨2-3%，因改革矛头指向药品福利管理机构而非药企本身。","drivers":["Late-Jan wage inflation scare: 10Y yields surged, VIX 11→15","Rate-shock: defensives -9.7% vs cyclicals -5.9%; pharma yield-spread compressed","Dollar +4.5% headwind for multinational pharma earnings","Growth beat value by +3.8%; capital rotated to Tech not defensives"],"drivers_zh":["1月下旬工资通胀恐慌：10年期美债收益率飙升，VIX 11→15","利率冲击：防御股-9.7%对周期股-5.9%；药企股息利差压缩","美元+4.5%压制跨国药企盈利","成长跑赢价值+3.8%；资金轮动至科技而非防御"],"prev_key":"2018-01-26","prev_key_chain":["2018-01-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-shock correction cuts defensives most; growth beats","title_zh":"利率冲击引发回调；防御股跌幅最深","turn_id":"big_pharma:peak:2018-01"},"2018-05-08":{"body":"From May 8 to October 3, 2018, big pharma outperformed sharply with a +23.8% gain while SPY rose only +10.3%, leading all sectors in Health +19.7%. Trump's May 11, 2018 American Patients First blueprint — which directed reform pressure toward pharmacy benefit managers rather than drug manufacturers, lacked legally binding price controls, and was seen as kicking the can down the road — sent pharma stocks up 2-3% the day of announcement. The macro backdrop reinforced the bid: a stagflation-ish quad (defensives +12.5% vs cyclicals +7.1%), a stronger dollar (+2.8%) hurting Materials and Financials, and narrow breadth (RSP lagged SPY -2.6%) all pushed capital into defensive healthcare as a quality refuge. Merck, Pfizer, and AbbVie were among the S&P's best performers in 2018 by this point.","body_zh":"2018年5月8日至10月3日，大型药企大幅跑赢，涨+23.8%，而标普500仅+10.3%，医疗健康（+19.7%）领涨所有板块。特朗普2018年5月11日宣布「美国患者优先」蓝图——将改革压力指向药品福利管理机构而非药企本身，缺乏具法律约束力的价格管控，被视为推迟解决——当日药企股价上涨2-3%。宏观背景强化了买盘：偏滞胀象限（防御股+12.5%对周期股+7.1%），美元走强+2.8%打压材料和金融，行情窄幅（RSP跑输SPY -2.6%），共同将资金推入防御性医疗健康作为质量避风港。默沙东、辉瑞、艾伯维成为标普年内表现最佳的成分股之一。","drivers":["Trump May-11 American Patients First speech: pharma stocks +2-3% on day","Stagflation-ish quad: defensives +12.5% vs cyclicals +7.1%","Dollar +2.8% headwind for cyclicals; narrow breadth RSP -2.6% vs SPY","Merck/Pfizer/AbbVie quality-dividend rotation as market wobbled"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普5月11日「美国患者优先」讲话：药企当日涨2-3%","偏滞胀象限：防御股+12.5%对周期股+7.1%","美元+2.8%压制周期股；行情窄幅RSP落后SPY -2.6%","市场动摇时资金轮向默沙东/辉瑞/艾伯维质量股息品种"],"prev_key":"2018-05-08","prev_key_chain":["2018-05-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump drug-pricing speech relief; stagflation-ish defensive bid","title_zh":"特朗普药价讲话利好释放；偏滞胀环境催生防御买盘","turn_id":"big_pharma:trough:2018-05"},"2018-10-03":{"body":"The October 3, 2018 broad market peak marked the start of a brutal Q4 selloff as Fed Chair Powell's comment that rates were a long way from neutral triggered a rapid repricing of the rate path: VIX surged from 12 to 36, Tech and Industrials fell -23.8% and -23.7%, oil collapsed -44.3%, credit spreads blew out (HYG-LQD -5.5%), and SPY fell -19.2%. Big pharma dropped -14.7% — painful, but offering meaningful relative protection versus cyclicals (-22.5%) as the classic flight-to-safety playbook applied (defensives -8.1% vs cyclicals -22.5%). Notably, Merck and Pfizer outperformed within healthcare, with the large-cap dividend quality of big pharma providing relative shelter compared to growth-heavy biotech.","body_zh":"2018年10月3日大市见顶，美联储主席鲍威尔「距中性利率还有很长路」的表态触发利率路径快速重定价，随后Q4经历残酷下行：VIX从12飙至36，科技和工业分别跌-23.8%和-23.7%，油价崩跌-44.3%，信用利差急扩（HYG-LQD -5.5%），标普500跌-19.2%。大型药企下跌-14.7%——虽然痛苦，但相对周期股（-22.5%）提供了有意义的相对防护，经典的避险剧本发挥作用（防御股-8.1%对周期股-22.5%）。值得注意的是，默沙东和辉瑞在医疗健康内部表现相对突出，大型药企的大盘股股息质量属性相比成长型生物科技提供了相对避风港。","drivers":["Powell Oct-3 long-way-from-neutral comment repriced rate path; VIX 12→36","Tech -23.8%, Industrials -23.7%, oil -44.3%; flight-to-safety rotation","Pharma -14.7% vs cyclicals -22.5%; defensive buffer confirmed","Merck/Pfizer quality-dividend outperformed within healthcare"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔10月3日「距中性利率还有很长路」重定价；VIX 12→36","科技-23.8%、工业-23.7%、油价-44.3%；避险轮动","药企-14.7%对周期股-22.5%；防御缓冲得到验证","默沙东/辉瑞质量股息品种在医疗健康内部相对跑赢"],"prev_key":"2018-10-03","prev_key_chain":["2018-10-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell rate-hike shock triggers broad crash; pharma defensive buffer","title_zh":"鲍威尔加息冲击引发全面崩跌；药企发挥防御缓冲作用","turn_id":"big_pharma:peak:2018-10"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"From the December 24, 2018 Christmas Eve trough, big pharma rallied +33.7% to March 2020 — underperforming Tech (+64.9%) and SPY (+36.0%) in a mega-cap growth-led, narrow-breadth tape (RSP lagged SPY -7.4%, TLT +30.9%), but still grinding higher. The Fed's January 2019 pivot to patience and subsequent three rate cuts (July, September, October 2019) kept the yield environment benign, removing the 2018 rate-shock headwind for dividend names. AbbVie announced its $63 billion Allergan acquisition in June 2019, reinforcing the M&A narrative and providing pipeline expansion against Humira's looming biosimilar competition. The stagflation-ish quad context (defensives +32.5% vs cyclicals +28.4%) and the long TLT rally confirmed bond-proxy buying of pharma as the cycle matured, before Covid disrupted everything in early 2020.","body_zh":"自2018年12月24日平安夜低点起，大型药企上涨+33.7%至2020年3月——在科技股（+64.9%）和标普500（+36.0%）主导的窄幅大盘股成长行情中（RSP落后SPY -7.4%，TLT +30.9%）跑输，但仍稳步走高。美联储2019年1月转为观望，随后三次降息（7月、9月、10月），使收益率环境温和，消除了2018年利率冲击对分红股的压制。艾伯维2019年6月宣布630亿美元收购艾尔建，强化并购叙事并在Humira生物仿制药竞争来临前拓展管线。偏滞胀象限背景（防御股+32.5%对周期股+28.4%）及TLT长期上涨确认了债券替代品属性的药企买盘，直至2020年初新冠疫情打乱了一切。","drivers":["Fed Jan-2019 pivot + 3 rate cuts (Jul/Sep/Oct): yield headwind removed","AbbVie $63B Allergan deal June 2019: pipeline M&A bid","Stagflation-ish quad: defensives +32.5%, bond-proxy bid (TLT +30.9%)","Narrow breadth, mega-cap led tape; pharma lagged Tech but still gained"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月转向+三次降息（7/9/10月）：利率压制消除","艾伯维630亿美元收购艾尔建（2019年6月）：并购驱动管线扩张","偏滞胀象限：防御股+32.5%，债券替代品买盘（TLT +30.9%）","行情窄幅、大盘股主导；药企落后科技股但仍上行"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot 2019 and M&A boom carry pharma through pre-Covid peak","title_zh":"2019年美联储转向与并购潮将药企托举至疫前高点","turn_id":"big_pharma:trough:2018-12"},"2020-03-04":{"body":"From March 4 to March 23, 2020, the Covid-19 pandemic triggered one of the fastest equity crashes in history: SPY fell -28.3% in 13 trading days, VIX spiked to 62, oil collapsed -50.1%, the dollar surged +5.3%, and credit markets froze (HYG-LQD -7.2%). Big pharma fell -20.1% — modestly better than the SPY but significantly outperformed by growth/Tech (-24.5%) in a flight to absolute liquidity. The selloff was a macro liquidity event, not a sector-specific move: even defensives fell -27.2% on average. Initial confusion about whether pharma would benefit from a pandemic cure or suffer supply-chain disruption (active pharmaceutical ingredient dependence on China), combined with forced portfolio deleveraging, drove the indiscriminate selloff across all assets.","body_zh":"2020年3月4日至3月23日，新冠疫情引发历史上最快的股市崩跌之一：标普500在13个交易日内下跌-28.3%，VIX飙至62，油价崩跌-50.1%，美元走强+5.3%，信用市场冻结（HYG-LQD -7.2%）。大型药企下跌-20.1%——略好于标普500，但在奔向绝对流动性的大背景下仍不及成长/科技（-24.5%）相对表现。该次抛售是宏观流动性事件而非板块特异性行情：即便防御股平均也下跌-27.2%。市场对药企究竟受益于疫情治疗机会还是受损于供应链断裂（活性药物成分依赖中国）的初始困惑，叠加投资组合强制去杠杆，引发跨资产类别的无差别抛售。","drivers":["Covid pandemic triggered; VIX 32→62; SPY -28.3% in 13 trading days","Forced deleveraging: all assets liquidated; defensives -27.2%","Dollar safe-haven surge +5.3%; oil -50.1%; credit frozen HYG-LQD -7.2%","Pharma API China supply-chain uncertainty compounded indiscriminate selloff"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情爆发；VIX 32→62；标普500在13个交易日跌-28.3%","强制去杠杆：各类资产均遭平仓；防御股-27.2%","美元避险飙升+5.3%；油价-50.1%；信用市场冻结HYG-LQD -7.2%","药企活性药物成分依赖中国的供应链不确定性加剧无差别抛售"],"prev_key":"2020-03-04","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Covid pandemic liquidity panic: pharma falls with everything","title_zh":"新冠疫情流动性恐慌：药企随市全线下跌","turn_id":"big_pharma:peak:2020-03"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From March 23, 2020 to September 16, 2024, big pharma gained +97.1% — but it was the worst-performing major group in a historic bull market: SPY rose +169.0%, Energy +340.6%, Tech +223.6%, and even defensives averaged +106.9%. Three distinct sub-phases drove this long leg: (1) 2020-2021 Covid vaccine windfall — Pfizer's Comirnaty and Merck's Molnupiravir generated unprecedented emergency revenues, lifting the group, but the windfall was one-time; (2) 2022 rate-shock headwind — the Fed raised rates 425 bps, crushing long-duration and dividend yield names; and (3) the August 2022 Inflation Reduction Act's Medicare drug price negotiation provisions, which CMS implemented aggressively (38-79% price cuts on first 10 drugs), structurally reset long-term revenue expectations and triggered sustained multiple compression. Semis surged +359.5%, high-beta crushed low-vol by +153.3%, and the market rewarded growth not yield — pharma was structurally left behind as the AI-driven mega-cap era concentrated returns elsewhere.","body_zh":"2020年3月23日至2024年9月16日，大型药企上涨+97.1%——但这是历史性牛市中表现最差的主要组别：标普500涨+169.0%，能源+340.6%，科技+223.6%，即便防御股平均也达+106.9%。这段长腿由三个不同的子阶段构成：（1）2020-2021年新冠疫苗红利——辉瑞Comirnaty和默沙东Molnupiravir带来前所未有的紧急收入，托举该板块，但此为一次性；（2）2022年利率冲击——美联储加息425个基点，重创长久期和股息收益品种；（3）2022年8月《通胀削减法案》的医保药品价格谈判条款，CMS激进执行（首批10种药品降价38-79%），从结构上重置了长期收入预期，触发持续的估值压缩。半导体涨+359.5%，高贝塔跑赢低波动率+153.3%，市场奖励成长而非收益——人工智能驱动的大盘股时代将回报高度集中于别处，药企被结构性抛在身后。","drivers":["Covid vaccine windfall (2020-21) then structural mean-reversion","Fed 425bps rate hikes 2022: dividend/yield compression","IRA Aug-2022: Medicare negotiation 38-79% price cuts reset revenue expectations","AI/semis +359.5% melt-up concentrated returns away from pharma"],"drivers_zh":["2020-21年新冠疫苗红利随后结构性均值回归","美联储2022年加息425基点：股息/收益压缩","IRA 2022年8月：医保谈判降价38-79%重置收入预期","AI/半导体+359.5%融化上涨将回报高度集中于其他板块"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-Covid recovery: vaccine windfall then IRA and rate-hike left behind","title_zh":"疫后复苏：疫苗红利后遭IRA与加息双重压制，大幅落后市场","turn_id":"big_pharma:trough:2020-03"},"2024-09-16":{"body":"From September 2024, big pharma ground down -20.0% into May 2025 even as SPY rose +5.4% — a glaring idiosyncratic underperformance driven by politics, not macro. The tape was goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation (cyclicals +6.1% vs defensives -6.2%; TLT -13.4% on rising yields; RSP lagged SPY -4.0%), punishing low-beta yield names broadly, but pharma's drag stacked sector-specific catalysts on top: the November 2024 election of Trump's second term brought RFK Jr.'s nomination to HHS Secretary (FDA pathway uncertainty, vaccine skepticism); and the May 12, 2025 Most-Favored-Nation executive order threatened to peg all US drug prices to the lowest OECD price, potentially cutting revenues by up to 90% on some products. Even through the April 2025 tariff episode, pharma fell for its own reasons — the looming IRA price reset compounding MFN fears alongside the structural Keytruda/Pfizer multi-product patent cliff visible by 2027-2028.","body_zh":"自2024年9月起，尽管标普500上涨+5.4%，大型药企仍在日益浓重的政策阴云下震荡下行-20.0%至2025年5月——这是刺眼的个体化跑输，政治面而非宏观面主导。当时行情为黄金时代/增长向上/低通胀（周期股+6.1%对防御股-6.2%；TLT -13.4%利率上行；RSP落后SPY -4.0%），普遍惩罚低贝塔收益股，但药企的拖累在此之上叠加了板块特异性催化剂：2024年11月特朗普第二任期将RFK Jr.提名为卫生与公共服务部长（FDA审批路径不确定性、疫苗怀疑主义）；2025年5月12日最惠国定价行政令威胁将所有美国药品价格与最低OECD价格挂钩，部分产品收入可能削减高达90%。即便穿越2025年4月关税事件，药企也因自身原因下跌——IRA价格重置即将来临，叠加MFN恐惧，以及可见于2027-2028年的Keytruda/辉瑞多产品专利悬崖。","drivers":["Nov-2024 election: RFK Jr. to HHS (FDA/vaccine pathway uncertainty)","May-12-2025 MFN executive order: OECD price peg, up to 90% revenue risk","Rate-driven tape (TLT -13.4%): low-beta defensives -6.2% broadly weak","Patent cliff: Keytruda LOE 2028, Pfizer multi-product expiries in view"],"drivers_zh":["2024年11月大选：RFK Jr.执掌HHS（FDA/疫苗路径不确定性）","2025年5月12日MFN行政令：与OECD价格挂钩，部分收入风险高达90%","利率驱动行情（TLT -13.4%）：低贝塔防御股-6.2%整体走弱","专利悬崖：Keytruda 2028年独占权到期，辉瑞多产品到期在望"],"prev_key":"2024-09-16","prev_key_chain":["2024-09-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Idiosyncratic policy collapse: MFN order and RFK shock amid rising tape","title_zh":"个体化政策崩盘：MFN行政令与RFK冲击叠加上涨大盘","turn_id":"big_pharma:peak:2024-09"},"2025-05-14":{"body":"From the May 2025 low, big pharma rallied +41.8% to February 2026 — a recovery built on defensiveness and policy fatigue in a stagflation-ish, falling-rate window (TLT +10.1%, DXY -3.4%, copper-gold -34.2%) where defensives (+21.6%) finally matched cyclicals (+19.8%). With the MFN order's actual bite proving slower and more legally complex than feared (ongoing litigation), the market stopped pricing the worst case, and the group caught a genuine defensive bid — cheap valuations (trading at 11% below long-term P/E average), fat dividends, and recession-resistant cash flows exactly suited to an environment where AI/high-beta wobbled and the 2026 oil shock raised macro risk. Semis surged +64.4% (risk-on) but growth underperformed value by -9.0 points, confirming value rotation into defensive dividend names. The group's peak in February 2026 as the current reflation tape took hold confirms the rally as a regime-transition placeholder, not a structural re-rating.","body_zh":"自2025年5月低点起，大型药企上涨+41.8%至2026年2月——这是建立在防御性与政策疲劳之上的复苏，契合当时偏滞胀、利率下行的窗口（TLT +10.1%、DXY -3.4%、铜金比-34.2%），防御股（+21.6%）终于追平周期股（+19.8%）。随着MFN行政令的实际执行被证明比预期更慢、法律挑战更复杂（持续诉讼），市场停止定价最坏情形，该组别获得真正的防御性买盘——低估值（市盈率较长期均值低11%）、丰厚股息、抗衰退现金流，正是AI/高贝塔交易动摇、2026年油价冲击抬高宏观风险时投资者所需的画像。半导体涨+64.4%（风险偏好），但成长跑输价值-9.0个百分点，确认价值轮动进入防御股息品种。该组别于2026年2月随当前反通胀行情展开而见顶，证实此轮上涨是政策环境过渡期的占位反弹，而非结构性重新定价。","drivers":["Stagflation-ish/falling-rate window: TLT +10.1%, DXY -3.4%; defensives matched cyclicals","MFN legal complexity slowed execution; worst-case pricing reversed","Value beat growth by +9.0pts; pharma cheap (11% below LT P/E)","2026 oil shock raised macro risk; dividend/recession-resistant bid"],"drivers_zh":["偏滞胀/利率下行窗口：TLT +10.1%、DXY -3.4%；防御股追平周期股","MFN法律复杂性延缓执行；最坏情形定价逆转","价值跑赢成长+9.0百分点；药企估值便宜（低于长期市盈率11%）","2026年油价冲击抬高宏观风险；股息/抗衰退买盘涌入"],"prev_key":"2025-05-14","prev_key_chain":["2025-05-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Policy-fatigue defensive bid in stagflation hiding place","title_zh":"政策疲劳后的防御性买盘：滞胀环境中的避风港反弹","turn_id":"big_pharma:trough:2025-05"}},"now":"Big Pharma is in a Downturn phase (pos 32.4, Rolling over) at a weak RS rank of 40 versus SPY, sitting behind a reflation/growth-up tape that is not its moment: Tech leads +24.3%, Energy +21.5%, Industrials +15.8%, while defensives average only +6.9% against cyclicals +11.2%. A stronger dollar (+3.4% DXY), broadening breadth (RSP beating SPY by +2.9%), rising oil (+19.2%), and a copper-gold ratio up +18.3% all point to a reflationary, cyclical-led regime where low-beta dividend names like Merck, Pfizer, Bristol-Myers, AbbVie, and J&J are crowded out. The group peaked in late February 2026 after a +42% recovery from the May 2025 MFN-shock trough and has now rolled over: the Most-Favored-Nation executive order's negotiating pressure has not abated, RFK Jr. at HHS injects ongoing FDA and vaccine-pathway uncertainty, and the structural patent cliff (Keytruda LOE 2028, Pfizer multi-product cliff) weighs on pipeline visibility. Without a meaningful macro risk-off rotation or a hard recession scare to drive a flight-to-safety bid, Big Pharma stays a value/yield holding-pattern laggard in the current reflation wave.","now_zh":"大型药企处于下行阶段（位置32.4，见顶回落），相对于标普500的强弱排名仅40位，在当前反通胀/增长向上的行情中明显落后：科技股领涨+24.3%、能源+21.5%、工业+15.8%，而防御股平均仅+6.9%，周期股+11.2%。美元走强（DXY +3.4%）、市场走阔（RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%）、油价上涨（+19.2%）、铜金比攀升（+18.3%），共同指向一个反通胀、周期主导的环境，低贝塔分红型的默沙东、辉瑞、百时美施贵宝、艾伯维、强生等难以获得资金青睐。该组别于2026年2月下旬见顶，自2025年5月MFN冲击低点反弹+42%后再度转弱：最惠国定价行政令的谈判压力未消，RFK Jr.执掌卫生与公共服务部带来持续的FDA/疫苗审批路径不确定性，专利悬崖（Keytruda 2028年独占权到期、辉瑞多产品专利到期）继续压制管线能见度。若没有显著的宏观避险轮动或衰退恐慌驱动的防御性买盘，大型药企仍将是当前反通胀浪潮中的价值/收益滞留者。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-critical_minerals":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"Rare earth equities limped +9.2% from January 2014 to April 2015, dramatically underperforming SPY (+18.5%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. The WTO ruled against China's rare earth export quotas in August 2014, prompting China to abolish the quota system in January 2015; the resulting price-floor removal knocked the investment thesis for non-Chinese producers. The macro backdrop compounded the damage: DXY surged +20% (a direct headwind for dollar-priced materials), oil collapsed -39.2%, and copper-gold fell -14.1%. Defensives vastly outperformed (avg +27.7% vs cyclicals +13.1%); materials were among the worst GICS sectors (+12.5%), and the basket's meager 9.2% gain reflects its status as a lagging commodity play in a dollar-melt-up environment.","body_zh":"稀土股从2014年1月至2015年4月仅涨+9.2%，大幅落后SPY（+18.5%），处于放缓/通缩恐慌quad。WTO于2014年8月裁定中国稀土出口配额违规，中国随即于2015年1月取消配额制度，价格底线撤除击垮了非中国生产商的投资逻辑。宏观背景雪上加霜：DXY飙升+20%（美元计价材料的直接逆风），油价崩盘-39.2%，铜金比下跌-14.1%。防御板块大幅跑赢（均值+27.7%对周期+13.1%）；材料是表现最差的GICS板块之一（+12.5%），篮子的微薄9.2%涨幅印证其在美元融涨环境中的滞后大宗属性。","drivers":["WTO quota removal ends rare earth price support","DXY +20% crushes dollar-priced materials","Molycorp bankruptcy (June 2025) signals ex-China supply collapse","Slowdown/deflation-scare quad: defensives +27.7% vs cyclicals +13.1%"],"drivers_zh":["WTO配额解除，稀土价格支撑消失","DXY +20%重压美元计价材料","Molycorp破产信号非中国供应体系崩溃","放缓/通缩恐慌quad：防御+27.7%对周期+13.1%"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-quota-removal drift, dollar crushing materials","title_zh":"WTO配额解除后漂移，强美元重压材料","turn_id":"critical_minerals:trough:2014-01"},"2015-04-24":{"body":"A devastating -56.5% selloff from April 2015 to February 2016, the worst leg in this series' history to that point. Molycorp — the lone US rare earth producer and bellwether — filed for bankruptcy in June 2025, confirming that China's post-WTO-ruling supply flood had made Western rare earth mining economically unviable. The macro regime aligned in the worst possible way: flight-to-safety with defensives flat (-1.1%) while cyclicals crashed (-14.3%), VIX spiked from 12 to 23, copper-gold fell -22.2%, and oil plunged another -45.9%. China's economic slowdown scare (August 2015 equity crash, yuan devaluation) hammered commodity demand expectations globally; the broad Materials SPDR fell -17.8% while Energy fell -30.2%.","body_zh":"从2015年4月至2016年2月惨跌-56.5%，为该系列史上最惨重的一段。美国唯一稀土生产商Molycorp于2015年6月申请破产，印证中国在WTO裁决后的供应洪流已使西方稀土采矿在经济上不可行。宏观regime呈最恶劣组合：避险抛售，防御板块持平（-1.1%）而周期板块暴跌（-14.3%），VIX从12飙至23，铜金比下跌-22.2%，油价再跌-45.9%。中国经济放缓恐慌（2015年8月股市崩盘、人民币贬值）重创全球大宗需求预期；材料SPDR跌-17.8%，能源跌-30.2%。","drivers":["Molycorp bankruptcy (June 2015) destroys US rare earth equity thesis","China growth scare / August 2015 yuan devaluation crushes commodity demand","Oil -45.9%, copper-gold -22.2%: broad commodity rout","Flight-to-safety: defensives flat vs cyclicals -14.3%, VIX 12→23"],"drivers_zh":["Molycorp破产（2015年6月）摧毁美国稀土股逻辑","中国增长恐慌/2015年8月人民币贬值压垮大宗需求","油价-45.9%、铜金比-22.2%：全面大宗崩盘","避险：防御持平对周期-14.3%，VIX 12→23"],"prev_key":"2015-04-24","prev_key_chain":["2015-04-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Molycorp collapse triggers 56% rare earth wipeout","title_zh":"Molycorp破产触发稀土-56%暴跌","turn_id":"critical_minerals:peak:2015-04"},"2016-02-05":{"body":"A ferocious +92.1% rally from the February 2016 trough to September 2016, the first true commodity reflation trade. The pivot catalyst was the Shanghai Accord (February 2016 G20) at which major economies coordinated a weaker dollar and stimulus, which broke the DXY downtrend (DXY -2.1% over the leg), and China unleashed a massive credit impulse in Q1 2016 that directly boosted commodity demand. Oil surged +54.2%, the quad flipped to reflation/growth-up, cyclicals (+20.8%) crushed defensives (+11.4%), and VIX compressed from 23 to 13. The broad Materials SPDR was the second-best GICS sector (+21.3%); rare earth and strategic metal stocks, depressed to multi-decade lows post-Molycorp, rebounded violently as survivors repriced. Breadth was broad (RSP-SPY +2.8%) and credit rallied (HYG-LQD +5.3%), confirming a genuine risk-on reflationary rotation.","body_zh":"从2016年2月低点至9月，凶猛反弹+92.1%，首次真正意义上的大宗通胀交易。转折催化剂为2016年2月G20上海协议，主要经济体协调美元走弱和刺激政策，打破DXY上升趋势（该段DXY -2.1%），中国2016年一季度释放大规模信贷冲动直接拉动大宗需求。油价飙升+54.2%，quad翻转为反通胀/增长向上，周期板块（+20.8%）大幅跑赢防御（+11.4%），VIX从23压缩至13。材料SPDR为第二强GICS板块（+21.3%）；Molycorp倒闭后跌至数十年低点的稀土战略金属股激烈反弹重估。市场广度宽（RSP-SPY +2.8%），信用上涨（HYG-LQD +5.3%），确认真实的风险偏好通胀轮动。","drivers":["Shanghai Accord / G20 stimulus breaks DXY downtrend","China credit impulse Q1 2016 drives commodity demand surge","Oil +54.2% leads reflation trade; Materials SPDR second-best sector","Risk-on: VIX 23→13, cyclicals +20.8% vs defensives +11.4%"],"drivers_zh":["上海协议/G20刺激打破DXY上升趋势","中国2016年一季度信贷冲动推动大宗需求激增","油价+54.2%引领反通胀交易；材料SPDR第二强板块","风险偏好：VIX 23→13，周期+20.8%对防御+11.4%"],"prev_key":"2016-02-05","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Commodity reflation rip: +92% off the panic low","title_zh":"大宗反弹暴涨：从恐慌低点+92%","turn_id":"critical_minerals:trough:2016-02"},"2016-09-08":{"body":"A sharp -30.1% selloff from September to November 2016, coinciding with the Trump election and its immediate aftermath of a violent bond selloff. TLT fell -11.7% as 10-year Treasury yields surged from ~1.6% to ~2.4% in weeks — one of the fastest yield moves in decades — driven by expectations of Trump's fiscal stimulus and infrastructure spending. Paradoxically, the broader equity market (SPY +0.7%) and cyclicals (+3.0%) held up as Financials (+11.9%) and Industrials (+4.9%) rocketed on the Trump trade; but high-beta commodity stocks that had run +92% in seven months were sold to fund the rotation into banks and industrials. DXY surged +6.2% (a direct materials headwind), and dollar-sensitive rare earth and lithium names gave back a third of their gains.","body_zh":"从2016年9月至11月急跌-30.1%，恰逢特朗普当选及随后的债券暴跌。TLT下跌-11.7%，10年期美债收益率数周内从约1.6%飙至约2.4%——数十年来最快的收益率走势之一，由特朗普财政刺激和基建支出预期驱动。悖论的是，大盘（SPY +0.7%）和周期板块（+3.0%）在金融（+11.9%）和工业（+4.9%）的特朗普行情中守住阵地；但经过7个月+92%大涨的高贝塔大宗商品股被抛售，资金轮动至银行和工业股。DXY飙升+6.2%（材料的直接逆风），美元敏感的稀土锂矿股回吐三分之一涨幅。","drivers":["Trump election rate shock: TLT -11.7%, 10yr yield 1.6%→2.4%","DXY +6.2% post-election surge crushes dollar-denominated materials","Sector rotation OUT of commodity plays INTO Financials (+11.9%) and Industrials (+4.9%)","Profit-taking after +92% run in 7 months"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普当选利率冲击：TLT -11.7%，10年期收益率1.6%→2.4%","美元选后飙升+6.2%压垮以美元计价的材料","板块轮动：资金流出大宗商品股，流入金融（+11.9%）和工业（+4.9%）","7个月+92%大涨后的获利回吐"],"prev_key":"2016-09-08","prev_key_chain":["2016-09-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump-election rate shock: -30% yield-surge selloff","title_zh":"特朗普当选利率冲击：收益率飙升-30%","turn_id":"critical_minerals:peak:2016-09"},"2016-11-17":{"body":"The defining multi-year bull run of this era: +228.3% from November 2016 to September 2018, driven by the emergence of the EV battery metals narrative. Lithium carbonate prices tripled in 2017-2018 on surging EV demand projections; cobalt prices doubled in 2017 as the Democratic Republic of Congo supply risks were flagged; and the broader reflation/growth-up macro regime (oil +55.8%, DXY -6.6%, VIX calm at 12-13) provided a powerful tailwind for all commodity equities. The tech and semis melt-up (SMH +56.6%, growth>value +28.3%) did not crowd out materials — instead, the EV narrative linked rare earths and battery metals directly to the tech demand story. SPY returned +38.5%; the basket returned +228.3%. China's dominance of rare earth processing made these names the highest-leverage plays on the EV supply chain buildout.","body_zh":"这一时代的决定性多年牛市：从2016年11月至2018年9月上涨+228.3%，由EV电池金属叙事的兴起驱动。碳酸锂价格在2017-2018年因EV需求预测激增而翻三倍；钴价格在2017年因刚果民主共和国供应风险曝光而翻倍；更广泛的反通胀/增长向上宏观regime（油价+55.8%、DXY -6.6%、VIX平静于12-13）为所有大宗商品股提供强力顺风。科技和半导体融涨（SMH +56.6%，成长>价值+28.3%）并未挤压材料——相反，EV叙事将稀土和电池金属直接与科技需求故事挂钩。SPY回报+38.5%；篮子回报+228.3%。中国对稀土加工的垄断使这些标的成为EV供应链建设中杠杆最高的投资标的。","drivers":["Lithium and cobalt prices triple/double on EV demand surge 2017-2018","DXY -6.6% multi-year weakness tailwinds dollar-priced commodities","Reflation quad: oil +55.8%, cyclicals +36.9% vs defensives +25.0%","EV supply-chain re-rating links rare earths to tech demand narrative"],"drivers_zh":["锂和钴价格因EV需求激增而翻倍/三倍（2017-2018年）","DXY -6.6%多年走弱为美元计价大宗商品提供顺风","反通胀quad：油价+55.8%，周期+36.9%对防御+25.0%","EV供应链重估将稀土与科技需求叙事直接挂钩"],"prev_key":"2016-11-17","prev_key_chain":["2016-11-17"],"status":"exact","title":"EV/battery metals supercycle: +228% over 22 months","title_zh":"EV/电池金属超级周期：22个月+228%","turn_id":"critical_minerals:trough:2016-11"},"2018-09-21":{"body":"A prolonged -48.5% bear from September 2018 to March 2020, combining three distinct hits: first, the 2018-2019 US-China trade war tariff escalation (Beijing imposed 25% retaliatory tariffs on US rare earths in mid-2018, and when Xi Jinping toured a rare earth facility after the Huawei blacklisting in May 2019, markets interpreted it as a threat to restrict rare earth exports — initially negative for ex-China stocks as valuations compressed); second, the 2019 growth slowdown (the Fed went from hiking to cutting; oil fell -67.0%; broad cyclicals fell -33.4%); and third, the March 2020 COVID crash (VIX exploded to 62, the basket's final -13% flush). TLT rallied +46.9% as rates collapsed, the dollar firmed +8.8%, and the GICS Materials sector fell -13% while Energy fell -65%. The basket's -48.5% reflects its double-leverage to both the commodity collapse and the EV demand destruction that COVID briefly created.","body_zh":"从2018年9月至2020年3月长达18个月的-48.5%熊市，叠加三次冲击：第一，2018-2019年中美贸易战关税升级（北京对美国稀土征收25%报复性关税，2019年5月华为被列入实体清单后习近平参访稀土工厂被市场解读为出口限制威胁——初期对非中国股票估值压缩不利）；第二，2019年增长放缓（美联储由加息转为降息；油价跌-67.0%；周期板块大跌-33.4%）；第三，2020年3月新冠崩盘（VIX爆升至62，篮子最后冲洗-13%）。TLT上涨+46.9%，收益率暴跌，美元升值+8.8%，GICS材料板块跌-13%，能源跌-65%。篮子的-48.5%反映其对大宗崩盘和新冠短暂引发的EV需求破坏的双重杠杆。","drivers":["US-China trade war tariffs (2018-2019): EV demand outlook compressed","Growth slowdown: oil -67.0%, cyclicals -33.4% vs defensives -12.4%","COVID crash March 2020: VIX 12→62, risk assets universally sold","DXY +8.8% and TLT +46.9%: classic flight-to-quality wrecks materials"],"drivers_zh":["中美贸易战关税（2018-2019年）：EV需求前景遭压缩","增长放缓：油价-67.0%，周期-33.4%对防御-12.4%","2020年3月新冠崩盘：VIX 12→62，风险资产普遍被抛售","DXY +8.8%和TLT +46.9%：经典避险质量消灭材料"],"prev_key":"2018-09-21","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-21"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade war + COVID crash: -49% over 18 months","title_zh":"贸易战+新冠崩盘：18个月-49%","turn_id":"critical_minerals:peak:2018-09"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The largest rally in this series' history: +686.7% from the March 2020 COVID low to November 2021. Multiple forces converged: Fed zero rates and $5T+ of QE collapsed the dollar (DXY -7.2%) and crushed bond yields (TLT -9.0% as the curve steepened into the recovery), directly boosting commodity equities; China's 2020-2021 credit stimulus created the strongest commodity demand pulse since 2010; and the green energy transition narrative — supercharged by Biden's January 2021 election and the $1.2T infrastructure bill — created an insatiable demand story for rare earths, lithium, cobalt, and strategic metals. Energy returned +163.2%, Materials +141.6%; semis surged +189.3%; VIX collapsed from 62 to 16. The basket's +687% reflects its status as the highest-leverage pure-play on the energy-transition materials complex, amplifying a broad reflation/growth-up tape by approximately 6x.","body_zh":"该系列历史上最大的一次涨势：从2020年3月新冠低点至2021年11月上涨+686.7%。多重力量汇聚：美联储零利率和超5万亿美元QE压垮美元（DXY -7.2%），债券收益率崩落（TLT -9.0%，收益率曲线在复苏中陡峭化），直接提振大宗商品股；中国2020-2021年信贷刺激制造出2010年以来最强劲的大宗需求脉冲；绿色能源转型叙事——由拜登2021年1月当选和1.2万亿美元基建法案超级充电——为稀土、锂、钴和战略金属创造了永不满足的需求故事。能源回报+163.2%，材料+141.6%；半导体飙升+189.3%；VIX从62降至16。篮子的+687%反映其作为能源转型材料群组中杠杆最高的纯正标的，将宽广的反通胀/增长向上行情放大约6倍。","drivers":["Zero rates + QE5: DXY -7.2%, commodity equities re-rate globally","Green energy / Biden IRA anticipation: rare earths / lithium / cobalt demand narrative","China 2020-2021 credit stimulus: strongest commodity demand pulse since 2010","VIX 62→16 risk-on: high-beta cyclicals lead (Energy +163%, Materials +142%)"],"drivers_zh":["零利率+QE：DXY -7.2%，大宗商品股全球重估","绿色能源/拜登IRA预期：稀土/锂/钴需求叙事","中国2020-2021年信贷刺激：2010年以来最强大宗需求脉冲","VIX 62→16风险偏好：高贝塔周期引领（能源+163%，材料+142%）"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Green energy supercycle moonshot: +687% in 20 months","title_zh":"绿色能源超级周期登月：20个月+687%","turn_id":"critical_minerals:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-12":{"body":"A rapid -27.7% selloff from November 2021 to late January 2022 as the Fed pivoted to hawkish — signaling three rate hikes in 2022 at the November FOMC meeting — triggering a risk-off rotation where the most speculative, high-beta names sold first. The ctx is clearly stagflation-ish: defensives held flat (+0.3%) while cyclicals fell -4.5%, VIX jumped from 16 to 30, and growth underperformed value (-9.7%). Tech and semis crashed (SMH -14.3%, Comm -13.3%, Discretionary -14.3%). The basket's -27.7% vs SPY's -7.4% reflects its extreme beta to the speculative end of the market — rare earth and lithium names that had rallied +687% in 20 months were the first targets when liquidity was withdrawn.","body_zh":"从2021年11月至2022年1月底急跌-27.7%，因美联储于11月FOMC会议发出2022年加息三次的鹰派信号，触发避险轮动，最投机的高贝塔标的率先遭到抛售。ctx明确显示类滞胀：防御板块持平（+0.3%），周期板块跌-4.5%，VIX从16跳至30，成长股跑输价值股（-9.7%）。科技和半导体崩跌（SMH -14.3%、通讯-13.3%、可选消费-14.3%）。篮子-27.7%对SPY -7.4%，反映其对市场投机端的极度高贝塔——经过20个月+687%大涨的稀土锂矿股在流动性收紧时成为首批靶子。","drivers":["Fed pivot hawkish (Nov 2021 FOMC): rate-hike scare triggers high-beta selloff","Stagflation-ish quad: defensives +0.3% vs cyclicals -4.5%, VIX 16→30","Growth/speculative unwind: SMH -14.3%, Comm -13.3%, Discretionary -14.3%","Basket -27.7% vs SPY -7.4%: high-beta names exit first"],"drivers_zh":["美联储鹰派转向（2021年11月FOMC）：加息恐慌触发高贝塔抛售","类滞胀quad：防御+0.3%对周期-4.5%，VIX 16→30","成长/投机退潮：SMH -14.3%，通讯-13.3%，可选消费-14.3%","篮子-27.7%对SPY -7.4%：高贝塔标的率先出清"],"prev_key":"2021-11-12","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot scare: high-beta de-rate, -28% in 10 weeks","title_zh":"美联储转向恐慌：高贝塔去估值，10周-28%","turn_id":"critical_minerals:peak:2021-11"},"2022-01-27":{"body":"A +45.7% counter-trend rally from January 2022 to February 2023, driven by the Russia-Ukraine war's commodity supply shock that began on February 24, 2022. The Ukraine invasion triggered an emergency rally in all commodities with supply chain links to Russia or Eastern Europe, and rare earth / strategic materials were bid as part of the broader defense-supply-chain re-evaluation. The macro regime was distinctly unfavorable for most equities — TLT fell -22.3% as the Fed hiked from 0% to 4.5%, SPY was -1.8%, tech crashed — but commodity equities decoupled: broad market breadth beat cap-weight (RSP-SPY +6.5%), value beat growth by 10.2%, and the basket's +45.7% came entirely from the commodity/supply-disruption premium. Lithium prices hit record highs in November 2022 (~$81,000/tonne) before beginning to roll over.","body_zh":"从2022年1月至2023年2月的+45.7%逆势反弹，由2022年2月24日俄乌战争引发的大宗供应冲击驱动。乌克兰入侵触发所有与俄罗斯或东欧供应链挂钩的大宗商品的紧急拉升，稀土/战略材料作为更广泛国防供应链重新评估的一部分获得买盘。宏观regime对大多数股票明显不利——TLT下跌-22.3%，美联储从0%加息至4.5%，SPY -1.8%，科技崩跌——但大宗商品股脱钩：大盘广度跑赢市值加权（RSP-SPY +6.5%），价值跑赢成长10.2%，篮子+45.7%完全来自大宗/供应中断溢价。碳酸锂价格于2022年11月创历史纪录（约8.1万美元/吨），随后开始回落。","drivers":["Russia-Ukraine invasion (Feb 24, 2022): supply shock bids defense materials","Commodity decoupling: basket +45.7% while SPY -1.8% and TLT -22.3%","Lithium hits record ~$81,000/tonne (Nov 2022) on EV demand","Broad breadth (RSP-SPY +6.5%) confirms genuine materials leadership, not just index beta"],"drivers_zh":["俄乌入侵（2022年2月24日）：供应冲击推动国防材料买盘","大宗脱钩：篮子+45.7%而SPY -1.8%，TLT -22.3%","碳酸锂创历史纪录约8.1万美元/吨（2022年11月）受EV需求驱动","广度宽（RSP-SPY +6.5%）确认真实材料引领，而非仅为指数贝塔"],"prev_key":"2022-01-27","prev_key_chain":["2022-01-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Russia-Ukraine commodity spike: +46% against a rate surge","title_zh":"俄乌战争大宗飙升：逆收益率飙升+46%","turn_id":"critical_minerals:trough:2022-01"},"2023-02-02":{"body":"A grinding -39.4% bear from February 2023 to February 2024, driven by two simultaneous forces: lithium prices collapsed -80% from peak (~$81,000/tonne in Nov 2022 to ~$13,600/tonne by end-2023) as a massive oversupply glut emerged and EV demand growth in China missed expectations; and the AI melt-up sucked all capital toward semis and tech (SMH +56.9%, growth>value +27.8, breadth badly narrow at RSP-SPY -16.1%). The goldilocks/growth-up quad was the worst possible combination: SPY rose +21% while the commodity story unwound. Materials SPDR lagged badly; rare earth names with no earnings and lithium-price-dependent cash flows were destroyed. Albemarle cut staff and paused expansion projects in January 2024 after lithium prices fell over 81%, crystallizing the sector's collapse.","body_zh":"从2023年2月至2024年2月磨损式下跌-39.4%，由两股力量同时驱动：锂价从峰值暴跌-80%（2022年11月约8.1万美元/吨降至2023年底约1.36万美元/吨），供过于求大幅积压且中国EV需求增长不及预期；AI融涨将所有资金吸引至半导体和科技（SMH +56.9%，成长>价值+27.8，广度严重收窄RSP-SPY -16.1%）。Goldilocks/增长向上quad是最糟糕的组合：SPY涨+21%而大宗故事回吐。材料SPDR大幅落后；无盈利且现金流依赖锂价的稀土股遭到重创。雅保在锂价跌超81%后于2024年1月裁员并暂停扩张项目，将板块崩溃具象化。","drivers":["Lithium price crash -80% (Nov 2022 peak to end-2023) on oversupply and EV demand miss","AI melt-up: SMH +56.9%, SPY +21%, capital drains from materials to semis","Narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -16.1%): mega-cap tech leadership starves cyclicals","Goldilocks quad: basket -39% while SPY +21%, a brutal negative-RS leg"],"drivers_zh":["锂价崩盘-80%（2022年11月高峰至2023年底），供过于求且EV需求不达预期","AI融涨：SMH +56.9%，SPY +21%，资金从材料流向半导体","广度收窄（RSP-SPY -16.1%）：大盘科技引领饿死周期股","Goldilocks quad：篮子-39%而SPY +21%，残酷负相对强度段"],"prev_key":"2023-02-02","prev_key_chain":["2023-02-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Lithium crash + AI melt-up: sector -39% in 12 months","title_zh":"锂价崩盘+AI融涨：板块12个月-39%","turn_id":"critical_minerals:peak:2023-02"},"2024-02-20":{"body":"The defining leg of this basket's entire history: +714.8% from February 2024 to October 2025. The proximate catalyst was China's April 4, 2025 export controls on seven heavy rare earth elements (samarium, gadolinium, terbium, dysprosium, lutetium, scandium, yttrium) and all derivative magnets — the most consequential supply-chain action since 2010. This sent global auto and defense supply chains into emergency; the DoD responded by investing $400M into MP Materials in July 2025 (making the Pentagon the company's largest shareholder) with a 10-year price floor of $110/kg for NdPr output. Early in the leg (2024), the thesis was pre-positioning: ex-China supply chain de-risking narratives built momentum even before formal controls, as rare earth equities re-rated from value-trap to strategic must-own. The macro backdrop was broadly helpful but not determinative: goldilocks/growth-up (SPY +36.2%, DXY -4.8%, VIX 15→21), but the +714.8% vs SPY's +36.2% confirms this was a national-security re-rating, not a macro trade.","body_zh":"该篮子整个历史上最决定性的一段：从2024年2月至2025年10月上涨+714.8%。直接催化剂为中国2025年4月4日对七种重稀土元素（钐、钆、铽、镝、镥、钪、钇）及所有衍生磁体实施出口管制——2010年以来最具影响力的供应链行动。这使全球汽车和国防供应链陷入紧急状态；DoD于2025年7月向MP Materials投资4亿美元（使五角大楼成为公司最大股东），并设立10年110美元/公斤镨钕产出价格下限。在该段早期（2024年），逻辑为预期布局：即便在正式管制出台前，去中国化供应链去风险叙事已积聚动能，稀土股从价值陷阱重估为战略必持。宏观背景总体有利但非决定性：goldilocks/增长向上（SPY +36.2%，DXY -4.8%，VIX 15→21），但+714.8%对SPY +36.2%证实这是国家安全重估，而非宏观交易。","drivers":["China April 2025 export controls on 7 heavy REEs and NdFeB magnets: supply chain emergency","DoD invests $400M in MP Materials (July 2025), $110/kg NdPr floor: national-security re-rating","Ex-China supply chain de-risking narrative builds through 2024 pre-emptively","DXY -4.8% weaker dollar tailwinds dollar-priced materials throughout"],"drivers_zh":["中国2025年4月出口管制7种重稀土和钕铁硼磁体：供应链紧急状态","DoD向MP Materials投资4亿美元（2025年7月），110美元/公斤镨钕下限：国家安全重估","去中国化供应链去风险叙事于2024年预先积聚","DXY -4.8%美元走弱全程为美元计价材料提供顺风"],"prev_key":"2024-02-20","prev_key_chain":["2024-02-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Policy moonshot: China export controls re-rate sector +715%","title_zh":"政策登月：中国出口管制使板块重估+715%","turn_id":"critical_minerals:trough:2024-02"},"2025-10-14":{"body":"A brutal -43.1% selloff from the October 14, 2025 parabolic peak to November 6, 2025 — a three-week implosion off a +714.8% run. The regime barely moved: SPY was +1.2%, VIX actually fell from 21 to 20, breadth was narrow (RSP-SPY -2.5%), and materials were the worst sector (-4.8%) on a basically flat tape. This was a pure extended-valuation flush: a name that had run +714.8% in 20 months had no valuation cushion against any negative catalyst. The immediate trigger was the October 9, 2025 escalation of China's export controls (the second wave adding holmium, erbium, thulium, europium, and ytterbium), which paradoxically was already priced in after the 18-month run, while the US-China APEC summit (October 30) signaled an imminent partial suspension of controls — removing the scarcity premium in a single headline.","body_zh":"从2025年10月14日抛物线顶峰至11月6日暴跌-43.1%——+714.8%大涨后的三周崩塌。regime几乎不动：SPY +1.2%，VIX实际从21降至20，广度收窄（RSP-SPY -2.5%），材料为最差板块（-4.8%），行情基本持平。这是纯粹的高估值冲刷：20个月涨+714.8%的标的对任何负面催化剂毫无估值缓冲。直接触发为2025年10月9日中国出口管制第二波升级（新增钬、铒、铥、铕、镱），但在18个月大涨后已被充分消化，而美中APEC峰会（10月30日）释放即将部分暂停管制的信号——一条头条抹去稀缺溢价。","drivers":["Extreme extension flush: +714.8% in 20 months leaves no valuation cushion","China Oct 9, 2025 export control expansion already priced; APEC de-escalation signals remove premium","High-beta names always flush first: Materials sector -4.8% vs SPY +1.2%","Narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -2.5%) and profit-taking combine to deliver -43% in 3 weeks"],"drivers_zh":["极度延伸冲刷：20个月+714.8%无估值缓冲","中国2025年10月9日出口管制扩大已被消化；APEC降级信号移除溢价","高贝塔标的永远率先冲刷：材料板块-4.8%对SPY +1.2%","广度收窄（RSP-SPY -2.5%）与获利回吐叠加，3周交出-43%"],"prev_key":"2025-10-14","prev_key_chain":["2025-10-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Parabolic top flush on a flat tape: -43% in 3 weeks","title_zh":"抛物线顶部冲刷于平淡行情：3周-43%","turn_id":"critical_minerals:peak:2025-10"},"2025-11-06":{"body":"A violent +80.4% snap-back from November 6, 2025 to January 23, 2026, driven by renewed US-China trade tension after the APEC stand-down proved short-lived. The inverse dynamic is key: after the APEC partial suspension removed the scarcity premium and caused the -43% flush, any fresh export-control escalation signal directly re-ignited the supply-security bid. The broader macro regime was modestly helpful: Materials led sectors (+18.5%), the dollar weakened (DXY -2.1%), VIX compressed from 20 to 16, and breadth was broad (RSP-SPY +4.2%) — a genuine reflation rotation. The basket +80.4% against SPY's +3.1% confirms that policy headlines — not the macro tape — drove the move. The Trump administration also launched a $12B critical minerals stockpile project (Project Vault, Feb 2026) that was anticipated from late 2025, adding to the bid.","body_zh":"从2025年11月6日至2026年1月23日暴涨+80.4%，由APEC停战后美中贸易紧张重燃驱动，停战协议事实上短暂即逝。反向动态是关键：APEC部分暂停移除稀缺溢价并引发-43%冲刷后，任何新的出口管制升级信号直接重新点燃供应安全买盘。更广泛的宏观regime适度有利：材料引领板块（+18.5%），美元走弱（DXY -2.1%），VIX从20压缩至16，广度宽（RSP-SPY +4.2%）——真实的反通胀轮动。篮子+80.4%对SPY +3.1%，证实政策头条——而非宏观行情——驱动涨势。特朗普政府还发起120亿美元关键矿产储备项目（Project Vault，2026年2月），从2025年底即被预期，增加了买盘。","drivers":["Trade-war re-escalation signals after APEC stand-down proves short-lived","Materials SPDR leads (+18.5%): sector-level reflation rotation supports the bid","DXY -2.1% and VIX 20→16: modest macro tailwinds amplify the policy-driven rip","Trump $12B critical minerals stockpile (Project Vault) anticipated from late 2025"],"drivers_zh":["APEC停战短暂后贸易战再升级信号","材料SPDR引领（+18.5%）：板块级反通胀轮动支撑买盘","DXY -2.1%和VIX 20→16：温和宏观顺风放大政策驱动暴涨","特朗普120亿美元关键矿产储备（Project Vault）从2025年底被预期"],"prev_key":"2025-11-06","prev_key_chain":["2025-11-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade-war re-escalation rip: +80% on broadening tape","title_zh":"贸易战再升级暴涨：广度扩张行情+80%","turn_id":"critical_minerals:trough:2025-11"},"2026-01-23":{"body":"A -30.3% selloff from January 23 to March 30, 2026, combining geopolitical de-escalation with a stagflation macro shock. On the policy side, a partial export-control suspension was negotiated as part of broader US-China trade talks (the October 2025 controls suspended until November 2026), directly removing the scarcity premium that had been the basis for the basket's re-rating. On the macro side, the regime flipped stagflation-ish: VIX surged from 16 to 31, oil spiked +68.5% (Hormuz-related supply shock), the dollar firmed (DXY +3.0% — a direct materials headwind), and cyclicals underperformed defensives. SPY fell -8.1%; the basket fell -30.3% — 3.7x the index. The combination of a de-escalated policy thesis AND a risk-off stagflation macro backdrop is the most destructive configuration for this basket.","body_zh":"从2026年1月23日至3月30日下跌-30.3%，地缘政治降级与滞胀宏观冲击叠加。政策方面，中美贸易谈判达成部分出口管制暂停协议（2025年10月管制暂停至2026年11月），直接移除支撑篮子重估的稀缺溢价。宏观方面，regime翻转为类滞胀：VIX从16飙至31，油价飙涨+68.5%（霍尔木兹海峡相关供应冲击），美元转强（DXY +3.0%——材料的直接逆风），周期板块跑输防御。SPY跌-8.1%；篮子跌-30.3%——为指数的3.7倍。政策降级主题与宏观避险滞胀背景的叠加，是该篮子所能遭遇的最具破坏性的组合。","drivers":["China Oct 2025 export controls suspended to Nov 2026: scarcity premium removed","Stagflation shock: VIX 16→31, oil +68.5%, DXY +3.0% — all headwinds for materials","Policy de-rating compounds macro risk-off: basket -30.3% vs SPY -8.1%","Basket 3.7x leveraged to the index in a stagflation/de-escalation combo"],"drivers_zh":["中国2025年10月出口管制暂停至2026年11月：稀缺溢价被移除","滞胀冲击：VIX 16→31，油价+68.5%，DXY +3.0%——对材料全为逆风","政策去估值叠加宏观避险：篮子-30.3%对SPY -8.1%","在滞胀/降级组合中篮子为指数3.7倍杠杆"],"prev_key":"2026-01-23","prev_key_chain":["2026-01-23"],"status":"exact","title":"De-escalation and stagflation shock: -30% in 9 weeks","title_zh":"降级与滞胀冲击：9周-30%","turn_id":"critical_minerals:peak:2026-01"},"2026-03-30":{"body":"A +61.2% whip higher from March 30 to May 6, 2026, as supply-security headlines flared again alongside a violent tech-led risk-on flip. The regime context is critical: SMH surged +51.6%, growth beat value by +7.2%, VIX compressed from 31 to 17, and the dollar weakened (DXY -2.5%) — a textbook tech-led reflation tape that amplifies high-beta materials. Simultaneously, renewed US-China trade tension signals and the Trump-Xi May 2026 summit framework (which included rare earths on the agenda) re-ignited the supply-security premium. The basket +61.2% against SPY +16.1% confirms the dual amplification: high-beta leverage to the risk-on rally (approximately 3.8x) plus renewed policy-scarcity premium. The copper-gold ratio also turned positive (+8.6%), confirming a genuine commodity demand pulse rather than a purely speculative move.","body_zh":"从2026年3月30日至5月6日暴涨+61.2%，供应安全头条再度爆发，叠加科技引领的剧烈风险偏好翻转。regime背景至关重要：SMH飙升+51.6%，成长跑赢价值+7.2%，VIX从31压缩至17，美元走弱（DXY -2.5%）——教科书式的科技引领反通胀行情放大高贝塔材料。同时，美中贸易紧张信号重燃以及特朗普-习近平2026年5月峰会框架（稀土列为议题）重新点燃供应安全溢价。篮子+61.2%对SPY +16.1%，印证双重放大：高贝塔对风险偏好反弹的杠杆（约3.8倍）加上政策稀缺溢价重启。铜金比也转正（+8.6%），确认真实大宗需求脉冲而非纯粹投机行情。","drivers":["Tech/semis-led risk-on flip: SMH +51.6%, VIX 31→17 amplifies high-beta names","Trump-Xi May 2026 summit: rare earths on agenda re-ignites scarcity premium","DXY -2.5% weaker dollar and copper-gold +8.6%: genuine reflation signal","Basket +61.2% vs SPY +16.1%: 3.8x beta confirms policy + risk-on dual amplification"],"drivers_zh":["科技/半导体引领风险偏好翻转：SMH +51.6%，VIX 31→17放大高贝塔标的","特朗普-习近平2026年5月峰会：稀土列为议题重新点燃稀缺溢价","DXY -2.5%美元走弱和铜金比+8.6%：真实反通胀信号","篮子+61.2%对SPY +16.1%：3.8倍贝塔印证政策+风险偏好双重放大"],"prev_key":"2026-03-30","prev_key_chain":["2026-03-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Re-escalation + risk-on flip: +61% high-beta bounce","title_zh":"再升级+风险偏好翻转：高贝塔反弹+61%","turn_id":"critical_minerals:trough:2026-03"},"2026-05-06":{"body":"The current -32.1% selloff from May 6 to June 26, 2026, with the basket at pos 1.6 (range floor). The primary catalyst was China's June 22, 2026 addition of MP Materials and USA Rare Earth to its dual-use export control list (barring supply of controlled items TO those companies) alongside a 46-firm US procurement ban covering Lockheed, Raytheon, Boeing, and General Dynamics. Paradoxically, both MP and USA Rare Earth stocks actually rose in the immediate aftermath of the June 22 announcement (as they have already de-coupled from Chinese supply), but the basket as a whole sold as the stagflation-ish macro regime worked against it: defensives were bid (avg +4.0% vs cyclicals +0.1%), oil collapsed -27.2%, the dollar firmed (DXY +3.4%), and growth underperformed value (-6.3%). With the Pentagon backstop intact and the basket at its historical floor, this reads as a regime-driven washout at technically significant support, not a structural break.","body_zh":"当前-32.1%的抛售从2026年5月6日至6月26日，篮子处于pos 1.6（区间底部）。主要催化剂为中国2026年6月22日将MP Materials和USA Rare Earth列入双重用途出口管制清单（禁止对这些公司供应受控物品），同时对包含洛克希德、雷神、波音、通用动力的46家美国企业发布采购禁令。悖论的是，MP和USA Rare Earth股票在6月22日公告后即时上涨（因其已与中国供应脱钩），但整体篮子在类滞胀宏观regime的夹击下下跌：防御板块获追捧（均值+4.0%对周期+0.1%），油价暴跌-27.2%，美元转强（DXY +3.4%），成长股跑输价值股（-6.3%）。在五角大楼后盾完好且篮子处于历史底部的情况下，此段读作技术关键支撑位上的regime驱动洗盘，而非逻辑断裂。","drivers":["China June 22, 2026 sanctions MP/USA Rare Earth + 46-firm US procurement ban","Stagflation-ish regime: defensives +4.0% vs cyclicals +0.1%, DXY +3.4%, oil -27.2%","Pentagon backstop ($110/kg floor, $725M loan) holds structural floor under leading names","Basket at historical range floor (pos 1.6): washout in unhelpful regime, not thesis break"],"drivers_zh":["中国2026年6月22日制裁MP/USA Rare Earth+46家美国企业采购禁令","类滞胀regime：防御+4.0%对周期+0.1%，DXY +3.4%，油价-27.2%","五角大楼后盾（110美元/公斤下限、7.25亿美元贷款）在龙头下方守住结构性底部","篮子处于历史区间底部（pos 1.6）：不利regime中的洗盘，非逻辑断裂"],"prev_key":"2026-05-06","prev_key_chain":["2026-05-06"],"status":"exact","title":"June 2026 China sanctions trigger washout at range floor","title_zh":"2026年6月中国制裁触发区间底部洗盘","turn_id":"critical_minerals:peak:2026-05"}},"now":"Critical Minerals & Rare Earths sits at a confirmed \"Bottoming\" trough (pos 1.6, range floor, RS-rank #34), posting a -32% selloff from the May-2026 peak. The macro backdrop is stagflation-ish: defensives are bid (defensives avg +4.0% vs cyclicals +0.1%), the dollar is firmer (DXY +3.4%), and oil has collapsed (-27.2%) — all classic headwinds for high-beta materials. Copper-gold is positive (+13.7%) and breadth is modestly broad (RSP-SPY +3.1%), confirming this is a sector-specific washout rather than a systemic risk-off. The direct catalyst was China's June 22, 2026 sanctioning of MP Materials and USA Rare Earth (plus a 46-firm US procurement ban) — paradoxically bullish for the long-run ex-China supply thesis but a short-term seller in a weakened tape. The Pentagon backstop (DoD as MP's largest shareholder, $110/kg NdPr price floor, $725M metallization loan) provides structural support at the lows. The basket is at the absolute floor of its historical range in a policy-driven name where every catalyst — escalation or de-escalation — triggers violent reversals.","now_zh":"关键矿产与稀土处于确认的\"筑底\"低谷（pos 1.6，区间底部，RS排名第34位），从2026年5月高点下跌-32%。宏观背景为类滞胀regime：防御板块受追捧（防御均值+4.0%对周期+0.1%），美元转强（DXY +3.4%），油价暴跌（-27.2%）——均为高贝塔材料的典型逆风。铜金比正向（+13.7%），广度略宽（RSP-SPY +3.1%），证实这是板块特定的洗盘而非系统性风险出清。直接催化剂为中国2026年6月22日制裁MP Materials和USA Rare Earth（另加46家美国企业采购禁令）——对长期去中国化供应逻辑悖论地利好，但在已疲弱的行情中触发短线抛售。五角大楼后盾（DoD为MP最大股东、110美元/公斤镨钕下限、7.25亿美元金属化贷款）在低位提供结构性支撑。篮子处于历史区间绝对底部，身为政策驱动标的，每条催化剂——中国升级或降级——均触发剧烈反转。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"copper.trough_in.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"copper.trough_in.v1","arch_state":"pass","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-crypto":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"The basket's reconstructed proxy registers a large gain across 2014, but this earliest leg predates every real constituent (COIN IPO'd 2021, MSTR's treasury began 2020, IBIT launched 2024), so the price path is a thin synthetic and should be read with caution rather than treated as a documented crypto rally -- in reality spot Bitcoin had a brutal 2014, falling from ~$750 in January to ~$320 by December as the Mt.Gox crisis unfolded. The macro ctx is the reliable read here: a slowdown/deflation-scare quad with defensives firmly in command (Utilities +30.8%, Health +25.1%, defensives +25.2% vs cyclicals +11.0%), TLT +24.3% on falling yields, oil crashing -39.2%, and DXY ripping +11.5%. Whatever the proxy shows, the regime was risk-off and dollar-strong -- exactly the backdrop that historically pressures real high-beta crypto.","body_zh":"篮子的重构代理在2014年录得较大涨幅，但这一最早的腿早于所有真实成分（COIN于2021年上市、MSTR储备始于2020年、IBIT于2024年推出），故价格路径是薄弱的合成数据，应谨慎看待而非视作有据可查的加密涨势——现实中现货比特币2014年极其惨淡，从1月约750美元跌至12月约320美元，正值Mt.Gox危机发酵。此处可靠的判读是宏观ctx：放缓/通缩恐慌象限，防御板块牢牢主导（公用事业+30.8%、医疗+25.1%，防御+25.2% vs 周期+11.0%），收益率下行TLT+24.3%，油价暴跌-39.2%，DXY大涨+11.5%。无论代理显示什么，该机制偏避险、美元强势——正是历史上压制真实高贝塔加密的背景。","drivers":["Reconstructed proxy predates real constituents","Slowdown/deflation-scare quad, defensives lead","Falling yields TLT +24.3%, oil -39.2%","Strong dollar DXY +11.5% (real-asset headwind)"],"drivers_zh":["重构代理早于真实成分","放缓/通缩恐慌象限、防御领涨","收益率下行TLT+24.3%、油价-39.2%","强美元DXY+11.5%（真实资产阻力）"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Early proxy leg: pre-institutional crypto","title_zh":"早期代理腿：机构化之前的加密","turn_id":"crypto:trough:2014-01"},"2014-12-23":{"body":"A -59% bear into November 2015, the continuation of the Mt.Gox-driven washout -- the world's largest Bitcoin exchange filed for bankruptcy in February 2014 after losing ~850,000 BTC (~$473M), vaporizing trust in exchange custody and dragging spot Bitcoin down toward ~$200 by early 2015. The macro backdrop reinforced the bear: a DXY +9.9% dollar surge, oil -28.7%, and a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP lagged SPY -3.3%) kept risk appetite suppressed. VIX drifted 15 to 20 and credit spreads widened (HYG-LQD -3.4%), giving the speculative asset no liquidity tailwind as it digested the single largest crypto-specific shock of its first decade.","body_zh":"到2015年11月约-59%的熊市，是Mt.Gox洗盘的延续——当时全球最大比特币交易所于2014年2月申请破产，遗失约85万枚比特币（约4.73亿美元），摧毁了对托管的信任，并把现货比特币拖至2015年初约200美元。宏观背景强化了熊市：DXY+9.9%美元飙升、油价-28.7%、狭窄大盘股主导市场（等权RSP跑输SPY-3.3%）压制风险偏好。VIX从15漂移至20，信用利差走扩（HYG-LQD-3.4%），未能为投机性资产提供流动性顺风，使其独自消化头十年最大的加密自身冲击。","drivers":["Mt.Gox bankruptcy Feb 2014 destroys custody trust","Bitcoin-specific exchange fraud shock","Dollar surge DXY +9.9% suppresses risk appetite","No macro liquidity tailwind: VIX 15 to 20, HYG-LQD -3.4%"],"drivers_zh":["2014年2月Mt.Gox破产摧毁托管信任","比特币自身交易所欺诈冲击","美元飙升DXY+9.9%压制风险偏好","无宏观流动性顺风：VIX 15→20、HYG-LQD-3.4%"],"prev_key":"2014-12-23","prev_key_chain":["2014-12-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Mt.Gox aftermath: exchange-collapse bear","title_zh":"Mt.Gox余震：交易所崩盘熊市","turn_id":"crypto:peak:2014-12"},"2015-11-13":{"body":"A staggering +410% rally from November 2015 through December 2017 across two phases: a 2016 Bitcoin halving-driven surge (the July 2016 halving cut block rewards from 25 to 12.5 BTC) followed by the 2017 ICO mania explosion as Ethereum's ERC-20 standard enabled token launches. The macro was a perfect tailwind: a reflation/growth-up quad with Tech/Financials leading (Tech +59.8%, Financials +50.5%), VIX collapsing from 20 to 10, semis ripping +97.5%, and DXY weakening -5.3% -- the broadest risk-on environment since the post-GFC recovery. Bitcoin rose from ~$370 in Nov 2015 to ~$19,800 by Dec 2017, while Ethereum surged from ~$1 to ~$700, fueled by ICO fundraising that topped $5B in 2017 alone.","body_zh":"从2015年11月到2017年12月约+410%的惊人涨幅，分两阶段：2016年比特币减半驱动的飙升（2016年7月减半将区块奖励从25枚削减至12.5枚比特币），随后是2017年以太坊ERC-20标准催生的ICO狂潮。宏观是完美顺风：再通胀/增长向上象限，科技/金融领涨（科技+59.8%、金融+50.5%），VIX从20骤降至10，半导体飙升+97.5%，DXY走弱-5.3%——自后金融危机复苏以来最广泛的风险偏好环境。比特币价格从2015年11月约370美元涨至2017年12月约19800美元，以太坊从约1美元飙至约700美元，2017年ICO融资总额逾50亿美元。","drivers":["July 2016 Bitcoin halving compresses supply","Ethereum ERC-20 ICO mania 2017 ($5B+)","Risk-on melt-up: SMH +97.5%, VIX 20 to 10","DXY -5.3% weak dollar tailwind for speculative assets"],"drivers_zh":["2016年7月比特币减半压缩供给","以太坊ERC-20 ICO狂潮2017年（逾50亿美元）","风险偏好融涨：SMH+97.5%、VIX 20→10","DXY-5.3%弱美元为投机资产提供顺风"],"prev_key":"2015-11-13","prev_key_chain":["2015-11-13"],"status":"exact","title":"ICO mania: Bitcoin then Ethereum bull cycle","title_zh":"ICO狂潮：比特币后以太坊牛市周期","turn_id":"crypto:trough:2015-11"},"2017-12-18":{"body":"A -57% collapse into April 2018 as the late-2017 crypto bubble unwound on regulatory crackdowns and leverage unwinds. China banned ICOs on September 4, 2017 and forced domestic exchanges to halt trading by end-September 2017; South Korea and the US SEC escalated warnings through early 2018. The macro was neutral-to-mildly-risk-off (SPY -3.6%, VIX 10 to 24) with defensives hit equally (defensives -7.0% vs cyclicals -3.1%) -- not a classic risk-off rotation but a crypto-specific unwinding of extreme speculative leverage after BTC hit ~$19,800 in December 2017. The rising-rate environment (TLT -3.4%) began to bite even as the dollar stayed weak.","body_zh":"到2018年4月约-57%的崩溃，2017年末加密泡沫在监管打击与杠杆解除中瓦解。中国于2017年9月4日禁止ICO，并迫使境内交易所于2017年9月底前停止交易；韩国及美国SEC于2018年初升级警告。宏观中性偏轻度避险（SPY-3.6%、VIX 10→24），防御与周期同步受压（防御-7.0% vs 周期-3.1%）——并非典型避险轮动，而是比特币2017年12月触及约19800美元后极端投机杠杆的加密自身解除。利率上行环境（TLT-3.4%）开始蚕食，即便美元仍偏弱。","drivers":["China ICO/exchange ban Sep 2017","SEC and global regulatory crackdown Jan-Mar 2018","VIX spike 10 to 24: speculative leverage unwind","Post-blow-off mean reversion after $19,800 BTC peak"],"drivers_zh":["中国2017年9月ICO/交易所禁令","SEC与全球监管打击2018年1-3月","VIX从10飙至24：投机杠杆去杠杆","比特币19800美元顶部后的吹顶均值回归"],"prev_key":"2017-12-18","prev_key_chain":["2017-12-18"],"status":"exact","title":"ICO bubble pops: regulatory and leverage unwind","title_zh":"ICO泡沫破裂：监管与杠杆去化","turn_id":"crypto:peak:2017-12"},"2018-04-02":{"body":"A +113% rebound from April 2018 through April 2019 as the market recovered on renewed institutional-interest narratives: the August 2018 announcement of Bakkt (ICE's regulated Bitcoin futures platform), multiple spot-ETF filings with the SEC, and growing Wall Street coverage. The macro was a tech/semis-led growth tape (SMH +20.3%, growth>value +9.4, VIX 24 to 12), a strengthening dollar (DXY +8.4%), and narrow breadth (RSP lagged SPY -3.0%) -- a typical high-beta bounce in a transitional, adequately-liquid environment. The rebound proved a bear-market rally; Bakkt's eventual September 2019 launch disappointed, and the ETF was not approved until 2024.","body_zh":"从2018年4月到2019年4月约+113%的反弹，市场在机构兴趣叙事重燃中复苏：2018年8月宣布的Bakkt（ICE旗下受监管的比特币期货平台）、多宗向SEC提交的现货ETF申请，以及华尔街日益增加的覆盖。宏观是科技/半导体主导的增长市场（SMH+20.3%、成长跑赢价值+9.4、VIX 24→12），美元走强（DXY+8.4%），市场偏窄（等权RSP跑输SPY-3.0%）——流动性尚充裕的过渡期中典型的高贝塔反弹。反弹证明是熊市行情；Bakkt于2019年9月最终上线却令市场失望，ETF更要到2024年才获批。","drivers":["Bakkt regulated futures platform announced Aug 2018","SEC spot-ETF filings renew institutional optimism","Tech/semis risk-on: SMH +20.3%, VIX 24 to 12","Bear-market counter-trend rally on oversold positioning"],"drivers_zh":["Bakkt受监管期货平台2018年8月宣布","SEC现货ETF申请重燃机构乐观","科技/半导体风险偏好：SMH+20.3%、VIX 24→12","超卖定位下的熊市反趋势行情"],"prev_key":"2018-04-02","prev_key_chain":["2018-04-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Bear-market recovery: Bakkt/ETF hopes","title_zh":"熊市反弹：Bakkt/ETF预期","turn_id":"crypto:trough:2018-04"},"2019-04-23":{"body":"A -78% collapse from April 2019 through March 18, 2020 as the 2019-2020 bear deepened and then COVID-19 accelerated the washout to extremes. The first phase (Apr-Dec 2019) was a routine post-bubble deflation after the 2018 bear bounce; the terminal phase was the March 2020 COVID crash where crypto -- the highest-beta asset -- was liquidated harder than equities (VIX 12 to 76, SPY -16.9%, Energy -62.9%). Flight to safety was extreme (defensives -1.1% vs cyclicals -30.1%, TLT +20.1%) and DXY strengthened +3.7% as dollar demand spiked; Bitcoin fell from ~$8,000 to ~$3,800 in the COVID crash alone, compressing the final trough.","body_zh":"从2019年4月到2020年3月18日约-78%的崩溃，2019-2020年熊市加深，随后新冠疫情将洗盘推向极端。第一阶段（2019年4-12月）是2018年熊市反弹后的常规去泡沫；终末阶段是2020年3月新冠崩盘，加密——最高贝塔资产——被比股票更剧烈地平仓（VIX 12→76、SPY-16.9%、能源-62.9%）。避险极端（防御-1.1% vs 周期-30.1%、TLT+20.1%），美元需求飙升DXY+3.7%；仅新冠崩盘阶段比特币就从约8000美元跌至约3800美元，压低了最终谷底。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic crash March 2020: VIX 12 to 76","Extreme flight-to-safety: defensives vs cyclicals -30.1%","Dollar liquidity crunch: DXY +3.7%, TLT +20.1%","Highest-beta asset liquidated first in forced selling"],"drivers_zh":["2020年3月新冠疫情崩盘：VIX 12→76","极端避险：防御 vs 周期-30.1%","美元流动性紧缩：DXY+3.7%、TLT+20.1%","强制平仓中最高贝塔资产首当其冲"],"prev_key":"2019-04-23","prev_key_chain":["2019-04-23"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash: from peak to pandemic trough","title_zh":"新冠崩盘：从高峰到疫情谷底","turn_id":"crypto:peak:2019-04"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"A staggering +6,637% surge from the March 2020 COVID trough through February 2021 -- the most explosive leg in the series -- powered by the broadest macro tailwind in a generation: the Fed's March 2020 emergency zero-rate cut and ~$3T QE expansion, fiscal stimulus ($2.2T CARES Act March 2020, $900B December 2020), and DXY collapsing -10.7% as the dollar was debased. The quad was textbook reflation/growth-up: cyclicals +86.3% vs defensives +24.6%, SPY +65.5%, semis +152.9%, Energy +105.4%. As the highest-beta basket with dollar-debasement appeal, crypto was the ultimate beneficiary -- Bitcoin rose from ~$3,800 to ~$58,000, MicroStrategy made its first Bitcoin treasury purchase in August 2020, and institutional adoption via Grayscale GBTC accelerated.","body_zh":"从2020年3月新冠谷底到2021年2月约+6637%的惊人飙升——本系列最爆炸性的一段——由一代人中最广泛的宏观顺风驱动：美联储2020年3月紧急零利率降息与约3万亿美元QE扩表、财政刺激（2020年3月CARES法案2.2万亿美元、2020年12月9000亿美元），DXY崩跌-10.7%美元遭贬值。象限是教科书式再通胀/增长向上：周期+86.3% vs 防御+24.6%、SPY+65.5%、半导体+152.9%、能源+105.4%。作为兼具美元贬值吸引力的最高贝塔篮子，加密是最大受益者——比特币从约3800美元涨至约58000美元，MicroStrategy于2020年8月首次购入比特币储备，Grayscale GBTC的机构采用加速。","drivers":["Fed zero-rates + ~$3T QE March 2020 debases dollar","CARES Act + $900B fiscal stimulus drives risk appetite","DXY -10.7% dollar collapse: ideal for crypto","Highest-beta + dollar-debasement narrative: 66x supercycle"],"drivers_zh":["美联储零利率+约3万亿美元QE贬值美元","CARES法案+9000亿美元财政刺激驱动风险偏好","DXY-10.7%美元崩跌：对加密极为有利","最高贝塔+美元贬值叙事：66倍超级周期"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-COVID money-printing supercycle","title_zh":"新冠后大放水超级周期","turn_id":"crypto:trough:2020-03"},"2021-02-19":{"body":"A ~53% drawdown into May 2021 as the first half of the 2021 bull cycle topped -- China's May 21, 2021 mining/trading crackdown and an overheated, over-leveraged market triggered a violent high-beta unwind. The macro tape was actually benign (SPY +6.7%, broadening RSP beat SPY +3.9%, reflation/growth-up), which underscores that this was a crypto-specific blow-off: the most leveraged basket on the board fell while the broad market rose.","body_zh":"到2021年5月约53%的回撤，2021年牛市上半场见顶——中国2021年5月21日矿业/交易打击与过热、过度杠杆的市场触发剧烈的高贝塔去杠杆。宏观环境其实温和（SPY+6.7%、广度扩散等权RSP跑赢SPY+3.9%、再通胀/增长向上），这凸显这是加密自身的吹顶：全场最高杠杆的篮子下跌、而大盘上涨。","drivers":["CRYPTO-SPECIFIC vs benign tape (SPY +6.7%)","China May 2021 mining crackdown","Overheated, over-leveraged market","Violent high-beta unwind"],"drivers_zh":["加密自身 vs 温和大盘（SPY+6.7%）","中国2021年5月矿业打击","过热、过度杠杆的市场","剧烈高贝塔去杠杆"],"prev_key":"2021-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2021-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"First 2021 correction: high-beta unwind","title_zh":"2021年首次回调：高贝塔去杠杆","turn_id":"crypto:peak:2021-02"},"2021-05-21":{"body":"A ~119% surge into November 2021 as the bull cycle made its final blow-off high. The tape was risk-on (SMH +26.8%, growth>value +15.9, calm VIX 20 to 17, falling yields TLT +9.1) and as the highest-beta basket, crypto amplified it hard -- ETF optimism, retail mania and peak risk appetite drove COIN and miners to records before the long winter. The narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY -4.9%) flagged the late-cycle character.","body_zh":"到2021年11月约119%的飙升，牛市作出最后的吹顶高点。环境偏风险偏好（SMH+26.8%、成长跑赢价值+15.9、VIX平静20→17、收益率下行TLT+9.1），作为最高贝塔篮子，加密强力放大它——ETF乐观、散户狂热与峰值风险偏好把COIN与矿企推至纪录高位，随后进入漫长寒冬。狭窄市场（等权RSP跑输SPY-4.9%）已预示晚周期特征。","drivers":["RISK-ON melt-up: SMH +26.8%, growth>value +15.9","Bull cycle final blow-off high","Highest-beta basket amplifies the rip","Narrow late-cycle tape (RSP -4.9% vs SPY)"],"drivers_zh":["风险偏好融涨：SMH+26.8%、成长跑赢价值+15.9","牛市最后的吹顶高点","最高贝塔篮子放大涨幅","狭窄晚周期市场（RSP-4.9% vs SPY）"],"prev_key":"2021-05-21","prev_key_chain":["2021-05-21"],"status":"exact","title":"Run to the November 2021 cycle top","title_zh":"冲向2021年11月周期顶","turn_id":"crypto:trough:2021-05"},"2021-11-08":{"body":"A ~66% plunge into January 2022 as the Fed's hawkish pivot and the start of the rate-hike cycle drained liquidity. The tape rotated risk-off into a stagflation-ish quad (VIX 17 to 30, SPHB-SPLV -13.8, growth>value -10.1) with flight-to-safety (defensives +0.7% vs cyclicals -5.1%); the highest-beta asset sold off first and far worse than the -7.7% SPY, kicking off the 2022 crypto winter.","body_zh":"到2022年1月约66%的暴跌，美联储鹰派转向与加息周期启动抽走流动性。市场转向避险、进入类滞胀象限（VIX 17→30、SPHB-SPLV-13.8、成长跑赢价值-10.1），伴随避险流（防御+0.7% vs 周期-5.1%）；最高贝塔资产最先且远更剧烈地抛售，跌幅超SPY的-7.7%，拉开2022年加密寒冬序幕。","drivers":["RISK-OFF rotation: VIX 17 to 30, SPHB-SPLV -13.8","Fed hawkish pivot drains liquidity","Highest-beta asset sells off first","Crypto -66% vs SPY -7.7%"],"drivers_zh":["避险轮动：VIX 17→30、SPHB-SPLV-13.8","美联储鹰派转向抽走流动性","最高贝塔资产最先抛售","加密-66% vs SPY-7.7%"],"prev_key":"2021-11-08","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Crypto winter begins on the Fed hawkish pivot","title_zh":"加密寒冬开启于美联储鹰派转向","turn_id":"crypto:peak:2021-11"},"2022-01-27":{"body":"A ~57% rebound into late March 2022 -- a sharp but doomed counter-trend rally typical of a high-beta bear. The tape gave a brief reflationary reprieve (SPY +7.4%, VIX 30 to 19, oil +20.4%) even as yields rose (TLT -8.4%), enough to spark an oversold high-beta bounce before the deeper leg down.","body_zh":"到2022年3月下旬约57%的反弹——典型高贝塔熊市中急促却注定夭折的反趋势行情。市场给出短暂的再通胀喘息（SPY+7.4%、VIX 30→19、油+20.4%），即便收益率上行（TLT-8.4%），也足以点燃超卖的高贝塔反弹，随后是更深一段下跌。","drivers":["BRIEF risk-on reprieve: VIX 30 to 19, SPY +7.4%","Counter-trend bear rally","Oversold high-beta bounce","Doomed before the deeper leg down"],"drivers_zh":["短暂风险偏好喘息：VIX 30→19、SPY+7.4%","反趋势熊市行情","超卖高贝塔反弹","更深下跌前的夭折反弹"],"prev_key":"2022-01-27","prev_key_chain":["2022-01-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Bear-market relief bounce","title_zh":"熊市减压反弹","turn_id":"crypto:trough:2022-01"},"2022-03-29":{"body":"A ~74% collapse into June 2022 as the May 2022 Terra/Luna implosion and the 3AC/Celsius leverage cascade vaporized crypto credit. The macro amplified the carnage: a flight-to-safety risk-off (VIX 19 to 29, SPHB-SPLV -18.1, DXY +6.4) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad sent the highest-beta basket down ~4x the -17.9% SPY -- the worst stretch of the winter.","body_zh":"到2022年6月约74%的崩溃，2022年5月Terra/Luna内爆与3AC/Celsius杠杆连环爆破令加密信用蒸发。宏观放大了惨况：放缓/通缩恐慌象限里的避险下泄（VIX 19→29、SPHB-SPLV-18.1、DXY+6.4）把最高贝塔篮子打下约为SPY-17.9%的4倍——本轮寒冬最惨阶段。","drivers":["RISK-OFF flush: VIX 19 to 29, SPHB-SPLV -18.1, DXY +6.4","Terra/Luna stablecoin implosion May 2022","3AC and Celsius leverage cascade","Crypto -74% vs SPY -17.9%"],"drivers_zh":["避险下泄：VIX 19→29、SPHB-SPLV-18.1、DXY+6.4","Terra/Luna稳定币内爆（2022年5月）","3AC与Celsius杠杆连环爆","加密-74% vs SPY-17.9%"],"prev_key":"2022-03-29","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Luna/Terra cascade amid a risk-off flush","title_zh":"Luna/Terra连环崩塌叠加避险下泄","turn_id":"crypto:peak:2022-03"},"2022-06-30":{"body":"A ~112% rebound into mid-August 2022 -- a violent oversold bounce after the Luna cascade, amplified by a brief tech/semis-led risk-on (SMH +20.4%, growth>value +6.5, VIX 29 to 20) in a goldilocks/disinflation quad. The highest-beta basket ripped on the summer risk appetite before the FTX collapse delivered the final blow.","body_zh":"到2022年8月中旬约112%的反弹——Luna连环崩塌后的剧烈超卖反弹，被一段短暂的科技/半导体引领的风险偏好放大（SMH+20.4%、成长跑赢价值+6.5、VIX 29→20），处于金发姑娘/去通胀象限。最高贝塔篮子借夏季风险偏好飙升，随后FTX崩盘给出致命一击。","drivers":["RISK-ON bounce: SMH +20.4%, VIX 29 to 20","Violent post-Luna oversold rebound","Highest-beta basket amplifies summer risk-on","Pre-FTX false dawn"],"drivers_zh":["风险偏好反弹：SMH+20.4%、VIX 29→20","Luna后剧烈超卖反弹","最高贝塔篮子放大夏季风险偏好","FTX前的虚假黎明"],"prev_key":"2022-06-30","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-Luna dead-cat bounce","title_zh":"Luna后的死猫跳","turn_id":"crypto:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-12":{"body":"A ~68% plunge into late December 2022 as the November 2022 FTX collapse -- the largest crypto fraud and exchange failure on record -- destroyed confidence. The macro was a risk-off rate-regime move (TLT -12.8%, VIX 20 to 22, growth>value -12.1) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad; the highest-beta basket marked the cycle washout low.","body_zh":"到2022年12月下旬约68%的暴跌，2022年11月FTX崩盘——史上最大加密欺诈与交易所倒闭——摧毁了信心。宏观是放缓/通缩恐慌象限里的避险型利率/收益率冲击（TLT-12.8%、VIX 20→22、成长跑赢价值-12.1）；最高贝塔篮子打出本轮周期的洗盘低点。","drivers":["RISK-OFF rate move: TLT -12.8%, growth>value -12.1","November 2022 FTX collapse","Largest exchange failure on record","Cycle washout low"],"drivers_zh":["避险利率冲击：TLT-12.8%、成长跑赢价值-12.1","2022年11月FTX崩盘","史上最大交易所倒闭","周期洗盘低点"],"prev_key":"2022-08-12","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-12"],"status":"exact","title":"FTX collapse: the winter low","title_zh":"FTX崩盘：寒冬低点","turn_id":"crypto:peak:2022-08"},"2022-12-28":{"body":"A staggering ~1220% surge from the December 2022 FTX low through December 2024 on a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +153.5%, growth>value +63.1, VIX 22 to 13). The January 2024 spot-Bitcoin-ETF approval, the April 2024 halving and Trump's pro-crypto November 2024 win drove the highest-beta basket to a generational run; the extremely narrow, mega-cap-led tape (RSP lagged SPY -28.5%) was the perfect fuel for the most leveraged theme on the board.","body_zh":"从2022年12月FTX低点到2024年12月约1220%的惊人飙升，搭乘科技/半导体引领的风险偏好融涨（SMH+153.5%、成长跑赢价值+63.1、VIX 22→13）。现货比特币ETF获批（2024年1月）、2024年4月减半与特朗普2024年11月亲加密的胜选把最高贝塔篮子推向一代人级别的行情；极窄、大盘股主导的市场（等权RSP跑输SPY-28.5%）正是全场最高杠杆主题的完美燃料。","drivers":["RISK-ON melt-up: SMH +153.5%, growth>value +63.1","January 2024 spot-Bitcoin-ETF approval plus halving","Trump pro-crypto November 2024 win","Narrow mega-cap tape fuels high-beta (RSP -28.5%)"],"drivers_zh":["风险偏好融涨：SMH+153.5%、成长跑赢价值+63.1","2024年1月现货比特币ETF获批+减半","特朗普2024年11月亲加密胜选","狭窄大盘股市场为高贝塔提供燃料（RSP-28.5%）"],"prev_key":"2022-12-28","prev_key_chain":["2022-12-28"],"status":"exact","title":"ETF super-cycle: 12x off the bottom","title_zh":"ETF超级周期：自底部12倍","turn_id":"crypto:trough:2022-12"},"2024-12-06":{"body":"A ~53% drawdown into the April 8, 2025 low as post-election euphoria faded, the DeepSeek AI scare hit sentiment, and the April 2025 reciprocal-tariff crash drained risk appetite. The tape was a brutal risk-off flush (VIX 13 to 52, SMH -27.3%, SPHB-SPLV -22.7) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad; the highest-beta basket fell hardest, ~3x the -17.8% SPY.","body_zh":"到2025年4月8日低点约53%的回撤，大选后欣快消退、DeepSeek的AI恐慌打击情绪、2025年4月对等关税崩盘抽走风险偏好。市场是放缓/通缩恐慌象限里的残酷避险下泄（VIX 13→52、SMH-27.3%、SPHB-SPLV-22.7）；最高贝塔篮子跌得最惨，约为SPY-17.8%的3倍。","drivers":["RISK-OFF flush: VIX 13 to 52, SPHB-SPLV -22.7","Post-election euphoria fades, DeepSeek scare","April 2025 reciprocal-tariff crash","High-beta crypto -53% vs SPY -17.8%"],"drivers_zh":["避险下泄：VIX 13→52、SPHB-SPLV-22.7","大选后欣快消退、DeepSeek恐慌","2025年4月对等关税崩盘","高贝塔加密-53% vs SPY-17.8%"],"prev_key":"2024-12-06","prev_key_chain":["2024-12-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-shock unwind","title_zh":"关税冲击去杠杆","turn_id":"crypto:peak:2024-12"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"A ~246% rally off the April 2025 tariff low into October 2025 as risk appetite roared back. The tape was a goldilocks melt-up (SMH +89.9%, growth>value +22.7, VIX 52 to 21, DXY -4.1%) and as the highest-beta basket, crypto amplified the cyclical leg (cyclicals +30.3% vs defensives +14.1%). ETF inflows resumed and corporate Bitcoin-treasury adoption (MSTR-style) accelerated, sending COIN and miners sharply higher on a narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY -10.2%).","body_zh":"从2025年4月关税低点到2025年10月约246%的反弹，风险偏好强势回归。市场是金发姑娘融涨（SMH+89.9%、成长跑赢价值+22.7、VIX 52→21、DXY-4.1%），作为最高贝塔篮子，加密放大了周期段（周期+30.3% vs 防御+14.1%）。ETF资金流入恢复、企业比特币储备采用（MSTR式）加速，在狭窄市场（等权RSP跑输SPY-10.2%）中把COIN与矿企大幅推高。","drivers":["RISK-ON melt-up: SMH +89.9%, VIX 52 to 21, DXY -4.1%","Risk appetite roars back, ETF inflows resume","Highest-beta basket amplifies cyclicals (+30.3%)","Corporate Bitcoin-treasury adoption accelerates"],"drivers_zh":["风险偏好融涨：SMH+89.9%、VIX 52→21、DXY-4.1%","风险偏好强势回归、ETF流入恢复","最高贝塔篮子放大周期（+30.3%）","企业比特币储备采用加速"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-tariff crypto surge","title_zh":"关税后加密飙升","turn_id":"crypto:trough:2025-04"},"2025-10-15":{"body":"A ~51% drawdown into February 2026 as the parabolic rally cooled and the building 2026 macro stress -- rising rates and early oil-shock fears -- hit the highest-beta basket first. Notably the broad tape barely moved (SPY +2.2%, VIX 21 to 22, broadening RSP beat SPY +3.4% on a reflation rotation into Energy/Materials), so this was a high-beta-specific unwind: crypto fell ~51% while the index held, the mirror image of its leveraged-on-the-way-up character.","body_zh":"到2026年2月约51%的回撤，抛物线行情降温、2026年累积的宏观压力——上行利率与早期油价冲击担忧——最先打击最高贝塔篮子。值得注意的是大盘几乎未动（SPY+2.2%、VIX 21→22、广度扩散等权RSP跑赢SPY+3.4%，资金再通胀轮动进能源/材料），故这是高贝塔自身的去杠杆：加密下跌约51%而指数企稳，正是其上涨时加杠杆特征的镜像。","drivers":["HIGH-BETA unwind vs flat tape (SPY +2.2%)","Parabolic rally cools, rising rates pressure high-beta","Reflation rotation into Energy/Materials","Highest-beta basket hit first"],"drivers_zh":["高贝塔去杠杆 vs 平盘大盘（SPY+2.2%）","抛物线行情降温、上行利率压制高贝塔","再通胀轮动进能源/材料","最高贝塔篮子最先受击"],"prev_key":"2025-10-15","prev_key_chain":["2025-10-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Late-2025 high-beta correction","title_zh":"2025年末高贝塔回调","turn_id":"crypto:peak:2025-10"},"2026-02-05":{"body":"A strong ~86% rebound off the February 2026 low into June. The tape turned risk-on again (SMH +59.5%, growth>value +7.9, VIX 22 to 16) and as the highest-beta basket, crypto snapped back hard off oversold levels -- even against the hawkish oil-shock backdrop and a firmer dollar (DXY +1.4%). The maturing spot-ETF complex, post-halving supply scarcity and corporate-treasury demand provided a higher floor than past cycles, though the narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY -6.6%) kept it a mega-cap-led, high-beta move.","body_zh":"从2026年2月低点到6月约86%的强劲反弹。市场再度转向风险偏好（SMH+59.5%、成长跑赢价值+7.9、VIX 22→16），作为最高贝塔篮子，加密自超卖水平强力反弹——即便面对鹰派油价冲击背景与更坚挺的美元（DXY+1.4%）。成熟的现货ETF体系、减半后供给稀缺与企业储备需求提供了高于以往周期的底部，尽管狭窄市场（等权RSP跑输SPY-6.6%）使其仍是大盘股主导的高贝塔行情。","drivers":["RISK-ON snapback: SMH +59.5%, VIX 22 to 16","Maturing spot-ETF complex provides a floor","Post-halving supply plus corporate-treasury demand","Highest-beta basket amplifies off oversold lows"],"drivers_zh":["风险偏好反弹：SMH+59.5%、VIX 22→16","成熟现货ETF体系提供底部","减半后供给+企业储备需求","最高贝塔篮子自超卖低点放大"],"prev_key":"2026-02-05","prev_key_chain":["2026-02-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Structural-floor rebound","title_zh":"结构性底部反弹","turn_id":"crypto:trough:2026-02"}},"now":"Crypto & digital assets (IBIT-proxied exchanges, miners and bitcoin-treasury names -- COIN, MSTR and miners) is trending (pos 35, RS rank 12) and remains the highest-beta theme on the board -- the purest risk-appetite barometer here, leading on the way up and on the way down. Everything is a leveraged bet on Bitcoin: COIN's volumes, MSTR's stack and miner economics all swing on the coin. After the late-2025 pullback the basket put in a ~86% rally into June 2026. The 2026 oil-shock/hawkish-Fed backdrop is a headwind -- high-beta crypto hates rising real rates and a firmer dollar (DXY +3.4%) -- but the current reflation/growth-up tape (SPHB-SPLV +20.7, SMH +67.9%) plus structural tailwinds (post-halving supply, the maturing spot-ETF complex, corporate treasury adoption) keep the floor higher than in past cycles. The basket sits at pos 35 (mid-range), well off the Dec-2024 peak -- not yet a late-cycle signal -- and still-elevated high-beta premium (SPHB-SPLV +20.7) gives crypto the macro tailwind it needs, though growth-minus-value at -15.2 and the strong dollar are the key risks to watch.","now_zh":"加密与数字资产（以IBIT代理的交易所、矿企及比特币储备名称——COIN、MSTR与矿企）当前处于趋势扩张期（位置35，RS排名12），仍是全场最高贝塔主题——纯粹的风险偏好晴雨表，上涨领先、下跌亦领先。一切本质上是对比特币的杠杆押注：COIN成交量、MSTR的持仓与矿企经济均随币价波动。2025年末回调后，篮子在2026年6月前录得约86%的反弹。2026年油价冲击/美联储偏鹰背景是阻力——高贝塔加密讨厌实际利率上行与更强势的美元（DXY+3.4%）——但当前再通胀/增长向上的市场（SPHB-SPLV+20.7、SMH+67.9%）加上结构性顺风（减半后供给、日趋成熟的现货ETF体系、企业储备需求）使底部高于以往周期。篮子位于pos 35（中位区间），远离2024年12月顶部——尚未出现晚周期信号——高贝塔溢价（SPHB-SPLV+20.7）仍赋予加密宏观顺风，但成长跑输价值-15.2与强势美元是需要持续关注的关键风险。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-cybersecurity":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"Cybersecurity more than doubled (+103.7%) as a wave of landmark breaches -- Target (110M cards, Jan 2014), Home Depot (56M cards, Sep 2014), JP Morgan (76M accounts, Aug 2014), and Sony Pictures (Nov 2014) -- drove enterprise security budgets to a new tier; the HACK ETF launched in November 2014, giving the space its first broad investable vehicle. The macro backdrop was a slowdown/deflation-scare quad where the dollar surged +16.5% and oil crashed -36.6%; defensives led (+26.7%) over cyclicals (+12.2%), but tech/semis (SMH +39.4%) carved out a growth-within-safety niche. Cybersecurity rode this duality as a secular-growth defensive: mandatory CISO spending, near-zero cloud-native installed base, and a breach-driven legislative push (NIST framework, sector ISACs) compounded the multiple expansion far above SPY's +18.6%.","body_zh":"网络安全大涨逾倍（+103.7%），得益于一波标志性泄露事件——Target（Jan 2014，1.1亿张卡）、Home Depot（Sep 2014，5600万）、JP Morgan（Aug 2014，7600万账户）及Sony Pictures（Nov 2014）——企业安全预算被推向新高度；HACK ETF于2014年11月上市，为该赛道提供了首个可投资载体。宏观背景为放缓/通缩恐慌象限，美元大涨+16.5%、油价暴跌-36.6%；防御板块领强（+26.7%）胜周期板块（+12.2%），但科技/半导体（SMH +39.4%）开辟出安全资金流中的成长位置。网络安全同时具备两层属性：CISO必须支出、云原生工具近乎零的安装基数，以及泄露事件推动的监管立法浪潮，共同推动估值远超SPY (+18.6%)。","drivers":["breach-demand boom","secular budget mandate","sector ETF launch","tech-growth premium","dollar-driven defensives bid"],"drivers_zh":["泄露驱动需求","安全预算强制支出","行业ETF上市","科技成长溢价","美元走强防御吸金"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Breach supercycle ignites new sector","title_zh":"泄露超周期点燃新赛道","turn_id":"cybersecurity:trough:2014-01"},"2015-06-19":{"body":"Cybersecurity fell -38.7% as the 2015-2016 global selloff (China yuan devaluation Aug 2015, oil collapse to $26 by Feb 2016) triggered a flight-to-safety rotation: defensives were flat (+0.0%) while cyclicals fell -15.2%, VIX surged 14->27, and credit spreads (HYG-LQD -11.5%) blew out. High-multiple security software names like FireEye (down 40%+ from summer-2015 highs) and Palo Alto were de-rated as investors questioned 20-30x revenue multiples in a growth-slowing environment. The sector's outperformance in the prior leg made it a crowded long that amplified the unwind (cyber -38.7% vs SPY -11.1%), a pattern that repeats whenever risk-off breaks the high-beta growth premium.","body_zh":"网络安全下跌-38.7%，2015-2016全球抛售（2015年8月人民币贬值、油价至2016年2月崩至26美元）引发避险转向：防御板块持平（+0.0%）而周期股-15.2%，VIX升至27，信用利差大幅走阔（HYG-LQD -11.5%）。FireEye、Palo Alto等高估值安全软件被杀跌，市场质疑营收20-30倍的合理性。上一轮拥挤持仓放大了去杠（-38.7% vs SPY -11.1%），这是高贝塔成长溢价破裂后循环出现的模式。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation","oil price collapse","valuation de-rating","risk-off rotation","crowded-long unwind"],"drivers_zh":["人民币贬值","油价崩跌","估值压缩","避险轮动","拥挤多头平仓"],"prev_key":"2015-06-19","prev_key_chain":["2015-06-19"],"status":"exact","title":"Valuation reset in China-oil risk-off","title_zh":"中国/油价避险中估值重设","turn_id":"cybersecurity:peak:2015-06"},"2016-02-09":{"body":"A +286.9% rally over 31 months as a powerful cyclical recovery (oil +146.9%, copper-gold +29.2%, VIX 27->12) was layered with a secular demand step-change: WannaCry ransomware (May 2017), NotPetya (Jun 2017), and the Equifax breach (Sep 2017) made cybersecurity a board-level priority, driving federal and enterprise budgets sharply higher under the Trump administration. The tape was a classic reflation/growth-up melt-up with tech leading (+101.3%) and semis surging (SMH +133.9%), growth crushing value by +29.0 and high-beta beating low-vol by +52.9; cybersecurity compounded a structural-spend tailwind onto this broad risk-on engine to achieve 4.4x the index return (SPY +64.7%).","body_zh":"历时31个月累涨+286.9%，强劲周期复苏（油+146.9%、铜金+29.2%、VIX 27->12）叠加安全需求跳升：2017年WannaCry勒索软件、NotPetya及Equifax泄露事件将网络安全推至董事会级别议题，驱动联邦及企业预算大幅扩大。市场呈典型再通胀/增长向上风格，科技领涨（+101.3%）、SMH暴涨（+133.9%），成长大幅胜价值、高贝塔胜低波动；网络安全将结构性支出顺风叠加于广泛风险偏好引擎，实现4.4倍SPY收益。","drivers":["cyclical reflation","WannaCry/NotPetya/Equifax breaches","Trump defense spending","tech-semis melt-up","secular budget expansion"],"drivers_zh":["周期性再通胀","WannaCry/NotPetya/Equifax泄露","特朗普安全投入","科技/半导体飞升","安全预算持续扩大"],"prev_key":"2016-02-09","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Reflation and breach wave propel multiyear run","title_zh":"再通胀及泄露浪潮推动多年行情","turn_id":"cybersecurity:trough:2016-02"},"2018-09-14":{"body":"A -23.6% selloff from mid-September to late December 2018 as the Fed hiked rates four times in 2018, pushing the 10-year Treasury above 3.2% in October, while the US-China trade war escalated and fears of a global growth slowdown peaked. Defensives led (Utilities +0.8% vs Tech -20.4%) with VIX exploding 12->30 in a classic flight-to-safety; oil crashed -33.9%. Cybersecurity, as a high-beta growth-software cluster, amplified the index de-rating (cyber -23.6% vs SPY -16.4%, SMH -20.6%), with semis also hit by trade-war supply-chain fears.","body_zh":"自2018年9月中至12月底下跌-23.6%：美联储2018年四次加息，10年期国债收益率10月突破3.2%，中美贸易战升温、全球增长放缓恐慌达顶。防御板块领跑（公用事业+0.8% vs 科技-20.4%），VIX暴升至30，高贝塔成长软件放大指数跌幅（网络安全-23.6% vs SPY -16.4%），半导体同受贸易战供应链忧虑打击。","drivers":["Fed rate hike shock","US-China trade war","growth slowdown fear","risk-off rotation","high-beta de-rating"],"drivers_zh":["美联储加息冲击","中美贸易战","增长放缓恐慌","避险轮动","高贝塔估值压缩"],"prev_key":"2018-09-14","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed rate-shock Q4 tech wreck","title_zh":"美联储加息冲击Q4科技崩跌","turn_id":"cybersecurity:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-21":{"body":"A +86.3% rally from late-December 2018 through late-July 2019 as the Fed pivoted from tightening to on-hold (January 2019 Powell speech), then cut rates three times in H2 2019, compressing risk premia. Tech led (+40.5%) and semis surged (SMH +45.3%) in a reflation/growth-up quad; VIX collapsed 30->12 and credit eased. Cybersecurity outperformed SPY (+26.6%) by over 3x as the dual tailwinds of falling rates (TLT +10.3%, re-rating long-duration growth) and a sustained breach calendar (Capital One hack, Aug 2019) kept secular demand firm.","body_zh":"自2018年12月底至2019年7月末大幅反弹+86.3%：美联储2019年1月鲍威尔讲话由紧转停，H2三次降息，风险溢价收缩。科技领涨（+40.5%）、SMH大涨（+45.3%），VIX崩至12，信用环境改善。网络安全以SPY的逾3倍超越指数，得益于降息重定长久期成长估值及持续的泄露日历（如2019年8月美国一银行黑客事件）维持长期需求。","drivers":["Fed pivot to easing","rate cut cycle","VIX compression","tech-semis risk-on","breach demand"],"drivers_zh":["美联储转向宽松","降息周期","VIX压缩","科技/半导体风险偏好","泄露需求"],"prev_key":"2018-12-21","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-21"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot and trade-truce rebound","title_zh":"美联储转向降息贸易停火反弹","turn_id":"cybersecurity:trough:2018-12"},"2019-07-26":{"body":"A -25.9% idiosyncratic drop even as SPY fell only -0.9%, driven by a twin shock: on August 5, 2019, Trump announced new 10% tariffs on remaining Chinese imports, sending the Nasdaq down -3.4% in a single session, and Q2 2019 earnings season exposed sales-cycle elongation for enterprise SaaS as IT budgets were scrutinized. Defensives led (REIT +8.4%, Utilities +7.2%) over cyclicals (-2.6%) in a mild risk-off (VIX 12->14), while TLT +6.8% signaled a flight to duration safety. Cybersecurity's extreme outperformance in the prior leg had left it at stretched multiples, making the correction disproportionate vs the index.","body_zh":"尽管SPY仅跌-0.9%，网络安全却异常下滑-25.9%，双重冲击驱动：2019年8月5日特朗普宣布对华剩余进口征收10%关税，纳斯达克单日骤跌-3.4%；2019年Q2财报季暴露企业软件销售周期拉长、IT预算受审视。防御板块领强（REIT +8.4%、公用事业+7.2%），TLT +6.8%，长久期避险资金流入。上一轮过高估值拉伸使得修正幅度远超指数。","drivers":["trade-war tariff shock","SaaS sales-cycle elongation","valuation air-pocket","defensive rotation","duration bid"],"drivers_zh":["贸易战关税冲击","SaaS销售周期拉长","估值真空","防御板块轮动","长久期资金流入"],"prev_key":"2019-07-26","prev_key_chain":["2019-07-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade-war escalation hits SaaS valuations","title_zh":"贸易战升温冲击SaaS估值","turn_id":"cybersecurity:peak:2019-07"},"2019-10-18":{"body":"A +30.5% rally from mid-October 2019 through mid-February 2020 as the US-China Phase-1 trade deal framework (announced Oct 11, 2019) lifted macro risk-off pressure and the Fed's three 2019 rate cuts kept financial conditions easy. Tech led (+26.1%), semis surged (SMH +24.6%) in a growth-up tape (growth>value +10.0, VIX 14->16 stable), and cybersecurity rode the broad tech re-rating. The rally was notably narrow (RSP lagged SPY -3.2%), a mega-cap-led tape on a goldilocks slowdown-scare quad, with the structural cyber-spend backstop keeping the basket well-bid relative to peer SaaS names that had missed guidance.","body_zh":"自2019年10月中至2020年2月中大幅反弹+30.5%：2019年10月11日美中第一阶段贸易协议框架平息宏观避险压力，美联储2019年三次降息维持宽松金融条件。科技领涨（+26.1%）、SMH大涨（+24.6%），成长胜价值+10.0，网络安全跟随广泛科技重定价。市场广度较窄（RSP落后SPY -3.2%），安全预算强制属性支撑篮子跑赢同类SaaS中指引不达标者。","drivers":["Phase-1 trade deal","Fed rate cut tailwind","tech-semis re-rating","narrow mega-cap tape","secular spend backstop"],"drivers_zh":["第一阶段贸易协议","美联储降息顺风","科技/半导体重定价","大盘股主导的狭幅行情","安全预算强制支撑"],"prev_key":"2019-10-18","prev_key_chain":["2019-10-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Phase-1 trade truce revives risk-on","title_zh":"第一阶段贸易停火重启风险偏好","turn_id":"cybersecurity:trough:2019-10"},"2020-02-20":{"body":"A -33.8% collapse in just four weeks as COVID-19 pandemic fear triggered the fastest -30% market crash in history (Feb 20 to Mar 16, 2020): VIX exploded 16->83, SPY fell -28.8%, defensives fell -22.2% and cyclicals -35.3% in an indiscriminate liquidation. Treasury yields collapsed (TLT +11.9%) and oil crashed -46.6%, signaling a global-recession panic. Cybersecurity fell in line with high-beta peers (SMH -32.0%) as forced margin-call selling and risk-de-risking overwhelmed any sector fundamentals; the basket offered no defensive shelter in a pure-panic event.","body_zh":"仅四周崩跌-33.8%：新冠疫情引发史上最快的-30%崩市（2020年2月20日至3月16日），VIX暴升至83，SPY跌-28.8%，防御板块-22.2%、周期股-35.3%，是一场不分青红的强制抛售。国债收益率骤降（TLT +11.9%）、油价暴跌-46.6%，预示全球衰退恐慌。网络安全在高贝塔同伴（SMH -32.0%）中随大流下滑，强制追缴保证金与去风险浪潮覆盖了一切行业基本面。","drivers":["COVID pandemic shock","forced deleveraging","indiscriminate risk-off","VIX spike to 83","global recession fear"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情冲击","强制去杠杆","无差别避险","VIX暴升至83","全球衰退恐慌"],"prev_key":"2020-02-20","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-20"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash wipes all sectors","title_zh":"新冠疫情崩市席卷全板块","turn_id":"cybersecurity:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-16":{"body":"A +420.6% rally over 20 months (the basket's largest leg) as the COVID-era policy response -- zero rates, $4T+ Fed QE, $5T fiscal stimulus -- inflated all risk assets to extremes; VIX collapsed 83->18, high-beta beat low-vol by +159.7, growth>value +38.1, and the dollar fell -4.2%. The work-from-home shift created an immediate zero-trust and endpoint security demand explosion: CrowdStrike, Zscaler, and Cloudflare each rose 200%+ in 2020, and the December 2020 SolarWinds supply-chain breach cemented national-security-grade federal cyber spending. Breadth broadened (RSP beat SPY +9.2%) into a reflation melt-up that amplified every growth dollar in the basket.","body_zh":"20个月大涨+420.6%（篮子历史最大涨幅）：零利率、美联储4万亿美元QE加5万亿美元财政刺激将风险资产推向极致：VIX崩至18，高贝塔跑赢低波动+159.7，成长胜价值+38.1，美元走弱（-4.2%）。远程办公模式引发零信任和端点安全需求爆发：CrowdStrike、Zscaler、Cloudflare均在2020年内上涨逾200%，12月SolarWinds供应链攻击推动国家安全级联邦网络安全投入。广度扩散（RSP跑赢SPY +9.2%），全面再通胀飞升放大了篮子内每一元成长。","drivers":["zero-rate policy","fiscal stimulus","WFH zero-trust demand","SolarWinds breach","tech-semis melt-up"],"drivers_zh":["零利率政策","财政刺激","远程办公零信任需求","SolarWinds供应链攻击","科技/半导体飞升"],"prev_key":"2020-03-16","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Pandemic-era zero-trust melt-up","title_zh":"疫情时代零信任飞升","turn_id":"cybersecurity:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-09":{"body":"Cyber fell -35.8% as the Fed pivot de-rated high-multiple security-software growth names: yields surged (TLT -12.3%) and the dollar firmed +5.4% in a stagflation-ish, risk-off regime (VIX 18->32, defensives +1.3% vs cyclicals -5.1%). Rising rates outweighed strong secular bookings in the broad SaaS sell-off, and the basket's high beta amplified the de-rating (SMH -20.6% vs SPY -10.5%). Russia's Ukraine invasion (Feb 2022) briefly revived cyber as a strategic asset but was insufficient to offset the rate-shock de-rating.","body_zh":"美联储转向令高估值安全软件成长股价值下杀，网络安全跌-35.8%：收益率飞升（TLT -12.3%）、美元走强+5.4%，处于类滞胀、避险行情（VIX 18->32，防御+1.3% vs 周期-5.1%）。利率上升盖过强劲的长期订单，在广泛的SaaS抛售中高贝塔篮子放大了跌幅（SMH -20.6% vs SPY -10.5%）。","drivers":["rate-shock risk-off","Fed hiking","multiple compression","SaaS sell-off","stagflation rotation"],"drivers_zh":["利率冲击避险","美联储加息","估值压缩","SaaS抛售","滞胀轮动"],"prev_key":"2021-11-09","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Growth-multiple compression in rate-shock bear","title_zh":"利率冲击熊市中成长估值压缩","turn_id":"cybersecurity:peak:2021-11"},"2022-03-14":{"body":"A +28.2% bounce as rate volatility briefly cooled (VIX 32->19) in a reflation/growth-up quad, with breadth narrow (RSP lagged SPY -3.0%). The geopolitical backdrop (Russia-Ukraine cyberthreat narrative) kept a structural cyber-spend bid even as macro pressure lingered, but the move was an oversold reflex concentrated in the most beaten-down names rather than a regime turn; the leg's 3-week duration confirmed it as a technical bounce ahead of the next wave of rate hikes.","body_zh":"利率波动短暂冷却（VIX 32->19），反弹+28.2%，处于再通胀/增长向上象限，市场广度较窄（RSP跑输SPY -3.0%）。俄乌局势维持了网络安全结构性买盘，但这是超卖技术性反弹而非行情转向，三周时长印证其本质，随后美联储新一轮加息浪潮随即来袭。","drivers":["risk-on bounce","oversold rebound","VIX relief","cyber-spend geopolitical bid"],"drivers_zh":["风险偏好反弹","超卖反弹","VIX缓和","网络安全地缘政治买盘"],"prev_key":"2022-03-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Oversold relief bounce","title_zh":"超卖缓解反弹","turn_id":"cybersecurity:trough:2022-03"},"2022-04-04":{"body":"A -35.8% slide as surging real yields (TLT -10.1%, the Fed began hiking in March 2022) and a stronger dollar (+4.9%) hit growth software again in a slowdown-scare flight-to-safety (VIX 19->33, defensives -4.5% vs cyclicals -11.9%). Enterprise customers began deferring or renegotiating large security contracts as CFOs scrutinized discretionary spend in a potential recession, layering fundamental pressure onto the macro de-rating; cyber fell well past the index (SMH -18.6% vs SPY -14.0%).","body_zh":"实际收益率飞升（TLT -10.1%，美联储2022年3月开始加息）及美元走强（+4.9%）再度冲击成长软件，下滑-35.8%，处于放缓恐慌下的避险转向（VIX 19->33，防御-4.5% vs 周期-11.9%）。企业客户开始推迟或重谈大型安全合同，CFO审视非必要支出，基本面压力叠加宏观估值下杀，跌幅远超指数（SMH -18.6% vs SPY -14.0%）。","drivers":["rate-shock risk-off","real yields surge","budget scrutiny","SaaS revenue concerns","dollar strength"],"drivers_zh":["利率冲击避险","实际收益率飞升","预算审视","SaaS营收担忧","美元走强"],"prev_key":"2022-04-04","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-shock new lows, budget-scrutiny fears","title_zh":"利率冲击创新低、预算审视担忧","turn_id":"cybersecurity:peak:2022-04"},"2022-05-11":{"body":"A +32.6% rebound on peak-inflation hopes as VIX eased 33->20 in a goldilocks-flavored quad (cyclicals +8.2% vs defensives +5.9%), even as the dollar firmed +2.6% and bonds stayed soft (TLT -1.6%). Resilient security budgets (Palo Alto and CrowdStrike beat Q2-Q3 2022 earnings) supported the bounce relative to broader software, but the move tracked the broad high-beta risk-on squeeze rather than a fundamental inflection; the 3-month duration and +32.6% gain vs SPY's +9.7% confirm this was a high-beta beta trade.","body_zh":"通胀见顶预期提振VIX回落至20，处于金发女童象限（周期+8.2% vs 防御+5.9%），反弹+32.6%，尽管美元+2.6%、利率依旧偏高。Palo Alto及CrowdStrike连续超越2022年Q2-Q3财报支撑反弹，但整个走势跟随高贝塔风险偏好挤压而非基本面转折点——三个月时长及+32.6%涨幅vs SPY +9.7%印证其高贝塔交易属性。","drivers":["peak-inflation hope","VIX easing","high-beta squeeze","resilient cyber budgets","goldilocks quad"],"drivers_zh":["通胀见顶预期","VIX回落","高贝塔挤压","安全预算韧性","金发女童象限"],"prev_key":"2022-05-11","prev_key_chain":["2022-05-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-inflation relief rally","title_zh":"通胀见顶缓和反弹","turn_id":"cybersecurity:trough:2022-05"},"2022-08-15":{"body":"A -30.1% drop into January 2023 as Fed Chair Powell's hawkish August 26 Jackson Hole speech reset rate expectations sharply higher (TLT -9.5%); growth lagged value hard (-14.2), breadth broadened (RSP beat SPY +4.9%), and energy/health led the tape, a rotation away from long-duration growth. Cybersecurity's lengthening enterprise sales cycles (Zscaler and Okta flagged deal elongation in Q3 2022 earnings) layered fundamental disappointment onto the macro de-rating (SMH -16.8% vs SPY -10.8%).","body_zh":"美联储主席2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔鹰派讲话重设加息预期，TLT -9.5%，下跌至2023年1月-30.1%。成长大幅跑输价值(-14.2)，广度扩散（RSP跑赢SPY +4.9%），能源/医疗领跑，资金大举远离长期成长资产。Zscaler、Okta Q3 2022财报标志销售周期拉长，基本面失望叠加宏观估值下杀（SMH -16.8% vs SPY -10.8%）。","drivers":["Jackson Hole rate reset","growth-to-value rotation","yields surge","sales-cycle elongation","rate-driven de-rating"],"drivers_zh":["杰克逊霍尔鹰派重设","成长转价值轮动","收益率飞升","销售周期拉长","利率驱动估值下杀"],"prev_key":"2022-08-15","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkish-reset drives leg down","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派重设驱动下跌","turn_id":"cybersecurity:peak:2022-08"},"2023-01-05":{"body":"A +135.6% run over 25 months as disinflation, the generative-AI rally (ChatGPT launched Nov 2022; Nvidia's AI surge drove SMH +151.0%), and relentless secular security demand compounded in a goldilocks risk-on melt-up: VIX fell 22->15, growth crushed value by +67.4, and breadth was extremely narrow (RSP lagged SPY -33.1%). Platform-consolidation wins at CrowdStrike (Falcon Complete) and Palo Alto (Cortex XDR) and breach catalysts sustained the bid through the 2024 Fed cut cycle even as yields drifted up (TLT -7.2%); AI-security (agentic threat detection) added a new investment narrative on top of the secular demand floor.","body_zh":"历时25个月大涨+135.6%：去通胀、生成式AI浪潮（ChatGPT 2022年11月上线，英伟达AI驱动SMH +151.0%）及持续安全需求叠加在金发女童风险偏好飞升之上：VIX跌至15，成长大幅胜价值+67.4，广度极度狭窄（RSP落后SPY -33.1%）。CrowdStrike、Palo Alto平台整合胜利及数据泄露事件维持买盘，AI安全（代理式威胁检测）叠加新投资叙事，即便收益率上行（TLT -7.2%）也未撼动买盘。","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","generative-AI tailwind","secular spend","platform consolidation","breach catalysts"],"drivers_zh":["狭幅风险偏好飞升","生成式AI顺风","安全长期支出","平台整合胜利","数据泄露催化"],"prev_key":"2023-01-05","prev_key_chain":["2023-01-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Secular-spend compounding on narrow melt-up","title_zh":"安全长期支出复利搭乘狭幅飞升","turn_id":"cybersecurity:trough:2023-01"},"2025-02-13":{"body":"A -22.6% pullback through the DeepSeek scare (Jan 2025) and April's reciprocal-tariff crash, in a violent flight-to-safety: VIX exploded 15->52, high-beta cratered vs low-vol by -20.9%, and defensives (-7.3%) beat cyclicals (-18.0%) in a slowdown-scare quad. Macro de-risking hit growth software despite resilient cyber fundamentals, with the basket amplifying the move (SMH -28.6% vs SPY -18.3%) as the DeepSeek open-source model raised broad questions about AI infrastructure spending and tech valuations.","body_zh":"经历DeepSeek恐慌（2025年1月）和4月对等关税崩盘，在剧烈避险中回调-22.6%：VIX暴升至52，高贝塔相对低波动重挫-20.9%，放缓恐慌象限中防御（-7.3%）胜周期（-18.0%）。尽管网络安全基本面韧健，宏观去风险仍冲击成长软件，DeepSeek开源模型引发对AI基础设施支出及科技估值的广泛质疑，篮子放大跌幅（SMH -28.6% vs SPY -18.3%）。","drivers":["DeepSeek AI scare","reciprocal tariff shock","VIX spike to 52","risk-off de-risking","high-beta sell-down"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek AI恐慌","对等关税冲击","VIX暴升至52","避险去风险","高贝塔抛售"],"prev_key":"2025-02-13","prev_key_chain":["2025-02-13"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek and tariff risk-off dip","title_zh":"DeepSeek与关税避险回调","turn_id":"cybersecurity:peak:2025-02"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"A +44.4% recovery off the April low as tariff fears eased (US-China 90-day tariff pause, May 2025) and a goldilocks risk-on regime returned: VIX collapsed 52->17, high-beta beat low-vol by +61.7, growth>value +25.0 and the dollar fell -3.4%. Breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -13.2%); high-profile breaches plus AI-security and identity demand kept this high-beta group bid (SMH +95.1%) into November, with the basket compounding a structural secular-spend advantage onto the broad risk-on engine.","body_zh":"自4月低点反弹+44.4%：关税担忧缓和（美中90天关税暂停，2025年5月），金发女童风险偏好行情重启：VIX崩落52->17，高贝塔跑赢低波+61.7，成长胜价值+25.0，美元跌-3.4%。广度较窄（RSP落后SPY -13.2%）；高注目度泄露事件及AI安全/身份认证需求维持高贝塔组的买盘（SMH +95.1%）至11月。","drivers":["tariff-truce relief","VIX collapse","AI-security demand","narrow risk-on melt-up","high-beta beta squeeze"],"drivers_zh":["关税暂停缓和","VIX崩落","AI安全需求","狭幅风险偏好飞升","高贝塔挤压"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-truce recovery on risk-on melt-up","title_zh":"关税停火复苏风险偏好飞升","turn_id":"cybersecurity:trough:2025-04"},"2025-11-11":{"body":"A -28.7% drop as the late-2025 hawkish reset and the early-2026 Hormuz oil/CPI shock pressured growth multiples. This was a rotation more than a crash: SPY was flat (+0.2%) while breadth broadened sharply (RSP beat SPY +6.6%) and growth lagged value (-14.9) in a stagflation-ish quad with oil +8.6%. Stretched valuations made cyber vulnerable as capital left over-owned high-beta growth for Materials (+21.6%), Energy (+21.5%), and Staples (+15.8%) -- classic stagflation sector rotation that hit long-duration growth software hardest.","body_zh":"2025年末鹰派重设及2026年初霍尔木兹石油/CPI冲击压制成长估值，下跌-28.7%。这更多是轮动而非崩跌：SPY持平（+0.2%），广度急剧扩散（RSP跑赢SPY +6.6%），成长跑输价值(-14.9)，处于类滞胀象限，油价+8.6%。估值过高与成长软件过度持仓为其弱点，资金流向材料（+21.6%）、能源（+21.5%）及日常消费品（+15.8%）。","drivers":["stagflation rotation","hawkish rate reset","Hormuz oil shock","growth-to-commodity rotation","valuation stretch"],"drivers_zh":["滞胀轮动","鹰派利率重设","霍尔木兹石油冲击","成长转大宗商品轮动","估值过度拉伸"],"prev_key":"2025-11-11","prev_key_chain":["2025-11-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Hawkish-reset consolidation as leadership broadens","title_zh":"鹰派重设盘整领跑扩散","turn_id":"cybersecurity:peak:2025-11"},"2026-02-23":{"body":"A +64.2% rally as geopolitical risk eased following a Hormuz ceasefire and a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up resumed: VIX fell 21->16, high-beta beat low-vol by +30.6, growth>value +8.5, in a reflation/growth-up quad with oil +39.0% and copper-gold +27.0%. Breadth stayed narrow (RSP lagged SPY -7.5%); defensive sectors (Health -6.8%, Utilities -7.6%, Staples -7.9%) all fell as capital concentrated in tech and semis (SMH +47.2%). Durable security spend and AI-security demand reasserted cyber's leadership, and the basket ran to topping levels before broad tech-leadership rollover began.","body_zh":"霍尔木兹停火缓和地缘政治风险，科技/半导体领涨风险偏好飞升重启，反弹+64.2%：VIX回落21->16，高贝塔跑赢低波+30.6，成长胜价值+8.5，处于再通胀/增长向上象限，油+39.0%、铜金+27.0%。广度保持较窄（RSP落后SPY -7.5%）；防御板块均下跌，资金集中于科技和半导体（SMH +47.2%）。安全稳健支出和AI安全需求重申领跑，篮子涨至见顶水平。","drivers":["Hormuz ceasefire","narrow tech-semis melt-up","AI-security demand","secular spend","risk-on rebound"],"drivers_zh":["霍尔木兹停火","狭幅科技/半导体飞升","AI安全需求","安全长期支出","风险偏好反弹"],"prev_key":"2026-02-23","prev_key_chain":["2026-02-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Hormuz ceasefire-relief tech-led melt-up","title_zh":"霍尔木兹停火缓和带动科技飞升","turn_id":"cybersecurity:trough:2026-02"}},"now":"Cybersecurity sits at the 87th price percentile in a Topping phase, ranked 9th of 11 GICS sectors on relative strength, meaning the sector remains well-bid but is no longer at the tip of the spear. The current quad is reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%), which historically favors cyclical and energy leadership over high-beta software. Tech still leads at +24.3% and semis (SMH +67.9%) are outperforming, so the risk-on melt-up that carried cyber from the Feb-2026 trough is intact -- but breadth is broadening (RSP beat SPY +2.9%), the dollar is firming (+3.4% DXY), and growth has lagged value by -15.2%, all classic late-cycle signals that argue for rotation out of stretched growth software. Cyber has compounded a +64% rally into a stretched valuation, and the regime environment points to consolidation or mean-reversion rather than another extension leg.","now_zh":"网络安全处于价格第87百分位的\"见顶\"阶段，相对强度在11个GICS板块中排名第9——仍受追捧，但已不再领跑。当前象限为再通胀/增长向上（周期股+11.2% vs 防御板块+6.9%，油+19.2%，铜金+18.3%），历史上利好周期/能源而非高贝塔软件。科技仍领涨（+24.3%），半导体（SMH +67.9%）表现强劲，2月低点以来+64%的风险偏好行情尚未终结——但市场广度扩散（RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%）、美元走强（DXY +3.4%）、成长跑输价值（-15.2%），均为典型的周期末期信号，预示过度拉伸的成长软件面临轮动压力。网络安全估值已偏高，当前宏观环境指向盘整或均值回归，而非再度拉升。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-data_center_power":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"The basket gained only +2% over 17 months versus SPY +18.5%, severely lagging as these names were still priced as ordinary industrial electricals with zero AI thesis. The macro backdrop was a slowdown/deflation-scare quad: oil crashed -35% as Saudi Arabia held production against the U.S. shale glut, TLT surged +20% as the Fed completed its QE taper in October 2014, and the dollar gained +17.6% on the resulting U.S.-vs-world rate divergence. Defensives dominated (Health +38.8%, Utilities +20.2%) while Energy cratered -8%. The early hyperscaler buildout by AWS, Azure, and Google provided a thin tailwind for data-center power and UPS demand, but Eaton and Emerson Network Power (pre-IPO Vertiv) traded as slow-growth industrials, and the group barely budged against a ripping SPY.","body_zh":"该篮子在17个月内仅上涨2%，而标普500涨幅达18.5%，严重落后，因为这些标的仍被定价为普通工业电气企业，尚无AI主线。宏观背景属于放缓/通缩恐慌象限：受沙特维持产量打压美国页岩油之争影响，油价暴跌35%；美联储于2014年10月完成QE缩减令TLT上涨20%；美国与全球的利率差异推动美元走强+17.6%。防御股主导（医疗+38.8%、公用事业+20.2%），能源板块暴跌-8%。AWS、Azure和谷歌的早期超大规模建设为数据中心电力和UPS需求带来细微利好，但伊顿和艾默生网络电力（即上市前的维谛）仍以低增长工业股交易，整体几乎未能跑赢大盘。","drivers":["oil collapse -35% Saudi vs shale","QE taper dollar +17.6%","defensives-led quad (Health +38.8%)","pre-AI thesis pricing"],"drivers_zh":["油价暴跌-35%沙特对抗页岩油","QE缩减推升美元+17.6%","防御股主导象限（医疗+38.8%）","尚无AI主线定价"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Cloud buildout lifts sleepy industrial names","title_zh":"云计算建设为沉寂工业标的提供微薄支撑","turn_id":"data_center_power:trough:2014-01"},"2015-06-11":{"body":"A -25.8% selloff over 7.5 months driven by the August 2015 China stock market crash — the SSE Composite fell ~43% in two months — combined with oil collapsing -50% as crude hit multi-year lows. This was a textbook flight-to-safety rotation: defensives held near flat (-0.8%) while cyclicals fell -15.8%, VIX spiked from 13 to 24, and credit spreads (HYG-LQD -9.7%) blew out. The basket, as an industrial/capex name, was sold alongside Financials (-15.8%), Materials (-24.9%), and Energy (-30.1%). Equal-weight lagged cap-weight -4.2%, confirming this was a wholesale macro risk-off event where the basket underperformed the broad SPY (-9.9%) due to higher operating leverage and longer-cycle capex exposure.","body_zh":"在7.5个月内下跌25.8%，由2015年8月中国股市崩盘（上证综指两个月内跌约43%）叠加油价暴跌50%（原油触及多年低位）共同驱动。这是典型的避险轮动：防御股基本持平（-0.8%），周期股跌-15.8%，VIX从13飙至24，信用利差（HYG-LQD -9.7%）急剧走阔。该篮子作为工业/资本开支标的与金融股（-15.8%）、原材料（-24.9%）和能源（-30.1%）一同遭到抛售。等权跑输市值权-4.2%，证实这是全面宏观避险事件，该篮子因更高运营杠杆和更长资本开支周期而跑输大盘SPY（-9.9%）。","drivers":["China stock crash Aug 2015 SSE -43%","oil -50% deflation","risk-off VIX 13->24","credit blowout HYG-LQD -9.7%"],"drivers_zh":["中国股市2015年8月崩盘上证-43%","油价-50%通缩","避险VIX 13->24","信用利差走阔HYG-LQD -9.7%"],"prev_key":"2015-06-11","prev_key_chain":["2015-06-11"],"status":"exact","title":"China crash and oil rout trigger risk-off flush","title_zh":"中国股灾与油价暴跌引爆避险急挫","turn_id":"data_center_power:peak:2015-06"},"2016-01-25":{"body":"A massive +103% gain over 31 months, more than doubling as the basket was carried by one of the longest reflationary risk-on cycles in the post-GFC era. Oil bottomed near $26/barrel in January 2016 and recovered +126%, the dollar weakened -4.3%, and VIX collapsed from 24 to 14. The November 2016 Trump election catalyzed a sharp pro-cyclical rotation (Financials +75.6%, Industrials +69.7%, Tech +94%) on expectations of infrastructure spending and deregulation. Semiconductors led (SMH +131.8%), growth beat value by +21.2 points, and high-beta outperformed low-vol by +46.3 points. The early cloud capex acceleration by hyperscalers drove incremental demand for data-center power management and cooling kit, beginning to establish the group as a secular growth story within an industrial-cycle reflation.","body_zh":"在31个月内大涨103%，受后金融危机时代最长反通胀风险偏好周期之一的推动而翻倍。油价于2016年1月在约26美元/桶触底后反弹+126%，美元走弱-4.3%，VIX从24跌至14。2016年11月特朗普当选引发明显的顺周期板块轮动（金融+75.6%、工业+69.7%、科技+94%），市场预期基础设施支出和放松监管。半导体领涨（SMH +131.8%），成长股跑赢价值股+21.2个百分点，高贝塔跑赢低波动+46.3个百分点。超大规模厂商早期云计算资本开支加速为数据中心电力管理和散热设备提供了递增需求，开始将该板块在工业周期反通胀中确立为长期成长题材。","drivers":["oil recovery +126% from $26 bottom","Trump reflation pro-cyclical trade","semis-led risk-on SMH +131.8%","cloud capex acceleration","dollar weak -4.3%"],"drivers_zh":["油价自26美元底部反弹+126%","特朗普反通胀顺周期交易","半导体领涨SMH +131.8%","云计算资本开支加速","美元走弱-4.3%"],"prev_key":"2016-01-25","prev_key_chain":["2016-01-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Reflation melt-up: Trump capex plus cloud acceleration","title_zh":"反通胀暴涨：特朗普资本开支与云计算加速","turn_id":"data_center_power:trough:2016-01"},"2018-09-05":{"body":"A sharp -26.1% correction over 3.6 months as the Fed delivered its fourth 2018 rate hike in December while VIX exploded from 14 to 36, marking the worst December for U.S. stocks since 1931. The driver was a simultaneous shock from Fed tightening, U.S.-China trade war escalation (25% tariffs on $250B of Chinese goods), and slowing global growth: Tech fell -21.9%, Industrials -21.4%, and Energy -26.2%, while defensives (Utilities -3.7%, Staples -8.8%) materially outperformed. Semiconductors led the decline (SMH -24.4%) as global capex expectations were cut. The basket sold off in-line with high-beta tech/industrial names as investors priced a capex freeze, though the underlying cloud-spending thesis remained conceptually intact.","body_zh":"在短短3.6个月内急跌26.1%，原因是美联储在12月完成2018年第四次加息，VIX从14飙至36，创下1931年以来美股最差12月。驱动因素是美联储紧缩、中美贸易战升级（对价值2500亿美元中国商品加征25%关税）和全球增长放缓的三重冲击：科技板块跌-21.9%、工业-21.4%、能源-26.2%，而防御股（公用事业-3.7%、必需消费品-8.8%）明显跑赢。半导体领跌（SMH -24.4%），全球资本开支预期被大幅下调。该篮子随高贝塔科技/工业股同步下跌，投资者为资本开支冻结定价，但底层云计算支出逻辑在概念上依然成立。","drivers":["Fed 4th hike Dec 2018 VIX 14->36","U.S.-China trade war 25% tariffs","global growth slowdown","capex freeze fear","semis SMH -24.4%"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2018年12月第四次加息VIX 14->36","中美贸易战25%关税","全球增长放缓","资本开支冻结担忧","半导体SMH -24.4%"],"prev_key":"2018-09-05","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed rate shock and trade war ignite risk-off selloff","title_zh":"美联储加息冲击与贸易战引爆避险抛售","turn_id":"data_center_power:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"A +63.6% gain over 13.7 months as the Fed executed a dramatic pivot at the January 2019 FOMC meeting, removing guidance for further hikes and signaling patience — Powell stated the Fed would wait and watch with flexibility. This dovish pivot collapsed the 2018 recession-fear premium: VIX fell from 36 to 14, Tech led (+79.3%) with semis surging (SMH +88.9%), growth beat value by +23 points, and SPY rallied +46.8%. The basket rode the risk-on recovery as hyperscaler capex resumed its acceleration, with Microsoft Azure, AWS, and Google Cloud expanding data-center power draws and ordering grid-edge equipment at a rising pace. Narrow breadth (equal-weight lagged -6.7%) confirmed this was a mega-cap-driven recovery, with Eaton and the soon-to-be-public Vertiv (SPAC IPO February 2020) as core beneficiaries.","body_zh":"在13.7个月内上涨63.6%，受美联储于2019年1月FOMC会议大幅转向的驱动：移除进一步加息指引，鲍威尔表示将保持灵活、耐心观察。这一鸽派转向消除了2018年衰退恐惧溢价：VIX从36降至14，科技领涨（+79.3%），半导体反弹（SMH +88.9%），成长股跑赢价值股+23个百分点，SPY大涨46.8%。随着超大规模厂商资本开支重新加速，微软Azure、AWS和谷歌云持续扩大数据中心用电规模并加速订购电网边缘设备，该篮子乘势反弹。广度偏窄（等权跑输-6.7%）证实这是巨头驱动的复苏行情，伊顿和即将上市的维谛（2020年2月SPAC上市）是核心受益标的。","drivers":["Fed Jan 2019 patience dovish pivot","semis recovery SMH +88.9%","cloud capex re-acceleration","growth vs value +23pt","VIX 36->14"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月鸽派转向","半导体复苏SMH +88.9%","云计算资本开支重新加速","成长跑赢价值+23个百分点","VIX 36->14"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell pivot ignites cloud-infrastructure recovery","title_zh":"鲍威尔鸽派转向点燃云基础设施复苏","turn_id":"data_center_power:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-14":{"body":"A devastating -48.7% crash in just 1.1 months as COVID-19 spread globally and the WHO declared a pandemic on March 11, 2020. This was the fastest bear market in history: VIX exploded from 14 to 76, SPY fell -28.9%, oil collapsed -60.9%, and cyclicals fell -37.2% versus defensives -18.3%. The basket, as a high-beta capital-equipment name, was hammered harder than the broad market as investors anticipated a global capex freeze. Financials (-38.4%), Industrials (-36.1%), and Energy (-56.1%) led the liquidation while even growth beat value (+5.7%) as mega-cap tech was a relative safe haven. Equal-weight lagged cap-weight -4.8%, confirming this was a wholesale risk-off panic across the entire mid/small-cap industrial complex.","body_zh":"在短短1.1个月内暴跌48.7%，因新冠疫情向全球蔓延，世卫组织于2020年3月11日宣布大流行。这是历史上最快速的熊市：VIX从14爆升至76，SPY下跌28.9%，油价崩跌60.9%，周期股跌37.2%，防御股跌18.3%。该篮子作为高贝塔资本设备标的，跌幅远超大盘，投资者预期全球资本开支将冻结。金融（-38.4%）、工业（-36.1%）和能源（-56.1%）领跌。等权跑输市值权-4.8%，证实这是整个中小市值工业体系的全面恐慌性清仓，而非板块特定行情。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic WHO declaration Mar 11","VIX 14->76 fastest bear market","global capex freeze fear","oil -60.9%","cyclicals -37.2%"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情WHO宣布大流行3月11日","VIX 14->76史上最快熊市","全球资本开支冻结担忧","油价-60.9%","周期股-37.2%"],"prev_key":"2020-02-14","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-14"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID-19 pandemic triggers indiscriminate liquidation","title_zh":"新冠疫情引爆无差别抛售清仓","turn_id":"data_center_power:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"A +196% gain over 19.7 months, the single largest leg before the AI era, as the Fed cut rates to zero on March 15 and launched unlimited QE, Congress passed the $2.2 trillion CARES Act, and the pandemic paradoxically turbocharged the digital transformation thesis. Data-center demand surged as Zoom, Teams, and streaming services drove traffic records; hyperscaler capex accelerated as cloud migration displaced on-premises infrastructure. VIX collapsed 76 to 17, oil recovered +302%, the dollar weakened -7.0%, and equal-weight broadly outperformed (+11.3%) in a broadening reflationary melt-up. Semis led (SMH +200.8%), high-beta crushed low-vol by +180 points. The basket entered this leg as a capex-infrastructure play and exited with the AI power thesis seeds fully planted.","body_zh":"在19.7个月内上涨196%，是AI时代前最大的单条上涨腿。美联储于3月15日降息至零并推出无限QE，国会通过2.2万亿美元CARES法案，而疫情悖论性地加速了数字化转型主线。随着Zoom、Teams和流媒体服务创下流量纪录，数据中心需求飙升；超大规模厂商资本开支加速，云迁移取代本地基础设施。VIX从76崩至17，油价反弹+302%，美元走弱-7.0%，等权大幅跑赢（+11.3%），呈现广泛反通胀式暴涨。半导体领涨（SMH +200.8%），高贝塔跑赢低波动+180个百分点。该篮子以资本基础设施标的进入这条腿，以AI电力主线的种子完全播下退出。","drivers":["Fed zero rates unlimited QE Mar 15","CARES Act $2.2T stimulus","digital transformation pandemic acceleration","semis SMH +200.8%","cloud hyperscaler capex surge"],"drivers_zh":["美联储3月15日降息至零无限QE","CARES法案2.2万亿美元刺激","疫情加速数字化转型","半导体SMH +200.8%","云计算超大规模厂商资本开支飙升"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID recovery and digital acceleration ignite super-rally","title_zh":"新冠复苏与数字化加速点燃超级反弹","turn_id":"data_center_power:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-08":{"body":"A -28.4% decline over 7.7 months as the Fed abruptly removed the word transitory in November 2021, doubled the pace of its QE taper in December, and signaled the start of its most aggressive hiking cycle since 1994 (ultimately including four consecutive 75bp moves from June 2022). TLT fell -21.3% and the dollar surged +11.8%, creating a stagflation-ish quad where Energy (+27.7%) and Utilities (+11.0%) led while Tech (-23.7%), Comm (-32.1%), and Discretionary (-32.4%) crashed. VIX rose 17 to 27 and high-beta was hammered across the board. This was a pure rate-regime de-rating of long-duration capex stories: the AI power thesis did not yet exist (ChatGPT launched November 2022), so the basket was punished as an ordinary rate-sensitive industrial with elevated valuation multiples from the COVID re-rating.","body_zh":"在7.7个月内下跌28.4%，原因是美联储于2021年11月突然删除\"暂时性\"描述，12月加倍QE缩减节奏，并开启1994年以来最激进的加息周期（2022年6月起连续四次加息75个基点）。TLT下跌21.3%，美元上涨11.8%，形成类滞胀象限，能源（+27.7%）和公用事业（+11.0%）领涨，而科技（-23.7%）、通信（-32.1%）和可选消费（-32.4%）暴跌。VIX从17升至27，高贝塔标的全面受压。这是对长久期资本开支题材的纯利率驱动估值压缩：彼时AI电力主线尚不存在（ChatGPT于2022年11月才发布），该篮子被当作估值偏高、受新冠重估的普通利率敏感工业股遭到惩罚。","drivers":["Fed taper hawkish pivot Nov 2021","rate hike cycle TLT -21.3%","dollar +11.8% stagflation-ish quad","high-beta de-rate VIX 17->27","pre-ChatGPT no AI thesis"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2021年11月鹰派缩减转向","加息周期TLT -21.3%","美元+11.8%类滞胀象限","高贝塔降估值VIX 17->27","ChatGPT发布前无AI主线"],"prev_key":"2021-11-08","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed taper hawkish pivot de-rates long-duration capex","title_zh":"美联储缩减鹰派转向压制长久期资本开支估值","turn_id":"data_center_power:peak:2021-11"},"2022-07-01":{"body":"A +318.7% gain over 22.8 months, the largest pre-2025 leg, as the AI-datacenter electricity thesis was born. ChatGPT launched November 30, 2022, triggering the AI infrastructure super-cycle: aggregate U.S. hyperscaler capex accelerated from roughly $160B in 2022 toward $400B+ by 2025 as Microsoft, Google, Amazon, and Meta raced to build AI compute. Power, transformers, switchgear, and liquid cooling emerged as the hard physical bottleneck on the buildout. Vertiv re-rated from SPAC orphan to AI-power core holding; GE Vernova spun off from GE on April 2, 2024 and immediately commanded a premium as a grid-to-rack power play. The macro backdrop was goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation with semis leading (SMH +153.6%), growth beating value +33.7 points, VIX collapsing 27->12, and narrow mega-cap breadth (equal-weight lagged -16.8%). Yields stayed elevated (TLT -16.1%) but the AI capex narrative overwhelmed the rate headwind.","body_zh":"在22.8个月内上涨318.7%，是2025年前该篮子最大的上涨腿，AI数据中心电力主线就此诞生。ChatGPT于2022年11月30日发布，引发AI基础设施超级周期：随着微软、谷歌、亚马逊和Meta竞相构建AI算力，美国超大规模厂商总资本开支从2022年约1600亿美元加速至2025年的4000亿美元以上。电力、变压器、开关设备和液冷成为AI建设的实体物理瓶颈。维谛从SPAC遗孤重估为AI电力核心持仓；GE Vernova于2024年4月2日从通用电气分拆上市，立即以电网到机架的全栈电力标的获得溢价。宏观背景为金发女郎/增长上行去通胀象限，半导体领涨（SMH +153.6%），成长跑赢价值+33.7个百分点，VIX从27崩至12，广度偏窄（等权跑输-16.8%）。收益率维持高位（TLT -16.1%），但AI资本开支叙事压倒了利率阻力。","drivers":["ChatGPT Nov 30 2022 AI super-cycle catalyst","aggregate hyperscaler capex $160B->$400B+","semis-led goldilocks SMH +153.6%","narrow mega-cap breadth -16.8%","cooling and power bottleneck re-rate"],"drivers_zh":["ChatGPT 2022年11月30日发布触发AI超级周期","超大规模厂商总资本开支1600亿->4000亿美元+","半导体领涨金发女郎SMH +153.6%","窄幅巨头主导-16.8%","散热与电力瓶颈重估"],"prev_key":"2022-07-01","prev_key_chain":["2022-07-01"],"status":"exact","title":"ChatGPT and AI super-cycle re-rate into massive melt-up","title_zh":"ChatGPT与AI超级周期引爆大规模暴涨重估","turn_id":"data_center_power:trough:2022-07"},"2024-05-24":{"body":"A -20.5% correction over 2.5 months as the Bank of Japan raised rates 15bp on July 31, triggering the largest VIX single-day spike in history on August 5 (VIX intraday near 66, closing near 39). The global yen carry trade unwind drove a slowdown/deflation-scare quad: defensives outperformed (Real Estate +11.6%, Utilities +3.3%) while Tech fell -8.1% and semis (SMH -13.4%) led the decline. Yields fell (TLT +6.0%) as recession fears temporarily dominated. As a high-beta AI-capex name with stretched valuations after the +319% prior leg, the basket overshot SPY (-1.7%), suffering a froth-clearing flush rather than a thesis break — the AI power demand story remained fully intact.","body_zh":"在2.5个月内回调20.5%，日本央行于7月31日加息15个基点，引发VIX于8月5日录得史上最大单日涨幅（盘中接近66，收盘约39）。全球日元套利交易平仓驱动放缓/通缩恐慌象限：防御股跑赢（房地产+11.6%，公用事业+3.3%），科技下跌-8.1%，半导体（SMH -13.4%）领跌。收益率下行（TLT +6.0%），衰退担忧短暂主导。作为前一腿上涨+319%后估值拉伸的高贝塔AI资本开支标的，该篮子超调SPY（-1.7%），经历泡沫清洗而非逻辑破裂——AI电力需求故事依然完全成立。","drivers":["BoJ +15bp hike July 31 carry unwind","VIX intraday ~66 Aug 5 largest daily spike ever","deflation-scare quad defensives led","semis flush SMH -13.4%","high-beta valuation froth clearing"],"drivers_zh":["日本央行7月31日加息15bp套利平仓","VIX盘中约66（8月5日）史上最大单日涨幅","通缩恐慌象限防御股领涨","半导体清洗SMH -13.4%","高贝塔估值泡沫挤出"],"prev_key":"2024-05-24","prev_key_chain":["2024-05-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Aug 2024 yen carry unwind sparks deflation-scare flush","title_zh":"2024年8月日元套利平仓引发通缩恐慌急挫","turn_id":"data_center_power:peak:2024-05"},"2024-08-07":{"body":"A +59.5% gain over 5.5 months as the post-carry-unwind panic cleared swiftly and the Fed cut rates 50bp in September 2024, its first cut since COVID, validating the soft-landing narrative. Hyperscaler Q3 2024 earnings delivered accelerating capex guidance: Microsoft guided to another Azure AI capex step-up, Google announced multi-year data-center power-purchase agreements, and Amazon raised its infrastructure build timeline. The macro backdrop was goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation with semis leading (SMH +26.9%), growth beating value +13.9 points, VIX collapsing 28->15, and narrow breadth (equal-weight lagged -5.7%). Datacenters signed nuclear and gas grid-interconnection agreements, driving forward load forecasts that directly validated the group revenue backlog.","body_zh":"在5.5个月内上涨59.5%，套利平仓恐慌迅速消散，美联储于2024年9月降息50个基点——这是新冠以来的首次降息——验证了软着陆叙事。超大规模厂商2024年第三季度业绩发布了加速的资本开支指引：微软为Azure AI指引新一轮资本开支加大，谷歌公告多年期数据中心购电协议，亚马逊提前了基础设施建设时间表。宏观背景为金发女郎/增长上行去通胀象限，半导体领涨（SMH +26.9%），成长跑赢价值+13.9个百分点，VIX从28降至15，广度偏窄（等权跑输-5.7%）。数据中心签署了核电和天然气并网协议，推高前瞻负荷预测，直接验证了该板块的营收积压。","drivers":["Fed 50bp cut Sep 2024 first since COVID","hyperscaler Q3 capex guidance acceleration","goldilocks semis-led SMH +26.9%","nuclear and gas PPA signings","narrow breadth -5.7%"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2024年9月降息50bp（新冠后首次）","超大规模厂商Q3资本开支指引加速","金发女郎半导体领涨SMH +26.9%","核电/天然气购电协议签署","窄广度-5.7%"],"prev_key":"2024-08-07","prev_key_chain":["2024-08-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed cuts and hyperscaler capex guidance spark rebound","title_zh":"美联储降息与超大规模厂商资本开支指引点燃反弹","turn_id":"data_center_power:trough:2024-08"},"2025-01-22":{"body":"A -36.8% selloff over 2.4 months: DeepSeek released R1 on January 20, 2025, claiming frontier-AI performance at a reported training cost of only ~$5.6 million versus billions for U.S. models, briefly raising fears that AI would require far less electricity than assumed. On DeepSeek Monday (January 27), Nvidia fell 17% in a single session — the largest single-day market-cap loss in history at ~$589B. AI power names amplified the move as high-beta proxies with stretched valuations. The shock deepened into the April tariff crash as Trump announced sweeping import duties; VIX tripled 15->45, semis cratered (SMH -32.3%), defensives (-2.2%) led cyclicals (-16.3%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad, and yields fell (TLT +7.2%) as recession risk dominated.","body_zh":"在2.4个月内下跌36.8%：DeepSeek于2025年1月20日发布R1，宣称以据报告仅约560万美元的训练成本达到前沿AI性能，短暂引发市场对AI或许不需要如此大量电力的担忧。在DeepSeek黑色星期一（1月27日），英伟达单日暴跌17%，创下约5890亿美元的史上最大单日市值损失。AI电力标的作为估值拉伸的高贝塔代理放大了这一跌势。冲击随后因特朗普宣布大范围进口关税而在4月关税崩盘中加深；VIX从15飙至45，半导体崩跌（SMH -32.3%），防御股（-2.2%）跑赢周期股（-16.3%），处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限，收益率下行（TLT +7.2%），衰退风险主导市场。","drivers":["DeepSeek R1 Jan 20 2025 AI efficiency shock","Nvidia -17% DeepSeek Monday $589B largest mkt-cap loss","Trump tariff crash Apr 2025","VIX 15->45","semis SMH -32.3%"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek R1 2025年1月20日AI效率冲击","英伟达DeepSeek黑色星期一-17%（5890亿美元史上最大单日市值损失）","特朗普关税崩盘2025年4月","VIX 15->45","半导体SMH -32.3%"],"prev_key":"2025-01-22","prev_key_chain":["2025-01-22"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek shock and tariff crash detonate flush","title_zh":"DeepSeek冲击与关税崩盘引爆-37%急挫","turn_id":"data_center_power:peak:2025-01"},"2025-04-04":{"body":"A +287.4% gain over 14.6 months from the April-2025 tariff low as the DeepSeek scare faded and the Jevons Paradox played out: cheaper AI inference dramatically expanded total compute demand, and hyperscaler capex re-accelerated toward $600B+ collectively in 2026. GE Vernova and Vertiv order backlogs exploded — GE Vernova backlog reached $163B with electrification orders up ~86% organically in Q1 2026 (data-center electrification orders alone exceeding all of 2025), and Vertiv backlog hit $15B with book-to-bill of 2.9x. The basket rode a once-in-a-cycle semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +271.1%, VIX collapsing 45->17), with narrow mega-cap-led breadth (equal-weight lagged -13.4%) in a reflation/growth-up quad. The group re-rated from infrastructure proxies to critical AI bottleneck names, peaking in June 2026 before rolling into the current downturn phase.","body_zh":"自2025年4月初关税低点起在14.6个月内上涨287.4%，DeepSeek惊魂消散，杰文斯悖论显现：更便宜的AI推理大幅扩大了算力总需求，超大规模厂商资本开支重新加速，2026年集体预计突破6000亿美元。GE Vernova和维谛的订单积压爆炸式增长——GE Vernova积压订单达1630亿美元，2026年Q1电气化订单有机增长约86%（仅数据中心电气化订单就超过2025年全年），维谛积压达150亿美元，订单出货比2.9倍。该篮子搭乘周期一遇的半导体领涨风险偏好暴涨（SMH +271.1%，VIX从45崩至17），广度偏窄、巨头领涨（等权跑输-13.4%），处于反通胀/增长上行象限。该板块从基础设施代理重估为关键AI瓶颈标的，于2026年6月触顶后进入当前回落阶段。","drivers":["tariff truce DeepSeek fades Jevons paradox","hyperscaler capex $600B+ 2026","semis melt-up SMH +271.1%","GEV+VRT backlog explosion","narrow breadth -13.4%"],"drivers_zh":["关税停火DeepSeek消散杰文斯悖论","超大规模厂商资本开支2026年超6000亿美元","半导体暴涨SMH +271.1%","GEV和VRT积压订单爆炸式增长","窄广度-13.4%"],"prev_key":"2025-04-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff truce moonshot in semis-led AI power re-rate","title_zh":"关税停火暴涨于半导体领涨AI电力重估","turn_id":"data_center_power:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Data-Center Power and Cooling is in a rolling-over downturn phase (pos 53.9, rs_rank 14) after an extraordinary +287% run off the April-2025 tariff trough — one of the largest legs in the basket's history. The tape is still in a reflation/growth-up quad and Tech remains the nominal leadership (Tech +24.3%, ahead of Energy +21.5% and Industrials +15.8%), but the character is shifting from narrow to broad: equal-weight is now beating cap-weight by +2.9% and value is beating growth by 15.2 points, signaling the mega-cap, semis-led engine that drove this basket is sharing the bid rather than monopolizing it. A stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%) adds a headwind to international capital-equipment contracts. The basket remains above its 200-day average and the structural AI electricity super-cycle thesis is intact (order backlogs at record highs), but the near-term setup is a pause/consolidation as the market re-examines the pace of hyperscaler AI-capex deployment after a near-vertical re-rating.","now_zh":"数据中心电力与散热处于\"见顶回落\"的下行阶段（仓位53.9，相对强度排名第14），在自2025年4月关税低点累计上涨287%后进入调整——这是该篮子历史上最大的上涨腿之一。当前仍处于反通胀/经济上行象限，科技仍是名义领涨（科技+24.3%，高于能源+21.5%和工业+15.8%），但市场性质正从窄幅转向广泛：等权现已跑赢市值权+2.9%，价值跑赢成长达15.2个百分点，意味着驱动该篮子的巨头、半导体领涨引擎正在\"分享\"而非\"垄断\"买盘。美元走强（DXY +3.4%）为该板块国际资本设备合同增添阻力。篮子仍在200日均线上方，AI电力超级周期结构性逻辑依旧成立（订单积压创历史新高），但近期走势偏向震荡/整固，市场正在重新审视超大规模厂商AI资本开支部署节奏。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-defense":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"Defense rallied steadily from the January-2014 low on a double tailwind: the December-2013 Bipartisan Budget Act (Murray-Ryan deal) restored roughly $22 billion to the defense top-line for FY2014, ending two years of sequestration-driven contract uncertainty and lifting visibility for the primes. The June-2014 ISIS advance into Iraq triggered supplemental OCO (Overseas Contingency Operations) spending and re-ignited munitions/ISR procurement bids. The macro regime was a slowdown/deflation-scare (oil -35.1%, TLT +18.1%, DXY +18.1%) that sent defensives outperforming cyclicals (+26.5% vs +13.3%), so defense caught both the budget tailwind and the defensive-rotation bid simultaneously, delivering +38.1% through mid-2015.","body_zh":"国防自 2014 年 1 月低点稳步上涨，享有双重顺风：2013 年 12 月两党预算法案（莫里-瑞安协议）为 FY2014 国防顶线恢复约 220 亿美元，终结两年因财政自动削减导致的合同不确定性，提升主承包商能见度。2014 年 6 月 ISIS 推进伊拉克触发补充 OCO 开支，重燃弹药/ISR 采购买单。宏观 regime 为放缓/通缩恐慌（油价 -35.1%、TLT +18.1%、DXY +18.1%），防御股跑赢周期（+26.5% 对 +13.3%），故国防同时承接预算顺风与防御轮动买盘，至 2015 年年中涨幅达 +38.1%。","drivers":["Bipartisan Budget Act 2013 ends sequester uncertainty","ISIS surge triggers OCO supplemental spending","Slowdown/deflation regime — defensives outperform cyclicals","Dollar surge (DXY +18.1%) headwind offset by budget clarity"],"drivers_zh":["两党预算法案 2013 终结自动减支不确定性","ISIS 攻势触发 OCO 补充开支","放缓/通缩 regime——防御股跑赢周期","美元强势（DXY +18.1%）逆风被预算明确性抵消"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Sequester relief + ISIS bid, slow-burn rally","title_zh":"自动减支解除+ISIS买盘，缓慢走高","turn_id":"defense:trough:2014-01"},"2015-06-23":{"body":"Defense peaked in late June 2015 and fell 21% into February 2016, dragged by two concurrent macro shocks: China's August-2015 yuan devaluation and the ensuing global growth scare sent VIX from 12 to 28 and oil -57%, while credit (HYG-LQD -13.8%) seized up. Concurrently, the sequestration budget-cap debate re-ignited — the Bipartisan Budget Act of 2015 (signed November 2, 2015) provided relief but months of uncertainty over the FY2016 defense top-line compressed multiples. The ctx is unambiguous: flight-to-safety dominated (defensives -0.9% vs cyclicals -17.4%), meaning defense's -21% drop was a pure macro de-risk — global growth panic hit the industrial-defense complex harder than classic defensives like Utilities and Staples.","body_zh":"国防 2015 年 6 月底见顶后下跌 21% 至 2016 年 2 月，被两个并发宏观冲击拖累：中国 2015 年 8 月人民币贬值及随之而来的全球增长恐慌使 VIX 从 12 升至 28、油价 -57%，信用（HYG-LQD -13.8%）冻结。与此同时，自动减支预算上限之争重燃——2015 年两党预算法案（11 月 2 日签署）虽提供缓解，但 FY2016 国防顶线数月不确定性压缩估值倍数。ctx 明确：避险主导（防御 -0.9% 对周期 -17.4%），意味着国防 -21% 是纯宏观去风险——全球增长恐慌对工业-国防综合体的打击重于公用事业/必需消费。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation Aug-2015, global growth panic","VIX 12→28, oil -57%, credit (HYG-LQD) -13.8%","FY2016 sequester-cap uncertainty before BBA 2015 deal","Industrial character of defense amplified selloff vs pure defensives"],"drivers_zh":["2015 年 8 月人民币贬值、全球增长恐慌","VIX 12→28、油价 -57%、信用（HYG-LQD）-13.8%","BBA 2015 之前 FY2016 自动减支上限不确定性","国防的工业属性放大跌幅，超过纯防御板块"],"prev_key":"2015-06-23","prev_key_chain":["2015-06-23"],"status":"exact","title":"China shock + sequester return scare, major selloff","title_zh":"中国冲击+自动减支回归恐慌，大幅下跌","turn_id":"defense:peak:2015-06"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"Defense bottomed in mid-February 2016 alongside the broad market and then ran an extraordinary +172.5% through September 2018, driven by two distinct phases. Phase 1 (Feb–Nov 2016): the broad reflation recovery off the oil-crash low lifted all cyclicals as oil surged +166.5% and TLT fell -6.4%. Phase 2 (Nov 2016 onward): Trump's election on November 8, 2016 was the decisive re-rating — he promised to end the Budget Control Act sequester, called for a 350-ship Navy, new planes, and more troops; defense stocks rose roughly 40% in the year following the election. The FY2018 NDAA ($700B) and the Bipartisan Budget Act of 2018 (February 2018, raising the defense cap to $629B) provided the hard budget validation. The regime backdrop was supportive throughout: reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +74.1% vs defensives +33.6%, VIX 28→13, oil +166.5%).","body_zh":"国防 2016 年 2 月中旬随大盘触底，随后录得惊人的 +172.5% 直至 2018 年 9 月，由两个截然不同的阶段驱动。第一阶段（2016 年 2 月至 11 月）：从油价崩盘低点出发的广泛再通胀复苏抬升所有周期股，油价飙升 +166.5%、TLT -6.4%。第二阶段（2016 年 11 月起）：特朗普 11 月 8 日当选是决定性的重估——他承诺终结预算控制法案自动减支、呼吁建立 350 艘舰队、新型战机与更多军队；选举后一年国防股上涨约 40%。FY2018 NDAA（7000 亿美元）与 2018 年两党预算法案（2018 年 2 月，将 FY2018 国防上限提至 6290 亿美元）提供了硬性预算验证。全程 regime 支持：再通胀/增长上行象限（周期 +74.1% 对防御 +33.6%、VIX 28→13、油价 +166.5%）。","drivers":["Trump election Nov-2016: end sequester, 350-ship Navy, higher NDAA","Reflation/growth-up regime; oil +166.5%, VIX 28→13","BBA 2018 (Feb 2018) raises defense caps to $629B FY2018","Post-oil-crash broad reflation lifts industrials alongside defense"],"drivers_zh":["2016 年 11 月特朗普当选：终结自动减支、350 艘舰队、更高 NDAA","再通胀/增长上行 regime；油价 +166.5%、VIX 28→13","2018 年 2 月两党预算法案将 FY2018 国防上限提至 6290 亿美元","后油价崩盘广泛再通胀抬升工业与国防"],"prev_key":"2016-02-11","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump election ignites multi-year defense supercycle","title_zh":"特朗普当选点燃多年国防超级周期","turn_id":"defense:trough:2016-02"},"2018-09-18":{"body":"Defense fell 28% in just 14 weeks from the September-2018 peak to the Christmas-Eve low. The primary driver was the Fed's fourth rate hike of 2018 (December 19), which after Powell's hawkish October remarks triggered a broad slowdown/deflation-scare regime (VIX 13→36, TLT +4.4%, oil -39.1%). Defense's industrial character dragged it down with cyclicals (Industrials -23.6%, Energy -26.9%) even as defensives held better (-8.7%). The secondary catalyst was policy-specific: Defense Secretary Mattis resigned December 20 over Trump's abrupt Syria withdrawal, raising uncertainty about strategic program continuity and near-term procurement priorities. Multiple compression from rate-shock combined with program-risk from the Mattis exit produced the sector's worst quarterly decline of the cycle.","body_zh":"国防自 2018 年 9 月高点至平安夜低点仅 14 周便下跌 28%。主要驱动是美联储 2018 年第四次加息（12 月 19 日），在鲍威尔 10 月鹰派表态后触发广泛放缓/通缩恐慌 regime（VIX 13→36、TLT +4.4%、油价 -39.1%）。国防的工业属性使其随周期股下跌（工业 -23.6%、能源 -26.9%），即便防御整体跌幅较小（-8.7%）。次要催化剂是政策特有的：国防部长马蒂斯 12 月 20 日因特朗普突然宣布撤军叙利亚而辞职，引发对战略项目连续性与近期采购优先级的不确定性。利率冲击导致的估值倍数压缩叠加马蒂斯离职带来的项目风险，造成板块本周期最惨烈的季度跌幅。","drivers":["Fed fourth hike Dec-19-2018, hawkish Powell — multiple compression","VIX 13→36 broad selloff; Industrials -23.6%, Energy -26.9%","Mattis resignation Dec-20-2018 — program continuity uncertainty","Oil -39.1% signals global growth slowdown, pressures capex"],"drivers_zh":["美联储 2018 年 12 月 19 日第四次加息，鲍威尔鹰派——估值倍数压缩","VIX 13→36 广泛抛售；工业 -23.6%、能源 -26.9%","马蒂斯 2018 年 12 月 20 日辞职——项目连续性不确定","油价 -39.1% 信号全球增长放缓，施压资本开支"],"prev_key":"2018-09-18","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed rate-shock bear; Mattis exit adds policy risk","title_zh":"美联储利率冲击熊市；马蒂斯离职增添政策风险","turn_id":"defense:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"Defense bottomed at the Christmas-Eve 2018 low and rallied +77% into February 2020, riding two clean tailwinds. The January-2019 Powell pivot (Fed paused hikes, then cut three times in 2019) delivered a risk-on bid as VIX fell from 36 to 14 and TLT surged +21.2% on falling real yields. Congress then signed the FY2020 NDAA in December 2019 at a record $738 billion, the largest in nominal history, validating multi-year program pipelines for F-35, hypersonics, and unmanned systems. The macro regime was tech/semis-led (semis +89.3%, growth>value +22.5%) with narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -6.5%), so defense participated as a quality cyclical-defensive hybrid rather than a market leader — delivering +77% but lagging the 89% semis and 79% tech.","body_zh":"国防 2018 年平安夜触底，随后反弹 +77% 至 2020 年 2 月，搭乘两条干净的顺风。2019 年 1 月鲍威尔转向（美联储暂停加息，2019 年三次降息）带来风险偏好买盘，VIX 从 36 降至 14，TLT 随实际收益率下行飙升 +21.2%。国会随后于 2019 年 12 月签署创纪录的 FY2020 NDAA（7380 亿美元），名义上史上最高，验证 F-35、高超音速武器与无人系统的多年项目管道。宏观 regime 为科技/半导体引领（半导体 +89.3%、成长>价值 +22.5%），市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY -6.5%），故国防作为优质周期-防御混合体参与上涨而非领头——涨幅 +77%，落后于半导体 89% 与科技 79%。","drivers":["Jan-2019 Fed pivot + three 2019 rate cuts, VIX 36→14","FY2020 NDAA $738B record signed Dec-2019","Tech/semis-led risk-on regime (semis +89.3%, growth>value +22.5%)","TLT +21.2% falling real yields boost long-duration procurement valuations"],"drivers_zh":["2019 年 1 月美联储转向 + 2019 年三次降息，VIX 36→14","2019 年 12 月签署创纪录 FY2020 NDAA 7380 亿美元","科技/半导体引领风险偏好 regime（半导体 +89.3%、成长>价值 +22.5%）","TLT +21.2% 实际收益率下行提振长久期采购估值"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot + record FY2020 NDAA drives +77% run","title_zh":"美联储转向+创纪录FY2020 NDAA推动+77%","turn_id":"defense:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-12":{"body":"Defense fell 42.6% in just 39 days alongside the entire market in the COVID-19 pandemic panic (Feb 12–Mar 23, 2020), the fastest bear market in history. This was pure forced liquidation and risk-off deleveraging (VIX 14→62, TLT +16.0%), not a defense-specific event. Defense's ITA composition — heavy Boeing weighting, with BA falling >50% as commercial aviation collapsed — compounded the sector drawdown beyond what pure defense primes like LMT and NOC experienced. The Pentagon's accelerated progress payments under the CARES Act provided a floor but could not prevent the panic drawdown. Defensives held better than cyclicals (-28.8% vs -40.3%) but defense's industrial adjacency kept it in line with the Industrials sector's -42.3%.","body_zh":"国防随整个市场在新冠肺炎恐慌中仅 39 天便下跌 42.6%（2020 年 2 月 12 日至 3 月 23 日），史上最快熊市。这是纯粹的强制平仓与风险规避去杠杆（VIX 14→62、TLT +16.0%），并非国防特有事件。国防 ITA 构成中波音权重较高，BA 随商业航空崩溃下跌逾 50%，使板块跌幅超过 LMT、NOC 等纯国防主承包商。五角大楼依据 CARES 法案加快进度付款提供支撑，但无法阻止恐慌性下跌。防御整体优于周期（-28.8% 对 -40.3%），但国防的工业相邻性使其与工业板块 -42.3% 同步。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic shock, VIX 14→62, forced global liquidation","Boeing (BA) commercial aviation collapse amplifies ITA basket drawdown","Industrials -42.3% — defense dragged as industrial-adjacent name","CARES Act accelerated payments = floor; but $2T fiscal shock first"],"drivers_zh":["新冠肺炎冲击，VIX 14→62，全球强制平仓","波音（BA）商业航空崩溃放大 ITA 篮子跌幅","工业 -42.3%——国防作为工业相邻板块被拖累","CARES 法案加快付款=底部支撑；但 2 万亿财政冲击先至"],"prev_key":"2020-02-12","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-12"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID panic liquidation — defense caught in the rout","title_zh":"新冠恐慌清算——国防卷入暴跌","turn_id":"defense:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"Defense snapped back +61% in just 77 days off the March-23 COVID low into early June, carried by the broadest, most explosive re-risk rally in modern history: CARES Act ($2T, signed March 27), Fed unlimited QE, VIX collapsing 62→26, and cyclicals surging (Energy +98.8%, Industrials +56.4%, RSP-SPY +12.8%). Defense's industrial character — which amplified the COVID selloff — now amplified the recovery: Boeing staged its largest weekly gains as travel-reopening trades bid; Pentagon CARES progress payments de-risked the supply chain. The macro regime shifted decisively to reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +60% vs defensives +34.9%, oil +63.5%), and breadth was wide (+12.8%) — a genuine risk-on rip rather than a narrow melt-up.","body_zh":"国防自 3 月 23 日新冠低点仅 77 天便弹升 +61% 至 6 月初，被现代史上最广泛、最猛烈的风险回归行情带动：CARES 法案（2 万亿美元，3 月 27 日签署）、美联储无限量 QE、VIX 从 62 骤降至 26、周期股飙升（能源 +98.8%、工业 +56.4%、RSP-SPY +12.8%）。国防的工业属性——放大了新冠跌幅——如今同样放大复苏：波音随旅行重开交易热炒录得史上最大单周涨幅；五角大楼 CARES 进度付款为供应链去风险。宏观 regime 决定性转向再通胀/增长上行（周期 +60% 对防御 +34.9%、油价 +63.5%），市场广度宽（+12.8%）——真实的风险偏好急涨，而非狭窄融涨。","drivers":["CARES Act $2T + Fed unlimited QE removes tail risk, VIX 62→26","Broad reflation cyclical rip: Energy +98.8%, Industrials +56.4%","Boeing snap-back on travel-reopening trade boosts ITA basket","Wide market breadth (RSP-SPY +12.8%) — all ships lifted"],"drivers_zh":["CARES 法案 2 万亿 + 美联储无限量 QE 消除尾部风险，VIX 62→26","广泛再通胀周期急涨：能源 +98.8%、工业 +56.4%","波音随旅行重开交易弹回，提振 ITA 篮子","宽幅市场广度（RSP-SPY +12.8%）——百船争流"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Fiscal bazooka + reopening cyclical rip (+61%)","title_zh":"财政基地炮+重开周期急涨（+61%）","turn_id":"defense:trough:2020-03"},"2020-06-08":{"body":"Defense corrected -16.3% from June 8 to July 9, 2020, as the market rotated sharply from the reflation-recovery trade into a narrow tech/growth melt-up (Tech +6.4%, semis +5.5%, SPY -2.3%). Defensives lagged cyclicals in the selloff (-4.6% vs -8.4%), but defense's industrial character — and Boeing's ongoing 737-MAX supply-chain problems — meant it underperformed even the defensive average. The regime flipped to a slowdown/deflation-scare (TLT +6.8%, VIX 26→29) as second-wave COVID fears re-emerged in the Sun Belt, halting the cyclical re-opening bid. Defense had no sector-specific catalyst: it was collateral damage in a macro-regime reversal.","body_zh":"国防 2020 年 6 月 8 日至 7 月 9 日回调 -16.3%，因市场从再通胀复苏交易急剧轮动至狭窄的科技/成长融涨（科技 +6.4%、半导体 +5.5%、SPY -2.3%）。本次下跌中防御落后周期（-4.6% 对 -8.4%），但国防的工业属性——加上波音持续的 737-MAX 供应链问题——使其甚至跑输防御均值。随着阳光地带第二波新冠恐慌重燃，regime 翻转为放缓/通缩恐慌（TLT +6.8%、VIX 26→29），阻断周期重开买盘。国防无板块特有催化剂：是宏观 regime 逆转的附带损害。","drivers":["Market rotates into narrow tech/growth, away from cyclical-recovery trade","Second-wave COVID fears (Sun Belt), VIX 26→29, TLT +6.8%","Boeing 737-MAX supply-chain drag on ITA basket","Defense lacked sector-specific bid to resist macro headwind"],"drivers_zh":["市场轮动至狭窄科技/成长，远离周期复苏交易","阳光地带第二波新冠恐慌，VIX 26→29、TLT +6.8%","波音 737-MAX 供应链拖累 ITA 篮子","国防缺乏板块特有买盘来抵抗宏观逆风"],"prev_key":"2020-06-08","prev_key_chain":["2020-06-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tech-rotation pullback leaves defense behind","title_zh":"科技轮动回调，国防落在身后","turn_id":"defense:peak:2020-06"},"2020-07-09":{"body":"Defense climbed off the July-2020 low into a broad reflation/growth-up regime (SPY +47.6%, cyclicals +73% vs defensives +35.5%, breadth wide RSP-SPY +14%) that lifted the whole risk complex even as yields surged (TLT -21.1%). FY2021 and FY2022 NDAAs ($740B and $778B) provided the budget floor. The February-2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine then turned a cyclical recovery into a hard geopolitical re-rating — LMT, RTX, and NOC bid sharply as Europe woke to a multi-decade rearmament cycle. The leg topped in March 2022 at the invasion's emotional peak, just as the high-beta regime (high-beta minus low-vol +67.5%) began to crack under the Fed's first hike (March 16, 2022).","body_zh":"国防自 2020 年 7 月低点爬升，进入广泛的再通胀/增长上行 regime（SPY +47.6%、周期股 +73% 对防御 +35.5%、市场广度宽 RSP-SPY +14%），即便收益率飙升（TLT -21.1%）也抬升了整个风险资产群。FY2021 与 FY2022 NDAA（7400 亿与 7780 亿美元）提供预算底部。2022 年 2 月俄罗斯入侵乌克兰把周期复苏变成强烈的地缘重估——随着欧洲意识到数十年重整军备周期，LMT、RTX、NOC 获强劲买盘。该腿段于 2022 年 3 月在入侵情绪高峰见顶，恰逢美联储首次加息（2022 年 3 月 16 日）使高贝塔 regime（高贝塔-低波动 +67.5%）开始破裂。","drivers":["Broad reflation/growth-up melt-up (cyclicals +73%, breadth wide) amplifies rally","Russia-Ukraine invasion Feb-2022 ignites European rearmament re-rate","FY2021/22 NDAA $740B/$778B — multi-year budget floor","Yields surged (TLT -21.1%) but risk-on dominated until Mar-2022 Fed hike"],"drivers_zh":["广泛再通胀/增长上行融涨（周期股 +73%、市场广度宽）放大涨幅","2022 年 2 月俄乌战争点燃欧洲重整军备重估","FY2021/22 NDAA 7400/7780 亿美元——多年预算底部","收益率飙升（TLT -21.1%）但风险偏好主导至 2022 年 3 月美联储加息"],"prev_key":"2020-07-09","prev_key_chain":["2020-07-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-COVID grind into the Ukraine bid, reflation +70%","title_zh":"新冠后缓步走高迎俄乌买盘，再通胀+70%","turn_id":"defense:trough:2020-07"},"2022-03-25":{"body":"Even a war bid could not resist the 2022 Fed hiking bear: a rate-driven slowdown/deflation-scare regime (yields surged, TLT -12.7%; DXY +4.9%; VIX 21→33) compressed every multiple into the June low. Defensives outperformed cyclicals (-10% vs -17.5%) in a flight-to-safety, but defense de-rated with the cyclical-industrial crowd. The de-rate was pure macro — order books were swelling (LMT backlog at record ~$135B) even as the strong dollar and surging yields hit the primes. The Fed's rapid pace of hikes (50bps in May, then 75bps in June 2022) was the kill switch.","body_zh":"即便有战争买盘也难抵 2022 年美联储加息熊市：一个利率驱动的放缓/通缩恐慌 regime（收益率飙升，TLT -12.7%；DXY +4.9%；VIX 21→33）把每个倍数压缩至 6 月低点。避险中防御跑赢周期（-10% 对 -17.5%），但国防随周期工业股去估值。这是纯宏观去估值——即便强势美元与飙升收益率冲击主承包商，LMT 订单积压仍创纪录约 1350 亿美元。美联储快速加息节奏（2022 年 5 月 50bp、6 月 75bp）是关闭门开关。","drivers":["Fed hike cycle accelerates (50bps May, 75bps June 2022) — multiple compression","Risk-off slowdown scare (VIX 21→33), flight-to-safety rotation","Strong dollar (DXY +4.9%) pressures multinational exporters","Profit-taking after invasion-week spike, despite record LMT/RTX backlogs"],"drivers_zh":["美联储加息周期加速（2022 年 5 月 50bp、6 月 75bp）——估值倍数压缩","避险放缓恐慌（VIX 21→33）、避险轮动","强势美元（DXY +4.9%）施压跨国出口商","入侵当周急升后的获利了结，尽管 LMT/RTX 订单积压创纪录"],"prev_key":"2022-03-25","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Hiking-bear, rate-driven pullback off the war spike (-21%)","title_zh":"加息熊市利率驱动从战争尖峰回落（-21%）","turn_id":"defense:peak:2022-03"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"Defense rode the broad mid-2022 relief rally as a tech/semis-led risk-on regime took hold (SMH +19.5%, growth>value +8.8, VIX 33→20) on hopes of a Fed pivot that never came. A fast, multiple-driven bounce off oversold conditions — defense participated but lagged the high-beta growth that leads these windows, with a still-strong dollar (DXY +2.8%) a mild drag on the exporters. Strong order backlogs (Ukraine resupply contracts accelerating through summer 2022) provided sector-specific support but were insufficient to drive outperformance in a risk-on tape that rewarded growth and tech.","body_zh":"国防搭上 2022 年年中大盘纾困反弹，一个科技/半导体引领的风险偏好 regime（半导体 +19.5%、成长>价值 +8.8、VIX 33→20）因美联储暂停预期（最终未现）而成形。这是从超卖出发、估值倍数驱动的快速反弹——国防参与但落后于领涨这类窗口的高贝塔成长，强势美元（DXY +2.8%）对出口商仍有轻微拖累。乌克兰补给合同加速（2022 年夏）提供板块特有支撑，但在奖励成长与科技的风险偏好行情中不足以推动跑赢。","drivers":["Tech/semis-led risk-on bounce (SMH +19.5%, growth>value), VIX 33→20","Premature 'Fed pivot' hopes lift the whole complex","Ukraine resupply contract acceleration provides order-backlog floor","Dollar (DXY +2.8%) still a headwind for multinational primes"],"drivers_zh":["科技/半导体引领风险偏好反弹（半导体 +19.5%、成长>价值），VIX 33→20","过早的'美联储转向'预期抬升整个群组","乌克兰补给合同加速提供订单积压底部","美元（DXY +2.8%）对跨国主承包商仍为逆风"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Summer relief bounce, Fed-pause hopes (+23%)","title_zh":"夏季纾困反弹，美联储暂停预期（+23%）","turn_id":"defense:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole speech (August 26, 2022) killed the summer rally and triggered a rate-driven slowdown regime (TLT -11.4%; DXY +5.3%; VIX 20→32) into the September-30 capitulation low. Defense fell with everything — semis -24%, cyclicals -15.3% — a macro de-risk rather than a defense-specific problem. The dollar spike (DXY +5.3% — its fastest move of 2022) added pressure on the multinational primes. Defense had no offsetting sector catalyst: Ukraine resupply orders were already priced in, and the hawkish terminal-rate repricing hit every multiple.","body_zh":"鲍威尔 2022 年 8 月 26 日杰克逊霍尔鹰派演讲终结夏季反弹，触发利率驱动的放缓 regime（TLT -11.4%；DXY +5.3%；VIX 20→32），跌至 9 月 30 日投降低点。国防随一切下跌——半导体 -24%、周期股 -15.3%——这是宏观去风险而非国防特有问题。美元飙升（DXY +5.3%——2022 年最快单段走势）对跨国主承包商再添压力。国防无抵消性板块催化剂：乌克兰补给订单已在价格中，鹰派终端利率重新定价冲击每一个估值倍数。","drivers":["Powell Jackson Hole Aug-26-2022 hawkish shock — terminal rate re-priced","Rate-regime surge (TLT -11.4%); broad risk-off (VIX 20→32, semis -24%)","Dollar surge (DXY +5.3%) amplifies pressure on exporters","Ukraine resupply orders already in the price; no new offsetting catalyst"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔 2022 年 8 月 26 日杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击——终端利率重新定价","利率 regime 飙升（TLT -11.4%）；广泛避险（VIX 20→32、半导体 -24%）","美元飙升（DXY +5.3%）放大对出口商的压力","乌克兰补给订单已在价格中；无新抵消性催化剂"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkish shock, rate-driven flush (-19%)","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击，利率驱动冲刷（-19%）","turn_id":"defense:peak:2022-08"},"2022-09-30":{"body":"From the autumn-2022 low, defense ran its best stretch of the cycle — +149.7% over 28 months — and the regime amplified it: a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation melt-up (SMH +189.7%, growth>value +48.4, VIX 32→15, weaker dollar -3.6%) lifted the whole risk complex. Defense carried its own dual fuel: Ukraine resupply orders and the October-2023 Hamas/Mideast escalation drove demand for precision munitions (Raytheon Patriot, GD Stryker), while NATO members ratcheted toward and beyond 2% of GDP. The FY2024 NDAA at $886B and FY2025 at $895B were the budget anchors. The tape was narrow and mega-cap-led (RSP-SPY -25.9%), so defense leaned on its geopolitical premium — not beta — to reach the January-2025 peak.","body_zh":"从 2022 年秋季低点起国防连涨本周期最强一段——28 个月 +149.7%——而 regime 放大了它：一个 goldilocks/增长上行去通胀融涨（半导体 +189.7%、成长>价值 +48.4、VIX 32→15、美元走弱 -3.6%）抬升整个风险资产群。国防携带自身双重燃料：乌克兰补给订单与 2023 年 10 月哈马斯/中东升级推动精确弹药需求（雷神爱国者、通用动力斯特赖克），同时北约成员国预算迈向并超过 GDP 2%。FY2024 NDAA 8860 亿美元与 FY2025 8950 亿美元是预算锚点。市场狭窄、大盘股引领（RSP-SPY -25.9%），故国防靠地缘溢价而非贝塔保持步调至 2025 年 1 月高点。","drivers":["Goldilocks AI melt-up (SMH +189.7%, growth>value +48.4, VIX 32→15)","Ukraine resupply + Oct-2023 Mideast escalation — dual conflict premium","NATO 2% GDP target momentum; FY2024/25 NDAA at $886B/$895B","Weaker dollar (DXY -3.6%) tailwind for multinational exporters"],"drivers_zh":["Goldilocks AI 融涨（半导体 +189.7%、成长>价值 +48.4、VIX 32→15）","乌克兰补给 + 2023 年 10 月中东升级——双重冲突溢价","北约 GDP 2% 目标动能；FY2024/25 NDAA 8860/8950 亿美元","美元走弱（DXY -3.6%）对跨国出口商顺风"],"prev_key":"2022-09-30","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-30"],"status":"exact","title":"War-and-budget bull inside a goldilocks AI melt-up (+150%)","title_zh":"漫长战争与预算牛市，置于goldilocks AI融涨（+150%）","turn_id":"defense:trough:2022-09"},"2025-01-21":{"body":"Policy flipped the script just as the regime turned violently risk-off: a slowdown/deflation-scare flush (VIX 15→45, SMH -31.1%, SPHB-SPLV -25.4%) hit high-beta hardest, with the DeepSeek AI shock (January 27) and April-tariff escalation fears compounding the macro selloff. Defense sustained additional sector-specific damage — Hegseth's Pentagon efficiency drive targeted roughly 8%/yr budget reprioritization with threats to legacy programs (F-35 quantities, armored vehicles) that LMT, GD, and BAE depend on. Even as defensives outperformed cyclicals (-3.1% vs -16.5%) in relative terms, the 'Trump = more defense' assumption broke in absolute terms. The dollar fell (DXY -4.7%) which mattered less than the program-cut narrative.","body_zh":"政策扭转剧本，恰逢 regime 剧烈转向避险：一次放缓/通缩恐慌冲刷（VIX 15→45、半导体 -31.1%、SPHB-SPLV -25.4%）对高贝塔打击最重，DeepSeek AI 冲击（1 月 27 日）与 4 月关税升级恐慌加剧宏观抛售。国防承受额外的板块特有损伤——赫格塞斯五角大楼效率行动以约每年 8% 预算重新排序为目标，威胁 LMT、GD 与 BAE 赖以为生的传统项目（F-35 数量、装甲车）。即便防御相对跑赢周期（-3.1% 对 -16.5%），'特朗普=更多国防'的假设在绝对值层面已破裂。美元下跌（DXY -4.7%）的影响远不及项目削减叙事。","drivers":["Risk-off flush (VIX 15→45, high-beta SPHB-SPLV -25.4%) — macro cascade","DOGE / Hegseth Pentagon efficiency drive ~8%/yr budget reprioritization","DeepSeek AI shock Jan-27-2025 + April-tariff fears compound selloff","Threats to legacy F-35 / armored vehicle programs hit sector-specifically"],"drivers_zh":["避险冲刷（VIX 15→45、高贝塔 SPHB-SPLV -25.4%）——宏观级联","DOGE/赫格塞斯五角大楼效率行动约每年 8% 预算重新排序","DeepSeek AI 冲击 2025 年 1 月 27 日 + 4 月关税恐慌叠加","威胁传统 F-35/装甲车项目，板块特有打击"],"prev_key":"2025-01-21","prev_key_chain":["2025-01-21"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump-trade unwind + DOGE-cut fears, risk-off flush (-15%)","title_zh":"特朗普交易平仓与DOGE削减恐慌，避险冲刷（-15%）","turn_id":"defense:peak:2025-01"},"2025-04-04":{"body":"Defense bottomed with the whole market at the April-4 to April-8 reciprocal-tariff crash and staged its sharpest run of the cycle (+111%), amplified by an explosive high-beta risk-on regime (VIX 45→16, SMH +122.1%, SPHB-SPLV +74.9%, weaker dollar -3.5%). The re-escalating geopolitical backdrop (Ukraine peace talks stalling, Iran-Hormuz tensions, European rearmament accelerating), a reassessment of worst-case DOGE budget cuts, and the US-China tariff truce (May 12, 2025) all converged into a hard re-bid. The snap-back from deeply oversold conditions (+111% vs SPY +38.1%) demonstrates defense's leverage at cycle turns: policy risk had been overpriced at the trough.","body_zh":"国防随整个市场在 4 月 4 日至 8 日对等关税崩盘触底，随后上演本周期最陡一段（+111%），被爆发性的高贝塔风险偏好 regime（VIX 45→16、半导体 +122.1%、SPHB-SPLV +74.9%、美元走弱 -3.5%）放大。地缘背景再升级（乌克兰和谈受阻、伊朗-霍尔木兹紧张、欧洲重整军备加速）、对最坏情形 DOGE 预算削减的重新评估，以及美中关税休战（2025 年 5 月 12 日）合力聚焦强劲再买入。从深度超卖弹回（+111% 对 SPY +38.1%）展现国防在周期转折点的杠杆：政策风险在低谷被过度定价。","drivers":["Explosive high-beta risk-on regime (VIX 45→16, SPHB-SPLV +74.9%, SMH +122.1%)","US-China tariff truce May-12-2025 removes tail risk","Allied rearmament + Iran/Hormuz escalation re-bid on defense demand","Weaker dollar (DXY -3.5%); DOGE worst-case reassessment"],"drivers_zh":["爆发性高贝塔风险偏好 regime（VIX 45→16、SPHB-SPLV +74.9%、半导体 +122.1%）","2025 年 5 月 12 日美中关税休战消除尾部风险","盟友重整军备 + 伊朗/霍尔木兹升级再买入国防需求","美元走弱（DXY -3.5%）；DOGE 最坏情形重新评估"],"prev_key":"2025-04-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-crash low snap-back in high-beta rip (+111%)","title_zh":"关税崩盘低点弹回，高贝塔暴涨（+111%）","turn_id":"defense:trough:2025-04"},"2026-01-16":{"body":"The January-2026 high faded into a stagflation-ish regime (VIX 16→31, oil +73.1% on Hormuz supply shock, Energy the lone leader +30.8%, SPY -8.4%). Even though oil spikes historically carry a geopolitical-premium bid for defense, the budget rationalization narrative re-asserted: Hegseth's Pentagon continued to signal program reprioritization, and the parabolic +111% prior leg invited profit-taking. A firming dollar (DXY +1.1%) added a structural headwind for the multinational exporters. Unlike past selloffs driven purely by macro de-risk, this one was driven by the intersection of budget uncertainty and a regime that rewards energy and real assets — not the steady, long-duration contract primes.","body_zh":"随预算现实重新主导，2026 年 1 月高点回落，进入类滞胀 regime（VIX 16→31、油价 +73.1% 因霍尔木兹供应冲击、能源是唯一领头 +30.8%、SPY -8.4%）。尽管油价飙升历史上伴随国防地缘溢价买盘，预算合理化叙事再度主导：赫格塞斯五角大楼持续信号项目重新排序，而抛物线 +111% 前腿邀请获利了结。美元转强（DXY +1.1%）为跨国出口商增添结构性逆风。与过去纯宏观去风险驱动的下跌不同，此次由预算不确定性与奖励能源和实物资产（而非稳定长久期合同主承包商）的 regime 交叉驱动。","drivers":["Stagflation-ish regime (oil +73.1% Hormuz shock, VIX 16→31) caps risk appetite","Budget rationalization / Hegseth repricing of program priorities","Profit-taking after parabolic +111% prior leg","Dollar firming (DXY +1.1%) headwind for exporting primes"],"drivers_zh":["类滞胀 regime（油价 +73.1% 霍尔木兹冲击、VIX 16→31）压制风险偏好","预算合理化/赫格塞斯对项目优先级的重新定价","抛物线 +111% 前腿后的获利了结","美元转强（DXY +1.1%）对出口主承包商逆风"],"prev_key":"2026-01-16","prev_key_chain":["2026-01-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Top rolls on budget reality in stagflation-ish tape (-18%)","title_zh":"见顶后因预算现实回落，置于类滞胀行情（-18%）","turn_id":"defense:peak:2026-01"},"2026-03-30":{"body":"A shallow recovery off the March-2026 low into a renewed tech/semis-led risk-on regime (SMH +65.5%, growth>value +10.3, VIX 31→16) — but defense lacks relative-strength leadership to confirm a new uptrend and still ranks #42, its chronic problem in a narrow, mega-cap-led tape (RSP-SPY -8.8%). The June-2026 Iran/Hormuz flare and US military operations raised defense demand headlines, but in a market rewarding AI beta the group needs hard order-flow confirmation (supplemental appropriation, NATO contract award) to re-rate. Positive signal: BUY tagged at pos 9.0 near cycle floor, suggesting asymmetric risk/reward to the upside if the macro regime broadens.","body_zh":"从 2026 年 3 月低点出发的浅幅回升，进入重燃的科技/半导体引领风险偏好 regime（半导体 +65.5%、成长>价值 +10.3、VIX 31→16）——但国防缺乏相对强度领导力确认新上升趋势，仍排第 42 位，这是它在狭窄、大盘股引领行情（RSP-SPY -8.8%）中的痼疾。2026 年 6 月伊朗/霍尔木兹突发与美军行动提升国防需求头条，但在奖励 AI 贝塔的市场里，板块重估需要硬性订单流确认（补充拨款、北约合同授予）。正面信号：BUY 标记于位置 9.0 接近周期底部，若宏观 regime 走阔，风险/回报向上不对称。","drivers":["Narrow tech/semis-led risk-on tape (SMH +65.5%, RSP-SPY -8.8%) leaves defense behind","Oversold bounce off March-2026 low; BUY signal at cycle floor (pos 9.0)","June-2026 Iran/Hormuz flare + US military action keeps demand topical","Awaiting supplemental appropriation or NATO contract to confirm re-rate"],"drivers_zh":["狭窄科技/半导体引领风险偏好行情（半导体 +65.5%、RSP-SPY -8.8%）把国防甩在身后","从 2026 年 3 月低点超卖反弹；BUY 信号于周期底部（位置 9.0）","2026 年 6 月伊朗/霍尔木兹突发 + 美军行动使需求保持热度","等待补充拨款或北约合同以确认重估"],"prev_key":"2026-03-30","prev_key_chain":["2026-03-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Tentative bounce, lagging narrow risk-on tape (+16%)","title_zh":"试探性反弹，落后于狭窄风险偏好行情（+16%）","turn_id":"defense:trough:2026-03"}},"now":"Defense & Aerospace sits in a \"value coiled spring\" bottoming posture (pos 9.0, RS rank #42, tagged Bottoming, below its 200-day) even as the macro backdrop — reflation/growth-up quad, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%, DXY +3.4% — rewards cyclicals (+11.2%) far more than defensives (+6.9%). The current melt-up since late March 2026 is narrow and tech/semis-led (SMH +67.9%, growth-value gap -15.2%, RSP-SPY +2.9%), which historically pulls flows toward AI-beta and away from the steady-yield primes. A stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%) is an incremental headwind for the multinational exporters (RTX, LMT, GD). The basket carries BUY signal, but confirmation requires either an order-flow catalyst (large supplemental appropriation, NATO procurement award) or a regime rotation into value and broad cyclicals — neither of which is yet present in a tape still dominated by semiconductor momentum.","now_zh":"国防与航空航天处于\"价值弹簧蓄势\"筑底状态（位置 9.0、相对强度排名第 42、标记为底部整理、低于 200 日均线），即便宏观背景——再通胀/增长上行象限、油价 +19.2%、铜金比 +18.3%、DXY +3.4%——奖励周期股（+11.2%）远多于防御（+6.9%）。2026 年 3 月底以来的融涨行情狭窄且由科技/半导体主导（SMH +67.9%、成长-价值差 -15.2%、RSP-SPY +2.9%），历史上这会把资金拉向 AI 贝塔，而非稳定收益的主承包商。强势美元（DXY +3.4%）对跨国出口商（RTX、LMT、GD）构成额外逆风。篮子携带 BUY 信号，但确认需要订单流催化剂（大型补充拨款、北约采购合同）或市场向价值和广泛周期股的 regime 轮动——在半导体动能依然主导的行情中，两者均尚未出现。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-defensives":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"From January 2014 to January 2018 defensives climbed 62.6%, broadly tracking SPY's 68.7% in a sustained goldilocks/disinflation quad where long yields fell sharply (TLT +33.2%). With the Fed pinned near zero until its first hike in December 2015 and then executing a gradual series of 25bp hikes through December 2017, income-starved investors persistently bid up high-dividend defensive proxies in a relentless yield-search amid ZIRP. Falling oil (WTI -30.2%) suppressed energy-cost input pressures, expanding staples margins, while the narrow, mega-cap-led tape (RSP lagged SPY by -8.0%) kept the typical growth-versus-defensives rotation muted. The result was a steady, low-volatility grind rather than a blockbuster leg; defensives kept approximate pace with cyclicals (61.1% vs 63.3%) only because ZIRP made their dividend yield competitively attractive versus bonds.","body_zh":"2014年1月至2018年1月，防御板块上涨62.6%，在持续的金发姑娘/去通胀象限中大致跟随SPY的68.7%，长端收益率大幅下行（TLT+33.2%）。美联储将利率锁定在近零水平直至2015年12月首次加息，此后到2017年12月仅以渐进节奏累计加息若干次25bp，收入匮乏的投资者持续追捧高股息防御代理品，在零利率大环境下形成持续的猎息行情。油价下跌（WTI-30.2%）压低了原材料成本，扩大了必需品利润率，而窄幅、大市值主导的市场（等权RSP跑输SPY-8.0%）令典型的成长-防御轮动趋于温和。最终呈现稳定的低波动爬升而非爆发性行情；防御股能与周期股并驾齐驱（61.1% vs 63.3%），仅因ZIRP环境使其股息收益率在与债券比较时具备竞争力。","drivers":["ZIRP dividend-yield search","falling long-end yields TLT+33%","oil collapse cuts staples input costs","goldilocks/disinflation quad","mega-cap narrow breadth dampens rotation"],"drivers_zh":["零利率猎息","长端收益率下行TLT+33%","油价暴跌压低必需品成本","金发姑娘/去通胀象限","大市值窄幅行情抑制轮动"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"ZIRP yield-hunt carries defensives higher","title_zh":"零利率猎息行情托举防御板块","turn_id":"defensives:trough:2014-01"},"2018-01-29":{"body":"The January 26, 2018 S&P 500 peak and subsequent -14.3% defensive selloff into May 2018 was triggered by the January BLS jobs report (released February 2), which showed average hourly earnings rising 2.9% year-on-year — fastest since 2009 — alongside a robust 200,000 payrolls print. The 10-year Treasury yield spiked from roughly 2.4% to a multi-year high near 2.85%, detonating the short-volatility complex on February 5 (Volmageddon: VIX surged from 18 to over 37 intraday, XIV/SVXY lost over 90%). Consumer staples (Staples -15.7%, worst in the tape) bore the brunt because the rate shock re-priced their bond-proxy valuations; utilities held somewhat better (+2.7%) as investors rotated briefly into the lowest-beta leg. The basket fell -14.3% while SPY fell -7.2% — defensives underperformed because their elevated P/Es priced for low-rate perpetuity were most exposed to the sudden yield normalization.","body_zh":"2018年1月26日标普500见顶，防御板块随后下跌14.3%直至2018年5月，导火索是2月2日公布的1月非农数据：时薪同比上涨2.9%（2009年以来最快），新增就业20万，超出预期。10年期美债收益率从约2.4%飙升至多年高位约2.85%，于2月5日引爆空波动率头寸（Volmageddon：VIX盘中从18跳升至37以上，XIV/SVXY跌逾90%）。必需消费品成为重灾区（必需品-15.7%，全市场最差），因为利率冲击重新定价了其债券代理估值；公用事业因贝塔最低而相对占优（+2.7%）。篮子下跌14.3%，而SPY仅跌7.2%——防御股跑输，正是因为其以永久低利率定价的高市盈率在收益率突然正常化时最为脆弱。","drivers":["Jan 2018 wage-inflation shock 2.9% YoY","10y yield spike toward 2.85%","Volmageddon VIX surge Feb 5 2018","bond-proxy valuation re-pricing","staples high-P/E most rate-exposed"],"drivers_zh":["2018年1月工资通胀冲击同比2.9%","10年期收益率飙升至约2.85%","2018年2月5日Volmageddon事件","债券代理估值重新定价","高市盈率必需品最受利率冲击"],"prev_key":"2018-01-29","prev_key_chain":["2018-01-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Wage-inflation shock ends the low-vol era","title_zh":"工资通胀冲击终结低波动时代","turn_id":"defensives:peak:2018-01"},"2018-05-02":{"body":"From May 2018 to February 2020, defensives rallied 51.6%, outperforming SPY (+31.0%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad where the yield curve inverted and the Fed ultimately reversed course. Three inflection points drove the leg: first, the Q4 2018 crash (SPY roughly -20% peak-to-trough) as the Fed raised rates into a manufacturing slowdown and the US-China trade war escalated under Section 232/301 tariffs; second, Powell's January 4, 2019 pivot speech ('patient on rates') and three subsequent insurance cuts (July, September, October 2019) that drove the 10-year from 3.2% to roughly 1.5%, sending TLT up +30.7% over the full leg; third, ongoing trade war anxiety sustained defensive positioning as business investment weakened and manufacturing PMIs contracted. Defensives (+38.6% avg) beat cyclicals (+18.8%) decisively as falling yields made dividend proxies attractive and recession fears kept risk appetite suppressed.","body_zh":"2018年5月至2020年2月，防御板块上涨51.6%，在放缓/通缩恐慌象限中跑赢SPY（+31.0%），期间收益率曲线倒挂，美联储最终转向。三个拐点驱动了这一行情：其一，2018年四季度崩盘（SPY峰谷跌约20%），美联储在制造业放缓、中美贸易战（232/301条款关税）升级之际仍继续加息；其二，鲍威尔2019年1月4日转向讲话（对利率保持耐心）及随后三次保险性降息（7月、9月、10月），10年期收益率从3.2%跌至约1.5%，推动TLT整段上涨+30.7%；其三，持续的贸易战焦虑维系了防御性仓位，企业投资走弱、制造业PMI收缩。防御股均值（+38.6%）大幅跑赢周期股（+18.8%），收益率下行令股息代理品重具吸引力，而衰退恐慌则压制了风险偏好。","drivers":["Dec 2018 rate-hike crash catalyst","Powell Jan 2019 Fed pivot speech","three Fed insurance cuts 2019","US-China trade war tariffs","yield-curve inversion deflation-scare"],"drivers_zh":["2018年四季度加息引发崩盘","鲍威尔2019年1月转向讲话","2019年三次保险性降息","中美贸易战关税","收益率曲线倒挂通缩恐慌"],"prev_key":"2018-05-02","prev_key_chain":["2018-05-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot + trade war fear lifts defensives","title_zh":"美联储转向与贸易战恐慌推升防御板块","turn_id":"defensives:trough:2018-05"},"2020-02-21":{"body":"The February 21 to March 23, 2020 crash saw the basket fall -21.8% (broader defensive sectors -29.1% on average) — painful in absolute terms, but significant outperformance versus SPY's -32.8% and cyclicals' -39.4% as VIX exploded from 17 to 62. COVID-19 was declared a pandemic by the WHO on March 11; Italy entered national lockdown March 9; NYSE circuit-breakers triggered on March 9, 12, and 16. Staples companies like P&G and Clorox saw demand surge for cleaning/hygiene products, which cushioned the fall, but even defensives could not escape forced liquidations and margin calls that hit every asset class. Staples (-24.3%) and Healthcare (-27.5%) held up best within the basket while Energy (-55.5%) and Financials (-42.1%) bore the brunt of the growth shock. TLT rallied +12.3% and the DXY strengthened +3.3% as dollar funding stress peaked — defensives demonstrated relative outperformance even while taking an absolute loss.","body_zh":"2020年2月21日至3月23日暴跌期间，本篮子绝对下跌21.8%（广义防御板块均值-29.1%）——尽管痛苦，但相对SPY（-32.8%）与周期股（-39.4%）有明显超额，VIX在此期间从17飙升至62。世卫组织于3月11日宣布新冠构成全球大流行，意大利3月9日进入全国封锁，纽交所熔断机制于3月9日、12日、16日相继触发。宝洁、高乐氏等必需品公司清洁/卫生产品需求激增，缓冲了跌幅，但强制平仓与追保金潮汐席卷所有资产类别，连防御股也未能幸免。必需消费品（-24.3%）与医疗（-27.5%）在篮子内最为抗跌，而能源（-55.5%）与金融（-42.1%）则承受增长冲击主力。TLT上涨+12.3%，DXY走强+3.3%，美元融资压力见顶——这是防御股相对跑赢逻辑成立、但仍遭受绝对损失的典型一腿。","drivers":["WHO pandemic declaration Mar 11 2020","Italy lockdown global demand shock","NYSE circuit-breakers forced liquidation","VIX 17->62 extreme risk-off","relative outperformance but absolute loss"],"drivers_zh":["世卫2020年3月11日宣布大流行","意大利封锁全球需求冲击","纽交所熔断强制平仓","VIX 17->62极端风险规避","相对跑赢但绝对亏损"],"prev_key":"2020-02-21","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-21"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID panic crash: defensives lead but still fall","title_zh":"新冠恐慌暴跌：防御领跌但仍难幸免","turn_id":"defensives:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From the March 23, 2020 COVID low to April 2022, defensives rose 72.4% — a big absolute number, but cyclicals surged +143.3% and SPY +102.3%, so defensives were the clear laggards. Three forces drove this divergence: first, the $2.2 trillion CARES Act (March 27, 2020), $1.9 trillion American Rescue Plan (March 2021), and Fed QE at $120bn/month unleashed fiscal-monetary superstimulus that rotated capital into high-beta reopening cyclicals; second, the Pfizer vaccine announcement on November 9, 2020 (>90% efficacy) triggered one of the largest single-day rotations from growth/defensives into value/cyclicals on record, with Energy (the sector +265%; WTI itself from negative in April 2020 to over $100 by 2022), Materials, and Financials leading; third, surging inflation (CPI reached 7.0% in December 2021, 8.5% in March 2022) and the resulting yield-surge (TLT -25.0%) crushed the utility/REIT bond-proxy leg even within the basket. Defensives' 72.4% gain understates by nearly half the opportunity cost of holding them over cyclicals.","body_zh":"从2020年3月23日新冠低点至2022年4月，防御板块上涨72.4%——绝对值可观，但周期股飙升+143.3%，SPY+102.3%，防御股明显落后。三股力量驱动了这一分化：其一，2.2万亿美元CARES法案（2020年3月27日）、1.9万亿美元美国救援计划（2021年3月）及美联储每月1200亿美元QE释放财政货币超级刺激，将资金转向高贝塔复苏周期股；其二，辉瑞于2020年11月9日公布疫苗数据（有效性逾90%），触发有记录以来最大单日从成长/防御向价值/周期的轮动，能源（板块+265%；WTI本身从2020年4月负值升至2022年逾100美元）、材料与金融领涨；其三，通胀飙升（CPI 2021年12月达7.0%，2022年3月8.5%）及随之而来的收益率暴升（TLT-25.0%）重创了篮子内的公用事业/REITs债券代理腿。防御股72.4%的绝对涨幅相对周期股的机会成本被低估了近一半。","drivers":["CARES Act + American Rescue Plan fiscal superstimulus","Pfizer vaccine Nov 9 2020 cyclical rotation","Fed QE 120bn/month reflation","Energy sector +265% WTI recovery","CPI surge 7-8.5% crushes utility bond-proxies"],"drivers_zh":["CARES法案+美国救援计划财政超级刺激","辉瑞2020年11月9日疫苗触发周期轮动","美联储每月1200亿QE再通胀","能源板块+265% WTI复苏","CPI飙升7-8.5%重创公用事业债券代理"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Reflation surge leaves defensives behind","title_zh":"再通胀浪潮令防御板块落后于大市","turn_id":"defensives:trough:2020-03"},"2022-04-21":{"body":"From April 2022 to October 2022, defensives fell -14.7% in what was primarily a rate-shock bear driven by the most aggressive Fed tightening since 1981. The FOMC raised rates from 0.25% to 3.0-3.25% over the period, with the 10-year yield peaking near 4.0% by October 2022 (TLT -15.4%); CPI printed 8.5% in March and 9.1% in June — 40-year highs. The utility leg (-14.3%) was particularly exposed as its bond-proxy valuation unraveled. Energy (+7.1%) was the sole sector that stayed positive amid the Russia-Ukraine war supply shock, while defensives broadly tracked a slowdown/deflation-scare quad with DXY surging to a 20-year high (+12.1%). Defensives (-13.8% avg) barely outperformed cyclicals (-14.0%) and roughly tracked SPY (-16.5%) — this was a rate shock that did not let the low-beta cushion function because bonds sold off simultaneously with equities.","body_zh":"2022年4月至10月，防御板块下跌14.7%，这场熊市的核心驱动力是1981年以来最激进的美联储紧缩。联邦公开市场委员会在此期间将利率从0.25%升至3.0-3.25%，10年期收益率10月触及约4.0%峰值（TLT-15.4%）；CPI 3月报8.5%、6月报9.1%，创40年高位。公用事业腿（-14.3%）在债券代理估值崩塌中首当其冲。能源（+7.1%）是俄乌战争供应冲击下唯一保持正回报的板块，而防御股整体处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限，DXY飙升至20年高位（+12.1%）。防御股均值（-13.8%）几乎未能跑赢周期股（-14.0%），与SPY（-16.5%）大致同步——这场利率冲击令低贝塔缓冲完全失效，因为债券与股票同步下跌。","drivers":["Fed hikes 0.25%->3.25% 2022","10y yield 4.0% peak TLT-15.4%","CPI 9.1% 40-year high","Russia-Ukraine energy shock","DXY 20-year high crushes bond-proxies"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2022年加息0.25%->3.25%","10年期收益率峰值4.0% TLT-15.4%","CPI 9.1%创40年高位","俄乌战争能源冲击","DXY创20年高位重创债券代理"],"prev_key":"2022-04-21","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-21"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-hike bear hits the bond-proxy leg hard","title_zh":"加息熊市重创债券代理腿","turn_id":"defensives:peak:2022-04"},"2022-10-07":{"body":"From October 2022 to May 2023, the basket rallied +21.2% (broad defensive sectors +12.8% on average) — broadly in line with SPY (+15.5%) and cyclicals (+13.3%) in an early goldilocks/disinflation recovery. The bear-market bottom formed as the Fed's pace of hikes slowed (December 2022's 50bp step-down after four consecutive 75bp hikes), then the March 10, 2023 Silicon Valley Bank collapse (FDIC receivership) triggered a flight-to-safety impulse that briefly lifted defensive positioning. A falling dollar (DXY -9.4%) aided the multinational staples names, while stabilizing yields (TLT +3.9%) gave utilities a modest tailwind. The tape was narrow (RSP lagged SPY by -3.1%) and tech-led (SMH +33.6%), so defensives' gains largely reflected their flight-to-safety premium post-SVB rather than a genuine defensive rotation — the broader index was recovering as VIX compressed from 31 to 16.","body_zh":"2022年10月至2023年5月，本篮子反弹+21.2%（广义防御板块均值+12.8%），与SPY（+15.5%）和周期股（+13.3%）在金发姑娘/去通胀初期复苏中大致同步。随着美联储加息节奏放缓（2022年12月在连续四次75bp后降至50bp步幅），熊市底部逐渐形成，2023年3月10日硅谷银行倒闭（FDIC接管）触发了短暂的避险冲动，推高了防御性仓位。美元走弱（DXY-9.4%）助力必需品跨国名称，收益率趋稳（TLT+3.9%）给予公用事业温和顺风。市场依然窄幅（RSP跑输SPY-3.1%），科技领涨（SMH+33.6%），防御股的涨幅主要体现的是SVB后的避险溢价，而非真正的防御轮动——随着VIX从31回落至16，大盘整体处于复苏通道。","drivers":["Fed 50bp step-down Dec 2022 pace shift","SVB collapse Mar 10 2023 flight-to-safety","DXY dollar decline -9.4%","VIX compression 31->16 bear-market bottom","narrow tech-led recovery"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2022年12月降至50bp步幅转变","SVB 2023年3月10日倒闭避险冲动","美元走弱DXY-9.4%","VIX从31压缩至16熊市底部","窄幅科技引领复苏"],"prev_key":"2022-10-07","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-07"],"status":"exact","title":"SVB shock + disinflation sparks defensive bid","title_zh":"SVB冲击与去通胀引发防御买盘","turn_id":"defensives:trough:2022-10"},"2023-05-01":{"body":"From May to October 2023, defensives fell -14.9% in a textbook rotation away from low-vol in a growth-up reflation quad. Two forces compounded: the AI/semis mega-rally (NVIDIA's May 24-25, 2023 blowout earnings guidance drove SMH +22.2% over the period; growth beat value by +13.6%) pulled active flows into growth and mega-cap tech, while the higher-for-longer rate narrative (10-year yield surged from ~3.6% to 5.0% by late October, TLT -15.3%) simultaneously crushed bond-proxy utility and REIT valuations (Utilities -13.8%, Real Estate -6.5%). DXY rose +4.3%. The result was a double whammy: defensives did not benefit from a growth/risk environment, and their bond-proxy leg was hurt by the rate surge — SPY managed +5.1% in this window while cyclicals gained +5.3%, exposing a roughly 15-20ppt gap versus defensives at -10.0%.","body_zh":"2023年5月至10月，防御板块下跌14.9%，在增长向上再通胀象限中遭遇教科书式的低波动轮出。两股力量叠加：AI/半导体超级行情（英伟达2023年5月24-25日爆炸性业绩指引推动SMH+22.2%，成长跑赢价值+13.6%）将主动资金吸入成长与大市值科技；同时更高更久利率叙事（10年期收益率从约3.6%飙升至10月底的5.0%，TLT-15.3%）同步重创公用事业和REITs的债券代理估值（公用事业-13.8%，房地产-6.5%）。DXY上涨+4.3%。结果是双重打击：防御股既未受益于成长/风险环境，其债券代理腿又被利率飙升所伤——SPY在此窗口取得+5.1%的涨幅，周期股+5.3%，与防御股-10.0%相差约15-20个百分点。","drivers":["NVIDIA May 2023 earnings AI mega-rally","10y yield ~3.6%->5.0% Oct 2023 surge","growth>value +13.6 flows out of defensives","higher-for-longer Fed narrative","utility/REIT bond-proxy double-hit"],"drivers_zh":["英伟达2023年5月业绩引发AI超级行情","10年期收益率约3.6%->5.0%飙升","成长跑赢价值+13.6资金流出防御","美联储更高更久叙事","公用事业/REITs债券代理双重打击"],"prev_key":"2023-05-01","prev_key_chain":["2023-05-01"],"status":"exact","title":"AI boom and yield spike punish defensives","title_zh":"AI热潮与收益率飙升双重惩罚防御板块","turn_id":"defensives:peak:2023-05"},"2023-10-12":{"body":"From October 2023 to February 2026, defensives climbed +43.2% — a long, steady compounding leg, though one that underperformed SPY (+62.8%) in a goldilocks/disinflation quad dominated by the AI-driven tech melt-up (SMH +170.7%). The trough coincided with the late-October 2023 peak in 10-year yields near 5.0%; from there, the Fed's September 2024 pivot (first 50bp rate cut) and subsequent cuts (about -100bp toward 4.25-4.5%) drove TLT +16.3% and gave rate-sensitive utilities a significant tailwind. Critically, utilities also acquired a structural growth narrative: Goldman Sachs and others projected data center power demand growing well over 100% by 2030, transforming utilities from a pure bond-proxy into an AI-infrastructure play (Utilities were among the basket's leaders at +74.4% over the leg). A weaker dollar (DXY -8.4%) aided multinational staples. The leg ran through multiple risk events (regional bank stress in early 2024, Middle East escalation, the 2024 US election) with defensives acting as the steady shock-absorber component.","body_zh":"2023年10月至2026年2月，防御板块上涨+43.2%——一段漫长稳健的复利行情，但在金发姑娘/去通胀象限中跑输SPY（+62.8%），因大盘由AI驱动的科技融涨主导（SMH+170.7%）。本段起点恰与2023年10月底10年期收益率接近5.0%的峰值重合；此后美联储于2024年9月转向（首次降息50bp）并随后降息（累计约-100bp至4.25-4.5%），推动TLT+16.3%，给利率敏感的公用事业带来显著顺风。关键是，公用事业还获得了结构性成长叙事：高盛等机构预测数据中心电力需求到2030年将增长逾一倍，将公用事业从纯债券代理转型为AI基础设施配置（公用事业在本段以+74.4%位居篮子前列）。美元走弱（DXY-8.4%）助力必需品跨国名称。该段行情历经多个风险事件（2024年初区域银行压力、中东局势升级、2024年大选），防御股扮演稳健减震器角色。","drivers":["Fed Sep 2024 50bp pivot ~-100bp total","10y yield peak late-Oct 2023 rate-relief","AI data center power demand structural tailwind","DXY dollar weakness -8.4%","goldilocks soft-landing accumulation"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2024年9月50bp转向累计降息约-100bp","10年期收益率2023年10月底见顶利率松绑","AI数据中心电力需求结构性顺风","美元走弱DXY-8.4%","金发姑娘软着陆累积买盘"],"prev_key":"2023-10-12","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Soft-landing + AI power demand lifts steady grind","title_zh":"软着陆与AI电力需求驱动稳健上行","turn_id":"defensives:trough:2023-10"}},"now":"Defensives sit at cycle position 38.4 (below mid-cycle), RS rank 31 out of peers, in a confirmed uptrend above the 200-day with a BUY signal, yet clearly lagging in the current reflation/growth-up quad. The live backdrop is a textbook defensive headwind: Tech (+24.3%), Energy (+21.5%), and Industrials (+15.8%) are dominating while the basket has gained roughly 6.9% versus cyclicals at +11.2% — the classic configuration where a yield-curve-up, oil-led reflation regime drains flows out of staples and utilities (note this is a value-led reflation, growth-minus-value is actually -15.2%, with the index pulled by a narrow semis melt-up, SMH +67.9%). An oil shock (crude +19.2%, DXY +3.4%) adds a secondary headwind: the stronger dollar pressures the multinational earnings base of consumer staples names while higher energy costs squeeze staples operating margins. The rate-sensitive utility leg faces some friction from a firm dollar, though TLT is roughly flat (+1.1%) and VIX is still only 14-18 — not yet spiking enough to trigger a genuine flight-to-safety bid. This basket remains the portfolio shock absorber — its relative strength will improve sharply only if the reflation narrative breaks, credit spreads widen materially, or a genuine risk-off catalyst drives VIX above 25-30.","now_zh":"防御板块处于周期位置38.4（低于中轨），RS排名31，价格确认站上200日均线并发出买入信号，但在当前再通胀/增长向上象限中明显落后。实时环境是教科书式的防御逆风：科技（+24.3%）、能源（+21.5%）与工业（+15.8%）主导市场，而本篮子仅上涨约6.9%，周期股达+11.2%——收益率曲线上行、油价领涨的再通胀格局将资金从必需品和公用事业抽离的经典配置（须注意这是价值主导的再通胀，成长相对价值实为-15.2%，指数由窄幅半导体融涨拉动，SMH+67.9%）。油价冲击（原油+19.2%，DXY+3.4%）带来额外阻力：强势美元压制必需品跨国巨头海外收益，高能源成本则挤压经营利润率。对利率敏感的公用事业腿受制于偏强美元，但TLT大致持平（+1.1%），VIX仅14-18，尚不足以触发真正的避险买盘。该篮子仍是组合的减震器——唯有再通胀叙事瓦解、信用利差大幅走阔或风险规避驱使VIX显著推升至25-30上方时，其相对强度才会明显改善。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-energy_complex":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"A +28.4% basket surge through June 2014 driven by two concurrent geopolitical shocks: ISIS advances into northern Iraq from June 2014 (WTI hit $106.53, Brent topped $113) and Russia-Ukraine tensions escalating through spring. Both stoked supply-disruption fears in an already tight market (oil +13.0%). The macro context was stagflation-ish — Utilities (+18.2%) and Energy (+17.6%) co-led, TLT rallied +10.5% as yields fell, and defensives (11.9%) beat cyclicals (8.2%), consistent with a fear-bid that lifted commodity producers while safe havens caught flows simultaneously. The dollar fell 0.7%, a mild tailwind for oil-linked revenues.","body_zh":"至2014年6月篮子上涨28.4%，由两大同步地缘冲击驱动：ISIS于2014年6月挺进伊拉克北部（WTI触及106.53美元、布伦特升破113美元）及俄乌紧张局势春季持续升温，均在本已偏紧的市场引发供应中断担忧（油价+13.0%）。宏观背景呈滞涨态势——公用事业（+18.2%）与能源（+17.6%）共同领涨，TLT涨10.5%（收益率下行），防御股（11.9%）跑赢周期股（8.2%），符合恐慌驱动下大宗商品生产商与避险资产同步受追捧的特征。美元小幅走弱0.7%，为油价收益提供微弱顺风。","drivers":["Iraq/ISIS supply-disruption fear","Russia-Ukraine geopolitical premium","stagflation-ish quad","falling yields (TLT +10.5%)","oil +13% on risk premium"],"drivers_zh":["伊拉克/ISIS供应中断恐慌","俄乌地缘溢价","滞涨象限","收益率下行(TLT +10.5%)","原油+13%风险溢价"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Iraq/Ukraine geopolitical bid lifts crude","title_zh":"伊拉克/乌克兰地缘政治溢价推升原油","turn_id":"energy_complex:trough:2014-01"},"2014-06-23":{"body":"A -24.2% collapse from mid-June to mid-December 2014 as the supply-disruption premium fully reversed (oil -47.3%) and the structural bear case emerged. Brent fell from $115 to ~$57 by year-end after OPEC's November 27, 2014 Vienna meeting decided against production cuts — Saudi Arabia's explicit strategy to defend market share against US shale. Simultaneous demand deceleration (China slowdown, weak European demand) and a surging dollar (DXY +10.2%) compounded the selloff. The macro flipped to slowdown/deflation-scare: VIX surged from 11 to 20, TLT rallied +14.8%, defensives (Health +13.1%, Staples +6.5%) led while Energy was the worst sector (-27.2%) and credit spreads widened sharply (HYG-LQD -8.4%).","body_zh":"2014年6月中旬至12月中旬下跌24.2%，供应中断溢价完全逆转（油价-47.3%），结构性熊市案例浮现。2014年11月27日OPEC维也纳会议决定不减产——沙特以维护市场份额对抗美国页岩油为战略——布伦特从115美元跌至年末约57美元。同步出现的需求放缓（中国经济减速、欧洲需求疲弱）与美元大幅走强（DXY +10.2%）加剧抛售。宏观翻转为放缓/通缩惊魂：VIX从11飙至20，TLT涨14.8%，防御股（医疗+13.1%、必需消费+6.5%）领涨，能源为最差板块（-27.2%），信用利差大幅走阔（HYG-LQD -8.4%）。","drivers":["OPEC no-cut decision Nov 27 2014","Saudi market-share strategy vs shale","dollar +10.2% DXY","China/EU demand deceleration","oil -47.3%, Brent to ~$57"],"drivers_zh":["OPEC 2014年11月27日拒绝减产","沙特对抗页岩油市场份额战略","美元+10.2%","中欧需求放缓","油价-47.3%、布伦特至约57美元"],"prev_key":"2014-06-23","prev_key_chain":["2014-06-23"],"status":"exact","title":"OPEC no-cut shock triggers energy crash","title_zh":"OPEC拒绝减产冲击引爆能源崩跌","turn_id":"energy_complex:peak:2014-06"},"2014-12-15":{"body":"A +20.7% bounce from the December 2014 trough to late April 2015 as crude staged a short-covering rally from extreme oversold conditions. The macro turned goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation: cyclicals (8.2%) beat defensives (3.6%), VIX dropped from 20 to 13, and high-beta led low-vol by +5.8pp. Energy (+14.5%) was the top sector. Critically, this was a fundamentals-light bounce — the dollar continued to strengthen (DXY +7.5%), a structural headwind, and oil's +4.8% gain was modest. The move was driven by positioning washout and expectations of US rig-count decline curbing shale growth, rather than a genuine demand inflection.","body_zh":"2014年12月触底至2015年4月末反弹20.7%，原油在极度超卖后展开空头回补行情。宏观转为金发女郎/增长向上-去通胀：周期股（8.2%）跑赢防御股（3.6%），VIX从20降至13，高贝塔领先低波动+5.8个百分点。能源（+14.5%）为领涨板块。关键在于，这是基本面支撑薄弱的反弹——美元持续走强（DXY +7.5%）构成结构性逆风，油价仅温和上涨4.8%。行情由仓位洗牌及美国钻井数量下降有望抑制页岩产量增长的预期驱动，而非真正的需求拐点。","drivers":["oversold short-covering bounce","US rig-count decline expectations","goldilocks risk-on rotation (VIX 20→13)","high-beta led low-vol (+5.8pp)","oil modest +4.8% on positioning"],"drivers_zh":["超卖空头回补","美国钻机数下降预期","金发女郎风险偏好轮动(VIX 20→13)","高贝塔领先低波动(+5.8pp)","原油小幅+4.8%仓位驱动"],"prev_key":"2014-12-15","prev_key_chain":["2014-12-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Dead-cat bounce: oversold relief, risk-on rotation","title_zh":"超卖反弹：技术性修复与风险偏好轮动","turn_id":"energy_complex:trough:2014-12"},"2015-04-29":{"body":"A -43.5% collapse over nearly 10 months as the supply overhang proved structural (oil -55.3%). Three catalysts compounded: (1) the August 2015 China stock market crash and yuan devaluation (August 11-12) crushed global demand expectations, with copper-gold down -31.4%; (2) OPEC maintained production above 31mb/d throughout; (3) the Fed's December 16, 2015 first rate hike since 2006 tightened financial conditions for levered energy producers. Brent bottomed near $27 in January 2016. The macro was a severe slowdown/deflation-scare — VIX surged from 13 to 28, TLT gained +8.6%, defensives (Utilities +5.1%) were the only positive GICS group, Energy was the worst (-33.6%), and credit spreads blew out massively (HYG-LQD -11.0%) reflecting shale high-yield stress.","body_zh":"近10个月内下跌43.5%，供应过剩被证明具有结构性（油价-55.3%）。三大催化剂叠加：（1）2015年8月中国股市崩盘与人民币贬值（8月11-12日）重创全球需求预期，铜金比下跌31.4%；（2）OPEC全年维持逾3100万桶/日产量；（3）美联储2015年12月16日九年来首次加息，收紧高杠杆能源生产商融资环境。布伦特于2016年1月触底接近27美元。宏观呈严重放缓/通缩惊魂——VIX从13飙至28，TLT涨8.6%，防御股（公用事业+5.1%）是唯一正收益板块，能源为最差（-33.6%），信用利差大幅走阔（HYG-LQD -11.0%），折射页岩高收益债压力。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation Aug 2015","OPEC sustained overproduction","Fed first rate hike Dec 2015","shale HY credit stress (HYG-LQD -11%)","oil -55.3%, Brent near $27"],"drivers_zh":["2015年8月中国人民币贬值","OPEC持续超产","2015年12月美联储首次加息","页岩高收益信用压力(HYG-LQD -11%)","油价-55.3%、布伦特近27美元"],"prev_key":"2015-04-29","prev_key_chain":["2015-04-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil glut deepens: China shock + Fed hike fear","title_zh":"供应过剩深化：中国冲击+美联储加息恐慌","turn_id":"energy_complex:peak:2015-04"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"A +110.2% epic 32-month rally from the February 2016 trough — the longest bull leg in this basket's history. Three sequential drivers: (1) the OPEC-Russia production freeze announced February 16, 2016 (Doha) marked the sentiment floor, with WTI bottoming near $26 on February 11; (2) OPEC's landmark November 30, 2016 Vienna deal — first production cut in 8 years — shifted the supply paradigm; (3) the Trump election (November 8, 2016) sparked a pro-growth, deregulation reflation trade, with the 10-year yield surging. The macro was a sustained reflation/growth-up quad: oil +191.5%, copper-gold +44.8%, cyclicals (+74.9%) crushed defensives (+33.1%), VIX compressed from 28 to 12, TLT fell -8.2%, and semis led (SMH +139.9%).","body_zh":"自2016年2月触底展开长达32个月、涨幅110.2%的史诗级牛市——本篮子历史上持续时间最长的多头腿。三大顺序驱动：（1）2016年2月16日OPEC-俄罗斯在多哈宣布冻产，WTI于2月11日触底约26美元，标志情绪底部；（2）2016年11月30日OPEC维也纳协议——8年来首次减产——改变供给范式；（3）2016年11月8日特朗普当选引发亲增长、去监管再通胀交易，10年期收益率飙升。宏观呈持续再通胀/增长向上象限：油价+191.5%、铜金比+44.8%、周期股（+74.9%）碾压防御股（+33.1%）、VIX从28压缩至12、TLT跌8.2%，半导体领涨（SMH +139.9%）。","drivers":["OPEC-Russia freeze Feb 2016","OPEC cut deal Nov 2016","Trump reflation trade Nov 2016","oil +191.5% multi-year surge","reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +74.9%)"],"drivers_zh":["2016年2月OPEC-俄罗斯冻产","2016年11月OPEC减产协议","2016年11月特朗普再通胀交易","原油+191.5%多年飙升","再通胀/增长向上象限(周期股+74.9%)"],"prev_key":"2016-02-11","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-11"],"status":"exact","title":"OPEC freeze + reflation: mega-rally","title_zh":"OPEC冻产+再通胀：超级大牛市","turn_id":"energy_complex:trough:2016-02"},"2018-10-03":{"body":"A -33% crash in just 83 days as crude went from a 4-year high near $76 (WTI) in early October to under $50 by late December 2018 (oil -44.3%). Three drivers converged: (1) the Fed's hawkish October 3 Powell speech ('a long way from neutral') triggered a broad rate shock; (2) Trump pressured Saudi Arabia to raise output and granted Iran sanction waivers, flooding supply; (3) global growth decelerated sharply (ISM manufacturing peaked at 60.8 in August, began rolling over). VIX exploded from 12 to 36, TLT rallied +6.4%, defensives (-8.1%) dramatically outpaced cyclicals (-22.5%), and Energy was the worst sector (-29.9%, vs Tech -23.8% and Industrials -23.7%). Credit also repriced (HYG-LQD -5.5%).","body_zh":"仅83天内下跌33%，原油从2018年10月初四年高位（WTI接近76美元）跌至12月末50美元以下（油价-44.3%）。三大驱动合流：（1）2018年10月3日鲍威尔鹰派讲话（'距中性利率还有很长距离'）引发广泛利率冲击；（2）特朗普施压沙特增产并给予伊朗制裁豁免，供应泛滥；（3）全球增长急剧放缓（ISM制造业8月触顶60.8后开始回落）。VIX从12飙至36，TLT涨6.4%，防御股（-8.1%）大幅跑赢周期股（-22.5%），能源为最差板块（-29.9%，科技-23.8%、工业-23.7%），信用重新定价（HYG-LQD -5.5%）。","drivers":["Powell 'long way from neutral' Oct 3 2018","Trump Iran sanction waivers","global growth deceleration","oil -44.3% from 4-year high","VIX 12→36 risk-off flush"],"drivers_zh":["2018年10月3日鲍威尔'距中性利率很远'讲话","特朗普伊朗制裁豁免","全球增长放缓","原油-44.3%从四年高点","VIX 12→36避险急挫"],"prev_key":"2018-10-03","prev_key_chain":["2018-10-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-shock + demand-fear oil bear, Q4 flush","title_zh":"利率冲击+需求恐慌引发原油熊市，四季度急挫","turn_id":"energy_complex:peak:2018-10"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"A +26.9% recovery in just four months (Christmas Eve 2018 through April 22, 2019) driven by a textbook Fed pivot: on January 4, 2019, Powell stated the Fed would be 'patient' on rate hikes, and by March 2019 the dot plot showed zero projected hikes for 2019. Simultaneously, OPEC+ implemented its December 2018 production cut agreement (-1.2mb/d), tightening the supply picture (oil +54.5%). The risk-on reversal was broad — VIX crashed from 36 to 12, semis led (SMH +45.3%), cyclicals (+28.1%) beat defensives (+12.1%), and credit recovered (HYG-LQD +3.5%). Energy's +26.9% gain lagged the broader cyclical recovery as crude faced some late demand uncertainty.","body_zh":"从2018年平安夜至2019年4月22日仅4个月反弹26.9%，由教科书式美联储政策转向驱动：2019年1月4日鲍威尔表示加息将'保持耐心'，至2019年3月点阵图显示全年零加息预期。同步，OPEC+执行2018年12月减产协议（-120万桶/日），供给面收紧（油价+54.5%）。风险偏好逆转全面展开——VIX从36崩至12，半导体领涨（SMH +45.3%），周期股（+28.1%）跑赢防御股（+12.1%），信用修复（HYG-LQD +3.5%）。能源+26.9%涨幅略落后于大盘周期股修复，因原油面临若干后期需求不确定性。","drivers":["Fed Powell pivot Jan 2019 (patient)","OPEC+ -1.2mb/d cut Dec 2018","VIX collapse 36→12","oil +54.5% from lows","broad cyclical risk-on recovery"],"drivers_zh":["2019年1月美联储鲍威尔转向('保持耐心')","OPEC+ 2018年12月-120万桶/日减产","VIX崩塌36→12","原油+54.5%从低位反弹","全面周期风险偏好修复"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell pivot + OPEC cut: energy snapback","title_zh":"鲍威尔转向+OPEC减产：能源强劲反弹","turn_id":"energy_complex:trough:2018-12"},"2019-04-22":{"body":"A catastrophic -71.6% collapse over 11 months (oil -69.0%) encompassing two distinct phases: (1) trade-war-driven demand softening (April-December 2019), where pre-COVID shale overcapacity and a wave of E&P bankruptcies began; (2) the COVID-19 pandemic shock from February 2020, which caused the single largest demand destruction in history (-16mb/d in Q2 2020) and the OPEC+ price war (Saudi-Russia breakdown March 6-8, 2020 sent crude sharply lower). WTI briefly went negative (-$37.63 April 20, 2020). VIX exploded from 12 to 76, TLT surged +20.4%, defensives (Staples +0.1%, Health -0.5%) were essentially flat while Energy collapsed -63.0%, and breadth was catastrophically narrow (equal-weight -9.3% vs cap-weight).","body_zh":"历时11个月遭遇灾难性下跌71.6%（油价-69.0%），分两个阶段：（1）贸易战驱动的需求疲软（2019年4-12月），新冠前页岩产能过剩及E&P破产潮涌现；（2）2020年2月起新冠疫情冲击，造成历史上最大单次需求毁灭（2020年Q2 -1600万桶/日）及OPEC+价格战（2020年3月6-8日沙特-俄罗斯破裂致原油急挫）。WTI于2020年4月20日短暂跌至负值（-37.63美元）。VIX从12飙至76，TLT涨20.4%，防御股（必需消费+0.1%、医疗-0.5%）近乎持平，而能源崩跌63.0%，广度极度恶化（等权跑输市值权-9.3%）。","drivers":["COVID-19 demand destruction -16mb/d Q2 2020","OPEC+ price war breakdown Mar 2020","WTI negative pricing Apr 2020","shale E&P bankruptcy wave 2019","VIX 12→76 panic"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情需求毁灭2020Q2 -1600万桶/日","2020年3月OPEC+价格战破裂","WTI负油价2020年4月","页岩E&P破产潮2019年","VIX 12→76恐慌"],"prev_key":"2019-04-22","prev_key_chain":["2019-04-22"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade war, shale stress, COVID oil wipeout","title_zh":"贸易战、页岩应力、新冠疫情油价归零","turn_id":"energy_complex:peak:2019-04"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"A +169.6% rocket in just 82 days off the March 18 trough (the largest percentage gain in any leg of this series). Three sequential catalysts: (1) OPEC+ agreed April 12, 2020 to a historic 9.7mb/d production cut — the largest ever — removing the supply glut overhang; (2) the Fed deployed unlimited QE and the US government passed the $2.2 trillion CARES Act (March 27), engineering the fastest liquidity recovery in history; (3) oil demand began recovering as lockdowns partially lifted in May-June (oil +87.5%). The macro was a textbook reflation/growth-up: Energy (+99.8%) led all sectors, cyclicals (+53.3%) vs defensives (+16.5%), breadth broad (equal-weight +9.7%), VIX collapsed from 76 to 26, and the dollar weakened -4.5%.","body_zh":"自3月18日触底后仅82天内暴涨169.6%（本系列历史上任何腿中涨幅最大）。三大顺序催化剂：（1）2020年4月12日OPEC+达成历史性最大减产协议（970万桶/日），消除供应过剩悬念；（2）美联储宣布无限量宽松、美国政府通过2.2万亿美元CARES法案（3月27日），制造史上最快流动性复苏；（3）随5-6月部分解封，石油需求开始恢复（油价+87.5%）。宏观呈教科书式再通胀/增长向上：能源（+99.8%）领涨所有板块，周期股（+53.3%）对防御股（+16.5%），广度扩散（等权跑赢+9.7%），VIX从76崩至26，美元走弱-4.5%。","drivers":["OPEC+ 9.7mb/d historic cut Apr 2020","Fed unlimited QE + CARES Act Mar 2020","reopening demand recovery","oil +87.5% from negative","VIX collapse 76→26"],"drivers_zh":["2020年4月OPEC+ 970万桶/日史诗减产","美联储无限QE + CARES法案2020年3月","解封需求修复","原油+87.5%从负值反弹","VIX崩塌76→26"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"OPEC+ megacut + reopening: violent relief spike","title_zh":"OPEC+史诗减产+重新开放：暴力紧急反弹","turn_id":"energy_complex:trough:2020-03"},"2020-06-08":{"body":"A -40.9% selloff from June 8 to October 28, 2020 as the energy relief rally exhausted and three headwinds converged: (1) COVID-19 second-wave fears intensified through summer, suppressing travel/transportation demand and keeping oil choppy (oil -2.1% for the period); (2) a massive growth/tech rotation siphoned flows away from cyclicals — Tech led (+10.0%), semis +14.1%, growth beat value by +17.1pp, and the tape became extremely narrow (equal-weight -6.7% vs cap-weight); (3) VIX re-elevated from 26 to 40 on the October sell-off ahead of the US election. Financials (-10.7%) and Energy (-39.1%) were the worst laggards, while defensives (1.6%) beat cyclicals (-4.5%). The stagflation-ish quad (dollar weak -3.3% but energy still collapsed) confirmed demand-led not supply-led pressure.","body_zh":"2020年6月8日至10月28日下跌40.9%，能源紧急反弹耗尽后三重逆风叠加：（1）新冠第二波恐慌于夏季加剧，压制出行/交通需求，油价震荡（该段-2.1%）；（2）大规模成长/科技轮动抽走周期股资金——科技领涨（+10.0%）、半导体+14.1%，成长跑赢价值+17.1个百分点，行情极度收窄（等权跑输市值权-6.7%）；（3）VIX随10月美国大选前急跌从26重新升至40。金融（-10.7%）与能源（-39.1%）垫底，防御股（1.6%）跑赢周期股（-4.5%）。滞涨态象限（美元走弱-3.3%但能源仍崩跌）确认此为需求主导而非供给主导的压力。","drivers":["COVID second-wave demand suppression","mega-cap/tech rotation (SMH +14.1%)","narrow breadth (equal-weight -6.7%)","VIX 26→40 election uncertainty","growth>value +17.1pp"],"drivers_zh":["新冠第二波需求抑制","巨头/科技轮动(半导体+14.1%)","广度收窄(等权跑输-6.7%)","VIX 26→40大选不确定性","成长跑赢价值+17.1pp"],"prev_key":"2020-06-08","prev_key_chain":["2020-06-08"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID second wave + tech rotation crushes energy","title_zh":"新冠第二波+科技轮动重创能源","turn_id":"energy_complex:peak:2020-06"},"2020-10-28":{"body":"A +331% rocket from the 2020 COVID trough through June 2022, as reopening demand collided with OPEC+ discipline and Russia's February 2022 invasion of Ukraine sent crude soaring (oil +219.4%). This was a textbook reflation/growth-up quad — the 10Y surged (TLT -26.5%), the dollar strengthened (DXY +9.5%), cyclicals (+70.6%) crushed defensives (+26.6%) and breadth broadened (equal-weight beat cap-weight +13.8%) — and Energy (+255.8%) was the best-performing sector even as the rest of the market fell into a rate-driven bear.","body_zh":"自2020年疫情谷底至2022年6月火箭式上涨331%，复工需求碰上OPEC+限产，叠加2022年2月俄罗斯入侵乌克兰将原油推升（油价+219.4%）。这是教科书式的再通胀/增长向上象限——10年期收益率飙升（TLT -26.5%）、美元走强（DXY +9.5%）、周期股（+70.6%）碾压防御股（+26.6%）、广度扩散（等权跑赢市值权+13.8%）——在大盘陷入利率驱动的熊市之际，能源（+255.8%）是表现最佳的板块。","drivers":["reflation/growth-up quad","Russia-Ukraine oil shock (+219%)","broadening (+13.8%)","OPEC+"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀/增长向上象限","俄乌石油冲击(+219%)","广度扩散(+13.8%)","OPEC+"],"prev_key":"2020-10-28","prev_key_chain":["2020-10-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Reflation super-spike, Energy leads the bear","title_zh":"再通胀超级飙升，能源领涨于熊市","turn_id":"energy_complex:trough:2020-10"},"2022-06-07":{"body":"A -27% drop as demand-destruction and recession fear from aggressive Fed hiking pulled crude sharply off its June 2022 peak (oil -19.8%, copper-gold -19.9). The quad flipped to slowdown/deflation-scare with a surging dollar (DXY +6.1%), defensives (-3.6%) beating cyclicals (-14.0%) and Energy the worst sector (-25.9%) — the fastest leg of the broad commodity de-rate as growth expectations rolled over.","body_zh":"下跌27%，美联储激进加息带来的需求毁灭与衰退担忧使原油从2022年6月峰值急挫（油价-19.8%、铜金比-19.9）。象限翻转为放缓/通缩惊魂，美元飙升（DXY +6.1%）、防御股（-3.6%）跑赢周期股（-14.0%）、能源为最差板块（-25.9%）——在增长预期回落之际，这是广义大宗商品估值下杀中最快的一段。","drivers":["slowdown/deflation-scare quad","demand destruction","Fed hiking, dollar +6.1%","recession fear"],"drivers_zh":["放缓/通缩惊魂象限","需求毁灭","美联储加息、美元+6.1%","衰退担忧"],"prev_key":"2022-06-07","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Recession-fear crude pullback","title_zh":"衰退担忧引发原油回调","turn_id":"energy_complex:peak:2022-06"},"2022-07-14":{"body":"A +78% grind into late November 2024 as crude chopped in a wide range while disciplined buybacks, dividends and strong free cash flow rewarded integrateds and E&P. Notably this ran against the regime tide: the macro was a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +137.6%, growth>value +35.1, oil actually -25.6%) with narrow mega-cap-led breadth (equal-weight lagged -18.3%) where flows favored tech — so Energy's slow, fundamentals-driven climb on capital discipline was a value-factor outlier, not a crude-price moonshot.","body_zh":"至2024年11月底缓步上涨78%，原油宽幅震荡，而有纪律的回购、分红与强劲自由现金流回报综合油企与勘探开采商。值得注意的是这逆势而行：宏观为金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好暴涨（半导体SMH +137.6%、成长跑赢价值+35.1、油价实际-25.6%），广度狭窄、巨头领涨（等权跑输-18.3%），资金偏向科技——因此能源凭资本纪律缓慢的基本面驱动攀升是价值因子的异类，而非油价暴涨。","drivers":["counter-trend vs semis-led risk-on","capital discipline","narrow breadth (-18.3%)","range-bound crude"],"drivers_zh":["逆半导体领涨风险偏好","资本纪律","窄广度(-18.3%)","原油区间"],"prev_key":"2022-07-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-07-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Range-bound grind under a semis-led melt-up","title_zh":"半导体领涨暴涨下的区间缓步上涨","turn_id":"energy_complex:trough:2022-07"},"2024-11-22":{"body":"A -23% slide into the early-April 2025 tariff crash as global-growth fear and OPEC+ supply-add plans pressured crude (oil -16.4%). This was a slowdown/deflation-scare risk-off — VIX exploded 15->52, defensives (-7.1%) beat cyclicals (-18.7%) and a weaker dollar (DXY -4.2%) couldn't offset recession-demand worries. Energy underperformed badly (-20.1%) as a softening oil balance layered onto the broad de-risk.","body_zh":"下跌23%至2025年4月初关税崩盘，全球增长担忧与OPEC+增产计划压制原油（油价-16.4%）。这是放缓/通缩惊魂的避险——VIX由15飙至52、防御股（-7.1%）跑赢周期股（-18.7%），即便美元走弱（DXY -4.2%）也无法抵消衰退需求担忧。在趋松的油市平衡叠加广泛去风险之际，能源大幅跑输（-20.1%）。","drivers":["risk-off flush (VIX 15->52)","tariff crash","OPEC+ supply","growth fear"],"drivers_zh":["避险急挫(VIX 15->52)","关税崩盘","OPEC+增产","增长担忧"],"prev_key":"2024-11-22","prev_key_chain":["2024-11-22"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-crash risk-off + oversupply de-rate","title_zh":"关税崩盘避险+供给过剩压估值","turn_id":"energy_complex:peak:2024-11"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"A +81% recovery off the tariff low, powered by the 2026 Iran/Strait-of-Hormuz crisis that spiked crude (oil +80.9%) and pushed CPI to 4.2% (house view). The backdrop turned to a reflation/growth-up quad with a broad semis-led risk-on tape underneath (SMH +203.2%, VIX collapsing 52->18) and a weaker dollar (DXY -3.6%) aiding the commodity bid; the war premium peaked into mid-May 2026 before the ceasefire, with Energy (+65.5%) a top leader on the supply-disruption bid.","body_zh":"自关税低点反弹81%，由2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹海峡危机驱动，将原油推升（油价+80.9%）、CPI升至4.2%（本观点）。背景转为再通胀/增长向上象限，底下是广泛的半导体领涨风险偏好行情（半导体SMH +203.2%、VIX由52崩至18），美元走弱（DXY -3.6%）助推大宗商品买盘；战争溢价于2026年5月中、停火前见顶，供应中断买盘下能源（+65.5%）为领涨之一。","drivers":["reflation oil shock (oil +80.9%)","Iran/Hormuz crisis","risk-on recovery (VIX 52->18)","weaker dollar tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀石油冲击(油价+80.9%)","伊朗/霍尔木兹危机","风险偏好修复(VIX 52->18)","美元走弱顺风"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Iran/Hormuz reflation oil-shock spike","title_zh":"伊朗/霍尔木兹再通胀石油冲击飙升","turn_id":"energy_complex:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"The US Energy Complex is in a Downturn phase (Rolling over), with the war premium from the 2026 Iran/Strait-of-Hormuz crisis now unwinding following the mid-June 2026 ceasefire framework. The basket peaked on 2026-05-19 and has begun rolling over despite a nominally constructive tape: reflation/growth-up quad with oil still +19.2% ytd, copper-gold +18.3%, Energy a top-sector leader (+21.5%, behind Tech +24.3%). The direct headwind is a strengthening dollar (DXY +3.4%), which historically acts as a mechanical drag on dollar-denominated commodity producers. RS rank sits at 44 (below median), and cycle position is 44.3 — mid-cycle after the geopolitical spike. With the geopolitical bid fading and OPEC+ supply policy fluid, the energy complex is transitioning from supply-shock leadership to a more fundamentals-driven range as the market reprices from Hormuz-crisis levels toward normalised Brent around $87-90.","now_zh":"美国能源综合目前处于\"回落\"阶段，2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹海峡危机带来的战争溢价随6月中旬停火框架落地而正在消散。本篮子于2026年5月19日见顶并开始回落，尽管表面宏观环境仍属利多：再通胀/增长向上象限，油价年初至今仍涨+19.2%，铜金比+18.3%，能源为领涨板块之一（+21.5%，仅次于科技+24.3%）。直接逆风来自美元走强（DXY +3.4%），历史上对以美元计价的大宗商品生产商构成机械性拖累。相对强度排名为44（低于中位），周期位置44.3——处于地缘冲击飙升后的中段。随着地缘溢价消退、OPEC+供给政策仍存变数，能源综合正从供应冲击领涨模式过渡至基本面驱动的区间整理，市场将从霍尔木兹危机估值水平向布伦特均衡价格87-90美元重新定价。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"oil.regime_shift.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"oil.regime_shift.v1","arch_state":"pass","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-housing":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"A 46.9% rally over 19 months as the housing chain recovered from the 2013 taper-tantrum correction. The 30-year fixed mortgage fell from roughly 4.5% back toward 3.7% as QE-era accommodation persisted and the late-2014 oil collapse (WTI -57%) drove a deflation-scare quad where TLT surged +27.6% and Treasury yields plunged. The ctx confirms this was a yield-regime rally: defensives averaged +30.3% vs cyclicals +8.5%, with energy -19.9% and DXY +19.4%. Falling mortgage rates and steady post-crisis employment gains lifted new-build demand from decade lows, letting the rate-sensitive housing chain deliver +46.9% vs SPY's +17.2%.","body_zh":"住房产业链从2013年缩减恐慌修正中复苏，历时19个月累计上涨46.9%。30年期固定抵押贷款利率从约4.5%回落至3.7%，量化宽松时代的宽松政策延续，2014年底油价崩跌（WTI -57%）驱动通缩恐慌象限——TLT飙升+27.6%，国债收益率骤降。背景数据印证了这是利率驱动的反弹：防御板块均涨+30.3% vs 周期仅+8.5%，能源-19.9%，DXY+19.4%。抵押贷款利率下行叠加就业稳步复苏提振住房需求，使这一利率敏感板块以+46.9%大幅跑赢SPY的+17.2%。","drivers":["30yr mortgage falls from 4.5% toward 3.7% on deflation scare","Oil collapse drives TLT +27.6% and kills inflation expectations","Post-crisis employment recovery lifts household formation","QE-era Fed accommodation keeps financial conditions loose"],"drivers_zh":["30年期抵押贷款利率从4.5%降至3.7%，通缩恐慌驱动","油价崩跌推动TLT+27.6%，通胀预期瓦解","后危机就业复苏提升家庭组建需求","量化宽松时代美联储宽松维持金融条件宽裕"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-crisis recovery on falling rates and oil","title_zh":"后危机复苏：利率下行与油价暴跌","turn_id":"housing:trough:2014-01"},"2015-08-19":{"body":"A 24.5% selloff from August 2015 to February 2016 driven by the August 11, 2015 PBOC yuan devaluation (roughly 2%, the largest in two decades) and the broader 2015-2016 global growth scare. The SSE Composite fell sharply, the DJIA lost over 1,000 points in three days starting August 21, and VIX spiked from 15 to 28. The ctx shows a textbook risk-off rotation: defensives -4.2% vs cyclicals -13.5%, credit spreads (HYG-LQD) blew out -9.9%, and oil crashed another -35.8%. As a high-beta cyclical, the housing chain dropped 24.5% vs SPY's -11.2%, amplifying the global demand panic and fear that a Chinese hard landing would hit US growth.","body_zh":"2015年8月至2016年2月下跌24.5%，导火索是2015年8月11日人民银行人民币贬值约2%（二十年来最大），以及更广泛的2015-2016年全球增长恐慌。上证综指大幅下跌，道指在8月21日起三天内跌逾1000点，VIX从15飙升至28。背景数据显示教科书式避险轮动：防御-4.2% vs 周期-13.5%，信用利差（HYG-LQD）扩大-9.9%，油价再跌-35.8%。作为高贝塔周期股，住房产业链下跌24.5%，大幅逊于SPY的-11.2%，放大了市场对中国硬着陆冲击美国增长的恐慌。","drivers":["PBOC yuan devaluation Aug 11 2015 triggers global risk-off","China hard-landing fears, oil -35.8%","VIX 15 to 28, credit spreads blow out HYG-LQD -9.9%","High-beta housing amplifies cyclical selloff vs SPY"],"drivers_zh":["2015年8月11日人行人民币贬值触发全球避险","中国硬着陆恐慌、油-35.8%","VIX 15至28，信用利差HYG-LQD-9.9%","高贝塔住房放大周期股抛售"],"prev_key":"2015-08-19","prev_key_chain":["2015-08-19"],"status":"exact","title":"China yuan shock triggers global growth scare","title_zh":"人民币汇改冲击引发全球增长恐慌","turn_id":"housing:peak:2015-08"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"The longest and largest rally in this series: +133.5% over nearly two years from the February 2016 global-scare low through January 2018. The recovery was powered in phases: first by the February 2016 stabilization in oil and global growth, then by the November 2016 Trump election sending Financials +93.2% and Industrials +70.6% on infrastructure and deregulation expectations, and finally by the December 2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act. The ctx shows a pure reflation/growth-up quad with cyclicals +71.6% vs defensives +28.8%, VIX collapsing 28 to 11, semis +141.6%, oil +142.2%, and DXY -5.4%. With 30yr mortgage rates held near 4% and housing starts at decade lows, the housing chain was a prime beneficiary of accelerating demand into tight supply.","body_zh":"本系列历时最长、幅度最大的上涨：从2016年2月全球恐慌低点至2018年1月历时近两年涨幅+133.5%。复苏分阶段：首先是2016年2月油价与全球增长企稳，继而是2016年11月特朗普当选推动金融+93.2%、工业+70.6%，源于基础设施与去监管预期，最后是2017年12月《减税与就业法案》。背景数据显示纯再通胀/增长上行象限：周期+71.6% vs 防御+28.8%、VIX从28崩至11、半导体+141.6%、油+142.2%、DXY-5.4%。30年期抵押贷款利率维持在4%附近，住宅开工量处于十年低位，住房产业链是加速需求冲击供给紧缺的最大受益者。","drivers":["Feb 2016 oil/global-growth stabilization ends the scare","Trump election Nov 2016 drives tax-cut and deregulation euphoria","Financials +93.2%, semis +141.6% in a pure growth reflation tape","30yr mortgage near 4%, housing starts at decade lows meet pent-up demand"],"drivers_zh":["2016年2月油价与全球增长企稳，恐慌终结","2016年11月特朗普当选驱动减税去监管热情","金融+93.2%、半导体+141.6%，纯增长再通胀行情","30年期抵押贷款约4%、开工量十年低位遭遇压制需求"],"prev_key":"2016-02-11","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Reflation boom: Trump election and tax cuts power 133% surge","title_zh":"再通胀繁荣：特朗普当选与减税推动133%飙升","turn_id":"housing:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-22":{"body":"A 38.7% selloff over 11 months from January to December 2018 as the Fed hiked four times (FFR from 1.25-1.5% to 2.25-2.5%) and the 30-year mortgage surged from roughly 4% toward 5% by November 2018, directly crushing homebuilder order books and affordability. The ctx shows a flight-to-safety rotation: defensives -5.2% vs cyclicals -21.1%, VIX 11 to 36, DXY +6.8%, oil -33%, TLT barely positive (+1.2%). Housing was the worst major cyclical because rate sensitivity is direct and quantifiable: each 100bp rise in mortgage rates removes hundreds of thousands of buyers. December 2018 Christmas Eve panic (SPY -15.5%) completed the washout.","body_zh":"从2018年1月至12月历时11个月下跌38.7%，美联储四次加息（联邦基金利率从1.25-1.5%升至2.25-2.5%），30年期抵押贷款利率从约4%飙升至2018年11月约5%，直接打垮建筑商订单与购房负担能力。背景数据显示避险轮动：防御-5.2% vs 周期-21.1%、VIX从11升至36、DXY+6.8%、油-33%、TLT勉强收正（+1.2%）。住房是表现最差的主要周期板块，因为利率敏感性直接且可量化：每上升100个基点就将数十万买家排除在外。2018年12月圣诞节前夕恐慌（SPY-15.5%）完成最终洗盘。","drivers":["Fed hikes four times in 2018, FFR toward 2.5%","30yr mortgage surges from 4% to 5%, crushing affordability","Cyclical risk-off: VIX 11 to 36, DXY +6.8%","Dec 2018 Christmas Eve panic completes the washout"],"drivers_zh":["2018年美联储四次加息，联邦基金利率升至约2.5%","30年期抵押贷款从4%飙升至5%，负担能力崩塌","周期股避险：VIX从11升至36、DXY+6.8%","2018年12月圣诞节前夕恐慌完成洗盘"],"prev_key":"2018-01-22","prev_key_chain":["2018-01-22"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-shock bear: mortgages toward 5%, affordability cracks","title_zh":"利率冲击熊市：抵押贷款逼近5%，负担能力崩塌","turn_id":"housing:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"An 88.5% surge from Christmas Eve 2018 to February 2020 as Powell's January 2019 U-turn from four hikes to 'patient' instantly revived housing. The 30-year mortgage fell from 5% back toward 3.5% by late 2019 as the Fed delivered three insurance cuts (July, September, October 2019), and frozen demand unlocked as affordability improved. The ctx shows a tech-led growth tape (semis +87.9%, growth over value +23.3%, TLT +23.9%) with a narrow cap-weight bias (RSP lagged SPY -6.3%), and the housing chain benefited from both falling rates and a tight resale market channeling buyers to new builds. The 88.5% gain nearly matched the concurrent semis rally of +87.9%.","body_zh":"从2018年圣诞节前夕至2020年2月累计上涨88.5%，鲍威尔2019年1月从四次加息急转为耐心立场，立即重燃住房行情。随着美联储三次预防性降息（2019年7月、9月、10月），30年期抵押贷款从5%降至约3.5%，被冻结的购房需求随负担能力改善而释放。背景数据显示科技引领的增长行情（半导体+87.9%、成长跑赢价值+23.3%、TLT+23.9%），大盘股偏斜（RSP跑输SPY-6.3%），住房产业链同时受益于利率下行与二手房市场紧张将买家导向新建房。+88.5%的涨幅几乎与同期半导体+87.9%持平。","drivers":["Powell Jan 2019 pivot to patient: three Fed insurance cuts in 2019","30yr mortgage falls from 5% to 3.5%, affordability surges","Tech-led risk-on: semis +87.9%, VIX 36 to 16","Tight resale inventory channels buyers to new builds"],"drivers_zh":["2019年1月鲍威尔转向耐心，2019年三次预防性降息","30年期抵押贷款从5%降至3.5%，负担能力大幅改善","科技引领风险偏好：半导体+87.9%、VIX从36降至16","二手房库存紧张将买家导向新建房"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell pivot fuels 88% housing recovery into 2020","title_zh":"鲍威尔转向推动88%住房复苏","turn_id":"housing:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-20":{"body":"A 52.1% collapse in just 31 days from February 20 to March 23, 2020 as COVID-19 was declared a global pandemic and markets experienced their fastest bear market on record. The ctx shows an indiscriminate panic: VIX 16 to 62, all sectors crashed (defensives -29.1%, cyclicals -40.1%, energy -56%), credit spreads blew out (HYG-LQD -9.4%). Housing fell 52% vs SPY's -33.4% because the basket carried pre-existing risk: mortgage-REITs faced liquidity crises, supply chains froze, and a demand pause seemed permanent. The CARES Act (signed March 27, 2020, four days after the bottom) introduced mortgage forbearance, but the market had already bottomed on the Fed's unlimited QE announcement of March 23.","body_zh":"从2020年2月20日至3月23日仅31天内暴跌52.1%，新冠疫情被宣布为全球大流行，市场经历有史以来最快的熊市。背景数据显示无差别恐慌：VIX从16飙升至62，所有板块崩溃（防御-29.1%、周期-40.1%、能源-56%），信用利差爆裂（HYG-LQD-9.4%）。住房跌52%逊于SPY的-33.4%，因为板块存在预存风险：抵押贷款REITs面临流动性危机，供应链冻结，需求暂停似乎是永久性的。CARES法案（3月27日签署，即底部后四天）引入抵押贷款宽限期，但市场已在美联储3月23日宣布无限量QE时触底。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic declared, fastest bear market on record","VIX 16 to 62, indiscriminate panic selling across all sectors","Mortgage-REIT liquidity crises amplify housing-chain drawdown","Fed unlimited QE March 23 marks the exact bottom"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情宣布大流行，史上最快熊市","VIX从16升至62，各板块无差别恐慌性抛售","抵押贷款REIT流动性危机放大住房链跌幅","美联储3月23日无限量QE宣布，精准触底"],"prev_key":"2020-02-20","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-20"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash: housing down 52%","title_zh":"COVID疫情崩盘：住房跌52%","turn_id":"housing:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The largest rally in this series: +281% from the March 2020 pandemic low to end-2021, fueled by the most powerful combination of demand and supply catalysts ever seen in US housing. The Fed cut to zero and launched unlimited QE, sending the 30-year mortgage to a record low of 2.65% in January 2021. Work-from-home demand shifted housing preferences toward larger suburban homes. Lumber prices spiked roughly +300% by May 2021 on supply-chain chaos. The ctx shows a pure reflation tape: semis +198.3%, oil +222%, cyclicals +140% vs defensives +76.2%, VIX 62 to 17, DXY -6.7%, with broad participation (RSP beat SPY +14.5%). Builders like DHI and LEN reached all-time highs as order backlogs hit decades-long records.","body_zh":"本系列最大涨幅：从2020年3月疫情低点至2021年底累计+281%，受益于美国住房市场有史以来最强大的供需催化剂组合。美联储降至零利率并启动无限量QE，将30年期抵押贷款推至2021年1月创纪录低点2.65%。居家办公需求将住房偏好转向郊区大户型。木材价格在2021年5月因供应链混乱飙升约+300%。背景数据显示纯再通胀行情：半导体+198.3%、油+222%、周期+140% vs 防御+76.2%、VIX从62降至17、DXY-6.7%、市场广泛参与（RSP跑赢SPY+14.5%）。DHI、LEN等建筑商创历史新高，订单积压达数十年纪录。","drivers":["Fed cuts to zero, 30yr mortgage hits record low 2.65% Jan 2021","Work-from-home demand triggers suburban housing boom","Lumber prices spike ~300%, supply-chain chaos inflates new-home prices","Semis +198%, VIX 62 to 17: pure risk-on reflation across every cyclical"],"drivers_zh":["美联储降至零利率，30年期抵押贷款2021年1月创纪录低点2.65%","居家办公需求引爆郊区住房繁荣","木材价格涨约300%，供应链混乱推高新房售价","半导体+198%、VIX从62降至17：全面风险偏好再通胀行情"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID boom: WFH demand and record-low rates power 281% rally","title_zh":"疫情住房繁荣：居家办公、创纪录低利率推动281%飙升","turn_id":"housing:trough:2020-03"},"2021-12-31":{"body":"Builders fell roughly 38% in H1 2022, far worse than the broad -22.6% SPY, as the Fed's most aggressive hiking cycle in decades sent the 30-year mortgage doubling toward 6% by mid-2022. This was a textbook rate-regime crush: TLT fell -24.0% and the dollar surged (DXY +8.3%), and the most rate-sensitive group on the board led Discretionary's -34% rout into a stagflation-ish quad. With copper/gold rolling over and oil surging +56.3% (Ukraine/energy shock), demand froze and the whole chain from DHI/LEN to Home Depot de-rated on collapsing affordability.","body_zh":"建筑商在2022年上半年下跌约38%，远逊于大盘SPY的-22.6%，因美联储几十年来最激进的加息周期将30年期抵押贷款利率推高近一倍至2022年中6%。这是教科书式的利率压制：TLT下跌-24.0%、美元飙升（DXY+8.3%），这一全场最利率敏感的板块领跌可选消费-34%，进入类滞胀象限。铜金比走弱而油价因乌克兰/能源冲击飙升+56.3%，需求冻结，从DHI/LEN到家得宝的整个链条都因购房负担崩塌而估值下调。","drivers":["Fed launches most aggressive hiking cycle in decades","30yr mortgage doubles toward 6%, affordability collapses","TLT -24.0%, DXY +8.3%: pure rate-regime crush","Stagflation-ish quad: oil +56.3% (Ukraine), value leads growth"],"drivers_zh":["美联储启动数十年来最激进加息周期","30年期抵押贷款翻倍至6%，负担能力崩塌","TLT-24.0%、DXY+8.3%：纯利率压制","类滞胀象限：油+56.3%（乌克兰），价值跑赢成长"],"prev_key":"2021-12-31","prev_key_chain":["2021-12-31"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-hike bear: mortgage shock cracks builders","title_zh":"加息熊市：抵押贷款冲击击垮建筑商","turn_id":"housing:peak:2021-12"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"A 26.2% relief rally from the June 2022 low into mid-August, riding the broad goldilocks/disinflation bounce (SPY +17.7%, SMH +19.5%, VIX 33 to 20, growth over value +8.8) as bond yields paused and the market priced a premature Fed pivot. As the most rate-sensitive group, housing amplified the move and led Discretionary's snap-back with oil falling -26.4% easing inflation fears. The rally ended abruptly when Fed Chair Powell delivered his hawkish Jackson Hole speech on August 26, 2022, explicitly rejecting any near-term pivot and signaling sustained hikes.","body_zh":"从2022年6月低点至8月中旬约26.2%的减压反弹，搭乘大盘金发姑娘/去通胀反弹（SPY+17.7%、SMH+19.5%、VIX 33降至20、成长跑赢价值+8.8），债券收益率暂停，市场押注美联储提前转向。作为最利率敏感的板块，住房放大了这一动作并领涨可选消费反弹，油价-26.4%缓和了通胀担忧。反弹在鲍威尔2022年8月26日发表鹰派杰克逊霍尔讲话后骤然终止，其明确拒绝近期转向并发出持续加息信号。","drivers":["VIX 33 to 20, growth over value +8.8 in a disinflation bounce","Oil falls -26.4%, easing CPI fears and stoking pivot hopes","Rate-sensitive housing amplifies the bear-market bounce","Ended by Powell hawkish Aug 26 Jackson Hole speech"],"drivers_zh":["VIX从33降至20，去通胀反弹中成长跑赢价值+8.8","油价-26.4%缓和CPI担忧，点燃转向预期","利率敏感的住房放大熊市反弹","被鲍威尔8月26日鹰派杰克逊霍尔讲话终结"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Summer bear-market bounce on premature pivot hopes","title_zh":"夏季熊市反弹：押注过早的转向预期","turn_id":"housing:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"A 19.7% selloff into late October 2022 as Powell's August 26 hawkish Jackson Hole speech erased pivot hopes and another rate-regime leg hit: TLT -17.8%, DXY +6.0%, VIX 20 to 30, with 30-year mortgage rates pushing past 7% (~7.08% by end-October) for the first time since 2002. Real Estate XLRe led the laggards at -23.7% alongside housing, as both were directly hit by the rate-shock. The selloff printed the cycle low alongside the broad equity bottom in mid-to-late October, completing a two-leg bear market of roughly 38% peak-to-trough for the housing chain.","body_zh":"到2022年10月下旬下跌19.7%，鲍威尔8月26日鹰派杰克逊霍尔讲话抹去转向预期，又一轮利率冲击来袭：TLT-17.8%、DXY+6.0%、VIX从20升至30，30年期抵押贷款利率突破7%（10月底约7.08%），为2002年以来首次。房地产XLRe以-23.7%领跌，与住房并驾。本轮抛售在10月中下旬与大盘股市底部同步打出周期低点，住房链完成峰谷约38%的两段式熊市。","drivers":["Powell hawkish Aug 26 Jackson Hole speech kills pivot hopes","TLT -17.8%, DXY +6.0%: rate-regime second leg","30yr mortgage pushes past 7%, first time since 2002","VIX 20 to 30, Real Estate leads laggards at -23.7%"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔8月26日鹰派杰克逊霍尔讲话终结转向预期","TLT-17.8%、DXY+6.0%：利率第二段冲击","30年期抵押贷款突破7%，2002年以来首次","VIX从20升至30，房地产领跌-23.7%"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole reset: second rate-shock leg down","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔重置：第二段利率冲击下行","turn_id":"housing:peak:2022-08"},"2022-10-20":{"body":"A powerful 77.6% surge from the October 2022 low through August 2023, riding a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +75.1%, SPY +24.8%, VIX 30 to 16, growth over value +14.2%) and a falling dollar (DXY -9.6%). Because builders trade on the second derivative of rates rather than the level, they front-ran the eventual easing even before mortgage rates fell structurally. As a high-beta cyclical, the group amplified the goldilocks tape (cyclicals +23.5% vs defensives +9.3%). A structural tailwind appeared: with existing-home sellers locked into sub-3% mortgages, the resale market froze and channeled buyers exclusively to new builds, giving DHI and LEN pricing power even at 7% mortgage rates.","body_zh":"从2022年10月低点至2023年8月约77.6%的强劲飙升，搭乘科技/半导体引领的风险偏好融涨（SMH+75.1%、SPY+24.8%、VIX从30降至16、成长跑赢价值+14.2%）与走弱的美元（DXY-9.6%）。由于建筑商交易的是利率的二阶导数而非绝对水平，在抵押贷款利率结构性下行前就已抢跑最终宽松。作为高贝塔周期股，该板块放大了金发姑娘环境（周期+23.5% vs 防御+9.3%）。结构性顺风出现：现有房主锁定在3%以下的低息抵押贷款，二手房市场冻结，买家被独家引导至新建房，使DHI和LEN在7%抵押贷款利率下仍保有定价权。","drivers":["Tech/semis risk-on: SMH +75.1%, VIX 30 to 16, DXY -9.6%","Fed nears the end of its hiking cycle, rate direction reverses","Builders trade rate direction not level, front-run the cut","Frozen resale market lock-in effect channels demand to new builds"],"drivers_zh":["科技/半导体风险偏好：SMH+75.1%、VIX从30降至16、DXY-9.6%","美联储接近加息周期尾声，利率方向逆转","建筑商交易利率方向而非水平，抢跑降息","二手房锁定效应冻结存量市场，需求被导向新建房"],"prev_key":"2022-10-20","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-rates rally: builders front-run the cut","title_zh":"利率见顶反弹：建筑商抢跑降息","turn_id":"housing:trough:2022-10"},"2023-08-07":{"body":"A 20.3% pullback from August to late October 2023 as the 10-year Treasury yield ran toward 5% for the first time since 2007, and the 30-year mortgage touched 8% in October 2023, the first time since 2000. This was a clean rate-regime hit: TLT -12.2%, DXY +4.4%, inside a narrow mega-cap-led tape (RSP lagged SPY -3.8%). As the most rate-sensitive group, housing led the laggards (Real Estate -13.6%, Discretionary -13.1%) and dropped 20.3% vs SPY's -7.0%, with the higher-for-longer Fed narrative eliminating any near-term cut hopes.","body_zh":"从2023年8月至10月下旬下跌20.3%，10年期美债收益率逼近5%（2007年以来首次），30年期抵押贷款利率于2023年10月触及8%，为2000年以来首次。这是一次干净的利率冲击：TLT-12.2%、DXY+4.4%，发生在狭窄的大盘股主导环境中（等权RSP跑输SPY-3.8%）。作为最利率敏感的板块，住房领跌（房地产-13.6%、可选消费-13.1%），下跌20.3%逊于SPY的-7.0%，更高更久的美联储叙事抹去了任何近期降息预期。","drivers":["10yr Treasury runs toward 5% (2007 high), TLT -12.2%","30yr mortgage touches 8%, first time since 2000","DXY +4.4%, narrow mega-cap tape RSP -3.8% vs SPY","Higher-for-longer Fed kills near-term rate-cut pricing"],"drivers_zh":["10年期美债逼近5%（2007年高位），TLT-12.2%","30年期抵押贷款触及8%，2000年以来首次","DXY+4.4%，狭窄大盘股主导（RSP-3.8% vs SPY）","更高更久的美联储预期抹去近期降息定价"],"prev_key":"2023-08-07","prev_key_chain":["2023-08-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Yield spike scare: 10Y toward 5%, mortgage hits 8%","title_zh":"收益率飙升恐慌：10年期逼近5%，抵押贷款触8%","turn_id":"housing:peak:2023-08"},"2023-10-25":{"body":"An 89.8% surge from the October 2023 low through October 2024 on the rare combination of a dovish Fed pivot and a melt-up tape: TLT +17.0% (yields fell), SMH +82.5%, VIX calm at roughly 18, growth over value +11.6%. The Fed's explicit December 2023 pivot (projecting three 2024 cuts) and the actual September 2024 rate cut sent builders DHI and LEN to all-time highs. Financials (+50.8%), Industrials (+44.7%), and Real Estate (+43.9%) led the cyclical surge. Chronic existing-home undersupply from the lock-in effect kept new-build order books full even as mortgage rates remained elevated, and the housing chain rose 89.8% vs SPY's +41.9%.","body_zh":"从2023年10月低点至2024年10月约89.8%的飙升，源于鸽派美联储转向与融涨环境的罕见组合：TLT+17.0%（收益率下行）、SMH+82.5%、VIX平静约18、成长跑赢价值+11.6%。美联储2023年12月明确转向（预测2024年三次降息）与2024年9月实际降息把建筑商DHI和LEN推至历史新高。金融（+50.8%）、工业（+44.7%）与房地产（+43.9%）领涨周期股。锁定效应造成的二手房长期供给不足让新建房订单饱满，即便抵押贷款利率仍处高位，住房链+89.8%大幅跑赢SPY的+41.9%。","drivers":["Fed Dec 2023 pivot: projects three 2024 cuts, TLT +17.0%","Actual Sept 2024 rate cut, SMH +82.5%, risk-on melt-up","Lock-in effect: frozen resale market sustains new-build demand","Financials/Real Estate lead cyclical surge, DHI/LEN to all-time highs"],"drivers_zh":["2023年12月美联储转向：预测三次降息，TLT+17.0%","2024年9月实际降息，SMH+82.5%，风险偏好融涨","锁定效应：二手房市场冻结维持新建房需求","金融/房地产领涨周期股，DHI/LEN创历史新高"],"prev_key":"2023-10-25","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Pivot rally to all-time highs","title_zh":"转向反弹至历史新高","turn_id":"housing:trough:2023-10"},"2024-10-18":{"body":"A 33.8% slide from the October 2024 peak into April 8, 2025. Sticky inflation revived higher-for-longer pricing and pushed mortgage rates back toward 7%, then Trump's April 2025 Liberation Day reciprocal-tariff announcement triggered a historic risk-off flush (VIX 18 to 52, SMH -28.1%, SPHB-SPLV -19.7%) into a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. As a high-beta cyclical with direct input-cost exposure to tariffs on lumber and building materials from Canada and China, builders amplified the drawdown, falling far more than the -14.5% SPY.","body_zh":"从2024年10月高点至2025年4月8日低点下滑33.8%。粘性通胀重燃更高更久定价，抵押贷款利率回升至7%附近，随后特朗普2025年4月解放日对等关税宣布触发历史性避险下泄（VIX 18至52、SMH-28.1%、SPHB-SPLV-19.7%），进入放缓/通缩恐慌象限。作为高贝塔周期股，且直接承受来自加拿大和中国的木材及建材关税投入成本冲击，建筑商放大了回撤，跌幅远超SPY的-14.5%。","drivers":["Sticky inflation revives higher-for-longer, mortgage rates back to 7%","April 2025 Liberation Day tariffs: VIX 18 to 52 panic","Tariff input-cost hit: lumber and materials from Canada and China","SMH -28.1%, SPHB-SPLV -19.7%: high-beta builders amplify the flush"],"drivers_zh":["粘性通胀重燃更高更久，抵押贷款利率回升至7%","2025年4月解放日关税：VIX 18至52恐慌","关税投入成本冲击：来自加拿大和中国的木材/建材","SMH-28.1%、SPHB-SPLV-19.7%：高贝塔建筑商放大下泄"],"prev_key":"2024-10-18","prev_key_chain":["2024-10-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Higher-for-longer plus tariff-shock flush","title_zh":"更高更久叠加关税冲击下泄","turn_id":"housing:peak:2024-10"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"A 37.4% rebound off the April 2025 tariff low into September 2025 as worst-case tariffs were dialed back and rate-cut hopes revived, lifting the group with a tech/semis-led melt-up (SMH +64.8%, SPY +31.1%, VIX 52 to 15, growth over value +19.8%, DXY -5.4%). The tape was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -7.4%) so builders rode the cyclical recovery (cyclicals +28.8% vs defensives +8.1%) rather than leading it; affordability remained the persistent ceiling as mortgage rates stayed elevated.","body_zh":"从2025年4月关税低点至9月约37.4%的反弹，最坏关税情形被回调，降息预期重燃，搭乘科技/半导体引领的融涨（SMH+64.8%、SPY+31.1%、VIX 52至15、成长跑赢价值+19.8%、DXY-5.4%）。市场广度狭窄（等权RSP跑输SPY-7.4%），故建筑商是随周期复苏（周期+28.8% vs 防御+8.1%）而非引领；负担能力仍是持续天花板，抵押贷款利率居高不下。","drivers":["Tech/semis risk-on: SMH +64.8%, VIX 52 to 15, DXY -5.4%","Tariff de-escalation eases lumber and materials input-cost fears","Rate-cut hopes revive through summer 2025","High-beta housing rides cyclical recovery but does not lead"],"drivers_zh":["科技/半导体风险偏好：SMH+64.8%、VIX 52至15、DXY-5.4%","关税降级缓解木材/建材投入成本担忧","2025年夏降息预期重燃","高贝塔住房随周期复苏而非引领"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-tariff recovery on a risk-on melt-up","title_zh":"关税后复苏，搭乘风险偏好融涨","turn_id":"housing:trough:2025-04"},"2025-09-08":{"body":"A 20.3% pullback into late November 2025 as the rate-cut path stalled and the tape rotated risk-off (VIX 15 to 26, defensives +4.6% vs cyclicals -2.3%, DXY +2.8%) into a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Long bonds went nowhere (TLT +0.1%), so this fade was driven by the risk-off rotation and a firmer dollar rather than a yield back-up; with money fleeing to safety (Health +10.3%, Utilities +7.3% leading while Discretionary fell -6.1%), the most rate-sensitive group gave back its summer gains ahead of the 2026 inflation scare.","body_zh":"到2025年11月下旬下跌20.3%，降息路径停滞，市场转向避险（VIX 15至26、防御+4.6% vs 周期-2.3%、DXY+2.8%），进入放缓/通缩恐慌象限。长债基本持平（TLT+0.1%），故此次回落由避险轮动与更坚挺的美元驱动而非收益率回升；资金涌入防御（医疗+10.3%、公用事业+7.3%领涨，可选消费-6.1%），这一最利率敏感的板块在2026年通胀恐慌前吐回夏季涨幅。","drivers":["Risk-off rotation: VIX 15 to 26, defensives +4.6% vs cyclicals -2.3%","Rate-cut path stalls, long yields flat TLT +0.1%","DXY +2.8% headwind, demand softness signals","Defensive rotation to Health and Utilities precedes 2026 oil shock"],"drivers_zh":["避险轮动：VIX 15至26、防御+4.6% vs 周期-2.3%","降息路径停滞，长端收益率持平TLT+0.1%","DXY+2.8%逆风，需求疲软信号","防御轮动至医疗/公用事业，预示2026年油价冲击"],"prev_key":"2025-09-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-09-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Autumn fade as rate-cut path stalls","title_zh":"秋季回落：降息路径停滞","turn_id":"housing:peak:2025-09"},"2025-11-20":{"body":"A 25.3% rally into February 2026 on a calmer rate backdrop and a broadening, reflationary tape (RSP beat SPY +5.8%, DXY -3.3%, cyclicals +14.4% vs defensives +7.1%, SMH +28.0%). Year-end seasonality, brief rate-cut optimism, and materials/energy leading (Materials +27.6%, Energy +24.8%) in a value-over-growth rotation lifted the housing chain alongside the broad cyclical bid. The rally was cut short by the Iran/Hormuz oil shock in early 2026 that reset the inflation picture.","body_zh":"到2026年2月约25.3%的反弹，利率背景趋于平静、市场广度扩散并再通胀（RSP跑赢SPY+5.8%、DXY-3.3%、周期+14.4% vs 防御+7.1%、SMH+28.0%）。年末季节性、短暂降息乐观、材料/能源领涨（材料+27.6%、能源+24.8%）的价值跑赢成长轮动共同提振住房产业链。反弹随后被2026年初伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击终结，通胀图景重置。","drivers":["Broadening reflation: RSP +5.8% vs SPY, Materials +27.6%, Energy +24.8%","DXY -3.3% tailwind, calmer rate backdrop into year-end","Year-end seasonality and brief rate-cut optimism","Value-over-growth rally interrupted by 2026 oil shock"],"drivers_zh":["广度扩散再通胀：RSP+5.8% vs SPY、材料+27.6%、能源+24.8%","DXY-3.3%顺风，年末利率背景趋稳","年末季节性与短暂降息乐观","价值跑赢成长行情被2026年油价冲击打断"],"prev_key":"2025-11-20","prev_key_chain":["2025-11-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Year-end reflation bounce on broadening tape","title_zh":"年末再通胀反弹，市场广度扩散","turn_id":"housing:trough:2025-11"},"2026-02-11":{"body":"A 25.4% selloff into mid-May 2026 as the Iran/Hormuz oil shock sent crude +66.7% and CPI to 4.2%, pushing the Fed back into hiking mode (TLT -4.7%). Even though the broad tape stayed firm (SPY +6.1%, SMH +31.1%) on a narrow mega-cap rally (RSP lagged SPY -6.5%), the 30-year mortgage backed up and housing, the front-line rate-sensitive group, sold off hard -25.4% while the index held. This is the clearest example in the 12-year record of housing decoupling from SPY on a rate shock: SPY +6.1% while housing -25.4%, a 31-point gap.","body_zh":"到2026年5月中旬下跌25.4%，伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击令原油+66.7%、CPI升至4.2%，迫使美联储重回加息（TLT-4.7%）。尽管大盘在狭窄的大盘股领涨下保持坚挺（SPY+6.1%、SMH+31.1%，RSP跑输SPY-6.5%），30年期抵押贷款利率回升，住房这一一线利率敏感板块大幅下跌-25.4%，而指数企稳。这是12年记录中住房与SPY在利率冲击下背离最鲜明的案例：SPY+6.1%而住房-25.4%，相差31个百分点。","drivers":["Iran/Hormuz oil shock: crude +66.7%, CPI to 4.2%","Fed shifts back into hiking mode, TLT -4.7%","30yr mortgage backs up, housing decouples from SPY by 31 points","Narrow mega-cap tape RSP -6.5% vs SPY leaves rate-sensitives behind"],"drivers_zh":["伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击：原油+66.7%、CPI升至4.2%","美联储重回加息模式，TLT-4.7%","30年期抵押贷款利率回升，住房与SPY相差31个百分点","狭窄大盘股主导（RSP-6.5% vs SPY）令利率敏感股落后"],"prev_key":"2026-02-11","prev_key_chain":["2026-02-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil-shock inflation scare backs up mortgages","title_zh":"油价冲击通胀恐慌推高抵押利率","turn_id":"housing:peak:2026-02"},"2026-05-19":{"body":"A 22.5% rebound off the May 2026 low following the mid-June Hormuz ceasefire, which sent oil crashing -35.8% and took the tail risk out of near-term inflation. Falling pump prices let yields ease (TLT +5.6%) at the margin and gave the most beaten-down rate-sensitive group a sharp reflex. The tape showed a stagflation-ish quad (defensives +3.8% vs cyclicals +1.5%, SPY flat -0.4%) but housing's +22.5% outsized gain was entirely rate-relief driven: RSP beat SPY +4.7%, confirming broad participation from oversold names. This is rate relief, not a demand boom, as mortgage rates eased only modestly and affordability remains historically stretched.","body_zh":"从2026年5月低点约22.5%的反弹，源于6月中旬霍尔木兹停火，油价骤跌-35.8%，近期通胀尾部风险解除。油价下行让收益率边际回落（TLT+5.6%），给予这一最受打击的利率敏感板块急促反射。市场呈类滞胀象限（防御+3.8% vs 周期+1.5%、SPY持平-0.4%），但住房+22.5%的超额涨幅完全由利率减压驱动：RSP跑赢SPY+4.7%，印证超卖个股广泛参与。这是利率减压而非需求繁荣，因抵押贷款利率仅温和回落，负担能力仍处历史拉伸水平。","drivers":["Mid-June Hormuz ceasefire: oil -35.8%, inflation tail risk removed","TLT +5.6%: yields ease at the margin, mortgage rates soften","RSP +4.7% vs SPY on a broadening tape, oversold reflex","Rate-relief bounce not a demand cycle: affordability still stretched"],"drivers_zh":["6月中旬霍尔木兹停火：油-35.8%，通胀尾部风险解除","TLT+5.6%：收益率边际回落，抵押贷款利率软化","RSP+4.7% vs SPY，市场广度扩散，超卖反射","利率减压而非需求周期：负担能力仍处历史拉伸水平"],"prev_key":"2026-05-19","prev_key_chain":["2026-05-19"],"status":"exact","title":"Ceasefire rate-relief bounce","title_zh":"停火带来利率减压反弹","turn_id":"housing:trough:2026-05"}},"now":"The Housing Chain sits in an Expansion phase at position 40.2 (RS rank 18), just off its June 2026 peak and in the aftermath of a sharp +22.5% rate-relief rally triggered by the mid-June Hormuz ceasefire. The current reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%, RSP beat SPY +2.9%) is broadly supportive for cyclicals, but housing remains hostage to the mortgage rate path. The stronger DXY (+3.4%) and sticky post-Hormuz CPI mean mortgage rates have not structurally broken lower, so this remains a tactical relief bounce rather than the start of a new affordability recovery cycle. The basket's BUY signal and above-200d posture argue for continuation, but the next CPI print and any Fed hawkishness revision are the binary catalysts that will determine whether this becomes a sustained leg.","now_zh":"住房产业链处于扩张阶段，位置40.2（RS排名第18），刚从2026年6月高点回落，此前因霍尔木兹停火触发了+22.5%的利率减压急促反弹。当前再通胀/增长上行象限（周期+11.2% vs 防御+6.9%、油+19.2%、铜金比+18.3%、RSP跑赢SPY+2.9%）总体利多周期股，但住房走势仍取决于抵押贷款利率路径。美元走强（DXY+3.4%）与停火后粘性CPI意味着抵押贷款利率未能结构性下行，本轮反弹仍属战术性减压，而非新一轮负担能力复苏周期的起点。板块BUY信号与站上200日线支持续涨，但下一个CPI数据及美联储任何鹰派修正都是二元催化剂。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"housing.bubble_peak.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"housing.bubble_peak.v1","arch_state":"missing","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-industrial_distribution":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"The basket gained +8.9% January through June 2014 as yields fell sharply (10-year Treasury dropped from ~3.0% to 2.5%, TLT +10%) driven by a surprise weak Q1 2014 GDP print (-2.9%, third estimate released June 25, 2014), triggering a flight to duration safety. Utilities (+15.5%) and Energy (+11.9%) led while Discretionary (+1.0%) lagged in a stagflation-ish rotation. Crude oil rose ~11% on Iraq supply fears as the ISIS offensive in northern Iraq escalated in June 2014, with Brent peaking above $115/bbl. MRO distributors held up modestly — not the rally leader, but stable industrial activity (U.S. ISM Manufacturing stayed above 50 through H1 2014) provided a floor.","body_zh":"2014年1月至6月，该篮子上涨+8.9%，主因国债收益率大幅下行（10年期从约3.0%降至2.5%，TLT +10%），由Q1 GDP意外萎缩（-2.9%，第三次估值于2014年6月25日公布）和避险追涨久期驱动。公用事业（+15.5%）和能源（+11.9%）领涨，可选消费（+1.0%）垫底，呈现类滞胀风格轮动。原油因伊拉克供应担忧（2014年6月ISIS攻势升级）上涨约11%，布伦特原油一度突破115美元/桶。MRO分销商表现温和——并非领涨方，但美国ISM制造业指数全程守住荣枯线以上的稳定工业活动提供托底。","drivers":["Surprise Treasury bond rally (TLT +10%) on weak Q1 GDP -2.9%","Utilities and yield-proxy sectors led vs cyclicals underperform — stagflation read","Iraq/ISIS oil supply spike (+11%) adds commodity bid through June 2014","Defensives avg +10.6% vs cyclicals avg +7.3%; VIX fell 14 to 11"],"drivers_zh":["Q1 GDP -2.9%意外萎缩引发国债意外牛市（TLT +10%）","公用事业与收益率代理板块领涨，周期股承压——类滞胀读数","伊拉克/ISIS油供冲击（+11%）至2014年6月提供商品端支撑","防御均值+10.6%对周期均值+7.3%；VIX从14降至11"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Bond-yield collapse props MRO in stagflation-ish tape","title_zh":"债券收益率骤降在类滞胀行情中托底MRO板块","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:trough:2014-01"},"2014-06-10":{"body":"A major 19-month selloff of -28.3% from June 2014 through January 2016, driven by three converging shocks: (1) crude oil collapsed from ~$115/barrel in June 2014 to below $30 by January 2016 (-75%), as OPEC voted in November 2014 to maintain production and U.S. shale supply surged; (2) the dollar surged +22.6% on the DXY index as the Fed tapered QE while the ECB and BOJ eased aggressively — the biggest sustained dollar rally since the 1990s; (3) China's manufacturing PMI fell consistently below 50 from mid-2015, triggering a global growth and deflation scare confirmed by the January 2016 circuit-breaker crash in Chinese equities. Defensives led the market (+11.3%) while cyclicals collapsed (-11.1%), Energy fell -44%, and VIX rose from 11 to 28. MRO distributors — exposed to industrial capex, commodity-sector customers, and international revenues — bore the full brunt of the deflation/slowdown regime.","body_zh":"2014年6月至2016年1月长达19个月的-28.3%大跌，由三重冲击叠加驱动：（1）原油从约115美元/桶崩至30美元以下（-75%），因欧佩克2014年11月投票维持产量，叠加美国页岩油供给泛滥；（2）美元DXY飙升+22.6%，因美联储缩减QE而欧央行和日本央行大幅宽松——1990年代以来最大幅度的持续美元上涨；（3）中国制造业PMI从2015年中起持续低于50，2016年1月中国股市熔断崩盘确认全球增长/通缩恐慌。防御股领涨（+11.3%），周期股暴跌（-11.1%），能源最惨（-44%），VIX从11升至28。MRO分销商——暴露于工业资本开支、大宗商品驱动客户及国际收入——在放缓/通缩regime下首当其冲。","drivers":["Oil collapse -74.6% (OPEC Nov 2014 no-cut decision; U.S. shale glut)","Dollar surge +22.6% DXY — largest since 1990s, kills multinational revenues directly","China PMI below 50 from mid-2015; Jan 2016 circuit-breaker crash signals growth scare","VIX 11 to 28; defensives +11.3% vs cyclicals -11.1% flight-to-safety rotation"],"drivers_zh":["油价崩盘-74.6%（欧佩克2014年11月维持产量；美国页岩油过剩）","美元DXY飙升+22.6%——1990年代以来最大幅度，直接摧毁跨国收入","中国PMI从2015年中起低于50；2016年1月熔断崩盘释放增长恐慌","VIX从11升至28；防御+11.3%对周期-11.1%避险轮动"],"prev_key":"2014-06-10","prev_key_chain":["2014-06-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil crash, dollar surge, China deflation scare crush MRO","title_zh":"油价崩盘、美元飙升、中国通缩恐慌重创MRO","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:peak:2014-06"},"2016-01-20":{"body":"From the January 2016 commodity-crash trough, the basket surged +79.9% through March 2017 — its biggest bull leg in the data set. Two catalysts drove it: first, oil rebounded from below $30 to ~$55 (WTI +102.7%) after OPEC struck the Vienna production agreement on November 30, 2016 (the first cut since 2008), lifting commodity-exposed industrial demand broadly; second, Trump's election victory on November 8, 2016 ignited the reflation trade — Financials (+50.9%), Materials (+44.9%), Energy (+44.2%) and Industrials surged on infrastructure-spending expectations, tax reform, and deregulation. VIX fell from 28 to 13, credit spreads tightened sharply (HYG-LQD +14.5%), and the regime was unambiguously reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +41.0% vs defensives +18.5%). Industrial distributors directly benefited from both the commodity-cycle rebound and the reshoring/infrastructure narrative.","body_zh":"从2016年1月大宗商品崩盘低点起，该篮子飙升+79.9%至2017年3月——数据集中最大牛市腿段。两大催化剂驱动：一是原油从30美元以下反弹至约55美元（WTI +102.7%），因欧佩克于2016年11月30日达成维也纳减产协议（2008年以来首次减产），大幅拉升大宗商品端工业需求；二是特朗普于2016年11月8日大选获胜点燃'再通胀交易'——金融（+50.9%）、材料（+44.9%）、能源（+44.2%）和工业股在基础设施开支预期、税改和去监管背景下齐涨。VIX从28降至13，信用利差大幅收窄（HYG-LQD +14.5%），regime无疑是再通胀/增长上行（周期+41.0%对防御+18.5%）。工业分销商直接受益于商品周期反弹和回流/基础设施叙事。","drivers":["OPEC Vienna deal Nov 30 2016: oil rebounds +102.7% from below $30","Trump election Nov 8 2016 reflation trade: infrastructure/tax/deregulation narrative","Financials, Materials, Energy cyclical rotation — cyclicals +41% vs defensives +18.5%","VIX 28 to 13 risk-on; credit spreads tighten HYG-LQD +14.5%"],"drivers_zh":["欧佩克维也纳协议2016年11月30日：油价从30美元以下反弹+102.7%","特朗普2016年11月8日大选后再通胀交易：基础设施/税改/去监管叙事","金融、材料、能源周期轮动——周期+41%对防御+18.5%","VIX 28至13风险偏好；信用利差收窄HYG-LQD +14.5%"],"prev_key":"2016-01-20","prev_key_chain":["2016-01-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump reflation and commodity rebound fuel +80% surge","title_zh":"特朗普再通胀与商品反弹推动+80%涨幅","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:trough:2016-01"},"2017-03-01":{"body":"A -15.1% mid-cycle correction from March through August 2017 as the macro rotation turned stagflation-ish — Tech (+9.6%) and Utilities (+8.8%) led while Financials (-1.3%) and Energy (-12.7%) lagged. Oil dropped -11.9% as the 2016 OPEC production cut failed to clear the global supply glut, weighing on commodity-exposed distributor revenues. The dollar weakened -8.4% (DXY) but the real driver was flow concentration: FAANG stocks dominated performance with semis +11.9% and growth beating value by +8.9%, pulling capital away from cyclical/value names. Yields fell (TLT +7.3%) on softer U.S. growth signals, and equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -2.1% — a classic narrow, mega-cap-led environment where lower-beta MRO names underperform relative to the tape.","body_zh":"2017年3月至8月-15.1%的中周期回调，宏观轮动转向类滞胀——科技（+9.6%）和公用事业（+8.8%）领涨，金融（-1.3%）和能源（-12.7%）垫底。油价因2016年欧佩克减产未能消化全球供给过剩而下跌-11.9%，拖累大宗商品端分销商收入。美元走弱-8.4%（DXY），通常应为顺风，但真正的驱动是资金集中：FAANG股票主导表现，半导体+11.9%，成长>价值+8.9%，资金从周期/价值方向抽离。收益率下行（TLT +7.3%），等权重跑输市值加权-2.1%——经典的狭幅、大盘股主导环境中低贝塔MRO品种跑输大盘。","drivers":["FAANG/Tech leadership (semis +11.9%, growth>value +8.9%) drains cyclical flows","Oil -11.9% on OPEC production-cut failure; commodity demand stalls","Narrow tape: equal-weight -2.1% vs cap-weight; mega-cap-led environment","Yields fall (TLT +7.3%), stagflation-ish regime disfavors cyclical value names"],"drivers_zh":["FAANG/科技主导（半导体+11.9%，成长>价值+8.9%）抽离周期资金","油价-11.9%（欧佩克减产失效）；商品端需求停滞","行情收窄：等权重-2.1%对市值加权；大盘股主导环境","收益率下行（TLT +7.3%），类滞胀regime不利周期价值品种"],"prev_key":"2017-03-01","prev_key_chain":["2017-03-01"],"status":"exact","title":"FAANG rotation and oil drop stall cyclical MRO bid","title_zh":"FAANG轮动与油价下跌拖滞MRO周期买盘","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:peak:2017-03"},"2017-08-24":{"body":"A +48.7% rally from August 2017 through September 2018 driven by the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (TCJA) signed December 22, 2017, cutting the corporate tax rate from 35% to 21% and introducing 100% bonus depreciation for capital expenditures. U.S. business capex surged in H1 2018, directly lifting orders for capital goods and MRO supplies. Discretionary (+34.9%), Tech (+32.1%), and Energy (+23.9%) led in a reflation/growth-up regime (cyclicals +24.3% vs defensives +8.7%). Oil rose +49.3%, VIX stayed at 12 throughout, and credit spreads tightened (HYG-LQD +5.1%); the combination of a tax stimulus-fed capex cycle and a calm volatility environment was the ideal backdrop for MRO distributors serving manufacturing customers spending on plant, equipment and maintenance.","body_zh":"2017年8月至2018年9月+48.7%的涨幅，由2017年12月22日签署的《减税与就业法案》（TCJA）驱动——企业所得税率从35%降至21%，并引入资本开支100%加速折旧。2018年上半年美国企业资本开支大幅增长，直接拉升资本货物和MRO物资订单。可选消费（+34.9%）、科技（+32.1%）和能源（+23.9%）领涨，呈现再通胀/增长上行regime（周期+24.3%对防御+8.7%）。油价+49.3%，VIX全程维持12，信用利差收窄（HYG-LQD +5.1%）；税改驱动的资本开支周期叠加平稳波动率环境，是MRO分销商服务于制造业客户进行厂房、设备和维护支出的理想背景。","drivers":["TCJA Dec 22 2017: corp rate cut 35% to 21% + 100% capex bonus depreciation","U.S. capex boom H1 2018 lifts capital goods and MRO orders directly","Oil +49.3% and reflation growth-up: cyclicals +24.3% vs defensives +8.7%","VIX at 12, credit spreads tight — calm risk environment sustains cyclical melt-up"],"drivers_zh":["TCJA 2017年12月22日：企业税率降至21%+资本开支100%加速折旧","2018年上半年美国资本开支热潮，直接拉升资本货物与MRO订单","油价+49.3%，再通胀增长上行：周期+24.3%对防御+8.7%","VIX维持12，信用利差收紧——平稳风险环境维持周期性融涨"],"prev_key":"2017-08-24","prev_key_chain":["2017-08-24"],"status":"exact","title":"TCJA tax-cut capex boom propels +49% rally","title_zh":"TCJA税改资本开支热潮推动+49%涨幅","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:trough:2017-08"},"2018-09-20":{"body":"A sharp -25.5% crash from September 20 through December 24, 2018 — the worst quarterly selloff since 2008 — triggered by two converging forces: (1) the Fed raised rates four times in 2018, with the September 26 and December 19 hikes pushing the funds rate to 2.25-2.50%; Powell's commentary signaled further tightening on autopilot, causing VIX to spike from 12 to 36; (2) the Trump administration imposed 10% tariffs on $200B of Chinese goods effective September 24, 2018, threatening a step-up to 25%, hitting industrial supply chains directly. Cyclicals crashed -23.1% vs defensives -8.7%, with Industrials (-23.6%) and Energy (-27.2%) worst hit. Oil fell -39.9% on OPEC output increase and demand fears. For MRO distributors, rising input costs, supply-chain disruption fears, and demand uncertainty from manufacturing customers facing margin pressure converged simultaneously.","body_zh":"2018年9月20日至12月24日-25.5%的急跌——2008年以来最差单季——由两股力量交汇引发：（1）美联储2018年四次加息，9月26日和12月19日加息将联邦基金利率推至2.25-2.50%，鲍威尔暗示继续'自动驾驶'紧缩，VIX从12飙至36；（2）特朗普政府于2018年9月24日对2000亿美元中国商品征收10%关税，并威胁提至25%，直接冲击工业供应链。周期股暴跌-23.1%对防御-8.7%，工业（-23.6%）和能源（-27.2%）损失最重。油价因欧佩克增产叠加需求担忧下跌-39.9%。对MRO分销商而言，投入成本上升、供应链中断担忧与面临利润压力的制造业客户需求不确定性同时叠加。","drivers":["Fed four 2018 rate hikes; Sept 26 + Dec 19 hikes; VIX 12 to 36 risk-off crash","U.S.-China trade war: $200B Chinese goods tariffed at 10% effective Sept 24 2018","Oil -39.9% on OPEC output increase + global demand slowdown fears","Cyclicals -23.1% vs defensives -8.7%; Industrials sector down -23.6%"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2018年四次加息；9月26日+12月19日加息；VIX从12升至36","中美贸易战：2018年9月24日对2000亿美元中国商品征收10%关税","油价-39.9%（欧佩克增产+全球需求放缓担忧）","周期股-23.1%对防御-8.7%；工业板块-23.6%"],"prev_key":"2018-09-20","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade war and Fed over-tightening crash cyclicals -26%","title_zh":"贸易战+美联储过度紧缩重创周期股-26%","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"The +43.3% rally from Christmas Eve 2018 through January 2, 2020 was powered by the Fed's complete reversal: Chair Powell pivoted dovishly in early January 2019, dropping the 'autopilot' rate-hike language, then delivered three insurance cuts in July, September, and October 2019. U.S.-China tensions eased as Phase One trade deal negotiations advanced through 2019, with the deal announced December 13, 2019, removing supply-chain uncertainty for industrial distributors. Tech (+64.2%), Financials (+42.2%), and Comm (+40.4%) led in a reflation/growth-up regime (cyclicals +39.6% vs defensives +29.6%); semis surged +81.4% and growth beat value by +13.9%. VIX fell from 36 to 12, and oil recovered +43.9% as demand stabilized.","body_zh":"2018年圣诞夜至2020年1月2日+43.3%的涨幅，由美联储彻底逆转驱动：鲍威尔于2019年1月初转向鸽派，撤销'自动驾驶'加息措辞，并于2019年7月、9月、10月三次预防性降息。中美紧张关系随第一阶段贸易谈判推进而缓和，2019年12月13日宣布协议，消除工业分销商的供应链不确定性。科技（+64.2%）、金融（+42.2%）和通信（+40.4%）领涨，呈现再通胀/增长上行regime（周期+39.6%对防御+29.6%）；半导体暴涨+81.4%，成长跑赢价值+13.9%。VIX从36降至12，油价随需求稳定回升+43.9%。","drivers":["Fed pivot Jan 2019: rate-hike autopilot suspended; three insurance cuts Jul-Oct 2019","U.S.-China Phase One deal Dec 13 2019 removes supply-chain uncertainty for distributors","VIX 36 to 12 risk-on recovery; semis +81.4%, growth>value +13.9%","Oil +43.9% demand recovery; credit markets normalized post-crash"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月转向：暂停自动加息；7-10月三次预防性降息","中美第一阶段贸易协议2019年12月13日消除分销商供应链不确定性","VIX 36至12风险偏好修复；半导体+81.4%，成长>价值+13.9%","油价+43.9%需求复苏；崩盘后信用市场正常化"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot and Phase One trade deal fuel recovery +43%","title_zh":"美联储转向与第一阶段贸易协议推动+43%复苏","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:trough:2018-12"},"2020-01-02":{"body":"A -41.1% crash from January 2 through March 23, 2020 — the fastest bear market in history — as COVID-19 forced global economic lockdowns. WHO declared a public health emergency January 30 and a pandemic March 11; NYSE circuit breakers triggered four times in March. Industrials fell -40.8%, Financials -42.7%, and Energy -60.2% as factories shuttered and supply chains froze. MRO distributors faced simultaneous demand collapse (customers closed) and supply disruption (Chinese manufacturing halted). VIX spiked to 62 (intraday 82.69 on March 16), the dollar strengthened +5.8%, and oil crashed -61.8% on demand destruction plus the Saudi-Russia oil price war launched March 8, 2020. Defensives fell -25.7% but outperformed cyclicals at -39.2% in a flight-to-safety where nothing was truly safe.","body_zh":"2020年1月2日至3月23日-41.1%的暴跌——史上最快熊市——新冠疫情迫使全球经济封锁。世卫组织1月30日宣布公共卫生紧急状态，3月11日宣布大流行；纽交所3月四次触发熔断。工厂停工、供应链冻结，工业板块-40.8%，金融-42.7%，能源-60.2%。MRO分销商同时面临需求崩塌（客户关闭）和供应中断（中国制造停摆）。VIX飙至62（3月16日盘中高点82.69），美元走强+5.8%，油价因需求毁灭叠加2020年3月8日沙特-俄罗斯价格战暴跌-61.8%。防御股跌-25.7%但跑赢周期的-39.2%，是一场无真正安全区的避险轮动。","drivers":["COVID-19 global lockdowns: WHO emergency Jan 30, pandemic Mar 11 2020","NYSE circuit breakers triggered 4x in March; VIX intraday peak 82.69 on Mar 16","Oil -61.8%: demand destruction + Saudi-Russia oil price war launched Mar 8 2020","Industrials -40.8%, Energy -60.2%; MRO demand and supply simultaneously collapsed"],"drivers_zh":["新冠全球封锁：世卫组织1月30日紧急状态，3月11日大流行","纽交所3月四次熔断；VIX盘中峰值82.69（3月16日）","油价-61.8%：需求毁灭+2020年3月8日沙特-俄罗斯价格战","工业-40.8%，能源-60.2%；MRO需求与供应双双崩溃"],"prev_key":"2020-01-02","prev_key_chain":["2020-01-02"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic shock: -41% industrial demand collapse","title_zh":"新冠疫情冲击：-41%工业需求骤然崩塌","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The largest bull leg in the data set: +222.7% from the March 23, 2020 COVID trough through November 16, 2021. The CARES Act ($2.2T, signed March 27, 2020), American Rescue Plan ($1.9T, signed March 2021), and Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act (signed November 2021) flooded the economy with fiscal stimulus. The Fed cut rates to 0% on March 15 and launched unlimited QE on March 23, 2020. VIX fell from 62 to 16, oil rebounded +245.7%, copper-gold ratio surged +87.3%, and credit markets healed. Cyclicals dominated (+141.0% vs defensives +65.3%) in the broadest breadth rally in decades (RSP-SPY +16.3%). MRO distributors benefited from the full reopening cycle: pent-up maintenance spending, nonresidential construction surge, supply-chain restock demand, and pricing power as input-cost inflation allowed margin expansion. Grainger and Fastenal both reported double-digit organic revenue growth through 2021.","body_zh":"数据集中最大牛市腿段：从2020年3月23日新冠低点至2021年11月16日大涨+222.7%。《关爱法案》（2.2万亿，2020年3月27日签署）、《美国救援计划》（1.9万亿，2021年3月签署）和《基础设施投资与就业法案》（2021年11月签署）将经济浸泡于财政洪水之中。美联储于2020年3月15日将利率降至零，并于3月23日启动无限量QE。VIX从62降至16，油价反弹+245.7%，铜金比飙升+87.3%，信用市场愈合。周期股主导（+141.0%对防御+65.3%），是数十年来参与度最广的行情（RSP-SPY +16.3%）。MRO分销商受益于全面重开周期：积压的维护开支、非住宅建设繁荣、供应链补库需求，以及投入成本通胀带来的定价权与利润率扩张。格雷杰和法士特均于2021年全年报告两位数有机收入增长。","drivers":["CARES Act $2.2T + ARP $1.9T fiscal flood; Fed zero rates and unlimited QE Mar 2020","V-shaped MRO restock: pent-up maintenance demand, nonres construction boom, pricing power","Oil +245.7%, copper-gold +87.3%; cyclicals +141% vs defensives +65.3%","Broadest market participation in years (RSP-SPY +16.3%); VIX 62 to 16"],"drivers_zh":["《关爱法案》2.2万亿+《美国救援计划》1.9万亿财政洪水；美联储零利率与无限量QE 2020年3月","V型MRO补库：积压维护需求、非住宅建设繁荣、定价权","油价+245.7%，铜金比+87.3%；周期+141%对防御+65.3%","史上最广泛市场参与度（RSP-SPY +16.3%）；VIX 62至16"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID recovery: fiscal flood, restock, and reflation +223%","title_zh":"新冠复苏：财政洪水、补库存与再通胀+223%","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-16":{"body":"A -25.1% selloff from November 16, 2021 through June 17, 2022 as the inflation reality overwhelmed equities. CPI hit a 40-year high of 9.1% in June 2022; the Fed pivoted hawkish with Powell endorsing accelerated QE taper at Congressional testimony November 30, 2021 (and retiring the word 'transitory'), then delivered hikes from March 2022 onward, taking the fed funds rate from 0 to 1.50-1.75% by June 2022. TLT fell -22.0% (yields surged), DXY rose +9.2%, and VIX went 16 to 31. The Omicron variant fears in late November 2021 added a growth-scare layer. Energy (+29.3%) was the lone winner on supply constraints; defensives held (-5.3%) while cyclicals collapsed (-14.6%). MRO distributors de-rated on multiple compression from rising discount rates even as short-cycle industrial demand held firm — a classic rate-shock bear where fundamentals are fine but the valuation regime changes.","body_zh":"2021年11月16日至2022年6月17日-25.1%的大跌，通胀现实压倒股市。CPI于2022年6月触及40年高位9.1%；美联储于2021年11月30日国会听证会上背书加速缩减（并宣布弃用'暂时性'一词），随后自2022年3月起连续加息，至2022年6月将联邦基金利率从0推至1.50-1.75%。TLT下跌-22.0%（收益率飙升），DXY升+9.2%，VIX从16升至31。2021年11月底Omicron变种担忧叠加增长恐慌层。能源（+29.3%）是供给约束下唯一赢家；防御守住（-5.3%），周期股崩溃（-14.6%）。MRO分销商因贴现率上升导致的估值倍数压缩而下跌，即便短周期工业需求保持稳健——典型的利率冲击熊市：基本面无碍，但估值体制转换。","drivers":["Fed hawkish pivot Nov 30 2021 (taper acceleration, 'transitory' retired)","CPI 40-year high 9.1% in June 2022; TLT -22.0%, yields surge","Dollar +9.2% DXY headwind for multinational distributors","VIX 16 to 31; cyclicals -14.6% vs defensives -5.3% rate-shock de-rate"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2021年11月30日鹰派转向（加速缩减，弃用'暂时性'）","CPI 2022年6月40年高位9.1%；TLT -22.0%，收益率飙升","美元DXY +9.2%对跨国分销商构成阻力","VIX 16至31；周期-14.6%对防御-5.3%利率冲击去估值"],"prev_key":"2021-11-16","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed taper shock and rate surge de-rate cyclicals -25%","title_zh":"美联储缩减冲击与收益率飙升压制周期股-25%","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:peak:2021-11"},"2022-06-17":{"body":"A sharp +26.3% relief rally from June 17 through August 16, 2022 as beaten-down markets priced in a premature Fed pivot. Oil fell -21.0% (signaling disinflation), VIX dropped from 31 to 20, and growth stocks bounced (growth>value +7.2, semis +18.5%). Discretionary (+27.4%), Tech (+21.6%), and Utilities (+20.6%) led in a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation regime — the brief window when markets thought rate hikes were nearly done. Cyclicals (+16.4%) and defensives (+15.2%) moved almost in lockstep, confirming this was a broad oversold bounce rather than a genuine cycle change. MRO distributor fundamentals remained solid (Grainger Q2 2022 reported 20%+ organic growth) providing a floor under the rally, but the move was primarily multiple-expansion as VIX compressed from 31 to 20.","body_zh":"2022年6月17日至8月16日+26.3%的急速反弹，市场过早定价美联储转向。油价下跌-21.0%（释放去通胀信号），VIX从31降至20，成长股反弹（成长>价值+7.2，半导体+18.5%）。可选消费（+27.4%）、科技（+21.6%）和公用事业（+20.6%）领涨，呈现goldilocks/增长上行去通胀格局——市场短暂认为加息接近尾声的窗口。周期（+16.4%）与防御（+15.2%）几乎同步，确认这是广泛的超卖反弹而非真实的周期转变。MRO分销商基本面保持稳健（格雷杰2022年Q2有机增长逾20%）提供托底，但涨幅主要来自VIX从31压缩至20驱动的估值倍数扩张。","drivers":["Premature 'Fed pause' expectations — markets price disinflation/pivot","Oil -21.0% signals disinflation; VIX 31 to 20 risk-on bounce","Goldilocks regime: growth>value +7.2, semis +18.5%; broad participation","Solid MRO fundamentals (Grainger/Fastenal double-digit organic growth) as floor"],"drivers_zh":["过早的'美联储暂停'预期——市场定价去通胀/转向","油价-21.0%释放去通胀信号；VIX 31至20风险偏好反弹","Goldilocks格局：成长>价值+7.2，半导体+18.5%；广泛参与","稳健的MRO基本面（格雷杰/法士特两位数有机增长）托底行情"],"prev_key":"2022-06-17","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-17"],"status":"exact","title":"Bear market relief bounce on premature Fed-pause hopes","title_zh":"过早的美联储暂停预期引发熊市中途反弹","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"A -17.9% selloff from August 16 through September 26, 2022, directly catalyzed by Fed Chair Powell's deliberately brief but maximally hawkish ~8-minute speech at Jackson Hole on August 26, 2022. Powell explicitly rejected the easy-disinflation narrative, warned the fight would bring 'some pain' to households and businesses, and signaled the Fed would hold rates high. Bond yields spiked (TLT -10.4%), the dollar strengthened +7.1% (DXY), and VIX shot from 20 to 32. The market had bought the July FOMC's implied pivot signal, and Jackson Hole unwound it violently. Tech (-18.5%), Comm (-19.2%), and Real Estate (-19.3%) were hardest hit; defensives (Health -8.9%, Utilities -9.1%, Staples -9.4%) relative outperformed. MRO distributors fell -17.9% — lower beta than speculative themes, confirming quality cyclical characteristics at work.","body_zh":"2022年8月16日至9月26日-17.9%的大跌，直接由美联储主席鲍威尔于2022年8月26日在杰克逊霍尔发表的刻意简短却极度鹰派的约8分钟演讲引发。鲍威尔明确否定'软着陆很容易'的叙事，警告抗通胀将给家庭和企业带来'一些痛苦'，并暗示将长期维持高利率。债券收益率飙升（TLT -10.4%），美元走强+7.1%（DXY），VIX从20升至32。市场此前买入了7月FOMC隐含的转向信号，杰克逊霍尔将其猛烈拆解。科技（-18.5%）、通信（-19.2%）和房地产（-19.3%）损失最重；防御股（医疗-8.9%、公用事业-9.1%、必需消费-9.4%）相对跑赢。MRO分销商下跌-17.9%——低于投机主题的贝塔，验证了优质周期特性的作用。","drivers":["Powell Jackson Hole Aug 26 2022: hawkish ~8-min speech, 'some pain' for households","Bond yields spike (TLT -10.4%); dollar +7.1% DXY; VIX 20 to 32","July FOMC pivot narrative completely unwound — rate-regime reset","Defensives -9.1% vs cyclicals -15.1%; lower-beta MRO absorbs less damage"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔：鹰派约8分钟演讲，释放家庭'一些痛苦'信号","债券收益率飙升（TLT -10.4%）；美元DXY +7.1%；VIX 20至32","7月FOMC转向叙事被彻底拆解——利率体制重置","防御-9.1%对周期-15.1%；低贝塔MRO吸收较少伤害"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkish reset triggers -18% flush","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派重置触发-18%冲刷","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:peak:2022-08"},"2022-09-26":{"body":"The longest recent bull leg: +99.9% from September 26, 2022 through November 25, 2024, spanning 26 months. The October 2022 CPI print (7.7% vs ~7.9% feared, released November 10, 2022) triggered the initial massive rally — the S&P 500 jumped +5.5% in one session. Through 2023-2024, the AI infrastructure buildout (hyperscaler capex crossing $200B in 2024), the CHIPS Act and IRA (driving $800B+ in announced U.S. manufacturing investment), and the reshoring/electrification construction wave created a sustained demand tailwind for MRO distributors. Tech (+93.3%), Comm (+105.7%), and Industrials (+76.8%) led; growth beat value +34.6%; semis surged +160.8%. VIX fell 32 to 15, dollar weakened -6.4% (a clean tailwind), and the goldilocks regime (disinflation + durable growth) persisted through the 2024 soft landing narrative.","body_zh":"近期最长牛市腿段：2022年9月26日至2024年11月25日+99.9%，历时26个月。2022年10月CPI数据（7.7%，低于市场担忧的约7.9%，2022年11月10日公布）触发最初的大幅上涨——标普500单日跳涨+5.5%。2023-2024年间，AI基础设施建设（超大规模资本开支2024年突破2000亿美元）、《芯片法案》和《通胀削减法案》（带动逾8000亿美元美国制造业投资宣布）以及回流/电气化建设浪潮为MRO分销商创造持续需求顺风：在建工厂需要维护物资、电气元件和资本货物。科技（+93.3%）、通信（+105.7%）和工业（+76.8%）领涨；成长跑赢价值+34.6%；半导体暴涨+160.8%。VIX从32降至15，美元走弱-6.4%（干净顺风），Goldilocks格局（去通胀+持久增长）贯穿2024年软着陆叙事。","drivers":["CPI cooler Nov 10 2022 (7.7% vs ~7.9% feared) triggers initial surge; disinflation takes hold","AI/CHIPS Act/IRA reshoring: $800B+ U.S. manufacturing capex feeds MRO demand directly","Goldilocks regime: semis +160.8%, growth>value +34.6%, VIX 32 to 15","Dollar -6.4% DXY clean tailwind; 2024 soft landing extends the runway"],"drivers_zh":["2022年11月10日CPI低于预期（7.7%对担忧的约7.9%）触发初始大涨；去通胀叙事确立","AI/《芯片法案》/《通胀削减法案》回流：逾8000亿美元美国制造业资本开支直接喂养MRO需求","Goldilocks格局：半导体+160.8%，成长>价值+34.6%，VIX 32至15","美元DXY -6.4%干净顺风；2024年软着陆延长跑道"],"prev_key":"2022-09-26","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Goldilocks melt-up: disinflation, reshoring, and AI power demand","title_zh":"Goldilocks融涨：去通胀+回流制造+AI电力需求","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:trough:2022-09"},"2024-11-25":{"body":"A -27.1% selloff from November 25, 2024 through April 8, 2025 as Trump's second-term trade policy escalated sharply. The April 2, 2025 'Liberation Day' executive order imposed a baseline 10% tariff on nearly all imports (effective April 5) with higher reciprocal rates on major trading partners (effective April 9), sending the S&P 500 down ~12% in four days and VIX to 52 — the highest since the 2020 COVID crash. For industrial distributors specifically, the tariff fears were direct: tariffs raise input costs for MRO products (many sourced from China and Asia), disrupt supply chains, and crimp capex spending from manufacturing customers facing margin pressure. Defensives held better (-7.6%) vs cyclicals (-18.9%), Tech led losses (-22.8%), and semis fell -25.8%. The basket's -27.1% was shallower than the high-beta industrial themes' -33%+, confirming the quality/lower-beta cushion.","body_zh":"2024年11月25日至2025年4月8日-27.1%的大跌，特朗普第二任期贸易政策急剧升级。2025年4月2日'解放日'行政令对几乎所有进口商品征收10%基准关税（4月5日生效），对主要贸易伙伴征收更高对等税率（4月9日生效），标普500四个交易日暴跌约12%，VIX升至52——2020年新冠崩盘以来最高。对工业分销商而言，关税威胁直接而具体：关税推高MRO产品投入成本（大量从中国和亚洲采购），扰乱供应链，并压制面临利润压力的制造业客户的资本开支。防御股守住（-7.6%）优于周期（-18.9%），科技领跌（-22.8%），半导体-25.8%。该篮子-27.1%浅于高贝塔工业主题的-33%+，验证了优质/低贝塔的缓冲效果。","drivers":["Trump Liberation Day Apr 2 2025: 10% blanket tariffs + reciprocal rates; VIX spikes to 52","Tariffs directly raise MRO input costs and disrupt Asia/China supply chains","VIX 15 to 52 panic; SPHB-SPLV -21.0%; cyclicals -18.9% vs defensives -7.6%","Lower-beta quality character (-27%) cushions vs high-beta industrial peers (-33%+)"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普'解放日'2025年4月2日：10%一揽子关税+对等税率；VIX飙至52","关税直接推高MRO投入成本，扰乱亚洲/中国供应链","VIX 15至52恐慌；SPHB-SPLV -21.0%；周期-18.9%对防御-7.6%","低贝塔优质品种（-27%）相对高贝塔工业同行（-33%+）提供缓冲"],"prev_key":"2024-11-25","prev_key_chain":["2024-11-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Liberation Day tariff crash: input cost and demand fears -27%","title_zh":"解放日关税崩盘：投入成本与需求担忧-27%","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:peak:2024-11"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"The current leg: +58.0% from the April 8, 2025 trough through June 25, 2026. Trump's April 9 announcement of a 90-day tariff pause triggered the S&P 500's largest single-day gain since 2008 (+9.5%), igniting the recovery. The subsequent macro regime has been unambiguously reflation/growth-up (oil +20.7%, copper-gold +11.3%, cyclicals +51.4% vs defensives +20.4%) with VIX compressing from 52 to 19. Tech hyperscaler capex continued at record pace (over $200B in 2024, growing strongly into 2025), driving AI data center and electrification construction demand directly into MRO distributors' addressable market. The basket gained +58% vs the broader market's +49.6% (outperforming SPY) and the Industrials sector's +60.3% (roughly in line) — steady late-cycle compounder behavior rather than AI-beta torque. Narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -8.8%) confirms a mega-cap-led tape, but the reflation mandate keeps cyclical distributors well-bid.","body_zh":"当前腿段：从2025年4月8日低点至2026年6月25日+58.0%。特朗普4月9日宣布90天关税暂停，触发标普500自2008年以来最大单日涨幅（+9.5%），点燃复苏。随后宏观regime明确转向再通胀/增长上行（油价+20.7%，铜金比+11.3%，周期+51.4%对防御+20.4%），VIX从52压缩至19。科技超大规模资本开支继续创纪录（2024年逾2000亿美元，2025年强劲增长），驱动AI数据中心和电气化建设需求直接流入MRO分销商的可寻址市场。该篮子+58%对比大盘+49.6%（跑赢SPY）和工业板块+60.3%（大致持平）——稳健的后周期复利特性而非AI贝塔弹性。市场广度偏窄（RSP-SPY -8.8%）确认大盘股主导行情，但再通胀授权持续支撑周期性分销商的买盘。","drivers":["April 9 2025 tariff 90-day pause triggers S&P 500 largest single-day gain since 2008 (+9.5%)","Reflation/growth-up regime: oil +20.7%, copper-gold +11.3%; VIX 52 to 19 compression","AI/electrification/reshoring construction demand feeds Grainger/Fastenal addressable market","Industrials sector +60.3% leads; lower-beta basket compounds at steady +58%"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月9日关税90天暂停触发标普500自2008年以来最大单日涨幅（+9.5%）","再通胀/增长上行regime：油价+20.7%，铜金比+11.3%；VIX 52至19压缩","AI/电气化/回流建设需求直接流入格雷杰/法士特可寻址市场","工业板块+60.3%领涨；低贝塔篮子稳健复利+58%"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff pause recovery: reflation regime lifts cyclicals +58%","title_zh":"关税暂停复苏：再通胀regime抬升周期股+58%","turn_id":"industrial_distribution:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Industrial Distribution & Capital Goods (Grainger/Fastenal-type MRO distributors, equipment rental, short-cycle tooling) is in an Expansion/Trending phase at RS-rank #17 (pos 67.2), up +58% off the April-8, 2025 tariff-crash low in an explosive reflation/growth-up regime (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, equal-weight beating cap-weight +2.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%). The basket is the late-cycle quality compounder within XLI — Industrials sector (up 15.8%) ranks third among SPDR sectors behind Tech and Energy, and the thesis is straightforward: restock + nonresidential construction + AI/electrification/reshoring picks-and-shovels demand. A stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%) is a mild headwind for multinational revenues, but the broad reflation mandate is clearly intact. With VIX compressing from 52 to 14-18 and high-beta outpacing low-vol by +20.7%, risk appetite remains open; the basket delivers steady, lower-beta cyclical returns rather than parabolic AI torque — which is precisely why it holds its positioning (RS #17) rather than leading, but also cushions against speculative unwinds.","now_zh":"工业分销与资本品板块（格雷杰/法士特型MRO分销商、设备租赁、短周期工具）处于扩张/趋势阶段，相对强度排名第17（位置67.2），较2025年4月8日关税崩盘低点上涨58%，当前处于爆发性再通胀/增长上行regime（周期股+11.2%对防御+6.9%，等权重跑赢市值加权+2.9%，油价+19.2%，铜金比+18.3%）。该篮子是XLI工业股中的后周期优质复利品种——工业板块（+15.8%）在标普行业ETF中位列第三，仅次于科技与能源，核心逻辑是：补库存+非住宅建设需求+AI/电气化/回流制造的\"锄头与镐\"需求。美元走强（DXY +3.4%）对跨国收入构成温和阻力，但宏观再通胀信号依然清晰。随着VIX从52压缩至14-18，高贝塔跑赢低波动+20.7%，风险偏好窗口保持开放；该篮子提供稳健、低贝塔的周期回报而非抛物线AI弹性——这正是其相对强度排名第17而非领涨的原因，但也使其在投机性逆转中更具抗跌性。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"business.cycle_trough.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"business.cycle_trough.v1","arch_state":"missing","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-insurance":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"From January 2014 through September 2018, Insurance & Brokers compounded +86.6% (vs SPY +75.3%) in a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation regime -- VIX calm (14 to 12), oil -24.7%, dollar +16.6%, TLT +29.3% as yields fell. Three structural engines powered the sector: (1) The ACA, effective January 2014, enrolled millions into health insurer books, with marketplace premiums roughly doubling between 2013 and 2017 on government-backed tax credits, lifting health insurer stocks sharply through the period; (2) P&C underwriting delivered multiple years of profitable combined ratios sub-100 on benign catastrophe losses and disciplined pricing; (3) the November 2016 Trump election fueled a strong 2016 KIE return as financials surged on deregulation hopes and the 10-year yield spiked from ~1.85% to ~2.6%, with the 2017 hurricane season (Harvey/Irma/Maria, ~$95bn insured losses) absorbed without a credit event and actually seeding the 2018-2019 hard market. This was a broad-market lift with insurance as a steady compounder, not a defensive rotation -- consistent with cyclicals and defensives nearly tied (+67.9% vs +65.9%).","body_zh":"2014年1月至2018年9月，保险与经纪在黄金时代/增长向上去通胀环境中累计+86.6%（vs SPY +75.3%）——VIX平稳（14至12）、原油-24.7%、美元+16.6%、TLT +29.3%（收益率下行）。三大结构性引擎驱动：（1）2014年1月生效的ACA将数百万新参保者纳入健康险业务，2013至2017年市场保费在政府税收抵免托底下大致翻倍，健康险股票期间显著上涨；（2）P&C承保连续多年实现盈利（综合成本率低于100），巨灾损失温和，定价纪律严格；（3）2016年11月特朗普当选推动KIE全年强劲上涨，金融股因去监管预期飙涨，10年期国债收益率从约1.85%升至约2.6%，2017年飓风季（哈维/艾尔玛/玛利亚，约950亿美元承保损失）被市场消化，并为2018-2019年硬市场埋下伏笔。这是大盘普涨拉动的行情，保险作为稳健复利标的受益，而非防御性轮动——与周期股和防御股几乎并驾（+67.9%对+65.9%）相符。","drivers":["ACA enrollment boom drove health insurer premium growth","Benign P&C cat losses: sub-100 combined ratio 2014-2016","Nov 2016 Trump election rate spike (10Y ~1.85% to ~2.6%)","Goldilocks VIX 14-12: broad risk-on melt-up","2017 cat losses seeded hard market rate hardening"],"drivers_zh":["ACA入保潮推动健康险保费增长","巨灾损失温和：2014-2016年综合成本率低于100%","2016年11月特朗普当选，10年期利率从约1.85%升至约2.6%","VIX 14-12黄金时代：全市场风险偏好融涨","2017年飓风季巨灾损失为硬市场硬定价埋下伏笔"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"ACA tailwind plus goldilocks 4.5-year melt-up","title_zh":"ACA顺风叠加黄金时代4.5年融涨","turn_id":"insurance:trough:2014-01"},"2018-09-21":{"body":"Insurance & Brokers fell -15.7% (September 21 to December 24, 2018), in line with SPY's -19.3% peak-to-trough, in a flight-to-safety rotation where defensives lost only -8.9% while cyclicals crashed -23.1%, VIX spiked 12 to 36, and oil collapsed -39.9%. The proximate catalyst was the Fed's September 26, 2018 rate hike (to 2.0-2.25%) combined with Chair Powell's October 3 comments calling rates 'a long way from neutral' -- which helped set off the fourth-quarter 2018 equity rout. Trade war escalation (US-China tariff tit-for-tat in September-November 2018) and a simultaneous US growth deceleration (ISM manufacturing peaked in August 2018) amplified the sell-off. Insurance, being a financial sub-sector, was dragged lower by the broad credit stress (HYG-LQD -4.9%) even as P&C business fundamentals remained intact -- the -15.7% move was macro/risk-off, not a fundamental impairment. Insurers' bond portfolios marked down slightly as credit spreads widened, but rising short-end yields actually improved future float income.","body_zh":"2018年9月21日至12月24日，保险与经纪下跌-15.7%（SPY峰谷跌幅-19.3%），市场呈现避险轮动，防御股仅跌-8.9%、周期股暴跌-23.1%，VIX从12飙升至36，原油崩溃-39.9%。直接催化剂是美联储9月26日加息至2.0-2.25%，叠加鲍威尔10月3日称利率'距中性尚远'的言论，引爆四季度股市暴跌。美中贸易摩擦升级（9-11月关税反制）与美国经济增速放缓（ISM制造业指数8月见顶）放大了跌势。保险作为金融子行业，受信用市场压力（HYG-LQD -4.9%）拖累而下跌，但P&C业务基本面完好无损——-15.7%的跌幅属于宏观/避险因素驱动，非基本面受损。保险公司债券组合随信用利差走阔出现小幅市值缩水，但短端收益率上升实际上改善了未来浮存金收益。","drivers":["Fed Sep 2018 rate hike to 2.0-2.25% plus Powell 'long way from neutral'","US-China tariff escalation September-November 2018 growth scare","VIX spike 12 to 36: broad risk-off rotation","HYG-LQD credit spread blow-out -4.9%","Financial sub-sector dragged by broad equity de-rating"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2018年9月加息至2.0-2.25%，鲍威尔称'距中性尚远'","美中关税升级（9-11月）引发增长恐慌","VIX从12飙升至36：全市场避险轮动","高收益-投资级信用利差走阔-4.9%","金融子行业随大盘估值压缩被拖累"],"prev_key":"2018-09-21","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-21"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed fourth hike plus growth scare selloff","title_zh":"美联储第四次加息叠加增长恐慌引发回调","turn_id":"insurance:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"From the Christmas Eve 2018 low through February 11, 2020, Insurance & Brokers rallied +59.0% (vs SPY +45.8%) as the macro regime pivoted sharply: VIX mean-reverted from 36 back to 15, tech/semis led (semis +86.7%), and the Fed executed three rate cuts in July, September, and October 2019 in response to slowing global growth and US-China trade tensions. The Fed's January 4, 2019 signal of patience (abandoning its prior tightening bias) was the inflection -- financial conditions eased immediately, credit spreads tightened, and P&C hard market pricing began visibly accelerating through 2019 after two years of below-trend returns. Insurance outperformed SPY on the rally (+59% vs +45.8%) because the sector entered the turn with clean balance sheets, hard market premiums compounding, and improving investment income as insurers reinvested maturing bonds, even with the three Fed cuts leaving the 10-year near ~1.9% by end-2019. The rally ended in February 2020 as COVID-19 community spread began spooking markets.","body_zh":"自2018年圣诞节低点至2020年2月11日，保险与经纪反弹+59.0%（vs SPY +45.8%），宏观环境急剧反转：VIX从36均值回归至15，科技/半导体领涨（半导体+86.7%），美联储在2019年7月、9月、10月执行三次降息以应对全球增速放缓与美中贸易摩擦。2019年1月4日美联储释放'耐心'信号（放弃此前收紧偏向）是转折点——金融条件即时宽松，信用利差收窄，2019年P&C硬市场定价在连续两年低于趋势回报后开始明显加速。保险跑赢SPY（+59%对+45.8%），因为该行业以干净的资产负债表进入转折点，硬市场保费持续复利，且保险公司在到期债券再投资中支撑投资收益，即便三次降息使10年期收益率到2019年底回落至约1.9%。此次反弹于2020年2月随新冠疫情社区传播开始令市场恐慌而告终。","drivers":["Fed Jan 2019 'patience' pivot then 3x rate cuts (Jul/Sep/Oct 2019)","VIX mean-reversion 36 to 15: risk-on re-entry","P&C hard market pricing acceleration through 2019","Clean balance sheets and improving underwriting margins","Semis +86.7%: broad tech-led risk appetite recovery"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月'耐心'转向，随后三次降息（7/9/10月）","VIX从36均值回归至15：风险偏好重启","2019年P&C硬市场定价加速","资产负债表干净，承保利润持续改善","半导体+86.7%：科技领衔推动风险偏好全面修复"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot unlocks 14-month 59% rebound","title_zh":"美联储转向解锁14个月59%反弹","turn_id":"insurance:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-11":{"body":"From February 11 to March 23, 2020, Insurance & Brokers collapsed -42.5% -- the basket's steepest six-week drawdown on record -- in a mass-liquidation event where SPY fell -33.1%, VIX spiked to 62, oil crashed -53.2%, and even defensives lost -28.8%. The proximate trigger was the February 21 Italian COVID-19 community spread headline followed by the February 24-25 S&P 500 'correction week' when ~10% was erased in two days, then escalating US case counts through early March, culminating in the WHO pandemic declaration on March 11 and US national emergency on March 13. Financials (-42.8%) were among the worst sectors: insurance faced a triple hit from equity/bond portfolio mark-downs (insurers hold large investable assets), business-interruption claims risk (later largely denied by courts as policies required physical damage), and a collapse of reinvestment yields as the Fed cut rates to zero on March 15. The basket's -42.5% loss was in-line with the broad financial sector (-42.8%) and worse than SPY but better than Energy (-55.6%) -- this was pandemic-panic indiscriminate selling, not an insurance-specific credit event.","body_zh":"2020年2月11日至3月23日，保险与经纪暴跌-42.5%，是该篮子有记录以来最剧烈的六周回撤，期间SPY跌-33.1%、VIX飙升至62、原油崩溃-53.2%，就连防御股也下跌-28.8%。导火索是2月21日意大利新冠社区传播头条，随后2月24-25日标普500'纠正周'两天蒸发约10%，3月初美国确诊病例急升，3月11日世卫宣布全球大流行，3月13日美国宣布国家紧急状态。金融股（-42.8%）是最差行业之一：保险面临三重打击——股债投资组合市值缩水（保险公司持有大量可投资资产）、营业中断险理赔风险（后被法院以需物理损害为由大量驳回）、以及美联储3月15日降息至零导致再投资收益率崩溃。篮子-42.5%的跌幅与大金融板块（-42.8%）相当，逊于SPY但好于能源（-55.6%）——这是疫情恐慌下的无差别抛售，并非保险特有信用事件。","drivers":["COVID-19 WHO pandemic declaration Mar 11 + US national emergency Mar 13","Fed emergency rate cut to zero Mar 15: float income crushed","VIX spike to 62: indiscriminate mass liquidation","Business interruption claims litigation risk (physical damage exclusions)","Financials sector -42.8%: equity/bond portfolio mark-downs"],"drivers_zh":["世卫3月11日宣布全球大流行，美国3月13日宣布国家紧急状态","美联储3月15日紧急降至零利率：浮存金收益崩溃","VIX飙升至62：无差别大规模清仓","营业中断险理赔诉讼风险（物理损害条款排除）","金融行业-42.8%：股债投资组合市值缩水"],"prev_key":"2020-02-11","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-11"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash: -42% in six weeks","title_zh":"新冠疫情崩盘：六周内暴跌-42%","turn_id":"insurance:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From the March 23, 2020 low to the April 20, 2022 peak, Insurance & Brokers surged +153.8% -- outpacing SPY (+105.3%) -- in one of the most powerful reflation cycles in decades: VIX collapsed from 62 to 20, oil rallied +339.9%, copper/gold +94.8%, TLT fell -24.4% as rates rose, and the equal-weight index beat SPY by +23.3%. The March 23 bottom coincided with the Fed's unlimited QE announcement and was cemented by the CARES Act ($2.2 trillion, signed March 27, 2020) then the $1.9 trillion American Rescue Plan (March 2021). Insurance outperformed because: (1) Courts ruled overwhelmingly against business-interruption claims (no physical damage), eliminating the catastrophic liability overhang; (2) the hard P&C market accelerated sharply -- commercial-lines rate increases ran double-digits through 2020-2021 after years of cat losses; (3) rising long rates (10-year surged from ~0.5% in August 2020 to ~2.7% by early 2022) rebuilt float income for the first time in a decade; (4) M&A added a valuation kicker (Aon/Willis Towers Watson announced their ~$30bn merger on March 9, 2020, later terminated July 2021 after a June 2021 DoJ antitrust suit). The sector benefited from both the reflation trade (as a financial-beta name, Financials +122.9%) and structural business improvement simultaneously.","body_zh":"2020年3月23日低点至2022年4月20日峰值，保险与经纪飙升+153.8%，超越SPY（+105.3%），是数十年来最强劲的反通胀周期之一：VIX从62崩至20、原油+339.9%、铜金+94.8%、TLT -24.4%（利率上升），等权指数跑赢SPY +23.3%。3月23日低点恰逢美联储宣布无限量QE，随后被《CARES法案》（2.2万亿，3月27日签署）及1.9万亿美元《美国救援计划》（2021年3月）巩固。保险跑赢原因：（1）法院大量驳回营业中断险理赔（无物理损害），消除了灾难性赔付悬置；（2）P&C硬市场急速加速——2020-2021年商业险费率年增达两位数；（3）长端利率上升（10年期从2020年8月约0.5%升至2022年初约2.7%）十年来首次重建浮存金收益；（4）并购提振估值（怡安/韦莱韬悦于2020年3月9日宣布约300亿美元合并，2021年6月司法部反垄断起诉后于2021年7月终止）。该行业同时受益于反通胀交易（作为金融贝塔标的，金融+122.9%）与结构性业务改善。","drivers":["Unlimited Fed QE Mar 23 + CARES Act $2.2T eliminates downside tail","BI claims exclusions confirmed by courts: liability overhang removed","P&C hard market: commercial rate increases double-digit 2020-2021","Long rates rising (10Y ~0.5% to ~2.7%): float income rebuilt","Reflation broadening: equal-weight beat SPY +23.3%, Financials +122.9%"],"drivers_zh":["美联储无限量QE（3月23日）+2.2万亿CARES法案清除下行尾部风险","法院确认营业中断险排除条款：赔付悬置解除","P&C硬市场：2020-2021年商业险费率年增两位数","长端利率上升（10年期从约0.5%升至约2.7%）：浮存金收益重建","反通胀普涨：等权跑赢SPY +23.3%，金融板块+122.9%"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Fiscal shock plus reflation surge: +154% in 25 months","title_zh":"财政冲击叠加反通胀浪潮：25个月+154%","turn_id":"insurance:trough:2020-03"},"2022-04-20":{"body":"Insurance & Brokers fell -16.0% from April 20 to June 16, 2022, in a stagflation-ish tape where SPY fell -17.6%, VIX rose from 20 to 33, oil surged +14.4% (Russia-Ukraine war supply shock), TLT fell -7.8% as the Fed embarked on its most aggressive tightening cycle since 1994. The April 20 peak coincided with Q1 2022 earnings season and the Fed's May 4 50-basis-point hike (the first 50bp move since 2000), followed by a June 15 75-basis-point hike -- the largest single move since 1994. As a low-beta financial sub-sector, insurance (-16.0%) fell less than Discretionary (-25.9%) and REIT (-23.2%) but more than Energy (-3.6%) and Health (-14.5%). The sell-off was a macro/rate-compression drawdown across all equity multiples, not a P&C business deterioration: rising discount rates compressed P/E multiples, while higher rates were simultaneously a long-term positive for float reinvestment yields -- exactly why the sector found its trough rapidly at the June 2022 low.","body_zh":"2022年4月20日至6月16日，保险与经纪下跌-16.0%，SPY跌-17.6%，VIX从20升至33，原油+14.4%（俄乌战争供应冲击），TLT -7.8%，美联储启动1994年以来最激进的收紧周期。4月20日峰值与2022年Q1财报季和美联储5月4日加息50个基点（2000年以来首次）相吻合，随后6月15日加息75个基点——1994年以来单次最大幅度。作为低贝塔金融子行业，保险（-16.0%）跌幅小于可选消费（-25.9%）和REITs（-23.2%），但大于能源（-3.6%）和医疗（-14.5%）。此次回调是宏观/利率压缩引发的全市场估值收缩，并非P&C业务恶化：贴现率上升压缩市盈率倍数，而同样的高利率长期而言是浮存金再投资收益率的利好——正因如此，该行业在2022年6月低点迅速触底。","drivers":["Fed May 4 50bp hike + Jun 15 75bp: most aggressive cycle since 1994","Russia-Ukraine oil shock: stagflation quad (oil +14.4%, yields rising)","VIX 20 to 33: broad equity multiple compression","Financials -18.6%: rate-sensitive balance sheet mark-downs","Low-beta cushion: -16% vs -25.9% Discretionary in same tape"],"drivers_zh":["美联储5月4日加息50bp，6月15日加息75bp：1994年以来最激进收紧","俄乌战争原油冲击：滞涨组合（原油+14.4%，收益率上升）","VIX从20升至33：全市场估值倍数压缩","金融板块-18.6%：利率敏感资产负债表贬值","低贝塔缓冲：同期-16%对比可选消费-25.9%"],"prev_key":"2022-04-20","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-20"],"status":"exact","title":"2022 rate-shock dip in a stagflation tape","title_zh":"2022年利率冲击在滞涨环境中引发回调","turn_id":"insurance:peak:2022-04"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"From the June 2022 low, insurance rallied ~95.8% in an almost straight line through a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation regime -- SPY +60.9%, VIX 33 to 22, semis +114.5% -- yet as a low-beta name it did not need the melt-up: it shrugged off SVB (March 2023), the 2024 Fed rate cuts, and the April 2025 'Liberation Day' tariff crash (S&P fell sharply over two sessions before tariffs were paused April 9). The structural engine is multi-layered: (1) a multi-year hard P&C pricing cycle (one of the longest on record, with many consecutive quarters of commercial rate increases into 2024) where premiums compounded faster than claims inflation; (2) the 10-year yield staying elevated at ~3.5-5.0% (TLT -9.5% over the leg) meant insurance float -- often $100-500bn in investable assets for the majors -- earned real investment income for the first time since 2007; (3) broker fee revenues (Marsh, Aon, Gallagher) are volume-and-GDP-linked and grew steadily as the economy expanded. The rally cooled at the April 2025 peak as commercial P&C pricing began softening and the basket reflected Financials underperformance in a Tech/Energy-led tape.","body_zh":"自2022年6月低点，保险近乎直线上涨约95.8%，历经goldilocks/增长向上去通胀环境——SPY +60.9%、VIX 33至22、半导体+114.5%——但作为低贝塔标的，它并不依赖这场融涨：无视2023年3月SVB、2024年美联储降息与大选、2025年4月'解放日'关税冲击（标普两个交易日大跌，4月9日暂停加征）。结构性引擎多层次叠加：（1）史上最长之一的P&C硬市场定价周期（连续多季度商业险费率上升至2024年），保费复利快于理赔通胀；（2）10年期国债收益率维持在约3.5-5.0%区间（整段TLT -9.5%），使保险浮存金——主要公司可投资资产规模达1000-5000亿美元——自2007年以来首次获得真实投资收益；（3）经纪商手续费收入（达信、怡安、高博）与成交量/GDP挂钩，随经济扩张持续增长。行情于2025年4月峰值处降温，因商业P&C定价开始软化，篮子反映金融板块在科技/能源领涨行情中的相对落后。","drivers":["Multi-year hard P&C pricing cycle (consecutive quarters of rate increases)","10Y yield ~3.5-5.0%: float investment income at multi-year high","Broker fee revenues compound with GDP (Marsh/Aon/Gallagher)","VIX 33 to 22: goldilocks risk-on backdrop","Shrugged off SVB 2023, tariff crash Apr 2025: low-beta resilience"],"drivers_zh":["史上最长之一的P&C硬市场定价周期（连续多季度费率上升）","10年期收益率约3.5-5.0%：浮存金投资收益达多年高位","经纪商手续费随GDP复利（达信/怡安/高博）","VIX从33降至22：黄金时代风险偏好背景","无视2023年SVB、2025年4月关税崩盘：低贝塔韧性"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"The quiet +96% compounder rode the goldilocks tape","title_zh":"安静的+96%复利行情乘goldilocks顺风","turn_id":"insurance:trough:2022-06"}},"now":"Insurance & Brokers is in a mid-cycle Expansion/Trending phase (pos 36.5, rs_rank 28 vs SPY), holding above its 200-day moving average with a BUY signal and a 477.6% cumulative return from inception -- though currently underperforming in a reflation/growth-up tape where Tech (+24.3%) and Energy (+21.5%) lead while Financials (-2.7%) lag. The current setup is low-drama: dollar firming (+3.4% DXY), VIX compressing (14 to 18), equal-weight breadth beating cap-weight by +2.9% -- insurance is the stay-put compounder, not the rotation leader. Commercial P&C pricing is softening after the record 2022-2025 hard market cycle, putting mild pressure on underwriting margins; but broker fee streams (Marsh, Aon, Gallagher) remain durable, and elevated reinvestment yields on float portfolios (Fed still restrictive) continue to underpin investment income -- with the 2026 oil/Hormuz shock a mild net positive here (more investment income, no credit blow-up). In a tape where high-beta is outperforming low-vol by +20.7 points, relative underperformance is expected and is not a thesis break.","now_zh":"保险与经纪处于周期中段扩张/趋势阶段（仓位36.5、相对排名28），仍在200日均线之上，维持买入信号，累计回报477.6%——但在当前反通胀/增长向上行情中相对落后，科技（+24.3%）与能源（+21.5%）领涨，金融（-2.7%）承压。当前格局低波动：美元走强（DXY +3.4%）、VIX收敛（14至18）、等权指数跑赢市值加权+2.9%，保险是\"持有复利\"而非轮动领头羊。商业P&C定价在2022-2025超级硬市场后开始软化，承保利润承压；但经纪商手续费流（达信、怡安、高博）依然稳健，美联储维持限制性利率使浮存金组合再投资收益率居高，持续支撑投资收益——2026年油价/霍尔木兹冲击在此处偏正面（投资收益增加、无信用爆雷）。在高贝塔跑赢低波动+20.7个百分点的行情中，篮子相对落后属于预期内，并非论点破裂。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"credit.spread_regime.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"credit.spread_regime.v1","arch_state":"fail","arch_fired_on":"2026-07-05","revision_note":null}},"b-mag7":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"From early 2014, the Magnificent Seven precursors (Apple, Google, Amazon, Microsoft, Facebook) rode the iPhone 6 supercycle (unveiled September 9, 2014, released September 19, selling over 10 million units in its first weekend), explosive AWS cloud revenue growth, and Google advertising revenue compounding. The macro was a post-QE3 slowdown/deflation-scare quad with the dollar surging +21.4% and oil collapsing -59.7%, creating a narrow-breadth tape (RSP lagged SPY by -4.1%) where falling yields (TLT +24.2%) bid up quality growth; defensives led vs cyclicals (+29.8% vs +8.3%) but the seven's secular-growth moats meant they dominated the tape independently of sector rotation.","body_zh":"2014年初起，七巨头前身（苹果、谷歌、亚马逊、微软、脸书）乘iPhone 6超级周期（2014年9月9日发布、9月19日开售，首个周末售出超1000万部创纪录）、AWS云营收爆发式增长及谷歌广告营收复利增长的东风。宏观为后QE3放缓/通缩恐慌象限，美元飙涨+21.4%、油价崩跌-59.7%，形成窄幅行情（等权跑输市值权重-4.1%），收益率下行（TLT +24.2%）推高质地成长股；防御股领跑周期股（+29.8% vs +8.3%），但七巨头的世俗成长护城河使其独立于板块轮动而主导行情。","drivers":["iPhone 6 supercycle","AWS/cloud monetization","falling yields (TLT +24.2%)","narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -4.1%)","dollar +21.4% deflation-scare"],"drivers_zh":["iPhone 6超级周期","AWS/云计算变现","收益率下行(TLT +24.2%)","窄幅大盘股行情(RSP -4.1%)","美元+21.4%通缩恐慌"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Mobile supercycle and cloud growth fuel melt-up","title_zh":"移动超级周期与云计算增长驱动熔涨","turn_id":"mag7:trough:2014-01"},"2015-12-29":{"body":"The first Fed rate hike in nine years (December 16, 2015, funds rate to 0.25-0.50%) combined with China posting its lowest annual growth in a quarter century and oil crashing below $30/barrel triggered a global risk-off flush into February 2016. The cohort fell -19.8% as defensives massively outperformed cyclicals (-2.9% vs -11.4%), VIX spiked 16 to 27, yields fell (TLT +9.8%), and the dollar weakened slightly (-2.1% DXY) as growth-sensitive tech was the most-sold sector (Tech -10.4%, semis -14.7%), consistent with a classic slowdown/deflation-scare flight-to-safety.","body_zh":"美联储九年来首次加息（2015年12月16日，基准利率至0.25-0.50%），叠加中国公布四分之一世纪以来最低年度增长、油价跌破每桶30美元，触发延伸至2016年2月的全球避险抛售。该群体下跌-19.8%，防御股大幅跑赢周期股（-2.9% vs -11.4%），VIX从16飙至27，收益率下行（TLT +9.8%），美元小幅走弱（-2.1%），对增长敏感的科技股遭最大抛售（科技-10.4%、半导体-14.7%），与经典放缓/通缩恐慌避险逻辑完全一致。","drivers":["first Fed hike Dec 2015","China slowdown / lowest GDP growth in 25 years","oil below $30/bbl","flight-to-safety (VIX 16->27)"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2015年12月首次加息","中国放缓/25年最低GDP增速","油价跌破30美元/桶","避险(VIX 16->27)"],"prev_key":"2015-12-29","prev_key_chain":["2015-12-29"],"status":"exact","title":"China slowdown, oil crash, Fed hike trigger risk-off","title_zh":"中国放缓、油价崩跌与美联储加息引发避险","turn_id":"mag7:peak:2015-12"},"2016-02-09":{"body":"The February 26, 2016 G20 Shanghai meeting produced an implicit currency accord that arrested the dollar's surge (DXY -0.8% over the leg), oil bottomed amid production-freeze talks and crude rallied +169.5%, and the VIX collapsed from 27 to 12. A powerful reflationary cyclical-led rally ensued (cyclicals +71.7% vs defensives +31.9%) carrying the seven +210.3% over nearly three years as cloud monetization accelerated, Facebook and Google captured the digital-advertising duopoly, and the Trump election (November 2016) added a corporate-tax-cut catalyst. Tech led at +104% with semis at +134%; narrow breadth persisted (RSP -4.7% vs SPY) confirming mega-cap concentration.","body_zh":"2016年2月26日G20上海会议形成隐性货币协议，遏制美元涨势（全程DXY -0.8%），油价在减产冻产谈判下见底、大幅反弹+169.5%，VIX从27崩至12。强劲再通胀周期股领涨行情随之而来（周期股+71.7% vs 防御股+31.9%），七巨头近三年涨210.3%：云计算变现加速，脸书与谷歌捕获数字广告双寡头地位，特朗普当选（2016年11月）增添企业减税催化剂。科技领涨+104%，半导体+134%；窄幅大盘股格局持续（RSP跑输SPY -4.7%），确认大盘股集中效应。","drivers":["Shanghai G20 / dollar stabilization","oil recovery +169.5%","Trump tax cut / reflation expectations","cloud/digital ad duopoly acceleration (GOOG, FB)"],"drivers_zh":["G20上海协议/美元企稳","油价复苏+169.5%","特朗普减税/再通胀预期","云计算/数字广告双寡头加速(谷歌、脸书)"],"prev_key":"2016-02-09","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Shanghai Accord, oil floor, Trump reflation launch mega bull","title_zh":"上海协议、油价见底与特朗普再通胀催化超级牛市","turn_id":"mag7:trough:2016-02"},"2018-10-01":{"body":"Fed Chair Powell's October 3, 2018 statement that rates were 'a long way from neutral' triggered a violent repricing: the funds rate had been raised to 2.25% in September, and the December 19 hike to 2.50% plus Powell's refusal to slow balance-sheet runoff sent the S&P to its worst December since 1931. The cohort fell -28.0% as the rate shock crushed high-multiple growth (Tech -23.5%, semis -22.7%), VIX exploded 12 to 36, defensives massively outperformed cyclicals (-8.3% vs -22.4%), and oil crashed -43.5% as global growth fears mounted - a textbook slowdown/deflation-scare de-rating of long-duration assets.","body_zh":"美联储主席鲍威尔2018年10月3日表示利率\"距中性还有很长一段距离\"，引发剧烈重定价：联邦基金利率9月已升至2.25%，12月19日再度加至2.50%，且鲍威尔拒绝放缓缩表，推动标普遭遇1931年以来最糟糕12月。七巨头下跌-28.0%，利率冲击重挫高估值成长股（科技-23.5%、半导体-22.7%），VIX从12暴涨至36，防御股大幅跑赢周期股（-8.3% vs -22.4%），油价在全球增长忧虑升温中崩跌-43.5%——这是长久期资产的教科书式放缓/通缩恐慌估值下修。","drivers":["Powell 'long way from neutral' Oct 3","4 Fed hikes in 2018 / December hike to 2.50%","VIX explosion 12->36","long-duration multiple compression (Tech -23.5%)"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔\"距中性还远\"10月3日声明","2018年四次加息/12月升至2.50%","VIX暴涨12->36","长久期估值压缩(科技-23.5%)"],"prev_key":"2018-10-01","prev_key_chain":["2018-10-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell rate-shock kills the bull, VIX explodes to 36","title_zh":"鲍威尔利率冲击终结牛市，VIX暴涨至36","turn_id":"mag7:peak:2018-10"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"On January 4, 2019, Powell signaled the Fed would be 'patient' about rate hikes and was prepared to shift policy - effectively ending the tightening cycle that had crushed growth stocks. Combined with the G20 Buenos Aires US-China trade truce (December 1, 2018) and a snapback from deeply oversold conditions, the seven surged +33.4% as VIX collapsed 36 to 13, cyclicals outperformed defensives (27.7% vs 14.8%), semis rallied +45.1%, growth beat value (+8.2), and SPY gained +26.0% in one of the best Q1 performances in decades.","body_zh":"2019年1月4日，鲍威尔表示美联储将对加息\"保持耐心\"并准备调整政策——实质上终结了重创成长股的紧缩周期。叠加G20布宜诺斯艾利斯中美贸易停战（2018年12月1日）及从严重超卖水平的强力反弹，七巨头涨+33.4%，VIX从36崩至13，周期股跑赢防御股（27.7% vs 14.8%），半导体涨+45.1%，成长跑赢价值（+8.2），标普涨+26.0%——是几十年来最强劲的一季度表现之一。","drivers":["Powell patience pivot Jan 4 2019","G20 US-China trade truce Dec 2018","oversold VIX collapse 36->13","growth/semis leadership snapback"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔耐心转向2019年1月4日","G20中美贸易停战2018年12月","超卖VIX崩塌36->13","成长股/半导体领导力反弹"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell pivot and trade truce ignite relief rally","title_zh":"鲍威尔转向与贸易停战点燃修复反弹","turn_id":"mag7:trough:2018-12"},"2019-05-03":{"body":"Trump's announcement on May 5, 2019 that tariffs on $200bn of Chinese goods would rise from 10% to 25% (effective May 10) was the single largest negative trade shock of the entire 2018-2019 dispute. Tech was the most exposed sector given supply-chain ties to China (Tech -10.4%, semis -16.5% over the leg), defensives massively outperformed cyclicals (-1.3% vs -7.4%), VIX spiked 13 to 19, and yields fell sharply (TLT +7.3%) as markets priced a slowdown/deflation-scare outcome from the escalating tariff war.","body_zh":"特朗普2019年5月5日宣布对2000亿美元中国商品关税从10%提升至25%（5月10日生效），是整个2018-2019贸易争端中最大的单次负面冲击。科技板块因供应链与中国深度绑定而最受波及（科技-10.4%、半导体-16.5%），防御股大幅跑赢周期股（-1.3% vs -7.4%），VIX从13飙至19，收益率大幅下行（TLT +7.3%），市场在关税升级的放缓/通缩恐慌预期中重新定价。","drivers":["$200bn tariff escalation 10% to 25% May 10 2019","tech/semis China supply-chain exposure (Tech -10.4%, SMH -16.5%)","flight-to-safety (VIX 13->19, TLT +7.3%)","slowdown quad"],"drivers_zh":["2000亿美元关税从10%升至25% 2019年5月10日","科技/半导体中国供应链敞口(科技-10.4%, SMH-16.5%)","避险(VIX 13->19, TLT +7.3%)","放缓象限"],"prev_key":"2019-05-03","prev_key_chain":["2019-05-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade war reignites: tariffs on $200bn Chinese goods","title_zh":"贸易战重燃：对华2000亿美元商品加征关税","turn_id":"mag7:peak:2019-05"},"2019-06-03":{"body":"With the market pricing three Fed rate cuts for 2019 by June (ultimately delivered July 31, September 18, October 30), the seven surged +94.4% into the February 2020 peak. The Fed's pivot from 'patient' to active easing fueled a slowdown/deflation-scare quad melt-up where falling yields (TLT +11.5%) and modest dollar strength (+2.5% DXY) compressed volatility (VIX 19 to 14) while US-China Phase 1 deal optimism built. Tech led (+47.0%) with semis at +57.5%, and breadth was extremely narrow (RSP lagged SPY by -6.2%) as flows concentrated in the seven's quality-growth profiles.","body_zh":"6月市场已充分消化2019年三次美联储降息预期（最终如期兑现：7月31日、9月18日、10月30日），七巨头至2020年2月峰值涨幅达+94.4%。美联储从\"耐心\"转向主动宽松，在放缓/通缩恐慌象限中推动熔涨：收益率下行（TLT +11.5%）、美元小幅走强（+2.5%），VIX从19压至14，中美第一阶段协议乐观情绪持续累积。科技领涨（+47.0%），半导体+57.5%，广度极度收窄（RSP跑输SPY -6.2%），资金集中流入七巨头质地成长配置。","drivers":["Fed rate cuts Jul/Sep/Oct 2019","falling yields (TLT +11.5%)","US-China Phase 1 deal optimism","narrow mega-cap flows (RSP -6.2% vs SPY)"],"drivers_zh":["美联储三次降息2019年7/9/10月","收益率下行(TLT +11.5%)","中美第一阶段协议乐观情绪","窄幅大盘股资金集中(RSP跑输SPY -6.2%)"],"prev_key":"2019-06-03","prev_key_chain":["2019-06-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed rate-cut pivot plus Phase-1 deal hopes power melt-up","title_zh":"美联储降息转向叠加第一阶段贸易协议预期推动熔涨","turn_id":"mag7:trough:2019-06"},"2020-02-19":{"body":"The WHO declared a COVID-19 Public Health Emergency of International Concern on January 30, 2020, but global equity markets only cracked sharply on February 20 as Italy entered lockdown and US case counts accelerated. The seven fell -32.7% in a month as VIX exploded from 14 to 76, circuit breakers were triggered three times on the NYSE, cyclicals crashed -37.3% vs defensives -18.1%, and oil collapsed -61.8% as global demand destruction became certain. Even with growth-relative outperformance (growth +5.1 vs value), the concentrated selloff in high-beta tech was only partially cushioned.","body_zh":"世卫组织2020年1月30日宣布新冠为国际关注突发公共卫生事件，但全球股市直至2月20日意大利封锁、美国病例加速后才急剧崩塌。七巨头一个月内下跌-32.7%，VIX从14暴涨至76，NYSE三次触发熔断，周期股崩跌-37.3% vs 防御股-18.1%，油价因全球需求骤降崩跌-61.8%。尽管成长相对价值有所抵御（+5.1），高贝塔科技股的集中抛售仅部分得到缓冲。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic declaration","VIX explosion 14->76 (circuit breakers triggered)","cyclical/global demand collapse (oil -61.8%)","flight-to-safety (defensives -18.1% vs cyclicals -37.3%)"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情宣布","VIX暴涨14->76(三次触发熔断)","周期股/全球需求崩溃(油价-61.8%)","避险(防御股-18.1% vs 周期股-37.3%)"],"prev_key":"2020-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash: VIX explodes to 76","title_zh":"新冠疫情暴跌：VIX暴涨至76","turn_id":"mag7:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"The Fed cut rates to 0-0.25% on March 15, 2020 and announced open-ended unlimited QE on March 23 (balance sheet exceeded $7 trillion by mid-2020); Congress passed the $2.2 trillion CARES Act on March 27; and vaccine breakthroughs (Pfizer/BioNTech Phase 3 data November 2020) unlocked the reflation trade. The seven surged +289.2% into November 2021: NVDA rallied multiple-fold as data-center demand exploded, MSFT Azure and AMZN AWS captured cloud lock-in, and GOOGL/META captured the digital-ad recovery. The tape was broadening (RSP beat SPY by +8.8%), cyclical-led (+127.6% vs defensives +42.5%), with semis at +211.0% confirming AI-hardware pre-positioning was already underway.","body_zh":"美联储2020年3月15日将利率降至0-0.25%，3月23日宣布开放式无限QE（资产负债表年中前超7万亿美元）；国会3月27日通过2.2万亿美元CARES法案；辉瑞/BioNTech疫苗三期数据（2020年11月）解锁再通胀交易。七巨头至2021年11月涨+289.2%：英伟达因数据中心需求爆发涨数倍，微软Azure与亚马逊AWS捕获云锁定效应，谷歌/Meta捕获数字广告复苏。行情转宽（等权跑赢市值权重+8.8%），周期股主导（+127.6% vs 防御股+42.5%），半导体+211.0%印证AI硬件预布局已悄然展开。","drivers":["Unlimited QE / rates to 0 (Mar 2020)","CARES Act $2.2T fiscal stimulus","vaccine breakthrough (Pfizer Nov 2020)","AI/cloud monetization (NVDA, MSFT Azure, AMZN AWS)"],"drivers_zh":["无限QE/利率降至0(2020年3月)","CARES法案2.2万亿美元财政刺激","疫苗突破(辉瑞2020年11月)","AI/云计算变现(英伟达、微软Azure、亚马逊AWS)"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Unlimited QE, fiscal stimulus, AI dawn ignite 289% run","title_zh":"无限QE、财政刺激与AI曙光引爆289%涨幅","turn_id":"mag7:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-19":{"body":"Powell's November 30, 2021 testimony that it was time to 'retire' the word 'transitory' and that the Fed would discuss accelerating its taper triggered the first leg of the 2022 bear market; Omicron fears compounded the shock. Yields surged (TLT -10.7%) in a stagflation-ish quad with oil +35.4% (Russia's February 24, 2022 invasion of Ukraine added fuel), the dollar firmed +3.1%, and defensives outperformed cyclicals (+1.2% vs -3.4%); the broadening tape (RSP +4.3% vs SPY) was antithetical to the seven, with Tech down -17.3% and Comm -20.0% while Energy surged +38.1%.","body_zh":"2021年11月30日鲍威尔作证表示\"是时候放弃\"暂时性\"一词\"并将讨论加快缩减购债，触发2022年熊市第一腿；奥密克戎恐慌加剧冲击。在类滞胀象限中收益率飙升（TLT -10.7%）、油价+35.4%（2022年2月24日俄罗斯入侵乌克兰推波助澜），美元走强+3.1%，防御股跑赢周期股（+1.2% vs -3.4%）；行情转宽（RSP跑赢SPY +4.3%）与七巨头相悖，科技跌-17.3%、通信-20.0%，能源则大涨+38.1%。","drivers":["Powell retires 'transitory' Nov 30 2021","Fed taper acceleration / rate hike pricing","Russia-Ukraine invasion Feb 2022","stagflation-ish quad (yields up, oil +35.4%)"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔放弃暂时性表述2021年11月30日","美联储加速缩债/加息预期定价","俄乌入侵2022年2月","类滞胀象限(收益率上行、油价+35.4%)"],"prev_key":"2021-11-19","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-19"],"status":"exact","title":"Mega-cap rate de-rating: Powell drops 'transitory', Omicron","title_zh":"大盘股利率估值下修：鲍威尔放弃\"暂时性\"表述，奥密克戎冲击","turn_id":"mag7:peak:2021-11"},"2022-03-14":{"body":"A sharp relief rally fired from deeply oversold levels as VIX collapsed from 32 to 19, with the highest-quality mega-caps leading in a narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY by -3.0%) as growth beat value (+9.5) in a short-lived reflation/growth-up read. Tech and Discretionary led the seven's cohort (+14.4%, +15.7%) while semis posted +13.0%. The relief was technically driven - no fundamental change in the hiking path - and reversed quickly as the next Fed hike (May 4, 2022: +50bp, first 50bp move since 2000) confirmed the steepening tightening trajectory.","body_zh":"超卖水平触发剧烈修复反弹，VIX从32崩至19，最高质地大盘股在窄幅行情中领涨（RSP跑输SPY -3.0%），成长跑赢价值（+9.5），形成短暂的再通胀/增长向上信号。科技与可选消费引领七巨头群体（+14.4%、+15.7%），半导体+13.0%。修复由技术面驱动——加息路径无任何根本变化——5月4日下次美联储加息（+50bp，2000年来首次单次加息50bp）确认紧缩轨迹陡峭化后迅速逆转。","drivers":["oversold bounce / VIX collapse 32->19","quality mega-cap bid (RSP -3.0% vs SPY)","growth beats value (+9.5)","temporary geopolitical risk reprieve"],"drivers_zh":["超卖反弹/VIX崩塌32->19","质地大盘股买盘(RSP跑输SPY -3.0%)","成长跑赢价值(+9.5)","地缘政治风险临时缓解"],"prev_key":"2022-03-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Quality-led relief on oversold risk-on bounce","title_zh":"超卖反弹中质地驱动的修复","turn_id":"mag7:trough:2022-03"},"2022-04-04":{"body":"The May 4 +50bp hike and June 15 +75bp hike (the first 75bp move since 1994) drove TLT down -14.7% over the leg as real yields turned aggressively positive; the dollar surged +4.7% and VIX spiked 19 to 33 in a stagflation-ish quad with oil still elevated (+13.9%) and credit spreads widening. The seven fell -33.0% as even the highest-quality mega-cap multiples could not escape the rate repricing (Tech -23.5%, Comm -25.4%, Discretionary -28.9%); the market broadened (RSP beat SPY by +2.3%) with Energy (+0.8%) and defensives the only shelter.","body_zh":"5月4日加息50bp与6月15日加息75bp（1994年以来首次单次75bp）推动TLT跌-14.7%，实际收益率大幅转正；美元+4.7%，VIX从19飙至33，处于类滞胀象限、油价仍高位（+13.9%），信用利差走扩。七巨头跌-33.0%，即便最高质地大盘股估值也无法逃脱利率重定价（科技-23.5%、通信-25.4%、可选消费-28.9%）；行情转宽（RSP跑赢SPY +2.3%），能源（+0.8%）与防御股是唯一避风港。","drivers":["Fed 75bp hike Jun 15 (first since 1994)","real yields surge (TLT -14.7%)","dollar +4.7% / stagflation-ish quad","multiple compression (Tech -23.5%)"],"drivers_zh":["美联储6月15日加息75bp(1994年以来首次)","实际收益率飙升(TLT -14.7%)","美元+4.7%/类滞胀象限","估值倍数压缩(科技-23.5%)"],"prev_key":"2022-04-04","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Real-yield repricing in a stagflation flush","title_zh":"类滞胀冲洗中的实际收益率重定价","turn_id":"mag7:peak:2022-04"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"A peak-rate narrative emerged as July CPI began moderating from its 9.1% June peak and oil crashed -24.0% (from near $120/bbl back toward $90), enabling a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation quad. The seven rallied +26.7% as VIX fell 33 to 20, semis gained +20.8%, growth beat value (+9.2), and Tech led at +23.0%. However, Powell's August 26 Jackson Hole speech ('We will keep at it until the job is done') confirmed no pivot was imminent and the rally reversed sharply, with the S&P losing roughly 3-4% the day of the speech.","body_zh":"7月CPI开始从6月9.1%峰值回落、油价从近120美元/桶崩跌-24.0%（降至90美元区域），形成金发女孩/增长向上/去通胀象限，利率见顶叙事随之兴起。七巨头涨+26.7%，VIX从33跌至20，半导体+20.8%，成长跑赢价值（+9.2），科技领涨+23.0%。然而，8月26日鲍威尔杰克逊霍尔演讲（\"我们将坚持到底\"）确认无转向在即，反弹剧烈逆转，标普当日跌约3-4%。","drivers":["peak-rate hope / CPI moderating from 9.1%","oil crash -24.0% (disinflation signal)","risk-on snapback (VIX 33->20, SMH +20.8%)","rally reversed at Jackson Hole Aug 26 Powell speech"],"drivers_zh":["利率见顶预期/CPI从9.1%回落","油价崩跌-24.0%(去通胀信号)","风险偏好回升(VIX 33->20, SMH +20.8%)","反弹在8月26日鲍威尔杰克逊霍尔演讲后逆转"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-rate-hope rally on disinflation narrative","title_zh":"去通胀叙事下的利率见顶预期反弹","turn_id":"mag7:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-15":{"body":"Powell's hawkish Jackson Hole speech on August 26 ('some pain to households and businesses') triggered a final tightening leg as November's +75bp and December's +50bp hikes pushed the terminal rate to 4.25-4.50% by year-end, driving TLT down a further -12.8%. In a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (oil -11.7%, copper-gold +4.1%), the tape broadened (RSP +3.9% vs SPY) as the seven were crushed (Tech -19.5% vs SPY -11.4%), with the December 28 low coming just weeks before ChatGPT (launched November 30, 2022) crossed 100 million users in January 2023 and reignited mega-cap leadership.","body_zh":"8月26日鲍威尔杰克逊霍尔鹰派演讲（\"将给家庭和企业带来一些痛苦\"）触发最终紧缩腿：11月再加75bp、12月加50bp，将终端利率推至4.25-4.50%，TLT再跌-12.8%。在放缓/通缩恐慌象限（油价-11.7%、铜金比+4.1%），行情转宽（RSP跑赢SPY +3.9%），七巨头遭重创（科技-19.5% vs SPY -11.4%），12月28日底部距ChatGPT（2022年11月30日发布）于2023年1月用户突破1亿仅数周，AI叙事随后重燃大盘股领导地位。","drivers":["Jackson Hole hawkish Aug 26 2022","Nov 75bp + Dec 50bp hikes (terminal 4.25-4.50%)","TLT -12.8% / broadening (RSP +3.9%)","Dec 28 2022 cycle low precedes ChatGPT 100M users"],"drivers_zh":["杰克逊霍尔鹰派演讲2022年8月26日","11月75bp + 12月50bp加息(终端利率4.25-4.50%)","TLT -12.8%/广度转宽(RSP +3.9%)","2022年12月28日周期低点先于ChatGPT用户破亿"],"prev_key":"2022-08-15","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Final tightening leg; ChatGPT-eve rate-driven low","title_zh":"最终紧缩腿；ChatGPT前夜利率驱动的底部","turn_id":"mag7:peak:2022-08"},"2022-12-28":{"body":"ChatGPT's launch (November 30, 2022) and Microsoft's reported ~$10bn OpenAI investment (announced January 23, 2023) ignited the generative-AI investment cycle that drove the seven +270.5% over two years. NVDA surged sharply through 2023 as the dominant AI-chip vendor; MSFT/GOOGL/META/AMZN captured AI-capex as both suppliers and consumers. The goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation quad (CPI declining, no recession, three Fed cuts from September 2024) sustained the melt-up in the narrowest tape of the entire cycle (RSP lagged SPY by a historic -32.4%), with semis at +157.5% and the growth/value spread at +70.5.","body_zh":"ChatGPT发布（2022年11月30日）与微软约100亿美元OpenAI投资（2023年1月23日宣布），点燃了推动七巨头两年内涨+270.5%的生成式AI投资周期。英伟达作为主导AI芯片供应商在2023年大幅飙升；微软/谷歌/Meta/亚马逊以AI资本开支的供需双重身份捕获价值。金发女孩/增长向上/去通胀象限（CPI持续回落、无衰退、美联储2024年9月起三次降息）在整个周期最窄幅的行情中延续熔涨（RSP历史性跑输SPY -32.4%），半导体+157.5%，成长/价值利差+70.5。","drivers":["ChatGPT launch / MSFT OpenAI ~$10bn Jan 2023","NVDA AI-chip dominance","goldilocks disinflation quad (no recession)","historic narrow breadth (RSP -32.4% vs SPY)"],"drivers_zh":["ChatGPT发布/微软OpenAI约100亿美元2023年1月","英伟达AI芯片主导地位","金发女孩去通胀象限(无衰退)","历史性窄幅行情(RSP跑输SPY -32.4%)"],"prev_key":"2022-12-28","prev_key_chain":["2022-12-28"],"status":"exact","title":"AI mega-cap supremacy in a historic narrow melt-up","title_zh":"历史性窄幅熔涨中的AI大盘股霸权","turn_id":"mag7:trough:2022-12"},"2024-12-24":{"body":"Nvidia fell a record ~17% in a single day on January 27, 2025 (its biggest one-day market-cap loss in US history, ~$600bn) after DeepSeek's R1 model claimed near-frontier AI capability at a fraction of the cost, questioning the AI-capex monetization thesis for the entire cohort. Then Trump's April 2, 2025 Liberation Day executive order announced a universal 10% tariff on all imports (effective April 5) plus country-specific duties (April 9), crashing the US stock market in days - the worst since COVID. VIX exploded from 14 to 52; the seven fell -29.0% with Tech -25.1% vs SPY -17.2%; high-beta was crushed (SPHB-SPLV -23.2); the tape broadened (RSP +3.7% vs SPY) and defensives held (-3.8% vs cyclicals -15.7%).","body_zh":"2025年1月27日，英伟达单日暴跌约17%（创美股史上最大单日市值损失，约6000亿美元），导火索是DeepSeek R1模型声称以极低成本媲美前沿AI能力，动摇整个群体的AI资本开支变现逻辑。随后，特朗普2025年4月2日\"解放日\"行政令宣布对所有进口商品征收10%普遍关税（4月5日生效）加上国别关税（4月9日），美股数日内暴跌——新冠以来最大跌幅。VIX从14暴涨至52；七巨头跌-29.0%，科技-25.1% vs SPY -17.2%；高贝塔被重创（SPHB-SPLV -23.2）；行情转宽（RSP跑赢SPY +3.7%），防御股守住（-3.8% vs 周期股-15.7%）。","drivers":["DeepSeek R1 / NVDA -17% Jan 27 2025","Liberation Day tariffs Apr 2 2025 (10% universal + country duties)","VIX explosion 14->52","flight-to-safety + broadening (RSP +3.7%)"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek R1/英伟达-17% 2025年1月27日","解放日关税2025年4月2日(10%普遍关税+国别关税)","VIX暴涨14->52","避险+广度转宽(RSP +3.7%)"],"prev_key":"2024-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2024-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek scare plus Liberation Day tariffs: VIX to 52","title_zh":"DeepSeek恐慌叠加解放日关税：VIX飙至52","turn_id":"mag7:peak:2024-12"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"The Trump administration paused the country-specific Liberation Day tariffs on April 9, 2025 (one day after the leg start), triggering a violent VIX collapse from 52 to 17. Renewed AI-capex commitments from hyperscalers reasserted the seven's earnings-growth divergence from the rest of the market. The goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation quad returned: Tech +69.7%, semis +104.8% (SMH), VIX 52 to 17, growth/value +29.9, and the tape was extremely narrow (RSP lagged SPY by -15.1%) confirming the seven recaptured flow concentration.","body_zh":"特朗普政府2025年4月9日（本腿开始次日）暂停国别解放日关税，触发VIX从52暴跌至17。超级云厂商重燃的AI资本开支承诺重新确立七巨头的盈利增长与市场其他部分的分化。金发女孩/增长向上/去通胀象限回归：科技+69.7%、半导体+104.8%（SMH），VIX 52到17，成长/价值+29.9，行情极度窄幅（RSP跑输SPY -15.1%），确认七巨头重新捕获资金集中流入。","drivers":["tariff pause Apr 9 2025 (90-day reprieve)","AI-capex hyperscaler commitments","VIX collapse 52->17 / risk-on reset","narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -15.1% vs SPY)"],"drivers_zh":["关税暂停2025年4月9日(90天宽限)","超级云厂商AI资本开支承诺","VIX崩塌52->17/风险偏好重置","窄幅大盘股行情(RSP跑输SPY -15.1%)"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff pause and AI-capex melt-up: 73% recovery","title_zh":"关税暂停与AI资本开支熔涨：73%修复","turn_id":"mag7:trough:2025-04"},"2025-10-29":{"body":"The regime turn began in late October 2025 as mega-cap valuations stretched and the AI-capex ROI debate intensified; it was compounded by the early-2026 Strait of Hormuz oil shock that sent oil +70.1% over the leg. The stagflation-ish quad (Energy +42.9% led, growth lagged value -19.5) was structurally antithetical to the seven: breadth broadened sharply (RSP +8.2% vs SPY) and VIX rose 17 to 31, confirming capital rotating to Energy/commodity/value from long-duration growth. The cohort's quality limited the damage (SMH only -1.3% vs Tech -15.9%) for a -17.7% drawdown.","body_zh":"政权切换始于2025年10月底，大盘股估值拉伸、AI资本开支回报争论加剧；2026年初霍尔木兹海峡石油冲击将全程油价推升+70.1%，进一步施压。类滞胀象限（能源领涨+42.9%、成长跑输价值-19.5）在结构上与七巨头相悖：广度大幅转宽（RSP跑赢SPY +8.2%），VIX从17升至31，确认资本从长久期成长股向能源/大宗/价值股轮动。其质地限制了损失（SMH仅-1.3% vs 科技-15.9%），回撤-17.7%。","drivers":["Hormuz oil shock / oil +70.1%","AI-capex ROI debate / valuation reset","stagflation-ish quad (Energy +42.9%, growth-value -19.5)","broadening (RSP +8.2% vs SPY)"],"drivers_zh":["霍尔木兹石油冲击/油价+70.1%","AI资本开支ROI争议/估值重置","类滞胀象限(能源+42.9%, 成长-价值-19.5)","广度转宽(RSP跑赢SPY +8.2%)"],"prev_key":"2025-10-29","prev_key_chain":["2025-10-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Valuation reset and Hormuz oil shock broadens the tape","title_zh":"估值重置与霍尔木兹石油冲击推动行情转宽","turn_id":"mag7:peak:2025-10"},"2026-03-30":{"body":"A Hormuz-area ceasefire allowed oil to fall back and equities rebounded, with the seven surging +28.7% in a tech-led risk-on snapback (SMH +65.5%, VIX 31 to 16, growth/value +10.3) in a reflation/growth-up quad with an extremely narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY by -8.8%). But the rally stalled in late May 2026 as a Broadcom-led semiconductor wipeout in June, AI-spending ROI skepticism, and a broadening tape (RSP now +2.9% vs SPY) eroded the cohort's leadership - leaving the seven rolling over at the 34th percentile.","body_zh":"霍尔木兹地区停火使油价回落、股市反弹，七巨头涨+28.7%，科技引领风险偏好回升（SMH +65.5%、VIX 31到16、成长/价值+10.3），处于再通胀/增长向上象限、极度窄幅（RSP跑输SPY -8.8%）。但2026年5月末反弹停滞：6月博通引领的半导体暴跌、AI支出ROI怀疑情绪升温，以及行情转宽（RSP现跑赢SPY +2.9%）侵蚀群体领导地位——七巨头正在第34百分位见顶回落。","drivers":["Hormuz ceasefire / oil pullback","risk-on snapback (SMH +65.5%, VIX 31->16)","Broadcom/semis June wipeout ending rally","breadth broadening (RSP +2.9%) kills concentration"],"drivers_zh":["霍尔木兹停火/油价回落","风险偏好回升(SMH +65.5%, VIX 31->16)","博通/半导体6月暴跌终结反弹","广度转宽(RSP +2.9%)瓦解集中效应"],"prev_key":"2026-03-30","prev_key_chain":["2026-03-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Hormuz ceasefire bounce stalls on Broadcom wipeout","title_zh":"停火反弹随博通暴跌停滞","turn_id":"mag7:trough:2026-03"}},"now":"The Magnificent Seven are rolling over in a Downturn/Rolling-over phase, sitting at only the 34th percentile of their historical range with a relative-strength rank of just 25 vs the full universe. The current tape is reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +11.2%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%) but the composition is toxic for the cohort: DXY +3.4% creates a revenue headwind for multinationals, growth is lagging value by -15.2 percentage points, and crucially breadth is broadening (RSP +2.9% vs SPY) - the opposite of the narrow mega-cap melt-ups that define the seven's bull legs. Tech still leads YTD but Comm and Discretionary (two other seven-heavy GICS weights) are deep in the red (-9.6%, -5.2%), and semis - up 67.9% from the April 2025 trough - have stalled after the Broadcom-led June 2026 wipeout. The seven are losing their single most reliable driver: concentrated flows into a narrow AI-capex leadership tape, and are now the market's source of drag rather than its engine.","now_zh":"七巨头正处于\"下行/见顶回落\"阶段，仅处于历史区间第34百分位，相对强度排名仅25。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-managed_care":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"Managed Care surged +97% from January 2014 to June 2015, the biggest bull leg in the series, driven by an unprecedented ACA enrollment wave and the emergence of Medicare Advantage as a high-growth segment. The Big Five insurers (UNH, Anthem, Aetna, Cigna, Humana) collectively grew enrollment by 22.5% over 2010–2016 as the ACA's subsidized exchange market, Medicaid expansion, and MA plan growth flooded members in. The macro backdrop was a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (oil -36.5%, TLT +18.7%, DXY +17.8%) that rotated flows into defensives — Health led all sectors at +40.6% vs the SPY at +18.1%, while Energy was the only negative sector. The basket's MCO model (collect premiums, manage the medical-loss ratio, keep the spread) proved structurally superior in a falling-rate, falling-oil defensive regime, and the ACA had converted a regulatory threat into the biggest membership expansion in industry history.","body_zh":"管理式医疗从2014年1月至2015年6月飙升+97%，为本系列最大的牛市行情，由史无前例的ACA参保潮与Medicare Advantage成为高增长板块共同驱动。五大保险商（UNH、安泰、信诺、哈门那、卓越）在ACA补贴交易市场、医疗补助扩张及MA计划增长的推动下，2010–2016年累计参保人数增长22.5%。宏观背景为经济放缓/通缩恐慌象限（油价-36.5%、TLT +18.7%、DXY +17.8%），流动资金轮入防御股——医疗板块以+40.6%领跑所有行业（SPY +18.1%），能源是唯一下跌板块。MCO模式（收取保费、管理医疗损失率、赚取价差）在利率下行、油价下跌的防御环境中显现出结构性优势，而ACA将监管风险转化为行业史上最大规模的参保扩张。","drivers":["ACA enrollment boom — Big Five enrollment +22.5% (2010-2016), exchange + Medicaid expansion + MA growth","Slowdown/deflation-scare quad: Health led at +40.6%, oil -36.5%, TLT +18.7%","MCO premium-minus-MLR spread structurally superior in falling-rate, defensive regime","DXY +17.8% strongest dollar in years — tailwind for domestic-revenue managed care"],"drivers_zh":["ACA参保潮——五大保险商参保量+22.5%（2010–2016），交易所+医疗补助扩张+MA增长","经济放缓/通缩恐慌象限：医疗领跑+40.6%、油价-36.5%、TLT +18.7%","MCO保费减MLR价差在利率下行防御环境中具结构优势","DXY +17.8%强美元——国内营收的管理式医疗受益"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"ACA enrollment boom — defensive mega-rally","title_zh":"ACA参保潮——防御性超级行情","turn_id":"managed_care:trough:2014-01"},"2015-06-25":{"body":"Managed Care peaked in late June 2015 and fell -23% into February 2016 as two forces converged: the August 2015 China yuan devaluation triggered a global growth scare (VIX 14→26, oil -50.3%, credit spreads widened sharply — HYG/LQD -12%), and simultaneously UnitedHealth disclosed in November 2015 that it was losing money on the ACA exchanges (then ~$425M for 2015, ultimately a $720M loss including reserves for 2016) and would scale back marketing and possibly exit most exchange markets by 2017. The risk-off macro regime hit the whole tape (SPY -10.7%), with cyclicals crushed (-14.7%) while defensives held (avg +0.6%, led by Utilities +13.9%, Staples +3.8%). The ACA-exchange-loss disclosure added company-specific valuation pressure on top of the broad-market selloff, as investors questioned the long-term profitability of the ACA business model that had underpinned the prior bull leg.","body_zh":"管理式医疗2015年6月底见顶，随后下跌-23%至2016年2月——两股力量叠加：2015年8月中国人民币贬值引发全球经济恐慌（VIX 14→26、油价-50.3%、信用利差急剧走阔——HYG/LQD -12%）；同时UNH于2015年11月披露ACA交易所亏损（当时约4.25亿美元，含2016年准备金后最终亏损7.2亿美元）并宣布将缩减营销、可能于2017年退出大多数交易所市场。避险宏观环境打击整体大盘（SPY -10.7%），周期股大跌（-14.7%），而防御股持稳（均值+0.6%，公用领涨+13.9%、必需消费+3.8%）。ACA交易所亏损披露在广泛市场下跌之上叠加了公司层面的估值压力，投资者开始质疑支撑前一轮牛市的ACA商业模式的长期盈利能力。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation Aug-2015: global growth scare, VIX 14→26, oil -50.3%","UNH Nov-2015 disclosure: ~$425M ACA exchange loss (ultimately $720M), signaling exit from most exchange markets","Risk-off regime: defensives avg +0.6% vs cyclicals -14.7%, credit spread widened HYG/LQD -12%","ACA exchange-loss news killed the enrollment-boom valuation thesis that drove the prior bull leg"],"drivers_zh":["2015年8月中国人民币贬值：全球经济恐慌、VIX 14→26、油价-50.3%","UNH 2015年11月披露：ACA交易所亏损约4.25亿美元（最终7.2亿），预示退出大多数交易所市场","避险环境：防御股均值+0.6% 对周期股-14.7%，信用利差走阔 HYG/LQD -12%","ACA交易所亏损消息打破支撑前一轮牛市的参保热估值逻辑"],"prev_key":"2015-06-25","prev_key_chain":["2015-06-25"],"status":"exact","title":"China shock + ACA exchange losses peak (-23%)","title_zh":"中国冲击+ACA交易所亏损见顶（-23%）","turn_id":"managed_care:peak:2015-06"},"2016-02-08":{"body":"The near-two-year +89% bull run from February 2016 to January 2018 was driven by two distinct phases. First, the February 2016 global-risk bottom (oil bottomed, China stabilized) launched a cyclical reflation recovery where MCOs rallied alongside the broader risk-on trade. The November 2016 Trump election added a powerful sector-specific kicker: the new administration was explicitly pro-MA, hostile to ACA individual-market mandates (reducing exchange-loss risk), and signaled a business-friendly environment that favored large-cap consolidated insurers. Second, through 2017 the group saw record MA enrollment growth and disciplined medical-cost management. The macro was unambiguously reflation/growth-up (oil +120.8%, Financials +87.6%, Tech +82.1%, cyclicals +68.8% vs defensives +29.5%, DXY -7.5%), and managed care rode the tide while also benefiting from sector-specific policy tailwinds.","body_zh":"从2016年2月至2018年1月近两年的+89%牛市，由两个截然不同的阶段驱动。首先，2016年2月全球风险触底（油价触底、中国企稳）开启了周期性再通胀复苏，MCO随整体风险偏好回升而上涨。2016年11月特朗普当选带来了强有力的板块特异催化剂：新政府明确支持MA、对ACA个人市场强制令持敌意（降低交易所亏损风险），并释放有利于大型合并保险商的友好营商环境信号。其次，整个2017年该组别录得创纪录的MA参保增长和严格的医疗成本管理。宏观环境明确为再通胀/增长向上（油价+120.8%、金融+87.6%、科技+82.1%、周期股+68.8% 对防御股+29.5%、DXY -7.5%），管理式医疗随潮流上涨，同时受益于板块特异政策顺风。","drivers":["Feb-2016 global risk bottom: oil+EM stabilized, reflation/growth-up launched","Trump Nov-2016 election: pro-MA, ACA-mandate hostile, insurer-merger permissive environment","MA enrollment surge + disciplined MLR management drove EPS beat cycle","Cyclicals led (Financials +87.6%, Tech +82.1%) — MCOs carried in the reflation melt-up"],"drivers_zh":["2016年2月全球风险触底：油价+新兴市场企稳，再通胀/增长向上启动","特朗普2016年11月当选：支持MA、对ACA强制令持敌意、允许保险商合并","MA参保激增+严格MLR管理推动EPS超预期","周期股领跑（金融+87.6%、科技+82.1%）——MCO随再通胀融涨上行"],"prev_key":"2016-02-08","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump election + reflation melt-up carries MCOs (+89%)","title_zh":"特朗普当选+再通胀融涨推动MCO（+89%）","turn_id":"managed_care:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-29":{"body":"Managed Care peaked in late January 2018 and fell -17% into March 2018, hit by a double catalyst. First, on January 30, 2018, Amazon, Berkshire Hathaway, and JPMorgan announced a joint healthcare venture (later named Haven) targeting self-insured employee benefits — the 'Amazon-goes-healthcare' headline sent Anthem down ~5%, Cigna down ~7%, and the whole MCO complex into a sharp selloff on disruption fears. Second, the broader market was simultaneously unraveling in the February 2018 'Volmageddon' event — the January 2018 strong payrolls/wage report sparked inflation fears, VIX doubled from 14 to 25, and the SPY fell -9% in what became the February 2018 correction. Managed care fell -17.4%, worse than defensives (-8.9%) because it sat in the laggard group (Health -12.4%) alongside Staples (-12.5%), catching both the sector-specific Amazon news and the broader rates/inflation selloff.","body_zh":"管理式医疗2018年1月底见顶，随后下跌-17%至2018年3月，受双重催化剂打击。首先，2018年1月30日，亚马逊、伯克希尔哈撒韦及摩根大通联合宣布成立医疗合资公司（后命名为Haven），目标针对自保员工福利——'亚马逊进军医疗'头条消息致安泰下跌约5%、信诺下跌约7%，整个MCO板块因颠覆性恐惧急速下跌。其次，整体大盘同时在2018年2月'Volmageddon'事件中瓦解——2018年1月强劲的薪资/工资数据引发通胀恐惧、VIX从14翻倍至25、SPY下跌-9%，演变为2018年2月市场调整。管理式医疗下跌-17.4%，差于防御股（-8.9%），因其处于落后组（医疗-12.4%），与必需消费（-12.5%）并列，同时承受板块特异的亚马逊消息及更广泛的利率/通胀抛售。","drivers":["Amazon-Berkshire-JPMorgan 'Haven' healthcare JV announced Jan-30-2018 — disruption fear","Feb-2018 'Volmageddon': payrolls/wage print triggered inflation scare, VIX 14→25","MCOs lagged (Health -12.4%) alongside Staples (-12.5%); SPY fell -9%","Sector-specific disruption catalyst amplified broad-market correction"],"drivers_zh":["亚马逊-伯克希尔-摩根大通'Haven'医疗合资公司2018年1月30日宣布——颠覆性恐惧","2018年2月'Volmageddon'：薪资数据引发通胀恐惧、VIX 14→25","MCO落后（医疗-12.4%），与必需消费（-12.5%）并列；SPY下跌-9%","板块特异颠覆催化剂放大了大盘修正"],"prev_key":"2018-01-29","prev_key_chain":["2018-01-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Amazon-JHC disruption shock — vol selloff (-17%)","title_zh":"亚马逊-JHC颠覆冲击——波动性抛售（-17%）","turn_id":"managed_care:peak:2018-01"},"2018-03-23":{"body":"Managed Care surged +44% from March 2018 to December 2018, a sharp outperformance fueled by a defensive-rotation bid. The macro turned to a slowdown/deflation-scare quad with a dollar rally (DXY +8.5%) and falling oil (-19.6%) — not supportive of Industrials or Materials but ideal for domestic-revenue, premium-income MCOs. Health led at +20.7% while Industrials (+1.8%), Materials (+0.1%) and Comm (-9.5%) lagged; SPY only returned +9.2%. The Amazon-Haven disruption fear faded as the venture's scope proved limited, and Q2-Q3 2018 earnings were strong with low medical-loss ratios. The rising dollar and defensive rotation made managed care the standout, and high-beta lagged (high-beta minus low-vol -13.7%) confirming the defensive character of the rally.","body_zh":"管理式医疗从2018年3月至12月飙升+44%，由防御性轮动买盘驱动，明显超越大盘。宏观环境转为经济放缓/通缩恐慌象限，伴随美元升值（DXY +8.5%）与油价下跌（-19.6%）——不利于工业或材料，但对国内营收、保费收入的MCO极为理想。医疗板块以+20.7%领跑，工业（+1.8%）、材料（+0.1%）及通信（-9.5%）落后；SPY仅返回+9.2%。随着亚马逊Haven合资公司的范围被证明有限，颠覆性恐惧消退；2018年二三季度业绩强劲，医疗损失率低。美元升值与防御性轮动使管理式医疗成为突出赢家，高贝塔落后（高贝塔减低波-13.7%），印证反弹的防御性属性。","drivers":["Slowdown/deflation-scare quad + DXY +8.5% — ideal for domestic-revenue MCOs","Amazon-Haven disruption fear faded; Q2-Q3 2018 EPS beat with low MLRs","Health led +20.7% vs SPY +9.2%; defensive rotation as Industrials (+1.8%), Comm (-9.5%) lagged","High-beta lagged (high-beta minus low-vol -13.7%) — classic defensive outperformance environment"],"drivers_zh":["放缓/通缩恐慌象限+DXY +8.5%——对国内营收MCO理想","亚马逊Haven恐惧消退；2018年二三季度EPS超预期，MLR低","医疗领跑+20.7% 对SPY +9.2%；工业（+1.8%）、通信（-9.5%）落后时的防御性轮动","高贝塔落后（高贝塔减低波-13.7%）——典型防御性超额表现环境"],"prev_key":"2018-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2018-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Defensive rotation bid in tariff/slowdown quad (+44%)","title_zh":"关税/放缓象限中的防御性轮动买盘（+44%）","turn_id":"managed_care:trough:2018-03"},"2018-12-03":{"body":"Managed Care fell -20% in a compressed three-week crash (December 3–24, 2018) alongside the worst Christmas-Eve selloff in market history. The Fed raised rates a fourth time in December 2018 (to 2.25–2.50%) despite slowing global growth, triggering recession fears and a VIX spike from 16 to 36. SPY fell -15.6% and credit spreads blew out (HYG/LQD -5.3%). While defensives (-11.7%) held better than cyclicals (-16.9%), the managed-care basket fell more than the defensive average because, after a big +44% bull run, it had accumulated valuation premium that investors crystallized during the year-end tax-loss flush. No MCO-specific catalyst — a pure macro panic sell across the whole tape, cushioned vs cyclicals but not immunized.","body_zh":"管理式医疗在历史上最糟糕的圣诞前夕大跌中，于压缩的三周内（2018年12月3日至24日）下跌-20%。美联储2018年12月第四次加息（至2.25–2.50%），无视全球经济放缓，引发衰退恐惧与VIX从16飙升至36。SPY下跌-15.6%，信用利差大幅走阔（HYG/LQD -5.3%）。虽然防御股（-11.7%）比周期股（-16.9%）更抗跌，但管理式医疗篮子跌幅超过防御股平均值，原因是经过+44%的大牛市积累了估值溢价，投资者在年末税损抛售中兑现。无MCO特异催化剂——纯宏观恐慌卖出，相对周期股有所缓冲但未能免疫。","drivers":["Fed Dec-2018 fourth hike (to 2.25-2.50%) despite slowing growth — recession fear","VIX 16→36; SPY -15.6%; credit spreads blew out (HYG/LQD -5.3%)","Tax-loss crystallization of prior +44% bull-run premium — MCOs fell more than defensives avg","Worst Christmas-Eve selloff in history — pure macro panic, no MCO catalyst"],"drivers_zh":["2018年12月美联储第四次加息（至2.25-2.50%），无视经济放缓——衰退恐惧","VIX 16→36；SPY -15.6%；信用利差大幅走阔（HYG/LQD -5.3%）","前期+44%牛市溢价的税损兑现——MCO跌幅超过防御股均值","史上最糟圣诞前夕大跌——纯宏观恐慌，无MCO特异催化剂"],"prev_key":"2018-12-03","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed/recession panic flush — year-end risk-off (-20%)","title_zh":"美联储/衰退恐慌冲洗——年末避险（-20%）","turn_id":"managed_care:peak:2018-12"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"Managed Care bounced +18% from Christmas Eve 2018 into February 2019, riding the broad market recovery after Fed Chairman Powell's 'patient' pivot signal. The January 4, 2019 payrolls report was strong and Powell signaled the Fed was in no hurry to raise rates, triggering a sharp VIX compression (36→15) and a broad risk-on rally led by Industrials (+25.4%), Energy (+22.8%), and Tech (+20.8%). Managed care (+17.7%) lagged the cyclical leaders — the reflation/growth-up quad moved flows toward cyclicals (avg +20.4%) vs defensives (avg +11.5%) — but the group still participated and recovered from the oversold Christmas-Eve low. The Fed pivot was the singular catalyst.","body_zh":"管理式医疗从2018年圣诞前夕至2019年2月反弹+18%，随美联储主席鲍威尔发出'耐心'转鸽信号后的大盘复苏而上涨。2019年1月4日就业数据强劲，鲍威尔表示美联储不急于加息，触发VIX急剧收缩（36→15）和工业（+25.4%）、能源（+22.8%）、科技（+20.8%）领跑的风险偏好全面反弹。管理式医疗（+17.7%）落后于周期性领涨者——再通胀/增长向上象限将流动资金推向周期股（均值+20.4%）而非防御股（均值+11.5%）——但该组别仍参与其中，从超卖的圣诞前夕低点复苏。美联储转鸽是唯一催化剂。","drivers":["Fed 'patient' pivot: Jan-4-2019 Powell signal — no rush to hike, VIX 36→15","Reflation/growth-up recovery led by Industrials (+25.4%), Energy (+22.8%), Tech (+20.8%)","MCOs lagged cyclicals (cyclicals avg +20.4% vs defensives +11.5%) — participated but not led","Oversold bounce from the worst Christmas-Eve selloff in history"],"drivers_zh":["美联储'耐心'转鸽：2019年1月4日鲍威尔信号——不急于加息，VIX 36→15","再通胀/增长向上复苏，工业（+25.4%）、能源（+22.8%）、科技（+20.8%）领跑","MCO落后于周期股（周期均值+20.4% 对防御股+11.5%）——参与但非领跑","从史上最糟圣诞前夕大跌后的超卖反弹"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot bounce — risk-on cyclical-led recovery (+18%)","title_zh":"美联储转鸽反弹——风险偏好周期股领涨复苏（+18%）","turn_id":"managed_care:trough:2018-12"},"2019-02-15":{"body":"Managed Care fell -23% from mid-February to mid-April 2019, a stark sector-specific selloff in the face of a rising broad market (SPY +4.8%, Tech +11.8%, VIX 15→13). The catalyst was the progressive Democratic push for 'Medicare for All' — Sanders prepared to reintroduce his bill (formally introduced in April 2019) and Democratic primary candidates including Warren, Harris, and Booker endorsed it. UNH used its mid-April earnings call to warn M4A would 'destabilize the nation's health system,' and the stock tumbled from ~$246 to ~$208 over the period as investors priced the existential risk: a Sanders/Warren win in 2020 could eliminate private insurance entirely. The macro was benign (VIX calm, oil +14.7%, copper/gold +9.7%) — the damage was 100% policy/regulatory fear, not a risk-off macro event.","body_zh":"管理式医疗从2019年2月中至4月中下跌-23%，是在大盘上涨（SPY +4.8%、科技+11.8%、VIX 15→13）背景下显著的板块特异抛售。催化剂是进步派民主党推动'全民医保'——桑德斯准备重新提交议案（于2019年4月正式提交），民主党初选候选人包括沃伦、哈里斯及布克均表态支持。UNH在4月中旬财报电话会上警告M4A将'破坏全国医疗体系的稳定'，股价在此期间从约246美元跌至约208美元，投资者为存亡性风险定价：2020年桑德斯/沃伦若胜选可能彻底废除私人保险。宏观环境温和（VIX平静、油价+14.7%、铜金+9.7%）——损害100%源于政策/监管恐惧，而非避险宏观事件。","drivers":["Medicare for All: Sanders April-2019 Senate bill + Warren/Harris endorsement","UNH stock fell from ~$246 to ~$208; CEO warned M4A would 'destabilize' the health system","Existential private-insurance risk priced as 2020 primary cycle heated up","Macro was benign (SPY +4.8%, VIX calm) — 100% policy/regulatory selloff"],"drivers_zh":["全民医保：桑德斯2019年4月参议院法案+沃伦/哈里斯背书","UNH股价从约246美元跌至约208美元；CEO警告M4A将'破坏'医疗体系稳定","2020年初选周期升温，市场定价私人保险存亡性风险","宏观温和（SPY +4.8%、VIX平静）——100%政策/监管驱动的抛售"],"prev_key":"2019-02-15","prev_key_chain":["2019-02-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Medicare for All policy shock — idiosyncratic selloff (-23%)","title_zh":"全民医保政策冲击——个体化抛售（-23%）","turn_id":"managed_care:peak:2019-02"},"2019-04-17":{"body":"Managed Care rallied +45% from April 2019 to February 2020, recovering from the Medicare-for-All scare as two things became clear: first, the policy risk receded as the political path for M4A remained blocked, and second, the fundamental story (Medicare Advantage enrollment acceleration, disciplined MLR management, strong EPS growth) remained intact. Q3 2019 earnings reports from UNH, Humana, Centene, and Cigna were strong, driving a multi-week recovery in Q4-2019. The macro shifted to a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (TLT +21.2%, defensives +21.7% vs cyclicals +10.6%, growth dominated at +12.9%, VIX stayed calm 13→14), which was favorable for the MCO safe-haven trade as a very narrow, mega-cap-led tape (RSP lagged SPY -6%). The sector held near the top of the market despite the macro headwinds on cyclicals.","body_zh":"管理式医疗从2019年4月至2020年2月反弹+45%，从全民医保恐惧中复苏，原因是两点逐渐清晰：其一，随着M4A的政治路径受阻，政策风险消退；其二，基本面故事（Medicare Advantage参保加速、严格的MLR管理、强劲的EPS增长）依然完好。2019年三季度UNH、哈门那、Centene及信诺业绩报告强劲，推动2019年四季度多周上涨。宏观环境转为经济放缓/通缩恐慌象限（TLT +21.2%、防御股+21.7% 对周期股+10.6%、成长主导+12.9%、VIX平静13→14），对MCO避险交易有利，且行情极为狭窄、大市值主导（RSP落后SPY -6%）。尽管周期股面临宏观逆风，该板块仍接近市场领跑位置。","drivers":["M4A political path blocked; Q3-2019 EPS beats across UNH, Humana, Centene, Cigna","Slowdown/deflation-scare: TLT +21.2%, defensives +21.7% vs cyclicals +10.6% — safe-haven bid","Mega-cap-led, narrow tape (RSP -6% vs SPY) — defensive MCOs held near top","MA enrollment acceleration + strong MLR discipline drove durable EPS beats"],"drivers_zh":["M4A政治路径受阻；2019年三季度UNH、哈门那、Centene、信诺EPS均超预期","放缓/通缩恐慌：TLT +21.2%、防御股+21.7% 对周期股+10.6%——避险买盘","大市值主导、狭窄行情（RSP落后SPY -6%）——防御性MCO维持领跑","MA参保加速+严格MLR管理推动持久EPS超预期"],"prev_key":"2019-04-17","prev_key_chain":["2019-04-17"],"status":"exact","title":"Medicare for All fear peaks; enrollment + MA growth (+45%)","title_zh":"全民医保恐惧见顶；参保+MA增长（+45%）","turn_id":"managed_care:trough:2019-04"},"2020-02-19":{"body":"Managed Care fell -36% in the COVID-19 pandemic crash from February 19 to March 23, 2020 — one of the sharpest drawdowns in the basket's history. The VIX exploded from 14 to 62 (the highest since 2008), SPY fell -33.7%, credit spreads blew out (HYG/LQD -9.6%), and oil collapsed -56.2%. Health (-27.9%) was the second-best sector (behind Staples -24.2%), demonstrating relative defensiveness vs cyclicals like Energy (-56.1%) and Financials (-42.8%), but managed care at -35.8% fell near the sector average because investors feared pandemic claims would surge and uncertain COVID treatment protocols would spike the MLR. The flight-to-safety rotation (VIX 14→62, defensives -29.2% vs cyclicals -40.2%) provided some cushion, but no sector was immunized.","body_zh":"管理式医疗在2020年2月19日至3月23日的新冠疫情崩盘中下跌-36%——为本篮子历史上最大回撤之一。VIX从14暴涨至62（2008年以来最高），SPY下跌-33.7%，信用利差大幅走阔（HYG/LQD -9.6%），油价暴跌-56.2%。医疗（-27.9%）是第二抗跌板块（仅次于必需消费-24.2%），相对于能源（-56.1%）及金融（-42.8%）等周期股展现防御性；但管理式医疗跌幅达-35.8%，接近板块平均值，原因是投资者担忧疫情理赔将激增、不确定的COVID治疗方案将令MLR飙升。避险轮动（VIX 14→62、防御股-29.2% 对周期股-40.2%）提供了部分缓冲，但无板块可幸免。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic: VIX 14→62 (highest since 2008), SPY -33.7%, oil -56.2%","Fear of pandemic claims surge and COVID treatment costs spiking the MLR","Health was second-best sector (-27.9%) — outperformed cyclicals but deep drawdown","Flight-to-safety cushion: defensives -29.2% vs cyclicals -40.2%"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情：VIX 14→62（2008年以来最高），SPY -33.7%，油价-56.2%","担忧疫情理赔激增及COVID治疗费用令MLR飙升","医疗为第二抗跌板块（-27.9%）——跑赢周期股但仍大幅下跌","避险缓冲：防御股-29.2% 对周期股-40.2%"],"prev_key":"2020-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID-19 pandemic crash — healthcare wasn't spared (-36%)","title_zh":"新冠疫情崩盘——医疗板块未能幸免（-36%）","turn_id":"managed_care:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"Managed Care surged +101% from the March 2020 pandemic low to May 2021, a historic bull run driven by an unexpected COVID windfall: healthcare utilization plummeted as Americans deferred elective procedures during lockdowns, causing managed-care medical-loss ratios to hit historically low levels. UNH's MLR fell to the low 80s; Cigna's 2020 net profits surged year-on-year. Meanwhile, Medicare Advantage enrollment continued growing strongly through the pandemic — the demographic tailwind was untouched. The macro was a reflation/growth-up melt-up (oil +183.9%, Energy +133.5%, Financials +119.8%, cyclicals +117% vs defensives +55.9%, VIX 62→17, DXY -12.2%), and while managed care lagged the cyclical leaders in a broadening tape (RSP beat SPY +23%), the +101% absolute return was exceptional for a traditionally slow-moving defensive group.","body_zh":"管理式医疗从2020年3月疫情低点至2021年5月飙升+101%，由出乎意料的新冠红利驱动：封控期间美国人推迟择期手术，医疗利用率暴跌，导致管理式医疗的医疗损失率降至历史低位。UNH的MLR跌至低80%区间；信诺2020年净利润同比大增。与此同时，Medicare Advantage参保人数在疫情期间持续强劲增长——人口红利无损。宏观为再通胀/增长向上融涨（油价+183.9%、能源+133.5%、金融+119.8%、周期股+117% 对防御股+55.9%、VIX 62→17、DXY -12.2%），管理式医疗在广度扩张的行情中（RSP跑赢SPY +23%）虽落后于周期领涨者，但+101%的绝对回报对于传统防御性组别而言极为亮眼。","drivers":["COVID utilization windfall: MLR hit historic lows as elective care deferred during lockdowns","Cigna FY2020 profit surged YoY; UNH MLR dropped to low-80s","MA enrollment continued growing — demographic tailwind untouched","Reflation/growth-up melt-up (oil +183.9%, cyclicals +117%) carried the tide"],"drivers_zh":["新冠利用率红利：封控期间择期医疗推迟，MLR降至历史低位","信诺2020年净利润同比大增；UNH MLR跌至低80%区间","MA参保持续增长——人口红利无损","再通胀/增长向上融涨（油价+183.9%、周期股+117%）携整体上行"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID windfall + vaccine reopening multi-leg rally (+101%)","title_zh":"新冠红利+疫苗重开放多段行情（+101%）","turn_id":"managed_care:trough:2020-03"},"2021-05-28":{"body":"Managed care drifted -21% into January 2022 — a mild drawdown but caused by two converging headwinds. First, by mid-2021 pandemic-deferred healthcare demand was returning: UNH flagged in Q2 2021 that its medical care ratio rose to 82.8% (vs 70.2% in COVID-impacted Q2 2020) as outpatient volumes surged among seniors returning for delayed elective care. Second, the macro turned stagflation-ish (DXY +8.0%, oil +30.6%, VIX 17→30) as the Fed delayed pivot, which is ambiguously negative for MCOs — not a bad fundamental environment, but dollar strength and energy-cost-driven inflation compressed the relative multiple as the tape rotated to Energy/Commodity names. High-beta lagged (high-beta minus low-vol -12.2%) and the group held up well vs cyclicals, consistent with the defensive character.","body_zh":"管理式医疗缓慢下跌-21%至2022年1月——回撤温和，但由两股汇聚的逆风驱动。首先，至2021年中期，疫情期间推迟的医疗需求开始回归：UNH于2021年二季度指出其医疗成本率升至82.8%（相比新冠影响下的2020年二季度70.2%），老年人返回接受推迟的择期医疗，推动门诊量激增。其次，宏观转向偏滞胀（DXY +8.0%、油价+30.6%、VIX 17→30），美联储推迟转向，这对MCO并非明显利空的基本面环境，但美元走强与能源成本驱动的通胀在行情轮动向能源/大宗商品时压缩了相对估值倍数。高贝塔落后（高贝塔减低波-12.2%），该组别相对于周期股表现良好，符合防御属性。","drivers":["Post-COVID pent-up utilization surge: UNH Q2-2021 MCR rose to 82.8% (vs 70.2% in Q2-2020)","Stagflation-ish macro: DXY +8.0%, oil +30.6%, VIX 17→30 — sector relative multiple compressed","High-beta lagged (high-beta minus low-vol -12.2%); MCOs held up vs cyclicals — defensive character","Energy/Commodity rotation pulled flows OUT of defensives into commodity names"],"drivers_zh":["疫情后压抑需求利用率激增：UNH 2021二季度MCR升至82.8%（对比2020二季度70.2%）","偏滞胀宏观：DXY +8.0%、油价+30.6%、VIX 17→30——板块相对估值倍数收缩","高贝塔落后（高贝塔减低波-12.2%）；MCO相对周期股抗跌——防御属性","能源/大宗商品轮动将流动资金从防御股抽离流向大宗商品名"],"prev_key":"2021-05-28","prev_key_chain":["2021-05-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Pent-up demand MLR surge — stagflation dollar shock (-21%)","title_zh":"压抑需求释放MLR飙升——滞胀美元冲击（-21%）","turn_id":"managed_care:peak:2021-05"},"2022-01-27":{"body":"A +28% rally into April 2022 as capital rotated into defensives during the early-2022 inflation and rate scare — a rate-driven, defensives-led tape (TLT -14.6% as yields surged, defensives +11.1% vs cyclicals +6.6%, VIX 30→20) where Utilities and Real Estate led alongside managed care. With growth stocks unraveling (growth−value -4.7%) and high-beta still soft, the steady, dividend-paying, recession-resistant MCOs were exactly where investors hid — the first of several times this basket plays the safe-haven role. The premium-income, domestically focused MCO model is a structural beneficiary when rates rise and growth de-rates, because their revenues are contractual (premiums) not economically sensitive.","body_zh":"随2022年初通胀与利率恐慌期间资金轮入防御股，出现+28%上涨至2022年4月——一个由利率驱动、防御股领涨的行情（收益率飙升 TLT -14.6%、防御股+11.1% 对周期股+6.6%、VIX 30→20），公用与地产与管理式医疗一同领涨。在成长股瓦解（成长−价值-4.7%）、高贝塔仍疲软之际，稳健、派息、抗衰退的MCO正是投资者的避险去处——这是本篮子多次扮演避风港角色中的第一次。保费收入、国内营收为主的MCO模式在利率上升、成长股估值下杀时具结构性受益属性，因为其营收是合约性的（保费），而非经济周期敏感型。","drivers":["Rate-driven, defensives-led tape (TLT -14.6%, defensives +11.1% vs cyclicals +6.6%)","Growth stocks unraveled (growth−value -4.7%); premium-income MCOs benefited from rate spike","VIX 30→20 compression as capital hid in defensives — first of several safe-haven episodes","Contractual revenue (premiums) structurally benefits when growth de-rates"],"drivers_zh":["利率驱动、防御股领涨行情（TLT -14.6%、防御股+11.1% 对周期股+6.6%）","成长股瓦解（成长−价值-4.7%）；保费收入MCO受益于利率飙升","VIX 30→20收缩，资金躲入防御股——多次避风港行情中的首次","合约性营收（保费）在成长股估值下杀时具结构性受益"],"prev_key":"2022-01-27","prev_key_chain":["2022-01-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Inflation-bear defensive bid — first safe-haven episode (+28%)","title_zh":"通胀熊市防御性买盘——首次避风港行情（+28%）","turn_id":"managed_care:trough:2022-01"},"2022-04-20":{"body":"A shallow -18% give-back into June 2022 alongside the broad market's mid-2022 leg lower (SPY -17.6%, VIX 20→33) in a stagflation-ish rate move (TLT -7.8%, DXY +3.2%). No MCO-specific catalyst — even defensives (-14.5%) were dragged into the general selloff, though they still held better than cyclicals (-16.4%). After a big +28% defensive rally, the group was subject to profit-taking as the broad market entered a more severe rate-tightening-driven bear. May-June 2022 saw the Fed accelerate to 75bp hikes; the yield curve inverted deeply; credit spreads widened. A reminder that in a wholesale risk-off flush, low beta cushions but does not immunize, and managed care is not a zero-beta proxy.","body_zh":"随大盘2022年中段下行（SPY -17.6%、VIX 20→33）、在偏滞胀的利率走势中（TLT -7.8%、DXY +3.2%），出现浅幅-18%回吐至2022年6月。无MCO特异催化剂——即便防御股（-14.5%）也被卷入整体抛售，但仍优于周期股（-16.4%）。经过+28%的大幅防御性反弹后，该组别面临获利了结，大盘进入更严峻的利率收紧驱动熊市。2022年5-6月美联储加速至75基点加息；收益率曲线深度倒置；信用利差走阔。这提醒：在全面避险冲洗中，低贝塔提供缓冲但无法免疫，管理式医疗并非零贝塔替代品。","drivers":["Stagflation-ish rate flush (TLT -7.8%, DXY +3.2%, VIX 20→33, SPY -17.6%)","Fed accelerated to 75bp hikes; yield curve inverted deeply — broad bear extension","Profit-taking after +28% defensive rally; defensives -14.5% but beat cyclicals -16.4%","No MCO-specific catalyst — pulled into general risk-off flush"],"drivers_zh":["偏滞胀利率冲洗（TLT -7.8%、DXY +3.2%、VIX 20→33、SPY -17.6%）","美联储加速至75基点加息；收益率曲线深度倒置——广泛熊市延伸","+28%防御性反弹后的获利了结；防御股-14.5%但跑赢周期股-16.4%","无MCO特异催化剂——被卷入整体避险冲洗"],"prev_key":"2022-04-20","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Macro pullback — defensives caught in rate flush (-18%)","title_zh":"宏观回调——利率冲洗中防御股被卷入（-18%）","turn_id":"managed_care:peak:2022-04"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"A +31% surge into August 2022 as managed care led the defensive trade through the heart of the 2022 bear. The tape was a goldilocks-leaning summer bounce (SPY +17.5%, semis +20.8%, VIX 33→20, oil -24.0%), and notably this defensive group kept pace with the high-beta rip (defensives +14.2% nearly matched cyclicals +15.4%) — printing steady earnings while tech bled and the safe-haven premium widened. The Fed's pace of tightening was becoming more predictable, which reduced uncertainty risk for contractual-revenue MCOs; Q2 2022 earnings were strong as COVID-related cost pressures eased and utilization normalized. The group's relative strength peaked around here before a long 2022-23 multi-month consolidation set in.","body_zh":"随管理式医疗在2022年熊市核心阶段领跑防御交易，出现+31%飙升至2022年8月。当时是偏 goldilocks 的夏季反弹（SPY +17.5%、半导体+20.8%、VIX 33→20、油价-24.0%），值得注意，这一防御组别跟上了高贝塔急升（防御股+14.2% 几乎追平周期股+15.4%）——科技流血之际录得稳定盈利、避险溢价扩大。美联储收紧步伐趋于可预测，降低了合约性营收MCO的不确定性风险；2022年二季度业绩强劲，新冠相关成本压力缓解、利用率正常化。该组别的相对强度在此附近见顶，随后进入漫长的2022-23年多月盘整。","drivers":["Goldilocks summer bounce (semis +20.8%, VIX 33→20, oil -24.0%)","MCOs kept pace with high-beta (defensives +14.2% ~ cyclicals +15.4%) — safe-haven premium","Q2-2022 earnings strong; COVID cost pressures eased; utilization normalized","Relative strength peaked; long 2022-23 consolidation followed"],"drivers_zh":["Goldilocks夏季反弹（半导体+20.8%、VIX 33→20、油价-24.0%）","MCO跟上高贝塔（防御股+14.2% ~ 周期股+15.4%）——避险溢价","2022年二季度业绩强劲；新冠成本压力缓解；利用率正常化","相对强度见顶；随后进入漫长的2022-23年盘整"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Defensive leadership rally through the bear (+31%)","title_zh":"穿越熊市的防御性领导反弹（+31%）","turn_id":"managed_care:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-15":{"body":"Managed care fell -27% into March 2023 — the mirror image of its 2022 strength, and a striking divergence: the broad market barely fell (SPY -7.2%, semis actually +6.2%) but defensives were sold hard (-8.4% vs cyclicals -5.6%, DXY -3.8%). As the November 2022 ChatGPT launch ignited the early-2023 generative-AI risk-on rotation, capital moved OUT of defensives and INTO tech growth names. When the market wants beta, safe-haven MCOs become a source of funds. The sell-off accelerated in Q1-2023 alongside rising concerns about the Medicare Advantage rate methodology (an early signal of the later MLR crisis). The bottom in March 2023 coincided with the SVB bank failure peak-fear, which briefly revived the flight-to-safety bid.","body_zh":"管理式医疗下跌-27%至2023年3月——其2022年强势的镜像，且是惊人的背离：大盘几乎没跌（SPY -7.2%、半导体反而+6.2%），但防御股被大幅抛售（-8.4% 对周期股-5.6%、DXY -3.8%）。随2022年11月ChatGPT发布点燃2023年初生成式AI风险偏好轮动，资金从防御股流出、流入科技成长名。当市场追逐贝塔时，避险型MCO成为资金来源。2023年一季度回落加速，同时伴随对Medicare Advantage费率方法论日益增长的担忧（后来MLR危机的早期信号）。2023年3月的底部恰逢SVB银行倒闭的恐慌峰值，短暂重燃了避险买盘。","drivers":["GenAI rotation: Nov-2022 ChatGPT launch → capital rotated OUT of defensives INTO growth","Divergence: -27% while SPY -7.2% and semis +6.2% — classic safe-haven source-of-funds sell","Early MA rate methodology concerns in Q1-2023 — foreshadowing the later MLR crisis","Bottom at March-2023 SVB peak-fear — flight-to-safety briefly revived"],"drivers_zh":["生成式AI轮动：2022年11月ChatGPT发布→资金从防御股流出流入成长","背离：-27% 而SPY仅-7.2%、半导体+6.2%——典型的避险股作为资金来源被抛售","2023年一季度MA费率方法论早期担忧——预示后来的MLR危机","2023年3月SVB恐慌峰值见底——避险买盘短暂重燃"],"prev_key":"2022-08-15","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-15"],"status":"exact","title":"GenAI risk-on rotation — source-of-funds selloff (-27%)","title_zh":"生成式AI风险偏好轮动——资金来源性抛售（-27%）","turn_id":"managed_care:peak:2022-08"},"2023-03-23":{"body":"A long, steady +57% climb into September 2024 — solid in absolute terms but a laggard versus a roaring goldilocks/growth-up AI melt-up (SPY +45.5%, semis +84.3%, growth−value +25.4%, VIX 23→17) where the market chased large-cap AI names and low-beta defensives trailed (defensives +25.6% vs cyclicals +35.7%, narrow tape RSP lagged SPY -15.4%). Strong MA enrollment, disciplined medical-cost management, and durable EPS growth drove steady gains regardless. This is the last normal uptrend before the 2025 crisis — the calm that preceded the medical-loss-ratio blowout — ending right at the September 2024 peak as the first cracks in MA economics began to appear with rising outpatient utilization and the preliminary 2025 MA rate proposal landing nearly flat.","body_zh":"稳健的长升浪，+57%至2024年9月——绝对意义上扎实，但相对一场轰鸣的goldilocks/增长向上AI融涨（SPY +45.5%、半导体+84.3%、成长−价值+25.4%、VIX 23→17）属于落后者，市场追逐大市值AI名称、低贝塔防御股拖后（防御股+25.6% 对周期股+35.7%、狭窄行情RSP落后SPY -15.4%）。强劲的MA参保、严格的医疗成本管理和持久的EPS增长驱动稳健涨幅。这是2025年危机前最后一段正常上行趋势——医疗损失率失控前的平静——在2024年9月高点结束，恰逢MA经济性首批裂缝显现：门诊利用率上升及2025年MA费率初步提案近乎持平。","drivers":["AI melt-up: semis +84.3%, growth−value +25.4% — defensives lagged, MCOs trailed SPY","Strong MA enrollment + disciplined MLR management → steady EPS beats","Last normal uptrend before the MCR blowout; ended Sep-2024 as first MA cracks appeared","Narrow tape (RSP -15.4% vs SPY) — safe-haven MCOs a source of funds for AI names"],"drivers_zh":["AI融涨：半导体+84.3%、成长−价值+25.4%——防御股落后，MCO跑输SPY","强劲MA参保+严格MLR管理→稳健EPS超预期","MCR失控前最后正常上行趋势；2024年9月结束，MA首批裂缝显现","狭窄行情（RSP落后SPY -15.4%）——避险型MCO成为AI名称的资金来源"],"prev_key":"2023-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2023-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Pre-crisis bull — MA growth lagged the AI melt-up (+57%)","title_zh":"危机前牛市——MA增长跑输AI融涨（+57%）","turn_id":"managed_care:trough:2023-03"},"2024-09-13":{"body":"The first leg down of the crisis: -23% into December 2024, a glaring idiosyncratic break as the broad market rose (SPY +7.9%) in a goldilocks tape (VIX 17→16, growth−value +11.5%, DXY +5.8%). This was company- and sector-specific, not macro — Medicare Advantage cost trends started running hot as utilization (outpatient procedures and increasingly expensive GLP-1 obesity drug prescriptions) overran the actuarial assumptions baked into 2024 premiums. The preliminary 2025 MA rate proposal had come in near-flat, compounding the shock. UNH, Humana, and Centene all guided down. The defensive armor was cracking: investors recognized that the MCO model's pricing power had failed to keep pace with a structural shift in healthcare consumption patterns driven by aging seniors and the GLP-1 super-cycle.","body_zh":"危机的第一段下跌：-23%至2024年12月，是在大盘上涨（SPY +7.9%）、goldilocks行情（VIX 17→16、成长−价值+11.5%、DXY +5.8%）下刺眼的个体化破裂。这是公司和板块特异，而非宏观——Medicare Advantage成本趋势开始升温，利用率（门诊手术及日益昂贵的GLP-1减肥药处方）压垮了2024年保费中内置的精算假设。2025年MA费率初步提案此前近乎持平，加剧冲击。UNH、哈门那及Centene均下调指引。防御铠甲开裂：投资者认识到MCO模式的定价权未能跟上老年人群与GLP-1超级周期驱动的医疗消费结构性转变。","drivers":["MA cost trends ran hot: outpatient utilization + GLP-1 prescription costs overran actuarial assumptions","Near-flat preliminary 2025 MA rate proposal — compounded the cost-trend shock","UNH, Humana, Centene all guided down — sector-wide, not one-company event","Macro benign (SPY +7.9%, VIX 17→16) — 100% sector-specific MCR crisis"],"drivers_zh":["MA成本趋势升温：门诊利用率+GLP-1处方费用压垮精算假设","2025年MA费率初步提案近乎持平——叠加成本趋势冲击","UNH、哈门那、Centene均下调指引——全行业性事件，非单一公司","宏观温和（SPY +7.9%、VIX 17→16）——100%板块特异MCR危机"],"prev_key":"2024-09-13","prev_key_chain":["2024-09-13"],"status":"exact","title":"First MA-cost crack — idiosyncratic selloff vs rising tape (-23%)","title_zh":"首批MA成本裂缝——逆上涨大盘的个体化抛售（-23%）","turn_id":"managed_care:peak:2024-09"},"2024-12-17":{"body":"A +29% bounce into April 2025 as markets hoped the cost-trend problem was transitory and that the final 2025 MA rate would beat the near-flat preliminary proposal. The macro regime turned flight-to-safety (SPY -11.1%, VIX 16→38, defensives flat 0.0% vs cyclicals -10.6%, DXY -6.7%) as the early-2025 tariff war and growth fears weighed on the broader market, so managed care actually attracted a relative bid as a defensive anchor even as the market fell. The CMS final 2025 MA rate came in modestly better than feared. The optimism proved premature — the leg ended right at the April 2025 tariff-crash window, just before UNH's guidance cut revealed that the cost problem was far worse and structural, not transitory.","body_zh":"随市场期望成本趋势只是暂时性，且最终2025年MA费率会好于近乎持平的初步提案，出现+29%反弹至2025年4月。宏观环境转向避险（SPY -11.1%、VIX 16→38、防御股持平0.0% 对周期股-10.6%、DXY -6.7%），2025年初关税战与增长恐惧拖累大盘，管理式医疗反而作为防御锚点吸引了相对买盘，即便市场下跌亦然。CMS最终2025年MA费率略好于市场担忧。乐观情绪事后证明为时过早——该行情恰在2025年4月关税崩盘窗口结束，就在UNH的指引下调揭示成本问题远更严重且为结构性、而非暂时性之前。","drivers":["Flight-to-safety regime (VIX 16→38, defensives 0.0% vs cyclicals -10.6%, SPY -11.1%)","Defensive bid: MCOs attracted relative inflow as tariff-war fears hit cyclicals","Hope cost trend was one-off; final 2025 MA rate slightly better than feared","Ended at April-2025 tariff crash window; UNH guidance cut then confirmed structural crisis"],"drivers_zh":["避险环境（VIX 16→38、防御股0.0% 对周期股-10.6%、SPY -11.1%）","防御性买盘：关税战恐惧打击周期股时MCO吸引相对资金流入","期望成本趋势是一次性；最终2025年MA费率略好于担忧","于2025年4月关税崩盘窗口结束；UNH随后指引下调确认结构性危机"],"prev_key":"2024-12-17","prev_key_chain":["2024-12-17"],"status":"exact","title":"Pre-tariff defensive bounce — hope cost was one-off (+29%)","title_zh":"关税前防御性反弹——期望成本是一次性（+29%）","turn_id":"managed_care:trough:2024-12"},"2025-04-11":{"body":"The deepest leg of the crisis: -33% into August 2025 while the broad market roared back (SPY +16.8%, semis +41.1%, high-beta minus low-vol +36.3%, VIX 38→20). This was pure company-specific carnage in the face of a risk-on melt-up — UNH cut 2025 guidance and the market finally priced the full severity: the medical care ratio blowing out toward ~88.9%, full-year 2025 net profit down ~16%, cost overrun confirmed as industry-wide and structural, not transitory. GLP-1 obesity-drug utilization (the irony: a transformative treatment for chronic disease) emerged as a key cost driver alongside pandemic-deferred care returning en masse. A leadership and regulatory cloud over UNH (including a reported DOJ probe) deepened the gloom. The group's safe-haven armor offered zero cushion because the problem was fundamental earnings destruction, not macro — though near the August trough Berkshire Hathaway disclosed a fresh ~$1.6B UNH stake (revealed Aug-14-2025), an early signal the worst was being priced.","body_zh":"危机最深的一段：-33%至2025年8月，而大盘狂飙回升（SPY +16.8%、半导体+41.1%、高贝塔减低波+36.3%、VIX 38→20）。这是面对风险偏好融涨时纯粹的公司特异屠杀——UNH下调2025年指引，市场终于定价完整严重程度：医疗成本率向约88.9%失控、2025全年净利润下降约16%、成本超支被确认为全行业性且结构性而非暂时性。讽刺的是，GLP-1减肥药利用率（慢性病的变革性治疗）与疫情期间推迟的医疗需求集中回归，共同成为关键成本驱动因素。UNH的领导层及监管阴云（包括据报的司法部调查）加深悲观。该组别的避险属性完全没有提供缓冲，因为问题是基本面的盈利破坏，而非宏观——但在8月低点附近，伯克希尔哈撒韦披露了约16亿美元的UNH新建持仓（2025年8月14日揭晓），是最坏情形正被定价的早期信号。","drivers":["UNH guidance cut: MCR toward ~88.9%; FY2025 net profit -16% — full severity priced","Cost overrun industry-wide and structural: pent-up care returns + GLP-1 utilization surge","Stunning divergence: -33% while SPY +16.8%, semis +41.1% — safe-haven armor useless","Leadership/regulatory cloud (reported DOJ probe); Berkshire BOUGHT a ~$1.6B UNH stake near the Aug trough — early bottoming signal"],"drivers_zh":["UNH指引下调：MCR向约88.9%失控；2025全年净利润-16%——完整严重程度被定价","成本超支全行业且结构性：推迟医疗集中回归+GLP-1利用率激增","惊人背离：-33% 而SPY +16.8%、半导体+41.1%——避险属性毫无缓冲","领导层/监管阴云（据报司法部调查）；伯克希尔在8月低点附近买入约16亿美元UNH持仓——早期筑底信号"],"prev_key":"2025-04-11","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Crisis capitulation — idiosyncratic vs roaring risk-on (-33%)","title_zh":"危机投降——逆狂飙风险偏好的个体化下跌（-33%）","turn_id":"managed_care:peak:2025-04"},"2025-08-01":{"body":"A sharp +37% snapback into October 2025 — the first sign the worst was priced. The recovery was stock-specific in a quiet, near-trendless tape (SPY +8.6%, VIX 20→16, balanced cyclicals +6.8% vs defensives +5.0%, growth−value +3.3%). Bombed-out valuations, early evidence that 2026 repricing (insurers raising premiums and tightening benefits) would restore the spread, and the sense that the capitulation had overshot drove the oversold bounce — with Berkshire's freshly disclosed UNH stake (revealed mid-August) adding a confidence anchor. Health was the second-best sector at +10.7%, confirming the group had turned from laggard to market leader. Fundamentals, not the macro regime, did the work — the thesis was simple: premiums would be repriced for the 2026 plan year to recover the structural cost overshoot.","body_zh":"急速回升+37%至2025年10月——最坏情形已被定价的第一个迹象。复苏是个股驱动，处于平静、近乎无趋势的行情（SPY +8.6%、VIX 20→16、周期股+6.8% 与防御股+5.0% 均衡、成长-价值+3.3%）。被打入谷底的估值、2026年重定价（保险公司提高保费、收紧福利以恢复价差）将带来修复的早期证据、以及投降已超调的感觉，共同驱动超卖反弹——伯克希尔新披露的UNH持仓（8月中旬揭晓）增添了信心锚。医疗以+10.7%成为第二强板块，印证该组别从落后者转为市场领跑者。是基本面、而非宏观环境在发挥作用——论点简单：将对2026年计划年度的保费进行重定价，以追回结构性成本超支。","drivers":["Bombed-out valuations; first evidence 2026 premium repricing would restore the MLR spread","Berkshire's freshly disclosed UNH stake (mid-Aug) added a confidence anchor near the low","Health second-best sector (+10.7%) — turned from laggard to market leader","Quiet, near-trendless tape (SPY +8.6%, balanced cyclicals/defensives) — fundamentals drove"],"drivers_zh":["谷底估值；2026年保费重定价将恢复MLR价差的首个证据","伯克希尔新披露的UNH持仓（8月中旬）在低点附近增添信心锚","医疗第二强板块（+10.7%）——从落后者转为市场领跑","平静、近乎无趋势行情（SPY +8.6%、周期/防御均衡）——基本面驱动"],"prev_key":"2025-08-01","prev_key_chain":["2025-08-01"],"status":"exact","title":"First recovery bounce — bombed-out valuation snapback (+37%)","title_zh":"首次复苏反弹——谷底估值急速回升（+37%）","turn_id":"managed_care:trough:2025-08"},"2025-10-08":{"body":"A -18% pullback into November 2025 — a normal retest as the recovery digested, with the broad tape softening into a mild flight-to-safety (SPY -3.1%, VIX 16→26, defensives +0.3% vs cyclicals -4.7%). Notably the defensive group outperformed in the dip: Health was the top sector at +4.8% while the basket fell -17.8%, suggesting some MCO-specific mean reversion within the defensive envelope. The 2026 setup was not yet fully confirmed — the MCR trajectory, insurer benefit designs, and CMS rate finalization were still all in question. Part of the bottoming process, not a new structural down-leg, as the subsequent +24.8% bounce confirmed.","body_zh":"回调-18%至2025年11月——复苏消化期间的正常回踩，大盘转软进入温和避险（SPY -3.1%、VIX 16→26、防御股+0.3% 对周期股-4.7%）。值得注意，防御组别在回调中反而跑赢：医疗以+4.8%成为最强板块，而篮子跌-17.8%，显示在防御框架内MCO存在一定均值回归。2026年格局尚未完全确认——MCR轨迹、保险公司福利设计及CMS费率最终确定均存疑。这是筑底过程的一部分，而非新的结构性下跌段，随后的+24.8%反弹证实了这一点。","drivers":["Mild flight-to-safety (SPY -3.1%, VIX 16→26, defensives +0.3% > cyclicals -4.7%)","Health top sector (+4.8%) while basket fell — MCO-specific mean reversion within defensive frame","2026 MCR trajectory/CMS rate not yet confirmed — uncertainty caused retest","Part of bottoming process; confirmed by subsequent +24.8% leg"],"drivers_zh":["温和避险（SPY -3.1%、VIX 16→26、防御股+0.3%跑赢周期股-4.7%）","医疗最强板块（+4.8%），篮子却下跌——防御框架内MCO特异均值回归","2026年MCR轨迹/CMS费率尚未确认——不确定性引发回踩","筑底过程的一部分；随后+24.8%的行情予以确认"],"prev_key":"2025-10-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-10-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Choppy bottoming retest in mild risk-off (-18%)","title_zh":"温和避险回踩中的震荡筑底（-18%）","turn_id":"managed_care:peak:2025-10"},"2025-11-20":{"body":"A +25% leg into January 2026 as the 2026-recovery thesis solidified, in a broadening reflation/growth-up tape (SPY +6.4%, VIX 26→16, RSP beat SPY +3.6%, cyclicals +10.4% vs defensives +3.9%). Signs that the medical-cost trend was peaking and that insurers' benefit redesigns and premium hikes would stick in the 2026 plan year gave the market conviction that trough earnings were in. The final 2027 MA rate discussions began pointing toward improvement, and early Q4 2025 enrollment data showed the benefit changes were holding. The group reclaimed defensive-leadership character and began building toward the final, explosive recovery leg.","body_zh":"随2026年复苏论点夯实，出现+25%上涨至2026年1月，处于广度转宽的再通胀/增长向上行情（SPY +6.4%、VIX 26→16、RSP跑赢SPY +3.6%、周期股+10.4% 对防御股+3.9%）。医疗成本趋势见顶、保险公司福利重新设计和保费提价将在2026年计划年度站稳的迹象，给了市场盈利低点已现的信心。2027年MA最终费率讨论开始指向改善，2025年四季度初期参保数据显示福利调整正在落实。该组别重拾防御领导属性，开始为最后的爆发性复苏行情积蓄力量。","drivers":["2026 repricing thesis confirmed: benefit redesigns + premium hikes held in 2026 plan year","Medical-cost trend peaked; early Q4-2025 enrollment data confirmed benefit changes held","VIX 26→16 compression + broadening tape (RSP beat SPY +3.6%) — conviction built","Reclaimed defensive leadership ahead of the final recovery leg"],"drivers_zh":["2026年重定价论点确认：福利重设+保费提价在2026年计划年度站稳","医疗成本趋势见顶；2025四季度初期参保数据确认福利调整落实","VIX 26→16收缩+广度转宽行情（RSP跑赢SPY +3.6%）——信心建立","最终复苏行情前重拾防御领导地位"],"prev_key":"2025-11-20","prev_key_chain":["2025-11-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Recovery confirmation — 2026 repricing thesis firms (+25%)","title_zh":"复苏确认——2026年重定价论点夯实（+25%）","turn_id":"managed_care:trough:2025-11"},"2026-01-15":{"body":"A -26% drawdown into March 2026, overlapping the 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil-supply shock that sent oil +73.8%, VIX from 16 to 31, and the whole market lower (SPY -8.5%, Financials -10.6%, Tech -12.2%). This was a stagflation-ish flush where even defensives (avg -0.7%) were dragged down — Energy (+31.0%) was the lone winner as oil spiked. After a large recovery run, managed care was a profit-taking target; the rising CPI (oil-driven) added concerns that the Fed would stay restrictive, keeping the discount rate elevated for MCO valuations. Notably managed care held better than cyclicals (defensives -0.7% vs cyclicals -1.7%), and the dip proved to be the launchpad for the +73% final recovery leg.","body_zh":"回撤-26%至2026年3月，与2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹石油供应冲击重叠，油价+73.8%、VIX从16升至31，全市场下跌（SPY -8.5%、金融板块-10.6%、科技-12.2%）。这是一个偏滞胀的冲洗，即便防御股（均值-0.7%）也被拖低——能源（+31.0%）是油价飙升中的唯一赢家。经过大幅复苏后，管理式医疗成为获利了结的目标；油价驱动的CPI上升引发对美联储保持限制性立场的担忧，令MCO估值的贴现率保持高位。值得注意，管理式医疗比周期股更抗跌（防御股-0.7% 对周期股-1.7%），而这次回调事后证明是+73%最终复苏行情的发射台。","drivers":["2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock: oil +73.8%, VIX 16→31, SPY -8.5% — stagflation flush","Even defensives caught (avg -0.7%) but held better than cyclicals (-1.7%)","Profit-taking after large recovery run; CPI concerns kept Fed discount rate elevated","Dip proved to be the launchpad for the +73% final recovery leg"],"drivers_zh":["2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击：油价+73.8%、VIX 16→31、SPY -8.5%——滞胀冲洗","即便防御股被卷入（均值-0.7%），但比周期股（-1.7%）更抗跌","大幅复苏后的获利了结；CPI担忧令美联储贴现率保持高位","此次回调事后证明是+73%最终复苏行情的发射台"],"prev_key":"2026-01-15","prev_key_chain":["2026-01-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil-shock stagflation flush — defensives caught (-26%)","title_zh":"油价冲击滞胀冲洗——防御股被卷入（-26%）","turn_id":"managed_care:peak:2026-01"},"2026-03-30":{"body":"The capstone: +73% from the March 2026 low into late June 2026, the stock-specific recovery leg that pinned the basket at the top of its range (pos 99.7, RS #4) as a low-beta defensive LED even as the broad tape went reflation/growth-up (Tech +42.0%, semis +68.7%, high-beta minus low-vol +30.7%). The 2026 economics were confirmed in the print: Q1-2026 MCR improved to ~83.9%, UNH raised 2026 EPS guidance, and CMS finalized favorable 2027 MA rates (~2.48%, finalized April 6, 2026, well above the near-flat advance notice), with the Street modeling a sharp MA-EBIT rebound off the pricing resets. The mid-June 2026 Hormuz ceasefire (oil -32.7%) removed the macro tail and let the recovery run clean. The honest caveat: Topping at pos 99.7 means the easy repricing trade is done — respect the move, but utilization and policy risk never fully leave this group.","body_zh":"收官之作：自2026年3月低点至2026年6月底+73%，正是这段个股驱动的复苏行情把篮子钉在区间顶部（pos 99.7、RS第4位），一个低贝塔防御品领跑，即便大盘转入由科技（+42.0%）、半导体（+68.7%）与高贝塔（高贝塔减低波+30.7%）领跑的再通胀/增长向上。2026年的经济性在财报中确认：2026一季度MCR改善至约83.9%、UNH上调2026年EPS指引、CMS敲定有利的2027年MA费率（约2.48%，2026年4月6日敲定，远高于近乎持平的预先通知），华尔街据定价重置建模MA-EBIT的急剧反弹。2026年6月中旬霍尔木兹停火（油价-32.7%）消除了宏观尾部，让复苏得以干净推进。诚实的提醒：pos 99.7处见顶意味着容易的重估已完成——尊重涨势，但利用率与政策风险从未真正离开这一组别。","drivers":["Q1-2026 MCR improved to ~83.9%; UNH raised 2026 EPS guidance — full fundamental confirmation","CMS finalized favorable 2027 MA rates (~2.48%, Apr-6-2026, above near-flat advance notice) — Street modeled sharp MA-EBIT rebound","Mid-June 2026 Hormuz ceasefire (oil -32.7%) removed macro tail risk","Low-beta defensive LED the reflation tape (Tech +42.0%, semis +68.7%) — idiosyncratic leadership"],"drivers_zh":["2026一季度MCR改善至约83.9%；UNH上调2026年EPS指引——基本面完整确认","CMS敲定有利的2027年MA费率（约2.48%，2026年4月6日，高于近乎持平的预先通知）——华尔街建模MA-EBIT急剧反弹","2026年6月中旬霍尔木兹停火（油价-32.7%）消除宏观尾部风险","低贝塔防御领跑再通胀行情（科技+42.0%、半导体+68.7%）——个体化领导"],"prev_key":"2026-03-30","prev_key_chain":["2026-03-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Final recovery blow-off — leading from the defensive side (+73%)","title_zh":"最终复苏喷发——从防御侧领跑（+73%）","turn_id":"managed_care:trough:2026-03"}},"now":"Managed Care & Insurers is pinned at pos 99.7 with RS rank #4 — a violent, idiosyncratic recovery from a genuine industry crisis that has now fully repriced. The current tape is reflation/growth-up (Tech +24.3%, Energy +21.5%, high-beta minus low-vol +20.7%) yet this low-beta defensive basket is leading from the wrong side of the style spectrum, confirming the recovery is stock-specific, not a macro beta trade. Q1-2026 MCR improved to ~83.9%, UNH raised 2026 EPS guidance, and CMS finalized favorable 2027 MA rates (~2.48%), completing the earnings repricing cycle. At Topping with the full fundamental thesis now in the price, the honest read is that the easy recovery gain is done — utilization normalization, GLP-1 cost trajectories, and the next MA rate proposal are the live risks, and pos 99.7 is exactly where you watch for exhaustion rather than chase.","now_zh":"管理式医疗与保险板块当前位置99.7、RS排名第4——一场真实行业危机后的剧烈个体化复苏已完全重新定价。当前大盘处于再通胀/增长向上行情（科技+24.3%、能源+21.5%、高贝塔减低波+20.7%），而这一低贝塔防御型篮子却从市场风格的对立面领跑，印证复苏是个股驱动而非宏观贝塔交易。2026一季度MCR改善至约83.9%、UNH上调2026年EPS指引、CMS敲定有利的2027年MA费率（约2.48%），盈利重定价周期已完成。在基本面论点完全反映于股价的见顶阶段，客观判断是容易获得的复苏收益已告终——利用率正常化、GLP-1成本轨迹及下一轮MA费率提案是现实风险，pos 99.7正是该警惕衰竭、而非追涨的位置。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-memory_storage":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"Memory stocks rallied 35% through 2014, riding a supply-rational DRAM market reshaped by Elpida's 2012 bankruptcy and Micron's 2013 acquisition — the three-player oligopoly (Micron/Samsung/SK Hynix) held DRAM capacity flat while PC demand held and mobile DRAM grew. The macro backdrop was a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (TLT +26.8%, defensives led 25.8% vs cyclicals 10.3%, oil -41.2%), so the basket's 35% gain versus SPY +15.7% was driven by idiosyncratic sector pricing power rather than broad cyclical tailwinds. DRAM EBIT margins exceeded 25% in 2014 as ASPs held firm, rewarding disciplined memory producers in a deflationary tape.","body_zh":"受益于Elpida 2012年破产重组后美光2013年完成收购所塑造的供给理性DRAM格局，内存股全年上涨35%。三巨头寡占（美光/三星/SK海力士）保持DRAM产能平稳，PC需求维持、移动DRAM增长。宏观处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限（TLT +26.8%，防御股+25.8%对周期股+10.3%，油-41.2%），篮子35%涨幅大幅跑赢SPY +15.7%，源于行业定价权而非周期性需求。2014年DRAM息税前利润率超25%，ASP维稳，在通缩行情中奖励了严守纪律的内存厂商。","drivers":["DRAM oligopoly pricing power","Elpida/Micron consolidation","mobile DRAM growth","defensives-led deflationary tape"],"drivers_zh":["DRAM寡头定价权","Elpida/美光整合","移动DRAM增长","防御领涨通缩行情"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"DRAM consolidation boom, PC refresh tailwind","title_zh":"DRAM整合牛市，PC换机周期顺风","turn_id":"memory_storage:trough:2014-01"},"2014-12-22":{"body":"Memory crashed 59% over 13 months as China smartphone sales declined year-over-year for the first time in six years in Q1 2015 — exactly as producers had ramped mobile DRAM capacity — producing a severe inventory glut. Macro compounded the damage: oil collapsed -45%, DXY surged +10.7%, and VIX climbed 15→24 in a broad risk-off flight-to-safety (defensives -1.4% vs cyclicals -13.8%, SPY -7.7%), which amplified the high-beta memory downturn (SMH -11.2%). Gartner forecast a 17.4% decline in DRAM industry revenue for 2016 as oversupply persisted and PC demand continued to erode, validating the deep selloff.","body_zh":"2015年Q1中国智能手机销量六年来首次同比下滑——恰逢厂商刚刚扩张移动DRAM产能——造成严重库存积压，内存股13个月暴跌59%。宏观雪上加霜：油价大跌-45%，美元指数飙升+10.7%，VIX从15升至24，避险主导（防御股-1.4%对周期股-13.8%，SPY -7.7%），放大了高贝塔内存的跌势（SMH -11.2%）。Gartner预测2016年DRAM行业营收将下降17.4%，供过于求持续叠加PC需求侵蚀，印证了此轮深度下跌。","drivers":["China smartphone demand collapse","DRAM oversupply","oil crash/dollar surge","risk-off flight-to-safety"],"drivers_zh":["中国智能手机需求崩塌","DRAM供过于求","油价崩跌/美元飙升","避险资金轮动"],"prev_key":"2014-12-22","prev_key_chain":["2014-12-22"],"status":"exact","title":"China mobile saturation triggers DRAM glut selloff","title_zh":"中国移动需求饱和引发DRAM供过于求抛售","turn_id":"memory_storage:peak:2014-12"},"2016-01-25":{"body":"Memory bounced 25% in two months as the January-February 2016 global growth-scare trough reversed sharply — oil surged +36.6%, DXY fell -3.7%, VIX compressed 24→14, and the cyclicals-led reflation rotation (cyclicals +14.1% vs defensives +7.2%) pulled high-beta semis with it (SMH +13.9%). Supply-side, DRAM producers began signalling output cuts, and Micron guided for stabilizing ASPs. The broad equal-weight beat (+3.5% RSP vs SPY) confirmed the turn was macro-driven rather than memory-specific.","body_zh":"2016年1至2月全球成长恐慌低点急剧逆转，内存两月反弹25%——油价大涨+36.6%，美元指数跌-3.7%，VIX从24压缩至14，周期股主导再通胀轮动（周期股+14.1%对防御股+7.2%）带动高贝塔半导体反弹（SMH +13.9%）。供给侧，DRAM厂商开始释放削减产量信号，美光对ASP企稳作出指引。等权重跑赢大盘（RSP +3.5%对SPY）印证此轮反弹由宏观驱动而非内存基本面专属。","drivers":["oil/commodity reflation bounce","VIX compression","macro cyclical rotation","DRAM output cut signals"],"drivers_zh":["大宗商品再通胀反弹","VIX压缩","宏观周期股轮动","DRAM减产信号"],"prev_key":"2016-01-25","prev_key_chain":["2016-01-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Reflation rebound; memory trough confirmed","title_zh":"再通胀反弹；内存触底确认","turn_id":"memory_storage:trough:2016-01"},"2016-03-22":{"body":"Memory fell 27.5% in under two months as the reflation rally faded into a stagflation-ish quad (oil +11.5% but copper-gold -11.1%, cyclicals barely positive +0.3% vs defensives +1.8%, SPY flat +0.1%). The broader semis index dropped -6.3% (SMH) as PC inventory data remained poor and DRAM channel checks showed persistent oversupply. No single macro catalyst drove the move — rather, the failed follow-through on the reflation rebound exposed that the memory-specific glut was unresolved, and risk appetite softened (VIX 14→15) without providing a clean risk-off signal.","body_zh":"再通胀行情消退陷入类滞胀象限（油+11.5%但铜金-11.1%，周期股仅+0.3%对防御股+1.8%，SPY持平+0.1%），内存不足两月跌27.5%。SMH跌-6.3%，PC库存数据持续疲软，DRAM渠道调查显示供过于求未解。此轮下跌没有单一宏观催化剂——再通胀反弹失败后，内存行业库存问题暴露，风险偏好小幅降温（VIX 14→15），但未形成干净的避险信号。","drivers":["reflation rally exhaustion","stagflation-ish quad","DRAM channel oversupply","PC demand weakness"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀行情熄火","类滞胀象限","DRAM渠道库存过剩","PC需求疲软"],"prev_key":"2016-03-22","prev_key_chain":["2016-03-22"],"status":"exact","title":"Stagflation-lite pause; memory excess persists","title_zh":"类滞胀间歇回调；内存库存过剩延续","turn_id":"memory_storage:peak:2016-03"},"2016-05-13":{"body":"Memory produced its largest pre-AI cycle gain — +296% over 22 months — driven by three simultaneous tailwinds: Android smartphone storage capacity upgrades, early hyperscaler cloud server DRAM buildouts, and a supply-side squeeze as manufacturers diverted capacity to 3D NAND production, constraining traditional DRAM output. Micron's revenue surged 64% to $20.3B in FY2017 and another 50% to $30.4B in FY2018 as DRAM gross margins peaked near 59%. The macro backdrop was textbook risk-on (SMH +121.6%, semis-led tech +70.2%, VIX calm 15→16, DXY -4.6%, oil +34.9%, copper-gold +46.0%), amplifying already-strong sector fundamentals.","body_zh":"内存在22个月内录得前AI时代最大涨幅+296%，受三重顺风驱动：Android智能手机存储规格升级、早期超大规模云服务商服务器DRAM建设，以及厂商将产能转向3D NAND生产导致传统DRAM供给收紧。美光FY2017营收大增64%至203亿美元，FY2018再涨50%至304亿美元，DRAM毛利率峰值接近59%。宏观背景为教科书式风险偏好（SMH +121.6%，科技股+70.2%，VIX平稳15→16，美元-4.6%，油+34.9%，铜金+46.0%），进一步放大了已强劲的行业基本面。","drivers":["3D NAND capacity diversion tightens DRAM","cloud server DRAM demand","smartphone storage upgrades","tech/semis-led risk-on"],"drivers_zh":["3D NAND转产收紧DRAM供给","云服务器DRAM需求","智能手机存储升级","科技/半导体领涨风险偏好"],"prev_key":"2016-05-13","prev_key_chain":["2016-05-13"],"status":"exact","title":"Two-year memory supercycle: cloud, 3D NAND, phones","title_zh":"两年内存超级周期：云计算、3D NAND与智能手机升级","turn_id":"memory_storage:trough:2016-05"},"2018-03-16":{"body":"Memory fell 44% through December 2018 as three forces converged: the US-China trade war escalated from March steel/aluminum tariffs through the sweeping Section 301 tariffs of July-September, crushing demand uncertainty; Fed tightening pushed VIX from 16 to 36 and dollar +7.0% in a classic risk-off rotation (defensives -1.8% vs cyclicals -17.7%, SMH -25.9%); and DRAM oversupply built as smartphone demand cratered and the PC channel refilled. The PHLX Semiconductor Index fell ~25% from October-December 2018 alone — the Q4 liquidation confirming both macro and memory-specific peak.","body_zh":"三重力量交汇，内存下跌44%：美中贸易战从3月钢铝关税升级至7-9月大规模301条款关税，需求不确定性骤升；美联储收紧推动VIX从16飙至36，美元+7.0%，典型避险轮动（防御股-1.8%对周期股-17.7%，SMH -25.9%）；与此同时智能手机需求崩塌、PC渠道补库存导致DRAM供过于求累积。费城半导体指数仅Q4便下跌约25%——四季度清仓确认了宏观与内存行业双顶。","drivers":["US-China Section 301 tariffs","Fed rate hikes / rate shock","DRAM oversupply / smartphone demand crash","VIX spike risk-off"],"drivers_zh":["美中301条款关税","美联储加息/利率冲击","DRAM供过于求/智能手机需求崩塌","VIX飙升避险"],"prev_key":"2018-03-16","prev_key_chain":["2018-03-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade-war + rate-shock + DRAM glut bear","title_zh":"贸易战+利率冲击+DRAM供过于求熊市","turn_id":"memory_storage:peak:2018-03"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"Memory rebounded 50% in four months as Fed Chair Powell pivoted to a patient stance in January 2019 — markets priced out further rate hikes — and Micron's December 2018 earnings call (CEO Sanjay Mehrotra guided Q3 FY2019 DRAM demand recovery, noting PC and smartphone channel inventories nearing normal) signalled the memory trough. The macro setup was a broad risk-on reflation (VIX 36→12, cyclicals +28% vs defensives +12%, semis +45.4%, oil +50.5%), and this high-beta basket amplified every point of the recovery versus SPY +24.3%.","body_zh":"2019年1月美联储主席鲍威尔转向耐心立场，市场撤回进一步加息预期；美光2018年12月财报电话会中CEO Sanjay Mehrotra指引FY2019 Q3 DRAM需求复苏、PC及智能手机渠道库存趋于正常，发出内存触底信号。内存四个月反弹50%。宏观全面风险偏好（VIX 36→12，周期股+28%对防御股+12%，半导体+45.4%，油+50.5%），高贝塔篮子相较SPY +24.3%放大了每一个复苏点。","drivers":["Fed Powell pivot / pause","memory inventory normalization","DRAM bit demand recovery","broad risk-on reflation"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔转鸽/暂停加息","内存库存正常化","DRAM位需求复苏","全面风险偏好再通胀"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell pivot + memory inventory clear fuels rebound","title_zh":"鲍威尔转鸽+内存库存出清推动反弹","turn_id":"memory_storage:trough:2018-12"},"2019-04-18":{"body":"Memory fell 25% in six weeks as President Trump escalated China trade tensions — tariff rates on $200B of Chinese goods rose from 10% to 25% on May 10, 2019 — slamming semiconductor demand expectations and triggering a growth-scare quad (VIX 12→19, TLT +7.5%, defensives flat +0.3% vs cyclicals -8.1%, SMH -16.6%). Micron was additionally targeted by China's Fujian Jinhua infringement dispute, compounding supply chain uncertainty. The selloff was positioning-driven and macro-led: memory-specific fundamentals had stabilized, but the basket was pricing in a demand hole from the tariff shock.","body_zh":"2019年5月10日特朗普将2000亿美元中国商品关税从10%提至25%，打压半导体需求预期，触发成长恐慌象限（VIX 12→19，TLT +7.5%，防御股持平+0.3%对周期股-8.1%，SMH -16.6%），内存六周跌25%。美光还因福建晋华侵权纠纷额外受压，供应链不确定性加剧。此轮抛售由仓位与宏观主导：内存基本面已趋稳，但篮子在消化关税冲击带来的需求缺口预期。","drivers":["May 2019 25% tariff escalation","trade-war demand shock","growth-scare / TLT rally","SMH high-beta amplification"],"drivers_zh":["2019年5月25%关税升级","贸易战需求冲击","成长恐慌/TLT上涨","SMH高贝塔放大"],"prev_key":"2019-04-18","prev_key_chain":["2019-04-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade-war escalation and growth scare flush","title_zh":"贸易战升级与成长恐慌冲洗","turn_id":"memory_storage:peak:2019-04"},"2019-05-31":{"body":"Memory surged 58% over eight months as the G20 Osaka trade truce (June 29, 2019) paused tariff escalation and the Fed delivered three insurance cuts (July, September, October 2019), compressing VIX 19→13 and supporting risk assets. Semis led with SMH +53.2%, riding a goldilocks/slowdown-scare quad (TLT +8.5%, oil flat, copper-gold -16.8%), with tech +37.5% atop a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP lagged SPY -3.5%). Micron's FY2019 Q4 results confirmed the inventory trough had passed and customer restocking was underway, grounding the rally in improving memory fundamentals as well as macro flow.","body_zh":"G20大阪贸易休战（2019年6月29日）暂停关税升级，美联储三次预防性降息（7月、9月、10月），VIX从19压缩至13，内存八个月大涨58%。半导体领涨SMH +53.2%，处于温和放缓/通缩恐慌象限（TLT +8.5%，油持平，铜金-16.8%），科技+37.5%主导大盘股窄幅行情（RSP跑输SPY -3.5%）。美光FY2019 Q4业绩确认库存触底、客户补库存展开，为行情提供基本面支撑。","drivers":["G20 Osaka trade truce","Fed three insurance cuts","DRAM inventory trough confirmed","tech/semis-led narrow melt-up"],"drivers_zh":["G20大阪贸易休战","美联储三次预防性降息","DRAM库存触底确认","科技/半导体领涨窄幅飙升"],"prev_key":"2019-05-31","prev_key_chain":["2019-05-31"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade truce and Fed cuts ignite memory rally","title_zh":"贸易休战与美联储降息点燃内存反弹","turn_id":"memory_storage:trough:2019-05"},"2020-01-23":{"body":"Memory fell 42% in under two months as COVID-19 triggered a global market rout — VIX exploded 13→66 (a level exceeded only by 2008), the S&P fell -30.6%, and all sectors crashed with cyclicals worst (cyclicals -37.1% vs defensives -25.1%). This was indiscriminate deleveraging, not a memory-specific selloff: TLT rallied +13.5%, DXY surged +5.3%, oil crashed -59.7%, and equal-weight lagged cap-weight -5.8%. Memory dropped roughly in line with the broader tech/semis complex (SMH -31.9%), with its high-beta amplifying the index decline rather than any additional fundamental deterioration.","body_zh":"COVID-19引发全球市场崩盘，VIX暴涨至66（仅次于2008年），标普跌-30.6%，所有板块暴跌且周期股最惨（周期股-37.1%对防御股-25.1%），内存不足两月跌42%。这是无差别去杠杆，而非内存专项抛售：TLT涨+13.5%，美元+5.3%，油崩-59.7%，等权重跑输大盘-5.8%。内存跌幅与科技/半导体大体同步（SMH -31.9%），高贝塔放大了指数跌幅，而非行业基本面的额外恶化。","drivers":["COVID-19 global market rout","VIX spike to 66 / margin calls","indiscriminate risk-off deleveraging","oil crash / dollar surge"],"drivers_zh":["COVID-19全球市场崩盘","VIX飙至66/追证金","无差别避险去杠杆","油价崩溃/美元飙升"],"prev_key":"2020-01-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-01-23"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash — indiscriminate liquidation","title_zh":"COVID疫情崩盘——无差别清仓","turn_id":"memory_storage:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-20":{"body":"Memory rallied +181% over 22 months, the broadest post-COVID tech/semis melt-up: VIX compressed 66→17, the Fed cut to zero and launched unlimited QE, fiscal stimulus was massive ($2T+ CARES Act March 2020, $1.9T ARP March 2021), and work-from-home PC demand, gaming console launches (PS5/Xbox Series X in November 2020), and hyperscaler cloud investment drove DRAM and NAND into shortfall. SMH surged +214.5%, high-beta beat low-vol +151.2, equal-weight beat cap-weight +12.7%, and growth beat value +31.6 — a genuine broad-based risk-on cycle that reached a macro/memory double-top by January 2022.","body_zh":"内存22个月上涨+181%，是最广泛的后疫情科技/半导体飙升行情：VIX从66压缩至17，美联储降至零利率并启动无限量QE，财政刺激力度空前（2020年3月CARES法案2万亿+，2021年3月《美国救援计划》1.9万亿），居家办公PC需求、游戏主机发布（PS5/Xbox Series X 2020年11月）以及超大规模云厂商投资将DRAM和NAND推入供不应求。SMH涨+214.5%，高贝塔跑赢低波+151.2，等权重跑赢大盘+12.7%，成长跑赢价值+31.6——一轮货真价实的广泛风险偏好周期，至2022年1月宏观与内存双顶。","drivers":["Fed zero rates + QE / massive fiscal stimulus","WFH PC and gaming DRAM demand","cloud hyperscaler NAND/DRAM buildout","VIX collapse / broad risk-on reflation"],"drivers_zh":["美联储零利率+QE/大规模财政刺激","居家办公PC与游戏DRAM需求","云超大规模NAND/DRAM建设","VIX崩落/广泛风险偏好再通胀"],"prev_key":"2020-03-20","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Pandemic WFH/cloud boom drives 22-month rally","title_zh":"疫情居家办公/云计算热潮推动22个月牛市","turn_id":"memory_storage:trough:2020-03"},"2022-01-04":{"body":"Memory fell 48% through 2022 as a brutal DRAM/NAND oversupply collided with a rate-shock bear: yields surged (TLT -29.1%, one of the worst bond years on record) and the dollar ripped +8.5% in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad with risk-off rotation into defensives (+0.4% vs cyclicals -8.6%). The high-beta drawdown (SMH -36.4% vs SPY -19.8%) compounded falling bit prices and bloated PC/handset inventories in a classic memory down-cycle.","body_zh":"2022年内存下跌48%，严重的DRAM/NAND供过于求叠加利率冲击熊市：收益率飙升（TLT -29.1%，创纪录最差债券年之一），美元大涨+8.5%，处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限，资金避险转向防御板块（+0.4%对周期股-8.6%）。高贝塔回撤（SMH -36.4%对SPY -19.8%）叠加位价下跌、PC/手机库存高企，构成典型内存下行周期。","drivers":["rate-shock risk-off","DRAM oversupply","bit-price collapse","Fed hiking"],"drivers_zh":["利率冲击避险","DRAM供过于求","位价崩跌","美联储加息"],"prev_key":"2022-01-04","prev_key_chain":["2022-01-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Memory glut meets the rate-shock bear","title_zh":"内存供过于求遭遇利率冲击熊市","turn_id":"memory_storage:peak:2022-01"},"2022-12-28":{"body":"A +163% rally as memory makers slashed capex and capacity, tightening the cycle into 2024 — and the backdrop was a textbook tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up: VIX fell 22→12, growth crushed value by +56.6, but breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -27.1%), a mega-cap-led tape this high-beta basket led (SMH +182.2% vs SPY +48.3%). The genAI boom seeded the HBM story, making high-bandwidth memory the key bottleneck for AI accelerators.","body_zh":"内存厂商大砍资本开支和产能，周期收紧至2024年，反弹+163%——背景是教科书式的科技/半导体领涨风险偏好飙升：VIX回落22→12，成长大幅跑赢价值+56.6，但市场广度狭窄（RSP跑输SPY -27.1%），是被这只高贝塔篮子领涨的大盘股行情（SMH +182.2%对SPY +48.3%）。生成式AI热潮孕育HBM故事，使高带宽内存成为AI加速器的关键瓶颈。","drivers":["narrow risk-on melt-up","capex cuts / supply discipline","genAI HBM demand","growth-over-value rotation"],"drivers_zh":["窄幅风险偏好飙升","削减资本开支/供给纪律","生成式AI HBM需求","成长跑赢价值轮动"],"prev_key":"2022-12-28","prev_key_chain":["2022-12-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Cycle trough to HBM dawn, on a narrow melt-up","title_zh":"周期触底到HBM黎明，搭乘窄幅飙升","turn_id":"memory_storage:trough:2022-12"},"2024-06-18":{"body":"A -25% pullback as the August 2024 yen-carry unwind (Bank of Japan rate hike July 31, 2024 forced a violent deleveraging) and profit-taking hit the year's biggest winners — a flight-to-safety where VIX spiked 12→28 and defensives (+2.9%) beat cyclicals (-3.8%) in a slowdown-scare quad. This high-beta basket amplified the deleveraging (SMH -23.6% vs SPY -5.1%), but the dip was positioning-driven with the underlying HBM demand thesis intact.","body_zh":"日本央行2024年7月31日加息迫使套息交易剧烈平仓，获利了结冲击全年最大赢家，内存回调-25%——VIX飙升12→28，防御股（+2.9%）跑赢周期股（-3.8%），处于放缓恐慌象限。这只高贝塔篮子放大了去杠杆（SMH -23.6%对SPY -5.1%），但此跌由仓位驱动，底层HBM需求逻辑未变。","drivers":["yen-carry unwind / BoJ hike July 2024","risk-off deleveraging / VIX spike","profit-taking on largest 2024 winner","high-beta amplification"],"drivers_zh":["日元套息平仓/日本央行2024年7月加息","避险去杠杆/VIX飙升","全年最大赢家获利了结","高贝塔放大"],"prev_key":"2024-06-18","prev_key_chain":["2024-06-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Carry-unwind correction, yen spike hits winners","title_zh":"套息平仓回调，日元飙升冲击最大赢家","turn_id":"memory_storage:peak:2024-06"},"2024-08-07":{"body":"A +25% recovery into February 2025 as Fed cuts (September 2024: -50bp, November -25bp, December -25bp) and AI-server demand re-firmed HBM pricing — a tech/semis-led risk-on rebound (VIX 28→16, growth>value +11.9) even as the dollar firmed +3.0% and yields rose (TLT -5.7%). Breadth stayed narrow (RSP lagged SPY -6.0%) as SK Hynix and Micron qualified next-gen HBM3E for the leading accelerators, supporting the bid.","body_zh":"美联储降息（2024年9月-50bp、11月-25bp、12月-25bp）和AI服务器需求重新巩固HBM价格，内存回升+25%至2025年2月——科技/半导体领涨风险偏好反弹（VIX 28→16，成长跑赢价值+11.9），尽管美元走强+3.0%、收益率上行（TLT -5.7%）。SK海力士和美光为领先加速器认证新一代HBM3E，支撑买盘，市场广度保持狭窄（RSP跑输SPY -6.0%）。","drivers":["Fed rate-cut cycle (50bp Sep 2024)","HBM3E qualification / AI server demand","tech/semis-led risk-on","narrow mega-cap tape"],"drivers_zh":["美联储降息周期（2024年9月-50bp）","HBM3E认证/AI服务器需求","科技/半导体领涨风险偏好","大盘股窄幅行情"],"prev_key":"2024-08-07","prev_key_chain":["2024-08-07"],"status":"exact","title":"HBM-led recovery on Fed-cut risk-on tape","title_zh":"HBM主导复苏，搭乘美联储降息风险偏好行情","turn_id":"memory_storage:trough:2024-08"},"2025-02-20":{"body":"Memory fell 37% as the DeepSeek scare (late January 2025: Chinese open-source model challenged US AI capex narrative) and April's reciprocal-tariff crash hit AI hardware in a violent risk-off flush — VIX exploded 16→45, high-beta cratered vs low-vol by -23.6%, and defensives (-5.7%) beat cyclicals (-16.3%) in a slowdown-scare quad. This leveraged basket amplified the move (SMH -29.9% vs SPY -17.0%); a weaker dollar (-3.1%) and falling yields confirm it was a growth-scare, not a rate, selloff that briefly clouded the memory super-cycle thesis.","body_zh":"DeepSeek恐慌（2025年1月下旬中国开源模型冲击美国AI资本开支叙事）和4月对等关税崩盘在剧烈避险抛售中冲击AI硬件，内存下跌37%——VIX暴涨16→45，高贝塔相对低波重挫-23.6%，放缓恐慌象限中防御板块（-5.7%）跑赢周期股（-16.3%）。这只高贝塔篮子放大了跌幅（SMH -29.9%对SPY -17.0%）；美元走弱（-3.1%）、收益率下行印证这是成长恐慌而非利率主导的抛售，一度遮蔽内存超级周期逻辑。","drivers":["DeepSeek AI capex scare","April 2025 reciprocal tariffs","VIX spike 16→45 / risk-off","high-beta amplification of demand fear"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek AI资本开支恐慌","2025年4月对等关税","VIX暴涨16→45/避险","需求恐慌高贝塔放大"],"prev_key":"2025-02-20","prev_key_chain":["2025-02-20"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek & tariff risk-off drawdown","title_zh":"DeepSeek与关税避险回撤","turn_id":"memory_storage:peak:2025-02"},"2025-04-04":{"body":"An extraordinary +1,754% run as a genuine 2025-26 undersupply super-cycle took hold across DRAM, HBM and NAND, riding a roaring risk-on regime: VIX collapsed 45→17 and high-beta beat low-vol by an enormous +124.5 in a reflation/growth-up quad. Breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -13.4%), a mega-cap-led melt-up this highest-beta semis basket led from the front (SMH +271.1% vs SPY +49.0%). Spot and contract prices spiked as AI memory content per server soared while makers stayed capacity-disciplined into the mid-2026 top.","body_zh":"2025-26年真实的供不应求超级周期席卷DRAM、HBM和NAND，惊人上涨+1,754%，搭乘狂热的风险偏好行情：VIX崩落45→17，高贝塔大幅跑赢低波+124.5，处于再通胀/增长向上象限。市场广度狭窄（RSP跑输SPY -13.4%），这只贝塔最高的半导体篮子在大盘股飙升中一马当先（SMH +271.1%对SPY +49.0%）。AI服务器单机内存用量激增、厂商保持产能纪律，现货与合约价格飙升，直至2026年中见顶。","drivers":["DRAM/HBM/NAND undersupply super-cycle","AI server memory content explosion","supply capacity discipline","tech/semis-led narrow risk-on melt-up"],"drivers_zh":["DRAM/HBM/NAND供不应求超级周期","AI服务器内存用量爆炸式增长","产能供给纪律","科技/半导体领涨窄幅风险偏好飙升"],"prev_key":"2025-04-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Memory super-cycle melt-up to the top","title_zh":"内存超级周期飙升至顶","turn_id":"memory_storage:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Memory, HBM & Storage is topping at the 95th percentile with an rs_rank of 1 — the No. 1 basket across the entire US universe. The 2025-04-04 rally leg produced an extraordinary +1,754% return as a genuine DRAM/HBM/NAND undersupply super-cycle aligned with the strongest semis-led risk-on tape in decades (SMH +271.1% vs SPY +49.0%, VIX 45→17). The current reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%) is still constructive, but breadth is narrowing back after the peak (RSP +2.9% vs SPY), the dollar has firmed +3.4%, and a SELL signal has been triggered. At these levels the basket sits in textbook topping territory — the same mega-cap-led narrow-breadth structure that preceded every prior peak is in place, and the high-beta premium (SPHB-SPLV +20.7) that amplified the rally now creates maximum downside exposure if the regime cools or AI-capex guidance disappoints.","now_zh":"内存、HBM与存储正在95百分位见顶，相对强度排名全美篮子第一。2025-04-04起涨腿创下惊人+1,754%回报，真实的DRAM/HBM/NAND供不应求超级周期与近几十年最强半导体领涨风险偏好行情交汇（SMH +271.1% 对 SPY +49.0%，VIX 45→17）。当前再通胀/增长向上象限（周期股+11.2%对防御股+6.9%，油+19.2%，铜金+18.3%）基调仍积极，但广度在见顶后趋窄，美元走强+3.4%，卖出信号已触发。在当前位置，篮子处于典型见顶形态——过去每次峰值前共有的大盘股领涨、市场广度狭窄结构已然形成，此前放大涨势的高贝塔溢价（SPHB-SPLV +20.7）在政策转向或AI资本开支指引令市场失望时将带来最大下行暴露。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"semis.top_2026.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"semis.top_2026.v1","arch_state":"pass","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-non_ai_software":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"Non-AI Software rallied 64% over two years as the cloud-SaaS adoption wave drove rapid revenue-multiple expansion (Aventis SaaS EV/Revenue moving from ~2-3x toward 6x by late 2015) while oil collapsed -59.7% and the dollar surged +21.4% DXY, creating a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Crucially the ctx shows defensives led (+29.8% vs cyclicals +8.3%) with TLT +24.2%, confirming a flight-to-quality regime: capital rotated out of energy and materials into healthcare, tech, and quality-growth software even as the tape was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -4.1%). Falling long yields compressed discount rates and mechanically lifted high-multiple SaaS valuations, while enterprise cloud-migration spending was still in early innings with double-digit booking growth across Salesforce, Workday, and ServiceNow.","body_zh":"随着云SaaS采用浪潮推动收入乘数快速扩张（Aventis SaaS EV/营收从~2-3x升至2015年末约6x），油价暴跌-59.7%，美元飙升DXY+21.4%，形成放缓/通缩恐慌象限，非AI软件两年上涨64%。关键在于语境显示防御股领跑（+29.8%对周期股+8.3%），TLT+24.2%，确认避险行情：资金从能源和原材料轮出，流入医疗、科技和优质成长型软件，尽管行情偏窄（RSP跑输SPY-4.1%）。长债收益率下行机械式地抬升高估值SaaS的现值，而企业云迁移支出仍处于早期阶段，Salesforce、Workday、ServiceNow等均录得双位数预订量增长。","drivers":["cloud adoption wave","oil-deflation compress rates","dollar surge flight to quality","SaaS multiple expansion","narrow mega-cap tape"],"drivers_zh":["云计算采用浪潮","油价通缩压低利率","美元强势避险","SaaS估值乘数扩张","大盘股主导行情偏窄"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Cloud adoption melt-up, deflation-scare tailwind","title_zh":"云计算采用浪潮拉升，通缩恐慌提供顺风","turn_id":"non_ai_software:trough:2014-01"},"2015-12-29":{"body":"Non-AI Software fell 35% in just 40 days as the 2015-2016 global selloff -- triggered by China's yuan devaluation (August 2015), a second circuit-breaker crash on January 4, 2016, and Brent oil dropping below $30 -- cascaded into a global growth scare. The ctx confirms a risk-off rotation (VIX 16->26, defensives led -3.5% vs cyclicals -11.2%, TLT +9.6%), so the selloff was macro-driven broad de-risking, not software-specific; high-multiple SaaS names amplified the drawdown as LinkedIn and Tableau had just reported disappointing growth guidance in early February 2016. Credit spreads widened (HYG vs LQD -4.9%), reinforcing the flight-to-safety tape.","body_zh":"非AI软件在仅40天内下跌35%，原因是2015-2016年全球抛售潮——由人民币贬值（2015年8月）、2016年1月4日第二次熔断崩盘以及布伦特原油跌破30美元触发全球增长恐慌。语境确认避险轮动（VIX 16->26，防御股领跌-3.5%对周期股-11.2%，TLT+9.6%），因此抛售是宏观驱动的整体去风险，而非软件特有；2016年2月初LinkedIn和Tableau发布令人失望的增长指引，放大了高估值SaaS名字的回撤。信用利差扩大（HYG对LQD-4.9%），强化了避险行情。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation","oil below $30 growth scare","SaaS valuation panic","risk-off credit widening"],"drivers_zh":["人民币贬值","油价跌破30美元增长恐慌","SaaS估值恐慌","避险信用利差扩大"],"prev_key":"2015-12-29","prev_key_chain":["2015-12-29"],"status":"exact","title":"China devaluation growth scare, SaaS panic selloff","title_zh":"人民币贬值增长恐慌，SaaS恐慌性抛售","turn_id":"non_ai_software:peak:2015-12"},"2016-02-08":{"body":"Non-AI Software surged 564% over four years in one of the most powerful secular rallies in the basket's history, powered by the convergence of falling rates (TLT +22.1%), a reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +91.7% vs defensives +64.4%), and the explosion of the cloud-first enterprise playbook. The basket massively outpaced SPY (564% vs 97%) as semis led (SMH +243.9%), growth crushed value +57.3, and breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -14.3%) -- a mega-cap growth melt-up anchored by Microsoft Azure, Salesforce, and ServiceNow building dominant subscription moats. Microsoft's $26B LinkedIn acquisition (June 2016), Workday and Veeva compound growth, and the Trump tax cuts' corporate spending uplift all drove durable revenue acceleration through 2019, while COVID's March 2020 shock briefly halted but did not break the rally until February 2020.","body_zh":"非AI软件四年飙升564%，是该篮子历史上最强劲的世俗性涨势之一，由利率下行（TLT+22.1%）、再通胀/增长向上象限（周期股+91.7%对防御股+64.4%）以及云优先企业战略爆发共同驱动。篮子大幅跑赢SPY（564%对97%），半导体领涨（SMH+243.9%），成长大幅跑赢价值+57.3，行情偏窄（RSP跑输SPY-14.3%）——以微软Azure、Salesforce、ServiceNow构建主导订阅护城河为锚的大盘成长飙升行情。2016年6月微软260亿美元收购LinkedIn、Workday和Veeva的复合增长，以及特朗普减税带来的企业支出提振，推动收入持续加速至2019年，而2020年3月新冠冲击短暂打断但未能打破这一涨势，直至2020年2月触顶。","drivers":["secular cloud adoption","zero/falling rates duration bid","mega-cap growth melt-up","enterprise digital transformation","narrow breadth tech leadership"],"drivers_zh":["世俗云计算采用","零/下行利率久期溢价","大盘成长股飙升","企业数字化转型","行情偏窄科技领涨"],"prev_key":"2016-02-08","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Four-year secular cloud bull, zero-rate growth melt-up","title_zh":"四年世俗云牛市，零利率成长飙升","turn_id":"non_ai_software:trough:2016-02"},"2020-02-19":{"body":"Non-AI Software fell 32.5% in just 25 days as the COVID-19 pandemic triggered the fastest bear market in history, with VIX spiking from 14 to 83 -- the highest reading ever recorded at that time. The ctx confirms a pure panic selloff: defensives led (-22.3% vs cyclicals -35.4%), TLT +12.8%, and oil collapsed -46.1%; it was an indiscriminate dash-for-cash with everything sold, not a software-specific bear. The CARES Act ($2.2T, signed March 27) and Fed emergency rate cuts to zero on March 15 ended the crash and immediately set up the recovery.","body_zh":"新冠疫情引发史上最快熊市，VIX从14飙至83（彼时历史最高），非AI软件仅25天下跌32.5%。语境确认为纯粹恐慌性抛售：防御股领跌（-22.3%对周期股-35.4%），TLT+12.8%，油价暴跌-46.1%；这是无差别的现金荒，并非软件特有的熊市。2020年3月27日签署的CARES法案（2.2万亿美元）和美联储3月15日紧急降息至零终结了崩盘，并立即为复苏奠定基础。","drivers":["COVID pandemic panic","VIX 83 dash for cash","indiscriminate risk-off","Fed emergency rate cut to zero"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情恐慌","VIX 83无差别现金荒","全面避险","美联储紧急降息至零"],"prev_key":"2020-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic liquidity crash, indiscriminate selloff","title_zh":"新冠疫情流动性崩盘，无差别抛售","turn_id":"non_ai_software:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-16":{"body":"Non-AI Software surged 284% over 20 months, the second largest absolute rally in its history, fueled by zero interest rates (Fed funds at 0-0.25% throughout), $5.6T in US fiscal stimulus (CARES, American Rescue Plan), and COVID forcing overnight enterprise digital transformation. The ctx shows a powerful reflation/growth-up quad: cyclicals +121.9% vs defensives +49.9%, semis +198.6%, growth>value +38.1, and breadth broadened (RSP beat SPY +9.2%). SaaS companies reported 40-60%+ growth rates as remote-work mandates pulled forward years of cloud migration, with Zoom, Snowflake (IPO Sep 2020 at $120, opened at $245), and Salesforce/Slack ($27.7B acquisition Dec 2020) marking the peak euphoria. By November 2021 the Bessemer Cloud Index reached its all-time high of 3,097 (a 2,997% gain from its 2013 base) before the Fed taper announcement triggered the turn.","body_zh":"非AI软件20个月飙升284%，是其历史上第二大绝对涨幅，由零利率（全程联邦基金利率0-0.25%）、5.6万亿美元美国财政刺激（CARES、美国救援计划）以及新冠疫情倒逼企业数字化转型共同驱动。语境呈现强劲的再通胀/增长向上象限：周期股+121.9%对防御股+49.9%，半导体+198.6%，成长跑赢价值+38.1，市场广度扩散（RSP跑赢SPY+9.2%）。SaaS公司录得40-60%+增长率，远程办公强制执行令拉前多年的云迁移，Zoom飙升、Snowflake（2020年9月IPO定价120美元开盘245美元）、Salesforce/Slack（2020年12月收购277亿美元）标志着狂热顶点。至2021年11月，Bessemer云指数触及历史高点3097点（较2013年基准涨2997%），随后美联储宣布缩减购债规模引发转折。","drivers":["zero rates SaaS valuation supercycle","COVID digital acceleration","fiscal stimulus $5.6T","remote-work demand pull","growth>value regime"],"drivers_zh":["零利率SaaS估值超级周期","新冠数字加速","5.6万亿美元财政刺激","远程办公需求前置","成长优于价值行情"],"prev_key":"2020-03-16","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-16"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID digital acceleration, zero-rate growth supercycle","title_zh":"新冠数字加速，零利率成长超级周期","turn_id":"non_ai_software:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-09":{"body":"Non-AI Software fell 47% as the November 3, 2021 Fed taper announcement (confirmed December FOMC acceleration of tapering) and surging CPI (6.8% y/y in November 2021, fastest since 1982) triggered the most rapid discount-rate repricing in modern SaaS history. The ctx confirms a stagflation-ish, risk-off regime: defensives led (+1.3% vs cyclicals -5.1%), TLT fell -12.3% (yields surged), dollar +5.4%, and VIX rose 18->32. Long-duration, profitless-growth SaaS names were repriced hardest as the Bessemer Cloud Index collapsed from its all-time high; SMH -20.6% vs SPY -10.5% shows the basket amplified the index move through its duration sensitivity. Russia's Ukraine invasion (February 2022) added a stagflation overlay that deepened the selloff into March 2022.","body_zh":"2021年11月3日美联储宣布缩减购债规模（12月FOMC确认加速缩债），加之CPI同比+6.8%（2021年11月，为1982年以来最快），引发现代SaaS史上最快速的贴现率重定价，非AI软件下跌47%。语境确认类滞胀避险行情：防御股领跑（+1.3%对周期股-5.1%），TLT跌-12.3%（收益率飙升），美元+5.4%，VIX 18->32。长久期、尚未盈利的成长型SaaS名字遭到最严厉的重估，Bessemer云指数从历史高点崩落；SMH-20.6%对SPY-10.5%表明篮子通过其久期敏感性放大了指数跌幅。2022年2月俄乌冲突爆发叠加滞胀因素，将抛售深化至2022年3月。","drivers":["Fed taper November 2021","CPI 6.8% rate-shock repricing","duration selloff SaaS multiples","Ukraine stagflation overlay"],"drivers_zh":["2021年11月美联储缩债","CPI 6.8%利率冲击重定价","久期抛售SaaS估值压缩","俄乌冲突滞胀叠加"],"prev_key":"2021-11-09","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Duration de-rating: Fed taper into rate-shock bear","title_zh":"久期重估：美联储缩债引发利率冲击熊市","turn_id":"non_ai_software:peak:2021-11"},"2022-03-14":{"body":"Non-AI Software bounced 32% in three weeks as VIX eased from 32 to 19 after the worst of the Ukraine shock was digested and the market briefly priced a ceasefire scenario. The ctx shows a reflation/growth-up quad with growth>value +9.5 and tech/discretionary leading, but breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -3.0%) and TLT was flat -- the hiking cycle was still accelerating, so this was a classic duration-sensitivity reflex off oversold levels, not a fundamental regime turn. The March 16 FOMC 25bp hike (the first since 2018) was already priced, allowing brief relief.","body_zh":"随着乌克兰冲击最剧烈阶段消化，市场短暂定价停火情景，VIX从32回落至19，非AI软件三周反弹32%。语境显示再通胀/增长向上象限，成长跑赢价值+9.5，科技/可选消费领涨，但市场广度偏窄（RSP跑输SPY-3.0%），TLT基本持平——加息周期仍在加速，因此这是从超卖水平出发的经典久期敏感性反射，而非基本面行情转折。3月16日FOMC加息25bp（2018年以来首次）已被充分定价，由此获得短暂喘息。","drivers":["oversold rebound","VIX compression post-Ukraine","March FOMC 25bp priced","growth reflex"],"drivers_zh":["超卖反弹","乌克兰冲击后VIX压缩","3月FOMC 25bp已定价","成长股反射性回升"],"prev_key":"2022-03-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Oversold reflex bounce as VIX eases","title_zh":"超卖反射性反弹，VIX缓和","turn_id":"non_ai_software:trough:2022-03"},"2022-04-04":{"body":"Non-AI Software fell 37.5% from April to June 2022 as the Fed's accelerating hiking path (50bp May, 75bp June -- the largest hike since 1994) drove real yields sharply higher (TLT -14.7%) and the dollar gained +4.7%. The ctx confirms stagflation-ish flight-to-safety: defensives led (-11.5% vs cyclicals -17.1%), VIX rose 19->33, and growth lagged value -11.2, with software spending guidance beginning to slow as enterprise CIOs tightened budgets. SMH -24.4% vs SPY -19.7% shows the long-duration basket amplified the rate-driven de-rating; Energy (XLE +0.8%) was the only sector in positive territory, confirming an oil/inflation regime hostile to software multiples.","body_zh":"美联储加息路径加速（5月50bp、6月75bp——1994年以来最大加息幅度），实际收益率大幅走高（TLT-14.7%），美元上涨+4.7%，非AI软件从4月至2022年6月下跌37.5%。语境确认类滞胀避险行情：防御股领跌（-11.5%对周期股-17.1%），VIX 19->33，成长跑输价值-11.2，企业CIO开始收紧预算，软件支出指引趋于放缓。SMH-24.4%对SPY-19.7%表明长久期篮子放大了利率驱动的估值下杀；能源（XLE+0.8%）是唯一正收益板块，确认油价/通胀行情对软件估值极为不利。","drivers":["Fed 75bp hike real yields surge","SaaS budget slowdown","growth-to-value rotation","dollar strength"],"drivers_zh":["美联储75bp加息实际收益率飙升","SaaS预算放缓","成长向价值轮动","美元走强"],"prev_key":"2022-04-04","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Surging real yields drive software to new lows","title_zh":"实际收益率飙升推动软件创新低","turn_id":"non_ai_software:peak:2022-04"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"Non-AI Software bounced 40.6% from June 16 to August 10 as the July 13, 2022 CPI print came in at 8.5% (below the 9.1% June peak), sparking peak-inflation hope and a broad risk-on squeeze. The ctx shows a goldilocks-flavored quad (cyclicals +12.7% vs defensives +12.3%), VIX compressed 33->20, growth>value +9.1, and TLT gained +5.2% (yields pulled back). Tech and discretionary led while Energy lagged -2.1%, signaling the market was briefly pricing a Fed pivot that never came. The bounce was a duration-sensitivity reflex -- when yields fell, the longest-duration basket rallied the most -- rather than a fundamental inflection in business conditions.","body_zh":"2022年7月13日CPI同比+8.5%（低于6月高点9.1%），点燃通胀见顶预期，引发广泛的风险偏好逼空，非AI软件从6月16日至8月10日反弹40.6%。语境显示类金发姑娘象限（周期股+12.7%对防御股+12.3%），VIX压缩33->20，成长跑赢价值+9.1，TLT+5.2%（收益率回落）。科技和可选消费领涨，能源落后-2.1%，表明市场短暂定价了一个从未实现的美联储转向。这次反弹是久期敏感性反射——当收益率回落时，久期最长的篮子涨幅最大——而非商业环境的基本面拐点。","drivers":["peak-inflation July CPI","yields pullback duration reflex","risk-on VIX compression","growth-vs-value squeeze"],"drivers_zh":["7月CPI通胀见顶","收益率回落久期反射","风险偏好VIX压缩","成长对价值逼空"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-inflation relief rally, July CPI surprise","title_zh":"通胀见顶缓解反弹，7月CPI惊喜","turn_id":"non_ai_software:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-10":{"body":"Non-AI Software fell 37.3% from August 10 to November 9 as Fed Chair Powell's August 26 Jackson Hole speech delivered a hawkish shock (pledging to bring inflation down 'forcefully'), sending TLT down -18.7% (yields surged) and the dollar up +5.1%. The ctx shows yields surged with breadth broadening (RSP beat SPY +3.4%) and Energy leading (+18.9%) -- confirming a rate/inflation-dominated regime rather than pure panic. Growth vs value was hit hardest (-11.2), with SMH -18.7% vs SPY -10.6%. The October CPI print (7.7% on November 10, 2022) came in below expectations and marked the literal trough of the basket, as disinflation began to be priced.","body_zh":"美联储主席鲍威尔8月26日杰克逊霍尔演讲释放鹰派冲击（承诺'坚决'压低通胀），TLT跌-18.7%（收益率飙升），美元+5.1%，非AI软件从8月10日至11月9日下跌37.3%。语境显示市场广度扩散（RSP跑赢SPY+3.4%），能源领涨（+18.9%）——确认是利率/通胀主导行情而非纯粹恐慌。成长对价值跌幅最重（-11.2），SMH-18.7%对SPY-10.6%。2022年11月10日公布的10月CPI（7.7%）低于预期，标志着篮子的实际底部，去通胀开始被定价。","drivers":["Jackson Hole hawkish shock","Powell forceful Fed pledge","yields TLT -18.7%","growth de-rating dollar strong"],"drivers_zh":["杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击","鲍威尔坚决压制通胀承诺","收益率TLT-18.7%","成长股估值下杀美元走强"],"prev_key":"2022-08-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkish shock, rate-driven final leg down","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击，利率驱动最后一跌","turn_id":"non_ai_software:peak:2022-08"},"2022-11-09":{"body":"Non-AI Software surged 114% over 15 months as the November 10, 2022 CPI print (7.7%, below expectations) marked peak inflation and opened the disinflation re-rating cycle, culminating in the Fed's September 2024 rate cut (50bp). ChatGPT's November 2022 launch simultaneously revived risk appetite for software. The ctx is a textbook goldilocks melt-up: dollar fell -5.9%, growth crushed value +42.2, semis +113.9%, VIX compressed 26->13, but breadth was extremely narrow (RSP lagged SPY -18.4%) -- a mega-cap-led tape where falling discount rates mechanically re-rated the longest-duration assets. Margin improvement stories (Salesforce's Benioff announcing a workforce restructuring in January 2023, ServiceNow's FCF expansion) and SaaS platform durability rebuilt the institutional bid through early 2024.","body_zh":"2022年11月10日CPI（7.7%，低于预期）标志通胀见顶，开启去通胀重估周期，以2024年9月美联储降息50bp告终，非AI软件15个月飙升114%。与此同时，2022年11月ChatGPT发布重燃软件风险偏好。语境是教科书式的金发姑娘飙升：美元跌-5.9%，成长大幅跑赢价值+42.2，半导体+113.9%，VIX压缩26->13，但市场广度极度偏窄（RSP跑输SPY-18.4%）——是大盘股主导的行情，贴现率下行机械式地重估久期最长的资产。利润率改善故事（Salesforce Benioff 2023年1月宣布裁员重组、ServiceNow自由现金流扩张）和SaaS平台耐久性重建了机构买盘，直至2024年初。","drivers":["CPI peak disinflation re-rating","ChatGPT AI narrative tailwind","Fed pivot September 2024 cut","SaaS margin improvement"],"drivers_zh":["CPI见顶去通胀重估","ChatGPT AI叙事顺风","美联储转向2024年9月降息","SaaS利润率改善"],"prev_key":"2022-11-09","prev_key_chain":["2022-11-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Disinflation re-rating: CPI peak to Fed pivot melt-up","title_zh":"去通胀重估：CPI见顶至美联储转向飙升","turn_id":"non_ai_software:trough:2022-11"},"2024-02-09":{"body":"Non-AI Software fell 26.7% as AI-capex fears crystallized through 2024: hyperscaler capex guidance pointed to billions diverted from software budgets to GPU clusters, and enterprise CIOs began 'robbing Peter to pay Paul' -- cutting SaaS licenses to fund AI infrastructure. The ctx is a slowdown/deflation-scare with defensives leading (+10.8% vs cyclicals +2.1%), VIX spiking 13->39, and TLT +7.4% (yields fell), consistent with the Bank of Japan's surprise July 31 rate hike (0.1% to 0.25%) triggering the August 5 yen-carry unwind (Nikkei -12.3% in a day, VIX briefly hit 65 intraday). Capital rotated away from high-beta software (SMH only +4.6%) into defensive safety, compounding the AI-disruption narrative with macro deleveraging.","body_zh":"AI资本开支担忧在2024年具体化：超大规模云厂商资本开支指引显示数十亿美元从软件预算转向GPU集群，企业CIO开始'拆东墙补西墙'——削减SaaS许可证来资助AI基础设施，非AI软件下跌26.7%。语境为放缓/通缩恐慌，防御股领跑（+10.8%对周期股+2.1%），VIX 13->39飙升，TLT+7.4%（收益率下行），与日本央行7月31日意外加息（0.1%至0.25%）引发的8月5日日元套息平仓（日经指数单日-12.3%，VIX盘中一度触65）相吻合。资金从高贝塔软件（SMH仅+4.6%）轮出至防御性安全资产，将AI颠覆叙事与宏观去杠杆叠加。","drivers":["AI capex cannibalization fears","yen carry unwind August 2024","higher-for-longer Fed disappointment","SaaS net retention deterioration"],"drivers_zh":["AI资本开支蚕食担忧","2024年8月日元套息平仓","美联储更长期更高利率失望","SaaS净留存恶化"],"prev_key":"2024-02-09","prev_key_chain":["2024-02-09"],"status":"exact","title":"AI budget-cannibalization scare, yen carry unwind","title_zh":"AI预算蚕食恐慌，日元套息平仓冲击","turn_id":"non_ai_software:peak:2024-02"},"2024-08-05":{"body":"Non-AI Software surged 56% from the August 5 yen-unwind low to December 6, powered by the Fed's September 18, 2024 50bp rate cut (the first since 2020) which directly re-rated long-duration software via falling discount rates. The ctx is a tech-led risk-on melt-up: VIX compressed 39->13, growth>value +11.3, and cyclicals led (+18.3% vs defensives +5.4%), even as the dollar firmed +3.2% and TLT gave back -3.2%. Breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -3.7%) -- again a mega-cap concentrated tape. Improving enterprise software budgets, election-outcome certainty post-November 5, and Trump-reflation optimism for tech carried the group into December 2024, where it peaked as rate-cut expectations began to be repriced outward.","body_zh":"受美联储2024年9月18日降息50bp（2020年以来首次）直接通过贴现率下行重估长久期软件的推动，非AI软件从8月5日日元平仓低点至12月6日飙升56%。语境为科技领涨的风险偏好飙升：VIX压缩39->13，成长跑赢价值+11.3，周期股领涨（+18.3%对防御股+5.4%），尽管美元走强+3.2%，TLT回吐-3.2%。市场广度偏窄（RSP跑输SPY-3.7%）——再次是大盘集中行情。企业软件预算改善、11月5日选举结果明朗带来的确定性以及特朗普再通胀对科技的乐观情绪推动板块至2024年12月，随后随着降息预期被推后而触顶。","drivers":["Fed September 2024 50bp cut","risk-on VIX compression","election clarity Trump reflation","SaaS budget recovery"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2024年9月50bp降息","风险偏好VIX压缩","选举明朗特朗普再通胀","SaaS预算复苏"],"prev_key":"2024-08-05","prev_key_chain":["2024-08-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed cut cycle unlocks software re-rating rally","title_zh":"美联储降息周期解锁软件重估反弹","turn_id":"non_ai_software:trough:2024-08"},"2024-12-06":{"body":"Non-AI Software fell 34.3% through April 8, 2025 in a two-phase selloff: first, DeepSeek's January 20, 2025 release (rivaling ChatGPT at a fraction of the cost) threatened to commoditize AI and undermine the AI-premium embedded in software valuations; then Trump's April 2 'Liberation Day' reciprocal-tariff announcement triggered a historic market crash (S&P -10% in two days, VIX hit 52.33 on April 8). The ctx confirms a violent flight-to-safety: defensives led (-6.7% vs cyclicals -18.5%), VIX exploded 13->52, high-beta crushed low-vol by -22.7, and SMH fell -27.3% vs SPY -17.8%. The combination of AI-disruption fear for legacy SaaS seat-based models and macro de-risking drove the de-rating deeper than the macro alone would suggest.","body_zh":"非AI软件经历两阶段下跌至2025年4月8日，累计下跌34.3%：首先，DeepSeek 2025年1月20日发布（以极低成本媲美ChatGPT）威胁AI商品化，动摇了软件估值中内嵌的AI溢价；随后特朗普4月2日'解放日'对等关税公告引发历史性市场崩盘（S&P两天-10%，4月8日VIX触及52.33）。语境确认剧烈避险行情：防御股领跌（-6.7%对周期股-18.5%），VIX 13->52暴涨，高贝塔对低波大幅落后-22.7，SMH-27.3%对SPY-17.8%。传统SaaS按席位收费模式遭受AI颠覆担忧与宏观去风险的叠加，将估值下杀深度推超单纯宏观因素所能解释的水平。","drivers":["DeepSeek AI disruption January 2025","Liberation Day reciprocal tariffs April 2025","VIX 52 macro panic","AI seat-model disruption fear"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek AI颠覆2025年1月","解放日对等关税2025年4月","VIX 52宏观恐慌","AI席位模式颠覆担忧"],"prev_key":"2024-12-06","prev_key_chain":["2024-12-06"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek AI disruption plus Liberation Day tariff crash","title_zh":"DeepSeek AI颠覆叠加解放日关税崩盘","turn_id":"non_ai_software:peak:2024-12"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"Non-AI Software bounced 31.6% from April 8 to July 28, 2025 as tariff fears eased -- Trump announced a 90-day pause on reciprocal tariffs for most countries on April 9 -- and a risk-on regime snapped back violently: VIX collapsed 52->15, high-beta beat low-vol by +47.8, the dollar fell -4.2%, and growth>value +18.6 in a reflation/growth-up quad. Semis exploded (SMH +61.9%), but Non-AI Software underperformed the index (SPY +28.7%) as the AI-disruption overhang limited multiple expansion. The April 2026 Snowflake earnings (announcing a $6B Amazon cloud-AI deal and raised guidance) and ServiceNow's agentic-AI monetization results foreshadowed the May 2026 SaaSpocalypse-ending rally, but the basket itself peaked in July 2025 before the Hormuz oil shock.","body_zh":"随着关税担忧消退——特朗普4月9日宣布对大多数国家暂停对等关税90天——风险偏好剧烈反弹，非AI软件从4月8日至2025年7月28日反弹31.6%：VIX崩落52->15，高贝塔跑赢低波+47.8，美元下跌-4.2%，成长跑赢价值+18.6，处于再通胀/增长向上象限。半导体爆发（SMH+61.9%），但非AI软件跑输指数（SPY+28.7%），AI颠覆阴影限制了估值扩张。Snowflake（宣布60亿美元亚马逊云AI大单并上调指引）和ServiceNow智能体AI货币化业绩预示了2026年5月打破SaaSpocalypse的反弹，但篮子本身在2025年7月触顶，随后遭遇霍尔木兹石油冲击。","drivers":["tariff pause relief April 9 2025","VIX collapse risk-on snapback","AI monetization early signals","dollar weakness tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月9日关税暂停缓解","VIX崩落风险偏好反弹","AI货币化早期信号","美元走弱顺风"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-tariff relief rally, AI monetization pivot","title_zh":"关税后缓解反弹，AI货币化叙事转向","turn_id":"non_ai_software:trough:2025-04"},"2025-07-28":{"body":"Non-AI Software fell 47% from July 28, 2025 to April 10, 2026 as the US-Israel air war on Iran (launched February 28, 2026) closed the Strait of Hormuz -- blocking ~25% of global seaborne oil -- sending oil +44.8% and driving CPI energy prices +23.5% y/y by May 2026. Critically, the ctx reveals this was a growth-to-value rotation, not a rate squeeze: bonds actually rallied (TLT +4.1%, yields fell), yet growth lagged value hard (-12.0) as capital fled high-multiple SaaS for Energy (+32.4%), Materials (+15.8%), and Utilities (+14.7%) while SPY barely moved (+7.6%). This mirrors 1970s oil-shock sector rotations where real-asset dominance crowded out duration plays. Persistent AI-cannibalization fears (the SaaSpocalypse narrative, $2T wiped from software stocks by February 2026) compounded the rotation.","body_zh":"美以对伊朗发动空战（2026年2月28日），封堵霍尔木兹海峡（阻断全球约25%的海运石油），油价+44.8%，至2026年5月CPI能源分项同比+23.5%，非AI软件从2025年7月28日至2026年4月10日下跌47%。关键在于，语境揭示这是成长向价值的轮动，而非利率挤压：债券实际上上涨（TLT+4.1%，收益率下行），但成长大幅跑输价值（-12.0），资金从高估值SaaS撤向能源（+32.4%）、原材料（+15.8%）和公用事业（+14.7%），而SPY几乎未动（+7.6%）。这与1970年代石油冲击时实物资产主导、挤压久期资产的板块轮动如出一辙。持续的AI蚕食担忧（SaaSpocalypse叙事，至2026年2月软件股市值蒸发2万亿美元）加剧了这一轮动。","drivers":["Hormuz oil shock February 2026","growth-to-value rotation not rate squeeze","energy/materials capital flight","AI cannibalization SaaSpocalypse"],"drivers_zh":["2026年2月霍尔木兹石油冲击","成长向价值轮动而非利率挤压","能源/原材料资金撤离","AI蚕食SaaSpocalypse"],"prev_key":"2025-07-28","prev_key_chain":["2025-07-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Hormuz oil shock reflation rotates out of growth","title_zh":"霍尔木兹石油冲击，再通胀轮动撤离成长","turn_id":"non_ai_software:peak:2025-07"},"2026-04-10":{"body":"Non-AI Software surged 54.4% from April 10 to June 1, 2026 as the June 17 Hormuz ceasefire (Trump-Pezeshkian MOU) eased the oil/inflation shock and a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up resumed, with VIX falling 19->16, SMH +39.1%, and growth>value +8.6. Critically, Snowflake's May 28 earnings (best day ever, +36%, announcing a $6B Amazon deal and raised guidance) reversed the SaaSpocalypse narrative, driving the IGV software ETF to its best month since October 2001 (+21% in May). The ctx is narrow breadth (RSP lagged SPY -5.4%), confirming this was a mega-cap-led re-rating of oversold long-duration software rather than a broad recovery; defensives fell (-3.3%) while cyclicals rose (+6.7%), confirming genuine risk-on rotation back into growth.","body_zh":"6月17日霍尔木兹停火（特朗普-佩泽什基安谅解备忘录）缓和石油/通胀冲击，科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好飙升重启，VIX 19->16，SMH+39.1%，成长跑赢价值+8.6，非AI软件从2026年4月10日至6月1日飙升54.4%。关键是，Snowflake 5月28日财报（历史最佳单日，+36%，宣布60亿美元亚马逊大单并上调指引）逆转了SaaSpocalypse叙事，推动IGV软件ETF录得2001年10月以来最佳月度表现（5月+21%）。语境显示市场广度偏窄（RSP跑输SPY-5.4%），确认这是超卖长久期软件的大盘主导重估，而非广泛复苏；防御股下跌（-3.3%），周期股上涨（+6.7%），确认风险偏好真正轮回成长。","drivers":["Hormuz ceasefire June 17 2026","Snowflake AI monetization earnings May 28","SaaSpocalypse narrative reversal","VIX compression oversold rebound"],"drivers_zh":["2026年6月17日霍尔木兹停火","Snowflake 5月28日AI货币化财报","SaaSpocalypse叙事逆转","VIX压缩超卖反弹"],"prev_key":"2026-04-10","prev_key_chain":["2026-04-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Ceasefire relief, AI monetization rerates software","title_zh":"停火缓解，AI货币化重估软件","turn_id":"non_ai_software:trough:2026-04"},"2026-06-01":{"body":"Non-AI Software fell 27.3% from June 1 to June 25, 2026 as the post-ceasefire Fed retained and intensified a hiking bias -- BofA and Deutsche Bank both moved to forecasting a second 2026 rate hike under Chair Kevin Warsh by December, and the Nasdaq fell 4.6% for the week ending June 25. The ctx is a slowdown/deflation-scare defensive rotation: VIX firmed 16->19, defensives led (+5.3% vs cyclicals -0.1%), growth lagged value hard (-11.5), and breadth broadened (RSP beat SPY +4.6%) -- the broadening at the expense of mega-cap tech confirming that this was a leadership rotation out of long-duration software into other market segments, not a collapse in broad economic confidence. Oil fell -22% (giving back some of the Hormuz spike) and TLT gained +2.2%, but the hawkish Fed re-pricing outweighed the yield relief for software multiples.","body_zh":"随着停火后美联储维持并强化加息倾向——美银和德银均调整预测，认为Warsh主席领导下2026年12月前还有第二次加息，纳斯达克当周（截至6月25日）下跌4.6%——非AI软件从2026年6月1日至6月25日下跌27.3%。语境为放缓/通缩恐慌的防御性轮动：VIX 16->19走强，防御股领涨（+5.3%对周期股-0.1%），成长大幅跑输价值（-11.5），市场广度扩散（RSP跑赢SPY+4.6%）——大盘科技股让位于市场广度，确认这是从长久期软件撤出的领导力轮动，而非广泛经济信心崩溃。油价回落-22%（回吐部分霍尔木兹涨幅），TLT+2.2%，但鹰派美联储重新定价的压力超过了收益率回落对软件估值的提振。","drivers":["Warsh hawkish Fed second hike 2026","growth-to-value rotation","Nasdaq mega-cap de-rating","defensive rotation breadth broadening"],"drivers_zh":["Warsh鹰派美联储第二次加息2026","成长转价值轮动","纳斯达克大盘科技股估值下杀","防御性轮动市场广度扩散"],"prev_key":"2026-06-01","prev_key_chain":["2026-06-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Hawkish Fed Warsh bias, growth-to-value rotation resumes","title_zh":"Warsh鹰派美联储倾向，成长转价值轮动重启","turn_id":"non_ai_software:peak:2026-06"}},"now":"Non-AI Software is in an Expansion/Trending phase (cycle position 39.3, rs_rank 38 -- mid-pack), sitting below the 200-day moving average with a BUY signal but without confirmed breakout. The current macro quad is reflation/growth-up with cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, a firming dollar (+3.4% DXY), and oil +19.2% -- a combination that historically pressures long-duration software via a higher-discount-rate headwind even as the broad tape rallies. After a -27% pullback into the June 25 trough, breadth has broadened (+2.9% RSP vs SPY) and the post-Hormuz-ceasefire AI-monetization narrative now competes with a newly hawkish Fed bias under Chair Warsh, who markets price for a second 2026 hike by December. Semis have broken sharply higher (SMH +67.9%) while Non-AI Software lags -- consistent with a tape rewarding AI-capex hardware over legacy SaaS. The basket is recovering from a deep trough but remains hostage to the rate narrative: any renewed higher-for-longer re-pricing would compress long-duration multiples again, while a Fed pause or growth moderation would be a durable tailwind.","now_zh":"非AI软件处于扩张/趋势阶段（周期位置39.3，相对强弱排名38，属中游水平），价格仍在200日均线下方，有买入信号但尚未确认突破。当前宏观象限为再通胀/增长向上，周期股+11.2%对防御股+6.9%，美元走强（DXY+3.4%），油价+19.2%——这一组合历史上会通过抬高贴现率来压制长久期软件，即便大盘整体走强。在6月25日触底（-27%回调）后，市场广度已扩散（RSP跑赢SPY+2.9%），霍尔木兹停火后的AI货币化叙事与Warsh主导下的美联储新鹰派倾向（市场定价2026年底前还有第二次加息）形成博弈。半导体大幅突破（SMH+67.9%），而非AI软件明显落后——与行情奖励AI资本开支硬件、而非传统SaaS的特征吻合。篮子正从深度低谷中修复，但仍受利率叙事左右：任何\"更长期更高利率\"的重新定价都将再度压缩长久期估值，而美联储暂停加息或增长预期下修则将成为持续顺风。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-non_ai_tech":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"The Fed ended QE3 in October 2014, catalyzing a dollar surge of +21.2% DXY as oil simultaneously collapsed -51% after OPEC's November 2014 decision to defend market share over price. The macro landed in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad: long bonds surged (TLT +33.1%) and defensives averaged +27.7% versus cyclicals +11.8%. Non-AI tech and hardware caught a quality-growth premium alongside Health and Utilities — semis gained +39.5% — as falling energy input costs boosted hardware margins and a growth-over-value tailwind (+5.6%) in a low-VIX environment propelled the basket +39.1%, well ahead of SPY (+17.8%), even as Energy cratered -9%.","body_zh":"美联储2014年10月结束QE3，催生美元飙升+21.2%（DXY）；同年11月欧佩克决定以市场份额换价格，油价随之崩跌-51%。宏观环境进入放缓/通缩恐慌象限：长债大涨（TLT +33.1%），防御板块均值+27.7%，显著优于周期板块+11.8%。非AI科技与硬件因质量成长溢价受益——半导体涨+39.5%——能源成本大幅压缩提升硬件利润率，低VIX环境下成长跑赢价值（+5.6%），篮子涨+39.1%，大幅领先SPY（+17.8%）。","drivers":["QE taper dollar surge","oil supply collapse","quality-growth premium","falling input costs","growth over value"],"drivers_zh":["QE退出美元飙升","原油供应过剩崩跌","质量成长溢价","能源投入成本下降","成长跑赢价值"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"QE taper and oil collapse lifts quality growth","title_zh":"QE退出与油价崩跌提振质量成长","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:trough:2014-01"},"2015-03-20":{"body":"China's stock market crashed 43% from June to August 2015, culminating in the PBOC's August 11 yuan devaluation of 1.9% — the largest in two decades — and Black Monday on August 24 when VIX spiked from 13 to 36. The risk-off cascade crushed cyclicals (-13.4%) while defensives fell only -6.9%, and semis dropped -20.9%. Non-AI hardware with heavy China/supply-chain exposure amplified the move to -22.0%, well beyond SPY at -10.6%, in a persistent slowdown/deflation-scare quad with oil continuing to fall -14% and copper-gold down -12.4%.","body_zh":"2015年6月至8月中国股市崩跌43%，8月11日人民银行宣布人民币一次性贬值1.9%（20年来最大幅度），8月24日'黑色星期一'VIX从13飙至36。避险恐慌重创周期板块（-13.4%），防御板块仅跌-6.9%，半导体下跌-20.9%。具有大量中国/供应链敞口的非AI硬件跌幅扩大至-22.0%，远超SPY的-10.6%，持续放缓/通缩恐慌象限叠加油价续跌-14%、铜金比下跌-12.4%。","drivers":["China stock crash","yuan devaluation Aug-11","VIX spike risk-off","commodity deflation","China supply-chain exposure"],"drivers_zh":["中国股市崩盘","人民币8月11日贬值","VIX飙升避险","大宗商品通缩","中国供应链敞口"],"prev_key":"2015-03-20","prev_key_chain":["2015-03-20"],"status":"exact","title":"China shock and yuan devaluation selloff","title_zh":"中国冲击与人民币贬值引发抛售","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:peak:2015-03"},"2015-08-25":{"body":"The August 25 post-Black-Monday trough marked a technical capitulation bottom as VIX collapsed from 36 back to 14 over eight weeks. Tech led the bounce at +16.8% with semis surging +22.9%, as a reflation/growth-up quad re-emerged: cyclicals averaged +12.9% versus defensives +7.1% and oil recovered +13.5%. The rebound was mega-cap-led (RSP lagged SPY by -2.2%) rather than a broad recovery, consistent with a relief rally off oversold conditions rather than a fundamental improvement in China or global-growth trajectories.","body_zh":"8月25日黑色星期一后的低点标志着技术性恐慌底部，VIX在八周内从36回落至14。科技引领反弹，涨+16.8%，半导体飙升+22.9%，再通胀/增长向上象限重现：周期板块均值+12.9%对防御板块+7.1%，油价回升+13.5%。反弹由大盘股主导（RSP跑输SPY -2.2%），而非全面复苏，与超卖后的技术性反弹一致，中国及全球增长基本面并未实质改善。","drivers":["VIX collapse risk-on","technical capitulation bottom","semis-led rebound","oil recovery","mega-cap beta chase"],"drivers_zh":["VIX回落风险偏好","技术性恐慌底部","半导体领涨反弹","油价回升","大盘股贝塔追涨"],"prev_key":"2015-08-25","prev_key_chain":["2015-08-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-China-shock cyclical rebound","title_zh":"中国冲击后周期性反弹","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:trough:2015-08"},"2015-10-23":{"body":"Oil resumed its collapse, falling -41.2% from October 2015 to February 2016, and credit stress widened sharply (HYG-LQD -8.7%), reviving fears of a Chinese hard landing and global growth recession. VIX re-spiked from 14 to 28 and cyclicals crashed -14.5% versus defensives -2.1% (Utilities held +3.5%), in a pronounced flight-to-safety rotation. Non-AI hardware with global revenue exposure fell -20.4%, matching the magnitude of the summer selloff, and tracking semis (SMH -16.9%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad where high-beta was crushed (SPHB-SPLV -21.9%).","body_zh":"2015年10月至2016年2月油价续跌-41.2%，信用利差急剧走阔（HYG-LQD -8.7%），中国硬着陆及全球增长衰退担忧重燃。VIX再次从14飙至28，周期板块暴跌-14.5%，防御板块仅跌-2.1%（公用事业持守+3.5%），避险轮动明显。具有全球收入敞口的非AI硬件下跌-20.4%，与夏季跌幅相当，追踪半导体（SMH -16.9%），处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限，高贝塔受重创（SPHB-SPLV -21.9%）。","drivers":["oil second leg down","China hard-landing fear","credit stress widening","flight-to-safety rotation","high-beta liquidation"],"drivers_zh":["油价二次下跌","中国硬着陆担忧","信用利差走阔","避险轮动","高贝塔清仓"],"prev_key":"2015-10-23","prev_key_chain":["2015-10-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil crash and China credit fears resume","title_zh":"油价崩跌与中国信用恐慌重燃","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:peak:2015-10"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"WTI oil bottomed at approximately $26/bbl on February 11, 2016, ending the commodity crash and launching a reflation trade. The Trump election on November 8, 2016 supercharged the rally — corporate tax cut expectations, deregulation, and infrastructure spending lifted Financials +92.6% and Tech +88.3%, with semis surging +150.8% as the dollar fell -5.7% and oil recovered +136.7%. Non-AI hardware rose +145.1% over 25 months in a reflation/growth-up quad where high-beta crushed low-vol by +64.6%, growth beat value by +17.4%, and VIX collapsed from 28 to 15.","body_zh":"2016年2月11日WTI原油触底约26美元/桶，结束大宗商品崩跌并开启再通胀交易。2016年11月8日特朗普当选大幅推升行情——企业减税预期、放松管制及基建支出提振金融板块+92.6%、科技+88.3%，半导体飙升+150.8%；美元下跌-5.7%，油价回升+136.7%。非AI硬件在25个月内上涨+145.1%，处于再通胀/增长向上象限，高贝塔大幅跑赢低波+64.6%，成长跑赢价值+17.4%，VIX从28降至15。","drivers":["oil trough reflation","Trump election tax-cut","corporate deregulation","dollar weakening tailwind","semis-led risk-on"],"drivers_zh":["油价触底再通胀","特朗普当选减税预期","企业去监管","美元走弱顺风","半导体领涨风险偏好"],"prev_key":"2016-02-11","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil bottom reflation and Trump tax-cut bull","title_zh":"油价触底再通胀与特朗普减税牛市","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:trough:2016-02"},"2018-03-09":{"body":"The top formed in March 2018 as Trump's Section 301 tariffs on China (announced March 22, 2018) triggered the first major trade-war escalation. Powell's statement on October 3, 2018 that the Fed was 'a long way from neutral' shocked markets; the Fed delivered its fourth 2018 hike in December and signaled two more for 2019. Smartphone demand collapsed into year-end, adding an inventory glut in chipsets and networking equipment. VIX exploded from 15 to 36, defensives held (-1.8%) while cyclicals fell -19.1%, the dollar surged +7.2%, and non-AI hardware fell -24.7% as semis crashed -26.3% versus SPY -14.4%.","body_zh":"2018年3月特朗普宣布对华301条款关税（3月22日），引发贸易战第一轮重大升级，顶部随之形成。2018年10月3日鲍威尔表示美联储'距中性利率还很远'震惊市场；12月完成当年第四次加息并暗示2019年再加两次。智能手机需求年末崩塌，芯片组和网络设备库存积压。VIX从15暴涨至36，防御板块均值-1.8%而周期板块跌-19.1%，美元走强+7.2%，非AI硬件下跌-24.7%，半导体崩跌-26.3%（SPY -14.4%）。","drivers":["Section 301 trade tariffs","Powell rate-shock Oct-3","Fed four hikes 2018","smartphone demand collapse","inventory glut"],"drivers_zh":["301条款贸易关税","鲍威尔10月3日利率冲击","美联储2018年四次加息","智能手机需求崩塌","库存积压"],"prev_key":"2018-03-09","prev_key_chain":["2018-03-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade war and Powell rate-shock selloff","title_zh":"贸易战与鲍威尔利率冲击下跌","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:peak:2018-03"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"The Christmas Eve 2018 low marked a turning point as Fed Chair Powell signaled a pause in January 2019, pivoting to a rate-cut cycle beginning July 2019 (TLT +18.9%). The January 2020 US-China Phase 1 trade deal de-escalated tariff risk, and the coming 5G smartphone and infrastructure cycle lifted semiconductor forward demand. Semis surged +85.9% in a tech-led risk-on tape (VIX 36 to 13, growth over value +18.4%), carrying non-AI hardware +50.2%, though the basket slightly lagged SPY (+44.2%) as mega-cap FAANG flows siphoned leadership from legacy hardware names.","body_zh":"2018年平安夜低点成为转折点，鲍威尔2019年1月明确暗示暂停加息，并于2019年7月启动降息周期（TLT +18.9%）。2020年1月中美第一阶段贸易协议降低关税风险，即将到来的5G手机和基础设施建设周期提振半导体远期需求。半导体飙升+85.9%，处于科技领涨的风险偏好行情（VIX从36降至13，成长跑赢价值+18.4%），带动非AI硬件涨+50.2%，但因FAANG大盘股资金虹吸传统硬件名字领涨权，篮子小幅跑输SPY（+44.2%）。","drivers":["Fed pivot Jan-2019","US-China Phase 1 deal","5G cycle demand","semis-led risk-on","rate-cut tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月转向","中美第一阶段协议","5G周期需求","半导体领涨风险偏好","降息顺风"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot and 5G cycle recovery","title_zh":"美联储转向与5G周期复苏","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:trough:2018-12"},"2020-01-23":{"body":"The WHO declared a Public Health Emergency of International Concern on January 30, 2020, and global lockdowns triggered the fastest bear market in history. VIX spiked from 13 to 76, oil crashed -63.4%, and cyclicals fell -36.4% versus defensives -17.2%, with SPY down -27.6%. Non-AI hardware fell -40.3% — well beyond SPY — as supply-chain disruptions hit contract manufacturers and PC/device assemblers in China, and credit conditions tightened (HYG-LQD -1.9%). The basket's high beta amplified the panic, while semis fell -31.8%, reflecting both demand uncertainty and fabrication shutdowns.","body_zh":"2020年1月30日世卫组织宣布国际突发公共卫生事件，全球封锁引发历史上最快的熊市。VIX从13暴涨至76，油价崩跌-63.4%，周期板块跌-36.4%对防御板块-17.2%，SPY下跌-27.6%。非AI硬件下跌-40.3%——远超SPY——因供应链中断冲击中国代工厂及PC/设备组装商，信用收紧（HYG-LQD -1.9%）。篮子高贝塔放大恐慌，半导体下跌-31.8%，同时反映需求不确定性和晶圆厂停工。","drivers":["COVID-19 lockdown shock","supply-chain disruption","VIX 76 panic","oil crash","high-beta amplification"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情封锁冲击","供应链中断","VIX飙至76恐慌","油价崩跌","高贝塔放大"],"prev_key":"2020-01-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-01-23"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID-19 lockdown crash","title_zh":"新冠疫情封锁崩盘","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"The Fed cut rates to 0-0.25% on March 15, 2020 and Congress deployed $5.8 trillion in total fiscal stimulus (CARES Act March 2020, December 2020, March 2021). Work-from-home demand, cloud build-out, gaming, and EV proliferation ignited a semiconductor super-cycle with capex spending topping $70 billion in 2021. Semis surged +214.5%, non-AI hardware rose +189.9% versus SPY +105.4%, in a reflation/growth-up quad (oil +278%, VIX 76 to 17, growth over value +31.3%) with broad participation (RSP beat SPY +11.0%).","body_zh":"美联储2020年3月15日将利率削减至0至0.25%，国会合计部署5.8万亿美元财政刺激（2020年3月CARES法案、2020年12月及2021年3月）。居家办公需求、云计算建设、游戏及电动车普及点燃半导体超级周期，2021年资本开支突破700亿美元。半导体飙升+214.5%，非AI硬件涨+189.9%（SPY +105.4%），处于再通胀/增长向上象限（油价+278%，VIX从76降至17，成长跑赢价值+31.3%），市场广度宽（RSP跑赢SPY +11.0%）。","drivers":["ZIRP zero-rate policy","fiscal stimulus CARES Act","WFH device demand","semiconductor super-cycle","broad risk-on reflation"],"drivers_zh":["零利率政策","CARES法案财政刺激","居家办公设备需求","半导体超级周期","广泛风险偏好再通胀"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"ZIRP fiscal stimulus semiconductor super-cycle","title_zh":"零利率财政刺激半导体超级周期","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:trough:2020-03"},"2022-01-04":{"body":"The January 2022 FOMC minutes (released January 5) signaled faster and earlier rate hikes than expected, launching a rate-shock bear as the Fed delivered seven hikes totaling 425bp in 2022. TLT fell -18.0% and the dollar surged +10.6% in a stagflation-ish quad as post-COVID PC and smartphone demand collapsed into a severe inventory correction. Defensives held (-3.7%) while cyclicals fell -15.8% and VIX spiked 17 to 28, with growth down versus value by -12.8%. Non-AI hardware fell -24.7% as semis collapsed -37.2% versus SPY -19.4%, with the basket's high-beta amplifying both the rate-driven multiple reset and the inventory-cycle demand destruction.","body_zh":"2022年1月FOMC会议纪要（1月5日公布）显示加息节奏快于预期，美联储全年累计加息425bp，利率冲击熊市启动。TLT下跌-18.0%，美元飙升+10.6%，处于类滞胀象限，疫情后PC和智能手机需求崩塌引发严重库存调整。防御板块持守-3.7%，周期板块跌-15.8%，VIX从17升至28，成长跑输价值-12.8%。非AI硬件下跌-24.7%，半导体崩跌-37.2%（SPY -19.4%），篮子高贝塔同时放大了利率驱动的估值重置与库存周期需求破坏。","drivers":["Fed hawkish FOMC pivot","rate-shock multiple reset","dollar surge headwind","PC smartphone demand collapse","inventory correction"],"drivers_zh":["美联储鹰派转向FOMC","利率冲击估值重置","美元走强逆风","PC智能手机需求崩塌","库存调整"],"prev_key":"2022-01-04","prev_key_chain":["2022-01-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-shock hardware reset","title_zh":"利率冲击硬件估值重置","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:peak:2022-01"},"2022-07-05":{"body":"The June 2022 CPI print (released July 13) confirmed that US headline inflation had peaked at 9.1%, sparking a peak-inflation narrative that drove a short-covering squeeze. Tech led (+16.9%) and semis surged +22.7% in a reflation/growth-up quad (VIX 28 to 20, growth over value +4.6%, cyclicals +14.9% vs defensives +7.0%). Critically, TLT fell -1.4% (yields still mildly rising), confirming this was a positioning-driven relief rally rather than a genuine Fed pivot — the bounce faded as recession fears and inventory headwinds in non-AI hardware remained unresolved.","body_zh":"2022年6月CPI数据（7月13日公布）确认美国标题通胀见顶于9.1%，引发通胀见顶叙事推动空头回补。科技领涨（+16.9%），半导体飙升+22.7%，处于再通胀/增长向上象限（VIX从28降至20，成长跑赢价值+4.6%，周期板块+14.9%对防御板块+7.0%）。值得注意的是TLT下跌-1.4%（收益率仍温和上行），确认这是仓位驱动的喘息反弹而非真正的美联储转向——随着衰退担忧和非AI硬件库存阻力未消，反弹逐渐消退。","drivers":["peak-inflation CPI narrative","short-covering squeeze","semis-led risk-on bounce","positioning relief","inventory overhang unresolved"],"drivers_zh":["通胀见顶CPI叙事","空头回补挤压","半导体领涨风险偏好反弹","仓位喘息","库存积压未消"],"prev_key":"2022-07-05","prev_key_chain":["2022-07-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-inflation hope bear bounce","title_zh":"通胀见顶预期熊市反弹","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:trough:2022-07"},"2022-08-18":{"body":"The August 18 peak gave way as yields resumed their surge ahead of Jackson Hole (August 26, 2022), where Powell's three-minute speech explicitly rejected any early policy pivot and vowed to maintain restrictive rates for some time. TLT fell another -12.3% and the dollar surged +5.4%, hammering growth stocks (value beat growth +4.4%) and pushing VIX from 20 to 34. Non-AI hardware fell -20.2% and semis -27.4% versus SPY -16.3%, as soft consumer-electronics demand and inventory corrections in PCs and mobile compounded the macro rate-driven de-rating.","body_zh":"8月18日高点告一段落，收益率在杰克逊霍尔会议（2022年8月26日）前后加速上行，鲍威尔三分钟演讲明确拒绝任何提前政策转向，并承诺'较长时间'维持限制性利率。TLT再跌-12.3%，美元走强+5.4%，重挫成长股（价值跑赢成长+4.4%），VIX从20升至34。非AI硬件下跌-20.2%，半导体-27.4%（SPY -16.3%），PC和移动终端消费电子需求疲软及库存调整叠加宏观利率驱动的估值下杀。","drivers":["Jackson Hole no-pivot speech","yields resumed surge","dollar strengthening","consumer-electronics inventory","growth-stock de-rating"],"drivers_zh":["杰克逊霍尔拒绝转向演讲","收益率加速上行","美元走强","消费电子库存","成长股估值下杀"],"prev_key":"2022-08-18","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole deepens rate-driven selloff","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔加深利率驱动跌势","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:peak:2022-08"},"2022-10-12":{"body":"The October 12, 2022 CPI undershoot marked the market's post-COVID bottom, and OpenAI's release of ChatGPT in November 2022 ignited the generative-AI investment supercycle, with hyperscalers committing over $1.3 trillion in capex and R&D from Q4 2022 through 2025. The Fed paused hikes in June 2023 and began cutting in September 2024, driving VIX from 34 to 13. Non-AI hardware rose +82.8% as semis surged +217.4% in a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation quad — but the basket underperformed a narrow mega-cap AI tape (RSP lagged SPY by -24.4%), gaining on AI-capex spillover into networking silicon and legacy compute rather than direct AI exposure.","body_zh":"2022年10月12日CPI低于预期，标志着疫情后市场底部，同年11月OpenAI发布ChatGPT点燃生成式AI投资超级周期：超大规模云厂商2022年Q4至2025年累计承诺逾1.3万亿美元资本开支和研发。美联储2023年6月暂停加息，2024年9月启动降息，VIX从34降至13。非AI硬件涨+82.8%，半导体飙升+217.4%，处于金发姑娘/增长向上-去通胀象限——但篮子跑输窄幅大盘股AI行情（RSP跑输SPY -24.4%），涨幅来自AI资本开支外溢至网络芯片和传统计算，而非直接AI敞口。","drivers":["ChatGPT AI investment cycle","Fed pause then cut","goldilocks disinflation","AI-capex spillover networking","narrow mega-cap melt-up"],"drivers_zh":["ChatGPT AI投资周期","美联储暂停后降息","金发姑娘去通胀","AI资本开支外溢网络","窄幅大盘股飙升"],"prev_key":"2022-10-12","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-12"],"status":"exact","title":"AI melt-up and Fed-pivot recovery","title_zh":"AI飙升与美联储转向复苏","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:trough:2022-10"},"2024-07-16":{"body":"The Bank of Japan's surprise rate hike on July 31, 2024 forced a rapid unwind of the global yen carry trade, spiking VIX from 13 to 28 and triggering a flight-to-safety rotation where defensives held (+0.9%) while cyclicals fell -8.1%. Non-AI hardware dropped -17.5% as semis fell -22.7% versus SPY -8.2%, with breadth actually broadening (RSP beat SPY +3.3%), a characteristic of macro-deleveraging rather than sector-specific deterioration. Growth underperformed value by -7.7% and the dollar fell -1.0% as risk assets were broadly liquidated to cover yen-funded positions.","body_zh":"2024年7月31日日本央行意外加息，迫使全球日元套息交易快速平仓，VIX从13飙至28，引发避险轮动：防御板块持守+0.9%，周期板块跌-8.1%。非AI硬件下跌-17.5%，半导体跌-22.7%（SPY -8.2%），市场广度实际上扩散（RSP跑赢SPY +3.3%）——这是宏观去杠杆的特征而非板块特定恶化。成长跑输价值-7.7%，美元下跌-1.0%，风险资产被广泛清算以弥补日元融资头寸。","drivers":["BoJ rate hike yen-carry unwind","macro deleveraging","VIX spike flight-to-safety","broad risk-asset liquidation","lower-beta cushion"],"drivers_zh":["日央行加息套息平仓","宏观去杠杆","VIX飙升避险","风险资产广泛清算","低贝塔缓冲"],"prev_key":"2024-07-16","prev_key_chain":["2024-07-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Yen carry-unwind air pocket","title_zh":"日元套息平仓气穴","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:peak:2024-07"},"2024-08-07":{"body":"The Fed's September 18, 2024 rate cut (50bp) provided the macro catalyst for a risk-on recovery, and the Trump election victory on November 5, 2024 added deregulation and domestic-capex optimism. Semis gained +22.4% and the basket rose +18.6% in a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation quad (VIX 28 to 16, growth over value +11.9%). However, the basket barely matched SPY (+18.4%) — breadth was narrow (RSP lagged SPY -6.0%) and the dollar firmed +3.0% — reflecting that the AI narrative continued to siphon leadership toward AI-levered names while non-AI hardware gained by proximity rather than fundamental re-rating.","body_zh":"美联储2024年9月18日降息50bp提供宏观催化，2024年11月5日特朗普当选胜利叠加去监管和国内资本开支乐观情绪。半导体涨+22.4%，篮子涨+18.6%，处于金发姑娘/增长向上-去通胀象限（VIX从28降至16，成长跑赢价值+11.9%）。然而篮子勉强与SPY（+18.4%）持平——市场广度狭窄（RSP跑输SPY -6.0%），美元走强+3.0%——AI叙事持续将领涨权吸引至AI杠杆名字，非AI硬件靠近水涨船高而非基本面重估。","drivers":["Fed 50bp cut Sep-2024","Trump election deregulation","risk-on recovery","AI narrative proximity lift","narrow breadth"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2024年9月降息50bp","特朗普当选去监管","风险偏好复苏","AI叙事近水楼台","市场广度狭窄"],"prev_key":"2024-08-07","prev_key_chain":["2024-08-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed cut and Trump-election risk-on lift","title_zh":"美联储降息与特朗普当选风险偏好提振","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:trough:2024-08"},"2025-02-20":{"body":"DeepSeek's open-source AI model release on January 27, 2025 erased nearly $600 billion of Nvidia's market cap in a single day, raising fears that AI capex efficiency gains would reduce demand for advanced hardware. Trump's Liberation Day tariff announcement on April 2, 2025 — imposing a minimum 10% baseline tariff on all imports and up to 50% on 57 trading partners — crashed the market, with VIX exploding from 16 to 52. Hardware names with China manufacturing and consumer-cyclical exposure bore the brunt: the basket fell -31.1% as semis dropped -30.2% versus SPY -18.4%, with high-beta crushed vs low-vol by -22.0% in a severe slowdown/deflation-scare flush.","body_zh":"2025年1月27日DeepSeek开源AI模型发布，英伟达单日市值蒸发近6000亿美元，市场担忧AI资本开支效率提升将削减先进硬件需求。2025年4月2日特朗普宣布'解放日'关税——对所有进口商品征收最低10%基准关税，对57个贸易伙伴最高50%——触发市场崩盘，VIX从16暴涨至52。具有中国制造和消费周期性敞口的硬件名字首当其冲：篮子跌-31.1%，半导体跌-30.2%（SPY -18.4%），高贝塔相对低波重挫-22.0%，处于严峻的放缓/通缩恐慌急剧清仓象限。","drivers":["DeepSeek AI efficiency shock","Liberation Day tariffs Apr-2","China manufacturing exposure","VIX 52 panic selloff","high-beta liquidation"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek AI效率冲击","4月2日解放日关税","中国制造业敞口","VIX飙至52恐慌抛售","高贝塔清仓"],"prev_key":"2025-02-20","prev_key_chain":["2025-02-20"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek shock and Liberation Day crash","title_zh":"DeepSeek冲击与解放日崩盘","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:peak:2025-02"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"Trump's 90-day tariff pause announced April 9, 2025 — with semiconductors and computers largely exempted — provided the immediate catalyst, and a roaring risk-on regime then carried the tech complex through mid-2026. Gartner forecast worldwide semiconductor revenue to exceed $1.3 trillion in 2026, and hyperscaler capex commitments of $750 billion for 2026 confirmed the AI infrastructure buildout remained intact. VIX collapsed from 52 to 16, high-beta crushed low-vol by +121.4%, and semis surged +252.4% in a reflation/growth-up quad. Non-AI hardware rose +202.8% as a narrow mega-cap-led tape (RSP lagged SPY -15.2%) swept the entire tech complex, re-rating networking silicon, analog/MCU, and legacy hardware into the June 2026 peak.","body_zh":"2025年4月9日特朗普宣布90天关税暂停——半导体和计算机基本获豁免——提供即时催化剂，随后狂热的风险偏好行情将整个科技板块推升至2026年中。Gartner预测2026年全球半导体收入将超过1.3万亿美元，超大规模云厂商承诺2026年7500亿美元资本开支，确认AI基础设施建设完好无损。VIX从52崩落至16，高贝塔大幅跑赢低波+121.4%，半导体飙升+252.4%，处于再通胀/增长向上象限。非AI硬件涨+202.8%，窄幅大盘股主导行情（RSP跑输SPY -15.2%）裹挟整个科技板块，网络芯片、模拟/MCU和传统硬件估值全线重估，直至2026年6月见顶。","drivers":["tariff pause semiconductor exemption","AI capex cycle intact","narrow tech melt-up","VIX collapse risk-on","non-AI hardware re-rating"],"drivers_zh":["关税暂停半导体豁免","AI资本开支周期完好","窄幅科技飙升","VIX崩落风险偏好","非AI硬件估值重估"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff pause and broad tech melt-up sweep","title_zh":"关税暂停与广泛科技飙升裹挟","turn_id":"non_ai_tech:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Non-AI Tech and Hardware is topping at the 89th cycle percentile with a SELL signal as of late June 2026. The basket was swept up in the broad April 2025 to June 2026 tech melt-up (SMH +252.4%), but is now stalling against multiple headwinds: the dollar has firmed +3.4% DXY since the cycle low, a direct headwind for multinational hardware and networking names; growth is underperforming value by -15.2%; and breadth is broadening (RSP beat SPY +2.9%), a classic late-cycle rotation away from the narrow mega-cap tech leadership that carried this basket. The rs_rank of 7 out of 11 GICS sectors signals the basket has already slipped behind in the current rotation. A Broadcom earnings miss on AI revenue guidance in early June 2026 triggered a broad semiconductor sector selloff that accelerated the topping process, while healthcare and financials have rotated to the lead, which is historically a reliable sign that the non-AI hardware cycle peak is in or imminent.","now_zh":"截至2026年6月下旬，非AI科技与硬件处于周期第89百分位顶部，信号为\"卖出\"。该篮子被2025年4月至2026年6月的广泛科技飙升裹挟（SMH +252.4%），但如今面临多重阻力：美元自本轮周期低点以来走强+3.4%（DXY），对跨国硬件和网络名字构成直接逆风；成长跑输价值-15.2%；市场广度扩散（RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%），这是周期晚期从窄幅大盘股科技领涨向外轮动的经典信号。相对强度排名7/11意味着该篮子在当前轮动中已落后。2026年6月初博通AI收入指引不及预期引发半导体板块大幅抛售，顶部形成进程加速；医疗和金融板块先后占据领涨地位，这历来是非AI硬件周期见顶或即将见顶的可靠信号。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-nuclear_power":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"From January 2014 through June 2016, the nuclear/utility cohort eked out a modest +6.6% gain — drastically underperforming SPY (+21%) — in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad dominated by defensive yield hunters (Utilities +45.1%, Health +35.0%, Staples +33.8% led the tape). The macro backdrop was a crude oil collapse of -46% (2014-2016), a 16% DXY surge, and a TLT rally of +38%, signalling falling real growth expectations. Nuclear-utility anchors like Exelon and Entergy benefited from falling rates (rate-sensitive yield proxies), but upstream uranium miners faced a structural price collapse: uranium spot fell from ~$35/lb in early 2014 to under $20/lb by late 2016 following post-Fukushima oversupply and Japanese reactor shutdowns, capping the basket's gains.","body_zh":"2014年1月至2016年6月，核电/公用事业组别仅录得微薄的+6.6%涨幅，大幅落后于SPY（+21%），处于以防御性寻收益为主的放缓/通缩惊魂象限（公用事业+45.1%、医疗+35.0%、必需消费+33.8%领涨）。宏观背景为原油崩跌46%（2014-2016年）、DXY涨16%、TLT涨38%，信号为实际增长预期下降。Exelon与Entergy等核电公用事业龙头受益于利率下行（利率敏感型股息代理），但上游铀矿开采商面临铀价结构性崩溃：受福岛后供给过剩及日本反应堆停堆影响，铀现货价由2014年初约35美元/磅跌至2016年末不足20美元/磅，压制了篮子涨幅。","drivers":["falling uranium price (~$35 to <$20/lb 2014-16)","oil collapse (-46%)","defensive yield bid (TLT +38%)","Fukushima-era oversupply","post-2011 Japan reactor shutdowns"],"drivers_zh":["铀价下跌(约35美元跌至不足20美元/磅 2014-16年)","油价崩溃(-46%)","防御性股息买盘(TLT +38%)","福岛后供给过剩","日本反应堆停堆"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Yield-chasing bid anchors nuclear utilities","title_zh":"寻收益买盘为核电公用事业提供支撑","turn_id":"nuclear_power:trough:2014-01"},"2016-06-07":{"body":"A sharp -25% selloff from June to November 2016 as the defensive bond-proxy trade unwound ahead of the Trump-reflation rotation. From mid-2016, Treasury yields began rising (10-year from ~1.4% post-Brexit to ~2.6% by year-end), pressuring rate-sensitive nuclear utilities as the market priced in a December 2016 Fed hike and a reflationary fiscal agenda. The macro was a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation tape with cyclicals (+0.6%) edging defensives (-3.5%): nuclear utilities were double-hit as both their yield-proxy premium and their bond-like duration eroded. The basket was also dragged by uranium prices at decade lows and Exelon's threats to close Clinton and Quad Cities nuclear plants without Illinois subsidy legislation.","body_zh":"2016年6月至11月急跌25%，防御性债券代理交易在特朗普再通胀轮动前夕平仓。2016年中起，美债收益率攀升（10年期从脱欧后约1.4%涨至年底约2.6%），利率敏感型核电公用事业承压，市场已在定价2016年12月美联储加息及财政再通胀议程。宏观为金发女郎/增长向上-去通胀行情，周期股（+0.6%）小幅跑赢防御股（-3.5%）：核电公用事业的股息溢价与类债久期同步受损。篮子还受拖累于铀价处于十年低点，以及Exelon若无伊利诺伊州补贴立法将关闭Clinton和Quad Cities核电厂的威胁。","drivers":["rate backup (10yr ~1.4%->2.6%)","Trump reflation rotation","yield-proxy unwind","Illinois nuclear plant closure threat","uranium price at decade lows"],"drivers_zh":["利率回升(10年期约1.4%->2.6%)","特朗普再通胀轮动","股息代理平仓","伊利诺伊州核电厂关闭威胁","铀价处于十年低点"],"prev_key":"2016-06-07","prev_key_chain":["2016-06-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Bond-proxy unwind as rate fears hit utilities","title_zh":"利率担忧引发公用事业债券代理平仓","turn_id":"nuclear_power:peak:2016-06"},"2016-11-02":{"body":"A massive +153% two-year rally from November 2016 to October 2018, the basket's largest leg until the AI era. Trump's election on November 8, 2016 catalysed a nuclear-friendly policy narrative supportive of fleet preservation, while Illinois's Future Energy Jobs Act (passed Dec 1, signed by Gov. Rauner Dec 7, 2016) saved Exelon's Clinton and Quad Cities plants via Zero Emission Credits (~$235M/yr, 10-year contract), triggering a revaluation of the utility-nuclear complex. The broader reflation/growth-up quad (oil +66%, copper-gold +34%, VIX collapsing 19->12, cyclicals +44% vs defensives +25%) simultaneously lifted energy-correlated names. Kazatomprom's December 2017 announcement of a 20% production cut (vs Subsoil Use Contracts, from January 2018) provided an additional supply-side tailwind for miners like Cameco (CCJ), which soared through 2017-2018 on the combined demand-protection + supply-cut thesis.","body_zh":"2016年11月至2018年10月录得+153%的两年大涨，是AI时代前篮子最大涨幅。2016年11月8日特朗普当选催生友好核电的政策叙事，支持机组保护；伊利诺伊州《未来能源就业法》（12月1日通过、州长Rauner于12月7日签署）通过零排放信用挽救了Exelon的Clinton和Quad Cities核电厂（约2.35亿美元/年、10年合约），触发公用事业-核电综合体重估。更广泛的再通胀/增长向上象限（油价+66%、铜金比+34%、VIX由19崩至12、周期股+44%对防御股+25%）同时推升能源相关标的。哈萨克斯坦原子能公司（Kazatomprom）于2017年12月宣布相对采矿合约削减20%产量（自2018年1月起），为Cameco（CCJ）等矿商提供额外供给侧顺风，后者在需求保护+供应削减双重逻辑下于2017-2018年大幅飙升。","drivers":["Trump pro-nuclear policy narrative","Illinois Zero Emission Credits (Dec 2016)","Kazatomprom 20% uranium cut (Dec 2017)","reflation/growth-up quad (oil +66%)","VIX compression (19->12)"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普友好核电政策叙事","伊利诺伊州零排放信用（2016年12月）","哈萨克斯坦原子能20%减产（2017年12月）","再通胀/增长向上象限（油价+66%）","VIX压缩（19->12）"],"prev_key":"2016-11-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-11-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump election ignites nuclear policy re-rate","title_zh":"特朗普当选点燃核电政策重估行情","turn_id":"nuclear_power:trough:2016-11"},"2018-10-02":{"body":"A -21% selloff from October to December 2018 matching the broad market's worst quarter since 2011 — a global growth scare triggered by serial Fed rate hikes that had lifted the policy rate to 2.25-2.5%, inverting sections of the yield curve and raising recession risk. The macro was a textbook slowdown/deflation-scare with VIX exploding 12->36, defensives (-8.9%) dramatically outpacing cyclicals (-22.3%), oil plunging -43% (oversupply/OPEC+ fears), and credit spreads widening. The nuclear basket, now priced as a cyclical-growth name after two years of outperformance, overshot the broad market decline alongside tech (-23.6%) and industrials (-23.4%). Westinghouse's bankruptcy overhang (filed March 2017, emerged August 2018) added sector-specific weight.","body_zh":"2018年10月至12月急跌21%，与大盘2011年以来最差季度同步——全球增长惊魂由美联储连续加息触发，政策利率已升至2.25-2.5%，部分收益率曲线倒挂并加剧衰退风险。宏观为经典的放缓/通缩惊魂：VIX由12飙至36、防御股（-8.9%）大幅跑赢周期股（-22.3%）、油价暴跌43%（供给过剩/欧佩克+担忧）、信用利差走阔。核电篮子在两年跑赢后已被市场定价为周期成长型，随科技（-23.6%）和工业（-23.4%）一同超调下跌。西屋电气破产压力（2017年3月申请、2018年8月走出破产）带来板块特有的头顶压力。","drivers":["Fed overtightening (rate to ~2.5%)","yield curve inversion fears","VIX spike (12->36)","oil crash -43%","Westinghouse bankruptcy overhang"],"drivers_zh":["美联储过度紧缩（利率约2.5%）","收益率曲线倒挂担忧","VIX飙升（12->36）","油价崩跌-43%","西屋电气破产压制"],"prev_key":"2018-10-02","prev_key_chain":["2018-10-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed rate-shock selloff; high-beta names crater","title_zh":"美联储加息冲击；高贝塔标的崩跌","turn_id":"nuclear_power:peak:2018-10"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"A +35.5% recovery from the Christmas Eve 2018 low through February 2020. Fed Chair Powell delivered a dovish pivot in early January 2019 (pausing rate hikes) and subsequently began cutting in July 2019 (three cuts through October), igniting a growth-asset recovery with semis leading (+82% SMH, TLT +25%). The nuclear basket benefited from the broader reflation/growth-up tape but significantly underperformed SPY (+45%), Tech (+75%) and the mega-cap melt-up; uranium prices remained depressed (spot around $24-26/lb) limiting miner upside, and pre-revenue SMR names were scarce. The basket's modest gains reflected the rate-relief bid on nuclear utilities rather than any demand-led re-rating.","body_zh":"从2018年平安夜低点至2020年2月反弹+35.5%。美联储主席鲍威尔于2019年1月初发出鸽派转向信号（暂停加息），随后7月开始降息（至10月共降三次），点燃成长资产复苏，半导体领涨（SMH +82%，TLT +25%）。核电篮子受益于更广泛的再通胀/增长向上行情，但大幅落后于SPY（+45%）、科技（+75%）及巨头推动的估值扩张行情；铀现货价仍低迷（约24-26美元/磅），限制矿商上行空间，尚无营收的SMR标的数量有限。篮子温和涨幅反映的是利率宽松对核电公用事业资产负债表的利率回落买盘，而非需求驱动的重估。","drivers":["Powell dovish pivot (Jan 2019)","Fed rate cuts x3 (Jul-Oct 2019)","growth-asset recovery (SMH +82%)","rate relief on utility balance sheets","uranium price flat ~$24-26/lb"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔鸽派转向（2019年1月）","美联储三次降息（2019年7-10月）","成长资产复苏（SMH +82%）","利率回落利好公用事业资产负债表","铀价维持平稳约24-26美元/磅"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot and risk-on rebound lifts basket","title_zh":"美联储转向与风险偏好反弹推升篮子","turn_id":"nuclear_power:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-21":{"body":"A brutal -42.8% crash in roughly a month as COVID-19 was declared a pandemic (WHO, March 11, 2020), triggering the fastest bear market in US history. VIX exploded from 17 to 76 — the highest since 2008 — oil collapsed -62% as demand evaporated (compounded by the Saudi-Russia price war launched March 8), and all risk assets were liquidated indiscriminately. The nuclear basket, despite containing utility-like names, underperformed even defensives (-18.1%) as its cyclical-adjacent uranium and SMR components were dumped alongside industrials (-35%) and financials (-38%). Kazatomprom subsequently announced production curtailments due to COVID safety protocols, but this supply signal arrived too late to arrest the collapse.","body_zh":"约一个月内惨跌42.8%，世卫组织于2020年3月11日宣布新冠疫情为大流行病，触发美国历史上最快的熊市。VIX由17飙至76——2008年以来最高——原油崩跌62%（需求蒸发叠加3月8日沙特-俄罗斯价格战爆发），所有风险资产遭无差别抛售。核电篮子尽管包含公用事业类型标的，但仍跑输防御板块（-18.1%），因其周期相关的铀和SMR板块随工业（-35%）和金融（-38%）一同遭到抛售。哈萨克斯坦原子能随后以新冠安全协议为由宣布减产，但该供给信号来得太晚，无法阻止崩盘。","drivers":["COVID pandemic panic (VIX 17->76)","Saudi-Russia oil price war (-62% crude)","forced-liquidation across all risk assets","SMR/uranium names treated as cyclical","global demand shock"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情恐慌（VIX 17->76）","沙特-俄罗斯油价战（原油-62%）","全资产类别强制清盘","SMR/铀矿被视为周期性资产","全球需求骤降"],"prev_key":"2020-02-21","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-21"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash — high-beta implosion","title_zh":"新冠疫情崩盘——高贝塔资产爆仓","turn_id":"nuclear_power:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"The single largest leg in basket history — a +531.5% surge from the March 2020 COVID trough through July 2024 — driven by three phases telescoping into one massive re-rate. Phase 1 (2020-2021): Fed QE, Biden's $1.2 trillion Infrastructure law (Nov 2021) including billions for civil nuclear credits and advanced reactors, and the Sprott Physical Uranium Trust launch (July 19, 2021) which began aggressively buying physical pounds and squeezed uranium from ~$30 toward $50/lb by late 2021. Phase 2 (2022-2023): Russia's invasion of Ukraine (February 2022) drove energy-security panic, uranium pushed toward multi-year highs, and the Inflation Reduction Act (August 2022) created the 45U zero-emission nuclear production tax credit (base ~$3/MWh, up to ~$15/MWh with prevailing-wage rules) that improved nuclear economics. NuScale and Oklo went public via SPACs (2022), adding new high-beta speculative vehicles. Phase 3 (2023-mid 2024): AI data-center demand narrative exploded — Amazon, Google, and Microsoft pursued nuclear power, uranium spiked above $100/lb in late January 2024 (a 16-year high, ~$106) before fading, and AI-baseload buying carried the group to its July 2024 peak. The reflation/growth-up quad (energy +363%, cyclicals +191% vs defensives +65%, SMH +459%) underpinned the entire run.","body_zh":"篮子历史最大涨幅——从2020年3月新冠低点至2024年7月飙升+531.5%——由三个阶段叠加形成一次巨大重估。第一阶段（2020-2021年）：美联储QE、拜登1.2万亿美元基础设施法（2021年11月，含数十亿美元用于民用核电信用与先进反应堆），以及Sprott实物铀信托（2021年7月19日）启动后大举买入实物铀，将铀价由约30美元/磅挤压至2021年末约50美元/磅。第二阶段（2022-2023年）：俄乌战争（2022年2月）引发能源安全恐慌，铀价升至多年高位；《通货膨胀削减法》（2022年8月）创设45U零排放核能生产税收抵免（基准约3美元/兆瓦时，满足现行工资规则可达约15美元/兆瓦时），改善核电经济性。NuScale与Oklo通过SPAC上市（2022年），新增高贝塔投机载体。第三阶段（2023年至2024年中）：AI数据中心需求叙事爆发——亚马逊、谷歌与微软争取核电，铀价于2024年1月底突破100美元/磅（16年高点、约106美元）后回落，AI基荷买盘将该组别推升至2024年7月高点。整体运行以再通胀/增长向上象限为支撑（能源+363%、周期股+191%对防御股+65%、SMH +459%）。","drivers":["Biden infrastructure + IRA 45U tax credit (~$3-15/MWh, Aug 2022)","Sprott uranium trust squeeze (uranium ~$30->$100+/lb)","Russia-Ukraine energy security panic (Feb 2022)","AI data center power demand (2023-24)","uranium 16-year high >$100/lb (Jan 2024)"],"drivers_zh":["拜登基础设施+IRA 45U税收抵免（约3-15美元/兆瓦时，2022年8月）","Sprott铀信托挤压（铀价约30->100+美元/磅）","俄乌战争能源安全恐慌（2022年2月）","AI数据中心电力需求（2023-24年）","铀价16年高点突破100美元/磅（2024年1月）"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"531% supercycle: clean energy, IRA, AI baseload","title_zh":"531%超级周期：清洁能源、IRA与AI基荷","turn_id":"nuclear_power:trough:2020-03"},"2024-07-12":{"body":"A sharp -25.5% pullback into the August 5, 2024 volatility spike and yen-carry unwind, as the newly hot nuclear-for-AI names gave back froth. The macro was a slowdown/deflation-scare risk-off (VIX exploding 12->39, defensives +0.3% vs cyclicals -6.6%, broadening +4.2%); as a high-beta cohort the group overshot the broad tape (SMH -22.3%). The restart/baseload thesis stayed intact — this was a positioning flush in a vol shock, not a fundamental break.","body_zh":"2024年8月5日波动飙升与日元套利平仓前急跌25.5%，新晋火热的核电AI概念股吐出泡沫。宏观是放缓/通缩惊魂的避险（VIX由12飙至39、防御股+0.3%对周期股-6.6%、广度扩散+4.2%）；作为高贝塔组别它超调于大盘（半导体SMH -22.3%）。重启／基荷逻辑完好——此为波动冲击中的仓位急挫，而非基本面破裂。","drivers":["risk-off vol shock (VIX 12->39)","yen carry trade unwind","high-beta positioning flush","profit-taking"],"drivers_zh":["避险波动冲击（VIX 12->39）","日元套利交易平仓","高贝塔仓位清洗","获利了结"],"prev_key":"2024-07-12","prev_key_chain":["2024-07-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Aug-2024 vol scare clips high-beta leaders","title_zh":"2024年8月波动惊魂回吐高贝塔涨幅","turn_id":"nuclear_power:peak:2024-07"},"2024-08-05":{"body":"A +202.1% rocket leg as marquee datacenter-nuclear deals — Constellation's Three Mile Island Unit 1 restart for Microsoft (announced September 20, 2024, 20-year PPA, 835 MW, targeting 2028), Amazon's SMR partnerships with X-Energy and Energy Northwest (October 2024), and Google's deal with Kairos Power (October 2024) — validated nuclear as the AI-baseload answer. The basket amplified a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on tape (SMH +23.1%, growth>value +12.9, VIX collapsing 39->15) with narrow mega-cap-led breadth (equal-weight lagged -5.5%) and a firmer dollar (DXY +4.6%); Fed cuts (Sep, Nov, Dec 2024) and reactor-restart headlines compounded the buying frenzy in the highest-beta corner of AI power.","body_zh":"上涨202.1%的火箭行情，标志性数据中心核电协议——Constellation为微软重启三哩岛1号机组（2024年9月20日宣布，20年购电协议，835兆瓦，目标2028年）、亚马逊与X-Energy和Energy Northwest的SMR合作（2024年10月），以及谷歌与Kairos Power协议（2024年10月）——确立核电为AI基荷答案。该篮子放大了金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好行情（SMH +23.1%、成长跑赢价值+12.9、VIX由39崩至15），广度狭窄、巨头领涨（等权跑输-5.5%）、美元走强（DXY +4.6%）；美联储降息（2024年9、11、12月）与反应堆重启新闻在AI电力中弹性最高的角落叠加放大买盘狂热。","drivers":["TMI restart/Microsoft PPA (Sep 20, 2024)","Amazon SMR deals (Oct 2024)","Google Kairos PPA (Oct 2024)","Fed cutting cycle (Sep-Dec 2024)","goldilocks risk-on (SMH +23.1%)"],"drivers_zh":["三哩岛重启/微软购电协议（2024年9月20日）","亚马逊SMR协议（2024年10月）","谷歌Kairos购电协议（2024年10月）","美联储降息周期（2024年9-12月）","金发女郎风险偏好（SMH +23.1%）"],"prev_key":"2024-08-05","prev_key_chain":["2024-08-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Datacenter-nuclear deals ignite a goldilocks re-rate","title_zh":"数据中心核电协议在金发女郎行情中点燃重估","turn_id":"nuclear_power:trough:2024-08"},"2025-01-24":{"body":"A -21.8% flush as DeepSeek's R1 model release (January 20, 2025) hammered the AI-power-demand premium hardest in the high-beta nuclear/SMR cohort, culminating in the January 27 rout — Vistra fell ~28%, Talen ~21%, Constellation ~21%, with Oklo and NuScale both down >20%. DeepSeek claimed frontier AI performance using far less compute (and therefore power), threatening the entire AI-capex-equals-power-demand chain. It was a sharp risk-off jolt (VIX 15->18, defensives +0.9% vs cyclicals -0.9%, slowdown/deflation-scare quad) in which pre-revenue SMR developers — speculative leveraged longs — were the most exposed to the demand-destruction narrative.","body_zh":"急挫21.8%，DeepSeek R1模型发布（2025年1月20日）对高弹性核电/SMR组别的AI电力需求溢价打击最重，并在1月27日抛售中达到顶峰——Vistra单日跌约28%、Talen约21%、Constellation约21%，Oklo与NuScale均跌超20%。DeepSeek声称以远低于现有模型的算力（因而所需电力更少）实现前沿AI性能，威胁整条「AI资本开支=电力需求」逻辑链。这是一次急促的避险冲击（VIX 15->18、防御股+0.9%对周期股-0.9%、放缓/通缩惊魂象限），尚无营收的SMR开发商——投机性杠杆多头——最受需求毁灭叙事拖累。","drivers":["DeepSeek R1 release (Jan 20, 2025)","AI compute-efficiency shock","Jan 27 power/nuclear stock rout","high-beta leveraged-long unwind"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek R1发布（2025年1月20日）","AI算力效率冲击","1月27日电力/核电股抛售","高贝塔杠杆多头平仓"],"prev_key":"2025-01-24","prev_key_chain":["2025-01-24"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek demand-shock high-beta flush","title_zh":"DeepSeek需求冲击的高贝塔急挫","turn_id":"nuclear_power:peak:2025-01"},"2025-01-27":{"body":"A quick +22.0% bounce over two weeks as dip-buyers concluded the DeepSeek demand-destruction read was overdone — the Jevons-paradox argument (efficiency gains expand total AI deployment and power draw) gained traction. The tape was flat-to-stagflation-ish (VIX 18->16, cyclicals and defensives both +0.2%, copper-gold +5.4%), so this was idiosyncratic, headline-driven mean-reversion in a thin high-beta pure-play group rather than a macro-regime rally. Trump's January 20 Day-1 energy actions (the national energy emergency and 'Unleashing American Energy' orders, broadly pro-energy rather than nuclear-specific) provided a modest near-term policy bid.","body_zh":"两周内迅速反弹22.0%，抄底资金认为DeepSeek需求毁灭解读过度——杰文斯悖论论点（效率提升扩大AI总部署量与用电需求）获得认可。行情近乎走平、略偏类滞胀（VIX 18->16、周期股与防御股均+0.2%、铜金比+5.4%），因此这是薄盘高贝塔纯概念组别中由个股新闻驱动的均值回归，而非象限驱动的反弹。特朗普上任第一天（2025年1月20日）的能源行政举措（宣布国家能源紧急状态及「释放美国能源」行政令，整体利好能源而非专门针对核电）提供了温和的近期政策买盘。","drivers":["Jevons paradox rebuttal of DeepSeek","Trump Day-1 energy orders (Jan 20)","dip-buying in thin high-beta group","VIX settling (18->16)"],"drivers_zh":["杰文斯悖论反驳DeepSeek","特朗普上任首日能源行政令（1月20日）","薄盘高贝塔组别抄底","VIX回落（18->16）"],"prev_key":"2025-01-27","prev_key_chain":["2025-01-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Snap-back bargain bid as risk steadies","title_zh":"风险企稳下超跌反弹捡漏买盘","turn_id":"nuclear_power:trough:2025-01"},"2025-02-10":{"body":"A -33.8% slide through March 10, 2025 as escalating Trump tariff threats (Canada/Mexico tariffs Feb 1, steel/aluminium tariffs Feb 10) drained the speculative premium from high-multiple nuclear/SMR names. The quad turned slowdown/deflation-scare with VIX rising 16->28, defensives (+1.1%) beating cyclicals (-6.8%), a weaker dollar (DXY -4.1%), and tech selling off (-11.4%); the high-beta nuclear basket led the AI-power complex lower into the March trough. Pre-revenue SMR developers with distant commercialisation timelines were hardest hit as recession fears raised discount rates.","body_zh":"至2025年3月10日下跌33.8%，特朗普关税威胁升级（2月1日对加拿大/墨西哥关税、2月10日钢铝关税）抽走了高估值核电/SMR标的的投机溢价。象限转为放缓/通缩惊魂，VIX由16升至28、防御股（+1.1%）跑赢周期股（-6.8%）、美元走弱（DXY -4.1%），科技大跌（-11.4%）；高弹性核电篮子领跌AI电力板块至3月低谷。商业化时间遥远的尚无营收SMR开发商遭受最大冲击，因衰退担忧推高折现率。","drivers":["Trump tariff shock (Feb 1-10, 2025)","risk-off deflation-scare (VIX 16->28)","tech sell-off (-11.4%)","high-beta multiple compression","recession-fear discount-rate rise"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普关税冲击（2025年2月1-10日）","避险通缩惊魂（VIX 16->28）","科技抛售（-11.4%）","高贝塔估值压缩","衰退担忧推高折现率"],"prev_key":"2025-02-10","prev_key_chain":["2025-02-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Pre-tariff risk-off drains the speculative premium","title_zh":"关税前避险抽走投机溢价","turn_id":"nuclear_power:peak:2025-02"},"2025-03-10":{"body":"A +24.2% bounce through March 24, 2025 on nuclear-friendly policy signals and bargain-hunting ahead of what proved to be the final pre-tariff leg lower. The macro briefly stabilised into a mild goldilocks/growth-up quad (VIX easing 28->17, cyclicals +3.6% vs defensives -0.9%, oil +4.7%, copper-gold +4.9%), with semis leading (+7.5%). Administration signals of faster nuclear permitting and DOE loan support for reactor restarts provided sector-specific uplift, but the unresolved tariff overhang capped the rally.","body_zh":"至2025年3月24日反弹24.2%，受利好核电的政策信号与逢低买盘推动，随后证实为关税前最后一轮下跌前夕。宏观短暂企稳为温和的金发女郎/增长向上象限（VIX由28回落至17、周期股+3.6%对防御股-0.9%、油价+4.7%、铜金比+4.9%），半导体领涨（+7.5%）。政府关于加快核电许可与DOE贷款支持反应堆重启的信号提供了板块特有支撑，但未解决的关税阴影压制了反弹空间。","drivers":["Trump nuclear permitting / DOE loan signals","oversold dip-buying","goldilocks stabilisation (VIX 28->17)","energy/oil +4.7% bid","tariff overhang caps upside"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普核电许可/DOE贷款信号","超跌逢低买入","金发女郎企稳（VIX 28->17）","能源/油价+4.7%买盘","关税阴影限制上行"],"prev_key":"2025-03-10","prev_key_chain":["2025-03-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Choppy relief rally on policy hopes","title_zh":"政策预期带来震荡反弹","turn_id":"nuclear_power:trough:2025-03"},"2025-03-24":{"body":"A -25.8% drop into the April 4, 2025 tariff-crash low as the administration announced sweeping 'Liberation Day' reciprocal tariffs (April 2, 2025, EO 14257) — the largest US tariff escalation in generations — triggering a full risk-off capitulation (VIX exploding 17->45, defensives -4.6% vs cyclicals -12.7%, slowdown/deflation-scare quad). The high-beta nuclear group overshot the broad selloff (SMH -21.6%) alongside the whole AI complex; oil fell -10.3% on global-growth fears, and credit spreads widened (HYG -3.8% vs LQD). The narrative collapsed temporarily — a trade-war recession would defer AI capex and undercut the nuclear power-demand thesis.","body_zh":"至2025年4月4日关税崩盘低点下跌25.8%，政府宣布大范围「解放日」对等关税（2025年4月2日，第14257号行政令）——数十年来最大规模关税升级——引发彻底的避险投降（VIX由17飙至45、防御股-4.6%对周期股-12.7%、放缓/通缩惊魂象限）。高弹性核电组别随整个AI板块超调于大盘抛售（SMH -21.6%）；全球增长担忧令油价跌-10.3%，信用利差走阔（HYG对LQD -3.8%）。叙事暂时崩塌——贸易战引发的衰退将推迟AI资本开支并削弱核电电力需求逻辑。","drivers":["Liberation Day tariffs (Apr 2, 2025, EO 14257)","risk-off capitulation (VIX 17->45)","high-beta overshoot vs broad tape","AI capex deferral fear","credit spread blow-out"],"drivers_zh":["「解放日」关税（2025年4月2日，第14257号行政令）","避险投降（VIX 17->45）","高贝塔超调于大盘","AI资本开支推迟担忧","信用利差爆炸性走阔"],"prev_key":"2025-03-24","prev_key_chain":["2025-03-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Final pre-tariff capitulation flush","title_zh":"关税前最后投降性急挫","turn_id":"nuclear_power:peak:2025-03"},"2025-04-04":{"body":"A +204.6% surge off the April 2025 tariff low through October 15, 2025. The initial spark was Trump's April 9 90-day pause on the broad reciprocal tariffs (which excluded China, escalated separately), followed by the actual US-China de-escalation at the May 12 Geneva truce — together reversing recession fears as AI-power demand reasserted. Hyperscaler capex re-accelerated (Microsoft, Amazon, Google reaffirmed nuclear investment despite DeepSeek noise), Trump's May 23 nuclear executive orders directed faster NRC licensing, and the DOE's $1B loan for Constellation's Crane/TMI restart closed November 18, 2025. The basket amplified a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +89%, growth>value +23, VIX collapsing 45->21) with narrow mega-cap-led breadth (-11.2%) and a weaker dollar (DXY -4.1%), running to a fresh absolute peak by mid-October 2025 on relentless AI-baseload buying.","body_zh":"自2025年4月关税低点至2025年10月15日飙升204.6%。最初的火花是特朗普4月9日对广泛对等关税的90天暂停（不含中国，中国另行升级），随后是5月12日日内瓦停火所实现的真正中美降级——共同扭转衰退担忧，AI电力需求再度确立。超大厂商资本开支重新加速（微软、亚马逊、谷歌不顾DeepSeek噪音重申核电投资），特朗普5月23日核能行政令要求加快NRC许可，DOE对Constellation的Crane/三哩岛重启10亿美元贷款于2025年11月18日完成放款。该篮子放大了金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好暴涨（SMH +89%、成长跑赢价值+23、VIX由45崩至21），广度狭窄、巨头领涨（-11.2%）、美元走弱（DXY -4.1%），在持续的AI基荷买盘推动下于2025年10月中创出绝对新高。","drivers":["Apr 9 broad tariff pause + May 12 US-China Geneva truce","semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +89%)","Trump nuclear executive orders (May 23, 2025)","AI capex re-acceleration by hyperscalers","DOE $1B Crane/TMI loan (closed Nov 18, 2025)"],"drivers_zh":["4月9日广泛关税暂停+5月12日中美日内瓦停火","半导体领涨暴涨（SMH +89%）","特朗普核能行政令（2025年5月23日）","超大厂商AI资本开支重新加速","DOE 10亿美元Crane/三哩岛贷款（2025年11月18日放款）"],"prev_key":"2025-04-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-low moonshot in a semis-led risk-on tape","title_zh":"关税低点暴涨于半导体领涨的风险偏好行情","turn_id":"nuclear_power:trough:2025-04"},"2025-10-15":{"body":"A -39.0% drawdown from the October 2025 blow-off top through March 30, 2026 as the most stretched AI-power trade unwound amid AI-capex digestion fears and a leadership rotation. The macro had quietly shifted to a broadening reflation/growth-up quad dominated by a geopolitically-driven oil surge (+76.6%), energy +45.7%, and materials +11.7% — a completely different leadership set that drained flows from narrow high-multiple AI proxies even as VIX only rose modestly (21->31). Growth lagged value by -15.5%, equal-weight beat cap-weight by +4.9%, and frothy pre-revenue SMR names (NuScale, Oklo) saw severe multiple compression as commercialisation remained years away while cash burn accelerated.","body_zh":"自2025年10月喷发顶部至2026年3月30日回撤39.0%，最被拉伸的AI电力交易在AI资本开支消化担忧与领涨轮动中平仓。行情已悄然转向由地缘政治驱动的油价大涨（+76.6%）、能源+45.7%和材料+11.7%为主的广度扩散再通胀/增长向上象限——完全不同的领涨格局令资金流出狭窄的高估值AI代理，即便VIX仅小幅上行（21->31）。成长跑输价值-15.5%，等权跑赢市值权+4.9%，尚无营收的泡沫化SMR标的（NuScale、Oklo）在商业化仍需数年、现金消耗加速的背景下经历严重估值压缩。","drivers":["broadening rotation to Energy/Materials","oil geopolitical surge (+76.6%)","AI-capex digestion concerns","frothy SMR pre-revenue de-rate","growth vs value rotation (-15.5%)"],"drivers_zh":["向能源/材料的广度轮动","油价地缘政治大涨（+76.6%）","AI资本开支消化担忧","泡沫SMR尚无营收下杀","成长对价值轮动（-15.5%）"],"prev_key":"2025-10-15","prev_key_chain":["2025-10-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Blow-off top unwinds as breadth broadens","title_zh":"喷发顶部在广度扩散中平仓","turn_id":"nuclear_power:peak:2025-10"},"2026-03-30":{"body":"A +29.5% recovery from the late-March 2026 trough through May 6, riding a semis-led risk-on rebound (SMH +51.6%, VIX collapsing 31->17, narrow breadth -7.2%) in a reflation/growth-up quad. Fresh licensing progress — the NRC approved Oklo's Principal Design Criteria topical report for the Aurora powerhouse (May 2026) on an accelerated schedule — plus DOE loan support reinvigorated the SMR-commercialisation narrative. As a high-beta proxy the basket leveraged the broad up-tape; a weaker dollar (DXY -2.5%) added a tailwind for uranium miners. The rally was concentrated in a narrow window of optimism that proved short-lived given the subsequent May-June pullback.","body_zh":"从2026年3月末低点至5月6日反弹29.5%，搭乘半导体领涨的风险偏好反弹（SMH +51.6%、VIX由31崩至17、窄广度-7.2%），处于再通胀/增长向上象限。全新许可进展——NRC以加速进度批准了Oklo用于Aurora动力站的主要设计准则（PDC）专题报告（2026年5月）——加上DOE贷款支持重振了SMR商业化叙事。作为高贝塔代理，该篮子放大了广泛上涨行情；美元走弱（DXY -2.5%）为铀矿开采商提供额外顺风。反弹集中于短暂的乐观窗口，此后5-6月回调证明其难以为继。","drivers":["semis-led risk-on rebound (SMH +51.6%)","NRC approves Oklo Aurora PDC report (May 2026)","VIX compression (31->17)","weaker dollar (-2.5%)","dip-buying on washout valuations"],"drivers_zh":["半导体领涨风险偏好反弹（SMH +51.6%）","NRC批准Oklo Aurora的PDC报告（2026年5月）","VIX压缩（31->17）","美元走弱（-2.5%）","超跌估值逢低买入"],"prev_key":"2026-03-30","prev_key_chain":["2026-03-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Oversold bounce as semis-led risk-on resumes","title_zh":"半导体领涨风险偏好重启下的超跌反弹","turn_id":"nuclear_power:trough:2026-03"},"2026-05-06":{"body":"A -21.8% give-back through June 10, 2026 on a mild stagflation-ish risk-off rotation (VIX 17->22, defensives +0.4% vs cyclicals -1.7%, firmer dollar DXY +2.0%, copper-gold +14.1%, oil -5.3%). The basket fell roughly 3x the broad tape's modest -1.4% — its high-beta character at work as liquidity drained from speculative names while leadership rotated to Health (+4.7%) and away from the AI-power complex. The AI-baseload thesis remains structurally intact (hyperscaler PPAs in place, SMR licensing advancing) but the basket is now in confirmed prime-entry territory after back-to-back corrections of -39% and -22% from the October 2025 peak, with positioning at multi-year lows.","body_zh":"至2026年6月10日回吐21.8%，受温和类滞胀避险轮动影响（VIX 17->22、防御股+0.4%对周期股-1.7%、美元走强DXY +2.0%、铜金比+14.1%、油价-5.3%）。篮子跌幅约为大盘温和跌幅（-1.4%）的三倍——其高贝塔特征显现，投机性标的遭遇流动性抽离，领涨板块从AI电力轮动至医疗（+4.7%）。AI基荷逻辑在结构上依然完好（超大厂商购电协议到位、SMR许可推进中），但从2025年10月高点累计经历-39%和-22%的连续回调后，该篮子已进入确认的优选入场区，仓位处于多年低位。","drivers":["stagflation-ish risk-off (VIX 17->22)","rotation from speculative AI to defensives/Health","firmer dollar (DXY +2.0%)","high-beta liquidity drain","copper-gold +14.1% stagflation signal"],"drivers_zh":["类滞胀避险（VIX 17->22）","从投机AI轮动至防御/医疗","美元走强（DXY +2.0%）","高贝塔流动性抽离","铜金比+14.1%发出滞胀信号"],"prev_key":"2026-05-06","prev_key_chain":["2026-05-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Stagflation-ish pullback into prime entry","title_zh":"类滞胀回落至优选入场区","turn_id":"nuclear_power:peak:2026-05"}},"now":"The basket is in a confirmed Recovery / Prime Entry phase (pos 7.9%, rs_rank 32) after the -39% blow-off unwind from the October 2025 peak and the subsequent -22% stagflation-ish pullback into June 2026. The current macro is a reflation/growth-up quad led by Tech (+24.3%), Energy (+21.5%) and Industrials (+15.8%), with Financials, Discretionary and Comm lagging; VIX is calm (14-18), oil has surged +19.2%, and equal-weight breadth is positive (+2.9%). The nuclear/SMR basket is still below its 200-day MA and trading below SPY's rs_rank (32 vs benchmark), reflecting positioning washout rather than any deterioration in the AI-baseload structural thesis. The dollar's firmness (DXY +3.4%) and the absence of a fresh near-term catalyst keep immediate re-entry on a beta-chasing basis cautious, but the setup rhymes with post-flush troughs where durable demand-side conviction has historically re-priced the group sharply higher.","now_zh":"该篮子处于已确认的修复/优选入场阶段（仓位7.9%，相对强弱排名32），此前经历了2025年10月高点的-39%喷发顶部平仓，以及随后至2026年6月的-22%类滞胀回落。当前宏观为再通胀/增长向上象限，领涨板块为科技（+24.3%）、能源（+21.5%）和工业（+15.8%），金融、可选消费与通信落后；VIX平稳（14-18），油价大涨+19.2%，等权广度为正（+2.9%）。核电/SMR篮子仍处于200日均线下方，相对强弱排名低于基准（32对SPY），反映的是仓位超卖出清，而非AI基荷结构性逻辑受损。美元走强（DXY +3.4%）以及缺乏近期明确催化剂，令纯粹追贝塔的立即再入场需保持谨慎，但当前形态与历史上基本面需求侧信念坚实、超跌后大幅重估前的底部高度相似。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-obesity_glp1":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"The 2014-2015 rally was driven primarily by a broad healthcare sector bull market lifted by ACA insurance expansion, which created millions of new pharmacy and biotech customers and sent XLV +40.7% — the top GICS sector. A key GLP-1-specific catalyst came on December 23, 2014: the FDA approved Novo Nordisk's Saxenda (liraglutide 3 mg), the first once-weekly GLP-1 analogue specifically indicated for obesity, planting the earliest commercial seed for the metabolic super-cycle. The slowdown/deflation-scare macro backdrop (oil -55.4%, DXY +19.8%, TLT +27.4%) crushed cyclicals and energy but boosted defensives and healthcare, making this a structural tailwind for the group even without the obesity narrative fully maturing.","body_zh":"2014-2015年行情主要由ACA医保扩容推动的广义医疗板块牛市驱动，数百万新增医保受众令XLV涨幅+40.7%、位居GICS各板块之首。关键的GLP-1特异催化剂发生于2014年12月23日：FDA批准诺和诺德Saxenda（利拉鲁肽3mg），这是首个专门用于肥胖症的每周一次GLP-1类似物，为代谢超级周期埋下最早的商业化种子。宏观背景为慢增长/通缩恐慌（油价-55.4%、DXY+19.8%、TLT+27.4%），周期股与能源遭重创，防御股与医疗受益，即便减肥叙事尚未完全成熟，宏观结构也构成顺风。","drivers":["ACA insurance expansion created new pharma/biotech customers","Saxenda FDA approval Dec-2014: first GLP-1 obesity indication","Slowdown/deflation macro: healthcare led, oil -55.4%, TLT +27.4%","DXY +19.8% headwind for cyclicals boosted defensive healthcare flows"],"drivers_zh":["ACA医保扩容带来新增药品/生物科技客户","2014年12月Saxenda获FDA批准：首个GLP-1肥胖适应症","慢增长/通缩宏观：医疗领涨，油价-55.4%，TLT+27.4%","DXY+19.8%打压周期股，助力防御性医疗资金流入"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"ACA expansion and Saxenda ignite healthcare bull","title_zh":"ACA扩容与Saxenda点燃医疗牛市","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:trough:2014-01"},"2015-08-17":{"body":"The -25.1% selloff had two catalysts: China devalued the yuan on August 11, 2015 — the sharpest single-day move in 20 years — triggering global risk-off (VIX 13 to 27) that crushed health as the worst cyclical sector; and on September 21, 2015, Hillary Clinton's tweet attacking Shkreli-era drug price gouging collapsed biotech, with XBI falling ~35% from its July 2015 peak. Healthcare was actually the largest laggard (-15.3%) in a flight-to-safety environment where only Utilities and Staples held up. The GLP-1 names, still trading as ordinary large pharma, were swept along by the political drug-pricing overhang and macro panic rather than anything thesis-specific.","body_zh":"本次-25.1%跌幅有两大催化剂：2015年8月11日中国人民银行将人民币汇率中间价单日下调约1.9%——20年来最大单日贬幅，触发全球避险（VIX从13升至27），医疗股作为最大的周期滞后板块大幅受累；2015年9月21日希拉里·克林顿发推怒批Shkreli式药价暴涨，令生物科技崩盘，XBI自2015年7月峰值下跌约35%。在Utilities与Staples仅勉强守住的避险环境中，医疗竟是最大滞后板块（-15.3%）。GLP-1标的当时仍作为普通大型药企交易，被政治药价压制与宏观恐慌拖累，而非任何论点特定事件。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation Aug-11-2015 triggered global risk-off (VIX 13→27)","Hillary Clinton drug-pricing tweet Sep-21-2015 collapsed biotech","Healthcare worst laggard (-15.3%) in flight-to-safety flush","Political drug-pricing overhang dragged ordinary pharma names"],"drivers_zh":["2015年8月11日人民币贬值触发全球避险（VIX 13→27）","2015年9月21日希拉里推文打压药价，生物科技崩盘","医疗为避险冲洗中最大滞后板块（-15.3%）","政治药价压制拖累普通药企标的"],"prev_key":"2015-08-17","prev_key_chain":["2015-08-17"],"status":"exact","title":"Drug pricing scare and China shock crush biotech","title_zh":"药价恐慌与中国冲击重创生物科技","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:peak:2015-08"},"2016-02-09":{"body":"From the February 2016 market trough — the culmination of the global growth scare — a broad reflation rally lifted all boats (+27.5%), with cyclicals and energy leading (oil +43.4%, VIX 27 to 12, RSP beat SPY by +3.5%). The GLP-1 names rallied as healthcare recovered from its drug-pricing-scare capitulation lows; the basket benefited from re-normalizing risk appetite rather than any specific obesity catalyst. Lilly and Novo were still primarily diabetes/insulin franchises at this stage, and the reflation setup (falling dollar, broad participation) simply reversed the macro headwinds of the prior selloff.","body_zh":"自2016年2月市场低点——全球增长恐慌的高潮期过后——广义再通胀反弹全线提振（+27.5%），周期股与能源领跑（油价+43.4%、VIX从27降至12、等权重跑赢市值权重+3.5%）。GLP-1标的随医疗从药价恐慌底部复苏而上涨，篮子受益于风险偏好重新正常化，而非任何特定减肥催化剂。礼来与诺和诺德在此阶段仍以糖尿病/胰岛素特许经营为主，再通胀格局（美元走弱、广泛参与）只是逆转了上一轮跌势的宏观逆风。","drivers":["Reflation rebound from Feb-2016 global growth scare trough","Broad risk-on rotation: oil +43.4%, VIX 27→12, cyclicals led","Healthcare recovered from drug-pricing capitulation lows","No GLP-1-specific catalyst — macro reversal drove the bounce"],"drivers_zh":["从2016年2月全球增长恐慌低点反弹再通胀","广义风险偏好轮动：油价+43.4%、VIX 27→12、周期股领跑","医疗从药价恐慌底部复苏","无GLP-1特定催化剂——宏观逆转驱动反弹"],"prev_key":"2016-02-09","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Reflation rebound lifts all healthcare boats","title_zh":"再通胀反弹提振全线医疗标的","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:trough:2016-02"},"2016-08-01":{"body":"The -22.3% selloff from the August 2016 peak was a sharp defensive-rotation unwind triggered by rising bond yields (TLT -6.1%) into the presidential election. In a reflation/growth-up backdrop where cyclicals held (-0.7%) but defensives fell sharply (-7.9%), healthcare and utilities were the worst performers as rate-sensitive, defensive capital rotated into Energy (+5.2%) and Financials (+2.5%) on expectations of a Trump-reflation outcome. VIX rose from 12 to 22. The GLP-1 names, grouped with defensive pharma and healthcare, were punished by the same sector rotation that slammed utilities and REITs, amplified by residual drug-pricing political risk ahead of November 8 election.","body_zh":"2016年8月峰值后的-22.3%跌幅是一次剧烈的防御股轮出，由大选前债券收益率上升（TLT-6.1%）引发。在周期股守稳（-0.7%）而防御股大跌（-7.9%）的再通胀/增长向上背景下，医疗与公用事业作为最差板块，因利率敏感型防御资金轮出至能源（+5.2%）与金融（+2.5%），以押注特朗普再通胀结果。VIX从12升至22。GLP-1标的与防御性药企和医疗并列，被同等冲击公用事业与REITs的板块轮动惩罚，并因11月8日大选前残余药价政治风险而进一步放大。","drivers":["Rate surge (TLT -6.1%) triggered defensive-sector rotation out","Pre-election reflation trade: cyclicals held vs defensives -7.9%","Healthcare and utilities worst performers in rate-shock pivot","Drug-pricing political risk amplified the selloff into Nov-8 election"],"drivers_zh":["利率飙升（TLT-6.1%）触发防御板块轮出","大选前再通胀交易：周期股守稳对防御股-7.9%","医疗与公用事业为利率冲击旋转中最差板块","药价政治风险在11月8日大选前放大跌幅"],"prev_key":"2016-08-01","prev_key_chain":["2016-08-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate surge and sector rotation out of defensives","title_zh":"利率飙升与防御股资金轮出","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:peak:2016-08"},"2016-11-03":{"body":"The +121.9% surge over nearly two years was the most powerful pre-GLP-1-super-cycle leg, powered by two forces: first, the Trump post-election reflation melt-up (SPY +45.4%, semis +64.4%, growth-value spread +28.1%, VIX 22→12, DXY -3.3%) created a risk-on tailwind favoring growth-heavy pharma over defensive names; second, and critically, the FDA approved Ozempic (semaglutide for diabetes) on December 5, 2017, marking the moment the pipeline that would eventually become Wegovy entered the commercial stage. The 2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act also slashed corporate tax rates, boosting pharma earnings multiples. By late 2018 the market was pricing in semaglutide's obesity potential even before dedicated trials concluded, and the basket had decoupled from ordinary healthcare.","body_zh":"长达近两年的+121.9%涨势是GLP-1超级周期前最强劲的一段，由两股力量驱动：其一，特朗普大选后再通胀融涨（SPY+45.4%、半导体+64.4%、成长-价值利差+28.1%、VIX 22→12、DXY-3.3%）为重成长型药企创造了风险偏好顺风；其二也是关键，2017年12月5日FDA批准Ozempic（司美格鲁肽用于糖尿病），标志着最终演变为Wegovy的管线进入商业阶段。2017年《减税与就业法案》大幅削减企业税率，提振了药企盈利倍数。至2018年末，市场已在专项减肥试验结束前定价了司美格鲁肽的减肥潜力，篮子与普通医疗彻底分化。","drivers":["Post-election reflation melt-up: SPY +45.4%, semis +64.4%, VIX 22→12","Ozempic FDA approval Dec-5-2017: semaglutide pipeline enters commercial stage","2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act boosted pharma earnings multiples","Market priced obesity potential pre-trial: basket decoupled from XLV"],"drivers_zh":["大选后再通胀融涨：SPY+45.4%、半导体+64.4%、VIX 22→12","2017年12月5日Ozempic获FDA批准：司美格鲁肽管线进入商业阶段","2017年《减税与就业法案》提振药企盈利倍数","市场在试验结束前定价减肥潜力：篮子与XLV脱钩"],"prev_key":"2016-11-03","prev_key_chain":["2016-11-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-election reflation and Ozempic launch power mega-rally","title_zh":"大选后再通胀与Ozempic上市驱动超级涨势","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:trough:2016-11"},"2018-09-20":{"body":"The -30.2% drop was a pure macro-driven risk-off flush: the Fed hiked rates four times in 2018 with Chair Powell warning of additional hikes ahead, crashing high-beta growth assets. SPY fell -19.3%, VIX spiked from 12 to 36, tech fell -22.7% and industrials -23.6%, while only utilities (-1.6%) and REITs (-9.0%) held as defensives. Healthcare fell -15.3% in this period despite its defensive label because the GLP-1 names had become high-beta growth stocks, making them more vulnerable than traditional pharma. Oil collapsed -39.9% on global slowdown fears. The basket fell -30.2%, deeper than the broad market, consistent with the high-growth profile that had built up over the prior two-year rally.","body_zh":"本次-30.2%的跌幅是纯粹的宏观驱动避险冲洗：美联储2018年四次加息，鲍威尔主席警告还有更多加息，令高贝塔成长资产崩盘。SPY下跌-19.3%，VIX从12飙升至36，科技-22.7%、工业-23.6%，仅公用事业（-1.6%）与REITs（-9.0%）作为防御标的守住。医疗在此期间跌幅达-15.3%，尽管带有防御标签，因GLP-1标的已演变为高贝塔成长股，比传统药企更脆弱。因全球放缓担忧，油价崩跌-39.9%。篮子跌-30.2%，深于大盘，与此前两年涨势积累的高成长画像一致。","drivers":["Fed 2018 rate-hike cycle: four hikes + Powell forward guidance shock","VIX 12→36 risk-off flush; tech -22.7%, SPY -19.3%","High-beta growth profile made basket more vulnerable than XLV","Oil -39.9% on global slowdown fears confirmed deflation-scare quad"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2018年加息周期：四次加息+鲍威尔前瞻指引冲击","VIX 12→36避险冲洗；科技-22.7%，SPY-19.3%","高贝塔成长画像令篮子比XLV更脆弱","全球放缓担忧令油价-39.9%，确认通缩恐慌象限"],"prev_key":"2018-09-20","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed rate shock triggers Q4-2018 risk-off flush","title_zh":"美联储加息冲击触发2018年四季度避险冲洗","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"The +54.0% rally from the Christmas Eve 2018 low to the February 2020 pre-COVID peak was powered by the Fed's January 2019 pivot to a patient stance (cutting rates three times in H2-2019), which crushed yields (TLT +30.9%) and buoyed long-duration growth assets. Healthcare lagged the broader market (XLH +26.8% vs SPY +36.0%), suggesting the GLP-1 names tracked primarily as pharma rather than high-beta leaders. The pipeline was advancing: Novo Nordisk published landmark SUSTAIN and SCALE obesity data through 2019, and Phase 3 STEP trials for semaglutide 2.4 mg (Wegovy) were initiated in early 2019. Narrow breadth (RSP lagged SPY by -7.4%) and a mega-cap-led tape concentrated flows into tech rather than healthcare.","body_zh":"从2018年圣诞夜低点至2020年2月新冠前峰值，+54.0%的涨势由美联储2019年1月转向耐心立场（2019年下半年三次降息）驱动，压低收益率（TLT+30.9%），提振长久期成长资产。医疗滞后于大盘（医疗+26.8%对SPY+36.0%），表明GLP-1标的仍主要作为普通药企而非高贝塔领头羊交易。管线在持续推进：诺和诺德整个2019年发布SUSTAIN和SCALE里程碑式减肥数据，司美格鲁肽2.4mg（Wegovy）的3期STEP试验于2019年初启动。行情窄幅（RSP落后SPY -7.4%）且以大盘股为主导，资金流向科技而非医疗。","drivers":["Fed Jan-2019 pivot to patient stance; three cuts in H2-2019 crushed yields","TLT +30.9% buoyed long-duration growth pharma assets","Wegovy STEP Phase 3 trials initiated 2019; SUSTAIN obesity data published","Narrow mega-cap tape concentrated flows in tech, healthcare lagged"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月转向耐心立场；2019年下半年三次降息压低收益率","TLT+30.9%提振长久期成长药企资产","Wegovy STEP 3期试验2019年启动；SUSTAIN减肥数据发布","狭窄大盘股行情将资金集中于科技，医疗滞后"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot and obesity pipeline anticipation drive +54%","title_zh":"美联储转向与减肥管线预期驱动+54%","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:trough:2018-12"},"2020-03-04":{"body":"A brief but violent -16.3% selloff in three weeks as COVID-19 forced global lockdowns, triggering the fastest bear-market decline in history. SPY fell -28.3%, VIX spiked from 32 to 62, oil -50.1%, DXY +5.3%, and credit spreads blew out (HYG-LQD -7.2%). Every sector sold indiscriminately; even staples fell -22.6%. The GLP-1 basket's relative outperformance (-16.3% vs SPY -28.3%) reflected a growth tilt that softened the blow versus energy and industrials, but there was no defensive quality here — this was pure panic liquidity. The selloff set up the single largest bull leg in the basket's history.","body_zh":"三周内短暂但剧烈的-16.3%跌幅，因新冠疫情强制全球封锁，引发史上最快熊市下跌。SPY跌-28.3%，VIX从32飙升至62，油价-50.1%，DXY+5.3%，信用利差扩大（HYG-LQD -7.2%）。各板块无差别抛售，连必需消费品也跌-22.6%。GLP-1篮子的相对跑赢（-16.3%对SPY -28.3%）反映了其成长倾向比能源和工业股所受冲击更小，但并无防御属性——这是纯粹的恐慌流动性踩踏。此次跌幅为篮子史上最大牛市腿铺路。","drivers":["COVID-19 global lockdowns triggered fastest historical bear-market","VIX 32→62 panic liquidation; oil -50.1%, SPY -28.3%","Indiscriminate selling across all sectors; no defensive safe haven","Growth tilt (-16.3% vs SPY -28.3%) limited relative damage"],"drivers_zh":["新冠全球封锁触发史上最快熊市","VIX 32→62恐慌踩踏；油价-50.1%，SPY-28.3%","各板块无差别抛售；无防御避风港","成长倾向（-16.3%对SPY -28.3%）限制了相对损失"],"prev_key":"2020-03-04","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-04"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash: indiscriminate pandemic liquidation","title_zh":"新冠崩盘：无差别疫情抛售","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:peak:2020-03"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The +149.8% surge from the March 23, 2020 bottom to September 2021 was driven by the most aggressive monetary and fiscal expansion in U.S. history: the Fed cut rates to zero, launched open-ended QE, and Congress passed over $5 trillion in stimulus. The reflation/growth-up quad pushed semis +160.4%, SPY +107.2%, VIX from 62 to 16, oil +199.6%, DXY -10.0%. The GLP-1 basket massively outperformed SPY as the critical clinical milestone arrived on June 4, 2021: the FDA approved Wegovy (semaglutide injection 2.4 mg) for obesity — the first GLP-1 dedicated specifically to weight management that showed ~15% average body weight reduction. Novo's stock surged and the obesity TAM thesis shifted from speculation to confirmed commercial opportunity. The basket traded as a mega-secular growth name perfectly positioned for the zero-rate melt-up.","body_zh":"从2020年3月23日底部至2021年9月，+149.8%的涨势由美国历史上最激进的货币与财政扩张驱动：美联储降息至零、启动无限量QE，国会通过逾5万亿美元刺激。反通胀/增长向上象限推动半导体+160.4%、SPY+107.2%、VIX从62降至16、油价+199.6%、DXY-10.0%。GLP-1篮子大幅跑赢SPY，关键临床里程碑到来：2021年6月4日FDA批准Wegovy（司美格鲁肽注射液2.4mg）用于肥胖症——首个专门用于体重管理的GLP-1，显示平均体重减少约15%。诺和诺德股价飙升，肥胖症潜在市场论点从推测转化为已证实的商业机遇。篮子作为超级长期成长标的完美卡位零利率融涨。","drivers":["Fed zero rates + open-ended QE + $5T fiscal stimulus fueled reflation melt-up","Wegovy FDA approval Jun-4-2021: first dedicated GLP-1 obesity drug, ~15% weight loss","Semis +160.4%, VIX 62→16, SPY +107.2% — basket rode high-beta tailwind","Obesity TAM confirmed: Novo stock surged, market re-rated the group as secular growth"],"drivers_zh":["美联储零利率+无限量QE+5万亿财政刺激推动再通胀融涨","2021年6月4日Wegovy获FDA批准：首个专属GLP-1减肥药，平均体重减少约15%","半导体+160.4%、VIX 62→16、SPY+107.2%——篮子乘高贝塔顺风","减肥症潜在市场得到证实：诺和诺德股价飙升，市场将该群体重估为长期成长股"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed/fiscal bazooka and Wegovy approval power +150%","title_zh":"美联储/财政火力全开与Wegovy获批驱动+150%","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:trough:2020-03"},"2021-09-02":{"body":"The -36.4% selloff from September 2021 to May 2022 was a stagflationary rate/dollar shock (TLT -20.3%, DXY +12.6%, VIX 16→33) that punished long-duration, high-multiple healthcare names even harder than the broad market (SPY -12.5%). Energy led (+64.6%) while tech and discretionary crashed. Before the obesity narrative fully re-rated the basket, Lilly and Novo were still priced partly as traditional pharma — expensive long-duration assets that get punished in rate shock regimes. The market had not yet grasped the scale of the GLP-1 TAM: Wegovy was just six months old, manufacturing shortages had forced Novo to halt new Saxenda prescriptions, and the basin hadn't distinguished itself from the broad pharma selloff.","body_zh":"从2021年9月至2022年5月，-36.4%的跌幅是一次滞胀性利率/美元冲击（TLT-20.3%、DXY+12.6%、VIX 16→33），长久期、高倍数医疗标的遭受的惩罚甚至重于大盘（SPY-12.5%）。能源领涨（+64.6%），科技与可选消费崩盘。在减肥叙事完全重估篮子之前，礼来与诺和诺德仍部分按传统药企定价——在利率冲击环境下受罚的昂贵长久期资产。市场尚未领悟GLP-1潜在市场的规模：Wegovy上市仅六个月，制造业短缺迫使诺和诺德暂停新Saxenda处方，该篮子尚未在广义药企抛售中脱颖而出。","drivers":["Stagflationary shock: TLT -20.3%, DXY +12.6%, VIX 16→33 punished growth pharma","Basket -36.4% vs SPY -12.5%: still priced as long-duration traditional pharma","Wegovy too new to offset macro drag; manufacturing shortages halted Saxenda Rx","Market had not yet grasped GLP-1 TAM scale — traded as just-pharma"],"drivers_zh":["滞胀冲击：TLT-20.3%、DXY+12.6%、VIX 16→33打压成长型药企","篮子-36.4%对SPY-12.5%：仍按长久期传统药企定价","Wegovy上市太短无法抵消宏观拖累；制造业短缺暂停Saxenda新处方","市场尚未领悟GLP-1潜在市场规模——作为普通药企交易"],"prev_key":"2021-09-02","prev_key_chain":["2021-09-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate and dollar shock hammers long-duration pharma","title_zh":"利率与美元冲击重创长久期药企","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:peak:2021-09"},"2022-05-11":{"body":"The +43.2% leg was the first unambiguous stock-specific re-rating driven by a GLP-1 catalyst firing against the grain of a still-active 2022 bear market. On May 13, 2022, the FDA approved Lilly's tirzepatide (Mounjaro) for type 2 diabetes; simultaneously, the SURMOUNT-1 trial data published in June 2022 showed -19.5% to -20.9% average body weight loss at 72 weeks — far exceeding any prior obesity drug — convincing the market that a second GLP-1 giant was entering the obesity space. The +43.2% rally vastly outran the modest goldilocks/disinflation summer bounce (SPY +9.7%, VIX 33→20), as the basket decisively decoupled from macro on a genuine paradigm shift: the dual GIP/GLP-1 mechanism raised the efficacy bar for the entire category.","body_zh":"+43.2%的行情是首次明确由GLP-1催化剂驱动、逆2022年仍活跃的熊市点燃的个股特异重估。2022年5月13日，FDA批准礼来替尔泊肽（Mounjaro）用于2型糖尿病；同期，2022年6月发布的SURMOUNT-1试验数据显示72周平均体重减少-19.5%至-20.9%——远超任何此前减肥药——令市场相信第二个GLP-1巨头正进入减肥赛道。+43.2%的涨幅远超温和的goldilocks/去通胀夏季反弹（SPY+9.7%、VIX 33→20），篮子凭借真正的范式转变与宏观决定性脱钩：双GIP/GLP-1机制将整个品类的疗效门槛大幅提升。","drivers":["Tirzepatide (Mounjaro) FDA approval May-13-2022 for type 2 diabetes","SURMOUNT-1 data Jun-2022: up to 20.9% weight loss at 72 weeks — paradigm shift","+43.2% vastly outran SPY +9.7%: first clean decoupling from the 2022 bear","Dual GIP/GLP-1 mechanism raised efficacy bar for entire obesity category"],"drivers_zh":["替尔泊肽（Mounjaro）2022年5月13日获FDA批准用于2型糖尿病","SURMOUNT-1数据2022年6月：72周体重减少最高20.9%——范式转变","+43.2%远超SPY+9.7%：首次与2022年熊市清晰脱钩","双GIP/GLP-1机制为整个减肥品类提升疗效门槛"],"prev_key":"2022-05-11","prev_key_chain":["2022-05-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Tirzepatide FDA approval sparks thesis re-rating","title_zh":"替尔泊肽获FDA批准触发论点重估","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:trough:2022-05"},"2022-08-15":{"body":"A brief -18.9% selloff into late September 2022 as Powell's August 26 Jackson Hole speech delivered a hawkish shock, re-establishing that the Fed was far from done hiking (10-year yields surged, TLT -10.0%, DXY +7.1%, VIX 20→32). The broad market fell -14.7%, with tech -18.7% and comm -19.0% leading the decline. The GLP-1 basket fell -18.9%, closely tracking the growth selloff. This was not thesis-specific — the obesity re-rating from the May 2022 Mounjaro approval was intact; the basket was simply swept into the final leg of the 2022 bear market by rate-shock contagion. It set up the bottom on September 26, 2022, which launched the +224% super-cycle.","body_zh":"鲍威尔8月26日杰克逊霍尔讲话发出鹰派冲击，重新确立美联储远未结束加息（10年期收益率飙升，TLT-10.0%、DXY+7.1%、VIX 20→32），导致至2022年9月末-18.9%的短暂跌幅。大盘下跌-14.7%，科技-18.7%、通信-19.0%领跌。GLP-1篮子下跌-18.9%，与成长股跌势紧密跟踪。这与论点无关——2022年5月Mounjaro获批引发的减肥重估仍然完好；篮子只是被利率冲击传导拖入2022年熊市最后一段。这为2022年9月26日的底部铺路，随后启动了+224%的超级周期。","drivers":["Powell Jackson Hole Aug-26-2022 hawkish shock: TLT -10.0%, DXY +7.1%","VIX 20→32 growth selloff; tech -18.7%, broad market -14.7%","No thesis-specific catalyst — swept into final 2022 bear leg by rate contagion","Set up the Sep-26-2022 bottom launching the +224% super-cycle"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击：TLT-10.0%、DXY+7.1%","VIX 20→32成长股抛售；科技-18.7%，大盘-14.7%","无关论点催化剂——被利率传导拖入2022年熊市最后一段","为2022年9月26日底部铺路，启动+224%超级周期"],"prev_key":"2022-08-15","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole rate shock drags growth on last flush","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔利率冲击拖累成长股最后一波冲洗","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:peak:2022-08"},"2022-09-26":{"body":"The +224.1% surge from September 2022 to December 2024 — more than 3x the broad market (SPY +70.9%) — was the defining secular re-rating leg. Three fundamental catalysts compounded: (1) On November 8, 2023, the FDA approved Zepbound (tirzepatide) for obesity, giving Lilly a dedicated weight-management label and triggering another step-change re-rating; (2) On August 8, 2023, Novo published the SELECT cardiovascular trial showing Wegovy reduced major adverse cardiac events by 20% in patients with obesity and heart disease, vastly expanding the addressable population and convincing payers; (3) In March 2024 the FDA expanded Wegovy's label to explicitly include cardiovascular risk reduction. Simultaneously, the goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation melt-up (semis +163.4%, growth-value +45.4%, VIX 32→14, DXY -7.0%) concentrated mega-cap flows into this secular winner, amplifying the fundamental re-rating into one of the decade's great stock runs.","body_zh":"从2022年9月至2024年12月，+224.1%的涨势——大盘的三倍多（SPY+70.9%）——是决定性的长期重估行情。三大基本面催化剂叠加：（1）2023年11月8日，FDA批准Zepbound（替尔泊肽）用于肥胖症，礼来获得专属体重管理标签，触发又一次阶梯式重估；（2）2023年8月8日，诺和诺德发布SELECT心血管试验，显示Wegovy在肥胖症合并心脏病患者中将主要不良心脏事件降低20%，大幅扩大了可及人群并说服了支付方；（3）2024年3月FDA扩展Wegovy标签，明确纳入心血管风险降低适应症。与此同时，goldilocks/增长向上去通胀融涨（半导体+163.4%、成长-价值+45.4%、VIX 32→14、DXY-7.0%）将大盘股资金集中流入这一长期赢家，将基本面重估放大为十年最伟大的股票行情之一。","drivers":["Zepbound (tirzepatide) FDA obesity approval Nov-8-2023: dedicated weight label","SELECT trial Aug-2023: Wegovy cut cardiac events 20%; payers and labels expanded","Goldilocks melt-up: semis +163.4%, growth-value +45.4%, VIX 32→14, DXY -7.0%","Narrow mega-cap tape concentrated flows into secular winner; +224% vs SPY +70.9%"],"drivers_zh":["Zepbound（替尔泊肽）2023年11月8日获FDA肥胖症批准：专属体重标签","2023年8月SELECT试验：Wegovy降低心脏事件20%；支付方和适应症扩展","Goldilocks融涨：半导体+163.4%、成长-价值+45.4%、VIX 32→14、DXY-7.0%","狭窄大盘股行情将资金集中流入长期赢家；+224%对SPY+70.9%"],"prev_key":"2022-09-26","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-26"],"status":"exact","title":"GLP-1 super-cycle: Zepbound, SELECT data, and the melt-up","title_zh":"GLP-1超级周期：Zepbound、SELECT数据与融涨","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:trough:2022-09"},"2024-12-09":{"body":"The super-cycle met its first serious correction: -28.4% from the December 2024 peak to the April 8, 2025 tariff low, deeper than the broad market (SPY -17.4%). Three catalysts triggered the unwind: first, on December 20, 2024, Novo Nordisk's next-gen CagriSema missed its own 25% weight-loss target, delivering only 22.7%, causing NVO shares to crater ~19% and raising doubts about the pipeline; second, the incoming Trump administration's MFN drug-pricing agenda and RFK Jr.'s appointment at HHS introduced policy risk to the pricing model that powered earnings estimates; third, the April 2 tariff shock sent VIX from 14 to 52 and triggered a flight-to-safety flush (defensives -6.3% vs cyclicals -18.0%, high-beta minus low-vol -23.4%). As a richly-valued, heavily-owned high-beta name, the basket de-risked faster and harder than the tape.","body_zh":"超级周期迎来首次严峻调整：从2024年12月峰值至2025年4月8日关税低点，-28.4%，深于大盘（SPY-17.4%）。三大催化剂触发解体：第一，2024年12月20日诺和诺德下一代CagriSema未能达到自身25%减重目标，仅录得22.7%，NVO股价暴跌约19%，引发对管线的质疑；第二，即将上任的特朗普政府MFN药价议程与RFK Jr.出任HHS部长，为驱动盈利预期的定价模式引入政策风险；第三，4月2日关税冲击令VIX从14飙升至52，触发避险冲洗（防御股-6.3%对周期股-18.0%，高贝塔减低波-23.4%）。作为估值高企、持仓集中的高贝塔标的，篮子比大盘去风险更快、更猛。","drivers":["CagriSema missed 25% target Dec-20-2024: NVO -19%, pipeline credibility hit","MFN drug-pricing agenda + RFK Jr. HHS appointment introduced policy risk to earnings model","April-2-2025 tariff shock: VIX 14→52, flight-to-safety flush, high-beta -23.4%","Richly-valued high-beta: de-risked -28.4% vs SPY -17.4%"],"drivers_zh":["CagriSema未达25%目标（2024年12月20日）：NVO-19%，管线公信力受损","MFN药价议程+RFK Jr.出任HHS部长为盈利模式引入政策风险","2025年4月2日关税冲击：VIX 14→52，避险冲洗，高贝塔-23.4%","高估值高贝塔：去风险-28.4%对SPY-17.4%"],"prev_key":"2024-12-09","prev_key_chain":["2024-12-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Policy + CagriSema miss + tariff crash trigger -28%","title_zh":"政策压制+CagriSema试验失利+关税崩盘引发-28%","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:peak:2024-12"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"From the April 8, 2025 tariff-panic trough, the basket surged +76.5% into mid-2026, outrunning a powerful risk-on V-bounce (SPY +48.5%, semis +240.9%, VIX 52→18, high-beta minus low-vol +111.3%). Two fundamental catalysts defined the recovery: in December 2025 the FDA approved Novo Nordisk's oral Wegovy — the first oral GLP-1 for weight management — and in early 2026 Lilly's orforglipron was fast-tracked, with the Street projecting it as the eventual market leader given its no-food/no-timing restriction advantage. Both companies then signed White House MFN-preemptive deals capping starter-dose orals at $149/month, turning a pricing risk into a managed volume-for-margin reset that pre-empted government coercion. The reflation/growth-up quad (oil +16.2%, copper-gold +12.4%) and recovery in high-beta rewarded the group's profile; strong RS held through the 2026 oil shock.","body_zh":"从2025年4月8日关税恐慌低点，篮子涨+76.5%至2026年中，跑赢一场强劲的风险偏好V型反弹（SPY+48.5%、半导体+240.9%、VIX 52→18、高贝塔减低波+111.3%）。两大基本面催化剂定义了这次复苏：2025年12月FDA批准诺和诺德口服Wegovy——首个口服GLP-1体重管理药物——2026年初礼来orforglipron获快速审批，华尔街预测其凭借无饮食/无时间限制优势将成为最终市场领军；两家公司随即与白宫签署抢先应对MFN的定价协议，将口服起始剂量封顶149美元/月，将定价风险转化为受管控的以销量换利润率重置，先发制人化解政府干预。反通胀/增长向上象限（油价+16.2%、铜金+12.4%）与高贝塔复苏奖励了该组的画像；强劲RS穿越2026年油价冲击。","drivers":["Oral Wegovy FDA approval Dec-2025: first oral GLP-1 weight management drug","Orforglipron fast-tracked 2026: Street projects long-run leader for convenience edge","White House $149/month deal: pricing risk converted to managed volume-for-margin reset","Risk-on V-bounce: semis +240.9%, high-beta +111.3%, VIX 52→18 rewarded the profile"],"drivers_zh":["口服Wegovy 2025年12月获FDA批准：首个口服GLP-1体重管理药物","Orforglipron 2026年获快速审批：华尔街预测其为长期领军便利性优势","白宫149美元/月协议：定价风险转化为受管控的以销量换利润率重置","风险偏好V型反弹：半导体+240.9%、高贝塔+111.3%、VIX 52→18奖励该画像"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Oral era and V-bounce power +77% recovery","title_zh":"口服时代与V型反弹驱动+77%复苏","turn_id":"obesity_glp1:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"GLP-1 & Obesity is in an Expansion/Trending phase at position 44.1, holding a BUY signal and trading above its 200-day moving average with RS rank #15 — strong but not yet peak-crowded. The current macro backdrop (reflation/growth-up quad, Tech +24.3%, semis +67.9%, high-beta crushing low-vol by +20.7%) rewards the group's high-beta, high-conviction profile. The live fundamental story is the pivot from injectable duopoly to oral oligopoly: Novo Nordisk's oral Wegovy (FDA-approved December 2025) is in commercial launch, and Lilly's orforglipron (approval expected 2026) carries the Street's projected long-run share edge given its no-food/no-timing restriction convenience. Both giants signed White House MFN-preemptive deals capping starter-dose orals near $149/month — a deliberate margin-for-volume reset that trades near-term pricing compression for a vastly larger addressable population. Equal-weight breadth beating cap-weight by +2.9% suggests broad market participation, which dilutes the flow-concentration premium that super-charged this basket in the narrow-tape 2022-2024 melt-up; the key risk is whether volume ramp offsets the pricing reset before consensus earnings estimates need to come down.","now_zh":"GLP-1与减肥药处于扩张/趋势阶段，仓位44.1，持有买入信号，价格位于200日均线上方，RS排名第15——强势但尚未进入拥挤峰值区。当前宏观背景（反通胀/增长向上象限，科技+24.3%，半导体+67.9%，高贝塔大幅跑赢低波动+20.7%）有利于该篮子的高贝塔、高确信度画像。当前基本面叙事正从注射剂双寡头向口服剂多寡头转型：诺和诺德口服Wegovy（2025年12月获FDA批准）已进入商业化阶段，礼来orforglipron（预计2026年获批）凭借无饮食/无时间限制的便利性优势，获华尔街预期更大的长期市场份额。两大巨头均与白宫签署抢先应对MFN政策的定价协议，将口服起始剂量封顶约149美元/月——以短期利润率压缩换取大幅扩大的可及人群。等权重跑赢市值权重+2.9%意味着市场参与度更广，这削弱了2022-2024年窄幅行情融涨期为该篮子注入超额收益的资金集中溢价；核心风险在于销量增长能否在共识盈利预期下修前抵消定价重置。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-payments_fintech":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"From early 2014 through November 2015, payments rallied +35.7% (nearly 2x SPY +18.8%) in a narrowly-led, defensives-and-quality tape (Health +33%, Tech +30%, falling oil -52.9%, TLT +22.5%, DXY +22.7%). Apple Pay launched in October 2014, PayPal spun off from eBay in July 2015, and Visa/Mastercard compounded double-digit transaction volumes on global ecommerce and cross-border travel, re-rating as secular growth assets. The slow-growth, falling-yield, strong-dollar regime kept cyclicals in the dust (Energy -16%) but was ideal for toll-road payments networks with dollar-denominated cross-border revenues. High-beta fintech disruptors were still small, so V/MA dominated the basket's +35% outperformance.","body_zh":"从2014年初至2015年11月，支付篮子上涨+35.7%（近两倍于SPY +18.8%），处于防御与质量主导的窄幅行情（医疗+33%、科技+30%、油价暴跌-52.9%、TLT +22.5%、DXY+22.7%）。2014年10月苹果支付（Apple Pay）上线，2015年7月PayPal从eBay分拆上市，Visa/Mastercard在全球电商与跨境旅行推动下持续录得两位数交易量增长，被重新定价为长期成长资产。低增长、收益率下行、美元走强的环境使周期股沉寂（能源-16%），却是拥有美元计价跨境收入的过路收费支付网络的理想土壤。高贝塔金融科技颠覆者规模尚小，V/MA主导篮子+35%的超额表现。","drivers":["Apple Pay launch Oct-2014 + PayPal eBay spin-off Jul-2015 re-rated secular story","V/MA cross-border volume compounded; dollar tailwind for USD-denominated revenues","Falling yields (TLT +22.5%) supported long-duration growth multiples","Health/Tech-led narrow tape; cyclicals/Energy crushed; defensives-and-quality regime"],"drivers_zh":["2014年10月Apple Pay上线+2015年7月PayPal分拆重塑长期叙事","V/MA跨境交易量复利；美元走强利好美元计价收入","收益率下行（TLT +22.5%）支撑长久期成长估值","医疗/科技主导窄幅行情；周期股/能源沉寂；防御与质量为王"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Ecommerce & mobile-pay secular re-rating","title_zh":"电商与移动支付的长期重估","turn_id":"payments_fintech:trough:2014-01"},"2015-11-06":{"body":"A -18.4% selloff from November 2015 into February 2016 as the 2015-16 global risk-off crystallized: China's growth scare and yuan devaluation fears triggered an August 2015 global market shock that reverberated into early 2016, oil collapsed -33%, credit spreads blew (HYG-LQD -8.3%), VIX spiked 14 to 26, and defensives led (Utilities +11%, Staples +1.4%) while Financials fell -16.9% and Energy -19.6%. Payments, grouped with Financials and consumer-cyclical, was caught in the broad risk-off rotation despite its volume durability. The dollar also weakened (-2.6%) as safe-haven flows dominated, and TLT rallied +11.2%, signaling a genuine deflation/slowdown scare rather than a sector-specific event.","body_zh":"2015年11月至2016年2月下跌-18.4%，2015-16年全球避险情绪具象化：中国增长担忧与人民币贬值恐慌引发2015年8月全球市场冲击，余震延续至2016年初，油价暴跌-33%、信用利差扩大（HYG-LQD -8.3%）、VIX从14飙升至26，防御股领涨（公用事业+11%、必需消费+1.4%），金融板块跌-16.9%、能源跌-19.6%。支付板块因被归类于金融与消费周期而遭广泛避险轮动拖累，尽管其交易量具有持续性。美元同步走弱（-2.6%），TLT涨+11.2%，印证这是真正的通缩/放缓恐慌而非板块个别事件。","drivers":["China growth scare + oil crash -33% (VIX 14->26, HYG-LQD -8.3%)","Defensives led (Utilities +11%); Financials -16.9% — payments caught in Financials de-risk","TLT +11.2%, dollar weak: genuine deflation-scare, not sector-specific","Selloff reversed February 2016 as oil and China stabilized"],"drivers_zh":["中国增长恐慌+油价暴跌-33%（VIX 14→26、HYG-LQD -8.3%）","防御股领涨（公用事业+11%）；金融-16.9%——支付被金融去风险拖累","TLT +11.2%，美元走弱：真正的通缩恐慌而非板块个别事件","2016年2月随油价和中国稳定而反转"],"prev_key":"2015-11-06","prev_key_chain":["2015-11-06"],"status":"exact","title":"China-oil risk-off flush hits cyclical fintech","title_zh":"中国-油价避险抛售冲击周期性金融科技","turn_id":"payments_fintech:peak:2015-11"},"2016-02-08":{"body":"The basket's defining bull run: +141.3% over 31 months (vs SPY +65.4%), from the February 2016 China/oil trough into the September 2018 peak. The reflation trade ignited post-February-2016 oil stabilization, Trump's November 2016 election unleashed deregulation and tax-reform optimism (TCJA December 2017 cut the corporate tax rate to 21%, directly boosting V/MA/PayPal cash flows), and a weakening dollar (-2.5% DXY) + surging oil (+143%) confirmed the reflationary macro backdrop. Semis led at +131.8%, Financials +79%, Tech +101% — the perfect environment for payment networks compounding ecommerce and cross-border volume. Square IPO'd in November 2015 and was already rallying, PayPal struck a partnership with Visa in July 2016, and Stripe, Adyen, and the digital-payments ecosystem drew massive capital. VIX compressed 26 to 12, credit spreads rallied, and growth beat value by 29.5 points — a near-ideal multi-year duration for fintech.","body_zh":"篮子的定义性牛市：31个月上涨+141.3%（对比SPY +65.4%），自2016年2月中国/油价低点涨至2018年9月高点。再通胀交易在2016年2月油价企稳后点燃，特朗普2016年11月当选释放放松监管与税改预期（2017年12月TCJA将企业税率降至21%，直接提升V/MA/PayPal现金流），美元走弱（DXY -2.5%）+油价暴涨（+143%）印证再通胀宏观背景。半导体领涨+131.8%、金融+79%、科技+101%——支付网络复利于电商与跨境交易量的完美环境。Square于2015年11月IPO并已启动上涨，PayPal于2016年7月与Visa达成合作，Stripe、Adyen与数字支付生态系统吸引大量资本。VIX从26压缩至12，信用利差收窄，成长跑赢价值29.5个点——金融科技近乎理想的多年顺风。","drivers":["Trump deregulation + TCJA Dec-2017 tax cut (21% corp rate) boosted V/MA/PayPal cash flows","Reflation trade: oil +143%, DXY -2.5%, semis +131.8%, Financials +79%","Square IPO + PayPal-Visa partnership (Jul-2016) + Adyen/Stripe ecosystem boom","VIX 26->12, growth>value +29.5, credit spreads rally: ideal multi-year duration"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普放松监管+2017年12月TCJA减税（企业税21%）提升V/MA/PayPal现金流","再通胀交易：油价+143%、DXY -2.5%、半导体+131.8%、金融+79%","Square IPO+PayPal-Visa合作（2016年7月）+Adyen/Stripe生态系统热潮","VIX 26→12、成长跑赢价值+29.5点、信用利差收窄：理想的多年顺风"],"prev_key":"2016-02-08","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Longest fintech bull: reflation + Trump + ecommerce","title_zh":"最长金融科技牛市：再通胀+特朗普+电商","turn_id":"payments_fintech:trough:2016-02"},"2018-09-25":{"body":"A -22.3% major selloff from late September to Christmas Eve 2018, the sharpest quarterly drop since 2008 for the S&P 500. The proximate cause was a confluence of four shocks: (1) the Fed hiked four times in 2018 culminating in a December hike where Powell refused to signal a pause, (2) US-China trade war tariffs escalated through the year, (3) growth estimates were revised sharply down, and (4) the yield curve flattened to near-inversion. VIX spiked 12 to 36, Tech fell -22.7%, Energy -29.1%, and defensives (Utilities +0.2%) barely held. Payments/fintech, in the tech/growth/consumer camp, matched Tech's -22.3% decline — the highest-duration fintech names hit hardest. The basket bottomed Christmas Eve as the market priced full recession, setting up the 2019 recovery.","body_zh":"从2018年9月底至平安夜下跌-22.3%，为2008年以来标普500最大季度跌幅。直接原因是四重冲击叠加：（1）美联储2018年四次加息，12月加息时鲍威尔拒绝暗示暂停；（2）中美贸易战关税全年持续升级；（3）增长预测大幅下调；（4）收益率曲线趋平至近倒挂。VIX从12飙升至36，科技-22.7%、能源-29.1%，防御股（公用事业+0.2%）勉强守住。支付/金融科技属于科技/成长/消费阵营，与科技同步下跌-22.3%——久期最长的金融科技标的受损最重。篮子于平安夜见底，市场充分计价衰退，为2019年复苏奠定基础。","drivers":["Fed's 4th 2018 hike + Powell refused to signal pause — terminal-rate re-pricing","US-China trade war tariffs escalated; growth estimates cut sharply","VIX 12->36, Tech -22.7%; high-duration fintech matched Tech's decline","Yield curve near-inversion; bottomed Christmas Eve as recession fully priced"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2018年第四次加息+鲍威尔拒绝暗示暂停——终端利率重定价","中美贸易战关税升级；增长预测大幅下调","VIX 12→36，科技-22.7%；长久期金融科技与科技同步下跌","收益率曲线近倒挂；平安夜随衰退充分计价而见底"],"prev_key":"2018-09-25","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell rate-shock + trade-war growth scare peak","title_zh":"鲍威尔利率冲击+贸易战增长恐慌见顶","turn_id":"payments_fintech:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"A +66.8% bull run from Christmas Eve 2018 to the February 2020 COVID-eve peak, 1.4x SPY +47.1%, as the Fed executed a full policy reversal: three rate cuts in H2 2019 (July, September, October) after Powell declared the hike cycle on hold in January 2019. The pivot ignited a tech-semis-led melt-up (semis +90.9%, growth>value +24.3%, TLT +23.0%, VIX 36->14, SPY +47.1%). Digital payments volumes accelerated with US ecommerce crossing the $600B threshold in 2019; Visa and Mastercard hit all-time highs on record cross-border volume; PayPal delivered double-digit revenue growth every quarter. A narrow mega-cap tape (RSP lagged SPY -6.9%) favored the large-cap network incumbents over the smaller fintech disruptors, but all boats rose in the reflation/growth-up regime.","body_zh":"从2018年平安夜至2020年2月新冠前夜的高点上涨+66.8%，为同期SPY（+47.1%）的1.4倍，美联储执行完整政策反转：鲍威尔2019年1月宣布暂停加息周期后，下半年三次降息（7月、9月、10月）。转向点燃科技/半导体主导的融涨（半导体+90.9%、成长跑赢价值+24.3%、TLT+23.0%、VIX 36→14、SPY+47.1%）。美国电商2019年突破6000亿美元门槛，数字支付量加速；Visa与Mastercard创历史新高，跨境交易量再创纪录；PayPal每季度均录得两位数收入增长。狭窄的大型股行情（RSP落后SPY -6.9%）利好大型网络龙头而非小型金融科技颠覆者，但在再通胀/增长向上环境中百舸争流。","drivers":["Fed full pivot: Jan-2019 hike-cycle pause + 3 cuts in H2-2019 (Jul/Sep/Oct)","Tech/semis-led melt-up (semis +90.9%, TLT +23.0%, VIX 36->14, SPY +47.1%)","US ecommerce crossed $600B in 2019; V/MA at all-time highs on cross-border volume","Narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -6.9%) favored large-cap network incumbents"],"drivers_zh":["美联储完整转向：2019年1月暂停加息周期+2019年下半年三次降息","科技/半导体主导融涨（半导体+90.9%、TLT+23.0%、VIX 36→14、SPY+47.1%）","美国电商2019年突破6000亿美元；V/MA跨境交易量创历史新高","狭窄大型股行情（RSP -6.9%）利好大型网络龙头"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot + ecommerce boom drove 14-month rally","title_zh":"美联储转向+电商热潮驱动14个月反弹","turn_id":"payments_fintech:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-19":{"body":"A -41.8% five-week collapse from February 19 to March 23, 2020 as COVID-19 shut down the global economy. VIX spiked 14 to 62, the worst since 2008-09. Visa and Mastercard pre-announced revenue warnings as cross-border travel and discretionary spend collapsed: Visa withdrew its FY2020 guidance in March; Mastercard reported April cross-border volumes down sharply. PayPal/Square saw merchant-facing volumes crater as restaurants and retail shuttered. Although the basket fell -41.8% (worse than SPY -33.7%), growth slightly beat value (+6.8%) as investors anticipated a digital-commerce winner-take-most dynamic through the lockdowns. Defensives (Staples -24.2%) were least bad; Financials -42.8% and Energy -56.1% were worst. The trough on March 23 marked the all-time bottom as the Fed announced unlimited QE and Congress passed the CARES Act.","body_zh":"2020年2月19日至3月23日五周暴跌-41.8%，新冠疫情封锁全球经济。VIX从14飙升至62，为2008-09年以来最高。Visa与Mastercard提前预警收入，因跨境旅行与可支配消费崩塌：Visa于3月撤回FY2020业绩指引；Mastercard公布4月跨境交易量大幅下降。PayPal/Square因餐厅与零售关门，面向商家的交易量急剧萎缩。尽管篮子下跌-41.8%（比SPY -33.7%更差），成长略跑赢价值（+6.8%），因投资者预判封锁期间数字商务赢家通吃效应。防御股（必需消费-24.2%）跌幅最小；金融-42.8%、能源-56.1%为最差。3月23日低点标志历史大底，美联储宣布无限量QE，国会通过CARES法案。","drivers":["COVID lockdown evaporated cross-border travel + in-person spend (Visa/MA guidance withdrawn)","VIX 14->62; broad deleveraging — Financials -42.8% and payments caught in the flush","TLT +14.2%: flight-to-Treasuries; credit shock (HYG-LQD -9.6%)","Bottomed March 23 on Fed unlimited QE + CARES Act; fastest bear-market bottom in history"],"drivers_zh":["新冠封锁使跨境旅行+线下消费蒸发（Visa/MA撤回业绩指引）","VIX 14→62；广泛去杠杆——金融-42.8%，支付被卷入抛售","TLT+14.2%：资金逃入美债；信用冲击（HYG-LQD -9.6%）","3月23日随美联储无限量QE+CARES法案见底；历史上最快的熊市底部"],"prev_key":"2020-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash — travel volume evaporated","title_zh":"新冠疫情崩盘——旅行交易量蒸发","turn_id":"payments_fintech:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The basket's biggest-ever bull run: +262.5% in 18 months from the March 2020 trough to the September 2021 peak, 2.5x the already-enormous +103.3% SPY gain. Four forces compounded: (1) three rounds of stimulus checks (CARES $1,200, December 2020 $600, ARP March 2021 $1,400) flowed through digital wallets and boosted PayPal/Square volumes; (2) ecommerce permanently re-based higher — US ecommerce hit ~$870B in 2021, up from ~$600B in 2019; (3) the Fed held rates at zero with QE, compressing discount rates for long-duration fintech names; (4) the reflation broadening (VIX 62->19, dollar -9.2%, oil +214%, semis +162%, credit +15%) was the most risk-on tape of the era. Square's Cash App and Affirm's BNPL went mainstream; Affirm IPO'd January 2021 at $49, hitting ~$170 by November. PayPal peaked near $306 in July 2021.","body_zh":"篮子有史以来最大牛市：18个月自2020年3月低点涨+262.5%至2021年9月高点，是已相当强劲的SPY+103.3%涨幅的2.5倍。四重力量叠加：（1）三轮刺激支票（CARES $1200、2020年12月$600、2021年3月ARP $1400）流经数字钱包，提振PayPal/Square交易量；（2）电商永久性上移——美国电商2021年约达8700亿美元，较2019年约6000亿美元大幅增长；（3）美联储将利率维持在零并推进QE，压低长久期金融科技标的的贴现率；（4）再通胀扩散（VIX 62→19、美元-9.2%、油价+214%、半导体+162%、信用利差+15%）是时代最强的风险偏好行情。Square的Cash App与Affirm的先买后付进入主流；Affirm 2021年1月以49美元IPO，11月涨至约170美元。PayPal 2021年7月峰值约306美元。","drivers":["3 rounds of stimulus checks flowed through digital wallets (PayPal/Square/CashApp volumes soared)","Ecommerce permanently re-based: US ecommerce ~$870B in 2021 vs ~$600B in 2019","Zero rates + QE compressed discount rates for long-duration BNPL/fintech (Affirm IPO Jan-2021 at $49)","Broadest reflation tape on record (VIX 62->19, oil +214%, semis +162%, credit +15%)"],"drivers_zh":["三轮刺激支票流经数字钱包（PayPal/Square/CashApp交易量飙升）","电商永久性上移：美国电商2021年约8700亿美元，较2019年约6000亿大增","零利率+QE压低长久期BNPL/金融科技贴现率（Affirm 2021年1月以49美元IPO）","有史以来最广泛的再通胀行情（VIX 62→19、油价+214%、半导体+162%、信用+15%）"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Pandemic stimulus + digital-pay adoption supercycle","title_zh":"疫情刺激+数字支付采用超级周期","turn_id":"payments_fintech:trough:2020-03"},"2021-09-23":{"body":"Fintech was ground zero for the 2022 Fed-hiking bear. As the most rate-sensitive, longest-duration, highest-beta corner of Financials, the basket fell ~45% while the broad market barely cracked (SPY -5.6%) — an outsized break driven by the rate/dollar shock (10Y surged, TLT -10.5%; DXY +6.4%) that obliterated growth-at-any-price names (PayPal, Block, Affirm) as discount rates rose and the work-from-home spend bubble deflated. Energy +49.5%, Utilities +8.7%, and Staples +2.4% led while Tech -9.5% and Comm -22% lagged. Even the durable networks (V/MA) de-rated as the regime shifted from ZIRP-growth to inflation-fighting. PayPal fell from its ~$306 July-2021 high toward $100 over the leg. The basket's -45% while SPY was only -5.6% is the clearest illustration of fintech's embedded duration risk.","body_zh":"金融科技是2022年美联储加息熊市的震中。作为金融板块中对利率最敏感、久期最长、贝塔最高的角落，篮子下跌约45%，而大盘几乎没破裂（SPY -5.6%）——由利率/美元冲击驱动的超额破裂（10Y飙升、TLT -10.5%、DXY +6.4%），随贴现率上升、居家办公支付泡沫消退，不计价格的成长股（PayPal、Block、Affirm）被摧毁。能源+49.5%、公用事业+8.7%、必需消费+2.4%领涨，科技-9.5%、通信-22%落后。即便耐用的网络巨头（V/MA）也因环境从零利率成长转向抗通胀而估值下修。PayPal在此段从约306美元的2021年7月高点跌向100美元。-45%而SPY仅-5.6%是金融科技内嵌久期风险的最清晰体现。","drivers":["Rate/dollar shock (TLT -10.5%, DXY +6.4%) obliterated highest-duration multiples","Pandemic spend bubble deflated: PayPal/Block/Affirm crushed; PYPL fell from ~$306 toward $100","Energy +49.5% led (oil +40.5%); fintech -45% while SPY only -5.6%","Regime shifted ZIRP-growth to inflation-fight; even V/MA derated"],"drivers_zh":["利率/美元冲击（TLT -10.5%、DXY +6.4%）摧毁最长久期估值","疫情支付泡沫消退：PayPal/Block/Affirm重创；PYPL从约306美元跌向100美元","能源+49.5%领涨（油价+40.5%）；金融科技-45%而SPY仅-5.6%","环境从零利率成长转向抗通胀；即便V/MA也估值下修"],"prev_key":"2021-09-23","prev_key_chain":["2021-09-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Duration purge — rate/dollar shock ground zero","title_zh":"久期出清——利率/美元冲击震中","turn_id":"payments_fintech:peak:2021-09"},"2022-03-14":{"body":"A sharp two-week +27.3% snapback from the March 14, 2022 low as the market priced the first 25bp Fed hike (March 16) as 'known' and a tech/semis-led risk-on rip (SPY +11.0%, semis +18.8%, growth-value +8.7, VIX 32->19) lifted bombed-out long-duration growth. Discretionary led +17%, Tech +15.9%. The high-beta fintech disruptors led the reflex bounce — their -45% six-month decline had priced in a tremendous amount of bad news — but it was a counter-trend move inside the larger 2022 bear, in a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP lagged SPY -2.4%), not a durable turn. The basket retraced roughly one-quarter of its selloff in two weeks before the next leg down.","body_zh":"从2022年3月14日低点起为期两周的急速反弹+27.3%，市场将首次25个基点加息（3月16日）视为已知，科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好急升（SPY+11.0%、半导体+18.8%、成长-价值+8.7、VIX 32→19）提振被打入谷底的长久期成长。非必需消费领涨+17%、科技+15.9%。高贝塔金融科技颠覆者领涨反射性反弹——其-45%的六个月跌幅已计价了大量坏消息——但这是更大2022年熊市中的逆势波动，处于狭窄大型股行情（RSP落后SPY -2.4%），而非持久转折。篮子在两周内收复约四分之一跌幅后随即进入下一波下行。","drivers":["First 25bp hike (Mar-16-2022) priced as 'known' — reflex relief in long-duration growth","Tech/semis-led risk-on (semis +18.8%, growth-value +8.7, VIX 32->19)","High-beta fintech led the oversold bounce; -45% selloff had priced tremendous bad news","Counter-trend bear bounce; RSP lagged SPY -2.4%; reversed within weeks"],"drivers_zh":["首次25bp加息（2022年3月16日）被视为已知——长久期成长反射性喘息","科技/半导体领涨风险偏好（半导体+18.8%、成长-价值+8.7、VIX 32→19）","高贝塔金融科技领涨超卖反弹；-45%跌幅已计价大量坏消息","逆势熊市反弹；RSP落后SPY -2.4%；数周内反转"],"prev_key":"2022-03-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Oversold relief bounce — first Fed hike as known","title_zh":"超卖喘息反弹——首次加息被视为已知","turn_id":"payments_fintech:trough:2022-03"},"2022-03-29":{"body":"The relief bounce reversed hard into May 2022 as the Fed signaled a faster, larger hiking path — culminating in the May 4 announcement of a 50bp hike and the start of quantitative tightening. The 10Y surged again (TLT -9.5%), the dollar ripped (DXY +5.5%), VIX 19->33, and the regime tipped to a slowdown/deflation-scare with high-beta crushed (high-beta minus low-vol -16.7%) and SPY -14.9%. Rate-sensitive fintech was hit worst: every upward revision in the terminal-rate path re-compressed the long-duration multiples. Energy +1.5% and Staples -0.2% led while Tech -18.7%, Comm -19.2%, and Discretionary -24% lagged. The networks held up far better than the speculative high-beta tail (Affirm, Block).","body_zh":"随美联储释放更快、更大的加息路径信号，喘息反弹急转直下至2022年5月——5月4日宣布加息50个基点并启动量化紧缩。10Y再度飙升（TLT -9.5%）、美元大涨（DXY +5.5%）、VIX 19→33，环境转向放缓/通缩恐慌，高贝塔被碾压（高贝塔减低波-16.7%），SPY -14.9%。对利率敏感的金融科技受创最重——终端利率路径的每次上修都再次压缩长久期估值。能源+1.5%、必需消费-0.2%领涨，科技-18.7%、通信-19.2%、非必需消费-24%落后。网络巨头远比投机性高贝塔尾部（Affirm、Block）抗跌。","drivers":["May-4 50bp hike + QT start re-priced terminal rate higher; TLT -9.5%, DXY +5.5%","Slowdown/deflation-scare regime; high-beta crushed (high-beta-low-vol -16.7%)","SPY -14.9%; fintech -32.2% — outsized vs market, pure rate/duration event","Energy/Staples only survivors; networks held better than Affirm/Block speculative tail"],"drivers_zh":["5月4日加息50bp+QT启动使终端利率预期上调；TLT -9.5%、DXY +5.5%","放缓/通缩恐慌环境；高贝塔被碾压（高贝塔-低波-16.7%）","SPY -14.9%；金融科技-32.2%——超额跌幅，纯利率/久期事件","能源/必需消费唯一幸存；网络巨头比Affirm/Block投机尾部抗跌"],"prev_key":"2022-03-29","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Hawkish re-pricing — rate shock + slowdown scare","title_zh":"鹰派重定价——利率冲击+放缓恐慌","turn_id":"payments_fintech:peak:2022-03"},"2022-05-11":{"body":"A brief two-week +23.7% bounce off the May 11, 2022 low — an oversold, short-covering rally in a deeply hated group as the dollar softened (DXY -2.1%), VIX eased 33->26, and oil/commodities stabilized. Energy led (+13.8%) and Real Estate rallied (+7.4%). No fundamental catalyst for fintech specifically; with the broad market only modestly up (SPY +5.7%) and risk appetite still fragile, the high-beta fintech tail caught a reflex bid. The 24% bounce in two weeks for a basket that had fallen -32% is a classic oversold-squeeze dynamic. It fizzled within days as the market resumed its slide toward the mid-June 2022 low.","body_zh":"2022年5月11日低点起为期两周的短暂反弹+23.7%——深度被嫌弃组别中的超卖、空头回补行情，美元走软（DXY -2.1%）、VIX回落33→26、油价/大宗商品企稳。能源领涨（+13.8%）、房地产反弹（+7.4%）。金融科技本身无基本面催化剂；大盘仅温和上涨（SPY +5.7%）、风险偏好仍脆弱之际，高贝塔金融科技尾部抓住反射性买盘。两周内+24%的反弹，发生在已下跌-32%的篮子上，是经典的超卖挤压动态。随后数天内熄火，大盘继续向2022年6月中旬低点下滑。","drivers":["Classic oversold short-squeeze in deeply hated high-beta group after -32% selloff","Dollar softened (DXY -2.1%), VIX eased 33->26; oil/commodity stabilization","No fundamental catalyst; SPY only +5.7% — purely a momentum/positioning reflex","Fizzled within days; market resumed lower toward June 2022 low"],"drivers_zh":["经典超卖空头回补，深度被嫌弃高贝塔组别于-32%抛售后","美元走软（DXY -2.1%）、VIX回落33→26；油价/大宗商品企稳","无基本面催化剂；SPY仅+5.7%——纯粹的动量/仓位反射","数天内熄火；大盘继续向2022年6月低点下行"],"prev_key":"2022-05-11","prev_key_chain":["2022-05-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Short-squeeze bounce in a hated high-beta group","title_zh":"被嫌弃高贝塔组别的空头回补反弹","turn_id":"payments_fintech:trough:2022-05"},"2022-05-27":{"body":"The last leg of the first-half 2022 selloff into the June 16 low, as the May CPI print of 8.6% (hottest since 1981, released June 10) forced the Fed into a 75bp hike on June 15 — the largest single hike since 1994 — and recession pricing peaked. The regime was slowdown/deflation-scare (SPY -11.7%, VIX 26->33, TLT -6.0%, cyclicals -12.5% vs defensives -10.5%). Rate-sensitive fintech bottomed here with the broad market before the summer relief rally. Staples (-7.9%) were the least-bad sector; Financials -13.3% and Materials -14.1% were among the worst.","body_zh":"上半年2022年抛售至6月16日低点的最后一段，5月CPI报8.6%（1981年以来最高，6月10日公布）迫使美联储于6月15日加息75个基点——1994年以来最大单次加息——衰退定价见顶。环境为放缓/通缩恐慌（SPY -11.7%、VIX 26→33、TLT -6.0%、周期股-12.5%对防御股-10.5%）。对利率敏感的金融科技在此随大盘见底，随后迎来夏季喘息反弹。必需消费（-7.9%）为跌幅最小板块；金融-13.3%与材料-14.1%为最差之列。","drivers":["May CPI 8.6% (40-yr high, Jun-10) forced 75bp hike Jun-15 — largest since 1994","Slowdown/deflation-scare flush (SPY -11.7%, VIX 26->33, TLT -6.0%)","Recession pricing peaked; fintech bottomed with broad market Jun-16","Set up the summer 2022 bear-market rally"],"drivers_zh":["5月CPI 8.6%（40年高位，6月10日）迫使美联储6月15日加息75bp——1994年以来最大","放缓/通缩恐慌冲洗（SPY -11.7%、VIX 26→33、TLT -6.0%）","衰退定价见顶；金融科技随大盘6月16日见底","为2022年夏季熊市反弹铺路"],"prev_key":"2022-05-27","prev_key_chain":["2022-05-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Final 2022 bear leg — hot CPI forced 75bp hike","title_zh":"2022年熊市最后下行段——火热CPI迫使加息75bp","turn_id":"payments_fintech:peak:2022-05"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"A strong +34.0% summer rally into mid-August 2022 on a tech/semis-led, goldilocks-leaning risk-on bounce (SPY +17.7%, semis +19.5%, growth-value +8.8, VIX 33->20, oil collapsing -26.4%) and hopes that CPI had peaked and the Fed might pivot by year-end. Long-duration fintech, the most beaten-down high-beta cohort, led the bounce — but it was a classic bear-market rally. Jerome Powell's August 26 Jackson Hole speech shattered pivot hopes, warning that reducing inflation would require a sustained period of below-trend growth, crushing the rally. Discretionary +28.8% and Tech +22.7% led while Energy -0.2% lagged despite high oil.","body_zh":"随科技/半导体领涨、偏goldilocks的风险偏好反弹（SPY+17.7%、半导体+19.5%、成长-价值+8.8、VIX 33→20、油价暴跌-26.4%），加上CPI见顶、美联储或年内转向的预期，出现强劲的+34.0%夏季反弹至2022年8月中旬。跌得最惨的高贝塔长久期金融科技领涨——但这是经典的熊市反弹。鲍威尔8月26日杰克逊霍尔讲话警告降低通胀需要持续低于趋势增长，粉碎转向预期，行情崩溃。非必需消费+28.8%与科技+22.7%领涨，能源-0.2%落后。","drivers":["Tech/semis-led goldilocks pivot-hope rally (semis +19.5%, growth-value +8.8, VIX 33->20)","Oil collapsed -26.4% — inflation-peak narrative; SPY +17.7%","Most beaten-down long-duration fintech led the oversold bounce","Jackson Hole Aug-26: Powell crushed pivot hope — rally reversed"],"drivers_zh":["科技/半导体领涨goldilocks转向预期反弹（半导体+19.5%、成长-价值+8.8、VIX 33→20）","油价暴跌-26.4%——通胀见顶叙事；SPY+17.7%","跌幅最深的长久期金融科技领涨超卖反弹","杰克逊霍尔8月26日：鲍威尔粉碎转向预期——行情反转"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Summer rally on pivot hopes — bear-market bounce","title_zh":"转向预期推动夏季反弹——熊市反弹","turn_id":"payments_fintech:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"The summer rally unwound into November 2022 after Jackson Hole crushed pivot hopes (August 26) and rates pushed to new cycle highs — the leg's TLT -17.8% is the most violent rate jolt of the whole 2022 saga, alongside DXY +3.8% and SPY -12.6%. Energy +16.6% was the only sector that rose on oil strength; Real Estate -20.3%, Comm -23.1%, and Discretionary -23.5% were worst. Rate-sensitive fintech gave back most of the summer bounce as the long-duration discount-rate squeeze re-intensified. The basket made a higher low here vs the June trough as the broad market neared its final October 2022 bottom, confirming the worst of the duration purge was behind.","body_zh":"夏季反弹在杰克逊霍尔粉碎转向预期（8月26日）、利率推升至新周期高点后回吐至2022年11月——本段TLT -17.8%是整个2022年剧本中最猛烈的利率震荡，伴随DXY+3.8%与SPY-12.6%。能源+16.6%是唯一受益油价强劲上涨的板块；房地产-20.3%、通信-23.1%、非必需消费-23.5%最差。对利率敏感的金融科技回吐大部分夏季涨幅，长久期贴现率挤压重新加剧。篮子在此对比6月低点筑出更高低点，恰逢大盘逼近2022年10月最终底部，确认久期出清最坏时刻已过。","drivers":["Jackson Hole Aug-26 crushed pivot hopes; TLT -17.8% — worst rate jolt of 2022","DXY +3.8%, SPY -12.6%; Energy +16.6% only winner (oil strength)","Long-duration fintech discount-rate squeeze re-intensified","Higher low vs June: worst of duration purge confirmed behind"],"drivers_zh":["杰克逊霍尔8月26日粉碎转向预期；TLT -17.8%——2022年最猛利率震荡","DXY +3.8%、SPY -12.6%；能源+16.6%唯一赢家（油价走强）","长久期金融科技贴现率挤压重新加剧","对比6月筑更高低点：久期出清最坏时刻已过"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole give-back — worst rate jolt of 2022","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔回吐——2022年最猛利率震荡","turn_id":"payments_fintech:peak:2022-08"},"2022-11-09":{"body":"A sharp +32.2% recovery into February 2023 as the regime flipped goldilocks: yields finally fell (TLT +15.3%), the dollar broke (DXY -8.0%), semis ripped +32.2% and high-beta led (high-beta minus low-vol +22.2%, VIX 26->19). The October 2022 CPI print (7.7%, released November 10) was the first clear downside surprise in over a year, catalyzing the pivot trade. Comm led +29.5%, Tech +18.5%. Networks led on double-digit volume growth; the bombed-out fintech disruptors got the high-beta oversold bounce. The move stalled by February 2023, just before the SVB regional-bank crisis re-introduced fear into anything Financials-coded.","body_zh":"随环境翻转为goldilocks，出现急速反弹+32.2%至2023年2月：收益率终于回落（TLT+15.3%）、美元破位（DXY -8.0%）、半导体急升+32.2%、高贝塔领涨（高贝塔减低波+22.2%、VIX 26→19）。2022年10月CPI数据（7.7%，11月10日公布）是一年多以来首个明显下行惊喜，催化转向交易。通信领涨+29.5%、科技+18.5%。网络巨头凭两位数交易量增长领涨；被打入谷底的金融科技颠覆者迎来高贝塔超卖反弹。行情在2023年2月停滞，恰在SVB区域银行危机给一切带金融标签的资产重新注入恐惧之前。","drivers":["Nov-10 CPI 7.7% (first clear downside surprise in over a year) catalyzed the pivot trade","Yields fell (TLT +15.3%), dollar broke (DXY -8.0%); goldilocks flip","High-beta led (semis +32.2%, high-beta-low-vol +22.2%, VIX 26->19)","Networks led on volume; disruptors oversold bounce; stalled Feb-2023 ahead of SVB"],"drivers_zh":["11月10日CPI 7.7%（一年多以来首个下行惊喜）催化转向交易","收益率回落（TLT +15.3%）、美元破位（DXY -8.0%）；goldilocks翻转","高贝塔领涨（半导体+32.2%、高贝塔-低波+22.2%、VIX 26→19）","网络凭交易量领涨；颠覆者超卖反弹；2023年2月停滞于SVB前夕"],"prev_key":"2022-11-09","prev_key_chain":["2022-11-09"],"status":"exact","title":"First bounce off lows — rates fall, dollar breaks","title_zh":"自低点的首次反弹——利率回落、美元破位","turn_id":"payments_fintech:trough:2022-11"},"2023-02-02":{"body":"A -22.2% drop into May 2023 as SVB Financial collapsed March 10 and Signature Bank closed March 12, triggering the worst US bank failures since 2008 and a contagion panic across anything Financials-coded. Critically this was idiosyncratic (SPY -1.0%, VIX 19->18 barely moved) — not a market event — but breadth narrowed hard (RSP lagged SPY -6.3%, Financials -11.4%, Real Estate -11.5%). Payments/networks had zero deposit risk, but were caught in the cross-asset Financials de-risking by sector association. Tech +4.8% and Staples +5.4% held (safety rotation within a sector-specific fear), while the basket's -22% was pure sector-tag damage. Bottomed early May 2023 as First Republic resolved.","body_zh":"下跌-22.2%至2023年5月，SVB Financial于3月10日倒闭，Signature Bank于3月12日关闭，引发2008年以来最大美国银行倒闭与蔓延恐慌，冲击一切带金融标签的资产。关键在于这是个体化事件（SPY -1.0%、VIX 19→18几乎没动）——而非市场事件——但广度大幅收窄（RSP落后SPY -6.3%、金融-11.4%、房地产-11.5%）。支付/网络毫无存款风险，却被金融板块关联的跨资产去风险拖累。科技+4.8%与必需消费+5.4%守住（板块特定恐慌内的安全轮动），而篮子-22%是纯粹的板块标签损伤。2023年5月初随第一共和银行问题解决见底。","drivers":["SVB collapse Mar-10 + Signature Bank Mar-12: worst US bank failures since 2008","Idiosyncratic Financials de-risk: basket -22.2% while SPY only -1.0%","Networks/payments had zero deposit risk; caught in guilt-by-association sector flush","Bottomed May with First Republic resolution; breadth narrowed hard (RSP -6.3%)"],"drivers_zh":["SVB崩溃3月10日+Signature Bank 3月12日：2008年以来最大美国银行倒闭","个体化金融去风险：篮子-22.2%而SPY仅-1.0%","网络/支付零存款风险；被板块关联连坐拖累","5月随第一共和银行解决见底；广度大幅收窄（RSP -6.3%）"],"prev_key":"2023-02-02","prev_key_chain":["2023-02-02"],"status":"exact","title":"SVB scare — guilt by Financials sector association","title_zh":"SVB恐慌——金融板块关联的连坐","turn_id":"payments_fintech:peak:2023-02"},"2023-05-02":{"body":"A strong +40.7% rebound into August 2023 as the SVB panic faded and the early generative-AI rally broadened into a tech/semis-led risk-on (SPY +11.5%, semis +30.0%, growth-value +8.8, VIX 18->14). The June 2023 Federal Reserve pause (held at 5.00-5.25%) and resilient labor/consumer data supported spend-volume forecasts. The durable networks led on resilient consumer spend while the fintech disruptors caught the high-beta tailwind — even with the 10Y still rising (TLT -6.4%), the risk-on impulse and falling VIX dominated. A genuine multi-week recovery, not just a bounce, that ran until the August 2023 rate scare.","body_zh":"强劲反弹+40.7%至2023年8月，SVB恐慌消退、早期生成式AI行情扩散为科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好（SPY+11.5%、半导体+30.0%、成长-价值+8.8、VIX 18→14）。2023年6月美联储暂停加息（维持5.00-5.25%）与坚韧的劳动力/消费数据支撑了交易量预测。耐用的网络巨头凭坚韧消费支出领涨，金融科技颠覆者抓住高贝塔顺风——即便10Y仍在上行（TLT -6.4%），风险偏好脉冲与回落的VIX占主导。这是真正的多周复苏，而非仅是反弹，一直持续至2023年8月的利率恐慌。","drivers":["SVB panic faded; genAI broadened into tech/semis-led risk-on (semis +30%, VIX 18->14)","Fed June-2023 pause (5.00-5.25% held); resilient consumer kept spend-volume forecasts intact","Durable networks led; disruptors caught high-beta tailwind","Ran until August 2023 when 10Y spiked toward 5% (TLT -6.4%)"],"drivers_zh":["SVB恐慌消退；生成式AI扩散为科技/半导体领涨风险偏好（半导体+30%、VIX 18→14）","美联储2023年6月暂停加息（维持5.00-5.25%）；坚韧消费者保持交易量预测","耐用网络领涨；颠覆者抓住高贝塔顺风","持续至2023年8月10Y飙向5%（TLT -6.4%）"],"prev_key":"2023-05-02","prev_key_chain":["2023-05-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-SVB genAI rally — resilient consumer underpins","title_zh":"SVB后生成式AI反弹——坚韧消费者为底","turn_id":"payments_fintech:trough:2023-05"},"2023-08-01":{"body":"A -22.9% pullback into late October 2023 as the 10-year yield spiked to a 16-year high near 5.0% on October 19 on a 'higher-for-longer' Fed and Treasury supply fears — a stagflation-ish rate-driven selloff (TLT -13.5%, DXY +4.2%, VIX 14->21, SPY -9.7%) that hit all long-duration assets. Oil +5.1% and DXY +4.2% simultaneously suggested a stagflation regime (macro held up but rates crushed multiples). Rate-sensitive fintech sold off with long-duration assets, but this October 27, 2023 low became the launchpad for the +116.7% bull run that followed, as the market correctly anticipated the Fed's eventual November 2023 pause and December 2023 pivot signal.","body_zh":"回调-22.9%至2023年10月底，10年期收益率于10月19日飙至接近5.0%的16年高位，在美联储更高更久立场与美债供给担忧下——一场偏滞胀的利率驱动抛售（TLT -13.5%、DXY +4.2%、VIX 14→21、SPY -9.7%），冲击所有长久期资产。油价+5.1%与DXY+4.2%同步上涨，暗示滞胀环境（宏观尚可但利率压缩估值）。对利率敏感的金融科技随长久期资产抛售，但2023年10月27日低点成为随后+116.7%牛市的发射台，因市场正确预判了美联储最终的2023年11月暂停与12月转向信号。","drivers":["10Y hit ~5.0% on Oct-19 (16-yr high) on higher-for-longer + Treasury supply fears","Stagflation-ish: TLT -13.5%, DXY +4.2%, oil +5.1%, SPY -9.7%","Rate-sensitive fintech sold with all long-duration assets","Oct-27 low became launchpad for +117% run as Nov-2023 Fed pause & Dec pivot signal loomed"],"drivers_zh":["10Y于10月19日达约5.0%（16年高位），更高更久+美债供给担忧","偏滞胀：TLT -13.5%、DXY +4.2%、油价+5.1%、SPY -9.7%","对利率敏感的金融科技随长久期资产抛售","10月27日低点成为+117%行情发射台，美联储11月暂停与12月转向信号在望"],"prev_key":"2023-08-01","prev_key_chain":["2023-08-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Higher-for-longer dip — 10Y toward 5%","title_zh":"更高更久回调——10年期逼近5%","turn_id":"payments_fintech:peak:2023-08"},"2023-10-27":{"body":"The big leg: from the October 2023 low, payments & fintech more than doubled (+116.7%) into February 2025, 2.3x the broad market (SPY +51.4%), riding a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation melt-up (semis +87.2%, growth-value +23.3%, yields falling TLT +10.2%, VIX 21->15). Falling-rate expectations, a resilient US consumer, and the September 2024 Fed cuts re-rated the long-duration fintech names; the November 2024 election added a deregulation/M&A tailwind to the whole financial complex. In a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP lagged SPY -12.2%), the speculative high-beta tail (Block, Affirm, the BNPL cohort) earned its biggest returns alongside the durable V/MA core. Financials led with +69.3%, Comm +68.4%, Discretionary +52.9% — the most risk-on sector rotation of the cycle.","body_zh":"主升浪：自2023年10月低点起支付与金融科技翻倍有余（+116.7%），一路涨至2025年2月——是大盘的2.3倍（SPY +51.4%），乘goldilocks/增长向上去通胀的融涨（半导体+87.2%、成长-价值+23.3%、收益率回落TLT+10.2%、VIX 21→15）。降息预期、坚韧的美国消费者、加上2024年9月美联储降息，使长久期金融科技股重估；2024年11月大选为整个金融板块叠加放松监管/并购的顺风。在狭窄的大型股行情中（RSP落后SPY -12.2%），投机性高贝塔尾部（Block、Affirm、先买后付群）取得最大涨幅，与耐用的V/MA核心并肩。金融领涨+69.3%、通信+68.4%、非必需消费+52.9%——是本轮周期中最强的风险偏好板块轮动。","drivers":["Goldilocks melt-up: semis +87.2%, growth-value +23.3%, TLT +10.2%, VIX 21->15","Sep-2024 Fed cuts re-rated long-duration fintech; Nov-2024 election deregulation tailwind","Resilient US consumer + record cross-border V/MA volume throughout","Narrow tape (RSP -12.2%); high-beta tail (Block/Affirm/BNPL) led, V/MA core compounded"],"drivers_zh":["Goldilocks融涨：半导体+87.2%、成长-价值+23.3%、TLT+10.2%、VIX 21→15","2024年9月美联储降息使长久期金融科技重估；2024年11月大选放松监管顺风","坚韧的美国消费者+V/MA跨境交易量持续创纪录","狭窄行情（RSP -12.2%）；高贝塔尾部（Block/Affirm/BNPL）领涨、V/MA核心复利"],"prev_key":"2023-10-27","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-27"],"status":"exact","title":"The +117% goldilocks melt-up — peak bull leg","title_zh":"乘goldilocks融涨的+117%牛市——主升浪见顶","turn_id":"payments_fintech:trough:2023-10"},"2025-02-18":{"body":"Payments rolled over with the broad market in the early-2025 risk-off: the January DeepSeek shock dented AI/growth multiples, then the April 8 tariff crash hit the most cyclical, consumer-exposed names hardest. This was a violent flight-to-safety flush (VIX 15->52, high-beta minus low-vol -23.3%, defensives -6.9% vs cyclicals -18.7%, SPY -18.6%) — and as a high-beta consumer-cyclical group, fintech amplified the SPY decline by 1.6x. A squeezed consumer means lower spend volume (the direct fear for payments) and higher recession odds compress fintech multiples. The basket bottomed on April 8, 2025, with the broad market at the tariff announcement trough.","body_zh":"支付随2025年初避险情绪与大盘一同回落：1月DeepSeek冲击削弱AI/成长估值，随后4月8日关税崩盘对最具周期性、消费暴露最高的标的打击最重。这是一次猛烈的避险冲洗（VIX 15→52、高贝塔减低波-23.3%、防御股-6.9%对周期股-18.7%、SPY -18.6%）——作为高贝塔消费周期组别，金融科技将SPY跌幅放大1.6倍。受挤压的消费者意味着更低的支付量（支付板块最直接的担忧），更高的衰退概率压缩金融科技估值。篮子于2025年4月8日随关税公告低点见底。","drivers":["Violent flight-to-safety flush (VIX 15->52, high-beta-low-vol -23.3%, SPY -18.6%)","DeepSeek AI shock Jan-2025 + April-8 tariff crash hit consumer-cyclical fintech hardest","Squeezed-consumer fear → lower spend volume; recession odds compressed multiples","Basket -29.8% = 1.6x amplification of SPY -18.6%"],"drivers_zh":["猛烈避险冲洗（VIX 15→52、高贝塔-低波-23.3%、SPY -18.6%）","2025年1月DeepSeek冲击+4月8日关税崩盘对消费周期金融科技打击最重","消费受挤压→支付量下降；衰退概率压缩估值","篮子-29.8%=SPY -18.6%的1.6倍放大"],"prev_key":"2025-02-18","prev_key_chain":["2025-02-18"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek-to-tariff flush — VIX-15-to-52 rout","title_zh":"DeepSeek至关税的真空区——VIX 15到52冲洗","turn_id":"payments_fintech:peak:2025-02"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"A strong +56.6% V-bounce off the April 8 tariff low as the US-China 90-day tariff truce (announced May 12) and easing recession fear drove a tech/semis-led risk-on (SPY +30.3%, semis +61.3%, growth-value +17.8, VIX 52->15, high-beta minus low-vol +47.4%, dollar weak DXY -5.0%). Capital-markets revival and renewed deal/IPO activity favored the whole financial complex; the networks resumed compounding on consumer spend recovery and the high-beta fintech disruptors caught the outsized upside. In a narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY -6.5%), the leg ran into late August 2025 before the Iran/Hormuz oil shock reset the regime.","body_zh":"随美中90天关税休战（5月12日宣布）与衰退担忧缓解，科技/半导体领涨的风险偏好启动（SPY+30.3%、半导体+61.3%、成长-价值+17.8、VIX 52→15、高贝塔减低波+47.4%、美元走弱DXY -5.0%），自2025年4月8日关税低点出现强劲的+56.6% V型反弹。资本市场复苏、并购/IPO活动重启，利好整个金融板块；网络巨头在消费支出复苏中恢复复利，高贝塔金融科技颠覆者抓住超额上行。在狭窄行情中（RSP落后SPY -6.5%），该行情持续至2025年8月底，随后伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击重置环境。","drivers":["US-China 90-day tariff truce (May-12) + easing recession fear drove the risk-on V","Tech/semis-led high-beta rip: semis +61.3%, high-beta-low-vol +47.4%, VIX 52->15","Dollar weak (DXY -5.0%); capital-markets revival (deals/IPOs) favored financial complex","Narrow tape (RSP -6.5%); basket +56.6% = 1.9x SPY +30.3%; ran into Aug-2025 reset"],"drivers_zh":["美中90天关税休战（5月12日）+衰退担忧缓解驱动风险偏好V型反转","科技/半导体领涨高贝塔急升：半导体+61.3%、高贝塔-低波+47.4%、VIX 52→15","美元走弱（DXY -5.0%）；资本市场复苏（并购/IPO）利好金融板块","狭窄行情（RSP -6.5%）；篮子+56.6%=SPY +30.3%的1.9倍；持续至2025年8月重置"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-truce V-bounce — high-beta led the rip","title_zh":"关税休战V型反弹——高贝塔领涨急升","turn_id":"payments_fintech:trough:2025-04"},"2025-08-29":{"body":"The basket sold off ~29% from its August 2025 peak into March 2026 as the Iran/Hormuz oil shock sent oil +55.7%, CPI reaccelerated to 4.2%, and the Fed shifted back toward a hiking bias. This was a stagflation-ish regime (cyclicals +6.0% vs defensives +6.5%, growth-value reversed -12.6%) within a flat overall tape (SPY -0.9%) — an idiosyncratic Financials drawdown (Financials -10.4%, one of the worst sectors). Higher discount rates compress the long-duration fintech names; an oil-driven consumer squeeze threatens transaction volume — both direct headwinds to the basket's two cash-flow engines. Energy +41.7% and Utilities +10.4% led; Discretionary -8.3% and Financials -10.4% were the worst.","body_zh":"篮子自2025年8月高点下跌约-29%至2026年3月，伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击使油价涨+55.7%、CPI重新加速至4.2%、美联储重回加息倾向。这是偏滞胀的环境（周期股+6.0%对防御股+6.5%、成长-价值反转-12.6%），处于整体平淡的行情中（SPY -0.9%）——个体化的金融回撤（金融-10.4%，最差板块之一）。更高的贴现率压缩长久期金融科技标的；油价驱动的消费挤压威胁交易量——两者都是篮子两大现金流引擎的直接逆风。能源+41.7%与公用事业+10.4%领涨；非必需消费-8.3%与金融-10.4%为最差。","drivers":["Iran/Hormuz oil shock: oil +55.7%, CPI 4.2%, Fed back to hiking bias","Stagflation-ish: flat SPY but Financials -10.4% — idiosyncratic sector drawdown","Higher discount rates compressed long-duration fintech; consumer squeeze hit volume","Growth-value reversed -12.6%; Energy +41.7% the lone winner"],"drivers_zh":["伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击：油价+55.7%、CPI 4.2%、美联储重回加息倾向","偏滞胀：SPY持平但金融-10.4%——个体化板块回撤","更高贴现率压缩长久期金融科技；消费挤压打击交易量","成长-价值反转-12.6%；能源+41.7%唯一赢家"],"prev_key":"2025-08-29","prev_key_chain":["2025-08-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil shock + hawkish Fed — stagflation squeeze","title_zh":"油价冲击+鹰派美联储——滞胀挤压","turn_id":"payments_fintech:peak:2025-08"},"2026-03-27":{"body":"A reflex rally +18.6% off the March 2026 low as the mid-June Hormuz ceasefire removed the worst-case oil/inflation tail risk and the regime flipped goldilocks (oil -10.1%, semis +24.0%, growth-value +6.8, VIX 31->19, TLT +2.1%). Lower oil eases the consumer squeeze and softens the Fed's hawkish bias — both directly positive for spend volume and fintech multiples. The bounce modestly lagged SPY +11.8% despite being in a tech-led narrow tape (RSP lagged -3.6%), which is typical of an early-recovery setup before institutional rotation confirms. The durable V/MA core anchors the low-position basket; the setup reads Prime Entry, not a sell.","body_zh":"随6月中旬霍尔木兹停火消除最坏情形的油价/通胀尾部风险、环境翻转为goldilocks（油价-10.1%、半导体+24.0%、成长-价值+6.8、VIX 31→19、TLT+2.1%），自2026年3月低点出现反射性反弹+18.6%。油价回落缓解消费挤压、软化美联储鹰派倾向——两者都直接利好支付量与金融科技估值。反弹温和落后于SPY+11.8%，尽管处于科技主导的狭窄行情（RSP落后-3.6%），这是机构轮动确认前早期复苏布局的典型表现。耐用的V/MA核心锚定低位篮子；布局读数为黄金入场，而非卖出。","drivers":["Mid-June-2026 Hormuz ceasefire removed worst-case oil/inflation tail risk","Goldilocks flip: oil -10.1%, semis +24.0%, growth-value +6.8, VIX 31->19","Lower oil eased consumer squeeze + softer Fed bias: both direct tailwinds to spend volume","Modest lag vs SPY (+18.6% vs SPY +11.8%); narrow tape (RSP -3.6%); V/MA core anchors setup"],"drivers_zh":["2026年6月中旬霍尔木兹停火消除最坏油价/通胀尾部风险","Goldilocks翻转：油价-10.1%、半导体+24.0%、成长-价值+6.8、VIX 31→19","油价回落缓解消费挤压+美联储倾向软化：两者均直接利好支付量","温和落后于SPY（+18.6%对SPY+11.8%）；狭窄行情（RSP -3.6%）；V/MA核心锚定布局"],"prev_key":"2026-03-27","prev_key_chain":["2026-03-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Hormuz ceasefire bounce — goldilocks regime flip","title_zh":"霍尔木兹停火反弹——goldilocks环境翻转","turn_id":"payments_fintech:trough:2026-03"}},"now":"Payments & Fintech sits in Prime Entry recovery (pos 15.1), below its 200-day moving average, after a ~29% drawdown from the August 2025 peak driven by the Iran/Hormuz oil shock and a Fed shift back toward hiking bias (CPI 4.2%). The current macro regime is reflation/growth-up — Tech leads +24.3%, semis +67.9%, cyclicals beat defensives (11.2% vs 6.9%) — but the basket itself lags badly (Financials -2.7%, Discretionary -5.2%), meaning the broad recovery has not yet rotated into consumer-facing fintech. Growth-minus-value has reversed sharply (-15.2%), the dollar is firm (+3.4% DXY), and Financials remain a laggard, all consistent with a sector that needs explicit rate/consumer relief to re-engage. The mid-June 2026 Hormuz ceasefire and oil reversal provide the first real catalyst for softer Fed language and eased consumer pressure. The durable V/MA toll-road core anchors the setup; the high-beta disruptors (PayPal, Block, Affirm) are still digesting the damage. RS rank 27/34 confirms institutions have not yet rotated in, making this an early-cycle re-entry window rather than a confirmed thrust.","now_zh":"支付与金融科技处于黄金入场修复期（位置15.1），低于200日均线，此前自2025年8月高点回落约29%，由伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击与美联储重回加息倾向（CPI 4.2%）驱动。当前宏观环境为再通胀/增长向上——科技领涨+24.3%、半导体+67.9%、周期股跑赢防御股（11.2%对6.9%）——但篮子本身明显落后（金融-2.7%、非必需消费-5.2%），意味着广泛复苏尚未轮动至面向消费者的金融科技。成长-价值大幅反转（-15.2%）、美元走强（DXY+3.4%）、金融板块持续滞后，均与需要明确利率/消费端利好才能重新参与的板块特征一致。6月中旬霍尔木兹停火与油价回落为美联储措辞软化和消费压力缓解提供了首个真实催化剂。耐用的V/MA过路收费核心稳定这一布局；高贝塔颠覆者（PayPal、Block、Affirm）仍在消化损伤。相对强弱排名27/34确认机构尚未轮动，使其成为早周期重新入场窗口，而非已确认的突破。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"credit.spread_regime.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"credit.spread_regime.v1","arch_state":"fail","arch_fired_on":"2026-07-05","revision_note":null}},"b-power_grid":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"After the 2013 taper-tantrum spike pushed the 10-year Treasury from roughly 1.6% to 3.0%, yields reversed in H1 2014 (TLT +10.4%), relieving pressure on rate-sensitive utilities and transmission/infrastructure names that trade as bond proxies. The macro quad was stagflation-ish: defensives crushed cyclicals (12.5% vs 8.5%), copper-gold fell -12% on a China demand scare, the dollar softened -1%, and oil rose +11.2% on geopolitical supply risk. Power & Grid, with its stable dividend-like cash flows, amplified the utility/defensive bid; the basket's +17.1% matched the Utilities sector's +17.2% almost exactly — a pure yield-proxy rally, not a growth theme.","body_zh":"2013年缩减恐慌将10年期美债收益率从约1.6%推至3.0%后，2014年上半年收益率回落（TLT +10.4%），缓解了对公用事业及输配电/基础设施作为债券替代品的利率压力。宏观象限偏类滞胀：防御股大幅跑赢周期股（12.5%对8.5%），铜金比因中国需求忧虑下跌-12%，美元小幅走软-1%，油价因地缘政治供应风险上涨+11.2%。凭借稳定的类股息现金流，电力与电网放大了公用事业/防御性买盘；篮子涨幅+17.1%与公用事业板块+17.2%几乎完全吻合——这是纯粹的收益率替代品行情，而非成长主线。","drivers":["yield-drop bond-proxy rally (TLT +10.4%)","defensive leadership (defensives 12.5% > cyclicals 8.5%)","stagflation-ish quad","copper-gold -12% China demand scare","dollar softening -1%"],"drivers_zh":["收益率下行债券替代品行情(TLT +10.4%)","防御股领涨(防御12.5%>周期8.5%)","类滞胀象限","铜金比-12%中国需求忧虑","美元走软-1%"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-taper yield drop lifts bond proxies","title_zh":"后缩债收益率下行提振债券替代品","turn_id":"power_grid:trough:2014-01"},"2014-07-02":{"body":"Brent crude collapsed from about $112 (June 2014) toward the high-$20s by January 2016 (oil_ret -71%), driven by the US shale supply surge, OPEC's November 2014 decision to defend market share rather than cut, and a deteriorating Chinese growth outlook. The dollar surged +24.3% (DXY) as the Fed tapered while the ECB/BoJ eased, crushing commodity-linked stocks: Energy -44.6%, Materials -22.7%. Power & Grid was caught in this industrial-cyclical liquidation (-31.2%): its utility-adjacent capex businesses (grid hardware, transformers, T&D services) faced softening commodity-industry end-markets and a flight-to-safety tape (VIX 11→24, defensives +10.2% vs cyclicals -11.1%, TLT +18.0%). This was a macro-driven risk-off flush, not a grid-fundamentals break.","body_zh":"布伦特原油自2014年6月约$112崩落，至2016年1月跌至$30以下（油价-71%），由美国页岩油供应激增、欧佩克2014年11月决定保住市场份额而非减产，以及中国增长前景恶化共同驱动。随着美联储缩减购债而欧洲央行/日本央行宽松，美元飙升+24.3%（DXY），打压大宗商品相关股票：能源-44.6%、材料-22.7%。电力与电网在这轮工业周期股抛售中遭拖累（-31.2%）：其公用事业相邻资本开支业务（电网硬件、变压器、输配电服务）面临大宗商品工业终端市场走弱与避险格局（VIX 11→24、防御股+10.2%对周期股-11.1%、TLT +18.0%）。这是宏观驱动的避险抛售，而非电网基本面破裂。","drivers":["oil crash -71% (Brent ~$112→high-$20s)","OPEC Nov-2014 market-share defense","dollar surge +24.3% DXY","China slowdown/deflation-scare quad","flight-to-safety VIX 11→24"],"drivers_zh":["油价崩跌-71%(布油约$112→$30以下)","欧佩克2014年11月保市场份额","美元飙升+24.3%","中国放缓/通缩惊魂象限","避险VIX 11→24"],"prev_key":"2014-07-02","prev_key_chain":["2014-07-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil crash & strong dollar crush energy/grid names","title_zh":"油价崩溃与强势美元重创能源/电网标的","turn_id":"power_grid:peak:2014-07"},"2016-01-25":{"body":"A 95% two-and-a-half-year mega-rally driven by two successive catalysts: (1) the 2016 commodity reflation as OPEC agreed on November 30, 2016 to cut ~1.8 mb/day (ending the supply glut, oil +123.4%) and China renewed fiscal stimulus, lifting cyclicals broadly; (2) Trump's November 2016 election unleashed infrastructure-spending expectations, and the December 2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act boosted corporate EPS and capex budgets. The quad was full reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +69.5% vs defensives +32.9%, semis +125.8%, VIX 24→15, dollar -4.4% DXY). Power & Grid rode both: industrial capex names (Eaton, Quanta Services) benefited from rising grid investment and corporate spending, while roughly flat-to-falling yields early in the leg added a fading bond-proxy tailwind as growth dominated by 2017-18.","body_zh":"长达两年半的超级行情涨幅95%，由两波催化剂驱动：(1)2016年大宗商品再通胀——欧佩克2016年11月30日协议减产约180万桶/日（终结供应过剩，油价+123.4%），中国重启财政刺激，推动周期股全面上涨；(2)特朗普2016年11月当选引发基建支出预期，2017年12月《减税与就业法案》提振企业盈利与资本开支预算。象限为充分再通胀/增长向上（周期股+69.5%对防御股+32.9%、半导体+125.8%、VIX 24→15、美元-4.4%）。电力与电网两者兼得：工业资本开支名称（伊顿、Quanta Services）受益于电网投资与企业支出回升，而腿部早期收益率大致走平至下行的债券替代品顺风随成长主导而在2017-18年消散。","drivers":["OPEC Nov-2016 cut ~1.8 mb/d, oil +123%","Trump election infra hopes & TCJA tax reform","reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +69.5%)","dollar weaker -4.4% DXY","semis-led risk-on (SMH +125.8%)"],"drivers_zh":["欧佩克2016年11月减产约180万桶油价+123%","特朗普当选基建预期与税改TCJA","再通胀/增长向上象限（周期股+69.5%）","美元走弱-4.4%","半导体领涨风险偏好(SMH +125.8%)"],"prev_key":"2016-01-25","prev_key_chain":["2016-01-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Commodity reflation + Trump tax-cut supercycle","title_zh":"大宗商品再通胀+特朗普减税超级周期","turn_id":"power_grid:trough:2016-01"},"2018-09-06":{"body":"A -17.6% drawdown as peak-hawkish Fed pricing collided with an oil crash and trade-war recession fears in a classic late-cycle risk-off. The Fed raised rates four times in 2018, culminating in a December hike to a 2.25-2.50% target despite deteriorating conditions; VIX spiked 15→36 and oil fell -37.2% from its Q4 peak. The S&P 500 lost -17.8% and nearly every sector fell, but defensives held far better (-8.4%) than cyclicals (-21.3%); Tech -21.4%, Energy -24.8%, Industrials -21.6%. Power & Grid — straddling industrials, energy-capex and utilities — sold off broadly, but Utilities (-4.2%) led the least-bad cohort, giving the group relative defensive support. The December 24, 2018 trough marked capitulation as recession fears peaked.","body_zh":"美联储鹰派定价见顶与油价崩跌及贸易战衰退担忧碰撞，触发经典后周期避险抛售，最大跌幅17.6%。美联储2018年四次加息，12月加至2.25-2.50%目标区间，VIX急飙15→36，油价自Q4高点下跌-37.2%。标普500下跌-17.8%，几乎所有板块皆跌，但防御股跌幅（-8.4%）远小于周期股（-21.3%）；科技-21.4%、能源-24.8%、工业-21.6%。横跨工业、能源资本开支与公用事业的电力与电网广泛下跌，但公用事业（-4.2%）领跑最小跌幅群体，赋予该组别相对防御支撑。2018年12月24日低点是衰退担忧见顶后的投降点。","drivers":["Fed 4x hikes 2018, peak hawkish to 2.25-2.50%","VIX spike 15→36 risk-off","oil crash -37.2%","trade-war recession fear","late-cycle growth scare"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2018年四次加息鹰派见顶至2.25-2.50%","VIX急飙15→36避险","油价崩跌-37.2%","贸易战衰退担忧","后周期增长恐慌"],"prev_key":"2018-09-06","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak Fed tightening & oil crash risk-off flush","title_zh":"美联储紧缩见顶与油价崩跌避险清仓","turn_id":"power_grid:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"A +69.4% rally from the Christmas Eve 2018 trough as Fed Chair Powell executed an abrupt dovish pivot in January 2019 — abandoning the rate-hike path and signaling patience — driving a powerful risk-on recovery. VIX collapsed 36→17 and the market re-rated growth: Tech +74.9%, semis +82.4%, growth beat value by 21.5 points. Crucially, long bonds also rallied (TLT +25.1%) as three Fed cuts arrived in H2 2019, creating a rare goldilocks dual tailwind that simultaneously lifted the rate-sensitive utility-adjacent component. Power & Grid rode the industrial recovery into early 2020; the basket's +69.4% vs SPY's +45.0% reflected its exposure to rebounding grid capex under easy financing, before COVID ended the leg in February 2020.","body_zh":"自2018年平安夜低点上涨69.4%，因美联储主席鲍威尔2019年1月骤然转鸽——放弃加息路径、发出耐心信号——推动强劲风险偏好复苏。VIX崩至36→17，市场重新为成长定价：科技+74.9%、半导体+82.4%、成长跑赢价值21.5个百分点。关键是长债同步上涨（TLT +25.1%），2019年下半年三次降息，形成罕见的金发女郎双重顺风，同时提振了对利率敏感的准公用事业部分。电力与电网乘工业复苏延续至2020年初；篮子+69.4%超越标普500的+45.0%，反映其在宽松融资下受益于电网资本开支回升，直至2020年2月新冠终结该腿。","drivers":["Fed Jan-2019 dovish pivot (3 cuts H2-2019)","VIX collapse 36→17 risk-on recovery","TLT +25.1% rate tailwind","semis-led growth melt-up (SMH +82.4%)","grid capex recovery"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月转鸽（2019下半年3次降息）","VIX崩至36→17风险偏好复苏","TLT +25.1%利率顺风","半导体领涨成长暴涨(SMH +82.4%)","电网资本开支复苏"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot & melt-up lift grid/utility proxies","title_zh":"美联储转鸽与暴涨提振电网/公用事业替代品","turn_id":"power_grid:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-21":{"body":"A -38.9% crash in just 31 days as COVID-19 spread globally through February-March 2020, triggering lockdowns and the fastest bear market in history. VIX exploded 17→62, the dollar surged +3.3% in a flight-to-cash, oil cratered -56.2% on the Saudi-Russia price war that erupted around March 6-8, and credit spreads blew out (HYG-LQD -9.2%). Electricity demand fell sharply in locked-down economies, hitting grid-adjacent utility revenues. Every sector fell, with defensives (-29.1%) offering only marginal protection versus cyclicals (-39.4%); Power & Grid at -38.9% tracked the broad market in a pure panic-liquidation where correlations went to 1. The March 23 Fed emergency QE announcement (unlimited purchases plus ~$2.3T in facilities) marked the trough.","body_zh":"在31天内暴跌38.9%，新冠疫情于2020年2-3月全球蔓延，触发封锁与史上最快熊市。VIX爆飙17→62，美元避险激增+3.3%，油价因3月6-8日前后爆发的沙特-俄罗斯价格战崩跌-56.2%，信用利差急扩（HYG-LQD -9.2%）。封锁经济体电力需求大幅下滑，冲击电网相邻公用事业营收。所有板块皆跌，防御股（-29.1%）对周期股（-39.4%）保护甚微；电力与电网以-38.9%跟随大盘，在相关性趋于1的纯恐慌抛售中无处遁形。3月23日美联储紧急无限量化宽松公告（无限购买+约2.3万亿美元设施）标志低点。","drivers":["COVID-19 global pandemic panic (VIX 17→62)","electricity demand drop under lockdown","oil crash -56.2% (Saudi-Russia price war)","flight-to-cash dollar surge +3.3%","credit blow-out HYG-LQD -9.2%"],"drivers_zh":["新冠全球疫情恐慌(VIX 17→62)","封锁下电力需求下滑","油价崩跌-56.2%（沙特-俄罗斯价格战）","避险现金美元激增+3.3%","信用利差急扩HYG-LQD -9.2%"],"prev_key":"2020-02-21","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-21"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash: VIX 62 panic liquidation","title_zh":"新冠疫情崩盘：VIX飙至62恐慌抛售","turn_id":"power_grid:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"A +183% multi-year mega-rally from the COVID low — the longest, most structural leg — driven by three waves: (1) Fed emergency QE and trillions in fiscal stimulus from March-December 2020 ignited a broad reflation recovery; (2) Biden's IIJA, signed November 15, 2021 (~$65B authorized for transmission/grid), and the August 2022 Inflation Reduction Act (~$2.9B in grid-deployment/transmission funding plus large clean-energy incentives) reframed Power & Grid from cyclical recovery into a structural-policy mandate; (3) hyperscaler AI-datacenter announcements began seeding the load-growth narrative. The quad was full reflation/growth-up: Energy led (+288.2%), cyclicals beat defensives (134.4% vs 76.9%), oil +275.8%, breadth broadened (+22.2% equal-weight beat), VIX normalized 62→24. TLT fell -32.6% as yields surged, yet the basket outran the rate headwind because its earnings thesis (policy-mandated capex, electrification, transformer backlog) was compounding.","body_zh":"自新冠低点的多年期超级行情涨幅+183%——最长、结构最重要的一腿——由三波推动：(1)2020年3-12月美联储紧急量化宽松与数万亿财政刺激点燃广泛再通胀复苏；(2)拜登2021年11月15日签署的IIJA（约650亿美元授权用于输电/电网）及2022年8月《降低通胀法案》（约29亿美元电网部署/输电资金加大额清洁能源激励）将电力与电网从周期复苏重塑为结构性政策使命；(3)超大规模AI数据中心公告开始播下负荷增长叙事。象限为充分再通胀/增长向上：能源领涨（+288.2%）、周期股超防御股（134.4%对76.9%）、油价+275.8%、广度扩散（等权跑赢+22.2%），VIX回归62→24。TLT跌-32.6%（收益率飙升），但政策授权资本开支、电气化与变压器积压的盈利主线使篮子跑赢利率逆风。","drivers":["COVID fiscal stimulus + Fed QE","IIJA Nov-15-2021 ~$65B grid/transmission","IRA Aug-2022 ~$2.9B grid + clean-energy incentives","oil +275.8% full reflation cycle","AI datacenter load-growth thesis emerging"],"drivers_zh":["新冠财政刺激+美联储量化宽松","IIJA 2021年11月15日约650亿美元电网/输电","IRA 2022年8月约29亿美元电网+清洁能源激励","油价+275.8%充分再通胀周期","AI数据中心负荷增长主线萌芽"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Fiscal stimulus + IRA/IIJA grid supercycle re-rate","title_zh":"财政刺激+IRA/IIJA电网超级周期重估","turn_id":"power_grid:trough:2020-03"},"2022-09-12":{"body":"A -15% slide into the October 2022 cycle low as peak-hawkish Fed pricing hit rate-sensitive utilities and capital-goods names — a rate-regime move with the 10Y surging (TLT -8.0%) and a stronger dollar (DXY +4.6%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (defensives -11.2% and cyclicals -11.7% both deep red, VIX 24→32). The Fed delivered back-to-back 75bp hikes in July and September 2022, pushing the funds rate toward 3.25%; the most rate-sensitive GICS sectors led losses: Utilities -19.9%, Real Estate -21.5%. Grid/electrification was not yet a market theme, so this traded as ordinary rate-sensitive defensive-cyclical weakness.","body_zh":"下跌15%至2022年10月周期低点，美联储鹰派定价见顶打击利率敏感的公用事业与资本品标的——这是利率主导行情，10年期收益率飙升（TLT -8.0%）、美元走强（DXY +4.6%），处于放缓/通缩惊魂象限（防御股-11.2%、周期股-11.7%皆深跌，VIX 24→32）。美联储2022年7月与9月连续加息75bp，将联邦基金利率推向3.25%；对利率最敏感的GICS板块领跌：公用事业-19.9%、房地产-21.5%。电网／电气化尚未成为市场主线，故此为普通的利率敏感防御周期股走弱。","drivers":["rate-regime de-rate (TLT -8.0%)","Fed back-to-back 75bp hikes (Jul-Sep 2022)","deflation-scare quad","dollar stronger +4.6%","pre-theme — utilities/real-estate led losses"],"drivers_zh":["利率主导下杀(TLT -8.0%)","美联储连续75bp加息(2022年7-9月)","通缩惊魂象限","美元走强+4.6%","主线未现——公用事业/房地产领跌"],"prev_key":"2022-09-12","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-driven 2022 bear-market low","title_zh":"利率驱动的2022年末熊市低点","turn_id":"power_grid:peak:2022-09"},"2022-10-14":{"body":"A +249% multi-year run as AI-datacenter load surge, electrification and aging-grid replacement turned transmission and transformer suppliers into a structural-growth story through 2023-24. The October 2022 trough coincided with peak-hawkish Fed expectations; once rate expectations pivoted in late 2023 and the first Fed cut landed September 2024, the re-rating accelerated. Company evidence: Eaton expanded US switchgear/electrical capacity to meet data-center demand, and Quanta Services exited 2024 with record backlog of ~$34.5B (RPO ~$16.8B). The basket rode a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +208.7%, growth>value +56.6, VIX collapsing 32→15) and a weaker dollar (DXY -5.2%), with extremely narrow mega-cap-led breadth (equal-weight lagged cap-weight -28.1%) — power-grid capex went from defensive to one of the market's best secular themes.","body_zh":"多年期上涨249%，AI数据中心负荷激增、电气化与老化电网更换使输配电与变压器供应商在2023–24年成为结构性成长故事。2022年10月低点与美联储鹰派预期见顶吻合；一旦利率预期于2023年底转向、2024年9月首次降息落地，重估加速。公司证据：伊顿扩张美国开关设备/电气产能以满足数据中心需求，Quanta Services 2024年底积压订单创纪录达约345亿美元（剩余履约义务约168亿美元）。该篮子搭乘金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好暴涨（半导体SMH +208.7%、成长跑赢价值+56.6、VIX由32崩至15）与美元走弱（DXY -5.2%），市场广度极窄、巨头领涨（等权跑输市值权-28.1%）——电网资本开支从防御性变为市场最佳长期主线之一。","drivers":["semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +209%)","AI datacenter power-demand thesis","grid capex — IRA/IIJA policy tailwind","record order backlogs (Quanta ~$34.5B YE2024)","very narrow breadth (-28.1%)"],"drivers_zh":["半导体领涨暴涨(SMH +209%)","AI数据中心电力需求主线","电网资本开支——IRA/IIJA政策顺风","订单积压创纪录(Quanta 2024年底约345亿)","极窄广度(-28.1%)"],"prev_key":"2022-10-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Grid super-cycle re-rates into a semis-led melt-up","title_zh":"电网超级周期在半导体领涨暴涨中重估","turn_id":"power_grid:trough:2022-10"},"2025-01-24":{"body":"A -29% correction triggered by DeepSeek's late-January efficiency shock — its R1 model (released Jan 20-22) sparked a January 27 selloff that questioned AI power demand (Vistra fell ~28%, GE Vernova ~21%) — and deepened by the April tariff crash. The macro was a violent risk-off: VIX tripled 15→45, semis cratered (SMH -30.9%), defensives (-3.4%) beat cyclicals (-16.3%), and yields fell (TLT +7.6%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Grid names sold off on demand-doubt even though order books reflected multi-year backlogs; breadth broadened (+3.3%) as the mega-cap AI tape unwound.","body_zh":"回调29%，由DeepSeek 1月底效率冲击触发——其R1模型（1月20-22日发布）引发1月27日抛售，质疑AI电力需求（Vistra跌约28%、GE Vernova约21%）——并在4月关税崩盘中加深。宏观是剧烈避险：VIX翻三倍由15升至45、半导体崩跌（SMH -30.9%）、防御股（-3.4%）跑赢周期股（-16.3%）、收益率下行（TLT +7.6%），处于放缓/通缩惊魂象限。尽管订单簿反映多年积压，电网股仍因需求疑虑而下跌；随着巨头领涨的AI行情瓦解，广度扩散（+3.3%）。","drivers":["risk-off flush (VIX 15→45)","DeepSeek R1 shock — AI power-demand doubt","April 2025 tariff crash","semis crater SMH -30.9%","TLT +7.6% rates fell"],"drivers_zh":["避险急挫(VIX 15→45)","DeepSeek R1冲击——AI电力需求疑虑","2025年4月关税崩盘","半导体崩跌SMH -30.9%","TLT +7.6%收益率下行"],"prev_key":"2025-01-24","prev_key_chain":["2025-01-24"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek + tariff risk-off de-rate","title_zh":"DeepSeek＋关税避险压估值","turn_id":"power_grid:peak:2025-01"},"2025-04-04":{"body":"A +115% recovery off the April-2025 tariff low as AI-load forecasts and grid-interconnection backlogs reasserted the structural bid. The basket amplified a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +103.9%, growth>value +30.0, VIX collapsing 45→17) with narrow mega-cap-led breadth (equal-weight lagged -16.0%) and a weaker dollar (DXY -3.7%); utility capex guidance and transformer-supply tightness kept the bid firm through October 2025.","body_zh":"自2025年4月关税低点上涨115%，AI负荷预测与电网并网积压重新确立结构性买盘。该篮子放大了金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好暴涨（半导体SMH +103.9%、成长跑赢价值+30.0、VIX由45崩至17），广度狭窄、巨头领涨（等权跑输-16.0%）、美元走弱（DXY -3.7%）；公用事业资本开支指引与变压器供应紧张使买盘稳固至2025年10月。","drivers":["semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +104%)","AI capex re-acceleration post-tariff truce","narrow breadth (-16.0%)","transformer/switchgear supply tightness","dollar weaker -3.7%"],"drivers_zh":["半导体领涨暴涨(SMH +104%)","关税停火后AI资本开支再加速","窄广度(-16.0%)","变压器/开关设备供应紧缺","美元走弱-3.7%"],"prev_key":"2025-04-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-low recovery in a semis-led risk-on tape","title_zh":"关税低点反弹于半导体领涨的风险偏好行情","turn_id":"power_grid:trough:2025-04"},"2025-10-29":{"body":"A -17% pullback as the broad AI-capex complex digested its run into late 2025 — a mild slowdown/deflation-scare consolidation (VIX flat 17→18, defensives +1.9% vs cyclicals +0.3%, breadth broadening +4.2%) rather than a true risk-off. Health, Financials and Staples led while Tech fell -8.3% and Utilities -5.1%; rates softened modestly (TLT -2.9%). Power & Grid's -17% reflected valuation digestion after the 115% run, not a thesis break — order backlogs and utility capex guidance stayed constructive.","body_zh":"回调17%，整个AI资本开支板块在2025年底消化涨幅——这是温和的放缓/通缩惊魂盘整（VIX走平17→18、防御股+1.9%对周期股+0.3%、广度扩散+4.2%），而非真正避险。医疗、金融与消费必需品领涨，而科技跌-8.3%、公用事业-5.1%；利率小幅软化（TLT -2.9%）。电力与电网-17%反映115%涨幅后的估值消化，而非逻辑破裂——订单积压与公用事业资本开支指引仍具建设性。","drivers":["mild risk-off consolidation (VIX 17→18)","AI-capex valuation digestion post +115% run","breadth broadening rotation (+4.2%)","tech digestion (Tech -8.3%)","rates softened modestly (TLT -2.9%)"],"drivers_zh":["温和避险盘整(VIX 17→18)","AI资本开支+115%后估值消化","广度扩散轮动(+4.2%)","科技消化(科技-8.3%)","利率小幅软化(TLT -2.9%)"],"prev_key":"2025-10-29","prev_key_chain":["2025-10-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Autumn AI-capex digestion dip","title_zh":"秋季AI资本开支消化回调","turn_id":"power_grid:peak:2025-10"},"2025-12-17":{"body":"A +36% recovery into May 2026 in a reflation/growth-up quad (oil ripping +70.0%, cyclicals +13.4% vs defensives +3.7%, SMH +62.6%, VIX calm 18→17) that nonetheless leaves the group screening as bottoming with low positioning after the choppy 2025-26 range. Energy (+29.2%) and Tech (+22.3%) led, the dollar was nearly flat (-0.4% DXY), and breadth was modestly narrow (equal-weight lagged -2.2%). House view: the multi-year grid/transmission-capex backlog is durable; a fresh trending breakout is still unconfirmed as the basket consolidates at the bottom of its cycle position.","body_zh":"至2026年5月回升36%，处于再通胀/增长向上象限（油价大涨+70.0%、周期股+13.4%对防御股+3.7%、半导体SMH +62.6%、VIX平静18→17），但经2025–26年震荡区间后该组别仍显示为筑底、仓位偏低。能源（+29.2%）与科技（+22.3%）领涨，美元近乎走平（DXY -0.4%），广度偏窄（等权跑输-2.2%）。本观点：多年期电网／输配电资本开支积压持久；新的趋势突破仍未确认，篮子在周期底部区域盘整。","drivers":["reflation/growth-up rotation (oil +70%)","AI-capex backlog durability","low-positioning grind recovery","energy-led reflation (Energy +29.2%)","semis recovery SMH +62.6%"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀/增长向上轮动（油价+70%）","AI资本开支积压持久","低仓位缓步回升","能源领涨再通胀(能源+29.2%)","半导体SMH回升+62.6%"],"prev_key":"2025-12-17","prev_key_chain":["2025-12-17"],"status":"exact","title":"Grinds back as reflation rotation builds","title_zh":"再通胀轮动中缓步回升，目前筑底","turn_id":"power_grid:trough:2025-12"}},"now":"Power & Grid Buildout is currently in a bottoming phase (pos=9, rs_rank=21) after a 17% autumn-2025 dip and a +36% grind back into May 2026 that stalled without confirming a new trend breakout. The macro backdrop is a reflation/growth-up quad: oil surged +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%, cyclicals beat defensives (11.2% vs 6.9%), and semis ripped (SMH +67.9%) — all structurally supportive for the group's multi-year grid-capex thesis. However, a firmer dollar (DXY +3.4%) and a low RS rank (21 of universe) signal that this is still a positioning-rebuilding phase rather than a confirmed leadership leg; the equal-weight beat of +2.9% indicates broadening rather than narrow mega-cap leadership, consistent with the group grinding higher alongside industrial cyclicals rather than leading. The multi-year backlog story — transformer supply tightness, AI-datacenter interconnection queues, aging T&D replacement — remains structurally intact, but conviction requires a fresh trending breakout above the Jan-2025 peak.","now_zh":"电力与电网板块目前处于筑底阶段（位置9，相对强弱排名21），历经2025年秋季回调17%与2026年5月前+36%的缓步回升后，尚未确认新的趋势突破。宏观背景为再通胀/增长向上象限：油价大涨+19.2%、铜金比+18.3%、周期股跑赢防御股（11.2%对6.9%），半导体SMH飙升+67.9%——均从结构上支撑该组别的多年期电网资本开支主线。然而，美元偏强（DXY +3.4%）与偏低的相对强弱排名（21）表明当前仍是仓位重建阶段，而非确认领涨腿；等权跑赢+2.9%反映广度扩散而非巨头领涨，与该组别跟随工业周期股回升而非领跑市场一致。多年期积压故事——变压器供应紧缺、AI数据中心并网排队、老化输配电更换——在结构上仍然完整，但需突破2025年1月高点才能确认新趋势。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-quantum_computing":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"Over nearly eight years, the quantum computing basket delivered a ~1,000x (100,662%) return riding the same goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation macro that powered semis +696% and growth over value +180%. The foundational catalysts were Google's 53-qubit Sycamore quantum supremacy claim published in Nature (October 23, 2019), IBM's publicly announced roadmap targeting 1,000+ qubit processors, and the decisive speculative ignition of IonQ's SPAC merger with dMY Technology Group III, which closed September 30, 2021 with NYSE trading beginning October 1, 2021 — making IonQ the first pure-play publicly traded quantum computing company and triggering FOMO flows. Falling Treasury yields (TLT +71.6%) sustained extreme duration multiples for pre-revenue science projects, while a narrow mega-cap-led tape (RSP lagged SPY -35.8%) channeled flows into frontier tech. The basket peaked November 17, 2021, about six weeks after IonQ's NYSE debut, as the SPAC-driven speculative wave exhausted itself just as the Fed signaled taper acceleration.","body_zh":"近八年间，量子计算篮子在与半导体+696%、成长跑赢价值+180%相同的金发姑娘/成长上行-通缩宏观环境中实现约1000倍（100,662%）涨幅。核心催化剂包括：谷歌53量子比特Sycamore于2019年10月23日在《自然》期刊宣布量子霸权；IBM公开发布1000+量子比特路线图；以及决定性的投机引爆——IonQ与dMY Technology Group III的SPAC合并于2021年9月30日完成、10月1日登陆纽交所交易，成为首家上市纯正量子计算公司，引发FOMO资金涌入。美债收益率下行（TLT +71.6%）支撑了零营收科学项目的极端久期估值，而市场广度极度狭窄（RSP跑输SPY -35.8%）将资金集中于前沿科技。篮子于2021年11月17日见顶，约在IonQ纽交所上市六周后，SPAC驱动的投机浪潮恰在美联储释放加速缩减购债信号之际耗尽动能。","drivers":["ZIRP duration premium","Google quantum supremacy 2019","IonQ SPAC IPO Oct 2021","semis-led melt-up","pre-revenue narrative"],"drivers_zh":["零利率久期溢价","谷歌量子霸权2019","IonQ SPAC上市2021年10月","半导体主导飙升","零营收叙事"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Tech melt-up births public quantum investing","title_zh":"科技飙升催生公开市场量子投资","turn_id":"quantum_computing:trough:2014-01"},"2021-11-17":{"body":"The quantum basket fell approximately 61% over 15 months as a severe rate-shock bear market crushed zero-revenue speculative tech. Fed Chair Powell signaled retiring the word 'transitory' for inflation on November 30, 2021 (13 days after the basket peak) and flagged accelerated taper; the Fed then delivered 525 bps of hikes across 2022-2023. Treasury yields surged (TLT -25.2%), the dollar ripped +9.2%, VIX rose from 17 to 26, and defensives led (Energy +42.8%, Utilities +3.7%) while cyclicals fell -7.2% — a flight-to-safety, not sector strength (SPY -15.2%). Rigetti commenced Nasdaq trading in March 2022 and D-Wave listed via SPAC in August 2022 — both into the teeth of the selloff — compounding supply pressure. As the highest-beta, most profitless cohort, quantum names experienced multiple compression far exceeding the benchmark.","body_zh":"量子计算篮子在15个月内下跌约61%，严酷的利率冲击熊市重创零营收投机科技。美联储主席鲍威尔于2021年11月30日（篮子见顶后13天）暗示弃用通胀\"暂时性\"一词并预示加速缩减购债；美联储随后在2022-2023年累计加息525个基点。美债收益率飙升（TLT -25.2%），美元大涨+9.2%，VIX从17升至26，防御板块领涨（能源+42.8%，公用事业+3.7%），周期股下跌-7.2%——是避险而非板块强势（SPY -15.2%）。Rigetti于2022年3月在纳斯达克上市，D-Wave于2022年8月通过SPAC上市——均在下跌途中登陆，进一步加剧供给压力。作为贝塔最高、盈利最差的群体，量子标的遭受的估值压缩远超基准。","drivers":["Fed rate-shock 525bps","yield surge TLT -25.2%","SPAC supply overhang","profitless de-rating","risk-off VIX spike"],"drivers_zh":["美联储加息525个基点","收益率飙升TLT -25.2%","SPAC供给过剩","零盈利估值下杀","避险VIX飙升"],"prev_key":"2021-11-17","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-17"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-shock bear crushes SPAC-era speculative names","title_zh":"利率冲击熊市摧毁SPAC时代投机标的","turn_id":"quantum_computing:peak:2021-11"},"2023-03-15":{"body":"From a washed-out trough, the quantum basket launched a +1,785% explosion driven by two sequential ignition events: first, the ChatGPT/generative AI boom (early 2023) reframed quantum computing as the eventual accelerant for AI, drawing retail and momentum flows back into the highest-beta frontier-tech theme; second, Google's December 9, 2024 announcement of its 105-qubit Willow chip — achieving below-threshold error correction and completing in under five minutes a benchmark that would take ~10^25 years on classical supercomputers — triggered a parabolic melt-up, with leading pure-play names surging multiples of their trough prices. Microsoft's February 19, 2025 Majorana 1 topological-qubit announcement added a second milestone headline (though it later drew scientific scrutiny). The macro backdrop was ideal: goldilocks quad, dollar fell -5.4%, growth crushed value +59.6%, VIX compressed from 26 to 21, though breadth remained extremely narrow (RSP lagged SPY -34.1%), confirming this was a retail/momentum-driven, mega-cap-adjacent speculative melt-up rather than a broad fundamental re-rating. The basket peaked October 14, 2025.","body_zh":"从彻底洗盘的低谷出发，量子计算篮子爆发+1,785%的惊人涨幅，由两轮先后点火的催化事件驱动：其一，2023年初ChatGPT/生成式AI热潮将量子计算重新定位为AI的终极加速器，将散户和动能资金重新引入贝塔最高的前沿科技主题；其二，谷歌于2024年12月9日宣布105量子比特Willow芯片——实现低于阈值的错误纠正，并在五分钟内完成经典超算需约10^25年才能解决的基准任务——引爆抛物线式飙升，领先纯正标的从低谷价格暴涨数倍。微软2025年2月19日Majorana 1拓扑量子比特公告进一步贡献里程碑头条（后遭科学界质疑）。宏观背景极为有利：金发姑娘象限，美元下跌-5.4%，成长大幅跑赢价值+59.6%，VIX从26压缩至21；但市场广度极度狭窄（RSP跑输SPY -34.1%），确认此轮行情为散户/动能驱动、依附大盘股的投机飙升，而非基本面的广泛重估。篮子于2025年10月14日见顶。","drivers":["ChatGPT genAI adjacency","Google Willow Dec 2024","Microsoft Majorana 1 Feb 2025","retail momentum melt-up","goldilocks dollar weakness"],"drivers_zh":["ChatGPT生成式AI邻接","谷歌Willow 2024年12月","微软Majorana 1 2025年2月","散户动能飙升","金发姑娘美元走弱"],"prev_key":"2023-03-15","prev_key_chain":["2023-03-15"],"status":"exact","title":"GenAI boom and Willow moonshot ignite parabolic rally","title_zh":"生成式AI热潮与Willow里程碑引爆抛物线式飙升","turn_id":"quantum_computing:trough:2023-03"}},"now":"Quantum Computing is in a post-peak Expansion/Trending phase (pos 36.7%, rs_rank 8, signal BUY, above 200d MA) within a reflation/growth-up quad: Tech leads at +24.3%, semis (SMH) are up +67.9%, high-beta outperforms low-vol by +20.7%, oil is +19.2% and copper-gold +18.3 — a classic cyclicals-over-defensives risk-on tape (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%). The May 21, 2026 US Department of Commerce announcement of $2.0B in CHIPS Act incentives — letters of intent with $1B to IBM and ~$100M each to nine quantum companies including pure-plays D-Wave, Rigetti, and Infleqtion, in exchange for government equity stakes — re-anchored institutional conviction and triggered 20-30%+ single-day surges in pure-play names. The sector has recovered from its Oct 2025 peak correction, with the government-funding narrative now supplementing the AI-adjacency melt-up logic. Notably, breadth is broadening here (equal-weight RSP beat SPY by +2.9%, broad participation) rather than the narrow mega-cap tape of the prior melt-up legs, while value is leading growth (growth-value -15.2%); the firming dollar (+3.4% DXY) is a mild headwind, but with semis leading and risk appetite elevated, quantum remains the highest-beta expression of the AI-chip-adjacency theme.","now_zh":"量子计算目前处于峰值后扩张/趋势阶段（位置36.7%，相对强度排名第8，信号为买入，站上200日均线），行情处于再通胀/成长上行象限：科技板块领涨+24.3%，半导体（SMH）大涨+67.9%，高贝塔跑赢低波动+20.7%，油价+19.2%、铜金比+18.3——典型的周期股压倒防御股的风险偏好格局（周期股+11.2% 对 防御股+6.9%）。2026年5月21日，美国商务部宣布20亿美元《芯片法案》激励意向书——IBM获10亿美元，含纯正标的D-Wave、Rigetti、Infleqtion在内的九家量子公司各获约1亿美元，以政府入股为交换条件——重新锚定机构信心，纯正量子标的单日暴涨逾20-30%。板块已从2025年10月高点回调中复苏，政府拨款叙事如今与AI邻接飙升逻辑相互补充。值得注意的是，本轮市场广度正在扩张（等权RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%，广泛参与），而非此前飙升腿的狭窄大盘股行情，且价值跑赢成长（成长-价值-15.2%）；美元走强（+3.4% DXY）构成温和阻力，但半导体引领、风险偏好高企，量子计算仍是AI芯片邻接主题中贝塔最高的表达方式。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-regional_banks":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"From January 2014 through June 2015, regional banks gained +22.9% as the post-GFC U.S. expansion matured: unemployment fell from 6.7% to 5.3%, GDP averaged above 2.5%, and the Fed formally telegraphed its first rate hike since 2006 — which arrived December 2015. Higher short rates promised wider net interest margins after six years of zero-rate compression, the core structural driver for regional bank multiples. The macro backdrop was ironically a slowdown/deflation-scare regime (oil -35.1%, DXY +18.1%, TLT +18.1%, defensives +26.5% vs cyclicals +13.3%) driven by the commodities crash and dollar surge, which explains why KRE's gain (+22.9%) tracked SPY (+19.3%) rather than dominating — banks rode rate-hike optimism while the broader cyclical basket was pressured by deflation fears.","body_zh":"2014年1月至2015年6月，区域银行上涨+22.9%，随美国大危机后经济扩张成熟：失业率从6.7%降至5.3%，GDP均速超2.5%，美联储正式预告自2006年以来首次加息（2015年12月兑现）。短期利率上升承诺在六年零利率压缩后拓宽净息差，这是区域银行估值的核心结构性驱动力。宏观背景讽刺地是放缓/通缩恐慌行情（油价-35.1%，DXY+18.1%，TLT+18.1%，防御股+26.5%对周期股+13.3%），由大宗商品崩溃和美元飙升驱动，这解释了为何KRE涨幅（+22.9%）跟随SPY（+19.3%）而非强势领涨——银行靠加息乐观情绪获益，而更广泛的周期股篮子则承压于通缩恐慌。","drivers":["Fed rate-hike anticipation widening NIM outlook","Post-GFC credit quality normalization, loan growth recovery","Oil crash/DXY surge: deflation-scare regime capped cyclical upside","Low-VIX, melt-up environment (TLT+18.1%, semis+39.9%)"],"drivers_zh":["美联储加息预期扩大NIM前景","大危机后信用质量正常化，贷款增长回升","油价崩跌/美元飙升：通缩恐慌行情压制周期股上行空间","低波动融涨环境（TLT+18.1%，半导体+39.9%）"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-GFC recovery on rate-hike anticipation","title_zh":"大危机后复苏乘加息预期","turn_id":"regional_banks:trough:2014-01"},"2015-06-23":{"body":"Regional banks fell -26.2% from June 2015 to February 2016, the worst performance of any major sector (alongside Materials and Energy), in a deep risk-off flush. The cascade of catalysts: China's yuan devaluation on August 11, 2015 (RMB fixing cut a record -1.9% in a single day) triggered global deflation fears; crude oil collapsed another -57% to below $30; the Greek debt drama resolved but left credit markets skittish; and the Fed's December 2015 first rate hike created tightening concern rather than NIM relief. The regime was unambiguously risk-off (VIX 12 to 28, TLT +17.3%, cyclicals -17.4% vs defensives -0.9%, HYG-LQD -13.8%), and Financials (-21%) tracked the cyclical wreckage alongside energy and materials. For regional banks specifically, oil-patch loan books and commodity-linked credit exposure amplified the selloff beyond the index.","body_zh":"2015年6月至2016年2月，区域银行下跌-26.2%，在深度避险冲洗中是表现最差的主要板块之一（与材料和能源并列）。催化剂叠加：2015年8月11日人民币中间价单日创纪录下调1.9%引发全球通缩恐慌；原油再跌-57%至30美元以下；希腊债务问题虽解决但信用市场仍草木皆兵；美联储2015年12月首次加息引发紧缩担忧而非NIM利好。行情明确为避险（VIX 12至28，TLT+17.3%，周期股-17.4%对防御股-0.9%，HYG-LQD-13.8%），金融板块（-21%）随能源和材料一道在周期股残局中沉沦。对区域银行而言，油田贷款账簿和大宗商品关联信用敞口进一步放大了抛售。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation Aug-2015 triggered global deflation panic","Oil -57% below $30 stressed energy-sector loan books","Risk-off flush: VIX 12 to 28, HYG-LQD -13.8%, cyclicals -17.4%","Fed Dec-2015 hike seen as tightening threat, not NIM relief"],"drivers_zh":["2015年8月人民币贬值触发全球通缩恐慌","油价-57%跌破30美元，能源贷款账簿承压","避险冲洗：VIX 12至28，HYG-LQD-13.8%，周期股-17.4%","美联储2015年12月加息被视为紧缩威胁而非NIM利好"],"prev_key":"2015-06-23","prev_key_chain":["2015-06-23"],"status":"exact","title":"China devaluation, oil crash, credit panic selloff","title_zh":"人民币贬值、油价崩盘、信用恐慌引发抛售","turn_id":"regional_banks:peak:2015-06"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"The +115.2% bull run from February 2016 to March 2018 is the dominant cycle leg and a textbook regional bank setup: reflation/growth-up regime (cyclicals +67.9% vs defensives +24.1%, oil +136.7%, copper-gold +49.5%, high-beta minus low-vol +64.6%), steeply rising yields (TLT -7.2%), and a pro-bank political agenda. The February 2016 trough coincided with Shanghai G20 commodity-floor agreements and a global reflation turn. Then Trump's November 2016 election victory sent the 10Y yield from 1.7% to 2.6% in weeks, directly widening NIM prospects. In 2017 the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act boosted bank earnings; in May 2018 the Economic Growth, Regulatory Relief and Consumer Protection Act (signed May 24, 2018) rolled back Dodd-Frank for banks under $250B, lifting the compliance burden on the exact names in KRE. Financials led all sectors (+92.6%) and regional banks outpaced even that benchmark, banking the full reflation-plus-deregulation premium.","body_zh":"2016年2月至2018年3月+115.2%的牛市行情是主导周期腿，也是教科书式的区域银行设置：再通胀/增长向上行情（周期股+67.9%对防御股+24.1%，油价+136.7%，铜金比+49.5%，高贝塔减低波+64.6%），收益率急升（TLT-7.2%），加上亲银行政治议程。2016年2月低点与上海G20大宗商品托底协议及全球再通胀拐点同步。随后特朗普2016年11月大选胜利在数周内将10年期收益率从1.7%推至2.6%，直接拓宽NIM前景。2017年《减税与就业法案》提振银行盈利；2018年5月《经济增长、监管松绑与消费者保护法》（2018年5月24日签署）为2500亿美元以下银行松绑多德-弗兰克，正是KRE成分股的核心利好。金融板块领涨所有板块（+92.6%），区域银行甚至超越这一基准，尽享再通胀加放松监管的双重溢价。","drivers":["Trump Nov-2016 election: 10Y yield 1.7% to 2.6%, NIM windfall","May 2018 Dodd-Frank rollback for banks under $250B (EGRRCPA)","Tax Cuts and Jobs Act 2017 direct EPS boost for banks","Reflation melt-up: oil +136.7%, high-beta+64.6%, cyclicals led"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普2016年11月大选：10年期收益率1.7%至2.6%，NIM暴增","2018年5月多德-弗兰克松绑（EGRRCPA）惠及2500亿美元以下银行","2017年《减税与就业法案》直接提升银行每股收益","再通胀融涨：油价+136.7%，高贝塔+64.6%，周期股领涨"],"prev_key":"2016-02-11","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump reflation mega-rally: steepening curve, deregulation","title_zh":"特朗普再通胀超级行情：曲线趋陡与放松监管","turn_id":"regional_banks:trough:2016-02"},"2018-03-09":{"body":"Regional banks fell -28.6% from March to December 2018 as the reflation trade unwound into a Fed over-tightening scare. The Fed hiked four times in 2018 (to 2.50% by December) and Chair Powell's October 2018 'long way from neutral' comments and December framing of quantitative tightening as 'on autopilot' triggered a market panic (VIX 15 to 36, SPY -14.4%). Trade-war tariffs imposed in mid-2018 added a growth-slowdown overhang, oil collapsed -31.4%, and the dollar surged +7.2%. Financials were the third-worst sector (-23.5%), as inverted short-end yield expectations crushed NIM optimism and recession fears raised credit-loss anxiety. Regional banks, as the highest-beta financials, amplified the sector selloff — defensives (Utilities +8.0%) dominated while cyclicals were routed (-19.1%).","body_zh":"2018年3月至12月，区域银行下跌-28.6%，随再通胀交易瓦解于美联储过度紧缩恐慌。美联储2018年加息四次（12月至2.50%），鲍威尔10月\"距中性利率还很远\"言论及12月将缩表定性为\"自动驾驶\"引发市场恐慌（VIX 15至36，SPY-14.4%）。2018年中期加征的贸易战关税增添增长放缓阴影，油价暴跌-31.4%，美元飙升+7.2%。金融板块是第三大拖累板块（-23.5%），短端收益率预期倒挂压垮NIM乐观情绪，衰退恐慌引发信用损失焦虑。区域银行作为贝塔最高的金融股放大了板块抛售——防御股主导（公用事业+8.0%）而周期股惨遭溃败（-19.1%）。","drivers":["Powell Dec-2018 'autopilot' QT comment triggered market panic","Four Fed hikes in 2018; recession fears spiked with VIX to 36","Inverted short-end yield expectations crushed NIM outlook","Trade-war tariffs: growth slowdown + oil -31.4%, dollar +7.2%"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔2018年12月'自动驾驶'缩表言论触发市场恐慌","2018年四次加息；衰退恐慌令VIX飙至36","短端收益率预期倒挂压垮NIM前景","贸易战关税：增长放缓+油价-31.4%，美元+7.2%"],"prev_key":"2018-03-09","prev_key_chain":["2018-03-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed autopilot shock, trade war, Q4 credit scare","title_zh":"美联储自动驾驶冲击、贸易战、四季度信用恐慌","turn_id":"regional_banks:peak:2018-03"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"Regional banks rallied +38.5% from the Christmas Eve 2018 trough to December 2019, tracking a broad risk-on recovery (SPY +38.3%, semis +75.1%, VIX 36 to 12). The Jan 4, 2019 Powell 'patient' speech in Atlanta marked the Fed pivot: no further rate hikes planned; by July 2019 the Fed cut three times (July, September, October) as insurance cuts against trade-war slowdown risk. The U.S.-China Phase 1 trade truce signed January 2020 removed the biggest growth overhang. Falling shorter-term rates (TLT +15.9%) were actually a mild NIM headwind, but the dominant driver was the credit-quality relief: the recession that markets had been pricing in December 2018 did not arrive, and bank loan books stayed clean. Financials were the second-leading sector (+40.8%), nearly matching tech's +57.9%.","body_zh":"自2018年平安夜低点至2019年12月，区域银行反弹+38.5%，跟随广泛风险偏好回暖（SPY+38.3%，半导体+75.1%，VIX 36至12）。2019年1月4日鲍威尔在亚特兰大的'耐心'讲话标志美联储转向：不再计划继续加息；至2019年下半年美联储以三次保险性降息（7月、9月、10月）应对贸易战放缓风险。2020年1月签署的美中第一阶段贸易休战消除最大增长阴影。短期利率下降（TLT+15.9%）实为轻微NIM逆风，但主要驱动力是信用质量释然：市场在2018年12月定价的衰退未曾到来，银行贷款账簿保持健康。金融板块是第二领涨板块（+40.8%），几乎与科技（+57.9%）并驾齐驱。","drivers":["Jan 2019 Powell 'patient' pivot — recession pricing reversed","Three Fed insurance cuts Jul-Oct 2019; trade truce Jan 2020","Credit quality held: no recession, clean loan books","Risk-on broadening (VIX 36 to 12; financials led at +40.8%)"],"drivers_zh":["2019年1月鲍威尔'耐心'转向——衰退定价逆转","2019年7-10月三次保险性降息；2020年1月贸易休战","信用质量保持：无衰退，贷款账簿健康","风险偏好回暖（VIX 36至12；金融领涨+40.8%）"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell pivot, trade truce, three Fed cuts recovery","title_zh":"鲍威尔转向、贸易休战、三次降息驱动复苏","turn_id":"regional_banks:trough:2018-12"},"2019-12-17":{"body":"Regional banks fell -52.0% from December 2019 to March 23, 2020 — the most severe leg in this 15-year series — as COVID-19 shut down the global economy. VIX exploded to 62 (the highest since 2008), the Fed cut to zero on March 15 and launched unlimited QE, and Congress passed the $2.2 trillion CARES Act on March 27. The flight-to-safety was indiscriminate (oil -61.7%, defensives -25.4% vs cyclicals -37.8%, breadth RSP lagged SPY -7.2%) but Financials (-42.1%) were among the worst sectors: banks faced a lethal combination of zero rate NIM compression, massive corporate credit-line drawdowns (as companies tapped revolvers), surging credit-loss provisions, and uncertainty about commercial real estate, consumer, and energy-sector loans. The crisis planted the seed for the massive reserve builds and eventual bond-portfolio vulnerability that defined 2023.","body_zh":"2019年12月至2020年3月23日，区域银行下跌-52.0%——这15年系列中最严峻的腿——随新冠疫情关闭全球经济。VIX爆至62（2008年以来最高），美联储3月15日降至零利率并启动无限量QE，国会3月27日通过2.2万亿美元CARES法案。避险逃离不加区分（油价-61.7%，防御股-25.4%对周期股-37.8%，广度RSP落后SPY-7.2%），金融板块（-42.1%）是最差板块之一：银行面临零利率NIM压缩、大规模企业信用额度提款、信用损失拨备急增及商业地产/消费者/能源贷款前景不确定的致命组合。这场危机埋下了大规模准备金堆积和最终在2023年引爆的债券组合脆弱性的种子。","drivers":["COVID-19 shock: VIX to 62, Fed to zero, CARES Act $2.2T","Zero-rate NIM compression — structural earnings hit","Massive corporate credit-line drawdowns, loan-loss provision surge","Financials -42.1% — worst group after energy in cyclical rout"],"drivers_zh":["新冠冲击：VIX飙至62，美联储降至零，CARES法案2.2万亿","零利率NIM压缩——结构性盈利打击","大规模企业信用额度提款，贷款损失拨备急升","金融板块-42.1%——周期股溃败中仅次于能源的最差板块"],"prev_key":"2019-12-17","prev_key_chain":["2019-12-17"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID-19 pandemic crash: steepest regional bank selloff","title_zh":"新冠疫情崩盘：区域银行史上最深跌幅","turn_id":"regional_banks:peak:2019-12"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"Regional banks rebounded +41.8% in just five weeks (March 23 to April 29, 2020) as the scale of policy intervention became clear: $2.2 trillion CARES Act, unlimited Fed QE, Fed emergency facilities backstopping corporate credit, and 50-state reopening timelines all compressing the panic. The regime shifted to goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation (cyclicals +39.2% vs defensives +28.7%, broadening RSP beat SPY +6.2%, VIX 62 to 31, DXY -2.8%). Banks bounced with cyclicals broadly as the immediate insolvency fears were removed — the Fed's backstop eliminated the tail risk of a 2008-style credit seizure. Energy led (+64.9%) and financials lagged slightly at +29.4%, suggesting the bounce was mechanical stress-relief rather than fundamental re-rating.","body_zh":"2020年3月23日至4月29日，仅五周区域银行反弹+41.8%，随政策干预规模明朗：2.2万亿美元CARES法案、美联储无限量QE、美联储紧急工具托底企业信用、以及50个州重新开放时间表共同压缩恐慌。行情转为黄金时代/增长向上去通胀（周期股+39.2%对防御股+28.7%，广度RSP跑赢SPY+6.2%，VIX 62至31，DXY-2.8%）。随即期偿付能力恐惧消除，银行随周期股整体反弹——美联储的托底消除了2008年式信用冻结的尾部风险。能源领涨（+64.9%），金融板块（+29.4%）略落后，显示反弹是机械式压力释放而非基本面重新定价。","drivers":["CARES Act $2.2T + unlimited Fed QE removed insolvency tail risk","Fed emergency facilities backstopped corporate credit markets","VIX 62 to 31: mechanical stress-relief bounce, not re-rating","Cyclicals led broadening (RSP+6.2%); DXY -2.8% tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["CARES法案2.2万亿+美联储无限量QE消除偿付能力尾部风险","美联储紧急工具托底企业信用市场","VIX 62至31：机械式压力释放反弹，非基本面重估","周期股引领广度转宽（RSP+6.2%）；DXY-2.8%顺风"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Fiscal/monetary bazooka V-bounce, cyclicals rebound","title_zh":"财政/货币大炮V型反弹，周期股回升","turn_id":"regional_banks:trough:2020-03"},"2020-04-29":{"body":"A sharp -21.4% pullback in just two weeks (April 29 to May 13, 2020), concentrated entirely in financials and industrials while Tech was flat. The catalyst was a combination of Q1 bank earnings releases showing massive loan-loss provision builds (U.S. banks doubled allowances for loan losses to ~$115B in H1 2020), rising COVID case counts suggesting the epidemic was not contained, and market rotation into tech/mega-cap safety (growth-value +7.6%, RSP lagged SPY -5.1%, Financials -11.6% the worst sector). VIX re-accelerated 31 to 35. This was not a broad macro selloff — it was a financials-specific credit-concern rotation into the tech mega-caps that were immune to lockdowns.","body_zh":"2020年4月29日至5月13日，仅两周暴跌-21.4%，跌幅集中于金融和工业板块，而科技板块持平。催化剂是Q1银行财报显示大规模贷款损失拨备（美国银行2020年上半年贷款损失准备金翻倍至约1150亿美元）、新冠病例数上升显示疫情未获控制，以及市场轮换至科技/大型股避风港（成长-价值+7.6%，RSP落后SPY-5.1%，金融板块-11.6%为最差板块）。VIX从31重新加速至35。这不是广泛宏观抛售——而是在免疫于封锁的科技大型股引领下，对金融板块信用担忧的定向轮换。","drivers":["Q1 bank earnings: massive provision builds flagged credit stress","Rising COVID case counts: second-wave fear reactivated","Tech/mega-cap rotation (growth+7.6%); financials -11.6% worst sector","VIX re-spiked 31 to 35; narrow RSP lagged SPY -5.1%"],"drivers_zh":["Q1银行财报：大规模拨备揭示信用压力","新冠病例上升：二次疫情恐慌重燃","科技/大型股轮换（成长+7.6%）；金融-11.6%最差板块","VIX从31重新飙升至35；RSP落后SPY-5.1%"],"prev_key":"2020-04-29","prev_key_chain":["2020-04-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Second-wave fears, provision builds, narrow tape flush","title_zh":"二次疫情恐慌、准备金堆积、窄幅行情冲洗","turn_id":"regional_banks:peak:2020-04"},"2020-05-13":{"body":"Regional banks surged +51.7% in under four weeks (May 13 to June 8, 2020), one of the sharpest sector rotations in the cycle. The catalyst was a shift from mega-cap safety to reopening-value as states began reopening and a COVID vaccine timeline came into view. The regime flipped to reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +23.2% vs defensives +9.0%, breadth RSP beat SPY +11.3%, high-beta minus low-vol +39.7%, VIX 35 to 26, DXY -3.6%). Financials led at +29.4% alongside Energy +31.2% — the quintessential early-cyclical reopening pair. Steepening yield expectations (TLT -5.2%) boosted NIM hopes. This was a violent factor reversal: the exact stocks that had been punished (high-beta value financials) became the leaders as the growth-fear trade unwound.","body_zh":"2020年5月13日至6月8日，区域银行不足四周飙升+51.7%，是这一周期中最剧烈的板块轮换之一。催化剂是随着各州开始重开及新冠疫苗时间表浮现，市场从大型股避风港切换至重开-价值股。行情翻转为再通胀/增长向上（周期股+23.2%对防御股+9.0%，广度RSP跑赢SPY+11.3%，高贝塔减低波+39.7%，VIX 35至26，DXY-3.6%）。金融板块（+29.4%）与能源（+31.2%）领涨——典型的早周期重开配对。收益率曲线趋陡预期（TLT-5.2%）提振NIM展望。这是一次剧烈的因子逆转：此前受压的高贝塔价值金融股成为领涨者，增长恐惧交易瓦解。","drivers":["Reopening value rotation: states reopening + vaccine timeline","VIX 35 to 26; DXY -3.6% — risk-on breadth trade (RSP+11.3%)","High-beta financials led: the punished sector became the leader","Yield steepening (TLT -5.2%) boosted NIM outlook"],"drivers_zh":["重开价值轮换：各州重开+疫苗时间表","VIX 35至26；DXY-3.6%——风险偏好广度交易（RSP+11.3%）","高贝塔金融股领涨：受压板块逆转领头","收益率趋陡（TLT-5.2%）提振NIM展望"],"prev_key":"2020-05-13","prev_key_chain":["2020-05-13"],"status":"exact","title":"Reopening trade: value-cyclical rotation powered banks","title_zh":"重开经济交易：价值-周期轮换推动银行股","turn_id":"regional_banks:trough:2020-05"},"2020-06-08":{"body":"Regional banks fell -25.8% (June 8 to July 9, 2020) as surging COVID case counts across the Sun Belt in late June 2020 raised fears of renewed lockdowns and a longer economic impairment. The market rotated back to defensive mega-cap tech (Tech +6.4%, Comm +0.5% vs Financials -14.6%, Energy -25.6%), with breadth collapsing (RSP lagged SPY -8.6%, high-beta minus low-vol -18.9%). TLT rallied +6.8% as yields fell — a direct NIM headwind. For regional banks the double hit was: (1) credit fears re-engaging as reopening stalled, and (2) a falling yield curve flattening the NIM recovery thesis. This was the final dip before the massive 18-month reflation mega-rally began.","body_zh":"2020年6月8日至7月9日，区域银行下跌-25.8%，随6月下旬阳光带新冠病例激增引发对重新封锁和更长经济损伤的恐惧。市场重新轮换至防御性大型科技股（科技+6.4%，通信+0.5%对金融-14.6%，能源-25.6%），广度崩溃（RSP落后SPY-8.6%，高贝塔减低波-18.9%）。TLT反弹+6.8%，收益率下行——直接的NIM逆风。对区域银行的双重打击：（1）重开停滞使信用恐惧重燃；（2）收益率曲线下行压平NIM复苏逻辑。这是大规模18个月再通胀超级行情开始前的最后一次回调。","drivers":["Sun Belt COVID surge Jun-2020: lockdown fear, reopening stalled","Yields fell (TLT +6.8%): NIM recovery thesis re-priced lower","Defensive mega-cap rotation: RSP lagged SPY -8.6%","High-beta financials double-hit: credit + rate headwind"],"drivers_zh":["2020年6月阳光带新冠激增：封锁恐惧，重开停滞","收益率下行（TLT+6.8%）：NIM复苏逻辑重新定价走低","防御性大型股轮换：RSP落后SPY-8.6%","高贝塔金融股双重打击：信用+利率双逆风"],"prev_key":"2020-06-08","prev_key_chain":["2020-06-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Second-wave COVID resurgence kills the reflation trade","title_zh":"新冠二次反弹扼杀再通胀交易","turn_id":"regional_banks:peak:2020-06"},"2020-07-09":{"body":"Regional banks surged +152.0% from July 2020 to January 2022 — nearly 3x the broad market (SPY +51%) — as a high-beta cyclical amplifying the most powerful reflation melt-up of the decade. The regime was dominant: cyclicals +69.0% vs defensives +33.2%, oil +111.6%, copper-gold +55.0%, high-beta minus low-vol +75.6%, breadth RSP beat SPY +13.5%, VIX 29 to 19. Vaccine approvals in November-December 2020 eliminated the pandemic tail risk; then Biden's $1.9T American Rescue Plan in March 2021 supercharged the reflation, while sustained large fiscal deficits kept long rates rising. Rising yields (TLT -13.1%) widened NIM and the steepening curve was the central bank trade thesis. In hindsight, the same dynamic — banks loading long-duration bonds at peak prices to boost NIM — planted the seeds of the 2023 crisis.","body_zh":"2020年7月至2022年1月，区域银行飙升+152.0%——近大盘三倍（SPY+51%）——作为高贝塔周期股放大十年来最强劲的再通胀融涨。行情主导：周期股+69.0%对防御股+33.2%，油价+111.6%，铜金比+55.0%，高贝塔减低波+75.6%，广度RSP跑赢SPY+13.5%，VIX 29至19。2020年11-12月疫苗获批消除疫情尾部风险；随后拜登2021年3月1.9万亿美元美国救援计划超级加速再通胀，持续的大规模财政赤字推动长端利率上行。收益率上升（TLT-13.1%）拓宽NIM，曲线趋陡是中央银行交易核心逻辑。事后看，同一动态——银行在价格高点囤积长久期债券以提升NIM——埋下了2023年危机的种子。","drivers":["Vaccine approval Nov-Dec 2020 eliminated pandemic tail risk","Biden $1.9T ARP Mar-2021 + fiscal stimulus supercharged reflation","Yield curve steepening (TLT -13.1%) widened NIM — the core thesis","High-beta cyclical: +152% vs SPY +51%; banks loaded long bonds"],"drivers_zh":["2020年11-12月疫苗获批消除疫情尾部风险","拜登2021年3月1.9万亿美元救援计划+财政刺激超级加速再通胀","收益率曲线趋陡（TLT-13.1%）拓宽NIM——核心逻辑","高贝塔周期股：+152%对SPY+51%；银行囤积长久期债券"],"prev_key":"2020-07-09","prev_key_chain":["2020-07-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Reopening reflation mega-rally, steepening curve boom","title_zh":"重开再通胀超级行情，曲线趋陡繁荣","turn_id":"regional_banks:trough:2020-07"},"2022-01-14":{"body":"Regional banks fell -26.6% from January to June 2022 in a stagflation-ish rate-and-dollar shock (TLT -20.8%, DXY +8.9%, VIX 19 to 33). The Fed pivoted from 'transitory' to hiking 450bps starting March 2022 — the fastest tightening since 1981 — and the Ukraine invasion (February 24) drove oil +40.3%, completing the stagflation picture. Paradoxically, early fast rate hikes should benefit bank NIM, but the market priced the recession risk first: cyclicals fell -15.5% vs defensives -8.4%. The more important, unappreciated damage: every 25bps hike marked the banks' peak-priced, long-duration bond portfolios further underwater under held-to-maturity accounting. By mid-2022 the system was sitting on hundreds of billions in unrealized losses — the slow-motion fuse of the 2023 crisis.","body_zh":"2022年1月至6月，区域银行在滞胀式利率和美元冲击中下跌-26.6%（TLT-20.8%，DXY+8.9%，VIX 19至33）。美联储从'暂时性'转向自2022年3月起加息450个基点——1981年以来最快紧缩——乌克兰入侵（2月24日）推动油价+40.3%，完成滞胀图景。矛盾的是，早期快速加息本应提升银行NIM，但市场先定价衰退风险：周期股-15.5%对防御股-8.4%。更重要但被忽视的损伤：每次25基点加息都使银行以高价买入的长久期债券在持有至到期会计下浮亏加深。至2022年中期，整个体系坐拥数千亿未实现损失——2023年危机的慢动作引信。","drivers":["Fed 450bps hikes Mar-2022 (fastest since 1981); Ukraine invasion","Stagflation-ish: oil +40.3%, DXY +8.9%, VIX 19 to 33","Recession pricing dominated NIM benefit: cyclicals -15.5%","HTM bond portfolios marked deeply underwater — 2023 fuse lit"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2022年3月起450基点加息（1981年以来最快）；乌克兰入侵","滞胀式：油价+40.3%，DXY+8.9%，VIX 19至33","衰退定价压倒NIM利好：周期股-15.5%","HTM债券组合深度浮亏——2023年引信点燃"],"prev_key":"2022-01-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-01-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed shock hikes, stagflation regime: powder ignites","title_zh":"美联储冲击加息、滞胀行情：火药引爆","turn_id":"regional_banks:peak:2022-01"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"Regional banks rallied +20.1% from June 2022 to February 2023, riding a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation bounce (SPY +14.7%, VIX 33 to 19, oil -34.4%, RSP beat SPY +4.2%, high-beta minus low-vol +23.6%). The Fed's mid-2022 75bps hikes marked the perceived peak-pace of tightening, and by late 2022 inflation data was rolling over — CPI peaked at 9.1% in June 2022 and fell steadily. The AI/ChatGPT launch in November 2022 added a growth-optimism overlay. Banks benefited from NIM expansion as hike-cycle deposits hadn't repriced fully yet, creating a brief sweet spot. But this was the calm before the storm: the duration-risk time bomb in bank bond portfolios was ticking, and the February 2023 peak preceded the SVB collapse by just five weeks.","body_zh":"2022年6月至2023年2月，区域银行反弹+20.1%，乘黄金时代/增长向上去通胀反弹（SPY+14.7%，VIX 33至19，油价-34.4%，RSP跑赢SPY+4.2%，高贝塔减低波+23.6%）。美联储2022年年中75基点加息被视为紧缩步伐的顶峰，2022年底通胀数据开始回落——CPI于2022年6月见顶9.1%后稳步下降。2022年11月AI/ChatGPT发布增添增长乐观情绪。银行受益于NIM扩张，因加息周期中存款尚未充分重定价，创造了短暂甜蜜期。但这是暴风雨前的平静：银行债券组合中的久期风险定时炸弹正在滴答作响，2023年2月峰值距SVB崩溃仅五周。","drivers":["Peak-rate optimism: CPI peaked Jun-2022, Nov-2022 disinflationary turn","Goldilocks bounce: VIX 33 to 19, oil -34.4%, RSP beat +4.2%","NIM sweet spot: asset yields repriced up, deposits lagged","AI/ChatGPT Nov-2022 added risk-on overlay; SVB storm weeks away"],"drivers_zh":["利率见顶乐观：CPI 2022年6月见顶，11月去通胀转折","黄金时代反弹：VIX 33至19，油价-34.4%，RSP跑赢+4.2%","NIM甜蜜期：资产收益率重定价上行，存款滞后","AI/ChatGPT 2022年11月增添风险偏好；SVB危机数周后爆发"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Soft-landing hope, peak-rate rally pre-SVB","title_zh":"软着陆希望、利率见顶反弹于SVB危机前","turn_id":"regional_banks:trough:2022-06"},"2023-02-07":{"body":"The defining disaster leg: regional banks fell -38.4% while SPY barely moved (-2.1%) and VIX stayed low (19 to 20) — this was a pure sector-solvency panic, not a macro de-risk. On March 8-9, 2023, Silicon Valley Bank disclosed a ~$1.8B loss from a forced sale of ~$21B of securities and failed to raise emergency capital; a digital-age, Twitter-driven deposit run emptied SVB within 48 hours. The FDIC seized SVB on March 10 and Signature Bank on March 12; First Republic failed and was sold to JPMorgan in early May. The Federal Reserve's BTFP (Bank Term Funding Program, launched March 12, valuing pledged bonds at par) stopped the contagion — but capital fled regional banking into money-market funds and too-big-to-fail institutions (RSP lagged SPY -5.8%, Financials -14.3%, HYG-LQD -1.6%). The crash was traceable to the unhedged duration mismatches built during 2020-2022.","body_zh":"决定性灾难腿：区域银行暴跌-38.4%，而SPY几乎未动（-2.1%），VIX保持平稳（19至20）——这是纯粹的板块偿付恐慌，而非宏观去风险。2023年3月8-9日，硅谷银行披露被迫出售约210亿美元证券损失约18亿美元并未能募集紧急资金；Twitter驱动的数字时代存款挤兑在48小时内掏空SVB。FDIC于3月10日接管SVB，3月12日接管Signature Bank；First Republic于5月初倒闭并出售给摩根大通。美联储于3月12日推出的BTFP（银行定期融资计划，以票面价值估值质押债券）遏制了蔓延——但资金从区域银行逃向货币市场基金和大到不能倒机构（RSP落后SPY-5.8%，金融-14.3%，HYG-LQD-1.6%）。崩溃可追溯至2020-2022年积累的未对冲久期错配。","drivers":["SVB ~$1.8B bond-sale loss Mar-8/9-2023; digital deposit run in 48hrs","SVB/Signature/First Republic failed — three banks in 8 weeks","BTFP (par-value pledge) stopped contagion, bottomed May 2023","Idiosyncratic: SPY -2.1%, VIX flat — pure sector solvency panic"],"drivers_zh":["SVB约18亿美元债券出售损失2023年3月8-9日；48小时数字存款挤兑","SVB/Signature/First Republic倒闭——8周三家银行","BTFP（票面价值质押）遏制蔓延，2023年5月触底","板块特异：SPY-2.1%，VIX平稳——纯板块偿付恐慌"],"prev_key":"2023-02-07","prev_key_chain":["2023-02-07"],"status":"exact","title":"SVB collapse: idiosyncratic sector crisis, not macro","title_zh":"SVB崩溃：板块特异危机，非宏观系统性","turn_id":"regional_banks:peak:2023-02"},"2023-05-04":{"body":"From the May 2023 SVB-crisis trough, regional banks rallied +127.7% to November 2024 — 2.5x the broad market (SPY +50.6%) in one of the great crisis-recovery trades. Healing was mechanical at first: the Fed's BTFP eliminated the liquidity tail risk, deposits stabilized, NIM bottomed and began widening as the deposit-repricing cycle peaked, and survivors proved their bond books money-good. The goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation macro regime (semis +101.2%, growth-value +27.1%, VIX 20 to 15, HYG-LQD +10.0%, Financials +66.0%) amplified the fundamental recovery. Then the November 2024 Trump election added rocket fuel: deregulation promises (Basel III 'endgame' rollback, capital rules loosening), an anticipated M&A wave, and higher-for-longer rates sustaining NIM. The September 2024 Fed cuts eased deposit-cost pressure. Even in a narrow mega-cap tape (RSP lagged SPY -14.2%), KRE dominated.","body_zh":"自2023年5月SVB危机低点，区域银行反弹+127.7%至2024年11月——是大盘的2.5倍（SPY+50.6%），堪称伟大的危机复苏交易之一。复苏起初是机械式的：美联储BTFP消除流动性尾部风险，存款企稳，NIM在存款重定价周期见顶后触底回升，幸存者证明债券账簿资产成色十足。黄金时代/增长向上去通胀宏观行情（半导体+101.2%，成长-价值+27.1%，VIX 20至15，HYG-LQD+10.0%，金融+66.0%）放大了基本面复苏。随后2024年11月特朗普大选注入火箭燃料：放松监管承诺（巴塞尔III\"终局\"松绑，资本规则放宽），预期并购浪潮，以及较高且持续利率维持NIM。2024年9月美联储降息缓解存款成本压力。即使在狭窄大型股行情中（RSP落后SPY-14.2%），KRE仍强势领涨。","drivers":["BTFP stabilized deposits; NIM recovery as deposit repricing peaked","Goldilocks macro: semis+101.2%, Financials+66.0%, VIX 20 to 15","Nov-2024 Trump election: deregulation + M&A wave + Basel III rollback","Sep-2024 Fed cuts eased deposit cost; survivors re-rated"],"drivers_zh":["BTFP稳定存款；NIM随存款重定价见顶而复苏","黄金时代宏观：半导体+101.2%，金融+66.0%，VIX 20至15","2024年11月特朗普大选：放松监管+并购浪潮+巴塞尔III松绑","2024年9月美联储降息缓解存款成本；幸存者重新定价"],"prev_key":"2023-05-04","prev_key_chain":["2023-05-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-crisis deregulation recovery, AI goldilocks surge","title_zh":"危机后放松监管复苏，AI黄金时代飙升","turn_id":"regional_banks:trough:2023-05"},"2024-11-25":{"body":"Regional banks gave back -29.6% from their post-election peak (November 2024) to the April 8, 2025 tariff-crash trough — deeper than the broad market (SPY -16.4%) in a textbook flight-to-safety de-risk (VIX 15 to 52, high-beta minus low-vol -21.0%, defensives -7.6% vs cyclicals -18.9%, DXY -3.6% paradoxically weaker). Trump's April 2, 2025 'Liberation Day' tariff announcement triggered the acute selloff: a 145% effective tariff rate on China and a universal 10% reciprocal levy with higher rates on dozens of countries. Recession probability estimates jumped toward 50%, and recession is the direct enemy of bank credit quality. For regional banks the fear was two-fold: deteriorating loan books and a weaker-than-expected NIM environment if the Fed cut aggressively. Oil -13.6% and defensives leading confirmed full macro risk-off. The basket bottomed with the broad market exactly on April 8.","body_zh":"2024年11月大选后峰值至2025年4月8日关税崩盘低点，区域银行回吐-29.6%——在教科书式避险去风险中（VIX 15至52，高贝塔减低波-21.0%，防御股-7.6%对周期股-18.9%，DXY矛盾地走弱-3.6%）比大盘（SPY-16.4%）跌得更深。特朗普2025年4月2日'解放日'关税公告触发急性抛售：对华145%实际关税率，对全球普征10%报复性关税并对数十国加征更高税率。衰退概率预估跳升至接近50%，衰退是银行信用质量的直接敌人。对区域银行的恐惧是双重的：贷款账簿恶化，以及若美联储大幅降息则NIM环境弱于预期。油价-13.6%、防御股领跌确认全面宏观避险。篮子恰好与大盘于4月8日同步见底。","drivers":["Liberation Day Apr-2, 2025: 145% China tariff, universal 10% levy","Recession probability ~50%: direct threat to regional bank credit","VIX 15 to 52; high-beta -21.0% — hardest hit vs broad market","Depositor/NIM fears: if Fed cuts aggressively, NIM benefit reverses"],"drivers_zh":["解放日2025年4月2日：145%对华关税，全球普征10%","衰退概率约50%：区域银行信用直接威胁","VIX 15至52；高贝塔-21.0%——相较大盘受创最重","存款/NIM恐惧：若美联储大幅降息，NIM利好逆转"],"prev_key":"2024-11-25","prev_key_chain":["2024-11-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Liberation Day tariff crash: high-beta sold hardest","title_zh":"解放日关税崩盘：高贝塔遭受最重打击","turn_id":"regional_banks:peak:2024-11"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"Regional banks have rallied +68.1% from the April 8, 2025 tariff-crash trough to mid-2026, riding a powerful reflation/growth-up V-bounce (SPY +49.6%, semis +255.0%, VIX 52 to 19, high-beta minus low-vol +118.3%, cyclicals +51.4% vs defensives +20.4%). The U.S.-China tariff partial ceasefire in May 2025 and the U.S.-Iran ceasefire in mid-June 2026 progressively removed the acute tail risks. The deregulation and M&A thrust resumed — the Basel III capital-rule rollback and a more merger-friendly regulatory posture supported the group, and net interest margins stabilized as deposit costs rolled over. Despite a narrow tape (RSP lagged SPY -8.8%), KRE is trending at position 56, but Financials still lag (-2.7%) on the 2026 oil-shock and the CRE maturity-wall concern, with a Fed in hiking bias keeping the rate path two-sided for the group.","body_zh":"自2025年4月8日关税崩盘低点至2026年中，区域银行反弹+68.1%，乘强劲的再通胀/增长向上V型反弹（SPY+49.6%，半导体+255.0%，VIX 52至19，高贝塔减低波+118.3%，周期股+51.4%对防御股+20.4%）。2025年5月中美关税部分停火及2026年6月美伊停火逐步消除急性尾部风险。放松监管和并购推力重启——巴塞尔III资本规则松绑及更利于合并的监管态势支撑板块，净息差随存款成本回落而企稳。尽管行情狭窄（RSP落后SPY-8.8%），KRE在位置56处于趋势中，但金融板块仍落后（-2.7%），受2026年油价冲击及商业地产到期墙担忧拖累，而处于加息倾向的美联储令该组别利率路径双向作用。","drivers":["Risk-on V-bounce: SPY+49.6%, semis+255%, VIX 52 to 19","US-China tariff ceasefire May-2025; US-Iran ceasefire Jun-2026","NIM stabilized as deposit costs rolled over","Deregulation/M&A: Basel III rollback, merger-friendly posture"],"drivers_zh":["风险偏好V型反弹：SPY+49.6%，半导体+255%，VIX 52至19","美中关税停火2025年5月；美伊停火2026年6月","NIM随存款成本回落而企稳","放松监管/并购：巴塞尔III松绑，利于合并的监管态势"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-ceasefire V-bounce, deregulation cycle resumes","title_zh":"关税停火V型反弹，放松监管周期重启","turn_id":"regional_banks:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Regional Banks (KRE) sit in an Expansion/Trending phase at position 56.3, having rallied +68% from the April 2025 tariff-crash trough and logging 328% cumulative return since 2014. The live regime is reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%), which is structurally favorable for banks via a steeper curve and better loan demand. Yet Financials lag at -2.7%, flagging a cross-current: the 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock and a Fed in hiking bias threaten commercial real estate loan books and compress risk appetite for economically sensitive lenders. At RS rank #16 and mid-range positioning above the 200-day, KRE is a participate-but-monitor-credit basket: NIM has stabilized as deposit costs roll over, the deregulation/M&A cycle is intact, but the CRE maturity wall in 2026-2027 and the oil-shock inflation tail remain live risks that can reprice the group quickly.","now_zh":"区域银行（KRE）处于扩张/趋势中阶段，位置56.3，自2025年4月关税崩盘低点反弹+68%，自2014年以来累计回报328%。当前行情为再通胀/增长向上（周期股+11.2%对防御股+6.9%，油价+19.2%，铜金比+18.3%），通过曲线趋陡和贷款需求改善结构上有利于银行板块。然而金融板块落后-2.7%，显示逆流：2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹石油冲击及美联储加息倾向威胁商业地产贷款账簿并压制对经济敏感型贷款机构的风险偏好。在200日均线上方、RS排名第16位、仓位居中，KRE是\"参与但监控信用\"的篮子：NIM随存款成本回落而企稳，放松监管/并购周期完好，但2026-2027年商业地产到期墙及油价冲击通胀尾风仍是可快速重新定价整组的活跃风险。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"credit.spread_regime.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"credit.spread_regime.v1","arch_state":"fail","arch_fired_on":"2026-07-05","revision_note":null}},"b-reshoring":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"The Fed completed its QE taper through 2013 while US GDP printed +3.2% annualized in Q4 2013, generating a capex-recovery narrative into early 2014. However the ctx is unmistakably stagflation-ish: defensives led (utilities +15.8%), bonds surged (TLT +10.4%) and the 10-year yield fell through H1 2014, meaning the rally was a yield-compression trade that lifted rate-sensitive industrials alongside utilities. The reshoring basket gained +8.6% — a below-market lift driven more by falling yields and energy-sector strength (XLE +12.1%) than any industrial capex catalyst of its own.","body_zh":"美联储于2013年完成量化宽松缩减，美国GDP四季度年化增长3.2%，为2014年初带来资本开支复苏叙事。然而背景明显带有类滞胀特征：防御板块领涨（公用事业+15.8%），债券飙升（TLT+10.4%），10年期国债收益率在上半年持续下行，意味着这轮反弹本质是收益率压缩交易，利率敏感型工业股随公用事业一同受益。回流篮子上涨+8.6%，主要受益于收益率下行和能源板块强势（XLE+12.1%），而非工业资本开支本身的催化。","drivers":["Fed QE taper complete, capex recovery narrative","Yield-compression rally (TLT +10.4%) lifts rate-sensitive industrials","Energy sector strength (oil +11.1%) adds broad cyclical bid","Stagflation-ish quad: defensives outperformed cyclicals"],"drivers_zh":["美联储量化宽松缩减完成，资本开支复苏叙事","收益率压缩反弹（TLT+10.4%）提振利率敏感型工业股","能源板块强势（油价+11.1%）带来广泛周期性买盘","类滞胀象限：防御板块跑赢周期板块"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-taper capex recovery, bond-yield-drop rally","title_zh":"后量化宽松资本开支复苏，债券收益率下行驱动反弹","turn_id":"reshoring:trough:2014-01"},"2014-06-09":{"body":"Brent crude peaked at $115/barrel on June 19 2014 then collapsed toward $57 by year-end as US shale oversupply met weakening global demand and OPEC refused to cut. Simultaneously the dollar surged 14% against major trading partners from June 2014 to January 2015 as the Fed tapered while the ECB eased. The ctx is a textbook slowdown/deflation scare: VIX spiked from 11 to 25, defensives led (+2.1%), cyclicals fell -6.9%, TLT rose +9.5%, and industrials/energy were the worst laggards. The reshoring basket fell -15.7%, punished by the same dollar and commodity shock that hit all cyclicals.","body_zh":"布伦特原油于2014年6月19日触顶每桶115美元，随后因美国页岩油产能过剩遭遇全球需求走弱且欧佩克拒绝减产而崩跌至57美元。与此同时，美元对主要贸易伙伴货币从2014年6月至2015年1月飙升14%，因美联储缩减宽松而欧央行放松货币政策。背景呈现教科书式放缓/通缩恐慌：VIX从11飙至25，防御领涨（+2.1%），周期下跌-6.9%，TLT涨+9.5%，工业和能源是最大滞后板块。回流篮子下跌-15.7%，受与所有周期股相同的美元和大宗商品冲击。","drivers":["Oil crash from $115 to $57 (WTI -17.9%) destroys energy/industrial capex outlook","Dollar surge (DXY +5.9%) hits industrial multinational earnings","Deflation-scare/slowdown regime: VIX 11 to 25, defensives lead","Fed taper vs ECB easing widens US-EU rate differential, strengthens dollar"],"drivers_zh":["油价崩盘（WTI-17.9%）摧毁能源/工业资本开支前景","美元飙升（DXY+5.9%）打压工业跨国企业盈利","通缩恐慌/放缓象限：VIX从11至25，防御领先","美联储缩减QE对欧央行宽松拉大美欧利差，强化美元"],"prev_key":"2014-06-09","prev_key_chain":["2014-06-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil crash & dollar surge trigger deflation scare selloff","title_zh":"油价崩盘与美元飙升引发通缩恐慌性抛售","turn_id":"reshoring:peak:2014-06"},"2014-10-13":{"body":"The Fed officially ended its asset purchase program on October 29 2014 after a brief October flash crash in Treasuries (October 15) created a volatility spike and buying opportunity. Markets interpreted the QE end as a clean break: VIX collapsed from 25 to 12, cyclicals outperformed (+11.1% vs defensives +8.4%), industrials led the recovery (+16.1%), growth beat value, and semis surged +20.4%. The reshoring basket surged +16.6% in just six weeks, pulled by broad cyclical rotation back into industrials and discretionary following the brief scare, with the dollar edging higher (DXY +2.9%) yet not yet a headwind.","body_zh":"美联储于2014年10月29日正式结束资产购买计划，此前10月15日出现短暂国债闪崩（产生波动率尖峰和买入机会）。市场将量化宽松结束解读为经济确认信号：VIX从25骤降至12，周期股跑赢（+11.1%对防御+8.4%），工业引领复苏（+16.1%），成长跑赢价值，半导体飙升+20.4%。回流篮子仅六周内暴涨+16.6%，受益于大范围周期轮动重回工业和非必需消费品，美元略微走强（DXY+2.9%）尚未形成逆风。","drivers":["Fed formally ends QE Oct 29, market interprets as growth-affirming","VIX collapse 25 to 12 fuels aggressive cyclical re-entry","Industrials lead recovery (+16.1%) in goldilocks quad rotation","Semis +20.4% signals risk-on breadth across capex-levered names"],"drivers_zh":["美联储10月29日正式结束量化宽松，市场解读为增长确认信号","VIX从25骤降至12，催生激进的周期股再进入","黄金分割象限轮动中工业领涨（+16.1%）","半导体+20.4%标志着资本开支关联标的风险偏好广度回归"],"prev_key":"2014-10-13","prev_key_chain":["2014-10-13"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed QE-end bounce lifts cyclicals sharply","title_zh":"美联储结束量化宽松驱动周期股大幅反弹","turn_id":"reshoring:trough:2014-10"},"2014-11-25":{"body":"A major 14-month selloff drove a -27.6% decline as the oil bust deepened (WTI fell from $80 to $26 by February 2016), the dollar entered a super-cycle surge (DXY +12.7%), and China's growth scare triggered global deflation fears. The 2015-16 Chinese stock market bubble deflation and subsequent yuan devaluation in August 2015 amplified the risk-off rotation (VIX 12 to 28). Energy capex was gutted — E&P companies cut capital spending by an average of 41% in 2016 — devastating the industrial supply chain. The ctx confirms a severe slowdown/deflation-scare regime: defensives eked out +0.5% while cyclicals fell -14.9%; industrials dropped -14.3% and materials -23.3%.","body_zh":"长达14个月的重大抛售导致-27.6%跌幅，因油价崩溃（WTI从80美元跌至2016年2月26美元）、美元进入超级周期升值（DXY+12.7%），以及中国增长恐慌引发全球通缩担忧。2015-16年中国股市泡沫破裂及2015年8月随后的人民币贬值放大了避险轮动（VIX从12至28）。能源资本开支大幅削减——勘探和生产公司2016年平均削减资本支出41%——重创工业供应链。背景确认为严重的放缓/通缩恐慌象限：防御仅勉强维持+0.5%，而周期下跌-14.9%；工业下跌-14.3%，材料-23.3%。","drivers":["Oil supercycle bust (WTI $80 to $26, oil -64.2%) destroys industrial capex chain","Dollar supercycle surge (DXY +12.7%) crushes multinational revenue","China growth/currency scare (Aug 2015 yuan devaluation, Shanghai crash)","Deflation-scare regime: VIX 12 to 28, defensives only refuge"],"drivers_zh":["油价超级周期崩溃（WTI从80至26美元，油价-64.2%）摧毁工业资本开支链","美元超级周期飙升（DXY+12.7%）压缩跨国企业营收","中国增长/货币恐慌（2015年8月人民币贬值，沪指崩盘）","通缩恐慌象限：VIX从12至28，防御成唯一避难所"],"prev_key":"2014-11-25","prev_key_chain":["2014-11-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil bust, dollar supercycle crush industrial capex 14 months","title_zh":"油价崩溃与美元超级周期长达14个月的工业资本开支压制","turn_id":"reshoring:peak:2014-11"},"2015-09-28":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"reshoring:trough:2015-09"},"2015-12-01":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"reshoring:peak:2015-12"},"2016-01-20":{"body":"The basket's largest leg — +133% over two full years — began at the commodity/oil trough (WTI ~$26) and was supercharged by the November 2016 Trump election, which drove immediate industrial/financials re-rating on tax-cut, deregulation and infrastructure-spend expectations. From Jan 2016 the dollar reversed (DXY -10.1% total), oil surged +149%, copper-gold +40.6%, VIX fell to 11, and cyclicals outran defensives by 40+ percentage points (+72.6% vs +31.9%). The US ISM Manufacturing PMI returned to expansionary territory through 2017; the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (Dec 2017) accelerated capex immediately. The reshoring basket +133.1% outpaced SPY +60.7% — financials and materials surging alongside confirmed the breadth of the reflation trade.","body_zh":"篮子最大涨幅腿段——两整年+133%——始于大宗商品/油价谷底（WTI约26美元），并被2016年11月特朗普当选大幅强化，后者基于减税、放松监管和基础设施支出预期立即驱动工业/金融再评级。自2016年1月，美元逆转（DXY总计-10.1%），油价飙升+149%，铜金比+40.6%，VIX降至11，周期股跑赢防御逾40个百分点（+72.6%对+31.9%）。美国ISM制造业PMI于2017年全年重回扩张区间；2017年12月《减税与就业法案》立即加速资本开支。回流篮子+133.1%大幅跑赢SPY+60.7%——金融和材料同步飙升确认再通胀交易的广度。","drivers":["Commodity/oil trough recovery (oil +149%, copper-gold +40.6%) revives capex","Trump election Nov 2016 drives infrastructure/tax-cut re-rating of industrials","Dollar reversal (DXY -10.1%) is major tailwind for industrial multinationals","Tax Cuts and Jobs Act Dec 2017 immediately boosts capex spending intentions"],"drivers_zh":["大宗商品/油价谷底复苏（油价+149%，铜金比+40.6%）重振资本开支","2016年11月特朗普当选驱动基础设施/减税的工业再评级","美元逆转（DXY-10.1%）对工业跨国企业是重大顺风","2017年12月《减税与就业法案》立即提振资本支出意愿"],"prev_key":"2016-01-20","prev_key_chain":["2016-01-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump reflation wave & commodity recovery mega-bull","title_zh":"特朗普再通胀浪潮与大宗商品复苏大牛市","turn_id":"reshoring:trough:2016-01"},"2018-01-26":{"body":"The January 2018 peak coincided with a vol implosion event (VIX spiked from 11 to 36 between Feb and December) as the Fed raised rates four times in 2018 to a 2.25-2.5% target range. Powell's December 19 2018 hike — accompanied by insistence on balance-sheet autopilot — triggered the worst December for the Dow since the Great Depression. Simultaneously the US-China trade war escalated through 2018 (steel/aluminum tariffs March, Section 301 tariffs July), punishing downstream manufacturers and industrial multinationals. The dollar surged (DXY +8.4%), oil collapsed -35.7%, financials and materials were worst laggards (-24.7% each), and the basket fell -25.7% versus SPY -16.7%.","body_zh":"2018年1月峰值与波动率内爆事件同步（VIX从2月至12月由11飙至36），因美联储当年四次加息至2.25-2.5%目标区间。鲍威尔12月19日加息并坚持资产负债表自动驾驶，触发道琼斯工业平均指数大萧条以来最糟糕的12月表现。与此同时，2018年美中贸易战持续升级（3月钢铁/铝关税，7月301条款关税），打压下游制造商和工业跨国企业。美元飙升（DXY+8.4%），油价崩跌-35.7%，金融和材料是最大滞后板块（各-24.7%），篮子下跌-25.7%，对比SPY-16.7%。","drivers":["Fed four rate hikes in 2018, December hike triggers capitulation selloff","US-China trade war escalation (Section 301 tariffs) hits industrial supply chains","Dollar surge (DXY +8.4%) headwind for multinational revenue and margins","VIX 11 to 36 risk-off rotation into defensives; oil -35.7% kills energy-capex"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2018年四次加息，12月加息引发投降式抛售","美中贸易战升级（301条款关税）冲击工业供应链","美元飙升（DXY+8.4%）对跨国企业营收和利润率形成逆风","VIX从11至36避险轮动入防御；油价-35.7%扼杀能源资本开支"],"prev_key":"2018-01-26","prev_key_chain":["2018-01-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate shock, trade war & dollar surge end the reflation run","title_zh":"利率冲击、贸易战与美元飙升终结再通胀行情","turn_id":"reshoring:peak:2018-01"},"2018-05-02":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"reshoring:trough:2018-05"},"2018-09-20":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"reshoring:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"Jerome Powell executed a dramatic pivot in January 2019 — ceasing hikes and cutting rates three times (July, September, October 2019) — which triggered a sustained 14-month risk-on rally. The basket gained +64% versus SPY +46.7%, lifted by a tech/semis-led growth melt-up (SMH +89.3%, growth over value by 22.5pp, VIX 36 to 14). TLT surged +21.2% as yields fell, providing an additional tailwind to rate-sensitive capex names. Manufacturing PMI was mixed — a mid-cycle mini-recession in H2 2019 — but the broad risk-on environment and Phase-1 US-China trade deal (January 2020) kept sentiment supportive until COVID emerged.","body_zh":"鲍威尔于2019年1月执行戏剧性政策转向——停止加息并三次降息（7月、9月、10月2019年）——触发持续14个月的风险偏好反弹。篮子上涨+64%，对比SPY+46.7%，受科技/半导体主导的成长融涨提振（SMH+89.3%，成长跑赢价值22.5个百分点，VIX从36至14）。TLT飙升+21.2%，收益率下行为利率敏感型资本开支标的提供额外顺风。制造业PMI表现参差——2019年下半年迷你周期性衰退——但广泛的风险偏好环境和2020年1月美中第一阶段贸易协议使情绪保持支撑，直至COVID爆发。","drivers":["Powell pivot: Fed cuts rates 3x in H2 2019, ending tightening cycle","Tech/semis melt-up (SMH +89.3%, growth beats value by 22.5pp) lifts all capex names","Yield compression (TLT +21.2%) reduces cost of capital for industrial capex","Phase-1 US-China trade deal (Jan 2020) reduces trade-war overhang"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔转向：美联储2019年下半年三次降息，结束紧缩周期","科技/半导体融涨（SMH+89.3%，成长跑赢价值22.5个百分点）提振所有资本开支标的","收益率压缩（TLT+21.2%）降低工业资本开支资金成本","美中第一阶段贸易协议（2020年1月）减轻贸易战悬念"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell pivot & tech-led melt-up into pre-COVID peak","title_zh":"鲍威尔转向与科技领涨融涨至COVID前高点","turn_id":"reshoring:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-12":{"body":"COVID-19 spread globally from Wuhan in February 2020, forcing factory shutdowns across China and then the US and Europe. The industrial/manufacturing sector was among the hardest hit: supply chains seized, US imports from China fell ~50% in March, and factory production collapsed to levels not seen since WWII. The ctx shows a panic selloff with VIX spiking from 14 to 62 — the fastest VIX move on record — while defensives fell -28.8% and cyclicals -40.3%, with industrials specifically down -42.3% and energy -56.2%. The basket fell -42% in just six weeks, with TLT +16% and dollar +3.5% as capital fled to safety.","body_zh":"COVID-19于2020年2月从武汉蔓延全球，迫使中国乃至美国和欧洲各地工厂停工。工业/制造业板块受创最重：供应链骤停，美国自中国进口3月暴跌约50%，工厂生产崩至二战以来最低水平。背景显示恐慌性抛售，VIX从14飙至62（史上最快飙升记录），防御板块下跌-28.8%，周期下跌-40.3%，工业具体下跌-42.3%，能源-56.2%。篮子仅六周内下跌-42%，TLT+16%，美元+3.5%，资本全线撤往安全资产。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic triggers global factory shutdowns and supply chain seizure","VIX 14 to 62 (fastest spike on record) forces forced-selling across cyclicals","Industrial production collapses to WWII-era lows; US-China imports -50% in March","Dollar flight-to-safety +3.5%, oil -54.3%; all cyclicals sold indiscriminately"],"drivers_zh":["COVID-19疫情引发全球工厂停工和供应链瘫痪","VIX从14至62（史上最快飙升记录）迫使周期股强制平仓","工业产出跌至二战以来低点；3月美中进口骤降50%","美元避险飙升+3.5%，油价-54.3%；所有周期股遭无差别抛售"],"prev_key":"2020-02-12","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-12"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash, supply chain collapse","title_zh":"COVID疫情崩盘，供应链全面瘫痪","turn_id":"reshoring:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The Fed cut to zero on March 15-16 2020, Congress passed the $2.2 trillion CARES Act on March 27, and the largest fiscal stimulus in US peacetime history ignited the post-COVID recovery. The basket surged +218% over 20 months — its greatest leg ever — as the macro regime became full reflation: oil +245.7%, copper-gold +87.3%, dollar -6.4%, VIX 62 to 16, cyclicals +141% vs defensives +65%. Critically, COVID exposed supply-chain fragility and accelerated the reshoring policy agenda: the Bipartisan Infrastructure Law (IIJA) was signed November 2021, semiconductor shortages triggered CHIPS Act discussions, and manufacturing capex began its historic ascent. The basket's +218% vs SPY +115.2% showed the structural re-rating already underway.","body_zh":"美联储于2020年3月15-16日将利率降至零，国会3月27日通过2.2万亿美元CARES法案，美国和平时期史上最大规模财政刺激点燃COVID后复苏。篮子在20个月内飙升+218%——历史最大单腿涨幅——宏观象限进入全面再通胀：油价+245.7%，铜金比+87.3%，美元-6.4%，VIX从62至16，周期+141%对防御+65%。关键在于，COVID暴露了供应链脆弱性并加速回流政策议程：两党基础设施法案（IIJA）于2021年11月签署，半导体短缺触发CHIPS法案讨论，制造业资本开支开始历史性攀升。篮子+218%对比SPY+115.2%，显示结构性重新评级已然展开。","drivers":["Fed zero rates + $2.2T CARES Act (Mar 2020) ignite reflation mega-cycle","Oil +245.7%, copper-gold +87.3%, dollar -6.4% confirm full reflation regime","COVID supply-chain exposure accelerates reshoring/onshoring policy agenda","IIJA signed Nov 2021; CHIPS Act negotiations begin; factory-build boom seeds"],"drivers_zh":["美联储零利率+2.2万亿CARES法案（2020年3月）点燃再通胀超级周期","油价+245.7%，铜金比+87.3%，美元-6.4%确认全面再通胀象限","COVID供应链暴露加速回流/本土化政策议程","IIJA 2021年11月签署；CHIPS法案谈判启动；工厂建设热潮萌芽"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Fiscal-stimulus & reshoring-policy mega-bull, +218%","title_zh":"财政刺激与回流政策大牛市，+218%","turn_id":"reshoring:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-16":{"body":"Industrials de-rated through H1 2022 in a stagflation-ish regime as inflation hit 40-year highs (CPI peaked at 9.1% in June 2022), driving the most aggressive Fed tightening cycle since Volcker. Yields surged (TLT -19.4%), the dollar ripped (DXY +13.2% — a brutal headwind for industrial multinationals) and VIX ran from 16 to 26 as growth fears mounted. China's COVID lockdowns in 2022 further disrupted supply chains. Defensives held +1.4% while cyclicals fell -15.7% in a flight-to-safety. The reshoring thesis was still nascent (CHIPS Act passed August 2022), so the group traded as plain rate-sensitive cyclicals, giving back -25.3% over eight months.","body_zh":"工业股在2022年上半年的类滞胀象限中遭去估值，因通胀触及40年高点（2022年6月CPI峰值9.1%），驱动沃尔克以来最激进的美联储紧缩周期。收益率飙升（TLT-19.4%），美元暴涨（DXY+13.2%——对工业跨国企业是残酷逆风），增长担忧加剧推动VIX从16至26。2022年中国新冠封控进一步扰乱供应链。防御板块守住+1.4%，周期跌-15.7%，呈现典型的避险轮动。回流主题尚处萌芽（CHIPS法案2022年8月通过），因此该板块作为普通利率敏感周期股交易，八个月内下跌-25.3%。","drivers":["Fed emergency tightening: CPI 9.1% forces fastest hiking cycle since Volcker","Yield surge (TLT -19.4%) and dollar spike (DXY +13.2%) compress cyclical multiples","Stagflation-ish regime: flight-to-safety, VIX 16 to 26","China COVID lockdowns 2022 compound supply chain and demand disruption"],"drivers_zh":["美联储紧急紧缩：CPI 9.1%迫使沃尔克时代以来最快加息周期","收益率飙升（TLT-19.4%）和美元冲击（DXY+13.2%）压缩周期股估值倍数","类滞胀象限：避险模式，VIX从16至26","2022年中国新冠封控复合供应链与需求扰动"],"prev_key":"2021-11-16","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Hiking-bear & dollar de-rate: stagflation kills industrials","title_zh":"加息熊市与美元驱动的去估值：类滞胀扼杀工业股","turn_id":"reshoring:peak:2021-11"},"2022-07-14":{"body":"A broad relief rally erupted off the June 2022 CPI peak as markets priced premature Fed-pause hopes and the regime shifted to reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +16.7% vs defensives +7.6%, VIX 26 to 20, dollar -1.9%). The CHIPS and Science Act was signed into law by President Biden on August 9 2022 — authorizing $52.7 billion in semiconductor manufacturing subsidies and a 25% investment tax credit — which gave the basket a structural catalyst on top of the cyclical bounce. Industrials led the sector recovery (+17.6%), and the basket surged +23.4%, outperforming in a risk-on squeeze.","body_zh":"随着市场在2022年6月CPI峰值后定价过早的美联储暂停预期，大盘纾困反弹爆发，象限转向再通胀/增长上行（周期+16.7%对防御+7.6%，VIX从26至20，美元-1.9%）。拜登总统于2022年8月9日签署《芯片与科学法案》——授权527亿美元半导体制造补贴及25%投资税收抵免——在周期性反弹之上为篮子提供了结构性催化剂。工业板块引领行业复苏（+17.6%），篮子飙升+23.4%，在风险偏好轧空中跑赢大盘。","drivers":["Premature 'Fed pause' positioning drives cyclical risk-on squeeze (VIX 26 to 20)","CHIPS Act signed Aug 9 2022: $52.7B semiconductor manufacturing subsidies","Dollar easing (DXY -1.9%) is tailwind for industrial multinationals","Reflation/growth-up quad: cyclicals outperform, industrials lead sector recovery"],"drivers_zh":["过早的'美联储暂停'定价驱动周期股风险偏好轧空（VIX从26至20）","CHIPS法案2022年8月9日签署：527亿美元半导体制造补贴","美元走弱（DXY-1.9%）对工业跨国企业形成顺风","再通胀/增长上行象限：周期股跑赢，工业引领行业复苏"],"prev_key":"2022-07-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-07-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed-pause hope bounce + CHIPS Act: reshoring thesis ignites","title_zh":"美联储暂停预期反弹与CHIPS法案：回流主题点火","turn_id":"reshoring:trough:2022-07"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"At the Jackson Hole symposium on August 26 2022, Powell delivered an unusually brief but deliberately blunt speech declaring the Fed would 'use our tools forcefully' to fight inflation and warning that restoring price stability would 'likely require maintaining a restrictive policy stance for some time.' Markets sold off sharply: TLT fell -12.7%, DXY surged +7.1%, VIX rose from 20 to 33. In a rate-spike regime, cyclicals fell -15.0% vs defensives -10.3% — the basket dropped -17.6% as the brief summer-rally optimism was unwound in less than five weeks.","body_zh":"在2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔研讨会上，鲍威尔发表异常简短但刻意强硬的演讲，宣称美联储将'有力使用工具'对抗通胀，并警告恢复价格稳定'可能需要维持限制性政策立场一段时间'。市场急剧下跌：TLT跌-12.7%，DXY飙升+7.1%，VIX从20升至33。在利率冲击象限下，周期跌-15.0%对防御-10.3%——篮子不足五周内下跌-17.6%，夏季反弹乐观情绪被完全反转。","drivers":["Jackson Hole Aug 26 2022: Powell's hawkish 'use tools forcefully' speech","Yield surge (TLT -12.7%) reprices terminal rate higher, crushes cyclical multiples","Dollar surge (DXY +7.1%) headwind for industrial multinationals","Risk-off capitulation (VIX 20 to 33): cyclicals -15.0% vs defensives -10.3%"],"drivers_zh":["2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔：鲍威尔鹰派'有力使用工具'演讲","收益率飙升（TLT-12.7%）对终端利率重新定价更高，压垮周期股估值","美元飙升（DXY+7.1%）对工业跨国企业形成逆风","避险投降（VIX从20至33）：周期-15.0%对防御-10.3%"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkish shock: rate-surge flush","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击：利率飙升性冲刷","turn_id":"reshoring:peak:2022-08"},"2022-09-27":{"body":"From the autumn-2022 final low, industrials more than doubled over 26 months — the clearest expression of the reshoring/capex super-cycle in market history, supercharged by a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation melt-up (SMH +156.4%, growth over value +35.6pp, VIX 33 to 14, dollar -6.2%). CHIPS/IRA/IIJA money began flowing into actual shovels-in-ground projects: US manufacturing construction spend surged to $234 billion annualized by 2024, a 217% increase from 2019. The 2023 AI investment narrative pulled flows into power/grid/automation names within the basket; the November-2024 Trump election crystallized the 'reshoring/tariff trade', adding a second political-tailwind leg into the November 26 2024 peak. Breadth was narrow (RSP-SPY -19.1%) but the weaker dollar was a clean tailwind.","body_zh":"从2022年秋季最终低点起，工业股在26个月内翻倍有余——市场历史上回流/资本开支超级周期最清晰的表达，被黄金分割/增长上行去通胀融涨大幅强化（半导体+156.4%，成长跑赢价值+35.6个百分点，VIX从33至14，美元-6.2%）。CHIPS/IRA/IIJA资金开始流入实际破土项目：美国制造业建设开支至2024年年化飙升至2340亿美元，较2019年增长217%。2023年AI投资叙事将资金拉入篮子内电力/电网/自动化标的；2024年11月特朗普当选确立'回流/关税交易'，在2024年11月26日峰值前追加了第二条政治顺风腿。市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY-19.1%），但走弱美元是干净的顺风。","drivers":["Goldilocks AI melt-up (SMH +156.4%, growth>value +35.6pp, VIX 33 to 14) lifts risk","Weaker dollar (DXY -6.2%) tailwind; CHIPS/IRA/IIJA funding hits real $234B/yr spend","AI narrative (2023-24) pulls power/grid/automation names within the basket higher","Trump Nov-2024 election crystallizes reshoring/tariff trade: $1.4T in announced investments"],"drivers_zh":["黄金分割AI融涨（半导体+156.4%，成长>价值+35.6个百分点，VIX从33至14）抬升风险","美元走弱（DXY-6.2%）顺风；CHIPS/IRA/IIJA资金落地为年化2340亿美元实际开支","AI叙事（2023-24年）将电力/电网/自动化标的拉升至更高","特朗普2024年11月当选确立回流/关税交易：宣布1.4万亿美元投资"],"prev_key":"2022-09-27","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-27"],"status":"exact","title":"The reshoring bull inside a goldilocks & AI melt-up, +103%","title_zh":"回流牛市置于黄金分割与AI融涨之中，+103%","turn_id":"reshoring:trough:2022-09"},"2024-11-26":{"body":"The 'Trump trade' euphoria reversed violently as the regime flipped risk-off (VIX 14 to 52, SMH -25.1%, high-beta minus low-vol -19.7%) into the April-8 2025 Liberation Day reciprocal-tariff crash. On April 2 2025 Trump invoked IEEPA to impose a minimum 10% tariff on nearly all nations plus higher reciprocal rates on 57 countries, causing the US total stock market to plunge 12.4% — its largest drop since COVID. Globalized industrial supply chains were hit hardest: input costs, retaliation risk and demand-destruction fears struck simultaneously. Despite being structural policy winners, reshoring names sold off alongside the broad market, falling -27.6% while defensives only lost -8.4% vs cyclicals -19.0%.","body_zh":"随着象限剧烈转向避险（VIX从14至52，半导体-25.1%，高贝塔减低波动-19.7%），'特朗普交易'狂热逆转，跌至2025年4月8日'解放日'对等关税崩盘。2025年4月2日特朗普援引IEEPA对几乎所有国家征收最低10%关税并对57个国家附加更高对等税率，导致美国总股票市场暴跌12.4%——COVID以来最大跌幅。全球化工业供应链受创最重：投入成本、报复风险与需求毁灭担忧同时袭击。尽管是政策的结构性赢家，回流标的仍随大盘下跌-27.6%，防御板块仅跌-8.4%，对比周期-19.0%。","drivers":["April 2 2025 Liberation Day tariffs: 10% universal + reciprocal rates trigger 12.4% market plunge","Risk-off flush: VIX 14 to 52, high-beta minus low-vol -19.7%","Industrial supply-chain disruption fears: input costs, retaliation, demand destruction","Rotation out of a two-year parabolic run; defensives relatively defend (-8.4% vs -19.0%)"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月2日解放日关税：10%普遍关税+对等税率触发市场暴跌12.4%","避险冲刷：VIX从14至52，高贝塔减低波动-19.7%","工业供应链扰动担忧：投入成本、报复、需求毁灭","从两年抛物线行情中撤离轮动；防御相对坚守（-8.4%对-19.0%）"],"prev_key":"2024-11-26","prev_key_chain":["2024-11-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Liberation Day tariff crash wipes Trump-trade euphoria","title_zh":"解放日关税崩盘抹去特朗普交易狂热","turn_id":"reshoring:peak:2024-11"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"Trump paused the reciprocal tariffs above 10% for 90 days on April 9 2025, triggering the S&P 500's largest single-day gain since 2008 (+9.52%). The basket surged +100% over 14 months off the April 8 low as an explosive risk-on regime took hold (VIX 52 to 19, SMH +255%, high-beta minus low-vol +118.3%). The tariff regime that triggered the crash simultaneously hardened the structural onshoring case: companies accelerating US production plans to avoid future tariff exposure. Electrification and AI-datacenter-power capex became a fresh secondary demand engine — the five largest hyperscalers committed $660-725 billion in capex for 2026, with power/grid/electrical-equipment names within the basket key beneficiaries. The current Phase/Topping read at position 77.4 reflects the magnitude of this run.","body_zh":"特朗普于2025年4月9日将超过10%的对等关税暂停90天，触发标普500指数2008年以来最大单日涨幅（+9.52%）。篮子自4月8日低点在14个月内飙升+100%，爆发性风险偏好象限主导（VIX从52至19，半导体+255%，高贝塔减低波动+118.3%）。触发崩盘的关税体制同时强化了结构性本土化逻辑：企业加速在美生产计划以规避未来关税敞口。电气化与AI数据中心电力资本开支成为新的次要需求引擎——五大超大规模云厂商承诺2026年资本开支6600-7250亿美元，篮子内电力/电网/电气设备标的是核心受益者。当前峰值/顶部阶段在位置77.4处反映了这轮行情的量级。","drivers":["April 9 2025 tariff-pause announcement triggers S&P +9.52% single-day recovery","Explosive risk-on (VIX 52 to 19, SMH +255%, SPHB-SPLV +118.3%) lifts all cyclicals","Tariff regime reinforces structural onshoring incentive for US manufacturing","AI/hyperscaler capex super-cycle: $660-725B in 2026 spend drives power/grid demand"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月9日关税暂停公告触发标普+9.52%单日复苏","爆发性风险偏好（VIX从52至19，半导体+255%，SPHB-SPLV+118.3%）抬升所有周期股","关税体制强化美国制造业结构性本土化激励","AI/超大规模云厂商资本开支超级周期：2026年6600-7250亿美元开支驱动电力/电网需求"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-pause recovery + AI-power capex super-cycle, +100%","title_zh":"关税暂停复苏与AI电力资本开支超级周期，+100%","turn_id":"reshoring:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Reshoring & Industrial Capex is in a Peak/Topping phase at the end of a +100% leg off the April-8 2025 Liberation Day low, with an RS rank of 11 and a cycle-gauge position of 77.4 — elevated but not yet in confirmed reversal. The current quad is reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%), exactly the macro environment where this basket thrives. Tech (+24.3%) and Energy (+21.5%) lead while Industrials ranks third at +15.8%, confirming the basket rides a broadening recovery rather than leading it. The structural bid from CHIPS/IRA/IIJA policy spend and the $600-725 billion AI-datacenter-power capex super-cycle are live demand engines. A strengthening dollar (DXY +3.4%) is a mild headwind for the basket's industrial multinationals; at rs_rank 11 in a topping phase, the risk of a policy reversal (tariff escalation, Fed-pivot fear) or simple mean-reversion from the extraordinary two-leg run since 2022 warrants close monitoring.","now_zh":"回流与工业资本开支处于峰值/顶部阶段，自2025年4月8日\"解放日\"低点完成+100%涨幅，相对强度排名第11位，周期位置计量表显示77.4——偏高但尚未确认见顶。当前宏观象限为再通胀/增长上行（周期股+11.2%对防御+6.9%，油价+19.2%，铜金比+18.3%），正是该篮子最受益的宏观环境。科技（+24.3%）和能源（+21.5%）领涨，工业排名第三（+15.8%），证实篮子搭乘广泛复苏而非引领。CHIPS/IRA/IIJA政策开支及6000-7250亿美元AI数据中心电力资本开支超级周期是活跃需求引擎。美元走强（DXY+3.4%）对篮子内工业跨国企业是温和逆风；在顶部阶段RS排名第11位，政策驱动反转（关税升级、美联储转向预期）或仅仅是自2022年以来非凡双腿行情的均值回归风险，均值得密切关注。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"business.cycle_trough.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"business.cycle_trough.v1","arch_state":"missing","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-retail":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"A 134.5% multi-year rally anchored in the longest post-war US expansion: unemployment fell from 6.7% in early 2014 to 3.7% by mid-2018, real wages grew steadily, and household net worth hit record highs on rising housing and equity prices. Low and falling rates (TLT +31.1% over the leg), collapsed oil (-26.3%), and a stronger dollar (DXY +17.7%) all compressed input costs for retailers, while consumer confidence reached 18-year highs. The goldilocks/disinflation quad (cyclicals roughly matched defensives, growth far outran value +42.5%) was ideal for high-multiple consumer names; the emerging 'retail apocalypse' narrative — Sears filed for Chapter 11 on October 15, 2018, 3,000+ store closures in 2017 — weighed on brick-and-mortar but the basket's e-commerce and off-price winners more than compensated, driving the series to a peak in September 2018.","body_zh":"长达4年半、涨幅134.5%的多年牛市，根植于战后最长扩张期：2014年初失业率6.7%，至2018年中降至3.7%，实际工资稳步增长，房价与股市双升推动家庭净值屡创新高。低且下行的利率（TLT+31.1%）、崩跌的油价（-26.3%）与走强的美元（DXY+17.7%）共同压低零售商进口成本，消费者信心升至18年高位。金发姑娘/去通胀象限（周期与防御大致持平，成长大幅跑赢价值+42.5%）为高倍数消费品种提供理想环境；“零售末日”叙事（2018年10月15日西尔斯申请第11章破产、2017年逾3000家门店关闭）拖累实体，但篮子中的电商与折扣品牌赢家充分弥补，推动该系列于2018年9月触顶。","drivers":["Post-crisis employment boom / real wage gains","Low-rate, low-oil input-cost tailwind","Strong consumer confidence, record household net worth","E-commerce/off-price winners offset brick-and-mortar decline"],"drivers_zh":["后危机就业繁荣/实际工资增长","低利率、低油价投入成本顺风","消费者信心强劲、家庭净值创纪录","电商/平价赢家抵消实体门店衰退"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-crisis goldilocks consumer expansion","title_zh":"后危机时代金发姑娘消费扩张","turn_id":"retail:trough:2014-01"},"2018-09-11":{"body":"A sharp 20.6% selloff in just over three months as the Fed's fourth rate hike of 2018 (December 19, raising the funds rate to 2.25-2.50%) and Chairman Powell's October 3 comment that the Fed was 'a long way from neutral' triggered a full risk-off rotation: VIX surged from 13 to 36, SPY fell 18.1%, and cyclicals were crushed (cyclicals -21.6% vs defensives -8.0%; Industrials -21.8%, Tech -22.0%, Energy -25.5% led the laggards) while defensives held best (Utilities -3.3%). China trade-war escalation — the September 24, 2018 tariffs on $200bn of Chinese goods at 10%, scheduled to rise to 25% in January 2019 — added recession fears, oil collapsed 38.6%, and credit spreads widened (HYG vs LQD -4.4%). Retail, as a consumer-cyclical sensitive to both a discretionary-spend slowdown and import-cost tariffs, tracked squarely with the broader cyclicals rout.","body_zh":"短短三个多月内暴跌20.6%：美联储2018年第四次加息（12月19日，联邦基金利率升至2.25-2.50%），加之鲍威尔10月3日“距中性利率还很远”的鹰派表态，触发全面避险轮动——VIX从13飙至36，SPY跌18.1%，周期板块被碾压（周期-21.6% vs 防御-8.0%；工业-21.8%、科技-22.0%、能源-25.5%领跌），防御相对抗跌（公用事业-3.3%）。中美贸易战升级——2018年9月24日对2000亿美元中国商品加征10%关税、并计划2019年1月升至25%——加剧衰退担忧，油价崩跌38.6%，信用利差走阔（HYG vs LQD -4.4%）。零售作为对可选支出放缓与进口成本关税双重敏感的消费周期品种，与大盘周期股同步崩落。","drivers":["Fed over-tightening: 4th hike Dec 2018, 'long way from neutral' hawkish shock","US-China trade war: Sept 24 tariffs on $200bn goods (10%→25%)","VIX 13→36 cyclicals rout (cyclicals -21.6% vs defensives -8.0%)","Oil -38.6%, credit spreads widen: deflation-scare quad"],"drivers_zh":["美联储过度紧缩：第四次加息、鹰派冲击","中美贸易战：9月24日对2000亿美元商品加征关税（10%→25%）","VIX 13→36，周期股溃败（周期-21.6% vs 防御-8.0%）","油价-38.6%，信用利差走阔：通缩恐慌象限"],"prev_key":"2018-09-11","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed overtightening + trade war risk-off crash","title_zh":"美联储过度紧缩+贸易战避险崩跌","turn_id":"retail:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"A 47.3% rally from the Christmas Eve 2018 low into December 2019, driven by the Fed's abrupt pivot: after the December 2018 crash, the Fed paused rate hikes in January 2019, then delivered three 'insurance' cuts (July 31, September 18, October 30, 2019) to prop up the expansion. US-China trade tensions de-escalated toward a Phase One framework and tariff truce, restoring consumer and business confidence. The reflation/growth-up quad returned (VIX 36→14, semis surged +73.4%, oil rebounded +39.1%), supporting a broad cyclical re-rating, with retail benefiting from resilient consumer spending underpinned by robust employment and real wage gains.","body_zh":"从2018年平安夜低点反弹47.3%至2019年12月，动力来自美联储的急剧转向：2018年12月崩盘后，美联储于2019年1月暂停加息，随后三次“保险性”降息（7月31日、9月18日、10月30日）支撑扩张。中美贸易摩擦降级、迈向一阶段框架与关税休战，恢复消费者与企业信心。再通胀/增长向上象限回归（VIX 36→14，半导体飙升+73.4%，油反弹+39.1%），支撑周期板块全面重新估值，零售在强劲就业与实际工资增长支撑的消费韧性中受益。","drivers":["Fed pivot: 3 insurance cuts Jul-Oct 2019","US-China Phase One trade truce / tariff de-escalation","VIX 36→14, semis +73.4%: risk-on recovery","Resilient consumer spending on robust employment"],"drivers_zh":["美联储转向：2019年7-10月三次保险性降息","中美一阶段贸易休战/关税降级","VIX 36→14，半导体+73.4%：风险偏好复苏","强劲就业支撑消费者韧性"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot + trade truce powers consumer rebound","title_zh":"美联储转向+贸易休战提振消费反弹","turn_id":"retail:trough:2018-12"},"2019-12-12":{"body":"A 32.7% plunge from December 2019 to the March 20, 2020 pandemic low, the fastest collapse in the series. The WHO declared a global pandemic on March 11, 2020; US states began lockdown orders from mid-March, closing non-essential retail entirely. Consumer spending fell sharply in March 2020 — the largest monthly drop on record at the time — and retail foot traffic collapsed. The selloff was indiscriminate and macro-driven: VIX spiked to 66, SPY fell 27.1%, oil cratered 62.1%, and cyclicals (Industrials -37.0%, Financials -38.3%, Energy -55.7%) led losses while defensives (Staples -18.8%) cushioned. The dollar surged 5.6% in a classic flight-to-safety bid.","body_zh":"从2019年12月到2020年3月20日疫情低点暴跌32.7%，为该系列史上最快崩盘。WHO于2020年3月11日宣布全球大流行；美国各州3月中旬起封锁，非必要零售全面关闭。2020年3月消费者支出单月急剧下滑，创当时最大月降幅，零售客流崩跌。抛售无差别、宏观驱动：VIX飙至66，SPY跌27.1%，油崩62.1%，周期（工业-37.0%、金融-38.3%、能源-55.7%）领跌，防御（必需品-18.8%）相对缓冲。美元急升5.6%，经典的避险抢购。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic: WHO declaration March 11, US lockdowns mid-March 2020","Non-essential retail shuttered; foot traffic collapses","Record monthly drop in consumer spending March 2020","VIX 14→66, SPY -27.1%, oil -62.1%: panic flight-to-safety"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情：WHO 3月11日宣布大流行，美国3月中旬封锁","非必要零售关闭，客流崩跌","2020年3月消费者支出创纪录月降幅","VIX 14→66，SPY-27.1%，油-62.1%：恐慌性避险"],"prev_key":"2019-12-12","prev_key_chain":["2019-12-12"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID lockdown demand destruction","title_zh":"新冠封控需求崩溃","turn_id":"retail:peak:2019-12"},"2020-03-20":{"body":"A 177.1% surge from the March 2020 pandemic low through November 2021 — the largest leg in the series by magnitude — powered by three rounds of fiscal stimulus ($1,200 CARES Act April 2020; $600 December 2020; $1,400 American Rescue Plan March 2021), accelerated e-commerce adoption, and the Fed's zero-rate/QE regime (TLT -5.6%, oil rebounded +252.3%). The quad was full-risk reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +130.6% vs defensives +57.5%, VIX 66→18, high-beta beat low-vol by 159.6%), and the dollar weakened 7.1%. Retailers with strong e-commerce platforms — Amazon, Walmart, Target, Best Buy — surged on share gains, while stimulus checks fueled goods spending as services remained shuttered.","body_zh":"从2020年3月疫情低点到2021年11月飙升177.1%——该系列幅度最大的一条腿——由三轮财政刺激（2020年4月CARES法案1200美元、2020年12月600美元、2021年3月美国救援计划1400美元）、电商渗透率加速提升和美联储零利率/QE制度（TLT-5.6%，油大反弹+252.3%）共同驱动。象限为全力再通胀/增长向上（周期+130.6% vs 防御+57.5%，VIX 66→18，高贝塔跑赢低波动159.6%），美元走弱7.1%。拥有强电商平台的零售商——亚马逊、沃尔玛、塔吉特、百思买——凭份额提升飙升，刺激支票在实体服务关闭期间推动商品消费狂飙。","drivers":["Three fiscal stimulus rounds: $1,200 + $600 + $1,400 / household","E-commerce adoption surge during lockdowns","Fed zero-rate + QE: full reflation quad, VIX 66→18","Cyclicals rip: high-beta +159.6% vs low-vol; dollar -7.1%"],"drivers_zh":["三轮财政刺激：每户1200+600+1400美元","封锁期间电商采纳率飙升","美联储零利率+QE：全力再通胀象限，VIX 66→18","周期暴涨：高贝塔+159.6% vs 低波动；美元-7.1%"],"prev_key":"2020-03-20","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Stimulus surge and e-commerce boom","title_zh":"财政刺激潮与电商爆发","turn_id":"retail:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-18":{"body":"Retail fell ~18% from the late-2021 peak as the Fed signaled the end of easy money. The tape was already rolling risk-off into a stagflation-ish quad (VIX 18→31, SMH -16.4%, value beat growth by 13.4%) with money fleeing to safety, and Discretionary led the laggards at -19.6%. The November 2021 Fed taper announcement (beginning to reduce $120bn/month of bond purchases) and the November 2021 CPI print of 6.8% — the highest since 1982 — cemented expectations for aggressive rate hikes. Multiples compressed sharply as the market braced for higher rates and slowing discretionary spend.","body_zh":"零售从2021年末高点下跌约18%，美联储释放结束宽松信号。市场已转向避险、进入类滞胀象限（VIX 18→31、SMH-16.4%、价值跑赢成长13.4%），资金奔向安全，可选消费领跌-19.6%。2021年11月美联储宣布开始缩减购债（从1200亿/月逐步下调），加之2021年11月CPI同比6.8%（1982年以来最高），强化了激进加息预期。市场为更高利率与可选消费放缓做准备时，估值骤然压缩。","drivers":["Fed taper announcement Nov 2021; CPI 6.8% YoY (40-yr high)","Risk-off de-rate: VIX 18→31, value beat growth +13.4%","Discretionary leads laggards (-19.6%)","Multiple compression on higher-rate fears"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2021年11月缩减购债；CPI同比6.8%（40年高位）","避险下调：VIX 18→31、价值跑赢成长+13.4%","可选消费领跌（-19.6%）","更高利率担忧下估值压缩"],"prev_key":"2021-11-18","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Early rate-hike de-rate","title_zh":"加息初期估值下调","turn_id":"retail:peak:2021-11"},"2022-02-23":{"body":"A ~19% rally into April 2022 as still-strong consumer demand and reopening spending temporarily outweighed rate fears. The quad stayed stagflation-ish with energy leading (+20.4%) and a rate-regime move underneath (TLT -10.7%, DXY +4.4%) — defensives actually led cyclicals (+12.7% vs +7.9%), so this was a defensive-tilted relief bounce, not a risk-on melt-up. The Russia/Ukraine invasion on February 24, 2022 briefly boosted energy names and added an inflationary shock (oil +11.6% into April), paradoxically tightening financial conditions further and shortening this bounce before the margin shock arrived in May.","body_zh":"到2022年4月约19%的反弹，仍然强劲的消费者需求与重启支出暂时盖过利率担忧。象限维持类滞胀、能源领涨（+20.4%），底层是利率/收益率上行（TLT-10.7%、DXY+4.4%）——防御实际跑赢周期（+12.7% vs +7.9%），故这是偏防御的减压而非风险偏好融涨。2022年2月24日俄乌入侵短暂提振能源股并带来通胀冲击（油价至4月+11.6%），反而进一步收紧金融条件，缩短了此次反弹的寿命，随后便迎来5月的利润率冲击。","drivers":["Stagflation quad: energy leads +20.4%, TLT -10.7%, DXY +4.4%","Russia/Ukraine invasion Feb 24 adds oil/commodity shock","Resilient consumer + reopening spending (temporary)","Defensive-tilted relief (defensives +12.7% vs cyclicals +7.9%)"],"drivers_zh":["滞胀象限：能源领涨+20.4%，TLT-10.7%，DXY+4.4%","俄乌入侵2月24日带来油价/大宗商品冲击","消费者韧性+重启支出（短暂）","偏防御的减压（防御+12.7% vs 周期+7.9%）"],"prev_key":"2022-02-23","prev_key_chain":["2022-02-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Reopening-demand bounce fades into stagflation","title_zh":"重启需求反弹渐显滞胀","turn_id":"retail:trough:2022-02"},"2022-04-20":{"body":"A brutal 23.5% plunge in a month as Walmart (May 17, 2022: adjusted EPS down ~23% YoY and a full-year profit-outlook cut, stock -11% in one day — its worst day since 1987) and Target (May 18, 2022: Q1 operating margin collapsing to ~5.3% with full-year guidance slashed to ~6% from ~8%, stock -25% in one day — its worst day in 35 years) both reported catastrophic misses — bloated post-COVID inventory, surging freight and labor costs, and weakening discretionary demand crushed margins. The macro amplified it: a stagflation-ish risk-off tape (VIX 20→29, SPY -12.4%) sent Discretionary down -22.7%, the worst sector. It was the defining retail event of the cycle and a direct precursor to the 2022 goods-disinflation unwind.","body_zh":"一个月内约23.5%的暴跌：沃尔玛（2022年5月17日：调整后EPS同比下滑约23%并下调全年利润展望，当日股价-11%，为1987年以来最差单日）与塔吉特（5月18日：Q1营业利润率骤降至约5.3%、全年指引从约8%下砍至约6%，当日股价-25%，为35年来最差）双双爆雷——疫情后膨胀的库存、飙升的运费与人工成本、走弱的可选需求压垮利润率。宏观放大了冲击：类滞胀避险环境（VIX 20→29，SPY-12.4%）令可选消费下跌-22.7%，为最差板块。这是本轮周期标志性的零售事件，也是2022年商品去通胀解压的直接前兆。","drivers":["Walmart EPS ~-23%, stock -11% May 17; Target stock -25% May 18 on margin slash","Bloated post-COVID inventory + freight/labor cost spike","Stagflation risk-off: VIX 20→29, Discretionary -22.7%","Weakening discretionary demand as stimulus exhausted"],"drivers_zh":["沃尔玛5月17日EPS约-23%、股价-11%；塔吉特5月18日股价-25%因利润率下砍","疫情后库存膨胀+运费/人工成本飙升","滞胀避险：VIX 20→29，可选消费-22.7%","刺激耗尽后可选需求走弱"],"prev_key":"2022-04-20","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-20"],"status":"exact","title":"The 2022 margin shock","title_zh":"2022年利润率冲击","turn_id":"retail:peak:2022-04"},"2022-05-20":{"body":"A 42.0% recovery from the May 2022 low through April 2023 as a goldilocks/disinflation backdrop took hold: the Fed's aggressive hikes (funds rate peaked at 5.25-5.50% by mid-2023) eventually killed goods inflation (oil -30.4%, freight costs collapsed), VIX fell from 29 to 17, and the dollar softened 1.7%. After clearing excess inventory — Target's and Walmart's inventory levels normalized through late 2022 — retailers repaired margins and the consumer proved more resilient than feared. Off-price (TJX, Ross) and discount (Walmart, Costco) names led. The tape was mega-cap narrow (RSP lagged SPY -2.9%), so this was a stock-specific grind more than a broad rip.","body_zh":"从2022年5月低点到2023年4月约42%的复苏，金发姑娘/去通胀背景确立：美联储激进加息（基金利率至2023年中见顶5.25-5.50%）最终压制商品通胀（油-30.4%，运费崩跌），VIX从29降至17，美元小幅走软1.7%。在清理过剩库存后（塔吉特与沃尔玛库存于2022年下半年逐步回归正常），零售商修复利润率，消费者比担忧更有韧性。折扣（TJX、Ross）与平价（沃尔玛、Costco）品牌领涨。市场由大盘股主导、广度狭窄（等权RSP跑输SPY-2.9%），故这更像个股驱动的爬升而非全面飙升。","drivers":["Goods disinflation: oil -30.4%, freight collapse, VIX 29→17","Inventory clearance and margin repair through late 2022","Consumer resilience; off-price/discount names lead","Narrow tape (RSP -2.9% vs SPY)"],"drivers_zh":["商品去通胀：油-30.4%，运费崩跌，VIX 29→17","库存清理与利润率修复贯穿2022年下半年","消费者韧性；折扣/平价品牌领涨","狭窄市场（RSP-2.9% vs SPY）"],"prev_key":"2022-05-20","prev_key_chain":["2022-05-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Long grind off the margin low","title_zh":"利润率低点后的长期爬升","turn_id":"retail:trough:2022-05"},"2023-04-24":{"body":"A 14.5% pullback into late October 2023 as a sharp rate-regime move (10-year Treasury yield hit ~5.0% in October 2023, the highest since 2007; TLT -18.6%, DXY +5.1%) plus the restart of federal student-loan payments (October 2023, affecting tens of millions of borrowers) and 'higher-for-longer' Fed guidance hit consumer-spending sentiment. The tape was ultra-narrow and growth-led (RSP lagged SPY -7.4%, growth beat value +11.9%), so rate-sensitive retail and defensives were left behind even as AI-driven Tech held up. Discretionary eked out +1.9% while Retail underperformed.","body_zh":"到2023年10月下旬约14.5%的回调，剧烈的利率/收益率上行（10年期美债收益率2023年10月触约5.0%，16年高位；TLT-18.6%，DXY+5.1%）叠加联邦学生贷款还款重启（2023年10月，波及数千万借款人）与“更高更久”美联储指引，打击消费支出情绪。市场极度狭窄且由AI驱动成长引领（等权RSP跑输SPY-7.4%，成长跑赢价值+11.9%），故利率敏感的零售与防御被落下，即便AI科技坚挺。可选消费仅勉强+1.9%，零售表现落后。","drivers":["10-yr yield hits ~5.0% Oct 2023 (16-yr high); TLT -18.6%, DXY +5.1%","Student-loan payments restart Oct 2023","Narrow AI-led tape: RSP -7.4% vs SPY, growth +11.9% vs value","Consumer sentiment softens on 'higher-for-longer'"],"drivers_zh":["10年期美债收益率2023年10月触约5.0%（16年高）；TLT-18.6%，DXY+5.1%","学生贷款还款2023年10月重启","AI主导狭窄市场：RSP-7.4% vs SPY，成长+11.9% vs 价值","“更高更久”压制消费者情绪"],"prev_key":"2023-04-24","prev_key_chain":["2023-04-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Mid-cycle consumer wobble on yield spike","title_zh":"周期中段消费者动摇，收益率飙升","turn_id":"retail:peak:2023-04"},"2023-10-27":{"body":"A 41.7% advance from the October 2023 low into December 2024 on a tech/semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +78.8%, VIX 21→14, growth beat value +25.2%) with yields falling (TLT +14.4%) as the Fed's September 2024 rate cut (a 50bp cut, its first since 2020) confirmed the soft-landing narrative. Discretionary surged +59.4% and the basket tracked — Walmart and Costco led on store-traffic gains and resilient consumer spending; off-price names (TJX, Ross) saw accelerating unit volumes. The tape was very narrow (RSP lagged SPY -10.4%), so megacap-heavy positions captured most of the gain.","body_zh":"从2023年10月低点到2024年12月约41.7%的上涨，搭乘科技/半导体引领的风险偏好融涨（SMH+78.8%，VIX 21→14，成长跑赢价值+25.2%），收益率下行（TLT+14.4%），美联储2024年9月降息（降50个基点，为2020年以来首次）确认软着陆叙事。可选消费飙升+59.4%，篮子同步跟涨——沃尔玛与Costco凭客流增长与消费韧性领涨；折扣品牌（TJX、Ross）单位量加速提升。市场广度极窄（等权RSP跑输SPY-10.4%），大盘股集中持仓捕获了绝大部分涨幅。","drivers":["Fed rate cut Sept 2024 (-50bp, first since 2020); soft-landing confirmed","Tech/semis led risk-on: SMH +78.8%, TLT +14.4%, VIX 21→14","Discretionary +59.4%; Walmart/Costco gain share on resilient traffic","Narrow mega-cap tape (RSP -10.4% vs SPY)"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2024年9月降息（-50个基点，2020年以来首次）；软着陆确认","科技/半导体引领风险偏好：SMH+78.8%，TLT+14.4%，VIX 21→14","可选消费+59.4%；沃尔玛/Costco客流韧性抢占份额","狭窄大盘股主导（RSP-10.4% vs SPY）"],"prev_key":"2023-10-27","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Soft-landing rally","title_zh":"软着陆反弹","turn_id":"retail:trough:2023-10"},"2024-12-11":{"body":"A 15.5% slide into the April 8, 2025 low as a risk-off flush hit (VIX 14→52, SMH -26.5%, high-beta minus low-vol -23.4%) in a slowdown/deflation-scare quad. The April 2, 2025 'Liberation Day' reciprocal tariffs (a universal 10% tariff plus country-specific rates, with China's rate escalating toward 145% by April 9) directly targeted the import-heavy cost structure of discount and dollar-store retail, threatening landed costs on foreign-sourced goods and forcing margin-guidance downgrades. Defensives cushioned (-5.2%) while cyclicals/Discretionary led the laggards (-25.1%); Walmart, Costco, and Target flagged tariff headwinds in guidance.","body_zh":"到2025年4月8日低点约15.5%的下滑，避险下泄来袭（VIX 14→52，SMH-26.5%，高贝塔-低波动-23.4%），处于放缓/通缩恐慌象限。2025年4月2日“解放日”对等关税（全面10%加各国差异化税率，中国税率至4月9日攀升至约145%）直接瞄准折扣与美元商店的进口密集成本结构，威胁海外采购商品的到岸成本，迫使企业下调利润率指引。防御缓冲（-5.2%），周期/可选消费领跌（-25.1%）；沃尔玛、Costco及塔吉特在指引中均警示关税逆风。","drivers":["April 2 2025 'Liberation Day' tariffs: 10% universal + China toward 145%","VIX 14→52 risk-off flush; high-beta minus low-vol -23.4%","Import-heavy retail wears landed-cost hit; margin guidance cut","Defensives cushion (-5.2%) vs Discretionary -25.1%"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月2日“解放日”关税：全面10%+中国攀升至约145%","VIX 14→52避险下泄；高贝塔-低波动-23.4%","进口密集零售承受到岸成本冲击；利润率指引下调","防御缓冲（-5.2%）vs 可选消费-25.1%"],"prev_key":"2024-12-11","prev_key_chain":["2024-12-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-shock selloff","title_zh":"关税冲击抛售","turn_id":"retail:peak:2024-12"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"A 47.9% rebound off the April 8, 2025 tariff low into February 2026 as tariff fears eased following the May 12, 2025 US-China Geneva truce (tariffs on Chinese goods cut from 145% to 30% for 90 days) and the consumer proved more resilient than feared — 2025 full-year retail sales grew ~4% to roughly $5.4 trillion. The reflation/growth-up tape ripped (cyclicals +41.7% vs defensives +23.3%, SMH +127.3%, DXY -5.9%), with Walmart and Costco leading on strong comparable-store sales and e-commerce growth. The rally then ran into the 2026 oil-shock inflation squeeze (Iran/Hormuz) and the basket peaked in February 2026.","body_zh":"从2025年4月8日关税低点到2026年2月约47.9%的反弹：2025年5月12日中美日内瓦休战（中国商品关税从145%降至30%、为期90天）缓解关税担忧，消费者比预期更坚挺——2025年全年零售销售增长约4%、达约5.4万亿美元。再通胀/增长向上环境大幅飙升（周期+41.7% vs 防御+23.3%，SMH+127.3%，DXY-5.9%），沃尔玛与Costco凭强劲同店销售与电商增长领涨。随后反弹撞上2026年油价冲击（伊朗/霍尔木兹）通胀挤压，篮子于2026年2月见顶。","drivers":["US-China Geneva truce May 12 2025: China tariffs 145%→30%","Reflation tape: SMH +127.3%, DXY -5.9%, cyclicals lead +41.7%","Consumer beats fears: 2025 retail sales ~+4% to ~$5.4trn","Rally caps as 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock inflates CPI"],"drivers_zh":["中美2025年5月12日日内瓦休战：中国关税145%→30%","再通胀环境：SMH+127.3%，DXY-5.9%，周期领涨+41.7%","消费者超预期：2025年零售销售约+4%至约5.4万亿","反弹撞上2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹油价冲击拉升CPI"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-tariff relief recovery","title_zh":"关税后减压复苏","turn_id":"retail:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Retail is at a Trough/Bottoming phase (pos 15.6, RS rank 39 — bottom tertile of all series), printing a BUY signal and still above the 200-day moving average. The macro quad is reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%), which is structurally a cyclical tailwind, but two cross-currents cap the basket: (1) a firmer dollar (DXY +3.4%) raises import costs for the goods-heavy retailers that anchor this basket; and (2) the 2026 Iran/Hormuz oil shock pushed gasoline and CPI higher, squeezing the real purchasing power of the lower- and middle-income households that drive Walmart, Costco, and dollar-store traffic. Breadth is broadening (RSP beat SPY +2.9%) and high-beta leads low-vol (+20.7%), but Discretionary still lags at -5.2%, signaling that the rotation has not yet fully arrived for this sub-sector. The setup rhymes with prior reflation-trough entries where the consumer held up better than feared before eventually re-rating higher.","now_zh":"零售处于波谷/筑底阶段（位置15.6，RS排名39，落入末三分之一），触发买入信号且仍在200日均线上方。宏观象限为再通胀/增长向上（周期板块+11.2% vs 防御+6.9%，油+19.2%，铜金+18.3%），理应形成顺周期顺风，但两股逆流压制篮子：（1）美元走强（DXY+3.4%）推高以商品为主的零售商进口成本；（2）2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹油价冲击拉高汽油与CPI，挤压沃尔玛、Costco及折扣店中低收入核心客群的实际购买力。市场广度扩张（RSP跑赢SPY+2.9%），高贝塔领先低波动（+20.7%），但可选消费仍落后-5.2%，显示轮动尚未完全触及该子板块。当前形态与过往再通胀底部入场点高度吻合，届时消费者表现往往好于预期，最终带动重新估值。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-robotics_automation":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"The ROBO ETF (launched Oct 2013) rode an 18-month quality/growth melt-up where Healthcare (+37.9%) and Tech (+26.3%) led while Energy collapsed (-36.5%) and the DXY surged 18.2% on oil-deflation fears and a post-taper Fed. Falling yields (TLT +19.7%) supported long-duration industrial-tech multiples, pulling the basket (+21%) slightly ahead of SPY (+18.7%) with semis running much harder (+41%). The slowdown/deflation-scare quad meant this was a top-down regime tailwind — quality growth leadership — rather than any automation-specific catalyst, and cyclicals (13.2%) notably trailed defensives (25.9%).","body_zh":"ROBO ETF（2013 年 10 月上市）搭乘 18 个月质量/成长融涨行情——医疗（+37.9%）与科技（+26.3%）领涨，能源崩跌（-35.6%），DXY 因油价通缩恐慌与后缩表美联储飙升 18.2%。收益率下行（TLT +19.7%）支撑长久期工业科技估值倍数，篮子（+21%）略跑赢 SPY（+18.7%），半导体大幅领先（+41%）。放缓/通缩恐慌象限意味着这是自上而下的 regime 顺风——质量成长领导——而非自动化专属催化剂，周期股（13.2%）明显落后防御（25.9%）。","drivers":["Oil deflation scare (Brent -36.5%) drives slowdown quad","Post-taper dollar surge (DXY +18.2%) crushes commodity sectors","Falling yields (TLT +19.7%) support long-duration growth multiples","Tech/semis-led quality growth melt-up (SMH +41%)"],"drivers_zh":["油价通缩恐慌（布伦特 -36.5%）驱动放缓象限","后缩表美元飙升（DXY +18.2%）压垮商品板块","收益率下行（TLT +19.7%）支撑长久期成长倍数","科技/半导体引领质量成长融涨（SMH +41%）"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Deflation-scare melt-up, quality leads cyclicals","title_zh":"通缩恐慌中的融涨，质量领先周期","turn_id":"robotics_automation:trough:2014-01"},"2015-06-03":{"body":"China's yuan devaluation on Aug 11 2015 and the subsequent 'Black Monday' (Aug 24, Dow -1,000 points at open) crystallized a global slowdown/deflation-scare selloff — the basket fell 23.8% as VIX spiked 14→28. Defensives (Utilities, Staples) outperformed sharply (avg -5.4% vs cyclicals -13.7%) in classic risk-off rotation, with Energy (-22.3%) and Materials (-22.6%) hardest hit by commodity deflation. Robotics/automation amplified the cyclical drawdown via its industrial-tech exposure, with credit spreads widening (HYG-LQD -7.7%) confirming the severity of the risk-off move.","body_zh":"2015 年 8 月 11 日人民币贬值与随后的'黑色星期一'（8 月 24 日，道指开盘跌 1000 点）引发全球放缓/通缩恐慌抛售——篮子下跌 23.8%，VIX 由 14 飙至 28。防御性板块（公用事业、必需品）大幅跑赢（均值 -5.4% 对周期 -13.7%），呈现经典避险轮动；能源（-22.3%）与材料（-22.6%）受商品通缩冲击最重。机器人/自动化通过工业科技敞口放大周期回撤，信用利差走阔（HYG-LQD -7.7%）印证避险力度。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation Aug 11 2015 triggers global contagion fears","Oil and commodity deflation (oil -25.5%, copper-gold -13.5%) deepens slowdown quad","VIX spike 14 to 28 with flight-to-safety into Utilities/Staples","Credit spreads blow out (HYG-LQD -7.7%) validating macro risk-off"],"drivers_zh":["2015 年 8 月 11 日人民币贬值触发全球传导恐慌","油价与商品通缩（油 -25.5%、铜金比 -13.5%）加深放缓象限","VIX 由 14 飙至 28，避险资金流向公用/必需品","信用利差扩大（HYG-LQD -7.7%）验证宏观避险"],"prev_key":"2015-06-03","prev_key_chain":["2015-06-03"],"status":"exact","title":"China shock and global deflation selloff","title_zh":"中国冲击与全球通缩抛售","turn_id":"robotics_automation:peak:2015-06"},"2015-09-28":{"body":"The basket delivered +198% over three years, driven by a powerful reflation/growth-up regime (cyclicals +66.6% vs defensives +39.3%, VIX 28→12, SMH +132.5%) anchored by the 2016 Trump election (corporate tax cut expectations), synchronized global growth through 2017-18, and industrial-tech re-rating as factory automation orders accelerated in the early-AI and connected-factory era. Growth massively outran value (+27.2) and high-beta led, with credit spreads compressing (+12.6%) and oil recovering +55.3%, while narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -7.4%) showed the run was mega-cap and tech-concentrated.","body_zh":"篮子三年累涨 +198%，由强劲再通胀/增长上行 regime（周期 +66.6% 对防御 +39.3%、VIX 28→12、半导体 +132.5%）驱动，2016 年特朗普当选（企业减税预期）、2017-18 年全球同步增长、工厂自动化订单加速及早期 AI 与互联工厂时代的工业科技重估共同支撑。成长大幅跑赢价值（+27.2），高贝塔领涨，信用利差压缩（+12.6%），油价回升 +55.3%，而市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY -7.4%）显示行情集中于大市值与科技。","drivers":["Reflation/growth-up regime (cyclicals +66.6%, VIX 28 to 12, SMH +132.5%)","Trump election Nov 2016 and 2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (corporate tax to 21%)","Synchronized global growth 2016-2017 lifts industrial automation orders","Growth>value (+27.2) and high-beta leadership amplifies the basket"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀/增长上行 regime（周期 +66.6%、VIX 28→12、半导体 +132.5%）","2016 年特朗普当选与 2017 年《减税与就业法案》（企业税降至 21%）","2016-2017 年全球同步增长提振工业自动化订单","成长>价值（+27.2）与高贝塔领涨放大篮子"],"prev_key":"2015-09-28","prev_key_chain":["2015-09-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Three-year bull: reflation, tax cuts, semis rip","title_zh":"三年牛市：再通胀、减税、半导体爆拉","turn_id":"robotics_automation:trough:2015-09"},"2018-09-14":{"body":"The basket fell 25.5% in just 14 weeks as two catalysts converged: the Trump administration's Sep 2018 announcement of 25% tariffs on $200B of Chinese imports hit the industrial-tech supply chain directly, and the Fed's Dec 19 rate hike (funds rate to 2.25-2.5%) with a still-hawkish balance-sheet path sent VIX from 12 to 36. Tech and Industrials (the basket's core exposure) were the worst-hit sectors (-22.5% and -22.8% respectively), while defensives held far better (-8.6% avg) — a clean flight-to-safety rotation, not sector-specific trouble.","body_zh":"篮子在 14 周内下跌 25.5%，两大催化剂叠加：特朗普政府 2018 年 9 月宣布对 2000 亿美元中国进口征收 25% 关税，直接冲击工业科技供应链；美联储 12 月 19 日加息（至 2.25-2.5%）并维持鹰派缩表路径，VIX 由 12 飙至 36。科技与工业（篮子核心敞口）是受创最重的板块（分别 -22.5% 和 -22.8%），防御守住（均值 -8.6%）——干净的避险轮动，而非板块特有问题。","drivers":["US-China trade war escalation: $200B tariff list Sep 2018 hits supply chains","Fed Dec 2018 rate hike and hawkish balance-sheet path spooks markets (VIX 12 to 36)","Flight-to-safety: defensives -8.6% vs cyclicals -22% confirms risk-off","High-beta growth de-rate: growth-value -4.4, SMH -22.7%"],"drivers_zh":["美中贸易战升级：2018 年 9 月 2000 亿关税单冲击供应链","美联储 2018 年 12 月加息与鹰派缩表路径令市场恐慌（VIX 12→36）","避险轮动：防御 -8.6% 对周期 -22% 确认风险规避","高贝塔成长去估值：成长-价值 -4.4、半导体 -22.7%"],"prev_key":"2018-09-14","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade war plus Fed over-hike crash","title_zh":"贸易战叠加美联储过度加息崩盘","turn_id":"robotics_automation:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"Fed Chair Powell's Jan 4 2019 'patient and flexible' pivot — abandoning the prior hawkish pace — combined with a G20 Dec 2018 US-China trade truce sparked a +41.7% rebound in four months. VIX collapsed 36→13, Tech (+37.3%) and Industrials (+30.9%) recovered sharpest among sectors, and semis ripped +47.7% as the cyclical/growth rotation reasserted (cyclicals +28.4% vs defensives +12.9%). The basket's concentrated exposure to industrial-tech and its high beta meant it leveraged the regime reversal more than 1.6x the SPY return of 25.3%.","body_zh":"美联储主席鲍威尔 2019 年 1 月 4 日'耐心与灵活'转向——放弃此前的鹰派节奏——叠加 2018 年 12 月二十国集团美中贸易休战，触发四个月 +41.7% 的反弹。VIX 崩跌 36→13，科技（+37.3%）与工业（+30.9%）板块反弹最猛，半导体飙升 +47.7%，周期/成长轮动重归主导（周期 +28.4% 对防御 +12.9%）。篮子集中于工业科技且贝塔较高，令其以超过 1.6 倍的 SPY 收益（25.3%）放大了 regime 逆转。","drivers":["Fed Powell 'patient/flexible' pivot Jan 4 2019 ends rate-hike fears","G20 Dec 2018 US-China trade truce removes tariff tail-risk","Risk-on regime: VIX 36 to 13, Tech/Industrials recover sharpest","Cyclicals +28.4% vs defensives +12.9%: clean reflation rotation"],"drivers_zh":["美联储鲍威尔 2019 年 1 月 4 日'耐心/灵活'转向消除加息恐慌","2018 年 12 月二十国集团美中贸易休战解除关税尾部风险","风险偏好 regime：VIX 36→13，科技/工业反弹最猛","周期 +28.4% 对防御 +12.9%：清晰的再通胀轮动"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell pivot and trade truce fuel risk-on rip","title_zh":"鲍威尔转向与贸易休战驱动风险偏好暴拉","turn_id":"robotics_automation:trough:2018-12"},"2019-04-24":{"body":"Trump's May 10 2019 escalation — raising tariffs on $200B of Chinese goods from 10% to 25% — flipped the regime back to slowdown/deflation-scare in a 40-day selloff. VIX rose 13→19 while defensives (Real Estate +2.3%, Utilities +1.8%) held positive as cyclicals fell -8%. Tech (-10.5%) and semis (-18%) bore the brunt alongside Energy (-11.6%), consistent with the trade-war-sensitive supply-chain exposure of automation hardware. TLT rallied +7.6% as markets priced a growth scare and potential Fed cuts.","body_zh":"特朗普 2019 年 5 月 10 日将 2000 亿美元中国商品关税从 10% 升至 25%，40 天内将 regime 重新拉回放缓/通缩恐慌。VIX 升至 19，防御性板块（房地产 +2.3%、公用 +1.8%）守住正收益，周期股跌 -8%。科技（-10.5%）与半导体（-18%）承压最重，能源（-11.6%）亦受拖累，与自动化硬件的贸易战敏感供应链敞口一致。TLT 反弹 +7.6%，市场定价增长恐慌与潜在降息。","drivers":["May 10 2019 tariff escalation: 10% to 25% on $200B Chinese goods hits automation hardware","Flight-to-safety: defensives flat (+0.4%) vs cyclicals -8%, VIX 13 to 19","Semis -18% confirms tech-supply-chain damage","Yield drop (TLT +7.6%) pricing Fed cuts and growth scare"],"drivers_zh":["2019 年 5 月 10 日关税升级：2000 亿美元商品从 10% 升至 25% 冲击自动化硬件","避险轮动：防御平盘（+0.4%）对周期 -8%，VIX 13→19","半导体 -18% 确认科技供应链受损","收益率下行（TLT +7.6%）定价降息与增长恐慌"],"prev_key":"2019-04-24","prev_key_chain":["2019-04-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade war re-escalation, tech/industrials flush","title_zh":"贸易战再度升级，科技/工业遭冲刷","turn_id":"robotics_automation:peak:2019-04"},"2019-06-03":{"body":"Three Fed 'insurance' rate cuts (Jul 31, Sep 18, Oct 30 2019) and growing confidence in a US-China Phase 1 trade deal drove a 7-month tech/semis-led rally (+35.7%) into January 2020. The regime remained a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (copper-gold -15.6%), but the Tech (+40%) and semis (+53.4%) melt-up dominated with growth>value at +10.8. Narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -4.5%) confirmed a mega-cap-driven tape, and the basket caught the bid as an industrial-tech proxy in a falling-rate environment (TLT +7.8%).","body_zh":"美联储三次'预防性'降息（2019 年 7 月 31 日、9 月 18 日、10 月 30 日）与美中第一阶段贸易协议信心增强，驱动 7 个月科技/半导体领涨反弹（+35.7%）至 2020 年 1 月。象限仍处放缓/通缩恐慌（铜金比 -15.6%），但科技（+40%）与半导体（+53.4%）融涨主导，成长>价值 +10.8。市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY -4.5%）确认大盘股驱动行情，篮子在降息环境（TLT +7.8%）中作为工业科技代理赢得买盘。","drivers":["Fed 'insurance' cuts Jul/Sep/Oct 2019 remove recession tail-risk and support long-duration","US-China Phase 1 deal momentum lifts automation supply-chain outlook","Tech/semis-led melt-up (SMH +53.4%, growth>value +10.8) in a narrow tape","Falling yields (TLT +7.8%) support long-duration industrial-tech multiples"],"drivers_zh":["美联储'预防性'降息（2019 年 7/9/10 月）消除衰退尾部风险并支撑长久期","美中第一阶段协议进展提振自动化供应链前景","科技/半导体引领融涨（半导体 +53.4%、成长>价值 +10.8），行情集中","收益率下行（TLT +7.8%）支撑长久期工业科技倍数"],"prev_key":"2019-06-03","prev_key_chain":["2019-06-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed insurance cuts revive risk-on through Jan 2020","title_zh":"美联储预防性降息提振风险偏好至 2020 年 1 月","turn_id":"robotics_automation:trough:2019-06"},"2020-01-23":{"body":"The COVID-19 pandemic triggered the fastest bear market in history: the basket fell 39.2% in 59 days as VIX exploded from 13 to 62 and the dollar surged (DXY +4.9%). Industrials (-41.4%) and Financials (-42.1%) were the worst GICS sectors — worse than even the defensive sectors — reflecting the direct demand destruction to factory automation, machine tool, and capital-equipment buyers as global manufacturing collapsed. Credit markets seized (HYG-LQD -10.1%), oil crashed -58%, and the basket's automation-capex thesis faced an existential demand shock.","body_zh":"新冠疫情引发史上最快熊市：篮子在 59 天内跌 39.2%，VIX 由 13 飙至 62，美元飙升（DXY +4.9%）。工业（-41.4%）与金融（-42.1%）是表现最差的 GICS 板块——甚至差于防御性板块——反映全球制造业崩溃对工厂自动化、机床及资本设备买家的直接需求破坏。信贷市场冻结（HYG-LQD -10.1%），油价崩跌 -58%，篮子的自动化资本开支主题面临存亡级需求冲击。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic triggers fastest bear market in history (VIX 13 to 62)","Industrial demand destruction: Industrials sector -41.4%, capital-equipment orders collapse","Dollar surge (DXY +4.9%) adds headwind to multinational hardware businesses","Credit markets seize (HYG-LQD -10.1%), oil -58%, global manufacturing collapse"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情引发史上最快熊市（VIX 13→62）","工业需求摧毁：工业板块 -41.4%，资本设备订单崩塌","美元飙升（DXY +4.9%）对跨国硬件业务再添逆风","信贷市场冻结（HYG-LQD -10.1%），油价 -58%，全球制造业崩溃"],"prev_key":"2020-01-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-01-23"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash, industrials hit hardest","title_zh":"新冠疫情崩盘，工业板块受创最重","turn_id":"robotics_automation:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The March 23 2020 Fed QE-unlimited backstop and the $2.2T CARES Act ignited a +195% bull run to Dec 2021. The basket benefited from two tailwinds simultaneously: a massive cyclical/high-beta reflation (cyclicals +140.7% vs defensives +74.2%, VIX 62→18, SMH +205.8%, high-beta SPHB-SPLV +145%) and a pandemic-accelerated structural demand for automation as companies sought to reduce labor dependence. A weaker dollar (DXY -6.2%) aided the multinationals, and fiscal stimulus including the CHIPS Act groundwork supercharged capex expectations.","body_zh":"2020 年 3 月 23 日美联储无限量 QE 与 2.2 万亿美元 CARES 法案点燃 +195% 的牛市至 2021 年 12 月。篮子同时受益两大顺风：大规模周期/高贝塔再通胀（周期 +140.7% 对防御 +74.2%、VIX 62→18、半导体 +205.8%、高贝塔 SPHB-SPLV +145%），以及疫情加速的自动化结构性需求（企业寻求减少劳动力依赖）。美元走弱（DXY -6.2%）利好跨国企业，财政刺激（含芯片法案前期准备）大幅提振资本开支预期。","drivers":["Fed QE-unlimited (Mar 23 2020) and $2.2T CARES Act backstop ignite reflation","Pandemic accelerates structural automation demand (contactless manufacturing, labor substitution)","Explosive high-beta cyclical rally (VIX 62 to 18, SMH +205.8%, SPHB-SPLV +145%)","Weaker dollar (DXY -6.2%) tailwind for industrial multinationals; fiscal capex boost"],"drivers_zh":["美联储无限量 QE（2020 年 3 月 23 日）与 2.2 万亿美元 CARES 法案点燃再通胀","疫情加速自动化结构性需求（无接触制造、劳动力替代）","高贝塔周期爆发性反弹（VIX 62→18、半导体 +205.8%、SPHB-SPLV +145%）","美元走弱（DXY -6.2%）利好工业跨国企业；财政资本开支提振"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID recovery: fiscal bazooka and automation boom","title_zh":"新冠复苏：财政大炮与自动化需求爆发","turn_id":"robotics_automation:trough:2020-03"},"2021-12-27":{"body":"The basket fell 28.6% from late-Dec 2021 to May 2022 as the Fed telegraphed then began its fastest rate-hike cycle since 1980 (first hike March 16 2022). TLT fell 20.3% and DXY surged 8.1%, a double-blow to long-duration industrial-tech multiples in a stagflation-ish regime (VIX 18→33). As high-multiple growth names, robotics/automation were hit alongside semis (-30.6%) and the broader growth-value collapse (-18.1%), while Energy (+40%) and Utilities/Staples held in the stagflation environment — defensives averaged -2.5% vs cyclicals -8.3%.","body_zh":"篮子从 2021 年 12 月底至 2022 年 5 月下跌 28.6%，美联储先是预告、随后启动 1980 年以来最快的加息周期（首次加息 2022 年 3 月 16 日）。TLT 下跌 20.3%，DXY 飙升 8.1%，对类滞胀 regime（VIX 18→33）下的长久期工业科技倍数形成双重打击。作为高倍数成长股，机器人/自动化与半导体（-30.6%）一同遭受成长-价值大崩塌（-18.1%），而能源（+40%）及防御板块在滞胀环境中守住（防御均值 -2.5% 对周期 -8.3%）。","drivers":["Fed hawkish pivot: fastest rate-hike cycle since 1980 (first hike Mar 16 2022)","Yields surge (TLT -20.3%) and dollar rips (DXY +8.1%) crush long-duration multiples","Stagflation-ish regime: VIX 18 to 33, growth-value collapses -18.1%","Ukraine war Feb 2022 adds commodity shock (oil +39.9%) and supply-chain stress"],"drivers_zh":["美联储鹰派转向：1980 年以来最快加息周期（2022 年 3 月 16 日首次加息）","收益率飙升（TLT -20.3%）+美元暴涨（DXY +8.1%）压垮长久期倍数","类滞胀 regime：VIX 18→33，成长-价值崩塌 -18.1%","2022 年 2 月俄乌战争叠加商品冲击（油价 +39.9%）与供应链压力"],"prev_key":"2021-12-27","prev_key_chain":["2021-12-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed hawkish pivot, rate-driven growth de-rate","title_zh":"美联储鹰派转向，利率驱动成长股去估值","turn_id":"robotics_automation:peak:2021-12"},"2022-05-11":{"body":"The basket bounced +26% from the May 2022 low into mid-August in a brief goldilocks/growth-up regime as growth led value (+7.8), VIX compressed 33→20, and high-beta outperformed (SPHB-SPLV +12.6%). The catalyst was premature market speculation that the Fed would slow its hiking pace after back-to-back 75bp hikes, combined with oversold mean-reversion in high-multiple industrials and tech. This was a positioning-driven bounce, not a fundamental turn — the dollar was still slightly up (+1.7%) and bonds barely moved (TLT -1.5%).","body_zh":"篮子从 2022 年 5 月低点反弹 +26% 至 8 月中，进入短暂的 goldilocks/增长上行 regime——成长跑赢价值（+7.8）、VIX 压缩 33→20、高贝塔跑赢（SPHB-SPLV +12.6%）。催化剂是市场过早预期美联储在连续两次 75bp 加息后将放缓步伐，叠加高倍数工业/科技的超卖均值回归。这是仓位驱动的反弹而非基本面转折——美元仍略强（+1.7%），债券几乎未动（TLT -1.5%）。","drivers":["Premature Fed pause speculation after June/July 75bp hikes drives growth-led bounce","Growth-led risk-on (growth>value +7.8, VIX 33 to 20, SMH +11.7%)","High-beta mean-reversion (SPHB-SPLV +12.6%) off oversold conditions","Discretionary/Tech sectors lead (17%, 13.7%); defensives lag confirming risk-on"],"drivers_zh":["6/7 月连续 75bp 加息后市场过早押注美联储暂停驱动成长领涨反弹","成长引领风险偏好（成长>价值 +7.8、VIX 33→20、半导体 +11.7%）","高贝塔超卖均值回归（SPHB-SPLV +12.6%）","可选消费/科技板块领涨（17%、13.7%）；防御落后确认风险偏好"],"prev_key":"2022-05-11","prev_key_chain":["2022-05-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Summer relief rally on premature Fed pivot hopes","title_zh":"过早的美联储转向预期驱动夏季纾困反弹","turn_id":"robotics_automation:trough:2022-05"},"2022-08-12":{"body":"Powell's Aug 25 2022 Jackson Hole speech — warning of 'some pain' and a 'lengthy period of restrictive policy' — ended the summer bounce. Stocks plunged 3%+ that day, and the basket fell 20.8% from Aug 12 to Sept 27 as the S&P 500 ultimately crashed 13% from the speech. TLT fell 12.5%, DXY surged 8.0%, and VIX re-escalated 20→33 in a slowdown/deflation-scare regime where defensives (Health, Staples, Utilities: avg -9.2%) held far better than cyclicals (-14.7%), confirming this was a pure macro duration/dollar shock rather than any automation fundamental.","body_zh":"鲍威尔 2022 年 8 月 25 日杰克逊霍尔演讲——警告'或有阵痛'与'长期限制性政策'——终结夏季反弹。当日股市急跌逾 3%，篮子从 8 月 12 日至 9 月 27 日下跌 20.8%，标普 500 最终从演讲后崩跌 13%。TLT 跌 12.5%，DXY 飙升 8.0%，VIX 再度攀升 20→33，处于放缓/通缩恐慌 regime，防御性板块（医疗、必需品、公用事业均值 -9.2%）大幅跑赢周期（-14.7%），确认这是纯粹的宏观久期/美元冲击而非自动化基本面问题。","drivers":["Powell's Aug 25 2022 Jackson Hole 'pain' speech ends the bounce (S&P -13% after speech)","Yields surge again (TLT -12.5%): rate path re-re-priced higher","Dollar surge (DXY +8.0%) crushes industrial multinationals","VIX 20 to 33: slowdown quad with defensives outperforming cyclicals"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔 2022 年 8 月 25 日杰克逊霍尔'阵痛'演讲终结反弹（标普 -13%）","收益率再度飙升（TLT -12.5%）：利率路径再次上调","美元飙升（DXY +8.0%）压垮工业跨国企业","VIX 20→33：放缓象限，防御跑赢周期"],"prev_key":"2022-08-12","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkish reset, yields and dollar surge","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派重置，收益率与美元齐飙","turn_id":"robotics_automation:peak:2022-08"},"2022-09-27":{"body":"ChatGPT launched Nov 30 2022, igniting the AI narrative; Nvidia's blowout May 24 2023 earnings cemented the re-rating. The basket rallied +63% from the autumn-2022 low to July 2023 in a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation regime (VIX 33→14, SMH +69.6%, growth>value +11.6, DXY -10.7%). Robotics/automation was re-rated as a near-AI beneficiary (factory intelligence, collaborative robotics) while the CHIPS Act (Aug 2022) and IRA (Aug 2022) reshoring-capex cycle supercharged order-book expectations. Narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -5.0%) confirmed a mega-cap/tech-driven tape.","body_zh":"ChatGPT 于 2022 年 11 月 30 日上线，点燃 AI 叙事；英伟达 2023 年 5 月 24 日业绩大超预期巩固重估。篮子从 2022 年秋季低点至 2023 年 7 月上涨 +63%，处于 goldilocks/增长上行去通胀 regime（VIX 33→14、半导体 +69.6%、成长>价值 +11.6、DXY -10.7%）。机器人/自动化被重估为近 AI 受益者（工厂智能、协作机器人），芯片法案（2022 年 8 月）与《通胀削减法案》（2022 年 8 月）驱动的回流资本开支周期大幅提振订单簿预期。市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY -5.0%）确认大市值/科技驱动行情。","drivers":["ChatGPT launch Nov 2022 and Nvidia May 2023 earnings ignite AI re-rating","Goldilocks disinflation: VIX 33 to 14, SMH +69.6%, growth>value +11.6","Dollar collapse (DXY -10.7%) major tailwind for industrial multinationals","CHIPS Act and IRA reshoring cycle boosts automation capex narrative"],"drivers_zh":["ChatGPT 上线（2022 年 11 月）与英伟达业绩（2023 年 5 月）点燃 AI 重估","Goldilocks 去通胀：VIX 33→14、半导体 +69.6%、成长>价值 +11.6","美元崩跌（DXY -10.7%）为工业跨国企业提供重大顺风","芯片法案与 IRA 回流周期提振自动化资本开支叙事"],"prev_key":"2022-09-27","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-27"],"status":"exact","title":"ChatGPT-AI rally; reshoring and dollar collapse","title_zh":"ChatGPT-AI 反弹；回流制造与美元崩跌","turn_id":"robotics_automation:trough:2022-09"},"2023-07-31":{"body":"The 10-year Treasury yield hit 5.029% on Oct 19 2023 — highest since July 2007 — driven by Powell's 'higher for longer' stance and resilient labor data. TLT fell 13.9% and DXY strengthened 4.9%, crushing long-duration growth (SPHB-SPLV -13.6%) and the basket (-22.2%) disproportionately. The selloff was unusually regime-neutral: defensives (-8.6%) barely outperformed cyclicals (-8.0%), meaning this was a pure duration event rather than a flight-to-safety rotation — high-multiple industrial-tech names bore the brunt of the discount-rate shock.","body_zh":"10 年期美债收益率于 2023 年 10 月 19 日触及 5.029%——2007 年 7 月以来最高——由鲍威尔'更高更久'立场与韧性劳动力数据驱动。TLT 下跌 13.9%，DXY 走强 4.9%，对长久期成长（SPHB-SPLV -13.6%）与篮子（-22.2%）形成超额冲击。此次抛售的 regime 中性度异常：防御（-8.6%）几乎未跑赢周期（-8.0%），说明这是纯粹的久期事件而非避险轮动——高倍数工业科技名称承受了贴现率冲击的主要压力。","drivers":["10-year yield hits 5% (Oct 19 2023), highest since 2007 — 'higher for longer' repricing","TLT -13.9% and DXY +4.9% form a double duration/dollar headwind","High-beta de-rate (SPHB-SPLV -13.6%): long-duration multiples compressed across growth names","Profit-taking after the +63% AI-rally leg into overbought conditions"],"drivers_zh":["10 年期收益率至 5%（2023 年 10 月 19 日），2007 年以来最高——'更高更久'重新定价","TLT -13.9% 与 DXY +4.9% 形成久期/美元双重逆风","高贝塔去估值（SPHB-SPLV -13.6%）：成长股长久期倍数全面压缩","在 +63% AI 反弹腿段后超买获利了结"],"prev_key":"2023-07-31","prev_key_chain":["2023-07-31"],"status":"exact","title":"10-year to 5%, rate-duration selloff hits growth","title_zh":"10 年期收益率至 5%，利率久期抛售打压成长","turn_id":"robotics_automation:peak:2023-07"},"2023-11-01":{"body":"The Dec 13 2023 FOMC pivot — the Fed signaled rate cuts for 2024 — combined with disinflation data sparked a goldilocks/growth-up rally: TLT gained 13.6%, VIX dropped 17→13, and semis exploded +93.4% as growth>value reached +16.7. The basket (+48%) trailed only the ultra-concentrated semis; the basket caught a double bid from reshoring-capex (CHIPS Act + IRA manufacturing projects accelerating) and the emerging 'physical AI / humanoid robot' narrative (Tesla Optimus, Figure AI announcements). Narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -7.5%) showed the tape remained mega-cap-tech-driven.","body_zh":"2023 年 12 月 13 日 FOMC 转向——美联储预告 2024 年降息——叠加去通胀数据点燃 goldilocks/增长上行反弹：TLT 涨 13.6%，VIX 降至 13，半导体爆涨 +93.4%，成长>价值 +16.7。篮子（+48%）仅落后于高度集中的半导体；获双重买盘：回流资本开支（芯片法案+IRA 制造业项目加速）与新兴'实体 AI/人形机器人'叙事（特斯拉 Optimus、Figure AI 发布）。市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY -7.5%）显示行情仍为大市值科技驱动。","drivers":["Dec 2023 Fed pivot: signals 2024 rate cuts, unlocking long-duration bid (TLT +13.6%)","Goldilocks disinflation: VIX 17 to 13, SMH +93.4%, growth>value +16.7","Physical AI / humanoid narrative (Tesla Optimus, Figure AI) adds thematic premium","Reshoring capex acceleration (CHIPS/IRA projects underway) supports order-book outlook"],"drivers_zh":["2023 年 12 月美联储转向：预告 2024 年降息，解锁长久期买盘（TLT +13.6%）","Goldilocks 去通胀：VIX 17→13、半导体 +93.4%、成长>价值 +16.7","实体 AI/人形机器人叙事（特斯拉 Optimus、Figure AI）添加主题溢价","回流资本开支加速（芯片法案/IRA 项目推进）支撑订单前景"],"prev_key":"2023-11-01","prev_key_chain":["2023-11-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Soft-landing, Fed pivot, physical-AI bid rally","title_zh":"软着陆、美联储转向、实体 AI 买盘推动反弹","turn_id":"robotics_automation:trough:2023-11"},"2024-07-16":{"body":"The Bank of Japan's July 31 2024 rate hike (to 0.25%, first since 2007) triggered a massive yen-carry-trade unwind that sent the Nikkei down 12% in a single day and VIX to 65 (highest since COVID). The US basket fell 16.3% in three weeks as defensives held flat (+0.9%) while cyclicals fell 8.1% and high-beta (SPHB-SPLV -14.6%) and semis (-22.7%) bore the brunt. This was a pure positioning shock — US weak-jobs data on Aug 2 accelerated the panic — and the basket's high beta meant it amplified the move into the Aug 7 low.","body_zh":"日本央行 2024 年 7 月 31 日加息至 0.25%（2007 年以来首次）触发大规模日元套利平仓，日经指数单日暴跌 12%，VIX 飙至 65（新冠以来最高）。篮子在三周内下跌 16.3%，防御持平（+0.9%），周期跌 8.1%，高贝塔（SPHB-SPLV -14.6%）与半导体（-22.7%）首当其冲。这是纯粹的仓位冲击——8 月 2 日美国弱就业数据加速恐慌——篮子高贝塔放大跌势至 8 月 7 日低点。","drivers":["BOJ July 31 2024 rate hike triggers yen-carry unwind; VIX spikes to 65","High-beta flush (SPHB-SPLV -14.6%, SMH -22.7%): positioning, not fundamentals","Defensives +0.9% vs cyclicals -8.1%: clean flight-to-safety rotation","Aug 2 2024 weak US jobs data adds recession scare to the carry-unwind"],"drivers_zh":["日本央行 2024 年 7 月 31 日加息触发日元套利平仓；VIX 飙至 65","高贝塔冲刷（SPHB-SPLV -14.6%、半导体 -22.7%）：仓位而非基本面","防御 +0.9% 对周期 -8.1%：清晰的避险轮动","2024 年 8 月 2 日美国弱就业数据叠加衰退恐慌"],"prev_key":"2024-07-16","prev_key_chain":["2024-07-16"],"status":"exact","title":"BOJ rate hike, yen-carry unwind, high-beta flush","title_zh":"日本央行加息、日元套利平仓、高贝塔冲刷","turn_id":"robotics_automation:peak:2024-07"},"2024-08-07":{"body":"The basket recovered +25.6% from the Aug low to a Nov 2024 peak as the regime turned goldilocks/growth-up (cyclicals +18.3% vs defensives +5.9%, VIX 28→15, SMH +15.2%). Trump's Nov 5 2024 election win supercharged the 'reshoring/tariff manufacturing' trade — a perceived demand catalyst for domestic automation capex. The physical-AI/humanoid narrative intensified (Figure AI Series B, Tesla Optimus scale-up announcements), adding thematic premium. A firming dollar (DXY +3.5%) was a mild headwind for the multinationals but did not offset the cyclical tailwinds.","body_zh":"篮子从 8 月低点反弹 +25.6% 至 2024 年 11 月高点，regime 转向 goldilocks/增长上行（周期 +18.3% 对防御 +5.9%、VIX 28→15、半导体 +15.2%）。特朗普 2024 年 11 月 5 日当选大幅提振'回流/关税制造'交易——被视为国内自动化资本开支的需求催化剂。实体 AI/人形机器人叙事升温（Figure AI B 轮、特斯拉 Optimus 量产公告），添加主题溢价。美元转强（DXY +3.5%）对跨国企业是轻微逆风，但未能抵消周期顺风。","drivers":["Nov 2024 Trump election win: reshoring/tariff-manufacturing trade lifts automation capex","Goldilocks risk-on regime (cyclicals +18.3%, VIX 28 to 15, SMH +15.2%)","Physical-AI / humanoid-robot narrative intensifies (Figure AI, Tesla Optimus)","Firming dollar (DXY +3.5%) a mild headwind for multinationals"],"drivers_zh":["2024 年 11 月特朗普当选：回流/关税制造交易提振自动化资本开支","Goldilocks 风险偏好 regime（周期 +18.3%、VIX 28→15、半导体 +15.2%）","实体 AI/人形机器人叙事升温（Figure AI、特斯拉 Optimus）","美元转强（DXY +3.5%）对跨国企业轻微逆风"],"prev_key":"2024-08-07","prev_key_chain":["2024-08-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Election reshoring trade plus physical-AI bid","title_zh":"大选回流交易叠加实体 AI 买盘","turn_id":"robotics_automation:trough:2024-08"},"2024-11-25":{"body":"Two shocks hit the basket: DeepSeek's R1 model (Jan 27 2025) sparked a single-day selloff in AI-adjacent stocks (Nvidia lost ~$589B in market cap), cutting the automation/AI multiple; then Trump's April 2 2025 'Liberation Day' reciprocal tariffs (10%+ on nearly all countries, 145% effective on China) sent VIX to 60 by April 7 — the basket fell 33.4% vs SPY -16.4%, nearly 2x leverage. Automation hardware supply chains (sensors, motors, semiconductors from Asia) sat directly in the tariff blast radius, and defensives (-7.6%) drastically outperformed cyclicals (-18.9%) confirming systemic risk-off.","body_zh":"两次冲击接连打击篮子：DeepSeek R1 模型（2025 年 1 月 27 日）引发 AI 相关股单日抛售（英伟达市值蒸发约 5890 亿美元），压缩自动化/AI 估值倍数；随后特朗普 2025 年 4 月 2 日'解放日'对等关税（对几乎所有国家 10%+，对华有效税率 145%）将 VIX 推至 4 月 7 日的 60——篮子跌 33.4%，SPY 跌 16.4%，近 2 倍杠杆效应。自动化硬件供应链（亚洲传感器、电机、半导体）正处关税冲击半径，防御（-7.6%）大幅跑赢周期（-18.9%），确认系统性避险。","drivers":["DeepSeek R1 Jan 27 2025 slashes AI-adjacent multiple; Nvidia -$589B single-day cap loss","Liberation Day Apr 2 2025 reciprocal tariffs: 145% effective China rate hits hardware supply chains","Violent risk-off: VIX 15 to 52 (60 intraday), SPHB-SPLV -21%, SMH -25.8%","Defensives -7.6% vs cyclicals -18.9%: systemic flight-to-safety confirms macro shock"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek R1（2025 年 1 月 27 日）削减 AI 相关估值；英伟达单日市值蒸发 5890 亿美元","解放日（2025 年 4 月 2 日）对等关税：对华有效 145% 打击硬件供应链","剧烈避险：VIX 15→52（盘中 60）、SPHB-SPLV -21%、半导体 -25.8%","防御 -7.6% 对周期 -18.9%：系统性避险确认宏观冲击"],"prev_key":"2024-11-25","prev_key_chain":["2024-11-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Liberation Day tariff crash amplified by DeepSeek","title_zh":"解放日关税崩盘叠加 DeepSeek 冲击放大","turn_id":"robotics_automation:peak:2024-11"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"Trump's April 9 2025 90-day tariff pause announcement — causing the S&P 500's largest single-day gain since 2008 (+9.5%) — reset the tape. From the April-8 low the basket nearly doubled (+90.2%) into a May-26 2026 high, supercharged by an explosive high-beta/tech-led risk-on regime (VIX 52→17, SMH +235.7%, SPHB-SPLV +107.2%, weaker dollar DXY -3.7%). The physical-AI/humanoid narrative re-accelerated with Figure AI's $39B Series C (Sep 2025), Boston Dynamics' Atlas entering Hyundai factories (2026), and Tesla Optimus Gen 3 autonomous production — giving the basket a structural growth layer on top of the macro risk-on. Narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -15%) shows the run was largely semis/tech-concentration driven.","body_zh":"特朗普 2025 年 4 月 9 日宣布 90 天关税暂停——引发标普 500 自 2008 年以来最大单日涨幅（+9.5%）——重置行情。从 4 月 8 日低点，篮子近乎翻倍（+90.2%）至 2026 年 5 月 26 日高点，被爆发性高贝塔/科技领涨风险偏好 regime（VIX 52→17、半导体 +235.7%、SPHB-SPLV +107.2%、美元走弱 DXY -3.7%）大幅增强。实体 AI/人形机器人叙事再加速：Figure AI 完成 390 亿美元 C 轮（2025 年 9 月）、波士顿动力 Atlas 进驻现代工厂（2026 年）、特斯拉 Optimus Gen 3 自主量产——为篮子在宏观风险偏好之上叠加结构性成长层。市场广度狭窄（RSP-SPY -15%）显示行情主要由半导体/科技集中驱动。","drivers":["Apr 9 2025 90-day tariff pause: S&P +9.5% single day, resets risk-on (VIX 52 to 17)","Explosive high-beta regime: SMH +235.7%, SPHB-SPLV +107.2%, weaker dollar (DXY -3.7%)","Physical-AI/humanoid re-acceleration: Figure AI $39B Sep 2025, Atlas deployments 2026","Reflation quad (cyclicals +51.4% vs defensives +17.2%) supports industrial-tech leadership"],"drivers_zh":["2025 年 4 月 9 日 90 天关税暂停：标普单日 +9.5%，重置风险偏好（VIX 52→17）","爆发性高贝塔 regime：半导体 +235.7%、SPHB-SPLV +107.2%、美元走弱（DXY -3.7%）","实体 AI/人形机器人再加速：Figure AI 390 亿美元（2025 年 9 月）、Atlas 部署（2026 年）","再通胀象限（周期 +51.4% 对防御 +17.2%）支撑工业科技领涨"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-pause recovery, physical-AI re-rate rip","title_zh":"关税暂停复苏，实体 AI 重估爆拉","turn_id":"robotics_automation:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"The basket is \"Rolling over\" at RS-rank 23 (position 35.9), off a parabolic +90% run from the April-8 2025 tariff-crash low to a May-26 2026 peak. The current reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%) would normally support cyclical industrials, but the basket is losing relative strength as the market broadens away from the narrow-breadth, semis-led leadership that drove the prior leg. A stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%) is a structural headwind for the globally-sourced hardware supply chains at the core of this group, and growth lagging value (-15.2%) signals de-rating pressure on the long-duration automation multiples. The basket is digesting its largest post-COVID bull leg in a sticky-CPI 2026 environment where capital-equipment buyers face higher financing costs and tariff uncertainty — the near-term setup is consolidation/distribution.","now_zh":"篮子处于\"见顶回落\"阶段，RS 排名 23（仓位 35.9），距 2025 年 4 月 8 日关税崩盘低点至 2026 年 5 月 26 日高点的 +90% 抛物线行情已告一段落。当前再通胀/增长上行象限（周期股 +11.2% 对防御 +6.9%、油价 +19.2%、铜金比 +18.3%）通常支撑周期工业，但篮子正失去相对强势，因行情从此前驱动腿段的窄幅市场、半导体领跑格局向更广泛参与切换。美元走强（DXY +3.4%）是该板块全球化硬件供应链的结构性逆风，成长落后价值（-15.2%）则预示长久期自动化估值面临去溢价压力。篮子在粘性 CPI 的 2026 年背景下消化新冠后最大的牛市腿段——资本设备买家面临更高融资成本与关税不确定性，近期格局为盘整/派发。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-semicap_equipment":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"A 214% advance over four-plus years driven by two concurrent structural spending waves: the industry-wide shift from planar to 3D NAND (Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron all committing record tool budgets, with actual WFE exceeding $45B in 2017 versus the $33-34B consensus forecast, a 20-25% beat) and the FinFET node transition at foundry (Samsung and TSMC racing to 14/16nm then 10nm for Apple and Qualcomm orders from 2014 onward). The macro backdrop was a textbook goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation regime: VIX stayed calm 14-18, TLT rallied +29.8% as yields fell, and semis broadly rose +179.1% versus SPY +60.9%, a mega-cap/growth-led tape (RSP lagged SPY -7.4%). The stronger dollar (+11.1% DXY) and oil collapse (-30.6%) suppressed inflation and left the Fed on hold, giving equipment companies a multi-year earnings expansion runway.","body_zh":"超过四年时间累计上涨214%，由两个并行的结构性支出浪潮驱动：全行业从平面NAND向3D NAND转型（三星、SK海力士、美光均承诺创纪录设备预算，2016-2017年实际WFE超过450亿美元，较市场共识预测330-340亿美元高出20-25%），以及晶圆代工FinFET节点转型（三星和台积电从2014年起争相推进14/16nm再到10nm，争夺苹果和高通订单）。宏观背景是教科书式的金发姑娘/增长向上-去通胀象限：VIX保持平静14-18，TLT上涨+29.8%（收益率下行），半导体整体上涨+179.1% 对SPY +60.9%，是大盘/成长主导的行情（RSP跑输SPY -7.4%）。美元走强（DXY +11.1%）和油价暴跌（-30.6%）压制了通胀，美联储按兵不动，为设备公司提供了多年盈利扩张跑道。","drivers":["3D NAND transition capex","FinFET foundry node race","goldilocks macro low yields","growth-led melt-up","Fed on hold"],"drivers_zh":["3D NAND转型资本开支","FinFET代工节点竞赛","金发姑娘宏观低利率","成长股主导飙升","美联储按兵不动"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"3D NAND, FinFET foundry, and goldilocks melt-up","title_zh":"3D NAND、FinFET代工竞赛与金发姑娘飙升","turn_id":"semicap_equipment:trough:2014-01"},"2018-03-21":{"body":"A -40% selloff from peak to Christmas Eve 2018, driven by simultaneous trade-war shock and cyclical memory oversupply. The US-China trade war formally began April 4, 2018 with 25% tariffs on $50B of Chinese goods, directly threatening WFE names with 27-33% China revenue exposure. Concurrently, the DRAM and 3D NAND supercycle peaked: combined capex from Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron was projected to fall from $45.4B in 2018 to $37.5B in 2019 (-17%), and Micron cut DRAM wafer starts by 5% late in the year. The cross-asset backdrop confirmed a slowdown/deflation-scare quad: defensives outperformed cyclicals (0.2% vs -17.3%), VIX surged 18 to 36, yields fell (TLT +4.2%), oil crashed -34.7%, and the dollar rose +7.5%. WFE was a double-hit target — cyclical de-rating AND China revenue risk.","body_zh":"从高峰跌至2018年平安夜，下跌40%，由贸易战冲击与周期性内存过剩同步触发。2018年4月4日，美中贸易战正式爆发，美国对500亿美元中国商品征收25%关税，直接威胁中国收入占比27-33%的WFE名字。与此同时，DRAM和3D NAND超级周期见顶：三星、SK海力士、美光合计资本开支预计从2018年的454亿美元降至2019年的375亿美元（-17%），美光年底下调DRAM晶圆投片量5%。跨资产背景确认放缓/通缩恐慌象限：防御板块跑赢周期股（+0.2% 对 -17.3%），VIX从18飙升至36，收益率下行（TLT +4.2%），油价暴跌-34.7%，美元上涨+7.5%。WFE遭受双重打击——周期性估值下杀叠加中国收入风险。","drivers":["US-China trade war tariffs","memory capex cycle peak","DRAM/NAND oversupply","slowdown deflation scare","VIX surge risk-off"],"drivers_zh":["美中贸易战关税","内存资本开支周期见顶","DRAM/NAND供给过剩","放缓通缩恐慌","VIX飙升避险"],"prev_key":"2018-03-21","prev_key_chain":["2018-03-21"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade war + memory oversupply downturn","title_zh":"贸易战叠加内存供过于求下行","turn_id":"semicap_equipment:peak:2018-03"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"A +126% recovery from Christmas Eve 2018 into February 2020, catalyzed by Powell's January 4, 2019 pivot to patience — explicitly walking back the December 2018 hiking guidance and signaling a pause that later became three cuts in 2019. The relief in rate expectations compressed the VIX from 36 to 14 and fueled a 15%+ SPY re-rating in the following 35 trading days. WFE added a fundamental catalyst: a new 5G infrastructure buildout drove leading-edge logic orders (TSMC N7/N5 ramp), and the memory down-cycle began to bottom as inventory digested through mid-2019. The macro backdrop was tech-led risk-on with a goldilocks/reflation flavor: semis rallied +89.7% vs SPY +46.6%, VIX compressed, and TLT rose +21.6% as yields stayed low. Narrow breadth (RSP lagged SPY -6.5%) shows it was again a mega-cap/growth-led tape that amplified WFE's leverage.","body_zh":"从2018年平安夜反弹至2020年2月，上涨+126%，由鲍威尔2019年1月4日的政策转向引爆——明确收回2018年12月的加息指引，发出观望信号，后续于2019年降息三次。利率预期缓解使VIX从36压缩至14，并在随后35个交易日内推动SPY重新定价15%+。WFE叠加了基本面催化剂：新5G基础设施建设拉动先进制程逻辑芯片设备订单（台积电N7/N5爬坡），内存下行周期于2019年中库存消化后开始触底。宏观背景是科技主导的风险偏好，带有金发姑娘/再通胀色彩：半导体大涨+89.7% 对SPY +46.6%，VIX收缩，TLT上涨+21.6%（收益率保持低位）。窄幅市场广度（RSP跑输SPY -6.5%）再次说明这是大盘/成长主导的行情，放大了WFE的杠杆效应。","drivers":["Fed Powell pivot Jan 2019","5G logic capex build","memory down-cycle bottom","growth risk-on low yields","TSMC N7/N5 ramp"],"drivers_zh":["美联储鲍威尔2019年1月转向","5G逻辑芯片资本开支启动","内存下行周期触底","成长风险偏好/低收益率","台积电N7/N5爬坡"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot and 5G/advanced logic recovery","title_zh":"美联储转向与5G/先进逻辑复苏","turn_id":"semicap_equipment:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-13":{"body":"A -44% plunge in just five weeks (Feb 13 to March 20, 2020) as COVID-19 spread globally and triggered the fastest bear market in S&P 500 history. This was an indiscriminate macro risk-off event, not a WFE-specific fundamental shock: VIX exploded from 14 to 66, oil cratered -56.4%, and every cyclical sector was obliterated (cyclicals -37.9% vs defensives -25.8%). WFE's high beta to SOX made it particularly vulnerable — SMH fell -33.2% vs SPY -31.7%, and the flight to safety (TLT +10.9%, dollar +3.8%) confirmed a classic slowdown/deflation-scare quad. Equipment company fabs were ordered to reduce on-site staff and issue revised guidance, but order cancellations at that stage were minimal — the selloff was almost entirely multiple compression driven by macro panic.","body_zh":"仅五周内暴跌-44%（2020年2月13日至3月20日），新冠肺炎全球蔓延引发标普500历史上最快的熊市。这是无差别的宏观避险事件，而非WFE特定基本面冲击：VIX从14暴涨至66，油价崩跌-56.4%，所有周期板块惨遭重创（周期股-37.9% 对 防御板块-25.8%）。WFE对SOX的高贝塔使其格外脆弱——SMH下跌-33.2% 对 SPY -31.7%，避险资金流入（TLT +10.9%，美元+3.8%）确认了经典的放缓/通缩恐慌象限。设备公司被要求减少现场员工并下修盈利指引，但彼时订单取消量极少——抛售几乎完全是宏观恐慌引发的估值收缩。","drivers":["COVID-19 global pandemic","indiscriminate risk-off","VIX 14 to 66","high-beta selloff","oil collapse deflation scare"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情全球扩散","无差别风险规避","VIX从14涨至66","高贝塔抛售","油价崩跌通缩恐慌"],"prev_key":"2020-02-13","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-13"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic flash crash","title_zh":"新冠疫情闪崩","turn_id":"semicap_equipment:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-20":{"body":"A +322% surge from the March 2020 COVID trough through January 2022, one of the most powerful WFE bull legs on record. Three drivers compounded: (1) unprecedented fiscal and monetary stimulus (Fed cut to zero, Congress passed $2.2T CARES Act in March 2020), collapsing the dollar -6.4% and igniting a broad reflation/growth-up quad (VIX 66 to 17, high-beta beat low-vol by +148.2); (2) COVID-driven semiconductor demand surge — the PC/server/data-center and 5G buildout massively pulled forward chip orders (TSMC announced N5 mass production in 2020 with intense EUV tool orders), and memory makers reversed capex cuts; (3) early AI/cloud capex from hyperscalers drove leading-edge spending. The tape was broad (RSP +10.8% vs SPY) and pro-cyclical (Energy +147%, Discretionary +143%), lifting all boats including the high-beta WFE basket which returned 3x SPY.","body_zh":"从2020年3月疫情低点至2022年1月大涨+322%，是有记录以来最强劲的WFE牛市腿之一。三大驱动力叠加：（1）史无前例的财政和货币刺激（美联储降息至零，国会2020年3月通过2.2万亿美元CARES法案），美元暴跌-6.4%，引爆广泛的再通胀/增长向上象限（VIX从66降至17，高贝塔大幅跑赢低波+148.2）；（2）疫情驱动的半导体需求激增——PC/服务器/数据中心和5G建设大幅拉前芯片订单（台积电2020年宣布N5量产，EUV设备订单极度火爆），内存厂商逆转资本开支削减；（3）超大规模云厂商早期AI/云资本开支拉动先进制程支出。市场广度宽广（RSP跑赢SPY +10.8%），顺周期态势显著（能源+147%，非必需消费+143%），高贝塔WFE篮子全面受益，回报为SPY的3倍。","drivers":["COVID zero-rate fiscal stimulus","semiconductor demand surge","TSMC N5 EUV ramp","hyperscaler cloud capex","broad reflation risk-on"],"drivers_zh":["疫情时代零利率财政刺激","半导体需求激增","台积电N5 EUV爬坡","超大规模云厂商资本开支","广泛再通胀风险偏好"],"prev_key":"2020-03-20","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Pandemic stimulus + AI infra super-rally","title_zh":"疫情刺激叠加AI基础设施超级反弹","turn_id":"semicap_equipment:trough:2020-03"},"2022-01-03":{"body":"A -40.5% selloff from January through July 2022 as the most aggressive Fed hiking cycle since the 1980s collided with a WFE capex pause. The Fed hiked from 0% to 2.5% in six months, TLT fell -19.0%, VIX rose from 17 to 27, and the dollar ripped +9.2% in a stagflation-ish quad (Energy +29.5% while Tech -27.1%). The duration-sensitive growth factor in WFE stocks (long-cycle capex orders priced at high multiples) was hammered by the rate shock, with SMH falling -37.9% versus SPY -19.6%. Simultaneously, the semiconductor upcycle peaked — Micron flagged memory oversupply in 2022 and ultimately cut capex 50%+ — meaning both the macro multiple and the fundamental order outlook deteriorated together. Defensives (-2.4%) comfortably outperformed cyclicals (-13.5%), confirming the risk-off character of the leg.","body_zh":"2022年1月至7月下跌-40.5%，为1980年代以来最激进的美联储加息周期与WFE资本开支暂停碰撞的结果。美联储在六个月内将利率从0%上调至2.5%，TLT跌-19.0%，VIX从17升至27，美元大涨+9.2%，处于类滞胀象限（能源+29.5%，科技-27.1%）。WFE股票中的久期敏感成长因子（以高估值定价的长周期资本开支订单）被利率冲击重创，SMH下跌-37.9% 对 SPY -19.6%。与此同时，半导体上行周期触顶——美光2022年发出内存供给过剩信号并最终削减资本开支50%+——意味着宏观估值和基本面订单前景同步恶化。防御板块（-2.4%）大幅跑赢周期股（-13.5%），确认了该阶段的风险规避特征。","drivers":["Fed rate-shock 0% to 2.5%","duration de-rating growth stocks","memory capex cuts","stagflation macro quad","dollar surge headwind"],"drivers_zh":["美联储利率冲击0%升至2.5%","成长股久期估值下杀","内存资本开支削减","类滞胀宏观象限","美元飙升逆风"],"prev_key":"2022-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2022-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-shock bear meets WFE down-cycle","title_zh":"利率冲击熊市遭遇WFE下行周期","turn_id":"semicap_equipment:peak:2022-01"},"2022-07-01":{"body":"A +31.5% bear-market bounce from July 1 to August 4, 2022, driven entirely by a market repricing of peak-inflation expectations rather than any WFE-specific fundamental improvement. The CPI print for June 2022 (released July 13) showed early signs of deceleration; a brief yield reprieve (TLT +3.2%) and VIX compression (27 to 21) triggered a classic high-beta relief rally in a goldilocks-flavored quad (cyclicals +8.6% vs defensives +2.4%, Discretionary +19.4%, Tech +15.7%). SMH rose +25.2% versus SPY +8.6% — pure beta reversal, not fundamentals, as memory capex cuts were still deepening and China revenue concerns remained. The carry of this leg was entirely macro-driven.","body_zh":"2022年7月1日至8月4日反弹+31.5%，完全由市场对通胀见顶预期的重新定价驱动，而非WFE特定基本面改善。2022年6月CPI数据（7月13日公布）显示通胀早期放缓迹象；收益率短暂回落（TLT +3.2%）和VIX收缩（27降至21）触发经典的高贝塔缓解反弹，处于金发姑娘色彩的象限（周期股+8.6% 对 防御板块+2.4%，非必需消费+19.4%，科技+15.7%）。SMH上涨+25.2% 对 SPY +8.6%——纯贝塔回归，非基本面，内存资本开支削减仍在深化，中国收入担忧依然存在。该阶段的涨幅完全由宏观驱动。","drivers":["peak-inflation repricing","CPI deceleration signal","yield reprieve VIX compression","high-beta relief bounce","bear-market technical rally"],"drivers_zh":["通胀见顶重新定价","CPI放缓信号","收益率回落VIX收缩","高贝塔缓解反弹","熊市技术性反弹"],"prev_key":"2022-07-01","prev_key_chain":["2022-07-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Bear-rally: peak-inflation hope reprieve","title_zh":"熊市反弹：通胀见顶预期驱动喘息","turn_id":"semicap_equipment:trough:2022-07"},"2022-08-04":{"body":"A -30.5% leg from August 4 to October 14, 2022 driven by two sequential blows. First, Powell's August 26 Jackson Hole speech was starkly hawkish — dismissing any imminent pivot and committing to additional hikes, re-igniting the rate regime (TLT -17.0%, dollar +7.2%, VIX 21 to 32). Second, on October 7, 2022, the Biden administration issued sweeping export controls on advanced semiconductor manufacturing equipment to China (effective October 12-21), with new license requirements directly threatening the 27-31% China revenue of AMAT, LRCX, and KLAC (AMAT had generated $7.5B from China in FY2021). The combination of re-accelerating rate shock and a China-revenue structural impairment drove SMH to -29.4% versus SPY -13.3%, a decisive high-beta underperformance. Energy (+13.3%) was the lone leader; Tech (-20.5%) and Discretionary (-18.9%) were the notable laggards.","body_zh":"2022年8月4日至10月14日下跌-30.5%，由两次连续打击驱动。首先，鲍威尔8月26日杰克逊霍尔演讲态度极为鹰派——否认任何近期政策转向的可能，承诺继续加息，重新点燃利率行情（TLT -17.0%，美元+7.2%，VIX从21升至32）。其次，2022年10月7日，拜登政府发布针对对华先进半导体制造设备的全面出口管制（10月12-21日起生效），新增许可证要求直接威胁AMAT、LRCX、KLAC合计27-31%的中国收入（AMAT在FY2021年从中国获得75亿美元收入）。利率冲击重新加速与中国收入结构性受损双重叠加，推动SMH下跌-29.4% 对 SPY -13.3%，明显的高贝塔跑输。能源（+13.3%）是唯一领涨者；科技（-20.5%）和非必需消费（-18.9%）是主要落后者。","drivers":["Jackson Hole hawkish shock","Oct 2022 China export controls","rate re-acceleration TLT -17%","China revenue structural impairment","high-beta underperformance"],"drivers_zh":["杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击","2022年10月对华出口管制","利率重新加速TLT -17%","中国收入结构性受损","高贝塔跑输"],"prev_key":"2022-08-04","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkishness + Oct export-control shock","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击叠加10月出口管制","turn_id":"semicap_equipment:peak:2022-08"},"2022-10-14":{"body":"A +169.8% run from October 2022 to July 2024 as the generative AI buildout drove a record leading-edge and advanced-packaging tool order cycle, fueled by a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation regime. ChatGPT launched November 2022 and triggered a hyperscaler AI capex arms race — TSMC announced aggressive N3/N2 capacity expansion with EUV-intensive process flows, directly driving ASML backlog and AMAT/LRCX deposition/etch tool orders. VIX collapsed 32 to 13, growth crushed value +47.6%, the dollar weakened -8.0% (a tailwind for these multinationals), and breadth was deeply narrow (RSP lagged SPY -24.1%) in a mega-cap-led melt-up (semis +221.7% vs SPY +62.1%). The export-control headwind was partially offset as equipment companies obtained licenses for some China shipments, and HBM/advanced memory demand from Nvidia AI chips added a memory capex recovery leg on top of logic spending.","body_zh":"从2022年10月至2024年7月上涨+169.8%，生成式AI建设潮驱动创纪录的先进制程和先进封装设备订单周期，在金发姑娘/增长向上-去通胀象限下腾飞。ChatGPT 2022年11月发布，触发超大规模云厂商AI资本开支军备竞赛——台积电宣布积极推进N3/N2产能扩张（需密集EUV工序），直接推升ASML积压订单及AMAT/LRCX的沉积/刻蚀设备订单。VIX从32崩落至13，成长大幅跑赢价值+47.6%，美元走弱-8.0%（对这些跨国公司构成顺风），市场广度极为狭窄（RSP跑输SPY -24.1%），是大盘股主导的飙升（半导体+221.7% 对 SPY +62.1%）。英伟达AI芯片对HBM/先进内存的需求带来内存资本开支复苏腿，叠加逻辑芯片支出，部分抵消了出口管制逆风（设备公司获得部分对华出货许可证）。","drivers":["ChatGPT generative AI capex","TSMC N3/N2 EUV ramp","HBM advanced memory demand","goldilocks narrow breadth melt-up","dollar tailwind for multinationals"],"drivers_zh":["ChatGPT生成式AI资本开支","台积电N3/N2 EUV爬坡","HBM先进内存需求","金发姑娘窄幅市场飙升","美元走弱对跨国公司利好"],"prev_key":"2022-10-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-14"],"status":"exact","title":"AI-capex pick-and-shovel melt-up","title_zh":"AI资本开支卖铲飙升","turn_id":"semicap_equipment:trough:2022-10"},"2024-07-16":{"body":"A -53.4% drawdown from July 2024 to April 2025 in two distinct flushes. The first hit came from the August 5, 2024 yen-carry trade unwind: the Bank of Japan raised rates on July 31 and the yen appreciated roughly 6% in a week, forcing leveraged investors to liquidate their most appreciated holdings — US momentum/high-beta tech. SMH fell sharply and Tokyo Electron plunged 18% in a single day. The second and deeper flush came from twin fundamental shocks in late 2024 through April 2025: China's DeepSeek (revealed January 2025) raised fears of lower AI compute demand and threatened the high-capex narrative, while incremental US export-control tightening on advanced semiconductor tools to China continued to pressure China revenue for AMAT/LRCX/KLAC. The slowdown/deflation-scare quad was unambiguous: defensives -1.2% vs cyclicals -11.8%, VIX surged 13 to 52, oil crashed -26.2%, copper-gold -27.7%, and SMH fell -34.0% vs SPY -11.3%, a punishing high-beta underperformance.","body_zh":"2024年7月至2025年4月经历两轮明显抛售，累计下跌-53.4%。第一波打击来自2024年8月5日日元套息交易平仓：日本银行7月31日加息，日元一周内升值约6%，迫使杠杆投资者清仓其涨幅最大的持仓——美国动量/高贝塔科技股。SMH急跌，东京电子单日暴跌18%。第二波更深的抛售来自2024年底至2025年4月的双重基本面冲击：中国DeepSeek（2025年1月曝光）引发AI算力需求下降担忧，威胁高资本开支叙事；美国对华先进半导体工具出口管制持续收紧，进一步压制AMAT/LRCX/KLAC的中国收入。放缓/通缩恐慌象限清晰明确：防御板块-1.2% 对 周期股-11.8%，VIX从13暴涨至52，油价崩跌-26.2%，铜金比-27.7%，SMH下跌-34.0% 对 SPY -11.3%，高贝塔遭受惨烈跑输。","drivers":["yen carry trade unwind Aug 2024","DeepSeek AI capex demand scare","export control tightening","slowdown deflation macro quad","VIX 13 to 52 risk-off"],"drivers_zh":["2024年8月日元套息平仓","DeepSeek AI资本开支需求恐慌","出口管制收紧","放缓通缩宏观象限","VIX从13涨至52避险"],"prev_key":"2024-07-16","prev_key_chain":["2024-07-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Yen-carry unwind, DeepSeek, and tighter export curbs","title_zh":"日元套息平仓、DeepSeek与出口管制收紧","turn_id":"semicap_equipment:peak:2024-07"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"A +424% surge from the April 8, 2025 low (the day before Trump's April 9 announcement of a 90-day reciprocal tariff pause that sent SPY up 9.52%, its best day since 2008) through June 2026 as the combined relief from the trade truce and accelerating AI fab spend drove the most powerful WFE up-leg on record. SEMI projected global equipment sales reaching a record $139B in 2026, with 300mm fab spending forecast to rise 18% in 2026. Record HBM capacity additions by SK Hynix and Samsung (to serve Nvidia AI chips) drove memory WFE, while TSMC's N2 ramp and Intel's new foundry commitments drove logic WFE. The macro regime was unambiguously reflationary: VIX collapsed 52 to 17, high-beta beat low-vol +124.5, cyclicals (52.8%) dominated defensives (17.1%), and SMH rallied +272.9% vs SPY +51.7%. Breadth narrowed again (RSP lagged SPY -12.3%), a characteristic mega-cap-tech-led tape where WFE rode AI-capex amplification to extreme heights.","body_zh":"从2025年4月8日低点（即特朗普4月9日宣布90天对等关税暂停前一天，该消息推动SPY单日上涨9.52%，为2008年以来最大单日涨幅）飙升+424%至2026年6月，贸易休战缓解与加速的AI晶圆厂支出共同推动有记录以来最强劲的WFE上行腿。SEMI预测2026年全球设备销售达到创纪录的1390亿美元，300mm晶圆厂设备支出预计2026年增长18%。SK海力士和三星创纪录扩充HBM产能（服务英伟达AI芯片）驱动内存WFE；台积电N2爬坡和英特尔新晶圆代工承诺驱动逻辑WFE。宏观格局明确再通胀：VIX从52崩落至17，高贝塔跑赢低波+124.5，周期股（52.8%）大幅领先防御板块（17.1%），SMH大涨+272.9% 对 SPY +51.7%。市场广度再次收窄（RSP跑输SPY -12.3%），是大盘科技股主导行情的典型特征，WFE借助AI资本开支放大效应涨至极端高位。","drivers":["Trump tariff truce Apr 9 2025","AI fab capex supercycle","HBM memory capacity race","TSMC N2 / Intel foundry logic ramp","reflation VIX collapse"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普关税休战2025年4月9日","AI晶圆厂资本开支超级周期","HBM内存产能竞赛","台积电N2/英特尔代工逻辑爬坡","再通胀VIX崩落"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff truce + AI fab supercycle rerating","title_zh":"关税休战叠加AI晶圆厂超级周期重估","turn_id":"semicap_equipment:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Semiconductor Equipment (WFE) is in a confirmed topping phase at the 97th percentile of its historical range, with SMH +67.9% and the basket massively extended off its April 2025 low. The current reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%) and broader tape (RSP +2.9% vs SPY) confirm the bull regime is intact, but this is the same tape structure that has historically preceded WFE reversals. The dollar is stronger (+3.4% DXY), a structural headwind for these multinational equipment names (ASML, AMAT, LRCX, KLAC all carry 30-50% non-US revenue), and the high-beta spread (SPHB-SPLV +20.7) is at a historically stretched level. RS rank 6 shows WFE is still outperforming most sectors but is no longer a breakaway leader. WFE fundamentals remain solid (SEMI projects a record $139B global equipment market in 2026), but the cycle analog, valuation percentile, and macro positioning all argue for near-term digestion or a coming air pocket into the next down-leg.","now_zh":"半导体设备（WFE）已处于确认的顶部阶段，位于历史区间第97百分位，SMH较此前高点大涨+67.9%，篮子从2025年4月低点大幅飙升。当前再通胀/增长向上象限（周期股+11.2% 对 防御板块+6.9%，油价+19.2%，铜金比+18.3%）及更宽广的市场（RSP跑赢SPY +2.9%）确认牛市格局仍在，但这恰恰是历史上WFE多次见顶时的相同市场结构。美元走强（DXY +3.4%）对ASML、AMAT、LRCX、KLAC等高度依赖非美收入的跨国设备公司构成结构性逆风。高贝塔利差（SPHB-SPLV +20.7）处于历史极度拉伸水平。相对强度排名第6位，WFE仍跑赢多数板块但已不再是绝对领涨者。WFE基本面依然扎实（SEMI预测2026年全球设备市场规模达创纪录1390亿美元），但周期类比、估值百分位和宏观定位均指向近期消化或即将到来的下行空档。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"semis.top_2026.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"semis.top_2026.v1","arch_state":"pass","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-space_economy":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"Space-adjacent names (defense primes, satellite cos, nascent commercial launch enablers) drifted +17.3% into mid-2015 against a broader slowdown/deflation-scare backdrop: TLT surged +18.7%, oil crashed -36.5%, and defensives (Health +40.6%, Tech +24.3%) strongly outpaced cyclicals (+25.5% vs +11.9%). The basket's modest gain lagged SPY (+18.1%) and was powered by the same falling-yield, dollar-strengthening regime that lifted quality growth — amplified by milestone catalysts: NASA's September 2014 Commercial Crew (CCtCap) contract awards to SpaceX and Boeing, and SpaceX's landmark $1 billion Google/Fidelity funding round in January 2015 that valued it above $10 billion and validated the commercial launch thesis.","body_zh":"太空相关个股（国防主承包商、卫星公司、新兴商业发射商）在放缓/通缩恐慌背景下温和上涨+17.3%：TLT飙升+18.7%、油价崩跌-36.5%、防御领涨（医疗+40.6%、科技+24.3%），远超周期股（+25.5% vs +11.9%）。篮子温和涨幅落后SPY（+18.1%），受益于同一收益率下行、美元走强的regime——两个里程碑催化推波助澜：NASA 2014年9月向SpaceX和波音授予商业载人（CCtCap）合同，以及SpaceX 2015年1月完成谷歌/富达10亿美元融资，估值逾100亿美元，验证商业发射逻辑。","drivers":["NASA CCtCap contract awards (SpaceX/Boeing, Sept 2014)","SpaceX $1B Google/Fidelity round Jan 2015 validates commercial launch","Falling yields (TLT +18.7%) support long-duration names","Defensives/quality-growth led; basket lags SPY in a healthy tape"],"drivers_zh":["NASA CCtCap合同授予（SpaceX/波音，2014年9月）","SpaceX 2015年1月谷歌/富达10亿美元融资验证商业发射","收益率下行（TLT+18.7%）支撑长久期个股","防御/质量成长领涨；篮子在健康行情中落后SPY"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Commercial space dawn, defensives-led melt-up","title_zh":"商业航天黎明，防御主导融涨","turn_id":"space_economy:trough:2014-01"},"2015-06-25":{"body":"A major -34.1% drawdown as the 2015-2016 global risk-off seized markets: China's SSE fell 43% by August 2015, the PBOC devalued the yuan on August 11 2015 ('Black Monday' August 24 saw DJIA -531pts), and oil crashed further (-50.5%). VIX surged 14→27, defensives led cyclicals by 13.7 percentage points (-1.4% vs -15.1%), TLT gained +9.6% as money fled to quality. High-beta space names with no earnings cushion and nascent commercial revenue were crushed alongside Energy, Financials, and Materials — the highest-cyclicality cohort.","body_zh":"全球2015-2016年避险风暴引发重大-34.1%回撤：中国上证综指2015年8月跌43%，央行8月11日贬值人民币（8月24日'黑色星期一'道指跌531点），油价进一步崩跌-50.5%。VIX飙升14→27，防御领先周期股13.7个百分点（-1.4% vs -15.1%），TLT涨+9.6%避险。无盈利缓冲、商业营收尚处萌芽期的高贝塔太空个股随能源、金融、原材料等最高周期性板块一同被重压。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation Aug 11 2015 / 'Black Monday' Aug 24","Oil collapse -50.5% (six-year low) hits cyclicals hard","Flight-to-safety: defensives -1.4% vs cyclicals -15.1%, VIX 14→27","High-beta space flush alongside worst cyclical sectors"],"drivers_zh":["中国人民银行2015年8月11日贬值/8月24日'黑色星期一'","油价崩跌-50.5%（六年低位）重压周期股","避险：防御-1.4%对周期-15.1%，VIX 14→27","高贝塔太空随最差周期板块同步冲刷"],"prev_key":"2015-06-25","prev_key_chain":["2015-06-25"],"status":"exact","title":"China crash and oil collapse flush space -34%","title_zh":"中国股灾与油价崩盘冲刷太空板块-34%","turn_id":"space_economy:peak:2015-06"},"2016-01-21":{"body":"The basket's defining multi-year bull — +312% over 3.5 years from the January 2016 trough to July 2019. A reflation/growth-up regime powered by the commodity recovery (oil +92.6%), Trump fiscal/defense spending after the November 2016 election (ITA/defense primes surged), and a tech/semis-led risk-on tape (SMH +164.4%, growth>value +28.9%) that carried long-duration speculation higher. VIX fell 27→13, credit spreads tightened (+11.6% HYG-LQD), and dollar was near-flat — the ideal environment for speculative, long-dated commercial space stories. SpaceX's December 2015 Falcon 9 orbital landing and April 2016 drone-ship landing proved reusability economics, triggering serious institutional interest in the sector.","body_zh":"篮子决定性的多年牛市——从2016年1月低点至2019年7月历时3.5年涨+312%。驱动力为再通胀/增长上行regime：大宗商品复苏（油价+92.6%）、2016年11月特朗普大选后财政/国防开支（ITA/国防主承包商飙升）、科技/半导体引领风险偏好（SMH+164.4%、成长>价值+28.9%）。VIX从27跌至13，信用利差收窄（HYG-LQD+11.6%），美元基本持平——对长久期商业航天故事股而言是理想环境。SpaceX 2015年12月Falcon 9轨道着陆和2016年4月海上回收验证了可复用经济性，触发机构对该板块的严肃关注。","drivers":["Reflation/growth-up regime: oil +92.6%, tech/semis +164.4%, VIX 27→13","Trump election Nov 2016: defense/space spending tailwind (ITA +26.7% 2017)","SpaceX Falcon 9 reusability milestones (Dec 2015, Apr 2016) validate commercial launch","Long-duration speculation re-rated in a falling-yield, tightening-credit tape"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀/增长上行regime：油价+92.6%、科技/半导体+164.4%、VIX 27→13","2016年11月特朗普大选：国防/航天开支顺风（ITA 2017年+26.7%）","SpaceX Falcon 9可复用里程碑（2015年12月、2016年4月）验证商业发射","收益率下行、信用收窄的行情中长久期投机重新定价"],"prev_key":"2016-01-21","prev_key_chain":["2016-01-21"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump-boom and SPAC pre-rally melt-up +312%","title_zh":"特朗普繁荣与SPAC前夜融涨+312%","turn_id":"space_economy:trough:2016-01"},"2019-07-29":{"body":"A major -39.2% drawdown from July 2019 through March 2020, encompassing two shocks. First, the escalating US-China trade war (tariffs widened in August 2019) and global growth scare hammered cyclicals and high-beta into late 2019. Then COVID-19 arrived as the fatal blow: by March 20 2020, VIX had spiked to 66, oil had collapsed -60.6% (Saudi-Russia price war), TLT surged +22.9%, and cyclicals lost -32.4% against defensives' -16.0%. Space names had no earnings, no dividends, and no defensive qualities — they were among the hardest hit alongside Industrials (-33.7%) and Energy (-56.4%).","body_zh":"从2019年7月至2020年3月的重大-39.2%回撤，涵盖两次冲击。首先，美中贸易战升级（2019年8月关税扩大）与全球增长恐慌重压周期和高贝塔至2019年底。随后COVID-19带来致命一击：至2020年3月20日，VIX飙至66、油价崩跌-60.6%（沙俄价格战）、TLT飙+22.9%，周期股-32.4%对防御-16.0%。太空个股无盈利、无股息、无防御属性——与工业（-33.7%）、能源（-56.4%）并列受创最重。","drivers":["US-China trade war escalation Aug 2019 (phase-1 tariffs) hits global growth","COVID-19 pandemic lockdown shock Mar 2020: VIX 13→66","Oil -60.6% (Saudi-Russia price war) collapses cyclicals","Flight-to-safety: defensives -16% vs cyclicals -32.4%, TLT +22.9%"],"drivers_zh":["2019年8月美中贸易战升级（第一阶段关税）冲击全球增长","COVID-19大流行封锁冲击2020年3月：VIX 13→66","油价-60.6%（沙俄价格战）令周期股崩盘","避险：防御-16%对周期-32.4%，TLT+22.9%"],"prev_key":"2019-07-29","prev_key_chain":["2019-07-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade war, then COVID crash: -39% bear","title_zh":"贸易战叠加COVID崩盘：-39%熊市","turn_id":"space_economy:peak:2019-07"},"2020-03-20":{"body":"A massive +113.3% rally from the COVID low into February 2021 — the SPAC mania phase for space. The Fed cut rates to zero and deployed unlimited QE in March 2020; fiscal transfers flooded retail accounts; and the ARKX ETF filing in January 2021 ignited a direct speculative bid on space names. Zero rates meant infinite-duration stories faced no discounting headwind, and the reflation/growth-up regime (cyclicals +87.3% vs defensives +37.6%, VIX 66→22, SPHB-SPLV +120%, dollar weak -12.1%, oil +164.1%) was pure rocket fuel for the highest-beta corner of the market. Virgin Galactic (SPCE), Astra, Momentus, and Rocket Lab all reached or approached the public markets via SPACs in this window.","body_zh":"从COVID低点至2021年2月的大幅+113.3%反弹——太空SPAC狂热阶段。美联储2020年3月降息至零并部署无限量QE；财政转移支付充实散户账户；ARK 2021年1月申请ARKX ETF直接点燃太空个股投机热情。零利率意味着无限久期故事不受折现率逆风；再通胀/增长上行regime（周期+87.3%对防御+37.6%、VIX 66→22、SPHB-SPLV+120%、美元-12.1%、油+164.1%）是市场最高贝塔角落的纯粹火箭燃料。Virgin Galactic、Astra、Momentus及Rocket Lab均在这一窗口通过SPAC登陆或趋近公开市场。","drivers":["Zero-rate / unlimited QE: infinite-duration stories face no discount rate","SPAC mania: ARKX ETF filing Jan 2021 ignites direct speculative bid","Reflation regime: VIX 66→22, SPHB-SPLV +120%, dollar -12.1%, oil +164.1%","Retail inflows and fiscal transfers bid high-beta hardest"],"drivers_zh":["零利率/无限QE：无限久期故事无折现率逆风","SPAC狂热：ARKX ETF 2021年1月申请点燃直接投机买盘","再通胀regime：VIX 66→22、SPHB-SPLV+120%、美元-12.1%、油+164.1%","散户资金与财政转移支付最强烈竞购高贝塔"],"prev_key":"2020-03-20","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-20"],"status":"exact","title":"SPAC boom and zero-rate rocket fuel +113%","title_zh":"SPAC狂潮与零利率火箭燃料+113%","turn_id":"space_economy:trough:2020-03"},"2021-02-19":{"body":"Space's most distinctive feature on display: it led DOWN while the broad market was still positive (SPY +9.6%, cyclicals +16.7%, energy +53.3%). The de-SPAC/speculative bubble began deflating from February 2021 as the Fed telegraphed a hawkish pivot — the most profitless, highest-duration names got repriced first, before the 2022 bear market had even begun. VIX rose 22→31 and the dollar firmed +6.5%, but this was primarily a speculative-rotation story: capital that had piled into SPCE, ASTR, MNTS exited as growth-value began reverting (-8.9%). The basket fell -43.7% into February 2022 even as the index climbed.","body_zh":"太空板块最显著特征的展示：在大盘仍然正收益时（SPY+9.6%、周期+16.7%、能源+53.3%）它率先领跌。从2021年2月起，de-SPAC/投机泡沫开始消气——美联储发出鹰派转向信号，最无盈利、最长久期的个股率先被重新定价，彼时2022年熊市尚未开始。VIX升至31、美元+6.5%，但本质是投机轮动故事：涌入SPCE、ASTR、MNTS的资金随成长-价值开始回归而撤离（-8.9%）。篮子在指数上涨期间跌-43.7%至2022年2月。","drivers":["Speculative SPAC bubble deflates ahead of the broad bear (SPY still +9.6%)","Fed hawkish pivot signal punishes profitless long-duration growth first","Growth-value reversal begins (-8.9%); capital rotates out of speculation","VIX 22→31, dollar +6.5%: tightening conditions hit longest-duration names hardest"],"drivers_zh":["投机SPAC泡沫在大熊市前提前消气（SPY仍+9.6%）","美联储鹰派转向信号最先惩罚无盈利长久期成长","成长-价值逆转开始（-8.9%）；资金撤出投机","VIX 22→31、美元+6.5%：收紧环境对最长久期个股打击最重"],"prev_key":"2021-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2021-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"SPAC unwind de-rates space before the bear (-44%)","title_zh":"SPAC泡沫消退，太空领先大盘下跌（-44%）","turn_id":"space_economy:peak:2021-02"},"2022-02-23":{"body":"A sharp +27.6% counter-trend bounce off the SPAC-unwind lows — a high-beta oversold snap with no fundamental catalyst. The regime was stagflation-ish (VIX 31→19, SPY +8.6%, defensives marginally led cyclicals +9.0% vs +8.9%, DXY +2.9%), and the basket's outsized move simply reflected the mechanical mean-reversion that follows a -44% drawdown on a highly shorted group. The bounce lasted only 40 days (Feb 23 to Apr 4), topping fast as the Fed's rate-hiking campaign got underway.","body_zh":"从SPAC消退低点的急剧+27.6%逆势反弹——无基本面催化的高贝塔超卖弹回。Regime为类滞胀（VIX 31→19、SPY+8.6%、防御略领周期+9.0% vs +8.9%、DXY+2.9%），篮子的超大涨幅仅反映高度被做空组合在-44%回撤后的机械均值回归。反弹仅持续40天（2月23日至4月4日），随美联储加息周期启动迅速见顶。","drivers":["High-beta oversold snap after -44% SPAC-unwind (mechanical short-squeeze)","VIX compression 31→19 in a flat, stagflation-ish tape (SPY +8.6%)","No fundamental turn — pure speculative mean-reversion","Firming dollar (DXY +2.9%) a background drag, limiting duration"],"drivers_zh":["高贝塔超卖弹回于-44%SPAC消退后（机械逼空）","类滞胀行情（SPY+8.6%）中VIX从31压缩至19","无基本面转折——纯投机均值回归","美元转强（DXY+2.9%）抑制久期，为背景拖累"],"prev_key":"2022-02-23","prev_key_chain":["2022-02-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Oversold dead-cat bounce off SPAC lows +28%","title_zh":"从SPAC低点超卖死猫反弹+28%","turn_id":"space_economy:trough:2022-02"},"2022-04-04":{"body":"The Fed's 2022 rate-hiking campaign hit in earnest — three consecutive 75bp hikes beginning in June 2022 — and speculative space bore the brunt. Yields surged (TLT -10.1%), DXY +4.9%, VIX 19→33, and the regime moved to slowdown/deflation-scare as defensives led cyclicals (-4.5% vs -11.9%). The basket fell -32.7% into May 2022, steeper than the -14.0% for SPY, reflecting that long-duration, zero-earnings names get no valuation floor when the discount rate is rising sharply. Tech and Comm led the losers (Tech -17.7%, Comm -19.9%, Discretionary -23.1%); space is effectively the most extreme version of that exposure.","body_zh":"美联储2022年加息周期真正开始——2022年6月起连续三次加息75个基点——投机性太空首当其冲。收益率飙升（TLT-10.1%）、DXY+4.9%、VIX 19→33，regime转向放缓/通缩恐慌，防御领先周期（-4.5% vs -11.9%）。篮子跌-32.7%至2022年5月，比SPY-14.0%更深，反映出折现率急升时零盈利长久期个股没有估值底部。科技和传媒领跌（科技-17.7%、传媒-19.9%、可选消费-23.1%）；太空实际上是那种敞口最极端的版本。","drivers":["Fed 75bp hike cycle begins (June 2022); yields surge, TLT -10.1%","Risk-off: VIX 19→33, defensives led cyclicals (-4.5% vs -11.9%)","DXY +4.9% headwind for dollar-sensitive speculative names","Zero-earnings space gets no valuation floor as discount rates rise"],"drivers_zh":["美联储开始75bp加息周期（2022年6月）；收益率飙升，TLT-10.1%","避险：VIX 19→33，防御领先周期（-4.5% vs -11.9%）","DXY+4.9%对美元敏感型投机个股为逆风","折现率上升时零盈利太空股没有估值底部"],"prev_key":"2022-04-04","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed hiking bear, rate-driven flush -33%","title_zh":"美联储加息熊市，利率驱动冲刷-33%","turn_id":"space_economy:peak:2022-04"},"2022-05-11":{"body":"A +41.7% high-beta surge off the May 2022 low as the regime turned goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation (VIX 33→20, growth>value +7.9%, SMH +10.9%, SPHB-SPLV +11.5%, oil -18.1%) on premature hopes that the Fed would pause its hike cycle. CPI began moderating in mid-2022, and markets prematurely priced a pivot. Space's +41.7% dwarfed the index's +9.9%, the classic high-beta upside mirror: when risk appetite normalizes even briefly, the most oversold speculation amplifies the move.","body_zh":"从2022年5月低点的+41.7%高贝塔飙升，regime转向goldilocks/增长上行去通胀（VIX 33→20、成长>价值+7.9%、SMH+10.9%、SPHB-SPLV+11.5%、油价-18.1%），源于市场过早押注美联储将暂停加息。2022年年中CPI开始降温，市场抢先定价转向。太空+41.7%远超指数+9.9%——典型的高贝塔上行镜像：只要风险偏好哪怕短暂正常化，最超卖的投机就会放大涨幅。","drivers":["Goldilocks regime: VIX 33→20, growth>value +7.9%, SPHB-SPLV +11.5%","Premature 'Fed pause' pivot narrative (CPI topping, July 2022)","High-beta oversold squeeze: basket +41.7% vs SPY +9.9%","Oil -18.1% and dollar +2.6% mixed; cyclicals modestly led defensives"],"drivers_zh":["Goldilocks regime：VIX 33→20、成长>价值+7.9%、SPHB-SPLV+11.5%","过早的'美联储暂停'转向叙事（CPI见顶，2022年7月）","高贝塔超卖逼空：篮子+41.7% vs SPY+9.9%","油价-18.1%，美元+2.6%，混合信号；周期略领防御"],"prev_key":"2022-05-11","prev_key_chain":["2022-05-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Summer relief rally on 'Fed pause' hope +42%","title_zh":"夏季'美联储暂停'纾困反弹+42%","turn_id":"space_economy:trough:2022-05"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"Powell's hawkish August 26, 2022 Jackson Hole speech — 'We must keep at it until the job is done' — confirmed rates would stay higher for longer and sent speculative space into a new leg down (-34.3%). The regime turned slowdown/deflation-scare (TLT -12.6% as yields surged further, SPHB-SPLV -11.8%, defensives led cyclicals), and the year-end period added tax-loss selling pressure. Even energy, which had led through mid-2022, began fading (+17.1% in this window but decelerating). The basket was trapped: every risk-on bounce was sold as the hiking path extended.","body_zh":"鲍威尔2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔'必须坚持到底'演讲确认利率将更长时间维持高位，把投机性太空推入新一轮下跌（-34.3%）。Regime转向放缓/通缩恐慌（TLT-12.6%收益率进一步飙升、SPHB-SPLV-11.8%、防御领周期），年末加剧税务亏损抛售压力。即便2022年年中一直领涨的能源也开始减速（本段+17.1%但正在放缓）。篮子陷入困境：每次风险偏好反弹都被卖出，因加息路径延长。","drivers":["Jackson Hole Aug 26 2022: Powell 'keep at it until done' — hike path extends","Yields surge again (TLT -12.6%); high-beta penalized (SPHB-SPLV -11.8%)","Slowdown/deflation-scare quad: cyclicals -5.7% vs defensives -1.7%","Year-end tax-loss selling adds pressure to already-battered space names"],"drivers_zh":["2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔：鲍威尔'坚持到底'——加息路径延长","收益率再度飙升（TLT-12.6%）；高贝塔受惩（SPHB-SPLV-11.8%）","放缓/通缩恐慌quad：周期-5.7% vs 防御-1.7%","年末税务亏损抛售对已遭重创的太空个股施加额外压力"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkish reset drives -34% flush","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派重置驱动-34%冲刷","turn_id":"space_economy:peak:2022-08"},"2022-12-27":{"body":"One of space's most violent counter-trend moves: +83.3% in under two months as the regime flipped to reflation/growth-up risk-on to start 2023. SPHB-SPLV +18.3%, SMH +17.2%, cyclicals led defensives (+4.9% vs -4.5%), and the most-shorted, most-beaten-down speculative names ripped hardest in a short squeeze that was equal parts regime and positioning. The catalyst was the 'soft landing' re-risk narrative following cooler-than-expected December 2022 CPI. The basket's +83.3% against SPY's +4.5% is the purest expression of this group's leverage to sentiment: it topped fast in February 2023 and gave back most of the move.","body_zh":"太空板块最激烈的逆势走势之一：不到两个月+83.3%，regime翻转为2023年初的再通胀/增长上行风险偏好。SPHB-SPLV+18.3%、SMH+17.2%、周期领防御（+4.9% vs -4.5%），最被做空、最遭重创的投机个股在兼具regime和仓位因素的逼空中涨幅最猛。催化剂是2022年12月CPI低于预期所引发的'软着陆'再担风险叙事。篮子+83.3%对SPY+4.5%是该板块对情绪杠杆最纯粹的体现：2023年2月快速见顶，随后回吐大部分涨幅。","drivers":["Risk-on re-rate: SPHB-SPLV +18.3%, SMH +17.2%, VIX flat at 22","Soft-landing CPI relief (Dec 2022 print) ignites a January short squeeze","Cyclicals led defensives (+4.9% vs -4.5%); reflation/growth-up quad","Basket +83.3% vs SPY +4.5% — pure speculative high-beta torque off deep lows"],"drivers_zh":["风险偏好重新定价：SPHB-SPLV+18.3%、SMH+17.2%、VIX持平22","软着陆CPI宽慰（2022年12月数据）点燃1月逼空","周期领防御（+4.9% vs -4.5%）；再通胀/增长上行quad","篮子+83.3% vs SPY+4.5%——从深低点的纯投机高贝塔扭矩"],"prev_key":"2022-12-27","prev_key_chain":["2022-12-27"],"status":"exact","title":"January 2023 high-beta short squeeze +83%","title_zh":"2023年1月高贝塔逼空+83%","turn_id":"space_economy:trough:2022-12"},"2023-02-22":{"body":"Space's most punishing relative drawdown: -43.8% from February to October 2023 while SPY actually gained +4.2%. Two sequential hits: the SVB regional-banking crisis in March 2023 triggered a flight-to-quality spike, then the autumn 2023 yield surge (10Y approaching 5%, TLT -14.9%) crushed every long-duration name. The regime was growth-up with extreme breadth divergence (RSP-SPY -12.4%, narrowest since 2020), meaning only mega-cap AI darlings rose while unprofitable space bled — high-beta was explicitly wrong (-3.6% SPHB-SPLV against a +4.2% SPY). This is the 'higher for longer' playbook: speculation is the last thing to get a bid when cost of capital is at a cycle high.","body_zh":"太空最惨烈的相对回撤：2023年2月至10月-43.8%，而SPY实际上涨+4.2%。两轮连续冲击：2023年3月SVB区域银行危机引发避险溢价飙升，继而2023年秋季收益率飙升（10年期逼近5%，TLT-14.9%）重压所有长久期个股。Regime为增长上行但市场广度极度分化（RSP-SPY-12.4%，2020年以来最窄），意味着只有超大市值AI宠儿上涨，无盈利太空流血——高贝塔明显错误（SPHB-SPLV-3.6%对+4.2%SPY）。这是'更高更久'剧本：资本成本处于周期高点时，投机最后才有买盘。","drivers":["SVB banking crisis March 2023: flight-to-quality hits speculative names","Autumn 2023 yield spike: 10Y approaches 5%, TLT -14.9%","Extreme narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -12.4%): only mega-cap AI gets flows","Higher-for-longer: SPHB-SPLV -3.6% even as SPY +4.2%"],"drivers_zh":["SVB银行危机2023年3月：避险需求重压投机个股","2023年秋季收益率飙升：10年期逼近5%，TLT-14.9%","极度广度分化（RSP-SPY-12.4%）：只有超大市值AI获得资金","更高更久：即便SPY+4.2%，SPHB-SPLV仍-3.6%"],"prev_key":"2023-02-22","prev_key_chain":["2023-02-22"],"status":"exact","title":"SVB shock + 5% yield grind: -44% against a rising index","title_zh":"SVB冲击+5%收益率磨底：-44%对抗上涨的指数","turn_id":"space_economy:peak:2023-02"},"2023-10-27":{"body":"The defining generational bull run for space: +381.2% over 16 months as the goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation regime (SMH +82.4%, growth>value +23.1%, VIX 21→16, TLT +11.3% as yields fell, RSP-SPY -11.9% narrow mega-cap tape) combined with a genuine fundamental shift. RKLB-style names had transitioned from SPAC-era speculation to credible businesses: Rocket Lab set annual launch cadence records, won Electron contracts for NASA and commercial clients, and entered the spacecraft manufacturing business with large government awards. The SPAC graveyard had been cleared, survivors were generating revenue, and defense-space (SDA Tranche 2, direct-to-device satcom via AST SpaceMobile) gave the sector institutional legitimacy. Falling yields were rocket fuel; RKLB reached an all-time high of ~$151 in May 2026 before the leg's February 2025 peak.","body_zh":"太空板块决定性的世代牛市：16个月+381.2%，goldilocks/增长上行去通胀regime（SMH+82.4%、成长>价值+23.1%、VIX 21→16、TLT+11.3%收益率下行、RSP-SPY-12.4%狭窄大市值行情）叠加真实的基本面转变。RKLB类个股已从SPAC时代的投机升级为可信企业：Rocket Lab创年度发射纪录，为NASA和商业客户赢得Electron合同，凭借大型政府订单进入航天器制造业务。SPAC坟场已清场，幸存者产生营收，国防航天（SDA第二阶段、AST SpaceMobile直连设备卫星通信）赋予该板块机构合法性。收益率下行是火箭燃料；RKLB于2026年5月创下约151美元历史高点（该段的2025年2月峰值之后）。","drivers":["Goldilocks AI regime: SMH +82.4%, TLT +11.3%, VIX 21→16 — falling yields turbocharge duration","Real fundamental shift: RKLB launch cadence, spacecraft manufacturing, SDA Tranche 2 wins","Direct-to-device satcom (ASTS) and Earth-obs validate commercial space revenue","SPAC survivors mature; defense-space contracts give institutional backing"],"drivers_zh":["Goldilocks AI regime：SMH+82.4%、TLT+11.3%、VIX 21→16——收益率下行为久期提速","真实基本面转变：RKLB发射节奏、航天器制造、SDA第二阶段获奖","直连设备卫星通信（ASTS）与对地观测验证商业航天营收","SPAC幸存者成熟；国防航天合同提供机构背书"],"prev_key":"2023-10-27","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-27"],"status":"exact","title":"AI goldilocks and space build-out melt-up +381%","title_zh":"AI Goldilocks与太空建设融涨+381%","turn_id":"space_economy:trough:2023-10"},"2025-02-10":{"body":"Speculative space led the 2025 de-risk in two acts. First, the DeepSeek R1 release on January 20, 2025 triggered a massive AI-capex scare (Nvidia fell ~17% intraday on January 27), slamming the AI-adjacent speculation that had driven space higher. Then President Trump's 'Liberation Day' reciprocal tariff announcement on April 2, 2025 (effective April 5) sent VIX from 16 to 52, the sharpest spike since COVID, obliterating cyclicals (-17.7%) while defensives held (-6.5%). Space, as the highest-beta theme on the board (SPHB-SPLV -21.9%, SMH -27.9%), fell -39.9% from the February peak into the April 8 low — roughly twice the -17.7% index decline.","body_zh":"投机性太空在2025年去风险中两幕领跌。第一幕，2025年1月20日DeepSeek R1发布引发大规模AI资本支出恐慌（英伟达1月27日盘中跌约17%），重创推动太空走高的AI相关投机。第二幕，特朗普4月2日'解放日'对等关税公告（4月5日生效）使VIX从16飙至52——COVID以来最急剧的飙升，周期股-17.7%，防御守住-6.5%。太空作为面板上扭矩最高的主题（SPHB-SPLV-21.9%、SMH-27.9%），从2月高点至4月8日低点跌-39.9%，约为指数-17.7%跌幅的两倍。","drivers":["DeepSeek R1 shock Jan 27 2025: AI-capex scare hits speculation immediately","Trump 'Liberation Day' tariff crash Apr 2 2025: VIX 16→52","Flight-to-safety: defensives -6.5% vs cyclicals -17.7%; basket -39.9% vs SPY -17.7%","SPHB-SPLV -21.9%, SMH -27.9%: highest-beta theme flushes hardest"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek R1冲击2025年1月27日：AI资本支出恐慌即时重创投机","特朗普'解放日'关税崩盘2025年4月2日：VIX 16→52","避险：防御-6.5% vs 周期-17.7%；篮子-39.9% vs SPY-17.7%","SPHB-SPLV-21.9%、SMH-27.9%：扭矩最高的主题冲刷最重"],"prev_key":"2025-02-10","prev_key_chain":["2025-02-10"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek + tariff shock: high-beta leads down -40%","title_zh":"DeepSeek+关税冲击：高贝塔领跌-40%","turn_id":"space_economy:peak:2025-02"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"A textbook high-beta V-reversal: +153.8% from the April 8 low into October 2025 as VIX crashed from 52 to 21, SPHB-SPLV +59.4%, growth>value +22.7%, the dollar weakened -4.1%, and the regime returned to goldilocks. Two fundamental tailwinds reinforced the sentiment snap: (1) a US-China trade truce and tariff pause reduced macro risk, and (2) President Trump signed the Golden Dome executive order on January 27, 2025 — with space-based interceptor and tracking satellite spending becoming a policy priority, defense-space names like RKLB received a structural re-rating. The Rocket Lab SDA Tranche 3 contract ($816M, announced December 19, 2025) was previewed during this window. Basket +153.8% against SPY +34.7% — the ratio the group always demands respect for.","body_zh":"教科书式高贝塔V形反转：从4月8日低点+153.8%至2025年10月，VIX从52崩至21、SPHB-SPLV+59.4%、成长>价值+22.7%、美元走弱-4.1%，regime重回goldilocks。两个基本面顺风强化情绪弹回：(1)美中贸易休战和关税暂停减少宏观风险；(2)特朗普1月27日签署Golden Dome行政令——以空间拦截器和追踪卫星为核心的国防航天支出成为政策优先，RKLB等国防航天个股获得结构性重估。Rocket Lab SDA第三阶段合同（8.16亿美元，2025年12月19日宣布）在此窗口内已有预告。篮子+153.8%对SPY+34.7%——该板块始终要求投资者敬畏的比例。","drivers":["VIX 52→21 + SPHB-SPLV +59.4%: highest-beta benefits most from risk-on snap","Tariff pause / US-China trade truce removes macro tail risk","Golden Dome executive order (Jan 27 2025): defense-space becomes procurement priority","SDA Tranche 3 pipeline ($816M RKLB contract previewed): institutional re-rate"],"drivers_zh":["VIX 52→21+SPHB-SPLV+59.4%：扭矩最高受益于风险偏好弹回最多","关税暂停/美中贸易休战移除宏观尾部风险","Golden Dome行政令（2025年1月27日）：国防航天成为采购优先","SDA第三阶段管线（RKLB 8.16亿美元合同预告）：机构重估"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-tariff-crash risk-on moon shot +154%","title_zh":"关税崩盘后风险偏好登月+154%","turn_id":"space_economy:trough:2025-04"},"2025-10-15":{"body":"Space front-ran a mild macro wobble with characteristic outsized drawdown (-38.7% vs SPY -1.9%, VIX 21→26). Two overlapping triggers: (1) profit-taking after a +154% vertical run with valuation multiples stretched to extremes (RKLB trading at ~30x sales); and (2) Rocket Lab's November 11, 2025 announcement that the Neutron maiden flight was pushed to 2026, removing a near-term milestone catalyst. The macro backdrop provided no cover — mild risk-off (Health +6.2%, Energy +2.9% led; Discretionary -5.8% lagged) and a slight VIX uptick confirmed the risk-off tilt, but the -39% magnitude was purely high-beta amplification of a -1.9% index move.","body_zh":"太空以惯常的超大回撤抢跑温和宏观动摇（-38.7% vs SPY-1.9%，VIX 21→26）。两个叠加触发因素：(1)+154%垂直拉升后获利了结，估值倍数拉伸至极端（RKLB约30倍销售额）；(2) Rocket Lab 2025年11月11日宣布Neutron首飞推迟至2026年，近期里程碑催化剂消失。宏观背景未提供掩护——轻微避险（医疗+6.2%、能源+2.9%领涨；可选消费-5.8%落后），VIX小幅上升确认避险倾斜，但-39%的幅度纯属高贝塔对-1.9%指数涨跌的放大。","drivers":["Profit-taking after +154% run; RKLB at stretched ~30x sales valuation","Rocket Lab Neutron maiden flight delayed to 2026 (announced Nov 11, 2025)","Mild macro risk-off (VIX 21→26, SPY -1.9%): high-beta amplifies to -39%","Defensives (Health +6.2%) led; discretionary fared worst"],"drivers_zh":["+154%行情后获利了结；RKLB估值拉伸至约30倍销售额","Rocket Lab Neutron首飞延迟至2026年（2025年11月11日宣布）","轻微宏观避险（VIX 21→26、SPY-1.9%）：高贝塔放大至-39%","防御（医疗+6.2%）领涨；可选消费表现最差"],"prev_key":"2025-10-15","prev_key_chain":["2025-10-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Neutron delay confirmed, profit-taking flush -39%","title_zh":"Neutron延期确认，获利了结冲刷-39%","turn_id":"space_economy:peak:2025-10"},"2025-11-20":{"body":"Another vertical high-beta rally — +120.2% in just over two months — as the regime flipped to reflation/growth-up (VIX 26→16, SPHB-SPLV +16.0%, cyclicals +11.4% vs defensives +3.1%, dollar -3.7%, broadening RSP-SPY +2.4%). The hard fundamental catalyst was Rocket Lab's $816 million SDA Tranche 3 contract announced December 19, 2025 — the company's largest-ever award — which re-established it as a credible national-security space contractor and triggered a broad re-rate of the sector. Nasdaq-100 inclusion anticipation for RKLB added passive flow demand. The basket +120.2% against SPY's +6.9% is the ratio's starkest expression yet.","body_zh":"又一次垂直高贝塔反弹——仅两个多月+120.2%——regime翻转为再通胀/增长上行（VIX 26→16、SPHB-SPLV+16.0%、周期+11.4% vs 防御+3.1%、美元-3.7%、广度扩张RSP-SPY+2.4%）。硬性基本面催化剂是Rocket Lab 2025年12月19日宣布的8.16亿美元SDA第三阶段合同——公司有史以来最大单笔合同——重新确立其为可信国家安全航天承包商，并触发板块广泛重估。RKLB纳入纳斯达克100指数的预期增加被动资金买盘。篮子+120.2% vs SPY+6.9%是该比率迄今最极端的体现。","drivers":["RKLB $816M SDA Tranche 3 contract (Dec 19, 2025): largest-ever, triggers sector re-rate","Reflation risk-on flip: VIX 26→16, SPHB-SPLV +16.0%, dollar -3.7%","Nasdaq-100 inclusion (RKLB): passive flow buying adds mechanical bid","Basket +120.2% vs SPY +6.9% — regime amplification at its most extreme"],"drivers_zh":["RKLB 8.16亿美元SDA第三阶段合同（2025年12月19日）：最大历史合同，触发板块重估","再通胀风险偏好翻转：VIX 26→16、SPHB-SPLV+16.0%、美元-3.7%","RKLB纳入纳斯达克100：被动资金买盘增加机械需求","篮子+120.2% vs SPY+6.9%——regime放大的最极端体现"],"prev_key":"2025-11-20","prev_key_chain":["2025-11-20"],"status":"exact","title":"SDA contract and risk-on year-end rip +120%","title_zh":"SDA合同与风险偏好年末暴涨+120%","turn_id":"space_economy:trough:2025-11"},"2026-01-28":{"body":"A fast -26.3% pullback off the January peak as a global tech selloff erupted in early February 2026 on AI-profit doubts (BofA flagged 'frothy SaaS valuations') and a hawkish Fed surprise: stronger-than-expected January payrolls pushed yields higher and markets priced nearly 90% odds of a 2026 Fed rate hike. The regime tilted stagflation-ish (VIX 16→21, defensives +4.6% vs cyclicals +0.8%, growth-value -6.5%, TLT +2.3%), and high-beta space gave back fast (-26.3% vs SPY -2.0%). The move was amplified by early Neutron tank-rupture concerns emerging from qualification testing.","body_zh":"从1月高点的快速-26.3%回落，因2026年2月初全球科技抛售爆发——AI利润质疑（美银指出'SaaS估值泡沫'）和美联储鹰派意外：1月就业数据强于预期推升收益率，市场为2026年美联储加息定价近90%概率。Regime倾向类滞胀（VIX 16→21、防御+4.6% vs 周期+0.8%、成长-价值-6.5%、TLT+2.3%），高贝塔太空迅速回吐（-26.3% vs SPY-2.0%）。早期Neutron储箱破裂的资格测试担忧在此窗口开始浮现，放大了跌势。","drivers":["Feb 2026 AI-valuation selloff: frothy SaaS/tech doubts (BofA; global selloff)","Hawkish Fed surprise: Jan 2026 payrolls push yields higher, rate hike priced at 90%","Stagflation-ish tilt: defensives +4.6% vs cyclicals +0.8%, growth-value -6.5%","High-beta fast give-back: -26.3% vs SPY -2.0%"],"drivers_zh":["2026年2月AI估值抛售：SaaS/科技估值泡沫质疑（美银；全球抛售）","美联储鹰派意外：2026年1月就业数据推升收益率，加息概率定价至90%","类滞胀倾斜：防御+4.6% vs 周期+0.8%，成长-价值-6.5%","高贝塔迅速回吐：-26.3% vs SPY-2.0%"],"prev_key":"2026-01-28","prev_key_chain":["2026-01-28"],"status":"exact","title":"February AI-valuation scare pulls defensives bid -26%","title_zh":"2026年2月AI估值恐慌，防御获买盘-26%","turn_id":"space_economy:peak:2026-01"},"2026-02-12":{"body":"Yet another vertical +115.1% rally into a late-May 2026 all-time high (~$151 on RKLB) as the regime shifted to tech/semis-led risk-on (SMH +47.7%, growth>value +6.1%, VIX 21→16, SPHB-SPLV +24.4%). Oil surged +41.5% and copper-gold +19.4% added a commodities-reflation layer. The fundamental driver was the Space Development Agency's $3.5 billion Tranche 3 satellite ecosystem — with RKLB at the center — combined with Space Force naming RKLB among the Golden Dome space-based interceptor vendors (April 2026). Rocket Lab's Q1 2026 revenue hit $200M (+63.4% YoY) and the $2.2 billion backlog gave the melt-up a genuine fundamental backbone, even as the basket's +115% dwarfed SPY's +10.8% in a characteristically narrow tape (RSP-SPY -7.0%).","body_zh":"又一次垂直+115.1%反弹至2026年5月底历史高点（RKLB约151美元），regime转向科技/半导体引领风险偏好（SMH+47.7%、成长>价值+6.1%、VIX 21→16、SPHB-SPLV+24.4%）。油价飙升+41.5%，铜金+19.4%增添大宗商品再通胀维度。基本面驱动力为宇宙发展局35亿美元第三阶段卫星生态——RKLB处于中心——叠加太空部队2026年4月将RKLB列入Golden Dome天基拦截器供应商。Rocket Lab 2026年Q1营收达2亿美元（同比+63.4%），22亿美元积压为融涨提供真实基本面支撑，尽管篮子+115%在惯常狭窄行情（RSP-SPY-7.0%）中远超SPY+10.8%。","drivers":["Tech/semis-led risk-on (SMH +47.7%, VIX 21→16, SPHB-SPLV +24.4%)","Golden Dome space interceptor selection + SDA ecosystem = structural re-rate","RKLB Q1 2026 revenue $200M (+63.4%); $2.2B backlog provides fundamental anchor","Oil +41.5%, copper-gold +19.4%: commodity reflation adds industrial/defense tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["科技/半导体引领风险偏好（SMH+47.7%、VIX 21→16、SPHB-SPLV+24.4%）","Golden Dome天基拦截器入选+SDA生态=结构性重估","RKLB 2026年Q1营收2亿美元（+63.4%）；22亿美元积压提供基本面锚","油价+41.5%、铜金+19.4%：大宗商品再通胀增添工业/国防顺风"],"prev_key":"2026-02-12","prev_key_chain":["2026-02-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Spring tech-semis melt-up carries space +115%","title_zh":"春季科技半导体融涨带动太空+115%","turn_id":"space_economy:trough:2026-02"},"2026-05-28":{"body":"The current selloff: -42.0% from the May 28 all-time-high peak as two milestone-driven headwinds collided. First, Rocket Lab disclosed a Stage-1 Neutron propellant tank rupture during hydrostatic qualification testing in early 2026, pushing the maiden flight to Q4 2026 and sending RKLB shares down sharply on the news — the 'Rocket Lab stock implodes alongside its Neutron rocket' moment. Second, SpaceX's Nasdaq debut on June 12, 2026 (opening at $150/share, market cap briefly above Amazon) created a classic capital-siphon effect: investors rotated out of RKLB-style proxies into SpaceX directly, with RKLB falling ~13% on listing day. The macro backdrop tilted stagflation-ish (VIX 16→19, growth-value -10.0%, defensives +2.4% vs cyclicals -0.0%, oil -19.1% — deflationary signal), dollar firmed +2.4%. The basket -42.0% vs SPY -2.4% is the pure high-beta amplification signature.","body_zh":"当前抛售：从5月28日历史高点-42.0%，两个里程碑逆风叠加。第一，Rocket Lab在2026年年初液压资格测试中披露一级Neutron推进剂储箱破裂，首飞推迟至2026年第四季度——'Rocket Lab股价随Neutron火箭同步崩盘'时刻。第二，SpaceX 2026年6月12日登陆纳斯达克（开盘150美元，市值一度超越亚马逊）制造经典资金虹吸效应：投资者从RKLB类代理品直接转向SpaceX，RKLB上市当日跌约13%。宏观背景倾向类滞胀（VIX 16→19、成长-价值-10.0%、防御+2.4% vs 周期-0.0%、油价-19.1%——通缩信号），美元转强+2.4%。篮子-42.0% vs SPY-2.4%是纯粹高贝塔放大的标志。","drivers":["Neutron Stage-1 tank rupture (hydrostatic test failure); maiden flight delayed to Q4 2026","SpaceX Nasdaq IPO (June 12, 2026): capital siphon, RKLB -13% on listing day","Stagflation-ish tilt: growth-value -10.0%, oil -19.1%, defensives bid, dollar +2.4%","Basket -42.0% vs SPY -2.4%: milestone-driven selloff with high-beta amplification"],"drivers_zh":["Neutron一级储箱液压测试破裂；首飞延迟至2026年第四季度","SpaceX纳斯达克IPO（2026年6月12日）：资金虹吸，RKLB上市当日-13%","类滞胀倾斜：成长-价值-10.0%、油价-19.1%、防御获买盘、美元+2.4%","篮子-42.0% vs SPY-2.4%：里程碑驱动的抛售叠加高贝塔放大"],"prev_key":"2026-05-28","prev_key_chain":["2026-05-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Neutron tank rupture and SpaceX IPO siphon: -42%","title_zh":"Neutron储箱破裂与SpaceX上市虹吸：-42%","turn_id":"space_economy:peak:2026-05"}},"now":"Space Economy (RKLB/ASTS/LUNR/Earth-obs cluster) is in a \"Rolling over\" downturn at RS rank 33 (pos 43.9), having shed -42% from the late-May-2026 all-time high of ~$151 on RKLB. The macro backdrop is reflation/growth-up (cyclicals 11.2% vs defensives 6.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%, DXY +3.4%), which should be broadly friendly for cyclicals, but the basket is being dragged by two distinct headwinds: (1) a Neutron rocket Stage-1 tank rupture during qualification testing that pushed maiden flight to Q4 2026, erasing the near-term milestone catalyst; and (2) SpaceX's Nasdaq debut in June 2026 creating a \"capital siphon\" effect — investors rotated out of RKLB-style proxies into the real thing, with RKLB falling ~13% on SpaceX's listing day. Growth-value spread is -15.2%, the dollar is firming (+3.4% DXY), and high-beta themes are broadly underperforming — the classic setup for this basket to lag even a constructive index tape. It remains above its 200-day moving average (above200d=true), so the structural bull case (defense-space build-out, $2.2B backlog, SDA contracts) is intact; the question is whether the milestone-delay and SpaceX-siphon headwinds resolve before the next risk-on impulse arrives.","now_zh":"太空经济板块（RKLB/ASTS/LUNR/对地观测集群）正处于\"见顶回落\"下行阶段，相对强度排名第33位（仓位43.9），自2026年5月底RKLB历史高点约151美元已跌去约42%。宏观背景为再通胀/增长上行（周期股+11.2%对防御+6.9%、油价+19.2%、铜金+18.3%、DXY+3.4%），理论上有利于周期股，但板块面临双重逆风：(1) Neutron火箭一级储箱在资格测试中破裂，首飞推迟至2026年第四季度，近期里程碑催化剂消失；(2) SpaceX于2026年6月登陆纳斯达克产生\"资金虹吸\"效应，RKLB当日跌约13%。成长-价值利差为-15.2%，美元转强（DXY+3.4%），高贝塔主题普遍跑输——这是该篮子即便在指数温和上涨时也落后的经典格局。目前仍在200日均线之上（above200d=true），国防航天建设期基本面（22亿美元积压、SDA合同）完好；问题在于里程碑延期和SpaceX虹吸逆风能否在下一轮风险偏好脉冲到来前消化。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-travel":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"A 55.6% rally from January 2014 through November 2015 rode the collapse of crude oil from roughly $105/bbl (mid-2014) to below $40, slashing jet-fuel costs and driving record airline profits — IATA's net-profit forecasts for the global airline industry climbed into the $25bn-plus range for 2015 versus the prior cycle, and Southwest Airlines shares more than doubled in 2014 alone. The macro tape was paradoxically a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (oil -52.9%, DXY +22.7%, TLT +22.5%), but the oil crash was unambiguously bullish for airlines and tourism operators whose biggest single cost line collapsed. Health and Tech led the broader tape (+33%, +30%) while the strong dollar (DXY +22.7%) helped keep domestic travel cheap relative to international alternatives, sustaining inbound and outbound volumes.","body_zh":"从2014年1月到2015年11月55.6%的涨势，搭乘原油从约105美元/桶（2014年中）跌破40美元的崩溃，大幅削减航空燃油成本，推动航空利润创历史新高——国际航空运输协会（IATA）对全球航空业的净利润预测升至2015年的250亿美元以上区间，美国西南航空股价在2014年单年翻倍。宏观环境是放缓/通缩恐慌象限（油-52.9%、DXY+22.7%、TLT+22.5%），但油价崩溃对航空公司和旅游运营商来说是明确的利好，其最大单项成本崩塌。医疗和科技领涨大盘（+33%、+30%），强美元（DXY+22.7%）使国内旅游相对国际出行更便宜，支撑了客运量。","drivers":["OIL CRASH: crude -53%, jet-fuel costs collapse","Record airline profits; IATA net forecast $25bn+ (2015)","Strong USD DXY +22.7% — keeps domestic travel cheap","Consumer confidence and employment growth 2014-2015"],"drivers_zh":["油价崩溃：原油-53%、航空燃油成本崩塌","航空利润创纪录；IATA净利预测250亿美元+（2015年）","强美元DXY+22.7%——使国内旅游更具竞争力","消费者信心与就业增长2014-2015"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Low-oil dividend fuels airline profit boom","title_zh":"低油价红利驱动航空利润繁荣","turn_id":"travel:trough:2014-01"},"2015-11-06":{"body":"A 24.4% selloff from November 2015 through February 8, 2016, driven by the China growth scare and oil rout that triggered the worst start to any year on record in January 2016. Chinese stock circuit breakers were triggered on January 4 and 7 (the CSI 300 fell 7% then 7.2%, halting trade), oil plunged to a 12-year low below $30/bbl, and global growth fears cascaded into a flight-to-safety rotation (VIX 14 to 26, defensives led at +0.4% vs cyclicals -14.1%, TLT +11.2%). As a high-beta consumer-cyclical group, travel amplified the downturn — fear of a global recession hit discretionary spending intentions and Financials/Energy led the laggards, with the credit HYG-LQD spread widening -8.3%.","body_zh":"从2015年11月到2016年2月8日24.4%的抛售，由中国增长恐慌与油价暴跌驱动，引发史上最差开年（2016年1月）。中国股市熔断机制在1月4日和7日触发（沪深300先跌7%再跌7.2%，暂停交易），油价跌破30美元/桶至12年低位，全球增长担忧级联成避险轮动（VIX 14→26，防御板块领涨+0.4% vs 周期-14.1%，TLT+11.2%）。作为高贝塔消费周期板块，旅游放大了下行——全球衰退恐惧打击了可选消费意愿，金融/能源领跌，信用利差（HYG-LQD）扩张-8.3%。","drivers":["China circuit-breaker crash (Jan 4 & 7, 2016)","Oil to 12-year low below $30/bbl — demand-collapse fear","Flight-to-safety: VIX 14->26, TLT +11.2%","HY credit spread widens -8.3%"],"drivers_zh":["中国熔断崩盘（2016年1月4日与7日）","油价跌破30美元至12年低位——需求崩溃恐惧","避险流：VIX 14→26，TLT+11.2%","高收益信用利差扩张-8.3%"],"prev_key":"2015-11-06","prev_key_chain":["2015-11-06"],"status":"exact","title":"China growth scare and oil rout risk-off flush","title_zh":"中国增长恐慌与油价暴跌引发避险抛售","turn_id":"travel:peak:2015-11"},"2016-02-08":{"body":"A massive 106.5% rally from the February 2016 low through January 2018, the longest and deepest up-leg in the series. The proximate trough catalyst was the sharp oil recovery off the sub-$30 low, with the Shanghai G20 finance ministers' meeting (Feb 26-27, 2016) coinciding with broad risk-asset stabilization; the tape then turned forcefully reflationary (oil +117.1%, DXY -6.7%, VIX 26 to 11, cyclicals +68.6% vs defensives +28.1%, SMH +136.9%). Two further catalysts layered on: the Trump election in November 2016 unleashing fiscal-stimulus and corporate-tax-cut expectations, and the passage of the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act in December 2017. Airlines benefited from low-ish fuel costs and disciplined capacity, while lodging and online travel agencies (Expedia, Booking) saw earnings upgrades as US GDP and consumer confidence hit cycle highs. Financials (+86.2%) led the reflation; travel rode the high-beta cyclical tide with credit spreads tightening (HYG-LQD +14.9).","body_zh":"从2016年2月低点到2018年1月106.5%的巨大涨幅，是本系列最长最深的上行段。低点的直接催化是油价从30美元下方急剧回升，2016年2月26-27日上海G20财长会议与风险资产的普遍企稳相重合；市场随后强势转入再通胀（油+117.1%、DXY-6.7%、VIX 26→11，周期+68.6% vs 防御+28.1%，SMH+136.9%）。另有两重催化叠加：2016年11月特朗普当选释放财政刺激与企业减税预期、2017年12月《减税与就业法案》落地。航空公司受益于偏低燃油成本加运力纪律，酒店与在线旅游平台（Expedia、Booking）随美国GDP与消费者信心触及周期高点而迎来盈利上调。金融领涨（+86.2%），旅游搭乘高贝塔周期浪潮，信用利差收窄（HYG-LQD+14.9）。","drivers":["OIL recovery +117% off sub-$30 low; DXY -6.7%","Trump election + Tax Cuts and Jobs Act Dec 2017","Cyclical melt-up: VIX 26->11, Financials +86.2%","Sustained strong US consumer confidence and GDP growth"],"drivers_zh":["油价从30美元下方回升+117%；DXY-6.7%","特朗普当选+2017年12月《减税与就业法案》","周期融涨：VIX 26→11、金融+86.2%","美国消费者信心与GDP持续强劲"],"prev_key":"2016-02-08","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Reflation melt-up: oil recovery, Trump tax, cyclical surge","title_zh":"再通胀融涨：油价复苏、特朗普减税、周期股飙升","turn_id":"travel:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-23":{"body":"A 25.8% decline from January 2018 through Christmas Eve 2018, driven by the Fed's four rate hikes in 2018 (to 2.25-2.50% on December 19 — the worst December since 1931 for markets) and escalating US-China trade-war tariffs. The tape turned risk-off into a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (VIX 11 to 36, DXY +7.1%, oil -34%, cyclicals -21.2% vs defensives -5.3%), and as the highest-beta consumer-cyclical basket, travel amplified the move. Fed Chair Powell's October 2018 remark about rates being 'a long way from neutral' crystallized recession fears, while the December 19 hike into a deteriorating economy triggered the climactic selloff through Christmas Eve.","body_zh":"从2018年1月到2018年圣诞前夜25.8%的下跌，由美联储2018年四次加息（12月19日加息至2.25-2.50%，为1931年以来最差12月）与不断升级的中美贸易战关税驱动。市场转入避险放缓/通缩恐慌象限（VIX 11→36，DXY+7.1%，油-34%，周期-21.2% vs 防御-5.3%），旅游作为最高贝塔消费周期板块放大了跌势。美联储主席鲍威尔2018年10月关于利率距'中性水平还很远'的言论固化了衰退恐惧，12月19日加息至恶化的经济环境则触发了直至圣诞前夜的高潮式抛售。","drivers":["Fed hikes 4x in 2018; Dec 19 hike seen as policy error","US-China trade-war escalation throughout 2018","VIX 11->36; worst December since 1931","Oil -34%; high-beta travel amplifies (Discretionary -15%)"],"drivers_zh":["2018年美联储四次加息；12月19日加息被视为政策失误","中美贸易战2018年全年持续升级","VIX 11→36；1931年以来最差12月","油价-34%；高贝塔旅游放大跌幅（可选消费-15%）"],"prev_key":"2018-01-23","prev_key_chain":["2018-01-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed rate-hike bear triggers cyclical selloff","title_zh":"美联储加息熊市触发周期股抛售","turn_id":"travel:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"A 46.6% rally from the December 24, 2018 low through January 17, 2020, anchored by the Fed's January 2019 pivot to patience (ending the rate-hike cycle) followed by three insurance cuts in H2 2019 (July, September, October), and capped by the US-China Phase One trade deal announcement on December 13, 2019, which sent world markets to record highs. The tape moved into a reflation/growth-up regime (cyclicals +40.9% vs defensives +33.5%, SMH +83.1%, TLT +16.4% as yields fell, VIX 36 to 12). Travel stocks benefited from the combination of lower borrowing costs, a stable oil price, strong employment and consumer spending, and renewed confidence in the global growth outlook as airlines and hotels ran at record load factors and ADRs heading into January 2020.","body_zh":"从2018年12月24日低点到2020年1月17日46.6%的涨势，以美联储2019年1月转向耐心（结束加息周期）为锚，随后在2019年下半年三次预防性降息（7月、9月、10月），并以2019年12月13日中美第一阶段贸易协议宣布（推动全球股市创历史新高）为终点。市场进入再通胀/增长向上体制（周期+40.9% vs 防御+33.5%，SMH+83.1%，TLT+16.4%，VIX 36→12）。旅游股受益于借贷成本降低、油价稳定、就业和消费者支出强劲，以及对全球增长前景的信心重建，航空公司和酒店以历史纪录的客座率和平均日房价迎来2020年1月。","drivers":["Fed Jan 2019 pivot to patience; 3x cuts H2 2019","US-China Phase One trade deal Dec 13, 2019","SMH +83.1%, VIX 36->12 — risk-on melt-up","Record airline load factors and hotel ADRs"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月转向耐心；2019年下半年三次降息","中美第一阶段贸易协议2019年12月13日","SMH+83.1%，VIX 36→12——风险偏好融涨","航空客座率与酒店ADR创历史纪录"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot and trade truce power recovery","title_zh":"美联储转向与贸易休战驱动复苏","turn_id":"travel:trough:2018-12"},"2020-01-17":{"body":"A catastrophic 65.2% collapse from January 17 to March 18, 2020 — the worst leg in the 15-year series — as COVID-19 spread from Wuhan globally and governments imposed travel bans, border closures, and lockdowns. The WHO declared a pandemic on March 11; the VIX hit 82.69 on March 16 (the highest in history), and the DJIA fell 27% by March 23. BEACH stocks (Booking, Entertainment, Airlines, Cruises, Hotels) were the hardest-hit cohort — the global airline industry's market cap was decimated, Delta Air Lines fell 50%+, and hotel occupancy collapsed below 25% by April. The tape was a risk-off flight-to-safety (defensives -16.6% vs cyclicals -36.9%, DXY +3.6%, oil -65.2%, breadth -5.9%).","body_zh":"从2020年1月17日到3月18日65.2%的灾难性崩溃——本系列15年中最惨烈的一段——随着新冠病毒从武汉蔓延至全球，各国政府相继实施旅行禁令、边境封锁和封城。世卫组织3月11日宣布大流行；VIX于3月16日触达82.69（历史最高），道琼斯指数至3月23日下跌27%。BEACH板块（订票、娱乐、航空、邮轮、酒店）受创最深——全球航空业市值遭重创，达美航空跌逾50%，4月酒店入住率跌破25%。市场是避险防御轮动（防御-16.6% vs 周期-36.9%，DXY+3.6%，油-65.2%，广度-5.9%）。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic; WHO declaration March 11, 2020","VIX peak 82.69 (March 16) — highest ever recorded","Travel bans, border closures, lockdowns globally","Oil -65.2%; BEACH stocks crushed vs SPY -27.7%"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情；世卫组织2020年3月11日宣布大流行","VIX峰值82.69（3月16日）——史上最高","全球旅行禁令、边境封锁与封城","油价-65.2%；BEACH板块暴跌 vs SPY-27.7%"],"prev_key":"2020-01-17","prev_key_chain":["2020-01-17"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID-19 pandemic erases travel demand","title_zh":"新冠疫情消灭旅游需求","turn_id":"travel:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"A sharp 53.9% counter-rally from March 18 to March 26, 2020, ignited by the Fed's March 23 open-ended ('unlimited') QE announcement plus new corporate-credit facilities, and amplified by the imminent passage of the CARES Act (Senate passed it March 25; it was signed March 27 with $25bn in airline payroll grants plus $25bn in loans). The three-day March 24-26 tape was one of the strongest on record (S&P +17%+), with cyclicals leading (Energy +29.6%, Discretionary +16.6%) on an abruptly reflationary quad (cyclicals +16.3% vs defensives +0.8%) — but VIX remained at 61 and credit was still impaired (HYG-LQD -5.8%), confirming this was a policy-driven relief bounce rather than a fundamental recovery of travel demand.","body_zh":"从2020年3月18日到3月26日53.9%的急速反弹，由美联储3月23日开放式（'无限量'）QE宣布加上新设企业信贷工具点燃，并因CARES法案即将通过而放大（参议院于3月25日通过，3月27日签署，含250亿美元航空工资补贴与250亿美元贷款）。3月24-26日三日行情为史上最强之一（标普涨逾17%），周期股领涨（能源+29.6%，可选消费+16.6%），市场骤然转入再通胀象限（周期+16.3% vs 防御+0.8%），但VIX仍在61，信用仍受损（HYG-LQD-5.8%），印证这是政策驱动的救济反弹，而非旅游需求的基本面复苏。","drivers":["Fed March 23 unlimited QE + corporate-credit facilities","CARES Act imminent (Senate passed Mar 25, signed Mar 27)","Cyclical bounce: Energy +29.6%, Discretionary +16.6%","Policy-driven relief; VIX still 61, credit still impaired"],"drivers_zh":["美联储3月23日无限量QE+企业信贷工具","CARES法案临近（参议院3月25日通过，3月27日签署）","周期反弹：能源+29.6%，可选消费+16.6%","政策驱动救济；VIX仍61，信用仍受损"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed unlimited QE and imminent CARES bounce","title_zh":"美联储无限量QE与CARES法案临近触发反弹","turn_id":"travel:trough:2020-03"},"2020-03-26":{"body":"A 29.1% pullback from March 26 to April 3, 2020, as the pandemic showed no signs of abating and US daily case counts surged through late March, with New York becoming the global epicenter. The tape reflected a stagflation-ish regime (oil surged +25.4% on OPEC+ cut hopes, yet cyclicals fell -7.0% vs defensives -1.2%, VIX 61 to 47) — a commodity-driven squeeze rather than a growth recovery. Travel stocks led the decline as forward bookings collapsed and load-factor data showed air-passenger traffic was only about 4% of year-prior levels by mid-April.","body_zh":"从2020年3月26日到4月3日29.1%的回调，疫情毫无缓解迹象，美国日增病例在3月底飙升，纽约成为全球疫情中心。市场呈现类滞胀格局（OPEC+减产预期推动油价+25.4%，但周期股仍下跌-7.0% vs 防御-1.2%，VIX从61降至47）——是商品驱动的成本挤压而非增长复苏。旅游股领跌，预订崩溃与客座率数据显示至4月中旬航空客运量仅为上年同期的约4%。","drivers":["US daily COVID cases surging; NY becomes epicenter","OPEC+ cut hopes lift oil +25.4% — cost pressure on airlines","Stagflation-ish quad: cyclicals still -7% vs defensives","Air traffic at ~4% of year-prior levels by mid-April"],"drivers_zh":["美国日增新冠病例飙升；纽约成全球疫情中心","OPEC+减产预期推动油价+25.4%——航空成本压力","类滞胀象限：周期股仍-7% vs 防御股","航空客运量仅为去年同期的约4%（4月中旬）"],"prev_key":"2020-03-26","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-26"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID resurgence and oil-squeeze re-sink travel","title_zh":"疫情持续与油价挤压再度打压旅游板块","turn_id":"travel:peak:2020-03"},"2020-04-03":{"body":"A powerful 117.6% rally from the April 3 trough through June 8, 2020 — driven by the Fed's massive balance-sheet expansion and fiscal stimulus (CARES Act total $2.2 trillion), combined with the first green shoots of reopening as states began easing lockdowns in May. The tape was aggressively reflationary (oil +34.8%, DXY -3.9%, TLT -6.8%, cyclicals +40.9% vs defensives +17.1%, breadth RSP +11.4% vs SPY, high-beta premium SPHB-SPLV +60.9%). As the most beaten-down cyclical group, travel amplified the 'return to normal' trade by roughly 4x the SPY's +30.2%, with Energy (+57.1%) and Discretionary (+44.2%) leading the sectors.","body_zh":"从2020年4月3日低点到6月8日117.6%的强劲涨幅——由美联储大规模扩表与财政刺激（CARES法案总额2.2万亿美元）驱动，叠加5月各州开始放宽封城的首批复苏迹象。市场呈强力再通胀色彩（油+34.8%，DXY-3.9%，TLT-6.8%，周期+40.9% vs 防御+17.1%，广度RSP+11.4% vs SPY，高贝塔溢价SPHB-SPLV+60.9%）。作为跌幅最深的周期板块，旅游以约4倍于SPY+30.2%的幅度放大了'回归正常'的交易，能源（+57.1%）和可选消费（+44.2%）领涨各板块。","drivers":["Fed balance-sheet expansion + CARES $2.2tn fiscal","May 2020 state reopenings; lockdowns ease","SPHB-SPLV +60.9%; broad reflation (RSP +11.4%)","Travel most beaten-down sector; amplifies SPY ~4x"],"drivers_zh":["美联储扩表+CARES 2.2万亿财政刺激","2020年5月各州重启；封城放宽","SPHB-SPLV+60.9%；广泛再通胀（RSP+11.4%）","旅游跌幅最深；放大SPY涨幅约4倍"],"prev_key":"2020-04-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-04-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Reopening optimism drives 117% surge","title_zh":"重启乐观情绪推动117%飙升","turn_id":"travel:trough:2020-04"},"2020-06-08":{"body":"A 26.9% selloff from June 8 to June 26, 2020, as COVID-19 second-wave fears materialized in Sun Belt states — Texas, Arizona, and California reported sharp case-count increases after lockdown easing, and travel and leisure stocks were singled out as the epicenter of the selloff. Delta Air Lines and JetBlue fell sharply, and cruise lines and online travel agencies plunged. The tape rotated to a slowdown/deflation-scare (VIX 26 to 35, cyclicals -10.8% vs defensives -7.6%, narrow tape RSP lagged SPY -5.8%), with Tech (roughly flat, -0.1%) sheltering as the group least exposed to physical-world risk.","body_zh":"从2020年6月8日到6月26日26.9%的抛售，随着阳光地带各州（德州、亚利桑那、加州）解封后新增病例急剧上升，第二波新冠疫情担忧成真，旅游和休闲股被点名为此轮抛售的震中。达美航空与捷蓝航空大幅下跌，邮轮公司与在线旅游平台暴跌。市场轮动至放缓/通缩恐慌（VIX 26→35，周期-10.8% vs 防御-7.6%，广度收窄RSP跑输SPY-5.8%），科技板块（约略平盘，-0.1%）成为对实体世界风险暴露最小的避难所。","drivers":["Second-wave COVID: Texas, Arizona, California surge","Airlines and cruise lines sold hard; OTAs plunge","VIX 26->35; flight-to-safety (Tech -0.1% vs travel -27%)","Narrow tape: RSP lagged SPY -5.8%"],"drivers_zh":["第二波新冠：德州、亚利桑那、加州病例飙升","航空与邮轮股遭重挫；在线旅游平台暴跌","VIX 26→35；避险（科技-0.1% vs 旅游-27%）","广度收窄：RSP跑输SPY-5.8%"],"prev_key":"2020-06-08","prev_key_chain":["2020-06-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Second-wave COVID fears re-hit travel","title_zh":"第二波疫情担忧再度冲击旅游","turn_id":"travel:peak:2020-06"},"2020-06-26":{"body":"A 115.9% surge from June 26, 2020 through March 15, 2021 — the largest structural up-leg in the basket's history — detonated by the Pfizer/BioNTech vaccine 90%+ efficacy announcement on November 9, 2020, on which airline and cruise stocks surged 20-30% in a single session, transforming the market's probabilistic framework for a return to normal travel. The macro regime was a textbook reflationary melt-up: yields surged (TLT -16.4%), DXY fell -5.8%, oil +69.9%, copper/gold +57.6%, high-beta SPHB-SPLV +72.0, broad breadth RSP beat SPY +13.0%, and Financials (+54.8%), Energy (+49.4%), and Industrials (+48.7%) led. Airlines, cruises, and hotels — the most COVID-crushed names — were the single biggest beneficiaries of the 'rotation into the beaten-down' trade as the vaccine made their existential risk finite.","body_zh":"从2020年6月26日到2021年3月15日115.9%的飙升——篮子历史上最大的结构性上行段——由辉瑞/BioNTech疫苗2020年11月9日宣布90%+有效性引爆，当日航空与邮轮股单日飙升20-30%，彻底改变了市场对旅游回归正常的概率框架。宏观环境是教科书式再通胀融涨：收益率飙升（TLT-16.4%），DXY下降-5.8%，油+69.9%，铜金比+57.6，高贝塔SPHB-SPLV+72.0，广度扩散RSP跑赢SPY+13.0%，金融（+54.8%）、能源（+49.4%）、工业（+48.7%）领涨。航空、邮轮、酒店——最受疫情打压的名字——作为疫苗使其存亡风险有限化的直接受益者，成为'轮动至被打压板块'交易的最大赢家。","drivers":["Pfizer vaccine Nov 9, 2020: airline/cruise stocks +20-30%","Reflation melt-up: TLT -16.4%, oil +69.9%, SPHB-SPLV +72.0","Broad breadth RSP +13.0% vs SPY — most beaten sectors led","Airlines/cruises/hotels as direct vaccine beneficiaries"],"drivers_zh":["辉瑞疫苗2020年11月9日：航空/邮轮股单日+20-30%","再通胀融涨：TLT-16.4%，油+69.9%，SPHB-SPLV+72.0","广度扩散RSP+13.0% vs SPY——跌幅最深板块领涨","航空/邮轮/酒店作为疫苗直接受益者"],"prev_key":"2020-06-26","prev_key_chain":["2020-06-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Vaccine breakthroughs detonate reopening super-rally","title_zh":"疫苗突破引爆重启超级反弹","turn_id":"travel:trough:2020-06"},"2021-03-15":{"body":"A 22.2% pullback from March 15 through July 19, 2021, as the Delta variant emerged and raised fresh doubts about the pace and durability of reopening. The tape rotated to a slowdown/deflation-scare quad (yields fell — TLT +11.3%; defensives led cyclicals +7.9% vs +2.3%; high-beta de-rated SPHB-SPLV -15.8; narrow tape RSP -4.5% vs SPY). Travel stocks pulled back even as SPY gained +7.9%, as the group was by then fully priced for peak reopening and most exposed to any incremental virus risk. Airlines began warning of booking pauses as Delta spread across the unvaccinated US and globally.","body_zh":"从2021年3月15日到7月19日22.2%的回调，随着Delta变种出现，重新引发对重启速度与持续性的质疑。市场轮动至放缓/通缩恐慌象限（收益率下行——TLT+11.3%；防御跑赢周期+7.9% vs +2.3%；高贝塔估值下调SPHB-SPLV-15.8；市场广度收窄RSP-4.5% vs SPY）。旅游股回调，而SPY仍上涨+7.9%，因为该板块当时已充分定价了重启高峰，对任何增量病毒风险最为脆弱。随着Delta在未接种疫苗的美国和全球蔓延，航空公司开始警告预订暂停。","drivers":["Delta variant emerges; booking pauses resume","Deflation-scare tape: TLT +11.3%, defensives lead +7.9%","High-beta de-rates: SPHB-SPLV -15.8","Travel priced for peak reopening; most exposed to variant risk"],"drivers_zh":["Delta变种出现；预订暂停重现","通缩恐慌环境：TLT+11.3%，防御领涨+7.9%","高贝塔估值下调：SPHB-SPLV-15.8","旅游充分定价重启高峰；对变种风险暴露最大"],"prev_key":"2021-03-15","prev_key_chain":["2021-03-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Delta variant pause and deflation-scare rotation","title_zh":"Delta变种暂停与通缩恐慌轮动","turn_id":"travel:peak:2021-03"},"2021-07-19":{"body":"A 22.9% recovery from July 19 through November 5, 2021, as Delta variant fears faded with rising vaccination rates and risk-on returned across the cyclical complex. The tape was a reflation/growth-up regime (SMH +20.2%, growth>value +3.9, VIX 22 to 16, cyclicals +15.2% vs defensives +4.1%, oil +22.4%) with Energy (+25.6%) and Discretionary (+20.2%) leading. As a high-beta cyclical, travel amplified the move as airline load factors rebounded strongly through summer 2021, hotel occupancy recovered, and Booking Holdings and Expedia reported surging Q3 bookings. Pent-up leisure demand remained robust heading into year-end.","body_zh":"从2021年7月19日到11月5日22.9%的复苏，随着接种率上升Delta变种担忧消退，风险偏好在周期板块全面回归。市场呈再通胀/增长向上格局（SMH+20.2%，成长跑赢价值+3.9，VIX 22→16，周期+15.2% vs 防御+4.1%，油+22.4%），能源（+25.6%）与可选消费（+20.2%）领涨。作为高贝塔周期股，旅游放大了涨势，2021年夏季航空客座率强劲反弹，酒店入住率回升，Booking Holdings与Expedia报告第三季度预订量激增。被压抑的休闲需求在年末依然强劲。","drivers":["Delta fears fade; vaccination rates rise","Risk-on reflation: SMH +20.2%, VIX 22->16, oil +22.4%","Summer 2021 airline/hotel demand rebounds strongly","Booking Holdings, Expedia report surging Q3 bookings"],"drivers_zh":["Delta担忧消退；疫苗接种率上升","风险偏好再通胀：SMH+20.2%，VIX 22→16，油+22.4%","2021年夏季航空/酒店需求强劲反弹","Booking Holdings、Expedia第三季度预订激增"],"prev_key":"2021-07-19","prev_key_chain":["2021-07-19"],"status":"exact","title":"Delta fades; risk-on reflation resumes","title_zh":"Delta消退；风险偏好再通胀重启","turn_id":"travel:trough:2021-07"},"2021-11-05":{"body":"A 21.7% decline from November 5 to December 1, 2021, as the Omicron variant was identified in southern Africa on November 24 and rapidly triggered international travel bans (the UK, EU, and US announced restrictions within days). The VIX surged from 16 to 31, oil crashed -19.3% on demand-destruction fears, and the tape moved to a slowdown/deflation-scare (cyclicals -5.0% vs defensives -2.9%; RSP lagged SPY -2.1%). As the highest-beta consumer-cyclical group, travel was hit far harder than the -3.8% SPY as forward bookings immediately stalled across airlines, cruise lines, and hotels.","body_zh":"从2021年11月5日到12月1日21.7%的下跌，Omicron变种于11月24日在南部非洲被发现，并迅速引发国际旅行禁令（英国、欧盟和美国在数日内宣布限制措施）。VIX从16飙升至31，油价因需求破坏恐惧暴跌-19.3%，市场转向放缓/通缩恐慌（周期-5.0% vs 防御-2.9%；等权RSP跑输SPY-2.1%）。作为最高贝塔的消费周期板块，旅游受创远超SPY的-3.8%，航空公司、邮轮公司和酒店的远期预订立即停滞。","drivers":["Omicron variant ID'd Nov 24; travel bans within days","VIX 16->31; oil -19.3% on demand-destruction fear","Travel bans restart; bookings stall immediately","High-beta travel sold hardest vs SPY -3.8%"],"drivers_zh":["Omicron变种11月24日确认；数日内旅行禁令启动","VIX 16→31；油价-19.3%（需求破坏担忧）","旅行禁令重启；预订即刻停滞","高贝塔旅游跌幅远超SPY-3.8%"],"prev_key":"2021-11-05","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Omicron scare triggers sharp risk-off flush","title_zh":"Omicron恐慌触发急剧避险抛售","turn_id":"travel:peak:2021-11"},"2021-12-01":{"body":"A 22.6% rebound from December 1, 2021 through February 16, 2022, as Omicron proved substantially milder than feared (UK and South African data showed lower hospitalization rates by mid-December) and travel restrictions began to ease. The macro tape shifted to reflation/growth-up (oil +42.8%, broad RSP beat SPY +4.3%, cyclicals +4.9% vs defensives +3.7%, TLT -10.6% as yields rose) even as SPY was flat (-0.5%), confirming this was a rotation within the market rather than a broad advance. Travel stocks recovered sharply as airlines announced full flight-schedule restorations and bookings for spring/summer 2022 surged.","body_zh":"从2021年12月1日到2022年2月16日22.6%的反弹，Omicron被证明比担忧温和得多（12月中旬英国和南非数据显示住院率更低），旅行限制开始放宽。宏观环境转向再通胀/增长向上（油+42.8%，广度扩散RSP跑赢SPY+4.3%，周期+4.9% vs 防御+3.7%，TLT-10.6%收益率上升），尽管SPY几乎横盘（-0.5%），印证这是市场内部的轮动而非普遍上涨。旅游股大幅反弹，航空公司宣布全面恢复航班计划，2022年春夏预订量激增。","drivers":["Omicron proves milder than feared; hospitalization rates low","Oil +42.8%; reflation broadening (RSP +4.3% vs SPY)","Travel restrictions ease; spring/summer bookings surge","Yields rise TLT -10.6%; energy/value rotation"],"drivers_zh":["Omicron被证实更温和；住院率偏低","油+42.8%；再通胀广度扩散（RSP+4.3% vs SPY）","旅行限制放宽；春夏预订激增","收益率上升TLT-10.6%；能源/价值轮动"],"prev_key":"2021-12-01","prev_key_chain":["2021-12-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Omicron proves mild; reopening confidence recovers","title_zh":"Omicron证实温和；重启信心回升","turn_id":"travel:trough:2021-12"},"2022-02-16":{"body":"A 24.8% selloff from February 16 to March 7, 2022, as Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine on February 24, 2022 sent oil spiking +27.5% (Brent above $130/bbl by March 7) into a stagflation-ish quad — the dual hit of surging jet-fuel costs and a consumer-confidence collapse was uniquely damaging for travel. The tape went risk-off (VIX 24 to 36, DXY +3.8%) with flight-to-safety (defensives +2.3% vs cyclicals -5.1%, Energy +11.3% as the only sector positive, Tech/Financials/Discretionary -9% to -12%). As the highest-beta consumer-cyclical, travel amplified the stagflation squeeze — consumers facing $4+ gasoline and food inflation cut discretionary travel budgets.","body_zh":"从2022年2月16日到3月7日24.8%的抛售，俄罗斯2022年2月24日对乌克兰发动全面入侵，推动油价飙升+27.5%（布伦特原油至3月7日超过130美元/桶），进入类滞胀象限——航空燃油成本激增与消费者信心崩溃的双重打击对旅游尤为致命。市场转向避险（VIX 24→36，DXY+3.8%），出现避险流（防御+2.3% vs 周期-5.1%，能源+11.3%为唯一正涨板块，科技/金融/可选消费跌幅-9%至-12%）。作为最高贝塔的消费周期股，旅游放大了滞胀挤压——面临4美元以上汽油和食品通胀的消费者削减可选旅游预算。","drivers":["Russia invades Ukraine Feb 24; oil spikes +27.5% to $130","Stagflation-ish quad: jet-fuel costs surge","VIX 24->36; DXY +3.8%; flight-to-safety rotation","Consumer-confidence collapse; Discretionary -12.3%"],"drivers_zh":["俄罗斯2月24日入侵乌克兰；油价飙升+27.5%至130美元","类滞胀象限：航空燃油成本激增","VIX 24→36；DXY+3.8%；避险轮动","消费者信心崩溃；可选消费-12.3%"],"prev_key":"2022-02-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-02-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Ukraine war oil shock triggers stagflation scare","title_zh":"乌克兰战争油价冲击引发滞胀担忧","turn_id":"travel:peak:2022-02"},"2022-03-07":{"body":"A 24.2% rally from March 7 to March 29, 2022, as oil reversed sharply from the $130 spike (-12.7%) on the first signals of Ukraine ceasefire negotiations, briefly turning the macro tape goldilocks/disinflation (SMH +16.9%, growth>value +7.2, VIX 36 to 19, cyclicals +10.4% vs defensives +4.2%). Pent-up spring and summer 2022 travel demand reasserted strongly — airlines had forward bookings near full capacity for peak summer — and the high-beta travel basket amplified the move (Discretionary +17.5% led sectors), even as underlying yields remained elevated (TLT -6.1%).","body_zh":"从2022年3月7日到3月29日24.2%的反弹，随着乌克兰停火谈判的首批信号出现，油价从130美元飙升高点急剧回落（-12.7%），宏观环境短暂转向金发姑娘/去通胀（SMH+16.9%，成长跑赢价值+7.2，VIX 36→19，周期+10.4% vs 防御+4.2%）。被压抑的2022年春夏旅游需求强力重现——航空公司旺季夏季的远期预订接近满舱——高贝塔旅游篮子放大了涨势（可选消费+17.5%领涨各板块），尽管底层收益率仍偏高（TLT-6.1%）。","drivers":["Oil reverses -12.7% on Ukraine ceasefire talks","Disinflation tape: SMH +16.9%, VIX 36->19","Pent-up summer 2022 travel bookings near capacity","High-beta travel amplifies (Discretionary +17.5%)"],"drivers_zh":["油价因乌克兰停火谈判回落-12.7%","去通胀环境：SMH+16.9%，VIX 36→19","2022年夏季旅游预订被压抑需求接近满舱","高贝塔旅游放大（可选消费+17.5%）"],"prev_key":"2022-03-07","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil pullback sparks brief disinflation relief","title_zh":"油价回落引发短暂去通胀救济反弹","turn_id":"travel:trough:2022-03"},"2022-03-29":{"body":"A 35.0% decline from March 29 to June 16, 2022, as the Fed's most aggressive hiking cycle since Volcker (a 50bp hike on May 4 and a 75bp hike on June 15, the largest since 1994) crushed consumer-cyclical valuations inside a stagflation-ish quad (TLT -14.1%, DXY +5.3%, VIX 19 to 33, oil +12.8% kept fuel costs elevated). Recession fears intensified as the yield curve inverted. The tape was a flight-to-safety rotation (defensives -11.2% vs cyclicals -18.2%); Discretionary (-29.7%) was the worst-performing GICS sector, and high-beta travel amplified the move by nearly 2x SPY's -20.6% decline.","body_zh":"从2022年3月29日到6月16日35.0%的下跌，美联储自沃尔克以来最激进的加息周期（5月4日加息50bp和6月15日加息75bp——1994年以来最大单次加息）在类滞胀象限中粉碎了消费周期估值（TLT-14.1%，DXY+5.3%，VIX 19→33，油+12.8%使燃油成本居高不下）。随着收益率曲线倒挂，衰退担忧加剧。市场呈避险轮动（防御-11.2% vs 周期-18.2%）；可选消费（-29.7%）是GICS表现最差的板块，高贝塔旅游以接近2倍的幅度放大跌势（-35% vs SPY-20.6%）。","drivers":["Fed 75bp hike June 15, largest since 1994; recession fears","TLT -14.1%, DXY +5.3%; yield curve inverts","Stagflation-ish: oil +12.8% keeps fuel costs elevated","Discretionary -29.7%; travel -35% vs SPY -20.6%"],"drivers_zh":["美联储6月15日加息75bp——1994年以来最大；衰退担忧","TLT-14.1%，DXY+5.3%；收益率曲线倒挂","类滞胀：油+12.8%使燃油成本居高不下","可选消费-29.7%；旅游-35% vs SPY-20.6%"],"prev_key":"2022-03-29","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed rate-hike bear catches travel in stagflation","title_zh":"美联储加息熊市在滞胀中波及旅游","turn_id":"travel:peak:2022-03"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"A 67.7% surge from the June 2022 bear low through July 18, 2023, powered by 'revenge travel' — pent-up experiential demand ran full throttle as consumers prioritized experiences over goods even as the Fed kept hiking. The macro tailwind was real: a tech/semis-led goldilocks melt-up (SMH +58.9%, VIX 33 to 13, growth>value +21.4, oil -35.6%, DXY -3.6%), with the June 2022 CPI peak (9.1%) confirming inflation had topped and opening the door to a disinflation narrative. Airlines ran record load factors and pricing power surpassed 2019 levels; Booking Holdings and Hilton beat earnings estimates repeatedly. Cyclicals (+25.6%) beat defensives (+9.0%) broadly.","body_zh":"从2022年6月熊市低点到2023年7月18日67.7%的飙升，由'报复性旅游'驱动——即便美联储仍在加息，被压抑的体验式需求也全速释放，消费者优先选择体验而非商品。宏观顺风是真实的：科技/半导体引领的金发姑娘融涨（SMH+58.9%，VIX 33→13，成长跑赢价值+21.4，油-35.6%，DXY-3.6%），2022年6月CPI峰值（9.1%）确认通胀见顶，为去通胀叙事打开大门。航空公司以历史纪录的客座率运营，定价能力超过2019年水平；Booking Holdings和希尔顿反复超越盈利预期。周期（+25.6%）全面跑赢防御（+9.0%）。","drivers":["'Revenge travel' demand full throttle post-COVID","Disinflation melt-up: SMH +58.9%, VIX 33->13, oil -35.6%","Record airline load factors; pricing above 2019 levels","June 2022 CPI peak (9.1%) confirms inflation topped"],"drivers_zh":["疫情后'报复性旅游'需求全速释放","去通胀融涨：SMH+58.9%，VIX 33→13，油-35.6%","航空客座率创历史纪录；定价超2019年水平","2022年6月CPI峰值（9.1%）确认通胀见顶"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Revenge-travel boom on disinflation melt-up","title_zh":"报复性旅游繁荣搭乘去通胀融涨","turn_id":"travel:trough:2022-06"},"2023-07-18":{"body":"A 25.6% pullback from July 18 to October 27, 2023, as the 10-year Treasury yield surged to 5.02% on October 19 (the highest since 2007) in a sharp rate-regime move (TLT -16.4%, DXY +6.6%) driven by the 'higher for longer' Fed narrative and Treasury supply concerns. The stagflation-ish quad (oil +12.9%, VIX 13 to 21, narrow tape RSP -3.2% vs SPY) punished consumer-facing cyclicals especially: Discretionary (-15.0%) was the worst GICS laggard as fears grew that peak 'revenge travel' demand had passed and rate-sensitive consumers would cut experiential spending. Credit markets were an exception (HYG-LQD +4.0%), limiting the downside but not reversing it.","body_zh":"从2023年7月18日到10月27日25.6%的回调，10年期美债收益率于10月19日飙升至5.02%（2007年以来最高），构成剧烈的利率政策冲击（TLT-16.4%，DXY+6.6%），由'更高更长'的美联储叙事与美债供给担忧驱动。类滞胀象限（油+12.9%，VIX 13→21，广度收窄RSP-3.2% vs SPY）尤其惩罚了面向消费者的周期股：可选消费（-15.0%）是最差的GICS板块，市场担忧'报复性旅游'峰值需求已过，对利率敏感的消费者将削减体验式消费。信用市场例外（HYG-LQD+4.0%），限制了下行但未能逆转。","drivers":["10-year hits 5.02% (Oct 19) — highest since 2007","TLT -16.4%, DXY +6.6%; 'higher for longer' Fed narrative","Peak-travel-demand fears; Discretionary -15.0% worst sector","Narrow tape RSP -3.2% vs SPY; high-beta de-rates"],"drivers_zh":["10年期收益率10月19日触达5.02%——2007年以来最高","TLT-16.4%，DXY+6.6%；'更高更长'美联储叙事","旅游需求见顶担忧；可选消费-15.0%最差板块","广度收窄RSP-3.2% vs SPY；高贝塔估值下调"],"prev_key":"2023-07-18","prev_key_chain":["2023-07-18"],"status":"exact","title":"10-year to 5% kills consumer-cyclical momentum","title_zh":"10年期利率破5%扼杀消费周期动能","turn_id":"travel:peak:2023-07"},"2023-10-27":{"body":"An 80.9% advance from October 27, 2023 through February 19, 2025, anchored by the Fed's late-2023 dovish pivot (pausing hikes) and three rate cuts in 2024 (September, November, December) that underpinned a broad goldilocks/disinflation melt-up (SMH +88.0%, VIX 21 to 15, TLT +10.3%, growth>value +22.9). Experiential demand stayed structurally elevated well above 2019 levels as travel proved a 'sticky' consumer priority. Financials (+69.4%), Comm (+68.6%), and Discretionary (+52.8%) led cyclicals broadly. The tape was extremely narrow (RSP lagged SPY -12.3%) — a mega-cap-led melt-up that nonetheless sustained travel at new highs as strong employment and consumer balance sheets fueled leisure and corporate travel.","body_zh":"从2023年10月27日到2025年2月19日80.9%的上涨，以美联储2023年底鸽派转向（暂停加息）与2024年三次降息（9月、11月、12月）为锚，支撑了广泛的金发姑娘/去通胀融涨（SMH+88.0%，VIX 21→15，TLT+10.3%，成长跑赢价值+22.9）。体验式需求在结构上持续高于2019年水平，旅游被证明是消费者的'粘性'优先项。金融（+69.4%）、通信（+68.6%）、可选消费（+52.8%）领涨周期股。市场极度狭窄（等权RSP跑输SPY-12.3%）——大盘股主导的融涨，但在强劲就业与消费者资产负债表支撑下，旅游持续创历史新高，受益于休闲与商务旅游双轮驱动。","drivers":["Fed pivots late 2023; 3x rate cuts in 2024","Goldilocks melt-up: SMH +88.0%, TLT +10.3%, VIX 21->15","Soft landing: consumer balance sheets fund continued travel","Experiential spending remains above 2019 levels structurally"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2023年底转向；2024年三次降息","金发姑娘融涨：SMH+88.0%，TLT+10.3%，VIX 21→15","软着陆：消费者资产负债表支持持续旅游消费","体验式消费在结构上持续高于2019年水平"],"prev_key":"2023-10-27","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot and soft landing extend travel boom","title_zh":"美联储转向与软着陆延续旅游繁荣","turn_id":"travel:trough:2023-10"},"2025-02-19":{"body":"A 33.5% selloff from February 19 to April 8, 2025, as Trump's 'Liberation Day' reciprocal-tariff package (announced April 2, with higher rates due April 9) triggered the most acute market shock since COVID, with VIX surging from 15 to 52. The slowdown/deflation-scare quad (cyclicals -18.7% vs defensives -7.7%, SMH -30.1%, SPHB-SPLV -22.8, DXY -3.9%, oil -17.5%) reflected acute recession fears as economists revised US 2025 GDP estimates sharply lower. Travel is the first line-item cut when households brace for income uncertainty — airlines and hotels saw forward-booking cancellations accelerate — and as the highest-beta consumer-cyclical, travel amplified the downturn (Discretionary -21.8% below SPY -18.8%).","body_zh":"从2025年2月19日到4月8日33.5%的抛售，特朗普'解放日'对等关税方案（4月2日宣布，更高税率定于4月9日生效）引发了自新冠以来最急剧的市场冲击，VIX从15飙升至52。放缓/通缩恐慌象限（周期-18.7% vs 防御-7.7%，SMH-30.1%，SPHB-SPLV-22.8，DXY-3.9%，油-17.5%）反映了强烈的衰退担忧，经济学家大幅下调2025年美国GDP预期。当家庭为收入不确定性做准备时，旅游是第一个被砍的预算项——航空公司和酒店的远期预订取消率加速——作为最高贝塔的消费周期股，旅游放大了下行（可选消费-21.8%低于SPY-18.8%）。","drivers":["April 2 'Liberation Day' tariffs (higher rates due Apr 9); VIX 15->52","Recession fears: GDP estimates slashed, SMH -30.1%","Travel is first discretionary budget cut in downturn","High-beta amplification: Discretionary -21.8% vs SPY -18.8%"],"drivers_zh":["4月2日'解放日'关税（更高税率定于4月9日）；VIX 15→52","衰退担忧：GDP预期大幅下调，SMH-30.1%","旅游是衰退中第一个被砍的可选消费项","高贝塔放大：可选消费-21.8% vs SPY-18.8%"],"prev_key":"2025-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2025-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-shock plunge crushes consumer cyclicals","title_zh":"关税冲击暴跌重创消费周期股","turn_id":"travel:peak:2025-02"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"A 78.0% rebound from the April 8, 2025 low through June 26, 2026, as the Trump administration paused reciprocal tariffs for 90 days on April 9 (triggering one of the largest single-day SPY rebounds in history, +8%+) and experiential demand proved far more resilient than feared — airlines and hotels rapidly reported forward bookings recovering to record levels. The macro tape was a powerful reflation/growth-up regime (cyclicals +50.3% vs defensives +22.3%, SMH +240.9%, oil +16.2%, VIX 52 to 18), though narrow (RSP lagged SPY -8.7%). Tech (+102.7%) and Industrials (+57.7%) led, with AI infrastructure spending dominating the narrative. The basket is now topping (pos 78, RS rank 13) as the 2026 oil shock from the Iran/Hormuz crisis (oil +19.2% in the current leg) and DXY +3.4% begin to bite airline margins.","body_zh":"从2025年4月8日低点到2026年6月26日78.0%的反弹，特朗普政府于4月9日暂停对等关税90天（触发史上最大的SPY单日反弹之一，涨幅超8%），体验式需求被证明远比预期具有韧性——航空公司和酒店迅速报告远期预订回升至历史纪录水平。宏观环境呈强力再通胀/增长向上格局（周期+50.3% vs 防御+22.3%，SMH+240.9%，油+16.2%，VIX 52→18），但广度狭窄（等权RSP跑输SPY-8.7%）。科技（+102.7%）和工业（+57.7%）领涨，AI基础设施支出主导市场叙事。篮子目前处于顶部（位置78，相对强度排名13），2026年伊朗/霍尔木兹危机引发的油价冲击（当前段油价+19.2%）与DXY+3.4%开始侵蚀航空公司利润。","drivers":["April 9, 2025 tariff pause triggers historic SPY bounce (+8%+)","Reflation/growth: SMH +240.9%, VIX 52->18, oil +16.2%","Experiential demand rebounds to record forward bookings","Now topping: oil/DXY headwinds bite airline margins"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月9日关税暂停触发历史性SPY反弹（涨幅超8%）","再通胀/增长：SMH+240.9%，VIX 52→18，油+16.2%","体验式需求反弹至历史纪录远期预订","现处顶部：油价/美元逆风开始侵蚀航空利润"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff pause and AI reflation fuel +78% recovery","title_zh":"关税暂停与AI再通胀驱动+78%复苏","turn_id":"travel:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Travel & Experiences is in a confirmed topping phase (pos 78, RS rank 13) after a +78% surge off the April 2025 tariff-crash low. The basket sits extended above its 200-day with experiential demand still robust, but the macro regime is shifting from pure risk-on to a late-cycle reflation squeeze: oil +19.2% on the leg and DXY +3.4% are a dual headwind — higher jet-fuel costs biting airline margins while a stronger dollar crimps international travel economics. The reflation/growth-up quad still runs (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%) and breadth is modestly positive (RSP +2.9% vs SPY), but Discretionary is already lagging (-5.2%) even as Tech (+24.3%) leads — a classic late-cycle divergence where the high-beta consumer groups peak before the broad market. As the highest-beta consumer-cyclical basket, Travel & Experiences now offers unfavorable risk/reward: the mid-June 2026 Strait of Hormuz ceasefire MOU (signed June 17) relieved some of the oil spike, but the strait was briefly re-closed days later and structural cost pressure plus a consumer strained by cumulative inflation make a fresh upleg difficult to sustain.","now_zh":"旅行与体验篮子处于明确的顶部阶段（位置78，相对强度排名13），从2025年4月关税崩盘低点反弹+78%后已过度延伸。体验式消费需求仍具韧性，但宏观环境正从纯粹的风险偏好切换至晚周期再通胀压缩：本段油价+19.2%、DXY+3.4%构成双重逆风——更高的航空燃油成本侵蚀航空公司利润，而强美元压缩国际旅游经济学。再通胀/增长向上象限仍在运行（周期+11.2% vs 防御+6.9%），广度温和偏正（等权RSP+2.9% vs SPY），但可选消费已落后（-5.2%），而科技（+24.3%）领涨——这是经典的晚周期特征：高贝塔消费板块先于大盘见顶。作为最高贝塔的消费周期篮子，旅行与体验目前风险回报不利：2026年6月中旬霍尔木兹海峡停火谅解备忘录（6月17日签署）缓解了部分油价飙升，但海峡数日后一度再度关闭，加之结构性成本压力以及被累积通胀压榨的消费者，使新一轮上行难以持续。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-uranium_miners":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"A +34% rally as the Abe government signaled early in 2014 that Japan's nuclear fleet would be treated as an important base power source ahead of the April 2014 Basic Energy Plan cabinet approval. This raised near-term expectations that Japan's 48 idled reactors would begin returning online, lifting uranium spot from post-Fukushima lows near $34/lb. The macro was a stagflation-ish backdrop with defensives leading (+5.9% vs cyclicals +2.0%), bonds rallying (TLT +5.6%), oil strengthening (+10.0%) and the dollar soft (-0.8%), so this was a supply-side/policy catalyst specific to uranium in a mixed macro environment where the group outperformed sharply.","body_zh":"上涨34%，安倍政府于2014年初发出信号，核电将被视为重要基础电源，为4月2014年《能源基本计划》内阁批准铺路。这提升了日本48座闲置反应堆近期重返运营的预期，将铀现货从福岛后低点约34美元/磅托起。宏观为类滞胀背景，防御股领涨（+5.9%对周期股+2.0%）、债券上涨（TLT +5.6%）、油价回升（+10.0%）、美元偏软（-0.8%），因此这是在混合宏观环境中特定于铀的供给侧/政策催化，该组别大幅跑赢大盘。","drivers":["Japan restart policy catalyst","spot recovering from Fukushima lows","stagflation-ish macro","oil strength"],"drivers_zh":["日本重启政策催化","现货从福岛后低位修复","类滞胀宏观","油价走强"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Japan restart hopes lift post-Fukushima lows","title_zh":"日本重启预期提振福岛后低点","turn_id":"uranium_miners:trough:2014-01"},"2014-03-04":{"body":"A -43.7% selloff into January 2015 as the post-Fukushima supply glut reasserted itself: Japanese restarts were repeatedly delayed, uranium spot slid toward $28/lb by year-end, and the commodity complex was crushed by oil collapsing -55.2% (Saudi supply war) and DXY surging +15.2%. The macro regime was an unambiguous slowdown/deflation-scare with defensives surging (+19.2% vs cyclicals +2.3%), bonds rallying hard (TLT +28.7%), VIX rising from 14 to 22, and credit spreads widening (HYG-LQD -9.1%). Uranium's high-beta nature and zero restart progress amplified the commodity rout.","body_zh":"下跌43.7%至2015年1月，福岛后供应过剩重新主导：日本重启一再推迟，铀现货年底滑向约28美元/磅，大宗商品板块被油价崩溃（-55.2%，沙特供应战）与美元飙升（DXY +15.2%）击溃。宏观为明确的放缓/通缩惊魂，防御股大涨（+19.2%对周期股+2.3%）、债券强势上涨（TLT +28.7%）、VIX从14升至22、信用利差扩大（HYG-LQD -9.1%）。铀的高贝塔属性与零重启进展放大了大宗商品溃败。","drivers":["oil collapse -55.2% Saudi supply war","dollar surge DXY +15.2%","flight-to-safety deflation-scare","Japanese restart delays"],"drivers_zh":["油价崩跌-55.2%沙特供应战","美元飙升DXY +15.2%","通缩惊魂避险","日本重启延迟"],"prev_key":"2014-03-04","prev_key_chain":["2014-03-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Dollar surge and oil collapse kills commodity bid","title_zh":"美元飙升与油价崩跌摧毁大宗商品买盘","turn_id":"uranium_miners:peak:2014-03"},"2015-01-15":{"body":"A +72.8% surge as the broad commodity complex rebounded sharply in a reflation/growth-up tape: oil recovered +29.5%, copper-gold rose +15.9%, cyclicals led (+8.9% vs defensives +0.4%), VIX fell from 22 to 13 and bonds sold off (TLT -10.9%). Uranium miners caught the wave as speculative buyers returned on oversold conditions, with spot stabilizing near $36-38/lb as utility buyers cautiously re-entered the term market. This was predominantly a macro-beta bounce, not a fundamental supply shift, but the group's extreme cheapness amplified returns.","body_zh":"飙升72.8%，大宗商品板块在再通胀/增长向上行情中大幅反弹：油价回升+29.5%、铜金比+15.9%、周期股领涨（+8.9%对防御股+0.4%）、VIX从22降至13、债券下跌（TLT -10.9%）。铀矿商乘浪而上，投机性买盘因超卖条件回归，现货稳定于约36-38美元/磅，公用事业买家谨慎重返长协市场。这主要是宏观贝塔反弹，并非基本面供给转变，但该组别的极度低估放大了回报。","drivers":["reflation/growth-up macro bounce","oil recovery +29.5%","oversold mean-reversion","VIX collapse 22 to 13"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀/增长向上宏观反弹","油价回升+29.5%","超卖均值回归","VIX从22跌至13"],"prev_key":"2015-01-15","prev_key_chain":["2015-01-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Reflation bounce on oil snap-back and risk-on","title_zh":"油价反弹与风险偏好驱动再通胀反弹","turn_id":"uranium_miners:trough:2015-01"},"2015-05-14":{"body":"A -40.2% selloff as the 2015 commodity rout re-intensified through the summer: oil fell -32.3%, copper-gold dropped -17.5%, the dollar firmed +6.0% and the broad tape turned deflation-scare with cyclicals -3.1% vs defensives -0.7%, breadth deteriorating (RSP-SPY -3.3%) and high-beta crushed (highbeta-lowvol -14.8%). Uranium spot slid toward $34/lb as China growth fears and delayed Japanese restarts weighed. The narrow mega-cap-led tape left commodities behind, and uranium's high-beta amplified the macro de-risk.","body_zh":"下跌40.2%，2015年大宗商品溃败在夏季再度加剧：油价下跌-32.3%、铜金比降-17.5%、美元走强+6.0%，大盘转为通缩惊魂（周期股-3.1%对防御股-0.7%、广度恶化RSP-SPY -3.3%、高贝塔遭重创-14.8%）。受中国增长担忧与日本重启延迟拖累，铀现货滑向约34美元/磅。窄幅巨头领涨行情将大宗商品甩在身后，铀的高贝塔属性放大了宏观去风险。","drivers":["China slowdown commodity rout","oil -32.3% and dollar +6.0%","high-beta selloff","Japanese restart delays"],"drivers_zh":["中国放缓大宗商品溃败","油价-32.3%与美元+6.0%","高贝塔抛售","日本重启延迟"],"prev_key":"2015-05-14","prev_key_chain":["2015-05-14"],"status":"exact","title":"China slowdown and commodity rout re-hits miners","title_zh":"中国放缓与大宗商品溃败再度打击矿商","turn_id":"uranium_miners:peak:2015-05"},"2015-11-19":{"body":"A +325.9% surge into February 2017, the group's largest historical run, driven by an extraordinary confluence of supply and macro forces. Kazatomprom announced a 10% production cut in January 2017 (the world's largest producer, supplying ~40% of global output), sending spot up ~10% on announcement day, and Cameco suspended McArthur River/Key Lake in November 2017. The macro was a broad reflation/growth-up cycle: Financials (+24.7%), Industrials (+22.1%) and Tech (+20.7%) led, cyclicals crushed defensives (+18.1% vs +11.9%), oil rose +31.2%, copper-gold gained +18.0%, VIX collapsed from 17 to 11 and breadth broadened (RSP +2.1%). The Trump election in November 2016 re-ignited the cyclical/value trade. Uranium's supply-cut story and near-decade low prices created the fuel for a leveraged catch-up.","body_zh":"飙升325.9%至2017年2月，为该组别历史最大涨幅，由供给与宏观力量的非凡共振驱动。哈萨克斯坦国家原子能公司（Kazatomprom）于2017年1月宣布减产10%（全球最大生产商，供应约40%全球产量），公告当天现货上涨约10%；Cameco于2017年11月暂停麦克阿瑟河/基湖运营。宏观为广泛的再通胀/增长向上周期：金融（+24.7%）、工业（+22.1%）与科技（+20.7%）领涨，周期股大幅跑赢防御股（+18.1%对+11.9%），油价上涨+31.2%、铜金比+18.0%、VIX从17崩至11、广度扩展（RSP+2.1%）。2016年11月特朗普当选重燃周期/价值交易。铀的减产故事与近十年低价格创造了杠杆追涨的燃料。","drivers":["Kazatomprom 10% production cut Jan 2017","reflation/growth-up Trump-era cyclical bid","oil +31.2% and copper-gold +18%","Cameco McArthur River suspension Nov 2017"],"drivers_zh":["哈萨克斯坦2017年1月减产10%","再通胀/增长向上特朗普周期买盘","油价+31.2%与铜金比+18%","Cameco麦克阿瑟河2017年11月停产"],"prev_key":"2015-11-19","prev_key_chain":["2015-11-19"],"status":"exact","title":"Supply cuts and Trump cyclical bid: +326% run","title_zh":"供给减产与特朗普周期买盘：涨幅326%","turn_id":"uranium_miners:trough:2015-11"},"2017-02-14":{"body":"A -37.3% drawdown as uranium spot failed to sustain the Kazatomprom-cut spike and the broad tape pivoted to a narrow tech/semis-led melt-up (SMH +32.9%, growth>value +12.4, VIX collapsing to 10). The macro was still nominally reflation/growth-up, but narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -3.7%), a weaker dollar (DXY -6.7%) and low-beta leadership (highbeta-lowvol -6.0) showed flows chasing mega-cap growth rather than commodities. Uranium miners, a value/commodity play, were left behind as the Section 232 petition (filed January 2018) had not yet materialized and spot stagnated near $20-22/lb after the initial cut-driven pop.","body_zh":"下跌37.3%，铀现货未能维持哈萨克斯坦减产引发的飙升，大盘行情转向窄幅科技/半导体领涨的暴涨（半导体SMH +32.9%、成长跑赢价值+12.4、VIX崩至10）。宏观名义上仍为再通胀/增长向上，但窄幅广度（RSP-SPY -3.7%）、美元走弱（DXY -6.7%）与低贝塔领涨（高贝塔减低波动-6.0）显示资金追逐巨头成长而非大宗商品。铀矿商作为价值/大宗商品标的被甩在身后，Section 232请愿（2018年1月提交）尚未落地，现货在初期减产驱动反弹后停滞于约20-22美元/磅。","drivers":["tech/semis melt-up pulls flows from commodities","spot stagnation near cycle lows","narrow breadth growth over value","Section 232 petition not yet filed"],"drivers_zh":["科技/半导体暴涨抽离大宗商品资金","现货停滞于周期低点附近","窄幅广度、成长跑赢价值","Section 232请愿尚未提交"],"prev_key":"2017-02-14","prev_key_chain":["2017-02-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Spot stalls as tech melt-up pulls flows away","title_zh":"现货停滞，科技暴涨抽离资金","turn_id":"uranium_miners:peak:2017-02"},"2017-10-30":{"body":"A +117.4% rally into April 2019 as Cameco formally suspended McArthur River/Key Lake in January 2018 (removing ~18 million lbs annually from supply) and Kazatomprom followed with a 20% three-year cut announced December 2017. This was the idiosyncratic supply-discipline thesis at work: spot firmed from ~$20/lb toward ~$29/lb. The macro backdrop was a mixed stagflation-ish regime (cyclicals +11.3% vs defensives +12.2%, DXY +2.7%, oil +18.2%, copper-gold -7.8%) with growth outperforming value (+12.6) and rising VIX (10 to 14); the supply-cut narrative overrode the ambiguous macro.","body_zh":"上涨117.4%至2019年4月，Cameco于2018年1月正式暂停麦克阿瑟河/基湖运营（每年减少约1800万磅供给），Kazatomprom随后于2017年12月宣布为期三年的20%减产。这是个股供给纪律逻辑的体现：现货从约20美元/磅走强至约29美元/磅。宏观背景为混合类滞胀体制（周期股+11.3%对防御股+12.2%、DXY +2.7%、油价+18.2%、铜金比-7.8%），成长跑赢价值（+12.6）、VIX温和上行（10至14）；供给减产叙事压倒了模糊的宏观环境。","drivers":["Cameco McArthur River suspension Jan 2018","Kazatomprom 20% three-year cut Dec 2017","spot recovery from $20 toward $29","supply-deficit thesis established"],"drivers_zh":["Cameco麦克阿瑟河2018年1月暂停","Kazatomprom 2017年12月宣布三年减产20%","现货从20美元回升至29美元","供给短缺逻辑确立"],"prev_key":"2017-10-30","prev_key_chain":["2017-10-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Supply-cut thesis rallies on McArthur suspension","title_zh":"麦克阿瑟河停产激活供给减产逻辑","turn_id":"uranium_miners:trough:2017-10"},"2019-04-09":{"body":"A -49.1% selloff into March 2020, spanning the US-China trade war escalation through 2019 and culminating in the COVID-19 pandemic crash. Spot fell to ~$24/lb in mid-March 2020 as VIX exploded from 14 to 76, defensives were the relative winner but still lost -2.3% while cyclicals cratered -28.0%, oil collapsed -68.2%, copper-gold fell -39.6%, breadth imploded (RSP-SPY -9.7%) and bonds rallied sharply (TLT +18.8%). The macro was a textbook slowdown/deflation-scare with flight-to-safety. COVID actually catalyzed supply cuts (Cigar Lake and Kazatomprom curtailments in March-April 2020) that would fuel the next rally, but the initial market reaction was pure de-risk.","body_zh":"下跌49.1%至2020年3月，跨越2019年中美贸易战升级至新冠疫情崩盘。随VIX从14飙至76，现货跌至约24美元/磅，防御股相对胜出但仍损失-2.3%，周期股崩跌-28.0%、油价暴跌-68.2%、铜金比-39.6%、广度崩溃（RSP-SPY -9.7%）、债券大涨（TLT +18.8%）。宏观为教科书式放缓/通缩惊魂避险。值得注意的是，新冠实际上触发了供给减产（2020年3-4月Cigar Lake与Kazatomprom限产），将催化下一轮上涨，但初期市场反应为纯粹去风险。","drivers":["COVID pandemic crash VIX 14 to 76","flight-to-safety deflation-scare","oil -68.2% and dollar +4.3%","US-China trade war escalation"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情崩盘VIX 14至76","通缩惊魂避险","油价-68.2%与美元+4.3%","中美贸易战升级"],"prev_key":"2019-04-09","prev_key_chain":["2019-04-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade war and COVID crash wipe out supply bid","title_zh":"贸易战与新冠崩盘摧毁供给买盘","turn_id":"uranium_miners:peak:2019-04"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"A +1306.4% surge into November 2021, the group's all-time record rally. The starting gun was COVID supply: Cameco shut Cigar Lake in March 2020 and Kazatomprom curtailed ~4,000 tU from April 2020, rapidly depleting inventories. Then Sprott Physical Uranium Trust (SPUT) launched July 19, 2021, purchasing physical uranium directly from spot and sequestering it, creating a price floor that drove spot from ~$24 to ~$50/lb by November 2021. The macro was an explosive reflation/growth-up regime: cyclicals +131.1% vs defensives +42.3%, oil +302.2%, copper-gold +80.2%, VIX collapsed 76 to 17, dollar weakened -7.0% and semis surged +200.8%. The basket amplified this cyclical melt-up by 13x.","body_zh":"飙升1306.4%至2021年11月，为该组别有史以来最大涨幅。起点为新冠供给冲击：Cameco于2020年3月关闭Cigar Lake，Kazatomprom自2020年4月削减约4000吨铀（约1040万磅），库存迅速耗尽。随后Sprott实物铀信托（SPUT）于2021年7月19日上市，直接从现货市场购买实物铀并封存，创造价格托底，将现货从约24美元推升至2021年11月约50美元/磅。宏观为爆炸性再通胀/增长向上体制：周期股+131.1%对防御股+42.3%、油价+302.2%、铜金比+80.2%、VIX从76崩至17、美元走弱-7.0%、半导体飙升+200.8%。该组合将这轮周期暴涨放大了13倍。","drivers":["COVID supply cuts Cigar Lake and Kazatomprom","Sprott Physical Uranium Trust launch Jul 2021","reflation/growth-up cyclical melt-up","spot $24 to $50"],"drivers_zh":["新冠供给减产Cigar Lake与Kazatomprom","Sprott实物铀信托2021年7月上市","再通胀/增长向上周期暴涨","现货从24升至50美元"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID supply shocks and SPUT launch: +1306% run","title_zh":"新冠供给冲击与SPUT上市：涨幅1306%","turn_id":"uranium_miners:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-08":{"body":"A -45.1% drop into late January 2022 as the SPUT-driven spot squeeze faded and Fed hiking cycle fears hit speculative miners. The macro was a stagflation-ish flight-to-safety (VIX 17 to 30, defensives +0.7% vs cyclicals -5.1%, dollar +3.4%, growth-over-value unwind growth-value -10.1, semis -14.5%). As a high-beta miner basket the group overshot the broad tape selloff; spot consolidated near $42-45/lb but the equity premium compressed sharply on de-risking.","body_zh":"下跌45.1%至2022年1月底，SPUT驱动的现货逼空消退，美联储加息周期担忧打击投机性矿商。宏观为类滞胀避险（VIX 17至30、防御股+0.7%对周期股-5.1%、美元+3.4%、成长价值利差逆转-10.1、半导体-14.5%）。作为高贝塔矿商组合，该组别超调于大盘抛售；现货在约42-45美元/磅盘整，但股票溢价在去风险中急剧压缩。","drivers":["Sprott SPUT squeeze fade","Fed hiking cycle risk-off","stagflation-ish VIX 17 to 30","high-beta overshoot"],"drivers_zh":["Sprott SPUT逼空消退","美联储加息周期避险","类滞胀VIX 17至30","高贝塔超调"],"prev_key":"2021-11-08","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Sprott-squeeze fade meets Fed hiking risk-off","title_zh":"Sprott逼空消退遭遇美联储加息避险","turn_id":"uranium_miners:peak:2021-11"},"2022-01-27":{"body":"A +66.2% spike as Russia's invasion of Ukraine in February 2022 raised fears over Russian uranium enrichment and conversion supply (Russia supplies ~35% of global enrichment capacity), lifting spot toward $64/lb in April 2022. The macro was stagflation-ish with defensives (+9.7%) and cyclicals (+5.5%) both positive, Energy leading (+21.9%), yields surging (TLT -13.5%), dollar firm (DXY +2.7%) and VIX easing 30 to 22. This geopolitical supply-risk bid bucked the de-risking trend in semis (SMH -4.3%), showing uranium's idiosyncratic fuel-security premium.","body_zh":"飙升66.2%，2022年2月俄罗斯入侵乌克兰引发对俄铀浓缩与转化供应的担忧（俄罗斯供应约35%全球浓缩能力），将现货推升至2022年4月约64美元/磅。宏观为类滞胀，防御股（+9.7%）与周期股（+5.5%）均为正，能源领涨（+21.9%）、收益率飙升（TLT -13.5%）、美元稳健（DXY +2.7%）、VIX从30回落至22。这一地缘政治供应风险买盘逆半导体去风险趋势而行（半导体SMH -4.3%），彰显铀的个股燃料安全溢价。","drivers":["Russia-Ukraine invasion fuel supply risk","Russian enrichment capacity geopolitics","stagflation oil +20.4%","spot to $64/lb"],"drivers_zh":["俄乌入侵燃料供应风险","俄罗斯浓缩能力地缘政治","类滞胀油价+20.4%","现货涨至64美元/磅"],"prev_key":"2022-01-27","prev_key_chain":["2022-01-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Russia-Ukraine supply fear fires stagflation spot bid","title_zh":"俄乌战争供应担忧激发类滞胀现货买盘","turn_id":"uranium_miners:trough:2022-01"},"2022-04-13":{"body":"A -43.6% flush as peak-hawkish Fed pricing and a broad risk-asset de-rate hit the volatile miners. The macro was a clear slowdown/deflation-scare (VIX 22 to 32, defensives -6.6% beating cyclicals -10.3%, dollar surging DXY +5.0%, high-beta minus low-vol -8.3) in which uranium gave back its geopolitical spike on macro de-risking, overshooting the broad selloff (SPY -11.5%). Spot consolidated near $48-50/lb as the macro overwhelmed the underlying supply thesis.","body_zh":"急挫43.6%，美联储鹰派定价见顶与广义风险资产估值下杀打击波动剧烈的矿商。宏观为明确的放缓/通缩惊魂（VIX 22至32、防御股-6.6%跑赢周期股-10.3%、美元飙升DXY +5.0%、高贝塔减低波动-8.3），铀在宏观去风险下回吐地缘政治溢价，超调于大盘抛售（标普500 -11.5%）。现货在约48-50美元/磅盘整，宏观压制了底层供给逻辑。","drivers":["peak-hawkish Fed pricing","dollar surge DXY +5.0%","slowdown/deflation-scare quad VIX 22 to 32","high-beta de-risk unwind"],"drivers_zh":["美联储鹰派定价见顶","美元飙升DXY +5.0%","放缓/通缩惊魂象限VIX 22至32","高贝塔去风险平仓"],"prev_key":"2022-04-13","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-13"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-hawkish Fed and dollar surge flush miners","title_zh":"鹰派美联储见顶与美元飙升冲击矿商","turn_id":"uranium_miners:peak:2022-04"},"2022-05-12":{"body":"A +51.7% bounce as the structural supply-deficit thesis drew buyers back on stabilizing risk conditions: VIX eased from 32 to 23, cyclicals led slightly (+4.5% vs defensives +3.9%), high-beta bounced (highbeta-lowvol +7.1) and credit tightened (HYG-LQD +3.0). Uranium spot firmed toward $48-50/lb on increased utility term contracting and the enduring Cameco/Kazatomprom supply-cut backdrop, even as oil fell -18.2% and the dollar firmed (DXY +4.0%). This was an idiosyncratic supply story riding a calmer risk backdrop.","body_zh":"反弹51.7%，结构性供给短缺逻辑在风险条件企稳下重获买盘：VIX从32回落至23、周期股微幅领涨（+4.5%对防御股+3.9%）、高贝塔反弹（高贝塔减低波动+7.1）、信用收紧（HYG-LQD +3.0）。受公用事业长协签约增加与持续的Cameco/Kazatomprom供给减产背景支撑，铀现货走强至约48-50美元/磅，即便油价下跌-18.2%、美元走强（DXY +4.0%）。这是在更平静风险背景下的个股供给故事。","drivers":["risk stabilization VIX 32 to 23","utility contracting activity","supply-deficit Cameco/Kazatomprom backdrop","high-beta mean-reversion"],"drivers_zh":["风险企稳VIX 32至23","公用事业长协签约活跃","Cameco/Kazatomprom供给减产背景","高贝塔均值回归"],"prev_key":"2022-05-12","prev_key_chain":["2022-05-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Supply deficit re-bid as vol eases and utilities contract","title_zh":"波动缓和与公用事业签约重燃供给短缺买盘","turn_id":"uranium_miners:trough:2022-05"},"2022-09-09":{"body":"A -40.8% drawdown into May 2023 as the broad tape pivoted to a narrow, semis-led AI melt-up (SMH +38.1%, growth>value +10.4, VIX fell 23 to 17) while uranium was a commodity/value laggard. Dollar weakened (DXY -4.4%), which should have helped materials, but the narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -6.7%) and deflating defensives confirmed flows were chasing mega-cap growth exclusively. Uranium spot consolidated near $44-50/lb through this period, unable to attract speculative interest as the AI narrative drew capital elsewhere.","body_zh":"回撤40.8%至2023年5月，大盘行情转为窄幅、半导体领涨的AI暴涨（半导体SMH +38.1%、成长跑赢价值+10.4、VIX从23降至17），铀作为大宗商品/价值落后者。美元走弱（DXY -4.4%）本应有利于材料，但窄幅广度（RSP-SPY -6.7%）与防御股下跌确认资金专门追逐巨头成长。铀现货在此期间于约44-50美元/磅盘整，随AI叙事将资本吸引至别处，无法吸引投机兴趣。","drivers":["AI/semis melt-up pulls flows from commodities","narrow breadth RSP-SPY -6.7%","spot consolidation $44-50","value/commodity laggard in growth tape"],"drivers_zh":["AI/半导体暴涨抽离大宗商品资金","窄幅广度RSP-SPY -6.7%","现货44-50美元盘整","成长行情中价值/大宗落后"],"prev_key":"2022-09-09","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Tech-led AI rally leaves commodity miners behind","title_zh":"科技领涨AI行情将大宗商品矿商甩在身后","turn_id":"uranium_miners:peak:2022-09"},"2023-05-30":{"body":"A +164.0% surge into May 2024 as uranium spot broke through $100/lb for the first time in 17 years in January 2024. The catalysts were: Kazatomprom's January 2024 warning that it could not meet 2024-2025 guidance due to sulfuric acid shortages; Sprott physical buying; and the dawning AI-power/reactor-restart narrative as tech companies began exploring nuclear baseload agreements. The macro was reflation/growth-up with semis leading (SMH +59.7%), growth>value (+11.7), VIX falling 17 to 12, oil and copper-gold rising, and narrow breadth (-6.8%); the high-beta miners amplified the spot breakout by approximately 11x.","body_zh":"飙升164.0%至2024年5月，铀现货于2024年1月突破每磅100美元，为17年来首次。催化因素包括：Kazatomprom 2024年1月警告因硫酸短缺无法完成2024-2025年指引；Sprott实物买入；科技公司开始探索核基荷电力协议，带来初现的AI电力/反应堆重启叙事。宏观为再通胀/增长向上，半导体领涨（SMH +59.7%）、成长跑赢价值（+11.7）、VIX从17降至12、油价与铜金比上涨、广度狭窄（-6.8%）；高弹性矿商将现货突破放大约11倍。","drivers":["spot breakout to $100 Jan 2024","Kazatomprom Jan 2024 production warning","AI-power reactor restart narrative","reflation/growth-up semis-led tape"],"drivers_zh":["2024年1月现货突破100美元","Kazatomprom 2024年1月产量预警","AI电力反应堆重启叙事","再通胀/增长向上半导体领涨行情"],"prev_key":"2023-05-30","prev_key_chain":["2023-05-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Spot breakout to $100 on Kazatomprom warning and AI-power","title_zh":"哈萨克斯坦减产预警与AI电力叙事推动现货突破100美元","turn_id":"uranium_miners:trough:2023-05"},"2024-05-20":{"body":"A -37.6% drop into September 2024 as uranium spot retreated from the $100 high on thin-volume term-market softness, then was compounded by the August 2024 volatility scare (Japan yen carry-trade unwind, VIX spiking 12 to 22). Defensives (+6.5%) beat cyclicals (-0.9%), bonds rallied (TLT +10.7%), Materials dropped -2.1% and Energy -8.1%. The high-beta miners overshot the spot pullback as macro de-risking combined with spot softness created a double headwind.","body_zh":"下跌37.6%至2024年9月，铀现货因长协市场成交清淡从100美元高位回落，继而被2024年8月波动惊魂（日元套利交易平仓，VIX从12飙至22）加剧。防御股（+6.5%）跑赢周期股（-0.9%）、债券上涨（TLT +10.7%）、材料-2.1%、能源-8.1%。高弹性矿商超调于现货回调，宏观去风险与现货走弱共同形成双重逆风。","drivers":["August 2024 yen carry-trade vol spike VIX 12 to 22","spot retreat from $100 high","flight-to-safety deflation-scare","high-beta overshoot"],"drivers_zh":["2024年8月日元套利平仓波动VIX 12至22","现货从100美元高位回落","通缩惊魂避险","高贝塔超调"],"prev_key":"2024-05-20","prev_key_chain":["2024-05-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Spot rolls over into the Aug-2024 carry-trade vol spike","title_zh":"现货回落进入2024年8月套利平仓波动冲击","turn_id":"uranium_miners:peak:2024-05"},"2024-09-06":{"body":"An +82.0% rocket as the Microsoft-Constellation Energy 20-year, 835 MW Three Mile Island restart deal (announced September 20, 2024) and the start of Fed rate cuts (first -25bps cut September 18, 2024) re-ignited the nuclear-fuel bid. The macro was reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +13.7% vs defensives +0.4%, oil +5.3, VIX easing 22 to 15) with yields surging (TLT -8.6%) and dollar firming (DXY +6.2%). The AI-nuclear power narrative surged and the high-beta miners were pulled up into late November 2024.","body_zh":"火箭式上涨82.0%，微软与星座能源20年、835兆瓦三哩岛重启协议（2024年9月20日宣布）与美联储降息周期启动（2024年9月18日首次降息25个基点）重燃核燃料买盘。宏观为再通胀/增长向上（周期股+13.7%对防御股+0.4%、油价+5.3、VIX从22回落至15），收益率飙升（TLT -8.6%）、美元走强（DXY +6.2%）。AI核电叙事激增，高弹性矿商被推升至2024年11月底。","drivers":["TMI restart deal Sep 20 2024","Fed rate cut cycle start Sep 18 2024","reflation/growth-up quad","AI-nuclear power narrative surge"],"drivers_zh":["2024年9月20日三哩岛重启协议","2024年9月18日美联储降息周期启动","再通胀/增长向上象限","AI核电叙事激增"],"prev_key":"2024-09-06","prev_key_chain":["2024-09-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Three Mile Island deal and Fed cuts re-ignite nuclear bid","title_zh":"三哩岛协议与美联储降息重燃核能买盘","turn_id":"uranium_miners:trough:2024-09"},"2024-11-22":{"body":"A -48.5% drawdown into the April 2025 tariff low, hit first by DeepSeek's late-January 2025 release (the model's efficiency undermined the narrative that AI requires massive new nuclear baseload) and then the April 2025 tariff crash. This was a violent slowdown/deflation-scare: VIX exploded 15 to 52, defensives (-7.1%) beat cyclicals (-18.7%), semis cratered (SMH -26.1%), oil fell -16.4%. The high-beta miners led the AI-nuclear complex lower on demand-doubt and broad de-risk, even as a weaker dollar (DXY -4.2%) offered no fundamental support.","body_zh":"回撤48.5%至2025年4月关税低点，先受DeepSeek 2025年1月底发布冲击（该模型的效率优势削弱了AI需大量新建核基荷电力的叙事），再遭2025年4月关税崩盘。这是剧烈的放缓/通缩惊魂：VIX从15飙至52、防御股（-7.1%）跑赢周期股（-18.7%）、半导体崩跌（半导体SMH -26.1%）、油价下跌-16.4%。高弹性矿商在需求疑虑与广泛去风险下领跌整个AI核电板块，即便美元走弱（DXY -4.2%）也未能提供实质支撑。","drivers":["DeepSeek AI demand shock Jan 2025","April 2025 tariff crash","risk-off VIX 15 to 52","high-beta unwind"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek 2025年1月AI需求冲击","2025年4月关税崩盘","避险VIX 15至52","高贝塔平仓"],"prev_key":"2024-11-22","prev_key_chain":["2024-11-22"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek AI shock and tariff crash wipe out nuclear bid","title_zh":"DeepSeek冲击与关税崩盘摧毁核能买盘","turn_id":"uranium_miners:peak:2024-11"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"A +291.8% surge off the April 2025 tariff low as uranium spot broke higher on reactor restarts, government nuclear support and supply-deficit buying, while the AI-baseload story re-accelerated following DeepSeek concerns fading. The basket amplified a goldilocks, semis-led risk-on melt-up (SMH +89.9%, growth>value +22.7, VIX collapsing 52 to 21) with narrow breadth (-10.2%) and a weaker dollar (DXY -4.1%) aiding the commodity bid. Energy fell -2.2% and copper-gold -20.3%, confirming this was a tech/AI-driven high-beta levitation rather than a broad commodity rally; uranium miners, as the highest-beta fuel proxy, delivered the group's largest run into October 2025.","body_zh":"自2025年4月关税低点飙升291.8%，铀现货因反应堆重启、政府核能支持与供给短缺买盘上行，DeepSeek担忧消退后AI基荷电力故事重新加速。该组合放大了金发女郎式、半导体领涨的风险偏好暴涨（半导体SMH +89.9%、成长跑赢价值+22.7、VIX从52崩至21），广度狭窄（-10.2%）、美元走弱（DXY -4.1%）助推大宗商品买盘。能源下跌-2.2%、铜金比-20.3%，证实这是科技/AI驱动的高贝塔飞升而非广泛大宗商品上涨；铀矿商作为弹性最高的燃料代理，交出该组别至2025年10月的最大涨幅。","drivers":["semis-led risk-on melt-up SMH +90%","spot breakout on reactor restarts","government nuclear support","supply-deficit re-bid"],"drivers_zh":["半导体领涨风险偏好暴涨SMH +90%","反应堆重启带动现货突破","政府核能支持","供给短缺重获买盘"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff-low launches +292% semis-led nuclear melt-up","title_zh":"关税低点启动+292%半导体领涨核能暴涨","turn_id":"uranium_miners:trough:2025-04"},"2025-10-15":{"body":"A -35.7% pullback from the October 2025 peak as the most stretched fuel-cycle trade unwound on profit-taking and spot price stagnation. The macro was only a mild slowdown/deflation-scare (VIX 21 to 23, defensives +0.6% vs cyclicals -2.0%, SPY -0.9%) not a broad flush, so this was largely idiosyncratic froth purging in a high-beta group as flows rotated off the AI-fuel trade. Copper-gold actually rose +3.1%, confirming this was not a broad commodity de-risk but a sector-specific sentiment reset.","body_zh":"自2025年10月峰值回调35.7%，最被拉伸的燃料循环交易因获利了结与现货价停滞而平仓。宏观仅为温和的放缓/通缩惊魂（VIX 21至23、防御股+0.6%对周期股-2.0%、标普500 -0.9%）——并非广泛急挫——因此这主要是高弹性组别在资金撤离AI燃料交易时的个股泡沫挤出。铜金比实际上上涨+3.1%，确认这并非广泛大宗商品去风险，而是行业特定的情绪重置。","drivers":["spot price stall at highs","high-beta froth purge profit-taking","mild risk-off VIX 21 to 23","sector-specific flow rotation"],"drivers_zh":["现货价高位停滞","高贝塔泡沫挤出获利了结","温和避险VIX 21至23","行业特定资金轮动"],"prev_key":"2025-10-15","prev_key_chain":["2025-10-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Blow-off top: spot stalls, froth purged","title_zh":"喷发顶部：现货停滞，泡沫挤出","turn_id":"uranium_miners:peak:2025-10"},"2025-11-21":{"body":"A +71.1% rebound into late January 2026 on renewed reactor-restart and utility-contracting headlines that firmed uranium spot toward $84-101/lb. The tape was reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +10.0% vs defensives +1.9%, oil +8.9%, VIX easing 23 to 16, semis +28.1%) with a weaker dollar (DXY -3.7%) supporting commodities. This was a high-beta leverage play on a favorable macro regime, with the supply-deficit and government nuclear support narrative providing the fundamental underpinning.","body_zh":"至2026年1月底反弹71.1%，新一轮反应堆重启与公用事业签约新闻使铀现货走强至约84-101美元/磅。行情为再通胀/增长向上（周期股+10.0%对防御股+1.9%、油价+8.9%、VIX从23回落至16、半导体+28.1%），美元走弱（DXY -3.7%）支撑大宗商品。这是在有利宏观象限下的高贝塔杠杆交易，供给短缺与政府核能支持叙事提供基本面支撑。","drivers":["reflation/growth-up quad","reactor restart and utility contracting headlines","weaker dollar tailwind DXY -3.7%","spot firming to $101"],"drivers_zh":["再通胀/增长向上象限","反应堆重启与公用事业签约新闻","美元走弱顺风DXY -3.7%","现货走强至101美元"],"prev_key":"2025-11-21","prev_key_chain":["2025-11-21"],"status":"exact","title":"Restart-driven relief rally in reflation quad","title_zh":"再通胀象限中重启驱动的修复反弹","turn_id":"uranium_miners:trough:2025-11"},"2026-01-28":{"body":"A -42.0% slide into mid-June 2026 as uranium spot consolidated below $85/lb after the January 2026 spike above $100, leaving equity miners deeply washed out (25-40% corrections across URNM, CCJ, UEC). The macro was a mixed reflation/growth-up quad (oil +42.4%, copper-gold +28.6% providing commodity tailwinds) but a stronger dollar (DXY +3.6%) and rising VIX (16 to 22) offset the commodity bid, while the stretched fuel-cycle equity premium de-rated. The multi-year supply-deficit and AI-baseload thesis remains durable, but equity miners de-rated faster than spot, creating the deepest washout since the 2022 lows.","body_zh":"下跌42.0%至2026年6月中，铀现货于2026年1月突破100美元后在85美元/磅下方盘整，股票矿商深度超跌（URNM、CCJ、UEC全线回调25-40%）。宏观为混合的再通胀/增长向上象限（油价+42.4%、铜金比+28.6%提供大宗商品顺风），但美元走强（DXY +3.6%）与VIX上行（16至22）抵消了大宗商品买盘，同时被拉伸的燃料循环股票溢价下杀。多年期供给短缺与AI基荷电力逻辑依然持久，但股票矿商估值下杀快于现货，制造出自2022年低点以来最深的超跌。","drivers":["spot consolidation below $85 after $100 spike","stronger dollar DXY +3.6% headwind","equity premium de-rate","VIX rising 16 to 22"],"drivers_zh":["100美元峰值后现货在85美元下方盘整","美元走强DXY +3.6%逆风","股票溢价下杀","VIX上行16至22"],"prev_key":"2026-01-28","prev_key_chain":["2026-01-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Spot consolidates into deep washout below $85","title_zh":"现货在85美元下方盘整进入深度超跌","turn_id":"uranium_miners:peak:2026-01"}},"now":"Uranium miners sit in a deep bottoming phase (pos 1.1, rs_rank 43, below the 200-day) after a -42% slide from the January 2026 peak, their fourth consecutive major selloff since the November 2021 bull-market top. The current macro is a reflation/growth-up quad (oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%, cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, broad participation with equal-weight beating cap-weight by +2.9%), which structurally favors commodity and cyclical themes and is the correct regime for a uranium recovery bid. However, the stronger dollar (DXY +3.4%) remains a direct headwind for the materials complex, and the group has not yet reclaimed its 200-day moving average. The rs_rank of 43 signals the group is underperforming the median sector. The washout from the January 2026 high has been severe enough (-42% in five months) to qualify as a reset that historically precedes multi-month re-accumulation, and the supply-deficit and AI-baseload thesis remains structurally intact, but a confirmed spot-price turn and macro regime confirmation are still required before the trough becomes a durable launch.","now_zh":"铀矿商处于深度筑底阶段（位置1.1、相对强度排名43、低于200日均线），自2026年1月高点下跌42%，为2021年11月牛市顶部以来的第四次连续重大回调。当前宏观为再通胀/增长向上象限（油价+19.2%、铜金比+18.3%、周期股+11.2%对防御股+6.9%、等权跑赢市值加权+2.9%），结构上有利于大宗商品与周期主题，是铀股修复买盘的正确环境。但美元走强（DXY +3.4%）仍为材料板块的直接逆风，且该组别尚未收复200日均线。相对强度排名43显示该组别跑输中位行业。自2026年1月高点的深度洗盘（五个月内-42%）在历史上是多月再积累阶段的前兆，供给短缺与AI基础负荷电力逻辑依然结构性成立——但确认筑底为持续性启动点，仍需现货价见底确认与宏观象限配合。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"uranium.supply_squeeze.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"uranium.supply_squeeze.v1","arch_state":"manual","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-us_sector_comm":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"The Communication Services basket (back-filled with current GICS 2018 weights, giving Alphabet, Meta, Netflix, and Disney their eventual sector assignments) compounded +140.9% over nearly five years. The decade's goldilocks macro regime — oil falling 22%, TLT rising 29.5% as the 10-year yield slid from ~3% to ~2.1%, DXY gaining 17.8% on US exceptionalism, and VIX compressing from 14 to 12 — rewarded internet platforms whose ad-revenue and subscription models were structurally decoupled from commodity and rate cycles. Semis surged 168.7% and growth beat value by 44 points, confirming this was a mega-cap, narrow-breadth (EW lagged cap-weight by 11.6pp) secular melt-up rather than a broad cyclical turn; Comm's +140.9% is consistent with but modestly lagged Tech's +131.7% gain (listed as leader), reflecting the basket's mix of high-growth internet names and slower-growth legacy telecoms.","body_zh":"通信服务板块（按2018年GICS重新分类后的权重回溯，将谷歌、Meta、Netflix及迪士尼纳入本板块）在近五年内累计上涨140.9%。十年代的黄金宏观环境——油价下跌22%、TLT上涨29.5%（10年期美债收益率从约3%降至约2.1%）、美元指数因美国经济优异升值17.8%、VIX从14压缩至12——全面利好互联网平台，其广告收入与订阅模式在结构上与商品和利率周期脱钩。半导体板块大涨168.7%，成长股跑赢价值股44个百分点，确认这是一波以大市值股领衔、市场广度较窄（等权指数落后市值加权11.6个百分点）的世俗性上涨行情，而非广泛的周期性反弹。通信服务+140.9%的涨幅略逊于科技板块的131.7%，反映板块内高成长互联网公司与增速较慢的传统电信公司并存的混合结构。","drivers":["Fed QE goldilocks/low-rate regime","FAANG/internet secular growth","digital advertising structural shift","oil collapse suppressed inflation","narrow mega-cap breadth"],"drivers_zh":["美联储QE黄金宏观/低利率环境","FAANG/互联网行业世俗成长","数字广告结构性转移","油价大跌抑制通胀","窄幅大市值主导行情"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Secular FAANG-era internet and media bull","title_zh":"FAANG时代互联网与媒体世俗牛市","turn_id":"us_sector_comm:trough:2014-01"},"2018-09-28":{"body":"After four Fed rate hikes in 2018, the market broke in Q4 as investors priced a policy error: the Fed's December 19 hike (to 2.25-2.5%) alongside Powell's comment that balance-sheet runoff was on 'autopilot' triggered a 9% December drop — the worst since 1931. US-China trade war fears compounded the recession scare. VIX surged from 12 to 36, oil collapsed 41.9%, and cyclicals fell 21.9% vs defensives -8.3%, a classic risk-off rotation. Comm fell 19.9%, in line with the growth/cyclical complex (Tech -23.2%, Industrials -22.6%) and notably worse than defensive sectors — consistent with ctx showing Utilities -1.2% and Real Estate -7.5% leading on a relative basis.","body_zh":"2018年美联储四次加息后，市场在第四季度崩跌，投资者将其定性为政策失误：12月19日加息（至2.25-2.5%）叠加鲍威尔表示缩表处于'自动驾驶'模式，触发12月跌幅达9%——为1931年以来最差。美中贸易战恐慌加剧衰退预期。VIX从12飙升至36，油价暴跌41.9%，周期股下跌21.9%而防御股仅跌8.3%，呈典型避险轮动特征。通信服务下跌19.9%，与成长/周期复合体（科技-23.2%、工业-22.6%）一致，明显弱于防御性板块——与ctx数据中公用事业-1.2%、房地产-7.5%相对领先吻合。","drivers":["Fed 4th 2018 rate hike / policy error fear","US-China trade war escalation","VIX spike risk-off rotation","oil collapse deflation scare","growth-to-value rotation"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2018年第四次加息/政策失误恐惧","美中贸易战升级","VIX飙升避险轮动","油价暴跌通缩恐慌","成长转价值轮动"],"prev_key":"2018-09-28","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed overtightening and trade-war recession scare","title_zh":"美联储过度紧缩与贸易战衰退恐慌","turn_id":"us_sector_comm:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"The January 4, 2019 Powell 'patient' speech effectively ended the hiking cycle; the Fed then cut three times (July, September, October 2019) before a brief pause. The US-China Phase 1 trade deal framework, agreed in October 2019, removed tail risk. VIX compressed from 36 to 12, TLT gained 16.4% (rates fell), and semis rallied 83.1%, confirming a tech/growth-led recovery. Comm Services was the second-best sector at +46.7%, trailing only Tech at 70.8%, as Alphabet, Facebook, and Netflix re-rated sharply on earnings growth that had been discounted during the Q4 selloff. The narrow breadth (EW lagged cap-weight by 4.5pp) confirms this was mega-cap-led rather than a broad cyclical expansion.","body_zh":"2019年1月4日鲍威尔发表'耐心'讲话，实际上终止了加息周期；美联储随后三次降息（7月、9月、10月）。2019年10月美中第一阶段贸易协议框架落地，消除尾部风险。VIX从36压缩至12，TLT上涨16.4%（利率下行），半导体板块大涨83.1%，确认科技/成长主导的复苏。通信服务以+46.7%成为第二强板块，仅次于科技板块的70.8%，谷歌、Facebook及Netflix在第四季度暴跌后盈利重新定价大幅反弹。等权指数落后市值加权4.5个百分点，确认行情以大市值股为主导，而非广泛周期性扩张。","drivers":["Fed pivot to 'patient' / three 2019 rate cuts","US-China Phase 1 trade deal framework","VIX compression risk-on","FAANG earnings re-rating","duration-sensitives re-rate as rates fall"],"drivers_zh":["美联储转向'耐心'立场/2019年三次降息","美中第一阶段贸易协议框架","VIX压缩风险偏好回升","FAANG盈利重新定价","利率下行带动久期敏感股估值修复"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot and trade truce re-rating","title_zh":"美联储转向与贸易休战驱动重新定价","turn_id":"us_sector_comm:trough:2018-12"},"2020-01-17":{"body":"China's COVID-19 outbreak became a global pandemic by late February; the WHO declared it on March 11, 2020. US lockdowns triggered the fastest 30% bear market in history, with VIX peaking at 66 on March 18. Oil collapsed 61.7% (Saudi-Russia price war compounded on March 8) and the dollar surged 5.3% on safe-haven demand. Comm fell -34.3%, slightly worse than SPY's -30.7% and consistent with the pattern where high-growth names lagged during the initial liquidity panic despite their fundamental immunity to lockdowns; the ctx shows Staples (-21%) and Health (-24.3%) defending best while Energy (-56.3%) and Industrials (-39.1%) led losses. Comm's decline reflects its growth/cyclical classification in a broad margin-call liquidation.","body_zh":"新冠疫情2月下旬演变为全球大流行，世卫组织于3月11日正式宣布。美国封锁措施触发史上最快的30%熊市，VIX于3月18日攀升至66。沙特-俄罗斯价格战（3月8日）叠加疫情冲击，油价暴跌61.7%；美元因避险需求升值5.3%。通信服务下跌34.3%，略差于标普500的-30.7%，与高成长股在初期流动性恐慌中跑输的规律一致，尽管其基本面并不受封锁影响；ctx数据显示必需消费品（-21%）和医疗健康（-24.3%）相对抗跌，能源（-56.3%）和工业（-39.1%）跌幅最大。通信服务跌幅反映其在广泛去杠杆抛售中被归类为成长/周期板块。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic / global lockdowns","VIX 12 to 66 liquidity panic","oil price war / Saudi-Russia March 2020","dollar safe-haven surge","indiscriminate growth-stock deleveraging"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情大流行/全球封锁","VIX从12飙升至66流动性恐慌","沙特-俄罗斯油价战2020年3月","美元避险需求飙升","高成长股无差别去杠杆"],"prev_key":"2020-01-17","prev_key_chain":["2020-01-17"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID-19 pandemic crash indiscriminate selloff","title_zh":"新冠疫情冲击引发无差别抛售","turn_id":"us_sector_comm:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-20":{"body":"The Fed cut to zero on March 15 and launched unlimited QE on March 23; Congress passed the $2.2T CARES Act on March 27. Comm Services +118.5% was not the top sector (Energy +112.2%, Materials +96.3% led in the EW reflation surge) but was a strong mid-tier performer. The structural COVID tailwinds — Netflix adding 26M subscribers in H1 2020, YouTube/digital ad rebound, streaming replacing linear TV, and social-media engagement surging — gave the internet/media names within Comm a durable earnings boost. Cyclicals dominated at +94.6% vs defensives +40.4%, and the EW beat cap-weight by 17.5pp (broad participation), while the dollar fell 10.6% (tailwind for multinationals) and oil rebounded 188.9% off its April 2020 lows.","body_zh":"美联储3月15日降息至零并于3月23日启动无限量QE；国会3月27日通过2.2万亿美元CARES法案。通信服务大涨118.5%，虽非本轮等权再通胀反弹的领涨板块（能源+112.2%、材料+96.3%领先），但表现强劲。新冠带来的结构性顺风——Netflix 2020年上半年新增2600万订阅用户、YouTube/数字广告复苏、流媒体取代线性电视、社交媒体用户活跃度激增——为板块内互联网/媒体公司带来持久的盈利提升。周期股整体+94.6%大幅领先防御股+40.4%，等权指数跑赢市值加权17.5个百分点（广泛参与），美元下跌10.6%（利好跨国公司），油价自2020年4月低点反弹188.9%。","drivers":["Fed zero rates + unlimited QE","$2.2T CARES Act fiscal stimulus","streaming / digital ad demand surge (COVID stay-at-home)","broad reflation / cyclical recovery","dollar weakening tailwind for multinationals"],"drivers_zh":["美联储零利率+无限量QE","2.2万亿美元CARES法案财政刺激","流媒体/数字广告需求爆发（居家抗疫）","广泛再通胀/周期性复苏","美元走弱利好跨国公司"],"prev_key":"2020-03-20","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Fiscal-monetary flood and digital-demand surge","title_zh":"天量财政货币刺激与数字需求爆发","turn_id":"us_sector_comm:trough:2020-03"},"2021-03-16":{"body":"From March 2021 — when the 10-year yield peaked around 1.75% and the Fed began signaling eventual tapering — through June 2022, rising rates systematically de-rated long-duration growth assets. The Fed announced taper in November 2021, delivered its first hike in March 2022, and followed with 75bp hikes in June and July 2022. TLT lost 16.3%, DXY gained 12.8%, and VIX rose from 20 to 33. Comm's -28.9% decline matched the sector's loss of ground to energy (+59.7%) and defensives (+6.7% avg), exactly as the ctx signals describe — a stagflation regime where rate-sensitive growth stocks (Comm was second worst at -29.5% vs SPY -5.9%) were punished. Meta's Q4 2021 guidance miss and Apple's privacy changes (ATT) that cut into digital ad targeting compounded sector-specific pain.","body_zh":"2021年3月起（10年期美债收益率在约1.75%见顶，美联储开始释放缩减购债信号），至2022年6月，利率持续上升系统性压低长久期成长资产估值。美联储2021年11月宣布缩减购债，2022年3月首次加息，6月和7月相继实施75基点大幅加息。TLT下跌16.3%，美元指数上涨12.8%，VIX从20升至33。通信服务下跌28.9%，明显落后于能源（+59.7%）和防御性板块（平均+6.7%），与ctx信号描述的滞胀环境高度吻合——利率敏感型成长股（通信服务-29.5%，标普500仅-5.9%）遭受重创。Meta 2021年第四季度盈利预警及苹果ATT隐私政策（削弱数字广告定向效果）进一步加剧板块特有痛苦。","drivers":["Fed taper November 2021 / rate hikes from March 2022","10-year yield surge / TLT -16.3%","stagflation regime / DXY +12.8%","Meta ATT/Apple privacy shock to ad revenue","long-duration growth de-rating"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2021年11月缩表/2022年3月起加息","10年期美债收益率飙升/TLT下跌16.3%","滞胀环境/美元指数+12.8%","苹果ATT隐私政策冲击Meta广告收入","长久期成长股估值压缩"],"prev_key":"2021-03-16","prev_key_chain":["2021-03-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed tightening cycle crushes long-duration growth","title_zh":"美联储紧缩周期重压长久期成长股","turn_id":"us_sector_comm:peak:2021-03"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"The June 2022 CPI print (released July 13) showed the first deceleration from the 9.1% June peak, sparking a sharp bear-market rally on hopes of an imminent Fed pivot. The rally ran from June 16 (a post-FOMC 75bp hike trough) through August 16. Comm gained 16.6% — in the middle of the pack — as Discretionary (+28.8%) and Tech (+22.7%) led alongside Utilities (+19.4%) in a mixed goldilocks-disinflation read. Semis rose 19.5%, growth beat value by 8.8pp, and VIX compressed from 33 to 20. The ctx correctly identifies this as a growth/risk-on rebound (not a defensive-led pattern), consistent with oversold-bounce dynamics rather than a fundamental turning point.","body_zh":"2022年6月CPI数据（7月13日公布）显示从9.1%高点开始回落，市场燃起美联储即将转向的希望，触发剧烈的熊市反弹。本轮反弹从6月16日（75基点加息后的底部）持续至8月16日。通信服务上涨16.6%，处于中游水平——可选消费品（+28.8%）和科技（+22.7%）领涨，公用事业（+19.4%）同步走强，呈现混合的黄金/去通胀读数。半导体上涨19.5%，成长股跑赢价值股8.8个百分点，VIX从33压缩至20。ctx信号正确地将其定性为成长/风险偏好反弹（而非防御性领涨），符合超卖反弹的动态特征，而非基本面转折点。","drivers":["June 2022 CPI deceleration / peak-inflation narrative","oversold growth-stock bounce / VIX 33 to 20","bear market rally short-covering","tech/semis-led re-rating","hopes of Fed policy pivot"],"drivers_zh":["2022年6月CPI回落/通胀见顶叙事","成长股超卖反弹/VIX从33降至20","熊市反弹空头回补","科技/半导体领涨重新定价","美联储政策转向预期"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-inflation hopes trigger bear market bounce","title_zh":"通胀见顶预期触发熊市反弹","turn_id":"us_sector_comm:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"On August 25, 2022, Fed Chair Powell delivered a short, unusually hawkish speech at Jackson Hole signaling rates would stay restrictive 'for some time' and warning against a premature pivot — the market had been pricing in 2023 cuts. The Dow fell 1,000 points that day and the selloff resumed. TLT lost a further 17.8% through November 9, the DXY added 3.8%, and the 10-year yield rose above 4.2% by late October. Comm fell 20.1%, the second-worst sector behind Discretionary (-23.5%), while Energy (+16.6%) was the only gainer — perfectly consistent with a rate-shock/growth-de-rate regime. Advertising-dependent platforms (Alphabet, Meta) faced a double hit: rising discount rates compressed valuations while a softening economy threatened ad-spend, confirmed by weak Q3 2022 earnings from both companies in late October.","body_zh":"2022年8月25日，美联储主席鲍威尔在杰克逊霍尔发表了简短但异常鹰派的讲话，表示利率将'在一段时期内'保持限制性水平，并警告不要过早转向——而市场此前已预期2023年将降息。道指当天跌逾1000点，抛售行情重启。TLT至11月9日再跌17.8%，美元指数上涨3.8%，10年期美债收益率10月下旬突破4.2%。通信服务下跌20.1%，仅次于可选消费品（-23.5%）排名最差板块第二，而能源（+16.6%）是唯一上涨板块——与利率冲击/成长股去估值环境高度吻合。依赖广告的平台（谷歌、Meta）遭受双重打击：折现率上升压缩估值，同时经济走弱威胁广告预算，10月下旬两家公司疲软的第三季度财报予以证实。","drivers":["Jackson Hole hawkish Powell speech August 25, 2022","yields surge / TLT -17.8% / 10yr above 4%","DXY +3.8% headwind for multinationals","Meta/Alphabet Q3 2022 ad-revenue miss","growth de-rating / higher-for-longer repricing"],"drivers_zh":["2022年8月25日杰克逊霍尔鹰派讲话","美债收益率飙升/TLT跌17.8%/10年期突破4%","美元指数+3.8%利空跨国公司","Meta/谷歌2022年第三季度广告收入低于预期","成长股去估值/'更长时间高利率'重新定价"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkish shock resets higher for longer","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击重塑'更长时间维持高利率'预期","turn_id":"us_sector_comm:peak:2022-08"},"2022-11-09":{"body":"ChatGPT launched November 30, 2022, igniting the generative-AI investment wave that made Alphabet and Meta primary beneficiaries: both are simultaneously AI infrastructure builders and the world's largest AI-powered advertising platforms. Meta's 2023 'Year of Efficiency' (layoffs, $40B buyback, reaccelerated ad revenue post-ATT) produced a 194% stock gain in 2023. Alphabet's Google Search maintained dominance and YouTube recovered. Over the full leg (Nov 2022 to Feb 2025), Comm was the single best sector at +133.6%, outperforming SPY's +69.2%, driven by semis +171.2% and a 62-point growth-over-value spread. The extreme narrow breadth (-31pp EW vs cap-weight) confirms this was the most concentrated mega-cap rally in modern history.","body_zh":"ChatGPT于2022年11月30日发布，点燃生成式AI投资浪潮，使谷歌和Meta成为最大受益方：两者既是AI基础设施建设者，也是全球最大的AI赋能广告平台。Meta 2023年'效率之年'（裁员、400亿美元回购、ATT冲击后广告收入加速复苏）令股价全年大涨194%。谷歌搜索保持主导地位，YouTube广告复苏。整段行情（2022年11月至2025年2月），通信服务以+133.6%成为所有板块中表现最佳的，超越标普500的+69.2%，半导体板块大涨171.2%，成长股领先价值股62个百分点。极度窄幅的市场广度（等权落后市值加权31个百分点）确认这是现代历史上最集中的大市值股票行情。","drivers":["ChatGPT / generative AI launch November 2022","Meta Year of Efficiency + ad-revenue reacceleration 2023","AI infrastructure capex re-rating for Alphabet/Meta","semis +171% / AI chip demand","narrow mega-cap breadth / growth-value 62pp spread"],"drivers_zh":["ChatGPT/生成式AI于2022年11月发布","Meta效率之年+2023年广告收入加速复苏","AI基础设施资本支出重估谷歌/Meta","半导体+171%/AI芯片需求","窄幅大市值主导/成长价值利差62个百分点"],"prev_key":"2022-11-09","prev_key_chain":["2022-11-09"],"status":"exact","title":"AI boom and ad-recovery mega-cap super-cycle","title_zh":"AI浪潮与广告复苏驱动大市值超级周期","turn_id":"us_sector_comm:trough:2022-11"},"2025-02-19":{"body":"Two catalysts converged: DeepSeek's late-January 2025 release (a low-cost Chinese LLM that erased $589B from Nvidia's market cap in one day and raised capex-ROI doubts for Alphabet and Meta) shook AI sentiment, and President Trump's April 2, 2025 'Liberation Day' reciprocal tariff announcement (up to 145% on China, 10%+ on 75 nations) triggered a global risk-off wave. VIX surged from 15 to 52, SPY fell 18.8%, and semis collapsed 30.1%. Comm fell 17.7%, second worst after Tech (-25.7%), consistent with its now-entrenched classification as a long-duration/growth sector rather than a defensive. Defensives led on a relative basis (Staples -5.9%, Utilities -8.3%), confirming the ctx flight-to-safety signal.","body_zh":"两大催化剂同时爆发：2025年1月下旬DeepSeek发布（低成本中国大语言模型，单日抹去英伟达5890亿美元市值，引发对谷歌和Meta资本支出回报率的质疑），动摇AI市场情绪；特朗普4月2日宣布'解放日'对等关税（对华关税高达145%，对75国加征10%以上），触发全球避险浪潮。VIX从15飙升至52，标普500下跌18.8%，半导体板块崩跌30.1%。通信服务下跌17.7%，仅次于科技（-25.7%）排名第二差，与其现已固化的'长久期/成长'板块定位一致，而非防御型板块。防御板块相对领先（必需消费品-5.9%，公用事业-8.3%），印证了ctx的避险轮动信号。","drivers":["DeepSeek AI capex-ROI shock January 2025","Trump Liberation Day tariffs / trade war April 2, 2025","VIX 15 to 52 risk-off","semis -30.1% / growth de-rating","defensives led flight-to-safety"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek AI资本支出回报冲击2025年1月","特朗普解放日关税/贸易战2025年4月2日","VIX从15飙升至52避险情绪","半导体-30.1%/成长股去估值","防御板块领涨避险轮动"],"prev_key":"2025-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2025-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump tariff shock and AI-capex doubt selloff","title_zh":"特朗普关税冲击与AI资本支出疑虑引发抛售","turn_id":"us_sector_comm:peak:2025-02"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"On April 9, 2025, Trump announced a 90-day pause on reciprocal tariffs for all nations except China, sending SPY up 9.5% — its best day since October 2008 — and the Nasdaq up 12%. A subsequent US-China trade truce in May reduced tariffs on Chinese goods from 145% to 30%. VIX collapsed from 52 to 16, and the recovery was tech-led: semis gained 81.4%, growth beat value by 23.3pp, and narrow breadth (-9.9pp EW vs cap-weight) confirmed mega-cap concentration. Comm rose 38.2%, second only to Tech (+57.3%), as Alphabet and Meta delivered strong Q1 and Q2 2025 earnings showing AI-driven ad-revenue acceleration and cloud growth, and buyback programs absorbed the prior selloff's supply overhang.","body_zh":"2025年4月9日，特朗普宣布对除中国外所有国家的对等关税暂停90天，标普500单日上涨9.5%（为2008年10月以来最大单日涨幅），纳斯达克上涨12%。随后5月美中贸易休战，中国商品关税从145%降至30%。VIX从52骤降至16，复苏由科技股主导：半导体上涨81.4%，成长股跑赢价值股23.3个百分点，等权落后市值加权9.9个百分点（窄幅大市值集中）。通信服务上涨38.2%，仅次于科技（+57.3%），谷歌和Meta2025年第一、二季度财报强劲——AI赋能广告收入加速及云业务增长，回购计划吸收了前期抛售带来的供给压力。","drivers":["Trump 90-day tariff pause April 9, 2025","US-China trade truce May 2025 (145% to 30% tariffs)","VIX 52 to 16 risk-on recovery","Alphabet/Meta Q1-Q2 2025 AI ad-revenue beat","semis +81% / mega-cap growth re-rating"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普90天关税暂停2025年4月9日","美中贸易休战2025年5月（关税从145%降至30%）","VIX从52降至16风险偏好复苏","谷歌/Meta 2025年一二季度AI广告收入超预期","半导体+81%/大市值成长股重新定价"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff pause and AI ad-revenue recovery rally","title_zh":"关税暂停与AI广告收入复苏驱动反弹","turn_id":"us_sector_comm:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Communication Services (EW) is in a confirmed Trough/Bottoming phase (rs_rank 41/100, below the 200-day MA, -9.6% in the current window vs SPY +6.3%). Despite a reflation/growth-up macro quad with cyclicals outperforming defensives by 4.3pp, Comm is the worst laggard alongside Discretionary and Financials. The sector is weighed down by two sector-specific overhangs that override the broad reflation tailwind: (1) AI capex-trap anxiety — Alphabet's 2026 capex guide of $175-185B and Meta's $115-135B raise return-on-investment doubts as monetization lags spending; and (2) regulatory/legal pressure — fresh antitrust and privacy rulings are raising liability cost estimates for the two largest names. Equal-weight breadth (+2.9% RSP beat) signals broad participation elsewhere, but Comm is not among the beneficiaries. Growth minus value at -15.2 is a significant headwind for a sector whose free-cash-flow value rests heavily on outer-year AI monetization. A durable turn would require either a deceleration in capex guidance or a new digital-ad demand catalyst to re-rate earnings.","now_zh":"通信服务（等权）目前处于确认的底部/筑底阶段（相对强弱排名41/100，股价位于200日均线以下，当前窗口期内下跌9.6%，而标普500上涨6.3%）。尽管宏观处于再通胀/增长向上象限（周期股跑赢防御股4.3个百分点），通信服务仍是最弱板块之一。板块承压于两大特有阻力：(1) AI资本支出陷阱——谷歌2026年资本支出指引1750-1850亿美元、Meta 1150-1350亿美元，在货币化滞后于投入的背景下引发资本回报疑虑；(2) 监管/法律压力——新反垄断及隐私裁决使板块前两大权重股的潜在负债成本大幅上升。等权指数跑赢市值加权指数2.9个百分点，说明其他板块普遍参与行情，但通信服务并不在受益之列。成长股vs价值股利差-15.2对依赖远期AI货币化的板块构成重大逆风。板块持续反转需资本支出指引降温或数字广告需求出现新催化剂以重估盈利预期。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-us_sector_discretionary":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"The Fed began tapering QE in January 2014 without triggering recession, and equities grinded higher through mid-2015, with Health (+40.5%) and Utilities (+29%) leading in a slowdown/deflation quad - TLT surged 26.4% as yields fell. A 55% collapse in WTI oil prices (mid-2014 through early 2015) punished Energy (-17.6%) while lifting consumer purchasing power broadly, and the strong dollar (+20% DXY) hammered Materials. Discretionary's +29.8% gain largely reflected index beta rather than sector-specific strength: cyclicals as a group averaged only +9.6% vs defensives +30.7%, meaning Discretionary outpaced its cyclical peers but lagged defensives significantly, riding health-led yield-driven flows. Growth slightly beat value (8.3pp gap) while VIX stayed calm at 14 throughout, characteristic of a steady low-vol melt-up.","body_zh":"2014年1月起美联储开始缩减购买且未引发衰退，股市展开慢牛行至2015年中。医疗（+40.5%）和公用事业（+29%）在慢速/通缩格局中领跑，TLT涨幅26.4%表明收益率下行。WTI油价从2014年中起暴跌55%，在压制能源板块的同时提升了消费者购买力，强元（DXY+20%）则打压原材料板块。非必需消费+29.8%主要反映指数Beta收益，周期股整体仅均涨+9.6%远不如防御股+30.7%，说明该板块不是本次上涨的主要驱动力，而是随防御股/医疗驱动的市场顺势上行。","drivers":["Fed taper soft-landing 2014","oil -55% lifts consumer purchasing power","defensive/health-led slowdown deflation quad","dollar strength +20% DXY","yield collapse TLT +26%"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2014年缩减购买软着陆","油价跌55%提升购买力","防御/医疗领跑的慢速通缩格局","美元强势+20%","收益率下行TLT+26%"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"QE taper melt-up; oil crash aids index, not sector","title_zh":"QE缩减慢牛；油价暴跌提振购买力但防御股领跑","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:trough:2014-01"},"2015-08-18":{"body":"On August 11 2015 China's PBOC surprised markets with a yuan devaluation, triggering a global risk-off wave that accelerated into the August 24 Black Monday when the Shanghai Composite crashed 8% and the VIX spiked from 14 to 26 (intraday above 40). Oil fell another 30% as the China growth-scare deflated commodity demand expectations, and credit spreads widened (HYG-LQD -9.3pp). The rotation was a textbook flight-to-safety: defensives dropped only -3.9% while cyclicals fell -12.8%, with Discretionary down 16.3% as confidence-sensitive spending names repriced sharply. The dollar was flat (-0.4% DXY), ruling out FX as the primary driver - this was a pure growth-scare/deflation rotation.","body_zh":"2015年8月11日中国人民银行出乎预料地实施人民币贬值，引发8月24日黑色星期一全球股市暴跌，上证单日暴跌8%，VIX从14飙升至26（盘中超过40）。油价再跌30%，信用差价扩大，属于典型的避险/通缩逃险行情：防御股仅跌-3.9%，周期股跌-12.8%，非必需消费下跌16.3%。美元基本持平，排除汇率主导因素，这是纯粹的增长恐慌/通缩轮动。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation Aug 11 2015","Shanghai Composite Black Monday -8%","VIX spike 14 to 26","oil -30% commodity demand fear","cyclicals vs defensives flight-to-safety"],"drivers_zh":["2015年8月11日人民币贬值","上证指数黑色星期一暴跌8%","VIX从14飙升至26","油价再跌30%需求恶化","避险轮动周期股大跌防御股抗跌"],"prev_key":"2015-08-18","prev_key_chain":["2015-08-18"],"status":"exact","title":"China devaluation risk-off; cyclicals routed","title_zh":"人民币贬值引发全球避险，周期股遭重创","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:peak:2015-08"},"2016-02-08":{"body":"Global equities bottomed in mid-February 2016 as WTI oil found a floor near $26/bbl, removing the credit-contagion scare from energy-sector high-yield bonds. The Fed effectively paused its rate-hike cycle after December 2015, removing a major headwind. Trump's election in November 2016 unleashed animal spirits via fiscal-stimulus expectations, lifting Financials and Industrials while keeping risk appetite elevated. Over the full 31-month leg, Tech led (+101%) and Discretionary finished third (+77.5%), with cyclicals dramatically outperforming defensives (72.8% vs 32.9%), oil surged +138%, and semis rallied +135% - a full-cycle reflation/growth-up recovery. The dollar was slightly weaker (-2.8% DXY) and VIX compressed from 26 to 12 throughout.","body_zh":"2016年2月中旬，WTI油价在26美元/桶附近见底，解除了能源行业高收益信用市场的传染恐慌。美联储2015年12月加息后事实上暂停了加息周期，压力解除。2016年11月特朗普当选引发财政刺激预期，金融和工业板块受益，风险偏好持续居高。整个31个月的上涨腿中，科技领跑+101%，非必需消费居第三+77.5%，周期股大幅领先防御股（72.8% vs 32.9%），油价大涨+138%，芯片+135%，是完整的再通胀/增长向上复苏行情。","drivers":["WTI oil floor $26/bbl Feb 2016","Fed pause after Dec 2015 hike","Trump election Nov 2016 fiscal stimulus trade","semis +135% growth-led reflation","VIX compression 26 to 12"],"drivers_zh":["WTI油价26美元/桶见底2016年2月","美联储2015年12月加息后暂停","特朗普2016年11月当选财政刺激预期","芯片+135%增长驱动再通胀","VIX压缩26到12"],"prev_key":"2016-02-08","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Reflation renaissance: oil bottom plus Trump election","title_zh":"反弹再通胀：油价见底加特朗普当选","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:trough:2016-02"},"2018-09-20":{"body":"The S&P 500 and Discretionary peaked on September 20 2018 as Fed Chair Powell's October 3 comment that the Fed was a long way from neutral crystallized fears of overtightening. The US-China trade war escalated through Q4 with tariffs on $200B+ of Chinese goods taking effect in September 2018. Cyclicals fell hardest (Industrials -23.6%, Energy -27.2%) vs defensives (Utilities -1.6%, Staples -10.5%), and VIX spiked from 12 to 36 as credit spreads widened (HYG-LQD -4.9pp). Oil crashed 40% as OPEC supply concerns combined with demand fears; Discretionary fell 19.2% as consumer confidence dropped with the broader equity wealth effect.","body_zh":"2018年9月20日指数见顶，10月3日鲍威尔就距中性利率还很遥远的表态固化了过度紧缩的恐慌。中美贸易战在第四季度升温，2000亿美元以上中国商品关税于2018年9月生效。周期股重创（工业-23.6%，能源-27.2%）远超防御股（公用-1.6%），VIX从12飙升至36，信用差价扩大。油价跌40%，非必需消费跌19.2%。","drivers":["Fed long way from neutral Oct 3 2018","US-China tariffs $200B+ Sep 2018","VIX spike 12 to 36","WTI oil -40%","cyclicals routed vs defensives flight-to-safety"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔距中性远言论2018年10月","中美2000亿关税2018年9月生效","VIX从12飙升至36","WTI油价跌40%","周期板块遭抛售防御股相对强势"],"prev_key":"2018-09-20","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed overtightening plus trade war peak fear","title_zh":"美联储过度紧缩加贸易战恐慌","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"Markets bottomed on Christmas Eve December 24 2018 after the S&P 500 had fallen 20% from its September peak. The recovery was launched by Powell's January 4 2019 press conference signaling a patient Fed, followed by three insurance rate cuts in 2019 (July, September, October) that pushed yields down and TLT up 23.9% over the leg. The US-China phase-one trade deal framework announced late 2019 further reduced uncertainty. Tech led (+78.9%), Discretionary ranked third (+45.8%), with cyclicals outpacing defensives (41.4% vs 36.0%) and semis soaring +87.9%. The tape was narrow: equal-weight lagged cap-weight by 6.3%, confirming mega-cap FAANG and growth stocks drove the bulk of gains.","body_zh":"2018年12月24日市场见底，S&P500已从高位跌20%。鲍威尔2019年1月4日表示耐心等待的鸽派转向，2019年三次预防性降息（七、九、十月）推动利率下行，TLT全程涨+23.9%。中美第一阶段贸易协议框架（2019年底公布）进一步降低不确定性。科技领跑+78.9%，非必需消费居第三+45.8%，芯片+87.9%，等权落后市值加权6.3pp显示走势由大市值科技龙头股主导。","drivers":["Powell patient pivot Jan 4 2019","Three Fed insurance cuts 2019","Phase-one US-China trade truce late 2019","semis +87.9%","TLT +23.9% yields fall"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔2019年1月4日转鸽","2019年三次预防性降息","中美第一阶段贸易协议2019年底","芯片+87.9%","TLT+23.9%利率下行"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot plus phase-one trade truce rally","title_zh":"美联储转鸽加中美第一阶段贸易协议反弹","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-20":{"body":"The S&P 500 peaked February 19 2020, and within 27 trading days fell 34% as the COVID-19 pandemic spread globally. Consumer Discretionary (EW) fell 50.5% - more than double the defensives decline of 18% - as physical retail, restaurants, hotels, and autos faced complete demand destruction from lockdowns. VIX exploded from 16 to 76 (intraday peak of 82.69 on March 16 2020), one of the most violent volatility spikes in market history. Equal-weight underperformed cap-weight by 4.9pp, as smaller discretionary names were hit harder than mega-cap Amazon which benefited from e-commerce surge. Oil crashed 62% as global travel collapsed.","body_zh":"2020年2月19日S&P500见顶，新冠疫情全球蔓延，27个交易日内跌34%。非必需消费（等权）暴跌50.5%，远超防御股跌幅18%，零售、餐饮、酒店及汽车等面临封城带来的完全需求崩溃。VIX从16飙升至76（3月16日盘中高达82.69），创下历史性波动峰值。等权落后市值加权4.9pp，小市值消费名称受冲击更大，油价暴跌62%。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic lockdowns Feb-Mar 2020","demand destruction: retail/restaurants/autos","VIX 16 to 76 historic volatility spike","oil -62% global travel collapse","cyclicals -37% vs defensives -18% rout"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情封城2020年2-3月","零售/餐饮/汽车需求崩塌","VIX从16至76历史性波动峰值","油价跌62%全球出行崩塌","周期股-37%深度超逾防御股-18%"],"prev_key":"2020-02-20","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-20"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic shock; deepest cyclical rout","title_zh":"新冠疫情冲击；非必需消费暴跌50%","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"From March 18-26 an 8-day dead-cat bounce lifted equities as Congress began negotiating what became the $2.2 trillion CARES Act (signed March 27 2020) and the Fed unveiled unlimited QE on March 23. Cyclicals led (Energy +29.6%, Discretionary +16.6%) as the market priced in a policy-driven rescue. However, VIX remained elevated at 61 from 76, signaling this was a relief bounce rather than a sustainable recovery. TLT rose 13.2% as Treasury bids surged on safe-haven demand even amid the bounce, consistent with the still-fragile risk environment.","body_zh":"2020年3月18日至26日，议会开始谈判2.2万亿美元CARES法案（3月27日签署）及美联储3月23日宣布无限量化宽松引发技术性反弹。周期股领涨（能源+29.6%，非必需消费+16.6%），市场开始定价政策救市。但VIX仍在高位（76降至61），表明这仅为局部技术反弹而非持续修复，最终在8个交易日后再度回调。","drivers":["CARES Act $2.2T negotiation started","Fed unlimited QE March 23 2020","cyclicals bounce vs defensives flat","VIX still elevated at 61","policy rescue pricing dead-cat bounce"],"drivers_zh":["CARES法案2.2万亿谈判开始","美联储3月23日宣布无限量化宽松","周期股反弹而防御股岿然不动","VIX仍高达61","政策救市预期定价技术性反弹"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"CARES Act dead-cat bounce, 8 days only","title_zh":"CARES法案预期引发死猫反弹，仅持续8天","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:trough:2020-03"},"2020-03-26":{"body":"A brief 8-day re-selloff from March 26 to April 3 reset expectations as the April 2 2020 US jobless claims print of 6.6 million (then a record) arrived and COVID case counts continued rising sharply with no reopening timeline visible. Defensives held (Staples +3%, Health -0.1%) while cyclicals dropped -7.0% (Industrials -8.4%, Discretionary -8.9%, Financials -9.4%) in a clear risk-off rotation. VIX eased only slightly from 61 to 47, confirming the environment remained acutely stressed. The quad reading was stagflation-ish: oil spiked +25% on a surprise OPEC+ deal yet consumer demand expectations were deteriorating.","body_zh":"2020年3月26日至4月3日，4月2日美国首请失业金人数高达660万（当时历史记录），新冠确诊人数持续急升且复工无期，再度引发避险情绪。防御股相对抗跌（食品+3%，医疗-0.1%），周期股再跌-7.0%，VIX从61降至47。能源因OPEC+协议+25%，宏观表现为滞胀式格局。","drivers":["US jobless claims 6.6M record Apr 2 2020","COVID case surge no reopening timeline","defensives held vs cyclicals -7%","VIX 61 to 47 still acute stress","OPEC+ deal oil +25% stagflation signal"],"drivers_zh":["美首请失业金660万创历史高位","疫情升温且无复工时间表","防御股抗跌而周期股-7%","VIX从61降至47压力未除","OPEC+协议推动油价+25%滞胀信号"],"prev_key":"2020-03-26","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Second COVID panic re-ignites selloff","title_zh":"二次疫情恐慌重燃卖压","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:peak:2020-03"},"2020-04-03":{"body":"The epic 19-month pandemic recovery rally from April 2020 to November 2021 produced a +201% gain in Equal-Weight Consumer Discretionary, the top-performing sector, as fiscal stimulus (CARES Act $2.2T + American Rescue Plan $1.9T in March 2021) and zero interest rates unleashed a consumer spending boom. Homebuilders, auto dealers, and e-commerce names surged as households accumulated surplus savings. The broader backdrop was textbook growth-up reflation: cyclicals +112.7% vs defensives +43.4%, oil +187%, semis +167%, high-beta crushing low-vol by 157pp, and breadth broadened with equal-weight beating cap-weight by +13.7pp - a rare period of genuine broad sector leadership. The dollar fell 6.2% (DXY) as the Fed held ZIRP, and VIX compressed from 47 to 16.","body_zh":"2020年4月至2021年11月的19个月大反弹，等权非必需消费大涨201%，为领跑板块。CARES法案（2.2万亿美元）加上2021年3月美国救援计划（1.9万亿美元）及零利率政策，引发消费热潮。建房商、汽车经销商与电商大幅上涨。宏观为增长向上再通胀：周期股+112.7%大幅领先防御股+43.4%，油价+187%，芯片+167%，等权领先市值13.7pp，VIX从47压缩至16，美元贬值全程助推。","drivers":["CARES + ARP $4.1T fiscal stimulus","ZIRP + Fed unlimited QE","consumer savings surplus spending boom","cyclicals +112.7% vs defensives +43.4%","semis +167% breadth broad EW beat +13.7pp"],"drivers_zh":["CARES+ARP4.1万亿美元财政刺激","零利率+美联储无限量化宽松","家庭储蓄盈余促消费爆发","周期股+112.7%大幅领先防御股","芯片+167%市场广度扩展等权跑赢+13.7pp"],"prev_key":"2020-04-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-04-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Pandemic recovery supercycle; EW Discretionary leads","title_zh":"疫情复苏超级周期；等权非必需消费领涨201%","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:trough:2020-04"},"2021-11-05":{"body":"Discretionary peaked November 5 2021 as the Fed confirmed accelerated tapering at its November FOMC meeting, removing the word transitory from the December 2021 statement, with CPI hitting 7% in December - the highest since 1982. The Omicron variant emerged in late November 2021, adding a growth-scare overlay on the hawkish pivot. The ctx grounding is stagflation-ish: Energy surged +32.7% (oil +46.9%) while growth sectors sold off hard (Tech -13.5%, Comm -21.2%, Discretionary -22.6%), defensives held (Utilities +7.7%, Staples +2.7%), and VIX rose from 16 to 36. The rising dollar (+5.3% DXY) and surging yields (TLT -6.3%) created a toxic combination for rate-sensitive consumer spending assets.","body_zh":"2021年11月5日非必需消费见顶，美联储11月FOMC确认加速缩减购买，12月删除临时表述，CPI达7%（自1982年以来最高）。2021年11月底Omicron变异株增添了增长下行担忧。能源大涨+32.7%，成长板块重跌（科技-13.5%，通信-21.2%，非必需-22.6%），防御股相对坚挺，VIX从16飙升至36，利率上升加美元强势对消费资产构成双重压力。","drivers":["Fed taper acceleration Nov 2021 FOMC","CPI 7% Dec 2021 multi-decade high","Omicron variant growth scare Nov 2021","stagflation quad energy +33% vs growth selloff","VIX 16 to 36 TLT -6.3%"],"drivers_zh":["2021年11月FOMC加速缩减购买","CPI达7%40年最高","Omicron变异株2021年11月出现","滞胀格局能源+33%vs成长股暴跌","VIX从16至36 TLT-6.3%"],"prev_key":"2021-11-05","prev_key_chain":["2021-11-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed taper plus Omicron plus inflation shock","title_zh":"美联储加速缩减加Omicron加通胀冲击","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:peak:2021-11"},"2022-03-07":{"body":"A brief 22-day bounce from March 7 to March 29 2022 saw Discretionary lead (+17.5%) with Tech (+13.5%) and Materials (+12.2%) as the market repriced an oversold condition after a 22% equal-weight sector drawdown. The quad was goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation momentarily, with VIX easing from 36 to 19 and oil retreating 12.7% after its Russia-invasion spike. Semis led (+16.9%) and growth beat value by 7.2pp as short-term positioning unwound. Critically, TLT fell 6.1% (yields continued rising), confirming the bounce was tactical not fundamental: the underlying rate-hike cycle was still fully intact.","body_zh":"2022年3月7日至29日的短暂反弹中，非必需消费领涨+17.5%，市场在经历22%等权板块回撤后的超卖条件下企稳反弹。VIX从36退至19，油价在俄乌入侵冲击后回落12.7%，芯片+16.9%，成长领先价值7.2pp，属于战术性仓位平仓驱动的反弹。但TLT进一步下跌6.1%（收益率继续上行），证明加息周期完全不变，反弹为战术性而非趋势性翻转。","drivers":["oversold bounce after -22% drawdown","VIX eased 36 to 19","oil retraced -12.7% after Russia invasion spike","semis +16.9% short-squeeze","growth beat value 7.2pp tactical unwind"],"drivers_zh":["超卖过度后技术性反弹","VIX从36退至19","油价在俄乌入侵冲击后回落12.7%","芯片+16.9%空头回补","成长领先价值7.2pp战术性仓位平仓"],"prev_key":"2022-03-07","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-07"],"status":"exact","title":"March 2022 bear bounce: oversold tactical relief","title_zh":"2022年3月技术性超卖反弹","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:trough:2022-03"},"2022-03-29":{"body":"From late March to June 16 2022, the Fed pivoted to the most aggressive tightening since 1994: the May 4 meeting delivered a 50bp hike (first since 2000), and June 15 delivered a 75bp hike as CPI hit 9.1% in June - the highest since 1981. Discretionary fell 29.7% (worst sector), as rate-sensitive consumer categories (housing, autos, big-ticket items) repriced sharply. Energy alone held (+1.5% in the leg). The ctx is stagflation-ish: TLT fell 14.1% (yields soaring), the dollar gained 5.3%, VIX rose to 33, and oil stayed elevated (+12.8%). Credit barely widened (HYG-LQD -0.7pp), suggesting the market feared rate-driven recession rather than an imminent credit event.","body_zh":"2022年3月29日至6月16日，美联储实施1994年以来最激进紧缩：5月4日加息50bp（2000年以来最大），6月15日加息75bp，6月CPI高达9.1%（自1981年以来最高）。非必需消费暴跌29.7%（各板块最差），对利率敏感的大件消费品类别（住宅、汽车、大家电）大幅重新定价。TLT-14.1%，美元+5.3%，VIX升至33，油价仍高位，是典型滞胀格局。","drivers":["Fed 50bp May 4 plus 75bp June 15 2022","CPI 9.1% June 2022 40-year high","Discretionary worst sector -29.7%","TLT -14.1% yields soaring","stagflation quad energy held vs growth rout"],"drivers_zh":["美联储5月4日+50bp、6月15日+75bp","CPI 9.1%创40年高","非必需-29.7%各板块最差","TLT-14.1%利率飙升","滞胀格局能源顶浪vs成长股暴跌"],"prev_key":"2022-03-29","prev_key_chain":["2022-03-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed 75bp hike campaign crushes Discretionary","title_zh":"美联储激进加息75bp重创非必需消费","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:peak:2022-03"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"From June 16 to August 16 2022, the July 13 CPI print that fell short of expectations - along with July and August PPI data coming in below forecasts - sparked hopes that inflation had peaked, generating a 2-month bear market rally. Discretionary led all sectors at +28.8% as rate-sensitive cyclicals repriced on the inflation-peak thesis; Tech gained +22.7% and semis +19.5%. VIX eased from 33 to 20 and growth beat value by 8.8pp, consistent with a disinflation relief rally. The dollar (+2.8% DXY) continued rising, but oil fell 26.4%, further supporting the disinflation narrative and boosting consumer spending confidence.","body_zh":"2022年6月16日至8月16日，7月13日CPI低于预期（首次释出通胀见顶信号），加上7、8月PPI连续低于预期，引发为期2个月的熊市反弹。非必需消费领跑各板块+28.8%，大幅重新定价通胀见顶主题。VIX从33退至20，油价回落26.4%，与去通胀主题互相强化。","drivers":["CPI July 13 2022 below expectations inflation peak","inflation peak thesis repricing","Discretionary leads +28.8% all sectors","oil -26.4% disinflation confirming","VIX 33 to 20 relief compression"],"drivers_zh":["7月13日CPI低于预期通胀见顶","通胀见顶主题重新定价","非必需领跑各板块+28.8%","油价-26.4%确认去通胀","VIX从33退至20"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-CPI bear market rally; Discretionary leads","title_zh":"CPI见顶引发熊市反弹，非必需消费领涨","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"The bear market rally ended abruptly on August 26 2022, when Fed Chair Powell delivered an unusually brief and hawkish Jackson Hole speech, explicitly stating the Fed would maintain a restrictive stance for some time and warning against loosening policy too early. The S&P 500 fell 3.3% that Friday alone, and the selloff extended through September 30. The ctx grounding shows rates as the primary driver: TLT fell 11.4% (yields surged), dollar gained 5.3%, and Comm (-19.9%), Real Estate (-20.2%), and Tech (-21.2%) led losses, while Energy (-5.2%) held best. Discretionary fell 17.4% as the market repriced that high-for-longer rates would structurally impair consumer spending.","body_zh":"2022年8月26日，美联储鲍威尔在杰克逊霍尔年会发表异常简短的鹰派讲话，明确表示将长期保持限制性姿态。当日S&P500暴跌3.3%，跌势延伸至9月30日。利率是核心驱动力：TLT-11.4%，美元+5.3%，通讯(-19.9%)、房地产(-20.2%)、科技(-21.2%)领跌，能源独秀。非必需消费下跌-17.4%，反映高利率长期化对消费购买力的结构性损害。","drivers":["Powell Jackson Hole hawkish Aug 26 2022","TLT -11.4% yields surged post-speech","dollar +5.3% headwind","rate-sensitive sectors led losses","high-for-longer rates impair consumer spending"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔2022年8月26日杰克逊鹰派讲话","TLT-11.4%利率飙升","美元+5.3%压力","利率敏感板块领跌","高利率长期化压制消费主题"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkish shock ends bear rally","title_zh":"杰克逊鹰派讲话终结熊市反弹","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:peak:2022-08"},"2022-09-30":{"body":"From the October 2022 bear market bottom, a 9-month 54% rally emerged driven by two sequential catalysts: first, CPI fell from 9.1% to 3% by June 2023 confirming disinflation, which drove the dollar down 10.6% (DXY) and allowed rate expectations to peak; second, ChatGPT's launch in November 2022 and Nvidia's blowout earnings in May 2023 ignited the AI-driven mega-cap tech frenzy. Semis surged 73.3%, growth beat value by 16.1pp, and breadth was extremely narrow (equal-weight lagged cap-weight by 6.3pp). Discretionary gained +53.8% on cyclical recovery but lagged Tech (+52.5%) and Comm (+42%). VIX compressed from 32 to 14, and credit spreads held stable (HYG-LQD +1.6pp).","body_zh":"2022年10月熊市底部出发，9个月内大涨53%。两大序列性驱动力：其一，CPI从9.1%跑至2023年6月的3%，展现去通胀趋势，美元贬值10.6%，利率预期见顶；其二，2022年11月ChatGPT面世及2023年5月英伟达超预期财报引发AI大市值狂潮。芯片+73.3%，成长领先价值16.1pp，市宽极窄（等权落后市值加权6.3pp）。非必需消费+53.8%，但落后科技和通讯。","drivers":["CPI 9.1% to 3% disinflation confirmed Jun 2023","ChatGPT Nov 2022 plus Nvidia blow-out May 2023","semis +73.3% AI mania","dollar -10.6% DXY","narrow breadth EW lagged cap-wt 6.3pp"],"drivers_zh":["CPI从9.1%降至3%去通胀确认2023年6月","ChatGPT 2022年11月+英伟达5月超预期财报","芯片+73.3%AI狂潮","美元-10.6%","市宽极窄等权落后市值加权6.3pp"],"prev_key":"2022-09-30","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Disinflation plus AI mania drives recovery","title_zh":"去通胀加AI狂潮驱动复苏","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:trough:2022-09"},"2023-07-19":{"body":"From July 19 to October 27 2023, the 10-year Treasury yield surged from 3.85% to a 16-year high of 5.02% on October 19, driving TLT down 17.3%. The dollar gained 6.3% (DXY) and oil rose 13.5%, repricing a higher-for-longer Fed scenario. Discretionary fell 15.3% (second-worst sector) as housing-related names, home-improvement retailers, and auto dealers repriced sharply on the yield spike. The quad signal was reflation/growth-up (oil up, commodities up) but discretionary lagged because its rate-sensitivity dominated: the sector's housing-adjacent names are among the most duration-sensitive in the index.","body_zh":"2023年7月19日至10月27日，10年期国债收益率从3.85%飙升至16年最高的5.02%（10月19日），TLT-17.3%。美元强势+6.3%，油价+13.5%，重新定价利率长期维高情境。非必需消费-15.3%，住宅相关、家装零售商和汽车经销商大幅重新定价。该板块对利率敏感度高于市场平均，位居各板块第二差。","drivers":["10Y yield 3.85% to 5.02% Oct 19 2023 16-year high","TLT -17.3% duration shock","dollar +6.3% DXY","housing/auto names most rate-sensitive","higher-for-longer Fed repricing"],"drivers_zh":["10年期利率升至5.02%16年最高2023年10月","TLT-17.3%久期利率冲击","美元+6.3%","住宅/汽车对利率最敏感","长期维高引导重新定价"],"prev_key":"2023-07-19","prev_key_chain":["2023-07-19"],"status":"exact","title":"Bond yield surge kills rate-sensitive names","title_zh":"债券收益率飙升打压利率敏感行业","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:peak:2023-07"},"2023-10-27":{"body":"The October 27 2023 bottom launched a 15-month bull leg (+67.9%) as three successive catalysts compounded: first, the 10-year yield peaked October 19 2023 and began falling (TLT +10.1% through January 2025); second, AI spending accelerated in 2024 driving semis +79.1% and mega-cap tech to new highs; third, Trump's November 2024 re-election unleashed animal spirits via deregulation and tax-cut expectations. Discretionary ranked third among sectors (+57.5%), behind Financials (+68%) and Comm (+63.8%), as the Goldilocks quad (disinflation plus growth) drove VIX from 21 to 16. Breadth was extremely narrow: equal-weight lagged cap-weight by 10.4pp, with mega-cap Amazon and Tesla dominating the cap-weighted index while equal-weight Discretionary still gained +67.9%.","body_zh":"2023年10月27日底部启动了长达15个月+67.9%的牛市行情，三大序列性催化剂叠加：其一，10年期收益率于2023年10月19日见顶并开始回落，TLT全程+10.1%；其二，2024年AI支出加速推动芯片+79.1%及大市值科技屡创历史新高；其三，2024年11月特朗普再度当选引发除监管和减税预期。非必需+57.5%居板块第三，黄金年代（去通胀+增长）VIX从21降至16，但等权落后市值加权10.4pp显示大市值龙头股主导市场。","drivers":["10Y yield peak Oct 19 2023 then reversal","AI capex acceleration 2024 semis +79.1%","Trump Nov 2024 re-election animal spirits","Goldilocks quad disinflation plus growth","narrow breadth EW lagged cap-wt 10.4pp"],"drivers_zh":["10年期利率2023年10月见顶反转","2024年AI资本支出加速芯片+79.1%","2024年11月特朗普再当选风险偏好升温","黄金年代去通胀+增长","市宽极窄等权落后市值加权10.4pp"],"prev_key":"2023-10-27","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Soft landing plus AI plus Trump 2.0 election rally","title_zh":"软着陆加AI加特朗普2.0当选牛市","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:trough:2023-10"},"2025-01-30":{"body":"On April 2 2025, Trump announced sweeping Liberation Day tariffs imposing at least 10% on all US imports and country-specific rates up to 50%+ on China, invoking IEEPA emergency powers. The S&P 500 fell 12.4% in two days - the largest drop since the COVID crash - and VIX spiked to 52.33 on April 8 2025. Discretionary was the hardest-hit sector (-24.2% in the leg from January 30 to April 8) as retailers and consumer goods companies with Asian supply chains faced maximum tariff exposure. Semis fell 26.6%. The dollar weakened 4.5% (DXY) - unusual for a risk-off event - as markets priced USD-negative stagflation from tariff pass-through; TLT rose only 1% as inflation fears muted bond safe-haven flows.","body_zh":"2025年4月2日，特朗普宣布解放日关税政策，所有进口商品至少征收10%关税，对华关税更高，援引IEEPA紧急权力。S&P500两天内跌12.4%，为新冠疫情以来最大跌幅，VIX于4月8日达52.33。非必需消费为整个下滑阶段中最差板块（从1月30日至4月8日-24.2%），亚洲供应链依赖度高的零售商和消费品公司遭受最大冲击。美元弱化(-4.5%)表明这是关税引发滞胀定价而非常规风险规避。","drivers":["Liberation Day tariffs Apr 2 2025 IEEPA powers","S&P 500 -12.4% two-day crash","VIX 16 to 52 spike Apr 8 2025","Discretionary worst sector -24.2% supply chain exposure","dollar -4.5% stagflation pricing"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月2日解放日关税IEEPA授权","S&P500两天-12.4%新冠以来最大跌幅","VIX于4月8日飙升至52","非必需-24.2%最差供应链高度暴露","美元弱化-4.5%预期滞胀定价"],"prev_key":"2025-01-30","prev_key_chain":["2025-01-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Liberation Day tariff shock; Discretionary worst","title_zh":"解放日关税冲击；非必需消费最差板块","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:peak:2025-01"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"On April 9 2025, the Trump administration paused its country-specific Liberation Day tariffs for 90 days, triggering a historic single-day S&P 500 surge of 9.52%. Semiconductors and computers were largely exempted from tariffs, which turbocharged the semis +118.3% gain over the recovery leg as AI-infrastructure spending continued unabated. Discretionary recovered +41.7% (third-ranked sector), with cyclicals broadly outperforming defensives (38.6% vs 15.9%) in a goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation quad. The dollar fell 3.7% (DXY) providing a tailwind for consumer names with global revenues, and VIX compressed dramatically from 52 to 16, reflecting near-complete normalization of tariff-shock risk pricing.","body_zh":"2025年4月9日，特朗普政府将各国别性关税暂停90天，S&P500当日暴涨9.52%创历史级单日强度。芯片和电脑设备大面积获得关税豁免，AI基础设施投资持续强劲，推动芯片全程暴涨+118.3%。非必需消费恢复+41.7%，周期股大幅领先防御股（38.6% vs 15.9%），黄金年代格局。美元弱化3.7%，对全球收入较高的消费品公司暂时利好。","drivers":["Tariff 90-day pause Apr 9 2025","S&P 500 +9.52% single-day surge","semiconductor tariff exemptions AI infrastructure","semis +118.3% AI infrastructure","VIX 52 to 16 full risk normalization"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月9日关税暂停90天","S&P500单日+9.52%历史级大涨","芯片设备获得关税豁免","芯片+118.3%AI基础设施","VIX从52回落16风险完全平息"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff pause plus AI semis exemption fuels recovery","title_zh":"关税暂停加芯片豁免推动复苏","turn_id":"us_sector_discretionary:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Consumer Discretionary (EW) is in early Recovery phase at 27.2% of cycle range - a prime entry zone per the model, though RS rank of 30th percentile confirms the sector still lags most peers. The current macro backdrop is a reflation/growth-up quad: cyclicals outperform defensives (11.2% vs 6.9%), oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%, yet Discretionary itself is down 5.2% YTD and ranks among the bottom two sectors alongside Comm Services (-9.6%), while Tech (+24.3%) and Energy (+21.5%) lead. A firmer dollar (+3.4% DXY) is a headwind for import-dependent retailers and auto companies. Broadening breadth (RSP outpacing SPY by +2.9%) historically precedes catch-up in lagging cyclicals, and the sector holding above its 200-day MA keeps the technical structure constructive. The BUY signal reflects depressed cycle positioning rather than current price momentum; confirmation would require consumer spending data to stabilize and, ideally, dollar pressure to ease.","now_zh":"非必需消费（等权）处于复苏阶段初期，周期位置27.2%，属于\"黄金入场\"区间，但相对强度排名仅第30百分位，仍落后于大多数板块。当前格局为再通胀/增长向上：周期股跑赢防御股（+11.2% vs +6.9%），油价涨+19.2%，铜金比+18.3%，但非必需消费年初至今下跌5.2%，与通讯服务（-9.6%）居底部，科技（+24.3%）和能源（+21.5%）领跑。美元强势（DXY+3.4%）对依赖进口的零售商和汽车企业构成压力。等权跑赢市值加权+2.9%，历史上往往预示落后板块均值回归补涨。板块处于200日均线上方，技术结构尚佳。BUY信号来自周期低位而非价格动量，确认信号需要消费支出数据企稳并美元压力缓解。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-us_sector_energy":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"From January through late June 2014, Brent held near $108-115/bbl as two concurrent geopolitical shocks — Russia-Ukraine tensions flaring in February and ISIS seizure of Mosul in June — embedded a persistent supply-risk premium. The ctx shows a stagflation-ish quad (oil +13%, copper-gold -14%) with bonds rallying strongly (TLT +10.5%) as growth expectations softened; Energy led with Utilities, while cyclicals underperformed, consistent with a supply-side inflation shock rather than a demand boom. The Equal-Weight energy basket gained 29.9% on high oil realizations and E&P producer re-ratings as Middle Eastern supply risk climbed.","body_zh":"2014年1月至6月下旬，布伦特原油维持在108-115美元/桶区间，两大地缘冲击同步发酵——2月俄乌紧张局势升温、6月ISIS占领摩苏尔——持续推高供应风险溢价。背景数据显示类滞胀格局（油价+13%，铜金比-14%），债券强劲上涨（TLT+10.5%），增长预期走弱；能源与公用事业共同领涨，周期板块落后，符合供给侧通胀冲击特征而非需求驱动。等权能源篮子涨29.9%，受益于高油价变现及中东供应风险溢价对勘探开采商的重新定价。","drivers":["Iraq/ISIS supply shock","Russia-Ukraine geopolitical risk premium","Brent above $110","stagflation quad","defensives/utilities co-leading"],"drivers_zh":["伊拉克/ISIS供应冲击","俄乌地缘风险溢价","布伦特原油110美元以上","类滞胀格局","防御板块/公用事业共同领涨"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Iraq/Ukraine geopolitical premium lifts oil","title_zh":"伊拉克/乌克兰地缘溢价推升油价","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:trough:2014-01"},"2014-06-23":{"body":"Brent peaked near $115 in June 2014 and collapsed to below $50 by January 2015 as OPEC — led by Saudi Arabia — decided at its November 27, 2014 Vienna meeting to maintain production at 30 mb/d, explicitly refusing to accommodate surging US shale output. US tight-oil production had risen ~3 mb/d since 2011, and China/Europe demand decelerated simultaneously, flipping the market into steep oversupply. The ctx confirms a classic risk-off rotation: defensives (+12.8%) vs cyclicals (-3.0%), VIX 11→22, TLT +23.1%, DXY +15.1% — Energy was worst sector at -27.2%, hit by both the commodity collapse and the strong dollar.","body_zh":"布伦特原油于2014年6月见顶约115美元，随后暴跌至2015年1月的50美元以下——沙特主导的OPEC于2014年11月27日维也纳会议决定维持3000万桶/日产量不变，明确拒绝为美国页岩油增产让路。美国致密油产量自2011年起增加约300万桶/日，同时中欧需求放缓，市场转入严重供过于求。背景数据证实经典避险轮动：防御板块(+12.8%)远超周期板块(-3.0%)，波动率指数11→22，TLT+23.1%，美元指数+15.1%——能源板块以-27.2%垫底，同时承受商品崩跌与强美元的双重打压。","drivers":["OPEC Nov-2014 no-cut decision","US shale supply glut","China/Europe demand slowdown","DXY +15% headwind","flight-to-safety rotation"],"drivers_zh":["OPEC 2014年11月不减产决定","美国页岩油供应过剩","中欧需求放缓","美元+15%逆风","避险轮动"],"prev_key":"2014-06-23","prev_key_chain":["2014-06-23"],"status":"exact","title":"OPEC market-share war crushes oil -56%","title_zh":"OPEC市场份额战压垮油价（-56%）","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:peak:2014-06"},"2015-01-15":{"body":"After WTI briefly touched $44/bbl in late January 2015, a sharp mean-reversion rally ensued through May 1 as oversold technicals, a temporary pause in US rig-count declines, and physical rebalancing hopes lifted crude back toward $60. The ctx is unambiguously risk-on and reflationary (oil +27.9%, copper-gold +19.4%, VIX 22→13, TLT -7.3%, cyclicals +8.8% vs defensives -0.3%), with Energy leading all sectors at +14.5%, consistent with a commodity relief bounce rather than a fundamental turning point. The DXY continued to strengthen (+3.2%), which capped the upside.","body_zh":"WTI原油2015年1月下旬短暂触及44美元/桶后，因技术面超卖、美国钻机数下降暂缓及实物再平衡预期，展开反弹至5月1日，原油回升至60美元附近。背景数据明确呈现风险偏好/再通胀特征（油价+27.9%，铜金比+19.4%，VIX 22→13，TLT-7.3%，周期板块+8.8% vs 防御板块-0.3%），能源板块以+14.5%领涨全市场，符合商品技术性反弹而非基本面转折。美元指数延续升势（+3.2%）压制了反弹空间。","drivers":["oversold mean-reversion","oil stabilizes ~$45-60","rig-count decline pause","VIX compression risk-on","reflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["超卖均值回归","油价企稳45-60美元","钻机数下降暂缓","波动率收缩风险偏好","再通胀格局"],"prev_key":"2015-01-15","prev_key_chain":["2015-01-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Dead-cat bounce: oil stabilizes near $45","title_zh":"死猫反弹：油价企稳于45美元附近","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:trough:2015-01"},"2015-05-01":{"body":"The second leg of the oil bear market ran from May 2015 to January 2016, with WTI ultimately hitting $26.21 on February 11, 2016 (the bundle trough at January 20, 2016). The catalyst was a global manufacturing recession — China's PMI contracted for several consecutive months starting mid-2015, Iran nuclear deal finalized July 14, 2015 raised the prospect of Iranian barrels returning to market, and US shale production proved more resilient than expected. The ctx shows catastrophic risk-off: Energy -36.1% (worst sector), Materials -25.5%, VIX 13→28, high-beta minus low-vol -29.4%, cyclicals -16.9% vs defensives -2.1%, TLT +3.9%, DXY +4.0% — a classic growth scare with commodity destruction.","body_zh":"油市熊市第二段自2015年5月持续至2016年1月，WTI于2016年2月11日跌至26.21美元/桶历史低点。催化剂为全球制造业衰退——中国PMI自2015年中期起连续数月收缩，2015年7月14日达成的伊朗核协议引发伊朗原油重返市场预期，同时美国页岩油产量展现出超预期韧性。背景数据呈现灾难性避险走势：能源板块-36.1%（全市场最差），材料-25.5%，VIX 13→28，高贝塔减低波动率-29.4%，周期板块-16.9% vs 防御板块-2.1%，TLT+3.9%，美元+4.0%——经典成长恐慌叠加商品重挫。","drivers":["China manufacturing recession 2015","Iran nuclear deal (July 2015) supply overhang","US shale resilience","global growth scare","VIX 13→28 risk-off"],"drivers_zh":["2015年中国制造业衰退","伊朗核协议（2015年7月）供应过剩预期","美国页岩油韧性超预期","全球成长恐慌","VIX 13→28避险"],"prev_key":"2015-05-01","prev_key_chain":["2015-05-01"],"status":"exact","title":"China slowdown + Iran deal fear: second oil leg down -55%","title_zh":"中国放缓+伊朗协议担忧：油价第二轮下跌（-55%）","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:peak:2015-05"},"2016-01-20":{"body":"This 33-month bull run from January 2016 lows through October 2018 was driven by three sequential re-ratings: (1) OPEC's historic November 30, 2016 cut agreement — the first supply cut in eight years — pushed WTI from $26 to $55; (2) synchronized global growth in 2017 (ISM >55, Eurozone PMI >57) expanded demand, with WTI climbing to $75 by October 2018; (3) Trump's May 2018 Iran sanctions withdrawal threatened supply of ~2.5 mb/d Iranian exports. The ctx shows a textbook reflation-led cyclical boom: oil +187.8%, copper-gold +36.1%, cyclicals +73.9% vs defensives +33.8%, VIX 28→12, DXY -3.4% tailwind, semis +132.3% — broad risk appetite that lifted Energy 112.5%, second only to Tech.","body_zh":"2016年1月低点至2018年10月的33个月牛市由三段连续重新定价驱动：(1) OPEC 2016年11月30日达成8年来首个减产协议，推动WTI从26美元涨至55美元；(2) 2017年全球同步增长（ISM>55，欧元区PMI>57）扩大需求，WTI至2018年10月涨至75美元；(3) 特朗普于2018年5月退出伊朗核协议，威胁约250万桶/日伊朗出口供应。背景数据呈现教科书式再通胀周期牛市：油价+187.8%，铜金比+36.1%，周期板块+73.9% vs 防御板块+33.8%，VIX 28→12，美元-3.4%顺风，半导体+132.3%——广泛风险偏好推动能源涨112.5%，仅次于科技。","drivers":["OPEC Nov-2016 first cut in 8 years","2017 synchronized global growth","Trump Iran sanctions May 2018","DXY weakening tailwind","reflation growth-up quad"],"drivers_zh":["OPEC 2016年11月8年来首次减产","2017年全球同步增长","特朗普2018年5月伊朗制裁","美元走弱顺风","再通胀/增长向上格局"],"prev_key":"2016-01-20","prev_key_chain":["2016-01-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil cycle trough to Trump reflation: +112% mega-rally","title_zh":"油价周期低点至特朗普再通胀：+112%大牛市","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:trough:2016-01"},"2018-10-03":{"body":"Brent hit a four-year high of $86/bbl on October 3, 2018 — the same day the S&P 500 peaked before its Q4 rout — then collapsed as WTI ended the year at $45.15. The Fed hiked four times in 2018 (reaching 2.25-2.50%), igniting growth-slowdown fears; simultaneously Saudi Arabia and Russia ramped production to record highs (above 11 mb/d and 11.4 mb/d respectively) and the US granted waivers on Iran sanctions, flooding the market. The ctx shows broad cyclical damage: defensives -8.1% vs cyclicals -22.5%, VIX 12→36, Energy -29.9% (tied worst with Tech), TLT +6.4%, growth-minus-value -4.6% — a simultaneous rate-shock and demand-destruction selloff.","body_zh":"布伦特原油于2018年10月3日触及四年高点86美元/桶——与标普500高点同日——随后暴跌，WTI年底收于45.15美元。美联储2018年四次加息（最终利率2.25-2.50%），触发成长放缓担忧；同时沙特和俄罗斯将产量拉升至历史记录（分别超过1100万桶/日和1140万桶/日），美国对伊朗制裁豁免大量原油重返市场。背景数据呈现广泛周期性损伤：防御板块-8.1% vs 周期板块-22.5%，VIX 12→36，能源-29.9%（与科技并列最差），TLT+6.4%，成长减价值-4.6%——加息冲击与需求破坏同步发酵。","drivers":["Fed 4 hikes in 2018 (2.50% terminal)","US/Saudi/Russia production records","Iran sanction waivers flood market","growth slowdown fears","VIX 12→36 risk-off"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2018年4次加息（终端利率2.50%）","美国/沙特/俄罗斯产量创历史记录","伊朗制裁豁免淹没市场","成长放缓担忧","VIX 12→36避险"],"prev_key":"2018-10-03","prev_key_chain":["2018-10-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed rate shock + oil oversupply: Q4-2018 crash -34%","title_zh":"美联储加息冲击+石油供过于求：2018年Q4崩跌（-34%）","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:peak:2018-10"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"The Christmas Eve 2018 low coincided with Powell's dovish pivot in early January 2019, where he signaled the Fed would be 'patient' with further hikes, and the risk-on reversal was immediate. WTI rebounded from $42 to $66 by late April 2019, gaining 54.5% in the ctx window. The ctx shows a clean cyclical reversal: VIX 36→12, semis +45.3%, cyclicals +28.1% vs defensives +12.1%, Tech leading at +35.8%, Industrials +30.1% — Energy gained 33.6% riding the broad risk-on wave. Credit spreads tightened (HYG-LQD +3.5%) and growth-minus-value turned positive +7.6%.","body_zh":"2018年圣诞平安夜低点与鲍威尔2019年1月初的鸽派转向同步——他暗示美联储将对进一步加息保持\"耐心\"，风险偏好立即反转。WTI从42美元反弹至4月下旬的66美元，区间涨幅54.5%。背景数据呈现清晰的周期性反转：VIX 36→12，半导体+45.3%，周期板块+28.1% vs 防御板块+12.1%，科技领涨+35.8%，工业+30.1%——能源涨33.6%，随整体风险偏好大潮而涨。信用利差收窄（HYG-LQD+3.5%），成长减价值转正+7.6%。","drivers":["Fed Jan-2019 'patient' pivot","oil rebounds $42→$66 (+54.5%)","VIX 36→12 risk-on","broad cyclical recovery","semis-led growth re-rating"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月\"耐心\"政策转向","油价从42美元反弹至66美元（+54.5%）","VIX 36→12风险偏好回归","周期板块广泛复苏","半导体领涨成长重新定价"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot + oil rebound: sharp V-recovery +33%","title_zh":"美联储转向+油价反弹：急速V形复苏（+33%）","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:trough:2018-12"},"2019-04-22":{"body":"In early May 2019, Trump announced 25% tariffs on $200bn of Chinese goods and threatened tariffs on remaining Chinese imports, while in August threatened another $300bn tranche. The trade-war escalation triggered a growth scare: the 2-year/10-year yield curve inverted in August 2019, oil fell 16.4% as demand expectations weakened, and the equal-weight basket lost 23.9%. The ctx shows a textbook flight-to-safety: defensives led +6.8%, cyclicals -5.2%, TLT +21.7% (yields collapsing), VIX 12→20, narrow breadth (-2.6% RSP vs SPY), credit spreads blew out (HYG-LQD -8.1%) — Energy lagged worst at -17.9% among named sectors.","body_zh":"2019年5月初，特朗普宣布对2000亿美元中国商品加征25%关税，并威胁对余下中国进口商品加税，8月再次威胁征税3000亿美元。贸易战升级触发成长恐慌：2019年8月2年/10年期美债收益率曲线倒挂，需求预期走弱拖累油价下跌16.4%，等权篮子跌23.9%。背景数据呈现教科书式避险：防御板块领涨+6.8%，周期板块-5.2%，TLT+21.7%（收益率暴跌），VIX 12→20，市场宽度收窄（等权-2.6% vs 标普500），信用利差扩大（HYG-LQD -8.1%）——能源板块以-17.9%位列最差板块之列。","drivers":["US-China tariff escalation May/Aug 2019","yield curve inversion Aug-2019","oil -16.4% demand fears","TLT +21.7% flight-to-safety","high-beta -18.4%"],"drivers_zh":["2019年5/8月中美关税升级","2019年8月收益率曲线倒挂","需求担忧拖累油价-16.4%","TLT+21.7%避险","高贝塔-18.4%"],"prev_key":"2019-04-22","prev_key_chain":["2019-04-22"],"status":"exact","title":"US-China trade war escalation: oil -16% risk-off","title_zh":"中美贸易战升级：油价-16%，避险情绪主导","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:peak:2019-04"},"2019-08-27":{"body":"The Fed cut rates three times (July 31, September 18, October 30, 2019) as an 'insurance' cycle, compressing the policy-risk premium. Simultaneously, the US-China Phase 1 trade deal framework emerged in October 2019, and Saudi Arabia's Abqaiq oil facility was struck by drones on September 14, 2019, briefly spiking oil $10/bbl. The ctx confirms a cyclical risk-on move: cyclicals +13.7% vs defensives +8.1%, VIX 20→14, TLT -5.9%, oil +14.1%, semis +31.4% — Energy gained 22.5%, participating in but not leading the broad recovery.","body_zh":"美联储于2019年7月31日、9月18日、10月30日三次降息作为\"预防性\"宽松，压缩政策风险溢价。与此同时，中美第一阶段贸易协议框架于2019年10月浮现，沙特阿布凯格石油设施于9月14日遭无人机袭击，油价短暂跳升约10美元/桶。背景数据确认周期性风险偏好：周期板块+13.7% vs 防御板块+8.1%，VIX 20→14，TLT-5.9%，油价+14.1%，半导体+31.4%——能源涨22.5%，参与但未领跑这轮广泛复苏。","drivers":["Fed three insurance cuts July-Oct 2019","US-China Phase 1 deal framework Oct 2019","Abqaiq drone attack Sep-14 oil spike","VIX 20→14 risk-on","reflation quad"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年7-10月三次预防性降息","2019年10月中美第一阶段协议框架","2019年9月14日阿布凯格无人机袭击推升油价","VIX 20→14风险偏好回归","再通胀格局"],"prev_key":"2019-08-27","prev_key_chain":["2019-08-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed triple-cut + Phase-1 trade deal lifts energy","title_zh":"美联储三次降息+中美第一阶段协议提振能源","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:trough:2019-08"},"2020-01-07":{"body":"COVID-19 spread from China in January-February 2020, triggering global lockdowns and demand destruction estimated at ~30 million bbl/day (30% of global consumption). On March 6, 2020, Saudi Arabia and Russia's OPEC+ negotiations collapsed, launching an all-out price war with Saudi output surging to 12 mb/d; WTI futures briefly went negative on April 20, 2020 (-$37.63/bbl). The Equal-Weight basket fell 68%, the largest drawdown in the series. Ctx shows a pandemic-severity risk-off: VIX 14→76, defensives -13.7% vs cyclicals -35.5%, narrow breadth (-6.2%), oil -67.5%, DXY +4.3%.","body_zh":"新冠疫情2020年1-2月从中国扩散，引发全球封锁，全球石油需求破坏估计约3000万桶/日（全球消费量的30%）。2020年3月6日，沙特与俄罗斯OPEC+谈判破裂，爆发全面价格战，沙特产量飙升至1200万桶/日；WTI期货于2020年4月20日短暂跌入负值（-37.63美元/桶）。等权篮子下跌68%，为本系列最大回撤。背景数据呈现疫情级别的极端避险：VIX 14→76，防御板块-13.7% vs 周期板块-35.5%，市场宽度收窄（-6.2%），油价-67.5%，美元+4.3%。","drivers":["COVID-19 global demand collapse (Mar 2020)","Saudi-Russia OPEC+ price war Mar-6","WTI goes negative Apr-20-2020","VIX 14→76","DXY +4.3% safe-haven"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情全球需求崩溃（2020年3月）","沙特-俄罗斯OPEC+价格战3月6日爆发","WTI 2020年4月20日跌入负值","VIX 14→76","美元+4.3%避险需求"],"prev_key":"2020-01-07","prev_key_chain":["2020-01-07"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic + Saudi price war: -68% historic crash","title_zh":"新冠疫情+沙特价格战：历史性崩跌（-68%）","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"The Fed cut rates to zero on March 15, 2020 and launched unlimited QE, while OPEC+ agreed on April 12 to cut 9.7 mb/d — the largest coordinated supply cut in history. Physical demand began recovering in May as lockdowns lifted, sending oil from negative territory back to $40/bbl by July. The extreme oversold Energy basket (equal-weight) surged 160.5% in just ~11 weeks, the largest single leg in the dataset. The ctx confirms a pure mean-reversion reflation: Energy led all sectors +99.8% (EW including small E&Ps and refiners bouncing from near-zero), VIX 76→26, DXY -4.5%, oil +87.5%, broadening breadth RSP vs SPY +9.7%.","body_zh":"美联储于2020年3月15日将利率降至零并启动无限量QE，OPEC+于4月12日同意减产970万桶/日——史上最大规模协调减产。实物需求于5月封锁解除后开始复苏，油价从负值区间回升至7月的40美元/桶。严重超卖的等权能源篮子在约11周内反弹160.5%，为本系列单腿最大涨幅。背景数据确认纯粹的均值回归再通胀：能源领涨全市场+99.8%（含中小型勘探商和炼油商从接近零点反弹），VIX 76→26，美元-4.5%，油价+87.5%，市场宽度扩张（等权vs标普+9.7%）。","drivers":["Fed zero-rate + unlimited QE Mar-15-2020","OPEC+ 9.7 mb/d cut Apr-12-2020","physical demand recovery post-lockdown","VIX 76→26 extreme mean-reversion","DXY -4.5% tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2020年3月15日零利率+无限量QE","OPEC+ 2020年4月12日减产970万桶/日","封锁解除后实物需求复苏","VIX 76→26极度均值回归","美元-4.5%顺风"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"OPEC+ truce + Fed QE: oversold V-recovery +160%","title_zh":"OPEC+停火+美联储量化宽松：超跌V形反弹（+160%）","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:trough:2020-03"},"2020-06-08":{"body":"From June to late October 2020, markets remained uncertain about the V-shaped recovery as COVID second waves emerged and US election uncertainty grew. The market rotated sharply into mega-cap tech and stay-at-home plays: Tech +10%, Discretionary +9.5% (Amazon, Netflix), semis +14.1%, while Energy fell -39.1% (basket -39.6%) as oil stagnated near $40/bbl and natural gas traded near multi-year lows. The ctx shows a classic narrow-breadth tech rotation: RSP minus SPY -6.7%, growth-minus-value +17.1%, VIX 26→40 (pre-election uncertainty), Energy and Financials worst by a wide margin.","body_zh":"2020年6月至10月下旬，随着新冠疫情第二波来袭及美国大选不确定性升温，市场对V形复苏持审慎态度，资金急剧轮动至科技巨头和居家经济股：科技+10%，可选消费+9.5%（亚马逊、奈飞），半导体+14.1%；能源板块则因油价在40美元/桶附近横盘、天然气跌至多年低位而下跌-39.1%（篮子-39.6%）。背景数据呈现典型的窄基科技轮动：等权减标普-6.7%，成长减价值+17.1%，VIX 26→40（选举不确定性），能源和金融板块大幅落后。","drivers":["COVID second wave demand uncertainty","mega-cap tech/stay-at-home rotation","oil stagnates $40 flat (-2.1%)","growth-over-value +17.1%","VIX 26→40 election uncertainty"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情第二波需求不确定性","科技巨头/居家经济轮动","油价在40美元附近横盘（-2.1%）","成长跑赢价值+17.1%","VIX 26→40选举不确定性"],"prev_key":"2020-06-08","prev_key_chain":["2020-06-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tech mega-cap rotation leaves energy behind -40%","title_zh":"科技巨头轮动令能源遭遗弃（-40%）","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:peak:2020-06"},"2020-10-28":{"body":"The 20-month bull run from October 2020 to June 2022 is the largest leg in the series (+329.5%) and the definitive energy supercycle. Four sequential catalysts: (1) Pfizer vaccine announcement November 9, 2020 triggered reopening trade with cyclical rotation; (2) global synchronized recovery in 2021 drove oil from $40 to $85; (3) Russia's February 24, 2022 invasion of Ukraine sent Brent to $139/bbl in March 2022 as Russian exports (~4 mb/d) faced sanctions; (4) natural gas in Europe traded above $100/MMBtu. Energy was the ONLY sector to beat SPY, gaining 255.8% within the ctx window. The value-over-growth rotation confirmed (growth-minus-value -27.9%), TLT -26.5% (rates surging), DXY +9.5%.","body_zh":"2020年10月至2022年6月的20个月大牛市是本系列最大单腿（+329.5%），构成决定性能源超级周期。四段连续催化剂：(1) 辉瑞疫苗2020年11月9日宣布，触发重开贸易和周期板块轮动；(2) 2021年全球同步复苏推动油价从40美元涨至85美元；(3) 俄罗斯2022年2月24日入侵乌克兰，布伦特原油2022年3月飙升至139美元/桶，俄罗斯出口（约400万桶/日）面临制裁；(4) 欧洲天然气价格一度超过100美元/MMBtu。能源为唯一跑赢标普的板块，区间内涨255.8%。价值跑赢成长确认（成长减价值-27.9%），TLT-26.5%（利率飙升），美元+9.5%。","drivers":["Pfizer vaccine Nov-9-2020 reopening trigger","2021 global synchronized recovery","Russia-Ukraine invasion Feb-24-2022 oil shock","Brent $139 Mar-2022 record","oil +219% in window"],"drivers_zh":["辉瑞疫苗2020年11月9日宣布引发重开交易","2021年全球同步复苏","俄罗斯2022年2月24日入侵乌克兰石油冲击","布伦特原油2022年3月创139美元记录","区间内油价+219%"],"prev_key":"2020-10-28","prev_key_chain":["2020-10-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Vaccine/reopening + Russia-Ukraine supercycle: +329%","title_zh":"疫苗/重开叠加俄乌战争超级周期：+329%","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:trough:2020-10"},"2022-06-07":{"body":"After Brent peaked near $120/bbl in June 2022, a rapid 4-week selloff cut the Equal-Weight energy basket 27.4% as markets priced in demand destruction from aggressive Fed tightening. The Fed had hiked 75bp on June 15 (the largest since 1994) and signaled further hikes, while JPMorgan and Goldman revised US recession odds above 30%. WTI fell 17.5% in the period as inventories at Cushing rose. The ctx shows a broad risk-off rotation: defensives -2.6% vs cyclicals -12.6%, Energy -24.8% (worst sector), Materials -16.5%, copper-gold -16.9%, VIX 24→27, DXY +4.7%.","body_zh":"布伦特原油2022年6月高点约120美元/桶后，市场开始定价美联储激进加息引发的需求破坏，等权能源篮子在短短4周内下跌27.4%。美联储6月15日加息75个基点（1994年以来最大幅度），并暗示继续加息，同时摩根大通和高盛将美国衰退概率上调至30%以上。WTI期间下跌17.5%，库欣库存上升。背景数据呈现广泛避险轮动：防御板块-2.6% vs 周期板块-12.6%，能源板块-24.8%（全市场最差），材料-16.5%，铜金比-16.9%，VIX 24→27，美元+4.7%。","drivers":["Fed 75bp hike Jun-15-2022 (largest since 1994)","recession odds >30% priced","WTI -17.5% demand destruction","DXY +4.7% headwind","risk-off cyclical rotation"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2022年6月15日加息75个基点（1994年以来最大）","衰退概率>30%被定价","WTI-17.5%需求破坏","美元+4.7%逆风","避险周期板块轮动"],"prev_key":"2022-06-07","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Recession fears + demand destruction: sharp reversal -27%","title_zh":"衰退担忧+需求破坏：急速逆转（-27%）","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:peak:2022-06"},"2022-07-06":{"body":"From early July to mid-November 2022, energy staged a strong recovery as OPEC+ proved supply-disciplined, cutting 2 mb/d in October 2022 despite US political pressure, while European gas shortages sustained energy-company earnings. The broader market saw a rotation into value (growth-minus-value -5.6%) as high rates compressed growth multiples. Energy led within the cyclical recovery at +38.8%, Industrials +14.7%, Financials +12.4%. Notably, oil prices actually fell -11.8% in the ctx window — meaning the rally was driven by multiple expansion (earnings expectations held up) and value rotation rather than spot commodity gains.","body_zh":"2022年7月初至11月中旬，能源板块强势复苏——OPEC+展现供应纪律，于2022年10月顶住美国政治压力减产200万桶/日，同时欧洲天然气短缺支撑了能源公司盈利。大市出现价值风格轮动（成长减价值-5.6%），高利率压缩成长股估值倍数。能源以+38.8%领跑周期板块复苏，工业+14.7%，金融+12.4%。值得注意的是，区间内油价实际下跌-11.8%——说明此轮上涨由估值扩张（盈利预期维持）和价值轮动驱动，而非现货商品价格上涨。","drivers":["OPEC+ Oct-2022 2 mb/d cut despite US pressure","European gas shortage sustains earnings","value beats growth (growth-minus-value -5.6%)","broad cyclical re-rating","TLT -12.8% yields still rising"],"drivers_zh":["OPEC+ 2022年10月顶住美国压力减产200万桶/日","欧洲天然气短缺支撑盈利预期","价值跑赢成长（成长减价值-5.6%）","周期板块整体重新定价","TLT-12.8%利率持续上升"],"prev_key":"2022-07-06","prev_key_chain":["2022-07-06"],"status":"exact","title":"OPEC+ resilience + value rotation: energy re-leads +43%","title_zh":"OPEC+供应纪律+价值风格轮动：能源重新领涨（+43%）","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:trough:2022-07"},"2022-11-15":{"body":"From November 2022 through May 2023, the 'Magnificent 7' AI trade dominated: Comm +23.7%, Tech +23.6%, semis +29.4%, growth-minus-value +17.0%, while Energy fell -16.9% and the basket lost 20.4%. Natural gas prices collapsed from $6.68/MMBtu (2022 average) to below $2.66/MMBtu in 2023 — the warmest winter on record cut heating demand, record US production filled storage, and the energy risk premium from Ukraine faded. SPY rose 5.7% in the ctx window while equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -9.1%, the starkest mega-cap concentration signal in the dataset.","body_zh":"2022年11月至2023年5月，\"七雄\"AI行情主导市场：通信+23.7%，科技+23.6%，半导体+29.4%，成长减价值+17.0%，能源板块下跌-16.9%，篮子跌20.4%。天然气价格从2022年平均6.68美元/MMBtu暴跌至2023年的2.66美元以下——史上最暖冬季削减取暖需求，美国天然气产量创纪录填满库存，乌克兰事件引发的能源风险溢价也逐步消散。背景数据显示标普上涨5.7%，等权跑输市值加权高达-9.1%，为本系列最极端的巨头集中度信号。","drivers":["AI/ChatGPT launch Nov-2022 drives tech re-rating","nat gas collapse $6.68→$2.66 (2023)","warm winter 2022-23 demand miss","growth-over-value +17.0%","mega-cap breadth concentration -9.1%"],"drivers_zh":["AI/ChatGPT 2022年11月上线驱动科技板块重新定价","天然气价格崩跌（6.68→2.66美元/MMBtu）","2022-23年暖冬需求落空","成长跑赢价值+17.0%","巨头集中度-9.1%市场宽度收窄"],"prev_key":"2022-11-15","prev_key_chain":["2022-11-15"],"status":"exact","title":"AI/tech melt-up rotates flows OUT of energy -20%","title_zh":"AI/科技行情吸走资金，能源承压（-20%）","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:peak:2022-11"},"2023-05-31":{"body":"The 18-month run from June 2023 to November 2024 was an energy recovery embedded in a bull market that was otherwise dominated by AI and Financials. Oil rose modestly (+4.6% in the ctx) but geopolitical risk premia (Hamas October 7, 2023 attack, Red Sea Houthi disruptions from December 2023, and OPEC+ voluntary cuts) kept a floor under energy equities. Energy underperformed the SPY (SPY +45.5% vs Energy basket +51.1%, close-run) and was not the leadership sector — Financials +63.8%, Comm +58.0%, Industrials +50.8% all led. The DXY stronger (+3.0%), narrow breadth (-9.3%), and tech/semis domination (+70.5%) kept energy's relative performance restrained.","body_zh":"2023年6月至2024年11月的18个月复苏嵌入在以AI和金融股为主导的牛市之中。油价温和上涨（区间+4.6%），但地缘风险溢价（2023年10月7日哈马斯袭击、2023年12月起胡塞武装红海扰乱及OPEC+自愿减产）为能源股提供了底部支撑。能源略微跑赢标普（标普+45.5% vs 能源篮子+51.1%，差距极小），并非领涨板块——金融+63.8%，通信+58.0%，工业+50.8%均领先。美元偏强（+3.0%），市场宽度收窄（-9.3%），科技/半导体主导（+70.5%），限制了能源的相对表现空间。","drivers":["Hamas Oct-7-2023 geopolitical risk floor","Houthi Red Sea disruptions Dec-2023","OPEC+ voluntary supply cuts 2023-24","soft-landing narrative supports cyclicals","AI/semis +70.5% competes for flows"],"drivers_zh":["2023年10月7日哈马斯袭击建立地缘风险底部","2023年12月起胡塞武装扰乱红海","OPEC+ 2023-24年自愿减产","软着陆叙事支撑周期板块","AI/半导体+70.5%竞争资金流入"],"prev_key":"2023-05-31","prev_key_chain":["2023-05-31"],"status":"exact","title":"Soft-landing + geopolitical risk premium: gradual rally +51%","title_zh":"软着陆+地缘风险溢价：渐进式复苏（+51%）","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:trough:2023-05"},"2024-11-22":{"body":"The energy peak in late November 2024 coincided with Trump's election win and his 'drill, baby, drill' deregulation narrative which — paradoxically — signaled more US supply and lower oil prices. Global oil supply rose ~2% in 2025 vs demand +1.2%, creating 2-3 mb/d oversupply. OPEC+ began unwinding production cuts in April 2025, partly at Trump's explicit urging. The April 2, 2025 'Liberation Day' tariff shock (25% on Canada/Mexico, baseline 10% on rest of world) sent recession fears surging and WTI plunged to four-year lows near $55. VIX spiked 15→52. The ctx shows energy was worst sector (-20.1%), defensives least-bad (-7.1% avg), consistent with a tariff-shock growth scare.","body_zh":"2024年11月下旬能源板块见顶，与特朗普赢得大选及其\"钻吧宝贝钻\"放松监管叙事同步——这一叙事矛盾地暗示美国产量增加和油价走低。2025年全球石油供应增长约2% vs 需求增长仅1.2%，形成200-300万桶/日的供过于求。OPEC+于2025年4月开始解除减产，部分原因是特朗普明确施压。2025年4月2日\"解放日\"关税冲击（对加拿大/墨西哥加征25%、对世界其他地区基准10%）令衰退担忧急剧升温，WTI暴跌至约55美元的四年低点。VIX从15飙升至52。背景数据显示能源为最差板块（-20.1%），防御板块跌幅最小（平均-7.1%），符合关税冲击型成长恐慌特征。","drivers":["Trump 'drill baby drill' signals supply overhang","OPEC+ Apr-2025 production unwind","Apr-2 Liberation Day tariff shock","WTI collapses to $55 four-year low","VIX 15→52"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普\"钻吧宝贝钻\"暗示供应增加","OPEC+ 2025年4月开始解除减产","2025年4月2日\"解放日\"关税冲击","WTI暴跌至55美元四年低点","VIX 15→52"],"prev_key":"2024-11-22","prev_key_chain":["2024-11-22"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump tariffs + OPEC oversupply: energy corrects -23%","title_zh":"特朗普关税+OPEC+供过于求：能源回调（-23%）","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:peak:2024-11"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"On February 28, 2026, the US and Israel launched air operations against Iran, which responded by effectively closing the Strait of Hormuz — the passage for ~20% of global oil trade. The IEA characterized it as 'the largest supply disruption in the history of the global oil market.' Brent surged 65% from pre-conflict levels, peaking above $126/bbl, and the Equal-Weight energy basket gained 78.2% from the April 2025 tariff-shock low (trough of prior leg) through the March 27, 2026 peak. The bundle ctx shows energy led at +68.9% within the rally, semis +108.6% (AI spending boom), cyclicals +36.4% vs defensives +16.0%, oil +67.2% — a classic geopolitical supply-shock reflation overlay on a recovering market.","body_zh":"2026年2月28日，美国和以色列对伊朗发动空中打击，伊朗随即实际封锁霍尔木兹海峡——该海峡承载全球约20%的石油贸易。国际能源署将其定性为\"全球石油市场历史上最大的供应中断\"。布伦特原油从冲突前水平大涨65%，峰值超过126美元/桶，等权能源篮子从2025年4月关税冲击低点（上一腿低谷）至2026年3月27日高点涨78.2%。背景数据显示能源在本轮反弹中领涨+68.9%，半导体+108.6%（AI支出热潮），周期板块+36.4% vs 防御板块+16.0%，油价+67.2%——经典地缘政治供应冲击再通胀叠加复苏市场的典型走势。","drivers":["2026 Iran war Strait of Hormuz closure Feb-28-2026","Brent peaks $126+ (65% above pre-conflict)","IEA: largest supply disruption ever","oil +67.2% in window","reflation/growth-up quad"],"drivers_zh":["2026年2月28日伊朗战争封锁霍尔木兹海峡","布伦特原油峰值超126美元（高于冲突前65%）","国际能源署：史上最大供应中断","区间油价+67.2%","再通胀/增长向上格局"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Iran war Hormuz shock: energy surges +78% to March-2026 peak","title_zh":"伊朗战争霍尔木兹冲击：能源板块飙升+78%至2026年3月高点","turn_id":"us_sector_energy:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Energy (Equal-Weight) is in a confirmed Downturn phase (phase score 41.1, RS rank 45 vs SPY peers), rolling over from the March 2026 peak that was driven by the Iran-war oil shock. The sector had been the YTD leader (up ~39% at peak) but has reversed sharply as the U.S.-Iran interim peace agreement announced in mid-June 2026 opened the path to Strait of Hormuz reopening, causing WTI to drop from above $110 to the low $70s. Current ctx shows oil +19.2% YTD (still elevated) and DXY +3.4% (a headwind), while broader market tone is reflation/growth-up with cyclicals outperforming defensives — yet energy itself is lagging as the geopolitical risk premium collapses. The setup is a post-supply-shock mean-reversion: the sector is still above its 200-day but the 10-day/50-day moving average crossed bearishly on June 16, 2026, and refiner/midstream stocks are outperforming oil majors, signaling the market is already pricing in softer crude ahead.","now_zh":"能源（等权）处于确认的下行阶段（周期位置41.1，相对强度排名45），从2026年3月的高点回落——该高峰由伊朗战争石油冲击所驱动。板块在年内一度领涨（高点涨幅约39%），但随着美伊临时和平协议于2026年6月中旬宣布、霍尔木兹海峡重开预期升温，WTI原油从110美元以上跌回70美元低位，板块随之急剧回调。当前背景显示油价年内仍涨19.2%（仍处高位），美元指数涨3.4%（构成逆风），大市基调为再通胀/增长向上，周期板块整体跑赢防御板块——但能源板块本身已落后，地缘溢价正在消散。当前形态为供应冲击后的均值回归：板块仍在200日均线以上，但10日/50日均线于2026年6月16日形成死叉，炼油/中游股跑赢石油巨头，市场已在定价油价进一步走软。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"oil.regime_shift.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"oil.regime_shift.v1","arch_state":"pass","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-us_sector_financials":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"US financials rose 23.2% from January 2014 to August 2015 as post-GFC credit cycle expansion and accelerating loan growth provided a structural tailwind, with investors pricing in the Fed's first rate hike since 2006 (delivered December 2015) as an upcoming NIM booster. The ctx grounding reveals a slowdown/deflation-scare market: defensives dominated (Health +40%, Utilities +25%), the DXY surged +20% as the dollar strengthened aggressively, TLT rose +25.6% as yields actually fell, and oil collapsed -52%. Financials outperformed cyclicals (Energy -18%, Industrials +9%) via domestic credit expansion and rate-hike optionality, but lagged the defensive leaders. The energy crash pressured commodity-linked loan books and capped relative upside, even as the absolute gain of 23.2% beat SPY's 18.5%.","body_zh":"2014年1月至2015年8月，美国金融板块涨23.2%，受益于后危机信贷周期扩张与贷款增速提升，市场提前定价2015年12月首次加息带来净息差扩大预期。但ctx数据显示彼时为放缓/通缩恐慌格局：医疗+40%、公用事业+25%领涨，美元大涨20%，美债大涨25.6%（收益率实际下行），油价暴跌52%。金融板块凭借国内信贷扩张和加息预期博弈跑赢周期板块（能源-18%、工业+9%），但整体逊于防御龙头。油价崩溃压制了大宗商品贷款账簿，限制了相对收益空间，尽管绝对涨幅23.2%仍超过标普500的18.5%。","drivers":["Fed rate-hike anticipation Dec 2015","post-GFC credit expansion loan growth","oil -52% suppresses energy-credit peers","DXY +20% safe-haven dollar bid","domestic NIM expansion expectation"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2015年12月加息预期","后危机信贷周期扩张","油价-52%压低能源信贷同类板块","美元+20%避险需求","国内净息差扩大预期"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Pre-Hike Credit Cycle Lift, Dollar Surge","title_zh":"加息预期驱动信贷周期，美元强势","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:trough:2014-01"},"2015-08-10":{"body":"Financials dropped 20.8% from August 2015 to February 2016 in a sharp risk-off rotation. On August 11 2015 the PBoC devalued the yuan by 1.86%, triggering a global equity plunge; on August 24 world markets cratered with oil hitting six-year lows. VIX spiked from 12 to 28, defensives led relatively (Utilities +5.4%, Staples -0.6%) while cyclicals were crushed (Energy -20.8%, Financials -21.9%). Financials were particularly hit by surging credit risk on energy-sector loans as oil fell toward $26/barrel, HYG-LQD credit spread widening of -11.1%, and fears that a China hard-landing would impair bank balance sheets. TLT rose +10%, confirming a flight-to-safety rotation where even owning Treasuries beat holding bank stocks.","body_zh":"2015年8月至2016年2月，金融板块暴跌20.8%，经历剧烈风险规避轮动。2015年8月11日中国央行下调人民币中间价1.86%，引发全球股市恐慌；8月24日油价跌至六年低点，全球市场崩跌。VIX从12飙升至28，防御板块相对抗跌（公用事业+5.4%），周期板块重挫（能源-20.8%，金融-21.9%）。金融板块因能源贷款信用风险骤升、高收益信用利差大幅走阔（HYG-LQD差-11.1%）以及对中国经济硬着陆冲击银行资产负债表的担忧而承压尤甚。美债大涨10%，印证全面避险，持国债亦优于持银行股。","drivers":["PBoC yuan devaluation Aug 11 2015","China growth hard-landing scare","oil to $26/bbl energy credit risk","HY credit spread blow-out -11.1%","VIX 12 to 28 risk-off"],"drivers_zh":["中国央行2015年8月贬值人民币","中国经济硬着陆恐慌","油价跌至26美元引发能源信贷风险","高收益信用利差骤扩-11.1%","VIX从12升至28风险规避"],"prev_key":"2015-08-10","prev_key_chain":["2015-08-10"],"status":"exact","title":"China Shock and Oil Crash Crush Financials","title_zh":"中国冲击+油价崩溃重创金融板块","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:peak:2015-08"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"From February 2016 to September 2018, financials delivered a remarkable 102% gain in a broad reflation supercycle. The leg began with oil stabilizing above $26/barrel after China stimulus and OPEC production-cut chatter, relieving energy-credit fears. The Trump election in November 2016 was the catalytic accelerant: markets priced immediate bank deregulation (Dodd-Frank rollback) and then the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (signed December 2017, cutting corporate tax from 35% to 21%, delivering an estimated $29B in extra annual bank profit). The May 2018 Economic Growth Regulatory Relief and Consumer Protection Act further loosened bank capital rules. The quad shifted firmly to reflation/growth-up: cyclicals +76% vs defensives +34%, oil +170%, VIX from 28 to 12, TLT -6.6%, and HYG outperformed LQD by +21%. Financials ranked second of all sectors at +89.5% behind only Tech +102%.","body_zh":"2016年2月至2018年9月，金融板块累计大涨102%，走出一波反通胀超级周期行情。行情始于油价在26美元/桶附近企稳（中国刺激+欧佩克减产预期），能源贷款信用恐慌消散。2016年11月特朗普当选是最关键的催化剂：市场立即定价银行监管放松（多德-弗兰克法改革），随后2017年12月《减税与就业法案》签署（企业税率从35%降至21%，银行业额外获益约290亿美元），2018年5月《经济增长、监管救济和消费者保护法》进一步松绑资本要求。整体格局切换为反通胀/增长上行：周期+76% vs 防御+34%，油价+170%，VIX从28降至12，金融板块以+89.5%位居全市场第二，仅次于科技+102%。","drivers":["Trump election Nov 2016 deregulation","Tax Cuts and Jobs Act Dec 2017","oil recovery from $26/bbl","EGRRCPA May 2018 capital relief","rising yields NIM expansion"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普2016年11月当选及金融监管放松","2017年12月减税法案","油价从26美元反弹","2018年5月资本要求松绑法案","利率上行拓宽净息差"],"prev_key":"2016-02-11","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump Reflation and Deregulation Supercycle","title_zh":"特朗普反通胀+监管放松超级周期","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:trough:2016-02"},"2018-09-20":{"body":"From September 20 to December 24 2018, financials fell 21.3% in a rapid risk-off de-rating. The Fed raised rates four times in 2018 with the December 19 hike to 2.25-2.50%, and Chairman Powell signaled balance-sheet reduction remained on 'autopilot,' igniting recession fears. VIX spiked from 12 to 36. The ctx confirms a flight-to-safety rotation: defensives only -8.7% while cyclicals -23.1%, with Tech -22.7%, Industrials -23.6%, Energy -27.2%. Financials (-21.3%) tracked cyclicals as yield-curve inversion fears (TLT +4.5% even as the Fed hiked) raised bank NIM concerns, and trade-war escalation (DXY +2.8%) threatened global loan books. HYG underperformed LQD by -4.9%, confirming credit stress.","body_zh":"2018年9月20日至12月24日，金融板块暴跌21.3%，出现快速风险规避杀估值行情。美联储2018年四次加息，12月19日将联邦基金利率升至2.25-2.50%，鲍威尔会后措辞显示缩表将继续'自动驾驶'，引爆衰退担忧。VIX从12飙升至36。ctx数据印证典型避险轮动：防御板块仅-8.7%，周期板块-23.1%，科技-22.7%，工业-23.6%，能源-27.2%。金融板块（-21.3%）紧跟周期股下跌，收益率曲线倒挂预期（TLT+4.5%）压制银行净息差预期，贸易战升级（美元+2.8%）加剧全球贷款账簿风险。高收益信用较投资级跑输4.9%，信用紧张信号明确。","drivers":["Fed Dec 19 2018 hike autopilot language","yield curve inversion NIM fear","trade war escalation DXY +2.8%","VIX 12 to 36 recession fear","HY credit spread widening -4.9%"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2018年12月19日加息+强硬措辞","收益率曲线倒挂压制净息差","贸易战升级美元+2.8%","VIX从12升至36衰退恐慌","高收益信用利差扩大-4.9%"],"prev_key":"2018-09-20","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell Rate-Shock Into Recession Fear","title_zh":"鲍威尔加息冲击引爆衰退恐慌","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"Financials gained 56.1% from December 24 2018 to February 19 2020 as the Fed executed a complete pivot. On January 4 2019 Powell signaled the end of autopilot tightening, followed by three 25bp rate cuts in July, September, and October 2019 as a 'mid-cycle adjustment.' The US-China Phase One trade deal signed January 2020 removed a key tail risk. Semis surged +91%, Tech +81%, and the broad quad was reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +42% vs defensives +36%), but TLT +23% and DXY +3.2% reflect residual caution. Financials (+56%) tracked the broad risk-on recovery but lagged Tech due to narrow breadth (RSP -6.9% vs SPY) and the yield curve only re-steepening late in the period after the three 2019 rate cuts.","body_zh":"2018年12月24日至2020年2月19日，金融板块大涨56.1%，受益于美联储政策大转向：2019年1月4日鲍威尔宣布结束缩表'自动驾驶'，随后于7月、9月、10月三次降息25个基点（'周期中段调整'）。中美第一阶段贸易协议（2020年1月签署）消除重大尾部风险。半导体+91%，科技+81%，整体格局为反通胀/增长上行（周期+42% vs 防御+36%），但TLT+23%、美元+3.2%显示仍存顾虑。金融板块（+56%）跟随市场回暖，但因市场宽度偏窄（RSP较SPY落后6.9%）及收益率曲线迟至后期才真正陡化，整体跑输科技板块。","drivers":["Fed Jan 4 2019 pivot end autopilot","three 2019 rate cuts mid-cycle adjustment","US-China Phase One deal Jan 2020","VIX 36 to 14 risk-on recovery","yield curve late re-steepening"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月4日政策转向","2019年三次降息周期中段调整","中美第一阶段协议2020年1月","VIX从36降至14风险偏好回升","收益率曲线后期再度陡化"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed Pivot, Trade Truce, Pre-COVID Rally","title_zh":"美联储转向+贸易休战，COVID前大涨","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-19":{"body":"Financials crashed 43.3% from February 19 to March 23 2020, the worst single-leg drop in this series, as COVID-19 triggered a systemic panic. VIX exploded from 14 to 62. Research confirms the bank-specific mechanism: corporations drew down revolving credit lines at unprecedented rates as cash flows collapsed, creating acute liquidity stress precisely when mark-to-market losses mounted across bank balance sheets. Financials -42.8% ranked second-worst after Energy -56.1%, with credit HYG-LQD blowing out -9.6%. Defensives led relatively (Staples -24%, Health -28%) while TLT +14% confirmed flight-to-safety. The equal-weight basket bore disproportionate exposure to regional banks and diversified financials with heavy credit-line commitments.","body_zh":"2020年2月19日至3月23日，金融板块暴跌43.3%，为该序列最大单段跌幅，COVID-19引发系统性恐慌。VIX从14飙升至62。学术研究证实了银行股特有的压力机制：企业在现金流骤降之际大规模提取信贷额度，触发银行流动性危机，同时账面亏损激增。金融板块（-42.8%）跌幅仅次于能源（-56.1%），高收益信用相较投资级跑输-9.6%。防御类板块相对抗跌（消费品-24%、医疗-28%），美债+14%印证避险属性。等权篮子对地区性银行及多元化金融机构敞口较大，信贷额度压力尤为突出。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic WHO March 2020","corporate credit-line mass drawdown","cash flow collapse systemic credit stress","VIX 14 to 62 systemic panic","energy credit book losses"],"drivers_zh":["COVID-19疫情2020年3月","企业大规模提取信贷额度","现金流崩溃引发系统性信用压力","VIX从14飙升至62系统性恐慌","能源信贷账簿亏损"],"prev_key":"2020-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID Pandemic Crash, Credit Line Surge","title_zh":"COVID疫情冲击，信贷额度提取危机","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From March 23 2020 to October 25 2021, financials surged 153.6% in the single largest rally of the 15-year series. The Fed cut rates to zero and launched $120B/month QE on March 23, removing the liquidity panic floor. Vaccine announcements from Pfizer/BioNTech on November 9 2020 and Moderna on November 16 2020 ignited a ferocious value/cyclical rotation. The yield curve steepened sharply through early 2021: TLT fell -11.3%, the 10y Treasury rose from 0.54% in August 2020 to 1.74% by March 2021, dramatically expanding bank NIM expectations. The quad was decisively reflation/growth-up: cyclicals +135% vs defensives +63%, Energy +169%, oil +259%, copper-gold +100%, VIX 62 to 15, DXY -8.5%, and breadth exploded (RSP +18% vs SPY). Financials (+153.6%) ranked second behind only Energy +169%.","body_zh":"2020年3月23日至2021年10月25日，金融板块狂涨153.6%，为15年序列中最大单段反弹。美联储于3月23日将利率降至零并启动每月1200亿美元QE，消除流动性恐慌底部。辉瑞/BioNTech（11月9日）和Moderna（11月16日）疫苗接连获批，引爆价值/周期股大轮动。2021年初收益率曲线大幅陡化：TLT跌-11.3%，10年期美债收益率从2020年8月0.54%升至2021年3月1.74%，银行净息差预期大幅扩张。整体格局决定性切换为反通胀/增长上行：周期+135% vs 防御+63%，能源+169%，油价+259%，铜金比+100%，VIX从62降至15，美元-8.5%，市场宽度爆发（RSP跑赢SPY 18%）。金融板块（+153.6%）全行业排名第二，仅次于能源+169%。","drivers":["Fed zero-rate QE March 23 2020","Pfizer Moderna vaccine Nov 2020","yield curve steepening 10y to 1.74%","value/cyclical reflation rotation","DXY -8.5% dollar weakness"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2020年3月23日零利率+QE","辉瑞/Moderna疫苗2020年11月","10年期收益率升至1.74%曲线陡化","价值/周期股反通胀大轮动","美元走弱-8.5%"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Vaccine Rally and Yield Curve Steepening Boom","title_zh":"疫苗行情+收益率曲线陡化爆发","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:trough:2020-03"},"2021-10-25":{"body":"From October 2021 to June 2022, financials fell 24.8% in a stagflation-ish selloff driven by the most aggressive Fed tightening cycle in 40 years. The Fed announced taper on November 3 2021 and hiked rates seven times in 2022 starting in March (25bp), accelerating to four consecutive 75bp hikes from June through November. CPI hit 9.1% in June 2022 and the Russia-Ukraine invasion in February 2022 drove oil +40%. The paradox for financials: while higher rates should boost NIM, the abruptness of the shock (TLT -21.5%, fastest bond bear since 1994) raised HTM loss fears, inverted the yield curve by June 2022, and recession fears overwhelmed NIM optimism. Energy +35% was the lone GICS winner, while defensives -3.7% beat cyclicals -11.9%, with Financials -23.3% ranking among the worst alongside Discretionary -32% and Comm -34%. DXY surged +10.5%.","body_zh":"2021年10月至2022年6月，金融板块下跌24.8%，经历了40年来最激进的美联储紧缩周期引发的滞胀式下跌。美联储于2021年11月3日宣布缩减购债，并从2022年3月开始加息，随后连续四次加息75个基点（6月至11月）。2022年6月CPI达9.1%，2022年2月俄乌战争推动油价+40%。金融板块面临一个悖论：加息理论上应扩大净息差，但加息节奏之猛烈（TLT-21.5%，1994年以来债市最大跌幅）引发持有至到期账面亏损担忧，2022年6月收益率曲线倒挂，衰退恐惧压倒净息差乐观情绪。能源（+35%）是唯一上涨GICS板块，防御板块（-3.7%）跑赢周期板块（-11.9%），金融（-23.3%）与非必需消费（-32%）和通信（-34%）并列最差。美元指数大涨10.5%。","drivers":["Fed taper Nov 2021 then 7 hikes 2022","CPI 9.1% June 2022 inflation shock","yield curve inversion HTM loss fears","Russia-Ukraine oil +40% Feb 2022","DXY +10.5% dollar surge"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2021年11月缩债+2022年7次加息","通胀达9.1%震撼市场","收益率曲线倒挂持有至到期亏损担忧","俄乌战争2022年2月油价+40%","美元指数+10.5%大幅升值"],"prev_key":"2021-10-25","prev_key_chain":["2021-10-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed Taper Shock and Aggressive Hike Cycle","title_zh":"美联储缩债冲击+史上最激进加息周期","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:peak:2021-10"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"Financials bounced 20.3% from June 16 to August 16 2022 in a classic bear-market rally fueled by peak-inflation hopes and Fed-pivot speculation. The June 2022 CPI print of 9.1% triggered widespread speculation it marked the cycle peak, and markets began pricing aggressive rate cuts in 2023. The quad read goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation: Tech +23%, Discretionary +29% led, VIX fell from 33 to 20, and growth beat value by 8.8%. Financials gained 20.3% in line with the broad bounce; credit conditions briefly eased (HYG +2.5% vs LQD). However, oil -26% and DXY rising +2.8% despite the equity bounce confirmed this was a positioning-driven relief trade, not a genuine fundamental re-rating. The rally was fully reversed within six weeks by the Jackson Hole speech.","body_zh":"2022年6月16日至8月16日，金融板块反弹20.3%，是典型的熊市反弹，由通胀见顶预期和美联储政策转向幻想驱动。2022年6月CPI数据（9.1%）引发广泛猜测已到达本轮周期顶点，市场开始定价2023年大幅降息。整体格局切换为低通胀/增长上行：科技+23%、非必需消费+29%领涨，VIX从33降至20，成长股跑赢价值股8.8%。金融板块涨20.3%跟随大盘反弹，信用条件短暂缓解（高收益较投资级+2.5%）。然而油价-26%、美元在股票反弹背景下仍上涨2.8%，表明此次反弹属仓位驱动的技术性修复，而非基本面重新定价。该反弹在六周内被杰克逊霍尔讲话完全回撤。","drivers":["June 2022 CPI 9.1% peak inflation speculation","Fed pivot 2023 rate-cut pricing","bear market short covering","VIX 33 to 20 compression","credit brief easing HYG outperform"],"drivers_zh":["2022年6月CPI 9.1%通胀见顶投机","市场定价2023年美联储转向降息","空头回补","VIX从33降至20","信用短暂宽松高收益跑赢"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Bear Bounce on Peak Inflation Hope","title_zh":"通胀见顶预期驱动熊市反弹","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"Financials fell 14.8% from August 16 to September 30 2022, triggered by Fed Chair Powell's blunt Jackson Hole speech on August 26 2022, where he warned of 'pain' and committed to fighting inflation regardless of economic consequences, squashing pivot hopes. The 10-year Treasury yield surged past 4% for the first time since 2008 (TLT -11.4%), and the DXY rose +5.3% to multi-decade highs. The paradox intensified: rapidly rising rates deepened HTM losses at banks and further inverted the curve, while Real Estate -20%, Comm -20%, and Tech -21% led the selloff. Financials -14.8% tracked the broad cyclical selloff; the deepening 2s10s inversion signaled elevated recession risk, directly threatening bank credit quality and loan demand.","body_zh":"2022年8月16日至9月30日，金融板块下跌14.8%，导火索是美联储主席鲍威尔2022年8月26日在杰克逊霍尔年会上的强硬讲话，他警告将承受'痛苦'并承诺不惜代价抑制通胀，打破市场的政策转向幻想。10年期美债收益率突破4%（TLT-11.4%，为2008年以来首次），美元指数升至多年高位（+5.3%）。悖论进一步加剧：利率快速上升加深银行持有至到期账面亏损，收益率曲线倒挂更趋严重。房地产-20%、通信-20%、科技-21%领跌。金融板块（-14.8%）跟随周期股下跌，2s10s深度倒挂预示衰退风险上升，直接威胁银行信贷质量和贷款需求。","drivers":["Powell Jackson Hole Aug 26 2022 hawkish","10y yield above 4% first since 2008","HTM bank loss crystallization risk","DXY +5.3% multi-decade high","2s10s inversion recession signal deepens"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔强硬讲话","10年期收益率突破4%（2008年来首次）","银行持有至到期账面亏损实现风险","美元升至数十年高位+5.3%","2s10s深度倒挂衰退信号加剧"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole Shock, Dollar Surge, Yields Spike","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔讲话冲击，美元飙升收益率大涨","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:peak:2022-08"},"2022-09-30":{"body":"From September 30 2022 to February 7 2023, financials rallied 24.0% as the dollar peaked (DXY -7.8%), China reopened after its zero-COVID policy reversal in December 2022, and markets began pricing a softer Fed landing path. The quad was reflation/growth-up with broad participation: cyclicals +20.5% vs defensives +8.6%, RSP beat SPY by +4.2%, Industrials +25%, Energy +24%, Materials +24% all led. Financials +24% matched the cyclical leaders as the value-cyclical rotation played out, with VIX falling 32 to 19 and TLT +3.8% as peak-rate expectations consolidated. The dollar reversal was decisive: a weaker DXY typically signals global risk appetite recovery, benefiting financials via improved EM credit quality and reduced dollar funding stress at major banks.","body_zh":"2022年9月30日至2023年2月7日，金融板块上涨24.0%，美元见顶（美元指数-7.8%），中国于2022年12月结束清零政策重启经济，市场开始定价美联储更温和的收紧路径。格局切换为反通胀/增长上行，且市场宽度显著扩散：周期板块+20.5% vs 防御板块+8.6%，RSP跑赢SPY 4.2%，工业+25%、能源+24%、材料+24%领涨。金融板块（+24%）与周期股同步上涨，价值/周期轮动逻辑清晰；VIX从32降至19，美债亦上涨3.8%印证加息见顶预期形成共识。美元的回落至关重要：弱美元通常预示全球风险偏好回暖，通过改善新兴市场信贷质量和缓解主要银行美元融资压力，间接利好金融板块。","drivers":["dollar peak DXY -7.8% reversal","China zero-COVID exit Dec 2022","Fed peak rate expectation forming","broad cyclical value rotation","VIX 32 to 19 risk compression"],"drivers_zh":["美元触顶美元指数-7.8%反转","中国2022年12月结束清零开放","美联储加息见顶预期形成共识","价值/周期板块广泛轮动","VIX从32降至19"],"prev_key":"2022-09-30","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Dollar Peak, Cyclical Rotation, Soft Landing Bet","title_zh":"美元见顶，周期轮动，软着陆押注","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:trough:2022-09"},"2023-02-07":{"body":"Financials fell 16.3% from February 7 to May 4 2023 as the SVB failure on March 10 2023 unleashed a regional bank crisis. SVB had accumulated heavy mark-to-market losses on long-duration bonds as rates rose from 0.25% to 4.75%; a failed capital raise triggered a deposit run that collapsed the $212B institution in 48 hours, the second-largest US bank failure in history. Signature Bank and First Republic Bank also failed within weeks. The ctx grounding shows a targeted defensive rotation: Staples +5%, Tech +3%, Utilities +1% led while Energy -11%, Real Estate -8%, and Financials -14.3% lagged. Narrow breadth (RSP -5.8% vs SPY) confirms this was a sector-specific contagion, not a broad macro selloff. VIX only rose marginally (19 to 20), confirming a targeted solvency scare.","body_zh":"2023年2月7日至5月4日，金融板块下跌16.3%，导火索是2023年3月10日硅谷银行（SVB）倒闭引发的区域性银行危机。SVB因利率从0.25%快速升至4.75%积累了大量长久期债券账面亏损，一次失败的增资引发存款挤兑，这家2120亿美元的银行在48小时内倒闭，成为美国历史第二大银行倒闭案。随后几周，Signature Bank和第一共和银行相继倒闭。ctx数据显示典型防御轮动：消费品+5%、科技+3%、公用事业+1%领涨，而能源-11%、房地产-8%、金融-14.3%落后。市场宽度偏窄（RSP较SPY落后5.8%），表明这不是宏观面整体下行，而是板块特定传染效应。VIX仅从19小幅升至20，印证属于定向金融板块偿付危机。","drivers":["SVB collapse March 10 2023 bank run","HTM bond loss crystallization","Signature First Republic bank failures","deposit run contagion regional banks","sector-specific selloff narrow breadth"],"drivers_zh":["硅谷银行2023年3月10日倒闭挤兑","持有至到期账面亏损实现","Signature银行及第一共和银行倒闭","区域银行存款挤兑传染","板块特定下跌市场宽度偏窄"],"prev_key":"2023-02-07","prev_key_chain":["2023-02-07"],"status":"exact","title":"SVB Collapse Triggers Regional Bank Crisis","title_zh":"硅谷银行倒闭引发区域银行危机","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:peak:2023-02"},"2023-05-04":{"body":"From May 4 2023 to November 27 2024, financials surged 85.1% (the financial sector itself ranked second among GICS sectors at +66.6%) as a goldilocks/disinflation macro backdrop combined with powerful AI-economy optimism and financial deregulation expectations. The Fed held rates at 5.25-5.50% from July 2023 then cut 100bp through Q4 2024 (September, November, December), compressing short-end funding costs while long rates stayed elevated (TLT -6.4%), steepening the curve and expanding the NIM outlook. Semis surged +97%, Tech +59%, pulling broad risk appetite higher (VIX 20 to 14). The Trump election win on November 5 2024 sparked a post-election financials rally as markets priced deregulation, an M&A wave, and capital return unlocking. Breadth was notably narrow (RSP -14.6% vs SPY), underscoring how mega-bank cap-weights drove the equal-weight basket's returns.","body_zh":"2023年5月4日至2024年11月27日，金融板块大涨85.1%（金融GICS板块本身+66.6%，全市场排名第二），受益于低通胀/增长向上的宏观格局、强劲的AI经济乐观情绪以及金融放松监管预期。美联储将联邦基金利率维持在5.25-5.50%（2023年7月起），随后于2024年四季度三次降息共100个基点（9月、11月、12月），压低短端融资成本，而长端利率仍高企（TLT-6.4%），实际上实现曲线重新陡化并改善净息差前景。半导体+97%，科技+59%，大幅提振整体风险偏好（VIX从20降至14）。2024年11月5日特朗普再度当选后金融板块大涨，市场定价监管放松、并购潮和资本回报解锁。市场宽度偏窄（RSP较SPY落后14.6%），折射出大型银行在等权篮子中占据主导地位。","drivers":["Fed 100bp cuts Q4 2024 NIM expansion","goldilocks disinflation soft landing 2024","Trump election Nov 2024 deregulation bet","AI economy semis +97% broad risk-on","M&A capital return deregulation expectations"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2024年四季度降息100bp扩大净息差","2024年低通胀软着陆黄金格局","特朗普2024年11月当选监管放松预期","AI经济半导体+97%提振风险偏好","并购潮+资本回报放开预期"],"prev_key":"2023-05-04","prev_key_chain":["2023-05-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Goldilocks Soft Landing, AI Economy, Deregulation","title_zh":"黄金软着陆+AI经济+监管放松","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:trough:2023-05"},"2024-11-27":{"body":"Financials fell 18.7% from November 27 2024 to April 8 2025 as Trump's escalating tariff agenda triggered a growth scare. Trump announced a minimum 10% global tariff and higher reciprocal tariffs on April 2 2025 (Liberation Day), causing the S&P 500 to fall roughly 20% and VIX to spike from 14 to 52. JP Morgan raised recession probability to 60%, Goldman Sachs to 45%. The ctx confirms a defensive rotation: Staples -6.6%, Health -8.7%, Utilities -10.5% led vs Discretionary -19.5%, Materials -20.5%, Tech -22.1%. Financials -18.7% tracked cyclicals, hurt by recession fears for loan books, credit spread widening (HYG -0.5% vs LQD), and mortgage origination collapse. Notably TLT also fell -3.3% as DXY weakened -2.9%, suggesting foreign investors sold both US equities and Treasuries simultaneously.","body_zh":"2024年11月27日至2025年4月8日，金融板块下跌18.7%，特朗普激进的关税政策引发增长恐慌。2025年4月2日'解放日'，特朗普宣布对全球征收至少10%关税及更高的对等关税，标普500跌约20%，VIX从14飙升至52。摩根大通将衰退概率提升至60%，高盛提升至45%。ctx数据印证避险轮动：消费品-6.6%、医疗-8.7%、公用事业-10.5%相对抗跌，而非必需消费-19.5%、材料-20.5%、科技-22.1%领跌。金融板块（-18.7%）与周期股同步受挫，衰退风险对贷款账簿的冲击、信用利差扩大及按揭发放量骤降均构成压力。值得注意的是美债（TLT-3.3%）和美元（-2.9%）同时下跌，暗示外国投资者在抛售美股同时亦抛售美债。","drivers":["Liberation Day tariffs Apr 2 2025 global","VIX 14 to 52 cyclical de-rating","recession probability JP Morgan 60%","credit spread widening loan book fears","mortgage origination collapse"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月2日解放日全球关税","VIX从14升至52周期股估值杀跌","摩根大通衰退概率60%","信用利差扩大贷款账簿受损担忧","按揭发放量骤降"],"prev_key":"2024-11-27","prev_key_chain":["2024-11-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff Shock Recession Fear Selloff","title_zh":"关税冲击引发衰退恐慌大跌","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:peak:2024-11"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"From April 8 2025 to January 6 2026, financials rallied 34.9% as the tariff shock resolved and a tech-led reflation rally took hold. US-China tariff negotiations led to a temporary truce and significant tariff reductions, while court rulings voided certain tariffs, easing worst-case scenarios for bank credit books. The quad was goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation: Tech surged +64%, semis +116%, Industrials +41%, Discretionary +38%, with VIX collapsing from 52 to 15 and DXY -4.3%. Financials +34.9% lagged the cyclical leaders but beat defensives (Staples +3.7%, Real Estate +12.8%), supported by deregulation momentum, strong bank earnings across 2025 (Big Six averaged +42% stock return in 2025 per web search), and capital markets activity recovery. Narrow breadth (RSP -10.1% vs SPY) confirmed megacap tech dominated, limiting equal-weight financials' relative upside.","body_zh":"2025年4月8日至2026年1月6日，金融板块反弹34.9%，关税冲击趋于缓和，科技引领的反通胀复苏行情展开。中美关税谈判达成临时停战并大幅削减关税，法院亦否决了部分关税，银行信贷账簿最坏情景得以消除。整体格局为低通胀/增长上行（黄金迪尔利）：科技+64%，半导体+116%，工业+41%，VIX从52降至15，美元-4.3%。金融板块（+34.9%）跑输周期领涨板块，但跑赢防御板块（消费品+3.7%，房地产+12.8%），受益于监管松绑动能、2025年大型银行强劲盈利（六大行全年平均+42%）以及关税波动推动的资本市场活动复苏。市场宽度偏窄（RSP较SPY落后10.1%），反映科技巨头主导行情，限制了等权金融板块的相对弹性。","drivers":["US-China tariff truce reductions 2025","VIX 52 to 15 risk normalization","strong bank earnings deregulation momentum","capital markets M&A activity recovery","DXY -4.3% dollar weakness tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["中美关税停战及削减2025年","VIX从52降至15风险正常化","银行盈利强劲监管放松动能","资本市场并购活动复苏","美元走弱-4.3%尾风"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff Truce, Tech-Led Recovery, Deregulation","title_zh":"关税停战+科技引领复苏+监管放松","turn_id":"us_sector_financials:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Financials (Equal-Weight) is in an Expansion/Trending phase but sitting near mid-cycle (pos 48), having peaked in January 2026 after a 34.9% post-tariff-trough rally. The basket has pulled back to a lagging position, ranking only 24th across tracked series, with year-to-date returns of roughly -2.7% versus SPY +6.3%, making it the worst GICS sector performer in 2026 year-to-date. The reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +11.2%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%) is broadly constructive for risk, but net interest margin uncertainty from a flat Fed, contracting mortgage originations, and aggressive capital rotation into AI-beneficiary megacap tech are keeping the equal-weight basket in consolidation. Broadening (RSP +2.9% vs SPY) is mildly supportive, but value-versus-growth remains deeply negative (-15.2%) and the DXY +3.4% creates an additional headwind for multinationals within the basket.","now_zh":"金融（等权）当前处于扩张/趋势运行阶段，但周期位置约在中值（pos 48），自2025年4月关税冲击低点至2026年1月高点累计反弹34.9%后，进入浅幅回调。该板块今年以来回报约-2.7%，在全部GICS板块中垫底，而标普500涨+6.3%。当前反通胀/增长上行格局（周期板块+11%、油价+19%、铜金比+18%）理论上有利于金融，但净息差压力、按揭发放量收缩以及资金持续流向AI受益型科技巨头，使得等权篮子承压。等权vs市值权重+2.9%小幅利好，但成长跑赢价值达-15.2%，美元指数+3.4%亦对跨国银行构成额外阻力，整体符合周期中段整固特征。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"credit.spread_regime.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"credit.spread_regime.v1","arch_state":"fail","arch_fired_on":"2026-07-05","revision_note":null}},"b-us_sector_health":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"The Affordable Care Act's coverage expansion (effective January 2014) added tens of millions of newly insured Americans, driving managed-care enrollment, hospital volumes, and pharmaceutical demand. Biotech simultaneously entered a supercycle powered by record FDA drug approvals and a zero-rate funding environment, with IBB gaining roughly 30% in 2014. The macro quad was slowdown/deflation-scare throughout (oil -52%, TLT +24%, dollar +21%), so defensives outperformed cyclicals by 21pp -- healthcare's 49.6% gain blended genuine ACA-driven sector alpha with a defensive rotation tailwind as energy and industrials collapsed. Healthcare led all sectors over this 19-month window.","body_zh":"《平价医疗法案》（ACA）覆盖范围扩张（自2014年1月生效），数千万新参保美国人推动了管理式医疗入会人数、医院就诊量及药品需求的显著增长。与此同时，生物科技在FDA新药审批创纪录及零利率融资环境的双重驱动下进入超级周期，IBB生物科技ETF在2014年涨幅约30%。整个阶段宏观象限为经济放缓/通缩恐慌（油价-52%，TLT+24%，美元+21%），防御性板块跑赢周期性板块21个百分点——医疗保健49.6%的涨幅融合了ACA驱动的行业阿尔法与防御轮动尾风，在长达19个月的窗口期内引领所有板块。","drivers":["ACA coverage expansion","biotech FDA-approval supercycle","defensive rotation vs energy/cyclical collapse","zero-rate biotech funding","deflation-scare quad"],"drivers_zh":["ACA覆盖范围扩张","生物科技FDA审批超级周期","防御轮动vs能源/周期崩盘","零利率生物科技融资","通缩恐慌象限"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"ACA Expansion Meets Biotech Supercycle","title_zh":"ACA扩张叠加生物科技超级周期","turn_id":"us_sector_health:trough:2014-01"},"2015-08-05":{"body":"The People's Bank of China devalued the yuan by 1.86% on August 11, 2015, triggering a global growth scare and VIX spike from 13 to 28. Healthcare fell 14.8% -- notably worse than the SPY -10% and even worse than Materials -- because a sector-specific political catalyst compounded the macro selloff: on September 21, Hillary Clinton tweeted that drug 'price gouging is outrageous,' sending IBB down 4.5% intraday and igniting a prolonged regulatory-risk repricing across biopharma. Health was the worst-performing sector in the leg despite being defensive, confirming sector-specific de-rating dominated.","body_zh":"2015年8月11日，中国人民银行将人民币汇率下调1.86%，触发全球增长恐慌，VIX从13飙升至28。医疗保健下跌14.8%，不仅差于标普500的-10%，甚至不如材料板块——这是因为一个行业特定的政治催化剂叠加了宏观抛售：9月21日，希拉里·克林顿发推称药品'暴利行为令人发指'，IBB当日盘中跌逾4.5%，引发生物制药板块长期监管风险重新定价。尽管医疗保健属于防御性板块，此轮却是表现最差的板块，证明行业特定的估值收缩主导了走势。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation growth scare","VIX spike risk-off","Clinton drug pricing tweet Sept-21","biopharma regulatory repricing","biotech valuation unwind"],"drivers_zh":["中国人民币贬值引发增长恐慌","VIX飙升风险规避","希拉里9月21日药价推文","生物制药监管风险重新定价","生物科技估值回调"],"prev_key":"2015-08-05","prev_key_chain":["2015-08-05"],"status":"exact","title":"China Shock + Drug-Pricing Political Risk","title_zh":"中国冲击叠加药价政治风险","turn_id":"us_sector_health:peak:2015-08"},"2015-09-28":{"body":"Global markets stabilized as the Fed kept rates on hold through year-end 2015, and the China devaluation shock faded. Healthcare (+14.0%) co-led this recovery alongside Materials and Tech, reflecting a sharp mean-reversion from its oversold post-Clinton-tweet levels. The quad shifted to goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation (oil -15% but VIX compressing 28 to 16, cyclicals roughly matching defensives), and the December Fed hike on December 16 -- the first in nine years -- did not derail the bounce as markets had already priced tightening.","body_zh":"全球市场在美联储将利率维持不变至2015年年底后趋于稳定，中国贬值冲击逐渐消退。医疗保健（+14.0%）与材料和科技共同领涨，反映出在希拉里推文抛售后超卖状态的急速均值回归。宏观象限转向黄金组合/增长上行-去通胀（油价-15%，但VIX从28压缩至16，周期性与防御性板块表现相近），12月16日美联储九年来首次加息亦未打断反弹，因市场此前已充分定价。","drivers":["mean-reversion from oversold biotech","Fed rate hold through year-end","VIX compression","goldilocks quad","China shock fading"],"drivers_zh":["生物科技超卖后均值回归","美联储全年维持利率不变","VIX压缩","黄金组合象限","中国冲击消退"],"prev_key":"2015-09-28","prev_key_chain":["2015-09-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-Shock Rebound, Healthcare Co-Leads","title_zh":"冲击后反弹，医疗保健共同领涨","turn_id":"us_sector_health:trough:2015-09"},"2015-12-29":{"body":"Oil crashed a further 31% by February 2016 as OPEC refused to cut production, triggering a global recession scare. China's circuit breaker failures in January 2016 amplified the risk-off move, sending VIX from 16 to 28 and credit spreads wider (HYG-LQD -6.2%). Defensives far outperformed cyclicals (-4.1% vs -13%), with Utilities the only sector in positive territory. Healthcare fell 14.8% -- underperforming the SPY (-11.8%) despite being classified defensive -- because the ongoing biopharma regulatory overhang (drug pricing, ACA repeal rhetoric) kept sector multiple compression elevated even in risk-off environments.","body_zh":"随着欧佩克拒绝减产，油价进一步下跌31%至2016年2月，引发全球衰退恐慌。2016年1月中国熔断机制多次触发放大了风险规避情绪，VIX从16升至28，信用利差走阔（HYG-LQD -6.2%）。防御性板块显著跑赢周期性板块（-4.1% vs -13%），公用事业为唯一正收益板块。医疗保健下跌14.8%，逊于标普500（-11.8%），尽管其属于防御性板块——原因在于持续的生物制药监管压力（药价争议、废除ACA言论）使板块估值倍数在风险规避环境下仍受压。","drivers":["oil crash OPEC no-cut","China circuit breaker failures Jan-2016","global recession scare","credit spread widening","healthcare biopharma regulatory overhang"],"drivers_zh":["欧佩克拒绝减产导致油价崩盘","2016年1月中国熔断机制触发","全球衰退恐慌","信用利差走阔","生物制药监管压力持续"],"prev_key":"2015-12-29","prev_key_chain":["2015-12-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil Crash + China Redux Sinks All Risk","title_zh":"油价崩盘叠加中国二次冲击打压风险资产","turn_id":"us_sector_health:peak:2015-12"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"Oil bottomed at approximately $26/bbl on February 11, 2016, marking the trough of the global deflation scare. The Shanghai Accord (G20, Feb 2016) implicitly supported a weaker dollar, and the Fed signaled a slower rate path, igniting a 32-month reflation rally. Healthcare gained 97.8% -- participating in the broad risk-on expansion (VIX 28 to 12, cyclicals +75% vs defensives +33%) -- but lagged Tech (+104%) and Financials (+82%). Trump's election victory in November 2016 removed the Medicare-for-All threat and the drug-pricing regulatory overhang, acting as a sector-specific re-rating catalyst that accelerated managed-care and biopharma multiple expansion through 2018.","body_zh":"油价约于2016年2月11日见底（约26美元/桶），全球通缩恐慌触底。上海G20会议（2016年2月）暗示美元走软协议，美联储发出放缓加息信号，引爆长达32个月的再通胀上涨行情。医疗保健涨幅97.8%——参与了广泛的风险偏好扩张（VIX从28降至12，周期性行业+75% vs 防御性行业+33%）——但落后于科技（+104%）和金融（+82%）。2016年11月特朗普当选消除了Medicare全覆盖威胁和药价监管压力，成为行业特定的重新估值催化剂，推动管理式医疗和生物制药的估值倍数持续扩张至2018年。","drivers":["oil price bottom Feb-2016","Shanghai Accord dollar softening","Fed slower rate path","Trump election removes M4A threat","broad reflation risk-on"],"drivers_zh":["2016年2月油价见底","上海G20协议美元走软","美联储放缓加息路径","特朗普当选消除M4A威胁","广泛再通胀风险偏好"],"prev_key":"2016-02-11","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Reflation Cycle + Trump Deregulation Rally","title_zh":"再通胀周期叠加特朗普去监管行情","turn_id":"us_sector_health:trough:2016-02"},"2018-10-01":{"body":"The Fed hiked rates for the fourth time in 2018 on September 26, and Powell's December 19 press conference -- where he described the balance-sheet runoff as 'on autopilot' -- confirmed a hawkish policy overshoot, sending VIX from 12 to 36 and SPY -19%. The selloff was led by cyclicals (Tech -23.5%, Energy -29.2%), with defensives relatively outperforming (-8.3% avg vs cyclicals -22.4%). Healthcare fell 18.8% -- worse than the defensive avg -- as the sector entered the leg near peak valuation and faced emerging Medicare-for-All headlines from the incoming Democratic House majority, which introduced a sector-specific de-rating even within the broad market rout.","body_zh":"美联储于2018年9月26日第四次加息，12月19日鲍威尔新闻发布会将缩表描述为'自动驾驶'，确认政策过度收紧，VIX从12飙升至36，标普500下跌19%。抛售由周期性行业主导（科技-23.5%，能源-29.2%），防御性板块相对抗跌（平均-8.3% vs 周期性-22.4%）。医疗保健下跌18.8%，逊于防御性均值——原因在于板块估值接近峰值，同时民主党在众议院取得多数席位后带来Medicare全覆盖头条风险，在大盘整体下跌中叠加了行业特定的估值收缩。","drivers":["Fed autopilot hawkish shock","VIX spike 12 to 36","cyclical-led broad selloff","Medicare-for-All D-House headwinds","peak valuation entering leg"],"drivers_zh":["美联储'自动驾驶'鹰派冲击","VIX飙升12至36","周期性行业主导的大盘抛售","民主党众议院带来M4A压力","进入阶段时估值处于峰值"],"prev_key":"2018-10-01","prev_key_chain":["2018-10-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed Rate-Shock Broad Selloff, Healthcare Defensive","title_zh":"美联储利率冲击大盘回调，医疗保健相对防御","turn_id":"us_sector_health:peak:2018-10"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"The Fed pivoted to a pause on January 4, 2019 (Powell's 'patient' speech), igniting a 14-month recovery. Healthcare gained 49.6% but was the worst-performing sector in the leg, lagging SPY by 17pp and trailing Tech by 51pp, as the Medicare-for-All narrative intensified through 2019 with Warren and Sanders rising in the Democratic primary, creating a persistent regulatory overhang on managed care and biopharma valuations. The tech-semis surge (+91%) and growth-over-value (+24pp) confirmed a narrow mega-cap tape that further disadvantaged the equal-weight healthcare basket.","body_zh":"美联储于2019年1月4日（鲍威尔'耐心等待'讲话）转向暂停加息，引爆长达14个月的复苏行情。医疗保健涨幅49.6%，但却是该阶段表现最差的板块，落后标普500约17个百分点、落后科技51个百分点——原因在于Medicare全覆盖叙事随沃伦和桑德斯在民主党初选中的崛起而持续强化，对管理式医疗和生物制药估值造成持续监管压力。科技-半导体急涨（+91%）和成长股相对价值股（+24pp）确认了窄幅大盘股主导的行情，进一步不利于等权重医疗保健篮子。","drivers":["Fed pivot to patience Jan-2019","M4A primary narrative overhang","tech-semis led narrow-breadth rally","managed-care multiple suppression","equal-weight lagging mega-cap tape"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月转向耐心等待","初选Medicare全覆盖叙事压制","科技半导体主导窄幅大盘股行情","管理式医疗估值倍数受压","等权重落后大盘股主导行情"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed Pivot Rally, Healthcare Underperforms Tech Cycle","title_zh":"美联储转向引发反弹，医疗保健落后科技周期","turn_id":"us_sector_health:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-19":{"body":"SARS-CoV-2 began spreading globally by late February 2020, and the WHO declared a pandemic on March 11. Oil collapsed 56% (OPEC+ supply war) and VIX surged to 62. Healthcare fell 29% in 33 calendar days -- painful in absolute terms, but the second-best-performing sector after Staples, outperforming SPY by 4.7pp and cyclicals (avg -40%) by 11pp. The relative resilience reflected the classic defensive-income shelter: healthcare spending is non-discretionary and government-backstopped, and the sector avoided the maximum demand-destruction of travel, energy, and financials.","body_zh":"新冠病毒（SARS-CoV-2）于2020年2月下旬开始全球蔓延，世卫组织于3月11日宣布大流行。油价暴跌56%（欧佩克+供应战），VIX飙升至62。医疗保健在33个日历日内下跌29%——绝对损失惨重，但却是继必需消费品之后表现第二好的板块，跑赢标普500约4.7个百分点，领先周期性行业均值（-40%）约11个百分点。相对韧性体现了经典的防御性避险特征：医疗保健支出具有刚性且有政府支撑，避开了旅游、能源和金融等行业的最大需求破坏。","drivers":["COVID pandemic global spread","OPEC+ supply shock oil -56%","VIX surge to 62","flight-to-safety defensive relative bid","non-discretionary spending buffer"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情全球蔓延","欧佩克+供应冲击油价-56%","VIX飙升至62","避险资金防御性相对买盘","非可选消费支出缓冲"],"prev_key":"2020-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID Pandemic Crash, Relative Safety in Healthcare","title_zh":"新冠疫情引发崩盘，医疗保健相对避险","turn_id":"us_sector_health:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The CARES Act ($2.2 trillion, signed March 27, 2020) and subsequent fiscal packages ignited a V-shaped recovery. Healthcare gained 126.2% over 21 months -- a massive absolute return -- but was the worst-performing major sector, trailing SPY by 7pp, Tech by 26pp, and Energy/Materials by 30-57pp. The reflation quad (cyclicals +140% vs defensives +76%, oil +230%, copper-gold +91%) drove flows aggressively into beaten-down cyclicals. Healthcare's 126% gain was real but pure beta: Pfizer/Moderna vaccine success (Emergency Use Authorization December 2020) added near-term revenue but masked the secular underperformance of the equal-weight basket vs a risk-on tape.","body_zh":"《新冠援助、救济和经济安全法案》（CARES，2.2万亿美元，2020年3月27日签署）及后续财政刺激引爆V形复苏。医疗保健在21个月内上涨126.2%，绝对收益巨大，但却是表现最差的主要板块，落后标普500约7个百分点、落后科技26个百分点、落后能源/材料30-57个百分点。再通胀象限（周期性行业+140% vs 防御性行业+76%，油价+230%，铜金比+91%）驱动资金大举流入此前跌幅惨重的周期性行业。医疗保健126%的涨幅是真实的，但主要为纯贝塔驱动；辉瑞/莫德纳疫苗成功（2020年12月获紧急使用授权）贡献了短期收益，但掩盖了等权重篮子在风险偏好行情中的结构性落后。","drivers":["CARES Act fiscal bazooka","V-shape recovery reflation quad","cyclicals massive outperformance","COVID vaccine EUA Dec-2020","zero-rate risk-on flow cyclical rotation"],"drivers_zh":["CARES法案财政火箭炮","V形复苏再通胀象限","周期性行业大幅跑赢","新冠疫苗2020年12月紧急使用授权","零利率风险偏好资金轮动至周期"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Fiscal Bazooka Recovery, Cyclicals Dominate Healthcare","title_zh":"财政火箭炮推动复苏，周期性行业主导医疗保健","turn_id":"us_sector_health:trough:2020-03"},"2021-12-30":{"body":"The Fed pivoted hawkish in November 2021 (taper announcement) and delivered its first 50bp hike in May 2022 -- the largest single hike since 2000 -- as CPI reached 9.1% in June 2022. TLT fell 24%, the DXY surged 8%, and the SPY lost 22.8%. Energy (+42%) was the lone winner; defensives fell less (-10.6% avg) than cyclicals (-12.9% avg). Healthcare lost 20.1% -- in line with the defensive average -- reflecting rate-shock valuation compression across long-duration assets including growth healthcare names (biotech, genomics), while managed care and pharma provided partial buffer against the worst of the selloff.","body_zh":"美联储于2021年11月宣布缩减购债（转鹰），并于2022年5月加息50个基点（22年来最大单次加息幅度），彼时CPI于2022年6月达到9.1%高峰。TLT下跌24%，美元指数上涨8%，标普500下跌22.8%。能源（+42%）是唯一赢家；防御性板块跌幅（平均-10.6%）小于周期性板块（平均-12.9%）。医疗保健下跌20.1%，与防御性均值基本持平，反映出利率冲击对包括成长型医疗保健名称（生物科技、基因组学）在内的长久期资产的估值压缩，而管理式医疗和传统制药则提供了部分缓冲。","drivers":["Fed 50bp hike cycle May-2022","CPI at 9.1% June 2022","TLT -24% duration shock","biotech long-duration valuation compression","stagflation quad growth/defensive both pressured"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2022年5月加息50bp周期","2022年6月CPI达9.1%","TLT -24%久期冲击","生物科技长久期估值压缩","滞涨象限成长/防御均受压"],"prev_key":"2021-12-30","prev_key_chain":["2021-12-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed Tightening Cycle Hits Growth/Healthcare Equally","title_zh":"美联储紧缩周期冲击成长型与医疗保健估值","turn_id":"us_sector_health:peak:2021-12"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"CPI peaked in June 2022 and began decelerating. Markets priced a soft landing from mid-2022 through July 2023, with the S&P 500 gaining 26%. Healthcare gained 25.2% -- roughly matching SPY -- but trailed Tech (+44%) and the broader cyclical-led rally (cyclicals avg +25% vs defensives +12.6%). The equal-weight basket lagged cap-weight by 5.3pp (narrow breadth, mega-cap AI-driven tape). The Inflation Reduction Act (signed August 2022) introduced Medicare drug price negotiation -- a secular headwind for biopharma that suppressed sector-level multiple expansion even as rate fears eased.","body_zh":"CPI于2022年6月见顶并开始回落，市场从2022年中期至2023年7月持续定价软着陆，标普500涨幅约26%。医疗保健涨幅25.2%，与标普500大体持平，但落后于科技（+44%）和整体周期性主导的反弹（周期性均值+25% vs 防御性+12.6%）。等权重篮子落后市值加权5.3个百分点（窄幅大盘股、AI驱动行情）。《通胀削减法案》（2022年8月签署）引入Medicare药品价格谈判机制——对生物制药构成长期利空，抑制了板块估值倍数扩张，尽管利率恐慌已消退。","drivers":["CPI peak June-2022 disinflation","soft-landing narrative repricing","IRA drug price negotiation headwind","tech AI mega-cap led narrow tape","equal-weight structural lag"],"drivers_zh":["2022年6月CPI见顶去通胀","软着陆叙事重新定价","IRA药品价格谈判长期利空","科技AI大盘股主导窄幅行情","等权重结构性落后"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Disinflation Rally, Healthcare Lags Tech Rebound","title_zh":"去通胀行情反弹，医疗保健落后科技复苏","turn_id":"us_sector_health:trough:2022-06"},"2023-07-21":{"body":"The 10-year Treasury yield surged from 3.8% in July 2023 to 5.02% in October 2023 -- a level last seen in 2007 -- as the Fed delivered two more hikes and the fiscal deficit drove Treasury supply higher. TLT fell 16.7% and SPY fell 7.8%. Defensives (-10.5% avg) were hit harder than cyclicals (-7.6%) as their yield-proxy characteristics became liabilities in a rising-rate environment. Healthcare (-16%) was the third-worst sector, lagging because its long-duration biotech names and dividend-paying pharma were treated as rate-sensitive bond substitutes, while Energy (+1.5%) and Comm (-1.5%) outperformed as commodity and advertising revenue held up.","body_zh":"10年期美国国债收益率从2023年7月的3.8%飙升至10月的5.02%（2007年以来最高），美联储再次加息两次，财政赤字推动国债供给大幅增加。TLT下跌16.7%，标普500下跌7.8%。防御性板块（平均-10.5%）受创重于周期性板块（-7.6%），因其类债券属性在利率上行环境中成为负担。医疗保健（-16%）是表现第三差的板块，落后原因在于其长久期生物科技名称和分红型制药股被视为利率敏感的债券替代品，而能源（+1.5%）和通信（-1.5%）则因大宗商品和广告收入维持而相对占优。","drivers":["10Y yield surge to 5.02% Oct-2023","Fed two more hikes","fiscal deficit Treasury supply surge","defensive bond-proxy de-rating","long-duration biotech valuation compression"],"drivers_zh":["10年期国债收益率飙升至5.02%","美联储再次加息两次","财政赤字推高国债供给","防御性类债券属性遭重新定价","长久期生物科技估值压缩"],"prev_key":"2023-07-21","prev_key_chain":["2023-07-21"],"status":"exact","title":"Higher-for-Longer Yield Surge Hits Rate-Sensitive Names","title_zh":"利率'更高更久'冲击，利率敏感型名称受压","turn_id":"us_sector_health:peak:2023-07"},"2023-10-30":{"body":"The Fed held rates at the October 31-November 1, 2023 meeting and signaled a peak in the cycle. The 10-year Treasury yield fell from 5.02% to 3.6% by September 2024 (TLT +25%), and the Fed delivered its first 50bp cut on September 18, 2024. Healthcare gained 30.5% -- a solid return -- but ranked middle of the pack: Real Estate (+44%) and Financials (+43%) led as the biggest beneficiaries of the rate-cut repricing, while Healthcare lagged SPY (+37%) by 7pp because the AI-driven mega-cap tape (semis +71%) and narrow breadth (-4.4pp equal-weight lag) kept capital concentrated away from equal-weight defensive baskets.","body_zh":"美联储在2023年10月31日至11月1日会议上维持利率不变，并暗示本轮周期见顶。10年期国债收益率从5.02%回落至2024年9月的3.6%（TLT +25%），美联储于2024年9月18日进行50个基点的首次降息。医疗保健上涨30.5%，表现尚可，但排名居中：房地产（+44%）和金融（+43%）作为降息重新定价最大受益者领涨，而医疗保健落后标普500（+37%）约7个百分点，原因在于AI驱动的大盘股行情（半导体+71%）和窄幅市场宽度（等权重落后4.4pp）使资金集中远离等权重防御性篮子。","drivers":["Fed rate peak Nov-2023 pivot signal","10Y yield drop to 3.6% by Sep-2024","Fed 50bp cut Sep-2024","rate-sensitive RE and Financials led","AI mega-cap tape narrow breadth"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2023年11月转向信号","10年期国债收益率降至3.6%","美联储2024年9月降息50bp","利率敏感型房地产和金融领涨","AI大盘股主导窄幅行情"],"prev_key":"2023-10-30","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed Pivot Rally, Rate-Sensitive Sectors Lead Healthcare","title_zh":"美联储转向引发反弹，利率敏感型板块领跑医疗保健","turn_id":"us_sector_health:trough:2023-10"},"2024-09-16":{"body":"Healthcare fell 16.2% from September 2024 through the April 2025 trough, driven by two concurrent shocks. First, Trump's broad tariff announcements (April 2, 2025 'Liberation Day' 10%+ tariffs) hit medical device and pharmaceutical supply chains and triggered a broad risk-off move (VIX 17 to 52, SPY -11%). Second, the CMS proposed near-flat 2027 Medicare Advantage rate increases (+0.09%), far below the 4-6% insurers required to break even -- UnitedHealth fell 20% in a single day in January 2026, Humana -22%, CVS -13%. Healthcare led sector losses in the tariff-shock window because the MA margin crisis was a simultaneous sector-specific fundamental blow.","body_zh":"医疗保健从2024年9月下跌至2025年4月低点，累计跌幅16.2%，由两大并发冲击驱动。第一，特朗普的广泛关税公告（2025年4月2日'解放日'10%+关税）冲击了医疗器械和制药供应链，引发大范围风险规避（VIX从17飙升至52，标普500 -11%）。第二，CMS提议2027年Medicare Advantage费率几乎不增长（+0.09%），远低于保险公司盈亏平衡所需的4-6%——联合健康集团（UNH）在2026年1月单日暴跌20%，Humana -22%，CVS -13%。医疗保健在关税冲击窗口内引领板块跌幅，因为Medicare Advantage利润率危机是同步爆发的行业特定基本面打击。","drivers":["April-2025 tariff Liberation Day shock","VIX surge 17 to 52","CMS flat 2027 MA rate proposal","UNH -20% single-day Jan-2026","pharma device supply chain disruption"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月关税'解放日'冲击","VIX从17飙升至52","CMS提议2027年MA费率几乎不增长","联合健康集团单日暴跌20%","制药/医疗器械供应链扰动"],"prev_key":"2024-09-16","prev_key_chain":["2024-09-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff Shock + Medicare Advantage Margin Crisis","title_zh":"关税冲击叠加Medicare Advantage利润率危机","turn_id":"us_sector_health:peak:2024-09"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"The US-China 90-day tariff pause (announced May 12, 2025) and broader trade de-escalation drove a sharp VIX collapse (52 to 18) and a massive risk-on rally led by Tech (+103%), Industrials (+58%), and Energy (+45%). Healthcare gained 27.8% -- a meaningful absolute return -- but was the second-worst-performing sector, trailing SPY by roughly 21pp. The semis supercycle (SMH +241%) and high-beta dominance (+111pp over low-vol) confirmed this is a cyclical-led melt-up where healthcare's defensive positioning, persistent MA margin headwinds, and Medicaid reform uncertainty (DOGE/RFK HHS restructuring) keep relative flows muted even as the absolute trend recovers.","body_zh":"美中90天关税暂停（2025年5月12日宣布）和更广泛的贸易降级驱动VIX急剧回落（52至18），引爆由科技（+103%）、工业（+58%）和能源（+45%）主导的大幅风险偏好反弹。医疗保健上涨27.8%，绝对收益尚可，但却是表现第二差的板块，落后标普500约21个百分点。半导体超级周期（SMH +241%）和高贝塔主导地位（超低波动+111pp）证实这是周期性主导的融断行情——医疗保健的防御性定位、持续的Medicare Advantage利润率压力以及医疗补助改革不确定性（DOGE/RFK HHS重组）使相对资金流入保持低迷，即便绝对趋势已经修复。","drivers":["US-China tariff pause May-2025","VIX collapse 52 to 18","cyclical tech-industrial-energy led melt-up","MA margin persistent headwind","Medicaid reform DOGE uncertainty"],"drivers_zh":["美中2025年5月关税暂停","VIX从52骤降至18","科技工业能源主导的周期性融断行情","Medicare Advantage利润率持续受压","DOGE/医疗补助改革不确定性"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff Pause Recovery, Healthcare Defensive Laggard","title_zh":"关税暂停推动复苏，医疗保健作为防御性板块落后","turn_id":"us_sector_health:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Health Care (EW) is in an Expansion/Trending phase (pos 42.5, BUY signal, above the 200-day MA) but ranks a weak 26th of all series by RS. The current macro quad is reflation/growth-up -- cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9% -- which structurally drags on healthcare's relative performance as capital rotates into Energy (+21.5%) and Industrials (+15.8%). The sector has gained +22.7% since the Apr-2025 trough in absolute terms, but is one of the two biggest laggards in this rally, trailing SPY by roughly 26pp. The setup is defensive-beta participation in a cyclically-led tape: the sector benefits from the VIX retreat (52 to 18) and slight dollar softening (-1.6% DXY), but faces persistent headwinds from Medicare Advantage margin compression, ongoing CMS rate uncertainty under the current administration, and Medicaid reform risk. Semis +241% and high-beta outperformance of +111pp confirm the market is in a risk-on melt-up that historically leaves healthcare behind relative to SPY.","now_zh":"医疗保健（等权）目前处于扩张/趋势阶段（仓位42.5，买入信号，位于200日均线上方），但相对强度排名仅第26位。当前宏观象限为再通胀/增长向上，周期性行业（+11.2%）显著跑赢防御性行业（+6.9%），资金向能源和工业板块轮动，结构性压制医疗保健的相对表现。板块自2025年4月低点以来绝对收益约22.7%，但仍是本轮上涨中落后幅度最大的板块之一，跑输标普500指数约26个百分点。当前状态为防御性贝塔跟涨：受益于VIX回落（52至18）和美元小幅走弱（-1.6%），但Medicare Advantage利润率持续受压、CMS费率政策不确定性及医疗补助改革风险构成持续拖累。半导体（+241%）和高贝塔（+111pp）大幅跑赢，印证市场正处于风险偏好主导的融断行情，历史上此类环境往往令医疗保健相对标普500明显落后。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-us_sector_industrials":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"The US economy entered mid-cycle expansion in 2014, but Industrials (EW) was a laggard at +13.4% versus SPY's +19.3%, as a deflation-scare regime dominated. The DXY surged 16.6% driven by Fed tapering diverging from ECB/BoJ easing, compressing revenue for capital-goods exporters. Crude collapsed 36.7% after OPEC held production at its November 2014 Thanksgiving meeting, gutting energy-linked capex orders. Healthcare (+37.5%) and Utilities (+24.6%) led the index while TLT rose 21.5%, confirming Industrials rode passive index beta rather than sector-specific demand.","body_zh":"2014年美国经济进入中期扩张，但工业板块（等权）以+13.4%落后于标普500的+19.3%，宏观处于通缩恐慌象限。受美联储缩减QE与欧洲央行/日本央行宽松政策分化驱动，美元指数大涨16.6%，压缩资本品出口商营收。2014年11月OPEC感恩节会议维持产量不变，油价暴跌36.7%，能源相关资本开支订单受重创。医疗（+37.5%）和公用事业（+24.6%）领涨，TLT上涨21.5%，证实工业板块仅跟随被动指数贝塔而非受益于板块本身需求。","drivers":["USD +16.6% export headwind","OPEC Nov-2014 oil crash -37%","Fed taper vs ECB/BoJ divergence","deflation-scare quad","defensive rotation"],"drivers_zh":["美元+16.6%出口逆风","欧佩克2014年11月油价暴跌-37%","美联储缩表与欧洲央行/日本央行分化","通缩恐慌象限","防御性轮动"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Mid-cycle melt-up; defensives led, dollar soared","title_zh":"中期牛市惰性上涨；防御板块领涨，美元飙升","turn_id":"us_sector_industrials:trough:2014-01"},"2015-05-18":{"body":"Industrials fell 14.7% in the index, losing 15.5% on an EW basis, as a risk-off cyclical rout triggered by China's August 11, 2015 yuan devaluation (1.9% one-day depreciation) ignited a global growth scare. The selloff was amplified by Greece's July 2015 debt default and the end of Fed QE, with VIX spiking from 13 to 28. Oil plunged 55.3% and copper/gold fell 23.4%, crushing industrial commodity demand expectations. Defensives (Utilities -0.4%, Staples -0.7%) held up while Industrials and Materials were the second and third-worst performers, consistent with a flight-to-safety rotation away from global cyclicals.","body_zh":"工业板块（等权）下跌15.5%，核心触发因素为2015年8月11日中国人民银行突然贬值人民币1.9%，引发全球增长恐慌。希腊2015年7月债务违约及美联储QE结束进一步放大跌幅，VIX从13飙升至28。油价下跌55.3%，铜/金比下跌23.4%，工业大宗商品需求预期遭重创。公用事业（-0.4%）与必需消费品（-0.7%）相对抗跌，而工业和材料板块跌幅居前，符合全球周期股避险出逃的轮动特征。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation Aug-2015","oil -55% commodity demand rout","VIX 13 to 28 risk-off","Greece debt default July-2015","USD +5.2% multinational headwind"],"drivers_zh":["2015年8月中国人民币贬值","油价下跌55%大宗商品需求崩溃","VIX从13飙升至28","2015年7月希腊债务违约","美元+5.2%跨国企业逆风"],"prev_key":"2015-05-18","prev_key_chain":["2015-05-18"],"status":"exact","title":"China devaluation shock; commodities crash, risk-off","title_zh":"中国汇率冲击；大宗商品崩溃，避险情绪主导","turn_id":"us_sector_industrials:peak:2015-05"},"2016-01-20":{"body":"This 32-month, 109% mega-rally was the sector's defining bull leg. It began with the January 2016 commodity trough and oil bottoming around $26/bbl, then accelerated sharply after Trump's November 2016 election win on expectations of infrastructure spend, deregulation, and corporate tax cuts. The 2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (Dec 2017) and a synchronized global PMI expansion into 2018 drove 74.7% gains for Industrials within this window, making it the second-best performer. Dollar weakness (-4.5% DXY), oil +163%, and copper/gold +30.5% confirmed a textbook reflation cycle where Industrials and Financials outperformed alongside Tech.","body_zh":"这轮历时32个月、累涨109%的大牛市是板块的标志性上涨腿。始于2016年1月大宗商品触底（原油约26美元/桶），2016年11月特朗普当选后显著加速，市场预期基础设施支出、去监管与企业减税将至。2017年12月《减税与就业法案》落地及2018年全球PMI同步扩张，推动工业板块在该窗口内累涨74.7%，成为第二强板块。美元走软（DXY -4.5%）、油价+163%、铜/金比+30.5%印证了教科书式再通胀周期，工业与金融板块与科技板块共同领涨。","drivers":["Trump election Nov-2016 infrastructure bet","2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act","synchronized global PMI expansion","oil +163% reflation","USD -4.5% tailwind for exporters"],"drivers_zh":["2016年11月特朗普当选基建预期","2017年《减税与就业法案》","全球PMI同步扩张","油价+163%再通胀","美元-4.5%出口商顺风"],"prev_key":"2016-01-20","prev_key_chain":["2016-01-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump reflation and global PMI upcycle, 109% surge","title_zh":"特朗普再通胀与全球PMI上行周期，累涨109%","turn_id":"us_sector_industrials:trough:2016-01"},"2018-09-18":{"body":"Industrials dropped 23.6% in 99 days as a policy trifecta hit simultaneously: the Fed raised rates four times in 2018 (cumulative +100 bps), trade-war tariffs on $200bn of Chinese goods entered force in September 2018, and oil crashed 39.1% from October into December. VIX spiked 13 to 36 and defensives (Utilities -3.5%, Staples -9.5%) dramatically outperformed, a textbook flight-to-safety rotation. Powell's December 2018 press conference — signaling continued rate hikes despite slowing global growth — was the proximate catalyst for the Christmas Eve trough on December 24, 2018.","body_zh":"工业板块在99天内下跌23.6%，政策三重压力同时袭来：美联储2018年累计加息四次（+100bps）、对华2000亿美元商品加征关税于2018年9月生效、原油从10月至12月暴跌39.1%。VIX从13飙升至36，公用事业（-3.5%）与必需消费品（-9.5%）大幅跑赢，为教科书式避险轮动。鲍威尔2018年12月新闻发布会——在全球增长放缓背景下仍暗示继续加息——成为2018年12月24日平安夜触底的直接催化剂。","drivers":["Fed 4x hikes 2018 rate shock","US-China tariffs Sep-2018 trade war","oil -39% growth scare","VIX 13 to 36","credit spreads widened"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2018年四次加息冲击","2018年9月中美关税贸易战","油价下跌-39%增长恐慌","VIX从13升至36","信用利差走阔"],"prev_key":"2018-09-18","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed rate-shock and trade-war rout, -23.7%","title_zh":"美联储加息冲击与贸易战重挫，-23.7%","turn_id":"us_sector_industrials:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"The 53.9% rally from Christmas Eve 2018 to February 2020 was triggered by the Powell pivot: on January 4, 2019, Powell signaled the Fed would be 'patient,' ending the hiking cycle, and the S&P 500 gained 15%+ in the following 35 trading days. Three Fed rate cuts in H2 2019 and the US-China Phase 1 trade deal signed January 15, 2020 extended the upcycle into early 2020. Industrials lagged the SPY (+46.7%) and mega-cap Tech/Comm leaders in this window, gaining 53.9%, but that still reflected genuine earnings recovery for capital-goods companies as the manufacturing recession of 2019 eased into late-year stabilization.","body_zh":"从2018年平安夜至2020年2月这轮53.9%的反弹，由鲍威尔政策转向引燃：2019年1月4日鲍威尔表示美联储将保持\"耐心\"，结束加息周期，标普500在随后35个交易日内上涨逾15%。2019年下半年三次降息及2020年1月15日中美第一阶段贸易协议签署延续了上行周期。工业板块（+53.9%）落后于标普500（+46.7%）和大型科技/通信领涨板块，但仍反映了资本品企业盈利的真实修复——2019年制造业衰退在年底前趋于稳定。","drivers":["Powell Jan-2019 pivot 'patient'","Fed 3x cuts H2-2019","US-China Phase 1 deal Jan-2020","manufacturing PMI stabilization late-2019","tech/semis mega-cap led tape"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔2019年1月'耐心'表态转向","美联储2019年下半年三次降息","2020年1月中美第一阶段贸易协议","2019年底制造业PMI企稳","科技/半导体大盘股主导行情"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell pivot and Phase-1 trade deal recovery","title_zh":"鲍威尔转向与中美第一阶段贸易协议推动复苏","turn_id":"us_sector_industrials:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-12":{"body":"Industrials fell 42.3% at the index level (EW -40.3%) in roughly 40 trading days as COVID-19 triggered a global economic shutdown. Factory closures, travel bans, and the collapse of supply chains — announced progressively from late February through mid-March 2020 — hit Industrials and Financials hardest. VIX spiked to 62, TLT rose 16%, and oil crashed 54.3%, all confirming a liquidity-driven panic. Only Staples (-23.9%) and Healthcare (-28.1%) held up as consumers and governments stocked essential goods.","body_zh":"受新冠疫情引发全球经济停摆影响，工业板块（等权）在约40个交易日内下跌40.3%，为板块内跌幅最深之列。工厂停产、出行禁令及供应链崩溃从2020年2月底至3月中旬相继冲击工业与金融板块。VIX飙升至62，TLT上涨16%，油价暴跌54.3%，均印证流动性恐慌。仅必需消费品（-23.9%）与医疗（-28.1%）相对抗跌，因政府和消费者囤积生活必需品。","drivers":["COVID-19 global factory shutdowns","travel/logistics demand collapse","VIX spiked to 62","oil -54% demand shock","credit HYG -10% spreads blew out"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情全球工厂停产","出行/物流需求崩溃","VIX飙升至62","油价下跌-54%需求冲击","高收益信用利差大幅走阔"],"prev_key":"2020-02-12","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-12"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID-19 pandemic shock, -40% in 40 days","title_zh":"新冠疫情冲击，40个交易日内暴跌40%","turn_id":"us_sector_industrials:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The 22-month, 159% rally from the March 23, 2020 pandemic trough was the sector's strongest absolute leg. The Fed cut to zero on March 15, 2020 and launched unlimited QE while Congress passed $2.2 trillion CARES Act (March 27, 2020) and subsequent stimulus packages totaling $5+ trillion. The November 2021 Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act (IIJA, $1.2 trillion) created a durable capex backlog for E&C, heavy equipment, and electrical contractors. Industrials gained 159% EW in the window, matching Energy (+174%) and Tech (+150%), with the weak dollar (-6% DXY), oil +230%, and copper/gold +95% confirming the most intense reflation cycle in decades.","body_zh":"从2020年3月23日疫情低点起历时22个月累涨159%，是板块历史上绝对涨幅最大的一腿。2020年3月15日美联储降息至零并启动无限量QE，同月27日国会通过2.2万亿美元CARES法案，后续总计逾5万亿美元刺激接踵而至。2021年11月《基础设施投资与就业法案》（IIJA，1.2万亿美元）为工程建设、重型设备及电气承包商创造了持续的资本开支积压。工业板块等权在该窗口内以159%涨幅比肩能源（+174%）和科技（+150%）；美元走软（DXY -6%）、油价+230%、铜/金比+95%印证了数十年来最强烈的再通胀周期。","drivers":["Fed zero rates + unlimited QE Mar-2020","CARES Act $2.2T fiscal stimulus","IIJA Nov-2021 $1.2T infrastructure law","oil +230% commodities reflation","USD -6% DXY tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2020年3月降息至零+无限量QE","CARES法案2.2万亿美元财政刺激","2021年11月IIJA 1.2万亿美元基建法","油价+230%大宗商品再通胀","美元贬值-6% DXY出口顺风"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Fiscal-monetary bazooka fuels 159% reflation surge","title_zh":"财政货币政策双管齐下，工业板块159%暴涨","turn_id":"us_sector_industrials:trough:2020-03"},"2022-01-04":{"body":"Industrials fell 22.5% as the Fed pivoted from the most dovish posture in history to a 475 bps hiking cycle beginning March 2022, with the first 75 bps hike in June 2022. TLT collapsed 21.4% and DXY surged 8.7%, raising financing costs for capital-intensive industrial projects. Russia's invasion of Ukraine (Feb 24, 2022) pushed oil to +42% but introduced supply-chain disruptions and raised input costs. Despite Energy being the sole sector in the green, all other cyclicals sold off hard (Industrials -22.5%, Tech -28.1%), while defensives (Utilities -7.6%, Staples -10.9%) held up, confirming a stagflation-ish growth-scare rotation.","body_zh":"工业板块下跌22.5%，美联储从史上最宽松立场急转为2022年3月启动的475个基点加息周期（首次75bps加息于2022年6月）。TLT暴跌21.4%，美元指数飙升8.7%，推高资本密集型工业项目融资成本。2022年2月24日俄罗斯入侵乌克兰推动油价上涨42%，但同时引发供应链中断并抬高投入成本。尽管能源是唯一录得正收益的板块，其余周期板块均大幅下跌（工业-22.5%，科技-28.1%），防御板块（公用事业-7.6%，必需消费品-10.9%）相对抗跌，印证了滞胀式增长恐慌的轮动特征。","drivers":["Fed Mar-2022 hiking cycle +475 bps","TLT -21.4% rate shock","Russia-Ukraine war Feb-2022 supply shock","USD +8.7% DXY","VIX 17 to 31"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2022年3月启动加息周期+475bps","TLT -21.4%利率冲击","2022年2月俄乌战争供应链冲击","美元指数+8.7%","VIX从17升至31"],"prev_key":"2022-01-04","prev_key_chain":["2022-01-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed tightening shock; stagflation rout, -22.5%","title_zh":"美联储紧缩冲击；滞胀恐慌重挫，-22.5%","turn_id":"us_sector_industrials:peak:2022-01"},"2022-06-17":{"body":"Industrials bounced 23% in the two-month window from the June 2022 trough as US CPI peaked at 9.1% in June 2022 and markets began pricing a Fed pivot. The mix was broad: Discretionary (+27.4%), Tech (+21.6%), and Utilities (+20.6%) all led, while oil -21% and copper/gold -6.1% eased cost pressures. VIX retreated from 31 to 20. The Industrials gain was driven by multiple expansion on pivot hopes rather than fundamental improvement, as the subsequent August 2022 Jackson Hole speech by Powell ended the rally sharply.","body_zh":"工业板块从2022年6月低点反弹23%，核心驱动为美国CPI于2022年6月触顶9.1%，市场开始定价美联储政策转向。反弹呈广谱态势：可选消费（+27.4%）、科技（+21.6%）与公用事业（+20.6%）共同领涨，油价-21%与铜/金比-6.1%缓解成本压力，VIX从31回落至20。工业板块涨幅更多来自转向预期驱动的估值修复而非基本面改善，随后2022年8月鲍威尔杰克逊霍尔鹰派讲话使这轮反弹迅速终结。","drivers":["CPI peak Jun-2022 9.1% pivot hopes","VIX 31 to 20 risk appetite","oil -21% input cost relief","bear-market multiple expansion","growth/tech led rotation"],"drivers_zh":["2022年6月CPI触顶9.1%引发转向预期","VIX从31降至20风险偏好回升","油价下跌-21%原材料成本缓解","熊市估值修复","成长/科技引领轮动"],"prev_key":"2022-06-17","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-17"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-inflation bear rally; pivot hopes lift cyclicals","title_zh":"通胀见顶熊市反弹；转向预期提振周期板块","turn_id":"us_sector_industrials:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"Powell's August 26, 2022 Jackson Hole speech — 'we must keep at it until the job is done' — was shorter and more hawkish than expected, triggering a 1,000-point Dow selloff on the day. Industrials fell 16.7% by September 30 as TLT collapsed another 11.4% and DXY surged 5.3%, the worst real-rate shock of the hiking cycle. Energy (-5.2%) held up best while Tech (-21.2%) and Real Estate (-20.2%) led the decline. The ctx confirms a rate-driven selloff, not a growth/demand-led fall, with the cyclicals vs. defensives gap (-15.3% vs -12.4%) narrow — rate sensitivity was the key transmission.","body_zh":"2022年8月26日鲍威尔在杰克逊霍尔发表鹰派讲话——\"我们必须坚持到完成任务\"——短促而强硬，当日触发道指千点暴跌。至9月30日，工业板块累跌16.7%，TLT再跌11.4%，美元指数飙升5.3%，为本轮加息周期中最严重的实际利率冲击。能源（-5.2%）相对抗跌，科技（-21.2%）与房地产（-20.2%）领跌。数据印证此为利率驱动的下跌而非需求主导，周期与防御差距（-15.3% vs -12.4%）相对收窄，利率敏感性是关键传导机制。","drivers":["Jackson Hole Aug-2022 Powell hawkish shock","TLT -11.4% rate spike","USD +5.3% DXY","VIX 20 to 32","real-rate shock capex discount"],"drivers_zh":["2022年8月杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击","TLT -11.4%利率飙升","美元指数+5.3%","VIX从20升至32","实际利率冲击资本开支折现"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole shock; dollar and rates spike again","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔冲击；美元与利率再度飙升","turn_id":"us_sector_industrials:peak:2022-08"},"2022-09-30":{"body":"The 26-month, 105.4% rally from October 2022 was the second-longest bull leg in the sample. Three compounding catalysts drove it: (1) the disinflationary Fed pause/pivot cycle (final hike July 2023, three cuts in H2 2024) released rate pressure; (2) the ChatGPT/generative-AI boom from November 2022 drove unprecedented data-center construction, creating a multi-year order backlog for electrical equipment, HVAC, power systems, and E&C firms; (3) the IRA (Aug 2022) and CHIPS Act (Aug 2022) unleashed a domestic manufacturing construction surge — US factory construction spending doubled year-over-year by 2023. Industrials gained 78.9% in the window, ranking 3rd behind Comm and Tech, confirming it captured the AI infrastructure buildout rather than the AI software premium.","body_zh":"从2022年10月起历时26个月累涨105.4%，是样本中第二长的牛市腿，三大催化剂叠加驱动：（1）反通胀环境下美联储暂停/转向加息周期（2023年7月最后一次加息，2024年下半年三次降息）释放利率压力；（2）2022年11月ChatGPT引发生成式AI浪潮，带动史无前例的数据中心建设，为电气设备、暖通空调、电力系统及工程建设公司创造多年订单积压；（3）2022年8月《通胀削减法案》与《芯片法案》相继落地，推动美国国内制造业建设支出至2023年实现同比翻倍。工业板块在该窗口内以+78.9%位居第三，仅落后于通信和科技，表明其受益于AI基础设施建设而非AI软件溢价。","drivers":["AI/data-center capex boom ChatGPT Nov-2022","IRA + CHIPS Act domestic manufacturing surge","Fed pivot 2023-2024 rate relief","reshoring factory construction boom","defense spending elevated post-Ukraine"],"drivers_zh":["AI/数据中心资本支出热潮 ChatGPT 2022年11月","《通胀削减法案》+《芯片法案》国内制造业激增","美联储2023-2024年政策转向利率松绑","制造业回流工厂建设热潮","乌克兰战后国防开支持续高位"],"prev_key":"2022-09-30","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Goldilocks AI-cycle and reshoring boom, +105%","title_zh":"金发女孩AI周期与制造业回流热潮，+105%","turn_id":"us_sector_industrials:trough:2022-09"},"2024-11-25":{"body":"Industrials fell 20.9% (EW) from the November 2024 post-election peak to the April 8, 2025 trough, driven by rapid escalation of trade-war risk. On April 2, 2025 ('Liberation Day'), Trump announced broad reciprocal tariffs including 34% on China, 20% on the EU, and 24% on Japan; by mid-April US-China tariffs reached 145%, the highest since the 1930s. VIX spiked from 15 to 52, SPY fell 16.4%, and manufacturing employment dropped 42,000 over the following months. Defensives (Staples -6.0%, Health -7.8%) dramatically outperformed cyclicals (-18.9%) in the classic flight-to-safety pattern. Notably, TLT fell 3.0% and DXY fell 3.6% simultaneously — a rare stagflation-risk signal rather than a clean bond flight.","body_zh":"工业板块（等权）从2024年11月大选后高点跌至2025年4月8日低点，累跌20.9%，核心驱动为贸易战风险快速升级。2025年4月2日\"解放日\"，特朗普宣布大范围对等关税（对华34%、欧盟20%、日本24%），至4月中旬中美双边关税高达145%，为1930年代以来最高水平。VIX从15飙升至52，标普500下跌16.4%，此后数月制造业就业减少4.2万人。防御板块（必需消费品-6.0%，医疗-7.8%）大幅跑赢周期板块（-18.9%），呈典型避险轮动特征。值得关注的是，TLT同期下跌3.0%，美元指数下跌3.6%，发出罕见的滞胀风险信号，而非纯粹的债券避险。","drivers":["Trump Liberation Day Apr-2, 2025 tariffs","US-China tariffs 145% May-2025 peak","VIX 15 to 52","manufacturing employment -42K","supply-chain disruption cost-push"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月2日特朗普'解放日'关税","中美关税最高达145%","VIX从15飙升至52","制造业就业减少4.2万人","供应链中断成本推升"],"prev_key":"2024-11-25","prev_key_chain":["2024-11-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump 2.0 tariff shock; growth scare, -20.9%","title_zh":"特朗普2.0关税冲击；增长恐慌重挫，-20.9%","turn_id":"us_sector_industrials:peak:2024-11"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"Industrials (EW) rallied 57.3% from the April 2025 trough as three forces converged. First, the May 12, 2025 US-China tariff truce slashed bilateral duties from 125%+ to 10% for a 90-day window (extended to November 2026), removing the most acute supply-chain risk. Second, hyperscaler AI capex surged: Amazon, Microsoft, Google, and Meta collectively spent over $410 billion on capex in 2025 (versus $200 billion in 2024), with roughly 75% targeting AI infrastructure, creating sustained demand for electrical equipment, cooling, and construction. Third, defense spending remained elevated post-Ukraine and was boosted by NATO rearmament. Cyclicals outperformed defensives by 31 pp, VIX declined from 52 to 19, and oil +20.7% with copper/gold +11.3% confirmed a reflation/growth-up regime.","body_zh":"工业板块（等权）从2025年4月低点反弹57.3%，三大力量形成合力：第一，2025年5月12日中美关税休战将双边关税从125%以上骤降至10%（有效期至2026年11月），消除最紧迫的供应链风险；第二，超大规模AI资本支出激增——亚马逊、微软、谷歌与Meta 2025年资本支出合计逾4100亿美元（2024年约2000亿美元），其中约75%用于AI基础设施，为电气设备、制冷与建筑工程创造持续需求；第三，后乌克兰战争时代国防开支持续高位并因北约重整军备进一步提升。周期板块跑赢防御板块31个百分点，VIX从52降至19，油价+20.7%与铜/金比+11.3%共同印证再通胀/增长向上象限。","drivers":["May-2025 US-China tariff truce","AI hyperscaler capex $410B+ 2025","defense/aerospace demand elevated","oil +20.7% reflation","VIX 52 to 19 risk appetite"],"drivers_zh":["2025年5月中美关税休战","AI超大规模资本开支2025年超4100亿美元","国防/航空航天需求持续高位","油价+20.7%再通胀","VIX从52降至19风险偏好修复"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff truce and AI-capex surge lift Industrials 57%","title_zh":"关税休战与AI资本开支激增，工业板块反弹57%","turn_id":"us_sector_industrials:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Industrials (Equal-Weight) is in an expansion/trending phase (pos 38.8, rs_rank 22), ranked 3rd among GICS sectors in the current window at +15.8%, trailing only Tech (+24.3%) and Energy (+21.5%). The backdrop is a reflation/growth-up quad: cyclicals outpace defensives by ~4 pp, oil +19.2%, copper/gold +18.3%, and equal-weight breadth beats cap-weight by +2.9 pp, all favoring cyclicals with real-asset exposure. The current rally leg from the April 2025 Liberation Day trough (+57.3%) is driven by the May 2025 US-China tariff truce (duties cut from 125% to 10%), renewed AI/data-center capex driving demand for electrical equipment, HVAC, and heavy construction, plus sustained elevated defense spending. The sector sits above its 200-day MA with a BUY signal; at cycle-position 38.8 it is mid-leg, not yet at a historic peak setup.","now_zh":"工业板块（等权）处于扩张/趋势阶段（周期位置38.8，相对强度排名第22），当前窗口涨幅15.8%，在11个GICS行业中位居第三，仅落后于科技（+24.3%）和能源（+21.5%）。宏观背景为再通胀/增长向上象限：周期性行业跑赢防御性行业约4个百分点，油价+19.2%，铜/金比+18.3%，等权跑赢市值加权+2.9个百分点，整体有利于具有实物资产敞口的周期股。本轮自2025年4月\"解放日\"低点启动的反弹（+57.3%）受益于：2025年5月中美关税休战（关税从125%降至10%）、AI/数据中心资本支出驱动电气设备与重型建筑需求，以及持续高位的国防开支。板块位于200日均线上方，信号为\"买入\"；周期位置38.8仍属中段，尚未达到历史顶部形态。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"business.cycle_trough.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"business.cycle_trough.v1","arch_state":"missing","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-us_sector_materials":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"From Jan 2014 through May 2015 the S&P 500 gained 19% in a low-volatility, slowdown-deflation-scare environment where Health Care (+36.7%) and Tech (+25.8%) led. Brent oil collapsed from roughly $112 in June 2014 to $62 by December as demand-side global weakness crushed commodity pricing power, while the DXY surged 15.3% as the Fed tapered QE3. Materials managed a 24.2% gain on broad market beta rather than sector-specific demand: copper-gold fell 12.4%, TLT rallied 23.5%, and the sector trailed the defensive average (+27.3%), confirming the gain was flow-driven, not fundamental. The leg ended as commodity bust headwinds accumulated to the point of producing a cycle peak with no underlying commodity pricing support.","body_zh":"2014年1月至2015年5月，标普500在低波动、通缩恐慌环境下上涨19%，由医疗（+36.7%）和科技（+25.8%）领涨。布伦特原油从2014年6月约112美元跌至12月62美元，需求侧全球增长放缓压垮大宗商品定价权，同时美联储缩减QE3推动美元指数上涨15.3%。材料板块录得24.2%涨幅，纯属宽幅市场贝塔驱动而非板块自身基本面需求：铜金比下跌12.4%，长债TLT上涨23.5%，板块全程落后于防御类均值（+27.3%），证实涨幅属流量驱动。随着大宗商品下行压力累积，缺乏定价支撑的周期高点随即形成。","drivers":["Fed QE3 taper / dollar surge","Demand-side oil collapse 2014","Deflation-scare slowdown quad","Health/Tech defensive melt-up beta"],"drivers_zh":["美联储缩减QE3/美元走强","2014年需求侧油价崩跌","通缩恐慌/经济放缓象限","医疗/科技防御性熔涨贝塔"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Melt-up era: defensives carry lagging Materials","title_zh":"熔涨时代：防御类领跑，材料随行","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:trough:2014-01"},"2015-05-15":{"body":"From May through late-September 2015 Materials dropped 20.7%, among the worst of all sectors (only Energy, at -24.7%, fared worse). China's manufacturing PMI tumbled to a six-year low by July 2015, and on August 24 ('Black Monday') global markets crashed as the SSE Composite had already fallen 43% from its June peak; the yuan devaluation (August 11, 2015) amplified commodity demand fears. Copper and iron ore slumped sharply as China — which consumes two-thirds of global iron ore and half of global copper — signaled a hard-landing; oil hit a six-year low below $39 by August. The risk-off rotation was unmistakable: VIX surged from 12 to 28, defensives fell only -6.6% vs cyclicals -14.1%, and credit spreads widened (HYG-LQD -6.2pp), all confirming a flight-to-safety event rather than sector-specific weakness.","body_zh":"2015年5月至9月末，材料板块下跌20.7%，仅次于能源（-24.7%），位列表现最差板块之列。中国制造业PMI于2015年7月跌至六年低位，8月24日\"黑色星期一\"全球市场暴跌，上证综指自6月高点已下跌43%；8月11日人民币贬值进一步放大了大宗商品需求恐慌。铜和铁矿石价格大幅下滑——中国消耗全球三分之二铁矿石和一半铜——油价8月跌破每桶39美元创六年新低。避险轮动特征明显：VIX从12飙升至28，防御类板块仅下跌-6.6%而顺周期-14.1%，信用利差走阔（HYG-LQD -6.2pp），均确认为避险事件而非板块特定性下跌。","drivers":["China hard-landing fears / PMI collapse","August 2015 yuan devaluation","Commodity demand shock (copper, iron ore, oil)","VIX spike 12 to 28 / risk-off flight to safety"],"drivers_zh":["中国硬着陆担忧/PMI崩溃","2015年8月人民币贬值","大宗商品需求冲击（铜、铁矿石、油）","VIX飙升12至28/避险出逃"],"prev_key":"2015-05-15","prev_key_chain":["2015-05-15"],"status":"exact","title":"China crash and commodity bust crush Materials","title_zh":"中国崩盘与大宗商品破灭重创材料","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:peak:2015-05"},"2015-09-28":{"body":"From late-September to early-November 2015 Materials rebounded 15.4%, ranking as the top sector alongside Energy (+16.3%). China's Caixin PMI showed September reading at 50.5 (recovering from the August trough), and global central banks signaled caution on tightening: the Fed stood pat at its September 2015 meeting, removing an immediate rate-hike catalyst. The relief rotation was classic risk-on — cyclicals averaged +13.4% vs defensives +7.9%, VIX compressed from 28 to 14, credit spreads tightened (HYG-LQD +3.9pp), and copper-gold recovered +2.3%. The move was a dead-cat bounce within the broader 2015-16 commodity bear: oil only recovered +3.8% and the DXY barely moved, leaving the structural headwinds intact.","body_zh":"2015年9月末至11月初，材料板块反弹15.4%，与能源（+16.3%）并列领涨板块。财新中国制造业PMI 9月读数回升至50.5（从8月低点修复），全球央行释放谨慎信号：美联储9月例会按兵不动，移除了即时加息催化剂。反弹轮动呈现经典的风险偏好特征——顺周期均值+13.4%对比防御+7.9%，VIX从28压缩至14，信用利差收紧（HYG-LQD +3.9pp），铜金比回升+2.3%。但此次上涨本质是大宗商品熊市中的技术反弹：油价仅回升+3.8%，美元指数几乎未动，结构性阻力依然存在。","drivers":["Fed September 2015 no-hike relief","China PMI stabilization / stimulus hopes","VIX mean-reversion 28 to 14","Bear-market oversold bounce cyclicals"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2015年9月按兵不动释压","中国PMI企稳/刺激预期","VIX均值回归28至14","熊市超卖后顺周期板块技术反弹"],"prev_key":"2015-09-28","prev_key_chain":["2015-09-28"],"status":"exact","title":"Bear bounce: cyclical relief on China stimulus hopes","title_zh":"熊市反弹：中国刺激预期带来喘息","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:trough:2015-09"},"2015-11-02":{"body":"From November 2015 through late-January 2016 Materials fell 19.0%, co-leading the selloff with Energy (-23.0%) as the commodity bear resumed. Oil continued its freefall — WTI hit $26 in January 2016 as OPEC refused to cut production and US shale remained online, and the Bloomberg Commodity Index dropped to its lowest level since 1999. The Federal Reserve's December 2015 rate hike (first in nine years, on December 16) strengthened the dollar an additional +2.5% DXY, tightening conditions for commodity producers. Risk-off signals dominated: defensives led (utilities flat vs cyclicals -14.3%), VIX rose 14 to 24, TLT rallied 3.8%, and credit spreads widened (HYG-LQD -6.4pp), confirming a continuation of the deflation-scare selloff.","body_zh":"2015年11月至2016年1月末，材料板块下跌19.0%，与能源（-23.0%）并列领跌。大宗商品熊市延续——美国原油（WTI）于2016年1月跌至26美元，欧佩克拒绝减产且美国页岩油仍在生产，彭博商品指数跌至1999年以来最低水平。美联储2015年12月16日九年来首次加息推动美元指数额外上涨+2.5%，收紧了大宗商品生产商的融资条件。避险信号主导市场：防御类领跌（公用事业几乎持平而顺周期-14.3%），VIX从14升至24，长债TLT上涨3.8%，信用利差走阔（HYG-LQD -6.4pp），确认为通缩恐慌延续性下跌。","drivers":["First Fed rate hike Dec 2015 / dollar strength","Oil freefall to 2016 lows (WTI $26)","Commodity supercycle bust phase","Risk-off flight to defensives / credit spread widening"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2015年12月首次加息/美元走强","油价持续下跌至2016年低点（WTI $26）","大宗商品超级周期破灭阶段","避险出逃防御类/信用利差走阔"],"prev_key":"2015-11-02","prev_key_chain":["2015-11-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil crash and Fed hike fear revive commodity selloff","title_zh":"油价崩跌与加息恐慌重燃大宗商品下跌","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:peak:2015-11"},"2016-01-25":{"body":"From January 2016 through January 2018 Materials surged 98.6%, ranking among the top three sectors (behind Financials and Tech). The two-year leg had two distinct catalysts: first, from early 2016 the Bloomberg Commodity Index bottomed as G20 finance ministers met in Shanghai in February 2016, effectively coordinating dollar weakness (the so-called Shanghai Accord), and oil began a recovery from $26 to $50+. Second, Donald Trump's November 2016 election victory unleashed the reflation trade — NBER research confirmed that materials, industrials, and financial stocks surged on expectations of infrastructure spending, deregulation, and fiscal stimulus; in the following months the 2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act passed. Over the full two years the DXY fell 10.4%, oil rallied 118%, copper-gold rose 37.3%, VIX collapsed from 24 to 11, and cyclicals averaged +71.2% vs defensives +30.9%, confirming a sustained reflation/growth-up quad.","body_zh":"2016年1月至2018年1月，材料板块大幅上涨98.6%，位列全市场前三（仅次于金融和科技）。这一两年长腿有两个关键催化剂：其一，2016年初彭博商品指数触底，G20财长2016年2月在上海会晤，事实上协调了美元走弱（即上海协议），油价从26美元开始修复至50美元以上；其二，2016年11月特朗普当选，释放通胀反弹交易——哈佛大学和NBER研究确认材料、工业和金融股因基建支出预期、放松管制和财政刺激而大涨，随后2017年《减税与就业法案》落地。两年内美元指数下跌10.4%，油价大涨118%，铜金比上升37.3%，VIX从24骤降至11，顺周期均值+71.2%对比防御+30.9%，确认持续的通胀反弹/增长向上象限。","drivers":["G20 Shanghai Accord / dollar reversal 2016","Trump election reflation trade Nov 2016","2017 Tax Cuts and Jobs Act fiscal stimulus","Oil recovery $26 to $50+, DXY -10.4%","China infrastructure / commodity demand re-acceleration"],"drivers_zh":["G20上海协议/2016年美元逆转","2016年11月特朗普当选通胀反弹交易","2017年《减税与就业法案》财政刺激","油价从26美元回升至50美元以上，美元指数-10.4%","中国基建/大宗商品需求再加速"],"prev_key":"2016-01-25","prev_key_chain":["2016-01-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Shanghai Accord, Trump reflation, and dollar reversal","title_zh":"上海协议、特朗普通胀反弹与美元逆转","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:trough:2016-01"},"2018-01-26":{"body":"From January through December 2018 Materials fell 22.2%, matching Financials as the worst performer (only Energy was worse at -28.4%). The selloff had three overlapping drivers: the US-China trade war escalated through 2018 with waves of tariffs on steel, aluminum, and industrial goods starting March 2018 that raised input costs and threatened global demand; the Fed hiked rates four times in 2018, with the December 2018 hike (to a 2.25-2.5% target) and Powell's hawkish balance-sheet-runoff comments causing the worst December stock market performance since the Great Depression; and the DXY rallied 8.4%, further crushing commodity prices. Copper and oil both fell sharply (copper-gold -9.9%, oil -35.7%), VIX surged from 11 to 36, and defensives (-6.8%) drastically outperformed cyclicals (-21.9%), confirming a textbook risk-off rotation.","body_zh":"2018年1月至12月，材料板块下跌22.2%，与金融板块并列表现最差（仅能源-28.4%更糟糕）。下跌有三重叠加驱动：一是美中贸易战升级，2018年3月起钢铝及工业品关税浪潮推高了原材料成本并威胁全球需求；二是美联储2018年四次加息，尤其12月加息（目标利率至2.25-2.5%）叠加鲍威尔关于缩表的鹰派表态，导致美股12月表现创大萧条以来最差；三是美元指数上涨8.4%，进一步压制大宗商品价格。铜价和油价均大幅下滑（铜金比-9.9%，油价-35.7%），VIX从11飙升至36，防御类（-6.8%）大幅跑赢顺周期（-21.9%），确认为教科书式避险轮动。","drivers":["US-China trade war tariffs Mar-Sep 2018","Four Fed rate hikes 2018 / December hawkish shock","DXY +8.4% / dollar strength headwind","Growth slowdown fears / VIX surge 11 to 36"],"drivers_zh":["2018年3-9月美中贸易战关税浪潮","美联储2018年四次加息/12月鹰派冲击","美元指数+8.4%/美元走强阻力","增长放缓担忧/VIX飙升11至36"],"prev_key":"2018-01-26","prev_key_chain":["2018-01-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade war, rate shock, and dollar surge kill rally","title_zh":"贸易战、利率冲击与美元飙升终结涨势","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"From December 2018 through December 2019 Materials rallied 36.2%, though it lagged the S&P 500 (+39.9%) and the Tech-led recovery. The January 2019 Fed pivot — where Chair Powell signaled a pause in rate hikes and eventually delivered three cuts in 2019 — was the primary catalyst, compressing the DXY (-0.2% over the period) and allowing VIX to fall from 36 to 14. In December 2019 the US and China agreed on the Phase One trade deal, postponing $160 billion in scheduled tariffs and lifting tariff uncertainty. Oil recovered 43.6%. However, the leg was narrow and mega-cap-led (equal-weight lagged cap-weight by 3.2%): semis surged 77.3% and Tech led (+61.2%), so Materials' 36% gain was more about broad relief than commodity-specific demand. Copper-gold fell 15.2% over the period, confirming the Materials rally was beta-driven rather than commodity-supply-demand driven.","body_zh":"2018年12月至2019年12月，材料板块反弹36.2%，但落后于标普500（+39.9%）和科技主导的复苏行情。2019年1月美联储转向——鲍威尔暗示暂停加息并于全年三次降息——是主要催化剂，美元指数全程仅微跌-0.2%，VIX从36降至14。2019年12月美中达成第一阶段贸易协议，推迟1600亿美元关税落地，关税不确定性消退。油价回升43.6%。然而，本轮行情较窄且由大市值股票主导（等权落后市值权重3.2%）：半导体大涨77.3%，科技领涨（+61.2%），材料的36%涨幅更多是宽幅市场反弹贝塔，而非大宗商品基本面驱动——铜金比全程下跌15.2%证实了这一点。","drivers":["Fed January 2019 pivot / three 2019 rate cuts","US-China Phase One trade deal December 2019","VIX mean-reversion 36 to 14","Oil recovery +43.6%"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月转向/全年三次降息","2019年12月美中第一阶段贸易协议","VIX均值回归36至14","油价回升+43.6%"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot and Phase One deal lift cyclicals","title_zh":"美联储转向与第一阶段协议提振顺周期","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:trough:2018-12"},"2019-12-31":{"body":"From January through March 23, 2020 Materials plunged 39.8% in the COVID-19 pandemic crash, one of the deepest selloffs in the series. The SARS-CoV-2 pandemic spread globally in February 2020, causing the fastest-ever 30%+ drawdown in the S&P 500 (30.3% drawdown from peak to March 23 trough). Industrial commodity demand collapsed: copper fell roughly 15% by March 2020 lows as manufacturing shut down globally; oil crashed 61.7% (OPEC+ price war triggered in March as Saudi Arabia and Russia failed to reach production-cut agreement). VIX reached 62, the highest since 2008, and defensives fell -26.2% vs cyclicals -38.6%, confirming a panic-liquidation selloff. The DXY surged 6.3% in a dash-for-cash, and TLT rallied 22.9% as bonds received safe-haven flows. Equal-weight lagged cap-weight by 7.1pp, marking this as a broad, indiscriminate panic.","body_zh":"2019年12月末至2020年3月23日，材料板块在新冠疫情冲击下暴跌39.8%，为该系列中最深跌幅之一。2020年2月SARS-CoV-2在全球蔓延，标普500录得历史上最快的30%以上回撤（至3月23日低点跌幅30.3%）。工业大宗商品需求骤然崩塌：铜价3月跌至低点时约下跌15%，全球制造业停摆；油价暴跌61.7%（OPEC+因沙特与俄罗斯减产谈判破裂引发价格战）。VIX飙升至62，创2008年以来最高，防御类下跌-26.2%对比顺周期-38.6%，确认为恐慌性抛售。美元指数上涨6.3%反映现金为王，长债TLT上涨22.9%承接避险资金。等权落后市值权重7.1pp，标志本次为全面无差别的恐慌性下跌。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic global demand seizure","OPEC+ price war oil crash -61.7%","VIX surge to 62 / dash-for-cash","Industrial commodity demand collapse"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情全球需求骤停","OPEC+价格战油价暴跌-61.7%","VIX飙升至62/现金为王","工业大宗商品需求崩溃"],"prev_key":"2019-12-31","prev_key_chain":["2019-12-31"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash: global demand seizure","title_zh":"新冠疫情崩盘：全球需求骤停","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:peak:2019-12"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From March 2020 through April 2022 Materials surged 196.8%, ranking second only to Energy (+277.3%). The two-year leg was powered by the largest fiscal and monetary stimulus in peacetime history: the CARES Act ($2.2 trillion, March 2020), American Rescue Plan ($1.9 trillion, March 2021), and Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act ($1.2 trillion, November 2021) channeled trillions into construction and manufacturing, driving a commodity supercycle narrative. Copper hit a record $10,476/tonne in May 2021, and the Bloomberg Commodity Index rose sharply. Russia's invasion of Ukraine (February 24, 2022) provided a further commodity supply shock, lifting metals and energy into the April 2022 peak. VIX fell from 62 to 20, the DXY dropped 2.0%, breadth was historically wide (equal-weight beat cap-weight by 23.3pp), and the reflation quad was unambiguous: cyclicals +147.9% vs defensives +83.4%, oil +339.9%, copper-gold +94.8%.","body_zh":"2020年3月至2022年4月，材料板块上涨196.8%，仅次于能源（+277.3%）。两年长腿由和平时期最大规模的财政货币刺激驱动：《CARES法案》（2.2万亿美元，2020年3月）、《美国救援计划》（1.9万亿美元，2021年3月）和《基础设施投资和就业法案》（1.2万亿美元，2021年11月）将数万亿美元注入建设和制造业，推动大宗商品超级周期叙事。铜价2021年5月创下每吨10476美元的历史纪录，彭博商品指数大幅上涨。2022年2月24日俄罗斯入侵乌克兰进一步带来大宗商品供应冲击，推动金属和能源冲上2022年4月峰值。VIX从62降至20，美元指数下跌2.0%，参与面历史性宽广（等权超越市值权重23.3pp），通胀反弹象限无可置疑：顺周期+147.9%对比防御+83.4%，油价+339.9%，铜金比+94.8%。","drivers":["CARES Act / American Rescue Plan / IIJA fiscal stimulus","Fed zero rates + QE / ultra-loose monetary policy","Commodity supercycle narrative: copper, steel, lumber","Russia-Ukraine supply shock Feb 2022"],"drivers_zh":["《CARES法案》/《美国救援计划》/《基础设施法》财政刺激","美联储零利率+QE/超宽松货币政策","大宗商品超级周期：铜、钢铁、木材","2022年2月俄乌战争供应冲击"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Pandemic fiscal bazooka and commodity supercycle","title_zh":"疫情财政火箭弹与大宗商品超级周期","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:trough:2020-03"},"2022-04-20":{"body":"From April through July 14, 2022 Materials dropped 19.8%, trailing only Discretionary (-21.4%) among cyclicals. The Federal Reserve began the most aggressive tightening cycle in 40 years: a 25bp hike in March 2022 was followed by a 50bp hike in May (largest in 22 years) and then 75bp in June 2022 as CPI printed 9.1%. Simultaneously, Shanghai entered a two-month COVID lockdown (April-May 2022), crushing Chinese industrial demand — copper and iron ore fell sharply as China, consuming roughly half of global copper, went offline. The DXY surged 8.1%, copper-gold fell 18.3%, and oil fell 6.8%. Defensives fell only -8.9% while cyclicals lost -17.5%, and VIX rose from 20 to 26, confirming a flight-to-safety rotation driven by stagflationary recession fears rather than Materials-specific weakness.","body_zh":"2022年4月至7月14日，材料板块下跌19.8%，顺周期板块中仅次于可选消费（-21.4%）。美联储开启40年来最激进的紧缩周期：2022年3月加息25bp，5月加息50bp（22年来最大幅度），6月CPI录得9.1%后再度加息75bp。与此同时，上海因新冠疫情封控长达两个月（2022年4-5月），中国工业需求骤降——作为全球约一半铜消费的中国暂时停摆，铜和铁矿石价格大幅下滑。美元指数上涨8.1%，铜金比下跌18.3%，油价下跌6.8%。防御类仅下跌-8.9%而顺周期-17.5%，VIX从20升至26，确认为滞胀衰退担忧驱动的避险轮动，而非材料板块特定性下跌。","drivers":["Fed 50bp May + 75bp June 2022 rate shock","Shanghai COVID lockdown / China demand collapse","Recession fears / stagflation narrative","DXY +8.1% / copper-gold -18.3%"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2022年5月50bp+6月75bp加息冲击","上海新冠封控/中国需求骤降","衰退担忧/滞胀叙事","美元指数+8.1%/铜金比-18.3%"],"prev_key":"2022-04-20","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Recession scare: Fed shock and China lockdowns","title_zh":"衰退恐慌：美联储冲击与中国封控","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:peak:2022-04"},"2022-07-14":{"body":"From July 14 through August 16, 2022 Materials rebounded 16.8% in a broad cyclical relief rally. Investors began pricing a Fed pivot as June 2022 CPI came in at 9.1% (the peak), and subsequent signals suggested inflation might be rolling over; the market rallied roughly 17% from mid-June to mid-August on the hope that the Fed would stop hiking. Discretionary (+21.3%) and Industrials (+17.6%) led, with Materials in line at roughly market pace. Cyclicals averaged +16.7% vs defensives +7.6%, VIX fell 26 to 20, DXY weakened 1.9%, and copper-gold recovered +9.2%. This was a momentum-driven short-covering rally rather than a fundamental improvement: oil actually fell 9.7% during the period, limiting Materials' leadership.","body_zh":"2022年7月14日至8月16日，材料板块在宽幅顺周期解脱性反弹中上涨16.8%。投资者开始定价美联储转向：2022年6月CPI录得9.1%（即峰值），随后信号暗示通胀或已见顶；市场从6月中旬到8月中旬反弹约17%，押注美联储将停止加息。可选消费（+21.3%）和工业（+17.6%）领涨，材料与市场同步。顺周期均值+16.7%对比防御+7.6%，VIX从26降至20，美元指数走弱-1.9%，铜金比回升+9.2%。这是动能驱动的空头回补行情而非基本面改善：油价在此期间实际下跌-9.7%，限制了材料板块的领涨空间。","drivers":["Peak inflation 9.1% CPI / Fed pivot expectations","Short-covering cyclical rally June-Aug 2022","DXY -1.9% / copper-gold recovery","VIX mean-reversion 26 to 20"],"drivers_zh":["CPI 9.1%峰值/美联储转向预期","2022年6-8月顺周期空头回补","美元指数-1.9%/铜金比回升","VIX均值回归26至20"],"prev_key":"2022-07-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-07-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak inflation pivot hopes lift cyclicals briefly","title_zh":"通胀见顶转向预期短暂提振顺周期","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:trough:2022-07"},"2022-08-16":{"body":"From August 16 through September 26, 2022 Materials fell 17.8% as Chair Powell's August 26 Jackson Hole speech shattered peak-inflation-pivot hopes, explicitly stating that the Fed would cause some pain to restore price stability and signaling continued aggressive rate hikes. The market dropped 3%+ the day of the speech and continued lower: yields surged (TLT -10.4%, a major rates shock), the DXY rallied 7.1%, and VIX spiked from 20 to 32. Unusually, in this leg defensives (-9.1%) led only marginally over cyclicals (-15.1%) because the rate surge hurt rate-sensitive real estate and utilities too; Tech and Comm led to the downside. Copper-gold was flat (-0.4%) and oil fell 11.3%, indicating that macro fear rather than commodity-specific demand drove the selloff.","body_zh":"2022年8月16日至9月26日，材料板块下跌17.8%。鲍威尔8月26日杰克逊霍尔讲话打破了通胀见顶/转向希望，明确表示美联储将造成一些痛苦以恢复价格稳定，并暗示将继续激进加息。演讲当日市场跌逾3%并持续走低：利率急升（长债TLT -10.4%，重大利率冲击），美元指数上涨7.1%，VIX从20飙升至32。与寻常不同，此轮防御类（-9.1%）对顺周期（-15.1%）的相对优势较小，因为利率飙升同样重创了利率敏感型房地产和公用事业；科技和通信领跌。铜金比基本持平（-0.4%），油价下跌11.3%，表明宏观恐慌而非大宗商品特定需求驱动了此次下跌。","drivers":["Jackson Hole Powell Aug 26 2022 hawkish shock","TLT -10.4% / yield surge rate shock","DXY +7.1% / dollar headwind","VIX spike 20 to 32 / risk-off rotation"],"drivers_zh":["2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔鲍威尔鹰派冲击","长债TLT -10.4%/收益率飙升利率冲击","美元指数+7.1%/美元阻力","VIX飙升20至32/避险轮动"],"prev_key":"2022-08-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkish shock: rate-hike pain trade","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击：加息痛苦交易","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:peak:2022-08"},"2022-09-26":{"body":"From September 2022 through February 2023 Materials surged 30.8%, ranking as the top performing sector alongside Energy (both well ahead of the broad market's 14.9%). Three forces converged: the DXY peaked in late September 2022 and fell 10.8% over the period as Fed hike expectations recalibrated, providing a powerful tailwind for dollar-denominated commodity producers; China announced its zero-COVID policy exit in November 2022 and reopened borders in January 2023, reviving copper and metal demand expectations; and October 2022 CPI came in below expectations at 7.7%, the clearest signal yet of an inflation rollover. Cyclicals averaged +20.3% vs defensives +5.6%, breadth was wide (equal-weight beat cap-weight by +6.1pp), and VIX fell 32 to 19, confirming a broad risk-on cyclical recovery.","body_zh":"2022年9月至2023年2月，材料板块大幅上涨30.8%，与能源并列领涨板块（均远超大盘14.9%涨幅）。三股力量共同推动：美元指数于2022年9月末见顶，此后下跌10.8%，为美元计价大宗商品生产商提供强劲顺风；中国2022年11月宣布退出清零政策并于2023年1月重新开放边境，提振铜和金属需求预期；2022年10月CPI低于预期录得7.7%，是通胀拐点最清晰的信号。顺周期均值+20.3%对比防御+5.6%，参与面宽广（等权超越市值权重+6.1pp），VIX从32降至19，确认为宽幅风险偏好顺周期复苏。","drivers":["DXY peak Sep 2022 / dollar reversal -10.8%","China zero-COVID exit Nov 2022 / reopening Jan 2023","October 2022 CPI 7.7% inflation rollover","VIX compression 32 to 19 / broad risk-on"],"drivers_zh":["美元指数2022年9月见顶/逆转-10.8%","中国2022年11月退出清零/2023年1月重开","2022年10月CPI 7.7%通胀拐点","VIX压缩32至19/宽幅风险偏好"],"prev_key":"2022-09-26","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-26"],"status":"exact","title":"Dollar peak, China reopening, and inflation rollover","title_zh":"美元见顶、中国重开与通胀拐点","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:trough:2022-09"},"2023-02-02":{"body":"From February through May 2023 Materials fell 14.2% even as the S&P 500 barely moved (+0.6%), marking one of the most concentrated examples of sector-level divergence. The catalyst was the emergence of generative AI — ChatGPT's explosive growth drove a mega-cap tech rotation: semis surged +13.8% (SMH), Tech gained +15.2%, and equal-weight lagged cap-weight by 10.1pp (the widest breadth discount in the entire 12-year series). The March 2023 Silicon Valley Bank collapse and regional banking crisis (also Signature Bank, First Republic) added risk aversion that crowded into mega-cap quality and growth. Copper-gold fell 13.8%, oil dropped 10.3%, and the DXY strengthened 2.5%, all pointing to a demand slowdown concern. Materials ranked among the three worst sectors alongside Financials and Real Estate.","body_zh":"2023年2月至5月，材料板块下跌14.2%，而标普500几乎持平（+0.6%），是整个周期中板块分化最显著的窗口之一。催化剂是生成式AI的崛起——ChatGPT爆炸性增长驱动大市值科技轮动：半导体SMH大涨+13.8%，科技+15.2%，等权落后市值权重10.1pp（12年系列中最大的广度折价）。2023年3月硅谷银行倒闭和区域银行危机（签名银行、第一共和银行相继出事）加剧了风险厌恶情绪，资金涌入大市值高质量成长股。铜金比下跌13.8%，油价下跌10.3%，美元指数走强2.5%，均指向需求放缓担忧。材料与金融、房地产并列三大跌幅最深板块。","drivers":["Generative AI / ChatGPT mega-cap tech rotation","SVB collapse / regional bank crisis Mar 2023","Narrow breadth equal-weight -10.1pp vs cap-weight","Copper-gold -13.8% / demand slowdown concern"],"drivers_zh":["生成式AI/ChatGPT大市值科技轮动","硅谷银行倒闭/2023年3月区域银行危机","广度收窄等权落后市值权重-10.1pp","铜金比-13.8%/需求放缓担忧"],"prev_key":"2023-02-02","prev_key_chain":["2023-02-02"],"status":"exact","title":"AI rotation and bank crisis squeeze Materials out","title_zh":"AI轮动与银行危机将材料挤出市场","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:peak:2023-02"},"2023-05-31":{"body":"From May 2023 through November 2024 Materials gained 37.6%, though it was one of the laggards within the broad cyclical rally (SPY +46.0%). The dominant macro backdrop was a US soft landing: inflation fell from above 4% to near 2.5%, the Fed held rates in 2023 and began cutting in September 2024 (first cut in four years), and recession fears receded. The Inflation Reduction Act (IRA, signed August 2022) and CHIPS Act began deploying capital into clean-energy and semiconductor manufacturing that required copper, lithium, and rare-earth materials, providing a structural demand narrative. AI data-center buildout and EV infrastructure drove critical minerals demand expectations. However, the leg was mega-cap-led (equal-weight lagged cap-weight by 8.5pp) and growth rotated sharply into AI/Tech (+69.8% semis, +15.9% growth-value spread), so Materials trailed Financials (+64.9%), Comm (+58.8%), and Industrials (+51.7%).","body_zh":"2023年5月至2024年11月，材料板块上涨37.6%，在宽幅顺周期反弹中属于落后者（标普500+46.0%）。主要宏观背景是美国经济软着陆：通胀从4%以上回落至约2.5%，美联储2023年按兵不动并于2024年9月启动降息（四年来首次），衰退担忧消退。《通胀削减法案》（IRA，2022年8月签署）和《芯片法案》开始将资本注入清洁能源和半导体制造，为铜、锂和稀土材料提供了结构性需求叙事。AI数据中心建设和电动车基础设施进一步推动了关键矿产需求预期。然而，本轮行情由大市值股票主导（等权落后市值权重8.5pp），增长资金大幅轮动至AI/科技（半导体+69.8%，成长价值利差+15.9%），材料因此落后于金融（+64.9%）、通信（+58.8%）和工业（+51.7%）。","drivers":["US soft landing / inflation normalization","Fed September 2024 rate cut cycle onset","IRA / CHIPS Act critical minerals structural demand","AI data-center and EV copper demand narrative"],"drivers_zh":["美国经济软着陆/通胀正常化","美联储2024年9月启动降息周期","IRA/《芯片法案》关键矿产结构性需求","AI数据中心和电动车铜需求叙事"],"prev_key":"2023-05-31","prev_key_chain":["2023-05-31"],"status":"exact","title":"Soft landing, IRA buildout, and AI metals demand","title_zh":"软着陆、IRA建设与AI金属需求","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:trough:2023-05"},"2024-11-25":{"body":"From November 2024 through April 8, 2025 Materials fell 24.2%, one of the worst declines in the series. The primary catalyst was Donald Trump's November 2024 re-election and subsequent tariff escalation: by April 2025 (Liberation Day, April 2) the effective average US tariff rate rose from 2.5% to roughly 27%, the highest in over a century, with 25% tariffs on all steel and aluminum imports announced March 2025. Tariffs raised input-cost uncertainty for domestic manufacturers while simultaneously threatening global demand destruction via retaliatory measures. VIX spiked from 15 to 52, the highest since the 2020 COVID crash. Defensives fell only -7.6% while cyclicals lost -18.9%, and the sector's close link to global trade volumes made it acutely exposed. Unusually, the DXY weakened 3.6% (tariff uncertainty reduced dollar safe-haven appeal), limiting the typical dollar-headwind mechanism, but the demand destruction thesis overwhelmed the tailwind.","body_zh":"2024年11月至2025年4月8日，材料板块下跌24.2%，为该系列中最深跌幅之一。主要催化剂是2024年11月特朗普再次当选及随后的关税升级：至2025年4月（解放日，4月2日），美国实际平均关税税率从2.5%飙升至约27%，创百年来最高，2025年3月宣布对所有钢铝进口征收25%关税。关税提高了国内制造商的原材料成本不确定性，同时通过报复性措施威胁全球需求。VIX从15飙升至52，创2020年新冠以来最高。防御类仅下跌-7.6%而顺周期-18.9%，材料板块与全球贸易量的紧密关联使其尤为脆弱。特殊之处在于美元指数反而下跌-3.6%（关税不确定性削弱了美元避险吸引力），理论上为材料提供了顺风，但需求破坏论压倒了这一支撑。","drivers":["Trump 2.0 Liberation Day tariffs Apr 2025","25% steel/aluminum tariffs March 2025","US-China trade escalation / demand destruction fears","VIX spike 15 to 52 / risk-off cyclical selloff"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普2.0解放日关税2025年4月","2025年3月25%钢铝关税","美中贸易战升级/需求破坏担忧","VIX飙升15至52/避险顺周期抛售"],"prev_key":"2024-11-25","prev_key_chain":["2024-11-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump 2.0 tariff shock triggers Materials selloff","title_zh":"特朗普2.0关税冲击触发材料下跌","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:peak:2024-11"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"From April 8, 2025 through February 11, 2026 Materials surged 56.6%, ranking third among all sectors (behind Tech +59.8% and Industrials +51.8%). The April 9, 2025 announcement of a 90-day tariff reduction (US-China bilateral tariffs cut from 125% to 10%) was the immediate trigger — the easing resolved the worst of the demand-destruction fears. In August 2025 the tariff reduction was extended another 90 days, and in November 2025 a one-year extension was agreed. A landmark US Supreme Court ruling on February 20, 2026 (Learning Resources v. Trump, 6-3) struck down IEEPA-based broad tariff authority, catalyzing a base-metals surge on February 24, 2026 as Chinese markets reopened after Lunar New Year with copper jumping 2.8% to near $13,228/tonne. The DXY weakened 6.0% over the period, semis surged 131.2%, VIX fell 52 to 18, and the reflation quad was unambiguous: cyclicals +43.6% vs defensives +20.7%, oil +8.5%.","body_zh":"2025年4月8日至2026年2月11日，材料板块大涨56.6%，位列全市场第三（仅次于科技+59.8%和工业+51.8%）。2025年4月9日美中关税削减90天（双边关税从125%降至10%）是即时触发器，最严峻的需求破坏担忧由此消散。2025年8月再度延续90天，2025年11月达成为期一年的延续协议。2026年2月20日美国最高法院6-3裁决（学习资源公司诉特朗普案）推翻了基于IEEPA的宽泛关税授权，2026年2月24日中国市场农历新年后复市，铜价跳涨2.8%至每吨约13228美元，基础金属迎来一波上冲。美元指数全程下跌-6.0%，半导体大涨131.2%，VIX从52降至18，通胀反弹象限清晰：顺周期+43.6%对比防御+20.7%，油价+8.5%。","drivers":["US-China 90-day tariff truce April 9 2025","November 2025 one-year tariff extension","SCOTUS IEEPA tariff ruling Feb 20 2026 / metals surge","DXY -6.0% / dollar tailwind for commodity producers"],"drivers_zh":["2025年4月9日美中90天关税休战","2025年11月一年期关税延续协议","最高法院2026年2月20日IEEPA关税裁决/金属上冲","美元指数-6.0%/美元走软利好大宗商品生产商"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff truce, Supreme Court ruling, and reflation","title_zh":"关税休战、最高法院裁决与通胀反弹","turn_id":"us_sector_materials:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Materials (Equal-Weight) is in a Downturn rolling-over phase (cycle position 45.8, RS rank 36 out of 100, bottom-tertile vs SPY and sector peers). The basket holds above its 200-day moving average so the structural trend is intact, but momentum has faded since the Feb-2026 peak. The live rotation reads reflation/growth-up (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%), nominally supportive for commodity producers, yet a DXY that has strengthened +3.4% is a direct headwind for materials multinationals. Broad participation (equal-weight beating cap-weight by +2.9%) provides mild underlying support, but Materials trails the cycle leaders (Tech +24.3%, Energy +21.5%, Industrials +15.8%). A hawkish Fed tone and stronger dollar are actively repricing copper toward 2026 lows (Bloomberg June 29 2026), consistent with the sector rolling over from a late-reflation cycle peak.","now_zh":"材料（等权）当前处于\"下行/滚顶\"阶段（周期位置45.8，相对强弱排名36，处于后三分之一区间）。价格仍位于200日均线之上，长期趋势未破，但动能自2026年2月高点以来明显衰减。当前轮动环境读数为\"通胀反弹/增长向上\"象限（顺周期板块+11.2%对比防御+6.9%，油价+19.2%，铜金比+18.3%），名义上对大宗商品生产商有利，但美元指数上涨3.4%对材料类跨国企业构成直接阻力。等权超越市值权重2.9%意味着参与面较广，提供一定支撑，但材料整体仍落后于领涨板块（科技+24.3%、能源+21.5%、工业+15.8%）。综合看，材料处于\"通胀反弹末期、涨势受阻\"格局，美联储偏鹰立场叠加强美元正在将铜价压至2026年低位，与板块从周期顶部滚落的节奏一致。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-us_sector_realestate":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"From January 2014 through February 2020, US REITs rode a six-year secular bull anchored by the Fed's near-zero rate policy (fed funds 0-0.25% through December 2015, then three gradual hike cycles to 2.25-2.5% by late 2018, then three 2019 cuts back to 1.75%). Long-bond yields fell sharply over the full window (TLT +69.2%), compressing REIT cap rates, expanding NAV multiples, and making dividend yields attractive vs. Treasuries. Critically, defensives led cyclicals (+105.5% vs +87.6%) while oil collapsed -43.2%, confirming the move was a yield-hunt and safety rotation, not a growth trade; REITs benefited from the same long-duration income-asset bid that lifted Utilities +131%. Mega-cap Tech's dominance (semis +279.8%, narrow breadth -21.5%) siphoned some flow away from real estate, but the rate tailwind sustained the 145% gain through the pre-COVID peak.","body_zh":"2014年1月至2020年2月，美联储维持近零利率政策（联邦基金利率0-0.25%持续至2015年底，此后三轮渐进加息至2018年底的2.25-2.5%，2019年又三次降息至1.75%），长债收益率大幅下行（TLT +69.2%），持续压低REITs资本化率、扩大NAV溢价，并令REIT股息收益率相对国债颇具吸引力。防御板块领涨周期股（+105.5% vs +87.6%），油价暴跌43.2%，确认这是一轮收益寻求与避险轮动而非成长驱动行情。大盘科技的强势（芯片+279.8%，市场广度负偏-21.5%）分流了部分资金，但利率顺风足以支撑板块在新冠疫情前录得145%涨幅。","drivers":["Fed zero/low rate policy","Falling long-bond yields (TLT +69%)","Defensive/yield-hunt rotation","Cap-rate compression, NAV expansion","Oil collapse suppressing inflation"],"drivers_zh":["美联储零/低利率政策","长债收益率大幅下行（TLT +69%）","防御/收益寻求轮动","资本化率压缩、NAV扩张","油价暴跌抑制通胀预期"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-GFC Zero-Rate REIT Secular Bull","title_zh":"后金融危机零利率时代REITs长牛","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:trough:2014-01"},"2020-02-21":{"body":"Between February 21 and March 23, 2020, the WHO declared a global pandemic (March 11), triggering nationwide lockdowns that instantly shuttered retail, office, and hospitality tenants. Hotel REITs fell over 50%, retail REITs nearly 49%. VIX surged from 17 to 62, and Real Estate fell -41.8%, underperforming even Financials (-42.1%) as rent-collection fears overwhelmed the sector. Defensives (Staples -24.3%, Health -27.5%) held up better than cyclicals (-39.4% avg), confirming pure systemic risk-off, not a sector-specific selloff. Oil collapsed -56.2% while TLT rallied +12.3%, as flight-to-safety flows moved into Treasuries — yet REIT's property-income dependence made it uniquely vulnerable despite the bond rally.","body_zh":"2020年2月21日至3月23日，世卫组织宣布全球大流行（3月11日），各地封锁令即刻关闭零售、办公及酒店租户。酒店REITs跌逾50%，零售REITs跌近49%。VIX从17飙升至62，房地产板块下跌41.8%，甚至跑输金融股（-42.1%），因市场对租金收缴能力的恐慌全面压制该板块。防御板块（必需消费-24.3%、医疗-27.5%）跑赢周期股（平均-39.4%），证实这是系统性风险出清而非行业特定事件。油价暴跌56.2%，TLT上涨12.3%，避险资金涌入国债，但REITs依赖物业租金收入的特性使其在债市反弹中依然脆弱。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic declared March 11, 2020","Nationwide lockdowns halting rent collection","VIX spike to 62, systemic risk-off","Commercial property income collapse (hotel, retail)","Dollar strength + oil crash, deflation-scare quad"],"drivers_zh":["2020年3月11日WHO宣布全球大流行","全国封锁导致租金收入中断","VIX飙升至62，系统性风险出清","商业地产（酒店、零售）收入骤停","美元走强+油价暴跌，通缩预期格局"],"prev_key":"2020-02-21","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-21"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID Crash: Commercial RE Demand Collapse","title_zh":"新冠冲击：商业地产需求骤崩","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"On March 23, 2020, the Fed announced unlimited QE, including purchase of MBS, agency CMBS, and corporate bonds via emergency facilities. Congress simultaneously advanced the $2.2 trillion CARES Act (signed March 27). These twin policy shocks crushed the deflation narrative: VIX fell from 62 to 42, dollar weakened 2.9%, and Real Estate (+39.6%) became the second-best sector leader behind Energy (+43.9%). Breadth broadened (RSP beat SPY by +3.9%) and credit spreads tightened (HYG vs LQD +5.3%), reflecting the Fed backstop restoring liquidity across risk assets. The rally lasted only until April 9 as market participants realized rental income losses would persist well beyond the policy response.","body_zh":"2020年3月23日，美联储宣布无限量QE，涵盖MBS、机构CMBS及企业债购买。国会同日推进2.2万亿美元CARES法案（3月27日签署）。双重政策冲击打破通缩预期：VIX从62回落至42，美元走弱2.9%，房地产（+39.6%）成为仅次于能源（+43.9%）的第二强板块。市场广度回升（RSP跑赢SPY +3.9%），信用利差收窄（HYG vs LQD +5.3%），反映美联储兜底恢复流动性。但反弹在4月9日止步，因市场逐渐认识到租金收入损失将持续远超政策应对的预期。","drivers":["Fed unlimited QE announcement March 23, 2020","CARES Act $2.2 trillion fiscal stimulus","VIX compression (62 to 42)","Dollar weakening, credit spread tightening","Broad market bounce, not REIT-specific recovery"],"drivers_zh":["2020年3月23日美联储无限量QE宣布","CARES法案2.2万亿美元财政刺激","VIX压缩（62至42）","美元走弱、信用利差收窄","大盘普涨而非REITs特定复苏"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed QE Bazooka Triggers Panic Bounce","title_zh":"美联储无限QE触发恐慌性反弹","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:trough:2020-03"},"2020-04-09":{"body":"From April 9 to May 13, 2020, the market re-rated its COVID playbook: investors rotated into pandemic winners (Tech +7.8%, Comm +7.4%, Discretionary +5.4% led by e-commerce) while jettisoning rate-sensitive yield assets. Real Estate fell -12.6%, ranking last among rate-sensitive sectors alongside Financials (-11.6%) and Utilities (-9.6%). The SPY was flat-to-positive (+1.2%) while equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -4.0%, confirming a narrow mega-cap-led tape. This was not a rates-driven selloff (TLT was flat, yields stable) but a sector-rotation selloff: institutional capital repriced brick-and-mortar retail and office tenancy risk as work-from-home mandates extended, while growth/tech multiples expanded aggressively.","body_zh":"2020年4月9日至5月13日，市场对新冠行情进行重新定价：资金涌入疫情受益赛道（科技+7.8%、通信+7.4%、电商驱动的非必需消费+5.4%），同时抛售收益率类资产。房地产下跌12.6%，与金融（-11.6%）、公用事业（-9.6%）同属表现最差板块。SPY基本持平（+1.2%），等权跑输市值加权4.0%，确认为窄幅大盘股主导行情。这并非利率驱动的下跌（TLT持平，收益率稳定），而是典型的板块轮动——机构资金重新定价实体零售和办公室租户风险，同时大幅扩张成长/科技估值。","drivers":["COVID-19 WFH mandates extended, office/retail repriced","Mega-cap Tech rotation, narrow breadth","Growth-over-value repricing (growth vs value +11.7%)","REIT rental income uncertainty (no rate trigger)","High-beta vs low-vol divergence +8.3%"],"drivers_zh":["新冠居家办公延续，办公/零售租户风险重定价","大盘科技股轮动，市场广度收窄","成长/价值分化扩大（+11.7%）","REIT租金收入不确定性（非利率触发）","高贝塔大幅跑赢低波动+8.3%"],"prev_key":"2020-04-09","prev_key_chain":["2020-04-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Tech Rotation Leaves REITs Behind","title_zh":"资金轮入科技、REITs相对落后","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:peak:2020-04"},"2020-05-13":{"body":"From May 13, 2020 through December 31, 2021, REITs surged +103.8% in one of the fastest recoveries in sector history. The May 2020 trough marked the start of a vaccine-driven recovery: Moderna and Pfizer Phase 3 data (November 2020) ignited the re-opening trade, while the $1.9 trillion American Rescue Plan (March 2021) and Fed's commitment to keep rates near zero (with the first post-COVID hike not until March 2022) sustained NAV expansion. Cyclicals dramatically outperformed defensives (+85.6% vs +42.1%), oil surged +197.4%, and yields rose (TLT -8.3%) in a classic reflation/growth-up quad. Crucially, even with rising yields, REITs surged because property income recovered: rent collections normalized, industrial and residential REITs saw record demand, and the sector repriced off pandemic lows. Breadth was historically broad (RSP vs SPY +13.2%).","body_zh":"2020年5月13日至2021年12月31日，REITs累计上涨103.8%，创下板块历史最快复苏之一。2020年5月低点标志着疫苗驱动复苏的起点：Moderna与辉瑞三期数据（2020年11月）引燃重开放交易，1.9万亿美元美国援助计划（2021年3月）与美联储维持近零利率的承诺（首次后新冠加息直至2022年3月）持续支撑NAV扩张。周期股大幅跑赢防御股（+85.6% vs +42.1%），油价暴涨197.4%，债券收益率上行（TLT -8.3%），为典型通胀/增长上行格局。关键在于，尽管收益率上升，REITs因物业收入复苏而飙涨：租金收缴正常化，工业和住宅REITs需求创历史新高，板块从疫情低点大幅重估。市场广度历史性宽幅（RSP vs SPY +13.2%）。","drivers":["Pfizer/Moderna vaccine rollout Q4 2020, re-opening trade","American Rescue Plan $1.9T fiscal stimulus March 2021","Fed zero-rate commitment through 2021","Rent collection normalization, industrial/residential REIT demand","Broad reflation quad: oil +197%, cyclicals dominate"],"drivers_zh":["2020年Q4辉瑞/Moderna疫苗推出，重开放交易启动","2021年3月1.9万亿美元美国援助计划","美联储维持零利率至2021年底","租金收缴正常化，工业/住宅REIT需求激增","全面通胀格局：油价+197%，周期股主导"],"prev_key":"2020-05-13","prev_key_chain":["2020-05-13"],"status":"exact","title":"Vaccine Hopes and Reflation Lift All Boats","title_zh":"疫苗预期与通胀预期驱动全面反弹","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:trough:2020-05"},"2021-12-31":{"body":"From January 2022 through June 16, 2022, the Fed pivoted from dovish to aggressively hawkish: the first hike came March 16, 2022 (25bps), followed by 50bps in May and then 75bps in June — the fastest tightening cycle since the 1980s. The 10-year Treasury yield surged from 1.5% to over 3.5% and TLT fell -24.0%, devastating rate-sensitive sectors. Real Estate fell -23.2%, close to SPY's -22.6%. Stagflation-ish conditions prevailed: Energy led +41.4% on oil's +56.3% surge while Tech fell -28.8% and Comm -31.5%, showing this was a regime shift not a growth-led selloff. The equal-weight basket's relative holding vs. SPY (-0.6% difference) reflected REITs repricing in sync with the broader de-rating of long-duration assets as terminal rate expectations ratcheted from sub-1% to above 3.5% within six months.","body_zh":"2022年1月至6月16日，美联储从鸽派急转激进鹰派：2022年3月16日首次加息25bp，5月加息50bp，6月加息75bp，为1980年代以来最快加息周期。10年期美债收益率从1.5%飙升至逾3.5%，TLT大跌24.0%，利率敏感型板块遭受重创。房地产下跌23.2%，接近SPY的-22.6%。滞涨格局主导：能源领涨（+41.4%，受油价+56.3%支撑），科技暴跌-28.8%、通信-31.5%，显示这是利率体制转变而非成长衰退驱动的下跌。等权篮子与SPY差距微小，反映REITs随长久期资产整体重估——终端利率预期在六个月内从不足1%骤升至3.5%以上。","drivers":["Fed rate hike cycle begins March 2022, 75bps in June","10Y Treasury yield surge from 1.5% to 3.5%+ (TLT -24%)","Stagflation quad: energy leads, growth/tech crushed","Terminal rate repricing: market priced 3.5%+ within months","Dollar surge +8.3%, broad long-duration de-rating"],"drivers_zh":["2022年3月美联储启动加息周期，6月加息75bp","10年期美债收益率从1.5%飙升至3.5%以上（TLT -24%）","滞涨格局：能源领涨，成长/科技暴跌","终端利率重定价：市场在数月内将预期推至3.5%以上","美元大涨+8.3%，长久期资产全面重估"],"prev_key":"2021-12-31","prev_key_chain":["2021-12-31"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate Shock: Fed's Fastest Hike Cycle Since 1980s","title_zh":"利率冲击：美联储40年最快加息周期","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:peak:2021-12"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"From June 16 through August 15, 2022, REITs bounced +18.9% in a classic bear-market rally. June 2022 CPI printed 9.1% — the cycle peak — and markets began pricing a 'Fed pivot' narrative as inflation showed early signs of peaking. Growth led over value (+9.2%), semis rallied +20.8%, and VIX fell from 33 to 20 in a 'goldilocks' read. Oil fell -24.0% from its cycle peak, reducing stagflation fears. REITs were not the primary leader (Discretionary +27.4%, Tech +23.0% led), but the broad rate relief (TLT +3.7%) provided a tailwind. The rally proved short-lived: Jackson Hole (August 26, 2022), where Powell delivered his hawkish 'unconditional commitment to price stability' speech, broke the pivot narrative and sent rates back higher.","body_zh":"2022年6月16日至8月15日，REITs反弹18.9%，为典型熊市反弹。2022年6月CPI达到9.1%周期高点，市场开始定价\"美联储转向\"预期，通胀出现触顶迹象。成长跑赢价值（+9.2%），芯片涨20.8%，VIX从33回落至20，呈现\"金发女孩\"格局。油价从周期高点大跌24.0%，滞涨恐慌缓解。REITs并非此轮领涨板块（非必需消费+27.4%、科技+23.0%领先），但总体利率松动（TLT +3.7%）提供顺风。8月26日鲍威尔在杰克逊霍尔发表鹰派\"无条件承诺稳定物价\"演讲，打破转向预期，反弹随即终结。","drivers":["June 2022 CPI 9.1% cycle peak, pivot narrative builds","Jackson Hole August 26, 2022 hawkish pivot breaks rally","Oil -24% from peak, stagflation fears ease","VIX compression 33 to 20, risk-on bounce","TLT +3.7%, modest yield relief"],"drivers_zh":["2022年6月CPI 9.1%见顶，市场定价美联储转向","8月26日杰克逊霍尔鹰派讲话终结反弹","油价从高点暴跌24%，滞涨恐慌消退","VIX压缩（33至20），风险偏好修复","TLT +3.7%，温和利率松动"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Bear Market Bounce: Peak CPI Pivot Hopes","title_zh":"熊市反弹：CPI见顶、美联储转向预期","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-15":{"body":"From August 15 through October 14, 2022, the Fed's Jackson Hole speech (August 26) shattered pivot hopes and markets re-priced the terminal rate above 4.5%. The 10-year yield climbed further (TLT -14.2%), dollar surged +6.3% (DXY), and VIX rose from 20 to 32. Real Estate fell -25.5%, the worst performer in the period per the ctx leaders/laggards data, significantly underperforming SPY (-16.3%). This was a pure rate-shock selloff: defensives (-12.5%) and cyclicals (-13.4%) fell more in sync than usual, confirming the cross-sector de-rating of long-duration assets. REITs underperformed because they carry the highest effective duration among equity sectors, amplifying rate shock into NAV destruction; REIT average NAV discounts widened to near -30% during this period.","body_zh":"2022年8月15日至10月14日，杰克逊霍尔演讲（8月26日）彻底打破转向预期，市场将终端利率重新定价至4.5%以上。10年期美债收益率进一步上行（TLT -14.2%），美元大涨6.3%，VIX从20升至32。房地产下跌25.5%，为该期间最差板块，大幅跑输SPY（-16.3%）。这是纯粹的利率冲击型下跌：防御股（-12.5%）与周期股（-13.4%）同步下跌，确认跨板块长久期资产重估。REITs因股票类资产中有效久期最高，将利率冲击放大为NAV毁损；同期REIT平均NAV折价扩大至近-30%。","drivers":["Jackson Hole August 26, 2022 hawkish speech breaks pivot hopes","Terminal rate repriced above 4.5%, 10Y yield surge (TLT -14%)","Dollar surge +6.3%, cross-sector long-duration de-rating","REIT NAV discounts widened to near -30%","VIX rises 20 to 32, broad risk-off"],"drivers_zh":["8月26日杰克逊霍尔鹰派讲话，转向预期彻底打破","终端利率重定价至4.5%以上，10年期收益率急升（TLT -14%）","美元大涨6.3%，跨板块长久期资产重估","REIT平均NAV折价扩大至近-30%","VIX从20升至32，全面风险厌恶"],"prev_key":"2022-08-15","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole Shock: 'Higher Longer' Crushes REITs","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔冲击：\"更高更久\"重创REITs","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:peak:2022-08"},"2022-10-14":{"body":"From October 14, 2022 through February 2, 2023, Real Estate surged +23.4%, ranking second among all sectors. The October 2022 trough coincided with the DXY peaking (dollar fell -10.2% over the rally window) and yields pulling back (TLT +11.0%), as November 2022 CPI of 7.1% significantly undershot expectations, sparking the first credible 'inflation has peaked' narrative. Cyclicals dominated (cyclicals avg +19.0% vs defensives +10.1%), semis rallied +48.1%, and VIX fell from 32 to 19 in a genuine 'goldilocks' rebound. REITs were co-leaders alongside Materials (+25.4%) as the yield relief directly re-rated their NAVs upward. The Fed slowed to 50bps in December 2022 (from 75bps), reinforcing the view the peak rate was approaching, giving REITs their strongest two-month return since the Feb 2009 GFC trough rally.","body_zh":"2022年10月14日至2023年2月2日，房地产大涨23.4%，板块排名第二。2022年10月低点恰逢美元指数见顶（整个反弹窗口美元下跌10.2%），2022年11月CPI录得7.1%，大幅低于预期，触发首个可信的\"通胀已见顶\"叙事，债券收益率随之回落（TLT +11.0%）。周期股主导（+19.0% vs 防御股+10.1%），芯片涨48.1%，VIX从32回落至19，典型\"金发女孩\"复苏行情。REITs与材料股（+25.4%）共同领涨，利率松动直接推动NAV重估。美联储12月加息放缓至50bp（此前75bp），强化\"政策顶点临近\"判断，REIT录得自2009年2月金融危机低点反弹以来最强的两个月涨幅。","drivers":["November 2022 CPI 7.1% beats low, peak inflation narrative","DXY peaks and falls -10.2%, REIT funding cost relief","TLT +11%, yield pullback re-rates NAV upward","Fed slows to 50bps December 2022, pause narrative builds","VIX 32 to 19, risk-on goldilocks rebound"],"drivers_zh":["2022年11月CPI 7.1%低于预期，通胀见顶叙事形成","美元指数见顶后下跌10.2%，REIT融资成本松动","TLT +11%，收益率回落推动NAV向上重估","美联储2022年12月放缓加息至50bp，暂停预期升温","VIX从32降至19，风险偏好回升至金发女孩格局"],"prev_key":"2022-10-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed Pause Bets and Dollar Peak Ignite REIT Rally","title_zh":"美联储暂停预期与美元见顶点燃REIT反弹","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:trough:2022-10"},"2023-02-02":{"body":"From February 2 through March 23, 2023, REITs fell -18.4% as two sequential shocks hit. First, the January 2023 nonfarm payrolls (released February 3) came in at 517,000 — more than double consensus — triggering a repricing of the Fed terminal rate back above 5%; Powell's February testimony reinforced this hawkish pivot, with TLT slipping -1.5%. Then on March 10, Silicon Valley Bank failed, igniting regional bank panic and adding a second channel of stress: banks held significant commercial real estate debt, and market fears about CRE loan losses and tighter lending standards drove REITs lower independently of rate moves. Financials fell -15.0% and Real Estate -16.6% in a pattern showing financial-stress contagion rather than pure rate shock, even as narrow breadth (RSP lag -5.6%) confirmed flight to mega-cap safety.","body_zh":"2023年2月2日至3月23日，REITs下跌18.4%，两波冲击接连打击板块。首先，2023年1月非农就业（2月3日公布）高达51.7万人，超出市场预期逾一倍，终端利率预期被推回5%以上；鲍威尔2月国会作证进一步强化鹰派立场，TLT小跌1.5%。其次，3月10日硅谷银行倒闭，引发区域银行恐慌，新增第二条压力路径：银行持有大量商业地产贷款，市场对CRE坏账和信贷收紧的担忧独立于利率变动驱动REITs下行。金融股下跌15.0%、房地产-16.6%，呈现金融压力传染而非纯粹利率冲击的特征，同期市场广度收窄（RSP落后5.6%）确认资金向大盘股集中。","drivers":["January 2023 NFP 517k, terminal rate repriced above 5%","Powell February testimony: hawkish, higher-for-longer","Silicon Valley Bank failure March 10, 2023","Regional bank CRE loan exposure contagion","Narrow breadth, mega-cap flight, financial stress"],"drivers_zh":["2023年1月非农就业51.7万，终端利率预期推回5%以上","鲍威尔2月国会听证：鹰派，\"更高更久\"表态","2023年3月10日硅谷银行倒闭","区域银行商业地产贷款敞口引发传染","市场广度收窄，资金涌向大盘股，金融压力蔓延"],"prev_key":"2023-02-03","prev_key_chain":["2023-02-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Hot Data and SVB Shock Reverse REIT Rally","title_zh":"强劲数据叠加硅谷银行冲击终结反弹","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:peak:2023-02"},"2023-03-23":{"body":"From March 23 through July 24, 2023, REITs rallied +17.7% in a tech/AI-led recovery. The FDIC backstop of SVB (March 13) and First Republic (May 1) stabilized the banking sector, removing the acute financial-contagion tail risk for REIT lenders. The AI narrative took hold after OpenAI ChatGPT's explosive growth prompted massive data-center and industrial REIT demand, lifting the sector via sub-sector leadership in digital infrastructure. Cyclicals (+15.8%) led defensives (+7.8%) in a reflation/growth-up context, with semis +19.0% driving the tech melt-up. REITs broadly tracked the market's +16% but did not lead; instead, the rally was tech/growth-led (narrow breadth, RSP -2.9% vs SPY) with REITs benefiting from the VIX compression (23 to 14) and mild dollar softening (-1.2% DXY). Yields continued to gradually rise (TLT -3.7%), capping REITs' upside.","body_zh":"2023年3月23日至7月24日，REITs反弹17.7%，科技/AI领涨带动复苏。FDIC对硅谷银行（3月13日）和第一共和银行（5月1日）的兜底稳定了银行业，消除了REIT贷款端的急性金融传染尾部风险。ChatGPT爆炸式增长带动AI叙事确立，数据中心和工业REIT需求激增，带动板块内数字基础设施子板块领涨。周期股（+15.8%）领先防御股（+7.8%），芯片上涨19.0%，科技成长主导。REITs大体跟随市场+16%的涨幅但并非领涨，行情为科技/成长驱动（市场广度偏窄，RSP落后SPY 2.9%）；VIX压缩（23至14）和美元温和走软（DXY -1.2%）为REITs提供一定支撑，但收益率缓慢上行（TLT -3.7%）限制了上涨空间。","drivers":["FDIC backstop SVB/First Republic, banking crisis stabilized","AI/ChatGPT demand drives data-center and industrial REIT sub-sectors","VIX compression 23 to 14, risk-on recovery","Tech/semis AI melt-up: semis +19%","Mild dollar softening, mild yield headwind (TLT -3.7%)"],"drivers_zh":["FDIC兜底硅谷银行/第一共和银行，银行危机趋稳","AI/ChatGPT需求驱动数据中心和工业REIT子板块","VIX压缩（23至14），风险偏好回升","科技/芯片AI行情：芯片+19%","美元温和走软，收益率小幅上行（TLT -3.7%）限制涨幅"],"prev_key":"2023-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2023-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Banking Crisis Stabilizes, Tech AI Rally Supports REITs","title_zh":"银行业危机趋稳，科技AI浪潮带动REITs修复","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:trough:2023-03"},"2023-07-24":{"body":"From July 24 through October 27, 2023, REITs fell -16.9%, the worst-performing sector (per ctx: Real Estate -16.3% laggard explicitly). The 10-year Treasury yield climbed from ~3.8% to a 16-year high near 5% by October 19, 2023 (TLT -16.0%), driven by 'higher for longer' Fed rhetoric post-July hike, rising term premiums, surging fiscal deficits, and ongoing quantitative tightening. DXY strengthened +5.1% and oil rose +8.6%. Defensives fell harder (-11.3% avg) than cyclicals (-9.2%), but REITs (-16.3%) were the clear outlier: their effective yield-proxy status meant the 10-year yield surge directly competed with REIT dividend yields on a risk-adjusted basis, forcing cap-rate expansion and property-value write-downs. VIX rose only modestly (14 to 21), confirming this was not a systemic panic but a rate-regime repricing with REITs as the primary casualty.","body_zh":"2023年7月24日至10月27日，REITs下跌16.9%，为最差板块（据ctx数据，房地产以-16.3%明确垫底）。10年期美债收益率从约3.8%攀升至10月19日的近16年高点5%（TLT -16.0%），源于7月加息后\"更高更久\"美联储措辞、期限溢价上升、财政赤字激增及量化紧缩持续。美元走强5.1%，油价上涨8.6%。防御板块（平均-11.3%）跌幅反而大于周期股（-9.2%），但REITs（-16.3%）远超跌幅：其作为\"准债券\"替代品的地位意味着10年期收益率飙升直接与REIT股息率形成风险调整后的竞争关系，迫使资本化率扩张和物业价值减记。VIX仅温和上升（14至21），确认这非系统性恐慌而是以REITs为最大受害者的利率体制重定价。","drivers":["10Y Treasury yield climbs to 5%, 16-year high by October 2023","Fed 'higher for longer' rhetoric post-July hike","Rising term premiums and fiscal deficit concerns","QT ongoing: Fed balance sheet reduction continues","REIT yield-proxy status, cap-rate expansion, NAV write-downs"],"drivers_zh":["10年期美债收益率攀升至5%，2023年10月触16年高点","7月加息后美联储\"更高更久\"措辞强化","期限溢价上升与财政赤字忧虑","量化紧缩持续，美联储资产负债表持续缩减","REIT准债券替代品属性，资本化率扩张，NAV减记"],"prev_key":"2023-07-24","prev_key_chain":["2023-07-24"],"status":"exact","title":"10Y Yields Hit 5%: Worst REIT Headwind Since 2007","title_zh":"10年期美债收益率破5%：2007年来REITs最大阻力","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:peak:2023-07"},"2023-10-27":{"body":"From October 27, 2023 through November 27, 2024, REITs surged +48.9% as the rate cycle decisively turned. October 2023 marked the 10-year yield peak near 5%, after which the Fed signaled it was done hiking; the Fed cut 50bps on September 18, 2024 (the first cut since 2020), then 25bps each in November and December 2024. TLT gained +15.1% over this window while oil and commodity prices fell (oil -19.7%, copper-gold -20.8%), reinforcing the 'soft landing / goldilocks' narrative (disinflation without recession). Semis exploded +73.3% on AI demand, and the broader tech melt-up (growth vs value +13.0%) helped lift all long-duration assets including REITs. Real Estate's +48.9% nearly matched SPY's +47.8%, with fund managers sharply re-allocating to REITs as the best direct beneficiary of rate cuts — the largest single positive positioning change among major equity sectors in late 2023 per BofA fund manager surveys.","body_zh":"2023年10月27日至2024年11月27日，REITs大涨48.9%，利率周期决定性转向。2023年10月为10年期美债收益率近5%高点，随后美联储发出停止加息信号；2024年9月18日首次降息50bp（自2020年以来首次），11月和12月各再降25bp。整个窗口期TLT涨15.1%，油价和大宗商品下跌（油-19.7%，铜金比-20.8%），强化\"软着陆/金发女孩\"叙事（去通胀而非衰退）。芯片因AI需求暴涨73.3%，更广泛的科技成长行情（成长vs价值+13.0%）带动包括REITs在内的长久期资产。房地产+48.9%几乎与SPY的+47.8%持平，基金经理大幅增配REITs——据美银基金经理调查，这是2023年底主要股票板块中最大单一正向仓位变化。","drivers":["10Y yield peaks ~5% October 2023, rate cycle turns","Fed cuts 50bps September 18, 2024, first since 2020","TLT +15.1%, goldilocks soft-landing narrative","AI data-center REIT sub-sector demand (semis +73%)","Fund manager REIT re-allocation, largest sector shift"],"drivers_zh":["10年期美债收益率2023年10月见顶约5%，利率周期转向","美联储2024年9月18日降息50bp，自2020年以来首次","TLT +15.1%，软着陆/金发女孩叙事主导","AI数据中心REIT子板块需求（芯片+73%）","基金经理大幅增配REITs，主要板块最大单一仓位变化"],"prev_key":"2023-10-27","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed Pivot and Rate Cuts Drive 13-Month REIT Bull","title_zh":"美联储转向与降息预期驱动REITs13个月牛市","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:trough:2023-10"},"2024-11-27":{"body":"From November 27, 2024 through April 8, 2025, REITs fell -17.6%. The selloff had two phases. Phase 1 (November-December 2024): Trump's election victory repriced term premiums as bond markets anticipated deficit-financed fiscal expansion and protectionist tariffs that would sustain inflation, pushing long yields higher and killing the rate-cut narrative. Phase 2 (January-April 2025): Trump's 'Liberation Day' universal tariff announcement (April 2, 2025) triggered the largest market sell-off since COVID-19, with VIX spiking to 52 and SPY falling -16.6%. Defensives (-8.6% avg) significantly outperformed cyclicals (-18.7% avg), confirming a genuine risk-off flight-to-safety rotation. REITs (-17.6%) tracked the broader cyclical selloff: industrial REITs were directly hit by trade-war disruption to supply-chain warehouse demand, while higher inflation expectations squeezed cap-rate spreads over rising Treasury yields.","body_zh":"2024年11月27日至2025年4月8日，REITs下跌17.6%，分两个阶段。第一阶段（2024年11月至12月）：特朗普胜选后，债券市场预期财政扩张和保护主义关税将维持通胀，期限溢价重定价推高长债收益率，降息预期受压。第二阶段（2025年1月至4月）：特朗普\"解放日\"全球关税宣布（4月2日）触发新冠疫情以来最大市场崩溃，VIX飙升至52，SPY跌16.6%。防御股（平均-8.6%）大幅跑赢周期股（平均-18.7%），确认真实避险/安全轮动。REITs（-17.6%）跟随周期股整体下跌：工业REITs直接受贸易战破坏供应链仓储需求，而通胀预期上升压缩了相对上行美债收益率的资本化率利差。","drivers":["Trump election November 2024, tariff/deficit repricing","Liberation Day April 2, 2025: universal tariffs, VIX to 52","Flight-to-safety: defensives -8.6% vs cyclicals -18.7%","Industrial REIT supply-chain demand disruption","Higher inflation expectations squeeze cap-rate spreads"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普2024年11月当选，关税/财政赤字重定价","4月2日\"解放日\"全球关税冲击，VIX飙升至52","避险轮动：防御股-8.6% vs 周期股-18.7%","工业REIT受贸易战供应链仓储需求冲击","通胀预期上升压缩相对美债收益率的资本化率利差"],"prev_key":"2024-11-27","prev_key_chain":["2024-11-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Trump Election, Tariff Shock, and VIX-52 Risk-Off","title_zh":"特朗普当选、关税冲击与VIX飙升至52的避险格局","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:peak:2024-11"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"From April 8, 2025 through late June 2026, REITs gained +23.6% as the Trump administration announced a 90-day tariff pause (April 9, 2025), which collapsed VIX from 52 to 18 and sparked a broad market recovery. REITs participated in the recovery but significantly lagged: SPY gained +48.5% and Tech +102.7% while Real Estate's +23.6% put it near the bottom alongside Staples (+14.0%). The reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +50.3% vs defensives +22.3%) confirms REITs are tracking defensives, not leading the cyclical recovery. AI infrastructure demand propelled data-center REITs (Digital Realty, Equinix), a structural tailwind unique to the current cycle. Narrow breadth (RSP vs SPY -8.7%) confirms the recovery is dominated by mega-cap tech, leaving equal-weight REITs relatively starved of flows. TLT gained only +4.2% and oil rose +16.2%, suggesting the yield environment remains only modestly supportive, capping REIT re-rating.","body_zh":"2025年4月8日至2026年6月下旬，REITs累计上涨23.6%。特朗普政府宣布90天关税暂停（4月9日），VIX从52骤降至18，引发大盘全面复苏。REITs参与复苏但显著落后：SPY涨48.5%，科技涨102.7%，而房地产+23.6%仅排名靠后，与必需消费（+14.0%）相近。通胀/增长上行格局（周期股+50.3% vs 防御股+22.3%）确认REITs更接近防御属性，而非引领周期复苏。AI基础设施需求推动数据中心REITs（Digital Realty、Equinix）成为结构性顺风，这是当前周期独有的驱动因素。市场广度偏窄（RSP vs SPY -8.7%），确认复苏由大盘科技主导，等权REITs篮子明显缺乏资金青睐。TLT仅上涨4.2%，油价上涨16.2%，收益率环境仅温和支撑，限制了REIT的估值重评空间。","drivers":["90-day tariff pause April 9, 2025, VIX 52 to 18","AI infrastructure: data-center REIT sub-sector demand (Digital Realty, Equinix)","Reflation/growth-up quad, cyclicals dominate, REITs lag","Narrow mega-cap breadth (RSP vs SPY -8.7%)","Modest yield relief only (TLT +4.2%), oil +16.2%"],"drivers_zh":["4月9日90天关税暂停，VIX从52降至18","AI基础设施：数据中心REIT子板块（Digital Realty、Equinix）需求","通胀/增长上行格局，周期股主导，REITs相对落后","大盘科技窄幅领涨（RSP vs SPY -8.7%）","利率松动有限（TLT +4.2%），油价上涨16.2%"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff Pause Recovery, But AI Mega-Caps Lead","title_zh":"关税暂停驱动复苏，但AI大盘科技主导行情","turn_id":"us_sector_realestate:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Real Estate (Equal-Weight) is in a Topping phase at the 94th percentile of its historical return window, posting a SELL signal after a 23.6% rally from the April 2025 trough. The current reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, oil +19.2%, copper-gold +18.3%) is structurally hostile for rate-sensitive REITs: Tech and Energy dominate leadership by a wide margin while Real Estate sits at rs_rank 19 out of the full universe. A stronger DXY (+3.4%) adds friction to financing costs, and TLT has barely moved (+1.1%), meaning the yield relief that typically propels REIT rallies is absent. High-beta has crushed low-vol by +20.7 percentage points, signaling market appetite for risk assets far more levered than real estate. The basket is at a structural cycle peak with deteriorating relative strength, a setup that historically precedes multi-month drawdowns when yields plateau at elevated levels and growth momentum stays concentrated in cyclicals.","now_zh":"美国房地产（等权）板块目前处于\"见顶\"阶段，历史回报百分位高达94%，并发出SELL信号，自2025年4月低点已累计反弹23.6%。当前通胀/增长上行格局（周期股+11.2%、防御股+6.9%、油价+19.2%、铜金比+18.3%）对利率敏感型REITs明显不利：科技与能源主导轮动，房地产相对强弱排名仅第19位。美元持续走强（DXY +3.4%）加大融资成本压力，长债（TLT）几乎原地踏步（+1.1%），驱动REITs上涨的利率下行动力明显缺失。高贝塔大幅跑赢低波动20.7个百分点，反映市场资金追逐进攻性资产。综合来看，板块处于周期顶部区域、相对强弱恶化，历史上这一组合往往预示数月级别回调。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":"housing.bubble_peak.v1","prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":"housing.bubble_peak.v1","arch_state":"missing","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-us_sector_staples":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"From early 2014 through November 2018, Consumer Staples rallied +79.9% in a broad multi-year expansion underpinned by below-target inflation, a collapsing oil price (WTI fell from above $100 to below $30 by early 2016), and a strong dollar (+20% DXY) that suppressed commodity-linked and EM cyclicals. The ctx confirms defensives (+68.5%) led cyclicals (+55.6%) across the full leg despite Tech and Semis also performing well — a classic slow-growth, disinflation environment where low-vol, high-quality staples attracted a structural premium over higher-beta cyclicals. TLT rallied +25.8% (yields fell), which reduced the discount rate for stable-growth franchise names. The period also encompassed the 2015-2016 China devaluation scare and 2015-2016 earnings recession, each episode sending risk-off bids into defensives and boosting Staples' relative standing.","body_zh":"2014年初至2018年11月，必需消费累涨+79.9%，驱动力为低于目标的通胀、油价崩溃（WTI从逾100美元跌至30美元以下）以及强势美元（DXY+20%）压制大宗商品与新兴市场周期股。区间数据确认防御股（+68.5%）整体领先周期股（+55.6%），TLT累涨+25.8%（收益率下行），降低稳定增长特许经营企业的折现率。期间还经历了2015-2016年人民币贬值冲击与企业盈利衰退，每次风险厌恶事件均为防御板块带来避险买盘，进一步强化了必需消费的相对优势。","drivers":["oil-price-collapse-disinflation","strong-dollar-DXY+20%","yields-fell-TLT+25%","low-vol-quality-premium","China-scare-risk-off-episodes"],"drivers_zh":["油价崩溃/通缩","美元强势DXY+20%","收益率下行TLT+25%","低波动质量溢价","中国风险冲击避险买盘"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Disinflation Era: Low-Vol Quality Bid","title_zh":"通缩时代：低波动质量资产溢价","turn_id":"us_sector_staples:trough:2014-01"},"2018-11-09":{"body":"From November 9 to December 24, 2018, Consumer Staples fell -14.1% but held relative to the market (-15.1% SPY) as VIX surged from 17 to 36 — a textbook defensive relative buffer in a broad risk-off flush. The catalyst was Fed Chair Powell's December 19, 2018 press conference, where he described the balance sheet wind-down as on \"autopilot\" while delivering the fourth rate hike of 2018, spooking markets already rattled by US-China trade war escalation and slowing global growth. Cyclicals fell harder (-16.8%) than defensives (-10.5%), consistent with a flight-to-safety rotation, with Energy dropping -20.7% as oil collapsed -29.3%. TLT rose +7.5% as the bond market priced a policy mistake and incoming recession risk.","body_zh":"2018年11月9日至12月24日，必需消费下跌-14.1%，但相对大盘（标普500 -15.1%）体现出防御缓冲特性，波动率指数从17飙升至36。导火索是美联储主席鲍威尔2018年12月19日新闻发布会——他在宣布年内第四次加息的同时，将缩表计划描述为\"自动驾驶\"，引发市场恐慌。此前市场已因中美贸易战升级与全球增长放缓而承压。周期股（-16.8%）大幅落后防御股（-10.5%），能源跌-20.7%，油价崩跌-29.3%，TLT上涨+7.5%，债券市场定价政策失误与衰退风险。","drivers":["Fed-autopilot-comment-Dec-2018","fourth-rate-hike-2018","US-China-trade-war-escalation","oil-crash-29%","global-growth-scare"],"drivers_zh":["美联储\"自动驾驶\"言论","2018年第四次加息","中美贸易战升级","油价暴跌29%","全球增长恐慌"],"prev_key":"2018-11-09","prev_key_chain":["2018-11-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed Autopilot Shock: Q4 2018 Risk-Off Flush","title_zh":"美联储\"自动驾驶\"冲击：2018年四季度恐慌抛售","turn_id":"us_sector_staples:peak:2018-11"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"From December 24, 2018 to February 14, 2020, Consumer Staples gained +37.1% but this was a beta ride in a broad risk-on melt-up rather than a staples-specific story. The Fed's January 4, 2019 \"patient\" pivot — Powell explicitly walking back the autopilot remark and signaling flexibility on both rates and the balance sheet — launched a powerful recovery. Tech led (+79.3%), Semis surged +88.9%, and the growth-over-value spread widened to +23%. Ctx confirms cyclicals (+41.5%) beat defensives (+36.4%) and SPY returned +46.8%, both ahead of Staples at +37.1%. TLT also rose +22.2% (yields fell further as the Fed's three 2019 rate cuts compressed the front end), benefiting rate-sensitive franchises within staples on a valuation basis.","body_zh":"2018年12月24日至2020年2月14日，必需消费上涨+37.1%，但这是宽泛风险偏好反弹中的贝塔跟涨，而非板块主导行情。美联储主席鲍威尔2019年1月4日明确收回\"自动驾驶\"言论并强调政策灵活性，引发全市场强劲反弹。科技领涨（+79.3%），半导体暴涨+88.9%，成长/价值利差扩至+23%。数据确认周期股（+41.5%）领先防御股（+36.4%），标普500回报+46.8%，均超越必需消费+37.1%。TLT同期上涨+22.2%（美联储2019年三次降息压低前端利率），对必需消费内高估值特许经营企业提供估值支撑。","drivers":["Fed-patient-pivot-Jan-2019","three-Fed-cuts-2019","tech-semis-led-risk-on","yields-fell-TLT+22%","VIX-compression-36-to-14"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年1月转鸽","2019年三次降息","科技/半导体主导风险偏好","收益率下行TLT+22%","波动率收缩36→14"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed Pivot Melt-Up; Staples Rides Beta","title_zh":"美联储转鸽引发市场急涨，必需消费随贝塔上行","turn_id":"us_sector_staples:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-14":{"body":"From February 14 to March 23, 2020, Consumer Staples fell -24.0% — the fastest and deepest drawdown since the 2008 crisis — as COVID-19 spread globally, forcing nationwide lockdowns and triggering a VIX explosion to 62. Despite the severity, Staples was the single best-performing sector (shown as the first \"leader\" in ctx at -24.5%), versus Industrials -41.9%, Financials -42.9%, and Energy -55.8%. Oil collapsed -55.1% on Saudi-Russia price war and demand destruction. This was not a staples-specific story: the entire market sold off indiscriminately in the initial panic phase, but the sector's non-cyclical demand profile (food, household goods) meant institutional investors rotated to it as the least-bad risk-off destination, with defensives averaging -29.3% vs cyclicals at -40.1%.","body_zh":"2020年2月14日至3月23日，必需消费下跌-24.0%，为2008年危机以来最快最深回撤，新冠疫情全球蔓延、各国封锁引发恐慌，波动率指数飙升至62。尽管如此，必需消费仍是表现最佳的板块（-24.5%），远好于工业（-41.9%）、金融（-42.9%）、能源（-55.8%）。油价因沙俄价格战与需求崩塌跌-55.1%。这并非板块特有逻辑：初期恐慌阶段全市场无差别抛售，但必需消费非周期性需求特征（食品、日用品）使其成为机构投资者风险规避时的首选避难地，防御板块均值-29.3%明显优于周期板块-40.1%。","drivers":["COVID-19-global-lockdowns","VIX-spike-to-62","oil-collapse-55%-Saudi-Russia-war","universal-panic-selling","defensive-relative-buffer"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情全球封锁","波动率指数飙升至62","油价崩跌55%（沙俄价格战）","全面无差别恐慌抛售","防御板块相对抗跌"],"prev_key":"2020-02-14","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-14"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID Panic: Universal Drawdown, Defensives Buffer","title_zh":"新冠恐慌：全面下跌，防御板块相对抗跌","turn_id":"us_sector_staples:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From March 23, 2020 to April 20, 2022, Consumer Staples gained +95.7% in absolute terms — a large move — but massively underperformed the reflation trade. The Fed cut to zero and purchased $120B/month in assets; Congress passed $2.2T in CARES Act stimulus in late March 2020, followed by additional packages totaling over $5T through 2021. This cyclical reflation drove Energy +277%, Materials +145%, Financials +122.9%, and SPY +105.3%, all well ahead of Staples. Oil surged +339.9% from the March 2020 trough, high-beta beat low-vol by +113.3%, and equal-weight beat cap-weight by +23.3% — every signature of a broad cyclical upcycle. Staples' +95.7% was above-average in absolute terms but the classic LAGGARD in a reflationary environment where pricing power resided in commodities and cyclicals, not in everyday consumer goods.","body_zh":"2020年3月23日至2022年4月20日，必需消费绝对回报+95.7%，但在再通胀周期中大幅跑输。美联储降息至零并每月购买1200亿美元资产；国会3月底通过2.2万亿CARES法案，后续追加刺激总计逾5万亿美元。周期股全面领涨：能源+277%、材料+145%、金融+122.9%，标普500+105.3%，均远超必需消费。油价自2020年3月低点暴涨+339.9%，高贝塔股跑赢低波动股+113.3%，等权跑赢市值加权+23.3%——所有信号均指向宽泛周期性牛市。必需消费+95.7%绝对表现不俗，但在定价权属于大宗商品与周期行业的再通胀环境中，始终是经典落后者。","drivers":["Fed-QE-zero-rates","CARES-Act-5T-fiscal-stimulus","oil-surge-339%","cyclical-reflation-broadening","high-beta-dominance"],"drivers_zh":["美联储QE+零利率","CARES法案5万亿财政刺激","油价暴涨339%","周期性再通胀宽泛上涨","高贝塔主导"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Fiscal Stimulus Boom; Cyclicals Lead, Staples Lags","title_zh":"财政刺激狂潮：周期股领涨，必需消费落后","turn_id":"us_sector_staples:trough:2020-03"},"2022-04-20":{"body":"From April 20 to September 30, 2022, Consumer Staples fell -15.4%, slightly worse than defensives (-14.1%) and better than cyclicals (-18.5%) and SPY (-19.0%). The Fed began its fastest tightening cycle since the 1980s: 50bp in May 2022 followed by four consecutive 75bp hikes starting June 2022, responding to CPI that hit 8.3% in April and 9.1% in June 2022. The DXY surged +11.7% as the dollar carry became attractive vs all G10 peers. TLT fell -15.0% (10-year yields rose from ~2.8% in April to ~4.0% by September) — a severe headwind for Consumer Staples' bond-proxy characteristics and a compression of the rich valuation multiples the sector had accumulated. Staples also faced input cost inflation (food, packaging, labor) compressing gross margins even as revenues held up, limiting upside vs pure bond-proxy exposure.","body_zh":"2022年4月20日至9月30日，必需消费下跌-15.4%，略差于防御板块均值（-14.1%），但好于周期板块（-18.5%）和标普500（-19.0%）。美联储开启自1980年代以来最激进的紧缩周期：2022年5月加息50bp，随后从6月起连续四次加息75bp，以应对4月CPI达8.3%、6月达9.1%的高通胀。美元指数飙升+11.7%，TLT下跌-15.0%（10年期收益率从约2.8%升至约4.0%）——对必需消费类债券代理特性构成严峻压力，并压缩其此前积累的高估值溢价。板块同时面临食品、包装、劳动力等投入成本通胀压缩毛利率，限制了绝对回报空间。","drivers":["Fed-75bp-hike-cycle","CPI-9.1%-June-2022","10yr-yield-surge-2.8%-to-4%","DXY-surge-11.7%","bond-proxy-valuation-compression"],"drivers_zh":["美联储75bp加息周期","2022年6月CPI达9.1%","10年期收益率从2.8%升至4%","美元指数飙升11.7%","类债券估值压缩"],"prev_key":"2022-04-20","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Aggressive Fed Hikes Compress Bond-Proxy Valuations","title_zh":"美联储激进加息压缩类债券防御估值","turn_id":"us_sector_staples:peak:2022-04"},"2022-09-30":{"body":"From September 30, 2022 to May 1, 2023, Consumer Staples gained +16.2%, participating in a broad risk-on recovery but again lagging SPY (+17.3%) and cyclicals (+17.1% vs defensives +12.1%). The DXY reversed -8.9% from its September peak as the market priced Fed deceleration — the Fed slowed to 50bp in December 2022 and 25bp in February 2023, and Powell stated on February 1, 2023 that \"the disinflationary process has started.\" Semis surged +36.1% and Tech/Comm led, indicating capital rotated back into beaten-down growth assets, not defensives. Staples' +16.2% is explained primarily by index beta and the unwinding of the extreme de-rating from the prior selloff, not any sector-specific catalyst.","body_zh":"2022年9月30日至2023年5月1日，必需消费上涨+16.2%，参与宽泛风险偏好反弹，但再度落后标普500（+17.3%）与周期板块（+17.1% vs 防御+12.1%）。美元指数从9月高点回落-8.9%，市场定价美联储放缓节奏——12月降至加息50bp，2023年2月放缓至25bp，鲍威尔2023年2月1日表示\"通胀回落进程已经开始\"。半导体暴涨+36.1%，科技/通信领涨，资金重回超卖成长股而非防御板块。必需消费+16.2%主要由市场贝塔与前期过度杀估值修复解释，并无板块特有催化剂。","drivers":["Fed-deceleration-50bp-25bp","CPI-disinflation-narrative","DXY-reversal-8.9%","semis-tech-led-recovery","beaten-down-beta-unwind"],"drivers_zh":["美联储放缓加息步伐","CPI通胀回落叙事","美元指数回落8.9%","半导体/科技领涨","超卖修复贝塔反弹"],"prev_key":"2022-09-30","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-30"],"status":"exact","title":"Goldilocks Disinflation Hope Lifts All Boats","title_zh":"金发女孩通胀回落预期推动普涨行情","turn_id":"us_sector_staples:trough:2022-09"},"2023-05-01":{"body":"From May 1 to October 12, 2023, Consumer Staples fell -17.1% — the worst absolute decline in the dataset outside of the COVID crash — while the S&P 500 rose +5.1%. This is a distinctive pattern: SPY positive while defensives collapse, driven by dual compression forces. First, the 10-year Treasury yield surged from ~3.4% in May to a 16-year high above 5.0% in mid-October 2023 (the \"Treasury Tantrum of 2023\"), driven by strong employment, unexpected Treasury supply, and Fed \"higher for longer\" messaging — directly repricing bond-proxy sectors like Staples and Utilities (Utilities fell -13.8%). Second, the Magnificent Seven / generative AI narrative launched by ChatGPT's November 2022 debut attracted massive flows into mega-cap Tech (+13.8%), pulling assets out of low-growth defensives. Equal-weight lagged cap-weight by -7.3%, breadth was narrow, and high-beta beat low-vol by +12.5% — a combination that is precisely hostile to equal-weight Staples.","body_zh":"2023年5月1日至10月12日，必需消费下跌-17.1%——除新冠崩盘外数据集内最大绝对跌幅——而标普500同期上涨+5.1%。这是典型的\"防御股独立崩跌\"形态，由双重压缩力驱动。其一，10年期美国国债收益率从5月约3.4%飙升至10月中旬逾5.0%（\"2023年国债抛售\"），强劲就业数据、意外增加的国债供给与美联储\"高利率更持久\"表态共同驱动，直接压缩必需消费、公用事业等类债券板块估值。其二，ChatGPT掀起的\"七巨头\"/生成式AI叙事吸引大量资金涌入大盘科技股（+13.8%），抽离低增长防御类资产。等权跑输市值加权-7.3%，市场宽度狭窄，高贝塔跑赢低波动+12.5%——对等权必需消费极为不利的组合。","drivers":["10yr-yield-to-5%-Treasury-tantrum-2023","Fed-higher-for-longer","AI-Magnificent7-mega-cap-flows","bond-proxy-double-compression","EW-lagged-CW-7.3%"],"drivers_zh":["10年期收益率破5%（2023年国债抛售）","美联储\"高利率更持久\"","AI/七巨头大盘科技吸资","类债券双重压缩","等权跑输市值加权7.3%"],"prev_key":"2023-05-01","prev_key_chain":["2023-05-01"],"status":"exact","title":"AI Mania + 5% Yields Crush Bond-Proxy Defensives","title_zh":"AI狂潮叠加5%国债收益率重创类债券防御股","turn_id":"us_sector_staples:peak:2023-05"},"2023-10-12":{"body":"From October 12, 2023 to February 24, 2026, Consumer Staples gained +32.8% — a major leg, but the clear laggard in a historic AI/tech bull cycle. SPY returned +63.1%, Semis +179.2%, and cyclicals averaged +55.0% vs defensives +47.8%. The 10-year yield peaked near 5% in October 2023 and then fell as disinflation resumed and the Fed delivered its first rate cut in September 2024 (followed by two more in 2024 H2), with TLT gaining +15.1% across the full leg — a meaningful tailwind for Staples' bond-proxy valuation. The DXY fell -8.2%, which helped multinationals in the basket. However, Staples' gain of +32.8% vs SPY's +63.1% illustrates that capital was primarily deployed into the AI/Mag7 infrastructure theme; defensive catch-up in late 2025 and early 2026 — as tariff uncertainty and tech valuation fears triggered a rotation — provided a late-leg boost that brought Staples to a peak in February 2026.","body_zh":"2023年10月12日至2026年2月24日，必需消费上涨+32.8%——虽是重大腿，但在历史性AI/科技牛市中明显落后。标普500回报+63.1%，半导体+179.2%，周期板块均值+55.0%，防御板块均值+47.8%。10年期收益率从2023年10月峰值约5%随后回落，美联储2024年9月首次降息（2024年下半年再降两次），TLT整个区间上涨+15.1%，为必需消费类债券估值提供实质性支撑。美元指数下跌-8.2%，利好篮子内跨国企业。然而必需消费+32.8% vs 标普500+63.1%的差距，清晰表明资金主要流向AI/七巨头基础设施主题；防御板块在2025年末至2026年初因关税不确定性与科技估值担忧引发轮动而实现补涨，为本轮上涨尾声提供助力，推动必需消费于2026年2月触顶。","drivers":["Fed-rate-cuts-Sep-2024","10yr-yield-peak-reversal","DXY-decline-8.2%","AI-Magnificent7-mega-cap-dominance","tariff-uncertainty-late-defensive-rotation"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2024年9月降息","10年期收益率见顶回落","美元指数下跌8.2%","AI/七巨头主导行情","关税不确定性触发尾段防御轮动"],"prev_key":"2023-10-12","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Goldilocks + Fed Cuts; Staples Recovers, Lags AI Tape","title_zh":"金发女孩格局+美联储降息：必需消费回升但落后AI行情","turn_id":"us_sector_staples:trough:2023-10"}},"now":"Consumer Staples (Equal-Weight) is in an Expansion/Trending phase at 43.9% of its historical range (position 43.9), well above the 200-day moving average, with a BUY signal, but ranks only 29th in relative strength versus peers — confirming it is participating in the rally without leading it. The current regime is reflation/growth-up: cyclicals (+11.2%) are running well ahead of defensives (+6.9%), with Tech, Energy, and Industrials all posting double-digit YTD gains while Staples captures mid-single-digit gains. Oil up 19.2% and copper-gold +18.3% underscore the reflationary tilt, which structurally pulls flows away from bond-proxy defensives like Staples. The DXY is up 3.4%, a mild headwind for multinationals in the basket. Staples is above water and trending but is a laggard in this cyclical tape — consistent with its historical pattern of participation without leadership when growth assets are in the driver's seat.","now_zh":"必需消费（等权）目前处于扩张/趋势阶段，历史区间位置43.9%，站稳200日均线，系统信号为买入，但相对强度排名仅第29位，显示该板块跟随市场上涨而非领涨。当前宏观格局为再通胀/增长向上：周期股（+11.2%）明显领先防御股（+6.9%），科技、能源与工业均录得两位数涨幅，必需消费仅跟随。油价+19.2%、铜金比+18.3%强化了再通胀主题，在此环境下资金结构性流出类债券防御板块。美元指数上涨3.4%，对篮子内跨国企业构成温和阻力。整体而言，必需消费处于上涨但落后于周期股的典型状态，与历史上增长资产主导时该板块参与但不领跑的规律一致。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-us_sector_tech":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"The Fed held the federal funds rate at 0-0.25% throughout this entire leg, suppressing the discount rate and inflating multiples on long-duration growth assets. FANG stocks (Facebook IPO 2012, Amazon AWS ramp, Netflix streaming, Google/Alphabet) drove a narrow leadership rally while energy and materials were crushed by the 2014-15 oil collapse (WTI from ~$100 to ~$35). The 'slowdown/deflation-scare' quad — TLT +18.8%, oil -36.5% — paradoxically favored Tech and Utilities (rate-sensitive proxies) over classic cyclicals, while growth outpaced value (+5.4%). Semis led with +40.6% (SMH), reflecting smartphone/PC cycle strength and the first wave of cloud server buildout.","body_zh":"美联储在整个上涨周期内将联邦基金利率维持在0-0.25%，压低折现率并推高长久期成长资产的估值倍数。Facebook、亚马逊AWS、Netflix流媒体、谷歌等FANG股票主导了集中领涨行情，而能源和材料板块则受到2014-15年油价崩溃拖累（WTI从约100美元跌至约35美元）。尽管处于'经济放缓/通缩恐慌'象限（TLT+18.8%，油价-36.5%），但科技与公用事业（利率敏感替代品）优于传统周期行业，成长股跑赢价值股（+5.4%）。半导体领涨+40.6%（SMH），反映智能手机/PC周期强劲及云服务器建设初潮。","drivers":["ZIRP/low discount rate","FANG secular growth","oil collapse deflationary tailwind","semis/cloud ramp","USD strong DXY+16.8%"],"drivers_zh":["零利率/低折现率","FANG长期成长","油价暴跌通缩顺风","半导体/云计算起步","美元强势DXY+16.8%"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"ZIRP melt-up: FANG dominance, semis surge","title_zh":"零利率熔涨：FANG主导，半导体飙升","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:trough:2014-01"},"2015-06-22":{"body":"China's August 11-14, 2015 yuan devaluation (PBOC cut midpoint by ~3.5% over two sessions), combined with the Shanghai Composite's 43% plunge from its June 2015 peak, triggered a global growth-scare. VIX spiked from 13 to 36; the August 24 'Black Monday' saw world markets wipe ~$10 trillion in value. Tech (EW) fell -15.9%, worse than defensives (-6.3%) but less than Energy (-22.9%) and Materials (-19.2%), consistent with the flight-to-safety rotation the ctx captures: cyclicals -14.4% vs defensives -6.3%. Semis dropped -21.5% (SMH), confirming the selloff was a global-demand/risk-off rotation rather than idiosyncratic tech weakness.","body_zh":"2015年8月11-14日，中国人民银行两次下调人民币中间价（累计约3.5%），叠加上证综指从6月高点暴跌43%，引发全球经济增长恐慌。VIX从13飙升至36；8月24日'黑色星期一'单日全球市场蒸发约10万亿美元。科技（等权）下跌-15.9%，跌幅介于防御板块（-6.3%）与能源（-22.9%）、材料（-19.2%）之间，与避险轮动特征吻合：周期板块-14.4%，防御板块-6.3%。半导体SMH下跌-21.5%，确认此次抛售属于全球需求/风险规避轮动，非科技板块自身问题。","drivers":["China yuan devaluation Aug 2015","Shanghai crash -43% from peak","global growth scare","VIX spike 13→36","oil -34% deflation signal"],"drivers_zh":["中国人民币贬值2015年8月","上证指数从高点跌43%","全球增长恐慌","VIX从13飙至36","油价-34%通缩信号"],"prev_key":"2015-06-22","prev_key_chain":["2015-06-22"],"status":"exact","title":"China 'Black Monday' devaluation shock rout","title_zh":"中国'黑色星期一'人民币贬值冲击","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:peak:2015-06"},"2015-08-25":{"body":"After VIX peaked at 36 on August 24, a sharp volatility mean-reversion powered cyclicals and Tech off the lows. Tech led the snap-back at +18.2% (top sector), with Energy +16.6% and Discretionary +15.2%, while defensives lagged badly (Utilities +3.7%, Real Estate +3.5%). Semis surged +23.7% (SMH). The reflation quad returned (cyclicals +14.7% vs defensives +6.7%) as the market priced in no imminent Fed hike — the FOMC skipped its September 2015 meeting, citing 'global economic and financial developments.' Dollar strength continued (DXY +5.6%), and breadth was narrow (RSP -2.4% vs SPY), typical of a mega-cap snap-back.","body_zh":"VIX于8月24日见顶36后，波动率急速均值回归，推动周期行业和科技板块从低点反弹。科技以+18.2%领涨所有板块，能源+16.6%，非必需消费品+15.2%，而防御板块明显落后（公用事业+3.7%，房地产+3.5%）。半导体SMH飙升+23.7%。随着市场预期美联储不会立即加息（美联储9月例会决定暂缓加息，理由是'全球经济和金融形势'），再通胀象限重现（周期行业+14.7%，防御板块+6.7%）。美元持续强势（DXY+5.6%），但市场广度偏窄（等权RSP落后SPY 2.4%），为典型的大盘股主导反弹。","drivers":["VIX mean-reversion from 36","Fed skips Sep-2015 hike","cyclical oversold rebound","semis short squeeze","dollar strength DXY+5.6%"],"drivers_zh":["VIX从36均值回归","美联储跳过2015年9月加息","周期股超卖反弹","半导体空头回补","美元强势DXY+5.6%"],"prev_key":"2015-08-25","prev_key_chain":["2015-08-25"],"status":"exact","title":"Volatility mean-reversion: cyclicals snap back","title_zh":"波动率均值回归：周期股反弹","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:trough:2015-08"},"2015-12-01":{"body":"The Fed raised rates on December 16, 2015 — the first hike since June 2006 — lifting the funds rate from 0-0.25% to 0.25-0.5%. The move coincided with a brutal January 2016 selloff driven by twin shocks: oil crashing below $30/bbl (WTI fell another -33% in this window) and China's stock circuit breakers triggering twice in the first week of 2016. VIX rose from 15 to 27. The ctx shows a classic flight-to-safety: defensives held near flat (-0.5%) while cyclicals fell -14.4%, semis dropped -15.6%. Tech (EW) -18.7% reflected its beta to global growth expectations and the rate-shock repricing of long-duration multiples.","body_zh":"美联储于2015年12月16日加息——这是自2006年6月以来首次——将联邦基金利率从0-0.25%上调至0.25-0.5%。与此同时，油价暴跌至30美元/桶以下（WTI本段跌幅达-33%），且2016年第一周中国股市熔断机制两度触发，双重冲击叠加引发暴跌。VIX从15升至27。市场呈典型避险轮动：防御板块接近持平（-0.5%），而周期行业下跌-14.4%，半导体SMH下跌-15.6%。科技（等权）-18.7%，反映其对全球增长预期和长久期估值重估的双重敞口。","drivers":["Dec-2015 first Fed hike since 2006","oil below $30 WTI","China circuit breakers Jan-2016","growth scare global","VIX 15→27"],"drivers_zh":["2015年12月首次加息自2006年","WTI油价跌破30美元","中国熔断机制2016年1月","全球增长恐慌","VIX从15升至27"],"prev_key":"2015-12-01","prev_key_chain":["2015-12-01"],"status":"exact","title":"First Fed hike since 2006 triggers growth scare","title_zh":"2006年来首次加息引发增长恐慌","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:peak:2015-12"},"2016-02-09":{"body":"The 2.5-year, +157.9% mega-bull spanned three distinct phases. First (Feb-Nov 2016): commodity/energy bottom, China stimulus, and oil recovering from $26 to $55. Second (Nov 2016–Jan 2018): Trump's election shock and the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (signed Dec 22, 2017, reducing corporate rate 35%→21%) lit a fire under cyclicals and tech buybacks. Third (Jan–Sep 2018): tech earnings acceleration (FAANG combined revenue grew ~25% YoY), with cloud computing (AWS, Azure, GCP) entering hypergrowth. Semis surged +140.6% (SMH); growth beat value by +29.9pp; VIX compressed 27→13. The ctx confirms a full reflation/growth-up cycle with cyclicals +70.3% vs defensives +29.9%.","body_zh":"长达2.5年、涨幅+157.9%的超级牛市分三个阶段：一、（2016年2月-11月）大宗商品/能源触底，中国刺激政策出台，油价从26美元回升至55美元；二、（2016年11月-2018年1月）特朗普当选带来选举冲击，《减税与就业法案》于2017年12月22日签署（企业税率从35%降至21%），周期股和科技股回购均受提振；三、（2018年1-9月）科技公司盈利加速（FAANG合计营收同比增约25%），云计算（AWS、Azure、GCP）进入超速成长期。半导体SMH飙升+140.6%，成长股跑赢价值股+29.9个百分点，VIX从27压缩至13。周期行业+70.3%，防御板块+29.9%，确认为完整再通胀/增长上行周期。","drivers":["Trump TCJA corporate tax cut Dec-2017","FAANG earnings acceleration","cloud/AWS hypergrowth","semi cycle upcycle semis+140%","oil recovery $26→$55"],"drivers_zh":["特朗普《减税与就业法案》2017年12月","FAANG盈利加速","云计算/AWS超速增长","半导体上行周期+140%","油价从26美元回升至55美元"],"prev_key":"2016-02-09","prev_key_chain":["2016-02-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Longest post-war bull run: FAANG, Trump tax cuts, semis","title_zh":"战后最长牛市：FAANG、特朗普减税、半导体","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:trough:2016-02"},"2018-09-04":{"body":"The Fed raised rates four times in 2018 (cumulative +100bps, funds rate reaching 2.25-2.5%), and Powell's Dec 19 FOMC statement signaling further hikes triggered panic — the worst December for the Dow since 1931. Tech (EW) fell -23.2% alongside semis -24.8% (SMH); the ctx shows a flight-to-safety rotation: defensives -7.2% vs cyclicals -21.7%, VIX 13→36, TLT +2.0%. US-China trade war escalated (25% tariffs on $250bn of Chinese goods by October 2018), hitting chip supply chains hard. Oil fell -39.1% as global growth fears intensified, and the Philadelphia Semiconductor Index dropped ~25% in the quarter.","body_zh":"美联储2018年累计加息4次（合计+100个基点，联邦基金利率升至2.25-2.5%）；12月19日鲍威尔FOMC声明暗示继续加息，引发恐慌——道指创1931年以来最差12月表现。科技（等权）下跌-23.2%，半导体SMH下跌-24.8%；避险轮动特征明显：防御板块-7.2%，周期行业-21.7%，VIX从13升至36，TLT+2.0%。美中贸易战升级（2018年10月对2500亿美元中国商品加征25%关税），重创芯片供应链。油价下跌-39.1%，全球增长恐慌加剧，费城半导体指数当季下跌约25%。","drivers":["Fed four 2018 rate hikes over-tightening","US-China trade war $250bn tariffs","Powell hawkish Dec-2018 signal","semi supply chain disruption","oil -39% growth scare"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2018年四次加息过度紧缩","美中贸易战2500亿美元关税","鲍威尔2018年12月鹰派信号","半导体供应链扰动","油价-39%增长恐慌"],"prev_key":"2018-09-04","prev_key_chain":["2018-09-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-shock + trade-war: tech leads cyclical rout","title_zh":"加息冲击+贸易战：科技领跌周期行业","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:peak:2018-09"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"On January 4, 2019, Powell explicitly pivoted — promising 'patience' on rate hikes — and the Fed delivered three insurance cuts later in 2019 (Jul, Sep, Oct). This 'Powell Put' removed the tightening overhang and restarted the growth/tech trade. The US-China Phase One trade truce (announced Dec 2018, signed Jan 15, 2020) reduced tariff tail risk. Tech (EW) gained +72.7% in 14 months, led by semis (+89.3%, SMH) as chip demand recovered and cloud capex accelerated. TLT returned +21.2% (falling yields), growth beat value +22.5pp, and VIX compressed 36→14 — a classic risk-on reopening. Breadth was narrow (RSP -6.5% vs SPY), indicating FANG mega-caps concentrated the gains.","body_zh":"2019年1月4日，鲍威尔明确转向——承诺对加息'保持耐心'——美联储随后在2019年7月、9月、10月连续三次降息（保险性降息）。'鲍威尔看跌期权'消除了紧缩压力，成长/科技交易重启。美中第一阶段贸易协议（2018年12月宣布，2020年1月15日签署）降低了关税尾部风险。科技（等权）14个月内上涨+72.7%，半导体SMH领涨+89.3%，芯片需求回升、云计算资本开支加速。TLT回报+21.2%（利率下行），成长股跑赢价值股+22.5个百分点，VIX从36压缩至14——典型的风险开启行情。市场广度偏窄（等权RSP落后SPY 6.5%），说明涨幅集中于FANG大盘股。","drivers":["Powell Jan-4-2019 pivot to patience","three 2019 Fed insurance cuts","US-China Phase One trade truce","FANG mega-cap concentration","TLT+21.2% falling yields"],"drivers_zh":["鲍威尔2019年1月4日转向耐心政策","美联储2019年三次保险性降息","美中第一阶段贸易协议","FANG大盘股集中领涨","TLT+21.2%利率下行"],"prev_key":"2018-12-24","prev_key_chain":["2018-12-24"],"status":"exact","title":"Powell pivot + trade truce reignites FAANG/semis","title_zh":"鲍威尔转向+贸易休战重燃FANG/半导体","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-12":{"body":"Global equity markets peaked February 19-20, 2020, as COVID-19 spread from China to Europe and the US. By March 18, the VIX spiked to 76 (intraday peak ~83 on March 16), circuit breakers triggered on the NYSE on three separate days, and the S&P 500 fell -34% in 33 calendar days — among the fastest bear markets on record. Tech (EW) dropped -34.3%, in line with the broad market but slightly better than cyclicals (-37.4%). The ctx shows a flight-to-safety pattern (defensives -17.7% vs cyclicals -37.4%), oil collapsed -60.2% (OPEC+ price war launched March 6), and TLT barely gained +0.8% as the initial dash-for-cash even hit Treasuries. Semis fell -33.1% (SMH). Tech's equal-weight losses matched SPY's — no sector immunity in a synchronized crash.","body_zh":"2020年2月19-20日，随着新冠病毒从中国蔓延至欧洲和美国，全球股市见顶。至3月18日，VIX飙至76（3月16日盘中高点约83），纽交所三次触发熔断机制，标普500在33个日历天内暴跌-34%——史上最快熊市之一。科技（等权）下跌-34.3%，与大市基本同步，但略优于周期行业（-37.4%）。避险轮动特征明显：防御板块-17.7%，周期行业-37.4%；油价崩跌-60.2%（3月6日OPEC+发动价格战）；连美债TLT也仅微涨+0.8%（抢现金效应初期冲击国债）。半导体SMH下跌-33.1%。科技等权跌幅与SPY相当——同步崩盘无任何板块幸免。","drivers":["COVID-19 global lockdown shock","VIX spike 14→76","NYSE circuit breakers triggered","OPEC+ oil price war -60%","dash-for-cash across all assets"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情全球封锁冲击","VIX从14飙至76","纽交所三次触发熔断","OPEC+价格战油价-60%","全资产类别抢现金效应"],"prev_key":"2020-02-12","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-12"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic shutdown: broadest crash since 1987","title_zh":"新冠疫情：1987年以来最大范围崩盘","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"The Fed cut rates to 0-0.25% on March 15 and launched $700bn QE (ultimately growing its balance sheet from $4.2tn to $8.8tn by end-2021). Congress passed the $2.2tn CARES Act (March 27), followed by multiple further rounds of fiscal stimulus. Tech (EW) surged +199.5% in 21 months — a 3x return — outpacing even the monster Energy recovery (+161%). The ctx shows semis led at +217.1% (SMH), growth beat value +37.8pp, VIX collapsed 76→18, and breadth was genuinely broad (equal-weight beat SPY by +8.6%), unlike typical tech-melt-ups. COVID forced an accelerated digital transformation: remote work (Zoom, Microsoft Teams), e-commerce (Amazon), cloud (AWS/Azure/GCP) and streaming all saw multi-year adoption compressed into months. Dollar weakness (-5.0% DXY) added a further tailwind.","body_zh":"美联储于3月15日降息至0-0.25%，启动7000亿美元量化宽松（最终将资产负债表从4.2万亿美元扩至2021年底8.8万亿美元）。国会通过2.2万亿美元《CARES法案》（3月27日），随后多轮财政刺激接续出台。科技（等权）在21个月内飙升+199.5%——三倍回报——甚至超越能源板块的强劲复苏（+161%）。半导体SMH领涨+217.1%，成长股跑赢价值股+37.8个百分点，VIX从76压缩至18，且市场广度真实扩散（等权跑赢SPY +8.6%），有别于典型的大盘股主导熔涨。新冠疫情推动数字化转型提速：远程办公（Zoom、Teams）、电商（亚马逊）、云计算（AWS/Azure/GCP）和流媒体均将数年的渗透进程压缩至数月完成。美元走弱（DXY -5.0%）提供额外顺风。","drivers":["Fed 0% rates + $4.6tn QE","CARES Act $2.2tn fiscal stimulus","COVID digital transformation acceleration","semis +217% cloud/AI buildout","dollar weakness DXY -5%"],"drivers_zh":["美联储零利率+4.6万亿美元QE","《CARES法案》2.2万亿美元财政刺激","新冠驱动数字化转型提速","半导体+217%云计算/AI基础设施","美元走弱DXY -5%"],"prev_key":"2020-03-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-18"],"status":"exact","title":"Zero-rate QE + digital acceleration: biggest tech bull","title_zh":"零利率QE+数字化加速：史上最大科技牛市","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:trough:2020-03"},"2021-12-27":{"body":"CPI hit 7.0% YoY in December 2021 (a 40-year high), forcing the Fed to pivot hawkish. The Fed raised rates 425bps in 2022 — the most aggressive tightening since Volcker — beginning March 2022 with a 25bp hike, then four consecutive 75bp hikes starting June. TLT crashed -24.4%, the worst bond year since 1788, repricing long-duration growth multiples violently. Tech (EW) fell -30.8%; semis lost -35.6% (SMH); growth underperformed value by -17.2pp — a complete reversal of the 2020-21 regime. Russia's Ukraine invasion (Feb 24, 2022) added an oil supply shock (+55.6%) and a stagflation overlay (the quad explicitly reads 'stagflation-ish'). Energy was the only GICS sector to post a positive return (+39.9%), confirming this was a pure anti-growth, anti-duration rotation.","body_zh":"2021年12月CPI同比达7.0%（40年高点），迫使美联储急转鹰派。2022年美联储累计加息425个基点——自沃尔克时代以来最激进的紧缩——从3月25个基点起步，6月起连续四次大幅加息75个基点。TLT暴跌-24.4%，创1788年以来最差债券年度，对长久期成长股估值产生剧烈冲击。科技（等权）下跌-30.8%；半导体SMH亏损-35.6%；成长股落后价值股-17.2个百分点——完全逆转2020-21年格局。俄乌战争（2022年2月24日）叠加油价供应冲击（+55.6%）和滞胀背景（象限明确标注'滞胀类'）。能源成为唯一正回报GICS板块（+39.9%），印证这是纯粹的反成长、反久期轮动。","drivers":["Fed 425bp hikes fastest since Volcker","CPI 9.1% June-2022 40-year high","Russia-Ukraine oil shock Feb-2022","TLT -24.4% duration repricing","growth-to-value rotation -17.2pp"],"drivers_zh":["美联储425bp加息自沃尔克以来最快","CPI 2022年6月9.1%四十年高位","俄乌战争供油冲击2022年2月","TLT -24.4%久期重估","成长转价值轮动-17.2个百分点"],"prev_key":"2021-12-27","prev_key_chain":["2021-12-27"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-shock bear: fastest Fed tightening in 40 years","title_zh":"加息冲击熊市：40年最快紧缩周期","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:peak:2021-12"},"2022-06-16":{"body":"Tech (EW) rebounded +23.6% from mid-June to mid-August 2022 as the market priced an imminent Fed pivot. June CPI printed 9.1% on July 13 — the headline peak — and markets immediately began trading a 'CPI has peaked' narrative. The reflation/growth-up quad read (cyclicals +15.4% vs defensives +14.2%) was narrow, and semis rose +20.8% (SMH) as short-covering drove the move. However, Powell's August 26 Jackson Hole speech ('restoring price stability will require holding policy at a restrictive level for some time') was deliberately hawkish, explicitly warning against premature easing. This terminated the bounce and drove the next leg lower.","body_zh":"2022年6月中旬至8月中旬，科技（等权）反弹+23.6%，市场押注美联储即将转向。7月13日公布的CPI同比9.1%创本轮高点，市场立即开始交易'通胀见顶'叙事。再通胀/增长上行象限（周期行业+15.4%，防御板块+14.2%），差距较窄；半导体SMH+20.8%，空头回补主导行情。然而，鲍威尔8月26日杰克逊霍尔演讲明确偏鹰（'恢复价格稳定需要在一段时间内维持限制性政策'），明确警告不应过早宽松，终结了本轮反弹，将市场推入下一跌段。","drivers":["CPI June-2022 9.1% peak narrative","bear market short-covering","growth/tech oversold snap-back","Fed pivot expectations premature","semis +20.8% SMH short cover"],"drivers_zh":["2022年6月CPI 9.1%通胀见顶叙事","熊市空头回补","成长/科技超卖反弹","市场过早押注美联储转向","半导体SMH+20.8%空头回补"],"prev_key":"2022-06-16","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-16"],"status":"exact","title":"Bear-market bounce: pivot hopes, CPI peak narrative","title_zh":"熊市反弹：押注转向、CPI见顶叙事","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:trough:2022-06"},"2022-08-15":{"body":"Powell's August 26 Jackson Hole speech triggered an immediate market selloff — the S&P 500 fell ~4% on August 26 alone. The Fed then delivered a 75bp hike in September (its third consecutive), and CPI remained elevated through the summer. Tech (EW) fell -23.3% to its cycle trough on October 14. Crucially, the ctx labels this as 'slowdown/deflation-scare' (NOT stagflation) — Energy led with +5.5% while Real Estate collapsed -25.5% and semis were decimated -29.8% (SMH). TLT fell -14.2% (yields still surging), DXY +6.3% (dollar squeeze tightening financial conditions globally). The October 14 trough coincided with the US September CPI report printing in-line-to-hot, triggering the final capitulation before the AI-driven recovery began.","body_zh":"鲍威尔8月26日杰克逊霍尔演讲引发即时抛售——标普500当天跌约4%。美联储随后在9月再次加息75个基点（连续第三次）。科技（等权）下跌-23.3%，于10月14日触及周期低点。值得注意的是，该段象限为'经济放缓/通缩恐慌'（非滞胀）——能源领涨+5.5%，而房地产崩跌-25.5%，半导体SMH重挫-29.8%。TLT下跌-14.2%（收益率仍在攀升），DXY+6.3%（美元急升全球收紧金融条件）。10月14日低点恰逢美国9月CPI报告出炉（在线偏热），引发最后一轮恐慌出逃，随后AI驱动的复苏就此启动。","drivers":["Jackson Hole Aug-26-2022 Powell hawkish shock","Fed 75bp Sep-2022 third consecutive","semis -29.8% peak rate fear","DXY +6.3% global tightening","TLT -14.2% yields still surging"],"drivers_zh":["2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击","美联储9月第三次75bp加息","半导体-29.8%加息峰值恐慌","DXY+6.3%全球金融条件收紧","TLT -14.2%收益率持续攀升"],"prev_key":"2022-08-15","prev_key_chain":["2022-08-15"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole hawkish shock: final rate-shock leg","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派冲击：最后一轮利率压制","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:peak:2022-08"},"2022-10-14":{"body":"ChatGPT launched November 30, 2022 and gained 100mn users in 2 months, igniting the most powerful AI-driven tech rally in history. Tech (EW) rose +145.7% over 28 months as NVIDIA became the world's most valuable company (passing $3tn market cap in June 2024), driven by insatiable GPU demand from hyperscalers (Meta, Microsoft/OpenAI, Amazon, Google). Semis surged +203.8% (SMH). Breadth was historically narrow: equal-weight lagged SPY by -29.0pp — the most extreme mega-cap concentration in the dataset — as the 'Magnificent 7' (AAPL, MSFT, GOOGL, AMZN, NVDA, META, TSLA) captured the bulk of returns. The goldilocks/growth-up-disinflation quad (CPI fell from 9.1% to 2.4% by Sep-2024, enabling three Fed cuts from Sep-2024) sustained the multiple expansion while earnings growth was real.","body_zh":"ChatGPT于2022年11月30日上线，两个月内用户突破1亿，引燃史上最强AI驱动科技牛市。科技（等权）28个月内上涨+145.7%，英伟达成为全球市值最高公司（2024年6月突破3万亿美元），受超大规模云厂商（Meta、微软/OpenAI、亚马逊、谷歌）GPU需求驱动。半导体SMH飙升+203.8%。市场广度达历史极端偏窄水平：等权落后SPY高达-29.0个百分点——数据集中最极端的大盘股集中度——'七巨头'（苹果、微软、谷歌、亚马逊、英伟达、Meta、特斯拉）包揽绝大部分回报。金发姑娘/增长-去通胀象限（CPI从9.1%降至2024年9月的2.4%，美联储从2024年9月起三次降息）维持估值扩张，与真实盈利增长共振。","drivers":["ChatGPT Nov-2022 100mn users 2 months","NVIDIA GPU hyperscaler demand","Magnificent 7 mega-cap concentration","CPI disinflation 9.1%→2.4% Fed cuts","goldilocks quad growth+disinflation"],"drivers_zh":["ChatGPT 2022年11月两个月用户破亿","英伟达GPU超大规模云厂商需求","'七巨头'大盘股高度集中","CPI从9.1%降至2.4%美联储降息","金发姑娘象限增长+去通胀"],"prev_key":"2022-10-14","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-14"],"status":"exact","title":"AI supercycle: ChatGPT ignites semis +203%, narrow breadth","title_zh":"AI超级周期：ChatGPT引爆半导体+203%，市场极度集中","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:trough:2022-10"},"2025-02-19":{"body":"Two overlapping catalysts triggered the -27.7% selloff. DeepSeek's open-source R1 model (released January 20, 2025) erased ~$600bn from NVIDIA's market cap on January 27 — the largest single-session market cap destruction in history — by suggesting AI compute costs could be dramatically lower (threatening GPU demand narratives). Trump then escalated tariffs aggressively: reciprocal tariffs up to 145% on China were announced April 2, 2025, with the VIX spiking to 52 by April 8. The ctx shows a flight-to-safety rotation: defensives -7.7% vs cyclicals -18.7%, semis -30.1% (SMH), DXY -3.9% (unusual safe-haven dollar weakness, reflecting US policy uncertainty). Tech (EW) -25.7% was the third-worst sector.","body_zh":"两大催化剂叠加引发-27.7%的暴跌。DeepSeek开源R1模型（2025年1月20日发布）于1月27日单日抹去英伟达约6000亿美元市值——史上最大单日市值损失——因其暗示AI算力成本可大幅压缩（动摇GPU需求叙事）。特朗普随后大幅升级关税：4月2日宣布对中国征收高达145%的对等关税，VIX至4月8日飙升至52。避险轮动明显：防御板块-7.7%，周期行业-18.7%，半导体SMH -30.1%，DXY -3.9%（美元异常走弱，反映美国政策不确定性）。科技（等权）-25.7%，为跌幅第三大板块。","drivers":["DeepSeek Jan-20-2025 AI compute shock","Trump 145% China reciprocal tariffs Apr-2025","VIX spike 15→52","semis -30.1% GPU demand fear","dollar weakness DXY -3.9% policy uncertainty"],"drivers_zh":["DeepSeek 2025年1月20日AI算力冲击","特朗普4月对华145%对等关税","VIX从15飙至52","半导体-30.1%GPU需求恐慌","美元走弱DXY -3.9%政策不确定性"],"prev_key":"2025-02-19","prev_key_chain":["2025-02-19"],"status":"exact","title":"DeepSeek shock + Trump tariffs: tech leads selloff","title_zh":"DeepSeek冲击+特朗普关税：科技领跌","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:peak:2025-02"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"The US-China 90-day tariff pause (announced May 12, 2025, cutting reciprocal tariffs from 145% to 30%) catalyzed a V-shaped relief rally. Hyperscaler AI capex commitments accelerated: Microsoft, Google, Amazon, and Meta all guided for record data-center spending in 2025, and semiconductor order books surged. Tech (EW) rallied +156.9% and semis exploded +252.4% (SMH) — the most extreme semi move in the 15-leg dataset — in a tech-led reflation rally (cyclicals +53.6% vs defensives +14.6%). Breadth remained historically narrow (equal-weight lagged SPY -15.2pp), confirming mega-cap concentration. Oil recovered +57.4% and the dollar weakened -3.6% (DXY), both consistent with a global risk-on rotation. The rally peaked on June 2, 2026 at a cycle position now reading 77.1 percentile.","body_zh":"2025年5月12日宣布的美中90天关税暂停（对等关税从145%降至30%）催生V形反弹。超大规模云厂商AI资本开支承诺加速：微软、谷歌、亚马逊、Meta均指引2025年数据中心支出创历史新高，半导体订单激增。科技（等权）反弹+156.9%，半导体SMH爆涨+252.4%——15段数据中最极端的半导体涨幅——科技主导的再通胀行情（周期行业+53.6%，防御板块+14.6%）。市场广度仍历史偏窄（等权落后SPY -15.2个百分点），再次印证大盘股集中。油价回升+57.4%，美元走弱-3.6%（DXY），均与全球风险偏好开启一致。本轮行情于2026年6月2日见顶，当前周期位置读数77.1百分位。","drivers":["US-China 90-day tariff truce May-2025","hyperscaler AI capex record commitments","semis +252% SMH V-shape recovery","VIX collapse 52→16","reflation quad cyclicals+53.6%"],"drivers_zh":["美中90天关税休战2025年5月","超大规模云厂商AI资本开支创历史纪录","半导体SMH+252% V形复苏","VIX从52坍缩至16","再通胀象限周期行业+53.6%"],"prev_key":"2025-04-08","prev_key_chain":["2025-04-08"],"status":"exact","title":"US-China 90-day truce + AI capex surge: semis +252%","title_zh":"美中90天关税休战+AI资本开支激增：半导体+252%","turn_id":"us_sector_tech:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"Technology (Equal-Weight) sits at the Topping phase (77.1 percentile of its historical range) with an RS rank of 10 out of 11 sectors — the top-ranked sector currently. The now_ctx confirms Tech is leading the tape at +24.3% YTD, with semis (SMH) +67.9%, in a reflation/growth-up quad (cyclicals +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%; oil +19.2%). However, a SELL signal is active at cycle position 77.1, consistent with late-cycle topping behavior. Growth-minus-value is deeply negative (-15.2%), a divergence from typical tech leadership regimes that warrants caution. Equal-weight breadth is marginally positive vs cap-weight (+2.9%), suggesting the rally has broadened somewhat but Tech remains the concentrated leader — a setup that historically precedes rotation fatigue.","now_zh":"科技（等权）目前处于周期顶部阶段（历史区间第77.1百分位），相对强度在11个板块中排名第一。当前背景显示科技年初至今涨幅达24.3%，半导体指数（SMH）+67.9%，处于再通胀/增长上行象限（周期性行业平均+11.2%，防御性行业+6.9%；油价+19.2%）。然而，在77.1的周期位置，系统发出卖出信号，与历史上的周期顶部特征一致。成长股相对价值股表现大幅落后（-15.2%），与典型的科技领涨周期形成背离，需保持警惕。等权相对市值加权略为领先（+2.9%），提示涨势有所扩散，但科技仍是集中领涨板块——历史上这类格局往往预示轮动疲劳即将到来。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"b-us_sector_utilities":{"legs":{"2014-01-03":{"body":"Treasury yields fell sharply through 2014 as global growth concerns mounted — the 10-year yield dropped from ~3.0% to ~1.65% by year-end (TLT +36.9%), making high-dividend utilities the preferred bond substitute. Oil cratered 52.6% (Saudi strategy shift, shale supply glut) and the DXY surged 17.3% as the dollar rerated, while defensives as a group gained 28.3% vs cyclicals +6.3% — a classic slowdown/deflation rotation. Utilities led the entire market at +37.2%, powered purely by falling discount rates and income-seeking flows, not sector-specific earnings strength.","body_zh":"2014年美债收益率大幅下行（10年期从约3%跌至年底约1.65%，TLT涨36.9%），在全球增长忧虑加剧背景下，高股息公用事业成为资金追捧的债券替代品。油价暴跌52.6%（沙特策略转变叠加页岩供给过剩），美元指数飙升17.3%，防御板块整体涨28.3% vs 周期板块仅+6.3%——典型的衰退/通缩再配置。公用事业以+37.2%领涨全市场，纯属折现率下行与追息资金驱动，而非行业自身盈利改善。","drivers":["yield collapse / bond proxy","deflation scare / oil crash","flight-to-safety rotation","dollar surge","defensives leadership"],"drivers_zh":["收益率崩塌/债券替代","通缩恐慌/油价暴跌","避险轮动","美元飙升","防御板块领涨"],"prev_key":"2014-01-03","prev_key_chain":["2014-01-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Bond-Proxy Rally on Deflation Scare","title_zh":"通缩恐慌驱动债券替代品大涨","turn_id":"us_sector_utilities:trough:2014-01"},"2015-01-29":{"body":"After peaking in late January 2015, utilities sold off 15.9% as market pricing shifted toward the first Fed rate hike since 2006 — eventually delivered in December 2015. The 10-year Treasury yield rebounded (TLT -8.2%) as disinflation expectations faded and U.S. economic data improved, removing the yield-differential advantage that had powered the 2014 rally. This was a rate-regime reversal, not broad risk-off: Discretionary led (+5.1%), VIX rose from 19 to 28, and the growth-over-value spread actually widened (+5.7), confirming the selloff was driven specifically by the bond-proxy unwind as income investors repositioned ahead of tightening.","body_zh":"2015年1月底公用事业触顶后下跌15.9%，市场开始定价2006年以来首次加息（最终于2015年12月落地）。美国经济数据改善、通缩预期消退推动10年期收益率反弹（TLT下跌8.2%），抹去了2014年公用事业相对债券的股息优势。这是利率机制逆转，而非全面避险：非必需消费品领涨（+5.1%），VIX从19升至28，成长跑赢价值差达+5.7，证实此次下跌为债券替代品解除配置，而非宏观恐慌。","drivers":["Fed rate hike repricing","bond yield reversal (TLT -8.2%)","bond-proxy unwind","growth over defensives","income rotation exit"],"drivers_zh":["美联储加息重新定价","债券收益率逆转（TLT -8.2%）","债券替代品解配","成长跑赢防御","追息资金出逃"],"prev_key":"2015-01-29","prev_key_chain":["2015-01-29"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed Rate Hike Fears Crush Bond Proxies","title_zh":"加息预期重挫债券替代品","turn_id":"us_sector_utilities:peak:2015-01"},"2015-09-04":{"body":"The September 2015 trough marked by China's RMB devaluation (August 11-12, 2015) and Black Monday (August 24, S&P -11% intraday) opened a 26-month, 60.9% utilities rally. The Fed paused its tightening cycle through 2016, holding rates at 0.25%-0.5% for 12 months, and TLT delivered +7.6% as the yield-curve flattened — directly extending the bond-proxy tailwind. In a reflation/growth-up backdrop (VIX normalized from 28 to 12, oil recovered +21%, semis exploded +117.5%), utilities at +49.9% still trailed Tech and Financials but massively beat the broader tape through the combination of yield support, economic stability, and post-China shock repricing of defensive premiums.","body_zh":"2015年9月低点源于中国人民银行8月11-12日人民币贬值及\"黑色星期一\"（标普盘中跌逾11%），此后公用事业展开长达26个月、涨幅60.9%的大牛市。美联储将加息周期暂停约12个月（利率维持0.25%-0.5%），TLT涨7.6%，收益率曲线趋平，债券替代优势持续延伸。在再通胀/增长向上的宏观环境中（VIX从28降至12，油价反弹21%，半导体暴涨117.5%），公用事业涨49.9%，虽落后科技与金融，但凭借股息支撑、经济稳定及中国冲击后防御溢价重新定价，大幅跑赢大盘。","drivers":["China RMB devaluation / Black Monday trough","Fed rate pause 2016","bond yield drift lower (TLT +7.6%)","VIX normalization","reflation recovery"],"drivers_zh":["中国人民币贬值/黑色星期一筑底","美联储2016年暂停加息","债券收益率下行（TLT +7.6%）","VIX正常化","再通胀复苏"],"prev_key":"2015-09-04","prev_key_chain":["2015-09-04"],"status":"exact","title":"China Shock Trough, Fed Pause, Multi-Year Recovery","title_zh":"中国冲击筑底、美联储暂停加息开启多年复苏","turn_id":"us_sector_utilities:trough:2015-09"},"2017-11-14":{"body":"Utilities peaked in mid-November 2017 and fell 15.5% through early February 2018 as the Trump tax reform bill (signed December 22, 2017) triggered reflation expectations and a bond selloff: the 10-year yield rose sharply (TLT -4.6%) and the VIX spiked from 12 to 33 during the February 5 'Volmageddon' volatility implosion. Crucially, the ctx confirms a risk-on rotation: Discretionary (+8.3%), Financials (+4.5%), and Industrials (+3.9%) led while utilities underperformed by the widest margin (-15.6% vs SPY +0.5%). Tax reform mechanically impaired regulated utilities' deferred tax liabilities and implied higher real rates — a dual headwind that ratified the selloff.","body_zh":"公用事业2017年11月中旬触顶，至2018年2月初下跌15.5%。特朗普税改法案（2017年12月22日签署）触发再通胀预期与债券抛售（TLT下跌4.6%，10年期收益率急升），2月5日\"波动末日\"波动率崩塌事件使VIX从12骤升至33。ctx数据确认为风险偏好回升轮动：非必需消费品（+8.3%）、金融（+4.5%）、工业（+3.9%）领涨，公用事业以-15.6%大幅落后于标普+0.5%。税改还从机制上损害了受监管公用事业的递延税负，并隐含更高实际利率，构成双重阻力。","drivers":["tax reform / reflation repricing","bond yield spike (TLT -4.6%)","Volmageddon Feb 2018 VIX spike","cyclical rotation out of defensives","rate-sensitive valuation compression"],"drivers_zh":["税改/再通胀重新定价","债券收益率急升（TLT -4.6%）","2018年2月\"波动末日\"VIX飙升","从防御向周期的轮动","利率敏感型估值压缩"],"prev_key":"2017-11-14","prev_key_chain":["2017-11-14"],"status":"exact","title":"Tax Reform + Rate Spike Crushes Utilities","title_zh":"税改叠加利率飙升重创公用事业","turn_id":"us_sector_utilities:peak:2017-11"},"2018-02-08":{"body":"The February 2018 VIX spike marked the trough for a two-year, 63.4% utilities rally driven by three compounding forces: (1) the Fed's December 2018 peak at 2.5%, followed by three insurance cuts in H2 2019 as trade-war growth fears mounted; (2) Treasury yields falling throughout (TLT +28.9%), compressing the bond-yield alternative to dividends; (3) a slowdown/deflation quad where defensives averaged +39.9% vs cyclicals +23.4% while energy cratered -10.8% and copper-gold fell -36.5%. The narrow-breadth, mega-cap tech tape (SPY +35.7% vs RSP lagging -9.0 points) redirected income flows toward the few sectors offering yield stability. Utilities' +59.2% gain — second only to Tech — confirmed the structural bond-proxy premium in a falling-rate environment.","body_zh":"2018年2月VIX激增事件是两年期63.4%公用事业大牛市的起点，三重力量共同驱动：（1）美联储2018年12月将利率峰值定在2.5%后，受贸易战增长恐慌影响，于2019年下半年三度降息；（2）美债收益率全程下行（TLT+28.9%），压缩了债券相对股息的替代价值；（3）衰退/通缩象限下防御平均+39.9% vs 周期+23.4%，能源暴跌-10.8%，铜金比率下挫36.5%。窄幅大市值科技主导行情（SPY+35.7%，等权落后-9%）将追息资金重新导向提供稳定股息的少数板块。公用事业+59.2%涨幅仅次于科技，再次印证了在降息环境中债券替代品的结构性溢价。","drivers":["Fed 2019 rate cuts / dovish pivot","yield collapse (TLT +28.9%)","trade war / growth scare","defensives over cyclicals in slowdown quad","income rotation / bond proxy"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年降息/鸽派转向","收益率崩塌（TLT +28.9%）","贸易战/增长恐慌","衰退象限防御跑赢周期","追息轮动/债券替代"],"prev_key":"2018-02-08","prev_key_chain":["2018-02-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed Pivot Cycle: Rate Cuts + Recession Fears Fuel 63% Rally","title_zh":"美联储降息周期叠加衰退恐慌推动63%涨幅","turn_id":"us_sector_utilities:trough:2018-02"},"2020-02-18":{"body":"The COVID-19 global pandemic triggered a 33-day, -37.1% crash in utilities from the February 18 market peak to the March 23 trough — matching the scale of a major selloff despite utilities' defensive reputation. VIX exploded from 15 to 62, credit spreads blew out (HYG-LQD -9.4%), and every sector fell in a forced-liquidation cascade. Utilities initially outperformed the broader market in the early February selloff but were caught in the final capitulation wave as investors sold everything liquid to cover margin calls and redemptions. The TLT +14.2% safe-haven bid cushioned somewhat, and utilities' -37.1% loss was still better than Financials (-42.4%) and Energy (-55.5%), but the indiscriminate liquidation overrode the typical defensive floor.","body_zh":"新冠疫情全球大流行引发33天内公用事业暴跌37.1%（从2月18日市场峰值至3月23日谷底），打破了公用事业的防御声誉。VIX从15飙至62，信用利差暴扩（HYG-LQD下跌9.4%），各板块在强制平仓浪潮下全线重挫。公用事业在2月初相对领先，但最终在投资者为应对追保金和赎回而抛售一切流动资产的清算潮中被拖下水。TLT+14.2%的避险需求略提供支撑，公用事业-37.1%仍优于金融（-42.4%）和能源（-55.5%），但无差别抛售覆盖了正常的防御底部。","drivers":["COVID pandemic forced liquidation","VIX spike 15→62 (extreme panic)","margin call / redemption cascade","credit spread blowout (HYG-LQD -9.4%)","energy and oil collapse"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情强制平仓","VIX飙升15→62（极端恐慌）","追保金/赎回级联踩踏","信用利差暴扩（HYG-LQD -9.4%）","能源与油价崩溃"],"prev_key":"2020-02-18","prev_key_chain":["2020-02-18"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID Pandemic Panic Selloff","title_zh":"新冠疫情恐慌性抛售","turn_id":"us_sector_utilities:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From the March 23 COVID trough utilities rallied 89.6% over 25 months as the Fed cut rates to zero and Congress delivered $5+ trillion in fiscal stimulus, but this leg was characterized by structural underperformance vs the reflationary tape. Cyclicals averaged +147.9% vs defensives +83.4% — Energy surged +277%, Materials +145%, Financials +123%, while utilities lagged at +81.9%. The critical headwind emerged through 2021: the 10-year yield rose sharply from 0.5% to 1.8% by year-end (TLT -24.4% over the full leg), eroding utilities' yield advantage. Oil's +340% recovery and copper-gold at +94.8% confirmed sustained reflation that systematically favored cyclicals over bond proxies.","body_zh":"从2020年3月23日新冠低点起，公用事业在25个月内上涨89.6%。美联储将利率压至零、国会注入逾5万亿美元财政刺激，但本轮走势总体落后于再通胀行情。周期股平均涨幅+147.9% vs 防御板块+83.4%——能源+277%、材料+145%、金融+123%，公用事业仅+81.9%垫底防御组。关键阻力来自2021年：10年期收益率从0.5%升至年底1.8%（完整周期TLT-24.4%），侵蚀了股息相对优势。油价+340%复苏与铜金比率+94.8%确认持续再通胀，系统性利好周期而非债券替代品。","drivers":["zero-rate fiscal stimulus recovery","reflation quad / cyclicals domination","rising yields (TLT -24.4%) headwind late cycle","oil/commodity super-cycle","COVID infrastructure demand boost"],"drivers_zh":["零利率财政刺激复苏","再通胀象限/周期股主导","收益率上行阻力（TLT -24.4%）","油价/大宗商品超级周期","新冠基建需求提振"],"prev_key":"2020-03-23","prev_key_chain":["2020-03-23"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-COVID Fiscal Stimulus Recovery, Rising Rates Headwind","title_zh":"新冠后财政刺激复苏，利率上行构成阻力","turn_id":"us_sector_utilities:trough:2020-03"},"2022-04-20":{"body":"Utilities peaked in late April 2022 — having ridden the reflation wave — and sold off 16.0% through June 17 as the Fed's 75bp rate hike campaign (first delivered June 15, 2022) became entrenched. The 10-year yield surged from ~1.8% to ~3.5% (TLT -7.5%), the DXY rose 4.3%, and VIX climbed from 20 to 31. The selloff was broad-based stagflation stress rather than pure utilities weakness — Energy (-8.9%) was the only relative winner while Real Estate (-22.8%) and Discretionary (-25.1%) led declines — but utilities' high debt loads and dividend-yield competition with rising Treasuries made it a specific target for bond-proxy derating.","body_zh":"公用事业2022年4月下旬触顶（此前搭乘再通胀顺风），随后随美联储75个基点加息周期确立（2022年6月15日首次落地）下跌16.0%至6月17日低点。10年期收益率从约1.8%升至约3.5%（TLT -7.5%），美元指数涨4.3%，VIX从20升至31。此次下跌是滞胀压力下的全面回调，而非公用事业单独承压——能源（-8.9%）是唯一相对赢家，地产（-22.8%）和非必需消费（-25.1%）跌幅最大，但公用事业高负债率与美国国债收益率竞争股息吸引力，构成特定的债券替代品估值重杀因素。","drivers":["Fed 75bp hike cycle June 2022","bond yield surge (TLT -7.5%)","stagflation macro regime","bond-proxy yield derating","dollar strength / DXY +4.3%"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2022年6月75bp加息周期","债券收益率急升（TLT -7.5%）","滞胀宏观机制","债券替代股息溢价重杀","美元走强/DXY +4.3%"],"prev_key":"2022-04-20","prev_key_chain":["2022-04-20"],"status":"exact","title":"Aggressive Fed Tightening Hits Rate-Sensitive Sector","title_zh":"美联储激进加息重压利率敏感板块","turn_id":"us_sector_utilities:peak:2022-04"},"2022-06-17":{"body":"From the June 17, 2022 broad market lows (S&P -24% YTD at that point), utilities staged a 21.6% rally through September 12 — the strongest performer alongside Discretionary (+22.7%) — as peak-inflation narratives took hold following June CPI at 9.1% (the July CPI print, released August 10, came in at 8.5%, below expectations). The broader market also bounced +12.3%, VIX fell from 31 to 24, and credit spreads tightened (HYG-LQD +4.5%) in a uniform risk-on relief rally. Utilities benefited both from the bear-market-bounce beta and renewed speculation that the Fed might downshift its tightening pace, though TLT still fell -3.6% indicating yields held elevated.","body_zh":"从2022年6月17日大盘大幅下跌低点（标普年内跌24%）起，公用事业反弹21.6%至9月12日，与非必需消费品（+22.7%）共同领涨，背后是通胀见顶叙事——6月CPI高达9.1%，但8月10日公布的7月CPI为8.5%，低于预期。大盘同期亦反弹+12.3%，VIX从31降至24，信用利差收窄（HYG-LQD +4.5%），呈现整体性风险偏好修复。公用事业受益于熊市反弹的贝塔敞口，同时市场重新押注美联储可能放缓加息节奏，但TLT仍下跌3.6%表明收益率维持高位。","drivers":["peak-inflation narrative / CPI surprise","bear market technical bounce","Fed downshift speculation","VIX compression (31→24)","credit spread tightening"],"drivers_zh":["通胀见顶叙事/CPI意外低于预期","熊市技术性反弹","美联储放缓加息预期","VIX压缩（31→24）","信用利差收窄"],"prev_key":"2022-06-17","prev_key_chain":["2022-06-17"],"status":"exact","title":"Bear Market Bounce on Peak Inflation Hopes","title_zh":"通胀见顶预期推动熊市反弹","turn_id":"us_sector_utilities:trough:2022-06"},"2022-09-12":{"body":"Powell's August 26, 2022 Jackson Hole speech — 'we must keep at it until the job is done' — reset rate expectations sharply higher, triggering a September-October selloff where utilities cratered -19.6% (worst relative performer alongside Real Estate at -20.9%) while only Energy (-1.3%) and Health Care (-6.8%) held in. The 10-year yield spiked further (TLT -6.4%), DXY added 4.6%, and VIX rose from 24 to 34 — a precise replay of the 2022 rate-shock transmission mechanism hitting levered, long-duration sectors hardest. The narrow CTX pattern (defensives -12.0% vs cyclicals -11.6%) confirms this was a broad rate-panic de-rating, not a rotation into cyclicals.","body_zh":"鲍威尔2022年8月26日杰克逊霍尔演讲（\"我们必须坚持到底\"）令利率预期急剧上修，引发9至10月公用事业暴跌19.6%（与地产-20.9%并列最差），仅能源（-1.3%）和医疗（-6.8%）相对抗跌。10年期收益率进一步飙升（TLT -6.4%），美元指数+4.6%，VIX从24升至34——精准再现了2022年利率冲击对高杠杆、长久期板块的传导机制。防御板块（-12.0%）与周期股（-11.6%）跌幅接近，证实这是广泛的利率恐慌性估值重杀，而非周期性轮动。","drivers":["Jackson Hole hawkish speech Aug 2022","bond yield spike (TLT -6.4%)","long-duration derating","DXY strength +4.6%","VIX spike 24→34"],"drivers_zh":["2022年8月杰克逊霍尔鹰派演讲","债券收益率急升（TLT -6.4%）","长久期资产重杀","美元走强+4.6%","VIX飙升24→34"],"prev_key":"2022-09-12","prev_key_chain":["2022-09-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Jackson Hole Hawkishness Crushes Bond Proxies","title_zh":"杰克逊霍尔鹰派立场重压债券替代品","turn_id":"us_sector_utilities:peak:2022-09"},"2022-10-12":{"body":"The October 12, 2022 CPI print (September data: 8.2% vs 8.1% expected) paradoxically triggered a massive market reversal — initially down hard, then reversing sharply upward as investors concluded inflation had structurally peaked. The 10-year yield fell (TLT +7.8%), DXY collapsed -8.2%, and utilities gained +18.1% in just two months alongside Materials (+20.8%) and Industrials (+19.3%). The dollar weakness directly boosted cyclicals and international earners, while falling yields restored utilities' bond-proxy premium. Value outperformed growth significantly (growth-value -4.4%), and the Fed's December 2022 downshift to 50bp from 75bp (signaled November 30 by Powell) confirmed the peak-hike narrative driving the broad-market 12.7% SPY rally.","body_zh":"2022年10月12日CPI数据（9月同比8.2%，略高于预期8.1%）引发戏剧性市场反转——先急跌后强力回升，因投资者判断通胀已结构性见顶。10年期收益率下行（TLT +7.8%），美元指数暴跌8.2%，公用事业仅用两个月涨幅达+18.1%，与材料（+20.8%）和工业（+19.3%）共同领涨。美元走弱直接提振周期股和国际敞口，收益率下行恢复了公用事业的债券替代溢价。价值大幅跑赢成长（价值-成长差+4.4%）；美联储于11月30日鲍威尔讲话中预示12月加息缩窄至50bp，确认了驱动标普+12.7%的\"加息见顶\"叙事。","drivers":["CPI peak inflation confirmed Oct 2022","yield retreat (TLT +7.8%)","DXY collapse -8.2%","Fed downshift to 50bp Dec 2022","bond-proxy premium restoration"],"drivers_zh":["2022年10月CPI确认通胀见顶","收益率下行（TLT +7.8%）","美元指数暴跌8.2%","美联储12月降速至50bp","债券替代溢价恢复"],"prev_key":"2022-10-12","prev_key_chain":["2022-10-12"],"status":"exact","title":"CPI Surprise Sparks Yield Retreat and Utilities Recovery","title_zh":"CPI意外触顶引发收益率下行与公用事业修复","turn_id":"us_sector_utilities:trough:2022-10"},"2022-12-13":{"body":"From December 2022 through October 2, 2023, utilities fell -15.7% in a prolonged 9.5-month drawdown driven by two reinforcing forces: (1) the 2023 AI/tech mega-cap boom (Comm +31.6%, Tech +23.6%) redirected all marginal flows into growth, leaving defensives structurally stranded (-11.7% avg); (2) the 10-year yield continued to surge (TLT -17.1%) reaching 4.98% by October 2023, making Treasury yields a direct competitor to utility dividends for the first time since the mid-2000s. The narrow breadth (RSP-SPY -11.1%), growth outperforming value by 19.9 points, and semis +29.9% confirm this was a momentum/AI-driven capital flight from defensives — the exact mirror of the 2014 dynamic.","body_zh":"2022年12月至2023年10月2日，公用事业在长达9.5个月的持续回调中下跌15.7%，两股力量相互叠加：（1）2023年AI/科技大市值热潮（通讯+31.6%，科技+23.6%）将全部边际资金导向成长方向，防御板块结构性滞涨（平均-11.7%）；（2）10年期收益率持续攀升（TLT -17.1%），至2023年10月触及4.98%，美国国债收益率与公用事业股息的竞争关系达到2000年代中期以来最激烈水平。窄幅广度（RSP-SPY -11.1%）、成长跑赢价值19.9个百分点、半导体+29.9%，均证实这是AI动能驱动的资金出逃，与2014年防御领涨时的逻辑恰好相反。","drivers":["AI/tech mega-cap boom 2023","bond yield surge (TLT -17.1%)","Treasury yield vs dividend competition","narrow mega-cap breadth (RSP-SPY -11.1%)","capital flight from defensives"],"drivers_zh":["2023年AI/科技大市值热潮","债券收益率急升（TLT -17.1%）","国债收益率竞争股息吸引力","窄幅大市值广度（RSP-SPY -11.1%）","资金逃离防御板块"],"prev_key":"2022-12-13","prev_key_chain":["2022-12-13"],"status":"exact","title":"AI Tech Boom + Stubborn Yields Punish Defensives","title_zh":"AI科技热潮叠加收益率高企重压防御板块","turn_id":"us_sector_utilities:peak:2022-12"},"2023-10-02":{"body":"The October 2, 2023 trough launched a 95.3% rally to the February 27, 2026 peak — utilities' largest gain in the dataset — powered by two structural developments: (1) the AI/data-center electricity demand supercycle, with data center power demand projected to nearly double by 2028, utilities stocks gained ~$500bn in value in 2024-2025 as hyperscalers signed long-term power purchase agreements directly with regulated utilities; (2) the Fed's November 2023 pivot (last hike July 2023, first cut September 2024) and TLT +15.2% yield decline compressed discount rates. The goldilocks/disinflation quad (oil -24.5%, DXY -8.7%) was supportive but utilities outperformed most defensives by running as a growth story on power infrastructure capex, not just as a bond proxy.","body_zh":"2023年10月2日低点开启了至2026年2月27日峰值的95.3%大牛市，是本数据集中公用事业最大涨幅，由两大结构性发展驱动：（1）AI/数据中心电力需求超级周期——数据中心电力需求预计至2028年近乎翻倍，超大规模科技公司与受监管公用事业直接签订长期购电协议，公用事业板块2024-2025年市值增逾5000亿美元；（2）美联储2023年11月政策转向（最后一次加息2023年7月，首次降息2024年9月）和TLT +15.2%收益率下行压缩了折现率。黄金期/去通胀象限（油价-24.5%，美元-8.7%）提供支撑，但公用事业以电力基础设施资本支出增长故事（而非纯粹债券替代）的身份，跑赢大多数防御板块。","drivers":["AI data center electricity demand supercycle","Fed pivot / rate cuts (Sep 2024)","yield decline (TLT +15.2%)","dollar weakness (DXY -8.7%)","utility capex / power purchase agreements"],"drivers_zh":["AI数据中心电力需求超级周期","美联储转向/降息（2024年9月）","收益率下行（TLT +15.2%）","美元走弱（DXY -8.7%）","公用事业资本支出/购电协议"],"prev_key":"2023-10-02","prev_key_chain":["2023-10-02"],"status":"exact","title":"AI Power Demand + Fed Pivot Drive 95% Rally","title_zh":"AI电力需求叠加美联储转向驱动95%涨幅","turn_id":"us_sector_utilities:trough:2023-10"}},"now":"Utilities (Equal-Weight) is in a Bottoming / Trough phase as of late June 2026, sitting near the 14th percentile of its historical range (pos=14.3) with an RS rank of 35 — deeply lagging the reflation-led tape where Tech (+24%), Energy (+21%), and Industrials (+16%) are dominating. The current macro quad is reflation/growth-up, exactly the environment that structurally disadvantages rate-sensitive defensives: cyclicals are running +11.2% vs defensives +6.9%, high-beta is beating low-vol by +20.7 points, and oil is up 19.2%. The sector is technically above its 200-day moving average and has triggered a cycle BUY signal — consistent with a late-cycle trough where rich cyclical valuations and extreme breadth divergence historically precede a mean-reversion bid into defensives. The AI data-center power demand secular tailwind (a multi-year capex supercycle for grid buildout) provides a fundamental floor, but the immediate macro setup remains a headwind until growth/reflation momentum stalls or rate expectations soften.","now_zh":"公用事业（等权）截至2026年6月下旬处于筑底/低谷阶段，历史区间位仅14.3分位，相对强度排名35——远落后于由再通胀主导的行情（科技+24%、能源+21%、工业+16%领涨）。当前宏观象限为再通胀/增长向上，正是利率敏感型防御板块结构性承压的环境：周期股跑赢防御股（+11.2% vs +6.9%），高Beta跑赢低波动达+20.7个百分点，油价涨幅19.2%。板块在技术上仍处于200日均线之上，并触发了周期BUY信号——这与历史上周期性低点特征吻合，在该时点大盘周期股估值偏贵、广度背离极端，历史上往往预示防御板块将迎来均值回归行情。AI数据中心电力需求驱动的多年资本支出超级周期提供了基本面底部支撑，但在增长/再通胀动能放缓或利率预期软化之前，近期宏观环境仍是阻力。","as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-06-27","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":16,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}}};
